COLLDATA("bazzar","en",[[1,"Do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity'? They said: 'Yes.'"],[2,"\"No prophet was ever taken in death until a man from his community led him (in prayer).\""],[3,"Some men among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, when the Messenger of God ﷺ died, grieved over him so intensely that some of them became afflicted with whispering (waswasa). 'Uthman said: 'I was among them. While I was sitting in one of the forts, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ passed by me and greeted me, but I did not notice him. 'Umar went on until he entered upon Abu Bakr—may God have mercy on them both—and said: 'Shall I tell you something astonishing? I passed by 'Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting.' So Abu Bakr and 'Umar came together until they arrived and both greeted me. Abu Bakr said: 'Your brother 'Umar came to me and claimed that he passed by you and greeted you, but you did not return the greeting.' 'Uthman said: 'I said: By God, I did not notice you when you passed or greeted.' Abu Bakr said: ''Uthman has spoken the truth; some matter must have preoccupied you from that.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is it?' I said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken before I could ask him about the salvation of this matter.' Abu Bakr, may God have mercy on him, said: 'I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that.' 'Uthman said: 'I said: May my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[4,"'Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us, from 'Abdullah b. Bishr, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from 'Uthman b. 'Affan, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, a narration similar to this hadith. Abu Bakr said: 'I do not think except that 'Abdullah b. Bishr is the one who erred, and the hadith is the hadith of Ma'mar and Salih b. Kaysan along with those who concurred with them. Muhammad b. 'Umar al-Waqidi narrated it from Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from 'Abdullah b. 'Amr, from 'Uthman, from Abu Bakr. And Abu Bakr said: This hadith is among those in which Muhammad b. 'Umar was not followed in his narration. We only wanted to mention it so that it may be known that he narrated it in this way.'"],[5,"\"No Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then comes to the mosque and prays two rak'ahs in it, then asks God for forgiveness, except that God forgives him.\""],[6,"The Messenger ﷺ said, then he mentioned something similar. Abu Bakr said: 'Sa'd b. Sa'id and 'Abdullah b. Sa'id—their hadiths in this have some weakness. Yet a group has narrated from both of them and from each of them individually, and we only write from their hadiths what has also been narrated from the Messenger of God—may peace and blessings be upon him—albeit through a different chain. This statement has also been narrated by Asma' b. al-Hakam from 'Ali from Abu Bakr.'"],[7,"\"No Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then comes to the mosque and prays two rak'ahs, then asks God for forgiveness, except that God forgives him.\""],[8,"Mis'ar and Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Uthman b. al-Mughirah, from 'Ali b. Rabi'ah, from Asma' b. al-Hakam, from 'Ali, from Abu Bakr. Sufyan raised it (to the Prophet), while Mis'ar did not raise it, and he mentioned something similar."],[9,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Uthman b. al-Mughirah, from 'Ali b. Rabi'ah, from Asma' b. al-Hakam al-Fazari, from 'Ali, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the like of the hadith of Shu'bah."],[10,"Sharik narrated to us, from 'Uthman b. al-Mughirah, from 'Ali b. Rabi'ah, from Asma' b. al-Hakam, from 'Ali, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar hadith to that of Shu'bah. Abu Bakr said: 'This statement—we do not know that it is narrated from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, except through these two routes. And the saying of 'Ali: \"I was a man who, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ...\"—this is only narrated by Asma' b. al-Hakam, and Asma' is unknown; he did not narrate anything other than this hadith, and no one narrated from him except 'Ali b. Rabi'ah. And the statement itself is not narrated from 'Ali except through this route.'"],[11,"That the two of them gave him glad tidings that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Ask, and you will be given.'"],[12,"That the two of them gave him glad tidings that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.'"],[13,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, al-'Abbas disputed with 'Ali concerning things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had left behind. They brought their dispute to Abu Bakr ؓ and asked him to divide it between them, but he refused and said: 'Something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left behind — I would not introduce anything new regarding it.'"],[14,"When \"Perish the hands of Abu Lahab\" was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came while the Messenger of Allah was sitting, and with him was Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said to him, 'If only you would move aside so she does not harm you, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A barrier will be placed between me and her.' She came forward until she stood before Abu Bakr and said, 'O Abu Bakr, has your companion satirized us?' Abu Bakr said, 'No, by the Lord of this building, he does not utter poetry or speak it.' She said, 'You are indeed truthful.' When she turned away, Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, said, 'Did she see you?' He said, 'No, an angel kept shielding me until she left.'"],[15,"When the polytheists expelled the Prophet ﷺ from Makkah, Abu Bakr ؓ said, 'They have expelled their Prophet; they will surely perish.' Then this verse was revealed: 'Permission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged.'"],[16,"Qays also narrated it from al-A'mash, from Muslim, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas. 'Umar b. al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. Yusuf narrated to us, from Qays."],[17,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, they differed about his burial. Abu Bakr said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No prophet passes away but he is buried where he passed away.'"],[18,"The Prophet ﷺ ate bread and meat, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[19,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this verse was revealed: 'Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it, and he will not find for himself besides Allah any protector or helper.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Abu Bakr, shall I not recite to you a verse that has been revealed to me?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'So he recited it to me.' I do not know except that I felt a break in my back, so I stretched for it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What is the matter with you, O Abu Bakr?' I said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. Which of us has not done evil? Indeed we will be recompensed for what we have done.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for you, O Abu Bakr, and your companions, the believers, you will be recompensed for that in this world until you meet Allah, and you will have no sins. As for the others, that will be accumulated for them until they are recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[20,"Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it in this world."],[21,"Whose feet become dusty in the cause of Allah, Allah has forbidden them to the Fire."],[22,"Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, stood among us and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I am standing among you today and said: 'People have not been given anything better than pardon and well-being, so ask Allah for them.'"],[23,"You have not been given, after the word of sincerity, anything better than well-being, so ask Allah for well-being."],[24,"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity."],[25,"Muhammad b. 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah's mercy be upon them both, something similar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith and connected it except Hammad b. Salamah, while 'Abd al-Wahhab and others narrate it from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, in mursal form."],[26,"In the story of Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan, he said: The Prophet ﷺ said to him when he wanted to slaughter a sheep: \"Beware of the one with milk.\""],[27,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act in a matter already decreed and finished, or in a matter newly begun? He said: \"No, rather in a matter already decreed and finished.\" I said: Then what is action for? He said: \"Act, for everyone is facilitated for what he was created.\""],[28,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication to call upon Allah with. He said: \"Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with a forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me. Indeed, You are the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\""],[29,"Abu Bakr ؓ wrote to 'Amr b. al-'As: To proceed: You have known the bequest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the Ansar at his death: \"Accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.\""],[30,"Abu Bakr ؓ sent for me and said: Gather the Qur'an, for you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah."],[31,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon us while we were in the Rawdah, ascended the minbar, praised and extolled Allah, then said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on these planks last year: \"No servant has been given anything better than excellent certainty and well-being, so ask Allah for excellent certainty and well-being.\""],[32,"Abu Bakr ؓ would not turn around during his prayer."],[33,"I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say — and he wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah, then it passed from him, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in this heat, or in heat like this: \"Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[34,"\"Am I not the most entitled of the people to it? Am I not the first to embrace Islam? Am I not the companion of such and such? Am I not the companion of such and such?\""],[35,"I said while we were in the cave: O Messenger of Allah, if a man were to look down he would see us. He said: \"What do you think of two when Allah is their third?\" And one of them said in his hadith: If one of them were to look at the place of his foot, he would see us. So he said: \"What do you think of two when Allah is their third?\""],[36,"After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr said: Let us go and visit Umm Ayman as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit her."],[37,"\"I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property, except for its due, and their reckoning is with Allah.\""],[38,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing those who pray.\""],[39,"That Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, when he was appointed caliph, sent him to Bahrain and wrote for him this document: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is the obligatory charity that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed on the Muslims, which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever among the believers is asked for it in its proper manner, let him give it. Whoever is asked above it, let him not give it. For twenty-four camels or less: for every five, a sheep. When they reach twenty-five up to thirty-five, there is a yearling female camel (bint makhad). If there is no yearling female camel, then a two-year-old male camel (ibn labun). When they reach thirty-six up to forty-five, there is a two-year-old female camel (bint labun). When they reach forty-six up to sixty, there is a three-year-old female camel (hiqqah) up to sixty. When they reach sixty-one, there is a four-year-old female camel (jadha'ah) up to seventy-five. When they reach seventy-six, there are two two-year-old female camels (bint labun) up to ninety. When they reach ninety-one up to one hundred and twenty, there are two three-year-old female camels (hiqqah), able to be mounted by a male camel. When they exceed one hundred and twenty, in every forty there is a two-year-old female camel, and in every fifty there is a three-year-old female camel. If someone's charity reaches a jadha'ah and he does not have a jadha'ah, but he has a hiqqah, it is accepted from him and he gives along with it two sheep if it is easy for him, or twenty dirhams. If someone's charity reaches a hiqqah and he does not have a hiqqah, but he has a jadha'ah, it is accepted from him as a jadha'ah, and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep. If someone's charity reaches a hiqqah and he has nothing but a bint labun, it is accepted from him, and he gives the collector two sheep or twenty dirhams. If someone's charity reaches a bint labun and he has a hiqqah, the hiqqah is accepted from him, and the collector gives him two sheep or twenty dirhams. He said: There is no charity on grazing sheep until they reach forty, nor on their increase until they reach one hundred and twenty. When they increase by one over one hundred and twenty, there are two sheep up to two hundred. When they exceed two hundred, there are three sheep up to three hundred. When they exceed three hundred, in every hundred sheep there is one sheep."],[40,"That Abu Bakr, when he was appointed caliph, wrote for him a document containing the obligatory charity that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed on the Muslims."],[41,"Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet ﷺ..."],[42,"\"No body nourished with forbidden sustenance will enter Paradise, nor will one with evil character enter Paradise. Cursed is the one who harms a Muslim or deceives him.\""],[43,"We were with Abu Bakr ؓ when he asked for water. He was brought water and honey. When he put it to his hand, he wept and sobbed until we thought something was wrong with him, but we did not ask him about anything. When he finished, we said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, what made you weep? He said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I saw him pushing something away from himself, but I saw nothing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it that I see you pushing away from yourself, but I see nothing? He said: The world was extended to me. I said: Away from me! It said to me: Indeed, you will not catch me. Abu Bakr said: It distressed me and I feared that I had contradicted the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the world had caught up with me."],[44,"\"Gold for gold, silver for silver, like for like. The one who increases and the one who seeks increase are in the Fire.\""],[45,"Abdullah b. Shawdhab narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughirah b. Subay', from 'Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet..."],[46,"\"Indeed, the Dajjal will emerge from a land called Khurasan in the east. He will be followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields.\""],[47,"Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughirah b. Subay', from 'Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah did not hear from Abu al-Tayyah. They think he only heard it from Ibn Shawdhab, or it reached him from him and he narrated it from Abu al-Tayyah. Ibn Abi 'Arubah used to narrate from a group, sending from them without hearing from them, and he did not say."],[48,"I was with Abu Bakr ؓ when he became angry with a man. I said: Shall I strike his neck? He said: That is not for anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[49,"Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us. Until when he drew near to us, and between us and him was the distance of two or three spears, I said, \"This is the pursuer who has caught up with us, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: And I wept, so he said, \"Why do you weep?\" I said, \"By Allah, I do not weep for myself, but I weep for you.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against him: \"Suffice us against him.\" Then his horse sank into the ground up to its belly, and he leapt from it to the ground and called out, \"O Muhammad, I think this is from you or your doing, so supplicate to Allah to save me from what I am in. By Allah, I will blind those behind me of the pursuers, and take an arrow from me, for you will pass by camels of mine at such-and-such a place, so take from them whatever you wish.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"We have no need of them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him, and he departed and returned to his companions. And I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached Madinah, and the people met him on the roads: women and servants in the roads saying, \"Allah is greatest! Muhammad has come, the Messenger of Allah has come.\" And the people disputed as to which of them he would stay with, so the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"We will stay tonight with Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of 'Abd al-Muttalib, to honor them by that.\" Then morning came and he went where he was commanded. Al-Bara' said: And the first to come to us was 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ with twenty riders, so we said, \"What has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ done?\" He said, \"He is on my track.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come until I had recited some surahs from the Mufassal."],[50,"Israel narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara', from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. : :"],[51,"Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Drink.\" So he drank until I was satisfied."],[52,"I saw Abu Bakr ؓ meet al-Hasan b. 'Ali, and he began saying, \"By my father, he resembles the Prophet, not resembling 'Ali,\" while his father 'Ali was laughing or almost laughing."],[53,"Fatimah, may Allah have mercy on her, sent to Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him: \"O successor of the Messenger of Allah, did you inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or his family?\" He said, \"Rather his family.\" She said, \"Then what about the share of the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'When Allah feeds a prophet a grant, then takes his soul, it belongs to the one who stands after him.' So I saw fit to return it to the Muslims.\" She said, \"You and the Messenger of Allah know best.\""],[54,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent back Ma'iz four times, then ordered him to be stoned."],[55,"When this verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet,' I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will not speak to you except as a confidant speaks in secret.\""],[56,"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity."],[57,"I recited about my father: 'A fair-faced one by whose face rain is sought, a spring for orphans, a protection for widows.' My father said, \"That is the Messenger of Allah.\""],[58,"When he wanted a matter, he would say, \"O Allah, choose for me and select for me.\""],[59,"No prophet is taken but he is buried where he is taken."],[60,"'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'A'ishah, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. Abu Bakr said: And this speech, we do not know that anyone narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ except Abu Bakr, and it was narrated from Abu Bakr by Ibn 'Abbas and 'A'ishah."],[61,"He said: 'Shall I not teach you a supplication that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me?' And he said: 'Isa ﷺ used to teach it to the disciples. If you had a debt like Mount Uhud, then you recited it, Allah would settle it for you.' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, reliever of distress, remover of grief, answerer of the call of the distressed, Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter, You are my Merciful, so have mercy on me with a mercy that suffices me from all besides You.'"],[62,"When the people turned away from the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I was the first to return to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I began looking at a man fighting in front of him, and I said: 'Be Talhah.' He said: 'Then I looked, and there was a person behind me as if he were a bird, and I did not realize that he had reached me until it was Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. And there was Talhah lying wounded in front of him. He said: \"Here is your brother, for he has fulfilled his duty.\" So we left him and turned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been struck in his face with two arrows. I wanted to pull them out, but Abu Ubaydah kept asking me and imploring me until I left it to him. He removed one of the two arrows, biting down on it with his teeth, and pulled it out. One of his front teeth fell out. Then he kept asking me and imploring me to let him remove the other. He placed his front tooth on the arrow and bit down hard, hating to cause pain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by it moving, and he removed it. His front tooth or one of his front teeth fell out. He said: 'And Abu Ubaydah became broken-toothed.'"],[63,"When Abdullah b. Abi Bakr died and was wept over, Abu Bakr ؓ came out and said: 'I apologize to you regarding the matter of these women, for they are newly out of ignorance. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The dead is tormented by the weeping of the living.\""],[64,"O people, you recite this verse: \"O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.\" And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When my Ummah sees an oppressor and does not restrain him, Allah will soon afflict them all with punishment from Him.\""],[65,"Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet."],[66,"Rawh narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet."],[67,"Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Mutamir, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ. And this hadith has been transmitted as marfu' from Shubah by Muadh b. Muadh, Rawh b. Ubadah, and Uthman b. Umar. Bayan narrated it from Qays, from Abu Bakr, as mawquf. Mujalid narrated it from Qays, from Abu Bakr, and Said b. Zayd, the brother of Hammad, transmitted it from him as marfu'."],[68,"O people, you recite this verse: \"O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.\" And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When my Ummah sees an oppressor and does not restrain him, Allah will soon afflict them all with punishment from Him.\""],[69,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found that he had passed away. I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Disbelief in Allah is disavowing one's lineage, even if it is remote.\""],[70,"Al-Dahhak b. Uthman narrated to us, from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yarbu, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet."],[71,"He was asked: 'What is the birr (righteousness) of Hajj?' He replied: 'Al-ajj (raising the voice in talbiyah) and al-thajj (slaughtering the sacrificial animal).'"],[72,"What is between my house and my prayer place is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[73,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood among the people, praised and extolled Allah, then said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us last year and was moved to tears, and wept, then sat down. Then he stood again and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us last year and said: You must be truthful, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness. Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not sever ties with one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers, as Allah has commanded you. Ask Allah for well-being, for no servant is given anything better than well-being after certainty."],[74,"It was shown to me what will happen until the Day of Resurrection, of the affairs of this world and the Hereafter. The first and the last were gathered on one plain, and the people were terrified by that, until they went to Adam ﷺ , while sweat nearly bridled them. They said: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, and Allah chose you; intercede for us with your Lord. He said: I have met the like of what you have met. Go to your father; go to Noah. Allah chose Adam and Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of Imran above the worlds. He said: So they go to Noah and say: Intercede for us with your Lord, for Allah chose you and answered your supplication, and you did not leave on the earth any of the disbelievers. He says: That is not with me; go to Abraham. So they go to Abraham and say the like of that to him, and he says: That is not with me; go to Moses, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, spoke to him directly. Moses says: That is not with me; go to Jesus, for he healed the blind and the leper and revived the dead by Allah's permission. Jesus says: That is not with me, but go to the master of the children of Adam, Muhammad ﷺ, for he is the first from whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection. Go to Muhammad, and let him intercede for you with your Lord. Then Gabriel ﷺ comes to his Lord, and He, Blessed and Exalted, says: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. I think he said: Gabriel brings him, and he falls prostrate for the length of a week. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. He said: So he raises his head, and when he looks at his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, he falls prostrate for another week. Then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: O Muhammad, raise your head, intercede and your intercession will be accepted, and ask and you will be given. So he goes and falls prostrate, and Gabriel takes hold of his upper arms, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, opens for him from supplication what He has never opened for anyone. He says: O Lord, You made me the master of the children of Adam and the first from whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. And he mentioned the cistern, saying: Its width—I think he said—is between San'a and Aylah. Then it is said: Call the truthful ones. He said: They intercede. He said: Then it is said: Call the prophets. He said: A prophet comes with a group, and a prophet with five or six, and a prophet with no one. Then it is said: Call the martyrs. He said: They intercede for whom they wish. When the martyrs have done that, he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful. Admit—meaning—into Paradise those who did not associate anything with Allah. He said: So they enter Paradise. And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Look at those in the Fire; is there anyone left who ever did any good? They say: No, I think. He said: So a man is brought, and He says: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I used to be lenient with people in trade. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Be lenient with My servant as he was lenient with My servants. Then they bring out another man from the Fire, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I commanded my children, when I die, to burn me in the fire, then grind me until I am like kohl, then go with me to the sea and scatter me in the wind. He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Why did you do that? He says: Out of fear of You. He says: Look at the kingdom of the greatest king; you have the like of it, or you shall have the like of it. He said: That is the one at which I laughed from the forenoon. And this hadith is a hadith in which there are two men whom we do not know to have narrated anything except this hadith: Abu Hunaydah al-Bara' b. Nawfal, for we do not know that he narrated any hadith other than this, and likewise al-An, we do not know that he narrated except this hadith, even though this chain, despite what is in it of the chain we mentioned, has been narrated by a group of eminent scholars by transmission, and they accepted it."],[75,"None of you should perform ablution from food that he has eaten, if it was lawful for him to eat it."],[76,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Asma' bint 'Umays, when she gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr, to perform ghusl and enter ihram."],[77,"I brought Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Why did you not leave the old man until I came to him? I said: Rather, he is more deserving to come to you. He said: We preserve him for the favors of his son toward us."],[78,"Umar said to Abu Bakr: O best of people. Abu Bakr said: Since you have said that, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The sun has not risen on anyone better than Umar."],[79,"My father died owing a debt. I offered his creditors to take the dates for what was owed, but they refused and did not see in it full repayment. So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: When you harvest it and place it in the drying yard, inform me. When I harvested it and placed it in the drying yard, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he came with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah have mercy on them. He sat and invoked blessing upon it, then said: Call your creditors and pay them. I did not leave anyone who had a debt against my father except that I paid him, and thirteen wasqs remained: seven of 'ajwah and six of lawn, or six of 'ajwah and seven of lawn. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he laughed and said: Go to Abu Bakr and Umar and inform them. So I went to Abu Bakr and Umar and informed them, and they said: We knew, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did what he did, that this would happen."],[80,"He said to his son: O my son, if something happens among the people, go to the cave in which you saw me hide with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and stay in it, for your provision will come to you morning and evening."],[81,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr ؓ was in a part of Madinah. He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placed his mouth on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and began kissing him and saying: May my father and mother be your ransom; you were good alive and dead. When he came out, he passed by Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, while he was saying: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not died, and he will not die until we kill the hypocrites. He said: They had rejoiced at the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and raised their heads. Abu Bakr passed by him and said: O man, calm yourself, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died. Have you not heard Allah, Blessed and Exalted, say: 'Indeed, you are to die, and indeed they are to die' and 'We did not grant immortality to any human before you; so if you die, will they live forever?' He said: Then he went to the pulpit, ascended it, praised and extolled Allah, then said: O people, if Muhammad was your god whom you worship, then your god has died; but if your god is Allah who is in heaven, then your god is alive and does not die. Then he recited: 'Muhammad is but a messenger; messengers have passed away before him,' until the end of the verse. Then he descended, and the believers rejoiced at that, and their joy increased, while the hypocrites were overcome with gloom. Abdullah b. Umar said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, it was as if there had been coverings on their faces and they were lifted."],[82,"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity."],[83,"When Abdullah b. Abi Bakr died, he was wept over. Abu Bakr came out and said: I apologize to you for the affair of these women; they are recently from ignorance. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The dead person is scalded with boiling water because of the weeping of the living."],[84,"I quoted about my father: 'A fair-skinned one, by whose face rain is sought, a spring for the orphans, a protection for the widows.' He said: That is the Messenger of Allah."],[85,"When he intended a matter, he would say: \"O Allah, choose for me and select for me.\""],[86,"Shall I not teach you a supplication that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me and that ʿĪsā used to teach the disciples? If you had a debt like Mount Uhud and you said it, Allah would settle it for you. She said: I said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Say: O Allah, Reliever of anxiety, Remover of distress, Answerer of the call of the distressed, Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter, You are my Merciful, so have mercy on me with a mercy that suffices me from all besides You.\""],[87,"No prophet was taken in death except that he was buried where he died."],[88,"When the people turned away from the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I was the first to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I began looking at a man fighting in front of him and said, \"Be Talhah.\" Then I looked and there was a person behind me as if he were a bird; I did not realize he had caught up with me, and it was Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah. There was Talhah lying fallen before him. He said, \"Your brother has fulfilled his duty.\" So we left him and turned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It turned out that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been struck in his face by two arrows. I wanted to pull them out, but Abu ʿUbaydah kept asking and imploring me until I let him. He pulled out one of the two arrows, biting on it with his teeth, and extracted it, and one of his front teeth fell out. Then he kept asking me to let him pull out the other. He placed his front tooth on the arrow and bit down, fearing to hurt the Messenger of Allah ﷺ if he moved, and he pulled it out, and his front tooth or one of his front teeth fell out. Thus Abu ʿUbaydah became gap-toothed."],[89,"Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿUthmān b. al-Mughīrah, from ʿAlī b. Rabīʿah, from Asmāʾ or Abū Asmāʾ, from ʿAlī, who said: I heard him say. [Hidden text link=\"19000901\" text=\"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed, and when\"]"],[90,"Misʿar and Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿUthmān b. al-Mughīrah, from ʿAlī b. Rabīʿah, from Asmāʾ b. al-Hakam, from ʿAlī. [Hidden text link=\"19000911\" text=\"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed, and when\"]"],[91,"Yahyā b. Ādam narrated to us, Sharīk narrated to us, from ʿUthmān, from ʿAlī b. Rabīʿah, from Asmāʾ b. al-Hakam, from ʿAlī. [Hidden text link=\"19000921\" text=\"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed, and when\"]"],[92,"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed. When one of his companions narrated to me, I would ask him to swear an oath, and when he swore, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke the truth—that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then comes to the mosque and prays two rakʿahs, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that Allah forgives him.\""],[93,"Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allah b. Saʿīd, from his grandfather Abū Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from ʿAlī, from Abū Bakr ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. [Hidden text link=\"19000941\" text=\"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed, and when\"]"],[94,"I heard ʿAlī b. Abī Tālib ؓ narrating from Abū Bakr al-Siddīq, may Allah have mercy on him, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of ʿAlī that Asmāʾ b. al-Hakam narrated. We do not know this hadith to be reported from the Prophet ﷺ except through this chain we mentioned. Both chains are defective. As for Asmāʾ b. al-Hakam, he is an unknown man who narrated only this hadith, and none narrated from him except ʿAlī b. Rabīʿah. One cannot rely on every hadith like this, especially since Shuʿbah doubted his name. As for ʿAbd Allah b. Saʿīd, he is a man of rejected hadith; scholars of transmission do not differ about the weakness of his hadith. Therefore, it is not obligatory to take him as proof in what he alone narrates. In what trustworthy narrators share with him, we are content with their narration over his. [Hidden text link=\"19000951\" text=\"I was a man such that when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me from it as He willed, and when\"]"],[95,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us like my standing among you today and said: \"People have not been given anything better than forgiveness and well-being, so ask Allah for both.\""],[96,"After the word of sincerity, you have not been given anything better than well-being, so ask Allah for well-being."],[97,"Abu Bakr entered upon us while we were in the Rawda. He ascended the minbar, praised and extolled Allah, then said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on these planks last year: A servant has not been given anything more excellent than sound certainty and well-being. So ask Allah for sound certainty and well-being."],[98,"He said in this intense heat or in similar intense heat: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being and certainty in this world and the Hereafter."],[99,"\"Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it in this world.\""],[100,"\"Whoever's feet become dusty in the cause of Allah, Allah will forbid them to the Fire.\""],[101,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this verse was revealed: 'Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it, and he will not find for himself besides Allah any protector or helper.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Abu Bakr, shall I not recite to you a verse that has been revealed to me?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He recited it to me, and I do not know except that I felt my back break, so I stretched for it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you, O Abu Bakr?' I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. Which of us has not done evil? Indeed we will be recompensed for what we have done.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for you, O Abu Bakr, and your believing companions, you will be recompensed in this world until you meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and you will have no sins. As for the others, that will be gathered for them until they are recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[102,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ said after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Let us go and visit Umm Ayman as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit her.'"],[103,"Hammam narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that Abu Bakr narrated to him."],[104,"I said, O Messenger of Allah, while we were in the cave: If a man were to look, he would see us. He said: What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?"],[105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade striking those who pray."],[106,"When the polytheists expelled the Prophet ﷺ from Makkah, Abu Bakr said: They have expelled their Prophet; they will surely perish. Then this verse was revealed: 'Permission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged...'"],[107,"Umar said to Abu Bakr: O best of people. He said: Since you have said that, I indeed heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The sun has not risen on a man better than Umar."],[108,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date, for it straightens the crooked, and it wards off from the hungry what it wards off from the full."],[109,"I said: O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication that I may supplicate with. He said: \"Say: O God, indeed I have wronged myself with much wrong, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me and have mercy on me. Indeed none forgives sins but You.\""],[110,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq wrote to 'Amr b. al-'As ؓ: To proceed: You have known the testament of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning the Ansar at his death: Accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[111,"We were with Abu Bakr ؓ when he asked for a drink, and water and honey were brought to him. When he placed it in his hand, he wept and sobbed until we thought something had happened to him, and we did not ask him about anything. When he finished, we said: O successor of the Messenger of God ﷺ, what made you weep? He said: While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, I saw him pushing something away from himself while I saw nothing. I said: O Messenger of God, what is it that I saw you pushing away from yourself while I saw nothing? He said: The world extended itself to me, and I said: Away from me! And it said: Indeed you will not catch me. That distressed me, and I feared that I had opposed the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the world had caught up with me."],[112,"\"No one with bad ownership will enter Paradise. Cursed is one who betrays a Muslim or deceives him.\""],[113,"I was with Abu Bakr when he became angry at a man. I said: Shall I strike his neck? He said: Wait. Indeed it is not for anyone after the Messenger of God."],[114,"\"The Dajjal will emerge from a land called Khurasan in the east, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields.\""],[115,"'Abd Allah b. Shawdhab narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay', from 'Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet."],[116,"Sa'id b. Abi 'Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay', from 'Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abu Ishaq al-Fazari. And this hadith: we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr except 'Amr b. Hurayth, nor from 'Amr except al-Mughira b. Subay'. And al-Mughira b. Subay': we do not remember that anyone narrated from him other than Abu al-Tayyah, and we do not know that he narrated other than this hadith. And Ibn Abi 'Aruba did not hear from Abu al-Tayyah; it is only said that he heard it from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah."],[117,"\"The Prophet ﷺ sent back Ma'iz four times.\""],[118,"I saw Abu Bakr meet al-Hasan b. 'Ali and he began to say: May my father be ransomed for the one who resembles the Prophet, not resembling 'Ali, whose father is 'Ali, laughing or barely laughing, smiling."],[119,"\"When this verse was revealed: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, I said: O Messenger of God, by God, I will not speak to you except as a confidential brother.\""],[120,"Fatima ؓ sent to Abu Bakr ؓ: O successor of the Messenger of God ﷺ, did you inherit the Messenger of God or his family? He said: Rather his family. She said: Then what about the share of the Prophet ﷺ? He said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: When God gives a prophet a provision and then takes him, it belongs to the one who stands after him, so I saw fit to return it to the Muslims. She said: You and the Messenger of God know best."],[121,"I said: O Messenger of God, do we act in a matter already decreed, or in one newly begun? He said: \"Rather, in a matter already decreed.\" He said: I said: Then what is the point of action? He said: \"Act, for everyone is facilitated toward that for which he was created.\""],[122,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: What is the birr of Hajj? He said: \"Raising the voice with talbiyah and shedding sacrificial blood.\""],[123,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ stood among the people, praised God and extolled Him, then said: \"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood before us last year\" — he was moved and wept, then sat down — then he stood again and said: \"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood before us last year and said: 'Adhere to truthfulness, for it is part of righteousness, and beware of lying, for it is part of wickedness. Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not sever ties, and be brothers as God has commanded you. Ask God for well-being, for no servant is given anything better than well-being after certainty.'\""],[124,"O people, you recite this verse: 'O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.' I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'When my community sees an oppressor and does not restrain his hands, it is likely that God will afflict them all with punishment from Him.'"],[125,"Rawh narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, and Za'idah also traced it back."],[126,"Rawh narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ. A group stopped it [as a Companion statement], and the hadith belongs to the one who added [the chain] if he is trustworthy. Shu'bah, Za'idah, al-Mu'tamir, and others traced it back, so we restricted ourselves to the hadith of those we mentioned rather than others."],[127,"I arrived to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found that he had passed away, and I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Disbelief in God is disavowing a lineage, even if it is distant.'"],[128,"No one who seeks forgiveness persists [in sin], even if he repeats it seventy times in a day."],[129,"They both brought him the good news that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.'"],[130,"Abu Bakr said to me: 'You used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so compile the Quran.'"],[131,"When it is the night of mid-Sha'ban, God, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and forgives His servants except a polytheist or one who harbors hatred against his brother."],[132,"None of you should perform ablution from food he has eaten that is lawful for him to eat."],[133,"I brought Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Why did you not leave the old man until we came to him?\" I said: \"Rather, he is more deserving to come to you.\" He said: \"We preserve him for the kindness of his son to us.\""],[134,"Gold for gold and silver for silver, like for like; the one who gives more and the one who asks for more are in the Fire."],[135,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, some men grieved over him until some of them were afflicted with whispers of madness. Uthman said: I was one of them. While I was sitting in the shade of a tower among the fortresses, Umar b. al-Khattab passed by me and greeted me, but I did not notice him nor return the greeting. Umar went until he entered upon Abu Bakr and said to him: Shall I not amaze you? I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting to me. Abu Bakr and Umar both came forward until they reached me and greeted me together. Abu Bakr said: Your brother Umar came to me and claimed that he passed by you and greeted you, but you did not return the greeting. Uthman said: I said: By Allah, I did not notice you when you passed nor when you greeted. Abu Bakr said: Uthman has spoken the truth; some matter preoccupied you from that. He said: Yes. He said: What is it? I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died before I could ask him about the salvation of this matter. Abu Bakr said: I already asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. Uthman said: I said: May my father and mother be your ransom."],[136,"I heard him narrating to Sa'id b. al-Musayyib: He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, some men grieved over him until some of them were afflicted with whispers of madness. Uthman said: I was one of them. While I was sitting in the shade of a tower among the fortresses, Umar b. al-Khattab passed by me and greeted me, but I did not notice him nor return the greeting. Umar went until he entered upon Abu Bakr and said to him: Shall I not amaze you? I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting to me. Abu Bakr and Umar both came forward until they reached me and greeted me together. Abu Bakr said: Your brother Umar came to me and claimed that he passed by you and greeted you, but you did not return the greeting. Uthman said: I said: By Allah, I did not notice you when you passed nor when you greeted. Abu Bakr said: Uthman has spoken the truth; some matter preoccupied you from that. He said: Yes. He said: What is it? I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died before I could ask him about the salvation of this matter. Abu Bakr said: I already asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. Uthman said: I said: May my father and mother be your ransom."],[137,"\"Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.\" Until when he drew near to us and there was between us and him the distance of two or three spears, I said: \"This pursuit has caught up with us, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: And I wept. He said: \"Why do you weep?\" I said: \"By Allah, I am not weeping for myself, but I weep for you.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against him: \"O Allah, suffice us against him.\" He said: His horse sank into the ground up to its belly, and he leaped off it to the ground, and he called out: \"O Muhammad, I think this is from you or your doing, so supplicate to Allah to save me from what I am in. By Allah, I will mislead those behind me of the pursuit, and take an arrow from me, for you will pass by camels of mine at such and such a place, so take from them whatever you wish.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"I have no need of them.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him, and he departed and returned to his companions. I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached Madinah, and the people met him, and men, women, and servants came out onto the roads saying: \"Allah is greater; Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has come.\" The people disputed which of them he would stay with, but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tonight we will stay with Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of Abd al-Muttalib, to honor them by that.\" Then he rose in the morning and went where he was commanded. Al-Bara said: The first to come to us was Umar b. al-Khattab with twenty riders, and we said: \"What happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"He is on my track.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived I had recited some surahs from the Mufassal. This hadith Shu'ba narrated from it a portion, namely that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank until I was satisfied."],[138,"Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from Abu Bakr likewise. And Israel's hadith was shared by a group in a similar narration, among them Zuhayr and Hudayj b. Mu'awiya and others, and it is one of the best chains of transmission narrated from Abu Bakr, may Allah's mercy and pleasure be upon him."],[139,"When \"Perish the hands of Abu Lahab\" was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said to him: \"If you move aside, she will not harm you with anything.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A barrier will be placed between me and her.\" She approached until she stood before Abu Bakr and said: \"O Abu Bakr, your companion has satirized us.\" Abu Bakr said: \"No, by the Lord of this structure, he does not utter poetry nor speak it.\" She said: \"You are indeed truthful.\" When she turned away, Abu Bakr said: \"She did not see you.\" He said: \"No, an angel kept covering me until she turned away.\""],[140,"No prophet ever dies until a man from his community leads him in prayer."],[141,"The deceased is punished by the weeping of his family over him."],[142,"Samura sold wine, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah cursed the Jews; fat was forbidden to them to eat, but they rendered it and sold it and consumed its price."],[143,"If I leave you, then one better than I, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, left you, meaning that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not appoint a successor; and if I appoint a successor, then one better than I, Abu Bakr, did appoint."],[144,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"May one of us sleep while he is in a state of major ritual impurity?\" He said: \"Yes, if he performs ablution as he does for prayer.\""],[145,"While 'Umar b. al-Khattab was delivering the sermon, 'Uthman b. 'Affan entered, and that was on Friday. 'Umar said to him: 'At this time?' He said: 'I only heard the call, performed ablution, and then came.' He said: 'And ablution too? You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to perform ghusl.'"],[146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with him while he was swearing by his father, and he was among a group of riders. He said: 'Do not swear by your fathers.' 'Umar said: 'I never did it again.'"],[147,"Whatever Allah gives you of this wealth without asking or self-aspiration, it is only provision that Allah has brought to you."],[148,"He gave a horse in the path of Allah, then later saw it being sold, or its owner had neglected it. So he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not grant him permission to take back his charity."],[149,"Whoever sells a slave who has property, the property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates. Whoever sells palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates."],[150,"A man from Thaqif divorced his wives and freed his slave. 'Umar said to him: 'You must take back your wealth and your wives, or if you die, I will stone your grave just as the Messenger of Allah stoned the grave of Abu Righal.'"],[151,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[152,"I am Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father. : :"],[153,"When Hafsah became a widow after Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ and had been present with him at Badr and died in Madinah, 'Umar said: 'I met 'Uthman b. 'Affan and offered Hafsah to him, saying: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsah bint 'Umar. He said: I will consider my situation. I waited for some nights, then he met me and said: I will not marry today. Then I met Abu Bakr and said to him: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsah bint 'Umar. Abu Bakr remained silent and did not respond to me at all, and I was more upset with him than with 'Uthman. I waited for some nights, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, and I married her to him. Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsah to me and I did not respond to you. I said: Yes. He said: Nothing prevented me from responding to you about what you offered except that I already knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had mentioned Hafsah, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had he left her, I would have accepted her.'"],[154,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[155,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream, and I saw that he would not look at me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with me? He said: 'Are you not the one who kisses while fasting?' I said: By the One in whose hand is 'Umar's soul, I will never kiss while fasting again."],[156,"He asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for 'Umrah, and he granted him permission and said: 'Do not forget us in your supplication, O my brother.'"],[157,"Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Salim, from his father, from 'Umar, that he asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission, then he mentioned something similar. And someone other than Mu'ammal narrated it, and did not say: from 'Umar."],[158,"That he said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Consider what we do—is it in a matter already decreed and finished, or in a matter newly begun?' He said: 'Rather, in a matter already decreed and finished.' He said: 'Then why not rely on that?' He said: 'Act, O Ibn al-Khattab, for everyone is facilitated for what he was created. As for one who is among the people of felicity, he will act with the deeds of the people of felicity, and as for one who is among the people of misery, he will act with the deeds of the people of misery.'"],[159,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over his leather socks.\""],[160,"\"Whoever you find has stolen from the spoils of war, burn his belongings.\""],[161,"\"Whoever sees someone afflicted and says: 'Praise be to Allah who has spared me from what He has afflicted you with, and favored me over many of those He created with a great favor,' Allah will spare him from that affliction, whatever it may be, as long as he lives.\""],[162,"\"Whoever enters a market of the markets and says: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of everything,' Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million bad deeds, and build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[163,"\"The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell.\""],[164,"Prices became high in Madinah and hardship became severe, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Be patient and rejoice, for I have blessed your sa' and your mudd. Eat and do not separate, for the food of one is enough for two, the food of two is enough for four, and the food of four is enough for five or six. Blessing is in the group. Whoever patiently endures its hardships and difficulties, I will be an intercessor or witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever leaves it out of dislike for what is in it, Allah will replace him with someone better than him in it. And whoever wishes evil upon it, Allah will melt him like salt melts in water.'"],[165,"\"The traveler wipes over his leather socks for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.\""],[166,"When he raised his hands in supplication, he would not lower them until he wiped his face with them."],[167,"\"Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears silk.\""],[168,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'May one of us sleep while he is in a state of major ritual impurity?' He said: 'If he performs ablution as he does for the prayer.'"],[169,"The Prophet ﷺ heard me while I was saying, 'By my father,' so he said: 'Indeed, Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers and by the false deities (ṭawāghīt).'"],[170,"'Abd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, from 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[171,"'Umar ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'What is the matter with people who engage in this mut'ah (temporary marriage), when the Prophet ﷺ forbade it' — I think he said: 'from it' — 'If anyone who engages in it is brought to me, I will surely stone him with rocks.'"],[172,"Indeed, silk is only worn by one who has no share in the Hereafter."],[173,"When My servant's remembrance of Me distracts him from asking Me, I give him better than what I give to those who ask."],[174,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks (khuffayn)."],[175,"'Umar said to the Stone: 'I know that you are a stone, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not kiss you.'"],[176,"He had made a vow during the pre-Islamic era (jāhiliyyah) to observe i'tikāf for one night. He said: 'When I embraced Islam, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Fulfill your vow.'"],[177,"Ḥafṣ b. Ghiyāth narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allāh b. 'Umar, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar."],[178,"He had a vow upon him."],[179,"He had a vow to observe i'tikāf for one night during the pre-Islamic era. When he embraced Islam, he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Fulfill your vow.'"],[180,"He saw a striped silk garment (ḥulla siyarā') being sold, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'If only you would buy it to wear for the delegations that come to you.' He said: 'Indeed, silk is only worn by one who has no share in the Hereafter.'"],[181,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar."],[182,"\"The deceased is punished as long as wailing is done over him, or as long as he is wept over.\""],[183,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"I am afflicted by major ritual impurity during the night.\" So he commanded him to perform the same ablution as for prayer."],[184,"Suspect opinion in matters of religion, for I saw myself on the day of Abu Jandal rejecting the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by my own opinion, while I did not fail to seek the truth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was writing between himself and the people of Makkah, and he said: \"Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\" They said: \"If we thought that, we would believe you in what you say; but write as we write: In Your name, O Allah.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted, but I refused, until he said to me: \"O 'Umar, do you see that I have accepted, yet you refuse?\" He said: Then I accepted."],[185,"\"I have not urinated standing since I embraced Islam.\""],[186,"That he favored Usamah in the stipend, so I said: \"You favor him over me?\" He said: \"He was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you.\""],[187,"\"Do not prevent women from the mosques.\""],[188,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the leather socks.\""],[189,"\"If I appoint a successor, then one better than me, Abu Bakr, appointed a successor; and if I leave you, then one better than me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, left you. The matter is with these six with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he passed away.\""],[190,"That the Prophet ﷺ stipulated with the Jews of Khaybar: \"We may expel them whenever we wish.\""],[191,"When we gathered for the emigration, I, 'Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah, and Hisham b. al-'Asi appointed a meeting at the water pool of Banu Ghifar above Sarif. We said: \"Whichever of us does not arrive there by morning has been detained, so let his two companions proceed.\" Hisham b. al-'Asi was detained from us. When we arrived in Madinah, we stayed among Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf in Quba'. Abu Jahl b. Hisham and al-Harith b. Hisham went out to 'Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah, who was their paternal cousin and their maternal brother, until they reached us in Madinah. They spoke to him, saying: \"Your mother has vowed not to touch her head with a comb until she sees you.\" He felt compassion for her. I said to him: \"O 'Ayyash, by Allah, the people only want to turn you away from your religion, so beware of them. By Allah, if lice harmed your mother, she would comb her hair, and if the heat of Makkah became intense for her—I think he said—she would seek shade.\" He said: \"I have wealth there, so I will take it.\" I said: \"By Allah, you know that I am among the wealthiest of Quraysh, so you may have half of my wealth, and do not go with them.\" He said: He refused me except to go out with them. When he refused me, I said to him: \"Since you have done what you have done, take this camel of mine, for it is a docile camel; stay on its back, and if you suspect any treachery from the people, escape on it.\" He went out with them on it until they were partway along the road. Abu Jahl b. Hisham said: \"By Allah, I have found my camel slow; will you not carry me on this camel of yours?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he made his camel kneel, and they made theirs kneel, so that he might move onto it. When they were all on the ground, they attacked him and bound him, then brought him into Makkah and tempted him, and he was tempted. We used to say: \"By Allah, Allah will not accept from anyone who is tempted any ransom or justice, and the repentance of a people who knew Allah and then returned to disbelief because of a trial that befell them will not be accepted.\" They used to say that about themselves. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, Allah revealed about them, about our words to them, and their words about themselves: \"Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins\" up to His saying: \"while you do not perceive.\" 'Umar said: I wrote it on a sheet and sent it to Hisham b. al-'Asi. Hisham said: I kept reading it at Dhu Tuwa, ascending with it until I understood it. He said: It was cast into my mind that it was revealed only about us and about what we used to say about ourselves, and it is said about us. So I returned, mounted my camel, and joined the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah."],[192,"When 'Umar embraced Islam, he said: \"Who is the most talkative of people?\" They said: \"So-and-so.\" He went to him and said: \"I have embraced Islam, so do not inform anyone.\" He said: He went out dragging his lower garment with its edge on his shoulder, saying: \"Indeed, 'Umar has turned renegade.\" I said: \"You lie, but I have embraced Islam,\" and he had a shirt on. A group of Quraysh stood against him and fought him, and he fought them until he fell and they piled on him. Then a man wearing a shirt came and said: \"What is the matter with you and this man? Do you think Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b will leave you alone concerning their companion, while you kill a man who chose for himself to follow Muhammad?\" He said: The people dispersed from him. I said to my father: \"Who is the man?\" He said: \"Al-'As b. Wa'il al-Sahmi.\""],[193,"Had it not been that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I intend to extend your qiblah,' I would not have extended it."],[194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not give as dowry to any of his wives more than twelve uqiyyah."],[195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give charity, and that coincided with wealth I had, so I said: Today I will outdo Abu Bakr if I ever outdo him one day. I brought half of my wealth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What have you left for your family?' I said: 'The like of it.' Abu Bakr brought all the wealth he had, and he said: 'O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family?' He said: 'Allah and His Messenger.' I said: 'I will never race you in anything ever again.'"],[196,"That Ibn 'Abbas asked 'Umar about the two women who backed each other against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Those are 'A'ishah and Hafsah.'"],[197,"Seven places where prayer is not to be performed: the roof of the House of Allah, the graveyard, the garbage dump, the slaughterhouse, the bathhouse, the resting place of camels, and the middle of the road."],[198,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he has taken possession of it."],[199,"When there are three people, two should not converse privately excluding their companion."],[200,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about major ritual impurity, and he said: 'Perform ablution as you do for prayer.'"],[201,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me urinating while standing and said: 'Stop.' 'Umar said: 'I never did that again.'"],[202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I am standing among you and said: 'Be good to my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Whoever loves the center of Paradise, let him adhere to the community. And whoever is pleased by his good deed and troubled by his evil deed is a believer.'"],[203,"Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. And whoever is pleased by his good deed and troubled by his evil deed is a believer."],[204,"When 'Some of them are wretched and some are blessed' was revealed, they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what about what we do? Is it something already decreed or something we begin?' He said: 'Rather, something already decreed.' They said: 'Then what is the point of action?' He said: 'Everyone is facilitated for what he was created for.'"],[205,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, 'What is Islam?' He replied, 'That you bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, that you establish the prayer, give the zakat, fast Ramadan, and perform the Hajj to the House.' He said, 'If I do that, then I have become a Muslim?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah. What is faith (iman)?' He said, 'That you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the resurrection after death, Paradise and Hell, and the divine decree, all of it, its good and its evil.' He said, 'If I do that, then I am a believer?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[206,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may I draw near to you?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then he drew near until he placed his hand on his knees and said, \"What is Islam?\" He said, \"That you bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, that you establish the prayer, give the zakat, fast Ramadan, and perform the Hajj to the House.\" He said, \"If I do that, then I have become a Muslim?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah. What is faith (iman)?\" He said, \"That you believe in Allah, the Last Day, the resurrection after death, Paradise and Hell, and the divine decree, all of it, its good and its evil.\" He said, \"If I do that, then I am a believer?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" He said, \"What is ihsan?\" He said, \"That you fear Allah as though you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you.\" He said, \"If I do that, then I have done ihsan?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" He said, \"Then he confirmed him, and the man turned away. So he said, 'Bring him to me.' He was looked for but not found. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This is Jibril ﷺ ; he came to teach you your religion.'"],[207,"Musa met Adam and said, 'O Adam, you are the one whom Allah created with His own hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and settled you in Paradise. Had it not been for what you did, many of your descendants would have entered Paradise.' He said, 'O Musa, you are the one whom Allah chose for His message and His speech. Then do you blame me for what had been decreed upon me before He created me?' They argued before Allah, and Adam prevailed over Musa."],[208,"Adam and Musa argued."],[209,"Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Yahya b. Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith was also narrated by Kahmas, from Abdullah b. Buraydah, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet."],[210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that it be proclaimed among the people that whoever bears witness that there is no deity but Allah will enter Paradise. Umar said, 'Then they will rely on it.' He said, 'Let them rely on it.'"],[211,"Whoever humbles himself for Me like this—and he gestured with the palm of his hand toward the ground—I will raise him like this—and he gestured with the back of his hand toward the sky."],[212,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ mentioned how much they let their garments trail. He said, 'A handspan.' They said, 'A handspan is little; the private parts may show.' He said, 'Then a forearm's length.' They said, 'Their feet will show.' He said, 'A forearm's length; they are not to exceed that.'"],[213,"He stood as a speaker on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, praised and extolled Allah, then said, 'To proceed: Verily, the prohibition of wine was revealed on the day it was revealed, and it is from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. Wine is whatever clouds the intellect. O people, I wish the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not left us until he made a covenant with us regarding it, a covenant we would abide by: the grandfather, the kalalah, and categories of riba.' I said, 'What do you think about the sixth, made from sind, called al-jahil, from which a man drinks a draught and it throws him down, made from rice?' He said, 'This did not exist in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; had it existed, he would have forbidden it. Do you not see that it encompasses all drinks?' He said, 'Wine is whatever clouds the intellect.'"],[214,"Al-Zubayr asked Umar for permission to go on jihad. He said, 'Sit down, for you have already fought alongside the Messenger of Allah.'"],[215,"Four rak'ahs before Zuhr after the sun has passed its zenith are equivalent to the prayer of the pre-dawn."],[216,"I asked Aisha about silk. She said, 'Go to Ibn Abbas and ask him.' I went to Ibn Abbas and asked him. He said, 'Ask Ibn Umar.' I asked him, and he said, 'Hafsah bint Umar told me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears silk.\""],[217,"We set out with ʿUmar until, when we were at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he entered iḥrām and we entered iḥrām. A rider passed by us from whom the scent of perfume emanated. ʿUmar said, “Who is this?” They said, “Muʿāwiyah.” He said, “What is this, O Muʿāwiyah?” He said, “I passed by Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān and she did this to me.” He said, “Go back and wash it off, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘The pilgrim is the one with disheveled hair and unperfumed.'”"],[218,"When ʿUmar became caliph, he praised God and extolled Him, then said: “O people, the Messenger of God ﷺ permitted us mutʿah, then he forbade it to us.”"],[219,"Muḥammad b. Abī ʿAdī narrated to us, from Saʿīd b. Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, from Ibn ʿAbbās:"],[220,"Men pleasing to me bore witness before me, among them ʿUmar, and the most pleasing of them to me is ʿUmar, that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[221,"He forbade fasting on the day of Fiṭr and the day of Sacrifice."],[222,"“The saddles are not to be fastened except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqṣā Mosque.”"],[223,"He forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises or shines, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets.” And he said: “You must enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, or God will set over you your wicked ones, and your good ones will supplicate but will not be answered.”"],[224,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah, then took her back.”"],[225,"“May God curse the Jews: fats were forbidden to them, so they melted them down and sold them, and consumed their price.”"],[226,"That he said to the Stone: “I know that you are a stone; were it not that I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you.”"],[227,"ʿUmar used to grant permission to the people of Badr, and he granted permission to me along with them. Some of them said, “Do you grant permission to this youth along with us, while among our own sons there are those like him?” ʿUmar said, “He is among those whom you know.” One day he granted them permission, and granted me permission along with them, and he asked them about this sūrah: “When the victory of God and the conquest comes.” They said, “God, mighty and majestic, commanded His Prophet, when God grants victory, to seek forgiveness and turn in repentance to Him.” He said, “What do you say, O Ibn ʿAbbās?” I said, “It is not like that; rather, He informed His Prophet of the imminence of his term. He said: ‘When the victory of God and the conquest comes’ — the conquest of Makkah — ‘and you see the people entering the religion of God in multitudes,’ that is a sign of your death, ‘so glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever-accepting of repentance.'” ʿUmar said to them, “How can you censure me regarding him after what you have seen?”"],[228,"When ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy b. Salūl died, his son ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my father has died, so pray over him.” The Messenger of God ﷺ stood, his companions stood with him, and I stood. When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood to pray over him, I stood facing him and said, “O Messenger of God, will you pray over the enemy of God, who on such-and-such a day said such-and-such, and on such-and-such a day said such-and-such?” enumerating his odious days. When I persisted, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Leave me, ʿUmar, for I have been given the choice: ‘Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, God will never forgive them.’ If I knew that by adding to the seventy times they would be forgiven, I would have done so.” He said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed, then stood at his grave. He said: I marveled at my boldness toward the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it was not long until the verse came down: “And do not ever pray over any of them who dies, and do not stand at his grave.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ never prayed over any of them, nor did he stand at his grave."],[229,"I was teaching the Qur'an to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf during the last caliphate of 'Umar, in his final Hajj, while we were at Mina. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came to us and said: \"If only you had witnessed the Commander of the Faithful today: a man came to him and said, 'I heard so-and-so saying, \"If the Commander of the Faithful were to die, we would pledge allegiance to so-and-so.\"' 'Umar said, 'I will stand before the people this evening and warn them against these groups who seek to snatch away the people's affairs.' I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, the season gathers the rabble of the people, and it is they who will dominate your gathering. If you were to postpone this until you reach Madinah, then say what you wish with full authority, and they will understand it from you and put it in its proper place.'\" He said: So we arrived in Madinah, and Friday came, and I remembered what 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf had told me, so I went early to the mosque. I found Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl had preceded me in arriving early, so I sat beside him, my knee touching his knee. When the sun declined and 'Umar entered, I said to Sa'id b. Zayd, \"The Commander of the Faithful will surely say today a statement that has not been said before him.\" Sa'id became angry and said, \"What statement could he say that has not been said before him?\" When 'Umar ascended the pulpit, the mu'adhdhin began his call to prayer. When he finished, 'Umar stood, praised and extolled Allah, and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then said: \"Now to the matter at hand. I intend to say a statement that has been decreed for me to say, and I do not know - perhaps it is before my appointed end. Whoever memorizes it and comprehends it, let him narrate it wherever his mount reaches him. And whoever does not memorize it or comprehend it, I do not permit anyone to lie about me. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent Muhammad and revealed to him the Book, and revealed to him the verse of stoning. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned and we stoned after him. Indeed, I fear that time may pass over the people until they say, 'We do not know the verse of stoning,' and thus they go astray by abandoning an obligation that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed. Indeed, stoning is true for one who commits fornication and is married, with evidence established, or pregnancy or confession. Indeed, we used to recite: Do not desire to be other than your fathers, for it is disbelief on your part to desire to be other than your fathers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not praise me excessively as the Christians praised Jesus, son of Mary, for I am only His servant; but say: His servant and His messenger. Indeed, part of our story: when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, 'Ali, al-'Abbas, and those with them stayed behind in the house of Fatimah, while the Muhajirun gathered to Abu Bakr and the Ansar gathered in the Saqifah of Banu Sa'idah. I said to Abu Bakr, 'Come with us to our brothers of the Ansar.' So we went out and met two righteous men from them. - Al-Zuhri said: They were 'Uwaym b. Sa'idah and Ma'n b. 'Adi. - They said, 'Where are you heading, O group of Quraysh?' We said, 'We want our brothers of the Ansar.' They said, 'Take your time until you settle your matter among yourselves.' We said, 'We will still go to them.' We came to them and found them gathered in the Saqifah of Banu Sa'idah, and there was a man wrapped in a cloak. I said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'This is Sa'd.' I said, 'What is wrong with him?' They said, 'He is ill.' A speaker from the Ansar stood up and said: 'Indeed, a company of you has come to us, O group of Quraysh, and you are our brothers, and we are the battalion of Islam. You want to exclude us or monopolize the matter without us.' I had composed a speech I intended to give before Abu Bakr spoke, but when I was about to speak, he said to me, 'Be patient.' By Allah, he did not leave anything I intended to say except that he said it, and better. He said: 'O group of Ansar, whatever good you say about yourselves, you are worthy of it, but the Arabs will not recognize this matter except for this clan of Quraysh. I am satisfied for you with one of these two men, so pledge allegiance to whichever of them you wish.' He took hold of my hand and the hand of Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. I would prefer to be brought forward and have my neck struck, with no sin on my part, than to be commander over a people among whom is Abu Bakr. Then Hubab b. al-Mundhir stood and said: 'I am its seasoned little palm tree of the tribe, its fruitful little date palm. From us a leader and from you a leader, otherwise we will renew the war between us and you like a new war.' I said: 'Two swords cannot fit in one scabbard; rather, from us the commanders, and from you the ministers. Stretch out your hand, O Abu Bakr, that I may pledge allegiance to you.' He stretched out his hand and I pledged allegiance to him, and the Muhajirun and Ansar pledged allegiance to him. Voices rose and clamor increased, and they trampled upon Sa'd. They said, 'You have killed Sa'd.' I said, 'May Allah kill Sa'd.' Whoever claims that the pledge to Abu Bakr was a hasty undertaking, it was indeed a hasty undertaking, but Allah averted its evil. Indeed, there is not among you one to whom necks are extended like Abu Bakr ؓ. Whoever pledges allegiance to a man without consultation of the Muslims, then neither he nor the one to whom allegiance was pledged is to be obeyed, for fear of being killed."],[230,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ withdrew from his wives, I entered the mosque and found the people tapping with pebbles and saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.\" That was before the command of hijab. He said: I entered upon 'A'ishah and said, \"O daughter of Abu Bakr, has your affair reached the point of harming the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"What have I to do with you, O son of al-Khattab? Attend to your own concerns.\" I entered upon Hafsah, daughter of 'Umar, and said, \"O Hafsah, has your affair reached the point of harming Allah and His Messenger? You know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ does not love you, and were it not for me, he would have divorced you.\" He said: She wept intensely. I said, \"Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: He is in his storeroom, in the upper room. I found the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Rabah, sitting on the threshold of the upper room, dangling his legs over a carved wooden trunk which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to climb. I called out, \"O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He looked at the room, then looked at me, and said nothing. I said, \"O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I think he supposes I came for Hafsah's sake. By Allah, if he ordered me to strike her neck, I would strike her neck.\" He gestured to me, and I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he was lying on a mat. I sat down, and he had only a waist wrapper on him, nothing else. The mat had left marks on his body. I cast my gaze around the storeroom of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I saw a small amount of barley, about a sa', and some leaves of the sant tree in a corner of the room. My eyes filled with tears. He said, \"What makes you weep, O son of al-Khattab?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why should I not weep when this mat has left marks on your body, and this is your storeroom with nothing in it but what I see, while Caesar and Chosroes live amidst fruits and rivers? You are the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one, and this is your storeroom.\" He said, \"Are you not pleased that they have this world and we have the Hereafter?\" I said, \"Yes.\" I had entered upon him while I could see anger in his face. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what hardship has come to you from the matter of the women? If you have divorced them, Allah is with you, and His angels, and Jibril, and Mika'il, and I, and Abu Bakr.\" Rarely did I speak words - and I praise Allah - except that I hoped Allah would confirm my saying. Then this verse was revealed: \"Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him in exchange wives better than you\" (Qur'an 66:5). And it was revealed: \"If you two support one another against him, then indeed Allah is his protector, and Jibril...\" (Qur'an 66:4) to the end of the verse. The daughter of Abu Bakr and Hafsah used to support one another against the rest of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you divorce them?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Should I go down and inform them that you have not divorced them?\" He said, \"Yes, if you wish.\" I kept talking to him until the anger left his face, and he smiled with his teeth showing, and he had the most beautiful mouth of all people. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ descended, and I descended, clinging to the wooden trunk. He descended as if walking on the ground without touching it with his hand. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you were in the upper room for twenty-nine days?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the month may be twenty-nine.\" I stood at the door of the mosque and called out at the top of my voice: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not divorced his wives.\" And the verse was revealed: \"When news of safety or fear comes to them, they spread it; but if they had referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them, those who can draw conclusions would have known it\" (Qur'an 4:83). He said: I was the one who drew that conclusion from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[231,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the polytheists, who were a thousand, and at his companions, who were three hundred and seventeen men. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the qiblah, then stretched out his hands and began calling upon his Lord, saying: \"Fulfill for me what You promised me. O Allah, if You destroy this band of the people of Islam, You will never be worshiped on earth.\" He said: He kept calling upon his Lord with his hands outstretched until his cloak fell from his shoulders. Abu Bakr came to him, took his cloak, and placed it back on his shoulders. Then he embraced him from behind and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, enough of your urgent plea to your Lord, for He will surely fulfill what He promised you.\" Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"When you sought help of your Lord, He answered you: 'Indeed, I will reinforce you with a thousand of the angels, one following another'\" (Qur'an 8:9). He said: And Allah reinforced him with the angels. Abu Zumayl said: Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me: While a man on that day was running in pursuit of a man from the polytheists, he heard a strike of a whip above him and the voice of a horseman saying, \"Advance, Hayzum!\" He looked at the polytheist ahead of him, who fell on his back, gazing up at him, and saw that he had been slashed on the side of his face like a whip mark. The Ansari went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said, \"You spoke the truth; that was reinforcement from the third heaven.\" On that day they killed seventy and took seventy captives. Abu Zumayl said: Ibn 'Abbas said: When they took the captives, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Abu Bakr, O 'Umar, what do you think about these captives?\" Abu Bakr said, \"They are our cousins and kinsmen. I think you should take, or we should take, ransom from them, so that it may be strength for us against the disbelievers.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O 'Umar, what do you think?\" I said, \"No, by Allah, I do not agree with Abu Bakr. O Prophet of Allah, I think you should let us strike their necks, and let 'Ali be given 'Aqil so that he may strike his neck, and give me so-and-so, a relative of 'Umar, so that I may strike his neck. For these are the leaders of disbelief and its champions.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ inclined to what Abu Bakr said and did not incline to what I said. The next day, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him and Abu Bakr sitting and weeping. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what makes you and your companion weep? If it is something I should weep over, I will weep with you; and if not, I will pretend to weep because of your weeping.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I weep because of what your companions proposed to me about taking ransom. The punishment for their proposal has been shown to me, closer than this tree\" - a tree near the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land. You desire the goods of this world, but Allah desires the Hereafter. And Allah is Mighty and Wise\" (Qur'an 8:67)."],[232,"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah wrote a letter to the people of Makkah, and Allah informed His Prophet of it. He sent 'Ali and al-Zubayr in pursuit of the letter, and they caught up with a woman on a camel, and extracted the letter from a braid among her braids, as the Prophet of Allah ﷺ had told them. He sent for Hatib and said, \"O Hatib, did you write this letter?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"What prompted you to do that?\" He said, \"By Allah, I am indeed sincere to Allah and His Messenger, but I was a stranger among the people of Makkah, and my family was among them, so I feared for them, and I wrote a letter that will not harm Allah and His Messenger at all, and perhaps there may be some benefit in it for my family.\" 'Umar said: I drew my sword and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, let me deal with Hatib, for he has disbelieved, and I will strike his neck.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O son of al-Khattab, what do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon this band of the people of Badr and said, 'Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you.'\""],[233,"On the day of Khaybar, a number of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ were killed. People said, \"So-and-so is a martyr, and so-and-so is a martyr,\" until they passed by a man and said, \"So-and-so is a martyr.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No, indeed I saw him in the Fire because of a cloak or a garment he had stolen from the spoils.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O son of al-Khattab, go and announce among the people: 'None will enter Paradise except the believers.'\" So I announced among the people."],[234,"When the cities were conquered, the people turned to the world, and I turned to 'Umar, so most of my talk was from 'Umar."],[235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a treaty with the people of Makkah. If it had been applied to anyone else or judged upon what I heard, that would have been remarkable. That is, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a treaty with the people of Makkah on the condition that whoever of them came to us, we would return him to them."],[236,"An angel came to me tonight from my Lord and said: 'Pray in this blessed valley and say: 'Umrah within a Hajj.'\""],[237,"We have from 'Ali b. al-Mubarak, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[238,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon him while he was riding and he was swearing by his father. He said: \"Do not swear by your fathers.\" He said: I never did it again."],[239,"Indeed, I am holding you back by your waist wrappers, saying, 'Come away from the Fire,' while you are rushing into it, or plunging like moths and locusts into the Fire. I am holding you back by your waist wrappers, and I will precede you to the Pond. You will come to me together and in scattered groups, and I will recognize you by your marks and your names, just as a man recognizes his horse - and someone else said: just as a man recognizes a stray camel among his camels. Then you will be taken to the left, and I will say, 'To me, O Lord, my community, my community!' It will be said, or He will say, 'O Muhammad, you do not know what they innovated after you; they went back on their heels after you.' So let me not see one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection carrying a bleating sheep, calling out, 'O Muhammad!' and I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything; I have conveyed the message.' And let me not see one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection carrying a bellowing camel, calling out, 'O Muhammad!' and I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything from Allah; I have conveyed the message.' And let me not see one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection carrying a leather bag, saying, 'O Muhammad, O Muhammad,' and I will say, 'I cannot avail you anything from Allah; I have conveyed the message.'\""],[240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day at noon and found Abu Bakr ؓ sitting in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What brought you out at this hour?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what brought you out?\" He said, \"The same that brought you out.\" Then 'Umar ؓ came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O son of al-Khattab, what brought you out at this hour?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the same that brought you two out.\" He sat with them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began talking to them. He said to them, \"Do you have enough strength to go to this palm grove and get some food and drink?\" We said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" So we set off until we came to the house of Malik b. al-Tayhan, Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went ahead of us and asked permission to enter. The mother of Abu al-Haytham heard the greeting and wanted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give them more greeting. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was about to leave, the mother of Abu al-Haytham came out running and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard your greeting, but I wanted you to increase your greeting to us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Where is Abu al-Haytham?\" She said, \"He is nearby, O Messenger of Allah; he went to fetch fresh water for us. Enter; he will come soon.\" She spread a mat for them under a tree, and Abu al-Haytham came with his donkey carrying two water skins. Abu al-Haytham rejoiced at them and brought them refreshment. Then Abu al-Haytham climbed a palm tree and cut down bunches of dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"That is enough, O Abu al-Haytham.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you will eat from its unripe dates and its ripe dates and enjoy them.\" Then he brought them water, and they drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is among the blessings about which you will be asked.\" Then Abu al-Haytham got up to slaughter a sheep, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Avoid the one that gives milk.\" Then Abu al-Haytham stood and kneaded dough for them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar put their heads down and slept. They woke up and found their food ready, and he placed it before them. They ate and were satisfied and praised Allah. Abu al-Haytham brought them the rest of the date bunches, and they ate some of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said farewell and supplicated for them with good. Then he said to Abu al-Haytham, \"When you hear that slaves have come to us, come to us.\" Abu al-Haytham said: When I heard that slaves had come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I went to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a slave. I made a contract with him for forty thousand dirhams, and I have never seen a slave with greater blessing than him."],[241,"\"The month is twenty-nine nights,\" said Aisha: \"Then Allah revealed the choice, and he began with me, the first of his wives, saying: 'I am presenting a matter to you. Do not hasten in it until you consult your parents.' He knew that my parents would not command me to separate from him. I said: 'What is it?' He said: 'Allah said: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, then come, I will provide for you and release you with a kind release. And if you desire Allah and His Messenger.' I said: 'In which of these should I consult my parents? Why did you not present this to one of your wives who is older than me?' He said: 'Rather, you.' Aisha said: 'I said: Before I consult my parents, I desire Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter.'\" He said: \"And it is said that Aisha said: 'I am content with Allah and His Messenger in hardship and ease.'\" Aisha said: \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon his wives and chose for them, and they were upon one word, as Aisha said.\""],[242,"It reached him that a man sold wine, so Umar said: \"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah cursed the Jews. Fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and consumed its price.'\""],[243,"He saw him kissing the Stone and saying: \"Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.\""],[244,"Umar b. al-Khattab, whenever he prayed a prayer, would sit for the people; whoever had a need would speak to him, otherwise he would rise. One day I attended at the door and said: 'O Yarfa!', so he came out, and Uthman was at the door. Yarfa went out and said: 'Rise, O son of Affan; rise, O son of Abbas.' We entered upon Umar, and he had heaps of wealth. He said: 'I examined the people of Madinah and saw that you two have the most kinsfolk among them. Take this wealth and divide it; if there is surplus, return it.' I said: 'And if there is shortage, will you give us more?' He said: 'A trait from Akhshan. You know that Muhammad and his family used to eat hard, coarse food.' I said: 'Yes, by Allah, if Allah had opened this upon Muhammad, he would have done with it other than what you have done.' He became angry and heaved until his ribs moved, and said: 'Then what would he have done?' I said: 'Then he would have eaten and fed us.' So it was relieved from him."],[245,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Night of Decree and said: 'Seek it in the last ten nights, in an odd night among them.'"],[246,"I wished to know the two who backed each other against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? It was said to me: 'Umar b. al-Khattab knew that.' I waited a year wanting to ask him, then I feared him. Then I asked him, and he said: 'They are Aisha and Hafsa.' I said: 'By Allah, I have wanted to ask you for a year, but I feared you.' He said: 'Why? Or from what?'\""],[247,"I asked Umar about the two who backed each other against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Aisha and Hafsa.'"],[248,"He used to command bathing on Friday."],[249,"It was said to Umar b. al-Khattab: 'Tell us about the affair of hardship.' Umar said: 'We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Tabuk in intense heat. We halted at a place where severe thirst afflicted us, until we thought our necks would snap. One of us would go to relieve himself and would not return until he thought his neck would snap. A man would slaughter his camel, squeeze its undigested food, drink it, and place it on his belly. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Would you like that, O Abu Bakr?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and did not lower them until the sky leaned over and poured down. They filled what they had with them. Then we went to look and did not find it had passed beyond the army.'"],[250,"I saw Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far kiss the Stone and then prostrate upon it. I said: 'What is this?' He said: 'I saw your maternal uncle Ibn Abbas kiss the Stone and then prostrate upon it, and he said: 'I saw Umar kiss it and prostrate upon it, and he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss it and prostrate upon it.'"],[251,"He said to Abu Bakr: 'How will you fight the people when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah'?' Abu Bakr said: 'If they withhold from me a young goat of what they used to pay to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I will fight them over it.'"],[252,"He used to command us to bathe on Friday."],[253,"When 'Umar was stabbed, Hafsah wailed for him, so 'Umar said: Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The one who is wailed over is punished."],[254,"I agreed with my Lord in three things. I said: O Messenger of God, if only you would take the Station [of Abraham] as a place of prayer, and it was revealed: \"And take the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer.\" And I said: If only you would veil the Mothers of the Believers, for both the righteous and the wicked enter upon you, and the verse of the veil was revealed. He said: And I heard something about the Mothers of the Believers, so I went to them, one woman after another, until I came to one of them, and she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ is before me, admonishing his wives, and so God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"It may be that his Lord, if he divorces you...\" to the end of the verse."],[255,"Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd and 'Ali b. Zayd, from Anas, from 'Umar, with a similar narration, or close to it."],[256,"We sighted the new moon – I was a man of sharp sight – so I said: O Commander of the Believers, do you not see it? He said: I hope to see it, and I am on my bed. Then he began to tell us, saying: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ showed us the places where the people would fall on the night of Badr: This is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, if God wills, and this is the place where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, if God wills. And none of them moved from the place the Messenger of God had mentioned.'"],[257,"The dabb (a type of lizard) was mentioned in the presence of 'Umar, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ only found it distasteful, but he did not prohibit it."],[258,"Two men entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him, and he ordered two dinars for them. They left his presence and met 'Umar, and they spoke well of him and thanked him for what the Messenger of God ﷺ had done for them. I went in to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him what they had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'But so-and-so – I gave him something between ten and a hundred, and he did not say that. Indeed, one of them asks me and then goes away with his asking to the Fire.' 'Umar said: Why do you give us what is Fire? He said: 'They refuse unless they ask me, and God refuses for me to be miserly.'"],[259,"When 'Umar was stabbed, Suhayb came from his house and entered upon him, and stood by him weeping. 'Umar said to him: Are you weeping for me? He said: Yes, by God, I weep for you, O Commander of the Believers. He said: By God, I know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever is wept over is punished."],[260,"He used to give fatwas to the people about tamattu' (the mut'a of Hajj). A man said to him: Take it easy with some of your fatwas, for you do not know what the Commander of the Believers has introduced into the rites of pilgrimage afterwards. Then he met him and asked him. 'Umar said: I know that the Messenger of God ﷺ did it, and his Companions, but I disliked that they should keep having intercourse with them among the arak trees and then go to Hajj with their heads dripping."],[261,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at al-Batha', and he said: For what have you entered ihram? I said: I have entered ihram for what the Messenger of God ﷺ has entered ihram for. He said: 'Have you brought a sacrificial animal?' I said: No. He said: 'Then circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwa, and then exit ihram.' So I circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwa, then I went to a woman of my people and she combed my hair. I used to give fatwas to the people during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the caliphate of 'Umar. While I was speaking in Madinah, a man said: Do you know what the Commander of the Believers has introduced regarding the rites of pilgrimage? I said: O people, whoever we have given a fatwa about something, let him wait, for the Commander of the Believers is coming to you, so follow him. When he arrived, I said: O Commander of the Believers, what is this that you have introduced regarding the rites of pilgrimage? He said: If we follow the Book of God, then God, Mighty and Majestic, said: \"And complete the Hajj and 'Umra for God.\" And if we follow the Sunnah of our Prophet, then the Messenger of God ﷺ did not exit ihram until he had slaughtered the sacrificial animal."],[262,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abu Musa, from 'Umar, with a similar narration. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with a better chain than this chain, and a group has narrated it from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abu Musa."],[263,"If I live, God willing, I will expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula, and if I live, God willing, I will forbid that names like Rabah, Najah, Aflah, and Yasar be given."],[264,"\"Expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula.\""],[265,"Abu Bakr said: This hadith was also narrated by Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Umar. Amr b. Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us."],[266,"A man performed wudu for the Zuhr prayer but left a spot the size of a fingernail on his foot that the water did not reach. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him and said: “Go back and perfect your wudu.” So he went back, performed wudu, and prayed."],[267,"The people of Madinah will leave it, then they will inhabit it only briefly; then they will leave it and never inhabit it again."],[268,"I will surely expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until I leave no one in it but a Muslim."],[269,"Two men entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he ordered for them two dinars. They left his presence and met Umar, praising him and speaking well of him, and thanking him for what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done for them. Then I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what they said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “But so-and-so, I gave him between ten and a hundred, yet he did not say that. Indeed, one of them asks me and goes off with his request into the Fire.” They said: “Why do you give us what is Fire?” He said: “They refuse except to ask me, and Allah refuses for me to be miserly.”"],[270,"I became cheerful and kissed while I was fasting. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I have done a great thing today.” He said: “What is it?” I said: “I became cheerful and kissed while I was fasting.” He said: “What do you think if you rinse your mouth with water?” I said: “Then it would not harm.” He said: “So then what?”"],[271,"Umar said, mentioning what the people had attained of worldly things: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spend the day writhing, unable to find even low-quality dates to fill his belly.”"],[272,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, “And when the buried girl is asked” (Qur'an 81:8), he said: Qays b. Asim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I buried daughters alive in the Jahiliyyah.” He said: “Free a slave for each one of them.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am a camel owner.” He said: “Then sacrifice a camel for each one of them.”"],[273,"I was a guest of Umar. In the middle of the night, he got up to strike his wife, so I interposed between them. When he returned to his bed and lay down, he said: “O Ash'ath, remember from me something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: A man is not to be asked about why he strikes his wife.”"],[274,"I was sitting with Umar when a rider came to him and claimed that he had seen the crescent of Shawwal alone. Umar said: “O people, break your fast.” Then he stood, went to some water, performed wudu from it, and wiped over his leather socks. Then he stood and prayed Maghrib. The rider stood and said: “O Commander of the Believers, by Allah, I will not ask about what I saw except from you.” He said: “Yes, I saw one better than me do it, and the best of this Ummah. I saw Abu al-Qasim ﷺ do it just as you saw me do.”"],[275,"Umar said the takbir over Zaynab bt. Jahsh four times. Then he sent to the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking, “Who will enter her grave?” They said: “Whoever used to enter upon her during her life.” Then Umar said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: ‘The one among you who will join me soonest is the one with the longest hand.’ So they would stretch out their hands to compare. That was only because she was a craftswoman who used to help with what she made in the cause of Allah.”"],[276,"Uqbah b. Amir narrated to him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat speaking to his companions and said: “Whoever performs wudu and perfects it, then stands and prays two rak'ahs, his sins will be expiated, and he will be as on the day his mother gave birth to him.” Uqbah said: “Praise be to Allah who granted me to hear this hadith.” Umar, who was sitting, said: “Are you amazed at this? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said before this, more than this. He said before you came.” I said to Umar: “What did he say?” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever performs wudu and perfects it, then raises his gaze to the sky and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.’”"],[277,"Mu'awiya b. Salih narrated to us, from Rabi'a b. Yazid, from Abu Idris, from 'Uqba b. 'Amir, from 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu Bakr said: This hadith has been narrated from 'Uqba through more than one route, so we sufficed with those we have mentioned."],[278,"Whatever Allah gives you of this wealth without your asking for it or coveting it, accept it."],[279,"'Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, appointed me over the sadaqa. When I finished, he ordered a payment for me as my wages. I said, 'I only worked for Allah, and my reward is with Allah.' He said, 'Take the wages for what you did, for I worked during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave me wages. I said something like what you said, and he said: If you are given something without asking for it, then eat and give charity.'"],[280,"The martyrs are four: A man of excellent faith who meets the enemy and is true to Allah, fighting until he is killed – that is the one at whom people will raise their necks looking on the Day of Resurrection. A believer who meets the enemy and it is as if he is being struck with the thorns of the talh tree out of cowardice, then a stray arrow hits and kills him – that is in the second degree. A man who mixes a righteous deed with an evil one, meets the enemy and is true to Allah, fighting until he is killed – that is in the third degree. A man who was excessive against himself, meets the enemy and is true to Allah, fighting until he is killed – that is in the fourth degree."],[281,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better than for it to be filled with poetry."],[282,"The best of people are my generation, the one I am among. Then those who follow them. Then a people will arise among whom obesity will spread; they will testify without being asked to testify, and they will have clamor in their markets."],[283,"That 'Umar appointed Nafi' b. 'Abd al-Harith over Makkah. He met him at 'Usfan and said, 'Whom did you appoint' or he said, 'Whom did you leave as your deputy over Makkah?' He said, 'I left Ibn Abza as my deputy over them.' He said, 'Who is Ibn Abza?' He said, 'A client of ours.' He said, 'You leave a client as your deputy over them?' He said, 'O Commander of the Believers, he is a reciter of the Book of Allah, knowledgeable in the obligatory shares, and a judge.' 'Umar said, 'Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, raises some people by this Book and lowers others by it.'"],[284,"I saw the little bald one – meaning 'Umar – kissing the Stone, and he was saying, 'Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you.'"],[285,"Abu Bakr was the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah."],[286,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, he ordered the women of the Ansar, so they were gathered in a house. Then he sent 'Umar to them. 'Umar came and greeted us and said, 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to you.' We said, 'Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'I only take your pledge that you will not commit adultery, nor steal, nor kill your children, nor bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, nor disobey in what is right.' Then he extended his hand from outside the house, and we extended our hands from inside the house. He said, 'O Allah, bear witness.' And he ordered us to go out on the two 'Ids, the free women and the menstruating women, and we were forbidden from following funerals, and there is no Friday prayer upon us."],[287,"Allah and His Messenger are the patron of the one who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir."],[288,"Gold for gold is usury except hand to hand, and wheat for wheat is usury except hand to hand."],[289,"\"The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was among what Allah granted His Messenger as fay', from what the Muslims did not obtain by racing horses or camels. The Messenger of Allah used to withhold a year's provision for his family.\""],[290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had three special shares: Banu al-Nadir, Khaybar, and Fadak. As for Banu al-Nadir, it was a reserve for his emergencies. As for Fadak, it was a reserve for wayfarers. As for Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah divided it into three portions: two portions he distributed among the people, and one portion for his family's expenses. Whatever remained after his family's expenses, he withheld it, or he made it for the poor among the Muhajirun."],[291,"Actions are only by intentions, and every person will have what he intended. So whoever's migration was to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration was to a worldly gain he might attain, or a woman he might marry, his migration is to what he migrated for."],[292,"\"When the mu'adhdhin says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, and one of you says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; then he says: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, and he says: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; then he says: Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, and he says: Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; then he says: Hayya 'ala al-salah, and he says: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah; then he says: Hayya 'ala al-falah, and he says: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah; then he says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah, and he says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah, from his heart, he will enter Paradise.\""],[293,"Hisham b. 'Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from 'Asim b. 'Umar, from his father."],[294,"\"\"When the night approaches from here and the day departs from here and the sun sets, the fasting person has broken his fast.\""],[295,"\"For the nose, if it is entirely cut off, the full blood money; for the eye, fifty; for the hand, fifty; for the foot, fifty; for the penetrating wound, one-third of the blood money; for the bone-displacing wound, fifteen; for the wound exposing bone, five; for the tooth, five; and for each finger of those, ten, ten.\""],[296,"\"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness that no one says it from the truth of his heart except that Allah protects him from the heat of the Fire.\""],[297,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[298,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. When we were on part of the road, I spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was silent. Then I spoke to the Messenger of Allah and he was silent. Then I spoke to the Messenger of Allah and he was silent. So I urged my mount and moved aside, and I said: You asked the Prophet ﷺ three times, and each time he did not speak to you. How likely it is that a Qur'an will be sent down concerning you! No sooner did I hear a caller shouting to me than he said to me: O Ibn al-Khattab, a surah was sent down to me tonight which I would not love to have anything over which the sun rises in exchange for it. Then he recited: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.'"],[299,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys, and when we were on part of the road."],[300,"I donated a horse in the path of Allah, but the one who had it neglected it. I wanted to buy it back, so I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He said: Do not buy it, even if he gives it to you for a single dirham, for the one who takes back his gift is like a dog returning to its vomit."],[301,"A letter was written to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said to 'Abd Allah b. Arqam: \"Answer these people.\" So 'Abd Allah b. Arqam took it and wrote it. Then he came with the letter and presented it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"You have done well.\" That did not enter my mind until I was appointed [to a position], and I placed him over the treasury."],[302,"Why the ramal now, and the uncovering of the shoulders? God has brought Islam, and expelled disbelief and its people. Yet, even so, we will not abandon anything that was done in the time of the Messenger of God."],[303,"There was a man in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ whose name was 'Abd Allah, and he was nicknamed Himar. He used to make the Messenger of God ﷺ laugh. The Messenger of God ﷺ had flogged him for drinking, so one day he was brought and he flogged him. A man among the people said: \"O God, curse him! How often he is brought!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not curse him, for he loves God and His Messenger.\""],[304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to give charity. That coincided with some wealth I had, so I said: \"Today I will outdo Abu Bakr if I ever outdo him.\" I came with half of my wealth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What have you left for your family?\" I said: \"The same amount.\" Abu Bakr came with all that he had. He said: \"What have you left for your family?\" He said: \"God and His Messenger.\" I said: \"I will never compete with you in anything again.\""],[305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to give me a gift, and I would say: \"Would that you gave it to someone more in need of it than me.\" He would say: \"O 'Umar, what God gives you of this wealth without you asking or craving for it, then eat it and give it in charity.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me something, and I returned it. When I came to him, he said: \"What made you return what I sent to you?\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, you said: 'It is better for you not to ask people for anything.'\" He said: \"That is only when you ask people. What comes to you without asking is a provision God has provided for you.\""],[306,"'Umar b. al-Khattab said to a freed slave of his called Hunayy: \"O Hunayy, bring near the owner of the small flock and the little sheep, and leave me from the sheep of Ibn 'Affan and Ibn 'Awf. For if their livestock perish, they will return to wealth; but if the owner of the little sheep and the small flock perishes, he will come and say: 'O 'Umar, O 'Umar.' And water and pasture are easier for me. Indeed, these are their wealth for which they fought in the Jahiliyyah and upon which they embraced Islam.\""],[307,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him. He said: \"I have nothing to give you, but borrow until something comes to us and we give you.\" 'Umar said: \"God has not burdened you with this. You gave what you had; if you do not have anything, you are not obligated.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked what 'Umar said, until it was seen in his face. The man said: \"O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Give and do not fear any lessening from the Owner of the Throne.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ smiled and said: \"With this I have been commanded.\""],[308,"Every lineage and tie will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my lineage and my tie."],[309,"Use olive oil as a condiment and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree."],[310,"Were it not that people would be a single indistinguishable mass, no village would have been conquered except that I would have divided it as the Messenger of God ﷺ divided the spoils of Khaybar."],[311,"'Umar said to the Stone: \"I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing you, I would not kiss you.\""],[312,"Anā Warqāʾ, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from 'Umar, with a similar report. This hadith has been narrated through several channels from 'Umar."],[313,"O Allah, strengthen the religion by whichever of these two men is more beloved to You—either ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb or Abū Jahl b. Hishām. And I hope that the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is for you. I said: Direct me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—where is he? When they recognized sincerity in me, they directed me to the dwelling where he was. I came and knocked on the door. He said: Who is this? I said: ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb—and they knew my harshness toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and did not know of my Islam—so none of them dared open the door for me until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: Open for him; if Allah wills good for him, He will guide him. He said: The door was opened for me, and two men took hold of my upper arms until I drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: Release him. So they released me, and I sat before him. He took hold of the collar of my shirt and then said: Become a Muslim, O son of al-Khaṭṭāb; O Allah, guide him. I said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: The Muslims shouted takbīr so loudly that it was heard in the streets of Makkah. He said: They had been seventy before that, and when a man became Muslim and people learned of it, they would beat him and he would beat them. He said: I went to a man and knocked on his door. He said: Who is this? I said: ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. He came out to me, and I said to him: Do you know that I have become a Ṣābiʾ (i.e., changed my religion)? He said: Have you done so? I said: Yes. He said: Do not do it. He said: Then he entered the house and shut the door in my face. He said: I went to another man of Quraysh and called him. He came out, and I said to him: Do you know that I have become a Ṣābiʾ? He said: Have you done so? I said: Yes. He said: Do not do it. Then he entered the house and shut the door in my face. I said: This is nothing. He said: And then I was not beaten, and nothing was said to me. The man said: Would you like your Islam to become known? He said: I said: Yes. He said: When the people sit in the Ḥijr, go to so-and-so and say to him privately: Do you realize that I have become a Ṣābiʾ? For he rarely conceals anything. So I went to him when the people had gathered in the Ḥijr and said to him privately: Do you realize that I have become a Ṣābiʾ? He said: Have you done so? I said: Yes. He said: Then he called out at the top of his voice: Indeed, ʿUmar has become a Ṣābiʾ. He said: Those people rushed at me and kept beating me while I beat them until my maternal uncle came. It was said to him: ʿUmar has become a Ṣābiʾ. He stood upon the Ḥijr and called out at the top of his voice: Indeed, I have granted protection to my sister's son, so let no one touch him. He said: They dispersed from me. And I did not wish to see any Muslim being beaten except that I saw it. I said: This is nothing—people are being beaten while I am not beaten, and nothing is said to me. When the people sat in the Ḥijr, I went to my maternal uncle and said: Listen, I return your protection to you. He said: Do not do it. He said: I refused, and I kept being beaten and beating others until Allah made Islam prevail. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from Usāma b. Zayd, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿUmar except by Isḥāq b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥunaynī, and we do not know of any chain for the story of ʿUmar's Islam more sound than this chain, although al-Ḥunaynī—as we mentioned—left Madinah and his hadith became confused and disordered."],[314,"Cool down the prayer when the heat is intense, for intense heat is from the raging of Hellfire. Hellfire complained to its Lord: My parts are consuming one another, so it sought permission for two breaths, and He granted it. Thus intense heat is from the raging of Hellfire, and intense cold is from its zamharīr (extreme cold)."],[315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in Makkah presenting himself to the tribes of the Arabs, tribe by tribe, during the season of pilgrimage, finding no one to respond to what he called them to until this clan of the Anṣār came to him—for Allah granted them felicity and brought them honor—and they gave him refuge and supported him. May Allah reward them well on behalf of their Prophet. By Allah, we have not fulfilled for them what we pledged to them. We said to them: We are the rulers and you are the ministers. And if I live until the beginning of next year, no governor of mine will remain except an Anṣārī."],[316,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and there was a black boy massaging his back. I asked him about it, and he said: The she-camel bolted with me."],[317,"Islam will prevail until horses wade across the seas, and until merchants cross the sea. Then a people will appear who recite the Qurʾān and say: Who recites better than us? Who understands more than us? Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Is there any good in those? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Those are fuel for the Fire—those are from you, from this Ummah."],[318,"We had thought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slow in coming to us. The Anṣār used to go out to the edge of the Ḥarra and sit until the day grew bright; when the day grew bright and the sun became hot, they returned to their homes. ʿUmar said: While we were waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a Jewish man pointed from one of their fortresses and cried out at the top of his voice: O assembly of Arabs, this is your companion whom you are waiting for. ʿUmar said: I heard the commotion among the Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf and went out through the gate, and there were the Muslims donning their weapons. I set out with the people at noon, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the right-hand path until he stopped among the Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf."],[319,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ exact retribution from himself."],[320,"When wealth comes to me from al-Baḥrayn, I will give you this much and this much and this much—three times—filling his two hands. He said: Take with your hands. So he took with his hands and found it to be five hundred. He said: Return to it. Then he gave him the like of it. Then he distributed the remainder among the people, and each received ten dirhams—that is, for each one. When the next year came, wealth greater than that came to him, and he distributed it among them, and each person received twenty dirhams, and there remained a surplus of wealth. He said to the people: O people, a surplus of this wealth remains, and you have servants who work for you and labor for you. If you wish, we will give them a small share. So he gave them five dirhams each. They said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, if only you had favored the Muhājirūn. He said: The reward of those is with Allah; these are livelihoods, and equality in them is better than preference. When Abū Bakr ؓ died and ʿUmar ؓ was appointed caliph, Allah opened conquests for him, and wealth greater than that came to him. He said: Abū Bakr had an opinion concerning this wealth, and I have another opinion. I will not make one who fought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like one who fought alongside him. So he favored the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār. He assigned five thousand, five thousand to those among them who participated in Badr; and to those whose Islam preceded the Islam of the people of Badr, he assigned four thousand, four thousand. He assigned twelve thousand to the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—to each wife—except Ṣafiyya and Juwayriyya, to each of whom he assigned six thousand, six thousand, but they refused to take it. He said: I assigned them according to their emigration. They said: You did not assign them because of emigration; you assigned them because of their status with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we have the same status as them. He saw that and made them equal like them. He assigned twelve thousand to al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib because of his kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He assigned four thousand to Usāma b. Zayd, and five thousand each to al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, joining them to their father because of their kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He assigned three thousand to ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar. He said: O father, you assigned four thousand to Usāma b. Zayd and three thousand to me? There was no virtue for his father that was not for you, and no virtue for him that was not for me. He said: His father was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than your father, and he was dearer to the Messenger of Allah than you. He assigned two thousand each to the sons of the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār who participated in Badr. ʿUmar b. Abī Salama passed by him, and he said: Increase him by a thousand—or he said: Increase him by a thousand, O boy. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaḥsh said: For what reason do you increase him over us? There was no virtue for his father that was not for our fathers. He said: I assigned him two thousand because of Abū Salama, and I increased him by a thousand because of Umm Salama. If you have a mother like Umm Salama, I will increase you by a thousand. He assigned eight hundred to the people of Makkah, and to ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUthmān—who was the nephew of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh—he assigned eight hundred. He assigned two thousand dirhams to the son of al-Naḍr b. Anas. Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh said to him: Ibn ʿUthmān came to you, and you assigned him eight hundred, while a young man from the Anṣār came to you, and you assigned him two thousand. He said: I met this one's father on the day of Uḥud, and he asked me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: I think he has been killed. He drew his sword and bared his forearm and said: If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been killed, then Allah is ever-living and does not die. Then he fought until he was killed. And this one tends sheep—do you want me to make them equal? ʿUmar acted according to this throughout his life, until the last year in which he performed Hajj. Some people said: If the Commander of the Believers dies, we will appoint so-and-so—meaning Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh—and they said: The pledge to Abū Bakr was a sudden affair (faltah). He wanted to speak in the middle of the days of Tashrīq at Minā, but ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf said to him: O Commander of the Believers, this gathering is dominated by the rabble, and they will not bear your speech. Wait or postpone until you come to the land of emigration, where your companions and the abode of faith, the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, are, and then speak your words so that your speech will be borne. He said: He hastened his travel until he arrived in Madinah. He went out on Friday, praised and extolled Allah, then said: The saying of your sayer has reached me: If ʿUmar dies—or if the Commander of the Believers dies—we will appoint so-and-so and pledge allegiance to him, and the rule of Abū Bakr was a sudden affair. Yes, by Allah, it was a sudden affair, but where can we find someone like Abū Bakr to whom we can stretch our necks as we stretched them to Abū Bakr? Abū Bakr had an opinion, and I have an opinion. Abū Bakr saw to distribute equally, and I saw to favor. If I live until this year, I will return to Abū Bakr's opinion, for his opinion is better than mine. I have seen a vision, and I do not think it is anything but the approach of my term: I saw a red rooster peck me three pecks. Asmāʾ wept and said: A non-Arab slave will kill you. If I die, your affair is entrusted to these six with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he passed away: ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān, ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām, Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh, and Saʿd b. Mālik. If I live, I will make a covenant so that you will not perish. And indeed, stoning—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned, and we stoned after him. Were it not that you would say ʿUmar wrote what is not in the Book of Allah, I would write it. We have indeed recited in the Book of Allah: 'The old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them absolutely as a punishment from Allah, and Allah is Mighty and Wise.' Then I looked into the paternal aunt and the brother's daughter, and I did not make them heirs, nor do they inherit. If I live, I will open for you a way regarding that which you will recognize; if I die, Allah is my successor, and you will choose according to your opinion. I have established the dīwān and founded the garrison towns. I fear for you only one of two men: a man who interprets the Qurʾān contrary to its proper interpretation and fights for it, and a man who thinks he is more entitled to sovereignty than his companion and fights for it. He spoke these words on Friday and died ؓ on Wednesday. And this hadith has been narrated in approximate wording from ʿUmar concerning the description of his killing through various chains, but we do not know of it being narrated from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, in this complete form except through the hadith of Abū Maʿshar, from Zayd, from his father."],[321,"Captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was a woman among them who, whenever she found an infant among the captives, took it, pressed it to her belly, and suckled it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: Do you think this woman would throw her child into the fire? We said: No, by Allah, while she is able not to throw him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah is more merciful to His servant than this woman is to her child."],[322,"Muḥammad b. Abī ʿAdī and Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. Abī Ḥumayd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, from the Prophet."],[323,"Tell me who will have the greatest station with Allah on the Day of Resurrection. They said: The angels. He said: What prevents them, despite their nearness to their Lord? Rather, others. They said: The prophets. He said: What prevents them, while revelation descends upon them? Rather, others. They said: Then tell us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A people who come after you, who believe in me though they have not seen me, and who find the written page and believe in it. Those are the greatest of creation in station, and those are the greatest of creation in faith with Allah on the Day of Resurrection."],[324,"Shall I not tell you of the best of your rulers and their worst? They said: Yes. He said: The best of your rulers are those whom you love and who love you, and the worst of your rulers are those whom you hate and who hate you."],[325,"\"Who accompanied you on this journey of yours?\" I said: \"A people from Bakr b. Wa'il.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Your Bakri brother, do not trust him.'\""],[326,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once (for each limb)."],[327,"\"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may God's mercy be upon them both, on the shoulders of the Prophet ﷺ, and I said: 'What a fine mount is beneath you two!' He said: 'And what fine riders they are.'\""],[328,"Two brothers had a dispute, and each of them swore not to speak to his brother. They came to 'Umar, and he said to one of them: \"Expiate your oath and speak to your brother.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no vow in disobedience (to God), nor in severing ties of kinship.\""],[329,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father wants to take my wealth.\" He said: \"You and your wealth belong to your father.\""],[330,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ during Ramadan, the expedition of the Conquest and the expedition of Badr, and we broke our fast on both of them."],[331,"\"Whoever recites at night (the verse) 'So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteousness and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord,' he will have a light from 'Adan Abyan to Makkah, filled with angels.\""],[332,"The first woman to seek khul' in Islam was Habibah bt. Sahl. She was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I cannot bear to be with Thabit.\" He said to her: \"Will you return to him what you took from him?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He had married her for a garden of palm trees. Thabit said: \"Is that lawful, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Yes.\" And he did not assign for her any maintenance or lodging."],[333,"Sabigh al-Tamimi came to 'Umar b. al-Khattab and said: \"O Commander of the Believers, tell me about 'By those that scatter with scattering' (al-Dhariyat 51:1).\" He said: \"They are the winds, and had I not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it, I would not have said it.\" He said: \"Then tell me about 'And those that bear a burden' (51:2).\" He said: \"They are the clouds, and had I not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it, I would not have said it.\" He said: \"Then tell me about 'And those that distribute by command' (51:4).\" He said: \"They are the angels, and had I not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it, I would not have said it.\" He said: \"Then tell me about 'And those that run with ease' (51:3).\" He said: \"They are the ships, and had I not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it, I would not have said it.\""],[334,"\"The Qur'an was revealed in seven modes of recitation.\""],[335,"When revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, a buzzing like the buzzing of bees was heard near his face. Once revelation came down upon him, we remained silent until it was relieved from him. Then he faced the qiblah, raised his hands, and said: \"O God, increase us and do not decrease us; honor us and do not disgrace us; give us and do not deprive us; show us (Your favor) and do not show (favor) against us; and be pleased with us.\""],[336,"\"Whoever sleeps through his nightly portion (of recitation) and then recites it between the Fajr prayer and the Zuhr prayer, it is recorded for him as if he recited it at night.\""],[337,"'Umar used to come to the mosque of Quba on Mondays and Thursdays. One day he came and found no one in it from the people, so he said: \"Why do I not see anyone from the people in this mosque?\" He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and some of his companions while we were carrying its stones on our bellies. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laid its foundation with his own hand, and Jibril ﷺ was directing him toward the Ka'bah.\""],[338,"\"Whoever shades a warrior or shades the head of a warrior — the doubt is from Abu Bakr — Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us against every hypocrite with a knowing tongue."],[340,"I heard Abu Ghassan Rawh b. Hatim mention from Sulayman b. Harb, from Hammad b. Zayd, from Abu Suwayd b. al-Mughirah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from 'Umar, something similar. We do not know this hadith to be reported from 'Umar except through the hadith of al-Ahnaf and Abu 'Uthman in connected form. Suwayd b. al-Mughirah is a noble man from the people of Basra."],[341,"He prohibited silk except the amount of two fingers."],[342,"\"When two Muslim men meet and one greets the other, the most beloved of them to Allah is the one who is more cheerful toward his companion. When they shake hands, one hundred mercies descend upon them: ninety for the one who initiated, and ten for the one who shook hands.\""],[343,"Dawud b. Shabib narrated to us, from Hammad b. Salamah, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from Abu Rafi', from 'Umar b. al-Khattab."],[344,"He was at al-Hajun, and the polytheists rejected him, so he said: \"O Allah, show me a sign today after which I will not care who denies me.\" Then he was told: \"Call a tree,\" so he called a tree, and it came forward, plowing the ground until it reached him and greeted him. Then he commanded it, and it returned.\" Dawud said: \"to its place of growth,\" and 'Affan said: \"to its place.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I do not care who denies me after this from my people.\""],[345,"\"The world does not enter upon a people except that Allah casts enmity and hatred among them until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[346,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they praised it with good, so he said: \"It has become due.\" And a funeral was passed by him, and they praised it with evil, so he said: \"It has become due. You are the witnesses of Allah on earth,\" or \"the believers are the witnesses of Allah.\""],[347,"\"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will defend this religion with Christians from Rabi'ah on the bank of the Euphrates. I have not left any Bedouin except that I have killed him or he submits.\""],[348,"'Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a sermon on Friday. He mentioned the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and mentioned Abu Bakr, then said: \"I saw a rooster peck me three times, and I do not think it is but for the approach of my term. Some people order me to appoint a successor, but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, would not let His religion or His caliphate be lost, by the One Who sent His Prophet ﷺ. If a matter hastens me, the caliphate is a consultation among these six with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was pleased with them. I know that some people criticize this matter; I struck them with this hand of mine for the sake of Islam. If they do so, they are the enemies of Allah, the disbelievers, the misguided. Then I will not leave after me anything more important to me than kalalah. I have not reviewed anything with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I reviewed kalalah, and he was not harsh with me about anything as he was harsh with me about it, until he poked his finger into my chest and said: 'O 'Umar, is not the verse of summer at the end of Surat al-Nisa' sufficient for you?' If I live, I will judge in it with a ruling by which those who read the Quran and those who do not read the Quran will judge. O Allah, I call You to witness over the commanders of the garrison cities, for I sent them only to teach the people the Sunnah of their Prophet ﷺ, to distribute their spoils among them, and to raise to me whatever is unclear to them of their affairs. Then, O people, you eat two plants that I do not see except as evil: this onion and garlic. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he found their smell on a man in the mosque, order him to be taken out to al-Baqi'. So whoever eats them, let him kill them by cooking.\""],[349,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim, from Ma'dan, from 'Umar similarly. We do not know that Ma'dan narrated from 'Umar except this hadith, and its chain is sound. It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the dislike of garlic and onions through several routes: Ma'qil b. Yasar, Jabir b. 'Abdullah, Abu Hurayra, Anas b. Malik, and al-Mughira b. Shu'ba narrated that. We have mentioned it from 'Umar alone."],[350,"He came to a land called Dumin, from Hims, at the head of some ten-odd miles, and prayed two rak'as. I said to him, 'You pray two rak'as?' He said, 'I saw 'Umar pray two rak'as at Dhu al-Hulayfa, and he said: I do as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[351,"Allah will surely raise from a city in the Levant called Hims seventy thousand upon whom there will be no reckoning, between the olive trees, the wall, and the red sandy tract."],[352,"I met 'Umar b. al-Khattab and he said: 'What is your name?' I said: 'Masruq b. al-Ajda'.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Al-Ajda' is a devil.\" You are Masruq b. 'Abd al-Rahman.'"],[353,"'Umar addressed us and said: 'Do not go to excess in the dowers of women. If that were a mark of honor in this world or piety before Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have been the foremost among you in it. He never gave any of his wives a dower exceeding twelve uqiyyas.'"],[354,"He mentioned kalala and said: 'I never argued with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about anything as much as I argued with him about kalala, and he was never harsh with me about anything as he was harsh with me about it, until he poked me in the chest with his finger and said: \"Does not the verse of summer, which is at the end of Surat al-Nisa', suffice you?\"'"],[355,"'Umar prayed the dawn prayer at Jam' and said: 'The idolaters would not depart until the sun rose, and they would say: \"Shine, O Thabir.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ opposed them and departed before sunrise.'"],[356,"He used to seek refuge from five things: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness and cowardice; I seek refuge in You from the evil of old age; I seek refuge in You from the trial of the heart; and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave.'"],[357,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Supplicate Allah to admit me to Paradise.' He magnified the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and said: 'His Kursi encompasses the heavens and the earth, and it creaks like the creaking of a new saddle when it is ridden, from His weight.'"],[358,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man praying while supplicating, and said: 'Ask and you will be given.' It was 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud."],[359,"He passed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night while a man was reciting, and he began listening to his recitation. When he sat down supplicating, he said: 'Ask and you will be given.'"],[360,"Al-Hasan b. 'Ubayd Allah narrated this hadith from Ibrahim, from 'Alqama, from Qays or Ibn Qays, from a man of Ju'fa, from 'Umar b. al-Khattab, from the Prophet ﷺ. Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, from 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad, from al-Hasan b. 'Ubayd Allah."],[361,"If you are three on a journey, appoint one of you as your leader. That is the commander whom the Messenger of God appointed."],[362,"The prayer of al-Adha is two rak'ahs, the prayer of al-Fitr is two rak'ahs, and the prayer of Jumu'ah is two rak'ahs. It is complete, not shortened, on the tongue of the Prophet."],[363,"The prayer of travel is two rak'ahs, the prayer of Jumu'ah is two rak'ahs, the prayer of al-Fitr is two rak'ahs, and the prayer of al-Adha is two rak'ahs, complete, not shortened, on the tongue of Muhammad."],[364,"Al-Zubayr asked Umar for permission to participate in jihad. He said: 'Stay, for you have already striven alongside the Messenger of God.'"],[365,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to them with silk in one hand and gold in the other, and said: 'These two are forbidden for the males of my community and lawful for its females.'"],[366,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded a caller, who proclaimed: 'No drunk person should approach the prayer.'"],[367,"Adi b. Hatim came to Umar while he was giving to the people and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, do you not know me?' He said: 'Indeed, with the best knowledge. I know you: you accepted Islam when they disbelieved, you gave when they withheld, you fulfilled when they betrayed, and you came forward when they turned back.'"],[368,"I came to Umar b. al-Khattab while he was giving to the people. I approached him from his right, and he turned away from me. Then I approached from his left, and he turned away from me. Then I came to him from in front and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, do you not know me?' He said: 'Indeed, may God greet you with the best knowledge. I know you: you accepted Islam when they disbelieved, you gave when they withheld, you fulfilled when they betrayed, and you came forward when they turned back. The first charity that brightened the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ was the charity of your people when you brought it carrying it to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: 'Then I said: Since you know me, I do not care.'"],[369,"I heard Umar b. al-Khattab mention Anaza and say: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A tribe that is wronged, yet victorious.'"],[370,"Beware of sitting on roadways. If you must do so, then give the road its right. It was said: What is its right? He said: 'Lowering the gaze and returning the greeting.' I think he said: 'And guiding the lost.'"],[371,"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not come to women in their anuses."],[372,"If you were to rely on God with true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out hungry and return full."],[373,"I saw Umar kissing the Stone and saying, “I kiss you while knowing that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit, but I saw Abu al-Qasim ﷺ showing affection toward you.”"],[374,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, whenever reinforcements from the people of Yemen came to him, would ask them, “Is Uways b. Amir among you?” until he came upon Uways. He said, “Are you Uways b. Amir?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “From Murad, from Qaran?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Did you have leprosy that healed except for a spot the size of a dirham?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you have a mother?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Uways b. Amir will come to you with the reinforcements from the people of Yemen, from Murad, from Qaran. He had leprosy that healed except for a spot the size of a dirham. He has a mother and is devoted to her. If he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. So if you can get him to ask forgiveness for you, do so.’ So ask forgiveness for me.” So he asked forgiveness for him. Umar said to him, “Where do you intend to go?” He said, “Kufa.” He said, “Shall I write for you to its governor?” He said, “Being among the common people is more beloved to me.” He said, “The following year, a man from their nobles performed Hajj and met Umar, who asked him about Uways. He said, ‘I left him with a shabby house and few possessions.’ Umar said, ‘I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Uways b. Amir will come to you with the reinforcements from the people of Yemen, from Murad, then from Qaran. He had leprosy that healed except for a spot the size of a dirham. He has a mother and is devoted to her. If he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. So if you can get him to ask forgiveness for you, do so.”’ So he went to Uways and said, ‘Ask forgiveness for me.’ He said, ‘You have just returned from a righteous journey, so ask forgiveness for me.’ He asked forgiveness for him. He said, ‘Did you meet Umar?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ So he asked forgiveness for him. Then people became aware of him, and he went on his way.” Usayr said, “I clothed him with a burda, and whenever anyone saw him, they would say, ‘Where did Uways get this burda?’”"],[375,"He performed ablution three times, three times, and said, “Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.”"],[376,"I said to Uthman, “What led you to take al-Anfal, which is one of the Mathani, and Bara’a, which is one of the Mi’in, and place them together without writing between them the line ‘Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,’ and put them in one place? What led you to that?” Uthman ؓ said, “Surahs of varying numbers used to be revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When a verse was revealed to him, he would say, ‘Place it in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.’ Al-Anfal was among the first revealed in Madinah, and Bara’a among the last revealed, and its story resembled its story. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not clarify anything for us about that, so for that reason we placed them together and did not write between them the line ‘Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim.’”"],[377,"Sa’id b. Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Ya’la b. Hakim, from Nafi’, from Ibn Umar, from Uthman, from the Prophet."],[378,"“It is not lawful to shed the blood of a Muslim except for one of three: adultery after marriage, disbelief after Islam, or killing a person intentionally, for which he is to be killed.”"],[379,"He looked down upon them and said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a dream, and he said, ‘O Uthman, you will break your fast with us tonight.’” So he began the day fasting and was killed that day."],[380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me behind from Badr and allotted me a share. Uthman said regarding the pledge of al-Ridwan, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck his right hand on his left for me, and the left hand of the Messenger of Allah is better than my right hand.”"],[381,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times, three times."],[382,"I am telling you a hadith that nothing prevented me from telling you except sparing you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever guards one night behind the vulnerable areas of the Muslims is better than a thousand nights in which the night is spent in prayer and the day in fasting.”"],[383,"He asked Uthman about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. He said, “He only needs ablution.” Uthman said, “I bear witness that I heard that from the Messenger of Allah.”"],[384,"Uthman went out for Hajj and saw Abdullah b. Ja’far wearing safflower-dyed clothes. Uthman said to him, “Why do you wear safflower-dyed clothes when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade safflower-dyed clothes?” Ali said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid you or him from safflower-dyed clothes; he only forbade me.”"],[385,"Uthman tied his waist wrapper up to the middle of his shin and said: \"This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ tied his waist wrapper.\""],[386,"\"Whoever cheats the Arabs will not enter into my intercession, and my affection will not reach him.\""],[387,"Abu Bakr ؓ sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was lying on his bed wearing Aisha's cloak. He granted Abu Bakr permission while he was like that, and he fulfilled his need and then left. Then Umar sought permission to enter upon him while he was in that same state, and he fulfilled his need and then left. Then Uthman sought permission to enter upon him, so he sat up and said to Aisha: \"Gather your garments around you.\" He said: \"So I fulfilled my need and then left.\" Aisha said: \"I did not see you alarmed for Abu Bakr and Umar as you were alarmed for Uthman.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Uthman is a shy man, and I feared that if I granted him permission while I was in that state, he would not reach me concerning his need.\""],[388,"\"Do you think that if one of you had a flowing stream between his house and his place of work in which he bathed five times every day, would any of his dirt remain?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"So it is with the five prayers.\""],[389,"\"Whoever says when he enters upon the morning and when he enters upon the evening: 'In the name of God with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm,' nothing will harm him. And if he says it in the morning, nothing will harm him until evening, and if he says it in the evening, nothing will harm him until morning.\""],[390,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Zamzam and said: \"Draw water, and were it not that you would be overcome for it, I would draw too.\""],[391,"He saw a funeral procession approaching, and when he saw it he stood up for it. Then he reported that he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ doing that."],[392,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ eat bread and meat and then pray without performing ablution."],[393,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik b. Anas, from Nafi', from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[394,"Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Aruba, narrated to us, from Matar and Ya'la b. Hakim, from Nafi', from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban b. Uthman, from Uthman: that the Prophet ﷺ."],[395,"Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[396,"Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[397,"Sulayman b. Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[398,"\"A person in ihram may not marry, nor arrange a marriage.\""],[399,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz sent to Aban: 'I intend to marry, so attend the wedding.' He said: 'That was in Makkah, while he was in ihram.' Aban sent back to him: 'I heard Uthman say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A person in ihram may not marry, nor arrange a marriage.'"],[400,"Ahmad said: Ishaq said: Fulayh said: And Abd al-A'la and Abd al-Jabbar, the two sons of Nubayh b. Wahb, narrated to me, from their father, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[401,"Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub b. Musa, from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban b. Uthman, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[402,"Muhammad b. Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub b. Musa, from Nubayh b. Wahb, from Aban, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[403,"\"If a person in ihram has a complaint in his eye, he should bandage it with aloe.\""],[404,"\"The first to intercede on the Day of Resurrection will be the prophets, then the martyrs, then the muezzins.\""],[405,"My father said to me: 'O my son, if you are given any authority over the people, honor the Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever wishes humiliation for the Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him.'"],[406,"I was present with Uthman on the day he was besieged, and the people were in the area of the funerals. If a pebble had been thrown, it would not have fallen except on a man's head. He said: I saw Uthman look out from the small door that is next to the Station of Jibril ﷺ and say: 'Is Talhah among you?' They remained silent. He said: 'Is Talhah among you?' They remained silent. He said: 'Is Talhah among you?' They remained silent three times. Then Uthman said: 'I never thought you would be in a group that hears my call three times and does not answer me.' He said: 'I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at such-and-such a place, and I and you were with him, no one else but me and you, and he said to you: O Talhah, every prophet has a companion from his nation in Paradise, and this Uthman is my companion in Paradise?' He said: 'O Allah, yes.' Then he turned away from him."],[407,"A ram from the Quraysh will be buried in Makkah, called Abdullah, upon him will be the like of half the sins of the people."],[408,"Uthman sat in a place and ate bread and meat, then stood up to pray and said: 'I ate what the Prophet ﷺ ate, I sat where the Prophet ﷺ sat, and I did as the Prophet ﷺ did.'"],[409,"Uthman performed wudu: he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nostrils three times, washed his face three times, his right hand three times, his left hand three times, wiped over his head, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform wudu like this."],[410,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu three times for each limb."],[411,"I heard Uthman say on the pulpit: I used to buy dates and measure them into my containers, then I would take them down to the market and say, for them, such and such [price], and I would take its profit and leave the buyers to deal with it. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: When you buy, measure; and when you sell, measure out."],[412,"Uthman raised his voice against Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. Abd al-Rahman said to him: Why do you raise your voice against me when I was present at Badr and you were not, and I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you did not, and you fled on the day of Uhud and I did not flee? Uthman said: As for your saying that you were present at Badr and I was not, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me behind to care for his daughter and allotted me a share and gave me my reward. As for your saying that you pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I did not, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to some people among the polytheists, and you knew that. When I was delayed, he struck his right hand over his left and said: This is for Uthman b. Affan. The left hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than my right hand. As for your saying that I fled on the day of Uhud and you did not flee, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Indeed, those of you who turned back on the day the two armies met, it was Satan who caused them to slip because of some of what they had earned, and Allah has already forgiven them. So why do you reproach me for a sin that Allah has already forgiven me?"],[413,"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a man who commits adultery after being married, or one who disbelieves after Islam, or one who kills a person deliberately."],[414,"Do not sell a dinar for two dinars, nor a dirham for two dirhams."],[415,"Nothing prevents me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that I might be the most retentive of his companions regarding him. But I testify that I heard him say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[416,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[417,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him something like it in Paradise."],[418,"He forbade silk, except the amount of two fingers."],[419,"Retaliation will be taken for the hornless sheep from the horned one."],[420,"No man's feet become dusty in the path of Allah—or no man's feet become dusty in the path of Allah—except that Allah makes the Fire forbidden for him. I never saw more people walking than on that day."],[421,"It reached ‘Uthmān that the delegation of the people of Egypt had set out, so he met them at a village of his outside al-Madīnah, and he disliked that they should enter upon him—or something like that. When they learned of his location, they came to him and said, “Call for the muṣḥaf for us.” So he called for one—meaning by it—and said, “Open it.” He recited until he reached this verse: “Say, ‘Have you seen what Allah has sent down for you of provision, and you made of it unlawful and lawful?’ Say, ‘Has Allah permitted you, or do you fabricate against Allah?’” They said, “Did Allah’s protected pasture permit you to do this, or do you fabricate against Allah?” He said, “Continue; it was revealed concerning such-and-such. As for the protected pasture, ‘Umar protected the pasture for the camels of the zakāh. When I was appointed, I did as he did, and I did not increase beyond what he increased.” I think he said, “And at that time I was a man of such-and-such years.” Then he said, “They asked him about matters, and he kept saying, ‘Continue; it was revealed concerning such-and-such.’ Then they asked him about matters he recognized for which he had no way out, and he said, ‘Seek Allah’s forgiveness.’ Then he said, ‘What do you want?’ They said, ‘We want that the people of al-Madīnah should not receive stipends, for this wealth belongs to those who fought for it and to these elders among the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.’” He said, “So he accepted and they accepted.” He said, “And they took an undertaking from him.” I think they wrote a document against him, and he took an undertaking from them that they would not split the stick or separate from the community. He said, “So he accepted and they accepted, and they set off with him to al-Madīnah. He ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said, ‘By Allah, I have never seen a delegation better than this delegation. Indeed, whoever has crops should go to his crops, and whoever has a milking animal should milk it. Indeed, you have no wealth with us; this wealth is for those who fought for it and for these elders among the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.’” He said, “The people became angry and said, ‘This is a trick of the Umayyads.’ The delegation returned satisfied. When they were on part of the road, a rider appeared to them, then left them, then returned to them and insulted them. They seized him and said, ‘What is your business? You have some matter.’ He said, ‘I am the messenger of the Commander of the Believers to his governor in Egypt.’ They searched him and found with him a letter in ‘Uthmān’s name, sealed with his seal, ordering that they be crucified or their necks struck or their hands and feet cut off.” He said, “So they returned and said, ‘He has broken the pact, and Allah has made his blood lawful.’ They came to al-Madīnah and went to ‘Alī and said, ‘Did you not see the enemy of Allah writing about us such-and-such? Stand with us against him.’ He said, ‘By Allah, I will not stand with you.’ They said, ‘Then why did you write to us?’ He said, ‘By Allah, I never wrote you any letter.’ They looked at one another, then some of them said, ‘Is it for this you fight, or for this you become angry?’ ‘Alī left and settled in a village outside al-Madīnah. They came to ‘Uthmān and said, ‘Did you write about us such-and-such?’ He said, ‘There are only two options: either you bring two witnesses, or I swear by Allah: I did not write, dictate, or know. You know that a letter can be written in a man’s name and a seal can be engraved on a seal.’” He said, “So they besieged him. One day he looked over them and said, ‘Peace be upon you.’ He said, ‘I did not hear anyone answer him except a man who answered in himself.’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, do you know that I bought the well of Rūmah with my own money to drink sweet water from it, and I made my rope like the rope of any Muslim?’ It was said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then why do you prevent me from drinking its water, until I am forced to seawater?’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, do you know that I bought such-and-such with my own money and added it to the mosque?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Do you know of anyone prevented from praying there before me?’ Then he mentioned things the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, and I think he mentioned his writing of al-Mufaṣṣal with his own hand.” He said, “So the prohibition spread, and it was said, ‘Wait regarding the Commander of the Believers.’” This ḥadīth we do not know anyone narrated except al-Mu‘tamir b. Sulaymān from his father."],[422,"We set out as pilgrims and entered al-Madīnah. While we were placing our saddles, a man came to us and said, “The people have gathered in the mosque in alarm.” He said, “So I and my companion went, and there were the people gathered in the middle of the mosque around a group. I made my way through them, and there were ‘Alī, al-Zubayr, Ṭalḥah, and Sa‘d. It was not long before ‘Uthmān came walking in the mosque wearing two yellow wraps or one yellow wrap, which he had raised over his head. I said to my companion, ‘Stay where you are until I see what he has come for.’ When he drew near them, it was said, ‘This is Ibn ‘Affān.’ He said, ‘Is ‘Alī here?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Is Ṭalḥah here?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Is al-Zubayr here?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Is Sa‘d here?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever buys the mirbad of Banū so-and-so, Allah will forgive him,” and I bought it for twenty or twenty-five thousand and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have bought it,” and he said, “Put it in the mosque—or he said, in the mosque of the Muslims—and its reward is yours”?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever buys the well of Rūmah, Allah will forgive him,” and I bought it for such-and-such and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I have bought it for such-and-such,” and he said, “Make it a watering place for the Muslims, and its reward is yours”?’ They said, ‘O Allah, yes.’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the faces of the people on the day of the army of hardship and said, “Whoever equips these men, Allah will forgive him,” and I equipped them until they lacked neither a nose-rein nor a hobble’? They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘O Allah, bear witness; O Allah, bear witness,’ three times, then he left."],[423,"May Allah forgive a man who is easygoing when he sells, easygoing when he buys, easygoing when he settles a debt, and easygoing when he collects a debt."],[424,"I saw ‘Uthmān perform ablution: he washed his palms three times, washed his face three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his forearms three times each, wiped his head and his ears, their outside and inside, passed his fingers between his toes, and passed his fingers through his beard three times. Then he washed his face before his hands. Then he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do just as you saw me do.”"],[425,"I saw ‘Alī and ‘Uthmān perform ablution three times each, and they said, “This is how we saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.”"],[426,"Al-Walīd b. ‘Uqbah met ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. ‘Awf and said, “Why do you not come to the Commander of the Believers and visit him?” ‘Abd al-Raḥmān said to him, “Convey to him from me that I was not absent from Badr, and I did not flee on the day of ‘Aynayn.” This reached ‘Uthmān, and he said, “As for his saying, ‘I was not absent from Badr,’ I stayed behind to care for the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he allotted me my share. Whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share, it is as if he was present. As for his saying, ‘I did not flee on the day of ‘Aynayn,’ Allah, mighty and majestic, has forgiven all those who fled. So why reproach me for a sin Allah has forgiven?”"],[427,"The best of you—and the other said: the most excellent of you—is the one who learns the Qur’an and teaches it."],[428,"Qays narrated to us, from ‘Alqamah b. Marthad, from Sa‘d b. ‘Ubaydah, from Abū ‘Abd al-Raḥmān, from ‘Uthmān, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[429,"He adjured them, saying, “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Ḥirā’ with me, and Abū Bakr, and he mentioned some people of his Companions, and it moved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Be still, for upon you is none but a prophet, a ṣiddīq, or a martyr.’ I think so.” He said, “They said, ‘Yes.’”"],[430,"My father narrated to me, from Shu‘bah, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ‘Abd al-Raḥmān, from ‘Uthmān, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This ḥadīth we do not know is reported from ‘Uthmān except through this channel that we mentioned, unless Yūnus b. Abī Isḥāq differed in its chain and reported it from his father, from Abū Salamah. We have not memorized it except from the ḥadīth of Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ‘Abd al-Raḥmān, and no one reported it from Shu‘bah except ‘Uthmān b. Jabalah."],[431,"We came with ‘Abdullāh to ‘Uthmān, and ‘Uthmān said to ‘Abdullāh, “What remains of your desire for women?” ‘Abdullāh said, “Come close, ‘Alqamah,” and I was a young man, so I came close. ‘Uthmān said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to a group of unmarried young men and said, ‘Whoever among you has the means should marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts; and whoever cannot, let him fast, for it is a shield for him.’”"],[432,"We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in travel and at home, and he used to visit the sick among the Muslims and attend their funerals—or he said, follow their funerals."],[433,"That Uthman said on the Day of the House: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with me, and I am patiently restraining myself for it.'"],[434,"Whoever prays Isha in congregation is like standing half the night in prayer, and whoever prays Isha and Fajr in congregation is like standing the whole night in prayer."],[435,"Uthman used to forbid mut'ah, and Ali used to command it. Uthman said to Ali about that. Ali said: 'You know that we performed mut'ah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Yes, but we were afraid.'"],[436,"Uthman sat on the benches and we sat with him. When the mu'adhdhin came, he called for water about a mudd, and performed wudu. Then he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu like this wudu of mine.' Then he said: 'Whoever performs wudu like my wudu, then stands and prays Zuhr, he will be forgiven for what is between it and Asr prayer. And whoever prays Asr, he will be forgiven for what is between it and Maghrib prayer. And whoever prays Maghrib, he will be forgiven for what is between it and Isha prayer. And whoever prays Isha, he will be forgiven for what is between it and Fajr prayer—or he said Subh prayer. Then if he gets up, performs wudu, and prays, he will be forgiven for what is between it and Zuhr. These are the good deeds that remove the evil deeds.' They said: 'These are the good deeds. So what are the enduring righteous deeds?' Uthman said: 'They are: La ilaha illa Allah, Subhan Allah wa bi-hamdih, Allahu Akbar, Al-hamdu lillah, and La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.'"],[437,"He said on the minbar: 'I used to conceal from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then it occurred to me to narrate it to you so that a man may choose for himself what seems best to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Ribat for one day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in any other station.\"'"],[438,"I saw Ali b. Abi Talib and Uthman praying on the day of Fitr and Adha, and they mentioned or said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days.'"],[439,"My family married me to a slave woman of theirs. She gave birth to a black boy like me. Then a Roman slave called Yuhannis had relations with her. She became pregnant and gave birth to another who was like a gecko of the geckos. I said: 'What is this?' She said: 'He belongs to Yuhannis.' I went to Uthman and mentioned that to him. He sent for her and said: 'I judge between you two by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged that the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Alone.' Then she became pregnant and gave birth to a boy like me, two black ones and a red one, and they were attributed to me."],[440,"I entered upon Ibn Dara in his house, and he heard me rinsing my mouth. He said: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'At your service.' He said: 'Shall I inform you about the wudu of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I saw Uthman b. Affan while he was at the benches. He called for water for wudu, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, wiped his head, washed his forearms, and washed his feet. Then he said: \"Whoever loves to look at the wudu of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him look at this wudu of mine.\"'"],[441,"Faith is Yemeni, and the support of faith is in Qahtan. Harshness is in the descendants of Adnan. Himyar is the head of the Arabs and their fang. Madhhij is their skull and their protection. Al-Azd is their shoulder and their cranium. Hamdan is their withers and their summit. O Allah, honor the Ansar, by whom Allah established the religion, who sheltered me, helped me, and protected me. They are my companions in this world and my followers in the Hereafter, and the first of my ummah to enter Paradise."],[442,"We were sitting with Uthman, and he called for water to perform wudu. He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no person for whom a prescribed prayer comes, and he perfects its wudu, its humility, and its bowing, except that it becomes an expiation for the sins before it.\"' I think he said: 'As long as it is not a major sin, and that for all time.'"],[443,"Uthman dozed on the day he was killed, then woke up. Then he said: 'Were it not that you would say that Uthman wished his wish, I would have narrated to you.' He said: 'We said.'"],[444,"I entered upon Uthman while he was besieged. He said: 'O Kathir, I do not think I will be anything but killed this day of mine.' He said: 'I said: \"May Allah give you victory over your enemy.\"' He said: 'Then he repeated to me, and I said to him: \"Were you told something about it?\" He said: \"No, but I stayed awake this night. When it was near dawn, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar. The Prophet of Allah said: 'O Uthman, do not detain us, for we are waiting for you.'\" So he was killed that day of his.' He said: 'I said: \"Was the one who said to Uthman, Kathir?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[445,"There are three things after which a son of Adam has no merit beyond that of a rough bedouin: this food, a garment to cover him, and a house to shelter him. Anything beyond that, a son of Adam has no merit in it."],[446,"Whoever dies knowing that Allah is true will enter Paradise."],[447,"Whoever completes the ablution as Allah has commanded him, the prescribed prayers are expiations for what is between them."],[448,"Mis'ar narrated to us, from Jami' b. Shaddad, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[449,"I saw Uthman perform ablution: he washed his hands three times, washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution like this, and he said: Whoever performs ablution with less than this, it suffices him."],[450,"He called for water for ablution."],[451,"He called for water for ablution, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, and his forearms three times each, wiped his head and the tops of his feet, then laughed and said: Will you not ask me what made me laugh? We said: What made you laugh, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I laughed because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water for ablution near this place, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed ablution as I have performed ablution, then laughed as I laughed, then said: Will you not ask me what made me laugh? We said: What made you laugh, O Prophet of Allah? He said: It made me laugh that when a servant performs ablution and washes his face, Allah removes from him every sin his face committed; when he washes his forearms, it is the same; when he wipes his head, it is the same; when he purifies his feet, it is the same."],[452,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh b. Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ, and Mu'adh b. Hisham did not say: from his father, from Qatada, from Muslim b. Yasar."],[453,"Uthman called for water for ablution, intending to go out for prayer on a cold night. I brought him water, and he washed his face and hands. I said: That is enough for you; you have completed the ablution, and the night is severely cold. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A servant does not complete the ablution except that Allah forgives him his past and future sins."],[454,"He was brought water and performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, and his hands three times each, and wiped his head until he completed the ablution, and said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution."],[455,"Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from his father, from 'Urwa, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This hadith was narrated from 'Urwa by Hisham, and it was narrated from Hisham by a group, one of them being Shu'ba, so we sufficed with those we mentioned from Hisham. Abu al-Aswad narrated it from 'Urwa, from Humran, from Uthman, and Ibn Lahi'a narrated it from him. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr narrated it from 'Urwa, from Humran, from Uthman."],[456,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times each."],[457,"One day the call to prayer was given while I was with Uthman. Uthman ؓ said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then goes to an obligatory prayer, except that it is an expiation for what occurred between it and the next prayer.\""],[458,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from 'Asim, from al-Musayyib, from Musa b. Talha, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith was narrated by Hammad b. Salama, from 'Asim b. Bahdala, but he did not connect it as Abu 'Awana connected it."],[459,"Uthman performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, his hands three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution just as I have performed ablution. Then he said: 'Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then prays two rak'ahs without letting his mind wander during them, his previous sins will be forgiven.'\""],[460,"And Ahmad b. Mansur b. Sayyar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' b. Yazid, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[461,"And 'Urwa narrated it to me, from Humran, from Uthman. We do not know that 'Ata' b. Yazid narrated from Humran, from Uthman, except this hadith."],[462,"I brought Uthman his ablution water. He said: \"Some people narrate hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I do not know what they are. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution like this ablution of mine, then he said: 'Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, his previous sins will be forgiven, and his prayer and his walking to the mosque will be an extra reward (nafilah).'\""],[463,"\"Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, sins depart from his body until they depart from beneath his fingernails.\""],[464,"Uthman called for a clay vessel of water in the area of the funerals. He rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times each, wiped his head and his ears—their outside and inside—once, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: \"I saw your Prophet ﷺ do this.\""],[465,"I was with Uthman. He called for ablution water and performed ablution. When he finished, he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution as I have performed ablution. When he finished, he smiled and said: 'Do you know why I smiled?'\" He said: We said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"When a Muslim servant performs ablution and completes his ablution, then enters his prayer and completes his prayer, he comes out of his prayer as he came out of his mother's womb.\""],[466,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and perfect it. Then he said: \"Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine—or like this ablution of mine—then comes to the mosque and prays two rak'ahs, his previous sins will be forgiven.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not be deceived.\""],[467,"\"Whoever performs ablution and completes it fully, then walks to an obligatory prayer, will be forgiven.\""],[468,"I saw Uthman ؓ call for water and perform ablution. Then he said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever purifies himself and perfects his purification, then prays, his previous sins will be expiated.'\" Then he turned to his companions and said: \"I adjure you by Allah—I think he said it three or four times—did you hear?\" They said: \"Yes, we heard.\""],[469,"Imran b. Hudayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Ubayd, from Humran, from Uthman."],[470,"\"Whoever knows that prayer is a right incumbent upon him—or a right obligatory—enters Paradise.\""],[471,"Uthman performed ablution: he washed his face three times, his hands three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times each. Then he said: \"I performed ablution as the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution.\" Then a bone with meat was brought and he picked it clean, saying: \"I ate as the Messenger of God ate.\""],[472,"He called for water for ablution and washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his right hand three times, his left hand three times, wiped his head and ears, then washed his right foot three times and his left three times. Then he said: \"Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution.\""],[473,"He called for water for ablution while some of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ were with him. He poured with his right hand over his left and washed them three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head and washed his feet, cleaning them thoroughly. Then he said: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution like this ablution, and he said: 'Perform ablution as you have seen me perform ablution.'\" Then he said: \"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs, his sins will be like the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[474,"When Uthman stood at a grave he would weep until his beard became wet. It was said to him: \"Paradise and the Fire are mentioned to you and you do not weep, yet you weep over this?\" He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The grave is the first stage of the Hereafter. If one is saved from it, what comes after is easier; if one is not saved from it, what comes after is more severe.'\""],[475,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at the grave of a man while he was being buried. When the burial was finished, he said: \"Ask forgiveness for your brother and ask God to make him steadfast, for he is being questioned now.\""],[476,"God has one hundred and seventeen divine laws; whoever meets Him with one of them will enter Paradise."],[477,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a woman from shaving her head.\""],[478,"Abd al-Rahman b. Udays al-Balawi, one of those who pledged allegiance under the tree, came and ascended the pulpit. He praised and extolled God and mentioned Uthman. Abu Thawr said: I entered upon Uthman and he said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me to his daughter, then to another daughter. Then I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with this—meaning his right hand—and I have never touched my private part with it, nor have I disappeared (to relieve myself) with it, nor wished with it, nor drunk wine in the time of ignorance or in Islam. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Who will buy this plot and add it to the mosque, and he will have a house in Paradise?' So I bought it and added it to the mosque.\""],[479,"Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said to us: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to recite as you have been taught.\""],[480,"Umar was brought wealth and divided it among the Muslims; some of it remained. He consulted about it, and they said: \"If only you would leave it for a contingency that may occur.\" Ali remained silent. He said: \"What is wrong with you, Abu al-Hasan, that you do not speak?\" He said: \"The people have told you.\" Umar said: \"You must speak.\" He said: \"God has already determined the division of this wealth,\" and he reminded him of the story of the wealth of Bahrain when it came to the Prophet ﷺ and night fell before he could divide it. He prayed the prayers in the mosque, and I saw that in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ until he finished. Then he said: \"By all means, you shall divide it,\" and Ali divided it. Talha said: I received eight hundred dirhams from it."],[481,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently. I felt too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ myself, so I told al-Miqdad to ask him. He asked him, and he said: \"It requires wudu.\""],[482,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently. I felt too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah myself, so I told a man to ask him while I was present. He said: \"It requires wudu.\""],[483,"He entered upon Umar while he was shrouded and said: I hope Allah will gather you with your two companions, because I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I went, Abu Bakr, and Umar; I did, Abu Bakr, and Umar.\""],[484,"The Prophet ﷺ \"permitted game meat for the pilgrim in ihram.\""],[485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[486,"When the verse 'And warn your closest kindred' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ali, prepare a leg of sheep with a sa' of food, and gather for me Banu Hashim\" – at that time they numbered forty men or forty minus one. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the food, placed it among them, and they ate until full, though among them was one who would eat a whole young she-camel with its condiments. Then he took the bowl, and they drank from it until quenched, meaning from the milk. Some of them said: \"We have never seen anything like this sorcery\" – they thought it was Abu Lahab who said it. He said: \"O Ali, prepare a leg of sheep with a sa' of food and prepare a cup of milk.\" He said: I did so, and they ate as they had eaten the first day and drank as they had drunk the first time, and there remained leftovers just as there had been the first time. He said: \"We have never seen sorcery like today.\" He said: \"O Ali, prepare a leg of sheep with a sa' of food and prepare a cup of milk.\" He said: I did so. He said: \"O Ali, gather for me Banu Hashim.\" So I gathered them, and they ate and drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then preempted them and said: \"Which of you will settle my debt on my behalf?\" He said: I remained silent, and the people remained silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated the words, and I said: \"I will, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"You, O Ali? You, O Ali?\""],[487,"My beloved forbade me from three things – I do not say he forbade the people: wearing gold rings, wearing qassi and mufaddam garments, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[488,"My beloved ﷺ forbade me from wearing gold rings, wearing qassi garments, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[489,"My beloved ﷺ forbade me – I do not say he forbade the people – from wearing gold rings, wearing qassi and mufaddam garments, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[490,"If your waist-wrapper is small or tight, wrap it around yourself; but if it is wide, then throw it over yourself."],[491,"When I proposed to Fatimah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"What do you have?\" I said: \"I have nothing.\" He said: \"Where is your Hutami shield?\" He said: So I brought it to him, and he married me to Fatimah."],[492,"And Sa'id b. Abi Arubah narrated it from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet ﷺ said to Ali. Thus Abda b. Sulayman narrated from Sa'id. Harun b. Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Abda b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id."],[493,"Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Muhammad b. Talha b. Yazid b. Rukana, from Ubayd Allah al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas:"],[494,"He said: Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ entered after he had urinated, and he called for water for ablution. We brought him a vessel, and he took about a mudd. When it was placed before him, he said: O Ibn Abbas, shall I not perform ablution as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution? He said: I said: Yes. He said: He tilted the vessel over his hand and washed it three times, then rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out. Then he took a handful of water with both hands and threw it onto his face, then the second time likewise, then the third time likewise. Then he inserted his thumbs into the front of his ears. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it over his forelock, then let it flow over his face. Then he washed his right hand up to the elbows, and the left likewise. Then he wiped his head and the backs of his ears. Then he took a handful of water with both hands and dashed it onto his feet, then the second time likewise, then the third time likewise."],[495,"\"Put Quraysh forward and do not go ahead of it. Were it not that Quraysh might become arrogant, I would tell it what it has with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[496,"I heard Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ say to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You are trustworthy in heaven and trustworthy on earth.\""],[497,"\"The best of its women is Maryam bt. Imran, and the best of its women is Khadija bt. Khuwaylid.\""],[498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, when distress befell me, to say: \"There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to \"wash him from his well, the well of Ghars.\""],[500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me words to say at times of distress when it befalls me, so memorize them, and I memorized them. He said: Say: \"There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\" He said: When a matter distresses you."],[501,"Usama b. Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ka'b, from Abdullah b. Shaddad, from Abdullah b. Ja'far, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[502,"I witnessed Uthman and Ali. Uthman used to forbid the Umrah and combining it with Hajj. He said: Ali would enter ihram for both of them together. He said: They met, and Uthman said to him: You want nothing but to oppose me. He said: I do not want to oppose you, but I will not abandon something I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do because of the saying of any person."],[503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was \"not tall, nor short, with a large head and beard, coarse palms and feet, his face tinged with redness. When he walked, he leaned forward as if descending a slope. I have not seen before him or after him anyone like him.\""],[504,"\"Ask Allah for guidance and right direction. And remember by guidance your guidance to the path, and by right direction your straightness in shooting the arrow.\""],[505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing yellow-dyed garments."],[506,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer, and I would have delayed the last evening prayer until a third of the night had passed. For when the first third of the night has passed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and remains there until dawn breaks, saying: 'Is there any who asks, that he may be given? Is there any who supplicates, that he may be answered? Is there any seeking intercession, that he may be granted it? Is there any penitent seeking forgiveness, that he may be forgiven?'"],[507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the evening of Arafat with Usama riding behind him and said: 'This is the standing place, and all of Arafat is a standing place.'"],[508,"I asked Ali b. Abi Talib: 'O Abu al-Hasan, which is better: walking behind the funeral procession or in front of it?' He said: 'O Abu Sa'id, does someone like you ask about this?' I said: 'Who would ask about this except someone like me? I saw Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of it.' He said: 'May Allah have mercy on them and forgive them. By Allah, they heard as we heard, but they were easy-going and liked ease. O Abu Sa'id, when you walk behind your Muslim brother, be silent and reflect within yourself, as though you have become like him. Your brother used to contend with you over worldly matters, but he left it destitute and stripped, with nothing except what he had stored up of righteous deeds. When you reach the grave and the people sit down, do not sit, but stand at the edge of his grave. When he is lowered into his pit, say: \"In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. O Allah, Your servant has come down to You, and You are the best to be come down to. He has left the world behind his back, so make what he has gone ahead to better than what he has left behind, for You have said: 'And what is with Allah is better for the righteous.'\" Then throw three handfuls of earth upon him.'"],[509,"A people will emerge who recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game."],[510,"Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is too just to repeat the punishment for His servant. And whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals it and forgives him, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is too generous to return to something He has already forgiven."],[511,"I will tell you a hadith which it is incumbent upon every Muslim or upon the Muslims to heed.' We said: 'Yes.' He related it to us at the beginning of the day and we forgot it by the end of the day. We came to him and said: 'The hadith you told us, that it is incumbent upon the Muslims to heed, we have forgotten it, so repeat it for us.' He said: 'There is no Muslim servant who commits a sin and Allah takes him to task for it in this world and punishes him for it, but that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is too generous to repeat his punishment on the Day of Resurrection. And no Muslim commits a sin and Allah forgives him for it in this world, but that Allah is too generous to repeat his punishment on the Day of Resurrection for what He has forgiven.' Then he recited this verse: 'And whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.'"],[512,"Two phrases I memorized from the Prophet ﷺ, and I would like you to memorize them from me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The barrier between you and the jinn is that you say: Bismillah (In the name of Allah).'"],[513,"When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, falling from the sky is dearer to me than saying what he did not say. So if I do not say to you: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then I am at war, and war is deception."],[514,"I said to Ali b. Abi Talib: 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrust you with anything he did not entrust to the people?' He said: 'No, except what is in this parchment.' And in it was: the ransom of the captive, a Muslim is not to be killed for a disbeliever, and the blood of Muslims is equal."],[515,"We went out with the Commander of the Faithful, Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, on a day of Eid. Some of his companions asked him: 'O Commander of the Faithful, what do you say about praying on the day of Eid before the imam and after him?' He said: 'He did not answer them anything.' Then another group came and asked him as the previous ones had asked, and he did not answer them. When we reached the prayer, he led the people in prayer and said the takbir seven times and five times, then he gave a sermon to the people, then he descended and mounted. They said: 'O Commander of the Faithful, these are people praying.' He said: 'What could I do? You asked me about the sunnah. The Prophet ﷺ did not pray before it or after it. Whoever wishes may do so, and whoever wishes may leave it. Do you think I should prevent people from praying and thus be like one who prevents a servant from praying?'"],[516,"The best of this community after its Prophet ﷺ is Abu Bakr, and after Abu Bakr is Umar, and if I wished to name the third, I would name him."],[517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed nine years without performing Hajj, then in the tenth year it was announced that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform Hajj. He mentioned the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he reached the point in the narration: 'Ali arrived from Yemen with camels for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and found that Fatimah had put on dyed clothes and applied kohl. 'Ali disapproved of that, so she said: 'My father commanded me to do this.' 'Ali went in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. 'Ali would say: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to stir up a complaint against Fatimah regarding what she had done, disapproving of her, and I informed him of what she said. He said: 'She has spoken the truth, she has spoken the truth.' Then he said: 'How did you enter ihram when you obligated the Hajj?' I said: 'O Allah, I enter ihram in the same way as Your Messenger enters ihram.' He said: 'I have with me the sacrificial animal.'"],[518,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and 'Umar came. He said: 'These two are the masters of the elderly of Paradise from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers. Do not inform them, O 'Ali.'"],[519,"I was with 'Ali when a man came to him and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, what did the Prophet ﷺ confide to you?' He became angry and said: 'He did not confide to me anything that he concealed from the people, except that...'"],[520,"I heard 'Ali appealing to the people in al-Rahbah: 'I adjure by Allah every Muslim who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm what he said.' Some people among the crowd responded and testified that they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take 'Ali by the hand, saying: 'Am I not more entitled to the Muslims than their own selves?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Whoever's mawla I am, O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.'"],[521,"'If only one day remained of this world, Allah would send a man from my household who would fill it with justice as it had been filled with oppression.'"],[522,"We said to 'Ali: 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leave any book with you other than the Qur'an?' He said: 'No, except this document in the sheath of his sword.' In it was: 'May Allah curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land,' meaning: taking something from the road."],[523,"May Allah curse whoever curses his parents, may Allah curse whoever sacrifices to other than Allah, and may Allah curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land."],[524,"I said to 'Ali—while he was conversing with him—: 'People disapprove that you go out in the heat wearing a heavy padded garment, and in winter wearing two light cloaks.' 'Ali said: 'Were you not with us?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Abu Bakr, tied the banner for him, and sent him out. He marched with the people and was defeated. When he reached and returned, he called 'Umar, tied a banner for him, and he marched, then returned defeated with the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger and whom Allah and His Messenger love. Allah will grant victory through him. He is not one to flee.\" He sent for me and called me. I came to him while I was suffering from ophthalmia and could not see anything. He spat in my eyes and said: \"O Allah, spare him the pain of heat and cold.\" After that, neither heat nor cold harmed me.'"],[525,"Abu Bakr and 'Umar were at a funeral walking in front of it, and 'Ali was walking behind it. I said to 'Ali: 'They knew that walking behind it is more virtuous, but they are lenient, making it easy for the people.'"],[526,"I used to come to the Prophet ﷺ and ask permission. If he was praying, he would clear his throat; if he was not praying, he would permit me."],[527,"There will be people at the end of time called the Rafidah, who reject Islam."],[528,"I stood with al-Husayn b. 'Ali at Muzdalifah and kept hearing him say: 'Labbayk, labbayk' until he threw the pebble. I said: 'O Abu 'Abd Allah, what is this talbiyah?' He said: 'I heard 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ reciting talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah, and he told me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited talbiyah until he reached it.'"],[529,"\"We performed tamattu' with 'umrah leading into hajj along with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[530,"\"I acquired a she-camel on the day of Badr, and he gave me ؓ .\" He said: \"I acquired a she-camel, and I made it kneel at the door of a man from the Ansar, intending to load upon the two of them idhkhir (a kind of grass) to sell it, and with me was a goldsmith from Banu Qaynuqa', and I intended to seek his help for the wedding feast of Fatimah. Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib was in the house drinking, and a singing-girl was singing to him: 'Abu Hamzah, possessor of the high honors.'\" He said: \"He charged at the two of them with the sword and slit open their sides, and he took some of their livers.\" He said: \"I said to Ibn Shihab: 'And from the hump, he had cut off their humps.'\" He said: \"So I looked at a matter that horrified me.\" He said: \"So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him was Zayd b. Harithah, and I went out with him until he came to Hamzah.\" He said: \"He became angry with him.\" He said: \"Hamzah raised his eyes and said: 'Are you not but the slaves of my father?'\" He said: \"So the Messenger of God ﷺ retreated, walking backward away from him.\""],[531,"The Prophet ﷺ came to him and Fatimah at night, and said: \"Will you two not pray?\" I said: \"O Prophet of God, indeed our souls are in the hand of God; when He wills to raise them, He raises them.\" So he turned away when he heard that and did not reply to me anything. Then I heard him as he was departing, saying: \"And man is the most quarrelsome of things.\""],[532,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Fatimah after he had prayed the morning prayer, and there she was, having prayed and then lain down."],[533,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed the devils have despaired of being worshipped in this city of mine—meaning al-Madinah—and in the Arabian Peninsula, but [they have not despaired] of stirring up discord among them.\""],[534,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took my hand and said: \"Indeed Musa asked his Lord to purify his mosque through Harun, and I asked my Lord to purify my mosque through you and your descendants.\" Then he sent to Abu Bakr, saying: \"Close your door.\" He said, \"We belong to God,\" then said: \"Hearing and obedience,\" and he closed his door. Then he sent to 'Umar, then he sent to al-'Abbas with the like of that. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I did not close your doors and open 'Ali's door; rather, God opened 'Ali's door and closed your doors.\""],[535,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the morning prayer. When he finished his prayer, a man called out: \"When is the Hour?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ rebuked him and silenced him, saying: \"Be quiet,\" until when the dawn became bright, he raised his eyes to the sky and said: \"Blessed is the One who raises it and ordains it.\" Then he cast his gaze to the earth and said: \"Blessed is the One who spread it out and created it.\" Then he said: \"Where is the one asking about the Hour?\" The man knelt on his knees and said: \"I, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, I asked you.\" He said: \"That is when leaders oppress, stars are believed, divine decree is denied, leadership is taken as spoils, charity is treated as a fine, and obscenity is increased. At that time your people will perish.\""],[536,"When God willed to teach His Messenger the adhan, Jibril (peace be upon them) came to him with a mount called al-Buraq. He went to mount it, but it became restless. Jibril said to it: \"Be still, for by God, no servant more honored by God than Muhammad ﷺ has ever ridden you.\" He said: \"So he rode it until he reached the veil that is next to the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted.\" He said: \"While he was thus, an angel came out from the veil. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Jibril, who is this?' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I am the closest of creation in position, and I have not seen this angel since I was created before this very hour.' The angel said: 'God is greatest, God is greatest.' It was said to him from behind the veil: 'My servant has spoken the truth; I am greatest, I am greatest.' Then the angel said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God.' It was said to him from behind the veil: 'My servant has spoken the truth; I am, there is no god but Me.' The angel said: 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' It was said from behind the veil: 'My servant has spoken the truth; I sent Muhammad.' The angel said: 'Come to prayer, come to success, the prayer has been established.' Then the angel said: 'God is greatest, God is greatest.' It was said from behind the veil: 'My servant has spoken the truth; I am greatest, I am greatest.' Then he said: 'There is no god but God.' It was said from behind the veil: 'My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me.' Then the angel took Muhammad ﷺ by the hand and brought him forward, and the people of heaven—among them Adam and Nuh—were concerned.\""],[537,"Do not make my grave a place of celebration, and do not make your houses graves. Send blessings upon me and greet me, for your blessings reach me."],[538,"From 'Ali, that he performed ablution washing each part three times, drank the leftover water of his ablution, washed his hands before putting them into the vessel, and said: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do that.\""],[539,"\"What is between my grave and my pulpit\"—or he said: \"my house and my pulpit—is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.\""],[540,"\"The people are followers of Quraysh; their righteous follow their righteous, and their wicked follow their wicked.\""],[541,"I saw Ali while he was saying on the pulpit: We have no book to read to you except the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and this sahifa, a sahifa hanging on his sword, and he mentioned that in it were the obligatory amounts of sadaqa which he had taken."],[542,"I witnessed Uthman and Ali ؓ between Makkah and Madinah, and Uthman was prohibiting mut'a and that one should combine them, meaning between Hajj and Umrah. When Ali ؓ saw that, he entered ihram for both of them together and said: Labbayk, a Hajj and an Umrah together. Uthman said: Do you think I prohibit the people while you do it? He said: I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the saying of any person."],[543,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim, from Ali b. Husayn, from Marwan b. al-Hakam, from Ali ؓ, from the Prophet."],[544,"Khalid b. Abdullah narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Ali b. Husayn, from Marwan b. al-Hakam, from Ali ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[545,"Umar ؓ adjured the people about it, among them Talha, al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman, and he said to Ali and al-Abbas ؓ: Do you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We are not inherited; what we leave is sadaqa? They said: Yes. And Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said: Yes."],[546,"When I washed the Prophet ﷺ, I went to look for what is usually found from the deceased, but I did not see anything. I said: He was good alive and dead."],[547,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combine his parents for anyone except Sa'd. On the day of Uhud, he kept saying: Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom."],[548,"Ali and Uthman ؓ met, and Uthman was prohibiting mut'a while Ali was commanding it. Uthman said: What do you want with this? Ali ؓ said: This is something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did, and I will not abandon it."],[549,"Sulayman b. Abi Dawud al-Jazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know that Ibn Harmala narrated from Sa'id, from Ali ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ except this hadith."],[550,"I prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came and saw pictures in the house, so he returned. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you return? He said: In the house there is something with pictures, and the angels do not enter a house in which there are pictures."],[551,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I point you to the most beautiful young woman in Quraysh? He said: Do you have someone? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamza. He said: She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, O Ali. Did you not know that Allah has made forbidden through suckling what is forbidden through lineage?"],[552,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: What thing is best for a woman? They remained silent. When I returned, I said to Fatima: What thing is best for women? She said: That men should not see them. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Indeed Fatima is a part of me."],[553,"Ali and Uthman ؓ met at Usfan. Uthman used to prohibit mut'ah or 'umrah. Ali ؓ said: What do you want with a matter the Messenger of God ﷺ did, that you prohibit it? Uthman said: Leave us from you. When Ali ؓ saw that, he entered ihram for both together."],[554,"\"Shall I not guide you to what God expiates sins by? Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, walking to the mosques, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer; it washes away sins completely.\""],[555,"Abu al-Abbas narrated to us, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[556,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, al-Miqdad, and al-Zubayr, and said: Go until you come to the meadow of Khakh, for there is a woman in a litter with a letter; take it from her. So we set off, our horses racing, until we reached the meadow, and there was the woman. We said: Bring out the letter. She said: I have no letter. I said: You will bring out the letter or you will shed your clothes. So she brought it out from her braids. We brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and in it was: From Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah to some people of the polytheists in Makkah, informing them of some of the affairs of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Hatib, what is this?\" He said: O Messenger of God, do not hasten against me. I was an ally attached to Quraysh and not one of their own. Those with you of the Emigrants had relatives in Makkah to protect their families, so I wanted to take a hand with them to protect my relatives. I did not do that out of disbelief or apostasy from my religion, nor preferring disbelief. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He has told you the truth.\" Umar—I think—said: O Messenger of God, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What do you know? Perhaps God looked upon this band of the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.\""],[557,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith, from Zayd b. Ali, from his father, from Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi', from Ali."],[558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at Arafah and said: \"This is Arafah, and it is the standing place.\" Then he departed when the sun had set, with Usamah riding behind him. He proceeded at his easy pace while the people were striking right and left, and he did not turn to them, saying: \"O people, you must be calm.\" Then he came to Muzdalifah and prayed the two prayers together. When morning came, he came to Quzah and stood, saying: \"This is Quzah, and it is a standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.\" Then he departed, and when he reached the top of Muhassir, he struck his she-camel and she trotted until he crossed the valley, then he stopped and mounted al-Fadl behind him. Then he came to the jamrah and threw pebbles, then he came to the place of sacrifice and said: \"This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.\" A young girl came to him and said: My father is an old man who has become senile, and God's obligation of Hajj has caught up with him; will it suffice for me to perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\" He turned al-Fadl's neck away. Al-Abbas said: Why did you turn the neck of your cousin? He said: \"I saw a young man and a young woman and did not trust Satan regarding them.\" A man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I departed before shaving. He said: \"Shave or shorten, and no harm.\" A man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered before throwing. He said: \"Throw, and no harm.\" Then he came to the House and circumambulated, then he came to Zamzam and said: \"O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, your water-giving; were it not that the people would overwhelm you, I would draw water with it.\""],[559,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw something he disliked, he said: \"Praise be to God in every situation.\" And when he saw something that pleased him, he said: \"Praise be to God by whose grace good deeds are completed.\""],[560,"\"It suffices the group if one of them greets, and it suffices those sitting if one of them returns the greeting.\""],[561,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited me from sleeping except after praying Witr.\""],[562,"When he stood for prayer, he said: \"God is most great. (I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds, with no partner, and with that I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims.) O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins; none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of morals; none guides to their best but You. Turn away from me their evil; none turns away from me their evil but You. Here I am at Your service and at Your command. All good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.\" When he bowed, he said: \"O God, to You I have bowed, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed. My hearing, sight, bones, marrow, and nerves are humbled before You.\" When he raised his head, he said: \"God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that.\" When he prostrated, he said: \"O God, to You I have prostrated, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed. My face has prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.\" When he said the salam, he said: \"O God, forgive me what I have sent ahead, what I have delayed, what I have concealed, and what I have done excessively, and what You know better than I. You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You.\""],[563,"He used to say about something: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. It was said to him: Is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: War is deception."],[564,"Ali ؓ mentioned the Khawarij and said: Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a deficient hand, or a shortened hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would tell you what God has promised those who fight them on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ. Ubayda said: I said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah; yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah."],[565,"Ismail b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[566,"And Amr b. Ali and Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated it to us. They said: Muadh b. Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[567,"Mubarak b. Fadala narrated to us, from Yunus b. Ubayd, from Ibn Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[568,"Yunus—meaning Ibn Ubayd—narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[569,"Al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[570,"Waki' narrated to us, from Yazid b. Ibrahim, from Ibn Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[571,"Abu Amr b. al-Ala' narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[572,"He mentioned the Khawarij and said: Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a stunted hand, or an incomplete hand. Were it not that you would become insolent, I would tell you what God has promised those who fight you on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ. Ubayda said: I said to Ali ؓ, 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba.'"],[573,"Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Ubayda, from Ali."],[574,"Fatima ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ complaining of the pain in her hand from the marks of the millstone."],[575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Confederates: They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May God fill their houses and graves with fire."],[576,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from wearing gold rings and from wearing qassi."],[577,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr and said: “Give your companions the choice between ransom or death, on condition that an equal number of them will be killed next year.” He said: “We choose ransom, and an equal number of us will be killed next year.”"],[578,"I was a man who emitted madhy (prostatic fluid), so I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he said: “It requires wudu.”"],[579,"Ash‘ath narrated to us, from Muhammad, from ‘Abida, from Ali ؓ something similar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ash‘ath except Rawh b. ‘Ubada."],[580,"He forbade wearing gold rings and wearing qassi garments."],[581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Confederates: “May Allah fill their houses and graves with fire against them, just as they kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set.”"],[582,"“Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.”"],[583,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of the Confederates: “They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their graves and houses with fire.”"],[584,"“They kept us from the prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their graves with fire, or their houses with fire, or their bellies with fire.”"],[585,"The Prophet ﷺ was on Hira when it shook, and he said: “Ten are in Paradise: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Abd al-Rahman, Sa‘d, and Sa‘id b. Zayd, ؓ .”"],[586,"By the One who split the grain and created the soul, it is indeed the covenant of the unlettered Prophet ﷺ to me: “No one loves me except a believer, and no one hates me except a hypocrite.”"],[587,"Ali ؓ was asked about the wudu of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He poured water in the courtyard, then called for water and said: “Where is the one asking about the wudu of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He washed his hands three times, his face three times, and his forearms three times. Then he wiped his head until it almost dripped. Then he washed his feet three times. Then he said: “This is how the Messenger of Allah used to perform wudu.”"],[588,"“O Ali, ask Allah for guidance and straightness, and remember by guidance your guiding of the way, and by straightness your straightening of the arrow.”"],[589,"A man came to ʿAlī ؓ and said: Help me with my mukātaba (contract of manumission). He said: Shall I not teach you words that the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me? If you had a debt like Mount Ṣīr, God would pay it off for you. Say: O God, suffice me with what You have made lawful against what You have made unlawful, and enrich me by Your bounty from all besides You."],[590,"I said to Shaqīq b. Salama: Tell me about Dhū al-Thudayya. He said: When we fought them, ʿAlī ؓ said: Look for a man whose mark is such and such. So we looked for him but did not find him. We said to him, 'We did not find him,' and he wept. Then he said: Look for him, for by God I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. So we looked for him and did not find him, and he wept. Then he said: Search, for by God I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. So we looked for him and did not find him. Then he mounted his grey mule and we searched, and found him beneath some papyrus. When he saw him, he prostrated."],[591,"It was said to ʿAlī ؓ: Will you not appoint a successor over us? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ did not appoint a successor, so I will not appoint a successor over you. If God, Blessed and Exalted, wills good for the people, He will gather them around the best of them, just as He gathered them after their Prophet ﷺ around the best of them."],[592,"\"A people will emerge at the end of time who recite the Qurʾān, but it will not pass beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game. Fighting them is a duty upon every Muslim.\""],[593,"\"A people will emerge at the end of time.\""],[594,"At the end of time there will emerge a people young in age, foolish in intellect, who speak the best of the speech of creation. Their faith will not pass beyond their throats. Wherever you find them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for the one who kills them."],[595,"When I narrate to you from the Messenger of God ﷺ a ḥadīth, falling from the sky is dearer to me than lying about the Messenger of God ﷺ. When I speak among ourselves, war is deception. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: At the end of time there will be peoples young in age, foolish in intellect, who speak the best of the speech of creation. They recite the Qurʾān, but their faith does not pass beyond their throats. When you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for the one who kills them on the Day of Resurrection."],[596,"Some zanādiqa (heretics) were brought to ʿAlī ؓ. He went out to the market, dug a pit, and burned them with fire. Then he raised his head to the sky and said: God and His Messenger spoke the truth. Then he left until he entered al-Raḥba, and I followed him. When he was about to enter the house, he said: What is the matter with you, O Suwayd? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, a word I heard when you burned those heretics: you said, 'God and His Messenger spoke the truth.' He said: O Suwayd, when you hear me say, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said,' know that falling from the sky is dearer to me than saying what I did not hear from him. When you see me speak of things like this, it is only something to anger them, or a word like that."],[597,"March out with us to the remnant of the confederates. March out with us to what God and His Messenger have said. We say: God and His Messenger spoke the truth, and they say: God and His Messenger lied."],[598,"Yūnus b. Arqam narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from al-Ḥakam, from Qays b. Abī Ḥāzim, from ʿAlī ؓ something similar."],[599,"ʿAlqama b. ʿUlātha entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he called for a head [of an animal] and began eating with him. Bilāl came and called him to prayer, but he did not respond. He returned and stayed in the mosque as long as God willed, then came and said: Prayer, O Messenger of God. By God, morning has come. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: May God have mercy on Bilāl. Were it not for Bilāl, we would have hoped for a dispensation for us between now and sunrise. ʿAlī ؓ said: Were it not that Bilāl swore, the Messenger of God ﷺ would have eaten until Gabriel said to him, 'Lift your hand.'"],[600,"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar used to walk in front of the funeral procession, and ʿAlī ؓ used to walk behind it. ʿAlī ؓ was asked about that, and he said: They know as I know, but they preferred to make it easy for the people."],[601,"I used to be given whenever I asked, and whenever I remained silent I was approached."],[602,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and commanded me to “not pass by any grave but level it.”"],[603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me a striped silk suit, so I wore it and saw anger in his face, so I divided it among my wives."],[604,"Ali ؓ stood before the people of the canal and said: What you hear me narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ, hold me to it; and what you hear me narrate other than that, war is deception. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “At the end of time there will be a people young in age, foolish in intellect, who pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its target, then they will not return to it. Wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is reward on the Day of Resurrection. I see them as none other than these.” Then he rose and advanced against them."],[605,"Ali ؓ addressed us and said: It has been mentioned to me that a group will come out toward the east. So he traveled until he reached them, and a man from the Kharijites said: Do not speak to them. A man from the companions of Ali ؓ said: Cut the bridges. He said: Then he killed twelve or thirteen, and Ali ؓ said: Look for the one with the breast-like protrusion for me. It was sought but not found, and he began to sweat on a winter day. Then he said: Bring me the gray mule of the Prophet ﷺ. He rode it until he came to a low-lying area of the ground and said: Turn over. The first thing that came out, he said: “By God, I did not lie nor was I lied to. Were I not afraid, I would tell you what God has decreed for you through his tongue, meaning his Prophet ﷺ. People in Yemen witnessed it.” They said: O Commander of the Faithful, how? He said: Their inclination was with us."],[606,"He was in the army that was with Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ that marched against the Kharijites. Ali ؓ said: O people, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A people from my community will come out who recite the Quran; your recitation is nothing compared to theirs, nor your prayer compared to theirs, nor your fasting compared to theirs. They recite the Quran but it does not pass beyond their collarbones. They pass out of Islam as an arrow passes through its target. If the army that encounters them knew what was decreed for them on the tongue of their Prophet ﷺ, they would refrain from action. The sign of that is that among them is a man with an upper arm but no forearm, and on his upper arm is something like a woman’s nipple with white hairs on it. You are going to Muawiyah and the people of Syria and leaving these to succeed you in your offspring and wealth. By God, I hope they are these people, for they shed sacred blood and raided people’s livestock. So march in the name of God.” When we met, the Kharijites that day were under Abdullah b. Wahb al-Rasibi. He said to them: Throw down your spears and draw your swords from their scabbards, for I fear they will appeal to you as they appealed to you on the day of Harura. He said: So they drew their swords, and the rest of the people engaged with their spears. Then they came at one another, and no one from the people was struck that day except two men. Then Ali ؓ said: Search among them for the maimed one. Ali ؓ stood up himself and searched for him and found him. He said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Ubaydah stood up to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, by God, other than whom there is no god, did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: By God, other than whom there is no god, I heard this hadith. He made him swear three times, and he kept swearing to him."],[607,"He took his hand and we set off walking until we reached the bank of the Euphrates. Ali ؓ said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There is no soul created but that misery or happiness has preceded it from God. A man said: O Messenger of God, then what is the point of action? He said: “Act, for everyone is facilitated for what he was created for.” As for one who gives and fears and believes in the best, We will facilitate him for ease; and as for one who withholds and considers himself self-sufficient and denies the best,"],[608,"He was at a funeral and took a stick and began to scrape the ground with it, then said: There is none of you but his seat in the Fire or his seat in Paradise has been written. They said: O Messenger of God, should we not then rely on that? He said: “Act, for everyone is facilitated.” As for one who gives and fears and believes in the best, We will facilitate him for ease; and as for one who withholds and considers himself self-sufficient and denies the best, We will facilitate him for hardship."],[609,"Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[610,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent a man from the Ansar on a military expedition and ordered them to obey him. When he went out, he became angry with them over something and said: Did not the Messenger of God ﷺ order you to obey me? They said: Yes. He said: Gather firewood. They gathered firewood, then he called for fire and set it ablaze in the wood, then said: I adjure you to enter it. The people were about to do that when a young man among their youngest said to them: Do not rush to enter the fire; you only fled to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the fire. Wait until you come to the Messenger of God ﷺ; if he orders you to enter, then enter. So they came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Had you entered it, you would never have come out of it."],[611,"There is no obedience in disobedience to God, Mighty and Majestic."],[612,"I said: O Messenger of God, you select women from Quraysh and leave us? He said: Do you have someone? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. He said: She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through suckling."],[613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with a stick in his hand, scratching the ground with it. He raised his head and said, \"There is no soul among you but its place in Paradise or Hell has been known.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not then rely on that and not work?\" He said, \"Work, for everyone is facilitated toward what he was created for.\" Then he recited: \"As for him who gives and fears (Allah), and believes in the best (reward),\" until His saying: \"But as for him who is stingy and thinks himself self-sufficient, and denies the best (reward), We will facilitate for him the path to hardship.\""],[614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an army and placed a man in command over them, and ordered them to obey him. He lit a fire and said, \"Enter it.\" Some people intended to enter it, while others said, \"We only fled from it, so we will not enter it.\" This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to those who had intended to enter it, \"Had they entered it, they would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection.\" He said a good word to the others who had refused, and said, \"There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Obedience is only in what is right.\""],[615,"Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sa'd b. Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali addressed us."],[616,"Ali ؓ addressed us and said, \"O people, enforce the prescribed punishments on your slaves, both those who are married and those who are not. A slave woman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed adultery, and he ordered me to flog her. I went to her and found that she had recently given birth, so I feared that if I flogged her she would die. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'You did well.'\""],[617,"When Abu Talib died, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This old man has died.\" He said, \"Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me.\" He said: So I buried him and then went to him. He said, \"Go and perform ghusl, and do not do anything until you come to me.\" So I performed ghusl and then went to him, and he made supplications for me that would please me more than having red camels and black ones."],[618,"\"And you make your provision that you deny (it).\" He said: \"Your gratitude; you say, 'We were given rain by such-and-such a star, and by such-and-such a star.'\""],[619,"Whoever lies about his dream will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection to tie a knot in a barley grain."],[620,"Whoever lies about his dream will be tasked with tying a knot in a barley grain on the Day of Resurrection."],[621,"I entered upon Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami after he had prayed the morning prayer while he was sitting in the mosque. I said to him, \"If you got up, meaning to your bed, it would be more comfortable for you.\" He said, \"I heard Ali say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever prays the morning prayer then remains seated in his place of prayer, the angels send blessings upon him, and their blessings upon him are: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. And whoever waits for the prayer, the angels send blessings upon him, and their blessings upon him are: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'\""],[622,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf prepared food for us and invited us. We ate and drank wine. When the wine took effect on us and the prayer time came, they ordered a man to lead them in prayer. He recited, 'Say: O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship, but we worship what you worship,' meaning he mixed up his recitation. Then Allah revealed: 'O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying.'"],[623,"He used to give the greeting of peace to his right and to his left."],[624,"He used to fast on Ashura."],[625,"He used to fast on Ashura."],[626,"He commanded the use of the siwak, and said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When a servant uses the siwak and then stands to pray, an angel stands behind him and listens to his recitation, drawing near to him' — or words to that effect — 'until he places his mouth upon his mouth. Nothing of the Quran leaves his mouth except that it enters the angel's belly, so purify your mouths for the Quran.'"],[627,"I have been commanded to fight the renegades, the deviators, and the seceders."],[628,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me during the illness in which he died: 'Give permission for the people to enter upon me.' So I did. Then he said: 'May Allah curse the people who took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.' Then he fell unconscious. When he regained consciousness, he said: 'O Ali, give permission for the people to enter upon me.' So I permitted the people to enter. Then he said: 'May Allah curse the people who took the graves of their prophets as a place of worship.' He said it three times during his illness."],[629,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: 'Shall I not teach you something to say when you go to bed?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times, for it will be written for you as a thousand good deeds.'"],[630,"Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ali ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report."],[631,"The Prophet ﷺ sent his sacrificial animals with him and ordered him to give their meat, hides, and coverings in charity."],[632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to take charge of his sacrificial camels, to give their hides and coverings in charity, and not to give the butcher anything from them."],[633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to take charge of his sacrificial camels, to distribute their hides and coverings, and he ordered me not to give the butcher anything from them, saying: 'We shall give him from our own.'"],[634,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take charge of his sacrificial camels."],[635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to take charge of his sacrificial camels and to distribute all of them — their meat, hides, and coverings — among the poor, and not to give anything for their slaughtering. He said: 'I asked: Did he name for you among whom to distribute them?' He said: 'No.'"],[636,"The Prophet ﷺ entrusted me with his sacrificial camels. I distributed their meat, then he ordered me and I distributed their hides, then he ordered me and I distributed their coverings."],[637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to “take charge of his sacrificial camels,” and he commanded me to distribute their hides and their saddle blankets."],[638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to take charge of his sacrificial camels, to give their hides and their saddle blankets as charity, and he commanded me not to give the butcher any part of them."],[639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “sacrificed one hundred camels during his Hajj, among them a camel of Abu Jahl with a gold nose ring.”"],[640,"A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent it to me. He then saw it on me and said: “I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself.” So he commanded me, and I cut it up and divided it among the women."],[641,"Fatimah complained about the marks of the millstone on her hand. She went to the Prophet ﷺ but did not find him. She met A’ishah and told her. When the Prophet ﷺ came, A’ishah informed him of Fatimah’s visit. The Prophet ﷺ came to us while we had already gone to bed. We started to get up, but he said: “Stay where you are.” He sat between us until I felt the coolness of his foot on my chest. Then he said: “Shall I not teach you something better than what you asked for? When you go to bed, say Allahu akbar thirty-four times, subhan Allah thirty-three times, and alhamdulillah thirty-three times. That is better for you than a servant.”"],[642,"Abu Musa came to visit al-Hasan b. Ali. Ali said to him: “Have you come as a visitor or as a gloater? If you have come as a visitor, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When a man visits his sick Muslim brother, he remains among the fresh fruits of Paradise until he sits down. When he sits, mercy envelops him. If it is in the morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and if it is in the evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning.’”"],[643,"“Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is false is one of the liars.”"],[644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, when he sent me with the sacrificial camels, to slaughter them and to give their meat as charity. I asked his permission regarding their hides and saddle blankets, and he said: “Give them as charity.”"],[645,"Muhammad b. Ma‘mar narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us; Muhammad b. ‘Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ali."],[646,"I had two slave boys who were brothers. I wanted to sell one of them, but the Prophet ﷺ said: “Sell them both together or keep them both together.”"],[647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and placed his foot between me and Fatimah. He taught us what to say when we went to bed: “Thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three takbirs, and thirty-three praises of Allah.” I have never abandoned it since.” A man asked him: “Not even on the night of Siffin?” He replied: “Not even on the night of Siffin.”"],[648,"I, Fatimah, al-Abbas, and Zayd b. Harithah gathered together. Al-Abbas said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old, my bones have become weak, and my expenses have increased. If you see fit to order for me such-and-such amounts of food, do so.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will do it.” Zayd b. Harithah said: “O Messenger of Allah, you had given me some land from which I earned my living, then you took it back. If you see fit to return it to me, please do.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We will do that.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to entrust me with this right that Allah has assigned to you in His Book from the fifth of the spoils, and let me distribute it during your lifetime so that no one disputes it with me after you, then do so.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We will do that.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted me with its distribution during his lifetime, and then Abu Bakr ؓ entrusted me with it, so I distributed it."],[649,"\"Shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven, even though you are already forgiven: 'There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'\""],[650,"The sun eclipsed, so Ali stood and bowed five times and prostrated twice, then did the same in the second rak'ah. Then he said: No one has prayed it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except me."],[651,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about prostatic fluid, and he said: In it is ablution and you wash it, and in semen is a full bath."],[652,"Ali and Abu Mas'ud were sitting, and a funeral procession passed by them. Abu Mas'ud stood, so Ali said to him: Sit down. He said: Do you not know that we used to stand for funerals? He said: That was only when you were Jews."],[653,"I heard Ali adjuring the people, saying: I adjure any Muslim man who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Ghadir Khumm to stand. So twelve men stood and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Ali by the hand, then said: O people, am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, then this is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him."],[654,"\"The key to prayer is purification, its sanctity is the takbir, and its release is the taslim.\""],[655,"Maria, the mother of Ibrahim, was suspected because of a Copt, a cousin of hers who used to visit her and come to her frequently. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Take this sword and go; if you find him with her, kill him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, when you send me on an errand, should I be like a heated iron that nothing turns back until I carry out what you commanded me, or should the witness see what the absent does not see? He said: Rather, the witness sees what the absent does not see. So I went with the sword slung over my shoulder and found him with her. I drew the sword, and when he saw me approaching him, he feared that I intended him. He went to a palm tree and climbed it, then threw himself on his back and spread his legs, and he was a eunuch with no male organ at all. So I sheathed the sword and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: \"Praise be to Allah who turns away [evil] from us, the people of the household.\""],[656,"\"We used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then depart while we could not recognize one another.\""],[657,"\"An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.\""],[658,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"running between al-Safa and al-Marwah.\""],[659,"I said to Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali: What do you think about this intercession that the people of Iraq talk about—is it true? He said: Intercession for what? I said: The intercession of Muhammad ﷺ. He said: It is true, by Allah. By Allah, my uncle Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyyah narrated to me, from Ali ؓ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I will intercede for my nation until my Lord, blessed and exalted, calls me and says: Are you satisfied, O Muhammad? And I will say: \"My Lord, I am satisfied.\""],[660,"\"The sun eclipsed during the time of Ali, and he stood and bowed five times and prostrated twice, then did the same in the second rak'ah, then said the taslim. Then he said: No one has prayed it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except me.\""],[661,"I never intended to do any of the things the people of the Jahiliyyah used to do except on two occasions, and each time Allah came between me and what I wanted to do. Then after that I never intended anything until Allah honored me with His message."],[662,"He forbade temporary marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar."],[663,"Yahya b. Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ismail b. Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah b. Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[664,"He forbade temporary marriage with women."],[665,"The Mahdi is from us, the People of the House; Allah will set him aright in a single night."],[666,"He was asked about the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"He was neither short nor tall, had beautiful hair, combed, with a reddish complexion, large joints, and a long line of hair from the chest to the navel. I have never seen anyone like him before or after. When he walked, he leaned forward as if descending a slope.\""],[667,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in seven garments."],[668,"My father sent me with a document to Uthman containing the shares of inheritance. He said: 'These are the shares of inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which he used to send collectors with.' Uthman said: 'We have no need of it.' So I went to my father and told him, and he said: 'Leave it.'"],[669,"If a son is born to you, give him my name and my kunyah."],[670,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what if a son is born to me after you?' He said: 'Give him my name and give him my kunyah.'"],[671,"I was a man who emitted a lot of prostatic fluid, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Perform ablution from it and pray.'"],[672,"Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mundhir, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali."],[673,"I was a man who emitted madhi frequently, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he said: 'Wudu is required for it.'"],[674,"The Prophet ﷺ saw some women at a funeral and said: 'Do you carry [the bier] along with those who carry it?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Then return burdened with sin, not rewarded.'"],[675,"There is no people in whose house—or with whom—there is a sheep, but that they are sanctified twice every day or are blessed twice."],[676,"Ismail b. Salman narrated to us, from Dinar Abu Umar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, similarly, but he did not trace it back to the Prophet. And this Ismail b. Salman is a Kufan; Israil, Qays, Muhammad b. Rabi'ah, and Abdullah b. Dawud narrated from him. He traced three hadiths back to the Prophet from Dinar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, and he narrates many hadiths from Dinar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah."],[677,"\"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: I was granted victory through awe; I was given comprehensive speech; the spoils of war were made lawful for me; and he mentioned two other qualities that I have forgotten.\""],[678,"When Hasan was born, I named him Hamzah. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What have you named my son?\" So I informed him. Then another was born to me, and he said: \"What have you named him?\" or \"What did you name him?\" So I mentioned it to him, and he said: \"Name the first one Hasan and the other Husayn.\""],[679,"I asked Ali about mut'ah. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—announced that mut'ah is forbidden.'"],[680,"I was a man who emitted madhi frequently, and I was too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ myself. So I told al-Miqdad to ask him, and he asked him. He said: 'Wudu is required for it.'"],[681,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a large head, large eyes, long eyelashes, a thick beard, and a fair complexion. When he walked, he leaned forward as if walking downhill; when he turned, he turned with his whole body. His palms and feet were thick."],[682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying facing another man, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I prayed while you were looking at me.'"],[683,"On the day of Badr, I fought for some time, then I came quickly to see what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was doing. I came and found him prostrating, saying: 'O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining! O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining!' He did not add anything to these two. Then I returned to the fighting. Then I came again, and he was prostrating, saying the same. Then I went back to the fighting. Then I returned, and he was still saying the same. Then Allah granted him victory."],[684,"\"The greatest reward for visiting the sick is the briefest visit, and condolence is offered once.\""],[685,"He was traveling with Ali b. Abi Talib, and the sun set, but he traveled on until it became dark. Then he dismounted and prayed Maghrib, then he called for supper and ate, then he prayed Isha. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he combined two prayers, or when he wanted to combine two prayers, would do like this."],[686,"It was said to Ali: Describe the Prophet ﷺ to us. He said: He was neither tall nor short, he had a large head, a reddish complexion, long eyelashes, a thick beard, and a fair skin color. When he walked, he leaned forward as if descending a slope, and when he turned, he turned with his whole body."],[687,"There is an hour on Friday when no Muslim coincides with it, asking Allah for something, except that He gives it to him."],[688,"He ordered that skulls be placed in the crops. I said: For what reason? He said: Because of the evil eye."],[689,"When this verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, offer something in charity before your private consultation' (Qur'an 58:12), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: What do you think: a dinar, or what can you afford? I said: I cannot manage that. He said: Then how much? I said: A grain of barley. He said: You are indeed of little means. Then was revealed: 'Are you afraid to offer charities before your private consultation?' (Qur'an 58:13). He said: So it was lightened for this community through me."],[690,"A mule was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: What is this? They said: A donkey mates with a mare, and this is produced between them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not mate donkeys with mares? He said: Only those who do not understand do that."],[691,"Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim b. Damrah, from Ali."],[692,"Indeed, Allah is witr (odd) and loves witr."],[693,"We said to Ali: How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: You would not be able to perform it. We said: Tell us. He said: You would not be able to perform it. We repeated that to him several times, then he said: When the sun was here, at the same height as here – meaning the west – he would pray two rak'ahs. Then he would wait until it was here, at the same height as at Zuhr, and pray four. Then he would remain until the shadow came and the sun declined, and pray four. Then he would pray four before Asr."],[694,"We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the day. He said: You will never be able to do that. We said: Whoever among us is able. He said: When the sun was here, as it is here at Asr, he would pray two rak'ahs. When the sun was here, as it is here at Zuhr, he would pray four. He would pray four before Zuhr and two after it, and four before Asr, separating every two rak'ahs with a salutation upon the angels brought near, and upon whoever followed them among the prophets and messengers."],[695,"He would pray two rak'ahs after every prescribed prayer, except Asr and Subh."],[696,"Ali was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ – the voluntary prayer during the day. He said: And who can do that? He said: We can do what we are able. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the sun was here, at the height it is at Asr, would pray two rak'ahs, offering salutation in them upon the angels brought near, the prophets, the messengers, and whoever followed them among the believers and Muslims. Then when the forenoon rose and the sun was here as it is here at Zuhr, he would pray four, separating between them with a salutation upon the angels brought near, the believers, the messengers, and whoever followed them among the believers and messengers. Then when the sun declined, he would pray four before Zuhr, and pray two after Zuhr, doing the same in them, and four before Asr, doing the same in them, separating between every two rak'ahs with a salutation upon the angels brought near, the prophets, the messengers, and whoever followed them among the believers and Muslims."],[697,"I heard Asim b. Damrah narrating from Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[698,"I asked Ali about the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ daytime prayer. He said: \"You will not be able to endure that.\" I said: \"Whoever among us can endure it?\" He said: \"When the sun was here, as it was there, he would pray two rak'ahs. And when the sun was here, as it was there, at noon he would pray the noon prayer, four rak'ahs. He would pray four rak'ahs before noon and two after it, and four before the afternoon prayer, separating between every two rak'ahs with the greeting of peace upon the angels brought near, the prophets, the messengers, and those who followed them among the believers and Muslims. That is twelve rak'ahs.\""],[699,"\"There is nothing due on one hundred and ninety silver coins, but when they reach two hundred, five dirhams are due.\""],[700,"\"There is nothing due on one hundred and ninety silver coins, but when they reach two hundred, five dirhams are due.\""],[701,"From any part of the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Witr: from its beginning, its middle, and its end, and his Witr finally settled at its end."],[702,"He would perform Witr at the beginning of the night, its middle, and its end; then Witr became fixed for him at its end."],[703,"He was asked: Is Witr obligatory? He said: \"As for the obligatory prayer, no, but it is a Sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions, and they continued upon that.\""],[704,"\"Witr is not compulsory, but it is a Sunnah.\""],[705,"\"Witr is not obligatory, but it is a Sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah.\""],[706,"Witr is not compulsory, but it is a Sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims after him."],[707,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim b. Damrah, from Ali."],[708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to flog a slave woman of his who had committed adultery, and I flogged her after she had recovered from her postpartum bleeding."],[709,"Fasting the month of patience, and three days of every month; they remove the ill-feeling of the chest."],[710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray any prayer except that he prayed two rak'ahs after it, except the morning and afternoon prayers."],[711,"In what the sky watered, or opened—meaning: or was opened—therein is a tenth, and what was watered by the bucket, therein is half a tenth."],[712,"Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim b. Damrah, from Ali, who said: And I think he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[713,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed four rak'ahs before the noon prayer."],[714,"Whoever loves to have his life extended, and increase in his provision, let him maintain his kinship ties."],[715,"Do not expose your thigh, and do not look at the thigh of a living or dead person."],[716,"Allah sent Yahya b. Zakariyya to the Children of Israel with five words. When He sent 'Isa, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: O 'Isa, say to Yahya b. Zakariyya: Either you convey what you have been sent with to the Children of Israel, or I will convey it to them. So Yahya went out until he came to the Children of Israel. He said: Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him. The likeness of that is like a man who freed another man, treated him well and gave him, then he went away and disbelieved in the patron of his blessings and befriended others. Allah commands you to establish prayer. The likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy captured and wanted to kill. He said: Do not kill me, for I have a treasure, and I will ransom myself. So he gave them his treasure, and he saved himself. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to give charity. The likeness of that is like a man who walked towards his enemy, having taken a shield for fighting, so he does not care from where he is attacked. Allah commands you to recite the Book. The likeness of that is like a people in their fortress; their enemy came to them, and they had placed people in every corner of the fortress. Their enemy does not come to them from any direction except that there are those before them who repel them from the fortress. That is the likeness of the one who recites the Qur'an; he does not cease to be in the most fortified fortress or in a strong fortress."],[717,"O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings."],[718,"I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing and prostrating. When you bow, magnify Allah, and when you prostrate, exert yourselves in supplication, for it is worthy that you be answered."],[719,"The best of you is the one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it."],[720,"I heard a man say to Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ : O Commander of the Believers, which month do you command me to fast after the month of Ramadan? Ali said: I have not heard anyone ask about this after a man I heard asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : Which month do you command me to fast after the month of Ramadan? He said: If you are fasting after Ramadan, then fast the month of Muharram, for it is Allah's month, and in it Allah relented towards a people."],[721,"The best of you are every repentant one who is tried."],[722,"O Ali, do not follow a glance with another glance; you have only the first glance."],[723,"Indeed in Paradise there are rooms whose outside can be seen from their inside, and their inside from their outside. A man said: O Messenger of God, are these the dwellings of the prophets? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God has prepared them for one who feeds food, spreads peace, keeps fasting continuously, and prays at night while people sleep."],[724,"Indeed in Paradise there is a market in which there is no buying or selling except of forms: whoever loves a form enters it, or desires a form enters it. And the houris have a gathering in which they meet, raising voices the like of which no one has heard, saying: 'We are the eternal ones and do not die; we are the soft ones and do not suffer; we are the content ones and do not become angry. Blessed is the one who is for us and we are for him.'"],[725,"From Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq, from al-Nu'man b. Sa'd, from Ali, as a mawquf report."],[726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: O Ali, shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven even though you are already forgiven? There is no god but You, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the mighty Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds."],[727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite the Quran. Hafs said: in every state except major ritual impurity. And Uqba said: except when he was junub."],[728,"From Hafs and Abu Mu'awiya, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr b. Murra, from Abdullah b. Salama, from Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the like of it."],[729,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would relieve himself, then recite the Quran, and eat with us. Nothing prevented him from reciting the Quran except major ritual impurity."],[730,"I was ill, and the Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was saying: O God, if my appointed time has come, then have mercy on me; if it is delayed, then make me content; and if it is a trial, then give me patience. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'How did you say?' I repeated it to him, and he struck me with his foot and said: 'Say: O God, heal me' or he said: 'Cure him.' I did not complain of that pain afterwards."],[731,"From al-Faryabi Muhammad b. Yusuf, from Sufyan, from Amr b. Murra, from Abdullah b. Salama, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner. And we do not know that anyone narrated this wording except Ali with this chain, and we do not know that anyone narrated it from Abdullah b. Salama except Amr b. Murra."],[732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of God, you send me while I am young and they are elders, and I have no knowledge of speech? He said: God, blessed and exalted, will guide your heart and make firm your tongue. He said: By God, I did not encounter difficulty in anything afterward."],[733,"O gathering of women, fear Allah, and seek the pleasure of your husbands, for if a woman knew the right of her husband, she would not cease standing as long as his lunch and dinner are present."],[734,"Al-Ashtar and I went to Ali and said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrust to you anything that he did not entrust to the people in general? He said: No, except what is in this book of mine. He brought out a book from the sheath of his sword, and in it was: \"The blood of Muslims is equal, and the lowest of them may undertake their protection. Indeed, a believer is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one who has a covenant while his covenant stands. Whoever commits a crime, it is against himself, and whoever shelters a criminal, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[735,"It was revealed concerning me, Hamzah, Ubaydah b. al-Harith, Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, and al-Walid b. Utbah: \"These two opponents disputed concerning their Lord.\""],[736,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was holding my hand, and we passed by a garden. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful a garden it is! He said: \"You have in Paradise something more beautiful than it.\" Then we passed by another, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful a garden it is! He said: \"You have in Paradise something more beautiful than it.\" Until we passed by seven gardens, each time I said how beautiful it is, and he said: \"You have in Paradise something more beautiful than it.\" When the road became empty for him, he embraced me and then burst into tears. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes you weep? He said: \"Grudges in the chests of people that they will not show to you except after me.\" I said: In safety of my religion? He said: \"In safety of your religion.\""],[737,"He said regarding the suckling infant: \"The urine of the boy is sprinkled, and the urine of the girl is washed.\""],[738,"Abdullah b. Salam said to me when I had placed my foot in the stirrup: Do not go to Iraq, for if you go there, the sword's fly will strike you. He said: By Allah, he said it, and the Prophet ﷺ had said it to me before him."],[739,"When we came to Madinah we found its climate disagreeable and we were afflicted with fever. The Prophet ﷺ was inquiring about Quraysh, and it reached him that they had encamped at Badr, which is a well. He sent two men, one of them al-Zubayr and the other Abu Ishaq thinks it was Ali. They came upon two men: a man from Quraysh and a freed slave of Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt. The Qurayshi escaped, and they brought the freed slave. They began questioning him and saying to him: How many are the people? Or how many are they? He said: By Allah, they are many in number and fierce in battle. Until they brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he questioned him, and he said that. He said: How many camels do the people slaughter each day? He said: Ten camels. He said: A camel for a hundred, so the people are a thousand. He said: A light rain fell upon us at night, so we dispersed under the trees and shields, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent his night supplicating and saying: O Allah, if You destroy this band, You will not be worshiped on earth. When dawn broke, he said: Prayer, O servants of Allah. We came out from under the trees and shields, and he urged or incited fighting and said: \"It is as if I am looking at their slain.\" He said: When the people drew near, there was a man among them riding on a red camel. The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Zubayr: Call one of your companions and ask him: Who is the owner of the red camel? For if there is anyone among the people who commands you to good, it is he. Al-Zubayr asked: Who is the owner of the red camel? They said: Utbah b. Rabi'ah, and he was discouraging fighting, saying: O people, I see a people seeking death. By Allah, I do not think you will reach them until you are destroyed. He said: When what he said reached Abu Jahl, he came to him and said: Your lungs are filled with fear until you saw Muhammad and his companions. Utbah said to him: Do you reproach me, O you with a dyed anus? You will know which of us is more cowardly. Utbah dismounted from his camel, and his brother Shaybah and his son al-Walid followed him. They called for single combat, and some youths from the Ansar rushed to them. He said: Who are you? They told him, and he said: We have no need of you; we only wanted our cousins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Arise, O Hamzah; arise, O Ali; arise, O Ubaydah b. al-Harith.\" He said: Hamzah went to Utbah, I went to Shaybah, and Ubaydah went to al-Walid. He said: Hamzah did not delay with his opponent until he finished him. He said: I did not delay with my opponent. He said: Two blows were exchanged between al-Walid and Ubaydah, and each of them killed his opponent. He said: Hamzah and I went to them, and we finished off al-Walid and carried away Ubaydah."],[740,"Whoever of Banu Abd al-Muttalib you are able to capture, for they were only brought out against their will."],[741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said: You send me to a people who are older than me, so how shall I judge between them? He said: Go, for Allah will guide your heart and make your tongue firm."],[742,"\"I give to a people to win their hearts, and I entrust a people to what they have,\" or \"to what Allah has placed in their hearts, among them Furat b. Hayyan.\""],[743,"\"When the battle grew intense and the two hosts met, we sought protection with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we did not see anyone closer to the enemy than him.\""],[744,"He used to wake his family during the last ten nights of Ramadan."],[745,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah b. Yarim, from Ali, in a similar manner. We do not know that this hadith is narrated from Ali except with this chain. It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ about his i'tikaf from more than one route, being narrated from Aisha via several routes, and from Abu Sa'id, and from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu Layla, and from Anas."],[746,"A silk hulla was gifted to him, and he sent it to me, so I wore it. He saw it on me and said, \"I would not be pleased for you with what I dislike for myself.\" He ordered me, so I tore it and divided it among the women."],[747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from al-ji'ah."],[748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from the red saddle cushion, al-qassi, and a gold ring."],[749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me and to Abu Bakr ؓ on the day of Badr: \"With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il, and Israfil is a mighty angel who witnesses the battle, or is in the ranks.\""],[750,"Ali said to the people: Ask me. Ibn al-Kawwa' said: Tell us about the two sisters who are owned as slaves, and about the daughter of the brother through breastfeeding. He said: You are wandering in error. He said: We ask you only about what we do not know; as for what we know, we do not ask you about it. He said: As for the two sisters who are owned as slaves, one verse made them forbidden and another made them permissible, so I do not make it lawful, nor forbidden, nor command it, nor forbid it, and I do not do it myself nor does anyone of my household. As for the daughter of the brother through breastfeeding, I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding.\""],[751,"A striped silk hulla was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gifted it to me, so I wore it, and I saw dislike on his face."],[752,"They dug a well in Yemen, and a lion fell into it. In the morning they were looking at it, when a man fell into the well and grabbed hold of another man, and that one grabbed another, until there were four, and they all fell into the well together. The lion wounded them. A man struck it with his spear and killed it. The people said to the first man: You killed our companions, and their blood money is upon you. His companions refused, and they almost fought. Ali arrived at that time, so they asked him. He said: I will judge among you with a judgment; whoever among you is satisfied, his approval will be binding on him, and whoever is displeased has no claim until he comes to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he judges among you. They said: Yes. He said: Collect from among the people who were present at the well a quarter of a diyah, a third of a diyah, half a diyah, and a full diyah. For the first is a quarter of a diyah because three died above him; for the second is a third of a diyah because two died above him; for the third is half a diyah because one died above him; and for the last is the full diyah. If you are satisfied, then this is a judgment among you, and if you are not satisfied, then you have no claim until you come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he judges among you. The following year they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story. He said: I will judge among you, if Allah wills, while he was sitting at the Station of Ibrahim ﷺ. A man stood up and said: Ali has already judged among us. He said: \"How did Ali judge among you?\" They told him the story, and he said: \"It is as he judged among you.\""],[753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said: You send me to a people who are older than me, and I have no knowledge of judging? He said: When two disputants come to you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says. He said: I ceased not to be a judge, or I never doubted in a judgment between two."],[754,"Ali performed ablution washing each part three times, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution."],[755,"Ali performed ablution washing each part three times, and wiped his head, and said: Whoever would like to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is how it was."],[756,"He saw Ali ؓ in the open courtyard performing ablution: he washed his palms, then rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, and his forearms three times each, and his head three times, and washed his feet up to the ankles three times each. Then he stood and drank the leftover water of his ablution while standing, and said: I wanted to show you how the purification of the Prophet ﷺ was."],[757,"I saw ʿAlī come to al-Raḥabah and urinate standing, then perform ablution, rinsing his mouth three times and washing his face three times, and drink while standing, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do as you have seen me do."],[758,"I would draw a bucket of water for a date, and I would stipulate that it be sweet and firm."],[759,"ʿAmmār asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: The good one, the one made good."],[760,"ʿAmmār b. Yāsir asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Give permission to the good one, the one made good; he has been filled with faith up to his bone marrow."],[761,"ʿAmmār asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Give permission to the good one, the one made good."],[762,"When al-Ḥasan was born, I named him Ḥarb. He said: Rather, he is Ḥasan. When al-Ḥusayn was born, I named him Ḥarb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: Show me my son; what have you named him? We said: Ḥarb. He said: Rather, he is Ḥusayn. When the third was born, I named him Ḥarb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: Show me my son; what have you named him? We said: Ḥarb. He said: Rather, he is Muḥassin. Then he said: I have named them after the names of the children of Hārūn: Jabbar, Jubayr, and Mujabbir."],[763,"When al-Ḥasan was born, I named him Ḥarb, and I liked to be called Abū Ḥarb. The Prophet ﷺ came and chewed a date and put it in his mouth, and said: What have you named my son? We said: Ḥarb. He said: He is al-Ḥasan. Then al-Ḥusayn was born, and I named him Ḥarb. The Prophet ﷺ came and chewed a date and put it in his mouth, and said: What have you named my son? We said: Ḥarb. He said: He is al-Ḥusayn."],[764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us—I, Jaʿfar, and Zayd—and he said to Zayd: You are our brother and our client. Zayd hopped, and he said to Jaʿfar: You resemble me in my physical appearance and my character. He said: So he hopped behind Zayd's hop. Then he said to me: You are from me and I am from you. So I hopped behind Jaʿfar's hop."],[765,"A person is with the one he loves."],[766,"ʿUqbah b. Khālid narrated to us, from Isrāʾīl, from Muslim, from Ḥabbah al-ʿUranī, from ʿAlī."],[767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to eat garlic. He said: And were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it."],[768,"I leaned the Prophet ﷺ against my chest, and he said to me: O ʿAlī, I enjoin you to treat the Arabs well."],[769,"\"Go and command them to close their doors.\" So I went and told them, and they did, except Hamzah. I said, \"O Messenger of God, they have done so except Hamzah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Tell Hamzah to relocate his door.\" So I told him, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to relocate your door,\" and he relocated it. Then I returned to him while he was standing praying, and he said, \"Return to your house.\""],[770,"I saw Ali b. Abi Talib delivering a sermon and he laughed. We were surprised at his laughter. When he descended, we said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, you laughed on the pulpit; why did you laugh?\" He said, \"I remembered Abu Talib. I saw myself with the Prophet ﷺ when the prayer time came—the afternoon prayer—and we had come to a place called Nakhlah. I think he said: we wanted to pray. Abu Talib looked at us and said, 'O sons of my brother, what are you doing?' We said, 'We are praying.' The Prophet ﷺ invited him to Islam, and he said, 'What you call me to is good, but by God, O son of my brother, my buttocks will never be above me.' I laughed at his words.\""],[771,"The first prayer we prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ was the afternoon prayer."],[772,"A man asked Ali about the cow. He said, \"It is for seven.\" The man said, \"The one with a broken horn?\" He said, \"It does not harm you.\" He said, \"The lame one?\" He said, \"If it reaches the place of sacrifice.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear."],[773,"I asked Ali or a man asked Ali about the cow. He said, \"It is for seven.\" He said, \"The horn?\" He said, \"It does not harm you.\" He said, \"Lameness?\" He said, \"If it reaches the place of sacrifice.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear."],[774,"When he entered the morning, he would say: \"O God, by You we enter the morning, and by You we enter the evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the resurrection.\" And he would say the like when he entered the evening, and he would say at the end of it: \"And to You is the final return.\""],[775,"\"Indeed, God is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness.\""],[776,"He came to Fatimah and said to her, \"I complain of my chest from drawing water with the bucket.\" She said, \"And I, by God, complain of my hands from grinding with the millstone.\" Ali said to her, \"Go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him to provide you with a servant.\" She went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, greeted him, then returned. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"What brought you?\" She said, \"I came to greet the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" When she returned to Ali, she said, \"By God, I could not speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ out of awe of him.\" So they both went to him together. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, \"What brought you both? Indeed a need has brought you—I think he said—.\" Ali said to him, \"Yes, O Messenger of God. I complained to Fatimah of my hands from drawing water with the bucket, and she complained to me of her hands from grinding with the millstone, so we came to you to provide us with a servant from what God has given you.\" He said, \"No, but I spend—or I spend it—on the people of the veranda whose livers are folded from hunger; I do not find what to feed them.\" He said, \"When they returned and took to their beds at night, the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them while they were under a khamil—the khamil is a thick cloak—and the Messenger of God ﷺ had equipped her with it and with a cushion stuffed with idhkhir. Ali and Fatimah had felt distressed when he turned them away. When they heard the sound of the Messenger of God ﷺ, they rose to stand, but the Prophet ﷺ said to them, 'Stay in your places.' Then he came and sat on the edge of the khamil and said, 'You came to me to provide you with a servant, but I will guide you—or something similar—to what is better for you than a servant: praise God ten times after every prayer, glorify Him ten times, and magnify Him ten times—or glorify Him thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times, making one hundred—when you take to your beds at night.'\" Ali said, \"I do not know that I ever left it after that.\" Abdullah b. al-Kawwa said to him, \"Not even on the night of Siffin?\" Ali said to him, \"May God fight you—and not even on the night of Siffin.\""],[777,"The Prophet ﷺ called me and said, \"O Ali, in you there is a likeness to Jesus son of Mary: the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him in a position that is not his.\""],[778,"\"The rulers are from Quraysh: its righteous are the rulers of its righteous, and its wicked are the rulers of its wicked.\""],[779,"\"The blood and flesh of Ammar are forbidden to the Fire to consume.\""],[780,"Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ addressed us and said, \"O people, tell me who is the bravest of people?\" They said—or he said: we said—\"You, O Commander of the Faithful.\" He said, \"Indeed, I have never dueled anyone except that I prevailed over him. But tell me who is the bravest of people.\" They said, \"We do not know. Who is it?\" He said, \"Abu Bakr ؓ. On the day of Badr, we made a shelter for the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'Who will stay with the Messenger of God ﷺ, lest one of the polytheists attack him?' By God, none came near him except Abu Bakr, brandishing a sword over the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ; no one attacked him except that Abu Bakr attacked him. So this is the bravest of people.\" Ali said, \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when Quraysh seized him: this one trampling him, this one shaking him, while they said, 'You are the one who made the gods one God.' By God, none came near him except Abu Bakr, striking this one, trampling that one, and shaking that one, while saying, 'Woe to you! Will you kill a man because he says, \"My Lord is God\"?'\" Then Ali lifted a cloak that was on him and wept until his beard was soaked, then said, \"I adjure you by God: is the believer of the family of Pharaoh better or Abu Bakr?\" The people remained silent. He said, \"Will you not answer me? By God, an hour of Abu Bakr is better than the earth filled with the believer of the family of Pharaoh. That was a man who concealed his faith, and this is a man who proclaimed his faith.\""],[781,"A slave girl of the Prophet ﷺ committed an offense—meaning she fornicated—so he ordered me to carry out the prescribed punishment on her. I went to her while her blood had not yet dried, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'When it dries, then carry out the punishment on her.' And he said: 'Carry out the prescribed punishments on those whom your right hands possess.'"],[782,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping and ordered me, so I gave the cupper his wage."],[783,"On Friday, Zayd b. Suhan was with him while he was delivering the sermon on a pulpit made of brick, with the clients around him. A man spoke some words—I do not know what they were—and he became angry until his face turned red. Then he fell silent. While we were like that, al-Ash'ath b. Qays came stepping over people and said: 'These red ones have prevailed over you on account of your face.' Zayd b. Suhan struck my shoulders and said: 'Indeed we belong to Allah. By Allah, the Arabs will surely reveal what they used to conceal.' Then he said: 'Who will excuse me from these idle, arrogant ones? One of them turns over on his bed while people go early to the remembrance of Allah. So what do you command me? Shall I drive them away and thus be among the wrongdoers?' Then he said: 'By the One who split the grain and created the soul, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: They will surely strike you away from the religion a second time just as you struck them for it the first time.'"],[784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from using gourds, pitch-coated vessels, and green jars."],[785,"Regarding the saying of Allah, blessed and exalted: 'And warn your nearest kindred,' he said: 'He called them and gathered them over a leg of mutton and a bowl of milk, though among them were those who could eat a whole young sheep.' He said: 'We ate until we were full and drank until we were satisfied.'"],[786,"The wife of al-Walid b. Uqba came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining that her husband beat her. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Go to him and say: The Prophet ﷺ says such-and-such.' She went, then came back and said: 'He has returned to beating me.' He said: 'Go and say to him: The Prophet ﷺ says such-and-such.' She went, then came back and said: 'He has returned to beating me.'"],[787,"The wife of al-Walid b. Uqba came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about al-Walid. He said to her: 'Go back and say to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has granted me protection.' She went away and stayed for a while, then she returned and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he has not stopped beating me.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off a fringe from his garment and said: Take this and say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is a fringe from my garment.' She went away and stayed for a while, then she returned and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he only increased me in beating.' So he raised his hands and said: 'O Allah, take al-Walid to account'—twice or three times."],[788,"I set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night until we came to the Kaaba. He said to me: 'Sit down.' Then I lifted him up, but when he saw my weakness beneath him, he said: 'Sit down.' So I sat down, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got down from me and sat for me, and said: 'Climb onto my shoulders.' So I climbed onto him, and he stood up with me until it seemed to me that if I wished, I could reach the horizon of the sky. Then I climbed onto the House and came to the idol of Quraysh, which was a figure of a man made of brass or copper. I kept working at it from the right and left, from in front of it and behind it, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Go on!' and I kept working at it. Then he said: 'Throw it down.' So I threw it down, and it shattered like glass breaks. Then we set off running until we hid among the houses, and nothing was ever put on it after that."],[789,"We came to Khaybar, and when he ﷺ reached it, he sent Umar with the people. They did not stay long before they were defeated and Umar and his companions were put to flight. He said: 'I will certainly send against them a man who loves Allah and His Messenger and whom Allah and His Messenger love; he will fight them until Allah grants him victory.' People stretched their necks and looked forward to it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent for a while, then said: 'Where is Ali?' They said: 'He is suffering from eye inflammation.' He said: 'Call him for me.' When I came to him, he opened my eyes, then spat into them, then gave me the banner. I set out until I reached them, and among them was Marhab, reciting battle verses. We met, and Allah killed him, and his companions fled and fortified themselves, closing the gate. I came to the gate and kept working at it until Allah opened it."],[790,"Ali made me ride behind him, then he traveled through the cemetery of Kufa, then raised his head to the sky and said: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins; none forgives sins but You.' Then he turned to me and laughed. I said: 'What is this?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made me ride behind him, then raised his head and said: Forgive me my sins; none forgives sins but You. Then he turned to me and laughed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you seek forgiveness from your Lord and turn to me laughing. He said: I laughed at the laughter of my Lord, blessed and exalted, at His servant, for He knew that none forgives sins but He.'"],[791,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him while he had traces of perfume on him. He refused to accept his pledge. The man went and washed off the traces of perfume, then came and pledged allegiance to him."],[792,"I saw Ali bring a riding animal and place his foot on it. When he was settled, he said: 'Praise be to Allah, glory to the One who subjected this to us, for we could not have subdued it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return.' Then he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he mounted his riding animal do the same.'"],[793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me the fighting of the oath-breakers, the oppressors, and the renegades."],[794,"The Prophet ﷺ loved [the surah] “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.”"],[795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved to recite “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.”"],[796,"Al-Hasan b. Ali fell ill, and Abu Musa came to visit him. Ali said to him: “Have you come as a visitor of the sick, O Abu Musa, or as a visitor? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No Muslim visits a Muslim at the beginning of the day except that seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and an orchard of Paradise is granted for him. If he visits him in the evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning, and an orchard of Paradise is granted for him.’”"],[797,"Chosroes sent a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he accepted it; Caesar sent a gift to him and he accepted it; kings sent gifts to him and he accepted them."],[798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while I, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn were sleeping under a blanket, or perhaps under a cover. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to our vessel and poured into a cup and brought it. Al-Husayn rushed to it, and he said with his hand, so Fatimah said: “It is as though he is more beloved to you than the other, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “He asked for water before him. I, you, these two, and this sleeping one will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[799,"Ali was brought water and he drank it while standing. Then he said: “Some people dislike drinking while standing, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink while standing.”"],[800,"He saw Ali perform ablution three times, then ask for water and drink while standing, and he said: “Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.”"],[801,"Ali prayed zuhr, then went out to the open area and sat attending to people’s needs until asr came. Then a jug of water was brought, and he took a handful and wiped his face, hands, head, and feet, then drank the leftover while standing. Then he said: “Some people dislike drinking while standing, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did as I did, and he said: ‘This is the ablution of one who has not invalidated his ritual state.’”"],[802,"“If you appoint Abu Bakr, you will find him abstinent in this world and desirous of the Hereafter. If you appoint Umar, you will find him strong and trustworthy; no blame of a blamer affects him concerning Allah. If you appoint Ali, you will find him guiding and guided; he will take you along the straight path. But you will not do so.”"],[803,"By Allah, I have nothing from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he did not entrust to the people except what is in this scroll of mine which is in the sheath of my sword: Makkah is sacred and Madinah is sacred. Whoever commits a crime therein or shelters a criminal, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him any compensation or substitute."],[804,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me with four instructions: no polytheist may circumambulate the House; no polytheist may approach the Sacred Mosque after this year; whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, it remains valid until its term; and none will enter Paradise except a believing soul."],[805,"I adjure God: a man who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm when he stood up, and thirteen men stood up to him and testified that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Then he took Ali by the hand and said: \"Whoever's mawla I am, this is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him, and love whoever loves him, and hate whoever hates him, and help whoever helps him, and forsake whoever forsakes him.\"'"],[806,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the Confederates: 'They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May God fill their graves, their bellies, and their houses with fire.'"],[807,"I did not think that the soles of the feet were more deserving of wiping than their tops, until I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the tops of his feet."],[808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform Witr at the rising of dawn."],[809,"Ali entered the Rahbah after performing the Fajr prayer, then said to a servant of his: 'Bring me water for purification.' The servant brought him a vessel containing water and a basin. Abd Khayr said: 'We were sitting, watching him. He took the vessel with his hand and poured it onto his left hand, then washed his palms. Then he took it with his right hand and poured onto his left hand and washed his palms. Then he took the vessel with his hand and poured onto his hand and washed his palms.' Thus said Abd Khayr: He did not insert his hand into the vessel until he had washed it three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the vessel, rinsed his mouth, then inhaled water and blew it out with his left hand three times. He washed his face three times, and washed his right hand three times, then washed his left hand three times up to the elbow. Then he inserted his hand into the vessel until the water covered it, then raised it with what it carried of water and wiped it with his left hand. Then he wiped his head with both hands once. Then he took with his right hand and poured onto his right foot, then washed it with his left hand three times. Then he took with his right palm and poured onto his left foot, then washed it with his left hand three times. Then he took with his palm and drank from it, then said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at the purification of the Prophet of God, this is the purification of the Prophet of God.'"],[810,"I saw Ali. Shu'bah narrated it from Malik b. Urfutah, and he erred in his name and his father's name. He is only Khalid b. Alqamah, from Abd Khayr."],[811,"I saw Ali bring a chair and sit on it. Then he brought a vessel of water and washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and inhaled water with one handful, then washed his face three times and his forearms three times each. Then he placed his hand in the vessel, then wiped his entire head. I do not know whether he passed his hands from the back of the head or from the front. Then he washed his feet three times each, then said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at the purification of the Messenger of God ﷺ, this is the purification of the Messenger of God.'"],[812,"I saw Ali perform ablution and wipe over the sandals, and he said: 'Had I not seen the Messenger of God ﷺ do as you have seen me do, I would have considered the soles of the feet more deserving of wiping than their tops.'"],[813,"He saw Ali perform ablution in the Rahbah. He washed his palms, then rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water three times, washed his face three times, his forearms three times each, his head three times, and washed his feet up to the ankles three times. Then he stood up and drank the leftover water of his ablution while standing, and said: 'I wanted to show you how the purification of the Prophet was.'"],[814,"I entered the mosque of Kufah, and there was Ali on the minbar, delivering a sermon to the people. In his sermon he said: 'O people, the best of you after your Prophet is Abu Bakr, and the best of you after Abu Bakr is Umar. If I wished to name the third, I would name him.' A group of people said: 'He only means himself.'"],[815,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not combine his parents for anyone except Sa'd. He said: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[816,"Mis'ar narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Ibrahim, from Ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Ali. (Narration incomplete)"],[817,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal and Qabisah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abdullah b. Shaddad say: I heard Ali say:"],[818,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not join his parents (in ransom) for anyone except Sa'd, for on the day of Uhud he said: 'Shoot, Sa'd, may my father and mother be your ransom.'\""],[819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade soaking (dates) in a gourd or a vessel smeared with pitch."],[820,"Ubaydah b. Humayd narrated to us, from al-Rukayn b. al-Rabi', from Husayn b. Qabisah, from Ali."],[821,"I was a man who emitted madhy (prostatic fluid), so I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'When you see it, perform ablution; and when you see the gushing of water (semen), perform ghusl.'"],[822,"When the Prophet ﷺ intended to travel, he would say: 'O Allah, with You I roam, with You I charge, and with You I fight.'"],[823,"\"Whoever eats from this tree (garlic) should not come near our mosque, or the mosque.\""],[824,"\"May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr: he married me to his daughter, carried me to the abode of the Hijrah, and freed Bilal with his own wealth. May Allah have mercy on Umar: he speaks the truth even if it is bitter; the truth left him without a friend. May Allah have mercy on Uthman: the angels are shy of him. May Allah have mercy on Ali: O Allah, make the truth turn with him wherever he turns.\""],[825,"The Prophet ﷺ amputated for (the theft of) an iron helmet worth twenty-one dirhams."],[826,"And thus Muhammad b. Marzuq narrated it to us, from Abu Attab, from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from Ali. Others narrated it from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Matar, from Ali b. Abi Talib."],[827,"I entered the mosque and found the Prophet ﷺ among a group of his companions. I said: 'Peace be upon you.' He replied: 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah: twenty (good deeds) for me and ten for you.' He said: Then I entered a second time and said: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.' He replied: 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and twenty for you.' Then I entered a third time and said: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.' He replied: 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and thirty for you. You and I, O Ali, are equal in the greeting. O Ali, whoever passes by a gathering and greets them, Allah records ten good deeds for him, erases ten bad deeds, and raises him ten degrees.'"],[828,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[829,"That he drank while standing, and people looked at him and disapproved of that. 'Ali said, 'What do you disapprove of in my drinking while standing? I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink while standing.'"],[830,"I saw 'Ali drinking while standing, and he saw people looking at him. He said, 'If I drink while standing, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink while standing; and if I drink while sitting, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink while sitting.'"],[831,"Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from 'Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[832,"\"Whoever leaves a spot of hair that the water does not reach — meaning, in the case of major ritual impurity — such and such will be done to him with the Fire.\""],[833,"The first prayer in which we bowed was the 'Asr prayer. I said, 'O Messenger of God, what is this?' He said, \"With this I was commanded.\""],[834,"\"Indeed, a miscarried fetus will dispute with its Lord, saying, 'Admit me to Paradise,' and it will be said to it, 'O miscarried fetus who disputes with its Lord, enter Paradise.' It will say, 'Until my parents enter.' It will be said, 'Return and admit your parents to Paradise,' so it will drag them by their umbilical cords until it brings them into Paradise.\""],[835,"That the Prophet ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the bed."],[836,"That the Prophet ﷺ intended to go on an expedition, so he called Ja'far and ordered him to remain behind in Madinah. Ja'far said, 'I will never remain behind after you.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent for me and adjured me to remain before I could speak, and I wept. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'What makes you weep?' I said, 'More than one thing makes me weep. Tomorrow the Quraysh will say, \"How quickly he remained behind his cousin and abandoned him!\" Another thing that makes me weep is that I wanted to seek fighting in the path of God, because God, mighty and sublime, says: \"Nor do they tread any ground that angers the disbelievers or achieve any gain from an enemy except that a righteous deed is written for them thereby; indeed, God does not waste the reward of the doers of good.\" So I wanted to seek the reward. And another thing that makes me weep is that I wanted to seek God's bounty.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'As for your saying that the Quraysh will say, \"How quickly he remained behind his cousin and abandoned him,\" you have in me an example: they have said to me, \"sorcerer, soothsayer, liar.\" As for your saying that you want to seek reward from God, are you not content to be to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? As for your saying that you want to seek God's bounty, here are two heavy loads of pepper that came to us from Yemen; sell it and enjoy it, you and Fatimah, until God brings you of His bounty.'"],[837,"\"Talhah and al-Zubayr are my two neighbors in Paradise.\""],[838,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man from the people of al-'Aliyah appeared before us and said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me the hardest thing in this religion and the softest of it.' He said, 'The softest of it is the testimony that there is no deity but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. The hardest of it, O brother of al-'Aliyah, is trustworthiness. Indeed, there is no religion for one who has no trustworthiness, and no prayer for him, and no zakat for him. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires wealth unlawfully and spends it is not rewarded for it, and if he hoards it, it becomes his provision to the Fire. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires wealth unlawfully and wears a jilbab — meaning a shirt — his prayer is not accepted until he removes that jilbab. God, blessed and exalted, is too generous and too majestic, O brother of al-'Aliyah, to accept the deed or prayer of a man who is wearing a jilbab of unlawful origin.'"],[839,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."],[840,"Mujalid narrated to us, from 'Amir, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."],[841,"He cursed ten people: the one who consumes interest, the one who pays it, the one who records it, its two witnesses, the woman who tattoos, the woman who gets tattooed, the one who withholds charity, and the one who makes [a divorced woman] lawful [for her former husband] and the one for whom that is done."],[842,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who consumes interest, the one who pays it, its two witnesses, the one who records it, the one who seeks to make [a divorced woman] lawful [for her former husband], the one for whom that is done, the woman who tattoos, the woman who gets tattooed, and the one who withholds his charity."],[843,"Cursed is the one who consumes interest and the one who pays it."],[844,"Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, similarly, but he did not say: from the Prophet."],[845,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[846,"Cursed is the one who consumes interest and the one who pays it."],[847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who consumes interest and the one who pays it."],[848,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Dawud, meaning al-Awdi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , from the Prophet."],[849,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , from the Prophet."],[850,"Ubayd b. al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Fudayl, meaning Ibn Marzuq, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet."],[851,"\"I was with him when Abu Bakr and Umar came. He said: 'These two are the masters of the elderly of Paradise, from the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers.'\""],[852,"The bed of Fatimah ؓ on the night she was given to me in marriage was nothing but a sheepskin."],[853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Abu Bakr and Umar and said: “These two are the masters of the mature men of Paradise, and do not inform them.”"],[854,"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: “O Muhammad, your community will differ after you.” I said: “What is the way out, O Jibril?” He said: “The Book of Allah, by which protection is sought from every tyrant. Whoever holds fast to it is saved, and whoever abandons it is destroyed. It is a decisive statement, not jest; tongues do not wear it out, it does not become burdensome from repeated rebuttal, and its wonders do not cease. In it is the news of what was before you, the judgment of what is between you, and the report of what will be after you.”"],[855,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: “You will be tested after you are gone,” so I asked him, or he was asked, “What is the way out?” He said: “The Book.”"],[856,"“There will be a fitnah.” I said: “What is the way out of it, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “The Book of Allah. In it is the news of what was before you and the report of what will be after you and the judgment of what is between you. It is the decisive criterion, not jest. If any tyrant rejects it, Allah will break him, and whoever seeks guidance in other than it, Allah will lead him astray. It is the firm rope of Allah and the wise reminder. It is the straight path by which desires do not deviate, and the scholars do not have their fill of it, and it does not become worn out by repetition, and its wonders do not come to an end. It is the one about which the jinn, when they heard it, could not refrain from saying: ‘Indeed, we have heard an amazing Qur’an.’ Whoever speaks according to it is truthful, whoever acts by it is rewarded, whoever judges by it is just, and whoever calls to it is guided to a straight path. Whoever holds fast to it is guided to a straight path.”"],[857,"“If I were to appoint anyone from my community as a leader without consulting them, I would appoint Ibn Umm ʿAbd over them.”"],[858,"Musa b. Masʿud narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. Abu Bakr said: “We know of this hadith being narrated from Ali from the Prophet ﷺ only through this route with this chain.”"],[859,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the debt should be paid before the bequest, though you recite, “after any bequest they make or debt,” and he ruled that full brothers inherit rather than half-brothers from the father’s side."],[860,"Allah has pardoned for you the sadaqah of horses and slaves."],[861,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred uqiyyahs and gave ten of them as sadaqah.” Another man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred dinars and gave ten of them as sadaqah.” Another man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I had ten dinars and gave one of them as sadaqah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of you are equal in reward, for each of you gave one tenth of his wealth as sadaqah.”"],[862,"“Among the worst of people are those who are alive when the Hour begins, those who take graves as mosques, and those who give testimony before they are asked for it.”"],[863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from reciting the Qur’an while bowing or prostrating."],[864,"“There is no zakat on one hundred and ninety - meaning dirhams of silver - unless its owner wishes, and when it reaches two hundred, five dirhams are due, and if it increases, it is according to that proportion.”"],[865,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ the fear prayer (salat al-khawf) as two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, which is three; and I prayed with him while traveling two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, which is three."],[866,"The Prophet ﷺ and his family used to bathe from a single vessel, and neither of them would bathe with the leftover water of the other."],[867,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would seek protection for a sick person, he would say: 'Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people, and heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness.'"],[868,"From the whole night, the Prophet ﷺ performed witr at its beginning, its middle, and its end, and he settled his witr at the end of the night."],[869,"The Hour will not be established until a man from among my Companions is sought as a lost camel is sought, and he will not be found."],[870,"The Muslim owes the Muslim six acts of kindness: he greets him with salam when he meets him, visits him when he is sick, answers his invitation when he calls him, attends his funeral when he dies, and gives him sincere counsel in his absence."],[871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr with nine surahs from the mufassal: in the first rak'ah, Alhakum al-takathur (102), Inna anzalnahu fi laylat al-qadr (97), and Idha zulzilat (99); in the second rak'ah, wa-al-'Asr (103), Idha ja'a nasr Allah wa-al-fath (110), and Inna a'taynaka al-kawthar (108); and in the third rak'ah, Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun (109), Tabbat yada Abi Lahab (111), and Qul huwa Allahu ahad (112)."],[872,"If I were to appoint anyone as a commander without consultation, I would appoint Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[873,"He forbade the red saddle cushion."],[874,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'I love for you what I love for myself. Do not prompt the imam during the prayer, do not fiddle with pebbles during the prayer, do not crack your fingers during the prayer, do not turn to your right or left during the prayer, and do not spread your forearms like a beast of prey during the prayer.'"],[875,"It is from the Sunnah that a man leads the prayer with two men behind him, and behind them a woman."],[876,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr at the time of the iqamah."],[877,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform Witr at the time of the Adhan and pray the two rak‘ahs at the time of the Iqamah."],[878,"He forbade prayer at sunrise until the sun has risen, at sunset until the sun has set, and at midday until the sun has declined."],[879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, the one who records it, and the one who makes it lawful."],[880,"Allah does not love an ignorant old man, a rich oppressor, or a poor deceiver."],[881,"Whoever owns provisions and a mount that can take him to the House of Allah but does not perform Hajj, it does not matter whether he dies a Jew or a Christian."],[882,"Fasting three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest."],[883,"Al-Walid b. al-Qasim narrated to us, from Yunus b. Abi Ishaq, from his father, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[884,"Indeed, I am about to be taken, and I have left among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my Ahl al-Bayt. You will never go astray after them. The Hour will not come until the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are sought as a lost camel is sought, but they will not be found."],[885,"He said concerning the Kharijites: A people at the end of time who recite the Qur'an but it does not pass beyond their collarbones. They pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game."],[886,"In the prayer of fear, he commanded the people to take up their weapons. One group stood behind them facing the enemy, and another group came and prayed with him. He prayed one rak‘ah with them, then they went to the group that had not prayed, and the group that had not prayed came forward and stood behind him. He prayed one rak‘ah and two prostrations with them, then he said the salam. When he had said the salam, those facing the enemy stood up and they all said takbir, bowed one rak‘ah and prostrated twice after the salam."],[887,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[888,"He forbade gold rings and the saddle cushion."],[889,"I heard 'Ali say from the minbar: By Allah, the covenant of the unlettered Prophet ﷺ to me is that the ummah will betray me."],[890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to level every raised grave and efface every idol, so I did, then I came to him and he said, 'Have you done it?' I said, 'Yes.'"],[891,"By Him who split the grain and created the soul, this [beard] shall surely be dyed from this [head] — from his head to his beard — and the most wretched of them shall not be restrained. 'Abdullah b. Subay' said, 'By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, if a man did that, we would annihilate his family.' He said: He said, 'I adjure you by Allah not to kill anyone but my killer for me.' They said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, will you not appoint a successor over us?' He said, 'No, but I leave you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left you.' [Someone] said, 'Then what will you say to your Lord when you come to Him, having left us neglected?' He said, 'I will say: You appointed me over them as long as You willed, then You took me, and I left You among them.'"],[892,"People's gatherings were the mosques until they returned from Siffin and disavowed the arbitration. Then people became careless and sat in the streets exchanging news. While we were sitting with 'Ali, who was discussing a matter concerning the people, a man stood up over him and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, permit me to speak.' He said: He was preoccupied with the people's affair. The man was brought and seated among us, and we asked, 'What is this you wanted to ask the Commander of the Faithful about?' He said, 'I was on 'umrah and entered upon the Mother of the Faithful 'A'ishah. She said, \"What are these people who went out near you, called Harura'?\" I said, \"A people who went out to a land near us called Harura'.\"' He said, 'You witnessed their destruction.' 'Asim said: I do not know whether the man said yes or no. 'A'ishah said, 'Indeed, if the son of Abu Talib had wished, he would have told you their story.' So I came to ask him about that. When 'Ali finished what he was doing, he said, 'Where is the man who sought permission?' He stood and recounted to him what he had told us. 'Ali raised his voice in talbiyah and takbir and said, 'I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when no one was with him but 'A'ishah. He said, \"How will you be, O son of Abu Talib, and a people of such and such?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He repeated it, and I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"A people who will come out from the east, reciting the Qur'an but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game. Among them is a man with a defective hand, as if his hand is a breast.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Allah, did I tell you that he is among them, and you came to me saying he is not among them, then you brought him dragging him?\" They said, \"Yes.\" Then 'Ali raised his voice in talbiyah and takbir.'"],[893,"I am Sa'id b. Maslamah, from 'Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, from 'Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[894,"'Ali was in the mosque — I think he said: the mosque of Kufa — and he heard a loud commotion, so he asked, 'What are these?' They said, 'A people reciting the Qur'an' or 'chanting the Qur'an.' He said, 'Indeed, they used to be the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or ear."],[896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sacrificing an animal with a slit ear or broken horn."],[897,"I saw 'Uthman b. 'Affan forbidding mut'ah, and 'Ali b. Abi Talib commanding it. I went to 'Ali and said, 'There is certainly evil between you two: you command it while 'Uthman forbids it.' He said, 'Between us there is nothing but good, but the best of us is the one who follows this religion most closely.'"],[898,"Fatimah ؓ came complaining to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the work. He said, 'Shall I not guide you to what is better for you? Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.'"],[899,"I had a standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that no one else had. I used to come to him every pre-dawn, greet him, and leave only when he cleared his throat, then return to my family. One day I came and greeted him, saying, 'Peace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah.' He said, 'Wait, O Abu al-Hasan, until I come out to you.' When he came out, I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, you did not speak to me before as you spoke to me tonight.' He said, 'I heard a movement in the room and asked, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"I am Jibril.\" I said, \"Enter.\" He said, \"No, come out to me.\" When I went out to him, he said, \"There is something in your house that no angel enters while it is there.\" I said, \"I do not know of it, O Jibril.\" He said, \"Go and look.\" I opened the door and found nothing but a puppy that al-Hasan was playing with. I said, \"I found nothing but a puppy.\" He said, \"None will enter it while one of them is present,\" meaning one of three: a dog, or a state of major ritual impurity, or an image of a living being.'"],[900,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a person in a state of major ritual impurity, or a dog, or an image."],[901,"I heard Abu Zur'ah narrate from 'Abdullah b. Nujayy, from 'Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[902,"I used to have a time of night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: I would come to him at that time. If he was praying, he would clear his throat; otherwise, he would give me permission."],[903,"\"I heard a sound in the house, so I went out and there was Jibril ﷺ . I said, 'What prevented you from entering?' He said, 'The angel does not enter a house in which there is a dog, or an image, or a person in a state of major ritual impurity.' In the house there was a puppy that al-Hasan b. 'Ali was playing with.\""],[904,"He traveled with 'Ali and was in charge of his water container. When he came parallel to Nineveh while heading to Siffin, 'Ali called out, 'Patience, Abu 'Abdullah.' I said, 'What is it, Abu 'Abdullah?' He said, 'I entered upon the Messenger of Allah one day while his eyes were flowing with tears. I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, has someone angered you? What is the matter with your eyes flowing?\" He said, \"Yes, Jibril left me and told me that al-Husayn will be killed on the bank of the Euphrates.\" He said, \"Would you like me to let you smell some of his soil?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He extended his hand and grasped a handful of soil. I could not control my eyes from overflowing.'"],[905,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Fatimah, 'Will you not be pleased to be the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise, and your two sons the masters of the youths of the people of Paradise?'"],[906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took gold in his right hand and silk in his left hand and said, 'These two are forbidden for the males of my nation and lawful for its females.'"],[907,"'Abd al-Hamid b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from 'Abdullah b. Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from 'Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[908,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[909,"A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it pleased him. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if we were to mate the donkeys with our horses, they would produce something like this.' He said, 'Only those who do not understand would do that.'"],[910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing leading them in prayer when he finished, then he came while his head was dripping water and said, 'I stood with you, then I remembered that I had been in a state of major ritual impurity and had not bathed, so I left and bathed. Whoever among you experiences what I experienced or feels a movement in his stomach should leave and bathe or perform ablution.'"],[911,"Zayd b. Harithah went out to Makkah and brought back the daughter of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. Ja'far b. Abi Talib said, 'I will take her; I have more right to her. She is my cousin, and her maternal aunt is with me, and the maternal aunt is like a mother.' 'Ali said, 'Rather, I have more right to her than both of you. She is my cousin, and I have the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she has more right to her. And I am raising my voice so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hears my argument before he comes out.' Zayd said, 'Rather, I have more right to her. I went out to her, traveled, and brought her.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, 'What is your matter?' They repeated their statements to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I will judge between you in this and in other matters.' 'Ali said, 'When he said \"in other matters,\" I said, \"The Qur'an was revealed regarding our raising our voices.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for you, Zayd, you are my mawla and their mawla.\" He said, 'I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah.' \"And as for you, Ja'far, you resemble my physical appearance and character, and you are from my tree from which I come.\" He said, 'I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah.' \"And as for you, 'Ali, you are my close friend and my trustee.\" He said, 'I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah.' \"And as for the girl, I judge her for Ja'far; she will be with her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt is like a mother.\" He said, 'We have submitted, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[912,"Captives were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, so 'Ali and Fatimah went until they came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'What is the matter with you two?' 'Ali said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, work has become difficult for us, and we wanted you to give us a servant to help us with the work.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Shall I direct you two to something better for you than red camels?' 'Ali said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Glorifications of Allah, praises of Allah, and declarations of His greatness, one hundred when you wish to sleep, so you will spend the night with a thousand good deeds.' 'Ali said, 'I have not missed them since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except on the night of Siffin, for I forgot them until I remembered them at the end of the night, then I said them.'"],[913,"I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists, so I said: 'You seek forgiveness for your parents while they are polytheists?' He said: 'Did not Ibrahim seek forgiveness for his father?' I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was revealed: 'It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists' to the end of the verse."],[914,"I said to al-'Abbas: 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the guardianship [of the Kaaba] for us.' He asked him, and he said: 'I give you the watering, which will harm you and you will not harm it.' He said: I said to al-'Abbas: 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to appoint you over the sadaqat.' He said: 'I would not appoint you over the washing of people's sins.'"],[915,"There was no prophet but he was given seven noble companions and ministers, and I was given fourteen: Hamza, Ja'far, 'Ali, Hasan, Husayn, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, Abu Dharr, al-Miqdad, Hudhayfa, 'Ammar, Salman, and Bilal."],[916,"When 'Ali killed the people of al-Nahar, he said: 'Search, for indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A people will emerge who speak the word of truth, but it will not pass their throats; they are the worst of people.\" So search for him.' We searched and found him, and we fell down in prostration, and 'Ali fell down with us in prostration."],[917,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ near al-Baqi', meaning Baqi' al-Gharqad, on a rainy day when a woman passed by on a donkey with a mule driver. She passed through a depression in the ground and fell, so he turned his face away from her. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, she is wearing trousers.' He said: 'O Allah, forgive the trouser-wearing women of my ummah.'"],[918,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, set the prices for us.' He said: 'Indeed, the rising and falling of prices is in the hand of Allah. I wish to meet my Lord with no one seeking recompense from me for an injustice I did to him.'"],[919,"I witnessed 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ on the day of the killing of the Haruriyya, while I was with my master. He said: 'Look, for among them is a man one of whose hands is like a woman's breast. The Prophet ﷺ informed me that I am his companion.' They turned over the slain but did not find him, and said: 'Seven individuals under the palm tree we have not yet turned over.' He said: 'Woe to you, look.' Abu Mu'min said: I saw two ropes on his legs, dragging him until they threw him before him. 'Ali fell down in prostration and said: 'Rejoice, your slain are in Paradise and their slain are in the Fire.'"],[920,"A man from the people of al-Suffa died and left behind a dinar and a dirham. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Two brands [of fire]. Pray over your companion.'"],[921,"Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."],[922,"A servant does not believe until he believes in four: he bears witness that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with the truth; he believes in the resurrection after death; and he believes in fate."],[923,"Quraysh gathered before the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Our slaves have joined you and entered with you into this affair though they are not worthy of it. Return them to us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until anger was seen on his face, then said: 'O assembly of Quraysh, you will desist, or Allah will surely send a man from among you whose heart Allah has tested with faith to strike your necks for the religion.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr?' He said: 'No.' It was said: 'Then 'Umar?' He said: 'No, but he is the mender of the sandal in the room.' 'Ali said: 'I was the mender of the sandal.' 'Ali said: The people asked 'Ali about that, and he said: 'Indeed, I heard him say: \"Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me deliberately, let him enter the Fire.\""],[924,"Three people set out for a need of theirs and took shelter in a mountain, which collapsed upon them. They said: 'O you, meaning some to others, think about the best of your deeds and call upon Allah through them, perhaps Allah will relieve us.' One of them said: 'O Allah, there was a woman I was close with, and I kept going to her until I got what I wanted from her. She said: \"I remind you of Allah not to do with me what Allah has forbidden you.\" I said: \"I am more deserving to fear.\" So I left her out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure. If You know that, then relieve us.' He said: The mountain split open for them until they hoped to get out but could not get out. The second said: 'O Allah, there were hired workers working on a job—I think he said—and each of them took his wages, but one left his wages and claimed that his wages were more than the wages of his companions. I set aside his wages from my wealth until it became much good and livestock. He came to me after he had become poor and old, and said: \"I remind you of Allah regarding my wages, for I am in greater need of it than ever.\" I went up on a house and showed him what Allah had increased from his wages in wealth and livestock in the open land, meaning in the deserts. I said: \"This is for you.\" He said: \"Are you mocking me, may Allah set you right? I wanted less than this and you refused me.\" So I gave it to him, O Lord, out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure. If You know that, then relieve us.' The mountain split open for them, but they could not get out. The third said: 'O Lord, I had two elderly poor parents who had no servant, no shepherd, and no guardian other than me. I pastured for them by day and returned to them by night. The pasture became distant, so I went far with the livestock. I came to them at night after part of the night had passed and they had slept. I milked into the vessel, then sat by their heads with the vessel, disliking to wake them until they woke up on their own. O Allah, if You know that I did that out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure, then relieve us.' The mountain split open and they came out."],[925,"\"O 'Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are the possessor of its two horns. Do not follow a glance with another glance, for the first is yours [and the second is not].\""],[926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood once, then he did not stand [again]."],[927,"He attended a funeral in Kufa with 'Ali. 'Ali passed by the people while they were standing, and he gestured to them to sit, saying, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I think, used to stand but then he sat.'"],[928,"Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa b. 'Uqbah, from Yusuf b. Mas'ud b. al-Hakam, from his father, from 'Ali, from the Prophet ﷺ , similarly. We do not know that Mas'ud b. al-Hakam transmitted anything as a musnad except this hadith from 'Ali, and it has been narrated from 'Ali through other than this route."],[929,"Shall I not send you with what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me? That I should not pass by any grave without leveling it, and to obliterate images."],[930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are sending me while I am a young man to judge among them, and I do not know what judgment is.' He struck my chest with his hand and said, 'O Allah, guide his heart and make his tongue steadfast.' He ['Ali] said, 'By the One who split the grain, I never doubted after that in any judgment between two people.'"],[931,"When this verse was revealed: 'And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way' [Quran 3:97], they said to the Messenger of Allah, 'Every year?' He remained silent. Then they said, 'Every year?' He said, 'No, and if I had said yes, it would have become obligatory.' Then Allah revealed: 'O you who have believed, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you' [Quran 5:101]."],[932,"My father was in charge of some affair of Makkah during the time of 'Uthman. 'Uthman came to Makkah, and he was met at Qudayd. The people of the water caught a partridge and cooked it with water and salt, making it a broth for tharid. It was presented to 'Uthman and his companions, but they refrained when they saw it. 'Uthman said, 'It is game that they caught for us; we did not command them to hunt it. A people in the state of ihram [actually halal, not muhrim] hunted it and fed us, so what is wrong with it? Who can speak about this?' Some said, ''Ali.' So he sent for him. He came - it is as if I can see him when he came brushing off leaves from his palms. 'Uthman said to him, 'Game that we did not hunt and did not command to be hunted; a people in the state of halal hunted it and fed us, so what is wrong with it?' 'Ali said, 'I adjure by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a leg of a wild donkey or its hindquarter was brought to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We are people in the state of ihram, so feed it to those who are not in ihram.\"' Twelve men from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ testified. Then he said, 'I adjure by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when ostrich eggs were brought to him, and he said, \"We are in the state of ihram, so feed them to those who are not in ihram.\"' Then a number less than them testified. 'Uthman turned his side away from the food, and the people of the water ate that food."],[933,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'Fasting is for Me, and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast and when he meets his Lord. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the change in the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk.'"],[934,"That you separate the mufassal [the surahs from Qaf to al-Nas] is more beloved to me than such and such a gate [i.e., a gate of Paradise]."],[935,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibrahim b. 'Abdullah b. Hunayn, from his father, from 'Ali."],[936,"He forbade wearing qassi [a type of silk-blend cloth], garments dyed with safflower, wearing gold rings, and reciting the Quran while bowing."],[937,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from wearing saffron-dyed garments, and from reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[938,"Muhammad b. Ja'far, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibrahim b. 'Abd Allah b. Hunayn, from his father, from 'Ali."],[939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wearing a gold ring, wearing qassi and saffron-dyed garments, and reciting during bowing and prostration. He did not say 'He forbade you.'"],[940,"He used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[941,"I saw 'Ali urinate, then wash his private part, perform ablution three times, wipe his head, take a handful of water and do like this with it, and wipe over his leather socks. He said: 'This is how the Messenger of God's ablution was.'"],[942,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray eight rak'ahs at night, and when it was near dawn he would perform witr with three rak'ahs, then when dawn broke he would pray two rak'ahs before dawn."],[943,"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me that no one should wash him except me, for if anyone saw my nakedness his eyes would be blinded. 'Ali said: Al-'Abbas and Usamah would hand me water from behind the curtain."],[944,"The Prophet ﷺ used to alternate between his feet, standing on each leg, until 'We have not sent down the Qur'an to you that you be distressed' was revealed."],[945,"I went out with my father to visit 'Ali when he was ill. My father said to him: 'What keeps you in this place? If you were to die here, only the Bedouin of Juhaynah would attend to you. If you entered Madinah, you would be among your companions, and if what you fear befalls you, your companions would take charge of you.' Abu Fadalah was one of the people of Badr. 'Ali said to him: 'I will not die in this illness of mine, or from this pain of mine. The Prophet ﷺ told me that I will not die until—I think he said—I am struck, or until this is dyed from this,' meaning his head. Abu Fadalah was killed with him at Siffin."],[946,"When Abu Bakr ؓ died, they shrouded him in a cloth, and Madinah shook with weeping, and the people were stunned as on the day the Messenger of God ﷺ was taken. 'Ali b. Abi Talib came hastening, saying 'Indeed we belong to God, and indeed to Him we return,' and he said: 'Today the succession of prophethood has been cut off.' He stood at the door of the house where Abu Bakr was and said: 'May God have mercy on you, Abu Bakr. You were the first of the people in Islam, the most sincere of them in faith, the strongest of them in certainty, the most fearful of them of God, the greatest of them in support, the most protective of them toward His Messenger, the most affectionate of them toward Islam, the most trustworthy of them over his companions, the best of them in companionship, the most excellent of them in virtues, the most numerous of them in precedents, the highest of them in rank, the closest of them to his Messenger, the most similar to him in guidance, character, and demeanor, the most reliable of them in his sight, the most honorable of them in station, and the most noble of them to him. May God reward you well on behalf of Islam, His Messenger, and the Muslims. You believed the Messenger of God when the people denied him, so He named you in His Book al-Siddiq, saying: \"And the one who brought the truth—Muhammad—and the one who believed in it—Abu Bakr.\" You supported him when they were miserly, you stood with him when they sat back, and you accompanied him in hardship with the noblest companionship. The one on whom tranquility descended was your companion in the emigration and in the places of distress. You succeeded him in his community with the best succession when the people apostatized, and you upheld God's religion with a stand that no successor of a prophet ever did. You were strong when your companions were weak, you rose when they faltered, and you adhered to the paths of his Messenger despite the spite of the hypocrites and the rage of the disbelievers. You undertook the affair when they failed, with God's light when they halted. You were the highest of them in elevation, the least of them in speech, the most correct of them in expression, the longest of them in silence, the most eloquent of them in words, the greatest of them in judgment, the bravest of them in heart, the strongest of them in certainty, the best of them in deeds, and the most knowledgeable of them in affairs. You were a chief for the religion, and you were a merciful father to the believers when they became dependent on you, so you carried the burdens they were too weak to bear, you preserved what they neglected, you tended what they abandoned, and you were patient when they despaired. Thus you attained the traces of what they sought, and through you they obtained what they had not expected. You were upon the disbelievers a pouring punishment, and for the Muslims rain and abundance. You were created with its richness, you dwelt in its protection, you attained its virtues, and you secured its precedents. Your argument did not diminish, your heart did not deviate, your insight did not weaken, and your soul did not falter. You were like a mountain that storms could not move and gales could not dislodge. You were as the Messenger of God ﷺ said: the most gracious of people to him in your companionship and your wealth, and as he said: weak in body, strong in the affair of God, humble, great in the sight of the Muslims, majestic on earth. No one had any fault to find in you, no speaker any criticism, no one any hope of favoritism, nor did you show leniency to anyone. The weak and abased were strong in your eyes until you secured their rights; the strong and mighty were abased and weak in your eyes until the right was taken from them; the near and the far were equal to you in that. Your concern was truth, sincerity, and gentleness. Your word was decisive, and the path was made clear, and by you the religion was set aright, faith was strengthened, and God's command prevailed, even if the disbelievers disliked it. By God, you raced ahead with a far-reaching lead, and you exhausted those after you with great exhaustion. You have attained Paradise, and your loss was magnified in heaven, and your calamity shook creation. Indeed we belong to God, and indeed to Him we return. We are content with God's decree and submit to His command. The Muslims will never be afflicted after the Messenger of God ﷺ with the like of you. You were for the religion a provision and a refuge, for the Muslims a fortress, a support, and a comfort, and upon the hypocrites harshness and wrath. May God join you with your Prophet, and may He not deprive us of your reward, and may He not lead us astray after you.' He said: The people were silent until he finished his speech, then the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ wept and said: 'You have spoken the truth, O cousin of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[947,"Two men were brothers. One of them was martyred, and the second remained alive for a year after the martyr. Talhah said: I saw the latter of the two men enter Paradise before the martyr. I told the people about that, and it reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: 'Did he not fast Ramadan after him and pray six thousand one hundred rak'ahs after him, meaning the prayer of the year?'"],[948,"I heard 'Umar b. al-Khattab say to Talhah, may God have mercy on them both: 'Why do I see you gloomy since the Messenger of God ﷺ died? Perhaps it is because of the leadership of your cousin.' He said: 'No, by God, and I am the most deserving of you not to do that.' He said: 'Then what is the matter with you?' He said: 'I heard him ﷺ say: I know a word that no man says at the time of death but that he finds relief for it when his soul leaves his body.' 'Umar said: 'I know it.' He said: 'What is it?' He said: 'The word he said to his uncle: There is no god but God.'"],[949,"We were with Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah while we were in a state of ihram, and a bird was gifted to him. Talhah was asleep, so some of us ate and some of us refrained. He said: When Talhah woke up, he was informed, and he agreed with those who ate it and said: 'We ate it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[950,"I was with Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah when a man entered and said: 'O Abu Muhammad, by Allah, we do not know whether this Yamani is more knowledgeable about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you, or whether he says about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say?' He meant Abu Hurayrah. Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah said: 'By Allah, we do not doubt that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what we did not hear and knew what we did not know. We were wealthy people with houses and families, and we used to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the two ends of the day. He was poor, with no wealth and no family; his hand was always with the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he used to go around with him wherever he went. We do not doubt that he knew what we did not know and heard what we did not hear, and we do not find anyone in whom there is good saying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say.'"],[951,"A Bedouin Arab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we heard a murmuring from him but did not know what he was saying. He asked him about Islam, and he said: 'Five prayers in the day and night.' He asked: 'Is there anything else due upon me?' He said: 'No.' He asked him about fasting, and he said: 'The month of Ramadan.' He asked: 'Is there anything else due upon me?' He said: 'No.' Then he mentioned zakah, and he said: 'Is there anything else due upon me?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add to these nor diminish from them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He will succeed if he is truthful.'"],[952,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, passed by Talhah when Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, was appointed caliph, and said: 'I see you sad; perhaps you dislike the leadership of your cousin.' He said: 'No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say a word which I did not ask him about until he passed away. He said: \"I know a word that no servant says at the time of his death except that it becomes light in his record, and his soul and body find rest for it at death.\"' 'Umar said: 'I know it; it is la ilaha illa Allah, the word for which he wanted his uncle.' He said: 'I do not think it is anything other than it.'"],[953,"I accompanied Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah and Sa'd, and I did not hear either of them narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except Talhah, for I heard him narrating about the Day of Uhud."],[954,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the road to Makkah: 'The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh, the most tender to a child and the most attentive to a husband.'"],[955,"I passed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through some palm trees, and he saw people on the tops of the palms pollinating them. He said: 'What are you doing, or what are these people doing?' They said: 'They take from the male and put into the female.' He said: 'I do not think this helps at all.' That reached them, so they abandoned it, and the palms became unproductive. He said: 'You know better what is beneficial for your worldly affairs. I only said what I thought was an opinion. What I said to you, if Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has said it, then I would never lie about Allah, Blessed and Exalted.'"],[956,"This is narrated by Hafs b. Jami', from Simak b. Harb, from Musa b. Talhah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. This hadith has been narrated from Simak by Isra'il, Asbat b. Nasr, and more than one. We do not know of it being narrated from Talhah except through this chain. A group narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ, including Anas, 'A'ishah, Rafi' b. Khadij, Jabir b. 'Abd Allah, and Yasir b. 'Amr."],[957,"\"If you place in front of you something like the back of a saddle, then it does not harm you whoever passes in front of you.\""],[958,"\"There is no zakah on vegetables.\""],[959,"Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Uthman b. 'Abd Allah b. Mawhab, from Musa b. Talhah, from his father."],[960,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you, so how should we send blessings upon you?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[961,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said to a Bedouin: \"Ask him about the one who has fulfilled his vow—who is he?\" But these [companions] did not dare ask him themselves. The Bedouin asked him: \"Who has fulfilled his vow?\" He turned away from him. Then he asked again, and he turned away from him. Then he went out of the mosque gate, and I was with him. He said: \"Where is the one asking about who has fulfilled his vow?\" He said: \"Here I am, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"This one is among those who have fulfilled their vows.\""],[962,"\"Indeed, 'Amr b. al-'As is sound in judgment.\""],[963,"The Messenger of God ﷺ received in advance from al-'Abbas the zakat of two years."],[964,"The Messenger of God ﷺ walked with us in Makkah while he was fasting, and the fast exhausted him. We milked a she-camel of ours into a wooden bowl and poured honey over it to honor the Messenger of God ﷺ at his breaking of the fast. When the sun set, we handed him the bowl. When he tasted it, he gestured with his hand as if to say: \"What is this?\" We said: \"Milk and honey; we wanted to honor you with it.\" I think he said: \"May God honor you as you have honored me,\" or a supplication of this meaning. Then he said: \"Whoever is moderate, God enriches him; whoever is extravagant, God impoverishes him; whoever is humble, God raises him; and whoever is arrogant, God breaks him.\""],[965,"When he saw the new moon, he would say: \"O God, let it appear over us with security, faith, safety, peace, and Islam. My Lord and your Lord is God.\""],[966,"He forbade branding on the face. He said: A camel that had been branded on its face was brought past the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"Would that fire were kept away from the face of this animal.\" So I said: \"I will certainly brand in the farthest place,\" and I branded on the tailbone."],[967,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and in his hand was a quince. He said: \"Take it, Abu Muhammad, for it strengthens the heart.\""],[968,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the meaning of 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to God), and he said: \"It is declaring God, Blessed and Exalted, free from evil.\""],[969,"Two men were sworn brothers. The one who was more virtuous in Talha's estimation died, and the other remained after him for such and such a time. He fasted Ramadan and prayed such and such, then he died. Talha saw in a dream that the one who died later was superior to the first and higher in rank. Talha said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"Did he not remain after him, living such and such, and fasting such and such?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"The distance between them is greater than that between heaven and earth.\""],[970,"A group of polytheists were around the Kaaba, among them Abu Jahl—may God curse him. The Messenger of God ﷺ approached and stood before them and said: \"Ugly are the faces!\" They fell silent, and not one of them uttered a word. I looked at Abu Jahl as he apologized to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: \"Hold back from us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I will not hold back from you until I kill you.\" Abu Jahl said: \"Can you do that?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God will kill you.\""],[971,"I witnessed 'Uthman b. 'Affan on the day he was besieged while the people were in the place of funerals. If a pebble had been thrown, it would not have fallen except on a person's head. I saw 'Uthman look out at them from the small door that faces the station—the station of Gabriel ﷺ —and he said: \"Is Talha among you?\" They remained silent. He said: \"Is Talha among you?\" They remained silent. He said: \"Is Talha among you?\" Then 'Uthman said: \"I did not think that in a gathering that hears my call three times, no one would answer me. I adjure you by God, O Talha: do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ was at such and such a place, with no one with him except me and you, and he said: 'O Talha, every prophet has a companion from his community in Paradise, and this 'Uthman is my companion in Paradise'?\" He said: \"O God, yes,\" and turned away."],[972,"Three men from the 'Udhri tribe came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He sent to some of his wives, but they had nothing to suffice them. He said: \"Who will take care of them?\" Talha said: \"I will take care of them for you.\" So I took care of them. Talha said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and one of them went out and was killed. Then he sent another expedition, and the second went out and was killed. Then the third fell ill and wasted away on his bed and died. Talha saw them in a dream: the first of them to enter Paradise was the one who died on his bed, then the second, then the third. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Did you not know that he prayed—or he said: with his prayer, fasting, glorification of God, and such and such?\""],[973,"I accompanied Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah, and I never heard him narrate anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the graves of the martyrs. When we descended from the Harrah of Waqim, we saw graves at the foot of the mountain, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, are these our brothers? He said: These are our companions. Then we went out until we came to the graves of the martyrs, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"These are the graves of our brothers,\" and he supplicated for them."],[974,"I came to Madinah with a milch camel of mine and met Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah. I mentioned that to him, and he said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a townsman to sell on behalf of a Bedouin, I would have sold it for you. But bargain and consult me, and I will advise you."],[975,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Salim al-Makki, from a man, from Talhah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. And this hadith we do not know of it being narrated from Talhah except from this route, and we do not know anyone who said: from Salim from his father from Talhah except Mu'ammal from Hammad, and other than Mu'ammal narrates it from a man."],[976,"I heard 'Ali, may Allah have mercy on him, say on the day of the Camel to Talhah: I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is hostile to him? He said: Yes. He said: Then he mentioned it and turned away."],[977,"I was with 'Uthman, may Allah have mercy on him, when he was besieged, and he said: Is Talhah here? Talhah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: Let each man of you take the hand of his companion. So you took the hand of so-and-so, and so-and-so took the hand of so-and-so, until every man took the hand of his companion, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand and said: This is my companion in this world and my ally in the Hereafter. He said: By Allah, yes."],[978,"I saw that the hand of Talhah with which he shielded the Prophet ﷺ had become paralyzed."],[979,"'Amr b. al-'As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and a blessed household is 'Abd Allah and Abu 'Abd Allah and Umm 'Abd Allah."],[980,"I was with Ibn 'Umar, and he passed by 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr while he was crucified, and he said: May Allah have mercy on you, Abu Khubayb. I heard your father, meaning al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever does an evil deed will be requited for it in this world and the Hereafter."],[981,"When the verse 'Then on that Day you will surely be asked about the bliss' was revealed, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss will we be asked about? There are only the two black things: dates and water. He said: That will indeed come to be."],[982,"When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Indeed, you are to die, and indeed, they are to die. Then indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, you will dispute before your Lord,' al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will what was between us in this world be repeated for us along with the specific sins? He said: Yes, it will be repeated for you until every rightful owner is given his due. Al-Zubayr said: Indeed, the matter is severe."],[983,"When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah"],[984,"I was in the fort on the day of the Trench, I and 'Umar b. Abi Salamah. He would bend down for me so I could look at the fighting, and I would bend down for him so he could look at the fighting. I saw my father that day going back and forth, attacking these and attacking those. When he returned, I said: O father, I saw you today going back and forth, attacking these once and those once. He said: Did you see me, my son? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined his parents for me."],[985,"One suckling or two, and one or two mouthfuls of milk, do not make [the suckled child] forbidden [in marriage to the suckler]."],[986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a cold night, or in a cold morning. I went, then I came back while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had some of his wives with him under a blanket, and he threw over me an edge of a garment or the edge of the garment."],[987,"A man from the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam about the streams of the Harrah with which they irrigated the palm trees. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Irrigate, O Zubayr, then release the water to your neighbor.\" The Ansari became angry and said: \"You judged in his favor because he is your aunt's son?\" The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color, then he said: \"O Zubayr, irrigate, then withhold the water until it reaches the walls.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave al-Zubayr his full right. Al-Zubayr said: \"I think the verse was revealed about that: 'But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge concerning what arises between them' (Quran 4:65).\""],[988,"I said to my father: \"O father, why do I not hear you narrate from the Messenger of Allah as so-and-so and so-and-so narrate?\" He said: \"Indeed, I have not separated from him since I embraced Islam, but I heard him say: 'Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[989,"I said to al-Zubayr: \"Why do I not hear you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as his companions narrate from him, so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so?\" He said: \"I have not separated from him since I embraced Islam, but I heard him say: 'Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[990,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ wore two coats of mail. He tried to climb a rock but could not, so Talha sat beneath him until he stood on the rock. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Talha has made [Paradise] obligatory [for himself].\""],[991,"On the day of Uhud, I was among those overcome by drowsiness, and I will never forget hearing the voice of Mu'attib b. Qushayr like in a dream."],[992,"I adjure you by Allah, by whose permission the heaven and the earth stand: did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'We are not inherited; what we leave is charity.' He said: 'O Allah, yes.'"],[993,"Umar b. al-Khattab adjured al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam in a group: \"Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We are not inherited; what we leave is charity'?\" They said: \"Yes.\""],[994,"Regarding the words of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'And fear a trial which will not afflict those who have wronged among you exclusively' (Quran 8:25), he said: \"We used to talk during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and we did not think that we were its people until it befell us.\""],[995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"No one will be killed in it after this day as a punishment except a man who killed Uthman b. Affan.\""],[996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Uhud and placed his wives and his paternal aunt Safiyya bt. Abd al-Muttalib in a fortress called Fari', and he put Hassan b. Thabit with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Uhud. A Jew climbed up until he looked over the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his aunt. Safiyya said: \"O Hassan, get up and kill him.\" He said: \"No, by Allah, that is not in me; if that were in me, I would have gone out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Safiyya said: \"Then tie the sword on my arm.\" He said: \"Then she advanced toward him until she killed him and cut off his head. She said to him: 'Take the head and throw it at the Jews.' He said: 'That is not in me.' So she took the head and threw it at the Jews. The Jews said: 'We know that Muhammad would not leave his family unprotected with no one with them.' So they dispersed and went away. A'isha said: Sa'd b. Mu'adh passed by saying: 'Take it easy; a little while and the battle will catch up with a carrier. No harm in death when the appointed time comes.' She said: 'I never saw anyone more handsome than him that day. He had traces of yellow on him, and he wore a short coat of mail. He had married and consummated with his wife a few days before, so he had traces of saffron.' He said: 'Hassan, when the Prophet ﷺ charged at the disbelievers, would open the fortress, and when they retreated, he would go back with them.'"],[997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held up a sword on the day of Uhud and said, \"Who will take this sword with its due?\" Abu Dujana Simak b. Kharasha stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I will take it with its due. What is its due?\" He said, \"That you strike the enemy with it until it bends.\" So he gave it to him, and he went out. I followed him, and he did not pass by anything except he split it and tore it apart, until he came to some women at the foot of a mountain, among them Hind, who was saying: \"We are the daughters of Tariq, we walk upon soft carpets, and musk is in the partings of our hair; if you advance, we embrace; or if you retreat, we part, a parting without love.\" He said, \"Then he attacked her, and she called out, 'O people of Sakhr!' but no one answered her. So he turned back. I said to him, 'I have seen all that you did, and it pleased me except that you did not kill the woman.' He said, 'She called out and no one answered her, so I disliked to strike with the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a woman who has no helper.'\""],[998,"On the day of Uhud, a woman came hurrying until she was about to overlook the slain. The Prophet ﷺ disliked that she should see them, so he said, \"The woman, the woman.\" Al-Zubayr said: \"I looked at her, and there she was—my mother, Safiyya. We went out hurrying to her, and I said, 'Go back.' I reached her before she came to the slain, and she struck me on the chest and said, 'Away from me, may you have no mother!' I said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to go back or stop.' So she stopped and brought out two garments she had with her. She said, 'These are two garments I brought for my brother Hamza, for I have heard of his killing, so shroud him in them.' He said: 'We came to Hamza to shroud him in them, and there beside him was a man of the Ansar who had been done to as was done to Hamza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt unease to shroud Hamza in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud. So we said, \"For Hamza one garment and for the Ansari one garment.\" We measured them, and one of them was larger than the other, so we cast lots between them, and we shrouded each one in the garment that fell to him.'\""],[999,"Concerning us this verse was revealed: 'And those of kin are nearer to one another in the Book of Allah' [8:75]. That is because we came to Madinah, and we established brotherhood with the Ansar. Abu Bakr had made brotherhood with Kharija b. Zayd, and Umar had made brotherhood with Itban b. Malik."],[1000,"\"For one of you to take his rope and go and bring a bundle of firewood and sell it, and thereby keep his face from begging—is better for him than asking people, whether they give him or refuse him.\""],[1001,"\"I was among those who were overcome by drowsiness on the day of Uhud.\""],[1002,"\"Indeed, perhaps one of you will strike his wife as he would strike a slave-girl. Indeed, the best of you are the best to their families.\""],[1003,"They slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ate it."],[1004,"He used to say: \"O Allah, bless me in my religion, which is the safeguard of my affair; in my Hereafter, to which is my return; and in my worldly life, in which is my sustenance. Make my life an increase in every good, and make death a relief from every evil.\""],[1005,"\"A morning's march or an evening's march in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[1006,"We gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah on the day of Uhud. There did not remain anyone of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah—meaning in Madinah—until there were many slain among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A crier cried out, \"Muhammad has been killed,\" and women wept. A woman said, \"Do not hasten to weep until I look.\" So she went out walking, with no concern other than for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asking about him."],[1007,"Malik b. Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Hamid b. Abd al-Rahman b. Zayd b. al-Khattab, from Abdullah b. Abdullah b. al-Harith b. Nawfal, from Ibn Abbas."],[1008,"Umar b. al-Khattab set out for Syria until, when he was at Sargh, the commanders of the armies met him and informed him—among them Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah and his companions—that the plague had broken out in Syria. Ibn Abbas said: Umar said, \"Summon the Muhajirun for me.\" So he summoned them and consulted them, informing them that the plague had broken out in Syria. Some of them said, \"You have set out for a matter, and we do not think you should turn back.\" Then Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If you hear of it in a land, do not go forward to it; and if it breaks out in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.'\" So Umar praised Allah and turned back."],[1009,"I am al-Rahman, and it is the womb (al-rahim). I have derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will cut him off."],[1010,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf visited Abu al-Raddad and said: \"What do I know? The most dutiful and most connecting of them is Abu Muhammad?\" Abd al-Rahman said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'God, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am al-Rahman, and it is the womb (al-rahim). I have derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will cut him off.'\""],[1011,"Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Raddad, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, from the Prophet."],[1012,"Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, narrated to me, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf."],[1013,"When one of you prays and doubts whether it is one or two, let him regard it as one. And when he doubts between two and three, let him regard it as two, so that the doubt is in the addition. Then let him prostrate twice, then give the salutation."],[1014,"Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. And the one who inserted a man between Muhammad b. Ishaq and Makhul: in his narration he came with the like of the narration of Ibrahim b. Sa'd and added a man whom Ibrahim omitted. And sufficient for you regarding the memory of Ismail b. Ibrahim is his precision."],[1015,"When you are in doubt regarding deficiency, then pray until you are in doubt regarding addition."],[1016,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrayed us on the night of Badr, for the day of Badr."],[1017,"My father narrated to me, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a manner similar to the hadith of Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Husayn, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, from the Prophet."],[1018,"I witnessed the Hilf al-Mutayyabin while I was a boy with my paternal uncles, and I would not love to break it, or that I broke it, even if I had red camels."],[1019,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took me by the hand and went to the palm grove, where he found Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ took him and placed him in his lap, and his eyes shed tears. Then he said: \"O my son, I cannot avail you against God in anything.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, do you weep? Did you not forbid weeping?\" He said: \"I only forbade wailing, two foolish and sinful voices: a voice at the time of blessing—play, amusement, and the flutes of Satan—and a voice at the time of calamity—scratching of faces, tearing of garments, and the lament of Satan. Indeed, the one who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. Were it not that it is a truth and a true promise, and that they are a path that must be traversed, from which there is no escape, until the last of us joins the first, we would have grieved with grief more intense than this—meaning for him. And indeed we are saddened by him. The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say what displeases the Lord, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[1020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Ikrima b. Abi Jahl: \"Who struck your father?\" Ikrima said: \"The one who cut off my father's leg.\" So he ruled that his spoils belonged to Mu'adh b. Amr b. Jamuh."],[1021,"From 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf that he married a woman for a gold weight of a date pit. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he saw upon me the cheerfulness of a wedding. I said: 'I have married a woman from the Ansar for a gold weight of a date pit.'"],[1022,"\"Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep.\""],[1023,"\"O 'Abd al-Rahman, indeed you are among the wealthy, and you will not enter Paradise except crawling, so lend to Allah and He will release your feet.\" 'Abd al-Rahman said: 'What shall I lend or give?' Then 'Abd al-Rahman went out, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to him saying: 'Tell 'Abd al-Rahman to host the guest, feed the poor, and give to the beggar, for that will suffice him for much of what he is in.'"],[1024,"The Prophet ﷺ was never without five or four of his companions at his side or at his door. One day he went out and I followed him. He entered one of the gardens of al-Aswaf and prayed, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration. I said to myself: 'Allah has taken the soul of His Messenger ﷺ; I will never see him again.' I grieved and wept. He raised his head, saw me, and called me. He said: 'What is wrong with you?' or 'What made you doubt?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the prostration, so I said that Allah had taken His Messenger and I would never see him again. I grieved and wept.' He said: 'I made this prostration in gratitude to my Lord for what He has bestowed on me regarding my nation.' Then he said: 'Whoever among them sends one prayer upon you, ten good deeds are written for him.'"],[1025,"My name was 'Abd 'Amr, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me 'Abd al-Rahman."],[1026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited hunting between its two lava fields."],[1027,"He was brought food - Shu'bah said: I think he was fasting - and he said: 'Hamzah was killed and we could not find anything to shroud him, though he is better than me. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr was killed and he is better than me, yet we could not find anything to shroud him. But now we have obtained from this world what we have obtained.' 'Abd al-Rahman said: 'I fear that our good deeds have been hastened for us in this world.' Sa'd said: 'I think he did not eat.'"],[1028,"Do not force your sick ones to eat and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink."],[1029,"While I was with al-Walid b. Ibrahim b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, he found two dates that had fallen. He took one and gave me the other. I refused to eat it, then he said to me:"],[1030,"A daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent word that her daughter was dying. He said to the messenger: 'Tell her: To Allah belongs what He takes and to Allah belongs what He leaves.' Then she sent to him a second time, and he replied to her similarly. Then she sent to him a third time, and he came to her with a group of his companions. The child was brought out to him, her soul rattling in her chest. He felt compassion for her, and his eyes filled with tears. Some of his companions noticed this while they were watching him. He said: 'What is the matter with you that you look? It is a mercy that Allah places wherever He wills. Indeed, Allah shows mercy to those of His servants who are merciful.'"],[1031,"While I was standing in the ranks on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and to my left, and I saw that I was between two young lads of the Ansar, their teeth newly grown. I wished I were between stronger men than they. One of them said to me: 'O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl?' I said: 'Yes, what do you need from him, O son of my brother?' He said: 'I have been told that he insults the Prophet ﷺ or reviles him. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if I see him, my body will not part from his until the more incapable of us dies.' I was amazed at that. Then the other one nudged me and said something similar. I was amazed at their words. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving about among the people. I said to them: 'Indeed, this is the man you were asking me about.' They both rushed at him with their swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: 'Which of you killed him?' Each of them said: 'I killed him.' He said: 'Did you wipe your swords?' They said: 'No.' He looked at the two swords and said: 'Both of you killed him.' He awarded his spoils to Mu'adh b. 'Amr b. al-Jamuh; and the two were Mu'adh b. 'Afra' and Mu'adh b. 'Amr b. al-Jamuh, the ones who struck Abu Jahl."],[1032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him while he was leading the people in prayer. He wanted to step back, but the Prophet gestured to him to stay in place. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed following the prayer of 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf."],[1033,"Umayyah b. Khalaf said to me,"],[1034,"Umayyah b. Khalaf said to me, “O servant of God, who was the man marked with an ostrich feather on his chest on the day of Badr?” I said, “That was the uncle of the Messenger of God ﷺ, Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.” He said, “That is the one who did those deeds to us.”"],[1035,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Saʿd b. Muʿādh came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “This is your chief.”"],[1036,"Quraysh, the Anṣār, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ghifār, and Ashjaʿ are allies, having no protector other than God and His Messenger."],[1037,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ and I were of the same age, and I was among the first people to embrace Islam.”"],[1038,"Abū Bakr is in Paradise, ʿUthmān is in Paradise, ʿAlī is in Paradise, Ṭalḥah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Saʿīd b. Zayd, and Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ—may God’s mercy be upon them."],[1039,"ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Darāwardī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥumayd, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner, but he did not say from his grandfather. This hadith includes Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ and makes him the tenth. We know of it being narrated only from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, although more than one has narrated it in mursal form."],[1040,"When death approached the Prophet ﷺ, they said, “O Messenger of God, advise us.” He said, “I enjoin you to honor the earliest forerunners, then their descendants after them, then their descendants after them, then their descendants after them. If you do not do so, neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed will be accepted from you.”"],[1041,"The short spear used to be brought out for the Messenger of God ﷺ on the two ʿĪds so that he would pray facing it. He used to say thirteen takbīrs, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar—may God’s mercy and good pleasure be upon them—used to do likewise."],[1042,"I witnessed the alliance of Banū Hāshim, Zuhrah, and Taym. It would not please me to break it even in exchange for red camels, and if I were called to it today, I would respond—on the condition that we enjoin good, forbid evil, and secure the rights of the wronged from the wrongdoer."],[1043,"One who fasts Ramadan while traveling is like one who breaks the fast while resident."],[1044,"The qasāmah oath in cases of bloodshed was instituted on the day of Khaybar. That is because a man from the Anṣār, one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, went missing during the night. The Anṣār came and said, “Our companion is writhing in his blood.” He said, “Do you know his killer?” They said, “No, but the Jews killed him.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Choose fifty men from among them and let them swear by God with their strongest oaths; then take the blood money from them.” So they did."],[1045,"The adornment of the world will be lifted in the year one hundred and twenty-five."],[1046,"The best of you is the one who is best to his family, and I am the best of you to my family."],[1047,"Afif b. Salim narrated to us, from al-Layth b. Sa'd, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman, from his father."],[1048,"Indeed Satan, may God curse him, said: The son of Adam will not escape me through one of three things: taking wealth without its right, placing it without its right, or preventing him from its right."],[1049,"The Hour will not be established until two great factions fight one another, their claim being one."],[1050,"Three things I swear by: no wealth is decreased by charity, so give charity; no man forgives an injustice done to him except that God increases him in honor, so forgive and God will honor you; and no man opens a door of begging upon himself except that God opens a door of poverty upon him."],[1051,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I would swear upon three things: no wealth decreases from charity, so give charity; no servant forgives an injustice seeking thereby the face of God except that God raises him in degree on the Day of Resurrection; and no man opens a door of begging upon himself except that God opens a door of poverty upon him."],[1052,"A false oath takes away wealth, or it takes away the wealth."],[1053,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[1054,"The one visiting the sick is in the harvest of Paradise; when he sits with him, mercy overwhelms him."],[1055,"The briber and the bribed are in the Fire."],[1056,"Islam came with dislike and hardship, and we found the best of good in disliked things. We went out with the Prophet ﷺ from Makkah and He gave us in that high rank and victory, and we went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to Badr in the condition that God, Blessed and Exalted, mentioned: 'And indeed, a party of the believers disliked it, disputing with you about the truth after it had become clear, as if they were being driven to death while they looked on. And when God promised you one of the two groups that it would be yours, and you wished that the one without thorns would be yours'—and the thorns are Quraysh. So God, Mighty and Majestic, gave us in that high rank and victory, and we found the best of good in disliked things."],[1057,"I had a promise from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Qurayzah was conquered, I came so he could fulfill what he had promised me. I heard him saying: “Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will enrich him; whoever is content, Allah will make him content.” I said to myself: No doubt, I will not ask him for anything."],[1058,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ prostrate in “When the sky splits open” ten times."],[1059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to look for a man from the Ansar and called him. The Ansari came out with his head dripping water. He said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “I feared I would keep you waiting, so I poured water over myself and then came out.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Did you ejaculate?” He said: “No.” He said: “If you do that, do not perform ghusl, but wash what of you touched the woman and perform wudu as you do for prayer.”"],[1060,"“The Muslim is under Allah’s protection from the day his mother gives birth to him until he stands before Allah, Blessed and Exalted. If he meets Allah with a sincere testimony of la ilaha illa Allah, or with sincere seeking of forgiveness, Allah writes for him a release from the Fire.”"],[1061,"“After me, none will care for you except the truthful, patient ones.” Abd al-Rahman said: So I sold something—he named it—to Abdullah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh for forty thousand and divided it among them, meaning among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, may Allah have mercy on them."],[1062,"Recite the Quran, but do not consume by it, do not hoard it, do not neglect it, and do not go to extremes in it."],[1063,"He used to say in the funeral prayer: “O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our male and our female, our young and our old. Whoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whoever of us You take in death, take him upon faith.”"],[1064,"When he finished his meal, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink. Praise be to Allah who sufficed us and sheltered us. Praise be to Allah who blessed us and bestowed favor upon us. We ask You by Your mercy to protect us from the Fire.”"],[1065,"“I was shown Paradise, and there only the poor will enter it, so I entered with them crawling. When I woke up, I said: My camels that I am waiting for from Syria, and their loads are in the way of Allah, until I enter it with them walking.”"],[1066,"“Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has obligated the fast of Ramadan upon you, and I have made its night prayer a sunnah. Whoever fasts it out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"],[1067,"He complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lice, so he ordered him to wear silk."],[1068,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, he went to al-Ta'if and besieged it for seventeen or nineteen days. Then he stood as a khutba, praised Allah, extolled Him, then said: “I enjoin you to good treatment of my family, and your appointed meeting is the Hawd. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you must establish prayer and pay zakat, or I will send to you a man from me—or like myself—who will strike your necks.” Then he took Ali by the hand and said: “This one.”"],[1069,"Whoever says in a day, when he rises in the morning and when he enters the evening: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is Ever-Living and does not die. In His hand is all good, and He is over all things capable,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."],[1070,"The womb will call out on the Day of Resurrection: 'Whoever maintained me, may Allah maintain him, and whoever severed me, may Allah sever him.'"],[1071,"A protection with which Ibrahim used to seek protection for Ishaq and Ismail (peace be upon them), and I use it to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ: 'Allah hears the caller for the one who calls; beyond Allah there is no target for the one who aims.'"],[1072,"Emigration comprises two qualities: one of them is that you abandon evil deeds, and the other is that you emigrate to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ. Emigration will not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance will continue to be accepted until the sun rises from the west. When it rises, a seal will be placed on every heart according to what it contains, and people will have enough of their deeds."],[1073,"Do not let the bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer, for in the Book of Allah it is al-'Isha', but the bedouins called it al-'Atamah because of their camels and their milking."],[1074,"Umar said: 'How do you deal with the Magians?' Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Treat them according to the practice of the People of the Book.\"'"],[1075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'How did you do concerning touching the two corners?' He said: I said: 'I did all of that: I touched and I left.' So he said: 'You have done right.'"],[1076,"Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, from the Prophet"],[1077,"The thief is not liable for what he stole after the prescribed punishment has been carried out on him."],[1078,"I was a scribe for Jaz' b. Mu'awiyah, reporting from al-Ahnaf b. Qays, when a letter from Umar came to us a month before his death: 'Kill every sorcerer and sorceress, and separate every man among the Magians from his close relative, and forbid them from zamzamah (low murmuring).' So we killed three sorceresses in one day, and we separated every Magian man from his wife in the Book of Allah. He prepared a large amount of food and invited them, then he placed a sword on his thigh. So they ate and did not murmur. They threw down a load of a mule or two mules of silver. Umar had not taken the jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman b. Awf testified that the Prophet ﷺ took it from the Magians of Hajar."],[1079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from this world without him or his family ever having had their fill of barley bread."],[1080,"The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd in everything, until they said: 'He does not know how to pray properly.' He said: Umar sent for him and said: 'They have complained about you in everything, even claiming that you do not know how to pray properly.' Sa'd said: 'By Allah, I used to lead them in prayer in the manner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, without deviating from it. I would pray the two 'Isha' prayers, prolonging the first two rak'ahs and shortening the last two.' Umar said: 'That is what is expected of you, Abu Ishaq.' Then he sent with him a man or two men to ask about him among the people of Kufah. When he arrived, he did not leave any mosque without asking its people, and they would mention good and say what is right, until he came to a mosque of Banu 'Abs. A man from among them, called Abu Sa'dah, stood up and said: 'Since you have adjured us, indeed Sa'd did not march with the raiding party, did not judge equitably, and did not distribute fairly.' Sa'd stood up and said: 'By Allah, I will supplicate against you with supplications: O Allah, if this servant of Yours is lying, then prolong his life, intensify his poverty, and expose him to trials.' Abd al-Malik b. Umayr said: I later saw him as an old man, afflicted. When he was asked, 'How are you this morning?' he would say: 'An old man, poor, and afflicted; the supplication of Sa'd has befallen me.' Sa'd said: I saw him after that as he was accosting slave girls in the streets, pinching them, his eyebrows having fallen over his eyes from old age."],[1081,"Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us from Shu'bah, from Abd al-Malik and Abu Awn, from Jabir b. Samurah, similar to the hadith of Abu Awanah from Abd al-Malik."],[1082,"Mis'ar narrated to us from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, from Jabir b. Samurah, similar to the hadith of Abu Awanah."],[1083,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[1084,"Isra'il narrated to us from Hakim b. Jubayr, from Ali b. al-Husayn, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1085,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom, gathering his parents for me."],[1086,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: You are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."],[1087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejected celibacy for Uthman b. Maz'un; if he had permitted celibacy for him, we would have castrated ourselves."],[1088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejected celibacy for Uthman b. Maz'un; if he had allowed it for him, we would have castrated ourselves."],[1089,"Usamah b. Hafs narrated to us from Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Sa'd."],[1090,"I will give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. He called Ali and gave him the banner."],[1091,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, who am I? He said: You are Sa'd b. Malik b. Wuhaib b. Abd Manaf; whoever says otherwise, upon him be the curse of Allah."],[1092,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[1093,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[1094,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[1095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at al-'Abbas and said: This is the uncle of your Prophet ﷺ, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most compassionate toward them."],[1096,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were playing on his belly. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you love them? He said: And why should I not love them, my two sweet basils?"],[1097,"No one embraced Islam on the day I embraced Islam, meaning not a single one, and I remained for seven nights as a third of Islam."],[1098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ emptied his quiver for me, or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took out arrows from his quiver for me, on the day of Uhud and said: Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom."],[1099,"We used to lease land in return for what grew on the stream banks and the water channels and what the spring irrigated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that and ordered us to lease it for gold or silver."],[1100,"There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hama. If there is any evil omen, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling."],[1101,"He proposed to a woman in Makkah while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Would that I had someone who saw her or someone to tell me about her. A effeminate man called Hit said: I can describe her. When she approaches, you would say she walks on four; when she turns away, I said: she walks on eight. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do I not see that this one knows women. He used to enter upon Sawdah, so he forbade her to let him enter upon her. When he came to Madinah, he banished him, and it remained so until the caliphate of 'Umar. He struggled, so he was permitted to enter Madinah and beg every Friday."],[1102,"The greatest crime of Muslims against Muslims is one who asks about a matter that was not forbidden, and it becomes forbidden because of his asking."],[1103,"I fell ill in Makkah in the year of the conquest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and I have only one daughter. Shall I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity? He said: No. I said: Half? He said: No. I said: A third? He said: A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better for you than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my emigration? He said: If you are left behind after me and you do a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the abode of the Hereafter, you will be rewarded or raised a degree thereby. Perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah, complete the emigration of my companions and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd b. Khawlah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieved for him that he died in Makkah."],[1104,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of geckos and called them little transgressors."],[1105,"He gave to some men and did not give to one man. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave to so-and-so and so-and-so, and you left so-and-so and did not give him, while he is a believer? The Prophet ﷺ said: Or a Muslim. Then he said: I give to some men and leave those who are dearer to me than them, fearing that they may be thrown on their faces into the Fire."],[1106,"A group came and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he gave them and left one man. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave to so-and-so and denied so-and-so while he is a believer. He said: Or a Muslim. Then he said: I give the gift to a man while another is dearer to me than him, fearing that Allah may cast him into the Fire."],[1107,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my father? He said: In the Fire. He said: Then where is your father? He said: Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him the tidings of the Fire."],[1108,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ performing the optional prayer on his mount, wherever it turned with him, but he did not do that for the obligatory prayer."],[1109,"Sa'd b. Mu'adh ruled regarding the Banu Qurayzah that every male among them who had reached puberty should be killed, and that their women and children and property should be divided. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: He has judged among them with the judgment of Allah, which He decreed from above seven heavens."],[1110,"When the funeral of Sa'd b. Mu'adh passed by, the Prophet ﷺ said: The Throne shook for him."],[1111,"Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Amir b. Sa'd, from his father Sa'd."],[1112,"I never heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ testify for anyone that he is among the people of Paradise except for Abdullah b. Salam. He said: A man from the people of Paradise will enter upon you, and Abdullah b. Salam entered."],[1113,"This disease is a punishment or a remnant of a torment with which those before you were punished. If it occurs in a land while you are not there, do not go there; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it."],[1114,"This disease is a punishment and a torment with which those before you were punished. If it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land while you are not there, do not go there."],[1115,"Among the happiness of a servant is his asking his Lord for guidance and his contentment with what He has decreed, and among the misery of a servant is his abandoning the asking for guidance and his displeasure with what Allah has decreed, or after the decree."],[1116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a small amount of whatever intoxicates in a large amount."],[1117,"Al-Walid b. Kathir b. Sinan narrated to us, from al-Dahhak b. Uthman, from Bukayr b. Abd Allah b. al-Ashajj, from Amir b. Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And this hadith we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this route. A group narrated it from al-Dahhak and attributed it to him, among them al-Darawardi, al-Walid b. Kathir, and Muhammad b. Ja'far b. Abi Kathir al-Madani."],[1118,"He would say the salam to his right until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[1119,"When death came to him he said: Make a lahd (niche) for me and set up bricks over me, as was done for the Messenger of Allah."],[1120,"He rode to his palace at al-Aqiq and found a slave cutting a tree, so he took his belongings (or stripped him). When Sa'd returned, the slave's people came asking him to return what he had taken from their slave, but he said: I seek refuge with Allah from returning anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me as spoils, and he refused to return it to them."],[1121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put on two coats of mail one over the other on the day of Uhud."],[1122,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Badr and I had only one hair on my face, then Allah increased my beard afterwards."],[1123,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to find out for him news of a people, so I went, running, until I reached the people. Then I came back, walking at my normal pace, until I reached the Prophet ﷺ. He asked me and I informed him, and he said: You went quickly and then came back at your own pace - or as he said. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I disliked to run lest the people think that I was afraid. The Prophet ﷺ said: Sa'd is indeed experienced."],[1124,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Umayr b. Abi Waqqas and considered him too young when he went out to Badr, then he let him go. Sa'd said: It is said that his sword failed him. Abd Allah said: He was killed on the day of Badr."],[1125,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined: I broke my fast deliberately during Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I am not able. He said: Feed sixty poor people."],[1126,"There was no prophet but he described the Dajjal to his nation, and I will describe him with a description no prophet before me gave: he is one-eyed, blind in the right eye."],[1127,"If the amount of a fingernail of what is in Paradise were to appear to the people of the earth, it would adorn for them all between the extremities of the heavens and the earth. And if a man were to put out his hand and his bracelet appeared, its light would obliterate the light of the sun as the sun obliterates the stars - or the light of the stars."],[1128,"And Abd al-Hamid b. Ja'far narrated from Dawud b. Amir b. Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, and some of Abd al-Hamid's companions said: from Dawud b. Umar b. Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the plague occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it.\" 1129 1110 - Al-Jarrah b. Makhlad narrated it to us, but we left this hadith due to disagreement in it, and we do not know of a son of Umar b. Sa'd called Dawud."],[1129,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded placing the hands and setting upright the feet in prayer."],[1130,"Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad reported to us, from Suhayl b. Abi Salih, from Muslim b. A'idh, from Amir b. Sa'd, from his father."],[1131,"A man came to the prayer while the Prophet ﷺ was leading us in prayer. When he reached the row, he said: 'O Allah, grant me the best of what You grant Your righteous servants.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'Who spoke just now?' The man said: 'I did.' He said: 'Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the path of Allah.'"],[1132,"Indeed Allah is Good and loves goodness, Clean and loves cleanliness, Generous and loves generosity, Magnanimous and loves magnanimity. So clean your courtyards and open spaces, and do not imitate the Jews, who gather refuse in their homes."],[1133,"He used to go out to the Eid prayer walking and return walking by a different route from the one he took going out."],[1134,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer without an adhan or an iqamah, and he used to deliver two sermons while standing, separating them with a sitting."],[1135,"Accept from the good-doers among the Ansar and overlook their wrongdoers."],[1136,"I used to see the sides of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to his right and to his left when he said the salam."],[1137,"Islam began as something strange and will return as it began, so blessed are the strangers."],[1138,"A man said to Sa'd: 'What prevents you from reviling Ali?' He said: 'I will not revile him as long as I remember three things the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him. If he had said even one of them to me, it would be dearer to me than red camels.' A man said to him: 'What are they, O Abu Ishaq?' He said: 'I will not revile him as long as I remember when the revelation descended upon him, and he wrapped him along with his daughter Fatimah and his two sons under his garment, then said: \"O Allah, these are my family and the people of my household.\" And I will not revile him as long as I remember when he left him behind during a military expedition, and Ali said to him: \"You have left me with the women and children.\" He said to him: \"Are you not pleased that you are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophethood after me?\" And I will not revile him as long as I remember the day of Khaybar, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, and Allah will grant victory at his hands.\" The people stretched their necks for it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Where is Ali?\" They said: \"There he is.\" He said: \"Call him.\" They called him, and he spat in his eye, then gave him the banner, and Allah granted victory at his hands.' He said: 'By Allah, that man did not mention him with a single letter until he left Madinah.'"],[1139,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the bed."],[1140,"I and al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam captured al-Walid b. al-Walid on the day of Badr. Hisham b. al-Walid came to ransom him, so I gave him my right, and al-Zubayr took his right from the ransom."],[1141,"Indeed in the Fire there is a rock called Wayl, upon which the appointed overseers climb and descend into it."],[1142,"No one patiently endures the hardship of Madinah except that I will be a witness or intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1143,"We approached with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and prayed two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him. Then he supplicated his Lord for a long time. Then he said: 'I asked my Lord for three things. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drought, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to destroy them by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make their might between them, but He withheld it from me.'"],[1144,"He rode to his palace at al-'Aqiq and found a slave boy cutting a tree, so he confiscated his belongings. When Sa'd returned, the family of the slave came asking him to return what he had taken from their slave boy. He said: 'I seek refuge with Allah from returning anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me as booty,' and he refused to return it to them."],[1145,"When one of you spits, let him conceal his spittle so it does not touch the skin or clothing of a believer and harm him."],[1146,"The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dinar."],[1147,"The believer is expiated."],[1148,"Whoever says when he hears the mu'adhdhin: 'And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion,' his sins will be forgiven."],[1149,"Sa'd said, mentioning the Prophet ﷺ: 'I saw him on the day of the Trench laughing until his molars showed.' He said: I said, 'How?' He said: 'There was a man with a shield, and Sa'd was an archer. He kept saying such and such with the shield, covering his forehead. Sa'd drew an arrow for him, and when he raised his head, he shot him. It did not miss this from him, meaning his forehead, and he fell over, raising his leg. The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars showed.' He said: I said, 'Why did he laugh?' He said: 'At the man's action.'"],[1150,"O Allah, suffice them against whoever overwhelms them with hardship, meaning the people of Madinah. No one intends evil for it except that Allah melts him as salt melts in water."],[1151,"Whoever eats seven dates in the morning of a day, no poison will harm him that day."],[1152,"At al-Nabawah or al-Nabah, he said: 'Soon you will recognize the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by what?' He said: 'By good praise and evil praise.'"],[1153,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ hasten in the valley of Muhassir."],[1154,"I fell ill in Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah that He not turn me back on my heels.' He said: 'Perhaps Allah will raise you—meaning, restore you from your illness—and some people will benefit through you.' I said, 'I want to make a will, and I have only a daughter.' I said, 'Should I bequeath half?' He said, 'Half is a lot.' I said, 'Then a third?' He said, 'A third, and a third is a lot or large—Zakariyya was uncertain.' He said: 'So the people made bequests of a third, and that was permitted.'"],[1155,"Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be made to carry it around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths, and neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed will be accepted from him. And whoever claims descent from other than his father or allegiance to other than his patrons has disbelieved."],[1156,"I marvel at the believer: he is rewarded in every matter. If good befalls him, he praises Allah and is rewarded; and if a calamity befalls him, he praises Allah and is rewarded. So he is rewarded in every matter, even the morsel he lifts to his wife's mouth."],[1157,"The believer is disposed to every trait except treachery and lying."],[1158,"I swore by al-Lat and al-'Uzza, and the covenant was recent. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I swore by al-Lat and al-'Uzza, and the covenant was recent.' He said: 'You have uttered an abominable saying. Spit or blow to your left three times, seek refuge in Allah from Satan, seek Allah's forgiveness, and do not repeat it.'"],[1159,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, from his father."],[1160,"Jarir narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, from his father."],[1161,"'Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd and 'Amr b. Maymun, from Sa'd."],[1162,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the worst age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave or from the punishment of the grave."],[1163,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the saying of Allah—Mighty and Majestic—: 'Those who are heedless of their prayer.' He said: 'They are those who delay it beyond its time.'"],[1164,"You must practice archery, for it is the best or among the best of your pastimes."],[1165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited me when I was ill, so I said: \"Shall I bequeath all of my wealth?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"Half?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"A third?\" He said: \"A third, and a third is a lot.\""],[1166,"From ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, from Muṣʿab b. Saʿd, from Saʿd, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1167,"Four verses were revealed concerning me. I obtained a sword and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have obtained a sword.\" Then this verse was revealed: \"They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war belong to God and the Messenger\" [Q 8:1]. A man prepared food and invited us, and we drank wine until we became intoxicated. The Anṣār and Quraysh boasted to one another, the Anṣār saying: \"We are better,\" and Quraysh saying: \"We are better.\" Then a man among them stood up and struck my nose, and Saʿd's nose was struck. Then this verse was revealed: \"O you who believe, indeed wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it\" [Q 5:90]. He said: My mother said: \"Do you not claim that God commands you to maintain ties of kinship and be dutiful to parents? By God, I will not eat food or drink drink until you disbelieve.\" So she would not eat food or drink drink, and when they wanted to feed her, they would pry open her mouth with a stick and put food and drink into it. Then this verse was revealed: \"And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents; but if they strive to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, then do not obey them\" [Q 29:8]. The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me while I was ill, and I said: \"Shall I bequeath all of my wealth?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"Half?\" He forbade me. I said: \"A third?\" He remained silent, and the people adopted that."],[1168,"The people most severely tested are the prophets, then the next best, then the next best."],[1169,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ granted safety to the people except for four men and two women, and he said: \"Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaʿbah: ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl, ʿAbd Allāh b. Khaṭal, Miqyas b. Ṣubābah, and ʿAbd Allāh b. Saʿd b. Abī Sarḥ.\" As for ʿAbd Allāh b. Khaṭal, he was found clinging to the curtains of the Kaʿbah, and Saʿd and ʿAmmār raced to him; Saʿd beat ʿAmmār and killed him. As for Miqyas b. Ṣubābah, the people caught him in the market and killed him. As for ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl, he set sail on the sea, and they were struck by a storm. The people of the ship said: \"Be sincere, for your deities will not avail you anything.\" ʿIkrimah said: \"If nothing saves me in the sea except sincerity, then nothing other than it will save me on land. O God, I make a covenant with You: if You deliver me from what I am in, I will surely go to Muḥammad and place my hand in his hand.\" He said: So he accepted Islam. He said: As for ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Sarḥ, ʿUthmān interceded for him. When the Messenger of God ﷺ called the people to pledge allegiance, he brought him and stood him before the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, accept the pledge of ʿAbd Allāh.\" He raised his head and looked at him, refusing each time, then accepted his pledge after three times. Then he turned and praised God and extolled Him, and said: \"Was there not among you a rightly guided man who, when he saw me withhold my hand from his pledge, would kill him?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, if only you had signaled to us with your eyes.\" He said: \"It is not proper for a prophet to have a deceitful look.\""],[1170,"Regarding the words of God, blessed and exalted be He: \"Alif Lām Rā. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qurʾān that you might understand. We relate to you the best of stories\" [Q 12:1–3]. He said: The Qurʾān was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he recited it to them for a time. They said: \"O Messenger of God, if only you would tell us stories.\" Then God, mighty and glorious, revealed: \"Alif Lām Rā. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qurʾān that you might understand. We relate to you the best of stories.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, if only you would narrate to us.\" Then God, mighty and glorious, revealed: \"God has sent down the best statement, a Book whose parts resemble each other\" [Q 39:23]. All of that, they were being commanded with the Qurʾān or disciplined with the Qurʾān. Khallād said: And he added to me in it: They said: \"O Messenger of God, if only you would remind us.\" Then God, mighty and glorious, revealed: \"Has the time not come for those who believed that their hearts should become humbly submissive at the remembrance of God\" [Q 57:16]."],[1171,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, which people are most severely tested?\" He said: \"The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A servant is tested according to his religion. If he is firm in his religion, his test is severe; and if his religion is weak, he is tested according to that. Trials do not cease to afflict the servant until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin upon him.\""],[1172,"From al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Musayyab, from ʿĀṣim, from Muṣʿab b. Saʿd, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1173,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a large bowl containing tharīd, and they ate from it, and some remained. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man from the people of Paradise will eat this leftover.\" I had left my brother ʿUmayr at home, so I hoped it would be him, but ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām came and ate it."],[1174,"The best of you is he who learns the Qurʾān and teaches it."],[1175,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday \"Alif Lām Mīm, the revelation\" [Q 32] and \"Has there come upon man\" [Q 76]."],[1176,"I used to think that I had virtue over those behind me—or he used to think that he had virtue over those behind him—until he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"You are only granted victory through your weak ones.\""],[1177,"\"Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?\" A questioner among his companions asked, \"O Messenger of God, how can any of us earn a thousand good deeds?\" He said, \"He should say subhan Allah one hundred times, and a thousand good deeds will be written for him, or a thousand sins will be erased from him.\""],[1178,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Teach me some words to say.\" He said, \"Say: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner; God is the Greatest, greatly; glory be to God, Lord of the worlds; and there is no might nor power except with God, the High, the Great' five times.\" He said, \"These are for my Lord; what is for me?\" He said, \"Say: 'O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, guide me, and grant me well-being.'\""],[1179,"\"Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, knowing who his father is, God has forbidden Paradise to him.\""],[1180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun. Then a bedouin came and distracted him, so I followed him, and he turned to me and said, \"Abu Ishaq.\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What is it?\" I said, \"You mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun, then a bedouin came and distracted you.\" He said, \"Yes, the supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he called out in the belly of the whale: 'There is no god but You; glory be to You; indeed I have been of the wrongdoers.' No one ever supplicates with it except that he is answered.\""],[1181,"I prayed with my father, and I placed my hand like this—Yahya placed his hands between his knees—so my father said, \"We used to do this, but we were commanded to raise them to the knees.\""],[1182,"Israel narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Zubayr b. 'Adi, from Mus'ab, from his father, something similar."],[1183,"\"Whoever harms 'Ali has harmed me.\""],[1184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man seeking a lost animal in the mosque, and he said, \"May you not find it.\""],[1185,"\"I am more fearful for you concerning prosperity than the trial of adversity. You have been tested with the trial of adversity and you were patient, but the world is sweet and green.\""],[1186,"\"Close every small door in the mosque except the small door of 'Ali.\""],[1187,"\"Are you not pleased that you are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?\""],[1188,"\"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days.\""],[1189,"Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[1190,"That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."],[1191,"O Messenger of Allah, should I bequeath all of my wealth? He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Half?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"A third?\" He said, \"A third, and a third is much.\""],[1192,"Whoever desires humiliation for Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."],[1193,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call out on the days of Tashriq: 'Indeed, they are days of eating and drinking.'"],[1194,"It is from a person's happiness to seek the guidance of his Lord and to be content with what He has decreed, and it is from a person's misery to abandon seeking guidance and to be displeased after the decree."],[1195,"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr b. Ubayd Allah, a man from Quraysh, narrated to us from Ismail b. Muhammad b. Sa'd, from his father, from Sa'd, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1196,"Three things are from happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious home, and a comfortable mount.\""],[1197,"Ismail b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet."],[1198,"The month is such and such, and he withheld a finger in the third."],[1199,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'So-and-so of Thaqif was killed, and he had embraced Islam.' He said: 'May Allah distance him, for he used to hate Quraysh.'"],[1200,"Umar b. al-Khattab asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, while some women from Quraysh were with him, raising their voices above his. When Umar asked permission, they hurried to the screen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him permission, and Umar entered while the Messenger of Allah was laughing. Umar said: 'May Allah keep you smiling, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah; what made you laugh?' He said: 'I marveled at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they rushed to the screen.' Umar said: 'You, O Messenger of Allah, are more deserving that they should fear you.' Then Umar said: 'O enemies of your own selves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said: 'Yes, you are harsher and rougher than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, by the One in whose hand is my soul, Satan never encounters you walking on a path except that he takes a path other than yours.'"],[1201,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[1202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the supplication of Dhū al-Nūn. He said: A Bedouin came and distracted him, so he got up. I followed him, and he turned to me and said, \"Abū Isḥāq?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What is it?\" I said, \"You mentioned the supplication of Dhū al-Nūn, then a Bedouin came and distracted you.\" He said, \"Yes, the supplication of Dhū al-Nūn when he called out from inside the whale: 'There is no god but You, glory be to You; indeed I was among the wrongdoers.' Indeed, no Muslim supplicates with it for anything except that it is answered for him.\""],[1203,"Part of happiness is: a righteous wife, a spacious dwelling, and a comfortable mount."],[1204,"Someone came to him and said, \"Your people have besieged this man,\" meaning ʿUthmān, and ʿUthmān was besieged in his house. He said, \"What do you command me? Should I be one who draws the sword? By Allah, I will not do so until I am given a sword that, if I strike a believer with it, it will bounce off him, and if I strike an unbeliever with it, it will kill him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah loves the wealthy, pious, and unassuming person.'\""],[1205,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān—meaning al-Thawrī—from Abū Isḥāq, from al-ʿAyyzār b. Ḥurayth, from ʿUmar b. Saʿd, from his father."],[1206,"I marvel at Allah's decree for the believer: if good befalls him, he praises Allah and is grateful; and if a calamity befalls him, he praises Allah and is patient. Thus the believer is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he lifts to his wife's mouth."],[1207,"You will be martyred by killing, plague, drowning, abdominal disease, and the death of a woman in childbirth: her death in her postpartum period."],[1208,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father\"—I think he said—\"and attributes himself to other than his masters, Paradise is forbidden to him."],[1209,"He had a need from his father, so he went and rehearsed some speech. Then he came to Saʿd and spoke to him with words he had never heard from him before. When he finished, Saʿd said to him, \"Have you finished with your need?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You were never farther from your need than you are from me now, and I have never been more indifferent to you than I am now. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There will be people who eat with their tongues as cattle eat with their tongues.'\""],[1210,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Madinah to Tabūk, he left ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ behind. ʿAlī said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you leave me behind after you when I have never stayed behind from you in any expedition?\" He said, \"O ʿAlī, go back.\" ʿAlī said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the hypocrites will say that you left me behind because you found me burdensome.\" He said, \"O ʿAlī, are you not pleased that you are to me as Hārūn was to Mūsā, except that there is no prophet after me? So go back and act as my deputy over my family and your family.\""],[1211,"Some people were with the Prophet ﷺ when ʿAlī came. When ʿAlī entered, they left. After they left, they blamed one another, and some said to others, \"By Allah, he did not make us leave; let us go back.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"By Allah, I did not bring him in and make you leave; rather Allah brought him in and made you leave.\""],[1212,"If the plague is in a land, do not go down to it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it."],[1213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"It is not lawful for anyone to be junub in this mosque except me and you.\""],[1214,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the road of al-Fur', he would enter ihram when his mount stood up with him; and when he took another road, he would enter ihram when he ascended the height of al-Bayda'."],[1215,"The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and the nights and days will not pass until my Ummah splits into the like of it."],[1216,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali during the expedition of Tabuk: \"Are you not content that you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?\""],[1217,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon a woman, and in front of her were date stones or pebbles with which she was making tasbih. He said: \"Shall I not inform you of what is easier for you than this or better?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Say: 'Subhan Allah' as many as what He created in the heaven, and 'Subhan Allah' as many as what He created in the earth, and 'Subhan Allah' as many as what is between that, and 'Subhan Allah' as He is worthy of it, and 'Allahu Akbar' the like of that, and 'La ilaha illa Allah' the like of that, and 'Alhamdulillah' the like of that, and 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' the like of that.\""],[1218,"\"The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.\""],[1219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took 'Ali by the hand and said: \"Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves? Whoever I am his mawla, then 'Ali is his mawla.\""],[1220,"I fell ill in Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me to visit me. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have not left anyone except a daughter, so shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"Shall I bequeath half?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"Shall I bequeath one-third and leave two-thirds for her?\" He said: \"One-third, and one-third is a lot,\" three times. He placed his hand on my forehead, face, and chest, and wiped my face, chest, and belly, and said: \"Heal Sa'd, and complete his hijrah for him.\" And I have not ceased to imagine that I feel the coolness of his hand on my liver until this hour."],[1221,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking while standing.\""],[1222,"Between my house and my minbar, or my grave and my minbar, is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[1223,"\"Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.\""],[1224,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in Makkah on the day of its conquest eight rak'ahs, lengthening the recitation and the bowing in them.\""],[1225,"\"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ and he found two dates, so he took one date and gave me the other.\""],[1226,"That the Prophet ﷺ had food before him, and he said: \"O Allah, send to this food a servant whom You love and who loves You.\" He said: Then he appeared."],[1227,"\"Whoever recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad, it is as if he has recited a third of the Quran.\""],[1228,"\"A people will come who eat with their tongues as cattle eat with their tongues.\""],[1229,"When the people turned away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the retreat on the day of Uhud, I said: I will remain, and either I will be martyred or I will survive until I meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While I was like that, suddenly there was a man with his face covered, and I did not know who he was. The polytheists came forward towards him, and when I thought that they had overcome him, he filled his hand with pebbles and threw them in their faces. They retreated on their heels, going backwards, until they crossed over and came to the side of the mountain. He did that several times, and I did not know who he was. Al-Miqdad was between me and him. While I was about to ask al-Miqdad about him, al-Miqdad said: \"O Sa'd, this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling you.\" I said: \"Where is he?\" Al-Miqdad pointed to him, and I stood up, and it was as if no harm had touched me. He said: \"Where have you been since today, O Sa'd?\" He seated me in front of him, and I sat and threw arrows, saying: \"O Allah, an arrow with which I strike Your enemy,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying: \"O Allah, answer Sa'd's supplication. O Allah, make his shot accurate. Go on, Sa'd, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" There was no arrow I threw but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, make his shot accurate and answer his supplication. Go on, Sa'd.\" When I finished my quiver, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emptied his quiver for me and handed me an arrow with no fletching, and it was more effective than the others."],[1230,"\"I am the first Arab to shoot an arrow in the cause of Allah. We used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no food to eat except the leaves of the hublah and this samur tree, so that one of us would defecate as a sheep defecates, with no mixture. Then the Banu Asad came to instruct me in the religion. If so, I have failed and my deeds have gone astray.\""],[1231,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, with something similar to it."],[1232,"\"A group of my ummah will continue to be upon the truth, manifest, until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1233,"That he prayed and stood up after two rak'ahs, and the people glorified Allah to alert him, but he continued his prayer and did not sit. Then when he finished, he said: \"Do you think I was going to sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[1234,"The Prophet ﷺ heard me while I was supplicating, and he said: \"O Allah, answer him when he calls upon You.\""],[1235,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never combined both his parents for anyone before me. I saw him saying: 'O Sa'd, shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'\""],[1236,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ performed witr with one rak'ah.\""],[1237,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father, knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."],[1238,"The people of the west will continue to prevail upon the truth until the Day of Resurrection."],[1239,"There will be a tribulation in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking."],[1240,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[1241,"If what amounts to a fingernail in Paradise were to appear to the people of this world, it would adorn for them all that is between the horizons of the heavens. And if a man from the people of Paradise were to extend his hand, the light of his bracelet would obscure the light of the sun, just as the sun obscures the stars."],[1242,"The devil of al-Radha is a camel herder or the son of a camel herder. A man from Bajila called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab will overtake him, as a sign among an unjust people."],[1243,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the polytheists said, \"Look, he draws these close to him and not us.\" And I, Abdullah b. Mas'ud, a man from Hudhayl, and two men whose names I have forgotten were present. This distressed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he spoke to himself about it. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face... up to: Thus We have tried some of them by others."],[1244,"People used to ask about something concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or they would ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while it was lawful. They would keep asking about it until it became forbidden for them."],[1245,"The Muslims will prevail over the Romans, the Muslims will prevail over Persia, and the Muslims will prevail over the Arabian Peninsula."],[1246,"Some people complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the drought (lack of rain), so he commanded them to kneel on their knees and say, 'O Lord, O Lord.' They did so, and they were given rain until they wished it would stop."],[1247,"I heard al-Dahhak b. Qays, in the year Mu'awiya performed Hajj, ask Sa'd about tamattu' in Hajj. He said, 'Umar used to forbid it.' Sa'd said, 'Rather, one better than Umar did it: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1248,"I asked Sa'd about [exchanging] white wheat for barley, and he disliked it. He narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about [exchanging] fresh dates for dry dates, and he said, 'Does it decrease?' They said, 'Yes.' So he forbade it."],[1249,"He is not one of us who does not chant the Quran."],[1250,"Recite the Quran and weep; and if you do not weep, then make yourselves weep."],[1251,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man pointing with two fingers and said: 'One, one.'"],[1252,"I mentioned Banu Najiyah to the Prophet ﷺ , and either the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The eye of what Samah b. Lu'ayy wept,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The attachment that was with Samah has clung,' or the man said it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1253,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Uhud, with a man on his right and a man on his left, wearing white garments. I had not seen them before, nor after."],[1254,"On the day of Uhud, I killed Sa'id b. al-'As and took his sword, which was a valuable sword of his. He said: I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, after my brother 'Umayr had been killed before that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Go and throw it,' meaning into the spoils of war. He said: I returned with what only Allah knows of grief over the killing of my brother and the taking of my spoil. He said: I had hardly gone far when Surat al-Anfal was revealed, and the Prophet ﷺ called me and said: 'Go and take your sword.'"],[1255,"The first commander to be appointed in Islam was 'Abd Allah b. Jahsh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him over us."],[1256,"The women said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are a burden upon our sons, fathers, and husbands. What is lawful for us from their wealth?' He said: 'Fresh food that you eat and give as a gift.'"],[1257,"If a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed again, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled."],[1258,"Whoever intends harm to the people of Madinah, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."],[1259,"He heard a man saying: 'Labbayka dha al-ma'arij (Here I am, O Lord of the Ascending Ways).' He said: 'Indeed He is the Lord of the Ascending Ways, but we did not used to say this with our Prophet.'"],[1260,"And al-Darawardi narrated it from Ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Salama, from 'Amir b. Sa'd, from his father. Ahmad b. al-Walid al-Bazzar narrated it to us, saying: Ya'qub b. Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Ibn 'Ajlan."],[1261,"Narrated to us ʿAbd al-Salām, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from Saʿd, and he said:"],[1262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us: when the ghoul appears to us, or when we see the ghoul, to call the adhān."],[1263,"Ibn ʿUmar from Saʿīd b. Zayd. The beginning of the Musnad of Saʿīd b. Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl. Ibn ʿUmar, from Saʿīd b. Zayd. 1264 1248 – ʿUmar b. ʿAlī and Bishr b. Ādam narrated to us, both said: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥanafī ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, he said: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from Saʿīd b. Zayd."],[1264,"\"Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths.\""],[1265,"\"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye.\""],[1266,"\"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye.\""],[1267,"\"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye.\""],[1268,"\"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye.\""],[1269,"\"O people, praise Allah since He has lifted the tithes from you.\""],[1270,"\"I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women.\""],[1271,"\"Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him, and there is no right for an unjust root.\""],[1272,"\"Whoever takes a handspan of land without his right will be made to wear it as a collar on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths.\""],[1273,"Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath, there is no blessing for him in it. And whoever aligns himself with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah; Allah will accept from him neither sarf nor adl."],[1274,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[1275,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, and whoever wrongfully takes a span of land will be made to wear it around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[1276,"My companions' portion is but killing."],[1277,"My companions' portion is but killing."],[1278,"I entered upon Sa'id b. Zayd, and he said: 'Do you not wonder at this oppressor? He has set up preachers who revile 'Ali.' He said: 'They have done it? Or he has done it? I bear witness that nine are in Paradise.' I said: 'Who are the nine?' He said: 'We were with the Prophet ﷺ on Hira', and it trembled, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Be still, Hira', for upon you are none but a Prophet, a Siddiq, and martyrs.\" I said: 'And who were on Hira'?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Sa'd, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf.' I said: 'Then who is the tenth?' He said: 'Me.'"],[1279,"Indeed, among the gravest of usury is a man's assault upon the honor of his brother."],[1280,"The womb is a branch of the Merciful, so whoever severs it, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him."],[1281,"Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he had with him Zayd b. Harithah, and they invited him to a meal of theirs, but he said: 'O son of my brother, I do not eat from what is slaughtered upon the stone altars.' He said: 'After that day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen eating from what was slaughtered upon the stone altars.'"],[1282,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'My father was as you have seen and as you have heard about; had he lived to see you, he would have believed in you. So ask forgiveness for him.' He said: 'Yes, for he will come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone.'"],[1283,"Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: the Prophet ﷺ is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'd; and the tenth of the Muslims, if I wished I would name him."],[1284,"Al-Hasan b. Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Juhadah, from al-Hurr, from Abd al-Rahman b. al-Akhnas, from Sa'id b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[1285,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he stood up."],[1286,"When the news of the Negus's death came, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Pray for forgiveness for him.'"],[1287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan: 'O Allah, I love him, so love him.'"],[1288,"Ten men of Quraysh are in Paradise: the Prophet ﷺ is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. And the tenth of the Muslims, if I wished I would name him."],[1289,"Whoever deliberately tells a lie against me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1290,"Indeed, lying about me is not like lying about anyone else. Whoever deliberately tells a lie against me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1291,"The neighbor has a right."],[1292,"May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship. I think he said: 'Expel the Jews from the land of the Hijaz.'"],[1293,"Indeed, the best prayer is the morning prayer on Friday in congregation, and I do not think anyone among you attends it except that he is forgiven."],[1294,"He mentioned the Dajjal and said: 'I will describe him with a description no prophet before me has given: there has been no prophet after Noah except that he warned his people about the Dajjal, and I warn you about him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ described him to us and said: 'Perhaps some of those who have seen me or heard my words will live to see him.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how will our hearts be on that day?' He said: 'Like they are today, or better.'"],[1295,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abdullah b. Shaqiq, from Abdullah b. Suraqa, from Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar or close to it."],[1296,"Indeed, the beginning of your religion was prophethood and mercy, then there will be a caliphate and mercy, then it will become kingship and tyranny, in which blood will be shed."],[1297,"Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'laba, from Abu Ubayda, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1298,"\"This affair will continue to prevail until a man from Banu Umayya breaches it.\""],[1299,"I said: O Messenger of God, which of the martyrs is most honored by God? He said: A man who stood before a tyrannical ruler, commanded him to do good and forbade him from evil, and the ruler killed him. It was said: Then which of the people is most severe in punishment? He said: \"A man who killed a prophet or killed a man who commanded him to do good or forbade him from evil.\" Then he recited: \"And they kill the prophets without right and kill those who order justice from among the people, so give them tidings of a painful punishment.\" Then he said: \"O Abu Ubayda, the Children of Israel killed forty-three prophets in a single hour, and one hundred and twelve men from the worshipers of the Children of Israel stood up, commanded good and forbade evil, and they were all killed.\""],[1300,"We visited Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah while he was ill, and at his head was his wife Tuhayfa. We said: How did Abu Ubayda spend the night? She said: He spent the night with reward. He raised his head and said: I did not spend the night with reward. We fell silent. He said: What is the matter with you that you do not ask me? We said: Your words surprised us. He said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The illness of a believer is a remission that removes his sins."],[1301,"My father narrated to me, from Bashshar b. Abi Sayf, from al-Harith b. Ghutayf, from Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1302,"\"Some of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.\""],[1303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to the dwelling of Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib and asked his wife Khawla: \"Where is Hamza? Where is Abu Umara?\" or he said: \"Is Abu Umara there?\" She said: No, and he had..."],[1304,"\"While a man was in his fine garment, looking at his own sides, God caused the earth to swallow him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1305,"I said: O Messenger of God, I have not seen anyone after Abu Bakr, or among the Quraysh who embraced Islam in Makkah on the day of the conquest. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O God, grant the Quraysh understanding in religion, and give them from this day of mine until the end of time a share of bounty, for You have given them a share of punishment."],[1306,"I took Abu Sufyan by the hand and brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves to hear something, so give him something. He said: \"Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, and whoever locks his door is safe.\" Then he stood, and I took him by the hand and seated him by the road. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ began passing by him in groups. He would say: Who are these? I would say: These are Muzayna. He would say: What do I have to do with Muzayna? There was no war between me and them in Jahiliyya or Islam. Then another group would pass, and he would say: Who are these? I would say: These are Juhayna. Until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by among the Muhajirun. When he saw them approaching, he turned to me and said: Your nephew has been given a great kingdom. And he mentioned much speech in this regard."],[1307,"I said: I do not know how long the Messenger of God ﷺ will remain among us, so I said: O Messenger of God, if only you would take a shelter to shade you. He said: I will not cease to be among them, with them treading on my heels and disputing my cloak until God gives me relief from them."],[1308,"I will surely know how long the Messenger of God ﷺ will remain among us."],[1309,"We were transporting stones to the House when Quraysh were building the House. Some men carried stones, two by two, and the women carried the mortar. I and my nephew carried stones, and we would place our garments under the stones so that when people came upon us we could wrap ourselves. He said: While I was walking with Muhammad ﷺ in front of me, wearing nothing, Muhammad ﷺ stepped back and fell flat on his face. I came running, threw down the two stones, and he was looking at something above him. I said, 'What is the matter with you?' He stood up, took his loincloth, and said, 'I was forbidden to walk naked.' I said, 'Keep it secret from the people for fear they would say he is possessed.'"],[1310,"I am Qays, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1311,"I said to my father, 'O father, how did Abu al-Yasar capture you when, if you wished, you could have crushed him in your palm?' He said, 'O my son, do not say that. He met me, and he was greater in my eyes than al-Khandamah.'"],[1312,"'The dreams of men'—I think he said 'of the believer'—'are glad tidings from Allah, a part of forty-six parts of prophethood.' He said: I narrated that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: My father al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib said what Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: 'A part of forty-six parts of prophethood.' Then Ibn Abbas said: Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A part of fifty parts of prophethood.'"],[1313,"'For me to sit from the dawn prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than freeing four slaves from the descendants of Ismail.'"],[1314,"'The Prophet ﷺ came out while Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer, and he recited from where Abu Bakr had reached.'"],[1315,"The Prophet ﷺ was on his gray mule on the day of Hunayn, and I was on one side and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith on the other, holding its bridle. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Abbas, call out to the people, to the companions of the Samurah tree.' Al-Abbas called them, and he was a man with a loud voice. When he called them, they turned like cattle turning to their young. Then the voice rose: 'O company of the Ansar.' Then the call became specific: 'O Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.' Then he said: 'O companions of Surat al-Baqarah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of pebbles and said: 'Now the battle has grown fierce.'"],[1316,"They used to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without having used the siwak. He said: 'You enter upon me with yellow teeth. Use the siwak. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would have made the siwak obligatory at every prayer, just as I made ablution obligatory upon them.'"],[1317,"'Allah has purified this peninsula from polytheism as long as the stars do not mislead them.'"],[1318,"Qays narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except from al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, from the Prophet ﷺ, and we do not know any chain from al-Abbas except this chain."],[1319,"'My Ummah will continue upon the natural disposition as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars become dense.'"],[1320,"Al-Awwam b. Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated to us, from his father, from Umar b. Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from al-Abbas except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Umar b. Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan. More than one narrator reported it from Umar b. Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Abbas, as mursal, and Ibrahim b. Musa reported it from Abbad b. al-Awwam as connected. This was disputed, so al-Awwam b. Abbad was asked about it, and he brought it out from his father's book as Ibrahim b. Musa narrated it as connected."],[1321,"Dawud ﷺ said, \"I ask You by the right of my forefathers Ibrahim, Ishaq, and Ya'qub.\" He said: \"As for Ibrahim, he was thrown into the fire and bore it patiently for My sake, and that was a trial that did not befall you. As for Ishaq, he offered himself for slaughter and bore it patiently for My sake, and that was a trial that did not befall you. As for Ya'qub, Yusuf was lost to him, and that was a trial that did not befall you.\""],[1322,"The one who was to be slaughtered is Ishaq."],[1323,"Amr b. Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Abdullah b. Umayra, from al-Ahnaf b. Qays, from al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah have mercy on him."],[1324,"He claimed that he was sitting in al-Batha' with a group of people, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with them, when a cloud passed over them and they looked at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know the name of this?\" They said: \"Yes, al-sahab (the cloud).\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes, and al-muzn and al-'anan.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"Do you know how much is the distance between the heaven and the earth?\" They said: \"No, by Allah, we do not know.\" He said: \"The distance between them is either one, or two, or seventy-three years, and the heaven that is next to it is likewise,\" until he counted for them seven heavens in this manner. Then he said: \"Above the seventh heaven is a sea, from its top to its bottom is like what is between one heaven and another. Then above that are eight mountain goats, the distance between their hooves and their knees is like what is between one heaven and another, and above their backs is the Throne, the distance between its bottom and its top is like what is between one heaven and another, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is above that.\""],[1325,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless you, have you benefited Abu Talib with anything? For he used to get angry for you and protect you.\" He said: \"Yes, he is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me, he would have been in the lowest pit of the Fire.\""],[1326,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I should say.\" He said: \"Ask Allah for pardon and well-being.\""],[1327,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I want to supplicate to Allah, so teach me a supplication with which I may call upon Him.\" He said: \"Ask Allah for well-being.\""],[1328,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me something with which I may ask my Lord.\" He said: \"O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[1329,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the Quraysh, when they meet each other, they meet each other with cheerful faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with faces we do not recognize.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became very angry, then he said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, faith will not enter a heart until they love you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.\""],[1330,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the Quraysh sat together and mentioned their lineages, and they made your example like a palm tree in a barren patch of land.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created the creation into two halves, and placed me in the better of them. Then He divided them into two groups, and placed me in the better group. Then He created the tribes, and placed me in the best tribe. Then He created the houses, and placed me in the best of their houses. So I am the best of them in person and the best of them in household.\""],[1331,"I saw in a dream as if the earth was being pulled up to the sky with strong ropes. I related that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"That is the death of your nephew.\""],[1332,"He has tasted the flavor of faith who is content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Messenger."],[1333,"A person has been commanded to prostrate on seven bones: his hands, his feet, his knees, and his face."],[1334,"Al-Abbas said to al-Zubayr: \"Is this where the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded you to plant the banner? He only commanded you to plant it at Kada'.\" He said: \"And the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah from its upper side.\""],[1335,"We sat with some people, and they interrupted their conversation. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"What is the matter with people who are conversing, and when a man from the people of my household sits with them, they interrupt their conversation?\""],[1336,"When the skin of a servant shivers from fear of God, his sins fall away from him just as the leaves fall away from a withered tree."],[1337,"The religion will certainly prevail until it crosses the sea, and until the seas are crossed with horses in the path of God. Then there will come a people who recite the Quran, saying: 'Who recites better than us? Who is more knowledgeable than us?'\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned and said: \"Is there any good in those?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"Those are from this nation; those are the fuel of the Fire.\""],[1338,"I was one day in the mosque, and Abu Jahl came and said: 'I have vowed to God that if I see Muhammad, I will step on his neck.' So I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ, entered upon him, and informed him of what Abu Jahl had said. He went out angry until he entered the mosque, and he was in a hurry to enter through the door, but he jumped over the wall. I said: 'This is an evil day.' I hurried, and the Messenger of God ﷺ entered and recited: 'Recite in the name of your Lord who created, created man from a clinging substance. Recite, and your Lord is the most Generous.' When he reached the part concerning Abu Jahl: 'No! Indeed, man transgresses because he sees himself self-sufficient,' a man said to Abu Jahl: 'O Abu al-Hakam, this is Muhammad.' Abu Jahl said: 'Do you not see what I see? The horizon of the sky has been blocked against me.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ reached the end of the surah, he prostrated."],[1339,"Ja'far b. Abi Talib said: 'O Messenger of God, permit me to go to a land where I worship God and fear no one until I die.' He said: 'So he permitted him, and he went to the Negus.' Mu'adh said: 'Ibn 'Awn narrated to me.' He said: 'Umayr b. Ishaq narrated to me.' He said: 'Amr b. al-As narrated to me.' He said: 'When I saw Ja'far and his companions safe in the land of Abyssinia, I said: I will certainly bring down this man and his companions. So I came to the Negus and said: Give permission for Amr b. al-As. He gave me permission, and I entered and said: In our land there is a paternal cousin of this man who claims that people have no god but one. By God, if you do not relieve us of him and his companions, I will never cross this sea to you again, nor will any of my companions. He said: Where is he? I said: He will come with your messenger, for he does not come with me. So he sent a messenger with me, and we found him sitting among his companions. He called him, and he came. When we reached the door, I called: Give permission for Amr b. al-As. And behind me he called: Give permission for the party of God, Mighty and Majestic. The Negus heard his voice, so he gave him permission, and he entered, and I entered. The Negus was on a throne, and Ja'far was sitting before him with his companions around him on cushions. Umayr described the throne. Amr said: When I saw his seat, I came and sat between him and the throne, and I put him behind my back. And I seated one of my companions between every two of his companions. He said: He was silent and we were silent, and he was silent and we were silent, until I said to myself: May this Abyssinian slave be cursed; will he not speak? Then he spoke and said: \"Speak.\" Amr said: That means, \"speak.\" I said: The paternal cousin of this man claims that people have no god but one, and by God, if you do not kill him, I will never cross this sea to you again, nor will any of my companions. He said: O companions of Amr, what do you say? They said: We are with what Amr said. He said: O party of God, speak. He said: Then Ja'far bore witness. Amr said: By God, that was the first day I ever heard the testimony of faith. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. He said: And you, what do you say? I said: I follow his religion. He said: Then he raised his hand and placed it on his forehead, as Ibn 'Awn described, then said: A law like the law of Moses? What does he say about Jesus? Ja'far said: He says: The spirit of God and His word. He said: Then he took something from the ground and did not miss, like this, and said: Were it not for my kingdom, I would follow you. Go, O Amr, for by God, I do not care if you never come to me again, nor anyone of your companions. And go, O party of God, for you are safe. Whoever fights you, I will kill him, and whoever robs you, I will compensate him. And he said to his doorkeeper: Look at this man; do not veil him from me unless I am with my family. If I am with my family, inform him. If he insists that you give him permission, then give him permission. He said: Then one evening I met him in the street, and I looked behind him and saw no one behind him. I took his hand and said: Do you know that I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: He squeezed my hand and said: You are upon this. And we parted. No sooner had I come to my companions than it was as if they had witnessed me and him, and they did not ask me about anything until they seized me and threw me down. They put a cloak over my face and began to squeeze me. I would sometimes get my head out until I slipped away naked, without a shred on me, and they left nothing of mine but took it. I took a woman's head covering from her head and put it over my private parts. She said to me: Like this? And I said: Like this, as if she was amazed at me. He said: And I came to Ja'far and entered his house. When he saw me, he said: What is the matter with you? I said: It is only that I came to my companions, and it was as if they had witnessed me and you, and they did not ask me about anything until they threw a cloak over my face and covered me with it, and they took everything of the world that belonged to me. You see nothing on me except the head covering of an Abyssinian woman that I took from her head. He said: Come with me. When we reached the door of the Negus, he called: Give permission for the party of God. His doorkeeper came and said: He is with his family. He said: Ask permission for me to enter upon him. So he asked permission for him, and he gave him permission. When he entered, he said: Amr has left his religion and followed my religion. The Negus said: No. He said: Yes. So he called his doorkeeper and said: Go to Amr and tell him that this man claims that you have left your religion and followed his religion. I said: Yes. My companions came to me until we stood at the door of the house, and I wrote down everything, even the towel. I did not leave anything that had gone but I took it. If I had wished to take from their wealth, I would have done so. He said: Then afterwards I was among those who came in the ships as Muslims. And we do not know that this hadith is narrated from Ja'far, from the Prophet ﷺ, with this wording except from this route with this chain."],[1340,"News of the departure of the Messenger of God ﷺ reached us, so we went out as emigrants until our ship cast us to the Negus in Abyssinia. We found Ja'far b. Abi Talib and his companions with the Negus. Ja'far said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent us here and commanded us to stay, so we stayed with him until we all arrived.'"],[1341,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to pray in the ship standing as long as he did not fear drowning."],[1342,"When we came to the Negus and wanted to leave him, he gave us mounts, provision, and gifts. Then he said: 'Tell your companion what I have done for you. Here are my messengers with you. I bear witness that there is no god but God and that he is the Messenger of God ﷺ. So tell him to ask forgiveness for me.' Ja'far said: 'We left him, and when we reached al-Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ met me and embraced me, and said: \"I do not know whether I am happier with the conquest of Khaybar or with the arrival of Ja'far.\" Then he sat down, and the messenger of the Negus stood up and said: \"This is Ja'far; ask him what our companion did for him.\" Ja'far said: 'He did such and such for us, gave us mounts and provision, and bore witness that there is no god but God and that you are the Messenger of God, and he said: Tell him to ask forgiveness for me.' He made supplication three times and said: \"O God, forgive the Negus.\" The Muslims said: Amin. Ja'far said: 'I said to the messenger: Go ahead and convey to your companion what you saw from the Prophet.'"],[1343,"n/a Khalid b. Abdullah narrated to us, from Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi."],[1344,"Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ja'far, and he mentioned the story of Ja'far and attributed it."],[1345,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had me riding behind him on a hot day from the days of Makkah. With us was a sheep that we had slaughtered and prepared, and we put it in a traveling bag. Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl met him, and each of them greeted the other with the greeting of the Jahiliyyah. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Zayd—meaning Zayd b. ʿAmr—why do I see your people have turned against you?\" He said, \"By Allah, O Muhammad, that is not because of any fault of mine toward them. But I went out seeking this religion until I came to the Jewish scholars of Khaybar, and I found them worshipping Allah yet associating partners with Him. I said, 'This is not the religion I seek.' Then I went on until I came to the scholars of Syria, and I found them worshipping Allah yet associating partners with Him. I said, 'This is not the religion I seek.' One of their men said, 'You are asking about a religion of which we know no one worshipping Allah by it except an old man in the Jazirah.' So I went out until I came to him. When he saw me, he said, 'Indeed, all those you have seen are in error. From where are you?' I said, 'I am from the people of the House of Allah, from the people of shirk and qaraz.' He said, 'Indeed, the one you seek has appeared in your land. A Prophet has been sent, whose star has risen.' And I have not perceived anything after that, O Muhammad.\" He said: Then he brought the traveling bag near to him, and he said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"A sheep we slaughtered for one of these stone idols.\" He said, \"I would never eat anything slaughtered for other than Allah.\" And they parted. Zayd b. Harithah said: The Prophet ﷺ came to the House with me, and he circumambulated it. At the House there were two idols, one of them of copper, one called Yasaf and the other Naʾilah. The polytheists, when they circumambulated, would wipe themselves on them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not wipe them, for they are filth.\" He said: I said to myself, 'I will certainly wipe them so that I may see what he says.' So I wiped them, and he said, \"O Zayd, were you not forbidden?\" He said: And revelation came down upon the Prophet ﷺ. He said: And Zayd b. ʿAmr died, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"He will be resurrected as a nation alone.\""],[1346,"That the Prophet ﷺ, in the beginning of what was revealed to him, Jibril came to him and taught him ablution. When he finished, he took a handful of water and sprinkled it on his private part."],[1347,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, you made brotherhood between me and Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib."],[1348,"The Prophet ﷺ said to one of his companions, \"Go.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went, and his companions were with him, until they entered between two walls in a long alley. When they reached the house, there was a woman sitting, and there was a large water-skin full of water. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I see a water-skin but I do not see its carrier.\" The woman pointed to a velvet cloth in a corner of the house. They went to the velvet cloth and uncovered it, and beneath it was a human being. He raised his head, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ugly is the face.\" He said, \"O Muhammad, why do you use obscene language against me?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"I have hidden something for you. Tell me what it is.\" The Prophet ﷺ had hidden for him Surah al-Dukhan. He said, \"Al-dukhkh.\" He said, \"Be off with you! What Allah willed has happened.\" Then he left."],[1349,"I came to Madinah to visit a cousin of mine who was married to al-Hasan b. ʿAli. I attended the dawn prayer with him in the Mosque of the Messenger. Ibn al-Zubayr had prepared a wedding feast that morning. A messenger of Ibn al-Zubayr came and said, \"O son of the Messenger of Allah, Ibn al-Zubayr has prepared a feast this morning and sent me to you.\" He did not pay attention to him, but went around the mosque and dispersed the people, calling them. Then he returned to al-Hasan and said, \"O son of the Messenger of Allah, Ibn al-Zubayr has prepared a feast and sent me to you.\" He turned to me and said, \"Has the sun risen?\" It was said, \"No, I think it has not risen.\" He said, \"Praise be to Allah who caused it to rise from its rising place.\" Then he said, \"I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, say: 'Whoever prays the morning prayer then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, Allah will place between him and the Fire a veil.'\" Then he said, \"Arise and answer Ibn al-Zubayr.\" When we reached the door, Ibn al-Zubayr met him at the door and said, \"O son of the Messenger of Allah, you have delayed coming to me today.\" He said, \"Indeed I have responded to you, but I am fasting.\" Then he said, \"Here is a gift.\" Al-Hasan b. ʿAli said, \"I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, say: 'The gift for a fasting visitor is that his beard be perfumed, his clothes be incensed and scented, and the gift for a fasting female visitor is that her head be combed, her clothes be incensed and scented.'\" He said: I said, \"O son of the Messenger of Allah, repeat the hadith to me.\" He said, \"I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, say: 'Whoever persists in coming to the mosque will attain a decisive verse, an awaited mercy, a novel piece of knowledge, a word that increases him in guidance, or turns him away from destruction, or he will abandon sins out of fear or modesty.'\""],[1350,"I said to al-Hasan b. ʿAli: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulled it out and threw it back among the dates. It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you took a date from this boy.\" He said, \"Indeed, we, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us,\" or he said, \"We do not eat charity.\" And he used to say, \"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, for truthfulness is tranquility, and falsehood is doubt.\" And he used to teach us this supplication: \"O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and take charge of me among those You have taken charge of, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree and none decrees against You. Indeed, no one is humiliated whom You befriend. Blessed and exalted are You.\""],[1351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to say in the qunut of the Witr: \"O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take charge of me among those You have taken charge of, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree and none decrees against You. Indeed, no one is humiliated whom You befriend. Blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted.\""],[1352,"I said to al-Hasan: Do you remember anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He brought me into a room, and I took a date from the dates of charity. He said, \"Indeed, it is not lawful for Muhammad, nor for anyone of his family.\""],[1353,"Al-Hasan b. ʿAli delivered a sermon to us and said: \"By Allah, tonight a man has been killed whom the first ones did not outstrip and the last ones will not overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send him on expeditions, with Jibril on his right and Mikaʾil on his left. By Allah, he left neither yellow nor white.\""],[1354,"When ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ was killed, al-Hasan b. ʿAli stood up to deliver a sermon and said: \"By Allah, you have killed tonight a man on the night in which the Quran was sent down, and in which ʿIsa son of Maryam was raised, and in which Yushaʿ b. Nun, the servant of Musa, was killed.\" Sukayn said."],[1355,"Al-Hasan b. ʿAli delivered a sermon to us when his father was struck, wearing a black turban, and said: \"O people, last night a man departed from you whom the first ones did not outstrip and the last ones will not overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send him on missions and give him the banner. When he smelled battle, meaning war, he fought. Jibril fought on his right and Mikaʾil on his left, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory. He has passed on, and he left neither yellow nor white except seven hundred dirhams left over from his stipend, with which he intended to buy a servant for his family. He died on the night in which ʿIsa son of Maryam ﷺ died, and on the night in which Yushaʿ b. Nun, the servant of Musa ﷺ , was taken, and it was the twenty-first of Ramadan.\""],[1356,"The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me."],[1357,"The beggar has a right, even if he comes on a horse."],[1358,"War is deception."],[1359,"When al-Hasan b. Ali died, al-Husayn said to Sa'id b. al-'As, who was the governor of Madinah: 'Step forward. Were it not that it is a sunnah, you would not have been put forward.'"],[1360,"I asked Bilal: 'Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray when he entered the Ka'bah?' He said: 'Between the two pillars.'"],[1361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out walking between Usamah b. Zayd and Bilal until he entered the Ka'bah, and in it there was a piece of wood placed across. When Usamah b. Zayd came out, I asked him: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do?' He said: 'He left one third of the wood on his right and prayed in the remaining third on his left.' I said: 'How many rak'ahs did he pray?' He said: 'I did not ask Bilal.'\""],[1362,"I asked Bilal: 'Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in the House?' He said: 'Between the two columns.'"],[1363,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, and with him were 'Uthman b. Shaybah and Bilal. I pushed through until I reached the door, and I met him as he was coming out. I asked them: 'What did he do?' They said: 'He prayed two rak'ahs between the two columns.'"],[1364,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, he and 'Uthman b. Talhah, Usamah b. Zayd, and Bilal. He said: 'I waited, and he stayed for a long time, then he came out. I was the first of the people to enter after him, and Bilal was at the House. I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray? He said: Between the two front columns.'"],[1365,"Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Bilal, similar to the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah."],[1366,"Sa'id b. Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Bilal, similar to the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Bilal."],[1367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Quba', and the Ansar came to greet him while he was praying. I said to Bilal: 'How did he respond to them while he was praying?' He said: 'He would gesture with his hand like this.'"],[1368,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it."],[1369,"Rawh b. al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Hisham b. Sa'd, from Nafi'."],[1370,"I made the call to prayer on a cold morning, and the people were slow to come to prayer. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with the people, O Bilal?\" He said: I replied, \"The cold has kept them back.\" He said, \"O Allah, remove the cold from them.\" He said: Then I saw them fanning themselves during the Fajr prayer."],[1371,"\"Perform the Fajr prayer when it is well-lit, for that is greater in reward.\""],[1372,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks — I think he said — and the turban.\""],[1373,"Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, meaning Ibn Qudamah, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from al-Bara', from Bilal, from the Prophet."],[1374,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban.\""],[1375,"\"That they slept with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey until the sun rose. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal when they got up, and he gave the call to prayer. Then he prayed two rak'ahs. Then Bilal gave the iqamah, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer after the sun had risen.\""],[1376,"I had some dates, so I sold them in the market for dates of better quality at half the measure of it. Then I brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"I have not seen dates of better quality than these today. Where are these from, O Bilal?\" I told him what I had done. He said, \"Go and return it to its owner, take your dates, and sell them for wheat or barley, then buy with that from these dates.\" So I did that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Dates for dates, like for like; wheat for wheat, like for like; barley for barley, like for like; salt for salt, like for like; gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, weight for weight. Whatever is extra is usury.\""],[1377,"Qatadah, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id; and Abd al-Majid b. Suhayl said, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id."],[1378,"When this verse was revealed: 'Their sides forsake their beds' (32:16), we would sit in the gathering, and some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ would pray after Maghrib until Isha. Then this verse was revealed: 'Their sides forsake their beds.'"],[1379,"\"The mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1380,"The Prophet ﷺ entered while there was a heap of wealth with him, and he said, \"Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[1381,"I had some dates, and I sold them for what was better than them, for half their measure or for part of their measure. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what I had done. He said: 'Go and return it to its owner and take your dates. Dates for dates, like for like.' So I did that."],[1382,"He used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1383,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks, and after him Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ wiped."],[1384,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Bilal."],[1385,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see that, pray the most recent prayer you have prayed.'"],[1386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to repeat the call to prayer in the Fajr prayer."],[1387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to repeat the call to prayer in the Fajr prayer, and not to repeat it in the Maghrib prayer."],[1388,"Do not give the call to prayer until the dawn becomes clear like this, and he extended his hands horizontally."],[1389,"Do not precede me in saying 'Amin'."],[1390,"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-fourth."],[1391,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1392,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1393,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1394,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1395,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ to call him for the dawn prayer, but 'A'ishah detained Bilal until dawn broke, and it became very light. Bilal stood and gave the call to prayer, and he announced the prayer, repeating his call. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out. When he came out to lead the people in prayer, Bilal informed him that 'A'ishah had detained him because of something she asked him about until it became very light, and that he was late in coming out. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I had prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr.\" Bilal said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it has already become morning.\" He said, \"Even if it became morning again and again, I would still pray them and do them well and perfectly.\""],[1396,"Rejoice, for Allah has brought about the payment of the debt. So I praised Allah. He said, \"Do you not see the four kneeling camels?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"They are for you, along with what is on them. On them are clothing and food, which the ruler of Fadak gifted to me. Take them and pay off your debt.\" He said, \"So I unloaded their saddles, then I prayed the morning prayer until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. Then I went out to al-Baqi', put my fingers in my ears, and said, 'Whoever has a debt owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him come forward.' I kept selling and paying until no debt remained owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone, and there remained in my hand two uqiyyahs or one and a half uqiyyah. Then I went to the mosque and found that most of the day had passed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing in the mosque. I greeted him, and he said, 'What happened with what was with you?' I said, 'Allah has taken care of everything that was owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so nothing remains.' He said, 'Is there anything left over?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'See that you relieve me of it, for I will not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it.' No one came to us until evening. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the 'atamah (night prayer), he called me and said, 'What happened with what was with you?' I said, 'It is still with me; no one has come to us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed until morning, and he remained in the mosque until the next day. Then two men came, and I went with them, fed them, and clothed them. When he prayed the 'atamah, he called me and said, 'What happened with what was with you?' I said, 'Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah.' He praised Allah for that, then he went to his wives and greeted each one of them.\" And we do not know of this hadith being reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except through this chain."],[1397,"I was among the people when the concession was revealed regarding wiping with dust when we could not find water. He ordered us, so we struck once for the face, then we struck another time for the hands up to the elbows."],[1398,"A man came to 'Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, and said, \"I became junub and could not find water.\" 'Umar said, \"Do not pray.\" 'Ammar said, \"Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you and I were on a military expedition and became junub and could not find water? As for you, you did not pray, but as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, I mentioned that to him, and he said, 'It would have been enough for you to do this,' and the Prophet ﷺ struck the ground with his hand, then blew on it, and wiped his face and palms with it.\""],[1399,"A man came to 'Umar and asked him about a junub person who cannot find water. He said, \"He should not pray until he finds water.\" 'Ammar said, \"Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent you and me to such-and-such a place, and I became junub and rolled in the dust? I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'It would have been enough for you to do this and this.' Then he placed his hands on the ground and wiped his hands and face with them.\""],[1400,"Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abza, from his father, from 'Ammar, from the Prophet."],[1401,"Al-Hasan b. Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from 'Ammar, and he did not mention 'Azrah."],[1402,"He said regarding tayammum: \"One strike for the face and the palms.\""],[1403,"Qatadah was asked about tayammum during travel, and he said, \"Ibn 'Umar used to say: up to the elbows, and al-Hasan and Ibrahim used to say: up to the elbows.\""],[1404,"\"Up to the elbows.\""],[1405,"‘Ammār b. Yāsir prayed a prayer and made it light, so a man said to him: “You have made it light.” He said: “Did I not complete the bowing and the prostration?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Indeed I supplicated, meaning during it, with supplications—or a supplication—that I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ: O God, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over Your creation, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me. I ask You for fear of You in the unseen and the witnessed, and I ask You for the word of truth in anger and contentment, and I ask You for moderation in poverty and wealth, and I ask You for bliss that never perishes and coolness of eyes that never ceases, and I ask You for contentment after the decree, and I ask You for a pleasant life after death, and I ask You for the look at Your face, and I ask You for yearning to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading trial.”"],[1406,"‘Ammār prayed one day with his companions a prayer and was brief in it, so it was said to him: “O Abū al-Yaqẓān, you have made it light.” He said: “Indeed, despite that I supplicated with supplications I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he stood, I followed him—or a man stood and followed him—and asked him, then came and informed the people.” He said: “O God, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over Your creation, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me. I ask You for fear of You in the unseen and the witnessed, and I ask You for the word of truth in anger and contentment, and I ask You for moderation in poverty and wealth, and I ask You for bliss that never perishes and coolness of eyes that never ceases, and I ask You for contentment after the decree, and I ask You for a pleasant life after death, and I ask You for the pleasure of looking at Your face, and I ask You for yearning to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading trial.”"],[1407,"We were with ‘Ammār, meaning on the day about which there is doubt concerning Ramaḍān, and a roasted sheep was brought. He said: “Eat.” Some of the people withdrew and one said: “I am fasting.” So ‘Ammār said: “Whoever fasts the day about which there is doubt has disobeyed Abū al-Qāsim.”"],[1408,"He used to greet to his right and to his left in the prayer."],[1409,"“Three are part of faith: spending despite straitened means, extending peace to the world, and being fair to oneself.”"],[1410,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came upon me while I was at a well drawing water into my waterskin, and he said: “What are you doing?” I said: “O Messenger of God, I am washing my garment from janābah that affected it.” He said: “O ‘Ammār, a garment is only washed from feces, urine, vomit, and blood.”"],[1411,"“Indeed, a man’s long prayer and short sermon are a sign of his understanding, so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons.”"],[1412,"“There is no man who strikes his slave except that retaliation will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1413,"Ishāq b. Idrīs narrated to us, Qays narrated to us from Ḥabīb b. Abī Thābit, from Maymūn b. Abī Shabīb, from ‘Ammār, with something similar, and he did not raise it."],[1414,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah, Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: “Take Ḥafṣah back, for she fasts much and prays much, and she is your wife in Paradise.”"],[1415,"I came to my family at night from a journey, and my hands had become cracked, so they perfumed me with saffron. Then I went in the morning to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting or welcome me. He said: “Wash this off yourself.” So I went and washed it, then returned to him and greeted him, and he welcomed me. He said: “The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever, nor of one smeared with saffron.”"],[1416,"“We performed tayammum with the Messenger of God ﷺ up to the shoulders and armpits.”"],[1417,"Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh, as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[1418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: \"Amin, Amin, Amin.\" When he descended, he was asked about it, and he said: \"Jibril came to me and said: 'May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven—or may Allah distance him. Say: Amin.' So I said: 'Amin.' And may the nose of a man be rubbed in dust who reaches his parents and they do not admit him to Paradise—or may Allah distance him. Say: Amin.' So I said: 'Amin.' And a man in whose presence you are mentioned, yet he does not send blessings upon you—may Allah distance him. Say: Amin.' So I said: 'Amin.'\""],[1419,"'Ammar b. Yasir delivered a sermon to us, and he was eloquent and concise. We said: 'O Abu al-Yaqzan, you have been eloquent and concise.' He said: 'Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Verily, the length of the prayer and the brevity of the sermon are a sign of a man's understanding. So lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons.\"'"],[1420,"Sa'id b. Bashir narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. Abjar—I think—from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Ammar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[1421,"And he mentioned 'A'ishah and said: 'She is indeed the wife of your Prophet ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[1422,"When 'Ali sent 'Ammar to Kufa, 'Ammar delivered a sermon and said: 'Indeed, I know that she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[1423,"On the day of Siffin, 'Ammar said: 'Today I shall meet the beloved ones, Muhammad and his party. Indeed, I have fought with this banner three times alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and this is the fourth.'"],[1424,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he had with him only five slaves, two women, and Abu Bakr."],[1425,"The likeness of my Ummah is that of rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[1426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not eat from a gift until its giver was put at ease or he ate from it, on account of the sheep that was gifted to him at Khaybar."],[1427,"Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind, and heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness behind."],[1428,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he returned my greeting."],[1429,"That he greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned the greeting while he was praying in the mosque."],[1430,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave 'Ali the kunya Abu Turab, and it became one of the most beloved of his kunyas to him."],[1431,"That 'Ammar b. Yasir, when he heard what people were saying about the marriage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khadijah, would say: 'Ammar said: I am one of the people most knowledgeable about the marriage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to her. I was one of his close friends, and I was a companion and intimate to him in the pre-Islamic era. One day I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we passed by Khadijah's sister while she was sitting on her leather mat. She called me, so I went to her while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped. She said: Does your companion have any need to marry Khadijah? I informed him, and he said: Yes, by my life. I returned to her and told her what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. She said: Come to us tomorrow morning. So we went to them in the morning, and we found that they had slaughtered a cow, dressed Khadijah's father in a fine garment, and set up a dome over him. I spoke to her brother, who spoke to her father, and he was told about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his location, and was asked to marry her to him. So he married her to him. They prepared food from the cow, and we ate from it. Her father slept, then woke up and said: What is this fine garment, this dome, and this food? The daughter who had spoken to 'Ammar said to him: This fine garment was given to you by Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah, your son-in-law, and he gifted you a cow which we slaughtered when you married him to Khadijah. He denied having married her and went out until he came to al-Hijr, and Banu Hashim went out until they came. He said: Where is your companion whom you claim I married to Khadijah? When he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and looked at him, he said: If I married her to him, then it is so; if not, then I have now married her to him."],[1432,"The table spread came down as bread and meat, and they were commanded not to betray, not to store up, and not to hide anything for the next day. But they betrayed, stored up, and hid for the next day, so it was taken up."],[1433,"That 'Ammar prayed two rak'ahs, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith said to him: You made them very light. He said: Did you see me reduce anything from its bowing or its limits? He said: No, but you made them light. He said: I hastened with them to avoid distraction. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man may pray the obligatory prayer, and perhaps he has only a tenth of his prayer, or a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, until he reaches the end of the count."],[1434,"Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from 'Umar b. al-Hakam, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Anama, from 'Ammar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And Ibn Ishaq said in it, from Muhammad b. Ibrahim, from 'Umar b. al-Hakam, from 'Ammar."],[1435,"'Ammar led us in a prayer and made it light, and a man said to him: You made it very light. He said: Did you see me reduce anything from its bowing or its limits? He said: No, but you made it light. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man may pray the prayer, and perhaps he has only a tenth, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, until he reaches the end of the count."],[1436,"The polytheists satirized us, and we complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: Answer them."],[1437,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: The most wretched of the former peoples was the one who hamstrung the she-camel, and the most wretched of the latter peoples is the one who strikes you a blow on this - and he pointed to his head - dyeing this - and he pointed to his beard."],[1438,"Allah has appointed over my grave an angel whom He has given the hearing of all creatures. No one sends blessings upon me until the Day of Resurrection except that he informs me of his name and his father's name: 'So-and-so, son of so-and-so, has sent blessings upon you.'"],[1439,"I heard 'Ammar narrating from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ammar except with this chain."],[1440,"Khadijah has been favored over the women of my community as Maryam was favored over the women of the worlds."],[1441,"He said to him: 'You will be killed by the transgressing group.'"],[1442,"I saw 'Ammar on the Day of the Camel, and with him was a horn which he had attached with urine in it. I said: 'I would like to fight alongside you.' He said: 'Fight under the banner of your people, for the Messenger of God ﷺ used to like a man to fight under the banner of his people.'"],[1443,"He spoke and was brief. It was said to him: 'You have said something; would that you had given us more?' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to shorten sermons.'"],[1444,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a tribe of Qays to teach them the laws of Islam. He said: 'And there was a people as if they were wild camels, their gazes wandering, having no concern except a sheep or a camel. So I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"O 'Ammar, what did you do?\" I related to him the story of the people and told him of their heedlessness. He said: \"O 'Ammar, shall I not tell you of something more astonishing than them? A people who knew what those others were ignorant of, then became heedless like their heedlessness.\""],[1445,"I said to 'Ammar: 'You have a return (to the afterlife)?' He said: 'I will pour it all out, for my beloved...'"],[1446,"\"By God, you are more intense in love for the Messenger of God ﷺ than those who saw him, or than most of those who saw him.\""],[1447,"\"The Hour will not come until every tribe is led by its hypocrites.\""],[1448,"\"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked: about his youth, in what he wore it out; about his life, in what he spent it; about his wealth, from where he acquired it and on what he spent it; and about his knowledge, what he did with it.\""],[1449,"I found Abu Jahl, may God curse him, among the slain of Badr while he still had a spark of life. So I cut off his head and brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'This, by the One besides whom there is no deity, is the head of Abu Jahl.' He said: 'This, by the One besides whom there is no deity, is the head of Abu Jahl?' He said: 'And that was the oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said: 'Yes.' So I placed it before him, and he praised God."],[1450,"He performed ablution for the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the jinn with nabīdh, and he performed ablution, and he said: \"Purifying water.\""],[1451,"I used to greet the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to me, or to us. When we returned from Abyssinia, we greeted him, but he did not respond to us. We said: 'We used to greet you and you would respond to us.' He said: 'God, Blessed and Exalted, brings about in the night and day whatever He wills.'"],[1452,"\"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[1453,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-'Ala' b. Ziyad, from 'Imran b. Husayn, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud."],[1454,"The prophets were presented to me tonight with their followers from their nations. A prophet would pass by with three men from his people, a prophet with a band from his people, a prophet with a small group from his people, and a prophet with no one from his people, until Musa b. 'Imran came to me in a throng of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they amazed me, so I said: 'My Lord, who are these?' He said: 'This is your brother Musa b. 'Imran and those who followed him from the Children of Israel.' I said: 'My Lord, where is my Ummah?' It was said: 'Look to your right.' And there were the hillocks, the hillocks of Makkah, filled with the faces of men. I said: 'My Lord, who are these?' It was said to me: 'Your Ummah.' Then it was said to me: 'Are you pleased?' I said: 'My Lord, I am pleased; my Lord, I am pleased.' Then it was said: 'Look to your left.' And there was the horizon filled with the faces of men. I said: 'My Lord, who are these?' It was said: 'Your Ummah.' Then it was said to me: 'Are you pleased?' I said: 'My Lord, I am pleased; my Lord, I am pleased.' Then it was said to me: 'With these, there are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.' So 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan, a man from Banu Asad b. Khuzaymah, stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'O Allah, make him one of them.' Then another man stood up and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' He said: ''Ukkashah beat you to it.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom! If you are able to be among the seventy, then be so. If you are unable or fall short, then be among the people of the hillocks. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon, for I saw many people gathered there.' Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'I hope that those who follow me from my Ummah will be a quarter of the people of Paradise.' He said: So we said 'Allahu Akbar.' Then he said: 'I hope that they will be a third.' He said: So we said 'Allahu Akbar.' Then he said: 'I hope that you will be half.' So we said 'Allahu Akbar.' Then the Prophet ﷺ recited: 'A multitude from the former generations and a multitude from the later generations.' The Muslims discussed among themselves: 'Who are these? We see them as none other than those who were born in Islam and continued to act upon it until they died upon it.' He said: Their talk reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'It is not so; rather, they are those who do not perform ruqyah, nor cauterize, nor believe in omens, and upon their Lord they rely.' And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, except through this route with this chain."],[1455,"The last man to enter Paradise will walk at times, stumble at times, and be touched by the Fire at times. When he passes beyond it, he will turn to it and say: 'Blessed is the One who saved me from you. Allah has given me something He has not given anyone from the first and the last.' He said: Then Allah will raise up for him a tree, or a tree will be raised up for him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may shade myself under its shade and drink from its water.' He will say: 'O son of Adam, perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask Me for something else.' He said: He will say: 'No, my Lord.' He said: He will say: And He makes him promise not to ask for anything else. He said: And his Lord excuses him, because he sees what he cannot bear to be without. So He brings him near to it, and he shades himself under its shade and drinks from its water. Then a tree better than the first will be raised up for him, and he will say: 'Bring me near to this tree so that I may drink from its water and shade myself under its shade; I will not ask You for anything else.' He will say: 'O son of Adam, did you not promise Me not to ask Me for anything else?' And his Lord excuses him, because he sees what he cannot bear to be without. He will say: 'Perhaps if I bring you near to it, you will ask Me for something else.' He will say: 'No, this one, this one.' So He brings him near to it, and he shades himself under its shade and drinks from its water. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two, will be raised up for him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may shade myself under its shade and drink from its water; I will not ask You for anything else.' He will say: 'O son of Adam, did you not promise Me not to ask Me for anything else?' He will say: 'Yes, this one; I will not ask You for anything else.' And his Lord excuses him, because he sees what he cannot bear to be without. So He brings him near to it. When he draws near to it, he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and says: 'O my Lord, admit me into it.' He will say: 'O son of Adam, what will satisfy you from Me? If I gave you the world and the like of it with it.' He will say: 'O my Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of the worlds?' 'Abdullah laughed and said: 'Will you not ask me why I laughed?' They said: 'Why did you laugh?' He said: 'This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, and he said: \"Will you not ask me why I laughed?\" They said: \"Why did you laugh?\" He said: \"From the laughter of the Lord of the worlds when he said: 'Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of the worlds?' He said: 'I do not mock you, but I am able to do whatever I will.'\"' And we do not know of Anas b. Malik narrating from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, except this hadith."],[1456,"There were only four years between their embracing Islam and the revelation of this verse by which Allah admonished them: 'And be not like those who were given the Scripture before, and the term was prolonged for them.'"],[1457,"I was in my house in Kufah when I heard at the door of the house: 'Peace be upon you, may I enter?' I said: 'And upon you be peace, enter.' When he entered, it was 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud. I said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what hour of visiting is this?' That was during midday. He said: 'The day grew long for me, and I remembered someone to converse with.' He began to narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I narrated to him. Then he began to narrate to me, saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be a tribulation in which the one sleeping is better than the one lying down, and the one lying down is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one running. All of its slain will be in the Fire.\" He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when is that time?' He said: 'That is the days of al-harj.' I said: 'What are the days of al-harj?' He said: 'When a man does not trust his companion.' I said: 'What do you command me to do if I live to see that time?' He said: 'Stay in your house.' I said: 'What if my house is entered upon me?' He said: 'Then enter your mosque, and put your hand like this' – and he grasped his right hand on his wrist – 'and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"until you are killed upon that.\"'"],[1458,"The Prophet ﷺ asked 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud to recite Surah al-Nisa' to him, so he recited. Al-Mas'udi said: Ja'far b. 'Amr b. Hurayth narrated to me from his father, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, who said: When I reached 'So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?' the one next to me nudged me, and I saw that the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had filled with tears, so I stopped reciting."],[1459,"The closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection will be those of you who send the most blessings upon me in this world."],[1460,"The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb. When the drop of semen settles in the womb, an angel descends to it. When Allah decrees the creation of what is in her womb, the angel says: 'O my Lord, male or female?' And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: 'O my Lord, what is his provision?' And Allah decrees to the angel, and the angel writes. Then he says: 'O my Lord, wretched or blessed?' And Allah decrees to the angel, and the angel writes."],[1461,"He used to mention the Tashahhud from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet."],[1462,"The sun eclipsed during the time of 'Uthman, so he prayed two rak'ahs and two prostrations with the people, in each rak'ah. Then 'Uthman departed and entered his house, and Ibn Mas'ud sat by the chamber of 'A'ishah, and we sat with him. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to pray when the sun or moon eclipsed, and he said: \"If you see that it has been afflicted\" – I think he said – \"then hasten to prayer, for if it is what you fear, otherwise you will have attained good or earned it.\"'"],[1463,"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down for it a cure. So upon you is the milk of cows, for they graze on every kind of tree."],[1464,"Al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Thawri from Qays b. Muslim."],[1465,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down for it a cure."],[1466,"No doer of good—whether Muslim or disbeliever—does good except that he is rewarded. We said: O Messenger of Allah, this reward of the believer we have known; what is the reward of the disbeliever? He said: If he gives charity, maintains family ties, or does a good deed, Allah rewards him, and his reward is wealth and children in this world, and a punishment less than the punishment—meaning in the Hereafter—and he recited: “Cause the people of Pharaoh to enter the severest punishment.”"],[1467,"I witnessed from al-Miqdad a scene that, if I were its protagonist, would be dearer to me than the earth full of anything. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he became angry, his cheeks reddened. He came while he was in that state and said: O Messenger of Allah, we will not say to you as the Children of Israel said to Moses: “Go, you and your Lord, and fight; indeed, we are sitting here.” But, by the One who sent you with the truth, we will be before you, behind you, on your right, and on your left."],[1468,"I witnessed from al-Miqdad."],[1469,"There will be in my nation a sinking, a metamorphosis, and a pummeling."],[1470,"Whoever is struck by poverty and brings it before the people, they will not satisfy his poverty; but if he brings it before Allah, Allah is about to satisfy his poverty."],[1471,"Among the signs of the Hour’s approach: greeting only by acquaintance, and a man passing through the mosque without praying in it."],[1472,"The deeds of the children of Adam are presented every Monday and every Thursday. Then He has mercy on those who show mercy, forgives those who seek forgiveness, and leaves the people of hatred with their rancor."],[1473,"A time will come upon you when you will envy a man for his light provisions, just as you envy him today for abundant wealth and children, until one of you passes by his brother’s grave and rolls about as an animal rolls about, saying: Would that I were in your place—not out of love for Allah or because of a righteous deed he sent forth, but because of the affliction that has befallen him."],[1474,"A woman is not married in the presence of her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt, and a woman does not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her own plate."],[1475,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the campaign of Hunayn. He wanted to relieve himself, and whenever he wanted that, he would go far away so that no one could see him. He said: “Look—do you see anything?” I looked and saw a single palm tree, and I told him. He said: “Look—do you see anything?” I looked and saw another palm tree far from its companion, and I told him. He said to me: “Tell them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to come together.” I told them that, and they came together. Then he came to them and screened himself with them, then stood up. When he had finished his need, each one of them went back to its place. Then the people were struck by severe thirst in that campaign. He said to Abdullah: “Seek for me”—meaning water. I brought him leftover water I had found in a water skin. He took it and poured it into a small vessel, then placed his hand in it and said “Bismillah.” The water began to flow from between his fingers, and the people drank and performed ablution as much as they wished. Abdullah said: I knew it was a blessing, so I began to drink from it and drink more, seeking its blessing. Then the Prophet ﷺ returned from the direction of Madinah, and a camel met him with tears in its eyes. He said: “Whose camel is this?” They said: “It belongs to Banu So-and-so.” He said: “It has sought refuge with me.” He said: They intended to slaughter it; they had worked it until it grew old and had sores on its back. He said: “Do not slaughter it; be kind to it. What an evil recompense you have given it.”"],[1476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it. I said: And the one who writes it and its two witnesses? He said: We only narrate what we have heard."],[1477,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zhuhr with five [rak'ahs]. It was said to him, 'Has something been added to the prayer?' He said, 'And what is that?' He said, 'You prayed five.' So he bent his leg and prostrated twice."],[1478,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[1479,"May Allah curse the women who tattoo and those who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck [eyebrows], and the women who file their teeth for beauty, altering Allah's creation. He said: This reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub. She came to him and said, 'What is this hadith that has reached me from you?' She mentioned it to him. He said, 'Should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah?'"],[1480,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the women who tattoo and those who have themselves tattooed."],[1481,"May Allah curse the women who tattoo and those who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck [eyebrows], and the women who file their teeth for beauty, altering Allah's creation. This reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub, who used to recite the Qur'an. She came to him and said, 'What is this hadith that has reached me from you, that you cursed the women who tattoo and those who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck [eyebrows], and the women who file their teeth for beauty, altering Allah's creation?' 'Abdullah said, 'And why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?' The woman said, 'I have read what is between the two covers of the mushaf, and I did not find that in it.' He said, 'And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it; and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it.' The woman said, 'The first instance of this is upon your wife.' He said, 'Go and look.' The woman entered and did not see anything. She came back to him and said, 'I did not see anything.' He said, 'But if it were that...' and he mentioned a word."],[1482,"Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet."],[1483,"When any of you doubts in prayer, let him strive to ascertain the correct [course], then let him prostrate for forgetfulness twice."],[1484,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the story of forgetfulness with wording similar to these expressions."],[1485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer and added to it or omitted from it. When he said the salam, it was said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, has something occurred in the prayer?' He said, 'No, and what is that?' They said, 'You prayed such and such.' So he bent his leg, faced the qiblah, prostrated twice, then said the salam. When he said the salam, he turned his face toward us and said, 'If something had occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you of it. But I am only a human being; I forget as you forget. So when I forget, remind me. And when any of you doubts in prayer, let him strive to ascertain what is correct, complete upon that, then say the salam, then prostrate twice.'"],[1486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us, and when he said the salam, he turned his face toward us."],[1487,"Rawh b. al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Jarir."],[1488,"O company of young men, whoever among you has the means, let him marry; otherwise, let him fast, for it is a means of curbing desire."],[1489,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when a snake came out, so we rushed towards it, but it outran us and entered a hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It has been protected from your evil, just as you have been protected from its evil.'"],[1490,"We used to count signs as a blessing, while you count them as a warning. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when water became scarce. He said: 'Search.' I said: 'Is there any water?' A vessel with a little water was brought, so he placed his hand in the vessel and said: 'Come to the blessed purification, and blessing is from Allah.' I saw water springing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we drank our fill. And we used to hear the food glorifying while it was being eaten."],[1491,"The two of them entered upon 'Abdullah, and he said: 'Have these prayed?' They said: 'Yes.' So he stood between them and placed one of them on his right and the other on his left. Then we bowed and placed our hands on our knees, and he struck our hands, then he placed his hands together and put them between his thighs. When he finished praying, he said: 'This is how the Messenger of Allah did.'"],[1492,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar at Mina two rak'ahs."],[1493,"When he ascended the pulpit, he faced us with his face."],[1494,"The Prophet ﷺ took in advance the zakat of al-'Abbas for two years."],[1495,"He was sitting among some people when al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by. He said: 'Bring me my two sons so that I may seek refuge for them with what Ibrahim sought refuge for his sons Isma'il and Ishaq: I seek refuge for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and poisonous creature, and from every evil eye.'"],[1496,"He prayed Zuhr with five (rak'ahs). It was said: 'Has something been added to the prayer?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' So he prostrated twice after having said the salam."],[1497,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five (rak'ahs). It was said to him: 'Has something been added to the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' So he bent his leg and prostrated twice."],[1498,"Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from al-Haytham al-Sayrafi, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to the hadith of Yahya b. Sa'id. The hadith of Shu'bah from al-Hakam has been narrated by more than one from Shu'bah, and the hadith of Haytham al-Sayrafi from al-Hakam we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Abu Bakr al-Nahshali."],[1499,"Indeed in prayer there is preoccupation."],[1500,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1501,"\"O assembly of young men, whoever among you has the means, let him marry; otherwise, let him fast, for it is a shield for him.\""],[1502,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and with him were his companions when a naked woman approached. A man from the people stood up to her, threw a garment over her, and embraced her. The face of the Messenger of God ﷺ changed. Some of his companions said, \"I think she is his wife.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I think she is jealous. God, Blessed and Exalted, has prescribed jealousy upon women and jihad upon men. Whoever among them is patient will have the reward of a martyr.\""],[1503,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned some young men of Banu Hashim and his eyes welled with tears. He mentioned the black banners and said, \"Whoever reaches them, let him come to them, even if crawling over snow.\""],[1504,"A man from the polytheists said to Abdullah, \"I think your companion has taught you everything, even how to relieve yourselves.\" He said, \"If you are mocking, then he taught us not to face the qiblah with our private parts, and I think he said: not to clean ourselves with our right hands, not to clean ourselves with dung, not to clean ourselves with bones, and not to clean ourselves with fewer than three stones.\""],[1505,"When the verse, 'Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing' was revealed, that was hard on the people, and they said, \"Which of us does not wrong himself?\" He said, \"It is not what you mean. Have you not heard what the righteous servant said: 'O my son, do not associate partners with God. Indeed, association is a great wrongdoing'?\""],[1506,"When this verse was revealed: 'Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing,' that was hard on the people, and they said, \"Which of us does not wrong himself?\" He said, \"It is not what you mean. Have you not heard what the righteous servant said: 'O my son, do not associate partners with God. Indeed, association is a great wrongdoing'?\""],[1507,"Muhammad b. Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Shu'bah narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."],[1508,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Abu al-Qasim, has it reached you that God, Blessed and Exalted, will carry the creation on a finger, the heavens on a finger, the earths on a finger, the trees on a finger, and the soil on a finger?\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, and he recited, 'They have not appraised God with true appraisal.'\""],[1509,"Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Thus al-A'mash narrated it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, and al-Thawri narrated it from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah."],[1510,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah, and Yahya said, \"Fudayl b. Iyad added, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah: The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed in amazement and affirmation.\""],[1511,"I was in Homs, and the people said to me, \"Recite to us,\" so I recited Surah Yusuf to them. A man from the people said, \"By God, it was not revealed like this.\" I said, \"Woe to you, by God, I recited it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said to me, 'You have done well.'\" While I was speaking to him, I smelled the odor of wine from him. I said, \"Do you drink wine and deny the Book? I will not leave until I flog you.\" So he flogged him the prescribed punishment."],[1512,"I recited it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, \"You have done well.\""],[1513,"One night on the eve of Friday, I was in the mosque when a man from the Ansar came and said: 'If a man finds another man with his wife, and he speaks [about it], you would flog him; or if he kills, you would kill him; and if he remains silent, he remains silent upon rage. By Allah, I will ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' When the next day came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, saying: 'If a man finds another man with his wife, and he speaks, you would flog him; if he kills, you would kill him; and if he remains silent, he remains silent upon rage. O Allah, open [a way].' He kept supplicating, and then the verse of li'an was revealed: 'And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves...' the verse. He said: 'That man was tested with it among the people.' He said: 'He came with his wife to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they performed li'an. The man testified four testimonies by Allah that he was indeed among the truthful, then invoked the curse the fifth time, that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was among the liars.' He said: 'She went to invoke the curse, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If she brings forth a black, curly-haired child, then it is for such and such.\" And she brought forth a black, curly-haired child.'"],[1514,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqama, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, except through this chain."],[1515,"I was walking with 'Abdullah when 'Uthman b. 'Affan met him and spoke with him. 'Uthman said to him: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, will you not marry, or shall I marry you to a young girl who will remind you of what has passed of your time?' 'Abdullah said: 'Since you have said that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed said to us: \"O company of young men, whoever among you is able to marry should marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze. And whoever is not able should fast, for it will be a shield for him.\"'"],[1516,"\"O company of young men, whoever among you has the means should marry, and whoever does not should fast, for it will be a shield for him.\""],[1517,"\"The Prophet ﷺ performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speaking.\""],[1518,"Khabbab b. al-Aratt entered while we were around 'Abdullah. He said to 'Abdullah: 'Does everyone of these recite what you recite?' He said: 'If you wish, I will order some of them to recite to you.' He said: 'Then he said to 'Alqama: \"Recite.\" Y azid b. Murra said: \"He recites, but he is not the best reciter among us.\" 'Abdullah said: \"If you wish, I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about your people and his people.\" He said: 'I then recited fifty verses from Surat Maryam to him, and he said: \"I do not recite anything except that he recites it, or he recites according to it.\"'"],[1519,"We used to greet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to us while in prayer. But when we returned from being with the Negus, we greeted him and he did not respond to us. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you and you would respond to us.' He said: 'Indeed, in prayer there is enough occupation.'"],[1520,"Shuja' b. al-Walid narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqama, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it."],[1521,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqama, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to the hadith of Ibn Fudayl from al-A'mash."],[1522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to recite Surat al-Nisa' while he was on the pulpit. I recited until I reached: 'So how [will it be] when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you, [O Muhammad], against these [people] as a witness?' He said: 'His eyes welled up with tears, and he said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Quran fresh, as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\"'"],[1523,"\"No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith.\""],[1524,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the Jews said: 'Were not your brothers who died drinking it?' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'There is no sin upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It was said to me: 'You are among them.'\""],[1525,"When this verse was revealed: “There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten” (5:93), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It was said to me: ‘You are one of them.’”"],[1526,"‘Āṣim b. ‘Alī narrated to us, from Qays, from al-A‘mash, from Ibrāhīm, from ‘Alqamah, from ‘Abd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1527,"An earthquake occurred during the time of ‘Abd Allāh, so ‘Abd Allāh said: “We used to consider signs along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as blessings, but you consider them as intimidation.”"],[1528,"Sa‘d used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr, fighting as both a horseman and a foot soldier."],[1529,"Abū Mu‘āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A‘mash, from Ibrāhīm, from ‘Abd Allāh, similarly, but he did not say “from ‘Alqamah.”"],[1530,"That he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was feverish, or he said: “suffering from fever,” and he said: “O Messenger of Allah, how severe is the fever from which you are suffering!” He replied: “I suffer fever as would two men among you.”"],[1531,"He used to sleep while in prostration, then stand up and continue with his prayer."],[1532,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when “By those sent forth in succession” (77:1) was revealed to him, and I received it from his mouth while it was still moist. Then a snake came out toward us, and we rushed toward it, but it entered a hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It has been protected from your evil just as you have been protected from its evil.”"],[1533,"Cursed are the women who tattoo, those who have their teeth filed for beauty, and those who pluck their eyebrows, changing the creation of Allah. A woman said something to him, which he mentioned, and ‘Abd Allāh said: “The Messenger of Allah said it.”"],[1534,"The believer is not one who slanders, curses, speaks obscenely, or is foul-mouthed."],[1535,"The nearest a servant is to Allah is while he is prostrating."],[1536,"I went out with ‘Abd Allāh on Friday. He entered the mosque and found three people who had arrived before him. He said: “The fourth of four, and what is the fourth of four? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘They sit according to the order of their coming to Friday prayer: the first, then the second, then the third, then the fourth.’”"],[1537,"\"Take the Qur'an from four: from Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah.\""],[1538,"\"The Prophet ﷺ invoked li'an for pregnancy.\""],[1539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us istikharah: \"O Allah, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your power through Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty and mercy, for they are in Your hand, no one else possesses them. You know and I do not know, and You have power and I have no power, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter is for the matter You intend as good for me in my religion and in my worldly life — I think he said: and the outcome of my affair — then make it possible and easy for me, and if other than that is better, then guide me to the good — I think he said: wherever it may be.\""],[1540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a palm grove, leaning — I think he said: on a palm stalk — when a Jew approached him and asked him about the spirit. He began to nod his head, and I thought that revelation was coming to him. Then he said: \"They ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.\""],[1541,"\"The death of a believer is with a sweaty forehead.\""],[1542,"\"Whatever was revealed beginning with 'O mankind' is in Makkah, and whatever was revealed beginning with 'O you who believe' is in Madinah.\""],[1543,"He was asked about the major sins, and he said: \"What is between the beginning of Surat al-Nisa' and the first thirty verses.\""],[1544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down on a straw mat, and it left marks on his side. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you ordered us, we would make a bed for you to protect you from the mat. He said: \"What do I have to do with this world? What am I and this world? My example and that of this world is like a rider who sought shade under a tree, then departed and left it.\""],[1545,"The two sons of Mulaykah al-Ju'fi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Our mother used to honor her husband and show affection to her children — and they mentioned affection — except that she buried an infant alive in the Jahiliyyah. He said: \"Your mother is in the Fire.\" They turned away with evil visible in their faces. Then he ordered them to be brought back, and joy could be seen in their faces. He said: \"My mother is with your mother.\" A man from the hypocrites said: This does not benefit his father or his parents at all, while we are treading on his heels. A man from the Ansar said: I have not seen anyone who asked more questions — I think he said: O Messenger of Allah, has your Lord promised you regarding her or them? He thought it was something he had heard. He said: \"I did not ask my Lord, nor did He make me covet, but I will stand at the Praised Station on the Day of Resurrection.\" The man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Praised Station? He said: \"That is when you are brought naked\" — I think he said: \"barefoot. The first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah. He will say: Clothe him, and he will be clothed with two white garments, which he will put on. Then he will stand facing the Throne. Then my clothing will be brought, and I will put it on, and I will stand to his right in a position no one but me will stand, for which the first and the last will envy me.\" He said: \"And a river from al-Kawthar will be opened to the Basin.\" The hypocrite said: Water rarely flows except over pebbles or smooth stones. He said: O Messenger of Allah, over pebbles or smooth stones? He said: \"Its pebbles are musk, and its smooth stones are pearls.\" The hypocrite said: I have not heard the like of today, for water rarely flows over pebbles or smooth stones without having vegetation. The Ansari said: Does it have vegetation? He said: \"Yes, stalks of gold.\" The hypocrite said: I have not heard the like of today, for a stalk rarely grows without bearing leaves and fruit. The Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have fruit? He said: \"Yes, colors of jewels, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst again, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched.\""],[1546,"\"Whoever wishes, I will make a pact with him or we will invoke li'an: 'And those who are pregnant, their term is that they give birth' was revealed after the verse of the deceased. So when the woman whose husband has died gives birth, she becomes lawful. And he recited: 'And those of you who die and leave wives behind...' to the end of the verse.\""],[1547,"He used to give salutation to his right and to his left."],[1548,"Uthman b. Farqad narrated to us, from 'Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abd Allah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know that 'Ubaydah narrated from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abd Allah except this hadith."],[1549,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah or al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah."],[1550,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I met a woman on one of the roads of Madinah, and I did everything with her except sexual intercourse.' He said: Then the verse was revealed: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds} (Qur'an 11:114). They said: 'O Messenger of God, is this for him specifically or for the people in general?' He said: 'Rather, for the people in general.'"],[1551,"\"Which charity is best?\" They said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"For a man to give his brother dirhams, or the use of a riding animal's back.\""],[1552,"\"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina when the moon split.\""],[1553,"The mother of 'Abdullah and the wife of 'Abdullah went to the Prophet ﷺ, each of them concealing her matter from her companion. They came to the room and said to Bilal: 'Go to the Prophet ﷺ and say: Two women, one of whom has surplus wealth and in her care are orphaned sons of her brother, and the other said: I have surplus wealth and a husband who is light-handed.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: 'Two shares, two shares.'"],[1554,"The Prophet ﷺ asked me to recite Surat al-Nisa', so I recited until I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?} (Qur'an 4:41). His eyes filled with tears, and he said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.'"],[1555,"\"Let those of you who are mature and wise stand nearest to me, then those next to them.\" And he forbade the clamor of the marketplaces."],[1556,"\"I was not with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the jinn, and I wish I had been with him.\""],[1557,"\"The believer's death is with sweat on the brow.\""],[1558,"\"The believer's death is with sweat on the brow.\""],[1559,"Husam b. Misakk narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1560,"He would fast while traveling and break the fast."],[1561,"A group of Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, if you are a prophet as you claim, tell us from where resemblance comes, such that a man sometimes resembles his paternal uncles and sometimes his maternal uncles.\" He said: \"The man's fluid is white and thick, and the woman's fluid is yellow and thin; whichever of them prevails, the resemblance follows it.\""],[1562,"\"The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then he becomes a clinging clot for the like of that—I think he said—then he becomes a lump of flesh for the like of that. Then Allah sends the angel to him, and he is commanded with four words, and it is said: 'Write his term, his deeds, his provision, and whether he is wretched or blessed.' One of you may do the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is but a cubit between him and it, then the writing overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is but a cubit between him and it, then the writing overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise—I think he said—and he enters it.\""],[1563,"He would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity and lead us in prayer while his head was dripping, then he would fast that day."],[1564,"\"A beautiful voice is an adornment for the Qur'an.\""],[1565,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see that, hasten to prayer, or pray.\""],[1566,"He used to teach them the tashahhud: \"All greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\""],[1567,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, some youths from Banu Hashim passed by, and his eyes brimmed with tears. We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing something in your face that we dislike.\" He said: \"We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and the people of my household will face after me dispossession and expulsion in the lands until Allah raises a people from here\"—and he gestured with his hand toward the east—\"who will ask for the truth and not be given it, then ask for the truth and not be given it three times, then they will fight and prevail until they hand it over to a man who will fill it with justice just as it was filled with oppression. Whoever of you lives to see that, let him go to him even if crawling over snow.\""],[1568,"Ali b. Salih narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. This hadith was narrated by more than one from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, and we do not know that Yazid b. Abi Ziyad narrated from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."],[1569,"While Abdullah was in his house, he said: \"Have these people prayed?\" We said: \"No.\" He said: \"Stand and pray.\" He did not order us to give the call to prayer or the iqamah. He said: We went to stand behind him, but he took our hands and positioned us, placing one of us on his right and the other on his left. He said: When he bowed, we placed our hands on our knees, but he struck our hands, and placed his palms together between his thighs. When he finished praying, he said: \"There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer from its appointed time until the time when the dead are on the verge of death. When you see them do that, pray the prayer at its appointed time, then make your prayer with them a supererogatory one. If you are three, pray together; if you are more than that, let the eldest of you lead. When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms and thighs, then place his palms together.\" It was as if I could see the interlocking of the Messenger of Allah's fingers."],[1570,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs. It was said to him: \"Has something been added to the prayer?\" He said: \"And what is that?\" They said: \"You prayed five.\" So he folded his leg and prostrated twice."],[1571,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. This hadith from al-Mughirah we do not know anyone narrated except Shu'bah, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Shu'bah except al-Nadr and Muhammad b. Bakr. As for the hadith of al-Hakam, more than one narrated it from Shu'bah, and others besides Shu'bah also narrated it."],[1572,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba. I said: \"And its writer and its two witnesses?\" He said: \"We only narrate what we have heard.\""],[1573,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave when Surat al-Mursalat descended upon him, and a snake came out. We hurried toward it, but it entered a hole. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have been protected from its evil just as it has been protected from your evil.\""],[1574,"A camel and a cow [can be shared] by seven [people]."],[1575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to recite Surat al-Nisa' to him while he was on the pulpit, so I recited. When I reached: \"So how [will it be] when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?\" his eyes welled up and he said: \"Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\""],[1576,"If you have doubt in the obligatory prayer, repeat it; and if you have doubt in the voluntary prayer, prostrate twice. He said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: \"What do you do with this?\""],[1577,"A man came to him and said: \"I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah.\" He said: \"[You recited it] hastily like the recitation of poetry. I know the pairs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite, two surahs from the Mufassal in one rak'ah.\""],[1578,"A man came to him and said to him: \"Do you know the pairs?\" He said: \"I recited the Mufassal tonight in one rak'ah.\" He said: \"[You recited it] hastily like the recitation of poetry, or like the scattered dates. I know the Quran that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite, twenty surahs from the beginning of the Mufassal, two surahs in one rak'ah.\""],[1579,"I was brought the Buraq and I mounted it. When it ascended a mountain, its hind legs rose, and when it descended, its forelegs rose. It traveled with us through a land of grief and stench, then we emerged into a spacious, pleasant land. He said—I think he was Jibril ﷺ —: \"That is the land of the people of the Fire, and this is the land of the people of Paradise.\" Then I came upon a man standing, and he said: \"Who is this with you, O Jibril?\" He said: \"Your brother Muhammad ﷺ.\" He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me. I said: \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"Your brother 'Isa ibn Maryam ﷺ .\" We continued and I heard a voice, then we came upon a man. He said: \"Who is this with you?\" He said: \"This is your brother Muhammad ﷺ.\" He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me, and said: \"Ask for ease for your ummah.\" I said: \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is your brother Musa.\" I said: \"Upon whom was his complaint?\" He said: \"Upon his Lord.\" I said: \"Upon his Lord?\" He said: \"Yes, he knew His sharpness.\" Then we continued and I saw something. I said: \"What is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is the tree of your father Ibrahim. Draw near to it.\" So we drew near to it, and he welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me. Then we proceeded until I came to Bayt al-Maqdis, and I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie it. Then we entered the mosque, and the prophets—those whom Allah has named and those He has not—were gathered for me, and I led them in prayer, except for these three: Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa.\""],[1580,"The Prophet ﷺ did not perform qunut except for one month; he did not perform it before that or after it."],[1581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took off his sandals, so those behind him took off their sandals. He said: \"What made you take off your sandals?\" They said: \"We saw you take them off, so we took ours off.\" He said: \"Jibril...\""],[1582,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah from the Quran, saying: \"Learn it, for there is no prayer without tashahhud.\" He said: \"All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\""],[1583,"Give every surah its due of bowing, for the Prophet ﷺ did not combine from the Quran except twenty surahs from the Mufassal."],[1584,"I was with 'Abdullah when al-Ash'ath b. Qays entered while he was eating lunch. He said: \"Lunch, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?\" Do you not know that today is the day of 'Ashura'? He said: \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I knew it. We were commanded to fast it before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, we were neither commanded nor forbidden to do so.\""],[1585,"I used to see the whiteness of the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his right and on his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,' twice."],[1586,"He forbade wailing over the dead and said: 'It is from the affairs of the Jahiliyyah.'"],[1587,"Part of the approach of the Hour is that greetings are given only to acquaintances."],[1588,"He disliked praying in the mihrab and said: 'They were only churches, so do not imitate the People of the Book.'"],[1589,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."],[1590,"I was about to command Bilal to call the iqamah for prayer, then go to a people who heard the call and did not respond, and burn their houses upon them."],[1591,"The Prophet ﷺ gave him a kunya before he had a child."],[1592,"Abdullah was teaching a man the tashahhud and said: 'All greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' Abdullah repeated it to him several times, each time saying: 'And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger,' while the man said: 'And that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' Abdullah said: 'Thus we were taught.'"],[1593,"Every act of kindness to a rich person or a poor person is charity."],[1594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the istikharah: 'O Allah, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your power through Your might, and I ask You of Your bounty and mercy, for they are in Your hand; no one but You possesses them. You know and I do not know, and You have power and I have no power, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this thing that he intends is good for me, then grant it success and make it easy; and if it is otherwise, then decree good for me wherever it may be, for You know and I do not know, and You have power and I have no power, and You are the Knower of the unseen.'"],[1595,"No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith."],[1596,"The Prophet ﷺ slept until he snored, then stood up and prayed."],[1597,"He used to erase the two protective surahs [al-Muʿawwidhatayn] from the mushaf and say: 'The Prophet ﷺ only commanded that one seek protection by means of them, and ʿAbdullah would not recite by them.'"],[1598,"He used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a saʿ."],[1599,"Israel reported it to us, from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it. And this statement we do not know anyone to have reported from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbdullah except Israel."],[1600,"Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity, and every act of kindness is charity."],[1601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a house in which there were twelve men, and he said: 'In this house there is one whose trial upon my ummah will be more severe than the trial of the Dajjal.'"],[1602,"The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim died, and some people said: 'The sun eclipsed only because of the death of Ibrahim.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. So when you see that, pray.'"],[1603,"We used to wipe over the leather socks with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."],[1604,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: 'Alif Lam Mim Tanzil' [Surat al-Sajdah] and 'Hal ata ʿala al-insan' [Surat al-Insan]."],[1605,"The one who was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the jinn said: 'None of us was with him, but we missed the Prophet ﷺ that night, so we searched for him in the mountain passes and valleys and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been taken away.\" We spent the worst night a people ever spent. When morning came, he appeared to us from the direction of Hira, and we said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we spent a night the like of which we never spent before.\" He said: \"A caller from the jinn came to me—I think he said—they came, so I went to recite the Quran to them. He took us and showed us their fires. They asked him for provision, and he said: 'Every bone—I think he said—over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned will fall into your hands.'\""],[1606,"Mansur reported to us, from al-Shaʿbi, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbdullah, that he narrated one day from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then said: 'This or something similar.'"],[1607,"The woman who buries her infant daughter alive and the buried infant daughter are in the Fire."],[1608,"The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim died, and some people said: 'It eclipsed only because of Ibrahim's death.' He ﷺ said: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. So when you see that, pray.'"],[1609,"Do not cleanse yourselves with bones, for they are the provision of your brothers among the jinn."],[1610,"Whoever wishes, I will swear to him: indeed, the shorter surah was revealed after the longer surah, and [the verse about] those with burdens—their term is that they deliver their burdens."],[1611,"He cursed the consumer of riba (usury/interest) and its payer, its two witnesses and its scribe, the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who requests it, the tattooer and the one tattooed, the woman who plucks facial hair and the one who requests it, and he forbade wailing."],[1612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed wine and its drinker, its server, its presser and the one who has it pressed, its carrier and the one to whom it is carried, its seller and its buyer, and the one who consumes its price."],[1613,"You will surely mount stage after stage, O Muhammad—meaning: state after state."],[1614,"There is no fixed time and no fixed number for the funeral prayer."],[1615,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in leather socks and sandals."],[1616,"The woman who buries her infant daughter alive and the buried infant daughter are in the Fire."],[1617,"That he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to relieve himself, and he said: Bring me three stones. He brought him two stones and a piece of dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung."],[1618,"A loan given twice equals charity given once."],[1619,"Shall I not show you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said the takbir and raised his hands when he began the prayer. When he bowed, he placed his hands together and put them between his thighs. When he finished the prayer, he said: This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it."],[1620,"He used to say the takbir in every lowering and raising, and he would give the greeting of peace to his right and to his left."],[1621,"Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad, from his father and Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1622,"The Prophet ﷺ wanted to relieve himself. He said: \"Bring me three stones.\" So I searched and found two stones and a piece of dung. He kept the two stones and threw away the dung, saying: \"It is filth.\""],[1623,"He used to give the people their gifts. A man came and he gave him a thousand dirhams, then said: \"Take it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Those before you were destroyed only by the dinar and the dirham, and they are your destroyers.'\""],[1624,"'Abdullah b. al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya b. Waththab, from Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from 'Abdullah from the Prophet ﷺ except through this route."],[1625,"The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."],[1626,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy b. Nuwayrah, from Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. He said: Abu 'Awanah did not mention Shibak."],[1627,"We used to say that the best of the people of Madinah was Ibn Abi Talib."],[1628,"Alqamah led us in the noon prayer, five rak'ahs. When he said the salam, the people said: \"You prayed five, O Abu Shibl.\" He said: \"No, I did not.\" They said: \"Yes.\" I was on the side of the people, a young boy, and I said: \"Yes, you prayed five.\" He said to me: \"You too, O one-eyed, say that?\" I said: \"Yes.\" So he turned and prostrated twice, then said the salam, then said: \"'Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in five rak'ahs. When he turned, the people whispered among themselves. He asked: 'What is the matter with you?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased?' He said: 'No.' They said: 'Then you prayed five.' So he turned, prostrated twice, then said the salam, then said: 'I am only human; I forget as you forget.'\""],[1629,"Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Hasan b. 'Ubaydillah, from Ibrahim b. Suwayd, from Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1630,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when Surat al-Mursalat was revealed to him. We were taking it from his mouth, fresh, when a snake came out upon us. He said: \"Kill it.\" We rushed to kill it, but it escaped us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah protected it from your evil just as He protected you from its evil.\""],[1631,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered the killing of a snake in the sanctuary."],[1632,"We came to 'Abdullah in his house. He said: \"Have these people prayed?\" We said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then stand and pray.\" He did not order us to give the adhan or the iqamah. He said: We went to stand behind him, but he took our hands and positioned us, placing one of us on his right and the other on his left. He said: When he bowed, we placed our hands on our knees, but he struck our hands and clasped his hands together, then inserted them between his thighs. When he finished praying, he said: \"There will be rulers over you who will delay the prayer from its time until the glow of the dead. If you see them do that, pray the prayer at its proper time, then make your prayer with them as supererogatory. If you are three, pray together; if you are more than that, let one of you lead. When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms on his thighs, then clasp his hands together. It is as if I am looking at the interlocking of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah.\""],[1633,"Seek Laylat al-Qadr among the seven that remain, and seek it among the nine, and seek it among the eleven that remain until the morning of Badr. For the sun rises every day between the two horns of Satan, except on the morning of Badr, for it rises white without rays."],[1634,"The two of them entered upon 'Abdullah and he said: Have these prayed? We said: No. So he stood among us."],[1635,"Which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That a man grants his brother dirhams or the use of a mount's back."],[1636,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah or al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah."],[1637,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I met a woman on one of the roads of Madinah and did with her what is short of intercourse. He said: Then the verse was revealed: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds' (Qur'an 11:114). They said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for him alone or for all people? He said: Rather, for all people."],[1638,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina when the moon split."],[1639,"He used to teach them the tashahhud in prayer: All greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."],[1640,"'Abdullah used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer and would make us precise in the alif and the waw."],[1641,"'Abdullah used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Qur'an."],[1642,"A loan given twice equals a charity given once."],[1643,"Whoever consoles an afflicted person has a reward like his."],[1644,"He entered the valley when he threw the Jamrat al-'Aqabah, making the mountain behind his back. Then he threw and said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."],[1645,"He would give the salutation to his right and to his left in the prayer."],[1646,"The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Muhammad, if you are a prophet as you claim, then tell us from where resemblance comes, that a man sometimes resembles his paternal uncles and sometimes his maternal uncles?"],[1647,"When the drop (of sperm) falls into the womb."],[1648,"Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim."],[1649,"Whoever makes all his concerns a single concern, the concern of the Hereafter, Allah will suffice him for the concern of this world. And whoever whose concerns are scattered among the concerns of this world, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will not care in which of its valleys he perishes."],[1650,"None of you should make it obligatory upon himself to depart from his right; I saw most of the departure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his left."],[1651,"Most of the time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would depart from his left."],[1652,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in this place two rak'ahs. Then the prayer was commenced, and he prayed behind Uthman four; so I said: Did you forget? He said: No, but dissension is evil."],[1653,"He and Alqamah entered upon Abdullah and he led us in prayer. He stood between them, placing one of them on his right and the other on his left. Then we bowed and placed our hands on our knees, so he struck our hands, then he clasped his hands, placing them between his thighs. When he finished he said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah do."],[1654,"It is part of the Sunnah to lower the voice in the tashahhud."],[1655,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five (rak'ahs). When he gave the salutation, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five. So he prostrated twice, then gave the salutation, then said: I am only a human being; I forget as you forget."],[1656,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his need or for some need. He said: Bring me three stones, and do not bring me a wall or a body."],[1657,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to relieve himself and said: 'Bring me three stones.' So I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, saying: 'It is filth.'"],[1658,"He used to give salutations to his right and to his left."],[1659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Seek it in the night of the seventeenth of Ramadan, or the night of the twenty-first, or the night of the twenty-third.' Then he fell silent."],[1660,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: 'Is there any that will receive admonition?'"],[1661,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five [rak'ahs]. When he gave salutation, he turned around and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five [rak'ahs].' So he prostrated twice, then gave salutation, then said: 'I am only a human; I forget as you forget.'"],[1662,"The Prophet ﷺ recited 'The Star' and prostrated."],[1663,"They were with Abdullah when a man came and greeted him, so he responded to him, then said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among the signs of the approach of the Hour is greeting only those one knows.\"'"],[1664,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was suffering from a fever. I placed my hand on him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering from a severe fever.' He said: 'We prophets have our reward multiplied—I think he said—and I suffer fever as two men of you would suffer.'"],[1665,"The believer sees his sins as if he is at the base of a mountain, fearing that it will fall upon him, whereas the hypocrite sees his sins like a fly that landed on something and he waved it off thus, and it flew away. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more pleased with the repentance of a believer than a man who goes out in a desolate, perilous land with his mount carrying his provisions, food, and drink. He loses her, so he goes out searching for her until, when death overtakes him, he says: I will return to the place where I lost her and die there. So he returns, his eyes overcome him, and he awakens to find his mount at his head, carrying his provisions, food, and drink.'"],[1666,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from al-Harith b. Suwayd, from Abdullah; and from al-Aswad b. Yazid, from Abdullah, with something similar."],[1667,"It is bad for one of them to say: 'I forgot such-and-such a verse.' Rather, he was made to forget. Rehearse the Quran, for it escapes from the chests of men more quickly than camels escape from their hobbles."],[1668,"Jarir b. Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1669,"Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to Shu'bah's hadith. We do not know of any chain for this wording from 'Abdullah better than this chain."],[1670,"The servant continues to be truthful and seek truthfulness until he is written with Allah as a siddiq (truthful one), and he continues to lie and seek lying until he is written with Allah as a kadhdhab (liar)."],[1671,"Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it. We do not know that this wording is reported from 'Abdullah with a chain better than this chain."],[1672,"Insulting a Muslim is fusuq (sinful disobedience) and fighting him is kufr (disbelief)."],[1673,"Whoever swears a false oath in order to seize thereby the property of a man—or the property of his brother—he will meet Allah while He is angry with him. And regarding that was revealed: Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price..."],[1674,"Three traits: whoever has them is a hypocrite, and whoever has one of them has one trait of hypocrisy: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his promise."],[1675,"Paradise is closer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise."],[1676,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we did in the Jahiliyyah? He said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what he did in the Jahiliyyah, and whoever does evil in Islam will be held accountable for the first and the last."],[1677,"Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Mansur, and by more than one from al-A'mash."],[1678,"When it was the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ favored some people in the distribution. He gave al-Aqra' b. Habis a hundred camels, and he gave 'Uyaynah b. Badr the like of that, and he gave some people from the Arabs and favored them in the distribution. A man said: By Allah, he did not give—or: this is a distribution in which justice was not done, or: the face of Allah was not intended by it. I said: By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of this. I came to him and informed him of what the man said. His face changed and he said: Musa was harmed with more than this, and he was patient."],[1679,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who slept through the night until morning. He said: That is a man in whose ears Shaytan urinated."],[1680,"A woman should not touch another woman and then describe her to her husband as if he were looking at her."],[1681,"We were at the door of 'Abdullah waiting for him, and he was delayed. Yazid b. Mu'awiyah said, 'I will bring him out for you.' He entered upon him, and 'Abdullah came out to us and said, 'I know you are there. Nothing prevents me from coming out to you except that I dislike wearying you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give us admonition intermittently, out of dislike of making it tedious for us.'"],[1682,"I have seen us while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send us out, not making the matter obligatory upon us until he himself did it. One of you will remain in good as long as he fears Allah. If something troubles his soul, he asks a man about it and is cured by that. It is imminent that he will not find him. By Allah, I have not likened what remains of this world except to a pool of water whose clear part has been drunk and its dregs remain."],[1683,"Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."],[1684,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, al-A'mash, Hammad, Abu Hashim, and al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."],[1685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[1686,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'How do I know that I am a good-doer?' He said, 'If your neighbors say, \"You are a good-doer,\" then you are a good-doer. And if your neighbors say, \"You are an evil-doer,\" then you are an evil-doer.'"],[1687,"When you are three, let not two converse secretly to the exclusion of the third until you mix with his conversation, so that it does not grieve him."],[1688,"He drew lines and said, 'These are paths. On each path is a devil calling to it.' Then he recited: 'And this is My straight path, so follow it.'"],[1689,"The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection is bloodshed."],[1690,"A person is with the one he loves."],[1691,"Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, by which he will be known: 'This is the treachery of so-and-so.'"],[1692,"Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah will enter the Fire. And I say: Whoever dies while not setting up a rival to Allah will enter Paradise."],[1693,"A man said to 'Abdullah: 'Come here,' and 'Abdullah said: 'Thus we were taught.'"],[1694,"It is not proper for a servant to say: 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[1695,"It was narrated to us by 'Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know of any chain for this hadith from 'Abdullah other than this chain."],[1696,"I am your forerunner at the Cistern, and I will surely contend for some people and be overcome concerning them, and I will say: 'O Lord, my companions!' It will be said: 'Indeed you do not know what they innovated after you.'"],[1697,"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imitating a prophet whom his people struck, while he was wiping the blood from his face and saying: 'Forgive my people, for indeed they do not know.'"],[1698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which sin is the greatest?' He said: 'That you set up a rival to Allah when He created you.' He said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you kill your child for fear that he will eat your food.' He said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor.' Then he recited: 'And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which...' the verse."],[1699,"No one is more jealous than Allah, and for that reason He prohibited indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is concealed. And no one loves praise more than Allah."],[1700,"We were walking with the Prophet ﷺ when he passed by Ibn Sayyad, and he said: 'Indeed I have hidden something for you.' He said: 'Dukh.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Be gone, for you will not exceed your station.' 'Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, let me strike his neck.' He said: 'If he is the one you fear, you will not be able to kill him.'"],[1701,"It was narrated to us by al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know that this hadith is reported from 'Abdullah except from this route."],[1702,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah and Abu Musa, and they both said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed before the Hour there will be days in which ignorance descends, knowledge is raised, and killing increases.' We said: 'What is killing?' He said: 'Murder.'"],[1703,"We used to say in the prayer: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon so-and-so, peace be upon so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed Allah is al-Salam, so say: Greetings are for Allah, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. For when you say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, it reaches every righteous servant of Allah between the heaven and the earth. Then let each of you choose whatever supplication he likes.'"],[1704,"When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding the third."],[1705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line for us one day and said, 'This is the path of Allah.' Then he drew lines and said, 'These are paths; on each path there is a devil calling to it.' And he recited, 'And this is My straight path, so follow it...' (Qur'an 6:153)."],[1706,"We were at the door of Abdullah and he was slow in coming out to us. Yazid b. Mu'awiyah said, 'I will bring him out to you.' He went in to him, and Abdullah came out to us and said, 'I hear that you are here, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except my dislike of boring you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to space out his preaching to us out of fear of causing us weariness.'"],[1707,"Let none of you say, 'I forgot such-and-such verse'; rather, he was made to forget."],[1708,"Answer the inviter, do not reject a gift, and do not strike the Muslims."],[1709,"Israel narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1710,"The sanctity of a believer's wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."],[1711,"When Allah intends good for a servant, He grants him understanding in the religion and inspires him with right guidance."],[1712,"When one of you goes to his wife, let him cover himself and not strip completely like two donkeys."],[1713,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, looked into the hearts of His servants and found the heart of Muhammad to be the best of the hearts of His servants."],[1714,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave preference to some people in the division of spoils. He gave al-Aqra' b. Habis one hundred camels, gave 'Uyaynah b. Badr the like of that, and gave some Arabs preference in the division. A man said, 'By Allah, this is a division in which justice was not observed, or by which the face of Allah was not intended.' I said, 'By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of this.' So I went to him and told him what the man had said. His face changed color, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Musa was harmed with more than this and he was patient.'"],[1715,"These five obligatory prayers are expiations for the sins committed between them, as long as major sins are avoided."],[1716,"Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."],[1717,"By Allah, it is as if I hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the campaign of Tabuk while he was at the grave of Abdullah Dhu al-Bijadayn, with Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah have mercy on them both), saying: 'Hand me down your companion,' until he placed him gently in his lahd. When he finished burying him, he faced the qiblah and said: 'O Allah, I have become pleased with him this evening, so be pleased with him.'"],[1718,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[1719,"I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs."],[1720,"I will be your predecessor at the Basin. I will surely contend with some people and be overcome concerning them. I will say: 'O Lord, my companions!' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you.'"],[1721,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ similar to it."],[1722,"In the tashahhud: All compliments, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."],[1723,"The child belongs to the bed."],[1724,"Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah will enter the Fire. And I say: Whoever dies while not setting up a rival to Allah will enter Paradise."],[1725,"No one is more jealous than Allah, and that is why He prohibited indecencies, both apparent and hidden. And no one loves praise more than Allah."],[1726,"A man came to him and said: 'I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah.' He said: 'You recited it hastily like the recitation of poetry. I know the corresponding surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: two surahs from the Mufassal in one rak'ah.'"],[1727,"A man from the people of the Suffah died, and two dinars were found in his blanket. The Prophet ﷺ mentioned that and said: 'Two branding marks.'"],[1728,"A woman should not describe another woman to her husband as if he is looking at her. (I think he said: 'A woman should not have close contact with another woman.')"],[1729,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line for us and said, \"This is in the path of Allah.\" Then he drew other lines and said, \"These are paths; on every one of them there is a devil calling to it.\" Then he recited: \"And this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow the [other] paths lest they divert you from His path.\""],[1730,"We used to consider al-ma'un, in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to be the bucket, the axe, and the cooking pot."],[1731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the morning prayer of Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil (Surat al-Sajdah) and Hal ata 'ala al-insan (Surat al-Insan)."],[1732,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1733,"Perform Hajj and 'Umrah repeatedly, for they eliminate poverty and sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron, gold, and silver; and there is no reward for them less than Paradise."],[1734,"Shall I inform you of the best among you? They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The best of you are those with the best character.\" I think he said, \"[They are] those who are easy-going and gentle.\""],[1735,"Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour will overtake while they are still alive, and those who take graves as mosques."],[1736,"And he mentioned the tashahhud: \"All greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\""],[1737,"The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another, and the Tulaqa' of Quraysh and the 'Utaqa' of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."],[1738,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the next closest, and the next closest."],[1739,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who killed a prophet, or whom a prophet killed, and a leader of misguidance."],[1740,"There is no Muslim who loses three children who have not reached puberty but Allah will admit him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. It was said, \"And two?\" He said, \"And two.\""],[1741,"He used to perform witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', 'Say, O disbelievers', and 'Say, He is Allah, [who is] One'."],[1742,"He used to greet to his right and to his left."],[1743,"A man may speak a word that causes him to fall into the Fire for such and such autumns."],[1744,"Ibn al-Nawwāḥah came as a messenger from Musaylimah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'I testify that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If I were to kill a messenger, I would kill you, or I would strike your neck.'"],[1745,"He used to perform witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', 'Say, O disbelievers', and 'Say, He is Allah, [who is] One'."],[1746,"None of you should say, 'I forgot such and such a verse,' but rather he was made to forget."],[1747,"The world is cursed, and everything in it is cursed, except for commanding what is right, forbidding what is wrong, or remembering Allah."],[1748,"Regarding the tashahhud,"],[1749,"When we sat in prayer for the tashahhud, we used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah before His servants, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us to say in the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[1750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Laylat al-Qadr. He said, 'I was informed of it, then it was taken away from me. So seek it in the last nine nights, or the last three.'"],[1751,"Jarīr, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ b. al-Sāʾib, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh."],[1752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ discouraged us from conversing after the evening prayer."],[1753,"The one who guides to good is like the one who does it."],[1754,"He taught them the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[1755,"There is no one who dies leaving wealth on which he did not pay zakat except that Allah will make it a bald-headed snake around his neck on the Day of Resurrection. He will flee from it while it follows him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to us its confirmation from the Book of Allah: 'And let not those who withhold what Allah has given them from His bounty think that it is better for them. Rather, it is worse for them. They will be collared with what they withheld on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1756,"He taught them the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' He said: 'And he taught us this supplication just as he taught us the Quran: O Allah, reconcile our hearts, unite them, guide us to the paths of peace, and keep us away from indecencies, both apparent and hidden. O Allah, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our spouses, and our offspring, and accept our repentance. Indeed, You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful. O Allah, make us grateful for Your blessings, praising You and accepting them, and complete them upon us, O Most Merciful of the merciful.'"],[1757,"Whoever swears an oath to wrongfully take the property of a Muslim will meet Allah while He is angry with him."],[1758,"I have learned the pairs of surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray with: al-Dhariyat and al-Tur and al-Najm, and Iqtarabat al-Sa'ah and al-Waqi'ah, and Nun wa al-Qalam and al-Haqqah, and Sa'ala Sa'il and al-Muzzammil and al-Muddaththir, and La Uqsimu bi Yawm al-Qiyamah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan and al-Mursalat and 'Amma Yatasa'alun and al-Nazi'at and 'Abasa, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat and Waylun li al-Mutaffifin and Ha Mim al-Dukhan."],[1759,"Umar surpassed the people in three things: regarding the captives on the day of Badr, he wanted to kill them, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'Had it not been for a decree from Allah that preceded, you would have been touched...' the verse; and regarding the command of the veil, he ordered the wives of the Prophet to veil themselves, so Zaynab said to him: 'What do you want, O Ibn al-Khattab, while revelation descends in our houses?' So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil'; and the supplication of the Prophet ﷺ: 'O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab.'"],[1760,"We have heard the recitation, and I indeed memorize what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: eighteen surahs from the Mufassal and two surahs from the family of Ha Mim."],[1761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Indeed your blood and your wealth are sacred to you - and this day of yours is a sacred day - like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours.'"],[1762,"On the day of Badr, I came upon Abu Jahl while he was still breathing, so I severed his head. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him."],[1763,"He used to breathe three times in the vessel."],[1764,"A bedouin, an old man, came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, when is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not prepared for it much prayer or fasting, except that I love Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'Then you will be with those you love.' He said: 'Then the old man jumped up and urinated in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for perhaps he will be among the people of Paradise,' and he poured water over his urine.'"],[1765,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: “And Hell, that Day, will be brought” (89:23), he said: It will be brought, driven by seventy thousand bridles, with each bridle [held by] seventy thousand angels."],[1766,"Sufyan narrated to us, from al-'Ala' b. Khalid, from Shaqiq, from 'Abdullah, with something similar, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1767,"Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-'Ala' b. Khalid, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, with something similar, but he did not raise it. And we do not know of anyone who raised this hadith except 'Umar b. Hafs, from his father. Al-'Ala' is well-known; al-Thawri narrated from him."],[1768,"I will be your forerunner at the Cistern. I will surely contend with some people but be overcome regarding them, and I will say, ‘My companions!’ Then it will be said, ‘You do not know what they innovated after you.’"],[1769,"This verse was revealed concerning a group of Arabs who used to worship a group of jinn. The jinn embraced Islam while the group of Arabs were unaware. That is His saying: “Say, ‘Call upon those you claimed besides Him; they have no power to remove harm from you or to change it’” (17:56), to the end of the verse."],[1770,"The one who remembers Allah among the heedless is like a fighter among those who flee."],[1771,"Whoever sheds tears from his eyes the size of a fly’s wing out of fear of Allah will not enter the Fire until the milk returns to the udder."],[1772,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he smiled. We said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, what made you smile?’ He said, ‘I marvel at the believer and his distress over sickness. If he knew what he has in sickness, he would love to remain sick until he meets Allah.’"],[1773,"Hudayj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah b. 'Utba, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and he mentioned the story of the Negus."],[1774,"A rooster crowed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a man cursed it. He forbade cursing the rooster."],[1775,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1776,"Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1777,"Indeed, the creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's belly for forty days, then he becomes a clinging clot (ʿalaqah) for the like of that, then he becomes a lump of flesh (muḍghah) for the like of that. Then Allah sends to him the angel, and he is commanded with four words, and it is said: write down his term, his deeds, his provision, and whether he is wretched or blessed. Then indeed one of you performs the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is between him and it only a cubit, then the decree overtakes him, so he performs the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And indeed a man performs the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is between him and it only a cubit, then the decree overtakes him, so he performs the deeds of the people of Paradise — I think he said — and enters it."],[1778,"Fiṭr — meaning Ibn Khalīfah — narrated to us, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Zayd b. Wahb, from ʿAbdullāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a manner similar to the hadith of al-Aʿmash."],[1779,"Indeed, after me there will be selfishness (atharah) and matters that you will disapprove of. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command one of us who lives to see that? He said: You fulfill the right that is upon you, and you ask Allah for that which is yours."],[1780,"It was said to ʿAbdullāh: Do you have anything to say about al-Walīd b. ʿUqbah, whose beard drips wine? He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from spying; but if something becomes clear to us, we will change it."],[1781,"Warqaʾ — meaning Ibn ʿUmar — narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from ʿAbdullāh, from the Prophet."],[1782,"Indeed, al-salām (peace) is a name from among the names of Allah, which He placed on the earth. So spread it among yourselves. Indeed, when a Muslim man passes by a people and greets them with peace, and they respond to him, he has over them the virtue of a degree because he reminded them of peace. But if they do not respond to him, one who is better and purer than them responds to him."],[1783,"O people of the chambers, the Fire has been kindled. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[1784,"If two men enter Islam and then forsake one another, one of them is outside Islam until he returns."],[1785,"We used not to perform ablution from (walking on) a place that had been trodden (with impurity)."],[1786,"ʿAbdullāh was in Ḥims, and he recited Sūrah Yūsuf. A man said: It was not revealed like this. He said: Then he smelled the odor of wine from him, and said: You drink the impurity and you deny the revelation."],[1787,"Indeed, after you there will come the days of patience. Patience in them is like grasping a live coal. For the one who acts (upon the faith) in them is the reward of fifty. They said: O Messenger of Allah, fifty of them or fifty of us? He said: Fifty of you."],[1788,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[1789,"A rabbi, or a man from the People of the Book, came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Aba al-Qasim, has it reached you that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will carry the creatures on one finger, the trees on one finger, and the earth on one finger?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed."],[1790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Recite to me.” I said: “Should I recite to you when it was taught to me by you?” He said: “I love to hear it from someone else.” So I recited Surah al-Nisa’ to him until I reached: “So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” (Quran 4:41). Then his eyes overflowed."],[1791,"Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour will overtake while they are still alive, and those who take graves as mosques."],[1792,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[1793,"The last of the people of Paradise to enter and the last of the people of Hell to come out will be a man who will say: “O Lord, bring me out of this fire to the shade of that tree.” When he feels some relief and looks at the trees of Paradise, he will say: “O Lord, this one.” So he will come out, having no deeds to support him, and will crawl until he reaches—meaning Paradise—but will not find a place in it. He will return to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and say: “O Lord, I did not find a place in it.” He will say: “Go, for you will have the like of this world and ten times its like.” He said: “You mock me while You are my Lord?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars and premolars showed."],[1794,"Qays narrated to us, from ‘Ata’ b. al-Sa’ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from ‘Abida, from ‘Abdullah."],[1795,"Qays narrated to us, from ‘Ata’ b. al-Sa’ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from ‘Abida, from ‘Abdullah."],[1796,"He used to teach them: “Greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.”"],[1797,"A man went out intending to mount his horse, and he passed by the mosque of Banu Hanifa and entered to pray. Their imam was reciting the words of Musaylima the liar. He came to ‘Abdullah and informed him, so he sent for them and asked them to repent. They repented, except ‘Abdullah b. al-Nawwaha. He said to him: “O ‘Abdullah b. al-Nawwaha, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Were it not that you are a messenger, I would strike your neck.’”"],[1798,"Muhammad b. Kathir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha b. Mudarrib, from ‘Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar or close to it. We do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of al-A‘mash from Abu Ishaq and attributed it as musnad except Abu Mu‘awiya, and we do not know anyone who attributed the hadith of al-Thawri as musnad except Muhammad b. Kathir."],[1799,"The closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection will be those who send the most blessings upon me in this world."],[1800,"Answer the caller when you are invited."],[1801,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Which deed is most virtuous?' He said, 'Prayer at its proper time.' I said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then kindness to parents.' I said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Jihad in the path of Allah.' He said: I did not refrain from asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [except out of respect for him]."],[1802,"Abu Ya'fur narrated to us, from al-Walid b. al-'Aizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Ya'fur except Sa'id b. Maslama."],[1803,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Walid b. al-'Aizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Shaybani, from al-Walid."],[1804,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Walid b. al-'Aizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani who said: The owner of this house narrated to me, and he pointed to the house of 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1805,"The most virtuous deed is prayer at its proper time and kindness to parents."],[1806,"The most virtuous deed is prayer at its proper time and kindness to parents."],[1807,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[1808,"An amir prayed and gave salutations to his right and to his left. 'Abdullah said: 'How did he learn it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give salutations to his right and to his left.'"],[1809,"I was hiding behind the wall of the Ka'bah when two men with large bellies and little understanding of religion came. One of them said to his companion: 'Do you think Allah hears what we say?' The other replied: 'If we raise our voices, He hears; if we lower them, He does not hear.' The other said to him: 'If He hears when we raise our voices, then He hears when we lower them.' I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: 'And you were not hiding yourselves, lest your hearing, your sight, and your skins should testify against you' up to His saying: 'But you thought that Allah did not know much of what you do.'"],[1810,"He used to teach them the tashahhud: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."],[1811,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah and around the House there were such and such idols. He began striking them, pointing at them with a stick that he had or with a piece of wood, and saying: 'The truth has come and falsehood has vanished.'"],[1812,"The moon was split while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Bear witness.'"],[1813,"The moon was split while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ — I think he said: at Mina."],[1814,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1815,"The world will not pass away until the Arabs are ruled by a man from my household whose name matches my name."],[1816,"The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name."],[1817,"My father narrated to me, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Shaybani, from Asim."],[1818,"The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name."],[1819,"Uthman b. Shubrumah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Thawri, from Asim. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Uthman b. Shubrumah except Muhammad b. Fudayl. Indeed, a group narrated this statement from Asim, among them: Fitr, Za'idah, Hammad b. Salamah, and others."],[1820,"And indeed he saw him another descent. He said: he saw Gabriel at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, having six hundred wings."],[1821,"They said: O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen? He said: (They will be) shining white with traces of ablution."],[1822,"Whoever prays over a funeral will have a qirat, and whoever waits until its burial is completed will have two qirats."],[1823,"Perhaps you will reach the prayer with people who pray it at other than its proper time. If you reach it, then pray it at its proper time that you know, then pray with them, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."],[1824,"The Prophet's ﷺ two companions on a mount were Ali and Abu Lubabah. When the turn came for the Messenger of God ﷺ to walk, they would say: Ride, and we will walk. He would say: You two are not stronger than me, and I am not less in need of the reward than you two."],[1825,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet"],[1826,"Whoever tells a lie against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1827,"Indeed, Allah looked into the hearts of His servants and found the heart of Muhammad to be the best of hearts. Then He looked into the hearts of His servants and found the hearts of his Companions to be the best of hearts among His servants, so He made them the supporters of His religion. Whatever the believers see as good is good in the sight of Allah, and whatever the believers see as evil is evil in the sight of Allah."],[1828,"The memorizers among the Companions of Muhammad knew that Ibn Umm 'Abd was the closest of them to Allah in means of approach."],[1829,"He used to fast three days from the beginning of every month, and I never saw him not fasting on a Friday."],[1830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the 'Isha' prayer, then he went out to the mosque and found the people waiting for the prayer. He said: 'There is no one among the followers of any religion who prays at this hour other than you.'"],[1831,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: 'O Allah, I love them, so love them, and whoever loves them has loved me.'"],[1832,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[1833,"Ahmad b. Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, who raised it with something similar."],[1834,"He forbade praying after 'Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr, or after the Subh prayer, until the sun rises, and at midday - I think he said: during intense heat."],[1835,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was a boy tending sheep belonging to 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and he mentioned some words, then he said: 'And he wiped my head and said: You are a taught boy.'"],[1836,"The woman who buries her daughter alive and the buried daughter will be in the Fire."],[1837,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition when “Wal-mursalāti ʿurfan” [Sūrat al-Mursalāt] was revealed to him. I received it from his mouth, and his mouth was moist with it. Then a snake came out and entered a hole, so we pursued it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “You have been spared its evil just as it was spared your evil.”"],[1838,"He climbed a tree to cut a miswāk from an arāk tree. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and were amazed at the thinness of his legs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They are heavier on the Scale than [Mount] Uḥud.”"],[1839,"Last night, nations were presented to me with their followers."],[1840,"Fāṭimah guarded her chastity, so Allah forbade her descendants to the Fire."],[1841,"I took seventy sūrahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1842,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Recite to me.” So I recited Sūrat al-Nisāʾ to him until I reached: “How will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” [Q 4:41]. He said: Then his eyes overflowed with tears and he said: “Whoever would like to recite the Qurʾān fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd [i.e., Ibn Masʿūd].”"],[1843,"The Hour will not come until a man from my family rules, whose name matches my name. He will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it was filled with tyranny and oppression."],[1844,"ʿAlī b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdallāh."],[1845,"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn used to come to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and they would climb on him and ride him. When they were told to stop, he gestured with his hand: “Leave them.” When he finished the prayer, he embraced them and said: “Whoever loves me should love these two.”"],[1846,"We used to be taught the istikhārah just as we were taught a sūrah from the Qurʾān. When one of you intends a matter, let him say: “O Allah, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your power through Your ability, and I ask You of Your immense bounty. You have power and I have none, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter which I intend”—and he names it—“is good for my religion, good for me in my worldly affair, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, then facilitate it for me”—I think he said—“and bless me in it. And if it is evil for me in my religious affair, evil for me in my worldly affair, and evil for me in the outcome of”—I think he said—“my affair, then turn it away from me, and facilitate for me the good, and decree it for me, and make me content with it.”"],[1847,"My father narrated to me, from Saʿīd b. Zayd, from ʿĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdallāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know this ḥadīth to be reported from the ḥadīth of Zirr, from ʿAbdallāh, except through this chain."],[1848,"Jarīr narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Razīn, from Zirr b. Ḥubaysh, from ʿAbdallāh."],[1849,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on an expedition when 'By those sent forth in succession' (al-Mursalat) was revealed. I received it from his mouth while it was still moist with it."],[1850,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Ubaydah related to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah."],[1851,"Believing in omens is part of shirk; and there is none of us but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, removes it through reliance on Him."],[1852,"He was asked, 'Which sin is greatest?' He said, 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then that you kill your child for fear that he will eat from your food.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.'"],[1853,"On the morning of Friday he used to recite 'Alif Lam Mim. The revelation...' (al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man...' (al-Insan)."],[1854,"In the two rak'ahs before dawn he used to recite 'Say, O disbelievers' (al-Kafirun) and 'Say, He is Allah, the One' (al-Ikhlas)."],[1855,"He used to give salutation to his right and to his left."],[1856,"The first to proclaim their Islam were seven: the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Bilal, and he mentioned a group. As for the Prophet ﷺ, Allah protected him through his uncle; as for Abu Bakr, Allah protected him through his people; as for the rest of them, they were tortured and exposed to the scorching sun."],[1857,"And when We turned towards you a group of jinn listening to the Quran; when they attended it they said, 'Listen attentively.' He said: 'Silence!' He said: They were seven, the eldest of them being Zawba'ah."],[1858,"Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed an unbeliever, or it is as if he killed an unbeliever."],[1859,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praising the Nakha' so much that I wished my people were from the Nakha'."],[1860,"When there are three people, two should not converse privately excluding the third."],[1861,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, about forty men, and he said: 'Would you be content to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Would you be content to be a third of the people of Paradise?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. Indeed, Paradise is entered only by a Muslim soul. And you among the people of polytheism are but like a white hair on the skin of a black ox, or a black hair on the skin of a red ox.'"],[1862,"Ja'far b. 'Awn narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr b. Maymun, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[1863,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was prostrating and around him were people from Quraysh, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt came with the placenta of a slaughtered camel and threw it on the back of the Messenger of God ﷺ, while the Messenger of God ﷺ did not raise his head. Then Fatimah came and removed it from his back and invoked God against the one who did that. He said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head, he said: 'O God, [I invoke] You against the group of Quraysh: Abu Jahl, 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah b. Khalaf—or Ibn Abi Khalaf'—Shu'bah was uncertain. He said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr and thrown into the well, except Umayyah—or Ubayy—whose limbs were torn apart and was not thrown into the well."],[1864,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the mosque and Abu Jahl b. Hisham, Shaybah and 'Utbah the two sons of Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah b. Khalaf—Abu Ishaq said: and two other men whose names I do not remember—making seven, were in the Hijr, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying. When he prostrated and prolonged the prostration, Abu Jahl said: 'Which of you will go to the slaughtered camel of the Banu so-and-so and bring us its stomach contents and throw it on Muhammad ﷺ?' The most wretched of them, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, went and brought it and threw it on his shoulders while the Messenger of God ﷺ was prostrating. Ibn Mas'ud said: I was standing and could not speak; I had no clan to protect me, so I was afraid. Then I heard Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she came and removed that from his shoulder, then turned to face Quraysh and reviled them, but they did not respond to her at all. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head as he would raise it at the completion of his prostration. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: 'O God, [I invoke] You against Quraysh'—three times—'against 'Utbah, 'Uqbah, Abu Jahl, and Shaybah.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ left the mosque, and Abu al-Bakhtari met him. Abu al-Bakhtari had a whip which he carried as a support. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ, he noticed a change in his face and said: 'What is the matter with you?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave me alone.' He said: 'God knows I will not leave you until you tell me what has happened to you, for something has befallen you.' When the Prophet ﷺ realized that he would not leave him, he told him: 'Abu Jahl ordered and stomach contents were thrown on me.' Abu al-Bakhtari said: 'Come to the mosque.' So the Prophet ﷺ and Abu al-Bakhtari came and entered the mosque. Then Abu al-Bakhtari went to Abu Jahl and said: 'O Abu al-Hakam, are you the one who ordered that stomach contents be thrown on Muhammad?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: Then he raised the whip and struck his head with it. He said: The men rose up against each other. He said: Abu Jahl shouted: 'Woe to you! This is for him [Muhammad]. He only wanted to stir up enmity between us and save himself and his companions.'"],[1865,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was prostrating near the Ka'bah and around him were people from Quraysh—then he mentioned a report similar to the hadith of Shu'bah and added: When the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head, he praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'To proceed: O God, [I invoke] You against the group of Quraysh.' Then he related the story."],[1866,"The first group of my community to enter Paradise will have faces like the moon on the night of the full moon. The second group will be like the most beautiful shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, each wife wearing seventy garments, the marrow of whose legs will be visible from behind the garments, just as red wine is seen in a white glass."],[1867,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his companions: 'Can any of you recite a third of the Quran in a night?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, who can do that?' He said: 'Can any of you recite, \"Say: He is God, the One\"? For it is equal to a third of the Quran.'"],[1868,"'Utbah b. Rabi'ah was a friend of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in pre-Islamic times. Whenever 'Utbah came to Madinah, he would stay with Sa'd b. Mu'adh, and whenever Sa'd came to Makkah, he would stay with 'Utbah. 'Utbah used to call him 'my Yathribi brother.' He said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, Sa'd b. Mu'adh came to Makkah as he used to, and stayed with 'Utbah. He said: 'I want to circumambulate the House.' 'Utbah said to him: 'Wait until the notables of Quraysh disperse from the mosque or from around the House.' He said: He waited a little, then said to him: 'Come with me.' When they came to the House, Abu Jahl met Sa'd and said: 'O Sa'd, you have given shelter to Muhammad, and now you circumambulate the House in safety?' Sa'd said to him: 'If you prevent me, I will certainly cut off your trade route to such-and-such a place'—a place he mentioned. He said: Their voices rose, and 'Utbah said to Sa'd: 'Do you raise your voice against Abu al-Hakam?' He said: Sa'd said to him: 'And you say this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"He [Abu Jahl] will kill you.\"' He said: He pulled his hand away from his and said: 'Muhammad does not lie.' He said: Sa'd circumambulated, then left. 'Utbah came to his wife and said: 'Did you not hear what my Yathribi brother said?' She said: 'What did he say?' He said: 'He claimed that Muhammad will kill me, and Muhammad does not lie.' He said: It was only a short time until the affair of Badr. He said: Abu Jahl began going around among the people,"],[1869,"He used to supplicate with this supplication: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from cowardice and miserliness, from the worst of life, from the trial of the heart, and from the punishment of the grave.'"],[1870,"And I think that 'Abdah b. 'Abdullah narrated it to us, from 'Ubaydullah b. Musa, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr b. Maymun, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ. Yunus b. Abi Ishaq also narrated this hadith from his father, from 'Amr b. Maymun, from 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1871,"Regarding the words of God, Blessed and Exalted: 'On the day the earth will be changed to another earth'—he said: 'A white earth on which no blood has been shed and on which no sin has been committed.'"],[1872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying near the House while a group of Quraysh were sitting, having slaughtered a camel. He said—I think it was Abu Jahl—: 'Which of you will take this stomach contents with its blood, then wait until Muhammad places his face in prostration and put it on his back?' 'Abdullah said: The most wretched of them went and took the stomach contents. When he [the Prophet] fell prostrate, he placed it on his back. Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, was told, and she was a young girl. She came running and removed it from his back. When he finished his prayer, he said: 'O God, [I invoke] You against Quraysh. O God, [I invoke] You against Abu Jahl b. Hisham, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, and 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt'—until he counted seven from Quraysh. 'Abdullah said: By Him who sent down the Book upon him, I saw them on the day of Badr in a single well."],[1873,"When I killed Abu Jahl, I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: 'This is the Pharaoh of this community.'"],[1874,"I sat with Abdullah for a year and he did not narrate a single hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ. One day he said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said...' and his face changed and he said: 'Something like this, or above this, or below this.'"],[1875,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Utbah, from Muslim al-Batin, from 'Amr b. Maymun, from Abdullah, something similar."],[1876,"A righteous dream is glad tidings, and it is one of seventy parts of prophethood. And your fire—meaning this one—is one of seventy parts of the scorching heat of Hell. And as long as a servant is waiting for the prayer, he is in prayer as long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[1877,"The Messenger of God ﷺ drew a line for us one day, and drew a line to its right, and drew a line to its left. Then he said: 'This is the path of God.' Then he drew other lines and said: 'These are paths; upon each of them is a devil calling to it.' And he recited: 'And this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow the [other] paths, lest they divert you.'"],[1878,"Say: He is God, the One, is equivalent to one-third of the Quran."],[1879,"Lending twice is equivalent to giving charity once."],[1880,"Sa'id b. Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir b. Murrah, from al-Rabi' b. Khuthaym, from Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1881,"There are no two Muslims except that there is a veil from God between them. If one of them says a hurtful word to his companion, he tears God's veil."],[1882,"Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[1883,"There is none of you except that there has been assigned to him a companion from the jinn. They said: 'Even you?' He said: 'Even me, except that God helped me against him, so he became a Muslim.'"],[1884,"If I knew that anyone was more knowledgeable of the Book of God than me, and a mount could reach him, I would go to him. I have taken seventy surahs directly from the mouth of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1885,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer or a sorcerer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad."],[1886,"Fasting is a shield, and the odor of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the fragrance of musk."],[1887,"He was asked, 'Which sin is greatest?' He said, 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then that you kill your child for fear that he will eat your food.' He said, 'Then which?' He said, 'Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.' Then he recited: 'And those who do not call upon another god with Allah...'"],[1888,"Whoever deliberately lies about me in order to mislead, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1889,"Behold, the overzealous are destroyed; behold, the overzealous are destroyed. He said it three times."],[1890,"Do not let the adhan of Bilal prevent you from eating the pre-dawn meal, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer."],[1891,"He looked at some people from the Zutt and said, 'These are the most similar of those I have seen to the jinn.'"],[1892,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that he had met a woman and that he had gotten from her a kiss or something he mentioned. It was as if he asked about its expiation, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night...' the verse."],[1893,"He forbade going out to meet the caravans."],[1894,"We were commanded, when we see someone announcing a lost item in the mosque, to say to him: 'May you not find it.'"],[1895,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride - or he said in prayer - will not be in Allah's security, neither in the lawful nor the forbidden."],[1896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I had placed my left hand on my right hand, so he took my right hand and placed it on my left hand."],[1897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the night prayer (Salat al-ʿIsha'), then departed and took my hand and went out to the plain, the plain of Makkah. Then he drew a line for him — meaning for ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud — then said: “Do not leave your line. If anyone reaches you, do not speak to him.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went where he intended. While I was sitting in my line, there came to me men resembling the Zut, their hair and their bodies — they did not cross the line, then they went on to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, until when it was the last part of the night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while I was sitting, and said: “These have troubled me tonight.” Then he entered upon me within my line and rested his head on my thigh and slept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he slept, would breathe audibly in his sleep. While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ resting his head on my thigh, suddenly there came to me men who seemed like men of the Hijaz, upon them white garments — Allah knows best how beautiful they were. A group of them sat at the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and a group at his feet. Then they said among themselves: “We have never seen anyone who has been given what this Prophet ﷺ was given: his eyes sleep while his heart remains awake. Strike a parable for him — I think he said: as a man who built a palace, then prepared a banquet and invited people to his food. Whoever answered him ate of his food and drank of his drink, and whoever did not answer him, he punished or was punished.” Then they departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and said to me: “Did you hear what these said, and do you know who they are?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “They are the angels.” He said: “Do you know the parable they struck?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The parable they struck is the Lord, Blessed and Exalted: He built Paradise and called His servants to it. Whoever answered Him entered Paradise, and whoever did not answer Him, He punished or tormented.”"],[1898,"We have not ceased to be mighty since ʿUmar accepted Islam."],[1899,"When Allah wills to take a servant from a certain land, He creates for him a need to go there."],[1900,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah has given the Qur'an, so he stands with it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to expend it in the truth."],[1901,"We used to go on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no women with us. Some of us sought his permission to castrate, or he said: “If you permitted us, we would castrate ourselves,” but he did not permit us. He permitted us to enjoy (temporary marriage) with a garment."],[1902,"ʿA'ishah had a vow to free a slave from the descendants of Ismaʿil. A group of captives from Balʿanbar arrived, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If it pleases you to fulfill your vow, then free one of these.”"],[1903,"Why should I not care about it, when the groin of one of you is between his fingertip and his nail?"],[1904,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[1905,"That he came to Abu Jahl while he was at his last breath and said: “May Allah disgrace you.” He said: “Is there anyone more accursed than a man whom you have killed?”"],[1906,"There will be rulers after me who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer; there is no faith after that."],[1907,"The Prophet ﷺ taught me to recite: “Indeed, Allah is the Provider, the Possessor of strength, the Firm.”"],[1908,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs at Mina."],[1909,"Al-A'mash narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, from Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know that anyone narrated this hadith from Idris except Musa b. A'yan."],[1910,"He went deep into the valley on the Day of Sacrifice and threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah, and he said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."],[1911,"The talbiyah of the Prophet ﷺ was: Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak."],[1912,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, from Abdullah."],[1913,"He threw the pebbles at the Jamrah with seven pebbles, making the House on his left and Mina on his right, and he said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."],[1914,"He prayed two rak'ahs at Mina."],[1915,"He prayed two rak'ahs at Mina."],[1916,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray any prayer at other than its appointed time except that he combined the two prayers at Jam', and he prayed Fajr that day at other than its appointed time."],[1917,"I did not see the Prophet ﷺ pray any prayer except at its time, except that he combined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah, and he prayed the morning prayer at other than its time."],[1918,"Indeed conciseness of the khutbah and length of the prayer are a sign of a man's understanding. So lengthen the prayer and shorten the khutbahs. Indeed some eloquent speech is magic. There will come after you people who lengthen the khutbahs and shorten the prayer."],[1919,"Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik b. al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know that anyone narrated the hadith of al-A'mash from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, nor the hadith of al-A'mash from Malik b. al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, except Qays."],[1920,"No one is more protective of his honor than Allah, and for that reason He forbade indecencies, both open and hidden. And no one loves praise more than Allah."],[1921,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the morning, he would say: 'We have entered the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, the word of sincerity, and the religion of our father Ibrahim, devoting the religion solely to Him.' And when he entered the evening, he would say the like of that."],[1922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Your permission to me is that you raise the veil and that you see my private conversation until I forbid you.'"],[1923,"Whoever asks while he has what suffices him will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches or sores on his face. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what suffices him?' He said: 'Fifty dirhams or their equivalent in gold.'"],[1924,"The believer is not one who taunts, nor curses, nor is obscene, nor vulgar."],[1925,"Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid, from Abdullah, that he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he said this, or something like it. We do not know this hadith as narrated from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman except through Hafs b. Ghiyath."],[1926,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud: 'All greetings are due to Allah, and all prayers and all pure words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[1927,"Al-Ash'ath b. Qays entered upon him on the day of Ashura while he was having lunch. He said: 'Come to lunch.' He said: 'Is not today the day of Ashura?' He said: 'Do you know what the day of Ashura is? It is a day that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, it was abandoned.'"],[1928,"I said to Abdullah, or it was said to Abdullah: 'Some people throw the pebble from above the Aqabah.' He said: 'Abdullah threw from the bottom of the valley, and said: \"Thus, by the One besides whom there is no god, did the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed throw it.\""],[1929,"Umm Habibah said: 'O Allah, bless me in my husband, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in my father Abu Sufyan, and in my brother Mu'awiyah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have asked Allah for fixed terms and apportioned provisions; nothing of them is hastened before its time. If you had asked Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to grant you well-being or to protect you from punishment in the Fire and punishment in the grave, it would have been better, or more excellent.' He said: 'And monkeys and pigs were mentioned. I said: \"Were they among those transformed from the Children of Israel?\" He said: \"Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, did not destroy a people and leave them offspring or posterity. Monkeys and pigs existed, I think, before that.'"],[1930,"Al-Aqib and al-Sayyid came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he wanted to invoke mutual curse (mubahalah) with them. One of them said to his companion: 'Let us not invoke mutual curse with him, for if he is a prophet and we curse him, neither we nor our descendants after us will prosper.' They said to him: 'We will give you what you asked for, so send with us a trustworthy man, and do not send with us anyone but a trustworthy man.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I will certainly send with you a truly trustworthy man, a man truly worthy of trust.' He said: 'Arise, O Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah.' When he stood, he said: 'This is the trustworthy one of this ummah.'"],[1931,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not relieve our complaint."],[1932,"He set the blood money for accidental killing in fifths."],[1933,"Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from ‘Abd Allah b. al-Sa’ib, from Zadhan, from ‘Abd Allah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1934,"“Indeed Allah has angels who travel about, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my ummah.”"],[1935,"“Indeed Allah has angels who travel about, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my ummah.”"],[1936,"I and my father entered upon ‘Abd Allah, and my father said to him: “O Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘Remorse is repentance’?” He said: “Yes.”"],[1937,"“Remorse is repentance.”"],[1938,"The first to reduce the takbir was al-Walid b. ‘Uqbah. ‘Abd Allah said: “They reduced it, so may Allah reduce them. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir whenever he bowed, whenever he prostrated, and whenever he raised.”"],[1939,"My father narrated to me, from al-A‘mash, from Thuwayr b. Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud."],[1940,"“I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs.”"],[1941,"“Whoever comes to a soothsayer or a sorcerer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad.”"],[1942,"“It is part of the Sunnah to perform ghusl on Friday.”"],[1943,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was feverish, and I placed my hand on him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, how severe your fever is! You are suffering a severe fever.” He said: “Yes, I suffer fever as two men of you would suffer. There is no believing servant, male or female, who falls ill with an illness but Allah sheds his sins from him just as leaves are shaken off a tree.”"],[1944,"“He is not one of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, or calls with the call of Jahiliyyah.”"],[1945,"Riba (usury) has seventy-some branches, and shirk (associating partners with Allah) is the like of that."],[1946,"Masruq b. al-Ajda' was sitting with al-Dahhak b. Qays, and with him was 'Umara b. 'Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt. Al-Dahhak wanted to appoint Masruq over some of his duties. 'Umara b. 'Uqba said to him, \"Will you appoint a man from among the remnants of the killers of 'Uthman?\" Masruq said [in response]..."],[1947,"\"There will be twelve caliphs after me,\" I think he said, \"the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel.\""],[1948,"Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari and Bishr b. Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us. They said: Abu Usama narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know of any chain for this hadith from 'Abdullah better than this chain, although the scholars have spoken about Mujalid."],[1949,"The judge will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand at the edge of Hell. If he is ordered and pushed, he will fall into it for seventy autumns."],[1950,"And I heard 'Amr b. 'Ali mention this hadith from Yahya b. Sa'id and Muhammad b. Fudayl, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ. I think 'Amr b. 'Ali carried the hadith of Ibn Fudayl onto the hadith of Yahya in the marfu' form, because I did not hear anyone else raise it from Ibn Fudayl except 'Amr b. 'Ali; he combined Yahya and Ibn Fudayl in it."],[1951,"When Abu Jahl was brought, being dragged to the well, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If Abu Talib were alive, he would know, or he would learn, that our swords have been put to work on the nobles.\""],[1952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the hunger in the faces of his Companions and said: \"Rejoice, for there will come upon you a time when one of you will be given a large bowl of tharid (bread soaked in broth) in the morning and the like of it in the evening.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we will be better then.\" He said, \"Rather, you are better today than you will be then.\""],[1953,"The mill of Islam will turn — meaning at the end of thirty-five years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; and if they remain, their affair will remain for seventy years."],[1954,"Sometimes he would narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his face would change color and his complexion would alter, and he would say something like this or close to this."],[1955,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Begin with those you support: your mother and your father, and your sister and your brother."],[1956,"One day he narrated and said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" and he was seized by trembling and his clothes trembled, then he said something like this or thus."],[1957,"The first grandmother to inherit during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a grandmother while her son was alive."],[1958,"It is from the Sunnah that a man says in his bowing: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent' three times, and in his prostration: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High' three times."],[1959,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man from the desert people, and I am wealthy, and I have a mother and a father, a brother and a sister, a paternal uncle and a paternal aunt, a maternal uncle and a maternal aunt. Which of them is most entitled to my kind treatment?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your mother and your father, and your sister and your brother, and the closest to you, then the closest.'"],[1960,"I approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on an elevated piece of ground until I sat facing his face, or with my face at his knees. I seized the opportunity of being alone with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest?' He turned away from me until I said it three times. Then he turned his face and said: 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' He said: 'Then I said: Then what?' He said: 'That you kill your child for fear that he might eat or be fed with you.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, then what?' or 'Then what?' He said: 'That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.' Then he stretched out his hand and recited: 'And those who do not call upon another god with Allah.'"],[1961,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, I love you' – I think he said: 'By Allah, I love you' – saying it three times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is this who swears on what he swears?' The man said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Go, for you are with the one you love, and upon you is what you have earned, and upon Allah is what you have hoped for reward.'"],[1962,"The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah is not lawful except for one of three: a life for a life, the previously married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."],[1963,"Ya'la b. 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah b. Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar meaning. We do not know of this hadith being reported from 'Abdullah except through this chain, except for a hadith."],[1964,"Al-Fadl narrated it to us, from Aswad b. 'Amir, from Zuhayr, from al-A'mash, from Muslim, who is Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar meaning. The hadith of Muslim is not preserved; it is only preserved from the hadith of 'Abdullah b. Murrah."],[1965,"He is not one of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of the pre-Islamic ignorance."],[1966,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among palm trees when some Jews confronted him and asked him about the soul. He paused for a while, and we thought that revelation was coming to him. Then he said: 'And they ask you about the soul. Say: The soul is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.'"],[1967,"The eyes commit adultery, the hands commit adultery, the feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery."],[1968,"I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs."],[1969,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, except Abu 'Awanah and Shayban."],[1970,"Do not revert after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks. And a man is not to be taken to account for the crime of his father, nor for the crime of his brother."],[1971,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Part of this speech has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through various chains with different wordings, and part of his speech has been narrated from 'Abdullah through another chain, but we do not know it being narrated with this wording except through this chain."],[1972,"He used to give salutation to his right and to his left in prayer."],[1973,"He used to give salutation in prayer to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[1974,"Selling animals whose udders have been tied up to make them appear full of milk is deception, and deception is not lawful."],[1975,"I was with Masruq in a house containing an image of Mary, and Masruq said: 'Is this an image of Kisra?' I said: 'No, rather it is an image of Mary.' Masruq said: 'I heard 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers.'"],[1976,"We were with 'Abdullah when a man entered upon us while 'Abdullah was lying down. He said: 'I have come to you from the mosque, and people met me at the gates of Kindah saying: the smoke, or the sign of the smoke will come and seize the breaths of the disbelievers, while the believer will be affected like a cold.' 'Abdullah became angry, sat up, and said: 'O people, whoever among you knows something, let him say what he knows, and whoever does not know, let him say: Allah knows best. For it is part of a person's knowledge, when asked about what he does not know, to say: Allah knows best. Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to His Prophet ﷺ: Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it, nor am I of the pretentious. The sign of the smoke has already passed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw people turning away, he said: O Allah, seven years like the seven years of Yusuf. Then a year of famine seized the people and destroyed everything, until they began to eat carrion and hides. Abu Sufyan came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Muhammad, you have come commanding obedience to Allah and maintaining family ties, and your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them.' Then 'Abdullah recited this verse: 'So watch for the day when the sky will bring a visible smoke' until he reached 'Indeed, you will return [to disbelief].' He said: Then it was lifted."],[1977,"I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: Five things have passed: the splitting of the moon, alif lam mim, the Romans have been defeated, the day when the sky will bring a visible smoke, the day We shall seize with the greatest seizure, and the Day of Badr."],[1978,"The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."],[1979,"I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud while he was with Abu Musa, and Hudhayfah was with him. Hudhayfah said: 'O 'Abdullah b. Qays, you were sent to the people of Basrah as a commander and teacher, and they took from your manners and your recitation.' Ibn Mas'ud said: 'There is no verse of the Qur'an but I know when it was revealed and concerning what it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable about the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would travel to him.'"],[1980,"Your Prophet ﷺ, when he was bowing or prostrating, used to say: 'Glory be to You with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance.'"],[1981,"The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the polytheists said: 'This is magic, but look and ask them.' So they asked Muhammad ﷺ."],[1982,"He would give the salam in prayer to his right: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[1983,"Every prophet has close allies from among the prophets, and my closest ally from among them is my father and the intimate friend of my Lord. Then he said: 'Indeed the closest of people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, and this prophet, and those who believe.'"],[1984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer, then he gave the salam to his right until the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[1985,"Sleep was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Sleep, for when you wake up, then do good.'"],[1986,"Indeed the impure does not expiate the impure, but the pure expiates the impure."],[1987,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Bilal while he had a heap of dates. He said: 'What is this, O Bilal?' He said: 'I am storing it for your guests.' He said: 'Do you not fear that it will have smoke in the Fire of Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Owner of the Throne.'"],[1988,"Indeed I know the pairs of surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite together."],[1989,"Every prophet has close allies from among the prophets, and my closest ally from among them is my father and the intimate friend of my Lord, meaning Ibrahim ﷺ . Then he recited: 'Indeed the closest of people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, and this prophet, and those who believe. And Allah is the ally of the believers.'"],[1990,"The people who will receive the most severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."],[1991,"Abdul-Aziz b. Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1992,"Who informed the Prophet ﷺ about the jinn on the night they listened to the Quran? He said..."],[1993,"Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he has killed a disbeliever."],[1994,"I am pleased for my Ummah with what Ibn Umm 'Abd is pleased with for them, and I dislike for my Ummah what Ibn Umm 'Abd dislikes for them."],[1995,"I saw myself as the sixth of six, and there was no Muslim on the face of the earth besides us."],[1996,"O 'Abdullah, there will come after me a people who will delay the prayers from their proper times. 'Abdullah said, 'How do you command me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'O Ibn Umm 'Abd, if you live to see them, there is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to the Creator.'"],[1997,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition, and we traveled at night. I said, 'Would that you alighted so we could rest.' He said, 'Who will guard us?' I said, 'I will guard you.' So they slept, and I slept as they slept until the sun rose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up, performed ablution, and we performed ablution for the morning prayer; then we prayed the morning prayer in the forenoon."],[1998,"The Children of Israel appointed a caliph over them after Musa ﷺ . He stood praying one moonlit night on the roof of Bayt al-Maqdis, and he recalled things he had done. He went out and let himself down by a rope, and by morning the rope was left hanging in the mosque while he had gone. He went on until he came to a people on the shore of the sea, and found them making bricks. He asked them, 'What do you charge for these bricks?' They told him, and he made bricks with them. He ate from the work of his own hands. When it was time for prayer, he stood and prayed. The workers reported to their landowner that among them was a man who did such-and-such. He sent for him, but he refused to come three times. Then he came to him riding on his mount. When he saw him, he fled, and the landowner followed him and overtook him. He said, 'Wait, let me speak to you.' He stood until he spoke to him and told him his story. When he told him that he had been a king and that he had fled out of fear of Allah, he said, 'I think I will follow you.' So he followed him and worshipped Allah until they both died at Rumaylah in Egypt. 'Abdullah said, 'If I had been there, I would have been guided to their graves from the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he described to us.'"],[1999,"'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Qasim b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud."],[2000,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I met Ibrahim ﷺ in the seventh heaven. He said, 'O Muhammad, convey greetings of peace to your Ummah and tell them that Paradise has sweet water and pleasant drink, that within it are level plains, and that the planting of its trees is: Subhan Allah, al-hamdu lillah, la ilaha illa Allah, Allahu akbar.'"],[2001,"'Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq, from al-Qasim b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly, but he did not say 'from al-Qasim, from his father, from 'Abdullah.' We do not know this speech to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this route with this chain of narration."],[2002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us this supplication: 'O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. My forelock is in Your hand. Your command over me is executed and Your decree concerning me is just. I ask You by every name by which You have named Yourself, or which You have revealed in Your Book, or which You have taught to any of Your creation, or which You have kept exclusively to Yourself in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Qur'an the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the removal of my sadness, and the departure of my anxiety.' No one says this except that Allah removes his anxiety and replaces his sadness with joy. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is fitting for us to learn these words.' He said, 'Yes, it is fitting for the one who hears them to learn them.'"],[2003,"If the two parties to a sale disagree and there is no evidence between them, then the word is that of the seller, or they may rescind the sale."],[2004,"The millstone of Islam revolves around thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven (years). If they perish, then the path of one who has perished; and if they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."],[2005,"Al-Qasim b. 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2006,"Al-Qasim narrated to me, from his father, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know that Mujalid narrated from al-Qasim any hadith with a full chain except this hadith, and no one narrated it from him except Sharik."],[2007,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. The people dispersed, and I remained with him among eighty men from the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and they are those upon whom Allah sent down tranquility. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on his mule. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Hand me a handful of dust.' He threw it in their faces, and their eyes filled with dust. The Muhajirun and the Ansar advanced with their swords in their right hands, like blazing fire, and the polytheists fled in retreat."],[2008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'How would you be if a quarter of the people of Paradise belonged to you, and the rest of the people had three quarters of it?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'How would you be if a third of it belonged to you?' They said: 'That would be more.' He said: 'How would you be if half of it belonged to you?' They said: 'That would be more.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my Ummah comprises eighty of those rows.'"],[2009,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about resemblance. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If the man's fluid prevails, the resemblance is dominated; and if the woman's fluid prevails, the resemblance is dominated.'"],[2010,"Mindal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla—who is Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla—from al-Qasim b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from 'Abdullah."],[2011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me placing my left hand on my right hand in prayer, and he said: 'Place your right hand on your left hand.'"],[2012,"If the two parties to a sale differ and there is no evidence between them, the word is what the seller says, or they may rescind the sale."],[2013,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and I said: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you know its interpretation?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'There is no turning away from disobedience to Allah except through Allah's protection, and no strength to obey Allah except through Allah's help.'"],[2014,"'Abdullah b. Khirash b. Hawshab narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Qasim b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and he did not say: from al-Qasim, from his father; he only transmitted it as mursal."],[2015,"If a man honors his brother, he only honors his Lord."],[2016,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought captives, and he began giving them to each household, and he disliked separating them."],[2017,"On the day of Badr I came upon Abu Jahl while iron armor was piled upon him, as if he were a piece of iron. He had been forced to sit down. I took his sword, and he raised his head and said, 'Are you our little shepherd in Makkah?' He said: So I struck him with my sword until he became cold. Then I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have killed Abu Jahl.' 'Aqil, who was a captive with the Prophet ﷺ, said, 'You lie; you did not kill him.' I said, 'Rather you are the liar, O enemy of Allah, you deaf one! By Allah, I have killed him.' He said, 'Then what is his mark?' I said, 'On his thigh there is a ring like the ring of such-and-such,' referring to a mark on his thigh. He said, 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[2018,"None punishes with fire except the Lord of fire."],[2019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey and entered a thicket. A man took the eggs of a red sparrow, and the sparrow came and began fluttering over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Which of you has bereaved this one of its eggs?' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I took its eggs.' He said, 'Return them as a mercy to it.'"],[2020,"You will be granted victory and conquests will be opened for you. Whoever lives to see that should fear Allah, enjoin good, and forbid evil."],[2021,"He cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, its scribe, and its two witnesses."],[2022,"The likeness of the one who helps his people in wrongdoing is like a camel that fell into a well and is trying to pull itself out by its tail."],[2023,"May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed is more mindful than the one who heard it."],[2024,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a red leather tent with about forty men. He said, 'You will be granted victory and conquests will be opened for you. Whoever lives to see that should fear Allah, enjoin good, and forbid evil. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[2025,"Two transactions in one transaction are not valid. He said: And the Messenger of Allah commanded us to perform wudu thoroughly."],[2026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two transactions in one transaction."],[2027,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet."],[2028,"May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed is more mindful than the one who heard it."],[2029,"Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."],[2030,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[2031,"They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun had set. May Allah fill their graves and their homes with fire."],[2032,"You will surely be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."],[2033,"If a man in ʿAdan Abyan intended it with evil, Allah would make him taste a painful punishment—meaning in the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"And whoever intends therein deviation with wrongdoing, We will make him taste a painful punishment.\""],[2034,"Be shy before Allah with the shyness due to Him. He (the questioner) said: We are shy, and praise be to Allah. He said: That is not it. Rather, whoever is shy before Allah with the shyness due to Him should guard the head and what it contains, guard the belly and what it gathers, and remember death and trial. Whoever does that has been shy before Allah with the shyness due to Him."],[2035,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gives the world to those He loves and those He does not love, but He does not give the religion except to those He loves. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no servant submits until his heart submits, and no servant believes until his neighbor is safe from his wrongful acts. They said: What are his wrongful acts? He said: His oppression and injustice. No servant earns unlawful wealth and gives charity from it and it is accepted from him, nor does he spend it and it is blessed for him, nor does he leave it behind his back except that it becomes his provision to the Fire. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not erase an evil deed with an evil deed, but He erases an evil deed with a good deed. The filthy does not erase the filthy. Whoever earns wealth from other than its lawful means and places it in its rightful due, then it is more righteous than that he not deprive the orphan and clothe the widow. Whoever earns wealth from other than its lawful means and places it in other than its rightful due, that is the chronic disease. Whoever earns wealth from its lawful means and places it in its rightful due, then the likeness of that is the likeness of rain falling."],[2036,"The angel has a touch, and Satan has a touch. The angel's touch is promising good and warning against evil, and Satan's touch is promising evil—I think he said—and warning against good."],[2037,"Our beloved and our Prophet—may my father and my soul be his ransom—was announced to us six days before his death. When the parting drew near, he gathered us in the house of our mother ʿĀʾishah and looked at us, and his eyes shed tears. Then he said: Welcome to you, and may Allah give you life, protect you, shelter you, support you, raise you, guide you, provide for you, grant you success, keep you safe, and accept you. I enjoin you to fear Allah, and I entrust you to Allah and appoint Him as successor over you. I am to you a clear warner: do not exalt yourselves above Allah in His servants and His lands, for Allah said to me and to you: \"That is the home of the Hereafter; We assign it to those who do not desire exaltation in the earth or corruption. And the outcome is for the righteous.\" Then he said: Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the arrogant? Then he said: The appointed time and the return to Allah have drawn near—and to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and to the Garden of Refuge, and the fullest cup, and the highest companion—I think he said. We said: O Prophet of Allah, who then will wash you? He said: The men of my household, the closest then the next closest. We said: In what shall we shroud you? He said: In these garments of mine if you wish, or in a Yemeni suit, or in Egyptian white cloth. He said: We said: Who among us will pray over you? We wept, and he wept. He said: Gently—may Allah forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. When you have washed me and placed me on my bier in this house of mine at the edge of my grave, leave me for a while. The first to pray over me will be my intimate friend and companion Jibrīl ﷺ , then Mīkāʾīl ﷺ , then Isrāfīl ﷺ , then the Angel of Death ﷺ with his troops, then the angels—may Allah bless them all. Then enter upon me group after group and pray over me and greet me with peace. Do not harm me with a weeping woman—I think he said—nor a wailing woman, nor a lamenting woman. Let the men of my household begin the prayer over me, then you after them. Convey peace from me to yourselves, and to whoever is absent from my brothers, convey peace from me to him. Whoever enters with you into your religion after me, I call upon you as witnesses that I convey peace—I think he said—upon myself and upon everyone who follows me in my religion from my day until the Day of Resurrection. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who among us will place you in your grave? He said: The men of my household along with many angels who see you from where you do not see them."],[2038,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-Ḥudaybiyyah, and he mentioned that they stopped at soft sandy ground—and dahās means sand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Who will guard us tonight? Bilāl said: I will. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Then you will sleep, or we will sleep. He said: They slept until the sun rose. Some people woke up, among them so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them ʿUmar. He said: We said: Speak up—meaning talk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and said: Do as you used to do. He said: We did so. He said: So do the same for whoever sleeps or forgets. He said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went astray, so I searched for it and found its rope caught on a tree. I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he mounted, and we traveled. He said: When revelation descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, it was hard on him, and we recognized that in him. He said: He withdrew, staying apart behind us. He said: He began covering his head, and it became hard on him until we knew that revelation had been sent down to him. Then he came to us and informed us that it had been revealed to him: \"Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.\""],[2039,"Two camel drivers were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night he slept through the prayer until the sun rose."],[2040,"On the day Allah spoke to Mūsā, he was wearing a woolen jubbah, a woolen cloak, woolen trousers, a woolen cap, and sandals made from the skin of a donkey not slaughtered properly."],[2041,"Indeed you will look at a bird in Paradise and desire it, and it will come to you roasted between your hands."],[2042,"When the verse 'Who is it that would loan Allah a goodly loan' was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us?' He said, 'Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah.' He said, 'Then I have loaned my Lord my walled garden, a garden containing six hundred palm trees.' Then he came walking until he reached the garden, and in it was Umm al-Dahdah with her family. He called to her, 'O Umm al-Dahdah.' She said, 'Here I am.' He said, 'Leave, for I have loaned my Lord a garden containing six hundred palm trees.'"],[2043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his prostration: 'My blackness and my imagination prostrate to You, and my heart believes in You. I acknowledge Your favor upon me; these are my hands and what I have earned against myself,' or 'with what I have earned against myself.'"],[2044,"Many a man in two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath."],[2045,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: 'Amin, Amin, Amin.'"],[2046,"We used to say in the prayer: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed Allah is al-Salam (the Peace), so say: All greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[2047,"Let none of you convey to me anything about any of my Companions, for I love to come out to you with a sound heart."],[2048,"Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal b. Yasaf, from Abu Hayyan, from Abdullah, from the Prophet."],[2049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Recite to me.' I said, 'Should I recite to you when it was revealed to you?'"],[2050,"A group of notables from Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while with him were Suhayb, Bilal, Ammar, Khabbab, and others like them from the weak Muslims. They said, 'O Muhammad, drive them away. Are you pleased with these from your people? Are we to be followers of those whom Allah has favored among us? Perhaps if you drive them away we will come to you.' He said, 'Then this verse was revealed: And warn with it those who fear that they will be gathered to their Lord; for them there is no protector or intercessor besides Him, that they may become righteous. And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. Not upon you is anything of their account, and not upon them is anything of your account. Were you to drive them away, you would be of the wrongdoers.'"],[2051,"Indeed usury, even if it increases, its end is to decrease."],[2052,"Regarding a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister: the daughter receives half, the son's daughter receives one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and what remains goes to the full sister."],[2053,"Minjab narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Mushir, from al-A'mash, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. And we do not know that this statement is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except through this chain, from 'Abdullah from him."],[2054,"He cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who asks to be tattooed, and the woman who extends hair (with false hair) and the one who asks for that."],[2055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined two prayers during travel."],[2056,"A man bequeathed a share of his wealth to a man, so the Prophet ﷺ made it one-sixth for him."],[2057,"You are the nation most resembling the Children of Israel in manner, mark, and guidance."],[2058,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so slept last night until morning. He said: That is a man in whose ears Satan urinated."],[2059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer just as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: \"Attahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu. As-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu. As-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh.\""],[2060,"They are only two: guidance and speech. The best speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ. The worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and everything that is coming is near."],[2061,"I declare myself free to every close friend from his close friendship. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."],[2062,"Indeed, I declare myself free to every close friend from his close friendship. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. But your companion is the close friend of Allah, meaning himself."],[2063,"The Hour will not begin except upon the worst of people."],[2064,"The most truthful speech is the Book of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ. The worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is misguidance. So adhere to this Quran, for it is the banquet of Allah. Whoever among you is able to take from the banquet of Allah, let him do so. Knowledge is only through learning."],[2065,"Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Ali b. al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, similarly."],[2066,"The excellence of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer— that is, alone—is twenty-five, meaning twenty-five prayers."],[2067,"Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah. Hammam also narrated it from Qatadah, from Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah."],[2068,"The congregational prayer surpasses a man's prayer alone by twenty-four degrees, and it is the fifth—all of it is like his prayer."],[2069,"A woman's prayer in her innermost chamber is more excellent than her prayer in her house, and her prayer in her house is more excellent than her prayer in her courtyard."],[2070,"Indeed, the woman is 'awrah; when she goes out, Satan seeks to tempt her, and she is closest to the face of her Lord when she is in the innermost part of her house."],[2071,"Al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. As for the hadith of Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, that the woman is 'awrah, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Hammam."],[2072,"A woman's prayer in her innermost chamber is more excellent than her prayer in her house, and her prayer in her house is more excellent than her prayer in her courtyard."],[2073,"The middle prayer is the 'Asr prayer."],[2074,"Indeed, the woman is 'awrah; when she leaves her house, Satan seeks to tempt her."],[2075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil, and Hal Ata."],[2076,"He used to give the greeting of peace to his right and to his left."],[2077,"The prayer of a group exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-some degrees."],[2078,"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers? He said: Those who withdraw from the tribes."],[2079,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us the sermon of the tashahhud and the sermon of need."],[2080,"In the pre-Islamic era, we used to consider the immaʿa to be the man who is invited and then brings along with him someone who was not invited."],[2081,"Had I taken a close friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr."],[2082,"O God, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and sufficiency."],[2083,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."],[2084,"O God, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well."],[2085,"The best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, the best narrative is the Book of God, the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is an innovation. Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[2086,"Regarding the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'If you had spent all that is on the earth, you could not have brought their hearts together, but God brought them together'—he said: It was revealed concerning those who love one another for the sake of God."],[2087,"They used to recite behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: You have mixed up the Qur'an for me."],[2088,"When a servant of one of you brings him food, let him feed him from it or hand him some of it."],[2089,"The Quran was revealed in seven ahruf. For every verse there is an outward meaning and an inward meaning. And he forbade a man from lying on his back—I think he said: in the mosque—and placing one of his legs upon the other."],[2090,"What is the matter with people who stay away from Jumu'ah? I was about to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go and burn down the houses of those who stay away from Jumu'ah."],[2091,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to Quba and people came to him and began greeting him while he was praying, and he would respond to them with a gesture."],[2092,"Whoever deems permissible its sacred prohibitions has not believed in the Quran."],[2093,"I was shown the land of your migration: a salty ground between two harrahs. Either it was Hajar or it was Yathrib. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Madinah, and Abu Bakr went out with him. I had intended to go out with him."],[2094,"Indeed I love you, were it not for some traits in you. He said: And what are they? He said: Your taking the kunyah Abu Yahya when you have no son, and your claiming affiliation with al-Namir b. Qasit while you are not of them. Suhayb said: As for my kunyah Abu Yahya, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me that kunyah, so I will never abandon it. As for your saying that I affiliate myself with al-Namir b. Qasit while I am not of them, I am from al-Namir b. Qasit, and if I were not of them I would not claim affiliation with them. As for my foreign accent, I was nursed in al-Ubullah, and the foreign accent in my tongue is from that."],[2095,"He recited: 'For those who have done good is the best [reward] and more.' He said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, a caller will call out: 'O people of Paradise, you have an appointment that you have not yet been given.' They will say: 'Has He not whitened our faces and admitted us into Paradise?' It will be said to them: 'You have an appointment that you have not yet been given.' They will say something similar. Then their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them. That is His saying: 'And no dust will touch their faces, nor humiliation.' He said: It means the promise of looking at the face of their Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[2096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the two evening prayers—either Zuhr or Asr. When he said the salam, he turned to us with a smiling face and said: 'Will you not ask me why I laughed?' The people said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'I marvel at Allah's decree for the Muslim servant. Indeed, every decree of Allah for him is good, and not everyone for whom Allah decrees has good in it except the Muslim servant.'"],[2097,"When he prayed, he sat and whispered, and he had not done that before. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Have you noticed what I am doing?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I remembered a prophet who was impressed by the large number of his people. He said: \"Nothing will defeat these people,\" or he said: \"These people will never be defeated.\" It was said to him: \"Give your people a choice of one of three things: either I unleash upon them an enemy from other than them who will annihilate them, or I unleash upon them hunger, or I unleash upon them death.\" He informed his people of that. They said: \"Choose for us, for your Lord has entrusted us to you.\" So he performed ablution and prayed.' Sulayman said: 'They used to resort to prayer in times of fear.' He said: 'O Lord, as for unleashing their enemy upon them to annihilate them, no. As for unleashing hunger upon them, no. But rather death.' Then seventy thousand died in three days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My whispering that you see is that I say: \"O Allah, with You I move; O Allah, with You I charge; O Allah, with You I fight.\"' Sulayman b. al-Mughirah said: 'And there is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[2098,"There was a king among those before you who entrusted a boy of his to a magician to teach him magic. And between the magician and the king there was a monk. The boy came upon the monk and heard his words, and he was impressed by his manner and his speech. Whenever he came to the magician, the magician said: 'What kept you?' He said: 'My family kept me.' And whenever he came to his family, he sat with the monk and was late, so when he came to his family they beat him. He complained to the monk. The monk said: 'If the magician wants to beat you, say: \"My family kept me.\" And if your family wants to beat you, say: \"The magician kept me.\"' While he was in that situation, one day he came upon a huge, fearsome beast that had blocked the people and they could not pass. He said: 'Today I will know whether the monk is more beloved to Allah or the magician.' He said: 'O Allah, if the affair of the monk is more beloved to You—more pleasing—than the affair of the magician, then kill this beast so that the people may pass.' He threw something at it and killed it, and the people passed. He informed the monk of that. The monk said: 'You are better than me, and you will be tested. If you are tested, do not point to me.' The boy used to heal the blind and the leper. He said: And there was a courtier of the king—meaning a man who used to sit with him—who became blind. He heard about him—meaning he heard about the boy—and came to him with many gifts and said: 'Heal me.' He said: 'I do not heal anyone. If you believe in Allah, I will call upon Allah and He will heal you.' So he believed, and he called upon Allah and He healed him. Then he came to the king—meaning the man who used to come to him—and sat as he used to sit. Someone said to him: 'Who restored your sight?' He said: 'My Lord.' He said: 'I am your lord.' He said: 'No, but my Lord is Allah.' He said: 'Do you have a lord other than me?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: And he kept torturing him until he pointed to the boy. So he sent for him and said: 'Has your magic reached the point that you heal the blind and the leper?' He said: 'I do not heal anyone; none heals except Allah.' He said: 'Do you have a lord other than me?' He said: 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' So he also seized him and tortured him, and he did not cease until he pointed to the monk. The monk was brought, and he said: 'Abandon your religion,' but he refused. So a saw was placed on the middle of his head until his two halves fell to the ground. He said to the blind man: 'Abandon your religion,' but he refused. He said: So a saw was placed on the middle of his head until his two halves fell to the ground. And he said to the boy: 'Abandon your religion,' but he refused. So he sent him with a group to such-and-such a mountain and said: 'When you reach the top with him, if he returns from his religion, then leave him; otherwise throw him down from it.' They went with him, and when they ascended the mountain with him, he said: 'O Allah, suffice me against them however You will.' The mountain shook with them, and the boy came walking to the king. He said: 'What happened to your companions?' He said: 'Allah sufficed me against them.' Then he sent him with others to the sea and said: 'If he returns from his religion, then leave him; otherwise drown him.' They took him out to sea, and the boy said: 'O Allah, suffice me against them however You will,' and they all drowned. The boy came walking until he entered upon the king. He said: 'What happened to your companions?' He said: 'Allah sufficed me against them.' Then he said to the king: 'You will not be able to kill me until you do what I command you. If you do what I command you, you will kill me; otherwise you will not be able to kill me.' He said: 'And what is that?' He said: 'Gather the people in one open plain, then crucify me on a trunk, then take an arrow from my quiver, then say: \"In the name of Allah, the Lord of the boy.\" For if you do that, you will kill me.' He said: So he placed the arrow in the middle of his bow, then shot it, then said: 'In the name of Allah, the Lord of the boy.' The arrow fell on his temple, and the boy placed his hand on the spot of the arrow and died. The people said: 'We believe in the Lord of the boy.' It was said to the king: 'Do you see what you were wary of? By Allah, it has befallen you. The people have all believed.' So he ordered trenches to be dug at the mouths of the streets, and fires were kindled in them. He said: 'Whoever returns from his religion, leave him; otherwise throw him into it.' They began pushing one another into it. Then a woman came with her infant son whom she was nursing, and it was as if she hesitated to fall into it. The boy said to her: 'O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth.'"],[2099,"I am Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Suhayb, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And this speech we do not know anyone reporting it from the Prophet ﷺ except Suhayb, and we do not know anyone reporting it except Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Suhayb."],[2100,"We find in the Torah that the Prophet of Allah Dawud, when he finished his prayer, would say: 'O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made the safeguard of my affair, and set right for me my worldly life in which You placed my livelihood. O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. None can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy will not avail him against You.' Ka'b al-Ahbar said: 'Indeed Suhayb the Good informed that Muhammad ﷺ used to finish his prayer with these words.'"],[2101,"Muhammad ﷺ did not come to a town intending to enter it except that he said when he saw it: \"O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people, or from its evil and the evil of what is in it.\" And Ka'b said: Indeed Suhayb narrated this hadith to him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2102,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya.\""],[2103,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I entered upon him while he was in the dwelling of Kulthum b. al-Hadm, and there was dates before them which they were eating. I had inflammation in one of my eyes, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not eat dates with your (affected) eye. I said: I eat from the side of my healthy eye, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed."],[2104,"\"You should use the black seed, for in it there is healing for every disease except al-sām.\" They said: What is al-sām? He said: \"Death. You should use the 'ajwa date, for it is a remedy for every poison. You should use the milk of wild camels, for it is a remedy for every disease.\""],[2105,"\"You should dye with black, for it is more awe-inspiring for you in the hearts of your enemy and makes your women more desirous of you.\""],[2106,"'Abd al-Hamid b. Sayfi b. Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2107,"'Abd al-Hamid b. Sayfi b. Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. And Ziyad b. 'Ubayd Allah omitted al-Daffa' b. Dagfal from the chain. And this hadith we do not know anyone to have narrated it except al-Daffa', and its chain is not strong."],[2108,"\"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[2109,"Sayyar, meaning Ibn Hatim, narrated to us from Ja'far b. Sulayman, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn Suhayb, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2110,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him love Suhayb as a mother loves her child.\""],[2111,"I accompanied the Prophet ﷺ before he entered Madinah."],[2112,"\"A man's prayer in congregation is equivalent to twenty-five times his prayer alone.\""],[2113,"Yazid b. Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet."],[2114,"\"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.\""],[2115,"\"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.\""],[2116,"We were with Uthman b. Affan ؓ, and a man began to praise him, so al-Miqdad began to throw dust in his face – meaning dirt – and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.\""],[2117,"\"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.\""],[2118,"\"O Allah, feed the one who feeds me, and give drink to the one who gives me drink.\" When I heard that, I tightened my cloak, took the knife, and went to the goats, looking and choosing which of them was fattest so that I could slaughter it for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I felt them and found that all of them were full of milk, so I went to a vessel belonging to the family of Muhammad which they had no hope of milking into, and I milked into it until the froth rose above it. Then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: \"Have you not drunk your drink?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, drink.\" So he drank, then handed it to me, and I said: \"Drink.\" So he drank, then handed it to me, and I took what remained. When I knew that the Prophet ﷺ had drunk and I was safe from his supplication, I laughed until I fell to the ground. He said: \"One of your misdeeds, O Miqdad?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my affair was such and such,\" and I told him what I had done. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This was nothing but a mercy from Allah. Why did you not inform me so that we could wake our two companions?\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not care if you and I get some of it, who among the people gets some of it.\" This wording we do not know to be narrated except from al-Miqdad alone, and we do not know any chain for it from al-Miqdad except this chain."],[2119,"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man I met who fought me and cut off one of my hands, then took refuge from me behind a tree and said: \"I have submitted to Allah.\" Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"If you kill him, he is in the same position as you were before you fought him, and you are in the same position as he was before he said the word he said.\""],[2120,"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad came for a need, so we said: \"Sit down until we seek your need for you.\" So he sat down and said: \"I am amazed at a people I passed by who wish for trials, claiming that Allah will test them in them as He tested His Messenger ﷺ and his companions ؓ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The happy one is the one who is kept away from trials, the happy one is the one who is kept away from trials' – he repeated it three times – 'except the one who is tested and is patient.'\" And by Allah, I will not testify for anyone that he is among the people of Paradise until I know what he dies upon, after a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The heart of the son of Adam changes more violently than a pot when it boils.\""],[2121,"\"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.\""],[2122,"Qays narrated to us, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet."],[2123,"\"What do you say about adultery?\" They said: \"It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: \"For a man to commit adultery with ten women is easier for him than to commit adultery with his neighbor's wife. What do you say about theft?\" They said: \"It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: \"For a man to steal from ten houses is easier for him than to steal from his neighbor's house.\""],[2124,"People used to go out for two or three days and defecate like camels defecate. One day, al-Miqdad went out for his need until he came to al-Baqi' – and it is Baqi' al-Gharqad – and entered an old ruin for his need. While he was sitting, a rat came out of a hole and brought out a dinar, and it kept bringing out dinar after dinar until it brought out seventeen dinars. Then it brought out the edge of a rag. Al-Miqdad said: I got up and took it, and I found in it a dinar, so they became eighteen dinars. I went out with them until I brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him their story. He said: \"Did you put your hand into the hole?\" I said: \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth.\" He said: \"There is no charity due on them; may Allah bless them for you.\" No sooner did the last of it end than I saw sacks of silver in the house of al-Miqdad."],[2125,"I do hope for them—meaning his wives—the siddiqun. We said: O Messenger of God, who are the siddiqun? Are they the children of those who die while they are young? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The siddiqun are those who give charity.\""],[2126,"\"He gave the horse two shares and its owner one share.\""],[2127,"\"O God, strengthen Islam with the more beloved of the two men to You: with Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.\""],[2128,"Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya—and I think he said—and do not practice augury, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[2129,"Indeed the believer is rewarded for everything except building in this dust."],[2130,"The Prophet ﷺ performed a prayer and lengthened it. It was said to him: You lengthened it. He said: I prayed a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to punish them with a punishment with which He destroyed those before them, and He granted it. I asked Him not to set on them an enemy who would ravage them, and He granted it. I asked Him not to make them into sects and make some taste the might of others, and He withheld it."],[2131,"\"There will be rulers over you who lie and oppress. Whoever disapproves has disassociated, and whoever hates has been safe, but whoever is pleased and follows\" They said: Should we not kill them? He said: \"No, as long as they establish prayer.\""],[2132,"I was a blacksmith, and al-As b. Wa'il owed me a debt. I went to him to demand it. He said: I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad. I said: I will not disbelieve in him until you die, then live, then die. He said: Do you claim that I will live? Then I will have wealth and children, and I will pay you. He said: Then God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our signs and said, 'I will surely be given wealth and children'? Has he looked into the unseen, or has he taken from the Merciful a covenant? No! We will record what he says and extend for him from the punishment extensively. And We will inherit from him what he says, and he will come to Us alone."],[2133,"We entered upon Khabbab after he had cauterized. He said: Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it."],[2134,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting at the Kaaba, using his cloak as a pillow. He said: You will be helped. And he said: \"Indeed those before you would be combed with iron combs, tearing the flesh from the bone, yet that would not turn him away from his religion.\""],[2135,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting at the Kaaba, using his cloak as a pillow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed those before you would be combed with iron combs, tearing the flesh from the bone, yet that would not turn him away from his religion."],[2136,"I used to make spears for the Messenger of God."],[2137,"Asbat b. Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sa'd, from Abu al-Kanud, from Khabbab."],[2138,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: “And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face.” He said: 'Uyaynah b. Hisn and al-Aqra' b. Habis came and found the Prophet ﷺ sitting with Bilal, 'Ammar, Suhayb, and Khabbab b. al-Aratt among some of the weak believers. When they saw them around him, they looked down on them. So they came to him and had a private audience with him, and said: “We would like you to give us a share of your time so that the Arabs will recognize us through you, for the delegations of the Arabs come to you, and we feel ashamed that the Arabs should see us with these slaves. So when we come to you, dismiss them, and when we have finished, seat them again if you wish.” He said: “Yes.” They said: “Write a document for us.” He called for a sheet to write for them, and he called 'Ali to write for them, while we were sitting in a corner when Gabriel ﷺ descended with this verse: “And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. You are not accountable for them in anything, nor are they accountable for you in anything, that you should drive them away and thus be among the wrongdoers.” Then he mentioned al-Aqra' and his companion, saying: “And thus We have tried some of them by others, that they may say: Are these the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor from among us? Does Allah not know best those who are grateful?” Then he mentioned: “And when those who believe in Our verses come to you, say: Peace be upon you. Your Lord has prescribed mercy for Himself: that whoever of you does evil out of ignorance…” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the sheet aside, and I will never forget him saying: “Peace be upon you.” We drew near to him that day until we placed our knees upon his knee. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sit with us before that, and when he wanted to stand, he would stand and leave us. Then Allah Almighty revealed: “And keep yourself patient with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face, and do not let your eyes pass beyond them, desiring the adornment of the worldly life.” He says: the assemblies of the nobles. “And do not obey one whose heart We have made heedless of Our remembrance and who follows his desire and whose affair is ever in neglect.” As for the one whose heart We have made heedless, he is 'Uyaynah and al-Aqra' b. Habis. And as for “in neglect” (furut), it means destruction. Then He struck for them the parable of two men and the parable of the worldly life. He said: We used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ, and when we reached the hour at which he used to stand, we would rise and leave him until he stood whenever he stood."],[2139,"Was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting anything in the daytime prayer? He said: “Yes.” We said: “How did you know that?” He said: “By the movement of his beard, or his two beards.”"],[2140,"“We emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and our reward fell upon Allah. Among us are those who passed away, and among us are those whose fruit has ripened and he is plucking it.”"],[2141,"I entered upon Khabbab during his illness, and he said: “Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'None of you should wish for death,' I would have wished for it.”"],[2142,"“We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, but he did not alleviate our complaint. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Zuhr at the hottest time.”"],[2143,"“None of you should wish for death.”"],[2144,"“We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, but he did not alleviate our complaint.”"],[2145,"“When you fast, use the toothstick in the morning, but do not use it in the evening, for when the fasting person's lips become dry, he will have light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2146,"Kaysan Abu 'Umar narrated to us, from Yazid b. Bilal, from Khabbab, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know that this wording is reported from Khabbab, from the Prophet ﷺ except through this route with this chain."],[2147,"“Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah—I think he said:—and do not practice tiyarah, and upon their Lord they rely.”"],[2148,"My father went out on a military campaign and left us only a ewe. He said to us: “When you want to milk her, bring her to the people of the Suffah.” So I went with her, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He took her and embraced her—or held her between his legs—and milked a full bowl. Then he said: “Go and bring me the largest vessel you have.” I found nothing but the large wooden dish in which dough is kneaded—I think she said:—and he milked until he filled it. Then he said: “Go, drink, and give drink to your neighbors. And when you want to milk her, bring her to me.” We became prosperous until my father arrived, and my father took her and embraced her and held her between his legs, and she returned to her original milk. My mother said to him: “You have spoiled our ewe for us. She used to milk a full dish like this.” He said: “Who used to milk her?” She said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Do you want from me the blessing of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is greater in blessing than my hands.”"],[2149,"Ibrahim b. Yusuf b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mudrik al-Akhmasi, from the daughter of Khabbab, from Khabbab, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2150,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah, throwing it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble."],[2151,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Muzdalifah, and a bedouin was traveling alongside him, and with him was a beautiful daughter of his whom he had seated behind him. I began to look at her, and the Prophet ﷺ began turning my face and averting it from her. He did not stop the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2152,"He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2153,"He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2154,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice from Jam', and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Quswa."],[2155,"He was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he was reciting the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2156,"The Prophet ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2157,"He did not cease reciting the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2158,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice from Jam', and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2159,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he reached Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2160,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2161,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded the weak among Banu Hashim and their children to depart from Muzdalifah at night, and he said: \"O my little son, do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises.\""],[2162,"That the Prophet ﷺ addressed them during the illness in which he died. He praised and extolled Allah, then said: \"Now then, my departure from among you has drawn near. Whoever I have insulted his honor, here is my honor; whoever I have struck his back, here is my back—let him take retaliation from me.\" Then he said: \"The truth after me is with Umar wherever he is.\""],[2163,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments."],[2164,"That the Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he reached Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, and when he stoned it, he stopped."],[2165,"That the Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[2166,"That the Prophet ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[2167,"Attab b. Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, something similar."],[2168,"That the Prophet ﷺ admonished the people concerning the two rak‘ahs after Fajr and before the Subh prayer. He admonished them, then raised his voice and said: \"Pray before Subh even if only one rak‘ah.\" Then after that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them praying those two rak‘ahs while the iqamah for the prayer was being given, so he said: \"Will you not stop? Two prayers together?\""],[2169,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at ‘Arafah with his hands extended like a beggar seeking food, or words to that effect."],[2170,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to the people on the evening of ‘Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah when they departed, while he was restraining his camel: \"You must be calm,\" until he entered Mina when he descended into Muhassir. Then he said: \"You must use the small pebbles like those thrown for the Jamrah,\" and the Prophet ﷺ gestured with his hand as a person does when throwing small pebbles."],[2171,"When it was the day of ‘Arafah, and al-Fadl was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Ibn Abbas said: \"The people were many around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the people crowded around him, I said: 'Al-Fadl will inform me about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.'\" Al-Fadl said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed with the people, and he began pulling the head of his camel and restraining it, and he kept calling out: 'O people, be calm!' until he reached Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha. Then he spent the night at Muzdalifah until dawn appeared, then prayed Subh there. Then he stood at al-Mash‘ar al-Haram, and the people departed with him until he reached Muhassir. He urged his mount on for a while and kept saying: 'You must use pebbles like those of khudhf (small pebbles).'\""],[2172,"Move away from Muhassir."],[2173,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[2174,"Whoever wakes up in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) during Ramadan, there is no fasting for him. Marwan sent to Umm Salamah to ask her about that, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up junub during Ramadan, then he would perform ghusl and fast.” He sent that to Abu Hurayrah, and he said: “Indeed,”"],[2175,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[2176,"When he prayed the two rak‘ahs of Fajr, he would lie down on his right side."],[2177,"Prayer is two rak‘ahs at a time; you should recite the tashahhud in every rak‘ah, then humble yourself, show reverence, and display neediness; then raise your hands to your ears, then turn them toward your face, and say: “O Lord, O Lord.” Whoever does not do that, it is deficient."],[2178,"Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said: “Your nephew harms us in our gathering place and our mosque, so forbid him from harming us.” He said: “O ‘Aqil, go to Muhammad and call him.” So I went and brought him. He came in the middle of the day, walking through the shade, and sat at the threshold of the door while Quraysh were with Abu Talib. He said: “O son of my brother, your cousins claim that you harm them in their gathering place and their mosque, so stop doing that.” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky, then said: ‘Do you see this sun?’ They said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘I am no more able to abandon that than you are able to bring me a flame from it.’” He said: “Abu Talib said: ‘My nephew has not lied to us, so go back.’” He said: “So they went back.”"],[2179,"He used to perform wudu with one mudd (of water) and perform ghusl with one sa‘."],[2180,"‘Aqil b. Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Hashim, and some people entered upon him. He said: “Will you not congratulate me?” They began to say: “With harmony and sons.” He said: “Do not say that, but say: ‘May Allah bless you, and may He bless upon you.’ Indeed, we were commanded to do that.”"],[2181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about praying in sheep pens. He said: “Pray in their pens and wipe their mucus, for they are among the animals of Paradise.”"],[2182,"The last prayer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us was Maghrib. In the first rak‘ah he recited Sabbih isma rabbika al-a‘la, and in the second Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun."],[2183,"Al-‘Abbas came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was angry. He said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, we go out and see Quraysh talking, but when they see us they fall silent.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, faith will not enter the heart of any person until he loves you for the sake of Allah and for my kinship.”"],[2184,"Al-‘Abbas stood before the Prophet ﷺ while he was angry, and he said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with us and Quraysh?” He said: “What is the matter with you and them?” He said: “Some of them meet each other with radiant faces, but when they meet us they meet us with something different.” He became angry until a vein between his eyes throbbed, then he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, faith will not enter the heart of any person until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.” Then he said: “What is wrong with men who harm me regarding al-‘Abbas? A man’s paternal uncle is the like of his father.”"],[2185,"Two men brought a dispute before the Messenger of God ﷺ. The defendant swore by God, besides whom there is no god. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has forgiven you because of your sincerity.\""],[2186,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ubaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. No one corroborated Shu'bah in this narration of his from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib; they contradicted him in it. Hammad b. Salamah and Jarir b. 'Abd al-Hamid said: from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, from Ibn 'Abbas, that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of God ﷺ. I think this discrepancy came only from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, because his hadith had become confused. 'Ubaydah did not narrate from Ibn al-Zubayr any hadith going back to the Prophet other than this one through a sound chain. He said: I heard Abu Musa Muhammad b. al-Muthanna say: I copied this hadith from the book of Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from 'Ata', from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ubaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet ﷺ, but I did not hear it from him."],[2187,"Every prophet has a close disciple, and my close disciple is al-Zubayr."],[2188,"\"One suckling or two does not make marriage unlawful.\""],[2189,"\"When this verse was revealed: 'Take to forgiveness' [Quran 7:199], the Messenger of God ﷺ was commanded to accept forgiveness from people's character.\""],[2190,"'Umar b. 'Ali narrated to us, from Hisham b. 'Urwah, and that is the correct version."],[2191,"This verse was revealed: 'And when they hear what has been revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflow with tears' [Quran 5:83]. He said: It was revealed concerning the Negus and his companions."],[2192,"\"A lifetime grant is permitted to its recipients.\""],[2193,"\"My front tooth fell out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered me to have a gold tooth made.\""],[2194,"I said to 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr: Tell me who among people most closely resembles the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"Al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ was the closest of people in resemblance to the Messenger of God ﷺ and the most beloved to him. He would come while the Messenger of God ﷺ was prostrating and fall upon his back, and he would not get up until he moved aside. He would come and go under his belly, and he would spread his legs for him until he came out.\""],[2195,"A caravan from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Abu Bakr ؓ said: Appoint al-Qa'qa' b. Ma'bad as commander. 'Umar ؓ said: Appoint al-Aqra' b. Habis as commander. Abu Bakr said: You only intended to oppose me. 'Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. They argued, and the verse was revealed: 'Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet' [Quran 49:2]."],[2196,"When a group from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ each suggested someone as commander: one of them suggested al-Aqra' b. Habis, and the other suggested someone else. Abu Bakr said to 'Umar ؓ: You only intended to oppose me. 'Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. Their voices rose in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet' [Quran 49:2]. Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: After that, 'Umar ؓ would speak to the Prophet ﷺ like a secret confidant."],[2197,"After that, ʿUmar ؓ, when he would narrate to the Prophet ﷺ, would narrate to him like one confiding a secret, not letting him hear until he sought clarification."],[2198,"As for the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken him as a close friend”—meaning Abū Bakr ؓ—he ruled that the grandfather is a father."],[2199,"“Whoever recites the Qur’an by heart or by looking, Allah will give him a tree in Paradise such that if a raven were to hatch in one of its branches and then fly, old age would overtake it before it could traverse its leaves.”"],[2200,"“He is not one of us who does not chant the Qur’an.”"],[2201,"“Fāṭimah ؓ is a piece of me; what angers her angers me.”"],[2202,"“If I were to take a close friend or a vizier, I would have taken Ibn Abī Quḥāfah as a close friend, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave.”"],[2203,"“The one consulted is trustworthy.”"],[2204,"“A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque, for it exceeds it by a hundred.”"],[2205,"“By the Lord of this House, Allah has cursed al-Ḥakam and what he begot upon the tongue of His Prophet.”"],[2206,"“Whoever has his account audited will be ruined.”"],[2207,"“There is no owner of camels who does not pay their due in their tractability and their hardship except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to lie flat for them in a vast open plain, and they will trample him with their cloven hooves. Every time the first of them pass over him, the last of them will be brought back upon him until judgment is passed among the people or he sees his way.”"],[2208,"ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtbah wrote to ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr—who had appointed him over the judiciary of Iraq—asking him about the grandfather. Ibn al-Zubayr wrote back to him that the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken him as a close friend,” made the grandfather a father."],[2209,"He used to say at the end of his prayer when he said the taslim: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent. There is no might nor power except with Allah. We worship none but Him. His is grace and bounty and excellent praise. There is no god but Him, making the religion purely for Him, even if the polytheists dislike it.' He said: And the Prophet ﷺ used to say these words of tahlil at the end of every prayer."],[2210,"Every prophet has a close disciple, and my close disciple is al-Zubayr."],[2211,"Ibn al-Zubayr went out to them on the day of Eid and prayed, then gave a sermon, then said: 'Indeed these are the sunnah of Allah and the sunnah of His Messenger.'"],[2212,"When he sat for the tashahhud, he folded his left leg and set up his right one, placed his right hand on his right thigh, and pointed with his index finger and made a circle."],[2213,"Ziyad – meaning Ibn Sa'd – reported to me from Ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2214,"When he sat for the tashahhud, he folded his left leg and set up his right one, and pointed with his index finger and made a circle."],[2215,"Uthman b. Hakim narrated to us from 'Amir b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to the hadith of Ibn 'Ajlan. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Uthman b. Hakim except 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad."],[2216,"Qaylah bt. al-'Uzza sent to her daughter Asma' bt. Abi Bakr – and Abu Bakr ؓ had divorced her in the Jahiliyyah – and she sent her gifts including dried curd and clarified butter. Asma' refused to accept her gift or admit her into her house. So Qaylah sent to 'A'ishah to ask the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'She should admit her into her house and accept her gift.' And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion.'"],[2217,"This verse was revealed: 'And no one has with him any favor to be repaid, except seeking the countenance of his Lord, the Most High. And he will surely be satisfied' concerning Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."],[2218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped and gave me the blood and said: 'Go and dispose of it.' I went and drank it. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me: 'What did you do with it?' I said: 'I disposed of it.' He said: 'Perhaps you drank it?' I said: 'I drank it.'"],[2219,"He used to point with his staff when he gave a sermon."],[2220,"Quraysh said: 'Indeed the likeness of Muhammad ﷺ is the likeness of a palm tree in a rubbish heap.'"],[2221,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Abu Bakr ؓ and said: \"This is 'Atiq Allah min al-nar (the one freed by Allah from the Fire).\" From that day he was called 'Atiq, whereas his name before that was 'Abd Allah b. 'Uthman."],[2222,"\"Proclaim marriages and beat the sieve for it.\""],[2223,"\"The House is called al-'Atiq only because it was freed from tyrants; no tyrant ever reached it, or no tyrant ever had power over it.\""],[2224,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people who were laughing and said: \"Do you laugh while the mention of Paradise and Hell is among you?\" He said: No one of them was seen laughing until he died. He said: And about them was revealed: 'Inform My servants that I am the Forgiving, the Merciful, and that My punishment is the painful punishment.'"],[2225,"When he broke his fast with a people, he would say: \"May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels send blessings upon you.\""],[2226,"Someone other than Muhammad narrated it from 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from Mus'ab b. Thabit, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet ﷺ, as Ibn Mirdas narrated it from 'Abd al-Wahhab. Muhammad b. 'Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us saying: Sulayman b. 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us saying: Sa'id b. Yahya narrated to us."],[2227,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed 'Isha', he would pray four rak'ahs and perform witr with one prostration, then sleep until he later prayed his night prayer.\""],[2228,"\"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.\""],[2229,"\"Abu al-Qasim ﷺ forbade silk.\""],[2230,"\"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would wish for a second valley to go with it; and if he had a second, he would wish for a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust.\""],[2231,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded fasting on the day of 'Ashura'.\""],[2232,"Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr b. Abi Fakhtah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This wording, we do not know it being narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route. Thuwayr: Shu'bah, Isra'il, and others narrated from him, and they accepted his hadith."],[2233,"Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Subay', from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2234,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be thirty lying dajjals."],[2235,"He forbade nabīdh made in earthen jars."],[2236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabīdh made in earthen jars and gourds."],[2237,"The tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to recite was: “In the name of Allah, and by Allah, the best of names. Greetings, pure words, and prayers are for Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He sent him with the truth as a bearer of good tidings and a warner, and that the Hour is coming, no doubt about it. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. O Allah, forgive me and guide me.”"],[2238,"Hisham b. Urwa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, the freed slave of Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr"],[2239,"He used to say at the end of his prayer, when he said the salam: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. There is no might and no strength except with Allah. We worship none but Him. His is the favor, the bounty, and the beautiful praise, making the religion sincerely His even if the disbelievers dislike it.” He said: “And the Prophet ﷺ used to say these words of tahlil at the end of every prayer.”"],[2240,"“The disease of the nations before you has crept upon you: hatred and envy. Hatred is the shaver; it is not the shaver of hair, but the shaver of religion. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not tell you—I think—what will make that firm for you? Spread peace among yourselves.”"],[2241,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enjoin the use of the siwak.”"],[2242,"“It is not appropriate for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus b. Matta.”"],[2243,"Ya'qub b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il b. Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Abd Allah b. Ja'far, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know this hadith to be reported from Abd Allah b. Ja'far except with this isnad."],[2244,"“He forbade killing the jinnan—I think he said—that are in the houses.”"],[2245,"And al-Qasim narrated to me, from Abdullah b. Umar, something similar. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abdullah b. Ja'far except with this chain. : :"],[2246,"\"It was forbidden to kill them, meaning the jinn that are in the houses.\""],[2247,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating cucumbers with fresh dates.\""],[2248,"I asked Abdullah b. Ja'far about the bequest—that is, did the Prophet ﷺ make a bequest? He said: \"I did not hear of it until I came to this land of yours.\""],[2249,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him, and the two sons of Fatimah or one of the two sons of Fatimah ؓ, on a mount.\""],[2250,"\"Indeed, the hand of Allah is with the debtor until he pays off his debt, as long as it is not in what Allah dislikes.\""],[2251,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done on the top of his head while he was in ihram.\""],[2252,"\"Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them that which preoccupies them,\" or \"a matter that preoccupies them.\""],[2253,"\"The Prophet ﷺ carried two boys from Banu Abd al-Muttalib on a mount.\""],[2254,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating cucumbers with fresh dates.\""],[2255,"\"Prompt your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah.\""],[2256,"When Ja'far arrived from Abyssinia, the Prophet ﷺ came to him and kissed him between his eyes, and said: \"I am not more delighted by the conquest of Khaybar than I am by the arrival of Ja'far ؓ.\""],[2257,"\"O people, repent to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for I repent one hundred times every day."],[2258,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw mercy descending, he said: 'Who will supplicate for me?' His daughter said: 'I will, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Call Ali ؓ.' So Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn ؓ were called. He placed al-Hasan on his right, al-Husayn on his left, and Fatimah in front of him. Then he covered them with a cloak and said: 'These are my family.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification.'"],[2259,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has commanded me to bring you near and not to distance you, and to teach you and not to be harsh with you.'"],[2260,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing two yellow garments."],[2261,"\"Do not take anything with a soul as a target."],[2262,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Uhud, while he was burying Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib ؓ, a striped cloak was brought to shroud him. His feet became exposed, so he covered his head and placed on his feet — I think he said: idhkhir (a kind of grass) — then he buried him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Were it not that our women would grieve for it, I would have left you in the open for the birds and beasts of prey.'"],[2263,"He used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[2264,"That the Prophet ﷺ mentioned the army of the commanders and said: 'Then Ja'far took the banner and was martyred. Then Zayd b. Harithah took it and was martyred. Then Abdullah b. Rawahah took it and was martyred. Then a sword from the swords of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, Khalid b. al-Walid, took it.'"],[2265,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to relieve himself, he liked to conceal himself behind a wall or a cluster of palm trees. He seated me behind him, then went to the base of a wall and concealed himself."],[2266,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing a ring on his right hand."],[2267,"\"He named Madinah Tabah."],[2268,"\"The best meat is the meat of the back."],[2269,"\"The best meat is the meat of the back.\""],[2270,"The people of the Suffah were poor people, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever has food for two should go with three, and whoever has food for four should go with five,” or as he said. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ came with three, and the Prophet of God ﷺ went with ten, and Abu Bakr with three. He said: He is myself, my father, and my mother. He said: I do not know if he said: and the servant of our house and the house of Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr had dinner with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then stayed until he prayed the night prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then returned after as much of the night had passed as God willed. His wife said: What kept you from your guests? Or she said: your guest? He said: Have you not fed them dinner? She said: They refused until you come. They had been offered to them. He said: I went and hid myself. He said: O Ghunthar! He said: He became upset and cursed, and said: Eat! By God, I will never eat it. They said: By God, we will not eat until you eat. He said: He took some, and by God, we would not take a morsel without it growing from beneath it. He said: We ate our fill, and it became more than it was before. Abu Bakr ؓ looked at it, and it was as it was or more. He said to his mother: O sister of Banu Firas, what is this? She said: No, by the delight of my eye, it is three times more than it was before. Abu Bakr ؓ ate from it and said: That was from Satan, meaning his oath. Then he ate a morsel from it, then carried it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it remained with him until morning. He said: There was a pact between us and a people, and the term ended, so they divided us into twelve men, with each man of them—God knows best how many followed each man—except that he was counted, and they all ate."],[2271,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, one hundred and thirty men. He said: “Does anyone of you have food?” He said: It was kneaded. Then a tall polytheist man came with sheep, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “For sale or as a gift?” Or he said: “A grant?” He said: “No, rather for sale.” He said: “He bought a sheep from them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the black of the belly to be cooked. By God, there was not one of the hundred and thirty but the Messenger of God ﷺ cut for him a piece from the black of its belly. If he was present, he gave it to him, and if he was absent, he kept it for him. He said: He made from it two bowls, and we all ate and were filled, and there was extra in the bowl, so he loaded it on the camel."],[2272,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know that anyone narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Amr b. Muhammad."],[2273,"\"That the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him to make Aisha perform Umrah from al-Tan'im.\""],[2274,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said one day: “Who among you has fasted today?” Abu Bakr ؓ said: “I intended it last night and woke up fasting.” He said: “Who has given charity today?” Abu Bakr ؓ said: “I did. A poor person came by, so I entered and found a piece of bread in Abd al-Rahman's hand, took it, and gave it to him.” He said: “Which of you has visited a sick person today?” Abu Bakr ؓ said: “I did. I was told that Abd al-Rahman—meaning Ibn Awf—was sick, so I went and visited him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “These qualities do not come together in a man in one day except that he enters Paradise.”"],[2275,"\"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, gave me seventy thousand of my community who will enter Paradise without reckoning.\" Umar ؓ said: \"Why did you not ask for more?\" He said: \"I asked for more, and He gave me with each—meaning each thousand—seventy thousand.\" He said: \"Why did you not ask for more?\" He said: \"I asked for more, and He gave me with each man seventy thousand.\" Umar ؓ said: \"Why did you not ask for more?\" He said: \"He gave me like this,\" and he spread his arm. He said: \"This is from God, Blessed and Exalted, whose number is not known.\""],[2276,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman: \"Mount your sister behind you and make her perform Umrah from al-Tan'im. When she descends from the hill, tell her to enter ihram, for it is an accepted Umrah.\""],[2277,"Dawud b. Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Yusuf b. Mahak, from Hafsah bt. Abd al-Rahman, from her father, that the Messenger of God ﷺ—then he mentioned something similar. We do not know that Hafsah narrated from her father except this hadith."],[2278,"\"Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is able-bodied and strong.\""],[2279,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, will call the debtor on the Day of Resurrection and stand him before Him. He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'O servant, how did you lose the people's wealth?' He will say: 'O Lord, You know that I did not squander it; it was lost in drowning, fire, or theft.' God, Blessed and Exalted, will call for something and place it in his scale, and his good deeds will outweigh.\""],[2280,"I was in the mosque while Marwan was delivering a sermon. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr said: \"By God, he did not appoint anyone from his family as successor.\" Marwan said: \"You are the one about whom it was revealed: 'And the one who said to his parents, Uff to you both.'\" Abd al-Rahman said: \"You lied. Rather, the Messenger of God ﷺ cursed your father.\""],[2281,"My father narrated to me: I heard al-Hasan relate from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2282,"Al-Hasan b. Abd al-Rahman—meaning Ibn al-ʿUryan—narrated to us from Ibn ʿAwn, from al-Hasan, who said: Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah said: from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2283,"Abd al-Aʿla b. Abd al-Aʿla narrated to us from Hisham b. Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2284,"Jarir—meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid—narrated to us from Mansur b. al-Muʿtamir, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2285,"Yunus b. Ubayd and Mansur b. Zadhan informed us from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2286,"Sharik narrated to us from Simak—meaning Ibn Harb—from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2287,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us from Hisham b. Hassan and Simak b. Atiyya, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2288,"Hammad narrated to us from Humayd and Habib—meaning Ibn al-Shahid—and Thabit al-Bunani, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2289,"Sahl al-Sarraj narrated to us from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2290,"Abd al-Aʿla narrated to us from Saʿid—meaning Ibn Abi ʿAruba—from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2291,"Misʿar narrated to us from Ali b. Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2292,"Awf and Ismail b. Muslim narrated to us from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2293,"Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2294,"Qurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2295,"My father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2296,"Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2297,"Ziyad al-Jassas – who is Ziyad b. Abi Ziyad – informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2298,"Yazid b. Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2299,"\"O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for authority, for if you are given it by asking, you will be left to it; and if you are given it without asking, you will be assisted in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do that which is better and expiate your oath.\""],[2300,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying standing and sitting.\""],[2301,"He used to supplicate, saying: \"O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight, and make them my heir.\""],[2302,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray in his sandals, then he spat, then he rubbed it with his sandal.\""],[2303,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Makkah, Abu Mahdhurah came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to give the call to prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Give the call to prayer.\" Bilal used to give the call to prayer, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, Abu Mahdhurah stayed behind."],[2304,"I fought with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in twenty military expeditions, one after another."],[2305,"The best of the Ansar are the Banu al-Najjar."],[2306,"I met a woman and embraced her, except that I did not have intercourse with her. Then I came to Umar and asked him about it, and he said: Fear Allah and conceal your own fault, and do not tell anyone. He said: I could not bear it until I came to Abu Bakr and asked him, and he said: Fear Allah and conceal your own fault, and do not tell anyone. I could not bear it until I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of it. He said: Have you equipped a warrior for an expedition? I said: No. He said: Have you taken the place of a warrior with his family? I said: No. He said to me something until I wished that I had entered Islam at that very moment. When I turned away, he called me and recited to me: “And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night.” His companions said: Is this for him specifically or for the people in general? He said: Rather for the people in general."],[2307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that dates and raisins be soaked together."],[2308,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: “Hold this,” and he pointed to his tongue. The man repeated the question, and he said: “May your mother lose you! Do people plunge on their faces into the Fire except because of what their tongues reap?”"],[2309,"Indeed, a man prays a prayer and has half of it, a third of it, a quarter of it, a fifth of it, a sixth of it, a seventh of it, an eighth of it, a ninth of it, a tenth of it."],[2310,"Abu al-Yasar saw me while I was praying the Duha prayer when the sun had risen, and he forbade me, then said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not pray until the sun has risen high, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."],[2311,"When you estimate the produce, take and leave a third; if you do not leave a third, then leave a quarter."],[2312,"Whoever gives a man a pledge of safety for his life and then kills him, he will carry a banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."],[2313,"From Amr b. al-Hamiq, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2314,"Whoever gives a man a pledge of safety for his life and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the slain person is a disbeliever."],[2315,"From Amr b. al-Hamiq, from the Prophet."],[2316,"When Allah wills good for a servant, He makes him honey. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what does making him honey mean? He said: “He grants him success to do a righteous deed, then takes his soul while he is upon it.”"],[2317,"\"There will be a trial in which the safest of people—or he said: the best of people in it—will be the western army.\" Ibn al-Hamiq said: \"For that reason I came to you in Egypt.\""],[2318,"The Prophet ﷺ sought forgiveness and prayed for the people of a graveyard in Ashkelon."],[2319,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer in which he recited aloud. When he finished, he said: \"Are you reciting behind me?\" Some of them said: \"Indeed we do.\" He said: \"Do not do so. I say: what is wrong with me that I am contended with regarding the Quran?\" He said: So the people stopped reciting in prayers in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud."],[2320,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not irrigate what another has planted.\""],[2321,"\"Whoever sends blessings upon Muhammad and says: 'O Allah, grant him the near seat with You on the Day of Resurrection,' my intercession becomes guaranteed for him.\""],[2322,"\"Whoever is turned back from something by an evil omen has committed an act of shirk.\""],[2323,"\"I should not be informed that anyone has tied a bowstring or cleaned himself with bones or dung. Whoever does that has disassociated himself from Muhammad ﷺ—or from what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[2324,"\"The last instruction the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me when I led people in prayer was to make the prayer light for them.\""],[2325,"\"Fasting is a shield like the shield of one of you for fighting—or from fighting.\""],[2326,"\"In the night there is an hour in which a caller calls out: 'Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?'\""],[2327,"\"Fasting is a shield with which the servant shields himself from the Fire.\""],[2328,"A client of his bought wine and made a profit from it. Uthman said to him: \"Return it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wine and prohibited its price.\""],[2329,"“I hear the crying of the child, so I shorten the prayer, disliking that his mother be tempted.”"],[2330,"“Whoever has three of his children precede him in Islam has surely been shielded by a thick covering from the Fire.”"],[2331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, mentioning snakes: “Whoever fears their cunning is not of us.”"],[2332,"When the wind blew strongly, the Prophet ﷺ would say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what has been sent in it.”"],[2333,"“The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to place the mosque of al-Ta’if where their idol had been.”"],[2334,"Abu ʿAwana reported to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father."],[2335,"“God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from ill-gotten gains.”"],[2336,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the skins of wild beasts.”"],[2337,"Yazid al-Rishk reported to us, from Abu al-Malih, from his father. Ahmad said: “No one else followed him in raising it from his father. As for the hadith of Matar, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, no one narrated it except Aban, and we know no one who narrated it from Aban except Ishaq b. Idris.”"],[2338,"Shuʿba reported to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, from the Prophet."],[2339,"My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, from the Prophet."],[2340,"“We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a rainy day, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded that it be announced: ‘The prayer is in the dwellings.’”"],[2341,"\"Fast from the appearance [of the new moon] to the appearance [of the next new moon].\""],[2342,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer. He said: I heard him say: \"Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, and Muhammad, protect me from the Fire.\""],[2343,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I enter prayer and I do not know whether I finish on an even or odd number due to my poor memory.\" He said: \"If you find that, place your index finger on your left thigh, for it is from Satan.\""],[2344,"\"The angels descended on the Day of Badr wearing the mark of al-Zubayr, with yellow turbans.\""],[2345,"\"A woman threw a stone at another woman, and she miscarried a dead fetus. The Prophet ﷺ ruled for it a ghurra: a male or female slave.\""],[2346,"\"The just will be on pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection, before the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, because of their justice in this world.\""],[2347,"I said: \"I will certainly fast the day and stand in prayer at night.\" Then I met the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Are you the one who said: 'I will certainly fast the day and stand in prayer at night'?\" He said: I said: \"I did say that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will not be able to do that. So pray and sleep, fast and break your fast. Fast three days every month, for that is like fasting a lifetime.\" He said: I said: \"I can do better than that.\" He said: \"Fast one day and break your fast for two days.\" I said: \"I can do better than that.\" He said: \"Fast one day and break your fast one day. That is the most just fasting, and it is the fasting of Dawud ﷺ.\" I said: \"I can do better than that.\" He said: \"There is nothing better than that.\""],[2348,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2349,"Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar b. Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abdullah b. Amr."],[2350,"\"Fast and break your fast, sleep and stand in prayer. Fast three days every month.\" I said: \"I can do more than that.\" He said: \"Fast one day and break your fast one day; fast the fasting of Dawud.\""],[2351,"I was a man of great effort in worship, then I married. My father came to the woman and said to her: \"How do you find your husband?\" She said: \"What a good man he is, from a good man. He does not sleep and he does not break his fast.\" Then there occurred between me and my father [a dispute]. He said: \"I married you to a Muslim woman, and you did to her what you did?\" I did not care what he said, because of the strength I found, until that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"But I sleep and pray, and I fast and break my fast. So fast, pray, sleep, and stand in prayer. Fast three days every month.\" I said: \"I am stronger than that.\" He said: \"Then fast the fasting of Dawud ﷺ: fast one day and break your fast one day, and read the Quran once every month.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger than that.\" He said: \"Read it in fifteen days.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger than that.\" He kept reducing until he reached seven. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every deed has a period of enthusiasm, and every enthusiasm has a period of slackness. Whoever's slackness is toward my Sunnah has been guided, and whoever's slackness is toward other than that has perished.\" Abdullah b. Amr said, when he grew old and weak: \"If I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, it would be more beloved to me than my family and my wealth.\""],[2352,"My father married me to a woman from Quraysh. When she entered upon me, I think he said: I did not turn to her, or I did not pay attention to her, because of the worship I was engaged in, of fasting and prayer. Amr b. al-As entered upon her and said to her: \"How did you find your husband?\" She said: \"Like the best of men, and like the best of husbands, from a man. He did not uncover any side for us, and he did not approach any bed for us.\" He came to me and bit me with his tongue, and said: \"I married you to a woman of noble lineage, and you did such and such.\" Then he went to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about me to him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ sent for me and said to me: \"Do you fast during the day?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Do you stand in prayer at night?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"But I fast and break my fast, and I pray and sleep.\" Then he said to me: \"Read the Quran in a month.\" He said: I said: \"I find myself stronger than that.\" He said: \"Then read it in fifteen days.\" I said: \"I find myself stronger than that.\" One of them, either Husayn or Mughirah, said: \"Then read it every three days.\" Then he said: \"And fast three days every month.\" I said: \"I am stronger than that.\" He said: He kept reducing for me until he said: \"Fast one day and break your fast one day. That is the best fasting, and it is the fasting of Dawud.\""],[2353,"Shuʿbah reported to us, from Ḥuṣayn, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the ḥadīth of Ḥuṣayn."],[2354,"ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Mubārak reported to us, from Shuʿbah, from Qatādah, from Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, from the Prophet."],[2355,"\"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not look at a woman who does not thank her husband while she cannot do without him.\""],[2356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Juwayriyah on a Friday while she was fasting. He said to her, \"Did you fast yesterday?\" She said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you fast tomorrow?\" She said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then break your fast.\""],[2357,"It is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better than Yaḥyā b. Zakariyyā,' for he never intended a sin— I think he said— nor committed it."],[2358,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and while we were with him, he said, 'A cursed man will certainly enter upon you.' I had left ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ putting on his clothes to catch up with me, and I kept looking and fearing, until al-Ḥakam b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ entered."],[2359,"\"The Hour will not come until you copulate in the roads like the copulation of donkeys.\""],[2360,"\"The Hour will not come until people copulate in the roads like the copulation of donkeys.\""],[2361,"\"Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone, for no one will extract the treasure of the Kaʿbah except the one with thin legs from the Abyssinians.\""],[2362,"\"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was announced, 'The prayer is congregational.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed twice in one prostration, then stood and bowed twice in one prostration— meaning he prostrated once in every two rakʿahs— then the sun became clear.\" ʿĀʾishah said, 'I never prostrated a longer prostration, nor bowed a longer bowing, than that.'"],[2363,"\"A man in Makkah called ʿAbd Allāh will deviate from the truth, upon him is half the punishment of the world.\""],[2364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do not be like so-and-so; he used to stand in night prayer, then he abandoned the night prayer.\""],[2365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Recite the Qur'an in a month."],[2366,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying the two rak'ahs of Fajr when the prayer had already been called—the Fajr prayer—so the Prophet ﷺ said: Al-subḥ is four [rak'ahs]."],[2367,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing. He said: So I came to him and found him praying sitting, so he said: What is the matter with you, O ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr? I said: You told us that the prayer of a man sitting is half the prayer, and you are praying sitting? He said: Yes, but I am not like any one of you."],[2368,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Madinah until, when we were on the road, we came to a people who had performed ablution while their feet were white, gleaming, untouched by water. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Complete the ablution. Woe to the heels from the Fire!"],[2369,"Woe to the heels from the Fire!"],[2370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: The most beloved fasting to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the fasting of Dāwūd—he used to fast one day and break fast one day. And the most beloved prayer to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the prayer of Dāwūd—he used to sleep half the night, stand in prayer a third of it, and sleep a sixth of it."],[2371,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and some returned and some remained. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came before the people called the iqamah for the ʿIshāʾ prayer and said: Rejoice, rejoice! Your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has opened a gate from the gates of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: Look at My servants—they have fulfilled an obligation and are awaiting another."],[2372,"Jarīr b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd reported to us, from Layth b. Abī Sulaym, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr, from the Prophet."],[2373,"Be steadfast, though you will not be able to encompass it all. And know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one guards his ablution except a believer."],[2374,"The transgressing faction will kill ʿAmmār."],[2375,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Quddūs reported to us, from Yūnus b. Khabbāb, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr, from the Prophet."],[2376,"It is near that Allah will fill your hands with non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee, fighting your fighters and consuming your spoils."],[2377,"The one who maintains ties is not the one who recompenses, but the one who maintains ties is he who, when his kinship ties are severed, joins them."],[2378,"The one who maintains ties is not the one who recompenses, but the one who maintains ties is he who, when his kinship ties are severed, joins them."],[2379,"Whoever kills a person from the people of the covenant will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and indeed its fragrance is found from a distance of forty years."],[2380,"When you see my Ummah fearing the wrongdoer to say to him, 'You are a wrongdoer,' then farewell has been bid to them."],[2381,"When you see my Ummah fearing the wrongdoer to say to him, 'Indeed you are a wrongdoer,' then farewell has been bid to them."],[2382,"Indeed in my Ummah there will be sinking, metamorphosis, and casting."],[2383,"Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet."],[2384,"Whoever drinks wine and makes it enter his stomach, his prayer will not be accepted for seven [days]. If he dies during that, he dies as a disbeliever. If it causes him to lose his intellect regarding any of the obligations, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he dies during that, he dies as a disbeliever."],[2385,"Fitr b. Khalifah narrated to us, from Yunus b. Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[2386,"Whoever becomes intoxicated from wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he dies during that, he dies as a worshipper of an idol."],[2387,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ wearing two red garments, and he greeted the Prophet ﷺ, but he did not return the greeting."],[2388,"The drinker of wine is like a worshipper of an idol."],[2389,"Whoever kills a mu'ahad will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and whoever claims descent from other than his father - I think he said - will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance is found from a distance of forty years' travel."],[2390,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; among us were those fasting and among us were those not fasting. The fasting one did not criticize the non-fasting one, nor did the non-fasting one criticize the fasting one."],[2391,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once (for each limb)."],[2392,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet"],[2393,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2394,"Jibril kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[2395,"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays four rak'ahs without being heedless in them, will be forgiven."],[2396,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man wearing a garment dyed with safflower and said: 'What is this?' So Abdullah went and burned it with fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'What did you do with your garment?' He said: 'I burned it.' He said: 'Why did you not clothe someone with it?'"],[2397,"Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abdullah b. Amr"],[2398,"What makes me not love death is the sadiqah. They said: 'What is the sadiqah?' He said: 'A scroll I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2399,"The passing away of the entire world is less significant to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, than the blood of a Muslim person shed without right - or he said - killed without right."],[2400,"The pleasure of the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is in the pleasure of the parent, and the wrath of the Lord is in the wrath of the parent."],[2401,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the Messenger of God prayed two rakʿas with four prostrations."],[2402,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking permission to go on jihād. He said: “Are your parents alive, or one of them?” He said: Yes. He said: “Then go back and devote yourself to serving them.”"],[2403,"“You fast all day and stand in prayer all night?” I said: Yes. He said: “Do not do that, for if you do that your eyes will become sunken and your soul will grow weary. Fast and break your fast, stand in prayer and sleep. Fast three days of the month, for that is like fasting a lifetime. Indeed your eyes have a right over you, your soul has a right over you, and your family has a right over you.” I said: O Prophet of God, I find strength. He said: “If you must do so, then fast the fast of the Prophet of God – meaning Dāwūd ﷺ – he would fast one day and break his fast one day, and he would not flee when he met the enemy.”"],[2404,"“He would not flee when the enemy was met.”"],[2405,"“Have I not been told that you stand in prayer all night and fast all day?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and I intend by that only good. He said: “Do not do that, for if you do that the eye will become sunken and the soul will grow weary. No one who fasts perpetually has fasted. But I will guide you to the fasting of a lifetime: three days of every month, for that is the fasting of a lifetime.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am able to do more. He said: “Then fast five days of the month.” I said: O Messenger of God, I am able to do more. He said: “Then fast ten days.” I said: I am able to do more. He said: “Then fast the fast of Dāwūd: he would fast one day and break his fast one day, and he would not flee when he met the enemy.”"],[2406,"“No one who fasts perpetually has fasted.”"],[2407,"A people were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ who exerted themselves intensely in worship. He said: “That is the fervor of Islam, and every fervor has a lull. Whoever’s lull is toward moderation is not to be blamed, or there is no blame on him; but whoever’s lull is toward sins, those are the ones who are destroyed.”"],[2408,"“Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed people; you will enter the gardens.”"],[2409,"“Two qualities no one counts except that he enters Paradise. They are easy, but those who act upon them are few: a man glorifies God after his prayer one hundred times, and says Allāhu akbar and lā ilāha illā Allāh.”"],[2410,"And how can one not count them, O Messenger of God? He said: “Satan comes to one of you and says to him: ‘Remember such-and-such need, remember such-and-such need,’ until he leaves.”"],[2411,"“Good is abundant, but those who act upon it are few.”"],[2412,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting glorifications on his fingers.”"],[2413,"A man went out walking proudly in the time of ignorance, wearing a fine suit. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded the earth, and it seized him, and he is sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection."],[2414,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah b. Amr."],[2415,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have come to pledge allegiance to you for emigration, and I left my parents weeping.' He said: 'Then go back and make them laugh as you made them weep.' And he refused to accept his pledge."],[2416,"The Jews greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and they said to themselves: 'Would that Allah would punish us.' He said: Then the verse was revealed: 'And when they come to you, they greet you with that with which Allah does not greet you, and say within themselves, \"Why does Allah not punish us for what we say?\"'"],[2417,"\"There was a kid among many sheep; its mother used to suckle it and satisfy it. It slipped away and suckled all the sheep, then it was still not full.\" He said: \"The likeness of this is the likeness of a people who will come after you: a man among them will be given what would suffice a tribe or a nation, then he will not be satisfied.\""],[2418,"\"There was a people among the Children of Israel who had a guest staying with them, and they had a pregnant bitch. The bitch said: 'I will not bark at the guest of my people tonight.' He said: Then her puppies howled in her belly. The Prophet ﷺ struck this as a parable for a people at the end of time, whose fools will overcome their best.\""],[2419,"When a Muslim servant falls ill, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands those who record his deeds, saying: 'Write down for him what he used to do when he was healthy, until I take him or release him.'"],[2420,"Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb b. Jabir, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet."],[2421,"\"It is enough sin for a man to neglect those whom he is responsible to feed.\""],[2422,"We were sitting with Abdullah b. Amr when his steward came to him and said: 'Have you given our family the flour?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then go and give it to them, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[2423,"We entered upon Abdullah b. Amr when he came with Mu'awiyah to Kufah, and he mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'He was neither obscene nor one who used obscene language.' And he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed among the best of you are those with the best character.\"'"],[2424,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina on a she-camel. A man came to him and said: 'I thought that shaving was before the sacrifice, so I shaved before I sacrificed.' He said: 'Sacrifice, and there is no harm.' Another came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I thought that shaving was before the throwing, so I shaved before I threw.' He said: 'Throw, and there is no harm.' He said: 'He was not asked that day about anything that a man had done before or after except that he said: \"Do it, and there is no harm.\"'"],[2425,"Sufyan b. Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa b. Talhah, from Abdullah b. Amr ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2426,"\"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing.\""],[2427,"Abu Muawiyah informed us, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet"],[2428,"\"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not take away knowledge by snatching it away, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars. When no scholar remains, the people take ignorant leaders, so they go astray and lead others astray.\""],[2429,"\"Indeed Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it away, but He takes it away by taking away the scholars. When no scholar remains, the people take ignorant leaders, so they are asked and they give fatwas without knowledge, thus they go astray and lead others astray.\""],[2430,"\"The affair of the Children of Israel remained upright until there appeared among them the sons of captives from the nations, and they gave fatwas based on opinion, so they went astray and led others astray.\""],[2431,"\"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from inability, laziness, senility, cowardice, and miserliness.\""],[2432,"Abdur-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah b. Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[2433,"\"When the sun passes the meridian, the Dhuhr prayer is a catch until the Asr prayer. Then the Asr prayer while the sun is white and clear is a catch until the first horn of the sun sets. When the sun sets, the Maghrib prayer is a catch until the twilight disappears. When the twilight disappears, the Isha prayer is a catch until midnight. When dawn breaks, the morning prayer is a catch until the first horn of the sun rises.\""],[2434,"\"The time of Dhuhr is as long as Asr has not come. The time of Asr is as long as the sun has not turned yellow. The time of Maghrib is as long as the twilight has not disappeared. The time of Isha prayer is until midnight. The time of the morning prayer is as long as the sun has not risen.\""],[2435,"\"When you pray the morning prayer, its time is until the first horn of the sun rises. Then when you pray Dhuhr, its time is until Asr comes. When you pray Asr, its time is until the sun turns yellow. When you pray Maghrib, its time is until the twilight falls. When you pray Isha, its time is until midnight.\""],[2436,"\"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days has not understood it.\""],[2437,"From Qatadah, from Yazid b. Abdullah b. al-Shikhkhir, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ. Muhammad b. al-Muthanna reported it to us from Muhammad b. Ja'far from Shu'bah."],[2438,"\"The Hour will not come until obscenity, severing ties of kinship, and bad neighborliness appear, and the trustworthy is betrayed.\" It was said: O Messenger of God, so how will the believer be then? He said: \"Like a palm tree that falls but does not break, is eaten but does not spoil, and yields fragrance; and like a piece of gold that is put into the fire and taken out, and only increases in quality.\""],[2439,"I said: O Messenger of God, is it from pride that I have a fine garment and wear it? He said: \"No.\" I said: Is it from pride that I have a riding camel and ride it? He said: \"No.\" I said: Is it from pride that I prepare food and invite my companions? He said: \"No. Pride is to reject the truth and belittle people.\""],[2440,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, tell us about emigration: is it to you wherever you are, or to you specifically, or to a known land, or when you die does it cease? The Messenger of God ﷺ was silent for a while, then said: \"Where is the questioner?\" He said: Here I am, O Messenger of God. He said: \"Emigration is that you abandon immoralities, whether apparent or hidden. Then you are an emigrant, even if you die in the town.\" He said: And Abdullah said: A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, tell us about the garments of the people of Paradise: are they created anew or woven? Some of the people laughed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Why are you laughing? At an ignorant man asking a learned one? Where is the questioner?\" He said: Here I am, O Messenger of God. He said: \"The fruits of Paradise will split open for them.\""],[2441,"The Pool was mentioned in the presence of Ibn Ziyad, and he sent for men including Ibn Amr al-Muzani—meaning A'idh b. Amr—and sent for Abu Barzah. He came to him in two cloaks. Ibn Ziyad said: \"This Muhammadite of yours is a short man.\" The old man heard it and said: \"I never thought I would live to be reproached for the companionship of Muhammad ﷺ.\" He said: Ibn Ziyad reclined, and when he was embarrassed by something he would recline. A man said to him: \"The emir called you to ask about the Pool: have you heard the Prophet ﷺ mention it?\" He said: \"Yes, I heard him, and whoever denies it, may God not give him to drink from it.\" Abu Sabrah al-Hudhali said: \"Your father sent me to Mu'awiyah, and I met Abdullah b. Amr, who narrated to me a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ. I understood it and wrote it down with my own hand.\" Ibn Ziyad said to him: \"I adjure you to ride the horse and make it sweat until you bring the writing.\" He said: \"I rode it, took out the page, and brought it to him.\" He said: \"Did you make the horse sweat?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He read the page: \"In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate. This is what Abdullah b. Amr narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: Indeed God does not love the obscene or the obscene-mouthed. Then he said: 'By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, the Hour will not come until obscenity and foul speech, bad neighborliness, and severing of ties of kinship appear, and until the trustworthy is betrayed and the treacherous is trusted.' Then he said: 'The likeness of the believer is like a palm tree: it falls and you eat good fruit, then it drops but does not spoil or break. And the likeness of the believer is like a piece of red gold: it is put into the fire and blown upon, but it does not change or diminish. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the best of martyrs are the just, and the best of Muslims is the one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe, and the best emigration is to abandon what God and His Messenger have forbidden.' And he said: 'Your appointment is my Pool, whose width is like its length, its expanse as between Aylah and Makkah. Its pitchers are as numerous as the stars of the sky. Its drink is whiter than silver. Whoever comes to it and drinks from it will never thirst after it.'\""],[2442,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me and my mother while we were repairing a hut of ours that had become dilapidated. He said: \"What is this, O Abdullah?\" I said: \"A hut of ours that has become dilapidated, so we are repairing it.\" He said: \"O Abdullah, the matter is swifter than that.\""],[2443,"\"Whoever has his head wounded in the way of God and seeks reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[2444,"\"Do not marry women for their beauty, for their beauty may ruin them; and do not marry them for their wealth, for their wealth may make them tyrannical. Marry them for their religion. A black slave woman with a split nose who has religion is better.\""],[2445,"\"Whoever loves a man for the sake of God and says: 'I love you for the sake of God,' both will enter Paradise, and the one who loved will be of a higher station than the other, and will be joined to the one he loved for the sake of God.\""],[2446,"He saw Fatimah, his daughter, and said to her: \"From where have you come, O Fatimah?\" She said: \"I have come from behind the funeral of this man.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Did you reach the outskirts with them?\" She said: \"No, and how could I reach them when I heard from you what I heard?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had reached with them, you would not have seen Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it.\""],[2447,"\"The whole world is but a possession, and there is nothing among the possessions of the world better than a righteous woman.\""],[2448,"\"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, is more protective of the blood of His believing servant than any of you of his valuable property, until He takes him while on his bed.\""],[2449,"Al-Thawri reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Sa'ib, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[2450,"\"He prayed two rak'ahs during a solar eclipse.\""],[2451,"\"There is no believing man or woman who falls ill except that Allah makes it an expiation for their past sins.\""],[2452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer, and when he said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" a man behind him said, \"O Allah, to You belongs abundant, good, blessed praise.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said, \"Who said that phrase?\" The man said, \"I did, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"I saw a group of angels surround it and ascend with it, and I kept watching it until it disappeared from me.\""],[2453,"Whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power or strength except with Allah,\" his sins will be forgiven, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."],[2454,"Hatim b. Abi Saghirah Abu Yunus reported to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, from Abdullah b. Amr ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu Yunus, and he is trustworthy."],[2455,"\"If people did not sin, Allah would create a creation that sins, then He would forgive them. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\""],[2456,"Shu'bah reported to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr b. Maymun, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Muhammad b. Ja'far did not trace this hadith to the Prophet, but Yahya b. Kathir and Shababah b. Sawwar did trace it."],[2457,"\"When the imam has completed his prayer and then has a ritual impurity before he gives the salutation, his prayer is complete.\""],[2458,"\"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, hates the eloquent man who rolls his tongue as a cow rolls its tongue.\""],[2459,"\"When you hear the mu'adhdhin, say what he says, then send blessings upon me, for there is no one who sends blessings upon me once except that Allah sends blessings upon him ten times. And ask Allah for the wasilah for me, for the wasilah is a station in Paradise that is not fitting for anyone except a servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I am the one. Whoever asks it for me, my intercession will be permitted for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2460,"He forbade wine, gambling, the kubah (a type of drum), and ghubayra' (an intoxicating drink), and said: \"Every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[2461,"Killing in the path of Allah atones for everything except debt."],[2462,"Allah decreed the measures fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth."],[2463,"\"Do you know who will be the first of Allah's creation to enter Paradise?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"The first of Allah's creation to enter Paradise will be the poor emigrants, by whom the frontier outposts are manned and through whom misfortunes are averted. One of them dies while his need remains in his chest, unable to fulfill it. The Compeller, Blessed and Exalted, will say to whomever He wills of His angels: 'Go to them and greet them.' The angels will say: 'Our Lord, we are the inhabitants of Your heaven and the chosen of Your creation. Do You command us to go to these and greet them?' He will say: 'They were servants of Mine who worshipped Me and associated nothing with Me, and by them the frontier outposts are manned and through them misfortunes are averted.'\" He said: \"Then the angels will come to them at that time and enter upon them from every gate, saying: 'Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured; and excellent is the final home.'\""],[2464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two gatherings in his mosque. One of the gatherings was supplicating to Allah and seeking His favor, while the other was learning jurisprudence and teaching it. He said: \"Both gatherings are upon good, but one of them is superior to the other. As for these, they call upon Allah and seek His favor; if He wills, He grants them, and if He wills, He withholds from them. As for those, they learn knowledge and teach the ignorant, and they are superior. I was sent only as a teacher.\" Then he sat with them."],[2465,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Teach me to recite, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah said to him, \"Recite three surahs from those beginning with Alif-Lam-Ra.\" The man said, \"I have grown old, my heart has hardened, and my tongue has become thick.\" He said, \"Then recite three surahs from those beginning with Ha-Mim.\" The man said the same as his first statement. He said, \"Then recite three surahs from the Musabbihat (those beginning with glorification).\" The man said the same as his first statement. Then he said, \"Teach me, O Messenger of Allah, a comprehensive surah.\" So he taught him \"When the earth is shaken\" until he completed it. The man said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never add anything to it.\" Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The little man has succeeded, the little man has succeeded.\" Then he said, \"Bring him to me.\" He said to him, \"I have been commanded with the Day of Sacrifice as a festival, which Allah has made for this nation.\" The man said, \"What do you think if I find nothing but a borrowed she-camel to sacrifice?\" He said, \"No, but you take from your hair, trim your nails, clip your mustache, and shave your pubic hair. That completes your sacrifice before Allah, Blessed and Exalted.\""],[2466,"The hearts of all the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted; He turns them wherever He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, Turner of the hearts, turn our hearts to Your obedience.\""],[2467,"My basin is a month's journey, its water is whiter than milk, its fragrance is more pleasant than musk, and its cups are like the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst thereafter, or after that, ever."],[2468,"Whoever kills a sparrow without its right, Allah will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said, \"What is its right?\" He said, \"He slaughters it properly and does not take it by the neck and cut it off.\""],[2469,"\"How do you fast?\" I said, \"I fast and do not break the fast.\" He said, \"Fast and break the fast; fast three days of the month.\" I said, \"Give me more, O Messenger of Allah, for I have strength.\" He said: I kept bargaining with him and he kept bargaining with me until he said, \"Fast the most beloved fast to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, the fast of Dawud; he used to fast one day and break the fast one day.\" When Abdullah grew old, he said, \"If I had ended at what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, it would be dearer to me than what the sun rises upon, but I do not abandon an obligation that the Messenger of Allah has made obligatory upon me.\""],[2470,"Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Ata' b. Farrukh, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2471,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Fast one day and you will have ten days' reward.\" He said, \"Give me more, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Fast two days and you will have nine days' reward.\" He said, \"Give me more, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Fast three days and you will have eight days' reward.\""],[2472,"\"This verse was not revealed - 'Indeed, the criminals are in error and madness. On the Day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces, \"Taste the touch of Saqar.\" Indeed, We have created all things by measure' - except concerning the people of qadar (those who deny divine decree).\""],[2473,"Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,' a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."],[2474,"Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks it a fourth time and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will not accept his repentance, and it will be a duty upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to give him to drink from the spring of khabal, or the river of khabal.\" It was said: \"And what is the spring of khabal or the river of khabal?\" He said: \"The pus of the people of Hell."],[2475,"He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should I write down what I hear from you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I said: What you say in pleasure and anger?\" He said: \"Yes, for I do not say in that regard any word except the truth.\""],[2476,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I gave my mother a garden during her lifetime, and she has died leaving no heir other than me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—I think he said—: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has returned to you your garden and accepted your charity.\""],[2477,"\"There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation before ownership,\" or he said: \"No emancipation except after ownership.\""],[2478,"\"Indeed, a man among those before you would have between his shoulders a measure of a mile.\""],[2479,"\"Indeed, a man among those before you would reach eighty years before having a wet dream.\""],[2480,"\"The angels were created from light.\""],[2481,"\"Indeed, the son of Adam who killed his brother will share equally with the people of Hell half of their punishment, an exact division.\""],[2482,"\"There is no creation of Allah more numerous than the angels; He creates them like flies, then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'Be a thousand, two thousand.'\""],[2483,"\"There will come upon Hell a time when its gates will flap, with no one in it.\""],[2484,"Two qualities, whoever guards them will enter Paradise; they are easy, but those who act upon them are few: You praise Allah, exalt Him, and glorify Him after every prescribed prayer ten times each, and when you retire to your bed you glorify Allah, praise Him, and exalt Him one hundred times. That is two hundred and fifty on the tongue, and two thousand five hundred in the balance. Which of you commits two thousand five hundred sins in a day and night?\" They said: \"How is it that those who act upon them are few?\" He said: \"Satan comes to one of you during his prayer and reminds him of such-and-such need, so he does not say them; and he comes to him at his sleep and puts him to sleep, so he does not say them.\""],[2485,"A man came to the prayer and said: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who said it?' The man said: 'I did.' He said: 'I saw the angels passing it to one another.'"],[2486,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Trumpet, and he said: 'It is a horn into which it is blown.'"],[2487,"Khallad b. Yahya reported to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr b. Shaghaf, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2488,"'Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents.' They said: 'How does he revile his parents?' He said: 'A man reviles another man's father, so he reviles his father, and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother.'"],[2489,"'O Abdullah b. Amr, how will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become disordered, and they have differed and become thus?'—and he interlaced his fingers. He said: 'What should I do, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Take—I think he said—what you recognize and leave what you reject, and keep to your private affairs and beware of their common folk.'"],[2490,"I heard Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Bilal mention, from Isa b. Abdullah, from Ubayd Allah b. Amr, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Uqba b. Aws, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith is reported from Abdullah b. Amr through several routes, and we do not know of a chain better than the chain of Uqba b. Aws, from Abdullah b. Amr."],[2491,"I came to Abdullah b. Amr in his house while two rows of people sat around him, and no one was on his bed, so I sat on his bed at the side of his feet. A red-faced, big-bellied man came and sat down. He said: 'Who is the man?' I said: 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakra.' He said: 'Who is Abu Bakra?' I said: 'Do you not remember the man who leaped to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the wall of al-Ta'if?' He said: 'Yes,' and welcomed me. Then he began to narrate to us, saying: 'Soon will emerge the son of the lamb's carrier'—three times. I said: 'What is the lamb's carrier?' A man said: 'One of his parents is a devil who rules the Byzantines. He will come with a million people, five hundred thousand on land and five hundred thousand at sea. They will land at a place called al-Amiq. He will say to his companions: \"I still have some of your ship left,\" so he will stay behind with it and burn it with fire. Then he will say: \"No Byzantium and no Constantinople; they are yours. Whoever wishes to flee, let him flee.\" The Muslims will reinforce one another until the people of Aden Abyan reinforce them. The Muslims will say to them: \"Join them and be a single group.\" They will fight for a month until the horses wade in blood up to their hooves. On that day, the believer will have a double reward compared to what came before him, except for the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. On the last day of the month, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: \"Today I will draw My sword, support My religion, and take vengeance on My enemy.\" Allah will turn the tide against them and defeat them, until Constantinople is conquered. Their commander will say: \"No embezzlement today.\" While they are thus dividing gold and silver with their shields, a call will come to them: \"Indeed, the Dajjal has succeeded you in your homes.\" So they will leave what is in their hands and head toward the Dajjal.'"],[2492,"In Paradise there is a palace called Adan, surrounded by towers and meadows. It has five thousand gates, and at each gate are five thousand enclosures. None enters it or dwells in it except a prophet, a truthful one, a martyr, or a just ruler."],[2493,"The dust has not carried, nor the green canopy shaded, a man more truthful than Abu Dharr."],[2494,"I went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and two men differed over a verse, and their voices rose. The Prophet ﷺ heard the sound, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out—I think he said: with anger recognizable on his face—and said: 'Indeed, those before you were destroyed only by their differences over the Book.'"],[2495,"Qays reported to us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Sabit, from Abdullah b. Amr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Muawiya, and he was his scribe."],[2497,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[2498,"I said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr: I have heard that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever drinks a sip of wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings.\" He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever drinks a sip of wine, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents—al-Awza'i said: I do not know whether in the third or fourth—it will be binding upon Allah to give him to drink from the mud of khabal or the pus of khabal."],[2499,"We descended with the Prophet ﷺ from the mountain pass of al-Adhakhir. The Prophet ﷺ looked and saw upon me a thin mantle dyed with saffron. He said: \"What is this?\" I realized that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked it. I went to my family while they were heating their oven, wrapped it up, threw it in, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"What happened to the mantle?\" I said: I knew that you disliked it, O Messenger of Allah, so I went to my family while they were heating their oven and threw it in. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not clothe some of your family with it?\" He said: And he mentioned that when he descended from the mountain pass of al-Adhakhir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with them facing a wall that he took as a qiblah. A young sheep came wanting to pass in front of the Prophet ﷺ. He kept drawing near and warding it off until I saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching the wall, and it passed behind him."],[2500,"Whoever says in a day one hundred times: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable,' no one before him will surpass him, and no one after him will overtake him except one who brings something better than his deed."],[2501,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and 'Umar came in a group of people, and their voices had risen. Abu Bakr sat near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and 'Umar sat near. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why did your voices rise?\" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr said: Good deeds are from Allah and evil deeds are from ourselves. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What did you say, O 'Umar?\" He said: I said: Good deeds and evil deeds are from Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The first to speak about this were Jibril and Mika'il. Mika'il said what you said, O Abu Bakr, and Jibril said what you said, O 'Umar. They said: Shall we differ, and then the people of heaven differ? If the people of heaven differ, the people of earth will differ. They referred the matter to Israfil, and he judged between them that good deeds and evil deeds are from Allah. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: \"Preserve my judgment between you two: if Allah had willed that we not disobey, He would not have created Iblis.\""],[2502,"I said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr: What is the worst thing you saw Quraysh inflict upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in their open enmity? He said: I was present when their nobles gathered one day in the Hijr. They mentioned and said: We have never seen anyone like the patience we have shown regarding this man's affair. He has belittled our dreams, insulted our forefathers, criticized our religion, and divided our community. We have been patient with him over a great matter. While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward and walked until he touched the corner. When he passed by them, they winked at him, and I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he passed by them the second time, they winked at him similarly, and I recognized that in his face. He passed by them the third time, and they winked at him similarly. Then he said: \"Listen, O assembly of Quraysh! By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I have brought you slaughter.\" He said: The people were seized with gloom, so that there was not a man among them but a bird was perched on his head. Even the severest of them against him before that would meet him with the best words he could find, saying: Depart, O Abu al-Qasim, depart rightly guided. By Allah, you were not ignorant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed. When it was the next day, they gathered and I was with them. They said to one another: You mentioned what he had reached of you and what reached you from him, until when he came to you with what you dislike, you left him. While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared. They said: Rise against him as one man. They kept saying: You are the one who says such and such about our gods—referring to what had reached them of his criticism of their gods. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: \"Yes, I am the one who says that.\" He said: I saw a man among them seize the collar of his cloak. He said: Abu Bakr stood in his defense, weeping and saying: \"Would you kill a man for saying, 'My Lord is Allah'?\" Then they turned away from him. That was the worst I ever saw Quraysh do to him ﷺ."],[2503,"He was compelled to eat, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The people who are fullest in this world will be the longest hungry in the Hereafter. O Sulayman, the world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise.\""],[2504,"\"Go, O Salman, and when you finish, let me know and I will be with you; I will plant them with my own hand.\" So I prepared the holes for them, and my companions helped me until when I finished, I came to him and told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with me to them, and we brought the young palm shoots near to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ planted them with his own hand until we finished. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Salman, not a single palm tree among them died. I paid off the palms, and the money remained due. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought something like a chicken's egg of gold from some mines. He said: \"What has the Persian slave who has a contract of manumission done?\" I was called to him, and he said: \"Take this and pay what you owe with it, O Salman.\" I said: Where will this fall, O Messenger of Allah, against what I owe? He said: \"Take it, for Allah will pay on your behalf with it.\" I weighed for him from it, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Salman, forty uqiyyahs, and I paid them their due. Salman became free, and I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Battle of the Trench; then no expedition with him ever missed me."],[2505,"Whoever gives a fasting person food and drink from what is lawful, the angels pray for him during the hours of the month of Ramadan, and Jibril ﷺ shakes his hand on the Night of Qadr and greets him. Whoever Jibril shakes his hand on the Night of Qadr is granted tears and tenderness.\" Salman said: If he cannot afford his own food, he said: \"With a piece of bread, or a sip of milk, or a drink of water, he will have this.\""],[2506,"Some of the polytheists said to him, mocking: \"Your companion has taught you everything, even how to defecate.\" Salman said: \"Yes, he commanded us not to face the qiblah, not to clean ourselves with our right hands, and not to be satisfied with less than three stones that contain no dung or bone.\""],[2507,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, does it thoroughly, purifies himself, applies perfume from his family's perfume, goes out to the Friday prayer, does not separate between two people, then prays whatever is decreed for him until the imam comes out, will be forgiven what is between that and the next Friday."],[2508,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the turban and the leather socks,\" or he said, \"the head-covering and the leather socks.\""],[2509,"Abu Mu'awiyah reported to us, from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from Abu 'Uthman, from Salman."],[2510,"Verily, when Allah created the heavens and the earth, He created one hundred mercies. Of these, one mercy He divided among the creatures, and He kept back ninety-nine with Him until the Day of Resurrection."],[2511,"When a Muslim performs wudu' and does it well, then prays the five prayers, his sins fall away just as these leaves fall away.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with evil deeds.'"],[2512,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about locusts, and he said: 'The largest of Allah's armies. I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.'"],[2513,"Al-Taymi reported to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah said:"],[2514,"Verily, Allah is modest and generous. He is ashamed when a servant raises his hands to Him to turn them away empty."],[2515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to visit a man from the Ansar. When he entered upon him, he placed his hand on his forehead and said: 'How do you find yourself?' The man gave him no answer, so it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he is distracted from you.' He said: 'Leave me alone with him.' The women left him, and left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hand, and the sick man gestured: 'Return your hand to where it was.' Then he called him: 'O so-and-so, what do you find?' He said: 'I find myself well. Two beings have come to me, one black and the other white.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Which of them is closer to you?' He said: 'The black one.' He said: 'Verily, good is little, and evil is much.' He said: 'Then give me the benefit of a supplication from you, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, forgive the much, and increase the little.' Then he said: 'What do you see?' He said: 'Good, may my father and mother be your ransom. I see the good increasing, and I see the evil fading away, and the black one has withdrawn from me.' He said: 'Which of your deeds was most controlling over you?' He said: 'I used to give water to drink.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Listen, O Salman, do you find anything strange in me?' He said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. I have seen you in many situations, but I have never seen you in a state like today.' He said: 'I know what he is facing. There is not a vein in him but it is suffering the pain of death on its own.'"],[2516,"O Salman, do not hate me, lest you depart from your religion. He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I hate you when through you Allah guided us?' He said: 'You hate the Arabs, and so you hate me.'"],[2517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to put ourselves to trouble for a guest with what we do not have."],[2518,"I came to Salman, and he brought me bread and salt, and said: 'Were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to put ourselves to trouble for a guest with what we do not have, I would have put myself to trouble for you.'"],[2519,"Burd reported to us, from Sulayman b. Musa, from Shurahbil b. al-Simt, from Salman."],[2520,"Ribat for one day in the path of Allah is better than fasting for a month."],[2521,"That a man never did any good at all, so he said: 'When I die, burn me.'"],[2522,"I read in the Torah: 'Among the blessings of food is ablution before it.' He said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Among the blessings of food is ablution before it, and ablution after it.'"],[2523,"Yahya b. Durays reported to us, from Qays, from Abu Hashim, from Zadhan, from Salman, and he mentioned something similar."],[2524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Ali: 'One who loves you loves me, and one who hates you hates me.'"],[2525,"I had a nosebleed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered me to perform a fresh ablution."],[2526,"God, Blessed and Exalted, said to the son of Adam: 'O son of Adam,' three times: 'One is for Me, one is for you, and one is between Me and you. As for the one that is for Me: you worship Me without associating anything with Me. As for the one that is for you: whatever deed you do, I will reward you for it; if I forgive, then I am the Forgiving, the Merciful. As for the one between Me and you: from you is supplication and asking, and upon Me is response and giving.'"],[2527,"A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds that he thinks will save him, but a man whom he wronged will keep standing up, and it will be taken from his good deeds and given to the wronged one, until no good deed remains for him. Then someone whom he wronged will come while none of his good deeds remain, and it will be taken from the wronged one's evil deeds and placed upon his evil deeds."],[2528,"The Messenger of God said to me."],[2529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'O Salman, do you know what Friday is?' I said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Do you know what Friday is?' three times — I do not know whether he mentioned the fourth time or not in the hadith of al-Mughirah — he said: 'It is the day on which your father gathered. I will first tell you your hadith about Friday: No Muslim performs ablution on Friday, then comes to the Friday prayer and remains silent until the imam finishes his prayer, but it will be an expiation for him for what is between that Friday and the following Friday, as long as major sins are avoided.'"],[2530,"Guarding the frontier for a day and a night in the path of God is like fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever — meaning dies while guarding — the reward of the one guarding will continue for him until he is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be safe from the trial, and his provision will be cut out for him from Paradise."],[2531,"Three will not enter Paradise: the elderly adulterer, the lying imam, and the arrogant poor person."],[2532,"When one of you marries a woman and it is the wedding night, let him pray two rak'ahs and let him order her to pray two rak'ahs behind him, for God will place good in the household."],[2533,"Whoever says: 'O Allah, I call upon You to witness, and I call upon Your angels, the bearers of Your Throne, and whoever is in the heavens to witness, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, with no partner; and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger.' Whoever says it once, one third of him is freed from the Fire; whoever says it twice, two thirds of him are freed from the Fire; and whoever says it three times, all of him is freed from the Fire."],[2534,"I am only a human being, and I become angry as you become angry. So any servant whom I have insulted, cursed, or supplicated against not in accordance with his due, make it a prayer and a mercy for him."],[2535,"Al-Husayn b. 'Ali reported to us from Za'ida, from 'Umar b. Qays, from 'Amr b. Abi Qurra, from Salman, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2536,"\"I was one of the sons of the leaders of Persia.\""],[2537,"I asked Salman al-Farisi about the tashahhud. He said: I will teach you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me. Then he took my hand and taught me the tashahhud word by word: The greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he said: 'O Salman, say it in your prayer, and do not add a word to it or omit a word from it.'"],[2538,"\"Whoever takes servant women other than those he marries, and then they commit adultery, then upon him is the like of their sins, without any of their sins being reduced.\""],[2539,"I asked Salman about the statement of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, 'That is because among them are qissisun and ruhban' (Quran 5:82). He said: Leave the qissisun in the churches and ruins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to me: 'That is because among them are siddiqun and ruhban.'"],[2540,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed. He said: 'Is there not a man who will give charity to this one by praying with him?'"],[2541,"What do you consider a martyr among you? They said: Being killed in the path of Allah. He said: 'Then the martyrs of my community are few. Being killed is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom—and I think he said—and a woman whom her child kills in her womb is martyrdom.'"],[2542,"Nothing repels divine decree except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness."],[2543,"If you can, do not be the first to enter the market or the last to leave it, for it is the battleground of Satan, and there he sets up his banner."],[2544,"Do not single out Friday for fasting or its night for night prayer."],[2545,"Allah said: \"When My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length; and when he draws near to Me an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him at a run.\""],[2546,"Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays.\" They left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ feeling heavy-hearted. Ali met them and said: \"Why do I see you two heavy-hearted?\" They said: \"A hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he makes a promise he breaks it.'\" Ali said: \"Why did you not ask him?\" They said: \"We were in awe of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"But I will ask him.\" He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Abu Bakr and Umar met me, and they were heavy-hearted,\" then he mentioned what they had said. He ﷺ said: \"I indeed told them that, but I did not put it in the place they put it. Rather, the hypocrite is the one who, when he speaks, tells himself that he is lying; when he promises, tells himself that he will break it; and when he is entrusted, tells himself that he will betray.\""],[2547,"Salman besieged a fortress among the fortresses of Qudayd. He said to his companions: \"Let me do what I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\" He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"I am a man from among you, and Allah has granted me Islam. You have seen the Arabs' obedience to me. If you believe and emigrate, you will have the same status as us. If you accept Islam but remain in your lands, you will be like the Bedouins: you will receive what they receive and bear what they bear. If you refuse and agree to pay the jizyah, you will have what the people of the jizyah have.\" He presented that to them for three days, then said to his companions: \"Advance against them,\" and they conquered it."],[2548,"Salman wrote to Abu al-Darda': \"O my brother, keep to the mosque and adhere to it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The mosque is the home of every pious person.'\""],[2549,"Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar."],[2550,"When Hafsah became widowed from Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi, one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ who had witnessed Badr and died in Madinah, Umar said: \"I met Uthman b. Affan and offered Hafsah to him, saying: 'If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsah bint Umar.' He said: 'I will consider my situation.' I waited some nights, then he met me and said: 'I do not want to marry at this time.' Then I met Abu Bakr and said: 'If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsah bint Umar.' Abu Bakr remained silent and did not give me any reply. I was more upset with him than with Uthman. I waited some nights, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, and I married her to him. Abu Bakr ؓ met me and said: 'Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsah to me and I did not reply?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Nothing prevented me from replying to your offer except that I already knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had mentioned Hafsah, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had he left her, I would have accepted her or married her.'\""],[2551,"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity."],[2552,"Sufyan b. Uyaynah informed us, from Amr b. Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet."],[2553,"\"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment).\""],[2554,"Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Aziz b. Rufay', from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet."],[2555,"Abd al-Rahman b. Sharik informed us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet."],[2556,"\"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment).\""],[2557,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[2558,"Isma'il b. 'Abd al-Malik reported to us, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas; and he said once: from 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufay', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd."],[2559,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[2560,"My father narrated to me, from 'Amir al-Ahwal, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2561,"Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah reported to us, from Kathir b. Shindhir, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2562,"'Ali b. al-Mubarak reported to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2563,"My father narrated to me, from Dawud b. Abi al-Furat, from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2564,"Abu 'Asim reported to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2565,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[2566,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[2567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed inside the House. He said: I said: How many (rak'ahs) did he pray? He said: He did not tell me how many he prayed."],[2568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us walking between Usamah b. Zayd and Bilal until he entered the Ka'bah. Inside it there was a piece of wood placed across. When Usamah b. Zayd came out, I asked him: What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do? He said: He left two-thirds of the wood on his right and prayed in the remaining third on his left. I said: How many (rak'ahs) did he pray? He said: I did not ask Bilal."],[2569,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[2570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked out over one of the fortresses of Madinah and said: 'Do you see what I see? Truly I see trials (fitan) [falling] among your houses like the falling of rain drops.'"],[2571,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to make a raid on Ubna in the morning, then to burn."],[2572,"The Messenger of God ﷺ rode a donkey with a packsaddle, and under him was a Fadakiyyah velvet cloth. He seated me behind him. He was going to visit Sa'd b. 'Ubadah in the [neighborhood of] Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and that was before the Battle of Badr. He passed by a gathering in which there was a mix of Muslims, idol-worshipping polytheists, and Jews, and among them were 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul and 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah. When the dust of the animal enveloped the gathering, 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy covered his nose with his cloak, then said: 'Do not raise dust on us.' The Prophet ﷺ greeted, then stopped and dismounted. He called them to God and recited the Qur'an to them. 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy said to him: 'O man, there is nothing better than this if what you say is true. So do not annoy us in our gatherings; return to your camp. Whoever of us comes to you, narrate to him.' 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah said: 'Rather, come to us in our gatherings, for we love that.' Then the Muslims, the polytheists, and the Jews began insulting one another until they were about to attack each other. The Prophet ﷺ kept calming them down. Then he mounted his animal and went to Sa'd b. 'Ubadah. He said: 'O Sa'd, did you not hear what Abu Hubab said?'—meaning 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy—'He said such-and-such.' Sa'd said: 'Pardon him, O Messenger of God, and overlook. For by God, God has given you what He has given you. The people of this lake had agreed to crown him and tie the headband on him, but when God rejected that with the truth that He gave you, he choked on it. That is why he did what you saw.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ pardoned him."],[2573,"Ya'qub b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd reported to us, from his father, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwa, from Usamah, from the Prophet."],[2574,"As for the hadith of Shu'ayb, Ibrahim b. Hani' and 'Umar b. al-Khattab reported it to us, both saying: Abu al-Yaman reported to us, from Shu'ayb, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwa, from Usamah, from the Prophet."],[2575,"And I heard one of our companions—he is Isma'il b. Ishaq—mention it from Isma'il b. Abi Uways, from his brother, from Sulayman b. Bilal, from Ibn Abi 'Atiq—he is Muhammad b. Abi 'Atiq—from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwa, from Usamah, from the Prophet ﷺ. And we do not know that this speech was reported connected from the Prophet ﷺ except from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from 'Urwa, from Usamah."],[2576,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy during the illness in which he died: 'I had forbidden you from loving the Jews.'"],[2577,"'Abd Allah b. Ubayy said: 'If we return to Madinah, the more mighty will surely expel the more lowly from it.' He said: Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah said: 'By God, you will not enter until you say: Muhammad is the mighty one, and you are the lowly one—or: you are the humiliated one.' He said: Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah asked permission to kill his father, but he said: 'Let not people say that Muhammad kills his companions.'"],[2578,"Usamah b. Zayd was asked about the Prophet's ﷺ journey from 'Arafat to Muzdalifah (Jam'). He said: 'He would travel at a brisk pace, and when he found an open space he would urge his mount faster.'"],[2579,"'If you hear of an outbreak of plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it.'"],[2580,"The Prophet ﷺ combined the two prayers at Muzdalifah (Jam') with one iqamah—meaning that he gave the adhan and iqamah for Maghrib, and then gave the iqamah for 'Isha', and he did not perform any voluntary prayer between them."],[2581,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ became gravely ill, I descended, and the people descended with me. I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he had been silenced, so he was not speaking. He began raising his hand toward the sky, then placing it upon me, so I knew that he was supplicating for me."],[2582,"Musa b. Uqbah reported to us, from Ibn Usamah b. Zayd, from his father — meaning Muhammad b. Usamah."],[2583,"The Messenger of God ﷺ clothed him with a Qibtiyyah garment, so he clothed his wife with it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What did you do with the Qibtiyyah?\" He said: \"I clothed the woman with it.\" He said: \"Order her to put an undergarment beneath it so that it does not describe the size of her bones.\""],[2584,"I knocked on the Messenger of God ﷺ's door one night for some need, and he came out to me wrapped in something I did not know what it was. When I finished my need, I said: \"What is this that you are wrapped in?\" Then behold, Hasan and Husayn were on his hips. He said: \"O God, You know that I love them, so love them\" three times."],[2585,"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim."],[2586,"We shall stop tomorrow, God willing, at the Khayf of Banu Kinanah where they swore together over disbelief. It was said: \"Shall we set up a place for you in Mina?\" He said: \"Has Aqil left us any place?\""],[2587,"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim."],[2588,"When you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter it, and when it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."],[2589,"This pain is a punishment with which some nations were tormented. It goes for a time and comes another. Whoever hears of it in a land, let him not go to it, and whoever is in a land where it occurs, let him not leave fleeing from it."],[2590,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I practice coitus interruptus with my wife.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Why do you do that? Or by what reason?\" He said: \"I fear for her child or for her children.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If that were so, it would not have harmed Persia or Rome, or the Romans.\""],[2591,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[2592,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw sadness upon him. It was said to him, and he said: \"Gabriel ﷺ has not come to me for three days, and I see a puppy in the house.\" He ordered it, and it was taken out, and then Gabriel appeared to him, ﷺ. He said: \"Why did you not come to me?\" He said: \"We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images.\""],[2593,"\"Is there any who will hasten to Paradise? For Paradise has no danger. By the Lord of the Kaaba, it is a light that glitters, a fragrant plant that sways, a lofty palace, a river with pleasing scent, ripe fruit, a beautiful and lovely spouse, and many garments, in an eternal abode in a secure home, with fruit and greenery and comfort and blessing in a high and splendid place.\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God, we are those who hasten to it.\" He said: \"Say: If God wills.\" The people said: \"If God wills.\""],[2594,"I departed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when he reached the mountain pass, he dismounted and urinated. I said: \"The prayer!\" He said: \"The prayer is ahead of you.\" When we reached Muzdalifah, he called the adhan and the iqamah and prayed Maghrib. Then he did not come to another until he called the iqamah and prayed Isha."],[2595,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when the messenger of one of his daughters came to him, calling him and saying: \"A boy of hers is dying.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Go back to her and tell her to seek reward from God, for to God belongs what He takes and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything with Him is for an appointed term.\" She sent to him adjuring him to come to her. He stood up, and with him stood Muadh b. Jabal and Sa'd b. Ubadah. He came to her, and the Prophet ﷺ placed the boy in his lap, and his breath was rattling as if in an old waterskin. The eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ shed tears. Sa'd b. Ubadah said: \"What is this, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"This is mercy which God has placed in the hearts of His servants, and God shows mercy to those of His servants who are merciful.\""],[2596,"Hisham b. Hassan reported to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usama b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2597,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take me and al-Hasan b. Ali and say: \"O God, I love them, so love them.\""],[2598,"Amr b. Ali and Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Yahya b. Sa'id reported to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2599,"\"I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women.\""],[2600,"\"I have not left after me a trial that is more harmful to men than women.\""],[2601,"\"Whoever claims descent from other than his father, God has forbidden Paradise to him.\""],[2602,"Whoever has a favor done to him and says to his companion: \"May God reward you with good,\" has fully praised him."],[2603,"I was informed that Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ, and Umm Salama was with him. He began to speak, then he stood up. The Prophet of God ﷺ said to Umm Salama: \"Who is this?\" or as he said. She said: \"This is Dihya.\" Umm Salama said: \"By God, I did not think it was anyone but him until I heard the sermon of the Prophet of God ﷺ informing—I think—about Jibril,\" or as he said."],[2604,"Al-Jurayri reported to us, from Abu Uthman, from Usama b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2605,"When he was in a hurry while traveling, he would combine Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[2606,"If you hear of a plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it."],[2607,"Jarir informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim b. Saʿd, from Usama b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[2608,"This disease is a punishment with which those before you were tormented. If it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land while you are not there, do not go to it."],[2609,"We entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was ill and found him sleeping, having covered his face with a striped Yemeni cloak. He uncovered his face and then said: May God curse the Jews; they forbid the fat of sheep yet sell it and consume its price."],[2610,"May God curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."],[2611,"I attacked a man and cut off his hand, and he said: There is no god but God. I finished him off. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, who said: O Usama, did you kill him while he was saying: There is no god but God? I said: O Messenger of God, he only said it seeking protection after I had cut him. He said: And he kept repeating it until I wished I had not embraced Islam before that day."],[2612,"I killed a man, and he said: There is no god but God. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, who said: How will you fare with 'There is no god but God'? He kept repeating it until I wished I had not known Islam before that day."],[2613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent us in the army to al-Huraqat. When we defeated them, I and a man from the Ansar pursued one of them. He said: There is no god but God. The Ansari held back, but I thought he said it only seeking protection, so I killed him. The Ansari raised that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: O Usama, did you kill him while he was saying: There is no god but God? How will you fare with 'There is no god but God' on the Day of Resurrection? He kept saying that until I felt that I had not embraced Islam except on that day."],[2614,"He was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ from Muzdalifah, and he did not raise his hands [to wave] until he had thrown the pebble at the Jamrah."],[2615,"Do not face the qiblah while defecating or urinating."],[2616,"When Zayd was killed, Usama came and stood facing him; his eyes teared, so he moved away. The next day, he came and stood, then said: Today I receive from you what I received yesterday, so he moved away."],[2617,"A man from one of the regions came, and when he drew near to Madinah, he thought that it had the epidemic, meaning the plague. He said: I recognized, or he recognized, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: I hope that the plague will not enter upon us in Madinah."],[2618,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast for days on end until it was said: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast for days on end until it was said: He scarcely fasts. And he did not fast in any month as much as he fasted in Sha'ban. I said: O Messenger of God, you fast until we say you do not break your fast, and you break your fast until we say you scarcely fast. I said: And you fast on Mondays and Thursdays. He said: These are two days on which deeds are presented to the Lord of the Worlds, so I love that my deeds be presented while I am fasting. And I fast during the month of Sha'ban, or from Sha'ban, for it is a month people are heedless of."],[2619,"We were sitting with Usamah b. Zayd in the mosque, and he was asked about the middle prayer, and he said: It is Zuhr. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray it at the time of intense heat."],[2620,"Abu 'Awana reported to us, from 'Umar b. Abi Salama, from his father, from Usamah b. Zayd."],[2621,"I was in the mosque when al-'Abbas and 'Ali b. Abi Talib came to me and said: O Usamah, ask permission for us to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him, saying: 'Ali and al-'Abbas seek permission. He said: \"Do you know what they need?\" I said: No, by God. He said: \"But I know.\" Then he gave them permission. They said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, we have come to you so that you tell us which of your family is most beloved to you. He said: The most beloved of my family to me is Fatimah bt. Muhammad. They said: O Messenger of God, we are not asking you about Fatimah. He said: \"Then Usamah b. Zayd, the son of the one upon whom God bestowed favor, and upon whom I bestowed favor.\""],[2622,"Yunus, meaning Ibn 'Ubayd, reported to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Hissan b. Kahil, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samura, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, from the Messenger of God."],[2623,"Habib b. al-Shahid reported to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Hissan b. Kahil, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samura, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, from the Messenger of God."],[2624,"Sahl b. Aslam al-'Adawi reported to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Hissan b. Kahil, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samura, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, from the Prophet."],[2625,"There is no soul that dies while bearing witness that there is no god but God, returning that to a heart that is certain, except that God forgives it."],[2626,"Whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise."],[2627,"Whoever's last words are 'there is no god but God' will enter Paradise."],[2628,"We came to Mu'adh b. Jabal and said: Narrate to us from the rare hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on a donkey, and he said: \"O Mu'adh.\" I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: \"Do you know what God's right upon His servants is?\" I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.\" Then he said: \"Do you know what the servants' right upon God is if they do that?\" I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"The servants' right upon God, if they do that, is that He will not punish them.\""],[2629,"The Hour will not come until Allah sends forth lying rulers, wicked ministers, treacherous trustees, and sinful reciters whose appearance is the appearance of monks, yet they have no desire [for good]—or he said: they have no awe—or he said: no piety. Then Allah will clothe them in a dusty, dark tribulation, and they will flounder in it like the Jews flounder in darkness."],[2630,"You are upon clear guidance from your Lord as long as two intoxications do not appear among you: the intoxication of ignorance and the intoxication of love of ease. And you will continue to enjoin good, forbid evil, and strive in the cause of Allah. But when love of this world appears among you, you will not enjoin good, nor forbid evil, nor strive in the cause of Allah. Those who speak by the Book and the Sunnah on that day will be like the foremost first ones among the Emigrants and the Helpers."],[2631,"\"If I take a pulpit, then my father Ibrahim took it; and if I take a staff, then my father Ibrahim took it.\""],[2632,"The first to deliver a sermon from the pulpits was Ibrahim."],[2633,"Al-Jurayri reported to us, from Abu al-Ward, from al-Lajlaj, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, from the Prophet."],[2634,"He passed by a man who was saying in his supplication: 'O Allah, I ask You for patience.' He said: 'You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Allah for well-being.' Then he came upon a man saying: 'O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing.' He stood over him and said: 'Do you know what the completion of blessing is?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a supplication I made hoping for good by it.' He said: 'Indeed, the completion of blessing is deliverance from the Fire and entry into Paradise.' Then he came upon a man saying: 'O Possessor of majesty and honor.' He said: 'It has been answered for you, so ask.'"],[2635,"\"Islam increases and does not decrease.\""],[2636,"Qurra b. Khalid reported to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[2637,"\"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and he used to combine the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers, and the Maghrib and 'Isha' prayers.\""],[2638,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and he would not set out until it had cooled, and he would combine the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers."],[2639,"\"The two feet of a servant will not move from before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, until he is asked about four things: about his life in what he spent it, about his body in what he wore it out, about his knowledge what he did with it, and about his wealth from where he earned it and on what he spent it.\""],[2640,"Layth reported to us, from 'Adi b. 'Adi, from al-Sunabihi, from Mu'adh, with something similar, but he did not attribute it to the Prophet."],[2641,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him to a people, so he said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: Spread peace/salutation, offer food generously, and be modest before God with the modesty of a man of dignity among your family. If you do wrong, then do good, and improve your character as much as you can."],[2642,"O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: Guard your tongue. He repeated it to him, so he said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh! Do people get thrown on their faces into the Fire except by the harvests of their tongues?"],[2643,"The people of Paradise are hairless, beardless, thirty-three years old."],[2644,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash reported to us, from 'Asim—meaning Ibn Abi al-Nujud—from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh."],[2645,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take a tenth from what the sky watered and what was watered by natural springs, and half a tenth from what was watered by buckets."],[2646,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him (Mu'adh) to Yemen, the Prophet ﷺ went out with him that day while Mu'adh was riding, and the Messenger of God was walking beside his mount. He said: O Mu'adh, perhaps you may not meet me after this year of mine, and you will pass by my grave and my mosque. Mu'adh wept out of grief for parting with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Do not weep, O Mu'adh, for weeping is from Satan."],[2647,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who loves praise. The Messenger of God ﷺ said a word which I think was: It is enough for you to live praiseworthy and die missed. I was only sent with the beauties of character."],[2648,"I exposed myself to the Messenger of God ﷺ, or I presented myself to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was circumambulating (the Ka'ba). I said: O Messenger of God, which people are the worst? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O God, forgiveness! Ask about good, not about evil. The worst of people are the worst scholars among the people."],[2649,"In the end of time there will be people who are brothers in public but enemies in private. It was said: O Messenger of God, how can that be? He said: Because of the desiring of some of them toward others, and the fearing of some of them of others."],[2650,"Jihad is the pillar of Islam and the peak of its hump."],[2651,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, he wiped his face with the edge of his garment."],[2652,"Some people entered upon Mu'adh b. Jabal while he was ill and said: Tell us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ which has not become confused for you. He said: Seat me. So some of the people took his hand and he sat. He said: I will not tell you except a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: There is no prophet except that he warned his people against the Dajjal, and I warn you against the Dajjal. He is one-eyed, with 'disbeliever' written between his eyes, which the literate and the illiterate can read. With him are a paradise and a fire: his paradise is fire, and his fire is paradise."],[2653,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he commanded him to take from thirty cattle a tabi' (one-year-old), and from forty a musinnah (two-year-old), and from every adult one dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments."],[2654,"Whoever among you prays at night should recite aloud, for the angels pray with his prayer and listen to his recitation. The believing jinn who are in the air, and his neighbors in his dwelling, pray with his prayer and listen to his recitation. And by his loud recitation he drives away from his house and from the houses around him the wicked jinn and the rebellious devils. The house in which the Quran is recited has over it a tent of light by which the people of heaven are guided, just as they are guided by a brilliant star in the depths of the seas and in the desolate land. When the companion of the Quran dies, that tent is lifted, and the angels look from heaven and no longer see that light, so the angels announce his death from heaven to heaven, and the angels pray over his soul among the souls. Then the angels meet the two guardian angels who were with him, and they seek forgiveness for him until the day he is resurrected. There is no man who learns the Book of Allah and then prays for a portion of the night but that the past night entrusts the coming night to wake him at that hour and to be light upon him. When he dies and his family is preparing his body, the Quran comes in a beautiful and comely form, standing at his head until he is wrapped in his shrouds, and the Quran is upon his chest rather than the shroud. When he is placed in his grave and the earth is leveled over him and his companions depart, Munkar and Nakir come to him and sit him up in his grave. The Quran comes until it is between him and them. They say to it: 'Move aside so we may question him.' It says: 'No, by the Lord of the Kaaba, he is my companion and my close friend, and I will not abandon him in any state. If you two have been commanded something, then proceed with what you were commanded and leave me in my place, for I will not part from him until I enter him into Paradise, if Allah wills.' Then the Quran looks at its companion and says to him: 'Rest, for you will find me a true neighbor among neighbors, a true friend among friends, and a true companion among companions.' He says to it: 'Who are you?' It says: 'I am the Quran which you used to recite aloud and in secret, and you loved me. I am your beloved, and whoever loves me, Allah loves him. After the questioning of Munkar and Nakir, there is no distress, worry, or grief upon you.' Munkar and Nakir ask him and then ascend, and he and the Quran remain. It says: 'I will spread for you a soft bed and cover you with a fine and beautiful covering as a reward for your staying awake at night and toiling by day.' Then the Quran ascends to heaven faster than the blink of an eye and asks Allah for that for him, and Allah grants it to him. Then a million of the angels brought near of the sixth heaven descend with it, and the Quran comes and says: 'Have you felt lonely? Since I parted from you, I have not ceased speaking to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, until I obtained for you a bed, a covering, and a lamp. I have brought them to you, so rise so the angels may spread them for you.' The angels raise him gently, and his grave is widened for him a distance of four hundred years. Then a bed is placed for him whose lining is green silk and whose filling is musk and sweet rush. Cushions of fine silk and brocade are placed at his feet and head, and two lamps from the light of Paradise are lit at his head and feet, shining until the Day of Resurrection. Then the angels lay him on his right side facing the qiblah. Then jasmine from the jasmine of Paradise is brought, and they ascend from him, leaving him and the Quran. The Quran takes the jasmine and places it fresh over his nose, and he inhales it until he is resurrected. The Quran returns to his family and informs him of their news every day and night, caring for him as a compassionate parent cares for his child. If one of his children learns the Quran, it gives him the good news of that. If his descendants are wicked, it supplicates for them for righteousness and acceptance, or as it was mentioned. We do not know this hadith being narrated from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except from this route. Khalid b. Ma'dan did not hear from Mu'adh, and we mentioned it only because we did not preserve it from the Prophet ﷺ except from this route, and so we mentioned it. The reward of the Quran is what comes, and the evidence for that is that it is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that the morsel or the piece of bread will come on the Day of Resurrection like Mount Uhud, and only its reward comes. Thus everything of that which is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ about what will happen in the Hereafter is only the reward."],[2655,"The most hateful of creation to me is one who believed then disbelieved."],[2656,"No servant stands in this world in a position of fame and showing off but that Allah will expose him before all creation on the Day of Resurrection."],[2657,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting."],[2658,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man wearing a jubbah trimmed or bordered with silk, and he said: 'A collar of fire on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2659,"The key to Paradise is the testimony that there is no god but Allah."],[2660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand one day and said: 'O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you.' Mu'adh said to him: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love you.' He said: 'I enjoin you, O Mu'adh, to say after every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.'"],[2661,"He used to seek refuge, saying: 'I seek refuge in You from greed that leads to sin, and I seek refuge in You from greed where there is nothing to be desired, or in other than what is desired.'"],[2662,"About the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteousness and associate none in the worship of his Lord.' He said: Abu Salih narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm was in the mosque of Damascus with a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Mu'adh b. Jabal. Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm said: 'O people, the thing I fear most for you is the hidden shirk.' Mu'adh said: 'O Allah, forgive.' He said: 'O Mu'adh, have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever fasts for show has committed shirk, whoever gives charity for show has committed shirk, and whoever prays for show has committed shirk?' He said: 'Yes, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord... and the verse was hard on the people and they were distressed. He said: Shall I relieve you of it? They said: Yes, may Allah relieve you of worry and harm. He said: It is like the verse in Surat al-Rum: 'And whatever you give for interest to increase within the wealth of people will not increase with Allah...' Whoever does a deed for show, it is not recorded for him nor against him; it is neither for him nor against him.'"],[2663,"The woman is continually cursed by the angels, or he said: Allah curses her, and His angels, and the keepers of mercy and punishment, as long as she commits any act of disobedience to Allah."],[2664,"If a woman knew the right of her husband, she would not sit while his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes."],[2665,"I said to Mu'adh b. Jabal: Did you perform ablution from what the fire had changed? He said: Yes; when one of us ate food from what the fire had changed, he washed his hands and his mouth, and we counted this as ablution."],[2666,"The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers."],[2667,"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, came to me in the most beautiful form and said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and at Your command. He said: About what do the Highest Assembly dispute? He said: I said: About expiations and degrees. He said: And what are expiations and degrees? I said: Performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, walking to the Friday prayers, and waiting for the prayers after the prayers. Say, O Muhammad: O Allah, I ask You for good things, the abandonment of evils, the doing of good deeds, and love of the poor; and if You will a trial among the people, then take me to You without my being afflicted. Whoever says that lives with good, dies with good, and comes out of his sins as on the day his mother bore him."],[2668,"O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise; I will not ask you about anything other than it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Bravo, bravo! You have asked about a great matter, and indeed it is easy for the one for whom Allah wills good. He said: You believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish the prayer, and worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, until you die while upon that. He said: O Prophet of Allah, repeat it, and he repeated it three times. Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: If you wish, I will tell you, O Mu'adh, of the foundation of this matter and its highest peak. Mu'adh said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed the head of this matter is the testimony that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that I am His servant and Messenger, the establishment of the prayer, and the giving of zakah; and the highest peak of it is jihad in the path of Allah. I have only been commanded to fight the people until they establish the prayer, give zakah, and testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am His servant and Messenger. When they do that, they have sought protection. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: No foot is covered with dust in a deed by which the degrees of Paradise are sought, after the prescribed prayer, like jihad in the path of Allah, nor is the scale of a servant made heavier than by a mount that dies for him in the path of Allah or that he rides in the path of Allah."],[2669,"Shu'ayb b. Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Husayn, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[2670,"He arrived with Mu'adh from Yemen and stayed with him in his house and his dwelling. Then the plague struck them, and Mu'adh, Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, Shurahbil b. Hasanah, and Abu Malik were all afflicted on a single day. 'Amr b. al-'As, when he sensed the plague, fled and was terrified with a great terror and said: O people, disperse into these mountain passes, for a matter from Allah has descended upon you; I see it as nothing but punishment and plague. Shurahbil b. Hasanah said to him: You lie; we accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you are more astray than the donkey of your household. 'Amr said: You speak the truth. Mu'adh b. Jabal said to 'Amr b. al-'As: You lie; it is not the plague, nor punishment, but it is the mercy of your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the taking of the righteous. O Allah, give the family of Mu'adh the fullest share of this mercy. He said: By evening, his son 'Abd al-Rahman was afflicted—the most beloved of creation to him, after whom he had his kunya. Mu'adh returned from the mosque and found him distressed, and said: O 'Abd al-Rahman, how are you? He replied: O my father, the truth from your Lord, so do not be among the doubters. Mu'adh said: And we, if Allah wills, you will find me among the patient. He died that night, and he buried him the next day. Mu'adh b. Jabal sent al-Harith b. 'Umayrah to Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah to ask how he was. Abu 'Ubaydah showed him his affliction in his hand, and al-Harith b. 'Umayrah wept and was frightened when he saw it. Abu 'Ubaydah swore by Allah that he would not love to have in its place red camels. He said: Al-Harith returned to Mu'adh and found him unconscious, so al-Harith wept and sought to make others weep. Then Mu'adh regained consciousness and said: O son of the Humayri woman, why do you weep over me? I seek refuge in Allah from you. Al-Harith said: By Allah, I do not weep over you. Mu'adh said: Then over what do you weep? He said: I weep over what I have missed from you—the two times of day, morning and evening. Mu'adh said: Sit me up. He sat him up in his lap and said: Listen to me, for I enjoin upon you a bequest. As for what you weep over—your coming in the morning and evening—knowledge is in its place between the two covers of the mushaf. If its interpretation is difficult for you, then seek it after me from three: 'Uwaymir Abu al-Darda', or Salman al-Farisi, or Ibn Umm 'Abd. And I warn you against the slip of the scholar and the argument of the hypocrite. Then death's agony intensified for Mu'adh; he struggled as no one had struggled. Whenever he recovered from a swoon, he opened his eyes and said: Choke me with Your choking, for by Your might, You know that I love You. He said: When he passed away, al-Harith set out until he came to Abu al-Darda' in Hims and stayed with him as long as Allah willed. Then al-Harith said: My brother Mu'adh enjoined me to you, Salman al-Farisi, and Ibn Umm 'Abd. I see myself as nothing but departing to Iraq. He came to Kufa and attended the gathering of Ibn Umm 'Abd morning and evening. While he was thus in the gathering one day, Ibn Umm 'Abd said: Who are you? I said: A man from the people of Syria. Ibn Umm 'Abd said: What an excellent tribe are the people of Syria, were it not for one thing. Al-Harith said: What is that one thing? He said: Were it not that they testify against themselves that they are among the people of Paradise. He said: Al-Harith said 'Indeed we belong to Allah' twice or three times and said: Mu'adh spoke the truth in what he told me. Ibn Umm 'Abd said: And what did he say, O son of my brother? He said: He warned me against the slip of the scholar. By Allah, O Ibn Mas'ud, you are but one of two men: either a man who has entered upon certainty and testifies that there is no god but Allah, so you are among the people of Paradise, or a man in doubt who does not know where your station is. Ibn Mas'ud said: My brother spoke the truth; it is a slip, so do not hold me to account for it. Ibn Mas'ud took al-Harith by the hand and went with him to his dwelling, and he stayed with him as long as Allah willed. Then al-Harith said: I must visit Abu 'Abd Allah Salman al-Farisi in al-Mada'in. Al-Harith set out until he came to Salman in al-Mada'in. When he greeted him, Salman said: Stay where you are until I come out to you. Al-Harith said: By Allah, I do not think you know me, O Abu 'Abd Allah. He said: Yes, my soul knew your soul before I knew you. Indeed souls are troops mustered by Allah; those that knew one another came together, and those that did not know one another separated over other than Allah. He stayed with him as long as Allah willed. Then he returned to Syria. Those are the ones who knew one another for the sake of Allah and visited one another for the sake of Allah."],[2671,"Indeed those who love one another for the majesty of Allah will be in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. Then when..."],[2672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. When I had set out, he sent after me, and I was brought back. He said: Do you know why I sent for you? Do not take anything without knowledge, for it is embezzlement, and whoever embezzles will come with what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection. For this I called you; go on to your work."],[2673,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled on a journey, those who accompanied him were the Muhajirun, then the Ansar. We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: My intercession is for whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with me."],[2674,"When the circumcised parts meet the circumcised parts, the full bath becomes obligatory."],[2675,"There is no servant who spends the night pure or upon purity, then wakes during the night asking Allah for a need of the needs of this world or the Hereafter, except that He gives it to him."],[2676,"The Arabs are equals to one another, and the clients are equals to one another."],[2677,"A believer's dream is one forty-sixth part of prophethood."],[2678,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[2679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, intending to inform us about the Night of Decree. Then two men began arguing. He said: \"I had come out to you intending to inform you about the Night of Decree, but so-and-so and so-and-so argued, and it was taken away from me\"—or he said something similar—\"and perhaps that is better for you. So seek it in the last ten nights, on the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.\""],[2680,"\"I have told you about the Dajjal until I feared\"—and he mentioned a word—\"indeed, he is a short man, bow-legged, with curly hair, one-eyed, with his eye wiped flat, neither protruding nor sunken. If it becomes unclear to you, know that you will not see your Lord until you die.\""],[2681,"\"Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that ʿĪsā son of Maryam is Allah's servant and His word which He conveyed to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true, and that the Fire is true, Allah will admit him to Paradise regardless of what deeds he has.\""],[2682,"\"Whoever says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that ʿĪsā is Allah's servant and the son of His maidservant, and His word which He conveyed to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true, and that the Fire is true, Allah will admit him through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise He wills.\""],[2683,"\"Jibrīl ﷺ came to him while he was ill and said: 'In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you, from everything that harms you, from the envy of an envier and from every eye'—I think he said—'and Allah will heal you.'\""],[2684,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ followed a funeral procession, he would not sit down until the body was placed in the grave. Once, a Jewish rabbi came and said, \"This is what we do.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and said, \"Do the opposite of them.\""],[2685,"\"Take from me: Allah has made a way for them. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year. The previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes and stoning.\""],[2686,"\"The first thing Allah created was the Pen. He said to it: Write. So it wrote what is to be until the Day of Resurrection. O my son, if you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire.\""],[2687,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about urine. He said: \"If any of you gets some on him, wash it, for I think that it is among the causes of the punishment of the grave.\""],[2688,"\"The last of my community will surely make wine lawful under a name they give it.\""],[2689,"Whoever prays the prescribed prayer, performs it fully, and prays it at its proper time will meet Allah, the Exalted, with a covenant that He will not punish him. And whoever does not establish the prescribed prayer and does not pray it at its proper time will meet Allah with no covenant—if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will have mercy on him."],[2690,"When a man prays, perfects his ablution, and completes its bowing and prostration—I think he said: and the recitation in it—it says: May Allah preserve you as you have preserved me. And when he performs its bowing poorly and does not complete its bowing or prostration, it says: May Allah waste you as you have wasted me."],[2691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me while I was ill, along with some of the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know who the martyr is?\" They remained silent. I said: Who knows who the martyr is? I said to my wife: Help me sit up. So she helped me sit up, and I said: The martyr is one who submits, then emigrates, then is killed in the way of Allah; he is a martyr. He said: \"The martyrs of my nation would then be few. Being killed in the way of Allah is martyrdom, stomach illness is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and a woman who dies in childbirth is martyrdom.\""],[2692,"Al-Mu'afa b. 'Imran reported to us, from al-Mughira b. Ziyad, from 'Ubada b. Nusayy, from al-Aswad b. Tha'laba, from 'Ubada b. al-Samit, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. This hadith is not known to be narrated from 'Ubada, from the Prophet ﷺ, except through this chain of transmission."],[2693,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ followed a funeral procession, he would not sit until the deceased was placed in the side niche of the grave. A Jewish rabbi approached him and said: This is what we do. He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and said: \"Differ from them.\""],[2694,"Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that 'Isa son of Maryam is the servant of Allah and His word which He cast to Maryam and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, Allah will admit him to Paradise regardless of whatever deeds he may have done."],[2695,"The martyr has six blessings with Allah: he is forgiven with the first drop of his blood, and he is clothed with the garment of honor—or he said: the garment of faith—and he is granted safety from the greatest terror, and he sees his seat in Paradise, and he is married to the wide-eyed maidens."],[2696,"I entered the mosque of Damascus and sat in a circle. A man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"It is reported from Allah, Mighty and Glorious: My love is due for those who love one another for My sake; My love is due for those who maintain ties for My sake; My love is due for those who visit one another for My sake; My love is due for those who are generous to one another for My sake.\" I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am 'Ubada b. al-Samit."],[2697,"You must obey in hardship and ease, and even when you are given preference over others, and you must not dispute the matter with its people unless they command you to clear disbelief."],[2698,"Hamza al-Zayyat reported to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umara b. 'Umayr, from al-Walid b. 'Ubada b. al-Samit, from his father, from the Prophet."],[2699,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey in hardship and ease."],[2700,"'Abd al-A'la reported to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Makhul, from Mahmud b. al-Rabi', from 'Ubada b. al-Samit."],[2701,"Muhammad b. Ishaq reported to us, from Makhul, from Mahmud b. al-Rabi, from Ubada b. al-Samit."],[2702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer, and the recitation became difficult for him. When he finished, he said: “I see that you are reciting behind your imam.” We said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Then do not do so, except for the Opening of the Book (Umm al-Qur’an), for there is no prayer without the Opening of the Book.”"],[2703,"“Whoever worships Allah without associating anything with Him, establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, and hears and obeys, Allah will admit him from whichever of the gates of Paradise He wills, and it has eight gates. And whoever worships Allah without associating anything with Him, establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, and hears but disobeys, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has the choice regarding his affair: if He wills, He will have mercy on him, and if He wills, He will punish him.”"],[2704,"“There is no servant who prostrates to Allah with a prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it, records for him a good deed by it, and erases from him an evil deed by it, so increase in prostration.”"],[2705,"Abu Asim reported to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman b. Musa, that Kathir b. Murra narrated to them that Ubada b. al-Samit informed them from the Messenger of Allah."],[2706,"“There is no Muslim soul that dies and would be pleased to return to this world except the martyr when he is killed, or until he is killed.”"],[2707,"“When a man prays and perfects his ablution, and completes the bowing and the prostration” – and I think he said: “and the recitation in it – she (the prayer) says: ‘May Allah preserve you as you have preserved me.’ But if he does badly in its bowing or does not complete its bowing or its prostration” – I think he said: “and the recitation in it – she says: ‘May Allah waste you as you have wasted me.’”"],[2708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer wearing a jubba, and once he said: “wearing a shamla that he had tied, having nothing else on him.”"],[2709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me while I was ill, along with some of the Ansar. He said: “Do you know who the martyr is?” They remained silent, so I said to my wife: “Support me.” She supported me, and I said: “The martyr is the one who embraces Islam, then emigrates, then is killed in the path of Allah – he is a martyr.” He said: “Then the martyrs of my community would be few. Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and a woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom.”"],[2710,"“The best shroud is the hulla, and the best sacrificial animal is the horned ram.”"],[2711,"He sat with Ubada b. al-Samit, Abu al-Darda’, and al-Harith b. Mu’awiya, and we discussed the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu al-Darda’ said: “O Ubada, repeat for me the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in such-and-such a expedition.” Ubada said: The Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer during one of his expeditions facing a camel from the spoils. When he said the salam, he took a piece of fur and turned to us, saying: “Sit down. This is from your spoils, and I have no right to it except the fay’ along with you, and the fifth. And the fifth is returned to you. So hand over the thread and the needle, and anything greater or smaller than that, and do not embezzle, for embezzlement is disgrace and fire upon its perpetrators in this world and the Hereafter. And strive against people in the cause of Allah.”"],[2712,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed facing a camel from the spoils, then took a piece of fur from the side of the camel, then said: “O people, nothing of the spoils is lawful for me, not even the like of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you.”"],[2713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us facing a camel from the spoils of war, then he took a piece of wool from the camel and placed it between his two fingers and said: O people, this is your booty, so return the thread and the needle, for embezzlement is a disgrace upon its perpetrator on the Day of Resurrection, and a shame and a fire."],[2714,"For the martyr there are special qualities with Allah: he is forgiven at the first drop of his blood, and the garment of faith is placed upon him—or he is adorned with the garment of faith—and he is granted safety from the greatest terror, and he sees his seat in Paradise, and he is married to the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise."],[2715,"There is no man who goes out in the path of Allah and asks Allah for martyrdom, while Allah knows that he has sincerely made the supplication, and then dies, except that he has the reward of a martyr. And there is no man for whom a grey hair appears in the path of Allah except that it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[2716,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: Is there any stranger among you? meaning the People of the Book. We said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Close the door. And he said: Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah. So we raised our hands for a while, then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ lowered his hand and said: Praise be to Allah, You sent me with this word, commanded me with it, and promised me Paradise for it, and You do not break the promise. Then he said: Rejoice, for Allah has forgiven you."],[2717,"He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young, respect our elders, and fulfill the rights of our scholars."],[2718,"The best of my community are those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered. And the worst of my community are those who spread slander, cause division between loved ones, and seek to harm the innocent."],[2719,"The last of my community will surely make wine lawful by a name they give it."],[2720,"Sa'd b. Aws informed us, from Bilal b. Yahya al-Absi, from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit b. al-Simt, from Ubada b. al-Samit, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2721,"The dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never gather in the belly of a Muslim man."],[2722,"Whoever prays the prescribed prayer and performs it at its proper time will meet Allah and have a covenant with Him that He will not punish him. And whoever does not establish the prescribed prayer at its proper time will meet Allah with no covenant; if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will have mercy on him."],[2723,"Zam'a informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Ubada, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly or close to it."],[2724,"Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah expiates sins and erases transgressions? They said: Yes. He said: Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the prayer. That is the guarding of the frontier; that is the guarding of the frontier."],[2725,"There is no soul that dies and has good with Allah that would love to return to you except the martyr, for he loves to return and be killed once again, because of what he sees of bliss."],[2726,"Forbear from one who treats you ignorantly, pardon one who wrongs you, give to one who deprives you, and maintain ties with one who cuts you off."],[2727,"We were hunting at the well of Ihab, which was a well belonging to them. Ubada b. al-Samit came to us while we had caught a sparrow, and he released the sparrow and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade hunting in it?"],[2728,"Khalid b. Dihqan reported to us, from Abdullah b. Abi Zakariyya, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda."],[2729,"Every sin Allah may forgive on the Day of Resurrection except one who dies as a polytheist or kills a believer deliberately."],[2730,"Some donkeys passed by him while he was in Syria carrying wine. He took a knife from the market, went to them, and slit them open. Then he said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey in activity and laziness, in hardship and ease, to enjoin good and forbid evil, to speak for Allah without fear of any blamer's blame, and to support—I think he said—the oppressed, and to prevent from him what we prevent from ourselves and our children. This is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pledged allegiance upon. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: After me, people will govern your affairs who will make you recognize what you disapprove of, and disapprove of what you recognize. So there is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah."],[2731,"Shu'ba reported to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Ubada b. al-Samit, from the Prophet."],[2732,"Hammam reported to us, from Qatada, from Muslim, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Ubada."],[2733,"Ibn Uyayna reported to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Ibn Sirin, from Muslim b. Yasar, from Ubada, from the Prophet."],[2734,"Gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, like for like; wheat for wheat; barley for barley; dates for dates; salt for salt. Whoever adds or asks for addition has engaged in usury."],[2735,"Visit the sick, and follow funerals. It is no harm if you do not attend the wedding feast, and it is no harm if you marry a woman for her beauty, though perhaps she will not bring good. It is no harm if you marry a woman for her wealth, though perhaps her wealth will not bring good. But marry those of religion and trustworthiness, and seek them out."],[2736,"Abu Hamza reported to us, from Ibn Jubayr b. Nufayr al-Hadrami, from his father, from Awf b. Malik, from the Prophet."],[2737,"Abdullah b. Salih reported to us, from Mu'awiya b. Salih, from Habib b. 'Ubayd, from Jubayr b. Nufayr, from 'Awf b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in a funeral prayer, and I memorized from his supplication: “O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, pardon him, and excuse him; honor his hospitality, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow, and hail, and purify him from sins as a white garment is purified from dirt; replace him with a home better than his home, a family better than his family, and a spouse better than his spouse; admit him to Paradise and protect him from the punishment of the grave and from the punishment of the Fire,” until I wished that I were that deceased person."],[2739,"\"Indeed, before the Hour there will be years of deceit, in which the liar is believed, the truthful is disbelieved, the treacherous is trusted, the trustworthy is betrayed, and the ruwaybida will speak.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybida?\" He said: \"The insignificant man who speaks about public affairs.\""],[2740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the sky and said: \"This is the time when knowledge will be lifted.\" A man from the Ansar called Ziyad b. Labid said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge be lifted when it is established and hearts have retained it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"I had considered you one of the most knowledgeable of the people of Madinah.\" Then he mentioned to him the misguidance of the Jews and Christians despite what was in their hands from the Book of Allah."],[2741,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. He said: \"'Awf?\" I said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"May I enter?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"All of me or some of me?\" He said: \"All of you.\" Then he said: \"Count, O 'Awf, six things before the Hour: the first of them is my death.\" He said: \"So I wept until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to quiet me. One. The second is the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. Two. The third is a plague that will be among my Ummah, taking them like the qa'as of sheep. Three. The fourth is a tribulation that will occur among my Ummah. Four.\" I said: \"Four.\" \"The fifth is that wealth will overflow and become abundant, until a man is given a hundred and he is displeased with it. Five. The sixth is a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar. They will gather against you under eighty banners.\" I said: \"What is a banner?\" He said: \"A banner, under each banner twelve thousand. The camp of the Muslims on that day will be in a city called al-Ghuta, in a city called Dimashq.\""],[2742,"\"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood.\""],[2743,"We used to perform ruqya in the Jahiliyya, so we said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about that?\" He said: \"Present to me your ruqas. There is no harm in ruqas as long as they do not involve shirk.\""],[2744,"\"Will you leave my commanders to me? For indeed, your example and theirs is like a man who bought camels and sheep, then brought them to a watering trough. They entered it and drank the clear water, leaving the murky water. So the clear water is for you, and the murky water is upon them.\""],[2745,"We went on an expedition toward Syria, and over us was Khalid b. al-Walid. A man from the reinforcements of Himyar joined us and remained with us until we entered. As soon as we met our enemy, among whom were groups of Romans and Arabs from Quda'a, they fought fiercely. Among the enemy was a Roman man on a chestnut horse with a gilded saddle, a gold belt, and a sword like that. He began attacking the people and cutting through them. A man came and kept maneuvering around the Roman until he struck him. He struck the horse's hamstring with his sword, and it fell. Then he followed up with blows of the sword until he killed him. When Allah granted victory, the young man came asking, and the people testified that he had killed him. Khalid gave him some of his spoils and kept the rest. When he returned to 'Awf, he mentioned to him what Khalid had done. So 'Awf went until he came to Khalid and said: \"Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the spoils belong to the killer?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What prevented you from giving him the spoils of his victim?\" Khalid said: \"I considered it too much for him.\" 'Awf said: \"If I see the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I will definitely mention that to him.\" When he arrived in Madinah, 'Awf followed him and complained to the Prophet ﷺ. He called Khalid while 'Awf was sitting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What prevented you, O Khalid, from giving this man the spoils of his victim?\" He said: \"I considered it too much, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Give it to him.\" Then he said: \"Arise, O 'Awf.\" So 'Awf pulled his cloak. Then 'Awf said: \"I have fulfilled what I mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ.\" The Prophet ﷺ heard him, and Khalid became angry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not give him. Will you leave my commanders to me? Indeed, my example and theirs is like a man who bought camels and sheep, tended them, then brought them to a watering trough. They entered it and drank the clear water, leaving its murky water. So the clarity of their affair is for you, and its murkiness is upon them.\""],[2746,"The Prophet ﷺ did not take the khums from the spoils."],[2747,"\"When wealth came to him, he would distribute it on the same day, giving the married man two shares and the unmarried man one share.\""],[2748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged between two men, and the one against whom judgment was given said: \"Sufficient for me is Allah, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Bring the man to me.\" He said to him: \"When a matter overwhelms you, say: Sufficient for me is Allah, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.\""],[2749,"I stood with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night and wanted to observe his prayer. He used the toothstick, then performed ablution, then stood to pray. I stood with him. He began and opened with Surah al-Baqarah. He did not pass by a verse of mercy but that he paused and asked, nor pass by a verse of punishment but that he paused and sought refuge. Then he bowed and remained bowing for the duration of his standing, saying in his bowing: \"Glory be to the One of might, dominion, pride, and greatness.\" Then he prostrated for the duration of his bowing, saying in his prostration: \"Glory be to the One of might, dominion, pride, and greatness.\" Then he recited Al 'Imran and did the same."],[2750,"I observed the Messenger of God ﷺ closely."],[2751,"\"The best of your leaders are those whom you love and they love you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and they hate you, and you curse them and they curse you.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, should we not then oppose them?\" He said: \"No, as long as they pray. Whoever has a ruler appointed over him and sees him committing something of disobedience to God, let him hate that act of disobedience to God but not withdraw his hand from obedience.\""],[2752,"\"Do not kill women.\""],[2753,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all of them except an idolater or one who harbors enmity.\""],[2754,"\"My nation will split into seventy-some sects. The greatest of them in tribulation upon my nation are people who measure matters by their own opinion, declaring the lawful unlawful and the unlawful lawful.\""],[2755,"\"Shall I inform you about leadership and what it is?\" I stood and called out at the top of my voice three times: \"What is it, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Its beginning is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who acts justly—and how can he act justly with his relatives?\""],[2756,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us during the Battle of Tabuk to wipe over the leather socks for three days and their nights for the traveler, and one day and night for the resident."],[2757,"He stood among his companions and said: \"Do you fear poverty or need, or are you distracted by the world? For God will open for you Persia and Byzantium, and the world will be poured upon you abundantly.\""],[2758,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque and there were clusters of dates hanging in the mosque, including a cluster of dry, inferior dates. He began poking it with a stick he had, saying: \"The owner of this will eat inferior dates on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2759,"\"I have learned the last of the people of Paradise to enter it: a man who used to say: 'O God, keep me away from the Fire,' and did not say: 'Admit me into Paradise.' So the people of Paradise entered Paradise and the people of the Fire entered the Fire, and that man remained. He said: 'O Lord, what is it for me here?' He said: 'That is what you used to ask for, O son of Adam.' He said: 'O Lord, bring me near Paradise.' He said: 'O son of Adam, you did not ask Me for that.' He said: 'Then God will create for him a tree at the gate of Paradise.' He will say: 'O Lord, bring me near this tree so I may eat from its fruit and shade myself with its shade.' He will say: 'O son of Adam, did you not ask Me to keep you away from the Fire?' He will not cease asking until it is said to him: 'Go, for you have what your feet reached and your eyes saw.'\""],[2760,"Whoever recites a letter of the Qur'an, God writes for him—I think he said—ten good deeds. I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter."],[2761,"No one tells stories except a ruler, one commanded to do so, or a vainglorious person."],[2762,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque and found clusters of dates hanging, and among them were inferior dates. He began poking at them with a stick in his hand, saying: 'The owner of this will eat or receive inferior dates on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2763,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, seven, eight, or nine of us, and he said: 'Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah?' We had recently pledged to him, so we said: 'We have already pledged to you. On what basis should we pledge to you?' He said: 'That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, perform the five prayers, listen and obey,' and he whispered a hidden word, 'and that you do not ask people for anything.' He (the narrator) said: 'Indeed, if one of those men's whip fell, he would not ask anyone to hand it to him.'"],[2764,"When a man embraced Islam, the first thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would teach us was prayer — or he said: He taught him prayer."],[2765,"I said to my father: 'O father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behind Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and 'Ali. Did you see any of them perform qunut?' He said: 'That is an innovation, my son.'"],[2766,"Enough for my Companions is the killing."],[2767,"Whoever affirms the oneness of Allah and rejects what is worshiped besides Him, I have made his wealth and blood inviolable, and his reckoning is with Allah."],[2768,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' If they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[2769,"I have never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, yet complete."],[2770,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on his riding camel, touching the corner with his staff."],[2771,"Our dye in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wars and saffron."],[2772,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me while awake, for Satan cannot assume my form."],[2773,"“Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[2774,"I heard Abu al-Tufayl when a man asked him, “Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “Yes, he was fair, handsome, and of moderate build.”"],[2775,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among the men were some taller than him and some shorter than him.”"],[2776,"“The best with which you can change grey hair is henna and katam,” or he said: “The Prophet ﷺ used to dye his hair with henna and katam.”"],[2777,"“Will not a man inform me about Mudar?” A man from the people said: “I will inform you about them, O Messenger of Allah. As for its face, in which are its hearing and sight, it is this tribe of Quraysh. As for its tongue, with which it speaks in its assemblies, it is this tribe of Asad b. Khuzaymah. As for its upper back, it is this tribe of Tamim b. Murr. As for its horsemen, it is this tribe of Qays b. Ghaylan.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ looked at him as if confirming what he said.”"],[2778,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ circumambulate the House on his mount, touching the corner with his staff.”"],[2779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, then said: “Will you not ask me why I laughed?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, why did you laugh?” He said: “I saw people being driven to Paradise in chains.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, who are they?” He said: “People from the non-Arabs whom the Emigrants take captive and bring into Islam.”"],[2780,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributing meat at al-Jiʿrānah when a Bedouin woman came to him, and he spread his cloak for her.” I said: “Who is this?” They said: “This is his mother who used to nurse him.”"],[2781,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come to Zamzam and say: “Draw water and give me to drink, for were it not that I fear you would be overcome for it, I would draw it myself.”"],[2782,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ on his she-camel al-Qaswāʾ raising his voice in talbiyah, while the people were jostling one another, wanting to look at him.”"],[2783,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House seven times, touching the corner with a staff and kissing the tip of the staff.”"],[2784,"“I saw in a dream black sheep followed by dusty-coloured sheep, and I interpreted the black sheep as the Arabs and the dusty-coloured ones as the non-Arabs.”"],[2785,"Mahdi b. Imran informed us, saying: I heard Abu al-Tufayl"],[2786,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was sent while I was a young boy carrying meat from the plain to the mountain.\""],[2787,"We said to Ammar, “Tell us about your fighting: was it an opinion you held? For opinion can be wrong or right. Or was it a covenant that the Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted to you?” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not entrust us with anything he did not entrust to all people.” And he said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'In my community'—I think he said—'there are hypocrites.' I heard him, and I think he said it.”"],[2788,"Hudhayfa asked a village chief for water, and he gave him water in a silver vessel, so he threw it at him with a stone. Then he said, “Had I not already warned you once or twice that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking from gold and silver vessels, and that we should wear silk and brocade—for these are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter.”"],[2789,"\"It is not for a believer to humiliate himself.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, how does he humiliate himself?\" He said, \"He exposes himself to trials he cannot bear.\""],[2790,"\"A leader of a trial will surely enter Paradise, while his followers will surely enter Hell.\""],[2791,"My father informed us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from Hudhayfa, with something similar, but he did not raise it to the Prophet. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Messenger of God ﷺ except through Hudhayfa with this wording. Umar b. Habib al-Adawi, who attributed this hadith, was not a good memorizer, though his hadith was accepted. Al-Taymi was a man of sound texts, so it is possible that he raised it once and did not raise it another time."],[2792,"\"I only fear for you a man who recites the Quran until its beauty is seen upon him and he becomes a support for Islam, then he withdraws to whatever God wills, and comes out against his neighbor with his sword, accusing him of polytheism.\""],[2793,"\"People used to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about good, while I used to ask him about evil.\""],[2794,"The Messenger of God ﷺ told me what will happen until the Hour is established, except that I did not ask him what will expel the people of Madinah from it."],[2795,"He was with his father Bashir b. Sa'd in the mosque when Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani came and said to him, \"O Bashir, do you remember the sermon of the Messenger of God ﷺ about the caliphs?\" He said, \"No.\" Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman, who was sitting, said, \"I remember it.\" Abu Tha'laba sat with them, and Hudhayfa said, \"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Prophethood will remain among you as long as God wills it to remain, then He will lift it—Blessed and Exalted is He—when He wills. Then there will be a caliphate on the pattern of prophethood, and it will remain as long as God wills it to remain, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be a biting kingship, and it will remain as long as God wills, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be a oppressive kingship. Then there will be a caliphate on the pattern of prophethood.' Then he fell silent.\" Habib said, \"When Umar b. Abd al-Aziz assumed power, Ibn al-Nu'man said, 'I hope that Umar b. Abd al-Aziz is that one.'\" He said, \"Habib was admitted to Umar b. Abd al-Aziz and narrated to him, and it pleased him, meaning that.\""],[2796,"We entered upon Hudhayfa and said, \"Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said, \"If I narrated to you what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, you would not wait for the near night.\" They said, \"We do not want that from you; narrate to us what benefits us and does not harm you.\" He said, \"No, by the darkness of Mudar, God will not leave a righteous servant except that they will kill him, or tempt him, or God, the angels, and the believers will strike them until you do not prevent even the tail of a watercourse.\""],[2797,"I entered, I and 'Amr b. Sulay', upon Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman, and we said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, narrate to us"],[2798,"The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the good, while I used to ask him about the evil. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good? He said: O Hudhayfa, learn the Book of Allah and act according to what is in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will there be good after this evil? He said: \"A truce upon corruption, and a community upon specks in it.\""],[2799,"When the expedition of Tabuk took place, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller, who announced that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taken the mountain pass, so they should not take it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled through the pass, with 'Ammar driving and Hudhayfa leading him. Suddenly they came upon mounts carrying veiled people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Lead, lead; and O 'Ammar, drive, drive. 'Ammar advanced upon the people and struck the faces of their mounts. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pass, he said: \"O 'Ammar, I recognized the people,\" or he said: \"I recognized most of the people or the mounts. Do you know what the people intended?\" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"They intended to startle the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2800,"What prevented my father and me from witnessing Badr was only that I came with him intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ, when the disbelievers of Quraysh intercepted us and said: Where do you intend to go? We said: To Madinah. They said: You intend to go to Muhammad. Give us a covenant by Allah and His pledge that you will turn back to Madinah and not fight with him. So we gave them what they wanted, and they let us go. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of the news. He said: Fulfill your pledge to them, and we seek Allah's help against them. So they went to Madinah, and we went, and that is what prevented us."],[2801,"\"Do not be imma'ah (people who follow others blindly), saying: If the people do good, we do good, and if they do wrong, we do wrong. But train yourselves: if they do good, do good, and if they do wrong, do not commit injustice.\""],[2802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the expedition of Tabuk: No one should reach the water before me."],[2803,"Mahdi b. Maymun reported to us, from 'Uthman b. 'Ubayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet"],[2804,"\"Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream, which a Muslim sees or is seen for him.\""],[2805,"His Ummah was shown to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I stood behind him. When he finished, he turned to me and said: \"You were here; did you hear?\" I said: Yes. And Hudhayfa used to say: Is there in this what a man could retain? He said: He stood among us and informed us of what will happen until the Day of Resurrection, or he said: He informed us of what is between us and the Hour. Whoever retained it retained it, and whoever forgot it forgot it."],[2806,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the Dajjal was mentioned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The tribulation of some of you is more feared by me than the tribulation of the Dajjal. There is no tribulation, small or great, except it prepares for the tribulation of the Dajjal. Whoever escapes the tribulation before it will escape it. By Allah, it will not harm a Muslim; written between his eyes is 'disbeliever.'"],[2807,"The Dajjal was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: I am more fearful for you of the tribulation of some of you than of the tribulation of the Dajjal."],[2808,"He asked a dihqan (village chief) for water, and he brought him a silver vessel. He struck his face with it and said: Do you know why I did this to him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to eat from gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade, for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."],[2809,"While we were around Hudhayfah, he suddenly said: \"How will you be when the people of your Prophet's ﷺ household go out in two factions, striking one another's faces with the sword?\" We said: \"O Abu 'Abd Allah, will that really happen?\" He said: \"Yes, by the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, that will surely happen.\" One of his companions said: \"O Abu 'Abd Allah, what should we do if we live to see that time?\" He said: \"Look for the faction that calls to the cause of 'Ali ؓ and keep to it, for it is upon guidance.\""],[2810,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this matter?\" He said: \"Yes, evil and tribulation.\" I said: \"Will there be good after this evil?\" He said: \"Yes, a truce upon corruption, and a community upon filth.\" He said: I said: \"Will there be evil after this good?\" He said: \"Yes, a blind and deaf tribulation, and callers inviting to calamity. For you to die, O Hudhayfah, biting onto the trunk of a tree—meaning a stick—is better than responding to any of them.\""],[2811,"No one more closely resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in guidance and manner, from the time he leaves his house until he returns, than 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud."],[2812,"The dabb lizard is a nation that was transformed into animals on the earth; or: the dabb lizards are animals that were transformed on the earth."],[2813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting eating when a Bedouin came and took a morsel from it. The Prophet ﷺ took hold of his hand and said: \"Satan attends food when the name of Allah is not mentioned over it.\""],[2814,"The people disapproved of something concerning a ruler in the time of Hudhayfah. A man came into the mosque, the Great Mosque, weaving through the people until he reached Hudhayfah, who was sitting in a circle. He stood over his head and said: \"O companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, will you not enjoin good and forbid evil?\" Hudhayfah raised his head and understood what he intended. Hudhayfah said to him: \"Enjoining good and forbidding evil is indeed good, but it is not from the Sunnah to brandish the sword against your ruler.\""],[2815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us. Whenever prayer time came, he would descend and pray, then return to his place and tell us what would happen from that moment until the Hour would be established. There is no commander over a hundred or more who goes astray or is guided except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him to us. Some retained it and some forgot. Hudhayfah said: \"As for me, I learned evil and retained it. I knew that if I retained evil, I would avoid it, so I fell only into good.\""],[2816,"He saw a man praying without completing his bowing or prostration, and said: \"Since when have you been praying this prayer?\" He said: \"Since such and such a time.\" He said: \"If you were to die, you would die upon other than the Sunnah of Muhammad.\""],[2817,"There remain of the hypocrites only four, and of the people of this verse only three remain. One of them is a very old man who, if he drank water, would die. A man said to Hudhayfah: \"Who are these who dig into our houses and steal our valuables?\" He said: \"These are the wicked.\""],[2818,"Hudhayfah saw a man praying without straightening his back in bowing and prostration. When he finished, Hudhayfah called him and said: \"Since when have you been praying?\" He said: \"For forty years.\" He said: \"No, by Allah, you have not prayed for forty years. If you were to die today, you would die upon other than the natural disposition upon which Muhammad ﷺ was created.\" Then Hudhayfah said: \"A man may make the prayer brief while completing the bowing and prostration.\""],[2819,"When the Dajjal emerges, there will be with him water and fire. What people see as fire is actually cold water, and what they see as a garden is actually burning fire. Whoever of you lives to see that should fall into what he sees as fire, for it is cold water."],[2820,"A man among those before you was visited by the angel to take his soul. It was said to him: 'Have you done any good?' He said: 'I do not know of anything.' It was said to him: 'Think.' He said: 'I do not know of anything except that I used to do business with people and would give respite to the one in difficulty and overlook the debts of the one in difficulty.'"],[2821,"A man was close to death, or he said: death was present, so he said to his sons: 'When I die, gather a lot of firewood for me, light a fire in it, and throw me into it until it consumes my flesh and reaches my bones and scorches them. Then take them—meaning the bones—and make them, or he said: crush them; then look for a windy day and scatter them in the sea.' Allah gathered him and said: 'Why did you do that?' He said: 'Out of fear of You,' so Allah forgave him."],[2822,"He said about the Dajjal: 'With him will be a fire and water, but his fire is cool water, and his water is fire, so do not destroy yourselves.'"],[2823,"A man died and entered Paradise. It was said to him: 'What did you use to do?' He said—either they mentioned or he was reminded—he said: 'I used to sell to people on credit, and I would give respite to the one in difficulty and be lenient in the currency,' or he said: 'in the money.' He said: 'So he was forgiven.'"],[2824,"When the Prophet ﷺ went to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.'"],[2825,"When he went to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die,' and when he got up from his sleep, he would say: 'Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.'"],[2826,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and 'Umar."],[2827,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and 'Umar."],[2828,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and 'Umar."],[2829,"The Jews said to the Muslims, or to a group among the Muslims: 'What a good people you are, if only you did not say, \"Whatever Allah wills and whatever Muhammad wills.\"' This reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: 'Do not say, \"Whatever Allah wills and whatever Muhammad wills,\" but say, \"Whatever Allah wills alone.\"'"],[2830,"Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, from Khalid b. Abi al-Salt, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet."],[2831,"There will be rulers over you who will oppress and lie. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their oppression is not from me and I am not from him, and he will never come to me at the Pond. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their oppression is from me and I am from him, and he will come to me at the Pond."],[2832,"Yunus b. 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Rib'i b. Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet."],[2833,"\"There will be rulers over you who will oppress and lie. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Pond. And whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their oppression is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond.\""],[2834,"\"Among what people have attained from the words of earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, do as you wish.\""],[2835,"\"The earth has been made for me a place of prayer and a means of purification.\""],[2836,"\"Allah created every craftsman and his craft.\""],[2837,"\"Islam will wear away as the embroidery of a garment wears away.\""],[2838,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, something similar, as his own statement (mawquf)."],[2839,"\"The people will be gathered—meaning on the Day of Resurrection—and they will come to Adam and say: 'O our father, intercede for us to open the gate of Paradise.' He will say: 'Was it not for the sin of your father Adam that you were expelled from Paradise? I am not the one for that. Go to Ibrahim, the close friend of his Lord.' Ibrahim will say: 'I am not the one for that; I was only a close friend from behind a veil beyond a veil. Go to the one to whom Allah spoke directly.' They will come to Musa, and he will say: 'I am not the one for that. Go to 'Isa, the Word of Allah and His spirit.' He will say: 'I am not the one for that. Go to Muhammad ﷺ.' They will come to Muhammad ﷺ, and he will intercede. Then the sirat will be laid across, and the first of you will pass like lightning. I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom.' Then like the wind, and birds, and the running of men. Your Prophet ﷺ will be on the sirat saying: 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety,' until the people cross, until a man comes who can only crawl. On the sides of the sirat are hanging hooks that seize whom they are commanded to seize. Some will be scratched but saved, and some will be piled into the Fire.\" Then he said: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, the depth of Jahannam is seventy years' fall.\""],[2840,"\"Allah caused those before us to miss the Friday prayer.\""],[2841,"\"O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the lifespans of your Ummah.\" He said: \"Between fifty and sixty years.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who reach seventy?\" He said: \"Few of my Ummah reach it. May Allah have mercy on those who reach seventy, and may Allah have mercy on those who reach eighty.\""],[2842,"\"We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity.\""],[2843,"\"I was sitting with 'Umar when his companions asked him about trials (fitan). He said: 'Which of you heard it?' They said: 'We did.' He said: 'Perhaps you mean the trial of a man in his family, wealth, and children.' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'No, those are expiated by prayer, fasting, and charity. But which of you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ speak about the trials that surge like the waves of the sea?' The people fell silent. I said: 'I did.' He said: 'You are—I think he said—bold.' I said: 'Trials are presented to the hearts. Any heart that rejects them will have a white mark made in it, and any heart that absorbs them or is made to absorb them will have a black mark made in it, until the heart becomes one of two hearts: a white heart like a smooth stone, unharmed by any trial as long as the heavens and the earth remain, and another black heart, murky, that neither recognizes good nor rejects evil except what it has absorbed of its own desire.' And I told him that between them and that is a closed door that is about to be broken. 'Umar said: 'If it were opened, it might be closed again.' I said: 'No, rather it will be broken.' And I told him that that door is the killing of a man or his death—a narration without errors.\""],[2844,"\"We have been favored over others with three things: the entire earth has been made for us a place of prayer and a means of purification when we do not find water; our rows have been made like the rows of the angels; and I have been given these verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure house beneath the Throne, which were not given to anyone before me or after me.\""],[2845,"Whoever wears a garment of silk, Allah will clothe him with a garment of Fire, not from your days, but from the long days of Allah."],[2846,"Kathir b. Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Rib’i b. Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2847,"No people walk to the authority of Allah to humiliate him except that Allah humiliates them before the Day of Resurrection."],[2848,"There will come upon my Ummah a time when they will wish for the Dajjal. It was said: And because of what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then he took his ears—or he said: he took his ear—and shook them, then said: Because of the trials they will encounter, or a word similar to that."],[2849,"I sat with Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari and Hudhayfah, and one of them said to the other: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: No, rather you narrate. So one of them narrated, and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will say: Look into his deeds. He will say: My Lord, I used not to do any good, except that I had wealth and I used to mix with people through it. Whoever was well-off, I made things easy for him, and whoever was in difficulty, I granted him respite until his ease. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: I am more deserving of making things easy, so He will forgive him."],[2850,"A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection who had said to his family: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then face me toward a violent wind and scatter me. Then Allah will gather him on the Day of Resurrection and say to him: Why did you do that? He will say: From fear of You. He said: So He will forgive him."],[2851,"I sat with Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman and Abu Mas'ud, and one of them said: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Rather you narrate. So one of them narrated, and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection who had said to his family: When I die, burn me, and crush me, then face a violent wind and scatter me. He said: Then Allah will gather him on the Day of Resurrection and say: Why did you do this? He said: From fear of You. He said: So He forgave him."],[2852,"Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud—one of them narrated, and the other confirmed him—said: There was a man among the Children of Israel, and he had abundant wealth. When death approached him, he said to his family: Obey me in what I command you, or else I will give this wealth of mine to others than you. When I die, take me and burn me, then grind me, then wait until there is a day of violent wind and scatter me in the wind. So they did that to him. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gathered him, and he had never done any good at all. His Lord said to him: Why did you do this? He said: From fear of You, O my Lord. He said: So the mercy of Allah reached him."],[2853,"Whoever is sealed with fasting a day will enter Paradise."],[2854,"Do not precede the month until you complete the count or sight the crescent, then fast and do not break the fast until you complete the count or sight the crescent."],[2855,"Al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who said in it 'from Hudhayfah' except Jarir."],[2856,"He forbade adorning with gold."],[2857,"\"Draw near, O company of Mudar! By Allah, you will not cease to test every believer and kill him, or Allah will surely strike you, and His angels, and the believers, until you do not withhold even the belly of a watercourse.\" They said: \"Then why did you put us forward while we are like that?\" He said: \"Indeed among you is the master of the children of Adam, ﷺ, and among you are forerunners like the forerunners of horses.\""],[2858,"\"I know more about what is with the Dajjal than he does. With him is a fire that does not burn, and cold water. Whoever reaches him, let him close his eyes and enter his fire, for it is only cold water.\""],[2859,"\"We were commanded to use the siwak when we got up at night.\""],[2860,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up at night, he would rub his mouth with the siwak.\""],[2861,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and informed us of what will happen until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2862,"\"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came to a people's garbage dump and urinated standing. I went to move away from him, but he called me until I was at his heels. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[2863,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ."],[2864,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a people's garbage dump and urinated standing, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[2865,"\"The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with curly hair. With him are a garden and a fire. His fire is a garden, and his garden is a fire.\""],[2866,"\"Indeed with the Dajjal are a garden and a fire, a mountain of bread, and a river of water. His fire is a garden and his garden is a fire. He has curly hair, and his left eye is effaced.\""],[2867,"\"Count for me how many have uttered Islam.\" He said: So we wrote them down and found them to be five hundred. We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us?\" He said: \"Even if one of us prays only in secret.\""],[2868,"\"Count for me how many have uttered Islam.\" So we counted them, and we were between six hundred and seven hundred. We said: \"Do you fear for us?\" He said: \"Indeed you do not know.\" Then we were tested until a man would pray only while hiding."],[2869,"The hypocrites who are among you today are worse than the hypocrites who were at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said, \"O Abu 'Abd Allah, how is that?\" He said, \"Those concealed their hypocrisy, while these make it public.\""],[2870,"'Amr b. 'Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, in similar fashion. We do not know this hadith with this wording except from Hudhayfah, and it has been narrated from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah through more than one route."],[2871,"'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah."],[2872,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah."],[2873,"\"Who among you has memorized the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the fitnah (tribulation)?\" He said, \"I said, 'I memorize it as I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'You are bold indeed.' I said, 'The fitnah of a man in his own self, his family, and his wealth, which the fasting, prayer, charity, enjoining good, and forbidding evil expiate.' Then 'Umar said, 'That is not what I want; I mean the one that surges like the waves of the sea.' He said, \"I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, you have nothing to fear from it, for between you and it there is a closed door.' He said, 'Will the door be broken or opened?' I said, 'It will be broken.' He said, 'Then if it is broken, it will never be closed again?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'We were too awed to ask him.' He said, 'So we said to Masruq, \"Ask him.\"' He said, 'So we said, \"Did 'Umar ؓ know whom he meant?\" He said, \"Yes, just as he knew that tonight precedes tomorrow. I narrated to him a hadith that contains no errors.\"\""],[2874,"\"No one resembles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more in outward conduct and manner than 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud.\""],[2875,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet."],[2876,"\"He forbade wearing silk and brocade, and drinking from vessels of gold and silver, and he said, 'These are for them in this world, and for you in the Hereafter.'\""],[2877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk and brocade, and drinking from vessels of gold and silver, and he said, \"These are for them in this world, and for us in the Hereafter.\""],[2878,"Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, who said, \"And I do not think it is except from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet.\""],[2879,"\"Woe to the owner from the owned, and woe to the owned from the owner.\""],[2880,"\"Gabriel ﷺ came to me with something like a mirror in his palm, in the middle of which was a black spot. I said, 'O Gabriel, what is this?' He said, 'This is the world, its clarity and beauty.' I said, 'What is this black spot?' He said, 'This is Friday.' I said, 'What is Friday?' He said, 'A great day among the days of your Lord.' Then he mentioned its honor, virtue, and its name in the Hereafter. When Allah admits the people of Paradise to Paradise and the people of the Fire to the Fire, there is neither night nor day. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows the duration of those hours. When it is Friday, at the time of Friday when the people of Friday go out to their Friday prayer, a caller will call out, 'O people of Paradise, come out to the Abode of Increase.' Then they will come out onto dunes of musk.\" Hudhayfah said, \"By Allah, it is whiter than your flour.\" When they sit down and the people take their places, Allah sends upon them a wind called al-Muthirah, which stirs up white musk over them so that it enters their garments and comes out of their collars. That wind knows more about that perfume than the wife of one of you would if the perfume of all the people of the world were given to her. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says, \"Where are My servants who obeyed Me without seeing Me, who believed My messengers and did not see Me? Ask of Me, for this is the Day of Increase.\" They will unite on a single statement: \"We are pleased, so be pleased with us.\" He will return to them in His speech: \"O people of Paradise, if I were not pleased with you, I would not have lodged you in My Paradise. This is the Day of Increase, so ask of Me.\" They will unite on a single statement: \"Show us Your face that we may look upon it.\" Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will remove the veils and manifest Himself to them. His light will cover them, and had Allah not decreed that they not die, they would have been burned. Then it will be said to them, \"Return to your dwellings.\" They will return, having become hidden from their spouses, and their spouses hidden from them, due to the light of His manifestation that enveloped them. The light will continue to settle until they return to their state, or to their dwellings, as they were before. Their spouses will say to them, \"You left us with one appearance and returned to us with another.\" They will say, \"Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, manifested Himself to us, and we beheld what made us hidden from you.\" Thus they will luxuriate in the musk of Paradise and its bliss every seven days, and that is the Day of Increase.\""],[2881,"\"God will soon fill your hands with the non-Arabs and make them lions who do not flee; they will strike your necks and consume your spoils.\""],[2882,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us and informed us of what will happen until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2883,"\"The preserved ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ knew that Ibn Mas'ud was the closest of them to God in means.\""],[2884,"Umar was invited to a funeral, and he went out for it or intended to. I clung to him and said: 'Sit down, O Commander of the Faithful, for he is one of those.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, am I one of them?' He said: 'No, and I do not absolve anyone after you.'"],[2885,"When the Prophet ﷺ rose at night, he would rub his mouth with the tooth-stick."],[2886,"While I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ on the road to Madinah, I heard him say: 'I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and the Prophet of Mercy, and the Gatherer, the One Who Comes Last, and the Prophet of the Epic Battle or Battles.'"],[2887,"\"Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.\""],[2888,"Shabath b. Rib'i prayed beside Hudhayfa and spat in front of him. Hudhayfa said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade this and said to me: When a man stands in prayer, God turns His face toward him, so he should not turn away until he leaves or breaks wind.'"],[2889,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a people's garbage dump and urinated standing, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[2890,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash reported to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2891,"Sharik informed us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfa."],[2892,"We were with Umar ؓ and he said: 'Which of you memorizes the hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ about the trial?' I said: 'I do.' He said: 'Bring it, may your father be for God! How is it?' I said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The trial of a man in himself, his family, his wealth, and his children is expiated by fasting, prayer, charity, and enjoining good and forbidding evil.' Umar said: 'This is not what I want. I want the one that surges like the waves of the sea.' He said: 'There is no harm on you from it, O Commander of the Faithful. Between you and it is a closed door.' He said: 'Will that door be broken or opened?' I said: 'Rather, it will be broken.' He said: 'If it is broken, it will never be closed again.' And I narrated to him a hadith that is not among the errors."],[2893,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up at night, he would cleanse his mouth with the siwāk."],[2894,"They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint a successor over us? He said: If I appoint a successor over you and you disobey my successor, punishment will descend upon you. They said: Will you not appoint Abu Bakr? He said: If you appoint him, you will find him weak in body, strong in the matter of Allah. They said: Will you not appoint ‘Umar? He said: If you appoint him, you will find him strong in body, strong in the matter of Allah. They said: Will you not appoint ‘Ali? He said: If you appoint him—and you will not—he will lead you on the path, and you will find him guiding and guided."],[2895,"‘Ubaydah b. Mu‘tibb, from Abu Wa’il, from Hudhayfah."],[2896,"The Prophet ﷺ met me while I was in a state of major impurity, and he wanted to shake my hand, so I said: I am in a state of major impurity. He said: The believer does not become impure."],[2897,"Mis‘ar informed us, from Waṣil, from Abu Wa’il, from Hudhayfah, similarly. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Waṣil, from Abu Wa’il, from Hudhayfah, so we have sufficed with those we named."],[2898,"A slanderer will not enter Paradise."],[2899,"He saw a man praying without properly performing his bowing or prostration, so he said: How long have you been praying this prayer? He said: For such-and-such. He said: If you were to die, you would die upon other than the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ."],[2900,"I said: O Abu ‘Abd Allah, is hypocrisy today more prevalent, or was it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said—striking his hand on his forehead—Alas! Indeed, today it is open, whereas they used to conceal it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2901,"The hypocrites among you today are worse than the hypocrites who were during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said: How is that? He said: Those concealed their hypocrisy, but these have made it public."],[2902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk and brocade, and drinking from vessels of gold and silver. He said: These are for them in this world, and for you in the Hereafter."],[2903,"I was with Hudhayfah ؓ when ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud and Abu Musa passed by. He said: The one who most resembles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the time he leaves his house until he returns to his family is ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud."],[2904,"When one of you spits in the mosque, let him not spit to his right, but to his left or under his foot."],[2905,"\"Whoever eats from this foul tree or this foul herb, let him not approach our mosque.\""],[2906,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Confederates: \"They distracted us from the middle prayer. May God fill their houses and their graves with fire.\""],[2907,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ met a number of men on the night of al-'Aqabah.\""],[2908,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met Gabriel at the stones of al-Murri. He said: \"I have been sent to an unlettered nation, and to those who have never read a book.\" Gabriel said: \"God commands you to recite the Qur'an according to one harf.\" Michael said: \"Ask him for more.\" He said: \"Recite according to two harfs.\" Michael said: \"Ask him for more,\" until it reached seven harfs."],[2909,"Abu 'Awanah reported to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy b. Ka'b, from the Prophet ﷺ, a report similar to the hadith of Hudhayfah."],[2910,"\"I had the pre-dawn meal with the Prophet ﷺ, then I went out for the morning prayer.\""],[2911,"\"The distance between the two ends of my basin is the distance between Aylah and Mudar, or more. Its vessels are as numerous as, or like the number of, the stars of the sky. It is sweeter than honey, whiter than milk, and more fragrant than the scent of musk. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst thereafter.\""],[2912,"I am Muhammad and Ahmad, and I am al-Muqaffi and al-Muhashshir, and the Prophet of Repentance."],[2913,"Umar said to us: \"Which of you will narrate to us about the tribulation as he heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" Hudhayfah said: \"I said: I will.\" He said: \"Speak, for you are indeed bold.\" I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, the tribulation of a man in his family, his wealth, and his neighbor is expiated by fasting, prayer, and charity.\" He said: \"I did not ask about this. Rather I asked about the one that surges like the sea surges.\" I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, between you and it there is a closed door.\" He said: \"Will it be broken or opened?\" I said: \"No, rather it will be broken.\" He said: \"That is more likely never to be closed.\" He said: \"I said to Hudhayfah: 'Does he know who the closed door is?' He said: 'Yes, by God, he knows it as one of you knows that tonight comes before tomorrow.' I narrated to him a hadith that is not among errors.\""],[2914,"The Prophet ﷺ stood and called the people, saying: \"Come to me.\" They came to him and sat down. He said: \"This is the messenger of the Lord of the Worlds, Gabriel, who breathed into my heart that no soul dies until it has completed its provision, even if it is delayed. So fear God and be graceful in seeking. Let not the delay of provision cause you to seek it through disobedience to God, for what is with God can only be attained through obedience to Him.\""],[2915,"\"Did the Prophet ﷺ not pray in the Bayt al-Maqdis?\" I said: \"Yes, he did.\" Hudhayfah said: \"What is your name?\" I said: \"Zirr.\" Hudhayfah said: \"Recite: 'Glory be to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque' (17:1). Do you find that he prayed? Had he prayed in it, prayer would have been prescribed for you in it just as circumambulation of the House has been prescribed for you. The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a long-backed, stretched-out beast called al-Buraq, whose stride was as far as the eye could see. He said: 'We did not leave its back—I and Gabriel, upon them be peace ﷺ , meaning the back of the beast or the back of al-Buraq—until we saw Paradise and Hell.'\""],[2916,"The people dispersed from the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the Confederates, and none remained with him except a few. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me while I was sleeping and said: \"Go to the camp of the Confederates and look.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not get up to come to you except out of shyness from the cold\"—or he said: \"from the severity of the cold.\" He said: \"Go.\" So I went until I reached their camp. I found Abu Sufyan lighting a fire, warming his back among a small group around him, and the Confederates had dispersed from him. I came and sat among them. Abu Sufyan sensed that someone not of their own had entered among them, so he said: \"Let each man among you take the hand of the one sitting next to him.\" I struck my hand to the one on my right and took his hand, then I struck my hand to the one on my left and took his hand. I remained a little while, then I got up and went to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying. He gestured to me to come close, so I drew near until he extended to me part of the garment he was wearing to warm me. When he finished his prayer, he said: \"O Ibn al-Yaman, sit down. What news of the people?\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, the people have dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and none remain except a small group kindling a fire. God has poured upon them cold like what He poured upon us.\" The Prophet ﷺ threw his garment over me and I slept. Then he said: \"Arise, O sleepy one.\""],[2917,"Khalid b. 'Abd Allah reported to us, from Abu Sa'd, meaning Sa'id b. al-Marzuban, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it or close to it. This statement we do not know anyone reported except Hudhayfah, and it has been reported from Hudhayfah via another route. As for the hadith of Abu Sa'd, we do not know anyone reported it except Khalid and Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash."],[2918,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Hudhayfah, do you know what is the right of Allah upon His servants?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" Then he rode on and said: \"O Hudhayfah.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, if they do that?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"He forgives them.\""],[2919,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while al-'Abbas was sitting on his right and Fatimah ؓ on his left. He said: \"O Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, do good deeds for Allah, for I cannot avail you anything against Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: meaning he said that three times. Then he said: \"O 'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, do good deeds for Allah, for I cannot avail you anything against Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said it three times. Then he said: \"O Hudhayfah, come closer.\" So I came closer. Then he said: \"O Hudhayfah, whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah\" and believes, I think he said, \"in what I have brought, Allah makes the Fire forbidden for him and Paradise obligatory for him. And whoever fasts Ramadan seeking the Face of Allah and the Hereafter, Allah seals it for him and makes the Fire forbidden for him. And whoever gives charity seeking thereby the Face of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and the Hereafter, and whoever performs Hajj to the House of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, seeking the Face of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and the Hereafter, Allah seals it for him and makes the Fire forbidden for him and Paradise obligatory for him.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should I keep this secret or make it public?\" He said: \"Make it public.\""],[2920,"\"Accustom yourselves to patience, for tribulation is about to descend upon you, although no tribulation will afflict you more severe than what afflicted us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2921,"He used to say in his bowing: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent, and with His praise,\" three times, and in his prostration: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, and with His praise,\" three times."],[2922,"I said: \"How did you recognize the hypocrites?\" He said: \"I was with the Prophet ﷺ one night and he named them.\""],[2923,"He used to say in his bowing: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,\" three times, and in his prostration: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,\" three times."],[2924,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed at the eclipse of the sun. He stood and said the takbir, then recited, then bowed for about as long as he recited, then raised for about as long as he bowed, then bowed for about as long as he recited, then raised for about as long as he bowed. He did that four rak'ahs before prostrating two prostrations. Then he stood for the second time and did the same, and he did not recite between the two bowings."],[2925,"The people of Najran came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Send us a trustworthy man.\" He said: \"I will certainly send you a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy.\" The people competed for it, and he sent Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah ؓ."],[2926,"People will be gathered on a single plain, and no soul will speak. The first one, I think he said, to speak will be Muhammad ﷺ, and he will say: \"At your service, and at your command. All good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. The guided one is the one You guide. Your servant is before You, and from You and to You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. Blessed and Exalted are You. Glory be to You, Lord of the House.\" This is His saying: 'It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.'"],[2927,"\"Islam is eight shares: Islam is one share, prayer is one share, zakah is one share, Hajj to the House is one share, fasting is one share, commanding good is one share, forbidding evil is one share, and jihad in the path of Allah is one share. And he has failed who has no share.\""],[2928,"Islam is eight shares."],[2929,"Verily, the slander of a chaste woman destroys the deeds of one hundred years."],[2930,"The polytheists seized me and my father while we were heading to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr. They said: Where are you going? We said: To Madinah. He said: You intend [to join] Muhammad. So give us a covenant by Allah and His solemn pledge that you will not fight alongside him and that you will return to Madinah. We gave them what they wanted, so they let us go. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the news. He said: 'Fulfill your covenant with them, and we will seek Allah's help against them.' That is what prevented us from witnessing Badr."],[2931,"He used to say in his bowing: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent' three times, and in his prostration: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High' three times."],[2932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to look carefully at the eye and the ear [when performing ablution]."],[2933,"Whoever separates from the community by a handspan has left Islam."],[2934,"He used to say between the two prostrations: 'O Allah, forgive me,' repeating it many times. And when he raised his head, he would say: 'Glory be to the Possessor of dominion, might, pride, and greatness.'"],[2935,"Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-'Ala' b. al-Musayyib, from 'Amr b. Murrah, from Talhah b. Yazid, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. Al-'Ala' b. al-Musayyib did not say in his hadith 'from a man of Banu 'Abs'; he only sent it as mursal, and the man of Banu 'Abs is considered to be Silah."],[2936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the choice between emigration and support, so I chose emigration."],[2937,"Every nation has Magians, and the Magians of this nation are those who say there is no decree. If they fall ill, do not visit them; if they die, do not attend their funerals. They are the followers of the Dajjal, and it is incumbent upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to gather them with him."],[2938,"All of you are children of Adam, and Adam was created from dust. People will certainly stop boasting about their ancestors, or they will surely be more insignificant in the sight of Allah than the dung beetle."],[2939,"The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, while I used to ask him about evil."],[2940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: 'If you saw a man with Umm Ruman, what would you do to him?' He said: 'By Allah, I would do evil to him.' He said: 'And you, Umar?' He said: 'By Allah, I would kill him. I would say: May Allah curse the most helpless, for he is wicked.' He said: 'Then the verse was revealed: And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves...'"],[2941,"Abu 'Asim reported to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd b. Yathi', and he did not say from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2942,"\"Sheep are a blessing, camels are a source of honor for their owners, horses have goodness in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, your slave is your brother, so be kind to him, and if you find him overwhelmed, then help him.\""],[2943,"The people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Confederates, and no one remained with him except twelve men. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was crouching from sleep and said: \"O Ibn al-Yaman, get up and go to the camp of the Confederates and look at their situation.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I only got up for you out of shyness from the cold.\" He said: \"Go, O Ibn al-Yaman, no harm will befall you from cold or heat until you return to me.\" So I went until I came to their camp and found Abu Sufyan lighting a fire among a small group around him, while the Confederates had already dispersed from him. I came and sat among them. Abu Sufyan sensed that someone other than his own had entered among them and said: \"Let each man of you take the hand of the one sitting next to him.\" He said: I struck my hand over the one on my right and took his hand, then I struck my hand over the one on my left and took his hand. He said: I stayed among them for a short while, then I got up and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing praying. He gestured to me to come closer, so I came closer, then gestured to me to come closer, so I came closer, until he wrapped over me some of the garment he had on to warm me. When he finished his prayer, he said: \"O Ibn al-Yaman, sit down. What is the news of the people?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the people have dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and no one remains with him except a small group lighting a fire. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has poured upon them cold like that which He poured upon us, but we hope from Allah what they do not hope.\""],[2944,"There are no tents after tents that were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that protect them as these tents protect, and no people intend them with evil except that Allah brings upon them what distracts them from them."],[2945,"When 'Uthman ؓ was killed, Hudhayfah was approached and it was said: \"O Abu 'Abd Allah, this man has been killed, and the people have differed. What do you say?\" He said: \"Support me.\" So they supported him against a man's chest, and he said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Abu al-Yaqzan is upon the natural disposition; Abu al-Yaqzan is upon the natural disposition. He will not abandon it until he dies or old age touches him.'\""],[2946,"\"How excellent is moderation in wealth, moderation in poverty, and moderation in worship.\""],[2947,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqabah, while 'Ammar was leading him and I was driving from behind, when some riding camels presented themselves, wanting the Messenger of Allah. 'Ammar ؓ struck their faces, and behold, there were masked men, twelve men. When they passed by, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What did the people intend?\" I said: \"They intended to startle the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Do you recognize them?\" I said: \"Yes.\""],[2948,"Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud met, and one of them said to his companion: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar,'\" and the other confirmed it."],[2949,"He asked a village chief for water, and he brought him a silver vessel. He struck his face with it and said: \"Do you know why I did this to him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to eat in gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade, for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter.\""],[2950,"As for the hadith of Ibn 'Awn, Muhammad b. al-Muthanna reported to us, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Ibn 'Awn, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2951,"Sufyan reported to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2952,"\"He forbade us to drink from vessels of gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade, and he said: 'They are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter.'\""],[2953,"He forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver."],[2954,"A slanderer will not enter Paradise."],[2955,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met me while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and he wanted to shake my hand, so I said, \"I am in a state of major ritual impurity.\" He said, \"Indeed the believer does not become impure.\""],[2956,"He passed by some people in the mosque and said, \"O assembly of reciters, follow the path, for by God, if you follow it, you will have gone far ahead, and if you take right or left, you will have strayed far.\""],[2957,"Hudhayfa ؓ saw a man sitting in the middle of the circle and said, \"As for this one, he is cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ,\" or he said, \"Cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ is whoever sits in the middle of the circle.\""],[2958,"The Prophet ﷺ shook my hand while I was in a state of major ritual impurity."],[2959,"I went out to Kufa at the time Tustar was conquered to buy mules from there. I entered the mosque and there was a group of men, whom if you saw them you would know they were from the men of the Hijaz. Among them was a man. I said, \"Who is this?\" The people indicated to me with their eyes and said, \"Do you not know him? This is Hudhayfa, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said, \"People used to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil. I said, 'O Messenger of God, do you think this good that God has given us will be followed by evil as there was before it?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the protection from that?' He said, 'The sword.' I said, 'Is there any remainder for the sword?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'Then what?' He said, 'A truce upon corruption, and a community upon division. If God, Blessed and Exalted, has a caliph on that day, he will strike your back and take your wealth, so listen and obey; otherwise die while biting onto the trunk of a tree.' He said, 'Then what?' He said, 'Then the Dajjal will emerge with him a river and a fire. Whoever falls into his fire, his reward becomes obligatory and his burden is lifted; whoever falls into his river, his burden becomes obligatory and his reward is lifted.' He said, 'Then what?' He said, 'Then it is the establishment of the Hour.'\""],[2960,"Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman b. Qurt, from Hudhayfa, or from a man, from Hudhayfa, something similar."],[2961,"People used to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil, fearing that it would overtake me. I said, \"O Messenger of God, we were in ignorance and evil, then God, Blessed and Exalted, brought this good. So is there any evil after this good?\" He said, \"Yes, tribulation and evil.\" I said, \"Is there any good after that evil?\" He said, \"Yes, a truce upon corruption.\" I said, \"What is its corruption?\" He said, \"You will be guided by other than guidance from them.\" I said, \"Is there any evil after that good?\" He said, \"Yes, callers at the gates of Hell. Whoever answers them, they will cast him into it.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, describe them to us.\" He said, \"They speak with our tongues.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you command me if it overtakes me?\" Meaning that time. He said, \"Cling to the community of the people and their imam.\" I said, \"What if they have no community?\" He said, \"Then be patient, even if you have to bite onto a tree until death overtakes you, while you are like that.\""],[2962,"\"Whoever establishes in Islam a good practice that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it without any of their rewards being diminished. And whoever establishes in Islam an evil practice that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it without any of their burdens being diminished.\""],[2963,"Khalid al-Hadhha and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu 'Ubaydah b. Hudhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This hadith was narrated by Abd al-Warith, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, and the hadith of Hudhayfa is more authentic than the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."],[2964,"The verse of inheritance without direct heirs (al-kalala) was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a journey. The Prophet ﷺ stopped, and there was Hudhayfa, with the head of Hudhayfa's she-camel at the Prophet's ﷺ waist-wrapper. He received it from him, and Hudhayfa looked and saw Umar b. al-Khattab, so he passed it to him. When it was during the caliphate of Umar ؓ, Umar looked into al-kalala and called Hudhayfa and asked him about it. Hudhayfa said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed it to me, and I pass it to you as he passed it to me. By God, I am truthful. By God, I will never add anything to that for you ever.\""],[2965,"Whoever imitates a people is one of them."],[2966,"Whoever sells a house or real estate and does not put some of its price into its like, he will not be blessed in it."],[2967,"We were with Hudhayfah in Tabaristan, and Sa'id b. al-'As said: 'Which of you prayed the prayer of fear with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Hudhayfah said: 'I did.' So he led these in one rak'ah and these in one rak'ah, and they did not make up—meaning neither of the two groups made up—as if they were satisfied with one rak'ah each."],[2968,"The excellence of knowledge is more beloved to me than the excellence of worship, and the best of your religion is piety (wara')."],[2969,"There was sharpness in my tongue against my family, and it did not go beyond them to others. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a hundred times a day.'"],[2970,"Hudhayfah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am sharp-tongued, and most of that is against my family.' He said: 'Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a hundred times a day.'"],[2971,"Sufyan reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Ubayd Abu al-Mughirah, from Hudhayfah, and he mentioned something similar from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2972,"Ziyad b. 'Abd Allah reported to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim b. Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[2973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my shin—or his shin—and said: 'The right of the lower garment is here. If you refuse, then here. If you refuse, then the lower garment has no right to the ankles—or the ankles have no right to the lower garment.'"],[2974,"I will precede you; if you do not find me, then I will be at the Pond. The Pond is between Aylah and Makkah. Some people—men and women—will come with vessels, but they will not taste anything from it."],[2975,"Whoever has a slave-girl, educates her well and treats her kindly, then frees her and marries her, will have two rewards."],[2976,"Any man who has a slave-girl, teaches her good manners, educates her well, and teaches her knowledge well, then frees her and marries her will have two rewards. Any slave who fulfills the right of Allah upon him and the right of his masters will have two rewards. Any man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then accepted Islam and believed in Muhammad ﷺ will have two rewards."],[2977,"Sufyan reported to us, from Salih b. Salih, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know of anyone who narrated this wording from the Prophet ﷺ except Abu Musa al-Ash'ari."],[2978,"\"Any man who has a slave girl, educates her well, teaches her, then frees her and marries her — he will have two rewards.\""],[2979,"\"Abu Musa asked permission to enter upon Umar three times, but he was not granted permission, so he left. Umar met him and said: 'What made you turn back?' He said: 'I asked permission three times and was not granted permission, so I returned. We ask permission as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us: if we are granted permission, we enter; otherwise, we return.' Umar said: 'You must bring me proof of this, or I will do something to you.' So Abu Musa went until he came to the gathering of his people and informed them. They said: 'No one will stand with you except the youngest among us. Get up, O Abu Sa'id.' So he stood with him before Umar and informed him, and Umar let him go.\""],[2980,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to us and said to us: \"Umar ordered me to bring him proof because I came to him and asked permission three times, but I was not granted permission, so I returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever asks permission three times and is not granted it, let him return.' Umar said: 'You must bring me proof of this or I will cause you pain.' So I came to you so that you may stand with me.\" Ubayy b. Ka'b said: \"No one will stand with you except the youngest of the people.\" I was the youngest of the people, so I stood with him."],[2981,"Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Aruba, reported to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet."],[2982,"Yahya b. Sa'id reported to us, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[2983,"And Abu Kamil and 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath reported to us, both saying: Abu 'Awana reported to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[2984,"\"The example of a believer who recites the Quran is like a citron: its fragrance is pleasant and its taste is pleasant. The example of a believer who does not recite the Quran is like a date fruit: its taste is pleasant but it has no fragrance. The example of a hypocrite — and Sa'id said in his hadith: the example of a wicked person — who recites the Quran is like sweet basil: its fragrance is pleasant but its taste is bitter. And the example of a hypocrite — and Sa'id said: a wicked person — who does not recite the Quran is like colocynth: its taste is bitter and its fragrance is unpleasant.\""],[2985,"\"The destruction of my nation will be through stabbing and the plague.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing, but what is the plague?\" He said: \"A poke from your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.\""],[2986,"I heard Abu Musa narrating from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu Bakr said: \"This hadith was also narrated by al-Hajjaj b. Arta'a, from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqa, but he differed from Shu'ba and from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali.\""],[2987,"\"The destruction of my nation will be through stabbing and the plague.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing, but what is the plague?\" He said: \"A poke from your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.\""],[2988,"Sa'dad b. Sulayman reported to us, from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqa, from Yazid b. al-Harith, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2989,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, and we raised our voices. He drew near to us and said: “O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent; you are only calling upon One who is All-Hearing, All-Seeing. Indeed, the One you call upon is closer to any one of you than the neck of his mount.” Then he said: “O ʿAbd Allah b. Qays, shall I not teach you a word that is one of the treasures of Paradise: There is no power and no strength except with God.”"],[2990,"Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd reported to us, from Sulaymān al-Taymī, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet."],[2991,"Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ reported to us, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet."],[2992,"Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm reported to us, from al-Jurayrī, from Abū Tamīmah, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Abū Mūsā. Abū Bakr said: We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Jurayrī, from Abū Tamīmah, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Abū Mūsā, except Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm."],[2993,"We were on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and whenever we ascended a hill or climbed a height—or he said: descended into a valley—we raised our voices with takbīr. The Messenger of God ﷺ drew near to us and said: “O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent; you are only calling upon One who is All-Hearing, All-Seeing. Indeed, the One you call upon is closer to any one of you than the neck of his mount.” Then he said: “O ʿAbd Allah b. Qays, shall I not teach you a word that is one of the treasures of Paradise: There is no power and no strength except with God.”"],[2994,"Shuʿbah and al-Thawrī, both together, reported to us, from Qays b. Muslim, from Ṭāriq b. Shihāb, from Abū Mūsā."],[2995,"I arrived from Yemen while the Messenger of God ﷺ was at al-Baṭḥāʾ. He said: “Did you perform Hajj?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “What did you say?” I said: “I said: Labbayka with an ihlāl like the ihlāl of the Prophet ﷺ.” He said: “You have done well. Go to the House and circumambulate it, then perform saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, then exit iḥrām.” He said: So I went to the House, circumambulated it, and performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah."],[2996,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded fasting on ʿĀshūrāʾ—or he said: he used to fast it."],[2997,"God, Blessed and Exalted, has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down for it a cure. So you should take to the milk of cows, for they graze on every kind of tree."],[2998,"Shuʿbah reported to us, from al-Rukayn b. al-Rabīʿ, from Qays b. Muslim, from Ṭāriq b. Shihāb, from ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd."],[2999,"Shuʿbah reported to us, from al-Rukayn b. al-Rabīʿ, from Qays b. Muslim, from Ṭāriq b. Shihāb, from ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd."],[3000,"Shuʿbah reported to us, from al-Rabīʿ b. al-Rukayn, from Qays b. Muslim, from Ṭāriq b. Shihāb, from ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd."],[3001,"Sufyan reported to us, from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abd Allah b. Mas'ud. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Sufyan except Muhammad b. Yusuf, and al-Mas'udi narrated it from Qays, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abd Allah b. Mas'ud."],[3002,"Umar b. Ali al-Muqaddami reported to us, from al-Mas'udi, and all of these agreed: from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abd Allah b. Mas'ud. And Muhammad b. Jabir said: from Qays b. Muslim, from Tariq b. Shihab, from Abu Musa, and he erred in it, and he was of poor memory. We mention these hadiths only to clarify the defect of this hadith."],[3003,"Al-A'mash reported to us, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3004,"\"No one is more patient in enduring harm that he hears than Allah, Blessed and Exalted: they ascribe a son to Him, yet He grants them well-being and provides for them.\""],[3005,"Al-A'mash reported to us, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And Abu Musa is Abd Allah b. Qays, so he said: from Abd Allah, without specifying his lineage."],[3006,"Ali b. Abi Talib reminded us of a prayer that we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which we had either forgotten or abandoned. He said: \"He used to say takbir when he bowed and when he raised his head from bowing.\""],[3007,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who fights out of courage, a man who fights out of tribal pride, and a man who fights to show off. Which of these is in the path of Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the path of Allah.\""],[3008,"Shu'ba reported to us, from Amr b. Murra, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3009,"That a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights for booty, and a man fights so that his position may be seen. Which of these is in the path of Allah? He said: \"Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the path of Allah.\""],[3010,"Al-A'mash reported to us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa."],[3011,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet caught up with them? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[3012,"\"Indeed, before the Hour there will be days in which ignorance descends and in which al-harj increases.\" We said: And what is al-harj? He said: \"Killing, killing.\""],[3013,"He was asked: 'Which aspect of Islam is best?' He said: 'One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.' It was said: 'Then which jihad is best?' He said: 'One whose horse is wounded and whose blood is shed.' It was said: 'Then which prayer is best?' He said: 'Long qunūt.'"],[3014,"Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and release the captive."],[3015,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us with four [statements] and said: 'Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, does not sleep, and it is not befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the scale'—Abū Bakr said: I think he said—'and raises it. The deed of the night is raised to Him by day, and the deed of the day by night. His veil is light; if He were to remove it, the splendors of His face would burn every creature that His sight reaches.'"],[3016,"He lowers the scale and raises it. And he said: 'Every thing that His sight reaches.'"],[3017,"Shuʿba informed us, from ʿAmr b. Murra, who said: I heard Abū ʿUbayda narrating from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet."],[3018,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, extends His hand by night so that the sinner of the day may repent, until the sun rises from its west."],[3019,"He named himself for us with names, some of which we remembered. He said: 'I am Muḥammad, Aḥmad, al-Ḥāshir, al-Muqaffī, the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of the great battle.'"],[3020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named himself for us with names, some of which we remembered. He said: 'I am Muḥammad, Aḥmad, al-Ḥāshir, al-Muqaffī, and the Prophet of the great battle.'"],[3021,"Abū Mūsā sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar three times, but he was not granted permission, as he was busy. When he finished, he said: 'Did I not hear ʿAbd Allah b. Qays? Let him enter.' It was said: 'He has gone back.' He said: 'Call him.' So he said: 'We were commanded to do that.' He said: 'You must bring clear proof for that.' He went to a gathering of the Anṣār, and they said: 'No one will testify for you except the youngest among us, Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī.' So he testified for him. Then ʿUmar said: 'Was this matter of the Messenger of God ﷺ hidden from me? The bargaining in the markets distracted me. But ask of me whatever you wish, and do not seek permission.'"],[3022,"Al-Ashʿarī informed us, from the Prophet."],[3023,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam from a handful that He took from all the earth. So his descendants came according to that: among them the white, the red, the black, the easy-going, the hard, the wicked, the good, and those in between."],[3024,"The example of the righteous companion is that of the perfume seller: either he will give you some of his perfume, or some of its fragrance will reach you. And the example of the bad companion is that of the blacksmith: either he will burn your garment, or make you stink, or his odor will harm you."],[3025,"The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is that of a citron: its taste is good and its fragrance is good. The parable of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is that of a date: its taste is good but it has no fragrance. The parable of the hypocrite who recites the Qur'an is that of sweet basil: its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. The parable of the hypocrite who does not recite the Qur'an is that of the colocynth: its taste is bitter and its fragrance is foul."],[3026,"When Adam was brought out of the Garden, he was given provision from the fruits of the Garden, and He taught him the craft of everything. So these fruits of yours are from the fruits of the Garden, except that these change while those do not change."],[3027,"Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Qasama, from Abu Musa something similar, and he did not raise it to the Prophet."],[3028,"When the verse 'And warn your closest kindred' was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ began calling them tribe by tribe."],[3029,"When God, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam ﷺ , He took from his clay two handfuls: a handful with His right hand and a handful with His other hand. He said concerning the one in His right hand: 'These are for the Garden, and I do not care.' He said concerning the one in His other hand: 'These are for the Fire, and I do not care.' Then He returned them to Adam's loins, so they multiply accordingly until now."],[3030,"Any woman who perfumes herself so that her scent is noticed is like an adulteress."],[3031,"Every eye commits adultery."],[3032,"The number of the people of Badr was the number of the companions of Talut on the day of Jalut: three hundred and seventeen."],[3033,"I supplicated for the Arabs, saying: 'O God, whoever among them meets You believing in You and certain, forgive him.'"],[3034,"The parable of the heart is like a feather in a desolate land, which the wind turns over from back to belly."],[3035,"There was a dispute between this tribe and the Ash'aris, so we were with Abu Musa. Food containing chicken meat was brought to him, and with him was a man from Banu Taym Allah, reddish as if he were from the clients. He called him to the food, but the man said: 'I saw it eating something, so I found it disgusting, and I swore not to eat it.' Abu Musa said: 'Come, let me tell you about that. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a group of Ash'aris asking him to provide us mounts. He said: By God, I will not provide you mounts, and I have nothing to mount you on. Then some camels were brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he asked about us, saying: Where are the Ash'ari group? He ordered for us five young camels with white humps. When we returned, we said: The Messenger of God ﷺ swore not to mount us and had nothing to mount us on, yet he mounted us. We overlooked the Messenger of God's ﷺ oath; by God, we will never succeed. So we went back to him and said: We asked you to mount us, and you swore not to mount us, but you mounted us. He said: I did not mount you; rather God mounted you. By God, I do not swear an oath and then see something better than it except that I do what is better and expiate my oath.'"],[3036,"Sufyan b. 'Uyayna informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3037,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3038,"Shu'bah informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to the hadith of 'Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam and al-Qasim al-Taymi, with something similar to it. And the hadith of Shu'bah from al-Taymi — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Badal b. al-Muhabbar."],[3039,"I entered upon Abu Musa ؓ while he was eating chicken meat, and he said: \"Come near and eat, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating chicken.\""],[3040,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating chicken meat."],[3041,"Mahdi b. Maymun informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[3042,"\"He is not one of us who shaves (the head), tears (the clothes), or wails.\""],[3043,"Abu Musa fell unconscious, and they wept over him. He said: \"I declare myself innocent before you of that from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared himself innocent to us.\" He said: \"He is not one of us who shaves, tears, or wails.\""],[3044,"We went out with the Ash'aris, and we returned, and a group of us, including myself, hurried ahead and became separated from the people. A slave girl came on a mule, so I brought her near a tree and helped her dismount, then I returned to my seat. Abu Musa said to me: \"Shall I not tell you a hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tell us?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Before the Hour is the harj.\" We said: \"What is the harj?\" He said: \"Killing and lying.\" We said to the Ash'ari: \"More than what we kill today?\" He said: \"It is not your killing the disbelievers.\" We fell silent, and none of us spoke a clear word. He said: \"We said: Then what?\" He said: \"A man killing his brother.\" We said: \"Will we have our minds on that day?\" He said: \"The minds of most of your time, or most of the people of your time, will not be taken away. A worthless multitude of people will succeed them, most of whom think they are upon something, but they are not upon anything. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I feared that those days would overtake me and you, and I do not know of any way out for me or for you from them, according to what our Prophet ﷺ enjoined upon us, except that we exit from them as we entered into them, without introducing anything new into them.\""],[3045,"Muhammad b. Ja'far and Ibn Abi 'Adi informed us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, from Usayd, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[3046,"I heard Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Hittan b. 'Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa with something similar to it, and he did not raise it to the Prophet."],[3047,"\"No one of this Ummah, nor any Jew or Christian, hears of me and then does not believe in me, except that he will be among the people of the Fire.\""],[3048,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he entered one of the gardens of the Ansar and performed ablution. Then he came and sat on the edge of the well. Then he said: \"O Abu Musa, guard the gate for me.\" A man asked permission to enter, and he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" It was Abu Bakr ؓ, so he entered and praised Allah. The Prophet ﷺ seated him on his right. Then 'Umar ؓ asked permission, and he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" He entered and he seated him on his left, and the edge of the well became full. Then 'Uthman ؓ asked permission, and he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial that will afflict him.\" He entered, and the edge of the well had become full, so he sat facing them."],[3049,"Sa'id b. Yazid Abu Maslama reported to us from Abu Nadra, from Abu Musa."],[3050,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi reported to us from Sa'id b. Abi 'Aruba, from Isma'il b. 'Imran, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa."],[3051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a walled garden in Madinah, wrapped himself in his garment, and I locked the gate—I think he said: behind him. A man came and knocked on the gate, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O 'Abd Allah b. Qays, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" I opened it and it was Abu Bakr. I said: \"Rejoice! May Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings; rejoice in Paradise.\" He entered, praised Allah, and sat down. Then another man came and knocked on the gate, so he said: \"O 'Abd Allah, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" I opened it and it was 'Umar. I said: \"Rejoice! May Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings; rejoice in Paradise.\" He praised Allah and sat down. Then another man came and knocked on the gate, so he said: \"O 'Abd Allah b. Qays, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and he will meet and will meet [tribulation].\" It was 'Uthman. I said: \"Rejoice! May Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings of Paradise.\" He praised Allah and sat down. Then he said: \"What is this word that you said to me and did not say to my two companions?\""],[3052,"A doorkeeper sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" It was Abu Bakr. Then another sought permission, so he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" It was 'Umar. Then another sought permission, so he said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise, upon affliction\"—I think he said: that will befall him. It was 'Uthman. 'Uthman said: \"I ask Allah for patience.\""],[3053,"Abu Musa ؓ led them in prayer. When he sat for the tashahhud, a man from the people said: \"You have joined prayer with righteousness and zakah.\" When Abu Musa finished, he said: \"Which of you said such-and-such a word?\" but the people remained silent. He said: \"Which of you said such-and-such?\" but the people remained silent. He said: \"O Hittan, perhaps you said it.\" I said: \"I did not say it, and I feared that you would rebuke me for it.\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, explained our sunnah and taught us our prayer, and said: 'When you pray, straighten your rows and let one of you lead you. When he says the takbir, say the takbir. When he says \"not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray,\" say \"Amin,\" and Allah will answer you. When he says the takbir and bows, then bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is for that.' 'When he says \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise,\" and Allah will hear you, for Allah, blessed and exalted, said on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him.\" When he says the takbir and prostrates, then say the takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is for that.' 'When it is time for sitting, let the first words of one of you be: al-tahiyyat al-tayyibat al-salawat lillah, I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[3054,"\"And when the imam recites, then listen attentively.\""],[3055,"\"And when the imam recites, then listen attentively.\""],[3056,"I said to a companion of mine: \"Come, let us devote this day of ours to Allah.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard our words, so he ascended the pulpit and said: \"One of you says: 'Come, let us devote this day of ours to Allah.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept repeating it until I wished I had sunk into the earth."],[3057,"\"Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell will be constricted for him like this,\" and he counted ninety."],[3058,"\"Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell will be constricted for him,\" and he counted ninety."],[3059,"\"Allah, mighty and majestic, does not love the men who taste frequently and divorce, nor the women who taste frequently and get divorced.\""],[3060,"'Imran al-Qattan reported to us from Qatada, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3061,"\"Women are not to be divorced except on grounds of suspicion. Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not love the tasters and the tasteresses.\""],[3062,"\"Whoever loves the world harms the Hereafter, and whoever loves the Hereafter harms the world. So harm the perishable for the sake of the everlasting.\""],[3063,"\"Whoever is pleased by his good deed and distressed by his bad deed is a believer.\""],[3064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at the door of a house in which there was a group of Quraysh. He took hold of the doorposts, then said: \"Is there anyone in the house except a Qurayshi?\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, except for so-and-so, the son of our sister.\" He said: \"The son of a people's sister is one of them.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"This matter belongs to Quraysh as long as they show mercy when asked for mercy, judge justly when they judge, and divide equitably when they divide. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor supererogatory acts will be accepted from him.\""],[3065,"\"Part of exalting the majesty of Allah is honoring the elderly Muslim, and the bearer of the Qur'an who is neither excessive in it nor neglectful of it.\""],[3066,"\"By Him in whose hand is my soul, good and evil are two creations that will be set up for people on the Day of Resurrection. As for good, it brings its companions near. As for evil, it says to its companions: 'Away with you, away with you!'\""],[3067,"\"When two Muslims meet with their swords and one kills the other, both are in the Fire.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer; what about the one killed?\" He said: \"He was eager to kill his companion.\""],[3068,"\"When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will be presented three times. As for the first two presentations, there will be argument and excuses. As for the third, the records will fly to the right and to the left.\""],[3069,"Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of light on the Day of Resurrection."],[3070,"Whoever plays backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[3071,"Abu Musa ؓ addressed the people in Basra and said: \"O people, beware of this backgammon, that you play with it. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever plays with it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.'\""],[3072,"Malik reported to us, from Musa b. Maysara, from Sa'id b. Abi Hind, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet ﷺ , similarly."],[3073,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has made silk lawful for the females of my Ummah, and forbidden it for its males."],[3074,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the prayer of a man upon whose body there is any trace of khaluq (perfume containing saffron)."],[3075,"Abu Ja'far al-Razi reported to us, from al-Rabi' b. Anas, from his two grandfathers Zayd and Ziyad, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3076,"He entered upon Abu Musa while he was cupping at night, and said: 'Would that this were during the day.' He (Abu Musa) said: 'Do you order me to shed my blood while I am fasting?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.'"],[3077,"Yazid b. Zuray' reported to us, from Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Masruq b. Aws, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3078,"Isma'il b. Ibrahim reported to us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Masruq b. Aws, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ. This is how Yazid b. Zuray' narrated it from Sa'id from Ghalib from Masruq from Abu Musa. Shu'bah also narrated it from Ghalib from Masruq from Abu Musa, and Ibn 'Ulayyah concurred with them. Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi 'Arubah and added a man to the chain."],[3079,"For the fingers: ten, ten (camels as diyah)."],[3080,"\"Paradise lies under the shadows of the swords.\" A young man stood up to him and said: \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He broke the scabbard of his sword, then said to his companions: \"Peace be upon you,\" then entered, meaning into the fighting."],[3081,"\"Two gardens of gold, their vessels and all that is in them, and two gardens of silver, their vessels and all that is in them. And between the people and seeing their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, there is only the veil of pride upon His face in the Garden of Eden.\""],[3082,"\"The tent is a hollow pearl, its width is sixty miles. In every corner of it there are inhabitants who do not see the others, and the believer goes around among them.\""],[3083,"Abu 'Imran al-Jawni reported to us, from Abu Bakr b. Abi Musa, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3084,"\"This Ummah is an Ummah upon which mercy is shown. It has no punishment in the Hereafter; its punishment is in this world: killing and the like.\""],[3085,"I asked Abu Musa ؓ about the plague, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, and he said: It is a prick from your enemies among the jinn, and for you it is martyrdom."],[3086,"That when the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said: Forbid them from every intoxicant."],[3087,"If a rock were thrown into Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns."],[3088,"That a questioner came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the times of prayer, but the Prophet ﷺ did not reply anything. Then he ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan for the Fajr prayer when dawn broke, and he prayed. Then he ordered him, and he called the adhan for the Zuhr prayer when the sun declined, while a speaker said: It has not declined, but he knew better, and he prayed Zuhr. Then he ordered Bilal, and he stood and called the adhan for Asr when the shadow of everything became equal to it. He ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set or fell. Then he ordered Bilal, and he made the iqamah for Isha at the falling of the twilight. Then he ordered Bilal, and he made the iqamah for the Fajr prayer while the speaker said: The sun has risen, but he knew better ﷺ, and he prayed Fajr. Then he ordered Bilal, and he stood for the Zuhr prayer at the time of yesterday's Asr, and he prayed Asr while the speaker said: The sun has become red or has it not become red, but he knew better, and he prayed Maghrib before the twilight disappeared, and he prayed Isha until a third of the night. Then he said: Where is the questioner about the time of prayer? \"Between these two is a time.\""],[3089,"Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise."],[3090,"Abu Talib went out to Syria, and the Prophet ﷺ went with him among elders of Quraysh. When they overlooked the monk, they descended and left their baggage behind. The monk came out to them, whereas before that they would pass by him and he would not come out to them nor pay attention to any of them. He came and began to make his way through them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said: This is the master of the worlds, this is the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds, this is one whom God has sent as a mercy to the worlds. The elders of Quraysh said to him: What is your knowledge? He said: When you overlooked the mountain pass, there remained no tree or stone but it prostrated, and none prostrates except to a prophet. And I recognize him by the seal of prophethood below the cartilage of his shoulder, like an apple. Then he returned and prepared food for them. When he brought it to them, he said: Send for him, and he was tending the camels. He came, and a cloud was shading him. When he approached the people, he found that they had preceded him to the shade of the tree. When he sat down, the shade of the tree inclined over him. He said: Look, the shade of the tree has inclined over him. While he was standing over him, he was adjuring them not to take him to the Romans, for if the Romans saw him, they would recognize him by the description and kill him. He said: Then he turned, and behold, nine horsemen had come from the Romans. He met them and said: What has brought you? They said: We have come to this prophet who is to emerge in this month, and there remains no road but people have been sent to it, and indeed we have..."],[3091,"Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, reported to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id b. Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa."],[3092,"That two men brought a dispute before the Messenger of God ﷺ over an animal, neither of them having proof, so he divided it between them in halves."],[3093,"My community is a community shown mercy; it will have no punishment in the Hereafter. Its punishment is only in this world: earthquakes and killing.\""],[3094,"Upon every Muslim is charity. They said: And what about one who does not find (anything)? He said: \"He works with his hands and benefits himself.\" They said: And what about one who does not find? He said: \"He assists the distressed person in need, commands what is right, forbids what is wrong, and refrains from evil. That is charity.\""],[3095,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, every man will take the hand of a man from the people of polytheism, and it will be said: O Muslim, or O believer, this is your ransom from the Fire."],[3096,"We prayed the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then we said: If only we sat until we pray Isha with him. So we sat, and he came out to us and said: \"You are still here?\" We said: Yes, we prayed Maghrib, then we said: We will pray Isha with you. He said: \"You have done well,\" and he raised his head to the sky, and he often raised his head to the sky, and said: The stars are a trust for the inhabitants of the sky; when the stars go, the inhabitants of the sky will receive what they are promised. I am a trust for my Companions; when I go, my Companions will receive what they are promised. My Companions are a trust for my community; when my Companions go, my community will receive what they are promised."],[3097,"\"When I heard a hadith I would write it down. My father said to me: 'My son, what are you doing?' I said: 'I write down what I hear from you.' He said: 'Bring it to me.' I read it to him, and he said: 'Yes, this is how I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but I fear you may add or omit.'\""],[3098,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"A drink called bit' made from honey, and mizr made from barley.\" He said: \"Do they intoxicate?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Every intoxicant is haram.\""],[3099,"Isra'il reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3100,"\"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[3101,"'Abd al-Rahman reported to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not mention Abu Musa. Abu Bakr said: \"Bishr b. Mansur and Ja'far b. 'Awn traced it back.\""],[3102,"\"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[3103,"\"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[3104,"Shu'bah reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not say 'from Abu Musa.'"],[3105,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[3106,"Sharik reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3107,"Qays b. al-Rabi' reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3108,"Yunus b. Abi Ishaq reported to us, from his father, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet."],[3109,"Abd al-Hamid b. al-Hasan al-Hilali reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[3110,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[3111,"What is the matter with men who play with the limits of Allah? One of them says: I have divorced you, I have taken you back."],[3112,"The orphan girl is consulted concerning herself. If she remains silent, then she has given permission; but if she dislikes it, then there is no compulsion upon her and no validity over her."],[3113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen and said: Give glad tidings and do not drive people away; make things easy and do not make them difficult. Mu'adh said: You are sending us to a land of many beverages, so what should we drink? He said: Drink, but do not drink any intoxicant."],[3114,"I had a sharp tongue toward my family, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I fear that my tongue will cause me to enter the Fire. He said: Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? Indeed, I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times a day."],[3115,"No one's deeds will save him. It was said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy from Him."],[3116,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out a military expedition, he would say: Raid in the name of Allah, fight those who disbelieve in Allah, do not steal from the spoils, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child."],[3117,"Indeed, I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times a day."],[3118,"I have become heavy. When I bow, then bow; when I rise, then rise; when I prostrate, then prostrate. And let me not find anyone preceding me to bowing or to prostration."],[3119,"I was with Abu Musa ؓ when a daughter or a son of his sneezed and he said the response for the girl but did not say it for the boy. Their mother said: Why did you respond for her and not for her brother? He said: She remembered Allah, so I remembered; and he forgot Allah, so I forgot. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever sneezes and praises Allah, then respond to him; and whoever does not praise Allah, then do not respond to him."],[3120,"Do not recite the Qur'an while you are in a state of major ritual impurity, nor while you are bowing, nor while you are prostrating, nor while you are squatting like a dog. Do not pray while you have your hair tied up, do not spread your forearms like a wild beast, do not wear qassi, do not wear gold rings, and do not wear your ring on these two fingers."],[3121,"Umar b. al-Khattab met Asma' bt. 'Umays and said: O Habashiyya, you all are a good people were it not that we preceded you in the hijrah; so we are more excellent than you. She said: By Allah, I will go in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and inform him of what you said, O Ibn al-Khattab. She went in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Rather, you have two hijrahs: your hijrah to the land of Abyssinia and your hijrah here."],[3122,"He used to wear wool and hold a goat."],[3123,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[3124,"Humayd b. Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa."],[3125,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with two men from the Ash'aris, one on my right and the other on my left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was using a siwak. Both of them asked for a position of authority. He said: O Abu Musa, or O 'Abd Allah b. Qays, we do not appoint to our work anyone who desires it. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in their hearts, and I did not realize that they were seeking the position. It is as if I can see his siwak under his lip. He said: Go, you, O Abu Musa, or O 'Abd Allah b. Qays. He sent him to Yemen. Then he sent Mu'adh b. Jabal. When he arrived, he placed a cushion for him and said: Alight. There was a man with him bound. He said: What is this? He said: This man was a Jew, then he accepted Islam, then he reverted to his religion, the evil religion, and became a Jew again. He said: I will not alight until he is killed. He ordered it and he was killed. Then they discussed night prayer. Mu'adh said: As for me, I pray and I sleep, and I hope for in my sleep what I hope for in my standing."],[3126,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen."],[3127,"He asked permission to enter upon 'Umar three times, but permission was not granted to him, and he was busy. When he finished, he said: Did I not hear 'Abd Allah b. Qays, or the voice of 'Abd Allah b. Qays? Give him permission. It was said: He has gone back. He said: Call him. He came and said: We were commanded to do that. He said to us: Bring me proof of that. He went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and he testified for him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Asking permission is three times."],[3128,"If you had seen us while we were with our Prophet ﷺ and rain fell on us, you would have thought—or you would have thought—that our smell was the smell of sheep."],[3129,"If you had seen us with our Prophet ﷺ and rain fell on us, you would have thought that our smell was the smell of sheep."],[3130,"When he feared a people, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from their evils, and I repel them by You in their throats."],[3131,"Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, informed us, from Hammam, from Matar, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Hammam, from Matar, from Qatadah except Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi."],[3132,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and sent Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen, and he said: Make things easy and do not make them difficult, and give good tidings and do not drive people away."],[3133,"Sa'd fell ill in Makkah, so the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him. He said to him: 'O Messenger of God, do you not dislike that a man should die in the land from which he emigrated?' He said: 'Indeed, but perhaps God, Blessed and Exalted, will raise you so that through you He will harm some people and benefit others.'"],[3134,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed whoever separates a parent from his child."],[3135,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ accompanied by two men from the Ash'aris, and they asked him for an appointment. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'We do not appoint to our work anyone who is eager for it or who seeks it.'"],[3136,"My father said to me: 'Do you not hear from me?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then bring it to me.' I said: 'I will write it down.' He said: 'Then bring it to me.' So I brought it to him and he erased it, then said: 'Memorize as we memorized from the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[3137,"Ziyad b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Khalid b. Salama, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, something similar, but he did not raise it to the Prophet."],[3138,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey; among us were those fasting and those not fasting. The fasting person did not criticize the one not fasting, nor did the one not fasting criticize the fasting person."],[3139,"The Jews used to sneeze in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ hoping that he would say, 'May God have mercy on you,' but he would say, 'May God guide you.'"],[3140,"I saw the Messenger of God praying on his mount, here and here and here—to his right, to his left, and in front of him."],[3141,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by, its people hurrying with it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Be moderate in your funeral processions.'"],[3142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer, then said: 'O people, God has commanded you to fear God and to speak a proper word.' Then the men made their way to the women, and he said: 'God commands me to order you women to fear God and to speak a proper word.'"],[3143,"When news of the Messenger of God ﷺ reached us, we set out to Abyssinia until our ship landed us near the Negus in Abyssinia. We met Ja'far b. Abi Talib while he was with the Negus. Ja'far said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent us here and ordered us to stay, so we stayed with him until we all returned together.'"],[3144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said: 'O Messenger of God, you send me to Yemen where there are drinks of bit' and mizr.' He said: 'I do not know what these names are, but I forbid you every intoxicant.'"],[3145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and Muʿādh b. Jabal to Yemen, and he said: \"Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give good tidings and do not repel; and do not disobey one another.\" Muʿādh said: \"We are coming to a land where drinks are abundant.\" He said: \"Drink, but do not drink any intoxicant.\""],[3146,"ʿĀṣim b. Kulayb reported to us, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and Muʿādh b. Jabal to Yemen, sending each of us to a separate district. He said: \"Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give good tidings and do not repel.\" Each of them went off to his assignment. Whenever one of them needed something from his companion, he would come to him, greet him, and renew his covenant with him. Muʿādh drew near to Abū Mūsā, riding his mule until he stopped at his place. There he found a man whose hands were bound to his neck. He said to Abū Mūsā: \"What is this?\" He replied: \"This is a man who apostatized from Islam, or disbelieved after his Islam.\" Muʿādh said: \"I will not dismount until he is killed.\" So the man was killed, then Muʿādh dismounted."],[3148,"ʿAbd al-Ḥakīm b. Manṣūr reported to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3149,"Whichever man has a slave girl, disciplines her well, teaches her, then frees her and marries her, he will have two rewards."],[3150,"Abū Bakr b. ʿAyyāsh reported to us, from Abū Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3151,"Whoever hears the call to prayer and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him. I think he said: \"except for an excuse.\""],[3152,"Whoever hears the call to prayer and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him."],[3153,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Makkah, and my two brothers were with me: Abū ʿĀmir b. Qays and Abū Burdah b. Qays, along with five men from the Ashʿarīs, until we reached Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"For the people there is one migration, but for you there are two.\""],[3154,"\"If you had seen me last night while I was listening to your recitation, you have indeed been given one of the flutes of the family of Dāwūd.\" He said: \"I said: Had I known that you were listening to my recitation, I would have beautified it for you beautifully.\""],[3155,"Two men from the Ashʿarīs came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and began to hint at wanting to be appointed to positions. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The most treacherous of you in my sight is the one who seeks it.\" So he did not appoint them to anything."],[3156,"Qays reported to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3157,"Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning land belonging to one of them in Hadramawt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the defendant: \"Will you swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god?\" The claimant said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but his oath; then he will take away my land.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If he swears falsely, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify him, and he will have a painful punishment.\" He (the narrator) said: The man refrained from it and returned it to him."],[3158,"\"Whatever sin Allah conceals for a servant in this world, He will not reproach him for it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked one day, and when questions were put to him repeatedly, he became angry. Then he said to the people: \"Ask me whatever you wish.\" A man stood up and said: \"Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Your father is Salim, the freed slave of Shaybah.\" Another man stood up and said: \"Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Your father is Hudhafah.\" When Umar saw the anger on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we repent to Allah. We are pleased with Allah as Lord and with you as Messenger.\" Then it was relieved from him."],[3160,"\"The greatest of people in reward for prayer is the one who is farthest from it in walking, and the one who waits for the prayer until he prays it with the imam in congregation has a greater reward than the one who prays it and then sleeps.\""],[3161,"A house in Madinah caught fire at night upon its inhabitants. When the Prophet ﷺ was told of their situation, he came to them and said: \"This fire is an enemy to you, so when you sleep, extinguish it.\" Or he said: \"This fire is your enemy, so when you sleep, extinguish it.\""],[3162,"\"You will come to the Cistern and you will be snatched away from me. I will say: 'O Lord, my companions, O Lord, my companions.' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you.' I will say: 'Away, away.'\""],[3163,"\"The example of the knowledge and guidance with which Allah sent me is like abundant rain that fell on the ground. Part of it was good soil that absorbed the water and brought forth herbage and abundant pasture. Part of it was hard ground that held the water, and Allah benefited people by it: they drank from it, let their animals graze, and irrigated. Another part of it was barren hollows that held no water and produced no pasture. That is the example of one who acquired understanding of the religion of Allah and was benefited by what Allah sent me with, so he learned and taught, and the example of one who did not raise his head to that and did not accept the guidance of Allah with which I was sent.\""],[3164,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Which Muslim is best?\" He said: \"One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""],[3165,"Burayd narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. This hadith is only known from the narration of Yahya b. Sa'id from Burayd, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Usamah from Buraydah except Ibrahim b. Sa'id."],[3166,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood up alarmed, fearing that the Hour had come, until he reached the mosque. He stood and prayed with the longest standing, bowing, and prostration. Then he said: \"These signs that Allah sends do not occur for the death or life of anyone, but Allah sends them to frighten His servants. So when you see anything of them, hasten to His remembrance, supplication, and seeking forgiveness.\""],[3167,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him.\""],[3168,"\"Whoever bears arms against us is not one of us.\""],[3169,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[3170,"Abu Usamah reported to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know this hadith to be reported from Abu Musa except through this route, and more than one has reported it from Abu Usamah, but the hadith is known through Abu Kurayb."],[3171,"When Allah wills mercy for a community, He takes its prophet before it and makes him a forerunner and a predecessor for it. When Allah wills the destruction of a community, He punishes it while its prophet is alive, and He destroys it while he looks on."],[3172,"I and my companions from the people of the ship wanted to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah, and they were camped at Baqi' Duhnan. We used to take turns attending the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the 'Isha' prayer every night. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions while he had some preoccupation with some of his affairs, until he delayed the prayer so much that the night became very dark. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and prayed with them. When he finished his prayer he said: 'Take your time. Rejoice, for among Allah's favors upon you is that no one among the people prays this prayer except you' - or he said: 'No one has prayed this prayer except you.' We returned as soon as we heard this from the Messenger of Allah."],[3173,"A time will surely come upon people when a man will go around with charity of gold and not find anyone to take it from him. A single man will be followed by - or will stand for - a hundred women or forty women, because of the scarcity of men and the abundance of women."],[3174,"Intercede and you will be rewarded, and Allah will decree through the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills or whatever He loves. The trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is commanded with a willing heart is one of the givers of charity."],[3175,"When a beggar came to him, he would say: Intercede and you will be rewarded, and Allah will decree through the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills."],[3176,"The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."],[3177,"Allah grants respite to the wrongdoer, but when He seizes him, He does not let him escape. Then he recited: 'Thus is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are doing wrong. Indeed, His seizure is painful and severe.'"],[3178,"Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari reported to us: Abu Usamah reported to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. Abu Bakr said: This hadith is known only through Abu Mu'awiyah from Burayd, and we did not know anyone who reported it other than Abu Mu'awiyah until Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari reported it to us from Abu Usamah. We have not seen it from anyone from Abu Usamah except from Ibrahim, and the hearing of Ibrahim b. Sa'id from Abu Usamah and the hearing of al-Mu'ayti were the same. I was told that he corroborated Ibrahim on this hadith."],[3179,"He has indeed been given from the melodious voices of the family of Dawud."],[3180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh b. Jabal and Abu Musa to Yemen, and he said: Give glad tidings and do not repel; make things easy and do not make them difficult."],[3181,"\"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the conquest of Khaybar, and he allotted shares to us, but he did not allot shares to anyone who had not witnessed it except us.\""],[3182,"\"Keep refreshing your knowledge of the Qur'an, for it slips away from men's chests more quickly than camels escape from their hobbles.\""],[3183,"\"The orphan girl is to be consulted about her own marriage; if she remains silent, she has given her permission, and if she dislikes it, there is no compulsion upon her.\""],[3184,"I heard Abu Musa al-Ash'ari ؓ on the pulpit saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of a good companion is that of a perfume seller: even if he does not give you some of his perfume, some of its fragrance will reach you. And the likeness of a bad companion is that of a blacksmith: if his sparks do not burn your clothes, you will still be affected by his smoke.\""],[3185,"Abu Musa came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[3186,"\"He brought the Prophet ﷺ a clay jar of nabidh that was bubbling, and he said: 'Strike it against this wall, for no one who believes in Allah and the Last Day drinks it.'\""],[3187,"My father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Awza'i, from Muhammad b. Abi Musa, from al-Qasim b. Mukhaymirah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Mu'adh, and we do not know that Qatadah narrated any musnad hadith from al-Awza'i except this hadith."],[3188,"Abu Musa fell ill until he lost consciousness, and his wife cried out over him. He said to her: 'Did you not know what I told you?' When he died, we said to her: 'What did he tell you?' She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who shaves (his head), tears (his clothes), or wails.\"'"],[3189,"\"He commanded fasting on 'Ashura', and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast it.'\""],[3190,"\"The pilgrim intercedes for four hundred members of his household—or he said: of his own household—and he emerges from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[3191,"\"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night besides the obligatory prayers, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[3192,"Harun Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, except Harun, and I do not know of anyone who agreed with Harun on this hadith, and I do not know of anyone who narrated from him except these two men."],[3193,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the Jews and the Christians will be brought, and it will be said: 'This is your ransom from the Fire, O Muslim.'"],[3194,"Isma'il b. Abi al-Wasim informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[3195,"He fainted, and his wife wept. When he regained consciousness, he said: 'Has not the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ reached you?' He said: 'So I asked her, and she said: \"He said: He is not of us who shaves [the head], rends [the garment], and wails.\"'"],[3196,"I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ seek revenge for himself for any injustice done to him at all."],[3197,"Whoever has committed an injustice against his brother, let him go to him and seek his pardon before [the Day when] it will be taken [from him], for there will be no dinar or dirham [to give]. If he has good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds; otherwise, sins will be taken from the [wronged] brother's sins and placed upon his sins."],[3198,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."],[3199,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ was wiping blood from his face and shaking it off like this, and saying: 'How can a people succeed who have wounded their Prophet and broken his tooth, while he is calling them to God?' Then God revealed: 'You have no part in the matter.'"],[3200,"I was certainly made to fear for the sake of God as no one else was made to fear, and I was certainly harmed for the sake of God as no one else was harmed, and there came upon me thirty nights when I and my family had no food that a living being could eat except something which Bilal hid under his armpit."],[3201,"Al-Hasan b. 'Amr, meaning al-Fuqaymi, informed us, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. Yazid, from his father, from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet."],[3202,"The believer is not one who slanders, curses, is obscene, or is vulgar."],[3203,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was with his companions, he said to them: 'Do you hear what I hear?' They said: 'We hear nothing.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The heaven creaked, and it is not to blame for creaking, for there is not a handspan in it except that an angel is prostrating or standing upon it.'"],[3204,"Usayd b. Hudayr had a beautiful voice in reciting the Qur'an, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'While I was reciting on the roof of my house, with the woman in the chamber and the horse tethered at the door of the chamber, something like a cloud covered me. I feared that the horse would bolt and the woman would be startled and fall, so I stopped.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Recite, O Usayd, for that was an angel listening to the Qur'an.'"],[3205,"Regarding the statement of Allah: “So that attentive ears may retain it” (Q 69:12), he said: “An ear that preserved it with understanding from Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[3206,"“To warn whoever is alive” (Q 36:70), he said: “Rationally capable.”"],[3207,"“Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, brings forth the clouds, then sends the wind, which gathers the clouds, so they flow with rain as a milch camel flows with milk.” And he recited: “Is it you who brought it down from the rain clouds, or are We the bringers down?” (Q 56:69)."],[3208,"“For their own souls they are preparing” (Q 30:44), he said: “In the grave.”"],[3209,"“I have warned you of the Fire, I have warned you of the Fire.”"],[3210,"The Prophet ﷺ used to straighten the row until he made it like an arrow or a spear. Then he saw a man standing away, so he said: “You will straighten your rows, or Allah will cause your faces to differ.”"],[3211,"Misʿar reported to us, from Simāk b. Ḥarb, from al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3212,"Zakariyyā b. Abī Zāʾidah reported to us, from Simāk, from al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. This wording is not known to be narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except through the narration of al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr from him."],[3213,"“The example of the believer is like the body: when one part of it aches, the rest of it responds with sleeplessness and fever.”"],[3214,"When we prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” none of us would bend his back until he saw the Prophet ﷺ had prostrated."],[3215,"“Allah is more pleased with the repentance of a servant than a man who has his riding camel with him in a desolate land, carrying his provisions and food. He came to the base of a tree and lay down with his forearm as a pillow, using the camel’s foreleg as support. Then he stood up and woke up, and his camel had gone. He went to a high place, climbed it, and did not see it. Then he went to another high place, until he did that several times. Then he said: ‘I will return to the place where I was until I die.’ So he returned, and behold, there was his camel, dragging its halter, with his provisions still on it. Allah is more intensely pleased with the repentance of a servant than that man with his camel.”"],[3216,"Sharīk reported to us, from Simāk, from al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3217,"\"The example of the one who fights in the cause of Allah is like the one who fasts and stands in prayer until he returns to his home.\""],[3218,"Simak reported to us from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, and he did not trace it back. We do not know of anyone who traced this hadith back from Simak, from al-Nu'man, from the Prophet ﷺ, except Husayn b. 'Ali, from Za'idah. Others narrated it as mawquf (stopped at a Companion)."],[3219,"\"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.\""],[3220,"\"Whoever grants a manihah (a she-camel or ewe given temporarily for its milk) or guides someone along a path, he has a charity.\""],[3221,"\"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[3222,"\"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, they protect their blood and their wealth from me, except for its right.\""],[3223,"'Abd al-Malik b. Husayn reported to us from Simak, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3224,"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik and Hilal b. Yahya reported it to us, saying: Abu 'Awanah reported to us from Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib b. Salim, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3225,"He used to recite in the Eid prayer: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' (Surat al-A'la) and 'Has there come to you the account of the Overwhelming?' (Surat al-Ghashiyah)."],[3226,"Abu 'Awanah reported to us from Abu Bishr, from Habib b. Salim, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith was also narrated by Shu'bah and others, who concurred with Abu 'Awanah and Ibn 'Uyaynah. We have limited ourselves to the hadith of Abu 'Awanah and Ibn 'Uyaynah."],[3227,"I am the most knowledgeable among you about the time of this prayer, meaning the 'Isha' prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it when the moon set on the third night."],[3228,"Shu'bah reported to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3229,"Shu'bah informed us, from Simak b. Harb, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3230,"\"The least punished of the people of Hell is a man with two sandals of fire on the soles of his feet, from which his brain boils.\""],[3231,"\"Indeed, what you mention of the majesty of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, of glorification (tasbih), magnification (takbir), and declaration of His oneness (tahlil), they circle around the Throne with a buzzing like the buzzing of bees, mentioning the one who said them. Would not one of you love that there should always be someone with Allah who mentions him by it?\""],[3232,"Al-Nu'man b. Bashir narrated to me."],[3233,"\"I was by the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a Friday, when a man said: 'I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except providing water for the pilgrims.' Another said: 'I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque.' Another said: 'Jihad in the path of Allah is better than what you have mentioned.' 'Umar rebuked them and said: 'Do not raise your voices by the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a Friday. But when I have prayed the Friday prayer, I will enter upon him and ask his ruling about what you have differed over.' So he entered upon him and asked him, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'Have you made the providing of water to pilgrims and the maintenance of the Sacred Mosque equal to one who believes in Allah and the Last Day and strives in the path of Allah? They are not equal before Allah, and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.'\""],[3234,"A man called 'Abd al-Rahman had intercourse with his wife's slave girl, and the case was brought to al-Nu'man b. Bashir. He said: 'I will judge you with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If she had made her lawful to you, I will flog you one hundred lashes; but if she had not made her lawful to you, I will stone you.' He said: She had made her lawful to him. So he was flogged one hundred lashes."],[3235,"What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite on Friday? He said: \"Surah al-Jumu'ah and 'Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?'\""],[3236,"Abdullah b. Idris informed us, from al-A'mash, from Dharr, from Yusay' al-Hadrami, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3237,"Supplication is worship. And your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell in humiliation.'"],[3238,"Retaliation is with the sword, and for every error there is compensation."],[3239,"Za'idah informed us, from 'Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3240,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[3241,"Shayban informed us, from 'Asim, from al-Sha'bi, and Khaythama, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know anyone who combined Khaythama and al-Sha'bi except Shayban. This hadith was narrated from 'Asim by a group, and all those who narrated it from 'Asim narrated it from Khaythama from al-Nu'man, except Shayban."],[3242,"\"Verily, the likeness of the one who turns a blind eye in matters of God is like a group of people who boarded a ship and cast lots for their places, and some got the lower part and some got the upper part. A man among those in the lower part wanted to make a hole in it, so some of those in the upper part said, 'What are you doing?' He said, 'I will make a hole in it and draw water from it, and that will be easier for me than going up to you.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If they leave him, he will drown and drown them, and if they stop him, he will be saved by God's permission and they will be saved.'\""],[3243,"Ajlah b. 'Abd Allah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet."],[3244,"My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salama b. Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Nu'aym b. Abi Hind from al-Sha'bi. We do not know that Nu'aym b. Abi Hind transmitted from al-Sha'bi from al-Nu'man, nor from anyone other than al-Nu'man, any hadith other than this one."],[3245,"The likeness of the one who acts in disobedience to God, and the one who turns a blind eye and persists in it, is like a people who cast lots on a ship, and one of them got its worst, roughest, and lowest part. He wanted to dig a hole in it. If they leave him, he will perish and they will perish, and if they take hold of his hands, they will be saved and he will be saved."],[3246,"Hammad b. Zayd informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except al-Nu'man b. Bashir."],[3247,"My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salama b. Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir al-Ansari, who raised the hadith to the Prophet."],[3248,"Al-Sari b. Isma'il informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet."],[3249,"'Amr b. Abi Qays informed us, from Ibrahim b. al-Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet."],[3250,"\"Wine is from five things,\" and Salama b. Kuhayl said in his hadith, \"Drinks are from five things: from wheat, barley, dates, raisins, and honey. Whatever you ferment is wine.\""],[3251,"Isra'il informed us, from Ibrahim b. al-Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3252,"Shu'ba informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet."],[3253,"Hammad b. Zayd reported to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3254,"Ja'far b. Ziyad al-Ahmar reported to us, from Bayan, Mujalid, and Abu Hayyan, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3255,"Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi reported to us, from Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3256,"Abu Bahr said: And Abu 'Awana reported to us, from al-Mughira, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3257,"'Ali ibn al-Mubarak reported to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3258,"Hammam reported to us, from Qatada, from 'Azra, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3259,"That his father Bashir gave him a gift, and his mother said: I will not be satisfied unless you have the Prophet ﷺ witness it. So he came to the Prophet to have him witness it, and he ﷺ said: \"Have you given every one of your children the like of this?\""],[3260,"That his father gave him a gift, and his mother 'Amra bt. Rawaha said: I will not be satisfied unless you have the Prophet ﷺ witness that. So he came to the Prophet, and he said: \"Have you given every one of your children the like of what you gave al-Nu'man?\" He said: No. He said: \"Then take it back.\""],[3261,"Ibn 'Awn reported to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir."],[3262,"\"Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between that are matters that are ambiguous. I will strike for you an example regarding that: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has protected a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is what He has forbidden. Indeed, whoever grazes around the sanctuary is on the verge of entering it, and whoever mingles with it is on the verge of daring to do so.\""],[3263,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between that are doubtful matters. So whoever leaves them is more likely to leave what has become clear to him."],[3264,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and matters that are ambiguous. So whoever leaves the doubtful matters safeguards his religion and is worthy of not falling into doubt, and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is on the verge of entering it. Indeed, Allah's sanctuary is His prohibitions."],[3265,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there are matters that are ambiguous that many people do not know. Whoever avoids the ambiguous matters safeguards his religion; he is worthy not to fall into ambiguity. Whoever grazes around a sanctuary will soon transgress into it. Surely, the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions."],[3266,"The example of the believer and death is like a man who has three friends. One of them is his wealth: he says, 'Take what you wish and leave what you wish.' The second says, 'I am with you; I will carry you, and when you die I will leave you.' The third says, 'I am with you; I will enter with you and exit with you.' One of them is his wealth, the second is his family and children, and the third is his deeds."],[3267,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and there are matters that are ambiguous. Whoever avoids the ambiguous matters, he is more likely to avoid what is clear to him."],[3268,"Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath reported to us: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[3269,"Abu Bakr asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard the voice of Aisha saying: 'I have known that Ali is more beloved to you than my father, twice or thrice.' He said: Then Abu Bakr asked permission and entered, and he leaned toward her and said: 'O daughter of so-and-so, should I not hear you raising your voice over the Messenger of Allah?'"],[3270,"In the human being there is a lump of flesh; if it is sound, the rest of the body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the rest of the body is corrupt: it is the heart."],[3271,"Mujalid reported to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say—then he mentioned something similar."],[3272,"Al-Nu'man b. Bashir addressed us and said: O people, be merciful to one another, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with these two ears of mine say: The Muslims are like a single man; if one of his limbs complains, the rest of his body responds with sleeplessness and fever."],[3273,"Abu Yahya al-Taymi reported to us, from al-Hasan b. Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[3274,"Mujalid reported to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[3275,"Ishaq b. Yusuf al-Azraq reported to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[3276,"Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah, and whoever does not thank for little does not thank for much. Speaking about Allah's blessing is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude. Unity is a blessing, and division is a punishment."],[3277,"My mother asked my father to give me a gift, so he gave it to me. She said: I will not be satisfied until you have the Prophet ﷺ witness it. So my father took me by the hand while I was a boy and brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The mother of this boy, the daughter of Rawaha, asked me to give him a gift, and I have given it to him, so I call upon you to witness that. He ﷺ said: \"Do you have a son other than this one?\" He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: \"Have you given him the like of what you gave this one?\" He said: No. He ﷺ said: \"Then do not call me as a witness, for I do not bear witness to injustice.\""],[3278,"\"Deal justly among your children.\""],[3279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his face toward us and said: \"Straighten your rows\" three times. \"You will straighten your rows or Allah will certainly cause discord among your faces.\" I saw a man among us press his shoulder to his companion's shoulder, his knee to his knee, and his ankle to his ankle."],[3280,"\"The likeness of the believers is that of a single body: when one part of it aches, the whole body aches, and when one part complains, the whole body complains.\""],[3281,"\"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.\""],[3282,"Three men set out on a journey, and night overtook them and forced them into a cave. A rock fell and blocked the entrance of the cave. They said to one another: You are not on the road, and you have been afflicted with a great matter that can only be relieved by supplicating to the One who afflicted you with it—or words to that effect. Let each man among you recall the best deed he has done, mention it, and then supplicate to Allah. One of them said: O Allah, You know that I had a cousin, and there was no one on earth more beloved to me than her. I desired her for myself and offered her one hundred dinars. When I sat from her as a man sits from his wife, a trembling seized her, and she said: By Allah, I have never committed a sin, and nothing compelled me to this except dire need. So I got up and said: It is yours (the money). O Allah, if You know that I only left her seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your wrath, then remove this rock from us. The rock shifted until they saw the light. The second man said: O Allah, if You know that I had parents and sheep that I pastured nearby, and I stayed away and came to them one night after being delayed, I milked a vessel of milk and brought it to my parents, but found them asleep. I disliked waking them from their sleep, so the vessel remained in my hands until they awoke—whenever they awoke. O Allah, if You know that I only did that seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your wrath, then remove this rock from us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The rock cracked until they saw the light and had hope. The third man said: O Allah, if You know that I hired men for a known wage, and among them was a man who did the work of two men. When I gave them their wages, he said: Give me the wages of two men. I said: You are only entitled to the work of one man. He refused and left his wages with me and went away. I kept working with it on his behalf until sixty head gathered, including bulls, cows, and male and female slaves. He came after a time and said: O servant of Allah, is it not time for you to give me my wages? I said: Who are you? He said: I am the one who did the work of two men with you, and you only gave me the work of one man, so I left it. I said: These are sixty head, including bulls, cows, and male and female slaves. He said: You have withheld from me as long as you have, and now you mock me. I said: It is yours, take it. He took it. O Allah, if You know that I only did that seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your wrath, then remove this rock from us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The rock moved aside, and they departed walking."],[3283,"Except that the first man said: I had a cousin who was among the most beautiful of women, and she was the most beloved of people to me. I proposed to her father, but he refused to marry her to me. I left, and her father died, so I returned and she became needy. She sent to me complaining of need. I said: No, unless you give yourself to me. She did that several times, and her need became severe. She sent to me the third or fourth time, and she made me desire her, so I went to her. When I sat from her as a man sits from his wife, a trembling seized her, and she said: I adjure you by Allah not to break this seal unlawfully, for by Allah I have never done this act. So I got up from her and returned her to herself, and I gave her her dowry. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your wrath, then remove from us."],[3284,"Abu Sa'd reported to us, from Simak, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Sa'd except Abu Mas'ud, and he was trustworthy. We do not know that Abu Sa'd narrated anything from Simak except this hadith, and we only heard it from 'Ali b. Harb. Wahb b. Munabbih also narrated it from al-Nu'man b. Bashir."],[3285,"From 'Amr b. Shurahbil, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, and 'Amr b. Shurahbil is of Bajilah."],[3286,"\"When one of you intends to pray at night, let him take a handful of dust and place it beside him. When he wakes, let him throw it to his right and to his left.\""],[3287,"\"When the sun and the moon are eclipsed, pray the most recent prayer you have prayed.\""],[3288,"'Abd al-Wahhab reported to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Nu'man, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[3289,"Verily, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, wrote a Book two thousand years before He created the earth, and He revealed in it two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights but that a devil comes near it."],[3290,"Abu Raja' Muhammad b. Sayf informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. We do not know that Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani reported with a chain from al-Nu'man b. Bashir except this hadith, and we do not know that Abu Raja' reported with a chain from Abu Qilabah other than this hadith, and no one narrated it from him except Yusuf b. Khalid."],[3291,"The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah and the one who compromises them is like the example of a group of people who drew lots for places on a ship at sea. Some of them got the upper deck and some got the lower deck. Those in the lower deck had to go up to get water, and they disturbed those on the upper deck. Those on the upper deck said: 'We will not let you pass by us and annoy us.' Those in the lower deck said: 'If you prevent us, we will open a hole in the bottom of the ship.' If they restrain their hands and prevent them, they will all be saved. But if they leave them, they will all perish."],[3292,"Verily, the example of the believers is like a single body: when one part complains, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever."],[3293,"Shu'bah informed us, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3294,"Fasting three days of every month is equivalent to fasting the entire time and breaking the fast."],[3295,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do you love him?' He said: 'May Allah love you as I love him.' Then the Prophet ﷺ lost sight of him, so he asked about him, and they said: 'His son died.' So he went to him and said: 'Would it not please you that you will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you will find him there opening it for you?'"],[3296,"When the people of Syria perish, there is no good in you. And a group of people from my nation will continue to uphold the truth, victorious over people until the Day of Resurrection."],[3297,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ having already milked and tied the udder; he only meant that he came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was a young, active boy."],[3298,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud climbed a tree to pick a tooth-stick from it, and he placed his feet on it. The companions of the Prophet ﷺ laughed at the thinness of his legs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They are heavier on the Scale than Mount Uhud.'"],[3299,"Bistam b. Muslim informed us, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from his father."],[3300,"Our food during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was nothing but the two black things (dates and water)."],[3301,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his buttons unfastened."],[3302,"I would never see Mu'awiyah except with his buttons unfastened."],[3303,"Whoever eats from these two plants should not come near our mosque. If you must do so, then kill them by cooking."],[3304,"When he sat, his companions would sit around him in circles."],[3305,"We were forbidden from praying between the pillars, and we were sternly driven away from it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3306,"Harun Abu Muslim informed us, from Qatadah, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from his father, with something similar. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Harun, and we do not know that Qatadah narrated any other hadith with a chain from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah from his father besides this one."],[3307,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission, and he permitted me to see the seal. I put my hand into his collar and found on the cartilage of his shoulder something like a gland."],[3308,"The Prophet ﷺ sent for a man who had married his father's wife, and he ordered that his neck be struck."],[3309,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[3310,"The Prophet ﷺ said about al-Hasan and al-Husayn: 'I love them, so love them,' or he said: 'O Allah, I love them, so love them.'"],[3311,"I was with my father heading to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we were partway along the road, we passed by a settlement and spent the night there. The shepherd came running to the people of the settlement, saying: 'I will not shepherd for you any longer, for a wolf comes every night and takes a sheep from the flock, while the idol looks on without changing or objecting.' They said: 'Stay with us' – I think he said – 'until we go to it.' They went to it and spoke around it, and they said to the shepherd: 'Stay tonight.' My father said: 'I will stay tonight so we can see.' We spent the night, and at dawn prayer, the shepherd came running to the people of the village, saying: 'Good news! Do you not see that the wolf is tied in front of the idol without any rope?' They came and we came with them. He said: 'Yes, do like this.' Then we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my father told him the story. He said: 'Satan is toying with them.'"],[3312,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I feel compassion for it.' He said: 'And the sheep, if you show it mercy, may Allah show mercy to you.'"],[3313,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Mahdi and said: He will surely fill the earth with equity and justice, just as it was filled with oppression and injustice."],[3314,"“Eat the pre-dawn meal (sahur), for indeed in the sahur there is blessing.”"],[3315,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and then I feel pity for it. He said: And the sheep—if you show it mercy, Allah will show you mercy."],[3316,"“The earth will surely be filled with oppression and injustice. When it is filled with oppression and injustice, Allah will send a man from me whose name is my name, or whose name is my father’s name. He will fill it with justice and equity, just as it was filled with oppression and injustice. Then the sky will not withhold any of its rain, nor the earth any of its vegetation. He will remain among you for seven, or eight, or nine.”"],[3317,"He forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[3318,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was fasting on a journey. When the sun set, he said to a man: “Dismount and mix barley drink for us.” The man said: O Messenger of Allah, if you would wait until evening. He said: “Dismount and mix for us.” The man said: O Messenger of Allah, it is still daytime for you. He said: “Dismount and mix for us.” So he dismounted and mixed, and the Messenger of Allah drank. Then he said: “When you see the night advancing from here, the fasting person has broken his fast.”"],[3319,"He forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars. I said: Which jars? He said: I do not know."],[3320,"Hammad b. Mas‘ada reported to us, from al-Taymi, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned (as a legal punishment)."],[3322,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."],[3323,"We went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we ate locusts."],[3324,"We went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we ate locusts."],[3325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, with no noise therein and no toil."],[3326,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house made of hollow pearl."],[3327,"My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet."],[3328,"Imran reported to us, from Husayn b. Abdullah, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa."],[3329,"\"Indeed, God is with the judge as long as he does not deviate\" or he said: \"God's hand is with the judge as long as he does not deviate.\""],[3330,"Imran al-Qattan reported to us, from al-Husayn b. Abdullah, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. And this hadith we do not know anyone to have narrated from al-Shaybani except Imran, and Muhammad b. Bilal inserted Husayn b. Abdullah between Ammar and al-Shaybani, and we do not know who this Husayn b. Abdullah is?"],[3331,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate against the confederates, saying: \"O God, Revealer of the Book, Swift in reckoning, defeat the confederates and shake them.\""],[3332,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed Umrah and circumambulated the House, then went out to perform Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. We screened him so that no one from the people of Makkah could strike him, or any of them could throw something at him."],[3333,"No one who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah will ever enter the Fire."],[3334,"That the Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House and shaved his head during his Umrah."],[3335,"From Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, who said: I witnessed him, and he said the takbir over a funeral bier four times, then stood for a while, meaning supplicating, then said: \"Did you think that I would say the takbir five times?\" They said: No. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say the takbir four times.\""],[3336,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to all of his companions and said: \"I was shown tonight your dwellings in Paradise and the nearness of your dwellings. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to Abu Bakr and said: 'O Abu Bakr, I know a man whose name, his father's name, and his mother's name I know; he will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that it will be said to him: Welcome, welcome.' Salman said to him: 'This man's status is indeed exalted, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'He is Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah.' Then he turned to Umar and said: 'O Umar, I saw in Paradise a palace of white pearl, its balconies of white pearl, built with rubies. I said: For whom is this? It was said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought it was for me, so I went to enter it, but it was said: O Muhammad, this is for Umar b. al-Khattab. Nothing prevented me from entering it except your jealousy, O Abu Hafs.' Umar wept and said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of God?' Then he turned to Uthman b. Affan and said: 'O Uthman, every Prophet has a companion in Paradise, and you are my companion in Paradise.' Then he took Ali by the hand and said: 'O Ali, would it not please you that your dwelling in Paradise is opposite my dwelling?' He said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Indeed, your dwelling in Paradise is opposite my dwelling.' Then he turned to Talhah and al-Zubayr and said: 'O Talhah and O Zubayr, every Prophet has disciples, and you two are my disciples.' Then he turned to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and said: 'You were delayed from me among my companions until I feared that you had perished and drowned in a severe drowning, so I said: What delayed you?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, because of the abundance of my wealth, I was kept standing for reckoning, being asked about my wealth: from where did I earn it? And on what did I spend it?' Abd al-Rahman wept and said: 'O Messenger of God, these are one hundred camels that came to me tonight from the merchants of Egypt; I call upon you to witness that they are for the people of Madinah and their children, so that perhaps God may lighten for me on that Day.'\""],[3337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Hajj and ‘Umrah only because he knew that he would not perform Hajj after that year of his."],[3338,"Mis‘ar reported to us, from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, from Ibn Abī Awfā."],[3339,"Al-Mas‘ūdī reported to us, from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, from Ibn Abī Awfā."],[3340,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about forgetting the Qur’an. He said: “Teach me something that will suffice me.” He said: “Say: Bismillāh, wal-ḥamdu lillāh, wa lā ilāha illā Allāh, wa Allāhu akbar, wa lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh.” He said: So he counted them on his hand, then closed five fingers and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is for my Lord, so what is for me?” He said: “Say: Allāhumma ighfir lī, wa-rḥamnī, wa-‘āfinī, wa-rzuqnī, wa-hdinī.” He said: So he counted them on his hand, five, and closed his other fingers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “As for this, he has filled his hands with good.”"],[3341,"A man displayed his merchandise after ‘Asr and swore by Allah falsely, saying he had been offered such-and-such a price for it. Then this verse was revealed: “Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price” (Qur’an 3:77)."],[3342,"The one who artificially inflates prices (al-nājish) is a consumer of usury."],[3343,"Sufyān b. ‘Uyaynah reported to us, from Mis‘ar, from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, from Ibn Abī Awfā."],[3344,"The most beloved of Allah’s servants to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are those who watch the sun and the moon."],[3345,"The one who serves water to the people is the last of them."],[3346,"When charity was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, he would say: “O Allah, bless the family of so-and-so.” My father brought him his charity, and he said: “O Allah, bless the family of Abū Awfā.”"],[3347,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does one plunder a plunder of high value—or he said: of high honor—while he is a believer."],[3348,"A daughter of his died, and he followed her on a mule, walking behind the funeral procession, while women were lamenting her. Ibn Abī Awfā said: “Do not lament, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade elegies. But let any of you shed tears as she wishes.” Then he prayed over her, saying four takbīrs. After the fourth he stood for the length between two takbīrs, seeking forgiveness for her and supplicating. He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do this.” He said: And the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: “Overturn the cooking pots,” so we overturned them."],[3349,"Shubah informed us, from Mijza'ah b. Zahir, from Ibn Abi Awfa."],[3350,"\"O Allah, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water; O Allah, purify me from sins and cleanse me from them as the white garment is cleansed from dirt.\""],[3351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of the days when he met [the enemy]. He stood among the people and delivered a sermon, saying: \"Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. But if you meet them, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shade of the swords.\" Then he supplicated, saying: \"O Allah, Sender down of the Book, Vanquisher of the confederates, defeat them and grant us victory over them.\""],[3352,"He used to supplicate with this supplication: \"O Allah, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.\""],[3353,"When his wife died, he began to say: \"Carry her and be eager to carry her, for she and her masters used to carry by night the stones of the mosque that was founded on piety, and we used to carry by day two stones at a time.\""],[3354,"Al-A'mash informed us, from Ubayd b. al-Hasan, from Ibn Abi Awfa."],[3355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and the earth and filling whatever You will after that.\""],[3356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"O Allah, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water; O Allah, cleanse me from sins and faults as the white garment is cleansed from dirt.\""],[3357,"I saw on the shin of Abdullah b. Abi Awfa a wound, and I said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I was struck with it alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn.\""],[3358,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf complained about Khalid b. al-Walid to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: \"Why do you harm a man from the companions of [Badr]? Even if you spent the like of Uhud in gold, you would not reach his deed.\" He said: \"They revile me, but I do not respond to them.\" He said: \"Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah that Allah has unleashed upon the disbelievers.\""],[3359,"The destructive things are three: a person's admiration of himself, obeyed miserliness, and followed desire."],[3360,"Ismail said: Muhammad b. Awn narrated to me, from Yahya b. Uqayl, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[3361,"I entered upon Ibn Abi Awfa and saw him pray the morning prayer as two rak'ahs. His wife said, 'You only prayed two rak'ahs.' He said, 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs when he was given glad tidings of the victory, and when he was given glad tidings of the head of Abu Jahl.'"],[3362,"Malik b. Mighwal informed us, from Talhah b. Musarrif, from Ibn Abi Awfa."],[3363,"I asked him, 'Did the Prophet ﷺ make a will?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'How is it that the will was prescribed upon the people and they were commanded to do it, yet he did not make a will?' He said, 'He bequeathed the Book of Allah.'"],[3364,"When Bilal said, 'The prayer has been established,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand up with the takbir."],[3365,"I prayed with him over a funeral, and he said the takbir over it four times, then he paused for a little while, until we thought he would say a fifth takbir. Then he said, 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.' Then he heard women wailing, so he said, 'We have been forbidden from lamentation,' and he said to his servant, 'Where am I?' He replied, 'In front of the funeral.' He said, 'Put me behind the funeral.'"],[3366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray witr with three rak'ahs. In them he would recite in the first: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'; in the second: 'Say, O disbelievers'; and in the third: 'Say, He is Allah, the One.' When he said the salam, he would say, 'Glory be to the King, the Holy,' and he would prolong his voice with it."],[3367,"Whoever has a need from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, or from any person, let him say: 'There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. I ask You for the means of Your mercy, the certainties of Your forgiveness, and the spoils of every righteousness, and safety from every sin and every offense. Do not leave for me any sin but that You forgive it, nor any worry but that You relieve it, nor any need that is pleasing to You but that You fulfill it, O Most Merciful of the merciful.'"],[3368,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a young boy came to him and said, 'May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. I am an orphan boy, and I have an orphan sister and a widowed mother. Feed us; may Allah give you from what He has until you are pleased.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'How well you have spoken, O boy. Go to our family and bring us whatever food you find with them.' Bilal brought twenty-one dates and placed them in the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his palms toward his mouth over the dates, and we thought he was supplicating for blessing upon the dates. Then he said, 'O boy, seven for you, seven for your mother, and seven for your sister. Dine with one date and lunch with another.' When the boy left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Mu'adh b. Jabal stood up to him, placed his hand on his head, and said, 'May Allah mend your orphanhood and make you a successor of your father.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You saw what I did with the boy, O Mu'adh.' He replied, 'O Messenger of Allah, mercy for the boy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, 'By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one among the Muslims takes charge of an orphan and treats him well, except that Allah grants him for every hair a degree, gives him for every hair a good deed, and expiates from him for every hair an evil deed.'"],[3369,"The Prophet ﷺ used to lead us in the noon prayer when the sun had passed its zenith, and if a seed were placed on the hot ground it would have been cooked. Then he would lengthen the first rak'ah, remaining standing and reciting until we heard the sound of the people's sandals [shifting]. Then he would bow, then stand for the second rak'ah, which was shorter than the first. Then he would make the third rak'ah shorter than the second, and the fourth shorter than the third. Then he would pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was still white and clear, enough time for a traveler to travel two or three farsakhs. He would lengthen the first rak'ah of the afternoon prayer and make the second shorter than the first. He would pray the sunset prayer when a person would say, 'Has the sun set or not?' He would lengthen the first rak'ah of the sunset prayer and make the second shorter than the first, and the third shorter than the second. And he would delay the last evening prayer a little."],[3370,"Yazid b. Mu'awiyah sent me to 'Abdullah b. Abi Awfa. I arrived with some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, 'What do you command the people to do?' He said, 'Abu al-Qasim ﷺ advised me that if I encounter any of this [civil strife], I should go to no one, break my sword, and sit in my house. If someone enters upon me in my house, he said, \"Sit in your private chamber. If someone enters upon you there, kneel on your knees.\" And he said, \"Bear your sin and my sin, and you will be among the companions of the Fire, and that is the recompense of the wrongdoers.\"' So I have broken my sword. If someone enters upon me in my house, I will enter my private chamber. If someone enters upon me in my private chamber, I will kneel on my knees and say what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to say."],[3371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command ablution for every prayer, but he left that and commanded them to use the tooth stick for every prayer."],[3372,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulating the House on his riding camel, touching the corner with his staff."],[3373,"We were in the residence of Qays b. Saʿd b. ʿUbādah, and with us were some people from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. We said to him, “Step forward,” but he said, “I would not do that.” Then ʿAbdullāh b. Ḥanẓalah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man is more entitled to the head of his bed, more entitled to the front of his mount, and more entitled to lead the prayer in his own house.” So he ordered a freed slave of his, and he stepped forward and prayed."],[3374,"A dirham of ribā that a man consumes while he knows is more severe than thirty-six acts of zinā."],[3375,"I said to him, “What do you think about ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar’s ablution for every prayer—from whom did he take it?” He said: Asmāʾ bt. Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to him from ʿAbdullāh b. Ḥanẓalah that he narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command ablution at every prayer. When that became difficult for them, he commanded the siwāk at every prayer."],[3376,"He used to command the zakāt al-fiṭr on the day of fiṭr, before praying the Eid prayer, and he would recite this verse: “He has certainly succeeded who purifies himself and remembers the name of his Lord and prays” [al-Aʿlā 87:14–15]."],[3377,"“Indeed I fear for my Ummah three things: the slip of a scholar, a followed whim, and a tyrannical judgment.”"],[3378,"“Whoever revives a Sunnah of mine that had died out after me will have the like of the reward of those who act upon it among the people, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever originates an innovation that Allah and His Messenger are not pleased with will bear the like of the burdens of those who act upon it among the people, without anything being reduced from their burdens.”"],[3379,"Abū Uways reported to us, from Kathīr b. ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAmr, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[3380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day urged people to give charity. ʿUlbah b. Zayd stood up and said, “I have nothing but my honor. I call upon you, O Messenger of Allah, to witness that I have given my honor as charity to anyone who has wronged me.” Then he sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—twice or three times—“Where is ʿUlbah b. Zayd?” ʿUlbah stood up, and he said, “You are the one who gave his honor as charity. Allah has accepted it from you.”"],[3381,"The hour in which hope is placed on Friday is from when the imam comes out until he finishes the sermon."],[3382,"The Prophet ﷺ said the takbīr in the two Eid prayers seven times in the first and five in the last."],[3383,"The world will not come to an end until there is a garrison of Muslims at a place called Būlān, fighting the Banū al-Aṣfar, striving in the path of Allah, not deterred by the blame of any blamer, until Allah grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome through glorification and magnification, and its fortress is demolished, and they divide the wealth by shields.” He said: “Then a crier will cry out, ‘O people of Islam, the Masīḥ al-Dajjāl has appeared in your lands and homes.’ They will say, ‘Who is this crier?’ but they will not know who he is. They will send a scouting party to see whether it is the Masīḥ. They will return to them and say, ‘We saw nothing and heard nothing.’ They will say, ‘By Allah, the crier cried out only from heaven or from the earth. Come, let us all go out. If the Masīḥ is there, we will fight him until Allah judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges. If it is something else, then it is your lands, your armies, and your clans to which you have returned.’”"],[3384,"Whoever raises a weapon against us is not one of us."],[3385,"Zakah is due upon the Muslims: one sa' of dates, or one sa' of raisins, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of aqit."],[3386,"Whoever revives dead land without any Muslim's right over it, it belongs to him, and an unjust root has no right, and the Muslims are bound by their conditions."],[3387,"Three things from the affairs of Jahiliyyah that people will not abandon, or people will not leave: slandering lineages, wailing, and saying, 'We have been given rain by such-and-such a star'."],[3388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and lowlands, and where cultivation is suitable from Quds."],[3389,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enjoin the use of ithmid at bedtime."],[3390,"Verily Islam began as something strange and will return as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."],[3391,"Do not go out to meet caravans, and a townsman must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin."],[3392,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came to Madinah, and he prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for seventeen months, then he turned towards the Ka'bah."],[3393,"We discussed ghusl from janabah in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'As for me, I pour three handfuls on my head.'"],[3394,"Shu'bah reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman b. Surad, from Jubayr b. Mut'im, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith has a sound chain, and similar wording has been narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through various routes. The highest narrator of this wording from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is Jubayr b. Mut'im, and we know of no chain for Jubayr b. Mut'im other than this one. A group narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, and we have limited ourselves to the hadith of al-Thawri and Shu'bah rather than others. Sulayman b. Surad was a Companion and narrated more than one hadith from the Prophet ﷺ, and we know of no Companion who narrated from Jubayr b. Mut'im except Sulayman b. Surad and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar."],[3395,"A Qurayshi man has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh. It was asked, 'What does he mean by that?' He said: 'In sound judgment.'"],[3396,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed the share of the near relatives between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I and 'Uthman b. 'Affan came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Hashim; we do not deny their virtue because of the position in which Allah has placed you among them. But what about Banu al-Muttalib? You gave them and refused us, although we and they are in the same position in relation to you.' He said: 'They never separated from me in Jahiliyyah nor in Islam. Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one and the same thing.' And he interlaced his fingers."],[3397,"\"If Mut'im b. 'Adi were alive and interceded with me on behalf of these stinking people, I would grant his intercession for them.\""],[3398,"One who severs ties of kinship will not enter Paradise."],[3399,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah and Nasar b. 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr, from his father."],[3400,"Malik reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3401,"I heard Burd, meaning Ibn Sinan, narrating from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3402,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer, \"al-Tur.\""],[3403,"Sufyan, meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah, reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3404,"Ibrahim b. Sa'd reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3405,"Sufyan b. Husayn reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3406,"\"I have names: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-'Aqib, al-Mahi, and al-Hashir, the one after whom people will be gathered, and al-'Aqib, the last of the prophets.\""],[3407,"From 'Abd al-Salam, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet."],[3408,"Ya'qub b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd reported to us, from his father, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet."],[3409,"\"May Allah brighten [the face of] a person who hears my statement, memorizes it, and conveys it as he heard it; for perhaps the one who carries understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him, and perhaps the one who carries understanding is not himself a jurist.\""],[3410,"\"There are three things regarding which the heart of a believer does not act treacherously: sincerity of action for Allah, good counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community; for their supplication encompasses those behind them.\""],[3411,"Salamah b. Shabib and al-Husayn b. Mahdi informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Umar b. Muhammad b. Jubayr, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3412,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was distributing the spoils of Hunayn, when a samurah tree snatched his cloak. He said: 'O people, return my cloak to me! For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you had as many gold [pieces] as the leaves of that tree, I would distribute them among you, and you would not find me miserly or cowardly. It is only the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you.'\""],[3413,"\"nor a liar\"—meaning, \"you will not find me miserly, cowardly, or a liar.\""],[3414,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Juhfah when he said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and that the Qur'an came from Allah?\" We said: \"Indeed.\" He said: \"Then rejoice, for this Qur'an—one end is in Allah's hand and the other end is in your hands. Hold fast to it, for you will never be destroyed nor go astray after it, ever.\""],[3415,"\"We were around an idol of ours a month before the Prophet ﷺ was sent, and we had slaughtered a camel, when a crier cried out from inside it: 'Listen to the wonder! Polytheism and defilement have gone, and the shooting stars have been sent for a prophet in Makkah whose name is Ahmad, and whose migration is to Yathrib.'\""],[3416,"\"I lost a camel of mine and went searching for it at 'Arafah on the Day of 'Arafah, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: 'What is the matter with this one? He is indeed one of the Hums.'\""],[3417,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before revelation came to him, while I was standing on a camel of mine and he was standing on a camel of his at 'Arafat with people from his tribe, until he moved on with them.\""],[3418,"\"Come with us to Banu Waqif to visit al-Basir\"—a man who was blind."],[3419,"\"Come with us to Waqif.\""],[3420,"Husayn b. 'Ali informed us, from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Jabir. We have mentioned this hadith despite the differences in its chain and its instability, because we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through any connected route other than this; so we mentioned it and clarified the defect in it."],[3421,"Ibn Abi Dhi'b reported to us, from al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3422,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"The people of Yemen have come to you, as if they are pieces of cloud; they are the best of the people of the earth.\" A man from the Ansar said: \"Except us.\" He said: \"Except you\"—a light word."],[3423,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, which lands are most beloved to God, and which lands are most hateful to God?\" He said: \"I do not know until I ask Jibril ﷺ .\" So he came to him, and Jibril informed him that the most beloved places to God are the mosques, and the most hateful places to God are the markets."],[3424,"I heard Ya'qub b. 'Utbah and Jubayr b. Muhammad b. Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather—this is how Abu Musa, Bundar, and 'Abd al-A'la b. Hammad narrated it to us, and they were followed in that, for they all agreed upon this chain, because the copy of Wahb b. Jarir, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, belonged to 'Abd al-A'la b. Hammad, and it was thus in his book, and Abu Musa and Bundar copied from the book of 'Abd al-A'la, so it fell in their books thus."],[3425,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, souls are exhausted, families are lost, and wealth is destroyed. Ask God for rain for us, for we seek intercession through you with God, and we seek intercession through God with you.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Woe to you! Do you know what you are saying?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ then glorified God until that was evident in his face and the faces of his companions, and he said: \"Woe to you! God is not to be sought as an intercessor with anyone. God is greater than that.\""],[3426,"Husayn b. 'Abd al-Rahman reported to us, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet."],[3427,"\"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[3428,"\"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, one part over this mountain and one part over that mountain.\""],[3429,"\"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God.\""],[3430,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned something to him. He said to her: \"Return to me.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, what if I do not see you?\" He said: \"Go to Abu Bakr.\""],[3431,"\"When one of you prays facing a sutrah, let him draw near to it, so that Satan does not cut off his prayer.\""],[3432,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and says: 'Is there any asker, that I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness, that I may forgive him?'\""],[3433,"Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Nafi' b. Jubayr, from a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from Jubayr b. Mut'im except through this route, and we do not know anyone who named the man other than Hammad b. Salamah."],[3434,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ was on a military expedition, and they slept until the sun rose. So he ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer. Then he ordered them, and they prayed two rak'ahs. Then he led them in the morning prayer.\""],[3435,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah and Ahmad b. Aban informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Nafi' b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. We do not know any route for this hadith from Jubayr b. Mut'im except this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it and named [the man] after Nafi' b. Jubayr except Hammad b. Salamah."],[3436,"\"All the days of tashriq are days of slaughter.\""],[3437,"\"All of 'Arafat is a stopping place, and keep away from 'Uranah. All of Muzdalifah is a stopping place, and keep away from Muhassir. All the ravines of Mina are slaughtering places, and on all the days of tashriq, slaughtering is permitted.\""],[3438,"Shu'bah informed us, from 'Amr b. Murrah, from 'Asim al-'Anazi, from Ibn Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father."],[3439,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he entered the prayer. He said: \"Allah is the Greatest, greatly; praise be to Allah, abundantly; and glory be to Allah morning and evening. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan—from his madness, his blowing, and his puffing.\""],[3440,"He used to say in his bowing: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,\" three times, and in his prostration: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,\" three times."],[3441,"You blame me for [wearing] coarse wool? I have worn wool and taken hold of the goat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does that has freed himself from pride.\""],[3442,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shorten [his hair] at al-Marwah with a blade, then he said: \"The 'umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3443,"Isma'il b. Muslim informed us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Nafi' b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet."],[3444,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Abdullah b. Babah, from Jubayr b. Mut'im, from the Prophet."],[3445,"“O Banū ʿAbd Manāf, I will surely know what you have prevented.”"],[3446,"He forbade that the legal punishments be carried out in the mosques."],[3447,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn passing through the people asking about the camp of Khālid b. al-Walīd. A drunkard was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered those around him to strike him with whatever was in their hands, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw dust on him. Then later a drunkard was brought to Abū Bakr, and he sought to emulate their beating of him that day—or we sought to emulate it—and he struck forty lashes. Then ʿUmar struck forty.”"],[3448,"“A drinker was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that he be beaten, so they beat him with whatever was in their hands. In the time of Abū Bakr, a drinker was brought, and he asked about the beating for it. We sought to emulate the beating we had administered to the drinker in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we estimated it at forty, so he beat him forty. Then ʿUmar beat eighty.”"],[3449,"“The example of the believer when he is afflicted with fever or illness is like an iron that enters the fire, so its impurities depart and its purity remains.”"],[3450,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered that dust be thrown in their faces.”"],[3451,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had wiped his head and supplicated for him while he was young.” He said: “ʿAbdullāh b. Hishām used to sacrifice one animal on behalf of all his family.”"],[3452,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ while he was holding the hand of ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. ʿUmar said: “By Allah, you are dearer to me, O Messenger of Allah, than everything except myself.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until I am dearer to you than yourself.” ʿUmar said: “Now you are dearer to me than myself.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Now, O ʿUmar.”"],[3453,"“The world in comparison to the Hereafter is only like one of you dipping his finger into the sea, then raising it and seeing what comes out.”"],[3454,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: “The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners.”"],[3455,"“I was sent in the final breath of the Hour; I preceded it as this one preceded this one,” and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."],[3456,"“The Hour will arise while the Romans are the majority of people.”"],[3457,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ interlacing his toes with his little finger when he performed ablution."],[3458,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Basin, so al-Mustawrid said to him: Did you not hear him mention the vessels? He said: No. He said: But I heard him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—saying: Vessels will be seen in it more numerous than the stars of the sky."],[3459,"Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet."],[3460,"Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to me, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet."],[3461,"God, Blessed and Exalted, has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his sacrificial animal."],[3462,"Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad, from the Prophet."],[3463,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from someone who narrated to him from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet."],[3464,"Ma'mar narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad b. Aws from the Prophet."],[3465,"Abu Ghifar al-Muthanna b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma' al-Rahabi, from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet."],[3466,"Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Abu Asma', from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet."],[3467,"He passed by a man who was being cupped on the seventeenth of Ramadan, so he said: The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast."],[3468,"When the strap of one of your sandals breaks, let him say 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return,' for it is among the calamities."],[3469,"Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad b. Aws, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. The hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha' which was narrated by Kharijah is the hadith of Shaddad b. Aws. We do not know it being narrated from Shaddad except through this route, and none narrated it from Khalid except Kharijah. I did not hear anyone narrating it from Shababah except Isma'il b. Abi al-Harith, and he is a trustworthy and reliable man, and no one corroborated him in it. As for Kharijah b. Mus'ab, he is not a strong memorizer."],[3470,"Whoever recites a verse of poetry after the last 'Isha' prayer, his prayer for that night will not be accepted."],[3471,"When you attend your dying ones, close their eyes, for the sight follows the soul, and say good words, for the angels say \"Ameen\" to what the family of the deceased says."],[3472,"He is not a liar who reconciles between people and conveys good or says good."],[3473,"Differ from the Jews and pray in your sandals, for they do not pray in their sandals or their leather socks."],[3474,"We used to consider minor shirk during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be showing off."],[3475,"Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk, and whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk."],[3476,"We gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Among you there is a stranger\"—meaning one of the People of the Book—so we said: \"No, O Messenger of Allah.\" Then he ordered the door to be closed and said: \"Raise your hands and say: La ilaha illa Allah.\" So we raised our hands for a while. Then he said: \"O Allah, You sent me with this word, commanded me with it, and promised me Paradise for it, and You do not break Your promise.\" Then he said: \"Rejoice, for Allah has forgiven you.\""],[3477,"We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how were you taken on the night journey?\" He said: \"I prayed the 'Isha' prayer for my companions in Makkah after darkness had set in. Then Jibril came to me with a white animal, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule. He said: 'Mount.' It became difficult for me, so he turned it by its ear until it carried me. It set off flying with us, placing its hooves wherever its gaze reached. We reached a land with palm trees. He said: 'Dismount.' So I dismounted. Then he said: 'Pray.' So I prayed. Then we mounted, and he asked me: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'You prayed in Yathrib; you prayed in Taybah.' Then it set off flying, placing its hooves wherever its gaze reached, until we reached a white land. He said: 'Dismount.' So I dismounted. Then he said: 'Pray.' So I prayed. Then we mounted, and he asked: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'You prayed in Madyan; you prayed at the tree of Musa.' Then it set off, placing its hooves—or its hoof would fall—wherever its gaze reached. Then we ascended, and he said: 'Dismount.' So I dismounted. He said: 'Pray.' So I prayed. Then we mounted, and he asked: 'Do you know where you prayed?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He said: 'You prayed in Bayt Lahm, where the Messiah 'Isa b. Maryam was born.' Then he took me until we entered the city from its eighth gate. He came to the qiblah of the mosque and tied his mount. We entered the mosque through a gate where the sun and the moon incline. I prayed in the mosque as much as Allah willed.\" This is how Ibn Zabraq said it. \"Then two vessels were brought to me, one containing milk and the other honey; both were sent to me. I considered them both, then Allah guided me to it. I took the milk and drank until it touched my forehead. In front of me was an old man reclining. He said: 'Your companion has taken the fitrah,' or he said: 'with the fitrah.' Then he took me until we came to the valley which is in the city, and behold, Hell was uncovered, resembling a kind of carpet.\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how did you find it?\" He said: \"Like...\" and he mentioned something that slipped my mind. \"Then we passed by a caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such a place; they had lost a camel of theirs. I greeted them, and some of them said: 'This is the voice of Muhammad.' Then I came to my companions before dawn in Makkah. Abu Bakr came to me and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, where were you tonight? I looked for you in your place.' He said: 'I went to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a month's journey; describe it to me.' So it was opened for me as clearly as if I were looking at it. They did not ask me about anything except that I informed them about it. Abu Bakr said: 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.' The polytheists said: 'Look at the son of Abu Kabshah; he claims that he went to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight.' He said: 'Yes, and I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such a place; they had lost a camel of theirs at such-and-such a place. I am directing them for you; they will encamp at such-and-such, then they will come to you on such-and-such a day, led by a brown camel, with a black saddlecloth and two black sacks.' When that day came, the people went out to look, until close to midday, when the caravan approached, led by that camel exactly as the Messenger of Allah had described."],[3478,"Indeed, the best of your days is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he passed away, and on it the trumpet will be blown. So send abundant blessings upon me on that day, for your blessings are presented to me. It was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah, how are they presented to you when you have decayed?\"—they meant, \"when you have turned to dust.\" He said: \"Indeed, Allah has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.\""],[3479,"There will be rulers after me who kill the prayer by delaying it from its proper times. So pray the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer. When al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer from its times, I used to pray the prayer at its proper time and make my prayer with them a supererogatory prayer."],[3480,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gathered the earth for me until I saw its easts and its wests. The dominion of my nation will reach what was gathered for me of it. My Lord gave me the two treasures: the red and the white. I asked my Lord not to destroy them with a widespread drought, not to set an enemy over them to annihilate them all, not to divide them into sects, and not to make some of them taste the violence of others. He said: \"O Muhammad, when I decree a matter, it cannot be repelled. I have granted you for your nation that I will not destroy them with a widespread drought, nor set an enemy over them to annihilate them all, until some of them kill others and some of them take others captive.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I do not fear for my nation except the misleading rulers. When the sword is placed in my nation, it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3481,"The master of seeking forgiveness, when one of you finishes his prayer, is to say: O Allah, You created me and I am Your servant; I am upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge with You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You."],[3482,"The shrewd one is he who calls himself to account and acts for what comes after death; and the helpless one is he who lets his soul follow its desires and yet hopes in Allah."],[3483,"Four narrated to me from Mutarrif b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Shikhkhir, among them Yazid b. 'Abd Allah the brother of Mutarrif, and al-'Ala' b. Ziyad al-'Adawi, and two men whom Hammam forgot, from 'Iyad b. Himar."],[3484,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to teach you what you did not know of what He taught me this day. Indeed, every property I have bestowed upon My servants is lawful. And I created My servants all as hunafa' (upright monotheists), but the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion, and forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, looked upon the people of the earth and loathed them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except for remnants of the People of the Book. He said: O Muhammad, I have sent you only to test you and to test by you, and I have sent down upon you a Book that water cannot wash away, which you recite while asleep and awake. And my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to burn Quraysh, so I said: O Lord, then they would smash my head and leave it like a piece of bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, and spend and I shall spend on you, and send an army and I shall send five times its like, and fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you. And He said: The people of Paradise are three: a ruler who is just, truthful, and granted success; a man who is tender-hearted toward every Muslim; and a chaste man who gives charity. And He said: The people of the Fire are five: a man for whom no desire arises except that he betrays it; a man who does not reach evening or morning except that he is deceiving you about your family and your wealth; the weak one who has no restraint, those among you who are followers.\" A man said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, is he from the clients or from the Arabs? He said: \"He is the follower, who follows a man and gets from his service illicitly, not through marriage.\" And he mentioned miserliness and lying, or he said: lying and miserliness."],[3485,"'Awf narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from 'Iyad b. Himar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And Hakim al-Athram is a Basran, from whom 'Awf and Hammad b. Salama narrated, but there is something in his hadith because Hammad b. Salama narrated from him a rejected hadith, so for that reason we began with the hadith of Qatada before his, and were it not for that we would have mentioned al-Hasan from Mutarrif since he is more distinguished."],[3486,"The two who revile each other are two devils who hurl falsehoods at each other and lie to each other."],[3487,"He gave the Prophet ﷺ a milch-camel while he was a polytheist, but he returned it and said: We have been forbidden the gift of polytheists."],[3488,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to me that you should humble yourselves so that no one boasts over another."],[3489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by my father while he was on a white mule, so my father took hold of its bridle and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you stay with us? So he stayed with him ﷺ, and he brought him some hais (a dish of dates, butter, and dried curd), and he ate. Then he brought him some dates, and the Prophet ﷺ began eating and doing like this with the date stones, and he joined his two fingers together (meaning the index and middle fingers). Then he was brought a drink and he drank, then he handed it to the one on his right. Then he said: O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them, and have mercy on them."],[3490,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Yazid, from 'Abd Allah b. Busr, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and my mother threw down for him a velvet cloth, so he sat on it. She brought him some dates, and he began eating and doing like this with the date stones. And he described that he would take them out of his mouth onto the back of his two fingers, the middle and index, then flip the index over the middle and throw the stone from above it. Then he called for a drink, drank, and handed it to the one on his right. Then he said: O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them, and have mercy on them."],[3492,"Do not enter houses from their doors, but enter them from their sides, then greet, and if permission is given to you, enter, and otherwise return."],[3493,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen?\" He said: \"By the radiant marks from the traces of ablution.\""],[3494,"Al-Hasan b. Ayyub narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah b. Busr. Abu Bakr said: And I saw it in my book in another place."],[3495,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"You will certainly live to see a generation.\" He said: It reached us that he lived a hundred years."],[3496,"\"Did you see the Messenger of God as an old man?\" He said: He placed his hand on the hair beneath his lower lip and said: \"There were some white hairs here.\""],[3497,"I said to Abdullah b. Busr ؓ: \"Was the Prophet ﷺ an old man?\" He said: \"There were some white hairs at the front of his beard,\" and he pointed to the front of his beard."],[3498,"\"Between the great battle and the conquest of the city are six years, and the emergence of the Dajjal is in the seventh.\""],[3499,"He was delivering the Friday sermon when a man came, so he said to him: \"Sit down, for you have caused harm and come late.\""],[3500,"The Messenger of God ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about a matter he intended. They said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Call Mu'awiya for me.\" When he stood before him, he said: \"Make him witness your affairs, bring him to your affairs, for he is strong and trustworthy.\""],[3501,"Glad tidings to one who finds in his scroll abundant seeking of forgiveness."],[3502,"The standing of one of you in the row for an hour is better than the worship of one of them for sixty years."],[3503,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away while he disliked three tribes: Banu Umayya, Banu Hanifa, and Thaqif."],[3504,"There is no obedience in disobedience to God."],[3505,"He used to walk barefoot and with sandals, drink standing and sitting, turn to his right and left (after prayer), and fast and break his fast during travel."],[3506,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one lying down is half of the prayer of one sitting."],[3507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us against every hypocrite with a eloquent tongue."],[3508,"I had hemorrhoids, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Pray sitting; if you cannot, then on your side.'"],[3509,"He asked, 'Did you fast any of the middle of this month?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'When you break your fast of Ramadan, fast two days.'"],[3510,"He forbade cauterization, but we cauterized and we did not succeed nor prosper."],[3511,"Cursing a believer is like killing him."],[3512,"When a man says to his brother, 'O disbeliever,' it is like killing him."],[3513,"Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter."],[3514,"The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them. And Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or said, 'Then a people will arise who testify though they are not asked to testify, and obesity will spread among them.'"],[3515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and 'Umrah without being prohibited, and no scripture came prohibiting it. And he said: He (the angel) used to greet me until I cauterized; when I cauterized, the greeting ceased."],[3516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: If you have fasted any of the middle of this month, then (it is sufficient); otherwise, when the people break their fast, fast two days."],[3517,"A group from my Ummah will continue to be upon the truth, manifest, fighting those who oppose them."],[3518,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: O Allah, forgive me for what I have erred in, what I have concealed, what I have declared, what I have been ignorant of, and what I have done deliberately."],[3519,"The standing of a man in a row in the path of Allah is better than his worship in his house for sixty years."],[3520,"The example of my Ummah is like the rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[3521,"A man freed six of his slaves at the time of death, having no wealth other than them, so he freed them upon his death. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he divided them into three parts: he freed two and kept four as slaves."],[3522,"Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from 'Imran b. Husayn."],[3523,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Hasan, from 'Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And this hadith has been reported from 'Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ through several routes and from other than 'Imran b. Husayn, and its chain is hasan. In it there is the fiqh that it is not permissible for a man to bequeath more than one-third, and if he bequeaths more than one-third, it is rejected; because the Prophet ﷺ returned the whole to one-third. In it there is also that a sick man has no right to dispose of his wealth when his illness becomes severe and his life is feared except up to one-third, and if he gives out more than one-third, it is returned, even if it is not a bequest, for it is treated like a bequest."],[3524,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, and they halted for rest and slept, and did not wake until the sun had risen. When it rose high, he ordered them and they prayed."],[3525,"When 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ came to al-Basrah and led them in prayer, he used to say the takbir every time he raised and lowered himself. 'Imran said: This old man reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3526,"Al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-'Ala', from Mutarrif, from 'Imran b. Husayn ؓ , from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And we have mentioned this hadith from Yunus, even though it is not continuous, due to the prestige of Yunus; and because we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith from Yunus except al-Mu'tamir; so for that reason we mentioned it. As for the hadith of al-Jurayri, it is continuous, and Abu al-'Ala' is Yazid b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Shikhkhir, the brother of Mutarrif. This statement has been reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through other than one route, and 'Imran is the highest authority who reported that from a sound route."],[3527,"He forbade shighar (a type of marriage where a man gives his daughter or sister in marriage to another on condition that the other gives his daughter or sister in marriage to him, without any dowry)."],[3528,"There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam, and whoever plunders is not one of us."],[3529,"We performed tamattu' during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no prohibition concerning it was revealed to us, nor did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid it."],[3530,"Modesty is all good."],[3531,"Modesty is all good."],[3532,"He forbade plundering."],[3533,"He forbade cauterization."],[3534,"Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This hadith has been narrated from Imran through more than one route, and we do not know of it being narrated except from Imran b. Husayn, and its chain is good. Ali b. Asim said in it: from Yunus b. Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Imran."],[3535,"Whoever supports his brother while he is able to support him, Allah will support him in this world and the Hereafter."],[3536,"Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran b. Husayn, but he did not attribute it to the Prophet."],[3537,"Whoever supports his brother in his absence while he is able to support him, Allah will support him in this world and the Hereafter."],[3538,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with a ring of brass on his hand. He said: 'What is this?' He replied: 'It was prescribed for me for a pain in the shoulder.' He said: 'Throw it away from you. Would you like to be left to it?'"],[3539,"Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran b. Husayn."],[3540,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a ring of brass on my hand. He said: 'What are you doing with this on your hand?' I said: 'For a pain in the shoulder.' He said: 'Would you like to be left to it? Throw it away from you.'"],[3541,"A morning or an evening journey in the path of God is better than the world and what it contains."],[3542,"I do not ride on purple [saddles], nor wear qassi [garments], nor wear a shirt hemmed with silk. Indeed, the perfume of men is a scent without color, and the perfume of women is a color without scent."],[3543,"He recited: 'And you will see the people intoxicated, yet they are not intoxicated.'"],[3544,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'The son of my son has died, so what do I inherit from him?' He said: 'You have one-sixth.' When he turned away, he called him and said: 'You have one-sixth.' When he turned away again, he called him and said: 'The other sixth is a gift.'"],[3545,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned [an adulterer]."],[3546,"We were with him at al-Basrah and passed by a man reciting Surah Yusuf. He sat down and said to us: 'Listen to the Quran.' When the reciter finished his recitation, he asked [for something]. Imran said: 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return.' Then Imran said to us: 'Leave, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever among you recites the Quran, let him ask God by it, for there will come people after you who ask people by it.'"],[3547,"Al-Sakan b. Sa'id narrated to us from Qabisah, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3548,"Shall I tell you a hadith that I have not told anyone since I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ, fearing that people would rely upon it? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever knows that God is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, with certainty from his heart'—and he pointed with his hand to his skin—'God will forbid him from the Fire, or God will forbid his skin from the Fire.'"],[3549,"A she-camel belonging to the Prophet ﷺ went missing, and a woman vowed to slaughter it. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No one has a vow in disobedience,' or he forbade vows in disobedience."],[3550,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Will the people of Paradise be known from the people of the Fire?' He said: 'Yes.' They said: 'Then what is the point of action?' He said: 'Act,' or he said: 'Each person acts according to what he was created for.' Shu'bah said: 'For what he was created for, or for what he was facilitated.'"],[3551,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition and appointed Ali b. Abi Talib as its commander."],[3552,"There is no vow in disobedience."],[3553,"Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us, from Muhammad b. al-Zubayr, from al-Hasan, from 'Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[3554,"There is no vow in disobedience [to Allah], and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."],[3555,"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[3556,"I met 'Imran b. Husayn and Abu Hurayrah ؓ and asked them about the interpretation of this verse: \"and goodly dwellings in the Gardens of 'Adn\" (Qur'an 9:72). They said: You have asked one who knows. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said: \"A palace of pearl, in which there are seventy thousand mansions of green emerald; in each house there are seventy thousand couches; on each couch are seventy thousand mattresses of every color; on each mattress is a wife from the h?r al-??n; in each house there are seventy thousand tables, on each table seventy thousand kinds of food; in each house there are seventy thousand young male or female servants. He will be given such strength that he can visit all of it in a single morning.\""],[3557,"We traveled by night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during a military expedition. When it was near dawn, we halted to rest, and nothing woke us but the heat of the sun. A man began to wake startled and alarmed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Mount up.\" So he mounted and we mounted until the sun had risen high. Then he dismounted, ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer, and we prayed the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer. Then he gave the iqamah and led us in prayer. We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not make it up at its proper time tomorrow?\" He said: \"No. Allah forbids you from usury and accepts it from you.\""],[3558,"\"Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning: they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not believe in omens, and put their trust in their Lord.\""],[3559,"He forbade mutilation; and indeed, part of mutilation is for a man to perform Hajj walking or to shave his head."],[3560,"He forbade wailing (over the dead)."],[3561,"Modesty is entirely good."],[3562,"\"The begging of a rich person is a disgrace on his face, and the begging of a rich person is fire. If he gives a little, it is little; and if he gives much, it is much.\""],[3563,"\"Whoever is summoned to a judge among the judges of the Muslims and does not come to him is a wrongdoer,\" or he said: \"has no right.\""],[3564,"The Dajjal has indeed eaten food and walked in the marketplaces."],[3565,"Hammad narrated to us, from Ali, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet."],[3566,"That some people came to Imran b. Husayn and said: Do not narrate to us except what is in the Book of Allah. He became angry and said: Where do you find in the Book of Allah the five prayers, and that in every two hundred [dirhams] five dirhams [of zakah], and in every forty dinars one dinar, and in every twenty half a dinar—things like these which he enumerated—but take as we have taken."],[3567,"\"The supplication of a brother for his brother in his absence is not rejected.\""],[3568,"\"He is not from us who practices augury or has it done for him, or practices divination or has it done for him, or practices sorcery or has it done for him. And whoever ties a knot—or he said: whoever ties a knot—and whoever comes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[3569,"Shabib b. Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran b. Husayn."],[3570,"\"O Husayn, how many gods do you worship today?\" He said: Seven—six on earth and one in heaven. He said: \"Which of them do you count for your desire and fear?\" He said: The one in heaven. Then he said: \"O Husayn, if you embrace Islam, I will teach you two words that will benefit you.\" When Husayn embraced Islam, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me what you promised me. He said: \"Say: O Allah, inspire me with my right guidance and protect me from the evil of my soul.\""],[3571,"\"There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah.\""],[3572,"\"I looked into the Fire, and most of its inhabitants were women.\""],[3573,"\"Your brother the Najashi has died, so pray over him.\""],[3574,"You must use the earth, for it suffices you. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled, and the people complained to him of thirst, so he dismounted. Then he called a certain man—Abu Raja named him but Awf forgot it—and he called Ali and said: \"Go and seek water for us.\" He said: They set out and met a woman between two water-skins or two leather containers of water on a camel of hers. They said to her: \"When did you last see water?\" She said: \"I saw it yesterday at this time, and our men are away.\" They said to her: \"Come with us.\" She said: \"To where?\" They said: \"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said: \"To this one who is called the Sabian?\" They said: \"He is the one you mean, so come to him.\" Then they brought her to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the story. They made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and poured into it from the mouths of the two water-skins or containers, then he tied their mouths and loosened the spouts. It was announced among the people: \"Give water,\" and those who wished drank and gave water. The last of that was that he gave the person who had become junub a vessel of water and said: \"Go and pour it over yourself.\" She was standing watching what was done with her water. He said: \"By Allah, it was lifted from her when it was lifted, and it seemed to me that it was fuller than when he gave her water.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Gather for her.\" They gathered for her from among ajwah dates, fine flour, and roasted barley, and they gathered much food, placed it in a cloth, loaded it on her camel, and put the cloth before her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Do you know, by Allah, we did not diminish your water at all, but Allah gave us to drink.\" He said: She came to her people, having been delayed, and they said: \"What delayed you, O so-and-so?\" She said: \"Amazing! Two men met me and took me to this one who is called the Sabian, and he did such and such with my water. By Allah, he is the greatest sorcerer between this and this,\" indicating her middle and index fingers, raising them to the sky, meaning between heaven and earth, \"or he is truly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: The people used to raid and attack those around her but did not attack her. One day she said to her people: \"Do you not see that the people raid and attack those around you but do not attack you?\" So they came and entered Islam."],[3575,"\"People will come out of the Fire by the intercession of Muhammad ﷺ; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun (the ones from Hell).\""],[3576,"Al-Hasan b. Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3577,"We performed tamattu‘ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no scripture was revealed concerning us, nor did the Prophet ﷺ forbid it."],[3578,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Peace be upon you,” and the Prophet ﷺ responded, then said, “Ten good deeds.” Another came and said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” and he responded, then said, “Twenty good deeds.” Then another came and said, “Peace be upon you, the mercy of Allah, and His blessings,” and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Thirty good deeds.”"],[3579,"He forbade selling weapons during times of tribulation."],[3580,"Whoever of you hears about the Dajjal should keep away from him, for a man will come to him thinking he is a believer or a Muslim, and will follow him because of the specious things he sees with him."],[3581,"Modesty is all good. Bushayr b. Ka‘b said, “We find in some of the scriptures that part of it is weakness and part of it is dignity.” He replied, “I am reporting to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you are telling me about the scriptures?”"],[3582,"Modesty is all good."],[3583,"Ya‘qub b. ‘Abd Allah b. Nujayd b. ‘Imran b. Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from ‘Imran b. Husayn."],[3584,"A man from Hudhayl killed a man from Khuza‘ah during the Jahiliyyah, and the Hudhali went into hiding. When the day of the conquest came, the Hudhali emerged. A man from Khuza‘ah met him and slaughtered him as a sheep is slaughtered. He said, “Did he kill him before the call or after the call?” They said, “After the call.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If I were to kill a believer for a disbeliever, I would have killed him. So bring out his blood money.” We brought out his blood money, and it was the first blood money in Islam."],[3585,"Ziyad sent ‘Imran b. Husayn as a collector of zakah, and he returned without bringing anything. He said to him, “Where is the wealth?” He replied, “We took it as we used to take it in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we did as we used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[3586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to narrate to us about the Children of Israel for most of his night, not rising except for the greatest of prayers."],[3587,"There is no ruqyah except for a venomous sting."],[3588,"The Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “Rejoice, O Banu Tamim.” They said, “Since you have given us glad tidings, then give us something.” The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed. Then some people from Yemen came, and he said, “Accept the glad tidings, since Banu Tamim did not accept them.” They said, “We accept them, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[3589,"There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah."],[3590,"A boy belonging to poor people cut off the ear of a boy belonging to rich people, so his family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We are poor people,\" so he let him go."],[3591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Zuhr prayer, and in it he recited \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said, \"Which of you was contending with me in it?\" or \"Which of you was the reciter?\" Some of the people said, \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"I knew that some of you was contending with me in it.\""],[3592,"A man bit another, and he pulled away, and his front tooth was pulled out. That was referred to the Prophet ﷺ, and he declared it void, saying, \"Does one of you want to bite the flesh of his brother like a stallion bites?\""],[3593,"The best of people — or the best of this Ummah — is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will arise a people who testify though they are not asked to testify, who make vows but do not fulfill them, and among whom obesity spreads."],[3594,"He used to perform witr with \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,\" \"Say, O disbelievers,\" and \"Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[3595,"Imran had a slave who ran away, and he vowed to Allah that if he got hold of him, he would cut off his hand. He sent me to ask Samura, and I asked him, and he said, \"Our Prophet ﷺ used to urge us to give charity and forbid us from mutilation.\" Then I came to Imran and asked him, and he said, \"Our Prophet ﷺ used to urge us to give charity and forbid us from mutilation.\""],[3596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his family never had their fill of barley bread for lunch and dinner until he met his Lord."],[3597,"Whoever helps his brother in his absence when he is able to help him, Allah will help him in this world and the Hereafter."],[3598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years, praying two rak'ahs, and he said, \"We are travelers, so complete [the prayer].\""],[3599,"Is one of you not able to do every day the equivalent of Uhud?\" He said, \"And who is able to do that?\" He said, \"All of you are able to do it.\" They said, \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Subhan Allah al-'Azim (Glory be to Allah, the Almighty) is greater than Uhud, and La ilaha illa Allah (There is no god but Allah) is greater than Uhud, and Al-hamdu lillah (Praise be to Allah) is greater than Uhud.\""],[3600,"Amr b. Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Abi Ja'far, from Muhammad b. Juhada:"],[3601,"Whoever swears a false oath of patience (ṣabr), let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3602,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3603,"A servant continues to be in prayer as long as he waits for the prayer."],[3604,"There is no obedience in disobedience to God."],[3605,"Time has returned to its original state as it was on the day God created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months, of which four are sacred: three consecutive, Dhū al-Qaʿdah, Dhū al-Ḥijjah, and al-Muḥarram, and Rajab of Muḍar, which is between Jumādā and Shaʿbān."],[3606,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks. Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under God's protection; whoever betrays God's protection, God will cast him into the Fire on his face. Let those present convey to those absent, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed may be more mindful than the one who heard it.\""],[3607,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed the people at Minā and said: \"Do you know which day this is?\" They said: \"God and His Messenger know best,\" until we thought he would name it with some other name. He said: \"Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?\" We said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"And what land is this?\" We said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He then remained silent until we thought he would name it with some other name. He said: \"Is it not the Sacred City?\" We said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Have I conveyed?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"O God, bear witness.\" He said: \"Let those present among you convey to those absent, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed may be more mindful than the one who heard it. Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\" When the day came that Ibn al-Ḥaḍramī was burned, when Jāriyah b. Qudāmah burned him, they said: \"Look at Abū Bakrah\"—he was in a walled garden of his—and they said: \"This is Abū Bakrah.\" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: My mother narrated to me from Abū Bakrah that he said: \"If they had entered upon me, I would not have stirred against them even with a reed.\""],[3608,"A judge should not judge between two people while he is angry."],[3609,"Do you think that if Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, and Ghifār are better than Banū Tamīm, Banū Asad, Banū ʿAbd Allāh b. Ghaṭafān, and Banū ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah? A man said: \"They have failed and lost.\" He said: \"Indeed, they are better than Banū Tamīm, Banū Asad, Banū ʿAbd Allāh b. Ghaṭafān, and Banū ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah.\""],[3610,"He ﷺ granted a concession to the traveler for three days and their nights, and to the resident for one day and one night, if he purified himself and then put on his leather socks. Abū Bakrah, when he broke his ablution, would perform ablution and remove his leather socks."],[3611,"Gabriel ﷺ said: \"Recite the Qurʾān in one ḥarf.\" He asked for more, so he said: \"In two ḥarfs.\" He kept asking for more until he reached seven ḥarfs, each one sufficient and complete, like your saying 'come here' and 'approach.'"],[3612,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Which of people is best?\" He said: \"One whose life is long and whose deeds are good.\" It was said: \"Then which of people is worst?\" He said: \"One whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.\""],[3613,"Ishāq b. Suwayd narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakrah, from his father."],[3614,"“The two months of festival do not decrease: Ramaḍān and Dhū al-Ḥijjah.”"],[3615,"“Go forth as a scholar, or a learner, or a listener, or a lover, and do not be the fifth, lest you perish.”"],[3616,"A man praised another man in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “You have cut his back.”"],[3617,"“The parents of the Dajjāl will remain for thirty years without a child being born to them. Then a boy will be born to them, one-eyed, most harmful of things and least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ described his parents: “His father is a tall man, lean-fleshed, as if his nose were a beak, and his mother is broad-chested with long breasts.” Abū Bakrah said: We heard of a newborn among the Jews, so I and al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām went until we entered upon his parents, and they matched the Prophet’s ﷺ description. We said: “Do you have a child?” They said: “We remained thirty years without a child being born to us, then a boy was born to us, one-eyed, most harmful of things and least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep.” He said: We came out from them and there he was, sprawled in a patch of sunlight, murmuring. I uncovered his head. He said: “What did you say?” We said: “Did you hear what we said?” He said: “Yes, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.”"],[3618,"Al-Jurayrī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3619,"“O Messenger of God, what are the major sins?” He said: “Associating partners with God, disobedience to parents,” and he was reclining, so he sat up and said: “Indeed, and false speech.” In the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Wahhāb: “or false testimony”—Abū Masʿūd was unsure. He said: He kept repeating it until we said: “If only he would stop.”"],[3620,"He used to pray in his sandals."],[3621,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on one of his ʿumrahs and I went out with him. He did not stop the talbiyah until he touched the Stone."],[3622,"“Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, nor silver for silver except like for like, nor wheat for wheat, nor barley for barley, nor dates for dates except like for like.”"],[3623,"Yaḥyā b. Abī Kathīr narrated to us, from Yaḥyā b. Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report. This ḥadīth is known only through Yaḥyā b. Abī Isḥāq, and we know no other chain for Abū Bakrah besides this one we have mentioned."],[3624,"He saw people praying al-ḍuḥā and said: “This is a prayer that the Messenger of God ﷺ never prayed, nor did most of his companions.”"],[3625,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was walking, he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said, “These two graves are being punished.” He called for a palm branch and was brought one. He split it into two halves and placed one on this grave and one on that grave. Then he said, “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they remain moist.” Then he said, “Indeed, they are being punished for something not major: backbiting and urine.”"],[3626,"“When two Muslims meet with their swords and one kills the other, the killer and the killed are in the Fire.” They said, “O Messenger of God, this killer we know, but what about the killed?” He said, “He was intent on killing his companion.”"],[3627,"Suwayd b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. We do not know anyone who narrates this hadith with this wording except Abu Bakrah, and it has multiple chains from Abu Bakrah."],[3628,"The fragrance of Paradise is found from a distance of a hundred years’ journey, and no servant kills a protected person but God has forbidden him Paradise, lest he find its fragrance. Abu Bakrah said, “May God deafen my ears if I did not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say this.”"],[3629,"“When a Muslim raises a weapon against his brother, the angels of God continue to curse him until he puts it down.”"],[3630,"“When two Muslims meet with their swords, the killer and the killed are in the Fire.”"],[3631,"Let none of you say, “I fasted Ramadan and stood in prayer its entirety.” He (the narrator) said, “I do not know whether he disliked self-praise or said, ‘There may be drowsiness and sleep.’”"],[3632,"Sa‘id b. Abi ‘Arubah narrated to us, from a man, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. End of the thirtieth, and praise be to God abundantly."],[3633,"“Let none of you say, ‘I fasted all of Ramadan and stood in prayer all of it,’ for God knows best whether he disliked self-praise or there must be heedlessness or sleep.”"],[3634,"“Fast upon seeing it and break your fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured for you, complete the number.” He said, “And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘The month is like this, like this, like this.’”"],[3635,"A man from Persia came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “My Lord has killed your lord,” meaning Chosroes. He said, “And after that it was said to him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, that he had appointed his daughter as successor.” He said, “A people will not succeed who are ruled by a woman.”"],[3636,"Ja‘far b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir Abu Sahl, who is trustworthy and reliable, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu Bakr said, “This statement has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through more than one route, but we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Bakrah from this route.”"],[3637,"Allah protected me by something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A people who entrust their affairs to a woman will never succeed.\""],[3638,"Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[3639,"He bowed before the row, and when the Prophet ﷺ finished praying, he said: \"May Allah increase you in keenness, but do not do it again.\""],[3640,"Hammād narrated to us, from ʿAlī b. Zayd, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakrah, from his father."],[3641,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if a scale was lowered from the sky, and I was weighed against Abū Bakr; then Abū Bakr was weighed against ʿUmar, and Abū Bakr outweighed ʿUmar; then ʿUmar was weighed against ʿUthmān, and ʿUmar outweighed ʿUthmān; then the scale was raised.\" The Messenger of Allah became delighted at that, saying: \"Succession of prophethood, then Allah gives kingship to whom He wills.\""],[3642,"Hammād b. Zayd narrated to us, from ʿAlī b. Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abū Bakrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3643,"Isrāʾīl Abū Mūsā narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abū Bakrah."],[3644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan b. ʿAlī: \"This son of mine is a sayyid, and Allah will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.\" When the matter of Muʿāwiyah occurred, no blood was shed even in a cupping glass."],[3645,"The Prophet ﷺ was leading us in prayer, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī, who was young, would come and, whenever the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he would climb onto his neck and back. The Prophet would raise his head gently until he put him down. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you do something with this boy that we have not seen you do with anyone.\" He said: \"He is my fragrant basil in this world. This son of mine is a sayyid, and perhaps Allah will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.\""],[3646,"In the prayer of fear, he prayed with these two rakʿahs and with those two rakʿahs, so the Prophet had four and these had two rakʿahs each."],[3647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear with his companions. He arranged them in two rows, one row facing the enemy, and prayed with them two rakʿahs, then he said the salām. Then these went to the position of those, and those came, and the Messenger of Allah prayed with them two rakʿahs, then he said the salām. Thus the Messenger of Allah had four rakʿahs, and those had two rakʿahs each."],[3648,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs during the solar eclipse."],[3649,"He bowed before reaching the row, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"May God increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat [it].\""],[3650,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the sun eclipsed. He rose and went to the mosque, dragging his cloak in haste. The people stood up to join him, and he prayed two rak'ahs as you pray. When he sat, he addressed us, saying: \"The sun and the moon are two of God's signs with which He frightens His servants. They do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. When you see an eclipse of either of them, pray and supplicate until what afflicts you is removed.\""],[3651,"\"There is no retaliation except with the sword.\""],[3652,"Whoever takes out something beyond its limit and strikes a person with it is liable."],[3653,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing on his mule when a woman came to him and said: \"She has committed adultery, so stone her, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Veil yourself with God's concealment.\" Then she came to him another day while he was on his mule, and she said: \"O Messenger of God, stone her.\" He said: \"Veil yourself with God's concealment.\" Then she came the third day while he was on his mule, and she took hold of the bridle and said: \"O Messenger of God, I adjure you by God to stone her.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Go until you give birth.\" She gave birth to a boy and brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God said to her: \"Go and purify yourself from the blood.\" She went and came back and said: \"She has purified herself from the blood.\" He sent for some women and ordered them to examine her. Then he dug a pit for her. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took a pebble the size of a chickpea and threw it, and the people threw at her."],[3654,"Al-'Awwam b. Hawshab narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Jumhan, from Ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father. Abu Bakr said: \"I only said 'from Ibn Abi Bakrah' because Abu Kurayb said 'from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakrah,' and I do not know that Abu Bakrah had a son called 'Abd Allah, so I made it 'from Ibn Abi Bakrah.'\""],[3655,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned a land called al-Basrah, near which or beside which is a place called Dijlah. They will settle there and their numbers will increase. Then Banu Qantura' will come to them, and the people will split into three groups: a group that follows them, a group that turns their backs to them and perishes, and a third group that fights them and God grants victory to the remnant of them."],[3656,"While I was sitting with Abu Bakrah, a man came and greeted him. He said: \"Do you not recognize me?\" Abu Bakrah said to him: \"Who are you?\" He said: \"Do you know a man who came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him that he had seen the dam?\" Abu Bakrah said to him: \"So you are him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Sit and narrate to us.\" He said: \"I set out until I reached a land whose people had nothing but iron that they worked. I entered a house and lay down on my back, placing my feet on its wall. When it was near sunset, I heard a sound the like of which I had never heard, and I was terrified and sat up. The owner of the house said to me: 'Do not be alarmed, for this will not harm you. This is the sound of people returning at this hour from that dam.' He said: 'Would you like to see it?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So I went to it in the morning, and there were bricks of iron'—or he said: 'a brick of iron'—'each one like a boulder, and it was like a striped cloak, and its nails were like tree trunks. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: \"Describe it to me.\" I said: \"It is like a striped cloak.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at a man who has come to the dam, let him look at this one.\" Abu Bakrah said: \"He spoke truth.\""],[3657,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Abu Salamah while he was dying. When his gaze became fixed, the Messenger of God ﷺ stretched out his hand to him and closed his eyes. When he closed his eyes, the family cried out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ silenced them. Then he said: \"When the soul departs, the sight follows it, and the angels attend the deceased and say 'Amen' to what the family says.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"O God, raise the degree of Abu Salamah among the rightly guided, and be his successor among those who remain, and forgive us and him on the Day of Judgment.\""],[3658,"Ibn 'Amir came out on Friday and ascended the pulpit wearing thin clothes. Abu Bilal said: \"Look at your commander wearing the clothes of the sinful.\" Abu Bakrah, who was below the pulpit, said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever humiliates God's authority on earth, God will humiliate him.'\""],[3659,"People will be carried upon the bridge on the Day of Resurrection, and the two sides of the bridge will cause them to tumble like moths tumbling into the fire. Then God will save by His mercy whomever He wills. Then permission will be given to the angels, the prophets, and the martyrs to intercede, and they will intercede and bring out people, and they will intercede and bring out people, and they will intercede and bring out those who had in their hearts the weight of a speck of faith."],[3660,"He recited: 'But yes, My signs came to you and you denied them and were arrogant.'"],[3661,"He used to recite: \"Reclining on green cushions and fine carpets.\""],[3662,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father in Islam, knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."],[3663,"My father used to say after the prayer: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave.\" He said: I used to say them, so I said to my father: \"You say them.\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say them after every prayer.\""],[3664,"Indeed, there will emerge from my nation people young in age, reciting the Quran, but it will not pass beyond their collarbones. Indeed, when you meet them—meaning kill them. Then when you meet them, put them to rest."],[3665,"\"There will be trials, then there will be a trial in which the one walking is better than the one rushing to it, and the one standing is better than the one walking to it, and the one lying down is better than the one sitting in it. When it descends, whoever has sheep should join his sheep, whoever has land should join his land, and whoever has camels should join his camels.\" He said: A man from the people said: \"O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom—what do you think of one who has no sheep, land, or camels?\" He said: \"He takes his sword, then heads with it to a rock, then strikes its edge until it is blunted. O Allah, have I conveyed?\" He said it three times."],[3666,"There is no sin more deserving that Allah hastens punishment for its perpetrator in this world, along with what He stores for him in the Hereafter, than oppression and severing ties of kinship."],[3667,"\"Whoever kills a mu'āhad (one with a covenant) without just cause will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.\""],[3668,"We went out with him in the funeral procession of Abdul-Rahman b. Samurah, and Ziyad was walking in front of the bier. Some men from his freedmen and family began walking on their heels in front of the bier, saying: \"Slowly, slowly, may Allah bless you.\" Abu Bakrah said, while on his mule, striking them with a whip: \"Leave it alone, for by the One who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim, I saw us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ almost jogging with it.\""],[3669,"He said: I mentioned the Night of Decree to Abu Bakrah, and he said: \"As for me, I do not seek it except in the last ten, after a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Seek it when nine remain, or seven remain, or five remain, or three remain, or the last night.'\" He said: Abu Bakrah used to pray twenty [rak'ahs] during Ramadan, and did not pray [them] during the rest of the year, but when the last ten entered, he exerted himself."],[3670,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delighted by something he was given glad tidings of, and he fell down in prostration.\""],[3671,"He forbade money exchange two months before his death."],[3672,"On the day of Ta'if, I let myself down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a pulley, and he said: \"You are Abu Bakrah.\""],[3673,"When Kisra died, he said: 'Whom did they appoint after him?' He said: 'His daughter Buran.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A people who entrust their affairs to a woman will never succeed.'"],[3674,"He used to say in his bowing: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,' three times, and in his prostration: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,' three times."],[3675,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution: he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his forearms up to the elbows, wiped his head by moving his hands from the front to the back and from the back to the front, then washed his feet three times, and ran his fingers between his toes and through his beard."],[3676,"It was said to him: 'What prevents you from having fought on the Day of the Camel?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A people will emerge who are ruined and will not succeed; their leader is a woman, and their leader will be in Paradise.\" '"],[3677,"He used to have nabidh made for him in a green earthenware jar. Abu Barzah returned from an absence and came first to the house of Abu Bakrah, but did not find him at home. He stood by his wife and asked her about Abu Bakrah, and she informed him. Then he noticed the jar containing the nabidh and said: 'What is in this jar?' She replied: 'Nabidh for Abu Bakrah.' He said: 'I wish you had put it in a waterskin.' Then he left. So she ordered that nabidh to be put into a waterskin. Then Abu Bakrah came and she told him about Abu Barzah al-Aslami. He said: 'What is in this waterskin?' She said: 'Abu Barzah instructed us to put your nabidh in it.' He said: 'I will not drink from what is in it. If wine is put in a waterskin, would it become lawful for me? And if honey is put in a jar, would it become unlawful for me? We have already learned what we were prohibited from. We were prohibited from dubba', hantam, naqir, and muzaffat.'"],[3678,"Abu Bakrah entered upon us and a man stood up from his seat for him. Abu Bakrah said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A man should not make another rise from his seat and then sit in it, and should not wipe his hand with the garment of one he does not own.\" '"],[3679,"Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; and whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make his intentions heard."],[3680,"The Prophet ﷺ received news of a conquest, so he prostrated and began asking the messenger about them, while he had their news: 'Whom did they appoint as ruler? Or to whom did they entrust their affairs?' He said: 'A woman.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Men are ruined when women rule over them.'"],[3681,"Allah postpones whatever He wills of all sins except oppression and severing ties of kinship; He hastens their punishment for the perpetrator before death."],[3682,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it."],[3683,"I saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were almost walking briskly (ramal) during it."],[3684,"Whoever kills a person under covenant without right, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and that he should smell its fragrance."],[3685,"The people will be carried on the Day of Resurrection upon the Sirat, and the two sides of the Sirat will cast them down just as the moth falls into the fire. Then permission will be given to the angels, the prophets, the martyrs, and the righteous, and they will intercede and bring people out; and they will intercede and bring people out."],[3686,"I was shown the Night of Decree and then I was made to forget it; and I was shown the Messiah of Misguidance. I saw two men disputing, so I intervened between them, and then I was made to forget it. So seek it in the last ten nights on the odd nights. As for the Messiah of Misguidance, he is a man with a broad forehead, blind in the left eye, with a wide chest, as if he were 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qatan."],[3687,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When it descended upon him, he opened his eyes and focused his hearing and sight on what came to him from God. When he finished, he said to the scribe: 'Write: The inactive among the believers and those who strive in the cause of God with their wealth and lives are not equal. God has favored those who strive over those who remain inactive by a degree.' Then Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man, stood up and said: 'O Messenger of God, excuse us.' Then God sent down while he was standing, and the scribe said: 'Write: except for those who have a disability.'"],[3688,"The Prophet ﷺ was sitting in the gathering when his gaze fell upon a man in the mosque who was walking. He said: 'O Abu Fulan.' The man replied: 'At your service, O Messenger of God,' and he did not respond to any speech except by saying: 'O Messenger of God.' He said to him: 'Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you read the Torah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And the Gospel?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And the Quran?' He said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if we wished we could read it.' Then he adjured him: 'Do you find me in the Torah and the Gospel?' He said: 'We find one like you, with your appearance and your coming forth. We hoped that he would be among us, but when you came forth, we feared that you might be him, so we looked and found that you are not him.' He said: 'And why is that?' He said: 'With him will be seventy thousand of his nation for whom there will be no reckoning and no punishment, while with you there are only a few people.' He said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I am indeed he, and they are indeed my nation, and they are more than seventy thousand and seventy thousand.'"],[3689,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God ﷺ, were you brought food from heaven?' He said: 'Yes, I was brought a dish.' The man said: 'Was there any left over from it after you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then what was done with it?' He said: 'It was taken up.'"],[3690,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, horses have become cheap and weapons have been laid down, and they claim that there will be no fighting.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'They have lied. Now has come the time for fighting. There will not cease to be a group from my nation standing upon the truth, victorious.' And he said, while turning his back toward Yemen: 'I find the breath of the Most Merciful from here. It has been revealed to me that I will be taken in death and not left to linger, and that after me will follow scattered groups. And good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and their people will be aided through them.'"],[3691,"He prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him reciting in the dawn prayer: Qaf, and the tall palm trees with clustered fruit."],[3692,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ and heard him reciting Qaf, and I heard him reciting: 'And the tall palm trees with clustered fruit.' He said: 'Their tallness is their height.'"],[3693,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting in the dawn prayer: 'And the tall palm trees with clustered fruit.'"],[3694,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ seeking refuge from vain desires, evil deeds, and diseases."],[3695,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man from the Asad tribe, called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah, to collect the zakat. He came and said: 'This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit, praised and extolled God, then said: 'What is the matter with the agent whom we send to do our work, and he comes and says: This was given to me as a gift, and this is for you? Why did he not sit in the house of his father or the house of his mother and see whether a gift comes to him or not? By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, none of you will bring anything from it secretly except that he will come with it on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on his neck: if it is a camel, it will be bellowing; if a cow, it will be mooing; or if a sheep, it will be bleating.' Then he raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: 'O God, have I conveyed?' three times."],[3696,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed a man called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah to collect the zakat. When he came, he settled accounts with him, and the man said: 'This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit, praised and extolled God, then said: 'Now then, what is the matter with the agent whom we send...'"],[3697,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed dates from a Bedouin. The Bedouin came to demand repayment, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"We have nothing with which to repay you.\""],[3698,"Muhammad b. 'Amr b. 'Ata' narrated to me, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi."],[3699,"I know the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ best.\" They said: \"You were not the earliest of us in his company, nor the most frequent of us in following him.\" He said: \"Indeed I am.\" He said: \"Then present it.\" He said: \"When he ﷺ stood for prayer, he stood straight. Then he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he wanted to bow, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then said: 'Allahu akbar.' Then he raised [his head], then stood straight, neither lowering his head nor raising it, and placed his hands on his knees. Then he said: 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' and raised [his head] and stood straight until every bone returned to its place, upright. Then he went down in prostration to the ground and said: 'Allahu akbar.' Then he kept his upper arms away from his sides and spread the toes of his feet. Then he folded his left leg and sat on it, and stayed upright until every bone returned to its place, upright. Then he went down to the ground and said: 'Allahu akbar.' Then he got up. Then he did the same in the second rak'ah. When he rose from the two prostrations, he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, just as he had done when starting the prayer. Then he did likewise until, in the rak'ah in which the prayer would end, he moved his left leg back and sat on his side, mutawarrikan, then said the salam."],[3700,"Fulayh b. Sulayman narrated to us, from al-'Abbas b. Sahl, from Abu Humayd, among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. We do not know of this hadith being reported from Abu Humayd with a better chain than these two chains."],[3701,"There is no harm in a man looking at a woman if he wants to marry her, from where she is unaware."],[3702,"Whoever is named with my name should not use my kunya."],[3703,"Every prophet has a special group, and my special group is this clan of the Ansar. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. If the people were to take one valley and the Ansar another, I would take the path of the Ansar. The Ansar are the inner garment, and the people are the outer garment. Whoever is entrusted with any affair, let him be good to their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[3704,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to take his brother's staff except with his willing consent. And that is part of what the Prophet ﷺ emphasized: what Allah has forbidden of one Muslim's property upon another Muslim."],[3705,"When you hear a hadith that your hearts recognize, and your hair and skin soften to it, and you see that it is close to you, then I am most deserving of it. But when you hear a hadith that makes your skins shiver, and your hearts or hair change, and you see that it is far from you, then I am the furthest of you from it."],[3706,"Be moderate in seeking worldly things, for each is facilitated to what is decreed for him of it."],[3707,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy.' And when he leaves, let him say: 'O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty.'"],[3708,"Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, from 'Abd al-Malik b. Sa'id, from Abu Humayd and Abu Usayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[3709,"I took part in a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we were at a place that he named, which was the Battle of Tabuk, we came upon a garden belonging to a woman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Estimate its yield,' or 'You all estimate its yield.' So we estimated it—or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ estimated it—at ten awsuq. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, he asked the woman about the yield of her garden: 'How much did its fruit amount to?' She said: 'It reached ten awsuq; it did not increase or decrease.'"],[3710,"\"The gifts of governors are embezzlement.\""],[3711,"On the day of Uhud, when the polytheists withdrew, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Form ranks and stand firm so that I may praise my Lord.' So they formed ranks behind him. He said: 'O Allah, to You belongs all praise. There is none who can withhold what You extend, and none who can extend what You withhold. There is none who can guide whom You leave astray, and none who can lead astray whom You guide. There is none who can give what You withhold, and none who can withhold what You give. There is none who can bring near what You keep distant, and none who can keep distant what You bring near. O Allah, spread upon us from Your blessings, mercy, bounty, and provision. O Allah, I ask You for the enduring bliss on the Day of Resurrection. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and from the evil of what You have withheld from us. O Allah, endear faith to us and beautify it in our hearts, and make disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among the rightly guided. O Allah, cause us to die as Muslims and join us with the righteous, not disgraced or put to trial. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who reject Your messengers. O Allah, place upon them Your wrath and punishment. O Allah, fight the disbelievers among the People of the Book.'"],[3712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Umar: 'Gather your people for me.' So 'Umar gathered them at the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he entered upon him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I bring them in to you, or will you come out to them?' He said: 'Rather, I will go out to them.' So he came to them and said: 'Is there anyone among you who is not from you?' They said: 'Yes, among us are our allies, and among us are the sons of our sisters, and among us are our freed slaves.' He said: 'Our allies are from us, the sons of our sisters are from us, and our freed slaves are from us. Do you not hear that my close friends among you are the God-fearing? If you are those, then that is so; otherwise, beware lest people come with deeds on the Day of Resurrection while you come with burdens and He turns away from you.' Then he raised his hands and said: 'O people, Quraysh are the people of trust. Whoever seeks to harm them, may Allah cast him down on his nose.' He said this three times."],[3713,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque when a man entered."],[3714,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the mosque with people around him, a man came, faced the qiblah, and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Prophet ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' So he went back and prayed. Then he came, and we began to observe his prayer. When he completed his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' He repeated this two or three times. The man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what you criticize in my prayer, and I have not fallen short.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The prayer of any of you is not complete until he performs ablution thoroughly as Allah commanded him: he washes his hands and face, and his hands to the elbows, wipes his head and his feet to the ankles. Then he says \"Allahu akbar\" and praises Allah, and recites from the Quran what Allah has permitted him. Then he says \"Allahu akbar\" and bows, placing his palms on his knees until his joints are at ease and relaxed. Then he says: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" until his back is straight and he stands upright, with every bone in its place. Then he places his face—and I heard him say: \"his forehead\"—until his joints are at ease and relaxed. Then he says \"Allahu akbar\" and raises his head until he sits upright on his sitting place and straightens his back. Then he says \"Allahu akbar\" and prostrates until he places his face firmly and his joints are relaxed and at ease. Then he says \"Allahu akbar\" and raises. He described it in this way. If he does not do this, his prayer is not complete.'"],[3715,"I set out with my brother Khallad to Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a lean camel of ours. When we were at the post station behind al-Rawha', our camel knelt down. We said: 'O Allah, we make a vow to You that if You bring us to Madinah, we will surely slaughter it.' While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us and said: 'What is the matter with you two?' We told him that it had knelt down on us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted, performed ablution, and then spat into his ablution water. Then he ordered us to open the camel's mouth, and he poured some of his ablution water into the young camel's mouth, then onto its head, then onto its neck, then onto its withers, then onto its hump, then onto its hindquarters, then onto its tail. Then he said: 'O Allah, carry Rafi' and Khallad.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on, and we got up to load. We mounted and caught up with the Prophet ﷺ at the beginning of the midway point, while our young camel was at the front of the caravan. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw us, he laughed. We continued until we reached Badr. When we were near Badr, it knelt down on us, so we said: 'Praise be to Allah,' and we slaughtered it and gave its meat as charity."],[3716,"On the day of Badr, people gathered around Umayyah b. Khalaf. I approached him and noticed a piece of his armor that had broken off from under his armpit, so I thrust my sword at him. I was struck by an arrow on the day of Badr and my eye was put out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat and supplicated for me regarding it, and it never hurt me after that."],[3717,"We used to do it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; if we did not ejaculate, we would not perform ghusl."],[3718,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which earning is best?' He said: 'A man's work with his own hands, and every righteous sale.'"],[3719,"A man entered the mosque while we were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he raised his head from bowing, the man said: 'Our Lord, and to You belongs praise, abundant, good, blessed praise therein.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: 'Who was the one who spoke just now?' The man said: 'I was.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw thirty-some angels rushing to it, each trying to be the first to write it down.'"],[3720,"Ma'n narrated to us, from Malik, from Nu'aym b. 'Abd Allah, from 'Ali b. Yahya al-Zuraqi, from his father, from Rifa'ah b. Rafi' al-Zuraqi, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3721,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the descendants of the Ansar, and the descendants of their descendants, and their neighbors."],[3722,"O Sa'd, upon you is listening and obedience in your hardship and your ease, your willingness and your reluctance, and preference over you [i.e., when others are given preference over you], and that you do not dispute authority with its rightful people unless they call you to contravene what is in the Book of Allah. If they call you to contravene what is in the Book of Allah, then follow the Book of Allah."],[3723,"The Ansar are a touchstone; none loves them but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite."],[3724,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Undertake the collection of the zakat of Banu so-and-so, and beware lest you come on the Day of Resurrection with a young camel carrying it on your neck while it bellows.\" He (Sa'd) said: \"Accept my zakat from me,\" and he accepted it from him."],[3725,"The chief of days is Friday. In it there are five merits: in it Adam was created; in it he was sent down; in it Allah caused Adam to die; in it there is an hour in which no servant asks his Lord for anything therein except that He gives it to him, as long as he does not ask for sin or severing ties of kinship; and in it the Hour will be established. There is no angel brought near, nor sky, nor earth, nor mountain, nor wind, nor sea but that it is apprehensive of Friday, lest the Hour be established on it."],[3726,"There is no man who learns the Quran then forgets it except that he meets Allah on the Day of Resurrection as one with a severed limb, and there is no worker of ten [i.e., one who commits ten sins] except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, nothing will release him except his deeds."],[3727,"If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from among the sons of Persia would attain it.\" And perhaps he said: \"From Banu al-Hamra', from Banu al-Mawali."],[3728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me one day, after I had prayed the dawn prayer and lain down, and he nudged me with his foot and said: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" He said: \"La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no might nor power except with Allah).\""],[3729,"Indeed, the worst of usury is a man's encroachment upon the honor of his brother."],[3730,"The Messenger of Allah came to the house of Sa'd and gave the greeting of peace. Sa'd returned the greeting but kept it low. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, and Sa'd caught up with him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what prompted me to do that was that I wanted you to increase us in the abundance of the greeting.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned until he entered upon Sa'd. Sa'd brought him a vessel containing water and he performed a full ablution. Then he brought him a dyed sheet of wars (yellow dye) and he wrapped himself in it. Qays said: \"I saw the trace of the wars on his folds.\" Then he said: \"O Allah, bless the Ansar and the progeny of the Ansar, and the progeny of the progeny of the Ansar.\" Then Sa'd saddled a donkey of his, upon which was a velvet cloth, and said to his son: \"Go and return the donkey.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ride on the front of your donkey.\" Sa'd said: \"O Messenger of Allah, ride.\" He said: \"You are its master.\" Sa'd said: \"It is yours, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[3731,"We used to fast Ashura before the month of Ramadan was revealed. When it was revealed, we were neither commanded nor forbidden regarding it, and we still do it. And we were commanded to give the zakat al-fitr before the zakat (on wealth) was revealed. When the zakat was revealed, we were neither commanded nor forbidden regarding it, and we still do it."],[3732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us."],[3733,"\"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[3734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man supplicating in his prayer without praising Allah and without sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This one has been hasty.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said to him and to others: \"When any of you prays, let him begin with praising Allah and extolling Him, then let him supplicate for whatever he wishes.\""],[3735,"There are three about whom you should not ask: a man who separated from the community and disobeyed his leader and died disobedient; a female slave or a male slave who fled from his master and died; and a woman whose husband was absent while he had provided for her worldly needs, and she displayed her adornment after him. And three about whom you should not ask: a man who contended with Allah for His cloak, for His cloak is pride and His lower garment is might; a man who was in doubt about Allah's command; and the one who despairs of Allah's mercy."],[3736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed with the people, men would fall down from their standing in prayer because of the severe hunger that afflicted them, and they were the people of the Suffah, until the Bedouins would say: \"These are madmen.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, the Prophet ﷺ turned and said: \"If you knew what I know of what you have with Allah, you would love to increase in poverty and need.\" Fadalah said: \"And I was with the Messenger of Allah that day.\""],[3737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was"],[3738,"That he said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"This is a sacred day, and a sacred land, so your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like this day and this land until the day you meet Him, and even a push that a Muslim gives to a Muslim intending harm by it is sacred. I shall tell you who the Muslim is: the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is the one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives, and the emigrant is the one who abandons sins and transgressions, and the mujahid is the one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah.\""],[3739,"Every deceased person's deeds are sealed upon his death, except the one stationed in the way of Allah, for his deeds continue to grow for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is safeguarded from the trial of the grave."],[3740,"I am a guarantor, and the guarantor is the one who bears responsibility, for whoever believes in Me, submits, and emigrates, I guarantee a house in the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the highest part of Paradise. Whoever does that and leaves no avenue of good unfulfilled and no escape from evil, let him die wherever he wishes to die.\""],[3741,"Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.\" A man said to him at that point: \"But some men pluck out gray hairs.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever wishes, let him pluck out his light.\""],[3742,"We were with Fadalah b. Ubayd at sea, and a necklace containing unrefined gold and pearls, or gems, fell to me and my companions. They said: \"Buy it from us, and we will give you a good price.\" I said: \"Not until I ask Fadalah b. Ubayd.\" So I went to Fadalah and asked him. Fadalah said: \"I bought a necklace on the day of Khaybar containing unrefined gold and gems for seven or nine dinars, and I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. He said to me: 'Separate it: remove the gems, and buy the unrefined gold with unrefined gold, like for like.'\""],[3743,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, trading with the Jews, an ounce of gold for two or three dinars. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not sell gold except weight for weight.\""],[3744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk. He said: \"The mounts became extremely exhausted.\" He said: \"That was complained about to him.\" He said: \"And he saw them as men.\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked from the narrow pass where the people were crowded, and he stood there while the people were passing by.\" He said: \"Then he blew upon them, then said: 'O Allah, make them a means of carrying in Your path, for You carry upon the strong and the weak, and upon the moist and the dry, on land and sea.'\" He said: \"And they went on from their setting out.\" He said: \"We did not enter Madinah except while they were vying with us for their reins.\""],[3745,"He used to recite in the Friday prayer Sūrat al-Jumuʿah and the sūrah in which the hypocrites are mentioned."],[3746,"When the Prophet ﷺ walked, he walked as if he were pulling up rocks."],[3747,"Do not cause hardship for my ummah. O Allah, whoever causes hardship for my ummah, take retribution on him, or something to that effect."],[3748,"Whoever touches his private part should perform wuḍūʾ."],[3749,"Jibrīl descended to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Allah commands you to command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is among the rites of Hajj."],[3750,"A man died and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Khaybar, so they informed the Prophet ﷺ about him. He said: Pray over your companion, for he has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah, and his color changed because of that. They searched his belongings and found in them beads from the beads of the Jews worth less than two dirhams."],[3751,"Hammād narrated to us, from Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd, from Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Ḥabbān, from a man, from Zayd b. Khālid, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[3752,"Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Thawrī, from Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd, from Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā, from Abū ʿAmrah, from Zayd b. Khālid, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3753,"Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk at every prayer. Abū Salamah said: I saw Zayd b. Khālid with his siwāk at his ear, like the pen at the ear of a scribe."],[3754,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a slave woman who commits adultery before she is married. He said: If she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, sell her, even for a rope of hair."],[3755,"A rooster crowed one day while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a man cursed it. He said: Do not curse it."],[3756,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man stood up to him and said: I adjure you by Allah, will you not judge between us according to the Book of Allah? His opponent stood up, and he was more knowledgeable than him, and said: Yes, judge between us according to the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak. He said: Speak. He said: My son was a laborer for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son must be stoned, so I ransomed him with one hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked men of knowledge and they told me that my son must be given one hundred lashes and banished for a year, and that the wife of this man must be stoned. The Prophet ﷺ said: By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. The one hundred sheep and the servant are to be returned to you, and your son is to be given one hundred lashes and banished for a year. And you, O Unays, go to the wife of this man, and if she confesses, stone her. So he went to her, and she confessed, and he stoned her."],[3757,"People were rained upon one night during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When morning came, he said: \"Did you not hear what your Lord said tonight? He said: I have not bestowed any blessing upon My servants except that a group among them became disbelievers by it, saying: 'We were given rain by such-and-such a star.' As for the one who believes in Me and praises Me for My sending down of rain, that is the one who believes in Me and disbelieves in the star. And as for the one who says: 'We were given rain by such-and-such a star,' that is the one who disbelieves in Me and believes in the star.\""],[3758,"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out without perfume."],[3759,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found item. He said: \"Keep its strap and its tie, then announce it for a year, then if its owner comes, return it to him.\""],[3760,"And the Prophet ﷺ was asked about a stray camel. He said: \"What concern is it of yours? It has its own shoes and its own water-skin; it can come to water and eat trees.\" And he was asked about a stray sheep. He said: \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\""],[3761,"\"Whoever breaks the fast of a fasting person will have the like of his reward, without reducing anything from the reward of the fasting person. And whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or takes his place in his family will have the like of the reward of the warrior, without reducing anything from the reward of the warrior.\""],[3762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions. He said: He sent me a young goat, and I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a young goat. He said: \"Sacrifice it.\""],[3763,"Pray in your houses and do not make them graves."],[3764,"\"The best of witnesses is the one who gives his testimony before he is asked for it.\""],[3765,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or remain silent. Hospitality is for three days; whatever is beyond that is charity.\""],[3766,"\"Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog.\" He said: And I heard him say: \"Except a figure on a cloth.\""],[3767,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sleep one night, then he woke up startled and stood and prayed two short rak'ahs. Then he stood and prayed two long rak'ahs. Then he prayed two short rak'ahs, which were less than the two before them. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were less than the two before them. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were less than the two before them. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were less than the two before them. Then he prayed witr, so that was thirteen rak'ahs.\""],[3768,"Abu Juhaym sent me to Zayd b. Khalid to ask him about one who passes in front of a person praying. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"If the one who passes in front of a person praying knew what is upon him, it would be better for him to stand for forty autumns than to pass in front of him.\""],[3769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that anyone cleanse himself with bones, dung, or charcoal."],[3770,"People will come out of the East and prepare the way for the Mahdi's authority."],[3771,"He and a companion of his passed by some people, and young men of Quraysh had lowered their loincloths, so they were naked, striking each other with them. Al-Zubaydi said: When we passed by them, they said, 'These are such-and-such, so leave them alone.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them, and when they saw him, they rushed away, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned angry. I was behind the room and I heard him saying: 'Glory be to Allah! They were not ashamed before Allah, nor did they cover themselves from His Messenger.'"],[3772,"I would love that there be a barrier between me and the people of Najran because of how intensely they used to argue with him."],[3773,"We never heard a loud sound in Madinah except that we thought it was the Dajjal, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tell us about him and bring him near to us."],[3774,"The Jews brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had committed adultery while they were married, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to be stoned, and they were stoned. Abdullah b. al-Harith said: I was among those who stoned them."],[3775,"A man died among those who had come to the Prophet ﷺ and embraced Islam as a stranger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while he was at the grave: 'What is your name?' I said, 'Al-Asi (the disobedient).' He said to Ibn Umar: 'What is your name?' He replied, 'Al-Asi.' And he said to al-Asi: 'What is your name?' He said, 'Al-Asi.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You are the servants of Allah, descend.' He said: So we buried our companion, then we came out of the grave and our names had been changed."],[3776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, ascended the pulpit, and said: 'Amin, amin, amin.' When he finished, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do something you had not done before.' He said: 'Jibril appeared to me at the first step and said: \"O Muhammad, whoever reaches one of his parents in old age and they do not cause him to enter Paradise, may Allah distance him, then distance him.\" So I said, \"Amin.\" Then he said to me at the second step: \"Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him, then distance him.\" So I said, \"Amin.\" Then he appeared to me at the third step and said: \"Whoever hears you mentioned and does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him, then distance him.\" So I said, \"Amin.\"'"],[3777,"Some people brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a hut, so he sent Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman to judge between them, and he ruled it for the one whose rope was attached to it. When he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, he said: 'You have judged correctly and done well.'"],[3778,"A man struck another man with a sword on his forearm and cut it off, so he sought redress from the Prophet ﷺ, who ordered blood money for him. He said: 'I want retaliation.' He said: 'Take the blood money, may Allah bless it for you.' So he did not rule retaliation for him."],[3779,"Take fresh water for the head."],[3780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who had married his father's wife, and ordered me to strike his neck."],[3781,"I met my maternal uncle and with him was the banner. He said, “Where are you heading?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father’s wife, and he ordered me to strike his neck.” And he said: “Kill him.”"],[3782,"Do not strike more than ten lashes except in a hadd from the hadd punishments of Allah."],[3783,"Whoever cheats us is not one of us."],[3784,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which earning is purest?” He said, “A man’s work with his own hand, and every righteous sale.”"],[3785,"Whoever sends blessings upon me of his own accord, Allah will send ten blessings upon him for it, remove ten sins from him, and raise him ten degrees."],[3786,"When a servant dies while Allah knows evil from him, and the people speak good of him, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to His angels, “I have accepted the testimony of My servants concerning My servant and have forgiven him for what I know of him.”"],[3787,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the mosque, and his sandal strap broke. I took his sandal to repair it, but he took it from my hand and said, “That would be a form of self-preference, and I do not like self-preference.”"],[3788,"The Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj in ifrād."],[3789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not touch any of the corners except the Yamani and the Black."],[3790,"Narrated to us Yahya b. Sa'id, from 'Ubayd Allah, who said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from Amir b. Rabi'ah."],[3791,"Narrated to us Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Amir b. Rabi'ah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3792,"I am Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Nafi' and Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, from Amir b. Rabi'ah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3793,"Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Amir b. Rabi'ah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[3794,"When one of you sees a funeral procession, if he is not walking with it, he should stand for it until it passes him by or is put down."],[3795,"He used to pray voluntary prayers on his mount."],[3796,"Whoever sends one prayer upon me from his own accord, Allah will send ten prayers upon him for it."],[3797,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and the sky became cloudy and the direction of the qiblah became unclear to us. He said: So we prayed, and when the sun rose, behold, we had prayed facing other than the qiblah. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah revealed: 'So wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah.'\""],[3798,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ countless times using the toothstick while he was fasting."],[3799,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim b. 'Ubayd Allah, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Amir b. Rabi'ah, from his father."],[3800,"A woman from Banu Fazarah married for a pair of sandals as her dower. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Are you content?\" She said: Yes. So he approved that. Sharik said in his hadith: He said: Then it is your affair and his affair."],[3801,"A man took another man's sandal and frightened him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The frightening of a Muslim is great in the sight of Allah.\""],[3802,"Whoever dies while not under an oath of allegiance dies a death of Jahiliyyah. Whoever removes it after having pledged it will meet Allah with no argument for him. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. And he is further from the two of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deeds and grieved by his evil deeds is a believer."],[3803,"The womb is a branch of mercy. Whoever maintains it, Allah maintains him; and whoever severs it, Allah severs him."],[3804,"A man entered the mosque and said: 'Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, until our Lord is pleased, and beyond His pleasure.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said: 'Which of you said these words?' The man said: I did. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I saw twelve angels rushing to it, each wanting to be the one to write it down.'"],[3805,"He used to eat with three fingers and lick them when he finished."],[3806,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ kiss 'Uthman b. Maz'un after he had died."],[3807,"The Prophet ﷺ stood over the grave of 'Uthman b. Maz'un after he had buried him and ordered that water be sprinkled."],[3808,"Let those of you who possess wisdom and understanding be nearest to me, then those who come after them."],[3809,"On buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[3810,"The Prophet ﷺ used to send us out on military expeditions when we had no food except the old dates, and we would take handful after handful until we were down to one date at a time."],[3811,"'Ali once hosted some guests and prepared food for them. Fatimah said, 'Would that we invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he ate with us.' So they invited him and he came, but when he placed his hand on the two doorposts he saw a decorated curtain that had been hung on one side of the house, and he turned back. Fatimah said to 'Ali, 'Go and see what made him turn back.' He asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what made you turn back?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I have been forbidden to enter a decorated house.'"],[3812,"Sa'id b. Jumhan narrated to us, from Safinah."],[3813,"\"The caliphate after me will last thirty years.\" Then Safinah said to me, 'Count: two years for Abu Bakr, ten for 'Umar, twelve for 'Uthman, and six for 'Ali.'"],[3814,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream as if a scale was lowered from heaven and you were weighed against Abu Bakr, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then Abu Bakr was weighed against 'Umar, and Abu Bakr outweighed 'Umar. Then 'Umar was weighed against 'Uthman, and 'Umar outweighed 'Uthman. Then the scale was raised.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ considered this a caliphate of prophethood, then Allah gives sovereignty to whomever He wills."],[3815,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. Whenever some of the people became exhausted, they would throw their shields onto Safinah until he carried a great amount of baggage from that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You are Safinah (a ship).'"],[3816,"He scorched the blood of a slaughtered camel with a wooden block, then asked the Prophet ﷺ about that. He said, 'Did you make the blood flow?' He replied, 'Yes.' So he ordered him to eat it."],[3817,"He used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'."],[3818,"Isma'il b. 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Abu Rayhanah, from Safinah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3819,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping and said to me: 'Dispose of the blood.' So I went and drank it, then I came, and he said to me: 'What did you do?' I said: 'I disposed of it.' He said: 'Did you drink it?' I said: 'Yes.'"],[3820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade traveling with the Qur'an to enemy territory, fearing that the enemy might get hold of it."],[3821,"Burayh b. 'Umar b. Safinah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather."],[3822,"I ate with the Prophet ﷺ the meat of a bustard."],[3823,"I was at sea and our ship broke, and we did not know the way. Then I saw a lion that had appeared before us. My companions fell back, so I approached it and said: 'I am Safinah, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we have lost our way.' It walked before me until it brought us to the road, then it withdrew and pushed me as if showing me the way, then it began to make a humming sound, and I thought that it was bidding us farewell."],[3824,"He was sitting when a man passed on a camel, with a driver before him and another behind him. He said: 'May Allah curse the driver, the one behind, and the rider.'"],[3825,"The Prophet ﷺ devoted himself to worship before his death, and he kept away from women until he became like a worn-out waterskin."],[3826,"Some birds were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I prepared some of them for him. When morning came, I brought it to him, and he said: 'Where did you get this?' I said: 'From what was brought to you yesterday.' He said: 'Did I not tell you not to store up food for tomorrow? Each day has its provision.' Then he said: 'O Allah, bring to me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird.' Then 'Ali entered, and he said: 'O Allah, and to me.'"],[3827,"We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a slave girl of the Ansar was on a camel of hers. She looked behind her at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for the mountain had narrowed the way for them, and she said: 'Go on! Go on! May Allah's curse be upon you!' — meaning her camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who is the owner of this camel, or this mount? Let no camel that carries Allah's curse accompany us.'"],[3828,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will benefit me.' He said: 'Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims.'"],[3829,"Indeed, I only fear for you the desires of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misguiding temptations of whims."],[3830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to a clan of the Arab clans, and they beat him and reviled him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, so he said: “Had you gone to the people of Oman, they would not have beaten you nor reviled you.”"],[3831,"I had been wishing to meet a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to ask him about the Kharijites. I met Abu Barzah on the day of Eid among a group of his companions, and I said to him: “Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention anything about the Kharijites?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own ears and saw him with my own eyes. A property was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave to those on his right and those on his left, but did not give anything to those behind him. A man stood up from behind him and said: ‘O Muhammad, by Allah you have not been just in dividing today.’ He was a black man with shaved hair, wearing two white garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became extremely angry and said: ‘By Allah, you will not find after me a man more just to you than me.’ Then he said: ‘In the latter days a people will emerge, as if this man is one of them. They recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They pass through the religion just as an arrow passes through its target. Their sign is shaving. They will continue to emerge until the last of them emerges with the False Messiah. If you meet them, kill them, for they are the worst of creation and creatures.’”"],[3832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the enemy, and Allah granted him victory. He said: “Do you miss anyone from the second or third?” They said: “No.” He said: “But I miss Julaybib. Go and search for him among the slain.” So they searched and found him beside seven whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed and came and stood over him, and said: “This one is from me and I am from him. He killed seven, then they killed him. This one is from me and I am from him,” saying it twice. Then he carried him on his forearms, for he had no bier other than the forearms of the Prophet ﷺ, until a grave was dug for him and he was buried, and he did not mention any washing."],[3833,"When the Prophet ﷺ sat in a gathering and wanted to get up, he would say: “Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, you say words that you did not use to say before.” He said: “This is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering.”"],[3834,"Indeed, I will have a cistern between Aylah and Sana’a, its width equal to its length. Two spouts from Paradise pour into it, one of silver and the other of gold. It is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and cooler than snow. In it are vessels as numerous as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst until he enters Paradise.”"],[3835,"I said to Abu Barzah ؓ: “Whom did the Prophet ﷺ stone?” He said: “A man from among us called Ma’iz b. Malik.”"],[3836,"I saw Abu Barzah when Ibn Ziyad sent for him to ask him about the Cistern. He said: “And tell me who entered with him.” When Ibn Ziyad saw him, he said: “This Muhammadan of yours is indeed short.” When he heard it, he said: “I never thought I would live to be reproached for the companionship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” It was said to him: “You are not reproached for that.” And Ibn Ziyad asked him about the Cistern, so he said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘I will have a cistern.’ Whoever denies it, may Allah not bring him to it.”"],[3837,"He forbade sleeping before it and talking after it."],[3838,"Muhammad narrated to us, from Shu’bah, from Khalid al-Hadhdha’, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3839,"Aslam—may Allah grant it peace—and Ghifar—may Allah forgive it."],[3840,"He performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[3841,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[3842,"The rulers are from Quraysh. They have a right over you and you have a right over them as long as they do three things: when they are asked for mercy they show mercy, when they judge they are just, and when they make a covenant they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[3843,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[3844,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at two men on the day of Uhud reciting this poetry about Hamzah: 'I left a companion whose bones gleam, war kept him away from being buried.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, cast them down into trial with a mighty cast, and drive them to punishment with a forceful drive.'"],[3845,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and a girl from the Ansar was on a camel of hers. She looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ behind her while the mountain was narrowing upon them, so she said: 'Come on, come on, may the curse of Allah be upon you' – meaning her camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who is the owner of this camel or mount? Let no camel accompany us upon which there is a curse from Allah.'"],[3846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the enemy and Allah granted him victory. He said: 'Do you miss anyone?' They said: 'Yes, so-and-so and so-and-so.' Then he said: 'Do you miss anyone?' a second and third time. They said: 'No.' He said: 'But I miss Julaybib. Go and search for him among the slain.' They searched for him and found him beside seven whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed and came to him until he stood over him. He said: 'This one is from me and I am from him. He killed seven. This one is from me and I am from him' – saying it twice. Then he carried him on his forearms, for he had no bier other than the forearms of the Prophet ﷺ, until a grave was dug for him and he was buried, without mentioning any washing."],[3847,"I wished to meet a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to ask him about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah on a day of Eid among a group of his companions, and I said to him: 'Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Khawarij?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my ears and saw him with my eyes. Wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave to those on his right and those on his left, but he did not give anything to those behind him. A man from behind him stood up and said: \"O Muhammad, by Allah, you have not been just to me today.\" He was a black man with shaved hair, wearing two white garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became extremely angry and said: \"By Allah, you will not find after me a man more just to you than me.\" Then he said: \"In the end of time a people will emerge, and this man is one of them. They recite the Quran but it does not pass beyond their throats. They leave Islam as an arrow passes through its target. Their mark is shaving. They will continue to emerge until the last of them emerges with the false messiah, the Dajjal. When you meet them, kill them. They are the worst of creation and creatures.\""],[3848,"The buyer and seller have the option as long as they have not separated."],[3849,"Hisham b. Hassan narrated to us, from Jamil b. Murrah, from Abu al-Wadi, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3850,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me something from which I can benefit.' He said: 'Remove harm from the path of the Muslims.'"],[3851,"I have a cistern between Aylah and Sana'a, its width like its length. Into it pour two spouts from Paradise, one of silver and the other of gold. It is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and colder than snow. In it are vessels as many as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst until he enters Paradise."],[3852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to a tribe of the Arabs, and they insulted him and beat him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, so he said: 'If you had gone to the people of Oman, they would not have beaten you or insulted you.'"],[3853,"When the Prophet ﷺ sat down and wanted to get up, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you are saying words that you did not say before.' He said: 'This is an expiation for what occurs in a gathering.'"],[3854,"He forbade sleeping before it and talking after it."],[3855,"Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And the hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha' from al-Mughirah b. Abi Barzah from his father—I think Uthman b. Uthman erred in it. The correct version is Khalid al-Hadhdha' from Abu al-Minhal from Abu Barzah. Abu al-Minhal's name is Sayyar b. Salamah."],[3856,"The rulers are from Quraysh. I have a right over them and they have a right over you as long as they do three things: when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[3857,"Indeed, I fear for you the desires of misguidance in your bellies and private parts, and the misleading whims."],[3858,"Aslam—may Allah grant it peace—and Ghifar—may Allah forgive it."],[3859,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from al-Mughirah b. Abi Barzah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Barzah except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ali b. Zayd except Shu'bah."],[3860,"I saw Abu Barzah when Ibn Ziyad sent for him to ask about the Hawd. He said: Then someone who entered with him informed me. He said: When Ibn Ziyad saw him, he said: 'This Muhammadan of yours is short and stout.' Abu Barzah heard that and said: 'I did not think I would live to be reproached for the companionship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Someone said to him: 'You are not reproached for that.' Then Ibn Ziyad asked him about the Hawd, and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say—I think he said: \"I have a Hawd. Whoever denies it, may Allah not let him drink from it.\"'"],[3861,"I asked Abu Barzah ؓ: 'Whom did the Prophet ﷺ stone?' He said: 'A man from among us called Ma'iz b. Malik.'"],[3862,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[3863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at two men on the day of Uhud reciting this poetry about Hamzah: 'I left a disciple whose bones glisten; war turned him away from going mad and being buried.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, cast them down headlong, and drive them harshly to the punishment.'"],[3864,"He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[3865,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[3866,"I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in such-and-such a campaign and such-and-such a campaign until he counted eight campaigns, and we saw from him nothing but facilitation and lightening."],[3867,"A guest stayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent me to get food for him. I went to a Jewish man and said, 'Muhammad ﷺ says to you: A guest has stayed with us and we do not have some of what would suit him, so sell to me or lend to me until the new moon of Rajab.' The Jew said, 'No, by Allah, I will not lend to him nor sell to him except with a pledge.' I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said, 'By Allah, I am indeed trustworthy in the eyes of the people of heaven, trustworthy in the eyes of the people of earth. If he had lent to me or sold to me, I would have paid him. Go with my breastplate.' Then this verse was revealed to console him regarding the world: Do not extend your eyes toward what We have bestowed upon some pairs of them."],[3868,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once, once."],[3869,"The Prophet ﷺ bit from a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[3870,"I was in charge of al-Abbas's wealth. Islam had entered us, the people of the household, and I embraced Islam, al-Abbas embraced Islam, and Umm al-Fadl embraced Islam. Al-Abbas feared his people and disliked opposing them, and he concealed his Islam. He had abundant wealth dispersed among his people. Abu Lahab had stayed behind and sent in his place al-Asi b. Hashim b. al-Mughirah, and that is what they used to do: no man stayed behind except that he sent a man in his place. When news came of the defeat of Quraysh at Badr, we found within ourselves strength and honor. I was a weak man and I used to make wooden bowls, carving them in the chamber of Zamzam. By Allah, I was sitting there carving my bowls with Umm al-Fadl sitting beside me, and what had come to us had pleased us, when Abu Lahab came and sat at the rope of the chamber and leaned his back against my back. Then people said, 'Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib has arrived.' The people were standing around him, and he said, 'O son of my brother...'"],[3871,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered a sacrifice, he would buy two fat, horned, black-and-white rams. When he had prayed and delivered the sermon, one of them would be brought to him while he was at his prayer place, and he would slaughter it, then say: 'O Allah, this is on behalf of my entire Ummah, those who testify to Your Oneness and testify that I have conveyed the message.' Then the other would be brought and he would slaughter it and say: 'This is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' He would feed both of them to the poor and he and his family would eat from them. He said: We remained for years, and no man of Banu Hashim offered a sacrifice; Allah had spared them the expense and burden through the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[3872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say as the muezzin says, and when he reached 'Hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-falah' (Come to prayer, come to success), he would say: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[3873,"O Abu Rafi', kill every dog in Madinah. I found some women of the Ansar who had a dog. They said, 'O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has taken our men on a raid, and this dog protects us after Allah. By Allah, no one can approach us until one of our women stands up. Mention him to the Prophet ﷺ .' He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ , and he said: 'Kill it, for Allah is the One who protects them.'"],[3874,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Baqi' al-Gharqad, walking behind him, he said: 'You are not guided, nor do you find guidance. You are not guided, nor do you find guidance. You are not guided, nor do you find guidance.' Abu Rafi' said, 'What is wrong with me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'I do not mean you. I mean the occupant of this grave. He was asked about me and claimed he did not know me.' And there was a grave sprinkled with water when its occupant was buried."],[3875,"The Prophet ﷺ was made a Prophet on Monday, and Ali embraced Islam on Tuesday."],[3876,"The first man to embrace Islam was Ali, and the first woman to embrace Islam was Khadijah."],[3877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali before his death: 'You will discharge my liability and be killed upon my Sunnah.'"],[3878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Ali as commander over Yemen, and a man from Aslam called 'Amr b. Shas went out with him. He returned while disparaging 'Ali and complaining about him. The Messenger of Allah sent for him and said: \""],[3879,"\"A sheep's stomach was cooked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he ate, then prayed and did not perform wudu'.\""],[3880,"I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg.' He said: 'Eat it.'"],[3881,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ circumambulate the House on his mount, touching the corner with his staff.\""],[3882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali b. Abi Talib: 'Allah commanded me to teach you and not to be harsh with you, and to draw you near and not to distance you. It is my duty to teach you, and your duty to retain it.'"],[3883,"\"The Prophet ﷺ called the adhan in the ear of al-Hasan b. 'Ali when his mother Fatimah gave birth to him, with the prayer.\""],[3884,"\"The Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl for the two Eids, and came to the Eid walking, and returned by a route other than the one he took out.\""],[3885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: 'There will be something between you and 'A'ishah.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, me?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Me among all my companions?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then I am the most wretched of them?' He said: 'No. When that happens, return her to her place of safety.'"],[3886,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and reached Baqi' al-Gharqad. He turned to me and said: 'Do you hear what I hear?' I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, no, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'This is So-and-so b. So-and-so being punished in his grave for a cloak he stole on the day of Khaybar.'"],[3887,"When you name someone Muhammad, do not strike him and do not deprive him."],[3888,"When one of you's ear rings, let him say: 'O Allah, remember with good whoever remembered us with good.'"],[3889,"We found a sheet in the scabbard of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after his death, in which was written: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Separate the beds of boys and girls, and brothers and sisters, at seven years. And strike your children for the prayer when they reach—I think he said—nine. Cursed, cursed is the one who claims descent from other than his people or affiliation to other than his patrons. Cursed is the one who encroaches upon any part of the boundaries of the land."],[3890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died with his head in the lap of 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and he was saying to 'Ali: 'Fear Allah, fear Allah regarding what your right hands possess; fear Allah, fear Allah regarding the prayer.' That was the last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke."],[3891,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in prayer, he struck something during his prayer, and it was a scorpion; he struck it and killed it, and he ordered the killing of the scorpion, the snake, the mouse, and the kite for the one in ihram."],[3892,"Ibn 'Abbas said to us: 'Shall I not tell you about the conversion of Abu Dharr?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: Abu Dharr said: 'I was a man from Banu Ghifar. It reached us that a man had appeared in Makkah claiming to be a prophet. I said to my brother: \"Go to this man, speak with him, and bring me news of him.\" He went and met him, then returned. I said: \"What do you have?\" He said: \"By Allah, I saw a man commanding good and forbidding evil.\" I said: \"You have not satisfied me with the news.\" So I took a provision bag and a staff, then set out for Makkah. I did not know him and disliked asking about him. I drank from the water of Zamzam and stayed in the mosque. A man passed by me and said: \"The man seems to be a stranger.\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Come to the house.\" I went with him, neither he asking me about anything nor I asking him. When morning came, I went to the mosque to ask about him, but no one told me anything about him. A man passed by me and said: \"Do you know his house?\" I still did not know his house. I said: \"No.\" He went with me and brought me into his house, then said to me: \"What brought you to this town?\" I said: \"It reached us that a man has appeared here claiming to be a prophet. I sent my brother, but he did not satisfy me with the news, so I wanted to meet him.\" He said to me: \"Indeed, you have been guided. This is my way to him. Follow me and enter where I enter. If I see someone I fear for you, I will stand by the wall as if fixing my sandal, and you go on.\" He went and I went with him until he entered and I entered with him. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, present Islam to me.\" He presented it to me, and I embraced Islam on the spot. He said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, return to your land, and when our appearance reaches you, come.\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will proclaim it among them.\" He came to the mosque while Quraysh were there and said: \"O assembly of Quraysh, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" They said: \"Rise against this apostate.\" They rose and beat me until I almost died. Al-'Abbas caught up with me, leaned over me, and said: \"Woe to you! You are killing a man from Banu Ghifar, and your trade route passes through Ghifar.\" So they left me. When morning came, I went to the mosque and said the same as I had said the day before, and they did to me the same as they had done the day before. Al-'Abbas caught up with me, leaned over me, and said: \"You are killing a man from Banu Ghifar,\" and he said the same as his statement the day before. This was the conversion of Abu Dharr.'"],[3893,"The most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me is the one who follows me upon what I have covenanted with him."],[3894,"I said to Abu Dharr: 'O uncle, advise me.' He said: 'You have asked me as I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"If you pray the forenoon prayer two rak'ahs, you will not be recorded among the heedless; if you pray four, you will be among the devoted worshippers; if you pray six, no sin will catch up with you; if you pray eight, you will be recorded among the obedient; and if you pray twelve, a house will be built for you in Paradise. And there is no day, no night, no hour, but Allah has in it a charity which He bestows upon whom He wills of His servants, and He has not bestowed upon a servant anything like inspiring him with His remembrance.\"'"],[3895,"Abu Dharr stood at the gathering of Banu Ghifar and said: 'O Banu Ghifar, say and do not swear three times that the truthful, the believed one told me that people will be gathered in three groups: a group well-fed and well-clothed, a group walking and running, and a group whom the Fire will gather and the angels will drag on their faces.' A speaker said: 'These we know and these we know. What about those who walk and run?' He said: 'Allah will cast affliction upon the riding animals, so that a man with a garden will offer it for an old camel—I think he said—and he will not give it, or he will not be able to.'"],[3896,"The roof of my house split open while I was in Makkah, and Gabriel ﷺ descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water. Then he brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith and poured it into my chest, then closed it. Then he took my hand—I think he said—and ascended with me to the heaven. When we came to the lowest heaven, Gabriel said to the keeper of the heaven: 'Open.' He said: 'Who is this?' Gabriel said: 'Gabriel.' He said: 'Is there anyone with you?' He said: 'With me is Muhammad ﷺ.' He said: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then he opened.' When we ascended to the lowest heaven, I saw a man sitting, and he said: 'Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous son.' I said to Gabriel: 'Who is this?' He said: 'This is Adam.' Then he ascended with me until he came to the second heaven, and Gabriel said to its keeper the same as he had said to the keeper of the lowest heaven. Anas said: He mentioned that he found in the heavens Idris, Musa, 'Isa, and Ibrahim, and he mentioned that he found Ibrahim in the sixth heaven, and he said: 'Welcome to the righteous prophet.' I said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Ibrahim.'"],[3897,"There is no Arabian horse but that it is given permission at every dawn to make two supplications, saying: 'O Allah, You have placed me in the charge of one of Your servants; make me the most beloved of his family and wealth to him, or the most beloved of his family and wealth to him.'"],[3898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'After me, affliction will befall you.' I said: 'For the sake of Allah?' He said: 'For the sake of Allah.' I said: 'Welcome to the command of Allah.' He said: 'O Abu Dharr, hear and obey,' and I think he said: 'even if to a black slave.'"],[3899,"I was in the mosque, and Abu Dharr entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs by a pillar. 'Uthman said to him: 'How are you?' He said: 'Fine. How are you?' Then he turned away and began reciting 'The mutual rivalry for piling up diverts you,' and he was a man with a strong voice, so he raised his voice and the mosque reverberated. Then he turned to the people. I said: 'O Abu Dharr,' or the people said to him..."],[3900,"For wheat, its charity is due."],[3901,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ left us, and there is no bird in the sky flapping its wings but that he has given us knowledge about it.\""],[3902,"He said to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib: \"You are the first to believe in me, and you are the first to shake my hand on the Day of Resurrection, and you are the greatest verifier (al-Ṣiddīq al-Akbar), and you are the distinguisher (al-Fārūq) who distinguishes between truth and falsehood, and you are the leader of the believers, while wealth is the leader of the disbelievers.\""],[3903,"Abū Dharr said to me: \"O son of my brother, I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ holding his hand, and he said: 'O Abā Dharr, I would not love to have a mountain of gold and silver that I spend in the path of God, and then die on the day I die leaving behind a qīrāṭ of it.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, a qinṭār?' He said: 'O Abā Dharr, you go to the lesser and I go to the greater; I desire the Hereafter and you desire this world: a qīrāṭ.'\" He repeated it to me three times."],[3904,"The likeness of my household is like the ark of Noah: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it drowns, and whoever fights us in the latter days is like one who fights alongside the Dajjāl."],[3905,"I was sitting among people of Quraysh when Abū Dharr came until he was near them and said: \"Give glad tidings to the hoarders of wealth of a branding on their backs that will come out from their bellies.\" I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"Abū Dharr.\" So I went to him and said: \"What is this that I heard you call out before?\" He said: \"I did not say anything to them except something I heard from their Prophet ﷺ.\" I said: \"What do you say about this grant?\" He said: \"Take it today, for in it there is assistance; but if it becomes a price for your religion, then leave it.\""],[3906,"I came to Madinah."],[3907,"There is no servant who prostrates to God a single prostration but that God raises him a degree by it and removes from him a sin by it."],[3908,"Fasting three days of every month is fasting the entire year. Then he said: \"God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. God says: 'Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times the like of it.'\""],[3909,"\"If I had seen the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would have asked him.\" He said: \"About what would you have asked him?\" I said: \"I would have asked him: 'Did you see your Lord?'\" He said: \"I did ask him, and he said: 'Light—how could I see Him?'\""],[3910,"I said to Abū Dharr: \"If I had seen the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would have asked him.\" He said: \"About what thing would you have asked him?\" I said: \"I would have asked him: 'Did you see your Lord?'\" He said: \"I did ask him, and he said: 'How could I see Him?'\""],[3911,"I came to Madinah, and there was a man standing over black sacks saying: \"Shall I not give glad tidings to the owners of treasures of a branding on the foreheads and the sides?\" They said: \"This is Abū Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[3912,"News of Abū Dharr used to reach me—a hadith that I desired to meet him for—I think he said—so I met him, and I said: \"I was eager to meet you.\" He said: \"May your father be for God, for you have indeed met me, so bring it on.\" I said: \"It used to reach me from you that you claim that the Messenger of God ﷺ told you that God, Blessed and Exalted, loves three and hates three.\" He said: \"Yes, and I do not think that I would lie about my close friend; yes, and I do not think that I would lie about my close friend; yes, and I do not think that I would lie about my close friend.\" I said: \"So who are these three whom God loves?\" He said: \"A man who goes out in the path of God seeking reward and striving, then meets the enemy and fights.\" He said: \"And you will find it in the revealed Book of God,\" then he recited this verse: 'Indeed, God loves those who fight in His path in rows as if they were a compact structure.' I said: \"And who else?\" He said: \"And a man who has a bad neighbor who harms him, and he bears his harm patiently and seeks reward until God suffices him or he dies.\" I said: \"And who else?\" He said: \"And a man who is an unbeliever among a people, and they travel at night until when they are in the last part of the night, exhaustion and sleepiness overcome them, so they dismount and lay down their heads; but he performs ablution and stands to purify himself and prays out of fear of God and desire for what is with Him.\" I said: \"So who are the three whom God hates?\" He said: \"The arrogant boastful one—and you will find it with you, meaning in the Book of God: 'Indeed, God does not love anyone who is arrogant and boastful.'\" I said: \"And who else?\" He said: \"The miser who reminds of his favors.\" I said: \"And who else?\" He said: \"The merchant who swears much,\" or \"the seller who swears much.\" Yazīd said: \"I do not know which of the two he said.\" I said: \"O Abā Dharr, what is wealth?\" He said: \"What has come in the morning and does not last till evening, and what has come in the evening and does not last till morning.\" I said: \"O Abā Dharr, what is the matter with you and your brothers of Quraysh?\" He said: \"By God, I will not seek their help in religion, nor will I ask them for worldly things until I meet God and His Messenger. By God, I will not seek their help in religion, nor will I ask them for worldly things until I meet God and His Messenger.\""],[3913,"There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He (the narrator) said: I said..."],[3914,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus, and Habib b. al-Shahid, and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Hidden text: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He said: I said...]"],[3915,"Abu Hurrah narrated to us, whose name is Wasil b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Hidden text: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He said: I said...]"],[3916,"Al-Mufaddal b. Lahiq narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Hidden text: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He said: I said...]"],[3917,"Jarir b. Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ. He mentioned all of these similar to the hadith of Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah b. Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Hidden text: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He said: I said...]"],[3918,"'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from 'Anbasah, who is 'Anbasah b. Abi Ra'itah, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ similar to the hadith of Bishr b. Yunus. As for the hadith of Humayd and Habib, we do not know that anyone narrated them except Hammad b. Salamah. As for the hadith of al-Mufaddal b. Lahiq, we do not know that anyone narrated it from him except 'Abd al-Samad, and we do not recall that al-Mufaddal attributed any hadith to al-Hasan other than this one. As for the hadith of Ash'ath, it was narrated by Quraysh b. Anas. As for the hadith of 'Anbasah, we do not know that anyone narrated it except 'Abd al-Wahhab. [Hidden text: There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. He said: I said...]"],[3919,"Whoever frees a believing slave, he will be rewarded for every limb, or he will protect every limb of his from the Fire."],[3920,"The deeds of my Ummah were presented to me, their good deeds and their bad deeds. I saw among the good deeds of my Ummah the removal of harmful things from the road, and I found among the bad deeds of my Ummah the phlegm that is in the mosque - I think he said - and is not buried."],[3921,"They said: O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken the rewards; they pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and give charity from the surplus of their wealth. He said: Has Allah not given you that from which you can give charity? Indeed, every glorification is charity, every praise is charity, every magnification is charity, every declaration of tawhid is charity, commanding good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and in the intimate relations of one of you - or he said: in the intimate relations of one of you with his wife - there is charity. They said: O Prophet of Allah, one of us satisfies his desire and he gets a reward for it? He said: Do you not see that if he placed it in what is forbidden, he would bear a burden? So likewise, if he places it in what is lawful, he gets a reward."],[3922,"Wasil narrated to us, from Yahya b. 'Uqayl, from Yahya b. Ya'mar, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ similar to it."],[3923,"No man accuses another man of wickedness, nor accuses him of disbelief, but it is returned to him if his companion is not as he said."],[3924,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was wearing a white garment and he was asleep. Then I came to him again and he was asleep. Then I came to him and he had woken up, so I sat next to him. He said: There is no servant who says: There is no god but Allah, and then dies upon that, but he will enter Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals. I said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals. He said: Then on the fourth time he said: In spite of Abu Dharr's nose. Abu Dharr went out saying: Even if Abu Dharr's nose is rubbed in the dust. Abu Dharr used to narrate this hadith, and he would narrate with it: Even if Abu Dharr's nose is rubbed in the dust."],[3925,"Aglah narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from Yahya b. Yaʿmar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[3926,"Indeed, the best with which gray hair is changed is henna and katam. And Yahya said: katam and henna."],[3927,"\"Those of your slaves who suit you, feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear. And those who do not suit you, sell them, and do not torture the creation of God.\""],[3928,"\"Indeed, I see what you do not see and hear what you do not hear. The sky groaned—meaning the heaven—and there is not in it a space of four fingers except that an angel is placing his forehead prostrating to God. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.\" He said: \"I would love to be a tree that is cut down.\""],[3929,"He was with Abu Dharr when his stipend came out, and with him was a slave-girl of his who took care of his needs. Some pieces of it were left over, so he ordered her to buy small coins with them. I said: If only you had saved it for a need that might befall you, or for a guest who might come to you. He said: My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me that any gold or silver that is tied up in a bag—or one of them—is a burning coal upon its owner until he spends it in the way of God."],[3930,"\"The prayer is cut off by the black dog, the donkey, and the woman.\""],[3931,"\"What will you do when hardship reaches you such that a man is unable to get up to his bed from exhaustion?\" He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Abstain.\" He said: \"O Abu Dharr, what will you do when death becomes so widespread that a house is sold for a slave?\" He said: I said to Abu ʿImran: What is the house? He said: The grave. I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Then be patient.\" He said: \"O Abu Dharr, I think he said: What will you do when killing becomes so widespread that the stones of the olive grove are submerged in blood?\" He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Stay in your house.\" He said: I said: What if I am not left alone? He said: \"Join those whom you are from.\" I said: Should I carry a weapon with me? He said: \"Then you have shared with them.\" He said: \"If you fear that the flash of the sword will dazzle you, then take the edge of your garment and throw it over your face; he will bear his sin and your sin.\""],[3932,"\"Zamzam is food that nourishes and a healing for sickness.\""],[3933,"\"The prayer of a man is cut off, if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle, by the donkey, the woman, and the black dog.\" He said: I said: What about the black one as opposed to the white or the red one? He said: Nephew, I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: \"The black dog is a devil.\""],[3934,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ: Did you see your Lord? He said: \"Light—how could I see Him?\""],[3935,"Saʿid narrated to us, from Qatadah, or Matar al-Warraq, from Humayd b. Hilal, from ʿAbd Allah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr."],[3936,"ʿAbd Allah b. Shawdhab narrated to us, from Matar, from Humayd b. Hilal, from ʿAbd Allah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3937,"Hisham, the companion of al-Dastuwa'i, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3938,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3939,"Hammad—meaning Ibn Salamah—narrated to us, from Ayyub, and Yunus b. 'Ubayd, and Habib b. al-Shahid, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3940,"Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus—meaning Ibn 'Ubayd—and Mansur—meaning Ibn Zadhan—from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3941,"Hisham—meaning Ibn Hassan—and Ash'ath b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3942,"Humayd b. Hilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3943,"'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3944,"And 'Amr b. 'Ali, Azhar b. Jamil, Ziyad b. Yahya, and Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us. They said: Al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Salm b. Abi al-Dhayyal, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3945,"\"The prayer of a man is cut off if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle: the donkey, the woman, and the black dog.\" He said: I said: \"O Abu Dharr, what is the matter with the black dog as opposed to the white or the red?\" He said: \"O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: 'The black dog is a devil.'\""],[3946,"Abu Dawud and Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us. They said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3947,"'Abdullah b. 'Umar al-Muzani narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3948,"\"The black dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off the prayer.\" He said: I said to Abu Dharr: \"What is the matter with the black dog as opposed to the yellow or the white?\" He said: \"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: 'The black dog is a devil.'\""],[3949,"He said to me: \"O son of my brother, I prayed for three years before I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: I said: \"So where did you turn (in prayer)?\" He said: \"I used to turn wherever Allah directed me. I would stand in prayer at night as long as Allah willed, and when it was the last part of the night I would throw myself down as if I were a garment, and we were with our maternal uncle. A man said to him: 'Unays is taking your place with your family.' He said: So he said to him: 'My brother Unays, O uncle, as for the good you have done, by Allah you have spoiled it, and as for us, we will not live with you in a land where you are.' He said: And we were with our mother at our herd, and my brother Unays challenged a man to a contest over our herd, and they referred the matter to a man among the soothsayers. Unays kept praising him until he defeated him, so he took his herd and added it to our herd. Then my brother Unays went to Makkah and said: 'I saw there a man who is the most similar of people to you, called the Sabian.' He said: I said: 'I will go and look.' He said: So I came to Makkah and approached a man and said: 'Where is this one called the Sabian?' He said: So he raised his voice and said: 'Sabian! Sabian!' He said: So I was stoned until I was left as if I were such-and-such - a word mentioned by Ibn Abi 'Adi - then I went off and stayed between Makkah and its veils. One night I went out, and there were two women circumambulating, calling upon Yasaf and Na'ilah. He said: I said: 'Marry one of them to the other.' They said: 'Sabian! Sabian!' He said: I said: 'I am a thing like a piece of wood in a thing, except that I do not use a kunyah.' He said: So they went off, and then they came upon the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr coming from the lower part of Makkah. They said: 'This Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its veils.' The Prophet ﷺ came and circumambulated the House and prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam. He said: So I came to him. He said: I was the first of people to greet him with the greeting of Islam. He said: I said: 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'And upon you, who are you?' I said: 'I am from Banu Ghifar.' He said: So he placed his hand on his face like this. He said: I said: He disliked the people to whom I attributed myself, so I went to remove his hand. He said: So his companion placed his hand below mine, and he was more knowledgeable than me. He said: So he raised his hand and said: 'How long have you been here?' He said: I said: 'For fifteen (days).' He said: 'What has been your food?' I said: 'The water of Zamzam, and I have not felt any weakness of hunger on my liver, and the folds of my belly have become creased.' He said: 'Indeed it is a food that nourishes and a cure for sickness.' He said: So Abu Bakr said: 'Let me host him tonight.' He said: So he took me to a house in the lower part of Makkah and gave me handfuls of raisins. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'A land with palm trees has been mentioned to me, so when you hear that we have come to it, come to us.' He said: So I returned to my family. Unays said: 'What did you do?' I said: 'I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam.' He said: 'I have no desire to turn away from your religion' or 'I have no desire away from your religion,' so my brother embraced Islam, and my mother said: 'I have no desire away from the religion of you two,' so she embraced Islam, and some people of our tribe embraced Islam. He said: 'The other half (will embrace Islam) when I meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we may stipulate conditions for ourselves.'"],[3950,"Muhammad b. 'Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, something similar."],[3951,"We went out with our tribe Ghifar, and they used to violate the sacred month. I, my brother Unays, and our mother went out until we came to a maternal uncle of ours who had wealth and good appearance. Our uncle treated us kindly, but his people envied us and said: 'Unays, when you go out, he takes your place with your family.' Our uncle came and told us what was said to him. We said to him: 'As for you, you have spoiled your past kindness, and there will be no gathering for us after this.' So we brought forward our herd, and our uncle covered himself with his cloak weeping. We went on until we were in a valley near Makkah. Unays competed over our herd and went to a soothsayer, and he came back to us with our herd and the like of it along with it. I had prayed, O son of my brother, for three years before I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I said: 'To whom?' He said: 'To Allah.' I said: 'Where did you turn?' He said: 'Wherever Allah directed me. I prayed at night until, when it was the time before dawn, I threw myself down as if I were a garment until the sun rose over me.' Unays said to me: 'I am going to Makkah, so suffice me until I come to you.' He went and was slow in returning to me. Then he came, and I said: 'What delayed you?' He said: 'I met in Makkah a man upon your religion who claims that Allah sent him.' He said: I said: 'What do people say about him?' He said: 'They say: a poet, a soothsayer. I have heard the speech of soothsayers, and it is not their speech. I have placed his speech upon the modes of poetry, and it does not fit upon the tongue of anyone.' Abu Dharr said: 'O son of my brother, Unays was one of the poets.' He said: 'By Allah, he is truthful.' He said: I said: 'Then suffice me until I go to Makkah.' He said: 'Yes, but be wary of the people of Makkah, for they are hostile to him.' He said: So I went and asked a man among them: 'Where is the one they call the Sabian?' He said: So he pointed at me and said: 'Sabian! Sabian!' He said: So the people of the valley pelted me with every stone and bone until I fell unconscious. When I regained consciousness, I was like a standing idol. I went to Zamzam and washed the blood off myself and drank from its water. I stayed, O son of my brother, thirty days and nights, having no food or drink except Zamzam, and I became fat until the folds of my belly became creased, and I did not feel any weakness of hunger on my liver. He said: While I was one night on a moonlit, bright night, Allah struck the ears of the people of Makkah, so none of them was circumambulating the House except two women calling upon Yasaf and Na'ilah. I put out my head and said: 'Marry one of them to the other.' By Allah, they did not stop. Then they came upon me while they were calling upon Yasaf and Na'ilah, and I said: 'A thing like a piece of wood, except that I am not called by a kunyah.' They went off wailing and saying: 'If only one of our people were here.' The first to meet them was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, coming down from the mountain. They said: 'The Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its veils.' He said: 'What did he say to you?' They said: 'He said to us a word that fills the mouth.' He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and began with the Black Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House seven times. I reached him while he and his companion were there, and I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam. He said: 'And upon you and the mercy of Allah. Who are you?' I said: 'A man from Banu Ghifar.' He said: So he placed his hand on his forehead. I said to myself: He disliked that I attributed myself to Ghifar, so I went to remove his hand from his forehead, but his companion prevented me, and he was more knowledgeable about him than I. He said: 'How long have you been here?' I said: 'For thirty days and nights.' He said: 'What has been your food?' I said: 'I had no food except the water of Zamzam, and I became fat until the folds of my belly became creased, and I did not feel any weakness of hunger on my liver.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed it is blessed, and it is a food that nourishes.' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, let me have the honor of feeding him tonight.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went, Abu Bakr went, and I went with them. He opened a door for us and gave us a handful of Ta'if raisins - I think he said: a handful. That was the first food I ate there. He said: I stayed for some time, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'I have been directed to a land of palm trees, which I think is only Yathrib. Will you convey from me to your people, that Allah may benefit them through you?' He said: So I went until I came to my brother Unays. He said to me: 'What did you do?' I said: 'I have embraced Islam and believed.' He said to me: 'I have no desire to turn away from your religion, so I have embraced Islam and believed.' Then we came to our mother and presented Islam to her, and she said: 'I have no desire to turn away from the religion of you two, so I have embraced Islam and believed.' Then we set out until we came to our tribe Ghifar and presented Islam to them. Half of them embraced Islam, and the remaining half said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrives in Madinah, we will embrace Islam.' Ima' - meaning Ibn Rahadah al-Ghifari - used to lead them in prayer, and he was their chief. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the rest of them embraced Islam. Then our brothers from Aslam came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we embrace Islam upon the same terms as Ghifar embraced Islam.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ghifar - may Allah forgive her, and Aslam - may Allah grant her peace.'"],[3952,"Al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Murrah, from Abu al-Nadr, that is Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, something similar to the hadith of Sulayman b. al-Mughirah concerning the mention of his embracing Islam, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned the story in full. This hadith from al-A'mash with this chain we have heard only from Yahya b. Mu'alla, from his father, from 'Aththam."],[3953,"Sulayman b. al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from 'Abdullah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3954,"O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but cannot do the deeds they do. He said: 'You, O Abu Dharr, will be with the one you love.'"],[3955,"I asked my close friend, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, and he struck my thigh and said: 'Pray the prayer at its appointed time. If you catch the prayer with them, then pray with them, and do not say: I have already prayed, so I will not pray with them.'"],[3956,"\"How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer?\" - I think he said: 'What do you command me?' - He said: \"Pray the prayer at its proper time, then if you are in the mosque until the prayer is established, pray with them.\""],[3957,"The Prophet ﷺ struck his thigh and then said: \"How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer?\" He said: \"Pray the prayer at its proper time, and if you are in the mosque until the prayer is established, then pray with them.\""],[3958,"O Messenger of Allah, a man does a good deed for himself and then people love him (for it). He said: 'That is the immediate glad tidings for the believer.'"],[3959,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a good deed for himself and then people love him (for it). He said: 'That is the immediate glad tidings for the believer.'"],[3960,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: to listen and obey even if the leader is a slave with maimed limbs; when I make a broth, to look to increase its water, then look to people among my neighbors and give them some of it, or words to that effect; and to pray the prayer at its proper time, and if you catch the imam and he has already prayed, then your prayer suffices you, otherwise it is a supererogatory prayer for you."],[3961,"Sālih b. Rustum narrated to us, from Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī, from ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ṣāmit, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3962,"\"How will you act when exhaustion reaches such a point that a man cannot even get up to his bed from exhaustion?\" He said: \"I said: Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Keep yourself chaste.\" He said: \"O Abū Dharr, how will you act when death becomes so widespread that a house is sold for a slave?\" He said: \"I said to Abū ʿImrān: What is the house?\" He said: \"The grave.\" He said: \"I said: Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Then be patient, or you will be patient.\" He said: \"O Abū Dharr, how will you act when killing becomes so widespread that the stones of al-Zayt are drowned in blood?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Stay in your house.\" I said: \"What if I am not left alone?\" He said: \"Then join those whom you are from.\" I said: \"Should I carry a weapon with me?\" He said: \"Then you have shared with the people in it.\" He said: \"I said: So what should I do?\" He said: \"If you fear that the flash of the sword will dazzle you, then take the edge of your garment and throw it over your face; he will bear your sin and his own sin.\""],[3963,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the vessels of the ḥawḍ like?\" He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, its vessels are more numerous than the number of stars in the sky on a clear night. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst again. The last of it: two spouts from Paradise pour into it, its width is like its length, from ʿAmmān to Aylah. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey.\""],[3964,"\"When you cook a pot, make more broth, and ladle out for your neighbors.\""],[3965,"\"Do not belittle any act of kindness, even if you only meet people with a cheerful face. And when you cook a pot, make more of its water, and ladle out for your neighbors.\""],[3966,"\"Visit occasionally and you will increase in love.\""],[3967,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked which of the two terms Mūsā fulfilled. He said: \"The more complete and more righteous of them. And if you are asked which of the two women he married, say: the younger of them.\""],[3968,"\"Al-Shām is the land of the gathering and the resurrection.\""],[3969,"\"My close friend ﷺ enjoined me to maintain ties with my relatives even if they turn away, to speak the truth even if it is bitter, to not let the blame of any blamer overtake me in the cause of Allah, to look at those who are below me and not at those who are above me, to sit with the poor, and to say frequently: lā ḥawla wa-lā quwwata illā billāh (There is no power and no strength except with Allah).\""],[3970,"\"The most beloved speech to Allah is subḥān Allāh wa-bi-ḥamdih (Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him).\""],[3971,"Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Jurayrī, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ṣāmit, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know this hadith being narrated with this wording from Abū Dharr except through this route."],[3972,"Al-Jurayrī narrated to us, from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ, from Nuʿaym b. Qaʿnab, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3973,"The likeness of a woman is like a rib: if you try to straighten it, you break it, and if you seek enjoyment from it, it has a crookedness."],[3974,"Abu Dharr claimed that they were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk, and they came upon a valley. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: 'You are in a cursed valley, so hurry.' He mounted his horse and pushed on, and the people pushed on. Then he said: 'Whoever has kneaded his dough or cooked a pot, let him overturn it.' Then we traveled on. Then he said: 'O people, there is no soul born today upon which a hundred years pass and God cares about it anything.'"],[3975,"The evil eye can indeed, by God's permission, make a man climb a high place and then fall from it."],[3976,"Clean earth is the ablution of the Muslim—or the believer—even if he does not find water for ten years. When he finds it, let him fear God and let the water touch his skin—or he said—his body, for that is better."],[3977,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from 'Amr b. Mihjan—or Mihjan—from Abu Dharr—Qabisah was uncertain—from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know of this wording being reported from Abu Dharr except through this chain."],[3978,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ on the stony ground of Madinah while we were looking at Uhud. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Abu Dharr.' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'I would not like to have gold equal to Uhud with me and let a third night pass while I have a dinar of it, except a dinar I set aside for a debt.' Then he walked and said: 'O Abu Dharr.' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Indeed, those who have the most are the ones with the least on the Day of Resurrection, except one who gives away wealth like this, and like this, and like this.' Then he walked and said: 'O Abu Dharr, stay where you are until I come to you.' He went off and hid from me, and I heard a murmur and voices. I said: 'Perhaps something has happened to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I wanted to follow him, but I remembered his words: 'Do not leave until I come to you.' I waited until he came back. I told him what I had heard. He said: 'That was Jibril ﷺ . He came to me and said: Whoever of his ummah dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals.'"],[3979,"Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[3980,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, al-A'mash, Hammad, and 'Abd al-'Aziz—meaning Ibn Rufay'—from Zayd b. Wahb, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah. This hadith was reported by al-A'mash, Habib b. Abi Thabit, Hammad b. Abi Sulayman, and 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufay' from Zayd b. Wahb from Abu Dharr from the Prophet ﷺ. And al-Hasan b. 'Ubayd Allah reported it from Zayd b. Wahb from Abu al-Darda' from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3981,"Jibril said to me: 'Whoever of your ummah dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise'—or 'will not enter the Fire.' I said: 'Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals?' He said: 'Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals.'"],[3982,"'O Abu Dharr, raise your eyes and look at the tallest man you see in the mosque.' I looked and saw a man wearing a fine garment. I said: 'This one.' He said: 'O Abu Dharr, look at the lowliest man you see in the mosque.' I looked and saw a man wrapped in patched clothes. I said: 'This one.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, this one is better in God's sight on the Day of Resurrection than the fill of the earth of that one.'"],[3983,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the shade of the Ka'bah, and he was saying: 'They are the losers, by the Lord of the Ka'bah'—he said it twice. I said: 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, who are they?' He said: 'Those with the most wealth, except one who gives like this and like this, and few are they. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one dies leaving camels, cattle, or sheep without paying their due right except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection larger and fatter than they were, goring him with their horns and trampling him with their hooves. Every time the last of them passes, the first of them will return to him, until judgment is passed among the people.'"],[3984,"I went out one night, and there was the Messenger of God ﷺ alone, with no one with him. I thought he disliked having anyone with him, so I walked in the moonlight. He turned and saw me and said: 'Who is this?' I said: 'Abu Dharr, may God make me your ransom.' He said: 'Walk with me for a while.' Then he said: 'Those who have the most are the ones with the least, except one who gives—meaning from his right, his left, in front of him, and behind him.' Then he walked with me for a while, then said: 'Sit here.' He stayed away from me for a long time. Then I heard him coming back, and he was saying: '...even if he steals.' I said: 'May God make me your ransom, who were you talking to on the side of the lava field? I did not hear anyone answer you.' He said: 'That was Jibril ﷺ . He appeared to me on the side of the lava field and said: Give glad tidings to your ummah that whoever dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise.' I said: 'Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Even if he commits adultery and even if he steals?' He said: 'Yes, even if he is disgraced.'"],[3985,"\"Indeed, the intensity of the heat is a blast from Jahannam, so cool down the prayer in intense heat.\""],[3986,"To swear several times that Ibn Ṣāʾid is the Dajjāl is dearer to me than to swear once that he is not. A child was born among the Jews, and the Prophet ﷺ sent to his mother asking how long she had carried him. I asked her, and she said, 'Twelve months.' I came to him and informed him, and he said, 'Ask her about his cry when he fell to the ground.' She said, 'A word that has left me.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'I have hidden something for you; what is it?' He said, 'The matter of ʿAfrāʾ and al-dukhān (smoke) is great.' Whenever he wanted to say 'al-dukhān,' he could not, so he said, 'al-dukhkh.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Be off! You will never outstrip the decree.'"],[3987,"A man from the desert said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the hyena has devoured us.' Then he repeated, 'The hyena has devoured us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am more fearful for you of other than the hyena, when the world is poured upon you abundantly. Would that my Ummah does not wear gold.'"],[3988,"Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Yazīd b. Abī Ziyād, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3989,"Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Yazīd b. Abī Ziyād, from Zayd b. Wahb, from a man, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the ḥadīth of Jarīr. We do not know this statement to be narrated except from Abū Dharr, nor do we know for it a path other than this path. The hyena is the year (i.e., famine), so they complained to him of the severity of the year's hardship."],[3990,"\"I indeed know the last of the people of Paradise to enter it, and the last of the people of the Fire to exit from the Fire. A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection,\" and it will be said, 'Present to him his minor sins, while his major sins are concealed from him.' It will be said to him, 'You did on such-and-such a day such-and-such,' and he will admit, not denying, while he is fearful of the major sins. It will be said, 'Give him, in place of every bad deed, a good deed.' He will say, 'I have sins that I do not see here.'\" He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh when he mentioned this ḥadīth until his molar teeth appeared."],[3991,"Whoever brings a good deed, for him is ten times its like or more; and whoever brings a bad deed, for him is its like or I forgive. Whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom. Whoever comes to Me with nearly the earth's fill — I think he said — of sins, provided he does not associate anything with Me, I will come to him with its fill of forgiveness."],[3992,"Ibrāhīm b. Ṭahmān narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Lāḥiq b. Ḥumayd, from al-Maʿrūr b. Suwayd, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3993,"Ibrāhīm said: And Manṣūr narrated it to me, from Ribʿī, from al-Maʿrūr, from Abū Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[3994,"\"O My servants, whoever of you performs a good deed, I will recompense him with ten or more; and whoever of you performs a bad deed, I will recompense him with a bad deed or I will forgive. Whoever meets Me without associating anything with Me, I will meet him with the earth's fill of forgiveness.\""],[3995,"There was between me and a man some words, and his mother was non-Arab, so I reproached him for her. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Abū Dharr, you are a man in whom there is ignorance. You reproach your brothers whom Allah has placed under your authority. So feed them from what you eat, clothe them from what you wear, and do not burden them — I think he said — with what they cannot bear. If you burden them, then help them.'"],[3996,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaʿbah. When he saw me, he said, 'They are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.' I said, 'Who are they?' He said, 'Those who have the most wealth, except one who says with wealth thus, thus, and thus. And there is no owner of camels, cattle, or sheep who does not pay their zakāh but they will come on the Day of Resurrection, as large as they ever were, goring him with their horns. Every time the last of them passes, the first of them returns to him, until judgment is passed among the people.'"],[3997,"Musa b. al-Musayyib narrated to us, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from al-Ma'rur b. Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3998,"\"O My servants, all of you are sinners except those whom I have pardoned, so seek forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. And all of you are astray except those whom I have guided, so ask Me for guidance and I will guide you. And all of you are poor except those whom I have enriched, so ask Me for provision and I will provide for you. And if the first of you and the last of you, your living and your dead, your fresh and your dry, were to unite upon the heart of the most devout servant among My servants, they would not increase My dominion by the wing of a mosquito. And if the first of you and the last of you, your living and your dead, your fresh and your dry, were to gather and each person were to ask for whatever his desire reached, and I gave every asker what he asked, that would not diminish Me except as when one of you passes by the shore of the sea and dips a needle into it and then pulls it out. That is because I am Most Generous, Most Glorious, All-Sufficient. My giving is a word, and My punishment is a word. When I intend something, I merely say to it, 'Be,' and it is.\""],[3999,"I saw Abu Dharr wearing a fine garment while his slave wore the same, so I asked him about that. He mentioned that he had insulted a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reviling him due to his mother. The man went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him about that. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Indeed you are a man in whom there is some pre-Islamic ignorance. Your brothers and your servants are those whom Allah has placed under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority should feed him from what he eats, clothe him from what he wears, and not burden them with what overwhelms them. If you burden them, then help them.'"],[4000,"\"Gabriel came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever from your nation dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise. I said, 'Even if he commits adultery and steals?' He said, 'Even if he commits adultery and steals.'\""],[4001,"Mahdi b. Maymun narrated to us, from Wasil, from al-Ma'rur, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4002,"\"If a servant were to fill the earth with sins and then not associate anything with Me, I would forgive him an earth full of sins, or nearly the earth's fill. And if he intends a good deed but does not perform it, one good deed is recorded for him, and if he performs it, ten good deeds are recorded. If he intends an evil deed and does not perform it, nothing is recorded. But if he performs it, one evil deed is recorded. And if he draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit. If he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom. And if he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed.\""],[4003,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from 'Asim, from al-Ma'rur b. Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4004,"We entered upon Abu Dharr and said, 'How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform tamattu' while you were with him?' He said, 'What do you have to do with that? That was something granted exclusively to us.'"],[4005,"\"Mut'ah was a concession that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us, or that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given.\""],[4006,"\"Mut'ah was a concession for us.\""],[4007,"\"Mut'ah was a concession for us.\""],[4008,"\"Mut'ah was exclusively for us.\""],[4009,"Regarding the mut'ah of the pilgrim: It is not for you, and you have nothing to do with it. It was only a concession for us, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ."],[4010,"Mut'ah was exclusively for us."],[4011,"I was with Ibrahim al-Nakha'i and Ibrahim al-Taymi, and I said: I have resolved to combine Hajj and 'Umrah this year. Ibrahim al-Nakha'i said: If your father were here, he would not have resolved to do that. And Ibrahim al-Taymi said, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr: Mut'ah was only a concession for us."],[4012,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a donkey, and the sun was near its setting. He said: O Abu Dharr, do you know where this sun goes when it sets? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It sets in a muddy spring, then it travels until it prostrates before its Lord beneath the Throne. When it is time for it to rise, Allah permits it. When Allah wills to make it rise from its west, He withholds it, and it says: O Lord, my journey is long. Then He says: Rise from where you set. That is the time when no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith."],[4013,"When the sun sets, it comes beneath the Throne and prostrates. It is said to it: Rise from where you used to rise. When it is night, it asks permission, and it is said to it: Rise from where you set, and it rises. Then he recited this verse: Do they await except that the angels should come to them or your Lord should come or that there come some of the signs of your Lord? The day that some of the signs of your Lord will come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith."],[4014,"Ibrahim b. Yazid al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not say: from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, but he sent it mursal."],[4015,"Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Harun b. Sa'd, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Hakam, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr."],[4016,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque when the sun set. He said: O Abu Dharr, do you know where the sun goes? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It goes until it prostrates and asks its Lord permission to return, and permission is granted to it. It is as if it is told: Return from where you came, so it returns to its west. That is His saying: And the sun runs to a fixed resting place."],[4017,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed first? He said: The Sacred Mosque, then the Aqsa Mosque. I said: How much was between them? He said: Forty years. So wherever the prayer overtakes you, pray, for that is a mosque."],[4018,"Waki' narrated to us, in the house, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from his father, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4019,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like the size of a partridge's nesting place, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[4020,"Raise your eyes and look: who is the highest man you see in the mosque? I looked and saw a man wearing a fine garment. I said: This one. Then he said: Look: who is the lowest man you see in the mosque? I looked and saw a man in worn-out clothes. I said: This one. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, this one is better in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the fill of the earth of the like of that one."],[4021,"Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Dharr"],[4022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"There is no might and no power except with Allah.\""],[4023,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping the pebbles (i.e., in prayer). He said: \"A single wipe.\""],[4024,"\"Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed and it will wipe it out, and behave well towards people.\""],[4025,"\"There are three with whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them: an old man who commits adultery, a king who is a liar, and a poor person who is arrogant.\""],[4026,"\"There are three with whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it three times. Abu Dharr said: \"Who are they? May they be disappointed and lose, may they be disappointed and lose, may they be disappointed and lose,\" three times. He said: \"The one who lets his garment hang below his ankles, the one who reminds others of his favours, and the one who sells his goods by a false oath.\""],[4027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sit among his companions, and a stranger would come and not know which of them he was. So we talked to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about setting up something for him by which a stranger would recognize him when he came. So we built for him a bench of clay, and he used to sit on it. I think he said: And we used to sit around him. While we were sitting and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his seat, a man approached, among the best of people in face, the most pleasant of people in scent, and the cleanest of people in clothing, as if his clothes had not been touched by dirt. He greeted from the edge of the mat and said: \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.\" He said: \"And upon you be peace.\" He said: \"May I come closer, O Muhammad?\" He said: \"Come closer.\" He kept saying: \"May I come closer, O Muhammad?\" and the Prophet ﷺ kept saying to him, several times, until he placed his hand on the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said: \"O Muhammad, what is Islam?\" He said: \"To worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to establish prayer, to give zakah, to perform Hajj to the House, and to fast Ramadan.\" He said: \"If I do this, then I have become a Muslim?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" When we heard the man's words to the Messenger of Allah, 'You have spoken the truth,' we found it strange. Then he said: \"Tell me, what is faith?\" He said: \"Faith in Allah, the angels, the Book, and the prophets, and to believe in the divine decree, all of it.\" He said: \"If I do that, then I have believed?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" He said: \"O Muhammad.\""],[4028,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most deserving of my good companionship? He said: \"Your mother, then your mother, then your mother.\" I said: \"Then who?\" He said: \"Then your father.\""],[4029,"\"There are three whom Allah loves, and three whom Allah hates. As for those whom Allah loves: a man who came to a people and asked them by Allah, not asking them by any kinship between them and him, but they refused him. Then a man remained behind them and gave him secretly, no one knowing of his gift except Allah and the one to whom he gave it. And a people who traveled through their night until sleep became dearer to them than anything they might equate with it; they dismounted and laid down their heads, but one man got up, seeking My favour and reciting My verses. And a man who was in a military detachment and they met the enemy and were defeated, so he advanced with his chest until he was killed or victory was granted to him. And the three whom Allah hates: the old man who commits adultery, the poor person who is conceited, and the rich person who is unjust.\""],[4030,"\"There are three whom Allah loves, and three whom Allah hates. Allah loves a man who was among a people when a beggar came to them asking by the countenance of Allah, not asking by any kinship between him and them, so they let him go. But he remained behind them where no one sees him except Allah and the one to whom he gave. And He loves a man who was in a battalion and it was routed, so he returned fighting until Allah granted him victory or he was killed. And He loves a man who was among a people and they traveled at night, and their night journey became long. Then they dismounted in the last part of the night, and sleep was dearer to one of them than anything he might equate with it, so they slept, but he got up reciting My verses and seeking My favour. And He hates the old man who commits adultery, the miser, and the arrogant. I think he said: 'And the conceited.'\""],[4031,"\"And the poor person who is conceited.\""],[4032,"We approached with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we halted at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Some men hurried on to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed the night, and we stayed with him. When morning came, he asked and said: \"They hurried to Madinah and to their wives. Indeed, they will leave it in the best condition it has ever been.\" And he said, for those who stayed with him, something good. Then he said: \"Would that I knew when a fire will emerge from Yemen, from the mountain of al-Warqan, by which the necks of camels will be illuminated in Busra.\""],[4033,"“Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom.” He said, “There is no might and no power except with Allah.”"],[4034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting while two sheep were fighting in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so one of them butted the other and caused it to miscarry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, and it was said, “What makes you laugh?” He said, “I marvel at her. By the One in whose hand is my soul, she will surely be brought to account for it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4035,"Hammad narrated to us, from Layth, from ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Tharwan, from al-Huzayl b. Sharahbil, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording except from Abu Dharr, and we do not know of anyone who traced it back as a musnad from Layth except Hammad b. Salama."],[4036,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat with him in the mosque. He said, “O Abu Dharr, seek refuge with Allah from the devils of mankind and jinn.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, do humans have devils?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “There is no might and no power except with Allah, for it is one of the treasures of Paradise.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is fasting?” He said, “An obligatory duty that suffices.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is prayer?” He said, “A good that is prescribed; whoever wishes may do less, and whoever wishes may do more.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is charity?” He said, “Multiplied many times over, and with Allah is more.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of them is best?” He said, “The effort of one with little, or a secret given to a poor person.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which verse revealed to you is greatest?” He said, “Allah—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living,” until he ended the verse. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of the prophets was first?” He said, “Adam.” I said, “Was he a prophet, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes, a prophet who was spoken to.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, how many prophets were there?” He said, “Three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude.”"],[4037,"Al-Hajjaj b. Artat narrated to us, from ‘Abd al-Malik b. al-Mughira, from ‘Abd Allah b. al-Miqdam, from Ibn Shaddad, from Abu Dharr."],[4038,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding, and a man came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, the other one has committed adultery.” He turned away from him. Then he came to him a second time and said, “The other one has committed adultery.” He turned away from him. Then he returned a third time and said, “The other one has committed adultery.” He turned away from him. Then he repeated a fourth time and said, “The other one has committed adultery.” He dismounted and ordered that he be stoned. Then he mounted, then he dismounted and said, “O Abu Dharr, your companion has been forgiven and admitted to Paradise.”"],[4039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.” It was said, “Which slaves are best to free?” He said, “The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.” He said, “If I cannot do that?” He said, “You help a lost person or make something for an unskilled person.” I said, “What if I am too weak for that?” He said, “You refrain from harming people, for it is a charity you give to yourself.”"],[4040,"Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from ‘Urwa, from Abu al-Marawih, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[4041,"I saw Abu Dharr sitting alone in the mosque, so I seized the opportunity and sat with him. I mentioned ‘Uthman to him, and he said, “I will never say anything about ‘Uthman except good, because of something I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I used to seek out the private moments of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to learn from him. One day I went and found that he had gone out, so I followed him. He sat in a spot and I sat with him. He said, ‘O Abu Dharr, what brought you?’ I said, ‘Allah and His Messenger.’ Then Abu Bakr came, greeted, and sat to the right of the Prophet ﷺ. He said to him, ‘What brought you, O Abu Bakr?’ He said, ‘Allah and His Messenger.’ Then ‘Umar came and sat to the right of Abu Bakr. He said, ‘O ‘Umar, what brought you?’ He said, ‘Allah and His Messenger.’ Then ‘Uthman came and sat to the right of ‘Umar. He said, ‘O ‘Uthman, what brought you?’ He said, ‘Allah and His Messenger.’ Then the Prophet ﷺ picked up seven pebbles—or nine pebbles—and they glorified Allah in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then they were placed in the hand of Abu Bakr and they glorified Allah in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he picked them up and placed them in the hand of ‘Umar, and they glorified Allah in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he picked them up and placed them in the hand of ‘Uthman, and they glorified Allah in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down and they fell silent.”"],[4042,"Sufyan—meaning al-Thawri—narrated to us, from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from al-Walid b. ‘Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr b. Nufayr, from Abu Dharr."],[4043,"We fasted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the month of Ramadan, and he did not lead us in night prayer until seven nights remained. Then he led us in prayer until a third of the night had passed, or about that. Then he did not lead us on the fourth night. He led us on the fifth night until about half the night had passed. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would let us pray the rest of our night as voluntary.” He said, “When a man prays with the imam until he finishes, the rest of his night is recorded for him.” Then he did not lead us on the sixth night. He led us on the seventh night, and he sent for his family and wives, and they gathered. He led us in prayer until we feared we would miss the falah.” I said, “What is the falah?” He said, “The pre-dawn meal.”"],[4044,"We fasted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[4045,"I used to seek out the private moments of the Messenger of God ﷺ. One day I went, and behold, he had gone out, so I followed him. He sat down in a place, and I sat near him. Then Abu Bakr came, greeted, and sat to the right of the Prophet ﷺ. Then Umar came and sat to the right of Abu Bakr. Then Uthman came and sat to the right of Umar. He said: The Prophet ﷺ took some pebbles, and they glorified God in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down, and they fell silent. Then he put them in the hand of Abu Bakr, and they glorified God in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down, and they fell silent. Then he took them and placed them in the hand of Umar, and they glorified God in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down, and they fell silent. Then he took them and placed them in the hand of Uthman, and they glorified God in his hand until I heard for them a humming like the humming of bees. Then he put them down, and they fell silent."],[4046,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'O Abu Dharr, I see that you are weak, and I love for you what I love for myself. Do not take command over two people, and do not take charge of the property of an orphan.'"],[4047,"He entered upon Abu Dharr among men from Aslam, among whom was a man from Juhaynah. Abu Dharr asked them, 'What has brought you?' They said, 'We have come to you to greet you and to hear from you.' He said, 'Shall I not give you glad tidings?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Whoever meets God without associating anything with Him will be forgiven, even if he has sins as much as the fill of the earth.' The Juhanī man said, 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' Abu Dharr glorified God and then said, 'Is it proper for a Muslim man to say about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say?' Then he said, 'Peace be upon you,' and rose."],[4048,"We entered upon Abu Dharr, and among us was a man from Aslam or a man from Juhaynah. He said, 'What has brought you?' We said, 'We have come to greet you.' He said, 'Rejoice! I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say...'"],[4049,"We said, 'O Messenger of God, how did you know that you are a prophet?' He said, 'I did not know until I was informed of that. O Abu Dharr, two angels came to me while I was in a part of the valley of Makkah. One of them said, \"Is he the one?\" The other said, \"Weigh him against a man.\" So I was weighed against a man, and I outweighed him. Then he said, \"Weigh him against ten.\" So he weighed me against ten, and I outweighed them. Then he said, \"Weigh him against a hundred.\" So he weighed me against a hundred, and I outweighed them. Then he said, \"Weigh him against a thousand.\" So he weighed me against a thousand, and I outweighed them. Then one of them said to the other, \"If you weighed him against his entire community, he would outweigh them.\" Then one of them said to the other, \"Split open his belly.\" So he split open my belly and removed from it the filth of Satan and the clot of blood, and he threw them away. Then one of them said to the other, \"Wash his belly as a vessel is washed, and wash his heart as a garment is washed.\" Then he called for tranquility, as if it were a white shining substance, and it was inserted into my heart. Then one of them said to his companion, \"Sew up his belly.\" So he sewed up my belly, and they placed the seal between my shoulders. It was not but that they turned away from me as if I were witnessing the matter with my own eyes.'"],[4050,"\"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? [It is] 'There is no might nor power except with God.'\""],[4051,"\"Whoever says at the end of the dawn prayer, while his leg is still folded, before speaking: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and death; in His hand is all good, and He is capable over everything' ten times, then for each one of them he will have ten good deeds, and ten evil deeds will be erased from him, and ten degrees will be raised for him, and for each one of them he will have the equivalent of freeing a slave, and that day he will be in protection from every disliked thing from Satan, and no sin will overtake him except associating partners with God.\""],[4052,"Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4053,"God, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'O My servants, all of you are sinful except those I have pardoned, so seek My forgiveness and I will forgive you. All of you are astray except those I have guided, so ask Me for guidance and I will guide you. All of you are poor except those I have enriched, so ask Me and I will provide for you. Whoever among you knows that I have power over forgiveness, I will forgive him by My power, and I do not care. If the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, your living and your dead, your fresh and your dry, were to unite upon the most pious heart of any servant among My servants, that would not increase My dominion by a mosquito's wing. And if the first of you and the last of you, your living and your dead, were to unite upon the most wicked heart of any servant among My servants, that would not decrease My dominion by a mosquito's wing. And if they were to unite and every asker asked for his wish, I would give every asker what he asked Me, and that would not diminish except as if one of you passed by the sea and dipped a needle into it and then withdrew it. For I am the Most Generous, the Majestic, the Finder. I do what I will. My giving is a word, and My punishment is a word. My command, when I desire a thing, is only that I say to it, \"Be,\" and it is.'"],[4054,"\"O My servants, I have forbidden injustice for Myself and have made it forbidden among you, so do not wrong one another. O My servants, you err by night and day, and I forgive all sins, so seek My forgiveness and I will forgive you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those I feed, so ask Me for food and I will feed you. O My servants, all of you are naked except those I clothe, so ask Me for clothing and I will clothe you. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were as pious as the most pious heart of any man among you, that would not increase My dominion in anything. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were to gather on a single plain and every person among them asked Me for what he asked, My dominion would not be diminished except as the sea is diminished when a needle is dipped into it once. O My servants, it is only your deeds that I keep count of for you. Whoever finds good, let him praise God; and whoever finds other than that, let him blame none but himself.\""],[4055,"I asked permission from the Messenger of God ﷺ to spend the night at his door so that he could wake me for his need. He gave me permission, so I spent a night remembering something or recollecting something I wanted to ask him about when morning came. He came out to me, and I said, 'O Messenger of God, I was sleepless last night wanting to ask you about something that preoccupied me. The wealthy companions have surpassed us with a clear lead: they pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and they do [good deeds] while they have wealth with which they give charity, and we do not have [wealth] to do that.' He said, 'Shall I not inform you, O Abu Dharr, of a deed by which you will catch up with those before you and surpass those after you, except one who does the like of your deed? You glorify God after every prayer thirty-three times, magnify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-four times.'"],[4056,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, accepts from - or forgives - His servant - or he said: accepts the repentance of His servant - as long as the veil has not fallen.\" It was said, \"What is the falling of the veil?\" He said, \"That the soul departs while it is associating partners with God.\""],[4057,"\"Indeed Allah forgives His servant as long as the veil has not fallen.\" They said: \"And what is the veil?\" He said: \"As long as the soul has not died while it is a polytheist.\""],[4058,"What will you do, O Abu Dharr, with the rulers after me who will seize this fay' for themselves? He said: I said: \"Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will place my sword until I meet you.\" He said: \"Shall I not guide you to what is better for you?\" He said: I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You should be patient until you meet me.\""],[4059,"\"Whoever separates from the community by a handspan has indeed cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck.\""],[4060,"\"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has placed the truth upon the tongue of 'Umar, and he speaks by it.\""],[4061,"When the pain of Abu Dharr intensified, or she said: he was attended, I said: \"You will die in a desert of the earth and I do not have anything to shroud him with.\" He said to me: \"Look at the road.\" So I began to go out and look, then return to him. While I was doing that, suddenly I saw men like vultures approaching. So I waved to them with my garment, and they hurried until they came towards me. I said to them: \"Would you like to attend a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?\" They said: \"Who is he?\" I said: \"Abu Dharr.\" So they ransomed him with their fathers and mothers. Then they entered upon him. He said to them: \"Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to a group of which I was one: 'A man from among you will certainly die in a desert of the earth, attended by a band of Muslims.' And there is none of that group except that he has died in a village and congregation other than I. And I heard him say: 'Whoever has three of his children die, he will not enter the Fire, or the Fire will not touch him.' So when I die, shroud me. I adjure Allah that a man who shrouds me should be an 'arif, a barid, or a naqib.\" He said: \"And there was none of that group except that he had done some of that, except a young man among them who said: 'I will shroud you in two garments in my bag from my mother's yarn.'\" He said: \"You, then shroud me.\" He said: \"So he died, and they washed him, shrouded him, prayed over him, and departed. And the group were all from Yemen.\""],[4062,"I performed 'umrah in Rajab, and I reached al-Rabadhah at the time of the 'Asr prayer. They called the adhan and the iqamah, then they said: \"O Abu Dharr, come forward and lead the people in prayer.\" He refused. Abu Dharr called a man, but he refused; he called the second and the third, but they refused, until the sun turned yellow or almost turned yellow. Then a man came forward and led them in prayer. When he finished, Abu Dharr turned his face towards them and spoke to them about some of their prayers. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah led us in the last 'Isha' prayer. When he finished, he stood to pray after the 'atamah (darkness of night), and some people stood behind him. When he saw them praying behind him, he returned to his camel saddle. When he saw that they had left the standing place, he returned to them and stood to pray. I came and stood behind him, and he gestured to me to his right. Ibn Mas'ud came and stood behind me and behind him, and he gestured to him to his left, so he stood. Between us, each person recited and prayed on his own. The Prophet ﷺ recited one verse: 'If You punish them, they are Your servants' to the end of the verse, until he prayed the morning prayer with it: he bowed with it, prostrated with it, stood with it, supplicated with it, and sat with it. Abu Dharr gestured to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud to ask him about what he did last night: he recited one verse, and Allah has taught you the entire Qur'an. If someone other than you did that, we would find fault with him. He said: 'I am not one to ask him about anything until he initiates it with me, so Abu Dharr asks him.' So Abu Dharr asked him, and he said: 'I supplicated for my Ummah.' He said: 'What was answered to you and what was rejected from you?' He said: 'What if they were to look upon it with a single look, many of them would abandon the prayer.' He said: 'Shall I go and give the people glad tidings of that?' So he went rebukingly, like a thrown stone. 'Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if you send this to the people, they will rely upon that and neglect worship.' He said: 'So he returned me, and I did not say anything.'\""],[4063,"\"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created a wind and put it in a house, and locked a door upon it. If the door were opened, it would flow abundantly between the heaven and the earth. And what comes to you comes only from the cracks of that door. You call it the south wind (al-janub), but with Allah it is al-azyab.\""],[4064,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to fast three days of every month, the white days: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.\""],[4065,"\"Indeed the treasure which Allah mentioned in His Book is a solid tablet of gold. I wonder at one who is certain of the divine decree, why does he toil? And I wonder at one who remembers the Fire, why does he laugh? And I wonder at one who remembers death, why is he heedless? There is no god but Allah; Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\""],[4066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"O 'Ali, whoever separates from me, Allah separates from him, and whoever separates from you, O 'Ali, separates from me.\""],[4067,"I met Abu Dharr at the middle jamrah and asked him about the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr). He said: \"No one was more eager to ask about it than I. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, was it sent down upon the prophets to whom revelation came, then it was lifted?' He said: 'Rather, it is until the Day of Resurrection.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which night is it?' He said: 'If I were permitted, I would inform you of it, but seek it in the nineties or the seventies, and do not ask me after this.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away and began to talk. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, in which of the seventies is it?' He became angry with me with an anger the like of which he had never been angry with me before or after. Then he said: 'Did I not forbid you from it? If I were permitted, I would inform you all, or inform you, of it, but'—and he mentioned a word—'that it is in the last seven.'\""],[4068,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about the Night of Decree: was it sent down upon the prophets to whom revelation came, then it was lifted?\" He said: \"Rather, it is until the Day of Resurrection.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me which night it is.\" He said: \"If I were permitted, I would inform you all, or inform you, of it, but it is in the nineties or the seventies, and do not ask me after this.\" I said: \"I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah, to inform me in which of the nineties it is.\" He became angry with me with an anger the like of which he had never been angry with me before or after. Then he said: \"Did I not forbid you from asking me about this, or about it?\" I said: \"I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah, to inform me.\" He said: \"Did I not forbid you from asking me? It is in the last seven.\""],[4069,"I was weighed against a thousand of my community and outweighed them, so they began to scatter over me from the scale pan."],[4070,"Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, and your emptying your bucket into your brother's bucket is charity, and your commanding the good and forbidding the evil are written as charity for you, and your removing a thorn or a stone from the path is charity, and your guiding a lost person on the way is charity."],[4071,"The wealthy are the poor on the Day of Resurrection, except for the one who says with his wealth, 'Thus and thus.'"],[4072,"The earth has not carried, nor the sky shaded, anyone more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr, who resembles Jesus son of Mary. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said, 'Do you acknowledge that for him?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then acknowledge it for him.'"],[4073,"O Abu Dharr, I saw as if I were weighed against forty, you being among them, and I outweighed them."],[4074,"Whoever drinks wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns, it will be the same. If he returns, it will be the same. He said: I do not know whether in the third or the fourth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he returns, it is incumbent upon Allah to make him drink from the mud of khabal.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal?' He said: 'The pus of the people of Hell.'"],[4075,"The thickness of the earth is a journey of five hundred years, and between the highest earth and the lowest heaven is five hundred years, and its thickness is five hundred years, and the thickness of the second is like that, and between each pair of earths is like that, and between the highest earth and the heaven is five hundred years, and the thickness of the heaven is five hundred years, and between the lowest heaven and the second is a journey of five hundred years and the thickness of the heaven is five hundred years. Then every heaven is like that until it reaches the seventh. Then between the seventh and the Throne is the distance of all that combined."],[4076,"The best deed is love for the sake of Allah and hatred for the sake of Allah."],[4077,"I was given five things that no one before me was given: the earth was made a purification and a mosque for me, war booty was made lawful for me and it was not lawful for any prophet before me, I was aided with awe for a month's distance over my enemy, I was sent to all red and black, and I was given intercession, which is attainable for my community—whoever dies without associating anything with Allah."],[4078,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about prayer?' He said: 'It is the completion of deeds.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about charity.' He said: 'Charity is something amazing.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have left the best deed in my soul or its good.' He said: 'What is it?' I said: 'Fasting.' He said: 'It is good, but there is nothing beyond it.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?' And he mentioned a word. I said: 'What if I cannot do it or am unable?' He said: 'With surplus food.' I said: 'What if I cannot do it?' He said: 'With half a date.' I said: 'What if I cannot do it?' He said: 'Then with a good word.' I said: 'What if I cannot do it?' He said: 'Refrain from harming people, for it is a charity you give to yourself.' I said: 'What if I cannot do it?' He said: 'Then remove harm.' I said: 'What if I cannot do it?' He said: 'You want to leave no good in you at all.'"],[4079,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends in three hours remaining from the night, and He opens the remembrance in the first hour, which no one has seen except Him. So Allah erases what He wills and confirms what He wills. Then He descends in the second hour to the Garden of Eden, which no one has seen except Him and no human heart has imagined, and none of the children of Adam will dwell with Him therein except three: the prophets, the truthful ones, and the martyrs. Then He says: 'Blessed is the one who enters you.' Then He descends in the third hour to the lowest heaven and says: 'Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him? Is there any asker who asks Me that I may give him? Is there any caller who calls upon Me that I may answer him?' until the dawn prayer. And likewise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'And the recitation of dawn, indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed.' He said: 'The angels of the night and the day witness it.'"],[4080,"Our Lord who is in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your command is in heaven and the earth. As Your mercy is in heaven, place Your mercy in the earth. Forgive us our sins and our errors. You are the Lord of the good. Send down a mercy from Your mercy upon this pain. They said it, and they were cured."],[4081,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and found a group of Arabs boasting to one another. So I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: \"What is this that I hear, O Abu al-Darda'?\" I said: \"O Messenger of God ﷺ, these Arabs are boasting to one another.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Abu al-Darda', if you boast, then boast of Quraysh. If you vie in numbers, then vie with Tamim. If you wage war, then wage war with Qays. Indeed, its faces are Kinanah, its tongue is Asad, and its horsemen are Qays. O Abu al-Darda', God has horsemen in His heaven with whom He fights His enemies, and they are the angels. And He has horsemen on His earth with whom He fights His enemies, and they are Qays. O Abu al-Darda', the last to fight for Islam, when nothing remains of it but its mention and of the Qur'an but its script, will be a man from Qays.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God ﷺ, which Qays?\" He said: \"From Sulaym.\""],[4082,"Regarding the saying of God, Blessed and Exalted, 'And beneath it was a treasure for them,' he said: It was \"gold and silver.\""],[4083,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw me while I was moving my lips, so he said: \"O Abu al-Darda', what are you saying?\" I said: \"I am remembering God.\" He said: \"Shall I teach you something better than the remembrance of God night with day and day with night?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Say: 'Glory be to God as many times as the number of what He has created, glory be to God as much as fills what He has created, glory be to God as many times as the number of everything, glory be to God as much as fills everything, glory be to God as many times as the number of what His Book has counted, glory be to God as much as fills what His Book has counted, praise be to God as many times as the number of what He has created, praise be to God as much as fills what He has created, praise be to God as much as fills everything, praise be to God as many times as the number of what His Book has counted, praise be to God as much as fills what His Book has counted.'\""],[4084,"\"When a person curses something, the curse ascends to heaven but its gates are closed before it. Then it descends to the earth, and its gates are closed before it. Then it goes right and left. When it finds no passage, it returns to the one who was cursed, if he is deserving of it; otherwise it returns to its speaker.\""],[4085,"\"The martyr will intercede for seventy members of his household,\" or \"the martyr will surely intercede for seventy members of his household.\""],[4086,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sat, we sat around him. When he wanted to leave, he left his sandals or some other thing that was on him."],[4087,"\"What God has made lawful in His Book is lawful, what He has made unlawful is unlawful, and what He has remained silent about is pardoned. So accept from God His pardon, for God would never forget anything.\" Then he recited this verse: 'And your Lord is never forgetful' (Maryam 19:64)."],[4088,"\"God says to Jesus son of Mary: 'I will raise up after you a nation who, if what they love befalls them, praise and give thanks; and if what they dislike befalls them, seek reward and are patient, though they have no forbearance and no knowledge.' He said: 'O Lord, how can this be when they have no forbearance and no knowledge?' He said: 'I will give them from My forbearance and My knowledge.'\""],[4089,"\"David used to say: 'O God, I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You, and for the deed that will bring me to Your love. O God, make Your love dearer to me than my family and cold water.'\" And when the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned David ﷺ , he said: \"He was the most devout of human beings.\""],[4090,"\"The servants have not asked for anything better than that He forgive them and grant them well-being.\""],[4091,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every fanged beast of prey, animals killed by being held and shot at (mujaththamah), and plunder. And I think he said: \"the domestic donkey.\""],[4092,"\"I am your share of the prophets, and you are my share of the nations.\""],[4093,"The example of one who gives charity at the time of his death is like the example of one who gives a gift after he is full."],[4094,"I was with Abu al-Darda when a man from the people of al-Madinah entered and asked him, saying: \"Where did you leave Abu Dharr?\" Abu al-Darda said: \"Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. If Abu Dharr had cut off a limb from me, I would not have provoked him because of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about him.\""],[4095,"Mutarrif narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Umm al-Darda', from Abu al-Darda'."],[4096,"Shu'bah, from al-Qasim b. Abi Bazzah, from 'Ata' al-Kaykharani, from Umm al-Darda', from Abu al-Darda', from the Prophet."],[4097,"Mutarrif narrated to us - meaning - from 'Ata' al-Kaykharani, from 'Ata' b. Nafi', from Umm al-Darda', from Abu al-Darda', from the Prophet."],[4098,"\"Nothing will be placed on the Scale on the Day of Resurrection heavier than good character.\" Ibn 'Uyaynah added in his hadith: \"And indeed good character will cause its possessor to attain the rank of fasting and prayer.\""],[4099,"\"Indeed, provision seeks the servant just as his appointed time seeks him.\""],[4100,"I heard him swear by Allah, and I had never heard him swear about anything before that. He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, Allah has chosen for you the best of speech, four phrases: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great.'\""],[4101,"He was asked about the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'Every day He is engaged in some affair.' He said: \"It is from His affair that He forgives a sin, relieves a distress, raises a people, and lowers others.\""],[4102,"\"Inform, and you will be hated.\""],[4103,"The rain withheld during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we asked the Prophet of Allah to pray for rain for us. He prayed for rain, and in the morning the Prophet of Allah ﷺ went out and found some people talking. They said: \"We were given rain last night by the rising of such-and-such a star.\" The Prophet of Allah said: \"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a people except that they wake up denying it.\""],[4104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Allah took Dawud from among his companions, and they were not put to trial nor did they turn back. And the companions of the Messiah remained on his guidance and his Sunnah for two hundred years.\""],[4105,"\"Give your food in charity and blessing will be placed in it for you.\""],[4106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with his head dripping, and he prayed with us in a single garment, wrapping himself in it, having crossed its two ends. When he finished, ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said to him, \"You pray in a single garment while there is [the impurity] in it?\" He said, \"Yes, I pray in it and [it still contains] that.\""],[4107,"\"One who is disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor one addicted to wine, nor one who denies divine decree.\""],[4108,"\"A servant will not attain the reality of faith until he knows that what has befallen him was not going to miss him, and what has missed him was not going to befall him.\""],[4109,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you think that what we do is something already decreed, or something we initiate?\" He said, \"Every person is facilitated for what he was created for.\""],[4110,"\"Shall I not direct you to something better than much prayer and charity?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Reconciling between people.\""],[4111,"\"Whoever gratifies a desire of his brother, forgiveness is granted to him.\""],[4112,"\"While I was sleeping, I saw the pillar of the Book being taken from beneath my head, and I thought it had been taken away, so I followed it with my gaze, and it was taken to Syria. Verily, faith, when tribulations occur, will be in Syria.\""],[4113,"\"Let me not find any of you disputing with me at the Basin, being told, 'You do not know what he introduced after you.'\" Abu al-Dardāʾ said, \"Supplicate to Allah that He not make me one of them.\" He said, \"You are not one of them\" — and this is not in anyone else's hadith."],[4114,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dung heap of a people in which there was a dead lamb. He said, \"Do its owners have any need of it?\" They said, \"O Prophet of Allah, if its owners had any need of it, they would not have discarded it.\" He said, \"By Allah, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this lamb is to its owners, so let me not find it having destroyed any of you.\""],[4115,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey in intense heat, and there was no one among the people fasting except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ʿAbdullāh b. Rawāḥah."],[4116,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and one of us would place his hand on his head due to the intense heat, and none of us was fasting except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ʿAbdullāh b. Rawāḥah."],[4117,"For everything there is a sense of pride, and the pride of prayer is the first takbir, so guard it carefully."],[4118,"The slaughtering of the fetus is the slaughtering of its mother."],[4119,"Indeed, before you lies a steep and difficult pass; none will be saved from it except one who travels light."],[4120,"Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Qur'an."],[4121,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'Is there recitation in every prayer?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[4122,"I was with Umm al-Darda' and I caught a flea and threw it into the fire. She said: I heard Abu al-Darda' say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'No one punishes with fire except the Lord of the fire.'"],[4123,"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery and steals, even if Abu al-Darda''s nose is rubbed in the dust."],[4124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ vomited and broke his fast. He said: Then I met Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said to him: Indeed Abu al-Darda'..."],[4125,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would go out to the high places seeking to be saved, yet you would not be saved. One of the two said: 'And I do not know whether you would be saved or not.'"],[4126,"Your love for a thing blinds and deafens."],[4127,"Satan has despaired of being worshipped in the Arabian Peninsula, but he is content with you through insignificant sins."],[4128,"The tent of the Muslims on the day of the great battle will be in the Ghuta, near a city called Damascus."],[4129,"\"The green canopy has not shaded, nor the dusty earth carried, anyone with a tongue more truthful than Abu Dharr.\""],[4130,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr ؓ came along, holding the edge of his garment and having exposed his knee. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: \"As for your companion—I think he said:—he has become distressed.\" He came forward until he greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, something happened between me and 'Umar, and I spoke harshly to him. Then I regretted what had happened, so I asked him to forgive me, but he refused. I followed him to al-Baqi' until he took refuge in his house from me, and then I came to you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah forgive you, Abu Bakr,\" three times. Then 'Umar regretted it when Abu Bakr asked him to forgive him and he refused. He left his house and came to the house of Abu Bakr and asked: \"Is Abu Bakr there?\" They said: \"We do not know; he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So 'Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to show displeasure, until Abu Bakr feared that something he disliked would come from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ toward 'Umar. When Abu Bakr saw that, he knelt down and said: \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I was the one who was more wrong.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people, Allah sent me to you, and you said: 'You have lied,' while Abu Bakr said: 'You have spoken the truth,' and he supported me with his own self and his wealth. So will you leave my companion to me?\" three times."],[4131,"\"The first thing my Lord forbade me after the worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men.\""],[4132,"\"Whoever takes land from the land of the jizya and puts it around his neck has turned his back on Islam.\""],[4133,"I will be the first one permitted to raise his head on the Day of Resurrection. I will raise my head and I will recognize my community to my right and to my left. It was said: How will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"They will have white marks on their foreheads and limbs from ablution, and their children will have light before them.\""],[4134,"\"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you as charity one-third of your wealth at your death.\""],[4135,"\"It is not fitting for a habitual curser to be prominent before Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[4136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to pray, and we heard him say: \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" Then he said: \"I curse you with the curse of Allah,\" three times. Then he reached out with his hand as if he was grabbing something. When he finished the prayer, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we heard you say something in prayer that we have not heard you say before, and we saw you extend your hand. He said: \"The enemy of Allah, Iblis, came with a flame of fire to put it in my face. I said: I seek refuge in Allah from you, and he did not retreat. Then I said to him, and he did not retreat. Then I said to him: May Allah curse you with the complete curse of Allah, and he did not retreat. Then I said it again, and he did not retreat. Then I said it again, and he did not retreat. Then I intended to grab him, and were it not for the supplication of our brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up and the children of Madinah would have played with him.\""],[4137,"My close friend advised me to do three things: to fast three days of every month, not to sleep except after praying Witr, and to pray the Duha prayer whether traveling or at home."],[4138,"Every day He is in a matter. He said: Among His matters is that He forgives a sin, or relieves a distress, or answers a supplicant, and raises a people and lowers others.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has finished with every servant regarding his lifespan, provision, resting place, and his traces.\""],[4139,"He passed by a woman who was far along in pregnancy at a tent belonging to a man, and he said: \"Perhaps he intends to have illicit relations with her.\" They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was about to curse him with a curse that would enter his grave with him. How can he make him an heir while he is not lawful for him? How can he use him as a servant while he is not lawful for him?\""],[4140,"\"You are only provided sustenance and granted victory because of your weak ones. Seek out your weak ones for me.\""],[4141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have flour sifted for him, and he had only one shirt."],[4142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were mentioning poverty and fearing it. He said: \"Do you fear poverty? By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world will be poured upon you until it cannot be lifted. And by Allah, I will leave you upon the like of the white plain; its night and day are equal.\" Abu al-Darda said: \"Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. By Allah, he left us upon the like of the white plain; its night and day are equal.\""],[4143,"The superiority of prayer in the Sacred Mosque over others is one hundred thousand prayers, in my mosque a thousand prayers, and in the mosque of Jerusalem five hundred prayers."],[4144,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam, He struck his right shoulder and brought forth white offspring like ants, and struck his left shoulder and brought forth black offspring like charcoal. Then He said to those on His right: 'To Paradise, and I do not care,' and to those on His left: 'To the Fire, and I do not care.'"],[4145,"You will be enlisted into armies: an army in Syria, Egypt, Iraq, and Yemen. They said: 'Choose for us, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'You must go to Syria.' They said: 'We are owners of livestock and cannot endure Syria.' He said: 'Whoever cannot endure Syria, let him join his Yemen, for Allah has guaranteed Syria for me.'"],[4146,"The scholars are the heirs of the prophets. The prophets did not leave behind dinars or dirhams; they only left behind knowledge."],[4147,"The acts of cleanliness are four: trimming the mustache, shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails, and using the tooth-stick."],[4148,"Rashid b. Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet."],[4149,"Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined me: not to associate anything with Allah even if I were burned; not to leave an obligatory prayer intentionally, for whoever leaves it intentionally has disbelieved; and not to drink wine, for it is the key to every evil."],[4150,"Ubadah and Abu al-Darda sat with al-Harith b. Mu'awiyah. Abu al-Darda said: 'Which of you remembers when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us facing a camel from the spoils? When he finished, he took a hair from the camel and said: \"Nothing of what Allah has granted you as spoils is lawful for me, not even the like of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you.\"'"],[4151,"Allah loves every sorrowful heart."],[4152,"A guest stayed with Abu al-Darda, and he said: 'Are you staying so we may pasture the animals, or departing so we may feed them?' Then Abu al-Darda said: 'Some poor people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken the worldly benefits and the Hereafter; they pray as we pray, fast as we fast, strive and give charity while we cannot give charity.\" He said: \"O Abu al-Darda, shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, you will catch up with those who preceded you, and no one will catch up with you except one who says the like of what you say? Glorify Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.\"'"],[4153,"Keep the mosques as your gathering place, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has guaranteed for one whose home is the mosques security and safe passage over the bridge on the Day of Resurrection."],[4154,"Whoever goes to his bed intending to get up and pray during the night, but his eyes overcome him until morning, what he intended is written for him, and his sleep is charity."],[4155,"Whoever leaves behind a treasure, it will be represented on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake with two fangs that follows him, saying: 'Woe to you, what are you?' He will say: 'I am your treasure that you hoarded.' It will not cease until it swallows his hand, then it follows the rest of his body, or in the rest of his body."],[4156,"Whoever asks for something while he is well off, it will be a blemish on his face on the Day of Resurrection."],[4157,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[4158,"Abd al-Rahman b. Thabit b. Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet ﷺ. Yahya b. Abi Kathir narrated this hadith from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban, as Yahya b. Abi Kathir said. The huffaz narrated it from Yahya. Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated it from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani from Shaddad b. Aws, and Khalid is a hafiz. Ayyub narrated it from Abu Qilabah from someone who narrated to him from Shaddad. Asim al-Ahwal and Abu Ghifar narrated it from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath from Abu Asma from Shaddad. The hadith of Khalid, in my view, is the best of them. We do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Abd al-Rahman b. Thabit from his father from Makhul from Abu Asma except Zufar b. Hubayrah."],[4159,"Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr b. Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman b. Ghanm, from Thawban, from the Prophet ﷺ with the like of it. These chains from Thawban regarding 'The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast' are good chains. As for Qatadah from Shahr, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Sa'id b. Abi Arubah. As for Qatadah from Salim, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Bukayr b. Abi al-Samit, who is a shaykh from Basra and is acceptable. However, this hadith is not preserved from Qatadah from Salim. I think Bukayr erred in it when he said 'from Salim.' Al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated it from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Thawban and made a mistake in it, because the reliable narrators narrate it from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah, and al-Layth erred in it. Ayyub b. Abi Sukayn al-Wasiti narrated it from Qatadah from Shahr b. Hawshab from Bilal and erred in it. He is also called Ibn Miskin, and Ayyub's kunyah is Abu al-Ala. In my view, the hadith is more likely the hadith of Ibn Abi Arubah because he is more retentive than others."],[4160,"Whoever's soul departs his body while he is free of three things: arrogance, debt, and misappropriation, Paradise is guaranteed for him, or he said: for him is Paradise."],[4161,"Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats, the smaller of which is like Uhud."],[4162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the briber, the bribed, and the one who mediates between them."],[4163,"Indeed, the women who seek khul' are the hypocrites."],[4164,"Lying is written down, except that by which a Muslim is benefited or harm is averted from him."],[4165,"\"Three will fight over this treasure of yours, all of them sons of a caliph. Then none of them will attain it. Then the black banners will advance from the east, and they will kill you in a manner no people have been killed before.\" Then he mentioned something, and said: \"When you see him, pledge allegiance to him even if crawling on snow, for he is the caliph of Allah, the Mahdi.\""],[4166,"\"Emigration will not cease as long as the disbelievers are fought.\""],[4167,"\"Whoever commits an offense, or shelters an offender, or claims descent from other than his father, or ascribes himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor voluntary acts will be accepted from him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"How will you be among a people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted and who have become worthless?\" He interlaced his fingers. They said: \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Be patient. Treat people according to their character, but oppose them in their deeds.\""],[4168,"He used to like to pray after midday until the sun rose high. 'A'ishah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that you prefer to pray at this hour.\" He said: \"In it the gates of heaven are opened, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, looks upon His creation with mercy. It is a prayer that Adam, Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus used to maintain.\""],[4169,"\"My cistern extends from 'Adan to 'Amman of al-Balqa'. Its water is sweeter than honey, more fragrant than musk, and whiter than milk. Its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst again.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who will be the first of people to come to you at it?\" He said: \"The emigrants with disheveled hair and dusty clothes, who do not marry pampered women, and for whom closed doors will not be opened.\""],[4170,"I was standing near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a rabbi from the Jewish scholars came and said: \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.\" I pushed him with a shove that almost knocked him down. He said: \"Why did you push me?\" I said: \"Why don't you say, 'O Messenger of Allah'?\" The Jew said: \"We call him by the name his family gave him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My name is Muhammad, the name my family gave me.\" The Jew said: \"I have come to ask you about something.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"It will benefit you if I tell you.\" He said: \"I am listening with my ears.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ poked the ground with a stick he had and said: \"Ask.\" The Jew said: \"Where will people be when the earth and the heavens are changed for other than them?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They will be in the darkness before the bridge over Hell.\" He said: \"Who will be the first of people to cross?\" He said: \"The poor among the emigrants.\" The Jew said: \"What will be their welcoming gift?\" He said: \"A fish of Paradise will be slaughtered for them, the one that eats from its edges.\" He said: \"What will they drink after it?\" He said: \"From a spring in it called Salsabil.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\""],[4171,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ emphasized the gravity of the matter of asking. He said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the people of the pre-Islamic ignorance will come carrying their idols on their backs. Their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will ask them, and they will say: 'Our Lord, You did not send us a messenger, and no command from You came to us. Had You sent us a messenger, we would have been the most obedient of Your servants.' Their Lord will say to them: 'If I command you something, will you obey Me?' They will say: 'Yes.' So He will command them to head toward Hell and enter it. They will set off until, when they draw near to it, they perceive its raging and roaring, so they return to their Lord and say: 'Our Lord, bring us out of it or save us from it.' He will say to them: 'Did you not claim that if I command you something, you would obey Me?' Then He will take their covenant on that and say: 'Head toward it and enter it.' They will set off until, when they see it, they become terrified and return, saying: 'Our Lord, we are terrified of it and cannot enter it.' He will say: 'Enter it in a state of humiliation.'\" Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Had they entered it the first time, it would have been coolness and peace for them.\""],[4172,"Aban b. Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma', from Thawban, similarly. And this hadith from Thawban we do not preserve except through this chain we mentioned. We do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma', from Thawban except 'Abbad b. Mansur, nor from 'Abbad except Rayhan b. Sa'id. We do not know of anyone who narrated the hadith of Aban except Ishaq b. Idris, and it is unusual from Ayyub and from Yahya b. Abi Kathir. The text of this hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is not well-known except from this route."],[4173,"\"Every Muslim must use the toothstick, perform the Friday ghusl, and touch some of his family's perfume if he has it.\""],[4174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us after the dawn prayer and said: \"My Lord came to me last night in the most beautiful form and said: 'O Muhammad, do you know what the highest assembly disputes about?'\" He said: \"I said: 'No.' He said: 'Then he mentioned something.' He said: \"Then I was shown what is between heaven and earth.\" He said: \"I said: 'Yes, O Lord. They dispute about expiations and ranks. As for the ranks: feeding others, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep. As for expiations: walking on foot to the congregational prayers, perfecting ablution in disliked circumstances, and sitting in the mosques after the prayers.' Then He said: 'O Muhammad, ask and you will be heard; request and you will be granted.'\" He said: \"I said: 'Then teach me.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, I ask You for doing good deeds, abandoning evil deeds, loving the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. If You intend a trial for a people, then take me to You without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and the love that will bring me to Your love.'\""],[4175,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the head covering."],[4176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while on a journey of his: \"We will travel tonight, if Allah wills, so let no weak person set out with us.\" Then a man came on a small she-camel of his and fell, fracturing his thigh, and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered prayer over him, then proclaimed: \"Paradise is not permitted for a disobedient person.\""],[4177,"And everything they are promised will occur within a hundred years."],[4178,"I was standing beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a rabbi from among the Jewish rabbis came and said: \"I ask you about something that no one on earth knows except a prophet.\" He ﷺ said: \"It will benefit you if I tell you?\" He said: \"I will listen with my two ears.\" He said: \"I have come to ask you about the child.\" He ﷺ said: \"As for the fluid of the man and the fluid of the woman, when they meet, if the man's semen prevails over the woman's semen, the child is male by Allah's permission; and if the woman's semen prevails over the man's semen, the child is female by Allah's permission.\" The Jew said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He asked me about this while I had no knowledge of any of it until ...\""],[4179,"When he ﷺ finished his prayer, he would seek Allah's forgiveness three times, then say: \"O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.\""],[4180,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted the entire year."],[4181,"Yahya b. al-Harith al-Dhimari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma' al-Rahabi, from Thawban, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar narration. This hadith has been reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through several routes; narrated by Abu Hurayrah, Jabir, Abu Ayyub, and others. We mentioned the hadith of Thawban in this place unless someone else adds some wording, in which case it would be recorded for the sake of the addition."],[4182,"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to look into a house until he seeks permission; if he does so, he has entered. And he should not lead a people in prayer and then single himself out for a supplication to the exclusion of them; if he does so, he has betrayed them. And he should not pray while restraining the urge to urinate or defecate until he relieves himself."],[4183,"Three things are suspended from the Throne: the womb says: 'O Allah, I am through You, so let me not be severed'; the trust says: 'O Allah, I am through You, so let me not be betrayed'; and the blessing says: 'O Allah, I am through You, so let me not be denied.'"],[4184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fasting outside of Ramadan when he experienced — I think — vomiting, so he performed ablution and then broke his fast. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, were you not fasting?' He said: 'Yes, but I vomited, so I broke my fast.' The next day I heard him say: 'This day is in place of my breaking the fast yesterday.'"],[4185,"He ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, I ask You for good things, abandonment of evil deeds, love of the poor, and that You accept my repentance; and if You intend a trial for Your servants, then take me to You without being tried.'"],[4186,"The visitor of a sick person is in the garden of Paradise until he returns."],[4187,"Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma', from Thawban, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar narration. This hadith from Thawban — we know of no one narrating this wording from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except Thawban, and its chain is good. We know of no one narrating the hadith of Qatadah except Sa'id b. Bashir, and the scholars have narrated from Sa'id b. Bashir and accepted his hadith, although among his hadiths are some in which no one else corroborated him."],[4188,"Wonderful, wonderful for five things, how heavy they are in the scale: La ilaha illa Allah, Subhan Allah, Alhamdulillah, Allahu Akbar, and a righteous child who dies for a Muslim man and he seeks reward for it."],[4189,"A man from the people of Paradise does not pluck any of its fruit except that the like of it is returned to its place."],[4190,"Aban narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma', from Thawban ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know this hadith from Thawban to be narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through a connected chain from him better than this isnad, and we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Ayyub except Abbad b. Mansur, and no one narrated it from Abbad except Rayhan, and we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Yahya b. Abi Kathir except Ishaq b. Idris from Aban."],[4191,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked; he said: \"The molar of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and the thickness of his skin is forty cubits by the cubit of the Compeller.\""],[4192,"\"My cistern, I drive people away from it for my family. Indeed I strike them with this staff of mine until it splinters.\" The Prophet ﷺ was asked, and he said: \"Its width is from my station to Amman; it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Two spouts pour into it, supplying it from Paradise: one of them is of silver and the other of gold.\""],[4193,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was escorting a funeral, a man came to him with a mount for him to ride, but he refused. When the funeral was lowered, another man came to him with a mount, and he rode it. Then the first man met him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I offered you my mount to ride but you refused, and so-and-so offered you his mount and you rode it.\" He said: \"You offered me your mount while the angels were escorting the funeral, and I was not going to ride while the angels were walking. If you had offered it after it was buried, I would have ridden it.\""],[4194,"Amir b. Yasaf narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. He did not trace it back."],[4195,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he said: \"This journey is toil and burden, so when one of you prays witr, let him pray two rak'ahs. If he wakes up [for tahajjud, he may pray more]; otherwise, they will be [written] for him.\""],[4196,"\"The martyrs and those who die on their beds will dispute before our Lord about those who die in the plague. The martyrs will say: 'Our brothers!' And those who die on their beds will say: 'Our brothers! They died on their beds as we died.' Then Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: 'Look at their wounds. If their wounds resemble the wounds of those killed, then they are with them and of them.' And their wounds will have resembled their wounds.\""],[4197,"He used to ask forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second row once."],[4198,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that female captives be had intercourse with until they give birth to what is in their wombs."],[4199,"On the day of Khaybar he forbade every possessor of fangs among wild beasts, every possessor of talons among birds, the meat of domestic donkeys, and the mutilated animal and the snatched [prey]."],[4200,"He would take a hair from the war spoils and say: \"I have no more right to anything like this than any one of you, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return even the thread and the needle and whatever is above them. Beware of unlawfully withholding war spoils, for it is disgrace, fire, and shame upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4201,"When I take from My servant his two precious things (his eyes) and he is loath to part with them, I will not be satisfied with any reward for them less than Paradise."],[4202,"I am, with Allah, the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still lying in his clay. I shall inform you of the interpretation of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of 'Isa, and the dream of my mother, who saw a light emanating from her that illuminated the palaces of Syria. Likewise did the mothers of the believers see."],[4203,"I sold a young camel to the Prophet ﷺ, then I came to him to collect its price. I said: 'Give me the price of my young camel.' He said: 'I will not pay you except with a small silver ingot.' He then paid me, and he gave me an excellent payment."],[4204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one morning and delivered an admonition that made hearts tremble and eyes shed tears. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant.' He said: 'I enjoin you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a black slave is appointed over you. You will see after me great discord. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, rightly-directed caliphs after me. Bite onto it with your molar teeth. Beware of newly-invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.'"],[4205,"O Allah, teach Mu'awiyah the Book and arithmetic, and protect him from the punishment. He said: And I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was eating the pre-dawn meal, and he said: 'Come to the blessed meal.'"],[4206,"When you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the highest part of Paradise."],[4207,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. 'Ali resembled him."],[4208,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. 'Ali resembled him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed among us twelve camels, and my father received a camel, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away before giving it to us. So we went to Abu Bakr, and he gave it to us."],[4209,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he distributed camels among us."],[4210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the midday heat and prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and 'Asr as two rak'ahs, with a short spear planted in front of him."],[4211,"Some people from Qays, wearing cloaks with torn edges and carrying swords, came unexpectedly to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Their appearance displeased him, so he prayed, then entered his house, then came out, prayed, and sat in his gathering. He commanded or urged charity, saying: 'Let a man give charity from his dinar, let a man give charity from his dirham, let a man give charity from a sa' of his wheat, let a man give charity from a sa' of his dates.' A man from the Ansar came with a purse of gold and placed it in his hand. Then the people followed suit until I saw two heaps of clothes and food. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shining as if it were gilded. Then he said: 'Whoever initiates a good practice that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the like of their rewards, without diminishing their rewards in the least. And whoever initiates an evil practice that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the like of their burdens, without diminishing their burdens in the least.'"],[4212,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray 'Asr as two rak'ahs at al-Abtah."],[4213,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw that the hair between his lower lip and chin was white. He was asked, 'What were you like at that time?' He said, 'I used to trim arrows and attach feathers to them.'"],[4214,"Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from 'Ali b. al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet."],[4215,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from 'Ali b. al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet."],[4216,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah b. Masqalah, from 'Ali b. al-Arqam, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet."],[4217,"As for me, I do not eat reclining."],[4218,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man praying with his garment hanging down, so he cut it off for him."],[4219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at al-Batha' in Makkah the traveler's prayer, two rak'ahs."],[4220,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Abtah in a red leather tent. Bilal came out to us with the leftover water of his ablution, so we rushed to him and took from his ablution water, or from the leftover of his ablution water. Then Bilal made the call to prayer, and he began turning his mouth here and there, right and left."],[4221,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah, and I prayed with him the noon and afternoon prayers, two rak'ahs each. Bilal made the call to prayer and placed his fingers in his ears, and he would turn around during his call."],[4222,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed with them at al-Batha' with a short spear in front of him: the noon prayer two rak'ahs and the afternoon prayer two rak'ahs, while women and donkeys passed in front of him."],[4223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Abtah when Bilal came to him and informed him of the prayer. He called for ablution water and performed ablution. The people began coming and taking the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wiping their faces with it."],[4224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Abtah when Bilal came to him and informed him of the prayer. He called for ablution water and performed ablution. The people began taking the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wiping themselves with it. He said: Then Bilal took the short spear and walked with it with him, and he made the call to commence the prayer. He planted it in front of him, while the riding camels passed in front of him: the woman, the donkey, and the camel."],[4225,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ in a red leather tent. He said: And I saw Bilal bring out his ablution water, and I saw the people rushing to get his ablution water. Whoever got some of it wiped his face with it, and whoever did not get any took from the palm of his companion. Then he brought out a short spear and planted it, then he prayed with them, while animals and people passed in front of him."],[4226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda'. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda' and saw Umm al-Darda' in a shabby state. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"Your brother has no need for anything from women.\" When Abu al-Darda' came, he welcomed Salman and brought food close to him. Salman said to him, 'Eat.' He said, 'I am fasting.' Salman said, 'I adjure you to eat, for I will not eat until you eat.' So he ate with him. Then he said to him, 'O Abu al-Darda', your body has a right over you, and your family has a right over you. Give every rightful person his due. Fast and break your fast, stand in prayer and sleep, and come to your family, and give every rightful person his due.' Then Salman stayed overnight with him until part of the night had passed, Abu al-Darda' got up, but Salman held him back. When it was near dawn, he said, 'Get up now.' So they both got up and prayed, then they went out to the prayer. When the Prophet ﷺ had prayed, Abu al-Darda' went to him and told him what Salman had said to him. He said: He told him the same as what Salman had told him."],[4227,"\"This matter will remain established until twelve – I think he said – 'from Quraysh' rule.\""],[4228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys when he heard a muezzin saying, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He has cast off rivals.' Then the muezzin said, 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'He has come out of the Fire.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You will find him to be a herder of goats kept far from dwellings, or a keeper of dogs.'"],[4229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, and they slept through until the sun had risen. He said: 'You were dead, and Allah returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes up, and whoever forgets, let him pray when he remembers.'"],[4230,"\"Indeed the world will be opened up to you until you decorate your houses as the Kaaba is decorated.\" We said, \"While we are upon our religion today?\" He said, \"And you are upon your religion today.\" We said, \"Will we be better then or today?\" He said, \"Rather, you are better today.\""],[4231,"He forbade the price of blood, the earnings of a prostitute, and the price of a dog."],[4232,"He bought a slave who was a cupper, and he ordered his cupping instruments to be broken. I said to him, 'Will you break them?' He said, 'Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a prostitute. And he cursed the one who consumes interest and the one who pays it, the woman who tattoos and the one who asks for tattooing, and he cursed the image-maker.'"],[4233,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, and Umar was in front of him in the gathering. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The affair of my nation will remain established until twelve caliphs pass, all of them from Quraysh.' He said: He lowered his voice. My father poked between the shoulders of my uncle and said, 'O uncle, what did he say?' He said, 'All of them from Quraysh.'"],[4234,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Madinah to Makkah, and he continued praying two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until he returned to his house."],[4235,"\"Whoever fills a gap in the row, he will be forgiven.\""],[4236,"\"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me.\""],[4237,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when 'judud' (good fortunes) were mentioned. It was said: 'The fortune of Banu so-and-so is in camels, and the fortune of Banu so-and-so—or the fortune of so-and-so—is in sheep.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until he prayed and raised his head from bowing, then he said: 'O Allah, there is no withholder for what You give, and no giver for what You withhold, and no fortune of a fortunate person avails him against You.'"],[4238,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about his neighbor. He said: 'He harms me.' He said: 'Place your belongings on the road, or on the side of the road.' So he placed them, and every passerby would say: 'What is the matter with you?' He would say: 'My neighbor harms me,' and they would curse him. Then the man came and said: 'Take back your belongings, for I will never harm you again,' or something like that."],[4239,"I ate tharid (a dish of bread and meat), then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and belched in his presence. He said: 'O Abu Juḥayfah, the people with the longest hunger on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were most satiated in this world.'"],[4240,"I belched in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ."],[4241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a collector among us with his command to take charity from our rich and distribute it among our poor."],[4242,"The Banu 'Amir came to the Prophet ﷺ, and when he saw them, he said: 'Welcome.'"],[4243,"I saw Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, making the call to prayer, and he placed his fingers in his ears."],[4244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named Madinah 'Tabah.'"],[4245,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak b. Harb, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4246,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over Abu al-Dahdah, then a horse was brought to him, and he mounted it. It began to prance with him, and he said a quiet word. A man among the people, while we were walking behind him, said: 'The Prophet ﷺ said: \"How many hanging clusters of dates are there for Abu al-Dahdah in Paradise!\"'"],[4247,"The Prophet ﷺ had a wide mouth, reddish-brown eyes, and lean heels."],[4248,"I saw the seal of prophethood on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, like a pigeon's egg."],[4249,"The religion will not cease to be established, with a band of Muslims upholding it, until the Hour begins."],[4250,"There will be twelve commanders.\" He said a word I did not hear. I said to my father, \"What did he say?\" He said, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[4251,"Abu 'Awanah reported to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ , similarly."],[4252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the sermon standing on the pulpit, except that he would sit for a short while, then stand."],[4253,"A hairy, short man with strong muscles was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ – or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought such a man – and he admitted that he had committed adultery. He sent him back twice, then ordered that he be stoned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whenever we set out as raiders in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind, bleating like a billy goat, and one of them gives a small amount of milk. If any one of them is brought to me, I will make him an example.\""],[4254,"A man asked him: How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ act when he prayed the dawn prayer? He said: He would remain in his place until the sun rose."],[4255,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars."],[4256,"The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."],[4257,"People from my ummah will certainly open the treasures of the white Kisra."],[4258,"I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me when I was sent."],[4259,"Ibrahim b. Tahman reported to us, from Simak, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Simak except Ibrahim and Sulayman b. Mu'adh."],[4260,"I prayed the first prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then he went out to his family. The children of Madinah met him, and he began to wipe the cheek of each one of them. As for me, he wiped my cheek, and I found a coolness and fragrance as if it had come from an attar's box."],[4261,"My father narrated to me, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except 'Uthman b. Jabalah, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it other than Shu'bah except Asbat b. Nasr."],[4262,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."],[4263,"He used to recite in the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and 'Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?'"],[4264,"He would pray Zuhr when the sun had passed its zenith."],[4265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until most of his prayers were performed sitting."],[4266,"The Prophet ﷺ did not have the adhan called for him on the two 'Eids."],[4267,"Bilal would not miss the time, and sometimes he would delay the iqamah a little."],[4268,"Regarding the Night of Decree: 'It is a night of wind and rain.'"],[4269,"'Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan; for I saw it and then was made to forget it. It is a night of rain or wind,' or he said, 'rain and wind.'"],[4270,"'Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan.'"],[4271,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would mention poetry in his presence and recite it to one another, and sometimes the Prophet would smile."],[4272,"Some people's mule died, and they had nothing to eat, so they came to the Prophet ﷺ and he gave them permission to eat it."],[4273,"Indeed, Satan exposed himself to me, and began casting sparks of fire upon me; had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, I would have seized him."],[4274,"Bilal would give the adhan, then wait; and when he saw the Prophet ﷺ, he would begin the iqamah."],[4275,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaning on a cushion on his left side."],[4276,"On the day of Fitr, the Prophet ﷺ would eat seven dates before going out; and on the day of sacrifice, he would not eat anything until he returned."],[4277,"For one of you to discipline his child is better for him than to give half a sa' in charity every day."],[4278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three white garments: a waist wrapper and a winding sheet."],[4279,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who will carry your banner on the Day of Resurrection?' He said, 'The one who carries it in this world: Ali b. Abi Talib.'"],[4280,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the minbar and said, 'Amin, amin, amin.' When he descended, he was asked about that, and he said, 'Jibril came to me and said, \"May his nose be rubbed in dust, the one who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven. Say: Amin.\" I said, \"Amin.\" \"And may his nose be rubbed in dust, a man before whom you are mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon you. Say: Amin.\" I said, \"Amin.\" \"And may his nose be rubbed in dust, a man who reaches his parents or one of them and is not forgiven, or they do not admit him into Paradise. Amin.\" I said, \"Amin.\"'"],[4281,"A man killed himself with broad arrowheads, and the Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him."],[4282,"'After me there will be twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh.' Then he returned to his house. I said, 'Then what will happen?' He said, 'Then there will be turmoil.'"],[4283,"Al-Muhajir b. Mismar narrated to us, from Amir b. Sa'd, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet."],[4284,"Ibn Awn narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-Aswad b. Sa'id, except that I do not remember in their hadith \"then there will be turmoil.\" We do not know of Amir b. Sa'd narrating from Jabir b. Samurah except this hadith, nor of al-Sha'bi narrating from Jabir b. Samurah except this hadith. It was also narrated by Ziyad b. 'Alaqah from Jabir b. Samurah."],[4285,"\"Whoever eats from this offensive vegetable—meaning garlic—let him sit in his house.\""],[4286,"Māʿiz came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God ﷺ, I have committed adultery.\" He turned his face away from him. Then he came to him from the direction of his face and he turned away from him. Then he came to him the third time and he turned away from him. Then he came to him the fourth time. When he said that to him, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to his companions: \"Get up to your companion, and if he is sound then stone him.\" He was asked about him and they found him sound, so he was stoned. When the stones struck him, he tried to flee, and a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ met him with the jawbones of a camel and struck him with them and killed him. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"To the Fire!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Not at all, for he has repented with a repentance that if a nation among the nations were to repent with it, it would be accepted from them.\""],[4287,"\"My community will continue to be upon the truth, victorious, and the affair of my community will remain righteous, not harmed by the enmity of those who oppose them, until twelve caliphs rule over them.\" Samurah, the father of Jābir, said: \"All of them are from Quraysh.\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[4288,"\"A woman traveler will soon set out from Madinah to al-Ḥīrah fearing no one.\""],[4289,"\"When Kisrā perishes, there will be no Kisrā after him, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the cause of God.\""],[4290,"The first to shoot an arrow with the Prophet ﷺ—and shed blood with it—was Saʿd."],[4291,"\"Three things I fear for my community: seeking rain by the stars, the injustice of rulers, and denying the divine decree.\""],[4292,"\"Will you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" He said: \"They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row.\""],[4293,"Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from al-Musayyib b. Rāfiʿ, from Tamīm b. Ṭarafah, from Jābir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know of anyone who narrates this statement from the Prophet ﷺ except Jābir b. Samurah, and we do not know of any route from Jābir except this route."],[4294,"That he entered the mosque and saw them raising their hands in prayer, and he said: \"What is the matter with them, raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer!\""],[4295,"Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from al-Musayyib b. Rāfiʿ, from Tamīm b. Ṭarafah, from Jābir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except through the narration of Jābir b. Samurah from him, and its meaning according to us is: that the people used to gesture with their hands in prayer to the right and left, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Be still in prayer!\""],[4296,"The Prophet ﷺ used to herd sheep, then he herded camels with a partner of his whom Khadījah's sister had hired the two of them. When they finished the journey, something remained owed to them. His partner kept coming to them to demand payment, and he would say to Muhammad: \"Come along,\" but he would say: \"You go, for I am shy.\" One time she—meaning the partner—came to them and said: \"Where is Muhammad? Why doesn't he come with you?\" He said: \"I told him, and he mentioned that he is shy.\" So she mentioned that to her sister Khadījah, who said: \"I have never seen anyone more shy or more chaste than Muhammad ﷺ.\" So something fell into the heart of her sister Khadījah, and she sent to him, saying: \"Come to my father and propose to him.\" He said: \"Your father is a man of great wealth, and he\"—I think he said—\"will not do it.\" She said: \"Then go, say a word, for I will suffice you, and come to him when he is drunk.\" So he did, and he came to him and he married him to her. When morning came, he sat among the people and it was said to him: \"You have done well; you married Muhammad.\" He said: \"Did I do that!?\" They said: \"Yes.\" So he got up and went in to her and said: \"The people say that I married Muhammad, but I did not.\" She said: \"Indeed you did, so do not act foolishly; for Muhammad is such and such.\" And she kept at him until he was satisfied. Then she sent to Muhammad ﷺ two ounces of silver or gold, and said: \"Buy a suit and give it to him as a gift, and such and such.\" He said, and I think he did it."],[4297,"I was sent while the Hour is as these two—like this one from this one."],[4298,"He said to Zayd b. Arqam: Do you not know that a limb of game was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in ihram, and he did not accept it? He said: Yes."],[4299,"Zayd b. Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas asked him, seeking his recollection: How did you inform me about the meat of game that was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in a state of sanctity? He said: Yes, a leg or a limb of game meat was gifted to him, and he returned it, saying: We do not eat it; we are in a state of sanctity."],[4300,"\"A group of my community will not cease to be upon the truth.\" He said: Indeed, I hope that you, O people of Syria, are they."],[4301,"\"Whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be at enmity with whoever is at enmity with him.\""],[4302,"Ali adjured the people in al-Rahbah: Who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Ghadir Khumm? Six stood up and testified that they heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: \"Am I not more entitled to the believers?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"And am I not more entitled to you than your own selves?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"O God, whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be at enmity with whoever is at enmity with him.\""],[4303,"Sharīk narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habīb b. Abī Thābit, from Abū al-Ṭufayl, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[4304,"A man from the Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Abū al-Qāsim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed a man among them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire. He said: Then the one who eats and drinks will have need to relieve himself? He said: \"A sweat that flows like the scent of musk; when that occurs, his belly will become lean.\""],[4305,"Ya'lā narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thumāmah, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. And other than Abū Mu'āwiyah said: And Ya'lā, from al-A'mash, from Yazīd b. Ḥayyān, from Zayd b. Arqam."],[4306,"Jarīr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thumāmah b. 'Uqbah al-Muḥallimī, from Zayd b. Arqam."],[4307,"A man from the Ansar tied knots against the Prophet ﷺ, and he suffered pain from that. The two angels came to visit him. One of them said to his companion: Do you know what is with him? So-and-so the Ansari tied knots against him and threw it into such-and-such a well. If he were to take it out and throw it away, he would be healed. So they were sent to the well, and they found the water had turned green. They took it out and threw it away, and the Prophet ﷺ was healed. Nothing was seen in his face, nor did he speak of it."],[4308,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us were people from the Bedouins. We would race to the water, and the Bedouins would outpace us. A Bedouin would outpace his companions and fill the trough, placing stones around it and putting a leather mat over it until his companions arrived. He said: A man from the Ansar came to a Bedouin and inserted the nose-rein of his camel to let it drink, but he refused to let him. He pulled out a stone, and the water sank. The Bedouin raised a piece of wood and struck the Ansari's head with it, wounding him. He went to Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul, the head of the hypocrites, and informed him, as he was one of his companions. Abdullah b. Ubayy became angry and said: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God, until they disperse from around him—meaning the Bedouins—and they used to attend the Messenger of God ﷺ at meals. Abdullah said to his companions: When they disperse from Muhammad, bring food to Muhammad; let him and those with him eat. Then he said to his companions: When you return to Madinah, the more mighty will expel the more lowly. Zayd said: I was riding behind my uncle, and I heard Abdullah b. Ubayy, and we were his maternal uncles. I informed my uncle, and he went and informed the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for him, and he swore and denied. He believed him and called me a liar. My uncle came to me and said: What did you intend? The Messenger of God ﷺ accepted his words and called you a liar, and the Muslims called you a liar. He said: Such worry fell upon me as had never fallen upon anyone. He said: While I was traveling with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, I dozed off with my head due to worry. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me, rubbed my ear, and smiled in my face. It would not have pleased me to have sovereignty or the world in exchange for that. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of God say to you? I said: He did not say anything to me except that he rubbed my ear and smiled in my face. He said: Rejoice. Then Umar caught up with me and said to me the like of Abu Bakr's words. When morning came, the Messenger of God ﷺ recited Surat al-Munafiqun."],[4309,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and 'Abdullah b. Ubayy said: 'If we return to Madinah, the most honorable will surely expel from it the most abased.' So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said to me, 'My people—what did you intend by this?' So I went back and slept sorrowful and sad. Then 'Abdullah b. Ubayy came and swore an oath, so I returned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Allah has indeed confirmed you, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: \"They are the ones who say: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse. And to Allah belong the treasures of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand.\"'"],[4310,"Shall I not teach you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us? 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from inability and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, from senility and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant our souls their taqwā; You are the best of those who purify them. You are their Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered.'"],[4311,"'Abd al-Wāḥid b. Ziyād reported to us, from 'Āṣim al-Aḥwal, from 'Abdullāh b. al-Ḥārith, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ, with its like. And this hadith—we do not know it to be narrated from Zayd b. Arqam except through this route, and we do not know anyone who combined Abū 'Uthmān and 'Abdullāh b. al-Ḥārith except Mu'āwiyah, from 'Āṣim."],[4312,"“O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the sons of the Anṣār, and the sons of the sons of the Anṣār.”"],[4313,"“O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the sons of the Anṣār, and the sons of the sons of the Anṣār.”"],[4314,"Abū Dāwūd reported to us, saying: Shu'bah, from 'Alī b. Zayd, from al-Naḍr b. Anas, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ, with its like. And this hadith—we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr b. Anas, from Zayd who is more trustworthy than Shu'bah, and more than one followed him in its narration, so we were content with Shu'bah. But Ma'mar disagreed with him and said: from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr b. Anas, from Anas."],[4315,"“Indeed these lavatories are attended. So when one of you goes to relieve himself, let him say: I seek refuge with Allah from the male and female devils.”"],[4316,"Shu'bah, from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr, from Zayd, and Ma'mar said: from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr b. Anas, from his father, while Ibn Abī 'Arūbah said: from Qatādah, from al-Qāsim b. 'Awf al-Shaybānī, from Zayd, and Ḥusām b. Miṣakk said: from Qatādah, from al-Qāsim b. Rabī'ah, from Zayd b. Arqam."],[4317,"Sa'īd—meaning Ibn Abī 'Arūbah—reported to us, from Qatādah, from al-Qāsim al-Shaybānī, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ ."],[4318,"He passed by the mosque of Qubā' and found them praying after the sun had risen bright, so he said: 'The prayer of the penitent: they used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat of the sun.'"],[4319,"He saw a people praying the forenoon prayer in the mosque of Qubā', so he said: 'Do they not know that prayer at other than this hour is better? Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun.'"],[4320,"“When a man calls his wife, let her respond, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle.”"],[4321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh b. Jabal to Syria. When Mu'adh arrived, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and patriarchs; should we not prostrate to you? He said: No. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband."],[4322,"Sadaqah - meaning Ibn 'Abd Allah - reported to us, from Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And this hadith has been disputed regarding al-Qasim al-Shaybani. Ayyub said: from al-Qasim b. Abi Awfa. Qatadah said: from al-Qasim, from Zayd b. Arqam. Hisham said: from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Mu'adh. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Abi 'Arubah except Sadaqah, and Sadaqah is not strong in hadith, but the scholars have written down his hadith."],[4323,"That he said to 'Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn ؓ: I am at war with those who fight you, and at peace with those who make peace with you."],[4324,"Zayd b. Arqam used to pray over our funerals and say four takbirs. One day he said five, so we asked him about that. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said five takbirs."],[4325,"I prayed behind Zayd b. Arqam over a funeral and he said five takbirs. Ibn Abi Layla said to him: Did you make a mistake? He said: No, I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over a funeral and he said five takbirs."],[4326,"Muhammad b. Fudayl reported to us, from Layth b. al-Muraqqi', from Zayd b. Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stopped at a valley between Makkah and Madinah and gave us a sermon. Then he said: I am only a human being; I am about to be called and I will answer. Indeed, I am leaving among you the two weighty things: one of them is the Book of Allah and my household. He said it three times. We said: Who are his household - his wives? He said: Have you not seen that a woman stays with a man for a time and then returns to her father and her people? His household are his family and his kin who are forbidden to receive charity after him: the family of 'Abbas, the family of 'Ali, the family of Ja'far, and the family of 'Aqil."],[4328,"Indeed, I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my household, and they will never separate until they return to me at the Pool."],[4329,"I met Zayd b. Arqam while he was entering upon al-Mukhtar and I was leaving from his presence. I said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Indeed, I am leaving among you the two weighty things? He said: Yes."],[4330,"We stopped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a valley called Wadi Khumm. The call to prayer was given and he prayed it at midday. Then he gave us a sermon, and a cloth was stretched over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a samurah tree to shade him from the sun. He said: Do you not know or testify that I am closer to every believer than his own self? They said: Yes. He said: So whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend those who befriend him and be hostile to those who are hostile to him."],[4331,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that pleurisy be treated with Indian aloeswood and olive oil."],[4332,"I asked Zayd b. Arqam: What was the name of the mother of the Prophet ﷺ? He said: Aminah bt. Wahb."],[4333,"I asked al-Bara' and Zayd b. Arqam ؓ about money exchange. They said: We were two merchants in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about money exchange. He said: Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm, and whatever is on credit is not proper."],[4334,"Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm, and whatever is on credit is not proper."],[4335,"Whoever does not trim his moustache is not one of us."],[4336,"We used to recite: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would desire a second, and nothing fills the son of Adam's soul except dust."],[4337,"We were sitting with Zayd b. Arqam, and a man came and sat down. He said: People have said much about these two men: 'Ali and 'Uthman. Tell me about them. He said: I will not tell you except what I witnessed and my heart retained. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out and faced us, praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: Do you not know that I have more right over the believers than their own selves? He repeated it to us three times, each time we said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, while 'Ali was silent. He said: Stand up, O 'Ali, and he took hold of his upper arm or his two upper arms and raised it or raised them, then said: Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla."],[4338,"'Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad sent for me, so I went to him. He said: What are these hadiths that reach us from you, which you narrate and relate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we do not find them in the Book of Allah? You narrate that he has a basin in Paradise. I said: He did."],[4339,"I, Husayn, and 'Amr b. Muslim, or 'Umar b. Muslim, went to Zayd b. Arqam at his house. Husayn said: O Zayd, you have encountered good and seen much good. You saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, heard his hadith, campaigned with him, and prayed behind him. Tell us what you saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and witnessed from him. He said: O son of my brother, my age has become old and my time has grown distant, and I have forgotten some of what I used to remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So whatever I narrate to you, accept it, and whatever I do not narrate to you, do not burden me with it. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, O people, I am only a human being; soon the messenger of my Lord will come to me and I will respond. I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the first is the Book of Allah, in it is guidance and light, so he urged adherence to the Book of Allah and encouraged it, and my household. I remind you of Allah concerning my household. Husayn said: O Zayd, who are his household? Are his wives from his household? He said: His wives are from his household, but his household are those who are forbidden charity after him. It was said: Who are they? He said: The family of 'Abbas, the family of 'Ali, the family of Ja'far, and the family of 'Aqil, for these are forbidden charity."],[4340,"I witnessed Mu'awiya ask Zayd b. Arqam ؓ: Did you witness the Eid prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Friday prayer? He said: I witnessed that with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: What did he do? He said: He prayed the Eid prayer and granted a concession regarding the Friday prayer, saying: Whoever wishes to stay may stay."],[4341,"Excellent is the man Bilal, and he is the master of the martyrs, and the mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection."],[4342,"Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Zayd b. Arqam."],[4343,"Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Zayd b. Arqam."],[4344,"I fell ill and the Prophet ﷺ visited me. Then I recovered and met him. He said: O Zayd, if your eye were afflicted with what it has, what would you do? I said: I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your eye were afflicted with what it has, and you were patient and sought reward, Paradise would be obligatory for you."],[4345,"A servant is not tested, after the loss of his religion, with anything more severe than his eyesight. Whoever is tested with his eyesight and remains patient until he meets Allah, he will meet Allah — Blessed and Exalted is He — and there will be no reckoning upon him."],[4346,"I went on nineteen military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4347,"When the Prophet ﷺ spent the night in the cave, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, commanded a tree and it grew at the mouth of the cave and concealed the Prophet ﷺ. Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, commanded the spider, and it spun a web over the mouth of the cave. Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, commanded two wild rock doves, and they alighted at the mouth of the cave. The polytheists came from every clan until, when they were about forty cubits from the Prophet ﷺ with their bows and staffs, one of their men stepped forward, looked, and saw the two doves. He went back and said to his companions: 'There is nothing in the cave. I saw two doves at its mouth, so I knew there was no one inside.' The Prophet ﷺ heard his words and knew that Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, had turned them away by means of those two doves. He blessed them and prescribed their recompense, and they became established in the sanctuary of Allah, hatching young there. I think he said: 'The origin of every dove in the sanctuary is from their offspring.'"],[4348,"Allah never sent any prophet except that he lived half as long as the prophet before him."],[4349,"You are one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to the Pond."],[4350,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his journeys, and there was a scarcity of riding animals. The people discussed among themselves the riding animals, and a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a stray animal?' He replied: 'When you find a stray animal or a lost item, announce it, and do not conceal it or alter it.' And I saw him in another place: 'Announce it, and do not conceal it or hide it. If you recognize its owner, then return it; otherwise, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"],[4351,"Hilal b. Hiqq reported to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-'Ala', from Mutarrif, from Abu Muslim, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4352,"The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire."],[4353,"The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire."],[4354,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking while standing."],[4355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and I noticed some roughness from him. When I returned, I complained about him to the Prophet ﷺ. He raised his head and said: 'O Buraydah, whoever I am his mawla, then 'Ali is his mawla.'"],[4356,"Abu Maryam reported to us, from 'Adi b. Thabit, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Buraydah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know of Ibn 'Abbas transmitting from Buraydah except this hadith."],[4357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition and appointed ʿAlī ؓ as our commander. When we returned, he said: \"How did you find your companion?\" He said: Either I complained about him or someone else complained about him. He said: I raised my head, for I was a man who kept his head lowered, and behold, the Prophet ﷺ's face had reddened and he was saying: \"Whoever I am the guardian of, ʿAlī is his guardian.\" So I said: \"I will never upset you regarding him again.\""],[4358,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a commander or appointed a commander over a military expedition or army, he would instruct him and counsel him personally to fear Allah and to treat well those Muslims with him. Then he would say: \"Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Raid, but do not embezzle spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy from the polytheists, call them to one of three traits or qualities. Whichever of them they respond to, accept from them and refrain from them. Call them to Islam; if they respond, accept from them and refrain from them. Then call them to emigrate from their land to the land of the emigrants, and inform them that if they do so, they will have what the emigrants have and bear what the emigrants bear. If they refuse to leave their land, inform them that they will be like the Bedouin Muslims, subject to the judgment of Allah that applies to the Muslims, and they will have no share in the fayʾ or the spoils. If they refuse, then ask them for the jizyah; if they accept, accept from them and leave them alone. If they refuse, then fight them. When you besiege the people of a fortress and they ask you to grant them the protection of Allah and His Messenger, do not grant them the protection of Allah and His Messenger, but grant them your protection, the protection of your father, and the protections of your companions. For if you violate your protections and those of your companions, it is lighter than violating the protection of Allah and His Messenger ﷺ. When you besiege the people of a fortress and they ask you to bring them down according to the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down according to the judgment of Allah, but bring them down according to your judgment; for you do not know whether you will hit the judgment of Allah regarding them or not.\""],[4359,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a commander over a military expedition or dispatched an army..."],[4360,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from al-Layth b. Saʿd, from Jarīr b. Ḥāzim, from Shuʿbah, from ʿAlqamah b. Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet."],[4361,"Whoever plays nardashīr (backgammon), it is as if he has dipped his hand into the flesh and blood of a pig."],[4362,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then a Bedouin stood up and said: \"Who will supplicate for the red camel?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May you not find it.\""],[4363,"Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAlqamah b. Marthad, from Sulaymān b. Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4364,"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my ummah comprises eighty rows of them."],[4365,"The nations on the Day of Resurrection will be one hundred and twenty rows; my ummah comprises eighty rows of them."],[4366,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[4367,"He used to perform ablution for every prayer until the day of the conquest of Makkah, for he prayed the prayers with a single ablution and wiped over his leather socks. ʿUmar said to him: \"You have done something today that you have not done before.\" He replied: \"I did it deliberately, O ʿUmar.\""],[4368,"Sufyān narrated to us, from Muḥārib b. Dithār, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4369,"The sanctity of the wives of the mujahidun over those who stay behind is like the sanctity of their mothers. There is no one among those who stay behind who takes the place of a man from the mujahidun concerning his family except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: 'Take whatever you wish of his good deeds.' He said: 'So what do you think?'"],[4370,"Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Alqamah b. Marthad, from Sulayman b. Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4371,"When he passed by graves, he would say: 'Peace be upon the abodes of a believing people. Indeed we, if Allah wills, will join you. May Allah the Almighty forgive us and you, and have mercy on us and you.'"],[4372,"Mu'awiyah b. Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Alqamah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And the hadith of Shu'bah, from 'Alqamah, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Harami b. 'Umarah."],[4373,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the times of prayer. He prayed Zuhr when the sun had declined, prayed 'Asr when the shadow of every object was equal to it, prayed Maghrib when the sun had set, prayed 'Isha' when the twilight had disappeared, and prayed Fajr when dawn broke. Then he prayed Zuhr when the shadow of every object was equal to it, 'Asr when the shadow of every object was twice its length, Maghrib when the sun had set at its time from yesterday, 'Isha' after it had become dark, and Fajr when it had brightened. Then he said: 'Where is the one who asked about the times of prayer? Between these two is a time.'"],[4374,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Alqamah b. Marthad, from Sulayman b. Buraydah, from his father ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the times of prayer. And Bundar did not have from his speech except this, and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Harami, nor from al-Thawri except Ishaq b. Yusuf."],[4375,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu' once (washing each limb) once."],[4376,"I had forbidden you from visiting graves, but permission has been granted to Muhammad ﷺ to visit the grave of his mother, so visit them as you wish; for they remind of the Hereafter. And I had forbidden you from eating the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, but we only intended by that for those with abundance to share with those without abundance, so eat as you wish. And I had forbidden you from certain vessels, but vessels do not make anything lawful or unlawful, and every intoxicant is forbidden."],[4377,"There is nothing except that it is more obedient to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, than the son of Adam."],[4378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited the grave of his mother with a thousand veiled men."],[4379,"Yahya b. al-Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Alqamah b. Marthad, as a mursal report."],[4380,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I love horses. Are there horses in Paradise?' He said: 'If Allah admits you to Paradise, you will not wish to ride a horse made of red ruby that flies with you wherever you wish in Paradise except that you will ride it.' He said: 'Then another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, are there camels in Paradise?' He said: 'If Allah admits you to Paradise, you will have therein whatever your soul desires and your eyes delight in.'"],[4381,"For the people of the covenant, they keep whatever wealth, lands, offspring, slaves, and livestock they had when they embraced Islam; nothing is due from them in that except the zakat."],[4382,"The topic of omens was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'If anyone is affected by any of that and cannot help it' — and the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ 'and cannot help it' became dearer to us than such-and-such — 'then let him say: O God, there is no omen except Your omen, and no good except Your good, and no god other than You.'"],[4383,"A man was performing tawaf carrying his mother, circumambulating with her. He asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'Have I fulfilled her right?' He said: 'No, not even for one of her labor pains.'"],[4384,"He mentioned the cistern (al-Hawd) and said: 'You will see in it pitchers as numerous as the stars of the sky.'"],[4385,"Do not call a hypocrite 'master,' for if you do, you will anger your Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[4386,"When you send a messenger to me, send one who is handsome in face and handsome in name."],[4387,"The death of a believer is accompanied by sweat on the forehead."],[4388,"Kahmas b. al-Hasan narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. We do not know of Kahmas having a chain from 'Abd Allah b. Buraydah from his father other than this hadith, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Kahmas except Yusuf b. Ya'qub."],[4389,"'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abd Allah b. Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet."],[4390,"The black seed is a cure for every disease except death."],[4391,"A servant will never be tested with anything more severe than associating partners with God. And after associating partners with God, a servant will never be tested with anything more severe than losing his sight. And no servant is tested with losing his sight and remains patient except that he is forgiven."],[4392,"He said: 'How do you speak, O Hamzah, when you retire to your bed?' He said: 'I say such-and-such.' He said: 'And how do you speak, O 'Ali?' He said: 'I say such-and-such.' I think he said: 'When you retire to your bed, say: Praise be to God who has bestowed favor upon me and been gracious. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, Lord of everything and God of everything. I seek refuge in You from the Fire.'"],[4393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led his companions in prayer one day. When he finished, he asked, \"How did you find my prayer?\" They replied, \"How excellent your prayer was!\" He said, \"I forgot such-and-such a verse. Part of the excellence of a person's prayer is that he memorizes the imam's recitation.\""],[4394,"The Prophet ﷺ sent two armies to Yemen, appointing Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ over one and Khalid b. al-Walid over the other. He told them: \"If you are together, Ali is in charge of the people; if you separate, each of you is in charge of his own companions.\" We met the enemy, and the Muslims prevailed over the polytheists. We killed the warriors and took the offspring captive. Ali ؓ selected a woman from the captives for himself. Khalid b. al-Walid wrote to the Prophet ﷺ about that and sent the letter with me, and he commanded me to speak ill of Ali ؓ. When the letter was read to the Prophet ﷺ, I spoke ill of Ali ؓ. I saw anger on his face, and I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, you sent me with a man and ordered me to obey him, so I did what I was sent to do.\" He said, \"O Buraydah, do not disparage Ali, for he is from me and I am from him.\""],[4395,"Al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet."],[4396,"The Negus gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two plain black leather socks. He wore them and used to wipe over them."],[4397,"\"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves four individuals and commanded me to love them.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they?\" He said, \"Ali is among them, Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, Salman al-Farisi, and al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad al-Kindi.\""],[4398,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali ؓ: \"The first glance is yours, but do not follow one glance with another.\""],[4399,"Some people came to my father and said, \"Give us privacy.\" He told my mother and those around him from the household, \"Get up.\" They got up, but I remained. They said, \"Give us privacy.\" He said, \"He is only my son.\" They asked, \"Who was the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Ali.\""],[4400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to a place in the desert: a salty patch of ground with water around it, near Makkah. He said, \"From this spot the Beast will emerge.\" It was a spot a hand-span by a cubit."],[4401,"On the night he was taken on the Night Journey, Jibril came to the rock at the Bayt al-Maqdis, placed his finger on it, pierced it, and tied al-Buraq to it."],[4402,"\"A people will come with small eyes, broad faces, as if their faces are hammered shields. They will drive the people of Islam to the places where wormwood grows. It is as if I am looking at them: they have tied their horses to the pillars of the mosque.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they?\" He said, \"They are the Turks.\""],[4403,"\"One hundred years will not pass while any eye that blinks [remains].\""],[4404,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when news reached him that a woman of the Ansar had lost a son and was grieving for him. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood up with his companions. When he reached the woman's door, it was said to her, \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ wants to enter to console you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, \"I have heard that you are grieving over your son.\" She said, \"O Prophet of Allah, why should I not grieve? I am a woman bereaved of children; no child of mine lives.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The truly bereaved is the one whose children live. No Muslim woman or Muslim man loses three children—or he said, three of offspring—and seeks reward for it, except that Paradise becomes obligatory for them.\" Umar ؓ, who was on the right of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said, \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you—and two?\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"And two.\""],[4405,"I was sent, and the Hour is as close as these two,\" and he joined his two fingers, the index and middle finger."],[4406,"\"Whoever utters in Islam a foul poem, his tongue is forfeited.\""],[4407,"\"Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.\""],[4408,"\"Whoever swears that he is free from Islam, if he is lying, then he is as he said; and if he is truthful, he will never return to Islam safely.\""],[4409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon when al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ came forward wearing two shirts, stumbling and getting up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit, took them, and placed them in front of him. Then he said: \"Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth: 'Your wealth and your children are only a trial.'\""],[4410,"When Salman al-Farisi came to Madinah, he brought a table to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with fresh dates on it. He said to him: \"What is this, O Salman?\" He said: \"It is charity I have given to you and your companions.\" He said: \"We do not eat charity.\" The next day he brought something similar and placed it before him, and he said: \"O Salman, what is this?\" He said: \"It is a gift.\" He said: \"Eat,\" and he ate. He looked at the seal on his back. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased him for such-and-such dirhams from some Jews, on condition that he plant such-and-such date palms for them, and work until they bear fruit. He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ planted the date palms except for one palm that someone else planted, and the palms bore fruit that year except for the palm that someone else planted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who planted it?\" They said: \"So-and-so.\" He uprooted it and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ planted it, and it bore fruit that same year."],[4411,"\"The nobility of the people of this world in this world is wealth.\""],[4412,"\"Five things no one knows except Allah, Blessed and Exalted: Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs; and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware.\""],[4413,"\"The rider of a mount is more entitled to its front, and a man is more entitled to the front of his horse.\""],[4414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in Maghrib and Isha and the night prayer: \"When it covers\" (al-Layl), and \"The Morning Brightness\" (al-Duha). And he used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\" (al-A'la) and \"Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?\" (al-Ghashiyah)."],[4415,"Mu'adh b. Jabal led his companions in Isha prayer and recited \"The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split\" (al-Qamar). A man prayed and left, so Mu'adh spoke harshly. The man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining that he had been working in his date-palm grove. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Recite in them (the prayers) with 'By the sun and its brightness' (al-Shams) and similar surahs.\""],[4416,"\"Between us and them is the abandonment of prayer; whoever abandons it has disbelieved.\""],[4417,"A black woman made a vow: if God, Blessed and Exalted, returned His Messenger safely from a military expedition he went on, she would beat the duff over his head. When the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived, she came and said, \"O Messenger of God! I had vowed that if God, Blessed and Exalted, returned you safely, I would beat the duff before you.\" He said, \"If you made the vow, then fulfill it; otherwise, do not.\" So she beat it. Abu Bakr ؓ entered while she was beating it, and others entered while she was beating it. When Umar came, she threw the duff aside. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Here I am, along with Abu Bakr ؓ; yet I reckon that Satan is certainly afraid of you, O Umar.\""],[4418,"\"I entered Paradise and saw a palace there. I asked, 'For whom is this?' They said, 'For an Arab man.' I said, 'I am an Arab.' I asked, 'For whom is this palace?' They said, 'For a man from the community of Muhammad ﷺ.' I said, 'I am Muhammad.' Then I asked, 'For whom is this palace?' They said, 'For Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. Were it not for your jealousy, I would have entered it.'\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, I would never be jealous of you.\""],[4419,"A man said on the day of Uhud, \"O God, if Muhammad is upon the truth, then cause the earth to swallow him.\" So it swallowed him."],[4420,"\"In the human being there are three hundred and sixty joints. For each joint, charity is due.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, who can bear that?\" He said, \"A gob of spittle you bury is charity, removing something harmful from the road is charity, and the two rak'ahs of Duha suffice for that.\""],[4421,"\"I heard a soft footstep ahead of me. I asked, 'Who is this?' It was said, 'Bilal.' I said, 'By what have you preceded me to Paradise?'\" He said, \"I never break my ablution but that I renew it, and I never renew ablution but that I see it as due to God, Blessed and Exalted, to pray two rak'ahs.\" He said, \"By that.\""],[4422,"He was on Hira and it trembled. He said, \"Settle, for upon you are none but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.\" Upon it were the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali ؓ all together."],[4423,"\"God, Blessed and Exalted, has a wind He sends at the head of every hundred years, and it seizes the soul of every believer.\""],[4424,"\"Learn Surat al-Baqarah and Surat Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for their companion. Learn Surat al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot overcome it.\""],[4425,"\"Between the two calls to prayer there is a prayer, except for Maghrib.\""],[4426,"Al-Muqawqis the Copt gifted the Messenger of God ﷺ two slave girls, sisters: one of them was Mariyah, mother of Ibrahim son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the other the Messenger of God ﷺ gave to Hassan b. Thabit; she is the mother of Abd al-Rahman b. Thabit. He also gifted him a mule, and the Messenger of God ﷺ accepted that from him."],[4427,"\"Three things are from rudeness: a man urinating standing, or wiping his forehead before finishing his prayer, or blowing in his prostration.\""],[4428,"\"He is not one of us who swears by al-Amanah, and he is not one of us who corrupts a woman or a slave.\""],[4429,"\"Whoever swears by al-Amanah (the trust) is not from us.\""],[4430,"\"Whomever we appoint over a task and provide a sustenance for it, then whatever he takes beyond his sustenance is embezzlement.\""],[4431,"\"Whoever of my Companions dies in a land, he will be an intercessor for that land, and a guide for them on the Day of Resurrection\" – or he said – \"an intercessor for the people of that land on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4432,"\"Whoever of my Companions dies in a land, he will be an intercessor for the people of that land on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4433,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and whenever anything remained, he would load it onto me and call me al-Zamilah (the pack animal)."],[4434,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing an iron ring. He said: \"Why do I find the smell of idols on you?\" So he went and made it of brass. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something about it. He asked: \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I make it from?\" He said: \"Make it from silver, and do not exceed one mithqal.\""],[4435,"Indeed, the seven heavens, the seven earths, and the mountains curse the adulterous old man; and indeed, the genitals of adulterers harm the people of Hell with their foul odor."],[4436,"Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Salih b. Hayyan, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know anyone who raised this hadith except Abu Mu'awiyah."],[4437,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in prayer: \"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would desire a second; if he were given a second, he would desire a third; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.\""],[4438,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, he heard noise. He said: \"What is this sound?\" They said: \"O Prophet of Allah, a people have a drink they are consuming.\" He sent for the people and called them, then said: \"Do not drink except what you have sealed.\" Then he said: \"Drink, but every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[4439,"\"I forbade you from visiting graves, but now visit them. I forbade you from keeping the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, but now keep it as long as you wish. I forbade you from nabidh except in a waterskin, so drink from waterskins, but do not consume intoxicants.\""],[4440,"The Prophet ﷺ gave permission for vessels after having forbidden them."],[4441,"The greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, withholding surplus water, and withholding the stallion."],[4442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched an idol and then performed ablution."],[4443,"He used to say: \"O Allah, make me grateful, make me patient, make me small in my own eyes, and great in the eyes of the people.\""],[4444,"The people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and no one remained with him except a man called Zayd, who was holding the bridle of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ gray mule. The Messenger of Allah said to him: \"Woe to you! Call the people.\" So Zayd called out: \"O people, this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling you,\" but no one came. He said: \"Call the Ansar.\" So he called out: \"O company of the Ansar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is calling you,\" but no one came. He said: \"Woe to you! Specifically call the Aws and the Khazraj.\" So he said: \"O company of the Aws and the Khazraj, this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling you,\" but no one came. He said: \"Woe to you! Specifically call the Muhajirun, for I have a pledge in their necks.\" Buraydah narrated to me that a thousand of them came forward, having thrown aside their shields, until they reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they advanced on foot until Allah granted them victory."],[4445,"A woman threw a stone at another woman, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled a compensation of five hundred for her child, and on that day he prohibited throwing stones."],[4446,"When one of you prays facing a sutrah, let him draw close to it so that Satan does not interrupt his prayer."],[4447,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped in the presence of the people of Khaybar. He gave the banner to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and those who went with him from the people advanced. They met the people of Khaybar, and Umar ؓ and his companions were exposed, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his companions accusing him of cowardice, and he accusing his companions of cowardice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.\" When the next day came, he called Ali ؓ and handed it to him while he was suffering from eye inflammation. He spat into his eye, gave him the banner, and the people set out with him. He came to the people of Khaybar, and there was Marhab reciting war poetry before them, saying: \"Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed with weapons, a tested hero; sometimes I thrust and sometimes I strike when swords advance blazing.\" He and Ali ؓ exchanged two blows, and Ali ؓ struck him on the crown of his head so that the sword bit into his molars. The people of the army heard the sound of his blow, and the last of the people had not yet joined when the first of them was already victorious."],[4448,"There is none among you except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will speak to him with no veil between Him and him and no interpreter."],[4449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ trained horses for racing, set a specific time for their training, and said: on such-and-such a day from such-and-such a place. And he sent the horses that were not trained from a shorter distance."],[4450,"Three types of people the angels do not approach: the drunkard, the one who is perfumed with saffron, and the menstruating woman or the one in a state of major ritual impurity."],[4451,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came during his emigration, he met a caravan. He said: \"O Abu Bakr, ask the people who they are.\" They said: \"We are from Aslam.\" He said: \"You are safe, O Abu Bakr. Ask them from which Aslam.\" They said: \"From Banu Sahm.\" He said: \"Cast your arrow, O Abu Bakr.\""],[4452,"Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[4453,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man from Quraysh approached, strutting in his fine garment. When he stood before the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “O Buraydah! This is one for whom Allah will not establish any weight on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4454,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Show me a sign.” He said: “Go to that tree and call it.” So he went to it and said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ calls you.” It swayed on every side until it uprooted itself, then came forward until it reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah commanded it to return, so the man stood up, kissed his head, his hands, and his feet, and embraced Islam."],[4455,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man say: “O Allah, I ask You by virtue that You are Allah, there is no god but You, the One, the Eternal Refuge, who neither begets nor is born, and there is none comparable to You.” He said: “He has asked Allah by His name, which when called upon He answers, and when asked by it He gives.”"],[4456,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[4457,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we were at Waddan or at al-Qubur, and he sought intercession for his mother. I think he said: Gabriel ﷺ struck his chest and said: “Do not seek forgiveness for one who died an idolater.” So he returned grieving."],[4458,"Sufyan narrated to us, from ‘Alqamah b. Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father."],[4459,"We had forbidden you from pairing dates, so pair them; for Allah has expanded the good."],[4460,"A man does not give charity until he loosens the jaws of seventy devils from it."],[4461,"The Prophet ﷺ sought forgiveness for Ma‘iz."],[4462,"Ma‘iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent him back repeatedly. Then he said: “Test him with the odor of wine.” They did so, then he stoned him."],[4463,"A stone falls into Hell and does not reach its bottom for seventy autumns."],[4464,"Whoever attacks us at night is not one of us."],[4465,"A woman from the Ghamid tribe came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said that she had committed adultery. The Prophet ﷺ turned away from her, but she said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you intend to turn me away as you turned away Maʿiz? She is pregnant from adultery.” He said, “When do you give birth?” She went away, and when she had given birth she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ carrying the child and said, “I have given birth.” He said, “Go away until you have weaned him.” She went away, then came back with him while in his hand was a piece of bread, and said, “I have weaned him.” He said, “Bring me someone who will take charge of him.” A man stood up and said, “I will take charge of him.” The Prophet’s companions ﷺ were astonished at the man and said, “What harm would it have been for him if he had not taken charge of him?” Then he ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. A man said, “How can you pray over her when she is like this?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among the people of Madinah, it would suffice them all,” or something like that."],[4466,"“O Buraydah, when it is the time for you to begin the prayer, say: ‘Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. There is no power and no strength except with Allah. There is no god but You, alone, with no partner. Blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You. I have wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins except You.’ Then recite whatever of the Qurʾan is easy for you. Then bow and say: ‘Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent’ three times. When you rise from bowing, say: ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever else You will.’ When you prostrate, say: ‘Glory be to my Lord the Most High’ three times. My face has prostrated to the One who created it and gave it hearing and sight. Blessed be Allah, the best of creators. When you rise from prostration, say: ‘My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me. I am truly in need of whatever good You send down to me.’ When you sit in your prayer, do not neglect in the tashahhud: ‘There is no god but Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah,’ and to send blessings upon me and upon all the prophets of Allah, and to greet the righteous servants of Allah.”"],[4467,"“No people ever break a covenant except that killing occurs among them. No immorality ever appears among a people except that Allah sends death upon them. No people ever withhold zakah except that Allah withholds rain from them.”"],[4468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Jaʿfar ؓ when he arrived from Abyssinia, “What was the most amazing thing you saw?” He said, “I saw a woman carrying on her head a basket of food. A horseman passed by and knocked it over, scattering it. She sat down gathering her food, then turned and said, ‘Woe to him when the King, Blessed and Exalted, places His throne and takes for the wronged from the wrongdoer.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in confirmation of her words, “A nation is not sanctified—or how can a nation be sanctified—when its weak cannot take their right from its strong without being hindered.”"],[4469,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ and saw him looking sad. A man said to him, “Why do I see you as if you are sad?” He said, “I remembered that I had forbidden you from eating the meat of sacrificial animals except for three days. So eat, feed others, and store whatever you wish. I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so whoever among you wants to visit a grave, let him visit it. I had forbidden you from using gourds, green jars, wooden vessels, and pitch-coated vessels, so avoid every intoxicant and drink in whatever vessels you wish.”"],[4470,"“The master of seeking forgiveness is for a man to say when he sits in his prayer: ‘O Allah, You are my Lord. There is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant. I remain faithful to my covenant and promise to You as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your blessings upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me. None forgives sins except You.’”"],[4471,"Khalf b. Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father."],[4472,"“Judges are of three types: two are in the Fire and one is in Paradise. A judge who rules unjustly is in the Fire. A judge who rules without knowledge is in the Fire. A judge who rules with truth is in Paradise.”"],[4473,"“No man is placed in authority over ten or more people except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck. If he was good, his shackle will be released; if he was bad, an additional shackle will be added to his shackle.”"],[4474,"“Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”"],[4475,"A group of people said to ʿAli ؓ, “If only you would propose to Fatimah ؓ.” He went to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “What is ʿAli’s need?” He said, “I have mentioned Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Welcome and greetings.” He did not add anything to those two words. So ʿAli ؓ went out to those people who were waiting for him. They said, “What do you have?” He said, “I do not know, except that he said to me, ‘Welcome and greetings.’” They said, “That is enough for you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: he granted you the family and he granted you the welcome.” Later, when some time had passed, he married him to her. He said, “O ʿAli, a wedding must have a feast.” Saʿd said, “I have a ram,” and he gathered a group from the Ansar. On the wedding night, he said, “O ʿAli, do not do anything until you meet me.” The Prophet ﷺ called for water, performed ablution with it, then poured the remaining water over ʿAli ؓ and said, “O Allah, bless them both and bless for them their two cubs (children).”"],[4476,"Salamah b. Yazid al-Juʿfi asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us to do if rulers are placed over us who demand their rights from us but deny us our rights?” He turned away from him. Then he asked again, and he turned away. Then he asked a third time, and he turned away. Then he said, “Listen and obey, for you are responsible for what you are burdened with, and they are responsible for what they are burdened with.”"],[4477,"Tariq b. Suwayd asked the Prophet ﷺ about wine used as medicine, so he said: \"It is not a cure, but rather it is a disease.\""],[4478,"\"Do not call grapes 'al-karm,' but rather 'al-habala.'\""],[4479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him a piece of land. He said: He sent Mu'awiya with me and said: 'Give it to him.' He said: I set out riding while Mu'awiya was walking in the midday heat. Mu'awiya said: 'Let me ride behind you.' I said: 'You are not one to ride behind kings.' He said: 'Then give me your sandal.' I said: 'Use the shade of the camel.' When Mu'awiya became caliph, I came to him and he seated me with him on the couch and reminded me of the incident. I wished that I had carried him in front of me."],[4480,"A man from Hadramawt and a man from Kinda came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Hadrami said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this man has seized land that belonged to my father.' The Kindi said: 'It is my land and in my possession; he has no right to it.' The Prophet ﷺ said to the Hadrami: 'Do you have evidence?' He said: 'I have no evidence.' He said: 'Then he must swear.' He said: 'If he swears, he will not care what he swears about; he does not refrain from anything.' He said: 'You have no other recourse.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever swears falsely to take his brother's property and consumes it unjustly will meet Allah while He is turned away from him.'"],[4481,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when two men came to him disputing over land. One of them said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this man encroached upon my land in the pre-Islamic era.' He was Imru' al-Qays, and the other was Rabi'a b. 'Abdan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your evidence.' He said: 'I have no evidence.' He said: 'His oath.' He said: 'Then he will take it.' He said: 'You have no other recourse.' When he stood up to swear, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever seizes land unjustly will meet Allah while He is angry with him.' Abu Bakr said: I think he said: 'Whoever is granted land unjustly by his oath.'"],[4482,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he prostrated, placing his forehead and nose on the ground."],[4483,"A woman was coerced during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he waived the punishment for the woman and imposed it on the one who had intercourse with her. It was not mentioned that he assigned her a dower."],[4484,"He prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, who recited the Opening of the Book. When he said, 'nor of those who go astray,' he said: 'Amin,' raising his voice with it."],[4485,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with long hair. He said: 'Dhubbab (a lock of hair).' So I went and cut it, then came back. He said: 'I did not mean you; this is better.'"],[4486,"When he prayed and wanted to prostrate, his knees fell to the ground before his hands; and when he rose, he raised his knees before his hands."],[4487,"I witnessed a man brought forward, led by a strap, who had killed another man. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain: 'Will you pardon?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you accept blood money?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then will you kill him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then go.' He said: So he went with him. When he was not far, he called him and said: 'Will you pardon?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you accept blood money?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you kill him?' He said: 'Yes.' And he went with him until he did that several times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he kills him, then he is like him.'"],[4488,"I watched the Prophet ﷺ. When he began the prayer, he raised his hands until they reached his ears and said the takbir. Then he placed his right hand over his left. When he bowed, he raised his hands, and he raised his hands when he rose. When he sat in the second rak'ah on his left foot, he folded it under him, then erected his right foot, placed his right hand on his right thigh, his left hand on his left thigh, and formed a circle with his right index finger."],[4489,"It reached us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared while we were in a great kingdom and obedience, so I abandoned it and went out desiring Allah and His Messenger. When I arrived before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he had already given them the good news of my coming. When I came to him and greeted him, he returned my greeting, spread his cloak for me, and seated me on it. Then he ascended his pulpit and seated me with him. He raised his hand, praised Allah, extolled Him, and invoked blessings upon the prophets. The people gathered around him, and he said to them: 'O people, this is Wa'il b. Hujr who has come to you from a distant land, from Hadramawt, willingly not under compulsion, desiring Allah and His Messenger and His religion, a remnant of the sons of kings.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is only that your appearance reached us while we were in a great kingdom and great obedience, so I came to you desiring Allah and His Messenger and His religion.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[4490,"He forbade the practice of shighar."],[4491,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when a vessel containing water was brought to him. He tilted it over his right hand three times, then dipped his right hand into the water and washed his left hand with it three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the water and scooped up a handful, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nostrils three times and blew it out. Then he inserted both palms into the vessel and raised them to his face, washing his face three times. He washed the inside of his ears, inserted his two fingers into the inside of his ears, and wiped the back of his neck and the inside of his beard three times. Then he inserted his right hand into the water and washed his right forearm with it until it passed the elbow, three times. Then he washed his left forearm with his right hand until it passed the elbow, three times. Then he wiped over his head three times, the outside of his ears three times, and the back of his neck, and I think he said: and the outside of his beard three times. Then with his right hand he washed his right foot three times, parted between his toes—or he said: ran his fingers between them—and raised the water until it passed the ankle, then raised it up the shin. Then he did the same with the left foot. Then he took a handful of water, filled his hand with it, and placed it on his head until the water flowed down its sides. He said: 'This is the complete ablution.' I did not see him dry himself with a cloth. Then he rose to the mosque and entered the mihrab—meaning the place of the mihrab—and lined up the people behind him and to his right and left. Then he raised his hands until they were level with the lobes of his ears, then placed his right hand over his left on his chest. Then he began the recitation aloud with al-Hamd. When he finished Surat al-Hamd, he said 'Amin' so that those behind him heard it. Then he recited another surah. Then he raised his hands with the takbir until they were level with the lobes of his ears, then bowed and placed his hands on his knees, spreading his fingers. He paused in the bowing until he was straight and his back became such that if a bowl of water were placed on it, it would not spill. Then he raised his head ﷺ with humility and said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him.' Then he raised his hands until they were level with the lobes of his ears, then descended for prostration with the takbir, raising his hands until they were level with the lobes of his ears. Then he fixed his forehead on the ground until I could see his nose in the sand, curved his forearms and head, spread his left thigh, and stood his right foot, fixing the toes of his feet. He did not prolong the prostration, then raised his head, raising his hands with the takbir until they were level with the lobes of his ears, and sat briefly. He placed his right palm on his knee and part of his thigh, and made a circle with his finger. Then he descended to prostrate similarly, then raised his head with the takbir, raising his hands until they were level with the lobes of his ears, until he stood upright and every bone returned to its place. Then he prayed four rak'ahs, doing in them what he did in this one. Then he sat for the tashahhud in the same manner. Then he said the salam to his right until the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen, and said the salam to his left until the whiteness of his right cheek could be seen. This hadith, we do not know it being narrated with this wording except from Wa'il b. Hujr with this chain."],[4492,"I carefully observed the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ and saw him raise his hands when he said the takbir, then place one hand over the other. Then when he intended to bow, he raised his hands and said the takbir. Then he said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' and raised them. I was unsure whether he raised them when he prostrated or not. He said: He prayed two rak'ahs. When he sat for the tashahhud, he spread his left leg, placed his right hand on his thigh, then clasped his fingers, then made a circle and pointed with his index finger. He said the salam to his right and to his left. He said: And I saw him say the takbir whenever he went down and came up."],[4493,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and a girl from the Ansar was on a camel of hers. She looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ behind her and the mountain had become narrow for them, so she said: 'Hal! Hal! May the curse of Allah be upon you'—meaning her camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who is the owner of this camel, or this mount? No camel carrying the curse of Allah should accompany us.'"],[4494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the enemy and Allah granted him spoils. He said: 'Do you miss anyone?' They said: 'Yes, so-and-so and so-and-so.' Then he said: 'Do you miss anyone?' a second and third time. They said: 'No.' He said: 'But I miss Julaybib. Go and look for him among the slain.' They looked for him and found him beside seven whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, so he came and stood over him and said: 'This one is from me and I am from him. He killed seven. This one is from me and I am from him'—he said it twice. Then he carried him on his forearms, with no bier except the forearms of the Prophet ﷺ, until a grave was dug for him and he was buried, and he did not mention washing him."],[4495,"I wished to meet a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to ask him about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah on a day of 'Id among a group of his companions. I said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own ears and saw him with my own eyes. Wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave to those on his right and those on his left, but did not give those behind him anything. A man from behind him stood up and said: 'O Muhammad, by Allah, you have not been just to me today.' He was a black man with shaved hair, wearing two white garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became very angry and said: 'By Allah, you will not find after me a man more just to you than me.' Then he said: 'In the last days, there will come a people, as if this man is from among them. They recite the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They pass through Islam as an arrow passes through its target. Their mark is shaving. They will keep emerging until the last of them comes out with the false Messiah, the Dajjal. So when you meet them, kill them. They are the worst of creation and creatures.'"],[4496,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[4497,"Hisham b. Hassan narrated to us, from Jamil b. Murrah, from Abu al-Wadi', from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4498,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something from which I may benefit. He said: 'Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims.'"],[4499,"I have a cistern between Aylah and Sana'a, its width like its length. Two spouts from Paradise pour into it, one of silver and the other of gold. Its water is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and colder than snow. In it are vessels as numerous as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst until he enters Paradise."],[4500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man to a tribe among the Arab tribes. They reviled him and beat him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: 'If you had come to the people of Oman, they would not have beaten you or reviled you.'"],[4501,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he sat and wanted to get up, would say: \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you are saying words that you did not use to say before.\" He said: \"This is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering.\""],[4502,"He forbade sleeping before it (the night prayer) and talking after it."],[4503,"Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And the hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha', from al-Mughirah b. Abi Barzah, from his father, I think 'Uthman b. 'Uthman erred in it, and the correct version is: Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah. Abu al-Minhal's name is Sayyar b. Salamah."],[4504,"\"The rulers are from Quraysh. I have a right over them, and they have a right over you as long as they do three things: when mercy is sought from them, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[4505,"\"Indeed, what I fear for you are the desires of error in your bellies and your private parts, and the misguidances of whims.\""],[4506,"\"Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it.\""],[4507,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from al-Mughirah b. Abi Barzah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from Abu Barzah except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ali b. Zayd except Shu'bah."],[4508,"I saw Abu Barzah when Ibn Ziyad sent for him asking him about the Hawd (the Pond). He said: Someone who entered with him informed me. He said: When Ibn Ziyad saw him, he said: \"This Muhammadan of yours is short and stout.\" When Abu Barzah heard it, he said: \"I never thought I would live to be reproached for the companionship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: It was said to him: \"You are not reproached for that.\" He said: Ibn Ziyad asked him about the Hawd, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say - I think he said: \"I will have a pond; whoever denies it, may Allah not let him reach it,\" meaning it."],[4509,"I said to Abu Barzah ؓ: \"Whom did the Prophet ﷺ stone?\" He said: \"A man from among us called Ma'iz b. Malik.\""],[4510,"\"The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.\""],[4511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at two men at Uhud who were reciting poetry about Hamzah: \"You left a companion whose bones gleam; war turned away from him so that he could be buried.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, topple them headlong into dissension and drive them harshly to the punishment.\""],[4512,"He performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[4513,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[4514,"I went on such-and-such a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ—until he counted eight expeditions—and we saw nothing from him but ease and lightening (of burdens)."],[4515,"\"Has any of you seen a dream?\" Then whoever God willed would relate it to him. He said: And one morning he said to us: \"Two visitors came to me and sent me (on a journey), and they said to me: 'Go.' So I went with them.\" And al-Muʿtamir said in his hadith: \"Two visitors came to me last night and said to me: 'Go.' So I went with them.\" Then they came upon a man lying down, with another man standing over him holding a rock. He was raising the rock and smashing his head with it, splitting his head open. The rock would roll away, and he would follow it, pick it up, and not return to him until his head had healed and become as it was before. Then he would return to him and do to him as he had done the first time. He said: I said: \"Glory be to God! What is this?\" They said to me: \"Go on, go on.\" So I went with them, and we came upon a man lying on his back, with another man standing over him holding an iron hook. He would come to one side of his face and tear his cheek from his mouth-corner to the back of his neck, and his nostril to the back of his neck, and his eye to the back of his neck. Then he would turn to the other side and do to it as he had done to the first side. He would not finish that side before the first had healed and become as it was. Then he would return and do to him as he had done the first time. He said: I said: \"Glory be to God! What is this?\" They said: \"Go on, go on.\" So I went on, and we came upon something like the structure of a tannur (oven). ʿAwf said: And I think he said: In it there was clamor and voices of men and women. Flames would come to them from below, and when the flames reached them, they would cry out. He said: I said: \"Who are these?\" They said to me: \"Go on, go on.\" So we went on, and we came upon a river—I think he said—red like blood. In the river there was a man swimming, and on the bank of the river there was a man who had gathered many stones. The swimming man would swim for a while, then come to the one who had gathered the stones, who would open his mouth and put a stone in it. He said: I said: \"What is this?\" They said to me: \"Go on, go on.\" So we went on, and we came upon a man with a hideous appearance, tending a fire and walking around it. He said: I said to them: \"What is this?\" They said to me: \"Go on, go on.\" So we went on, and we came upon a lush meadow containing every kind of spring blossom. In the middle of the meadow stood a tall man, and around him were more children than I had ever seen. I think he said: I said to them: \"What is this, or who are these?\" They said to me: \"Go on, go on.\" So we went on, and we came to a great staircase, the greatest and most beautiful I had ever seen. He said: They said to me: \"Climb it.\" So I climbed, and we came to a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver. We came to the gate of the city and asked for it to be opened, and it was opened for us. We entered, and we were met by men half of whose bodies were the most beautiful you could see, and the other half the ugliest you could see. He said: They said to them: \"Go and plunge into that river.\" There was a river flowing across, its water as pure white as milk. So they went and plunged into it, then returned to us with the ugliness gone and in the best of forms. He said: They said to me: \"This is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling.\" He said: My gaze rose upward, and there was a palace like a white cloud. He said: They said to me: \"This is your dwelling.\" I said: \"May God bless you both. Let me enter it.\" They said to me: \"Not now, but you will enter it.\" I said: \"I have seen wonders since last night. What is this that I have seen?\" They said to me: \"We will tell you. The first man you came upon, whose head was being smashed with a rock, is a man who takes the Quran and then abandons it, and sleeps through the prescribed prayer. The man you came upon whose cheek, eye, and nostril were being torn to the back of his neck is a man who leaves his house in the morning and tells a lie that spreads to the horizons. The naked men and women in the structure like a tannur are the adulterers and adulteresses. The man swimming in the river and being fed stones is the consumer of riba (usury). The hideous-looking man tending the fire is the keeper of Hell. The tall man in the meadow is Ibrahim ﷺ . The children around him are every newborn who died upon the fitrah (natural disposition). The people half of whom were beautiful and half ugly are a people who mixed a righteous deed with an evil one, and God, Blessed and Exalted, has forgiven them.\" [As in the printed edition of Maktabat al-ʿUlum wa-l-Hikam; perhaps the correct reading is \"Ibn al-Sabbah,\" and God knows best.]"],[4516,"When he had prayed the morning prayer, he would turn his face toward us and say: \"Has any of you seen a dream?\""],[4517,"Every newborn is born on the fitrah, and his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[4518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: \"They are servants of the people of Paradise.\""],[4519,"ʿAwf narrated to us, from Abu Rajaʾ, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4520,"The woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her; and if you enjoy her, you enjoy her while she has some crookedness."],[4521,"Wear white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[4522,"The best of your garments are white: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[4523,"Wear white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[4524,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a woman who died in childbirth. He stood and prayed over her, and he stood in the middle of her body."],[4525,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ibn Buraydah, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. And we do not know that anyone transmitted this hadith except Samurah, and we do not know that anyone transmitted it from Shu'bah except Abu Qutaybah."],[4526,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Zayd b. 'Uqbah, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4527,"'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Zayd b. 'Uqbah, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4528,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Zayd b. 'Uqbah, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4529,"\"Indeed these requests are scratches on a man's face, so whoever wishes may preserve his face, unless he comes to a person of authority or a matter from which he finds no alternative.\""],[4530,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Ma'bad b. Khalid, from Zayd b. 'Uqbah, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4531,"He used to recite in the two 'Eid prayers Sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la and Hal ataka hadithu al-ghashiyah."],[4532,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"What do you think about the lizard?\" He said, \"A nation that was transformed, and Allah knows best.\" He said: And 'Uyaynah b. Badr entered and saw a cupper cupping the Prophet ﷺ with a horn, so he said, \"You allow this one to cut your flesh?\" He said, \"Cupping is the best of what you treat yourselves with.\""],[4533,"Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from Abu Qaza'ah - and he is Suwayd b. Hujayr - from al-Asqa' b. al-Asla', from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet."],[4534,"\"What is below the two ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire.\""],[4535,"He forbade prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil."],[4536,"\"Do not name your boy Aflah, Najih, Yasar, or Rabah, for when you say, 'Is he there? Is so-and-so there?' they will say, 'No.'\""],[4537,"Four are the best of speech, and it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah), wal-hamdu lillah (praise be to Allah), wa la ilaha illa Allah (there is no god but Allah), wa Allahu akbar (and Allah is the Greatest)."],[4538,"Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he thinks it is false, then he is one of the liars."],[4539,"It is near that Allah will fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then He will make them lions who do not flee, and they will fight your fighters and consume your spoils."],[4540,"The neighbor of a house is more entitled to the house."],[4541,"The neighbor of a house is more entitled to the house or to the land."],[4542,"Yunus b. 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4543,"Whoever performs wudu' on Friday, then it is good and sufficient, and whoever performs ghusl, then ghusl is better."],[4544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two pauses: a pause when he began the prayer, and a pause when he finished his recitation."],[4545,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to pray at night, whether little or much, and to make the last of that witr."],[4546,"He used to command one of us to pray every night after the obligatory prayer, whether little or much, and to make - I think he said - the last of that witr."],[4547,"Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Yunus b. 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4548,"Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him."],[4549,"Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."],[4550,"The hand is responsible for what it takes until it returns it."],[4551,"Every boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah, which is slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, and he is named and his head is shaved."],[4552,"Sam is the father of the Arabs, Ham is the father of the Abyssinians, and Yafith is the father of the Romans."],[4553,"When one of you comes upon livestock, if the owner is present, let him call out to him. If he gives permission, let him milk and drink. If no one is present, let him call out three times; if someone answers him, then no, otherwise let him milk and drink but not carry away."],[4554,"Whoever encloses a wall around a piece of land, it belongs to him."],[4555,"Any woman whom two guardians give in marriage, she belongs to the first of them, and any man who sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them."],[4556,"The middle prayer is the 'Asr prayer."],[4557,"Khalid b. al-Harith and 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, they said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4558,"He prohibited selling an animal for another animal on credit."],[4559,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[4560,"And 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated it to us, from Hammad b. Salamah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. This hadith was narrated from Qatadah by a group, including Hisham b. Abi 'Abd Allah and Abu 'Awanah and others."],[4561,"My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4562,"\"Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with His wrath, nor with the Fire.\""],[4563,"We were caught by rain—or we were caught by a sky—while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: 'Indeed the prayer is to be performed in the dwellings.'"],[4564,"He forbade celibacy."],[4565,"\"The Quran was revealed in three modes.\""],[4566,"The Quran was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times. He said: 'They hold that'—he said—'I do not know whether in this hadith or another that our recitation is the final presentation.'"],[4567,"\"Whoever owns a close relative who is mahram, then he is free.\""],[4568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to greet our imams, and that some of us should greet one another during the prayer."],[4569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[4570,"\"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[4571,"\"Do not live alongside the polytheists; whoever lives alongside them is one of them.\""],[4572,"Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4573,"He forbade cutting the strap between two fingers."],[4574,"Suwayd b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4575,"When he prayed for rain, he would say: \"O Allah, place in our land its beauty and its tranquility.\""],[4576,"\"Kill the elderly of the polytheists and spare their young.\""],[4577,"The watchword of the Muhajirun was 'Abd Allah, and the watchword of the Ansar was 'Abd al-Rahman — meaning: during war — at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4578,"\"A man shall not propose to a woman to whom his brother has already proposed, nor shall he sell over the sale of his brother.\""],[4579,"This verse was revealed — 'This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you' — upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Arafah on a Friday."],[4580,"\"Nobility is wealth, and honor is piety.\""],[4581,"\"The deceased is punished because of the wailing over him.\""],[4582,"\"When Hawwa' became pregnant, Iblis circled her, and no child of hers would survive. He said: 'Name him 'Abd al-Harith, for he will live.' So she named him 'Abd al-Harith, and he lived. That was from the inspiration of Satan and his command.\""],[4583,"\"If a man becomes bankrupt, and another man finds his exact property with him, he has more right to it than the other creditors.\""],[4584,"\"Al-Firdaws is the highest part of Paradise. When you ask Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, ask Him for al-Firdaws.\""],[4585,"Satan has kohl and a lick. When he applies kohl to a person from his kohl, he distracts him from prayer; and when he makes him lick from his lick, his tongue becomes sharp with evil."],[4586,"Saʿīd b. Bashīr narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. And this statement—we do not know that anyone narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ except Samurah and Anas, nor do we know that anyone narrated it from Qatādah except al-Ḥakam b. ʿAbd al-Malik and Saʿīd b. Bashīr."],[4587,"The example of one who goes early to the Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, until he reaches the chicken and the egg, or something like that."],[4588,"He forbade tawarruk and iqʿāʾ, and that we should not sit on our heels (istawfaza) in our prayer, and that a city-dweller should not pray behind a desert Arab."],[4589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to sit on our heels (istawfaza) in our prayer."],[4590,"Ḥammād b. Salamah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas. And this ḥadīth—I think that Yaḥyā b. Isḥāq made a mistake in it. As for Saʿīd b. Bashīr, no ḥadīth of his is used as evidence when he alone narrates it. The preserved ḥadīth is the one narrated by Ḥammād b. Salamah and others, from Qatādah, from Anas, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"When one of you prays, let him not spread his forearms like a dog or a beast of prey spreads them.\" This is the ḥadīth as we have it, and Allah knows best."],[4591,"\"The best jihād is to speak a word of truth before a ruler,\" or he said, \"before a tyrannical ruler.\""],[4592,"The food of one person is enough for two, and the food of two is enough for four, and the hand of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is over the group."],[4593,"Do not take anything that has a soul as a target."],[4594,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[4595,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: You and your property belong to your father."],[4596,"When you come to the Friday prayer, draw near to the imam, listen to the sermon, and do not engage in idle talk."],[4597,"The boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah, so remove harm from him and shave his head."],[4598,"He forbade intercepting caravans (ajlab) before they reach the market, and he forbade a resident selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[4599,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah."],[4600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never delivered a sermon to us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[4601,"Fever is a piece of the punishment — and he mentioned a word meaning — so extinguish it from yourselves with cold water. He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a fever, he would call for a waterskin of water and pour it over his head and bathe."],[4602,"Do not precede the imam in bowing, for you will catch up with him by what he has preceded you with."],[4603,"When one of you becomes drowsy on Friday, let him move to his companion's place and let his companion move to his place. It was said to Isma'il: Even while the imam is delivering the sermon? He said: Yes."],[4604,"Do not deliberately aim your prayers at sunrise or sunset, for it rises between the two horns of a devil and sets between the two horns of a devil."],[4605,"The greatest regrets of the children of Adam in this world are three: A man who has land that is irrigated and he has a water-lifting device with which he irrigates his land. When it became strong and produced its fruit, his water-lifting device died, so he feels regret over his device which he knows he will not find its like, and he feels regret over the fruit of his land that it will spoil before he can find a solution. And a man who has a swift horse and he meets a group of disbelievers. When they drew near to one another, the enemies of Allah were defeated, and the man sped ahead on his horse, so he feels regret that he will not find its like, and he feels regret over the victory that he had been close to attaining but missed. And a man who has a wife whose appearance and religion he is pleased with, and she gives birth to a boy, and she dies in her postpartum bleeding, so he feels regret over his wife, thinking that he will never find her like, and he feels regret over his child, fearing his loss before he finds someone to nurse him. These are the greatest of those regrets."],[4606,"Khubayb b. Sulayman narrated to me, from his father Sulayman b. Samurah, from Samurah b. Jundub, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu Bakr said: We do not know of this statement being narrated except from Samurah from the Prophet."],[4607,"He wrote to his sons: From Samurah b. Jundub, peace be upon you. I praise Allah, besides whom there is no deity, to you. To proceed: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, that you establish prayer, give zakah, avoid wicked things, and obey Allah, His Messenger, and the caliphs who uphold the command of Allah. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to pray at night, or that one of us pray after the prescribed prayer whether little or much, and make it an odd number (witr)."],[4608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to pray at whatever hour of night or day we wished, except that he commanded us to avoid sunrise and sunset, and he said: Indeed, the devil disappears when it sets and rises with it when it rises."],[4609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to guard all the prayers, and he commanded us regarding the middle prayer, and he said: \"Indeed it is the 'Asr prayer.\""],[4610,"He forbade us from continuous fasting in the month of fasting, but it is not a firm command."],[4611,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us that some of us should greet others when we meet."],[4612,"And he ﷺ forbade us from invoking curses by the curse of Allah and His wrath, and he forbade us from invoking curses by the Fire."],[4613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from reviling one another, and he said: \"If one of you must revile his companion, then let him not go too far, and let him not revile his parents, nor his people. But if he knows that, let him say: 'You are arrogant,' or let him say: 'You are cowardly,' or let him say: 'You are a liar,' or let him say: 'You are miserly.'\""],[4614,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to recite the Qur'an as he taught us to recite it, and he said: \"It was revealed in three modes, so do not differ over it and do not turn away from it, for it is entirely blessed. Recite it as you have been taught to recite it.\""],[4615,"He used to command us that if one of us slept through a prayer or forgot it until its time for praying had passed, he should pray it with the following prescribed prayer."],[4616,"He used to command us that if we caught the prayer and we were three, one of us should lead us."],[4617,"\"When you stand for prayer, do not precede your reciter in bowing and prostrating, but he should precede you. Then when it is time for the salam, send peace upon the prophets, then send peace upon your reciter and upon yourselves.\""],[4618,"He used to command them, when they were in prayer, not to rest on the tips of their feet. And he said: \"If one of you spits during prayer, let him not spit in front of his face or to his right, but under his foot, then rub it with the earth.\""],[4619,"\"When two men engage in a transaction, each of them has the option until they part from one another, and each one chooses what he desires regarding the sale.\""],[4620,"He used to forbid women from lying down with one another except while there were clothes or a cloth between them, and a man should not lie down with his companion except while there was a cloth between them."],[4621,"He used to forbid a Muslim from unsheathing a weapon against another Muslim."],[4622,"The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[4623,"Any of you who prepares food enough for two men, it will suffice three; or prepares food enough for four, it will suffice five."],[4624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to build mosques in our homes, and to clean and purify them, if Allah wills."],[4625,"He used to command us to attend the Friday prayer and not to be absent from it, and he said: 'One of you is more entitled to his seat when he returns to it.'"],[4626,"If one of you becomes drowsy on Friday, let him move from his seat to another place."],[4627,"A man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for a ruling about what is forbidden for him and what is lawful for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Lawful for you are good things, and forbidden for you are impure things, unless you are compelled to eat food that is not lawful for you, then eat from it until you are no longer in need.'"],[4628,"He used to command us not to give charity from slaves."],[4629,"If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little."],[4630,"He used to say to us: When one of you prays, let him say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You have distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from turning Your face away from me on the Day of Resurrection. O Allah, cleanse me of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt. O Allah, cause me to live as a Muslim and cause me to die as a Muslim."],[4631,"He used to say to us: One of you is about to wish to look at me once, which would be dearer to him than all his wealth."],[4632,"He used to say to us: You will soon be among people like salt in food, and food is only sound with salt."],[4633,"\"There is no man among you but that I am holding onto his waist-wrapper lest he fall into the Fire.\""],[4634,"He used to forbid plundering."],[4635,"\"The Hour will not come until the stone points out the Jew, and it says: 'O servant of God, here is a Jew behind me' — I think he said that.\""],[4636,"\"The false Messiah (al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl) is blind in the left eye, upon it a thick white film. He heals the one born blind and revives the dead, and he says: 'I am your Lord.' So whoever clings to God and says: 'My Lord is God' until he dies, then there is no punishment upon him; and whoever says: 'You are my Lord,' then he has been put to trial.\""],[4637,"\"The false Messiah will remain on the earth, when he comes out, for as long as God wills. Then Jesus son of Mary ﷺ will come from the east, affirming Muhammad ﷺ and upon his religion, and he will kill the false Messiah. Then it is only after the coming of the Hour, and you will see before the Hour comes tremendous things, and you will say: 'Have we [seen such]?'\""],[4638,"\"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to cut off the limb of his slave or castrate him. Whoever does that to him, the like will be done to him.\""],[4639,"He used to enjoin entertaining guests, and he forbade us to milk a man's livestock except with his permission. And he would say: \"Its milk is just like what is in your bowls\" — or a word similar to it — \"one of them is not more lawful than the other.\""],[4640,"\"The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death of any one of you, but they are two signs among the signs of God by which He admonishes His servants, so that He may see who fears Him and who remembers Him. So when you see that, hasten to the remembrance of God and remember Him.\""],[4641,"\"Do not go out to meet the caravans before they reach their market, and do not sell on behalf of the Bedouins, even if it is the brother of one of you, or his father, or his mother.\""],[4642,"\"Whoever sells land or a house, the neighbor of the house or the land is more entitled to it.\""],[4643,"\"When two men both marry the same woman, the more entitled of the two husbands is the first of them. And in the case of a sale, when two men purchase the same commodity, the more entitled of them is the first of them.\""],[4644,"He used to forbid the practice of shighār between women."],[4645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid, when they were three, that two of them should hold a private conversation apart from the third."],[4646,"He used to command us when we went on a military expedition and a man called out to the rest of the people, saying, “O first one,” that we should wait for him until he caught up."],[4647,"He used to command the Emigrants to go forward and to be at the front of the rows, and he would say: “They are more knowledgeable about the prayer than the foolish and the Bedouins, and I do not like the Bedouins to be in front of them when they do not know how to pray.”"],[4648,"He used to forbid, when a man was invited to a meal, that he should invite anyone else with him unless the people of the meal ordered him to."],[4649,"“In Paradise there is a tree standing alone on a single trunk; the width of its trunk is seventy-two years.”"],[4650,"“The name of the man is al-karm (generosity), because of what God has honored him with over creation. You call the grapevine karm, but its name is al-jawhar (essence); it is the man who is al-karm.”"],[4651,"“Al-Firdaws is the central elevation of Paradise, which is its highest and most beautiful part.”"],[4652,"“A man’s soul is never filled with wealth until it is filled with dust. If one of you had a valley full of what is between its top and bottom, he would love to have another valley filled for him. If the other valley were filled, he would go off and find another valley and say: ‘By God, if I could, I would fill you too.’”"],[4653,"“I find among animals: one animal is better than a hundred, and among men: one man is better than a hundred men.”"],[4654,"When he went on a military expedition or traveled and then returned heading back to Madinah, he would say: “Returning, praising our Lord, worshiping.”"],[4655,"On the day they arrived at the Hijr of Thamud, he forbade them from a well near the side of the city that anyone should drink from it or draw water, and he forbade us to enter their houses."],[4656,"“Beware of exaggeration! For many of the Children of Israel went to extremes, until a short woman would take two wooden clogs and stuff them, then insert her feet into them, then stand beside a tall woman and walk with her, and there she was equal to her or taller than her.”"],[4657,"When he prayed for rain, he would say: “O Allah, place in our land its adornment; O Allah, place in our land its tranquility.”"],[4658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them on the Day of the Conquest: “This year the greater pilgrimage—the Hajj of the Muslims and the Hajj of the polytheists—has come together in three consecutive days, and the Hajj of the Christians and the Jews has come together in six consecutive days; it has not come together since the heavens and the earth were created, and it will not come together after this year until the Hour arises.”"],[4659,"“Ghifār—may Allah forgive it; and Aslam—may Allah grant it peace.”"],[4660,"“Do not swear by the idols, and do not swear by your fathers, but swear by Allah.”"],[4661,"“The Arabs are the descendants of Sām b. Nūḥ, the Byzantines are the descendants of Yāfith b. Nūḥ, and the Abyssinians are the descendants of Ḥām b. Nūḥ.”"],[4662,"“When the polytheists fight you, kill their old men and spare their young men.”"],[4663,"“Two months do not complete sixty nights.”"],[4664,"When he cursed the polytheists in prayer, he would begin with Quraysh, then after that he would follow them with many tribes of the Arabs. It was said to him: “Curse the disbelievers of Quraysh.” So the Prophet ﷺ, when he wanted to curse, would say: “O Allah, curse the disbelievers of Banū So-and-so.”"],[4665,"“It was said to me: ‘Recite to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb,’ so he called and commanded him to attend to the Qurʾān when it descended, so that he might recite it to him.”"],[4666,"He would seek forgiveness for the believing men and believing women, and the Muslim men and Muslim women, every Friday."],[4667,"“Abū Bakr interprets dreams, and a righteous dream is a portion of prophethood.”"],[4668,"“Whoever kills someone, the slain person’s belongings are his.”"],[4669,"Whoever of you is killed patiently, being killed in the path of Allah, then he will be in Paradise."],[4670,"There is no envy in this world except in two cases: a man who envies another man because Allah has given him abundant wealth and he spends from it and gives much in charity, so the other says, 'If I had wealth like this man's, I would spend like he spends, and I would spend it on the same things he spends on'—so he envies him. And a man whom Allah has taught the Qur'an—I think he said—so he stands in prayer reciting it, and another says, 'If Allah had taught me like this, I would stand in prayer as he does.'"],[4671,"The example of a woman is like a rib; if one tries to straighten the rib, he cannot straighten it until he breaks it, and she is crooked."],[4672,"You will be gathered to the Holy House, then you will assemble on the Day of Resurrection."],[4673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the battle cry of the Emigrants 'O Banu 'Abd al-Rahman,' the battle cry of Banu al-Khazraj 'O Banu 'Abd Allah,' and the battle cry of al-Aws 'O Banu 'Ubayd Allah.'"],[4674,"Seventy thousand will enter Paradise without reckoning—I think he said—from this Ummah."],[4675,"He used to command us, when we were afraid, to come together, be patient, and be calm, and when we fought."],[4676,"He used to forbid the owner of palm trees from borrowing against the fruit of his palm trees until some of its fruit could be eaten, for fear that he might incur a large debt and then the fruit would spoil. And he used to forbid the owner of crops from borrowing against his crops until the harvest was ready."],[4677,"By Allah, it would not please me to have a mountain of gold, all of it."],[4678,"A man came to the Messenger ﷺ seeking his ruling about eating lizard. He said, 'I do not command it, nor do I forbid it.'"],[4679,"He forbade us from eating domestic donkeys, and he ordered us to throw away what we had of it, so we threw it away."],[4680,"One of you has three friends on the day he dies: one of them prevents him from what he asks for—that is his wealth. One of them is a friend who goes with him until he enters the grave, but does not give him anything or prevent him—those are his relatives. And one of them is a friend who says, 'I am with you; I will go with you wherever you go, and I will never part from you'—that is his deeds, whether good or evil."],[4681,"He used to forbid that a man cut the strap between his two fingers, or he used to forbid any of us to cut the strap between his two fingers."],[4682,"If a man makes a claim against another and one of them calls his companion to the one who will judge between them, but he refuses to come, then he has no right."],[4683,"When we were rained upon during travel and the call to prayer was given, he would order the muezzin to call out: 'Pray in your dwellings'; out of dislike that he should cause hardship for us."],[4684,"Azhar b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[4685,"Those who pledged allegiance under the tree will surely enter Paradise, except the owner of the red camel."],[4687,"When one of you lies on his back, he should not place one of his legs over the other."],[4688,"Ali ؓ was brought some people from the Zutt and he wanted to burn them. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever changes his religion, kill him.'"],[4689,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'Your people claim that the Prophet ﷺ walked briskly and that it is a sunnah.' He said: 'They have lied and they have spoken truth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did walk briskly, but it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived while the polytheists were on Mount Qu'ayqi'an. It reached him that they were saying: There is weakness in the Messenger of Allah and his companions. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked briskly and ordered his companions to walk briskly so that the polytheists would see that they had strength.'"],[4690,"Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4691,"Al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Fitr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the arrival of the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through several routes, and it has been narrated from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn 'Abbas, through more than one route. In those we have mentioned there is sufficiency, except that Yazid has additional wording not mentioned by others, so it is written for the sake of the addition."],[4692,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Makkah and said: 'You are the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah, and were it not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have left.'"],[4693,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only touched the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner. Mu'awiyah said: 'Nothing of the House is to be abandoned,' and he touched all the corners."],[4694,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4695,"Ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Abi 'Aruba, from Qatada, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4696,"Al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Ali, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4697,"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."],[4698,"Whoever departs from the community by the measure of a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck; and whoever dies without having an imam, his death is a death of ignorance; and whoever dies under a banner of blind partisanship, calling to a faction or supporting a faction, his killing is a killing of ignorance."],[4699,"Whoever goes to his debtor with his right, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the water pray for him, and for every step a tree is planted for him in Paradise and a sin is forgiven."],[4700,"The delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people from Rabi'a, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in the sacred month, so command us with a matter that if we do it we will enter Paradise and call to it those behind us. So he commanded them and forbade them from four things: to worship Allah without associating anything with Him, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to fast Ramadan, to perform Hajj to the House, and to give the fifth from the spoils. And he forbade them from hantam, dubba', muzaffat, and naqir. They said: In what shall we drink? He said: Drink from those whose mouths are tied with a cord."],[4701,"'Abd al-Warith, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4702,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[4703,"My father narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Abi Ja'far, from Ayyub, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4704,"Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4705,"Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[4706,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven [bones] and not to tuck back my hair or my garment."],[4707,"The Prophet ﷺ did not prohibit leasing land, but he said: \"For a man to grant his brother his land [for cultivation] is better for him than taking a fixed rent for it.\""],[4708,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ in similar form through various channels, and this is one of the best chains transmitted regarding that."],[4709,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while in a state of ihram."],[4710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited selling fruits until they become ripe (i.e., safe from blight)."],[4711,"Every condition not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it be a hundred conditions."],[4712,"Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Tawus, from the Prophet ﷺ, without mentioning Ibn 'Abbas. We do not know of anyone who corroborated 'Amr b. Yahya in his narration from 'Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas. This wording is narrated from someone other than Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4713,"All of 'Arafah is a standing place, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice."],[4714,"From Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, except that Hawtharah [narrated it with this chain]; we do not know of anyone who corroborated him regarding that. The hadith is well-known from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, narrated through various channels, except that it is not transmitted from 'Amr, from Tawus except through this route."],[4715,"A Bedouin gave a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave him something in return. He said to him: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" Then he increased it and said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" Then he increased it and said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ then said: \"I had considered not accepting a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, or a Thaqafi.\""],[4716,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah transmitted it to us from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr, from Tawus, from the Prophet ﷺ. We do not know of this wording being transmitted from Ibn 'Abbas except through this route, and we do not recall anyone narrating it from Yunus, from Hammad except Ibrahim b. Sa'id. Some of our companions mentioned that Mujahid b. Musa also narrated it from Yunus, thus corroborating Ibrahim in his chain."],[4717,"Whoever is killed in blind violence — or he said: \"in blind violence\" — with a stone, a whip, or a stick, then upon [the killer] is the blood-money for accidental killing. Whoever is killed deliberately, then retaliation is due. And whoever intervenes between [the killer and retaliation], upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him."],[4718,"The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit."],[4719,"These words are a protection from every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and in all His names, in general, from the evil of what is venomous and what is common, and from the evil of the evil eye, and from the evil of the envious when he envies, and from the evil of every possessor of evil and what he has begotten. Thirty-three angels came with them, and he said: 'The pain has intensified.' Then he said: 'Take some dust from your land and wipe your foreheads.' And in it: whoever takes a bribe for it or conceals it from anyone will never succeed."],[4720,"That Ali ؓ handed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some dust, and he threw it in the faces of the polytheists on the day of Hunayn."],[4721,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Jibril to show himself in his true form. He said: 'Call upon your Lord.' So he called upon his Lord, and he appeared to him from the direction of the east, and he began to rise and move. When he saw him, he fell unconscious, and then he came to him."],[4722,"When the sun began to decline and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at a stopping place, he would combine the Zuhr and Asr prayers. If the sun had not declined before he set out, he would travel until the time of Asr, then he would stop and combine the Zuhr and Asr prayers. And when the sun set for him, he would combine the Maghrib and Isha prayers at his stopping place. And if he set out before sunset, he would travel until the twilight disappeared, then he would stop and combine the Maghrib and Isha prayers."],[4723,"When your brothers were killed, Allah placed their souls in the insides of green birds that come to the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and take shelter in lanterns hanging in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food and drink, they said: 'If only they knew what honor Allah has bestowed upon us.' Allah, blessed and exalted, said: 'I shall inform them about you.' So Allah revealed: 'And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision, rejoicing in what Allah has bestowed upon them of His bounty, and they receive good tidings about those who have not yet joined them from behind them, that there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.'"],[4724,"The east wind came to the north wind and said: 'Command me so that we may support the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The north wind said: 'The hot wind does not blow at night.' So the wind with which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was supported was the east wind."],[4725,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My sister has died and she owed two consecutive months of fasting.' He said: 'Tell me, if your sister had a debt, would you pay it?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then the right of Allah is more deserving of being fulfilled.'"],[4726,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the nabidh of the earthen jar."],[4727,"Regarding 'while you are proudly neglectful' (wa-antum samidun), he said: 'It means singing.'"],[4728,"The example of the one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like that of a donkey carrying books."],[4729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking among the palm trees in Madinah, and people began saying: 'There is a sa' in it, and there is a wasq in it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is such and such in it.' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I am only a human being. Whatever I tell you from Allah is the truth, but whatever I say on my own, I am only a human being; I may be right and I may be wrong.'"],[4730,"I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and at Your command. He said: About what do the highest assembly dispute? I said: My Lord, I do not know. He said: He placed His hand between my shoulders and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I learned what is between the East and the West. He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and at Your command. He said: About what do the highest assembly dispute? I said: My Lord, about expiations, walking on foot to congregational prayers, performing ablution thoroughly in disliked circumstances, and waiting for the next prayer after the prayer, until the prayers. Whoever maintains them lives in goodness and dies in goodness, and his sins become as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[4731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us the Quran. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Greetings, blessed prayers, and good words belong to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."],[4732,"O youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; guard your private parts. Indeed, whoever guards his private part will have Paradise."],[4733,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he placed me on his right."],[4734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Dubāʿah: Enter ihram, recite the talbiyah, and say: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me. For if you become ill, you will have exited ihram by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform Hajj after his migration except one Hajj, and that was the Hajj in which he entered ihram for ʿUmrah before the Hajj. ʿAbd Allah b. al-ʿAbbās said: Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did; he placed an ʿUmrah before the Hajj."],[4736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded ʿĀʾishah to perform ʿUmrah from al-Tanʿīm, then to circumambulate the House, as she had not circumambulated because of her menstruation. She had entered ihram for ʿUmrah."],[4737,"I would never perform Hajj without offering a sacrifice. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did."],[4738,"Whoever performs saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and does it in advance for his ʿUmrah, that suffices him for his ʿUmrah and his Hajj. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did when returning; he performed saʿy for his ʿUmrah, then stayed, then departed from Hajj, and he did not perform saʿy after Hajj until he departed."],[4739,"Saʿīd reported to us from Qatādah, from Abū Ṭālib al-Ḍubaʿī."],[4740,"A cupper called Abū Ṭaybah cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave him his wage and reduced his work, or removed a portion of his work."],[4741,"Allah's anger is intense upon the one whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed with his own hand, and Allah's anger is intense upon the people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4742,"The affair of this community will continue to be in harmony, or close to it (Jarir said: or a word similar to it) as long as they do not speak about predestination and children."],[4743,"He used to combine the two prayers while traveling and say: It is from the Sunnah."],[4744,"The black dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer. He said: I said: He used to mention a third. He said: What is it? I said: The donkey. He said: Wait, the donkey. I said: He mentioned a fourth. He said: What is it? I said: The disbeliever. He said: If you are able that no disbeliever or Muslim passes in front of you, then do so."],[4745,"Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us from Sa'id from Qatadah, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, similar to the hadith of Shu'bah, and he did not raise it to the Prophet."],[4746,"It was said: O Messenger of God, will a village be destroyed while there are righteous people in it? He said: Yes. It was said: By what? He said: By their complacency and silence regarding acts of disobedience to God."],[4747,"On the Day of Badr, a barren wind seized them."],[4748,"Whoever performs Hajj on foot, for every step there is written for him seven hundred good deeds from the good deeds of the Haram. Some of them said: What are the good deeds of the Haram? He said: Every good deed is multiplied by a hundred thousand good deeds."],[4749,"I bear witness that I know that the Messenger of God ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[4750,"A freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ fell from a palm tree and died, so the Prophet gave his inheritance to the people of his religion."],[4751,"Two young girls came out walking in front of the qiblah while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying. They clung to his sides. When he wanted to bow, he separated them, then bowed."],[4752,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My mother owes a slave and I have a black slave woman. The Prophet ﷺ said: Bring her to me. The Messenger of God said to her: Do you testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God? She said: Yes. He said: Then free her."],[4753,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: if the blood is fresh, let him give a dinar in charity; and if it is yellowish, then half a dinar."],[4754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Jamʿ — or ʿArafah — with Qutham before him and al-Faḍl behind him."],[4755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made two rakʿahs a sunnah while traveling, and they are complete, and the witr while traveling is a sunnah."],[4756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined in Madinah between Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr without fear or rain. I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: For what reason did he do that? He said: So as not to place his ummah in difficulty."],[4757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined between Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ, while he was residing in Madinah, without fear, so as not to place his ummah in difficulty."],[4758,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a military expedition, delaying Ẓuhr until it became cooler, then he prayed Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, then he did not dismount until the twilight disappeared, then he prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ."],[4759,"Some people of the Anṣār passed by me shooting at a dove, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade making a living creature a target."],[4760,"Whoever says something about the Qurʾān without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4761,"Whoever deliberately lies about me — or he said, says about me what I did not say — let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4762,"He used to recite in the witr in the first rakʿah: Sabbiḥisma rabbika l-aʿlā, in the second: Qul yā ayyuhā l-kāfirūn, and in the third: Qul huwa llāhu aḥad."],[4763,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with: Sabbiḥisma rabbika l-aʿlā, Qul yā ayyuhā l-kāfirūn, and Qul huwa llāhu aḥad."],[4764,"It was asked: How old were you when the Prophet ﷺ died? He said: I was circumcised that day."],[4765,"The Prophet ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant."],[4766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while a cloud had overshadowed us and we were hoping for rain from it. He said: ‘The angel who drives it—or drives this cloud—entered upon me, greeted me, and informed me that he was driving it to such-and-such a valley.’"],[4767,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he would say: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You, for all fortune is Yours.’"],[4768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that one-fifth is due on treasure trove (rikāz)."],[4769,"A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood."],[4770,"A man must not touch another man, nor a woman another woman."],[4771,"It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, when he finished at Badr, why did you not take the caravan? There is nothing beyond it.’ Al-ʿAbbās called out to him while he was a captive in his bonds: ‘It would not be right for you.’ He said: ‘Why?’ He said: ‘Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised.’"],[4772,"They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while drinking wine?’ He said: Then it was revealed: ‘There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten.’"],[4773,"It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while praying toward Jerusalem?’ Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ‘And Allah would never let your faith be lost.’"],[4774,"There is no contagion, no ṣafar, no evil omen, no hāmah. A man said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, a man takes a mangy sheep and throws it among a hundred sheep, and they become mangy.’ He said: ‘Then who made the first one mangy?’"],[4775,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began praising him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and some poetry is wisdom.’"],[4776,"Māʿiz b. Mālik was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he confessed twice. He said: ‘Take him away.’ Then they brought him back, and he confessed twice more, until he had confessed four times. He said: ‘Go and stone him.’"],[4777,"There were Qurayẓah and al-Naḍīr; al-Naḍīr was nobler than Qurayẓah. If a man of Qurayẓah killed a man of al-Naḍīr, he was killed for it, but if a man of al-Naḍīr killed a man of Qurayẓah, they said: ‘Hand him over to us and we will kill him.’ They said: ‘Between us and you is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ So they came to him, and it was revealed: ‘And if you judge, judge between them with justice,’ and justice means a life for a life. Then it was revealed: ‘Is it the judgment of ignorance they seek?’"],[4778,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: the earth was made a place of prostration and a means of purification for me, and no prophet among the prophets used to pray until he reached his prayer niche; I was granted victory by awe for a month's journey, it being before me toward the polytheists, and Allah casts awe into their hearts; a prophet used to be sent to his people specifically, but I was sent to the jinn and mankind; the prophets used to set aside the fifth, and the fire would come and consume it, but I was commanded to distribute it among the poor of my ummah; and no prophet remains but that he was granted intercession, whereas I have deferred my intercession for my ummah."],[4779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives: \"Would that I knew which of you is the owner of the hairy camel; she will set out and the dogs of Haw'ab will bark at her, and many will be killed to her right and to her left, then she will escape after having nearly perished.\""],[4780,"There were two co-wives between whom there was anger, and one of them threw something at the other and caused her to miscarry a dead boy whose hair had grown. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the 'aqilah (male relatives) should pay compensation. Her paternal uncle said: \"O Messenger of Allah, she miscarried a dead boy whose hair had grown.\" The father of the killer said: \"He is lying; by Allah, he did not cry, nor eat, nor drink, so one like him is to be disregarded.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Is it the rhyming prose of the Jahiliyyah and its soothsaying? For the child there is a ghurrah (compensation).\" He said: The name of one of them was Mulaykah and the other Umm 'Atraf."],[4781,"A mouse came and took to dragging the wick. He said: The slave girl went to drive it away, but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Leave it alone.\" He said: Then it brought it and cast it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ onto the mat he was sitting on, and it burned a spot the size of a dirham. He said: \"When you go to sleep, extinguish your lamps, for Satan guides this one to this and it will burn you.\""],[4782,"Twenty men from the mawali (freed slaves and their descendants) witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ."],[4783,"A thousand men from Banu Sulaym witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ the day of the conquest of Makkah."],[4784,"Three have no reckoning for what they eat, Allah willing, if it is lawful: the fasting person, the one eating the pre-dawn meal, and the one stationed in the way of Allah."],[4785,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Ibn Maslamah and his companions to Ibn al-Ashraf to kill him, he walked with them to Baqi' al-Gharqad, then sent them off, then said: \"Go forth in the name of Allah. O Allah, help them.\""],[4786,"There is no one but that he will meet Allah having intended a sin or committed it, except Yahya b. Zakariyya, for he neither intended it nor committed it."],[4787,"A slave belonging to Salam: when the Prophet ﷺ emigrated, his family feared that he would follow the Prophet, so they shackled him. He wrote to the Prophet ﷺ: \"You know of my Islam, so send me away or free me.\" The Prophet ﷺ sent seven men on a camel and said: \"Perhaps you will find in his house someone to help you against him.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ freed him."],[4788,"He used not to consider it proper to stop at al-Abtah, saying: \"It is only a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped or stayed and set up his arish (shelter).\""],[4789,"An 'umrah in Ramadan equals a hajj."],[4790,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a dead ewe lying with its legs apart and said: “What harm would it have done its owners if they had made use of its hide?” Sawdah tanned it and made nabīdh in it."],[4791,"He forbade selling palm trees for two or three years, that fruit on the palms be bought by measure, or that fruit be sold until its ripeness appears."],[4792,"The Prophet ﷺ would not throw the pebbles until the sun had declined."],[4793,"The Prophet ﷺ offered one hundred garlanded and draped camels as sacrificial animals."],[4794,"Al-Ṣaʿb b. Jaththāmah gave the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was in iḥrām, the hindquarter of a wild donkey, and he returned it and did not eat it."],[4795,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away while I — Abū al-Ḥasan said: I think he said — while I was circumcised."],[4796,"The Messenger of God, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar performed tamattuʿ, and the first to forbid it was Muʿāwiyah."],[4797,"God created Paradise white, and the most beloved thing to God is whiteness, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it."],[4798,"The first reward a servant receives after death is that forgiveness is sought for all who followed his funeral procession."],[4799,"A man said: “O Messenger of God, I declared my wife unlawful to myself as my mother’s back, then I saw her calf in the moonlight and had intercourse with her before I made expiation.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Make expiation and do not repeat it.”"],[4800,"The menstruating woman and the woman with postpartum bleeding perform all the rites except circumambulating the House until she becomes pure."],[4801,"God forbids you from going naked, so be ashamed before the noble recording angels of God who are with you and do not leave you except in one of three states: defecation, major ritual impurity, and bathing. When one of you bathes in the open, let him cover himself with his garment, or with a wall, or with his camel."],[4802,"He used to recite in the morning of Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil (Surah al-Sajdah) and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan (Surah al-Insan)."],[4803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Umm Salamah ahead from Muzdalifah at night, at the time of Jam'. Ibn 'Abbas said: I was also with them."],[4804,"Perhaps I saw the Prophet ﷺ while donkeys were braying in front of him."],[4805,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I threw the pebbles before shaving? He said: Shave, and there is no harm."],[4806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him with the baggage at night from Jam' (Muzdalifah) along with his family."],[4807,"He would spend consecutive nights hungry, while his family could not find supper, and most of their bread was barley bread."],[4808,"When he sent out a military expedition, he would say: Fight in the name of Allah, fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, do not kill a child, and do not kill the people of the monasteries."],[4809,"He used to teach them for fever and all pains: In the name of Allah, the Great, and praise be to Allah, the Great, the Mighty, from the evil of a gushing vein and from the evil of the heat of the Fire."],[4810,"He used to recite on the two Eids: 'Amma yatasa'alun (Surah al-Naba') and Wa al-Shamsi wa Duhaha (Surah al-Shams)."],[4811,"Three things do not break the fast: vomiting, cupping, and wet dreams."],[4812,"Ali married Fatimah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a body (dowry) of iron."],[4813,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of the chest (heart)."],[4814,"When any matter concerned him, he would say: “There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Magnificent; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, Lord of the Noble Throne.” Then he would supplicate."],[4815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping, and the cupper complained to him about his tax, so he sent word to his patrons to reduce his tax."],[4816,"Abu Jahl said: “If I see Muhammad praying, I will trample on his neck.” It was said: “There he is, praying.” He said: “I do not see him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Had he done so, the angels would have seized him openly. And if the Jews wished for death, they would have died.”"],[4817,"Between Adam and Nuh there were ten generations, all of them upon a law of truth. When Allah sent the Prophet and revealed His Book, the people were one community."],[4818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds and pitch-coated vessels, and said: “Do not drink except from a vessel that is covered.”"],[4819,"Wine was forbidden, a little of it and a lot of it, and the intoxicant from every drink."],[4820,"A man came to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about nabidh. He said: “The first people to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about nabidh were people who came from 'Abd al-Qays. They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of abundant vegetation.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Make nabidh in waterskins, but do not make it in hollowed-out stumps or green jars.’”"],[4821,"May Allah curse the Jews—fats were forbidden to them, but they sold them and consumed their price."],[4822,"He forbade the price of a dog and the earnings of a slave woman."],[4823,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[4824,"Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents, or settles a debt on their behalf after their death, will be raised with the righteous on the Day of Resurrection."],[4825,"“I do not accept prayer except from one who humbles himself before My greatness, does not exalt himself over My creation, does not persist in disobedience to Me through the night, spends his day in remembrance of Me, shows mercy to the poor, the wayfarer, and the widow, and shows mercy to the afflicted. That one’s light is like the light of the sun; I protect him by My might, entrust his guarding to My angels, give him light in darkness and forbearance in ignorance, and his likeness among My creation is like that of the Firdaws in Paradise.”"],[4826,"Be independent of people, even by [using] a piece of a tooth-stick."],[4827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis while the Kaaba was in front of him, and after he emigrated to Madinah for sixteen months."],[4828,"When it was Thursday—and what a Thursday it was—then Ibn Abbas wept regarding the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which he passed away. He said: 'Bring me a shoulder blade and an inkpot so that I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.'"],[4829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the mounting of a camel [for mating]."],[4830,"He forbade [the sale of] fetuses and unborn offspring and the offspring of an unborn offspring."],[4831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that if a dog laps into a vessel, it should be washed seven times."],[4832,"A man divorced his wife, and she came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'No maintenance and no lodging.'"],[4833,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Duba'ah to stipulate [a condition] during the Hajj and to say: 'My place of ending [the pilgrim state] is wherever You withhold me.'"],[4834,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet in the form of a pale, traveling man, until he placed his hand upon the Prophet's knee ﷺ and said: 'What is Islam?' He said: 'That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish the prayer, give the zakat, fast Ramadan, and perform the pilgrimage to the House.' He said: 'So if I do that, I have submitted?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'We were amazed at his questioning him and then confirming him.' Then he said: 'What is excellence (ihsan)?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That you fear Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.' He said: 'So if I do that, I have excelled?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'Then inform me what is faith (iman)?' He said: 'Faith in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, Paradise, Hell, resurrection after death, and destiny, its good and its evil.' He said: 'So if I do that, I have believed.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'Then when is the Hour?' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, the one asked about it is not more knowledgeable than the asker, but it has signs: when you see the woman give birth to her mistress, and you see the barefoot, naked, destitute—meaning the Arabs—become leaders of the people.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' Then he turned away. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring the man back to me.' But they looked and saw nothing. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do you know who this was?' We said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'This was Jibril, who came to teach you your religion. He never came in any form except that I recognized him, except this time.'"],[4835,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I made zihar from my wife, then I had intercourse with her before I made expiation.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Did not Allah, Blessed and Exalted, say: \"before they touch each other\"?' He said: 'She pleased me.' He said: 'Refrain until you make expiation.'"],[4836,"Hudud punishments are not carried out in mosques, and a father is not killed for [killing] his son."],[4837,"Umar b. Abd al-Rahman Abu Hafs al-Abbar reported to us from Ismail b. Muslim from Amr b. Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know this hadith being narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this route with this chain, and the hadith of Qatadah we do not know anyone narrating it except Sa'id b. Bashir from him. We mentioned it from Ismail b. Muslim, even though Ismail b. Muslim has been criticized, because the hadith of Sa'id we did not memorize except from Abu al-Mughirah, so we wanted to show that someone other than him also narrated it."],[4838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out with a piece of gold and a piece of silk in his hand and said: 'Verily, these two are forbidden for the males of my community, and lawful for its females.'"],[4839,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Bathe on Friday, wash your heads, and touch perfume.' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'As for the perfume, I do not know; as for the bath, yes.'"],[4840,"The saying of the Prophet ﷺ concerning the bath on Friday was mentioned to him, so I said to him: 'And he touches perfume if he finds it?' He said: 'I do not know it.'"],[4841,"Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'I am a heavy woman and I intend to perform Hajj; how should I enter ihram?' He said: 'Enter ihram and stipulate: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.'"],[4842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up in the middle of the night to pray and said: 'O God, to You be praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth. To You be praise; You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth. To You be praise; You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You be praise; You are the Truth, Your word is true, the meeting with You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. To You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have argued, and to You I have brought judgment. So forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are God; there is no god but You.'"],[4843,"Ibn 'Abbas was asked about sitting on the heels (iq'a') during prostration. He said: 'There is no harm in it.' Tawus said: 'I do not see it.' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'It is a Sunnah.'"],[4844,"It is part of the Sunnah to place one's buttocks on one's heels between the two prostrations."],[4845,"A life grant belongs to the one to whom it is given, and a ruqba belongs to the one to whom it is granted; the one who takes back his gift is like the one who swallows back his vomit. I think he said: 'It is not lawful for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except a parent in what he gives to his child.'"],[4846,"The Messenger of God ﷺ traveled during Ramadan and fasted until he reached 'Usfan. Then he called for a vessel of water during the day to show it to the people, and then he broke his fast. Ibn 'Abbas used to say: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted while traveling and broke his fast; so whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break the fast.'"],[4847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest: 'There is no emigration after today, but there is jihad and intention. When you are called to march, then march.'"],[4848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by two graves and said: 'They are both being punished, and they are not being punished for anything major. As for this one, he used to spread malicious gossip; and as for this one, he did not protect himself from his urine.' Then he called for a fresh palm stalk and placed one on this grave and one on that, and said: 'Perhaps their punishment will be lightened as long as they do not dry.'"],[4849,"Jarir narrated to us from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, and Tawus was not mentioned between Mujahid and Ibn 'Abbas."],[4850,"Isma'il b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Suhayl b. Abi Salih, from Habib b. Hassan, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4851,"Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, and he did not say, from Ibn 'Abbas. We have mentioned the hadith of Suhayl from Habib b. Hassan only because Suhayl did not transmit from Habib anything other than this hadith, and we have mentioned the hadith of 'Amr from Tawus so that no one may say that it is from Ibn 'Abbas, and we have thus made clear that it is not from Ibn 'Abbas. And we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas except Waki'."],[4852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman used to pray on the two 'Eids before the sermon."],[4853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed two rak'ahs while traveling and four rak'ahs when settled. Ibn 'Abbas said: Just as you pray before and after it while settled, likewise pray before and after it while traveling."],[4854,"Al-Awza'i narrated to me, from Usama b. Zayd al-Laythi, from al-Hasan b. Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas in a similar manner from other than this route and with wording other than this, and this chain of transmission is better and more authentic than the other chain that is narrated from him. And we do not know that al-Awza'i transmitted from Usama b. Zayd al-Laythi, from al-Hasan b. Muslim, except this hadith."],[4855,"Tawaf around the House is like prayer, except that you speak during it. So whoever speaks during it should speak only good."],[4856,"The measuring container is the measuring container of the people of Makkah, and the scale is the scale of the people of Madinah."],[4857,"I accept prayer only from one who humbles himself through it before My greatness, who does not exalt himself over My creation, who does not spend the night persisting in disobedience to Me, who spends his day in remembrance of Me, and who shows mercy to the poor, the wayfarer, and the widow, and shows mercy to the afflicted. Such a one's light is like the light of the sun. I protect him by My might, and I entrust him to My angels. I grant him light in darkness and forbearance in ignorance. His likeness among My creation is like that of Firdaws in Paradise."],[4858,"Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love each other."],[4859,"Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love each other."],[4860,"Sufyan b. 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Maysara, from Tawus, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not say: from Ibn 'Abbas. The hadith is famous only through Muhammad b. Muslim, from Ibrahim, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ. As for the hadith of Mu'ammal, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri other than him as being connected, insofar as it has reached us from a trustworthy man. Abu Bakr said: that is, for two who love each other, meaning: when a man loves a woman, it is appropriate that he should marry her."],[4861,"When he would perform the night prayer, he would say: O Allah, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Truth, and Your promise is true, and the meeting with You is true, and Paradise is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I submit, in You I believe, upon You I rely, to You I turn, with You I contend, and to You I bring judgment. O Allah, forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who defers. There is no god but You, and there is no might and no power except with You."],[4862,"The people used to disperse from every direction, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: No one should depart until his last act is at the House."],[4863,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by a man whose nose had been pierced."],[4864,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer without an adhan or an iqamah."],[4865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman who was in her howdah, and with her was a child. She took the child by its hands and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?' He said: 'Yes, and for you is a reward.'"],[4866,"That a woman lifted up a child and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?' He said: 'Yes, and for you is a reward.'"],[4867,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck up the hair or the garment."],[4868,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed when the sun eclipsed: eight bowings and four prostrations, reciting in each rak'ah."],[4869,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he commanded him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' or tabi'ah, a jadha' or jadha'ah, and from every forty cattle a musinnah. They said: 'What about the awqas?' He said: 'He did not command me anything regarding them, and I will ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I arrive.' When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he asked him, and he said: 'There is nothing due on them.'"],[4870,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday and then comes close where he can hear the imam's khutbah, and when he comes out he listens and remains silent until he prays it with him, there is written for him for every step he takes the worship of a year, its standing and its fasting."],[4871,"A man asked Ibn 'Abbas about the two rak'ahs after 'Asr. He said: 'It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, to have any choice in their affair.'"],[4872,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Hisham b. Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, something similar. We do not know that 'Amir b. Mus'ab transmitted from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, anything other than this hadith, nor did anyone transmit it from him except Ibn Jurayj. And Hisham b. Hujayr did not transmit from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, anything other than this hadith, nor do we know that anyone transmitted it from him except Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah."],[4873,"Teach and make things easy, and do not make things difficult. And when you become angry, remain silent."],[4874,"Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And this speech we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except from this route, except a hadith in whose chain there is disagreement. Layth b. Abi Sulaym is a Kufan, a devout worshipper, and the people of Kufa narrated from him and bore his hadith."],[4875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tamattu', as did Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and the first to prohibit it was Mu'awiyah."],[4876,"'Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And this hadith we do not know anyone to have narrated with this wording except Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know a route from Ibn 'Abbas except this route. And 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah and others narrated from Ibn 'Abbas about the tamattu' of the Prophet ﷺ with a wording other than this."],[4877,"That he never saw the Prophet ﷺ break his fast on any Friday."],[4878,"The evil eye is real, and if you are asked to wash, then wash."],[4879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shared among his companions on the day of Hudaybiyyah seven in a cow."],[4880,"I am taking hold of your lower garments, saying: Be mindful of the Fire; I am going and I am your forerunner at the Pond. Then some people will be brought and taken to the left. I will say: O Lord, my companions! It will be said: They kept turning back on their heels."],[4881,"Two insatiable ones never have enough: a seeker of knowledge and a seeker of this world."],[4882,"Five are all sinful, the muhrim may kill them: the mouse, the kite, the crow, the scorpion, and the biting dog."],[4883,"That the Prophet ﷺ hastened Umm Salamah from Jam' at night, from Muzdalifah. Ibn 'Abbas said: And I was with them."],[4884,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave the grandmother a sixth."],[4885,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr at 'Arafat."],[4886,"He used to call the Farewell Hajj the Hajj of Islam."],[4887,"Give the prescribed shares to those entitled to them, and whatever remains is for the nearest male relative."],[4888,"Ziyad b. Sa'd narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And I do not know of any defect in this chain; Wuhayb is a well-known, reliable memorizer from Basra, and the rest of the chain after him are so famous and trustworthy that they need no commendation."],[4889,"Beware of a house called the bathhouse. They said: O Messenger of God, it removes dirt. He said: Then cover yourselves."],[4890,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while fasting and applied treatment to his nose."],[4891,"A settled person should not sell on behalf of a Bedouin."],[4892,"Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Ma'mar said: I said to Ibn Tawus: What is the meaning of 'a settled person should not sell on behalf of a Bedouin'? He said: He should not be a broker for him. And we do not know this hadith being narrated from Ibn 'Abbas except through this route, and it has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through several routes with different wordings."],[4893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam. And he said: These are for them, and for anyone who comes upon them from other than their people, intending Hajj or 'Umrah. And whoever's family lives within the miqat, then from wherever he sets out."],[4894,"He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of the Dajjal, the trial of life, and the trial of death."],[4895,"I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind."],[4896,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ and from Ibn 'Abbas through several routes; we mentioned these two routes and limited ourselves to them. And we do not know of anyone who narrated the hadith of Abu Bishr from Sa'id b. Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas except 'Uthman b. 'Umar, while others besides 'Uthman narrated it from Abu Bishr from Sa'id b. Jubayr as mursal."],[4897,"I passed in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ on a donkey while he was leading the people in prayer, and he did not repeat that prayer because of that."],[4898,"When this verse was revealed: 'So judge between them or turn away from them,' he said: He was given a choice: if he wished, he could judge; and if he wished, he could turn away from them and refer them back to their own laws. He said: Then it was revealed: 'And judge between them by what Allah has sent down, and do not follow their whims.' He said: So he was commanded to judge between them by what is in our Book."],[4899,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My mother died and she owed two consecutive months of fasting.' He said: 'Do you think that if she owed a debt, you would pay it?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So the right of Allah is more deserving.'"],[4900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the campaign of Tabuk: 'Raid and you will gain the daughters of the pale-skinned ones.' Some of the hypocrites said: 'He is tempting you with women.' He said: Then Allah revealed: 'And among them is he who says, \"Permit me and do not put me to trial\"' – the verse."],[4901,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Ali and Khalid b. al-Walid, and appointed 'Ali over the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and appointed Khalid b. al-Walid over the Bedouins, and said: 'If there is fighting, then command of the people belongs to 'Ali.'"],[4902,"Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from al-Hakam from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4903,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, whereas those before me were sent only to their own people; the earth was made a mosque and a means of purification for me; I was aided with terror cast ahead of me for a month's journey; spoils of war were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; and I was given intercession, and I have delayed it for my Ummah, so it will reach whoever does not associate anything with Allah."],[4904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against one another."],[4905,"Whoever among you is unable to endure the night vigil, is too miserly to spend wealth, and is too cowardly to fight the enemy, let him increase in the remembrance of Allah."],[4906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man and saw his thigh exposed, so he said: 'Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is part of his 'awrah.'"],[4907,"It is not proper for anyone to say: 'I am better in the sight of Allah than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[4908,"Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so cleanse yourselves from urine."],[4909,"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads. They said: 'And those who shorten?' He said – on the third or fourth time –: 'And those who shorten.'"],[4910,"Hushaym narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, or Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This statement has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through various channels, and the best route narrated regarding that from Ibn 'Abbas is what Ibn Abi Najih narrated from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[4911,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed one hundred camels, among them a camel of Abu Jahl that had a silver nose ring."],[4912,"I read to Ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas through more than one route; Miqsam and others narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas, and the hadith of Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid has a better chain than the hadith of Miqsam."],[4913,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in the compensatory 'umrah for three [days]."],[4914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar that one should have intercourse with pregnant women, and he said: 'Do not water the crop of another.' He also forbade selling spoils until they were distributed, eating domestic donkeys, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[4915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of jallalah donkeys and plunder."],[4916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that pregnant captives should be had intercourse with until they delivered what was in their wombs, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[4917,"Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4918,"Use cupping on the seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first, lest the blood surge in you and kill you."],[4919,"If there is healing in any of your remedies, it is in the cut of the cupper and a sip of honey."],[4920,"I have two viziers from the people of heaven and two viziers from the people of earth. As for my two viziers from the people of heaven, they are Jibril and Mika'il, and as for my two viziers from the people of earth, they are Abu Bakr and 'Umar."],[4921,"He forbade on the day of the conquest the meat of jallalah animals, their milk, and their backs."],[4922,"I saw Jibril ﷺ twice, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for me for wisdom twice."],[4923,"Indeed Allah has angels on the earth, besides the recording angels, who write down whatever falls of tree leaves. So if one of you encounters a limp in a desolate land, let him call out: 'Help, O servants of Allah.'"],[4924,"Which of the two recitations do you consider was the last? They said: The recitation of Zayd. He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present the Quran to Jibril ﷺ every year. In the year in which he was taken, he presented it to him twice. Thus the recitation of Ibn Mas'ud was the last, or the last of it."],[4925,"Umar b. al-Khattab said to al-Abbas ؓ: Accept Islam, for by Allah, if you accept Islam, it is dearer to me than if al-Khattab accepted Islam, and that is only because he was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So accept Islam and your precedence will be yours."],[4926,"Allah made prayer obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rak'ahs when resident, two rak'ahs when traveling, and one rak'ah in fear."],[4927,"Indeed Makkah is sacred; Allah made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth and the sun and the moon. It was not permitted to anyone before me, nor will it be permitted to anyone after me. It was only permitted to me for an hour of the day, then it returned to being sacred. Its fresh herbage is not to be cut, its trees are not to be chopped down, its game is not to be startled, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it. Al-Abbas said: Except for the idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah, for the people of Makkah cannot do without it. He said: Except for the idhkhir."],[4928,"Al-Muharibi narrated to us from Ayyub b. A'idh, from Bukayr b. al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas."],[4929,"The Prophet ﷺ and his companions arrived as pilgrims. When he arrived, he said: O people, come out of ihram. If I had faced in my affair what I have now passed, I would not have done this. The umrah has been incorporated into the hajj until the Day of Resurrection."],[4930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade these vessels, then he permitted them. He forbade the dubba', the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat, then he permitted them. He said: Drink from whatever you wish, but avoid every intoxicant. And he forbade visiting graves, then he said: Visit them, for in them there is a lesson. And he forbade the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, then he permitted it. Mujahid said: A'ishah said: Indeed we would wake up, and the 'iraq of the meat of sacrificial animals was still there after ten days."],[4931,"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more excellent than these days, meaning the ten days, for they are days of tahlil and takbir."],[4932,"The menstruating woman may enter ihram and perform all the rites except that she does not circumambulate the House until she becomes pure."],[4933,"The one addicted to wine, the one disobedient to parents, and the one who reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise."],[4934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to our home, so I handed him a bucket and he drank, then he spat into the bucket."],[4935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “O you who believe, fear Allah as He should truly be feared.” He said: “If a drop of zaqqūm were to fall into the earth, it would ruin their livelihood. So how about one who has no food other than it?”"],[4936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis while the Kaʿbah was in front of him, and after he migrated to Madinah for sixteen months."],[4937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys, and pregnant women from being approached until they give birth—meaning what is in their wombs—and every fanged beast of prey, and the sale of the fifth until it is distributed."],[4938,"Whoever gives the call to prayer for seven years seeking reward, a clearance from the Fire is written for him."],[4939,"Were it not that it would be difficult for you, I would have commanded you to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."],[4940,"Muhammad b. Fuḍayl narrated to us from Muslim from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. This hadith has been narrated with similar wording from the Prophet ﷺ through other routes with a different expression, and we do not know it from Ibn ʿAbbās with this wording except through this route with this chain. Muslim al-Mulāʾī is acceptable; Shuʿbah, al-Thawrī, al-Aʿmash, Isrāʾīl, and many others narrated from him and accepted his hadith."],[4941,"A freedwoman of the Prophet ﷺ used to fast the day, so it was said to him: “She fasts the day and stands in prayer at night.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every deed has a zeal, and zeal leads to a period of slackness. Whoever’s slackness is toward my Sunnah has been guided, and whoever’s slackness is toward something else has gone astray.”"],[4942,"I was helped by the east wind, and ʿĀd was destroyed by the west wind, and nothing was sent upon them except the like of a ring."],[4943,"A group of Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “If he tells us about what we ask him, then he is a prophet.” They said: “Where does resemblance come from, O Muhammad?” He said: “The man’s seminal fluid is thick and white, and the woman’s is thin and yellow. Whichever prevails over the other, the resemblance belongs to it. If they combine, then it is from both.” They said: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[4944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted one day in the month of Ramadan until night. The next day he fasted until afternoon, then it was said to him: “Fasting has exhausted the people.” So he called for water and drank."],[4945,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿumrah in the month of Ramadan."],[4946,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ghusl behind the rooms, and his private part was never seen."],[4947,"“O Prophet, why do you prohibit [yourself from] what Allah has made lawful for you?” He said: “This was revealed concerning his concubine.”"],[4948,"Qays narrated to us from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, similarly. We do not know of it being narrated from Ibn Abbas in a connected chain except through these two routes."],[4949,"Regarding Allah's words, Blessed and Exalted: “And those who commit lewdness from among your women,” he said: “They used to be confined in houses until they died. Then when Surat al-Nur was revealed and the prescribed punishments came down, they abrogated it.”"],[4950,"Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, then his family becomes lawful for him."],[4951,"He recited Surah Sad and prostrated in it, then said: “Those are the ones whom Allah guided, so follow their guidance.” And what prevented him from prostrating in it when Allah had related to him the stories of the prophets?"],[4952,"I and al-Fadl came on a donkey, and we passed in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Arafah while he was praying the obligatory prayer, with nothing to screen him that would come between us and him."],[4953,"I was forbidden to pray facing those who are sleeping and those who are talking."],[4954,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer until as much of the night had passed as Allah willed. Umar said to him: “The women and children have gone to sleep.” He came out saying: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to pray at this hour.”"],[4955,"When he ate food, he would lick his fingers."],[4956,"The Muslims overtook a man with his small flock of sheep. He greeted them with salam, but they killed him and took his flock. So Allah revealed: “And do not say to one who offers you peace, 'You are not a believer,' seeking the transient goods of worldly life” — the flock."],[4957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead with the weak members of his family from Muzdalifah at night."],[4958,"The Prophet ﷺ only did ramal to show the polytheists his strength."],[4959,"Regarding the words of Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He: 'Have you not seen those who exchanged the favor of Allah for disbelief and led their people to the home of ruin?' He said: 'They are the disbelievers of Quraysh, the people of Makkah, who were killed on the Day of Badr.'"],[4960,"Abu 'Asim narrated to us from Zakariyya b. Ishaq, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas."],[4961,"'Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities except al-lamam.' He said: 'Al-lammah is a minor instance of zina.' And Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive abundantly; and which servant of Yours does not commit lammam?'"],[4962,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day of Fitr or Adha, prayed, then delivered a sermon, then came to the women and commanded them to give charity, and they began to throw [their jewelry]."],[4963,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4964,"He delivered the sermon after the prayer; he commanded us and forbade us. He thought that the women had not heard, so he came to them with Bilal, admonished them, commanded them, forbade them, and ordered them to give charity. Bilal spread out his garment, and a woman would throw in earrings and a ring."],[4965,"When he said: 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah,' he would say: 'Allahumma Rabbana laka al-hamd, mil'a al-samawati wa mil'a al-ardi wa mil'a ma shi'ta min shay'in ba'du' (O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that)."],[4966,"Al-'Abbas sent me to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the house of Maymunah, my maternal aunt. I spent that night with him. He got up to pray during the night, so I got up, performed ablution, and stood on his left. He took hold of me from behind his back and placed me on his right."],[4967,"Do you not know, O Zayd b. Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given a limb of game as a gift, and he did not eat it, saying: 'We are in ihram'? He said: 'Yes.'"],[4968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Jam' (Muzdalifah), as I think, with Usamah riding behind him."],[4969,"He forbade the sale of gharar (uncertainty)."],[4970,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[4971,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."],[4972,"Rabah b. Abi Ma'ruf narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4973,"He had himself cupped while he was in ihram."],[4974,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped at Lahyay Jamal while he was in ihram."],[4975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Musa on an expedition by sea. While they were thus, having raised the sail on a dark night, a caller from above them called out to the people of the ship: 'Stop, and I will inform you of a decree that Allah has decreed upon Himself.' Abu Musa said: 'Inform us if you are going to inform.' He said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has decreed upon Himself that whoever makes himself thirsty for His sake on a hot day, Allah will give him drink on the Day of Thirst.'"],[4976,"You will meet Allah tomorrow barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."],[4977,"When the Quran descended upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would recite it to memorize it. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation.'"],[4978,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah and al-Hasan b. al-Sabbah narrated it to us from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[4979,"Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[4980,"The Prophet ﷺ would not recognize the end of a surah until 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' was sent down. When 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' was sent down, he knew that the surah had been completed and another surah had been begun—or started."],[4981,"A man was standing on his mount with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he fell from his camel and it broke his neck while he was in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, and do not bring perfume near him; for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah—or saying labbayk.'"],[4982,"A man in a state of ihrām came with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then fell from atop his camel and it broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Wash him with water and lotus leaves, clothe him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will come on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.”"],[4983,"Abū al-Zubayr reported to me, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, the like of ʿAmr’s report: he narrated it to me from him: …"],[4984,"My father narrated to us, from Qays b. Saʿd, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4985,"Abān b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah. We do not know of this hadith being narrated with a better chain than these chains."],[4986,"Muslim b. Abī Ḥurrah also narrated that from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr. Aḥmad b. ʿAbdah narrated it to us, from Ibn ʿUyaynah, from Muslim b. Abī Ḥurrah, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās. Muslim b. Abī Ḥurrah did not narrate any hadith other than this one with a complete chain. Maṭar al-Warrāq and Abū Bishr narrated it from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, so we limited ourselves to those we have mentioned."],[4987,"Hushaym narrated to us, from Ashʿath b. Sawwār, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[4988,"ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[4989,"Qurrah narrated to us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[4990,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ in Madinah without fear, in order not to inconvenience his community."],[4991,"During the campaign of Tabūk, the Prophet ﷺ would delay Ẓuhr until it cooled, then pray Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr together; then he would not dismount until the twilight disappeared, and then pray Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ together."],[4992,"We were with Ibn ʿAbbās in the mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and something about divine decree was mentioned in his presence. He gestured with his hand—that was after he had lost his sight—and I said, “There is no one among the people.” He said, “I thought there was someone among them, and I would seize him by the neck. That is because I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God did not send a prophet and then take him without making after him a period of slackness, and from that period Gehenna will be filled. They are the Qadarites.”"],[4993,"Ṣadaqah b. Sābiq narrated to us, from Sulaymān b. Qarm, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly, or close to it. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except through this route that we have mentioned."],[4994,"Ismāʿīl b. Umayyah narrated to us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[4995,"When your brothers were killed, Allah placed their souls in the crops of green birds that come to the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and seek shelter in lanterns suspended in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food and drink, they said: 'If only our brothers knew what Allah has honored us with.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I shall convey it to them on your behalf.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision, rejoicing in what Allah has bestowed upon them of His bounty, and they receive good tidings about those who have not yet joined them from behind them, that there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.'"],[4996,"My father sent me to the Prophet ﷺ on the night that was my aunt's turn. I came and lay down on the bed. He said: 'Has the boy fallen asleep?' I had not slept, and I was listening to his words. He prayed four rakʿahs, prolonging the recitation, bowing, and prostration. Then he lay down. Then he got up and prayed five rakʿahs. I got up, performed ablution, and stood on his left, so he took my hand from behind him and placed me on his right. I understood from his supplication while he was saying: 'O Allah, place light in my hearing and light in my sight and light in my heart and light in my tongue, and light on my right and light on my left and light in front of me and light behind me and light beneath me and light above me. O Allah, make my light great.'"],[4997,"And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person. He said: It was a concession for the elderly man and the elderly woman who are able to fast, that they may break the fast and feed a poor person for each day. Then it was abrogated, and it was established that if they are unable to fast, they may break the fast and feed a poor person for each day, as well as the pregnant and nursing women if they fear. Ibn ʿAbbās used to say to a pregnant umm walad of his: 'You are in the position of one who cannot afford it, so you must pay the ransom and there is no makeup due on you.'"],[4998,"He used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: 'The revelation of the prostration' (Sūrat al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man' (Sūrat al-Insān)."],[4999,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man performing the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Perform the talbiyah for yourself, then perform the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah.'"],[5000,"On the day of Khaybar, he forbade every beast of prey with fangs and every bird with talons."],[5001,"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than these days, meaning the ten days. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the cause of Allah?' He said: 'Not even jihad in the cause of Allah, except a man who goes out with his life and his wealth and returns with nothing.'"],[5002,"This hadith was also narrated by al-Ḥakam b. ʿUtaybah from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās. Yūsuf narrated it to us from Salamah, from al-Ḥajjāj, from al-Ḥakam."],[5003,"Aṣbagh b. Zayd narrated to me, from al-Qāsim b. Abī Ayyūb, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[5004,"Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAṭiyyah narrated to us, from Qays, from Abū Isḥāq, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās."],[5005,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my mother died while she owed a month of fasting. Should I make it up on her behalf?' He said: 'Tell me, if your mother owed a debt, would you not pay it on her behalf?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then the debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being paid.'"],[5006,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My sister died while she owed fasting two consecutive months.” He said: “Tell me, if your sister had a debt, would you pay it off?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then the right of Allah is more deserving.”"],[5007,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."],[5008,"He used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: “Alif Lam Mim. The revelation…” and “Has there come upon man…”"],[5009,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: “Alif Lam Mim. The revelation, the prostration…” and “Has there come upon man…”"],[5010,"Allah sent down the Quran to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree all at once; Gabriel used to bring it down, that is, upon the Prophet ﷺ."],[5011,"“A man will enter upon you, entering with the eyes of a devil.” Then a blue-eyed man entered and said: “O Muhammad, why does he revile me, or why does this one insult me?” He said: “And he began to swear.” Then this verse was revealed: “They swear to a lie while they know” – the verse, and the other verse."],[5012,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed qunut for thirty mornings in the forenoon prayer."],[5013,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed qunut for thirty mornings."],[5014,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."],[5015,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was fifteen years old."],[5016,"He was asked: “How old were you when the Prophet ﷺ died?” He said: “I was circumcised at that time.”"],[5017,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” and “Say: O disbelievers,” and “Say: He is Allah, the One.”"],[5018,"The Prophet ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant."],[5019,"Jibril used to push mud into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that he would say 'There is no god but Allah'; and another said: fearing that mercy would reach him."],[5020,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My mother owes a believing slave, and I have a black slave woman.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring her to me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then set her free.'"],[5021,"A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: 'Ten [verses] were revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah and ten in Makkah.' He said: 'From whom did you hear this?' He said: 'It reached me,' or 'I heard people saying.' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Fifteen or more were revealed to him in Makkah.'"],[5022,"Ammār b. Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhāl, from Sa'īd, from Ibn 'Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5023,"Al-Sa'b b. Jaththāmah gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he was at Qudayd and in a state of iḥrām, the meat of a wild donkey, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it while it was dripping blood."],[5024,"Were we not in a state of iḥrām, we would have accepted it from you."],[5025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Ẓuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Ishā' in Madinah without fear or rain. It was said to him: 'What did he intend by that?' He said: 'He intended not to burden his community.'"],[5026,"Be moderate in prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs."],[5027,"Abū 'Awānah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habīb, from Sa'īd b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. We know no one who narrates this hadith from al-A'mash, from Habīb, except Abū 'Awānah."],[5028,"No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansār."],[5029,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I vowed to sacrifice at Buwānah.' He said: 'Perhaps there is something of the Jāhiliyyah in your heart?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then fulfill your vow.'"],[5030,"The first to stand up, or: the first to be called on the Day of Resurrection are those who praise Allah in every state."],[5031,"When [the verse] “And warn your closest kindred” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began calling them tribe by tribe."],[5032,"Sufyan narrated to us from Habib, from Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5033,"The Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[5034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while a cloud had overshadowed us and we were hopeful of [rain from] it. He said: “The angel who drives it came to me, greeted me, and informed me that he was driving it to such-and-such a valley.”"],[5035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was inspecting the palm trees in Madinah, and people began saying: “In it there is a sa'.” “In it there is a wasq.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In it there is such-and-such.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am only a human. Whatever I tell you from Allah is true, but whatever I say on my own, I am only a human: I err and I am right.”"],[5036,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, who are the allies (awliya') of Allah?” He replied: “Those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered.”"],[5037,"He would not break his fast on the white days (ayyam al-bid), whether traveling or resident."],[5038,"The people of Makkah asked the Prophet ﷺ to turn al-Safa into gold for them and to move the mountains away from them so that they could cultivate [the land]. It was said: “If you wish, We can give them what they asked for, but if they disbelieve, they will be destroyed as those before them were destroyed.” Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: “And nothing prevented Us from sending signs except that the former peoples denied them. And We gave Thamud the she-camel as a visible sign.”"],[5039,"Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us from Ja'far b. Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we did not hear this hadith except from Abu Hisham: the hadith of Talhah al-Qannad from Ja'far."],[5040,"The people of Makkah asked the Prophet ﷺ to turn al-Safa into gold for them."],[5041,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a man from the Ansar. When he approached his dwelling, he heard him talking inside. When he asked permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “I heard you talking to someone else.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I went inside feeling distressed because of what people were saying about my fever. Then a man came in to me, the likes of whom I have never seen after you, more noble in presence or better in speech.” He said: “That was Jibril. Indeed, among you there are men such that if one of them were to swear by Allah, He would honor his oath.”"],[5042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to raise his voice with the Qur'an and sometimes lower it, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: \"And do not be loud in your prayer nor too quiet therein, but seek between that a way.\""],[5043,"Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ja'far b. Abi Wahshiyya from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith with this wording with a connected chain except from Ibn Abbas with this chain."],[5044,"They used to dislike giving to their relatives while they were polytheists, so it was revealed: \"It is not upon you to guide them,\" until He reached: \"And whatever good you spend, Allah knows it well,\" so He permitted them."],[5045,"I was helped by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind."],[5046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast until we would say he does not intend to break his fast, and he would not fast until we would say he does not intend to fast, and he did not fast a whole month consecutively since he came to Madinah other than Ramadan."],[5047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: \"Allah knows best what they would have done.\""],[5048,"His maternal aunt sent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curds, and a dabb lizard. He ate from the clarified butter and the dried curds, but he did not eat from the dabb out of disgust, and he ate at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah of the Qur'an: \"All greetings, blessings, prayers, and good words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\""],[5050,"A man from the polytheists was killed, so the polytheists sought to bury him until they offered blood money, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused."],[5051,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My sister died and she owed two consecutive months of fasting.\" He said: \"Do you think if your sister had a debt, would you pay it?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the right of Allah is more deserving.\""],[5052,"Abd al-Hamid b. Abd al-Rahman Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us from al-A'mash from Tariq b. Abd al-Rahman from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5053,"O Allah, You gave the first of Quraysh a taste of punishment, so give its last a taste of bounty."],[5054,"I was sitting with Ibn ʿAbbās when ʿUrwah came to him and said: O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you think that when you give the fatwā of mutʿah, you know that Abū Bakr and ʿUmar used to forbid it and dislike it? Ibn ʿAbbās said: Indeed, it was the last covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with which he parted from the people. ʿUrwah said: By Allah, O Ibn ʿAbbās, Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were more knowledgeable of the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you. Ibn ʿAbbās said: O ʿUrayyah, I do not think that punishment is anything but about to descend upon you all. I inform you that it was the last covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with which he parted from the people, and you say: Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were..."],[5055,"Shaybān narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5056,"You hear, and it is heard from you, and it is heard from those who heard from you."],[5057,"When it was Thursday—and what a Thursday it was—then Ibn ʿAbbās wept during the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which he passed away. He said: Bring me a sheet and an inkpot so that I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray."],[5058,"Indeed, the Black Stone descended from Paradise, whiter than snow or hail, and nothing blackened it except the sins of the children of Adam."],[5059,"Regarding His saying: 'And if you are ill or on a journey,' he said: When a man has a wound in the path of Allah, or sores, or smallpox, and he fears that he will die if he bathes, he performs tayammum."],[5060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the two rakʿahs after ʿAṣr only because wealth came to him and he distributed it, and it distracted him from the two rakʿahs after Ẓuhr, so he prayed them after ʿAṣr, and he did not repeat them."],[5061,"The Jews disputed with the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Muḥammad, you eat what we slaughter but you do not eat what Allah has caused to die. Then Allah revealed: 'And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, for indeed it is disobedience, and indeed the devils inspire their allies.'"],[5062,"The Prophet of Allah, Sulaymān, when he stood to pray, would see a tree growing before him and say to it: What is your name? It would say: Such-and-such. He would say: For what purpose are you? It would say: For such-and-such. If it was for a remedy, it was recorded; and if it was for planting, it was planted. While he was praying one day, a tree grew before him, and he said to it: What is your name? It said: The carob tree. He said: For what purpose are you? It said: For the ruin of this house. Sulaymān said: O Allah, make my death unknown to the jinn, so that mankind may know that the jinn do not know the unseen. He took his staff and leaned upon it, and he died while the jinn were working. Termites ate it within a year, and he fell. Then 'the jinn realized that if they had known the unseen, they would not have remained in humiliating torment' [for a year]. Ibn ʿAbbās used to recite it in that way. He said: So the jinn thanked the termites, and they used to bring it water."],[5063,"Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ b. al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, similarly, but he did not attribute it to the Prophet. This ḥadīth has been narrated by a group from ʿAṭāʾ, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās as mawqūf, and we do not know anyone who attributed it except Ibrāhīm b. Ṭahmān."],[5064,"Information is not like seeing with one's own eyes."],[5065,"Muḥammad b. Fuḍayl narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ b. al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5066,"Verily, the blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its edges, and do not eat from its middle."],[5067,"I have not seen a people better than the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ; they did not ask him except about twelve questions, all of them in the Quran: 'They ask you about wine and gambling,' 'They ask you about the sacred month,' and 'They ask you about the orphans.' He said: When it was revealed: 'And do not approach the property of the orphan,' they separated their food from their food, then it was revealed: 'And if you mix with them, they are your brothers, and Allah knows the corrupter from the amender.'"],[5068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Eid while leaning on Usamah, and he prayed, then he gave a sermon, then he came to the women and admonished them and reminded them, and they began to give charity."],[5069,"When I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by a pleasant fragrance, so I said: 'What is this fragrance, O Jibril?' He said: 'This is the fragrance of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's wife. Her comb fell from her hand, and she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: My Lord and the Lord of your father. She said: Shall I inform my father of that? She said: Yes. So she informed him, and he summoned her and said: Do you have a lord other than me? She said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord. Then a brass cauldron was brought and heated, then she said: I have a request to you: gather my bones and the bones of my children. He said: You have a right upon us for so and so. Then he threw her and her children, until it reached an infant among them, and he said: Be patient, O slave woman, for you are upon the truth. So she and her children were thrown into the cauldron. Four spoke while they were infants: the witness of Yusuf, the companion of Jurayj, and 'Isa."],[5070,"One of them says: 'My father accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and was with my father; and a worn-out sandal is better than his father.'"],[5071,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I send my trained dog and it holds [the game].' He said: 'If it eats, then do not eat; and if it does not eat, then eat.'"],[5072,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to give an admonition and said: 'O people, you will be gathered barefoot and naked. As We began the first creation, We will repeat it; a promise upon Us. Indeed, We were doers. Indeed, the first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim ﷺ . Indeed, men from my nation will be brought and taken to the left side, and I will say: O Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. Then I will say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me, You were the Watcher over them, until His saying: And if You forgive them, indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise. Then it will be said: They did not cease turning back on their heels since you parted from them.'"],[5073,"A bowl of tharid was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Eat from its sides or from its edges, and do not eat from its middle, for the blessing is in its middle.'"],[5074,"The talbiyah of Musa ﷺ was: 'Here I am, Your servant and the son of Your two servants.' The talbiyah of 'Isa ﷺ was: 'Here I am, Your servant and the son of Your maidservant.' The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: 'Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, no partner has You.'"],[5075,"The Prophet ﷺ was in Makkah when a woman from the Ansar came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this wicked one has overcome me.' He said to her: 'If you are patient upon what you are, you will come on the Day of Resurrection with no sins upon you and no reckoning.' She said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will be patient until I meet Allah.' She said: 'I fear that the wicked one will strip me.' So he supplicated for her. Whenever she feared that he would come to her, she would go to the curtains of the Ka'bah, cling to them, and say to him: 'Begone!' and he would leave her."],[5076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing raisins and dates."],[5077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of Maymunah, and I placed for him water for ablution at night. Maymunah said: 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas placed this for you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, grant him understanding in religion and teach him the interpretation.'"],[5078,"Concession was given for the sick person to perform tayammum with clean earth if he was afflicted with smallpox."],[5079,"A man said: O Messenger of God, I find something in my chest; were I to become a black cinder, that would be more beloved to me than to speak of it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God is most great. Praise be to God who reduced his affair to a whisper."],[5080,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married while he was in ihrām."],[5081,"Whoever builds a mosque, even if like the scrape of a sandgrouse for its eggs, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[5082,"Be independent of people, even if by the splinter of a tooth-stick."],[5083,"When the Prophet ﷺ rose at night he began with a tooth-stick, or he said: he cleaned his teeth."],[5084,"A man reviled an ancestor of al-'Abbās from the time of ignorance, so al-'Abbās slapped him. His people came and said: By God, we will surely slap him as he slapped him, until they took up weapons, or until they put on weapons. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ascended the pulpit and said: O people, which of the people of the earth do you know to be most honored before God? They said: You. He said: Indeed al-'Abbās is of me and I am of him. Do not revile our dead, lest you harm our living. Then the people came and said: O Messenger of God, we seek refuge in God from your anger, so ask forgiveness for us."],[5085,"Whoever speaks about the Qur'ān without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5086,"Fosterage makes unlawful what lineage makes unlawful."],[5087,"Whoever dies addicted to wine will meet God as a worshipper of an idol."],[5088,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us our portion from Khaybar, and Abu Bakr gave it to us. When 'Umar came and the people became numerous on him, he sent to us and said: The people have become numerous on me, so if you wish I will give you wealth in place of your portion from Khaybar? Some of us looked at one another and we said: Yes. Then 'Umar was stabbed, and we did not take anything. Then 'Uthmān took it and refused to give it to us, saying: 'Umar had taken it from you."],[5089,"Hakīm b. Jubayr narrated to us, from Sa'īd b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This 'Abdullāh b. Bukayr is Kufan, a Shī'ī. And this hadīth we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from the hadīth of Hakīm b. Jubayr, from Sa'īd, from Ibn 'Abbās, and our mention of Hakīm has already passed, so we are free of the need to repeat mentioning him after."],[5090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended al-Safa one day and said: 'O calamity of the morning!' Quraysh gathered to him, and he said to them: 'If I told you that an enemy of yours would attack you in the morning or in the evening, would you believe me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Indeed, I am a warner to you before a severe punishment.' Abu Lahab stood up and said: 'Perish you, O Muhammad! Is it for this that you have gathered us?' Then it was revealed: 'Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he.'"],[5091,"And Ibrahim b. Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad b. Yahya b. Maymun narrated it to us. They said: Yahya b. Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us from al-A'mash, from 'Amr b. Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration. And we do not know this hadith to be reported from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except by this chain of transmission that we have mentioned. And we do not know anyone who said about it from 'Amr, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas except Yahya al-Umawi, and he is trustworthy. And we do not know that Abu al-Bakhtari transmitted from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas any other hadith than this one."],[5092,"He passed by a people who had set up a hen as a target and were shooting at it, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade taking any creature with a soul as a target.'"],[5093,"Khalid b. Sinan was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'That was a prophet whom his people neglected.'"],[5094,"Among the best of your clothes is white; let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it."],[5095,"Among the best of your kohl is ithmid; it clears the sight and grows the hair."],[5096,"'Uthman b. Hakim narrated to us from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration. And we do not know this hadith to be reported from the hadith of 'Uthman b. Hakim; rather, it is preserved from 'Abd Allah b. 'Uthman b. Khuthaym. And we have not heard anyone narrate it from al-Walid b. al-Qasim except Ishaq b. Bahlul. And we do not know that al-Walid b. al-Qasim narrated anything from Ibn Khuthaym."],[5097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Makkah and said: 'Indeed, you are the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah. And had not my people expelled me from you, I would not have left.'"],[5098,"He was in Makkah and recited Surah al-Najm until he reached: 'Have you considered al-Lat and al-'Uzza and Manat, the third, the other?' Then it slipped onto his tongue: 'Those are the high gharaniq; their intercession is to be hoped for.' He said: The idolaters of the people of Makkah heard that and were pleased by it. That was hard on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Allah, blessed and exalted is He, sent down: 'And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet except that when he wished, Satan cast into his wish. But Allah abolishes what Satan casts, then Allah establishes His verses.'"],[5099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only forbade pure silk. As for that whose warp is silk, there is no harm in it. And he forbade vessels of silver."],[5100,"A questioner asked. He said: It was revealed about al-Nadr b. al-Harith b. Kaladah."],[5101,"He used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn. He said: 'And your father Ibrahim used to seek protection for Isma'il and Ishaq with these words: I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from the evil of every devil and venomous creature and from every evil eye.'"],[5102,"A man from the Ansar married a woman from Bal'ajlan and spent a night with her. When morning came, he did not find her to be a virgin. Their case was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, who called the girl and she said, 'Yes, I was a virgin.' He ordered them to invoke curses upon each other, and he gave her the dower."],[5103,"When the Emigrants came to Madinah, they inherited from one another by pact rather than by kinship. Then this verse was revealed: 'And those of kinship are more entitled to inheritance from one another.'"],[5104,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the iron and leather be removed from those killed on the day of Uhud, and he said: 'Bury them in their clothes with their blood.'"],[5105,"When the verse 'The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord' was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ, he recited it. When he reached 'Our Lord, grant us Your forgiveness, and to You is the final return,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I have forgiven you.' When he said, 'Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or make a mistake,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I will not take you to task.' When he said, 'And do not lay upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I will not lay a burden upon you.' When he said, 'And do not make us bear what we have no strength for,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I will not make you bear it.' When he said, 'And pardon us,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I have pardoned you.' When he said, 'And forgive us,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I have forgiven you.' When he said, 'And have mercy on us,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I have had mercy on you.' When he said, 'And grant us victory over the disbelieving people,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I have granted you victory over the disbelieving people.'"],[5106,"Al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ghalib Abu al-Hudhayl, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5107,"Al-Sa'b b. Jaththamah gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the leg, or hindquarter, of a wild ass while he was in a state of ihram, and he returned it."],[5108,"Pride is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me over either of them, I will cast him into Hell."],[5109,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Does your Lord dye?' He said, 'Yes, with a dye that does not fade: red, yellow, and white.'"],[5110,"Amr b. 'Ali and al-Hasan b. al-Sabbah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Asbat b. Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5111,"Ibn 'Abbas said to me, 'O Sa'id, marry, for the best of this ummah was the one with the most wives.'"],[5112,"I am holding you by your waists, saying: 'Beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments, beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments, beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments,' three times. Then when I die, I will leave you, and I will be your forerunner at the Pond. Whoever arrives will succeed. Some people will be brought and taken to the left side. I will say, 'O Lord!' - I think he said - 'It will be said, \"They continued to turn back on their heels after you left.\"'"],[5113,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he stood up. He was asked about it, and he said, 'Death is a terror.'"],[5114,"It was revealed: “And whether you disclose what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it.” He said: That distressed them. They said: Which of us does not speak to himself? Then it was revealed: “Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity,” and the two verses after it."],[5115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ expiated his oath with a saa‘ of dates and commanded the people to do likewise; whoever could not find it, then half a saa‘ of wheat."],[5116,"Allah does not look at one who lets his garment hang below his ankles."],[5117,"Shu‘bah narrated to us, from Ash‘ath b. Sulaym, who is Ibn Abī al-Sha‘thā’, from Sa‘īd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ‘Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ. Shaybān also narrated it from Ash‘ath, from Sa‘īd, from Ibn ‘Abbās, as a marfū‘ report."],[5118,"The nations were displayed to me, and a prophet passed by me with a large group, and a prophet with a small band, until a great crowd passed by me. I said: My ummah? He said: That is Mūsā and his ummah. Then it was said to me: Look at the horizon, and there was a crowd that filled the entire horizon from all sides. It was said: This is your ummah, and besides these, seventy thousand of your ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. He said: The Prophet ﷺ went inside and did not clarify to us who they were, so the people speculated and spoke much. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: They are those who do not cauterize themselves, do not seek ruqyah, do not believe in omens, and upon their Lord they rely. ‘Ukkāshah b. Miḥṣan stood and said: Am I one of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. Then another stood and said: Am I one of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ‘Ukkāshah has preceded you to it."],[5119,"Muḥammad b. Fuḍayl narrated to us from Ḥuṣayn, from Sa‘īd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ‘Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. Shu‘bah also narrated this hadith and brought part of its wording, while Ibn Fuḍayl and Ziyād are more complete in the hadith than Shu‘bah. We do not know of Ḥuṣayn transmitting from Sa‘īd, from Ibn ‘Abbās, other than this hadith."],[5120,"Jibrīl was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he heard a sound and raised his head. He said: This is a gate of heaven that has been opened, never opened before except today. An angel descended through it and greeted him. Jibrīl said: This is an angel who has never descended to earth except today. He said to the Prophet ﷺ: Rejoice in what no one before you was given: the closing verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah. I think he said: No one will recite them and ask for anything except that it will be given to him."],[5121,"O my sons, go out from Makkah as pilgrims on foot until you return to Makkah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The pilgrim who rides has for every step his mount takes seventy good deeds, and the one who walks has for every step he takes seven hundred good deeds of the Ḥaram. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the good deeds of the Ḥaram? He said: A good deed is multiplied by a hundred thousand."],[5122,"Regarding the words of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: “And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution,” he said: It was revealed concerning ‘Abd Allāh b. Ubayy, who had a slave girl and would compel her to commit adultery. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: “Then indeed Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful.”"],[5123,"Mūsā ﷺ asked a request and it was given to Muḥammad ﷺ: His saying: “And Mūsā chose from his people seventy men,” up to His saying: “I shall write it for those who fear Me.”"],[5124,"These words are ruqyahs for every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and all His names, in general, from the evil of the venomous and the common, and the evil of an eye that strikes, and from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abū Qatarah and what he begot. Thirty-three of the angels came to their Lord and said: Sickness, sickness. He said: Take dust from your earth and wipe your sickness with it. Whoever takes a fee for it or conceals it from anyone will never succeed."],[5125,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade nabīdh made in earthenware jars."],[5126,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5127,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthen jars."],[5128,"Mansur b. Hayyan narrated to me, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition in which al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad was present. When they reached the people, they found that they had dispersed, and one man with abundant wealth remained and did not leave. He said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' Al-Miqdad lunged at him and killed him. One of his companions said to him, 'You killed a man who bears witness that there is no god but Allah? By Allah, I will mention that to the Prophet ﷺ.' When they came to the Prophet, they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a man bore witness that there is no god but Allah, and al-Miqdad killed him.' He said, 'Summon al-Miqdad for me. O Miqdad, did you kill a man who says \"there is no god but Allah\"? What will you do about \"there is no god but Allah\" tomorrow?' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, be discerning, and do not say to one who offers you peace'—or 'submission'; Abu Sa'id, meaning Ja'far b. Salama, was uncertain—'you are not a believer, seeking the goods of the life of this world. With Allah are abundant spoils. Thus you were before.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Miqdad, 'He was a believing man who concealed his faith among a disbelieving people, and he disclosed his faith, and you killed him. Likewise, you used to conceal your faith in Makkah before.'"],[5130,"He used to say between the two prostrations: 'My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me refuge, and grant me well-being,' or something similar."],[5131,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Who is in Paradise?' He said, 'The prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the buried infant girl is in Paradise.'"],[5132,"Whoever enters to visit a sick person whose time has not come, and says seven times: 'I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,' he will be healed."],[5133,"Ma'mar narrated to me, from Ayyub, from 'Abd Allah b. Sa'id b. Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5134,"Ibn 'Ulayya narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Abd Allah b. Sa'id, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5135,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah and found the Jews fasting on the day of 'Ashura'. They were asked about that, and they said, 'This is the day on which Allah made Moses and the Children of Israel prevail over Pharaoh, so we fast it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We are more entitled to Moses than you.' So he commanded fasting on it."],[5136,"A man was with the Prophet ﷺ while in a state of ihram, and his she-camel threw him, breaking his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his head, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with his hair matted.'"],[5137,"Qays narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet."],[5138,"Qays narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5139,"It was said: O Messenger of God, or they mentioned from the Messenger of God ﷺ something like this: O Prophet of God, what do you think about what we do? Is it something we initiate, or something already decreed? He said: No, rather it is something already decreed. He said: Then the people said to one another: Then striving is of no avail."],[5140,"O son of Adam, if you remember Me in private, I remember you in private; and if you remember Me in an assembly, I remember you in an assembly better than those in which you remember Me."],[5141,"No one will enter Paradise with an atom's weight of pride, and no one will enter Hell with an atom's weight of faith."],[5142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent someone to Khaybar—I think it was Abu Bakr—and he returned defeated, he and those with him. The next day, he sent 'Umar, and he returned defeated, calling his companions cowards and they calling him a coward. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'I will give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves God and His Messenger and whom God and His Messenger love. He will not return until God grants victory through him.' The people became eager. He said: 'Where is 'Ali?' It turned out he was suffering from an eye ailment. The Messenger of God ﷺ spat into his eye, then gave him the banner. He waved it, and God granted victory through him."],[5143,"The Banu Asad came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, we have submitted, and the Arabs fought you but we did not fight you. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Their understanding is little, and Satan speaks on their tongues.' Then this verse was revealed: 'They consider it a favor to you that they have submitted. Say: Do not consider your submission a favor to me...' (Qur'an 49:17)."],[5144,"The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind drowns."],[5145,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am ruined. He said: 'What has ruined you?' He said: I turned my mount around last night, but he did not reply to him. Then God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed this verse: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish.' He said: He means: approach from the front or the back, but avoid the anus and menstruation."],[5146,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then said: 'Is there anyone here from Hudhayl? Your companion is being held at the gate of Paradise'—I think he said: 'because of his debt.'"],[5147,"Regarding the words of God, Blessed and Exalted: 'Whatever you cut down of palm trees or left standing on their roots, it was by God's permission, and to disgrace the transgressors' (Qur'an 59:5). He said: 'Linah' means the date palm. 'And to disgrace the transgressors'—he said: They brought them down from their fortresses and were commanded to cut the palm trees. They said: We have cut some, so let us ask the Messenger of God ﷺ: Is there any reward for us in what we cut, and any sin upon us in what we left? So God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'Whatever you cut down of palm trees, it was by God's permission; and whatever you left, it was by God's permission.'"],[5148,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he said: 'Our Lord, to You be praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.'"],[5149,"'Umar ؓ used to give permission to the people of Badr, and he gave permission to me along with them. Some of them said: Do you give permission to this young man to join us when among our sons there are those like him? 'Umar said: He is one of those whom you know. One day he gave them permission, and gave me permission with them. He asked them about this surah: 'When God's help and victory comes' (Qur'an 110:1). They said: God, Blessed and Exalted, commanded His Prophet that when God grants him victory, he should seek His forgiveness and turn to Him in repentance. He said: What do you say, O Ibn 'Abbas? I said: It is not like that. Rather, He informed His Prophet of the approach of his term. He said: 'When God's help and victory comes'—the victory of Makkah—'and you see the people entering God's religion in multitudes,' that is a sign of your death. 'Then glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance.' 'Umar said to them: How can you blame me regarding him after what you have seen?"],[5150,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, Abu Bakr said: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we will return. The Messenger of Allah has been expelled; they will all perish.' Then when this verse was revealed: 'Permission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged. And indeed, Allah is competent to give them victory. [They are] those who have been evicted from their homes,' Abu Bakr knew that there would be fighting."],[5151,"The jinn used to sit in the sky and listen to the revelation. When they heard a word, they added to it many times over. As for the word, it would be true, and as for the rest, it would be false—until the Prophet ﷺ was sent, and they were prevented from their sitting places. The stars were not thrown with before that. Iblis said to them: 'This is only because of something that has happened on earth.' So he sent his troops, and they found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing praying. They informed him, and he said: 'This is the event that has happened on earth.'"],[5152,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Jibril ﷺ : 'Why do you not come to us more than you do?' Then it was revealed: 'And we do not descend except by the command of your Lord...' the verse."],[5153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade throwing the jamrah until the sun rises."],[5154,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer on Friday and recited: 'Alif Lam Mim. The revelation...' and 'Has there come upon man...'"],[5155,"A person is commanded to prostrate on seven bones: his hands, his feet, his knees, and his face."],[5156,"The people of Paradise are those who fill their ears with good that they hear, and the people of Hell are those who fill their ears with evil that they hear. I heard Hamdan b. Ali say: I heard Muslim say: It reached me that 'Uqbah b. Abi Thubayt used to call birds and they would answer him."],[5157,"The one who sees is not like the one who is told. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, informed Musa that his people had been tempted, but he did not throw the tablets. When he saw them, he threw the tablets."],[5158,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Paradise white. The most beloved of garments to Allah is white, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it."],[5159,"For a boy there are two 'aqiqahs, and for a girl one 'aqiqah."],[5160,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash reported to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ. There is disagreement about this hadith from 'Ata'; it is reported from 'Ata', from Habibah bt. Maysarah, from Umm Kurz, like this. 'Amr b. Dinar and al-Hajjaj b. Artah reported it. And Qays b. Sa'd reported it from 'Ata', from Umm Kurz, without inserting Habibah bt. Maysarah between them."],[5161,"The value of a shield at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ten dirhams."],[5162,"The first thing a servant is rewarded with after his death is that all those who followed his funeral procession are forgiven."],[5163,"Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās. He did not confirm it because we had already transmitted it from other than ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAṭāʾ, and two men narrated it from ʿAbd al-Malik: Khālid b. al-Ḥārith and Isḥāq b. Yūsuf."],[5164,"He forbade selling palm trees for two or three years, that they be bought while still on the palm trees by measure, or that the fruit be sold until its goodness becomes evident."],[5165,"The Prophet ﷺ would not throw the pebbles until the sun had declined."],[5166,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed one hundred garlanded and draped camels."],[5167,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away while I was circumcised."],[5168,"An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a ḥajj."],[5169,"Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5170,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a dead sheep lying with its legs raised, and said: 'What would it harm the owners of this if they made use of its hide?' So Sawdah tanned it and used it for soaking."],[5171,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, I declared my wife to be like my mother's back, then I saw her leg in the moonlight and had intercourse with her before I offered expiation.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Offer expiation and do not repeat.'"],[5172,"If the son of Adam had a valley full of wealth, he would wish for another like it. Nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam except dust, and God turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[5173,"He called his brother ʿUbayd Allāh on the day of ʿArafah, and food was brought. He said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'You are a household who are followed. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ being brought a milking vessel of milk on a day like this and he drank.'"],[5174,"I attended the funeral of Maymunah with Ibn 'Abbas, and he said: This is the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so do not shake her bier or jolt it, for the Prophet ﷺ had nine wives and he used to apportion his time among eight of them, but not for one."],[5175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked at a fast pace (ramal) in his Hajj and 'Umrah, as did Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and the caliphs. 'Amr b. 'Ali added: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked at a fast pace for three rounds and walked at a normal pace for four."],[5176,"Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents or settles a debt on their behalf will be resurrected among the righteous."],[5177,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[5178,"When one of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."],[5179,"No call to prayer (adhan) was given for the Prophet ﷺ on either the Fitr or the Adha prayer."],[5180,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed forty sa's from a man of the Ansar. The Ansari later became in need, so he came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Nothing has come to us yet. He said: Then he became in need again, so he came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Nothing has come to us yet. The man then wanted to speak, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say anything but good, for I am the best of those who give loans. Then he gave him forty extra and forty for his loan, giving him eighty."],[5181,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a sacrificial camel (badanah) and I can afford it, but I cannot find one. He said: Slaughter a sheep."],[5182,"The gate of Hellfire will be entered by no one except a man who seeks to quench his anger through Allah's wrath."],[5183,"He specified Dhat 'Irq as the miqat for the people of the east."],[5184,"Regarding the pilgrim in ihram: he may wear leather socks if he does not find sandals, and he did not say: let him cut them."],[5185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ghayl (intercourse with a nursing mother), and he said: If it were harmful to anyone, it would have harmed the Persians and the Romans."],[5186,"Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition, then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[5187,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord – meaning with his heart."],[5188,"The religion will remain firmly established as long as there remain twenty men from Quraysh."],[5189,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a crier to proclaim in the heart of Makkah, commanding the sadaqat al-fitr and saying: It is an obligatory right upon every Muslim, male or female, young or old, free or slave, present or desert-dweller: two mudds of wheat or a sa' of other food besides that. Surely the child belongs to the bed, and the stone is for the adulterer."],[5190,"A sheep died, and the Prophet ﷺ said to the owners of the sheep: Why did you not tan its skin and then make use of it?"],[5191,"A domestic animal belonging to Maymunah died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Why did you not make use of its hide?"],[5192,"A sheep belonging to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Why did you not make use of its hide?"],[5193,"My uncle al-Qasim b. Yahya b. 'Ata' b. Muqaddam narrated to me from 'Abd Allah b. 'Uthman b. Khuthaym, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5194,"Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash narrated to us from 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufay', from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5195,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: Slaughter, and there is no harm. Another said: I shaved before I threw the pebbles. He said: Throw, and there is no harm. Another said: I visited the House before I threw the pebbles. He said: Throw, and there is no harm."],[5196,"The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; and the worst rows of women are the first ones, and the best are the last ones."],[5197,"The best of you are those who are most gentle with their shoulders in prayer."],[5198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the beating of women. Then he heard a loud voice at night and said, “I certainly hear a loud voice.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, you permitted the beating of women.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best of you is the best of you to his family, and I am the best of you to my family.”"],[5199,"He used to send the baggage at the end of the night, and I was among them."],[5200,"The Prophet ﷺ buried a man in a grave at night, lit a lamp for him, dug a lahd for him from the direction of the qiblah, and said the takbir over him four times. And he said, “May Allah have mercy on you. You were indeed often sighing, a constant reciter of the Qur'an.”"],[5201,"Ibn al-Zubayr led the people in the Maghrib prayer and said the salam in the first two rak'ahs, then he went to the Black Stone to touch it. They glorified Allah because of that, so he returned and prayed the remaining rak'ah, then he said the salam and prostrated twice. That was mentioned to Ibn 'Abbas, and he said, “He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet ﷺ.”"],[5202,"He married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[5203,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[5204,"A sheep belonging to Maymunah died, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Why did you not make use of its hide?” He said, “Tanning the hide is its purification.”"],[5205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together on the Day of 'Arafah. He prayed Zuhr with an adhan and an iqamah, and 'Asr with an iqamah, and he did not pray any voluntary prayer between them."],[5206,"Whoever enters the House enters into a good deed, then he leaves forgiven."],[5207,"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's house and said, “I will certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” A cushion was placed for me, and I slept along its length, while he and his family slept. Then he got up in the middle of the night, or shortly before it, or shortly after it, and began wiping the sleep from his face. Then he recited the last verses of Al 'Imran until he finished. Then he got up, went to a hanging waterskin, took it, and performed wudu. Then he stood and prayed, and I got up and did as he had done. Then I came and stood at his side, and he placed his hand on my head, then turned me around and put me on his right. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then two, then two, then two, then he performed witr."],[5208,"I stood with the Prophet ﷺ on his left, so he moved me to his right."],[5209,"He used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his prodding and his blowing” — I think he said, “and his spitting” — “and from the punishment of the grave.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is this that you seek refuge from?” He said, “As for his prodding, it is the whispering he casts. As for his spitting, it is poetry. As for his blowing, it is the doubts he casts” — meaning in prayer, to interrupt his prayer, or a person's prayer. “As for the punishment of the grave, he used to say, ‘Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine.’”"],[5210,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I am the envoy of women to you. This jihad God has prescribed upon men: if they strive they are rewarded, and if they are killed they are alive with their Lord, provided for. We, the community of women, serve them, so what do we get from that?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Convey to the women you meet that obedience to the husband and recognition of his right equals that, and few of you do it.'"],[5211,"The likeness of one who prays with his head bound up is like one who prays with his hands tied."],[5212,"Juwayriyah's name was Barrah, so the Prophet ﷺ changed her name and called her Juwayriyah. He passed by her while she was in her prayer place glorifying God and remembering God after the day had risen, and he said: 'O Juwayriyah, have you been in your place all along?' She said: 'I have been in this place of mine.' He said: 'I have uttered four phrases that are better than what you have said.' She said: 'How?' He said: 'Glory be to God as many as His creation; Glory be to God as much as pleases Him; Glory be to God the weight of His Throne; Glory be to God the ink of His words; and praise be to God likewise.'"],[5213,"God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a man, or a woman in her anus."],[5214,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to al-Abbas: 'On the morning of Monday, come to me with your children so that I may supplicate for you with a supplication by which God may benefit you.' So he came early, and we came early with him. He said: 'O God, forgive al-Abbas and his children with a forgiveness outward and inward that leaves no sin. O God, protect him in his offspring.'"],[5215,"Thawr narrated to us, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Thawr except Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata', and we do not know anyone who agreed with him in its transmission, and we do not know it being narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this route, and we do not know that Makhul attributed to Kurayb any hadith other than this one. Abd al-Wahhab was from Basra, then moved to Baghdad; nothing was written from him in Basra. He came to Baghdad and narrated, and one of his companions informed me that he wrote to his family: 'He has written from me, so praise God.' This hadith, in my view, has no basis, and I think he narrated it during the days of al-Rashid because the latter gave him something."],[5216,"When he drank, he would breathe twice into the vessel."],[5217,"The Prophet ﷺ slept until he snored, then got up and prayed without performing ablution."],[5218,"Do not imitate the Persians; change the beards."],[5219,"Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad b. al-Walid b. Nuwayfi', from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas."],[5220,"Dimam b. Tha'labah, one of the Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He was a tough, hairy man with two braids. He hobbled his camel at the gate of the mosque, then entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and stood before him while he was among his companions. He said: 'Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Here I am, the son of Abd al-Muttalib.' He said: 'Are you Muhammad?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'O son of Abd al-Muttalib, I will ask you and be harsh in questioning, so do not resent it.' He said: 'Ask whatever appears to you, I will not resent it.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, your God, and the God of those before you, and the God of those after you: did God send you to us as a Messenger?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O God, yes.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, your God, and the God of those before you, and the God of those after you: did God command you to order us to cast off these rivals that our fathers worshipped and to worship God without associating anything with Him?' He said: 'O God, yes.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, your God, and the God of those before you, and the God of those after you: did God command you that we perform these five prayers?' He said: 'O God, yes.' Then he faced the obligations one by one, naming them to him, until he finished. He said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I will act upon these obligations, not adding to them nor subtracting from them.' Then he turned away. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If the man with two braids is truthful, he will enter Paradise.' He went to his camel and untied its hobble, then departed until he came to his people. When they gathered to him, they said: 'What is behind you, O Dimam?' He began to revile al-Lat and al-Uzza. They said: 'Stop, beware of leprosy, beware of elephantiasis, beware of madness.' He said: 'Woe to you, you are only in falsehood. By God, they neither harm nor benefit. God has sent a Messenger and revealed to him a Book and prescribed for him a religion. I have brought you that which he is upon.' By God, by the evening of that day there remained no man or woman in his settlement except as a Muslim. We have never heard of an envoy like Dimam b. Tha'labah."],[5221,"My father sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding some camels he had given him from the charity camels. When I came to him, it was the night of Maymunah, his maternal aunt. He went to the mosque and prayed Isha, then came to his house, threw off his garment, and entered with his wife in her clothes. Then I took my garment and wrapped myself in it, then lay down. I said: 'I will not sleep tonight until I see what the Messenger of God ﷺ does.' He slept until he snored, and when as much of the night passed as God willed, he got up and went out. He came to a tied waterskin or vessel, untied its cord, poured water on it, then pressed on the mouth of the waterskin and began washing his hands. He performed ablution until he finished. I wanted to get up and pour water for him. Then he stood up to pray, so I got up and did the same as he did. I stood on his left, and he took me and placed me on his right. He prayed thirteen rak'ahs, then lay down until Bilal came and called him to prayer. He got up and prayed two rak'ahs before Fajr."],[5222,"Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Minhal b. 'Amr, from 'Ali b. 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas, from his father. As for the hadith of al-Thawri:"],[5223,"Mu'awiyah b. Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib—meaning Ibn Abi Thabit—from Muhammad b. 'Ali, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5224,"Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn—meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman—from Habib, from Muhammad b. 'Ali, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, similar to the hadith of Sufyan from Habib."],[5225,"Mansur narrated to us, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5226,"If one of you, when he goes to his wife, says: 'O Allah, keep the devil away from me and keep the devil away from what You provide me,' then if a child is decreed between them, Shu'bah said: the devil will not be given power over him, or the devil will not attend him."],[5227,"Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it. This hadith was narrated by a group from Mansur, and we have limited ourselves to those we named. We do not know that this wording was narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except through this route. As for the hadith of al-A'mash, we know of no one who ascribed it except Abu Usamah; others besides Abu Usamah narrated it as mawquf."],[5228,"A woman raised a child to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Is there Hajj for this one?' He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[5229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gold ring on a man's hand, took it off, threw it, and said, 'One of you intends to take a coal from the Fire and put it in his hand.' After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, it was said to the man, 'Take your ring and benefit from it.' He said, 'No, by Allah, I will never take it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw it.'"],[5230,"A son of Ibn 'Abbas died, and he said, 'O Kurayb, go out and see if anyone has gathered for my son.' I went out and said, 'Forty or more have gathered.' He said, 'Bring him out, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no deceased person over whom forty or more pray, interceding for him, except that their intercession is accepted for him.\"'"],[5231,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'My sister vowed to perform Hajj on foot.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah does not benefit from your sister's hardship; let her perform Hajj riding and expiate for her oath.'"],[5232,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder or bit into a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."],[5233,"Do not sit in the roads. If you must, then return the greeting, lower the gaze, guide the way, and help with the burden."],[5234,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say"],[5235,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say when he finished his prayer: O Allah, I ask You for mercy from You by which You guide my heart, unite my affairs, gather my scattered state, set right my absent ones, raise my witness, purify my deeds, restore my affection, and make me free of need from anyone other than You. O Allah, grant me faith after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your generosity in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for the hospitality of the martyrs, the life of the fortunate, and victory over enemies. O Allah, I have brought my need to You, even if my judgment is short, my deeds are weak, and I am in need of Your mercy. O Allah, O Judge of affairs, O Healer of what is in the breasts, protect me from the punishment of the Blaze, from the call of destruction, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever good my judgment falls short of and my request does not reach—I think he said: which You have given to any of Your creation, or good which You will give to any of Your servants—I desire it from You and ask You for it by Your mercy, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You, O Possessor of the strong rope, O Possessor of the right command, O Allah, I ask You for security on the Day of Warning, and Paradise on the Day of Eternity, with the near ones, the witnesses, the bowing, the prostrating, the fulfillers of covenants. Indeed You are Merciful, Loving, and You are Witness over all things, You do what You will. O Allah, make us guides, guided, not astray and not leading astray, at peace with Your allies, enemies to Your enemies, loving people by Your love, and hostile by Your hostility to whoever opposes You. O Allah, this is the supplication, and upon You is the response, and this is the effort, and upon You is reliance. Make for me light in my grave, light in my heart, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light before me, light behind me, light above me, light below me, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, and light in my bones—I think he said: and make for me a great light with You. Glory be to the One who wore might and said by it, glory be to Allah who wore majesty and generosity, glory be to the One for whom glorification is not befitting except for Him, glory be to the Possessor of bounty and blessings, glory be to the Possessor of majesty and honor, glory be to the Possessor of glory and generosity."],[5236,"Isa b. al-Mukhtar narrated to us from Muhammad b. Abi Layla from Dawud b. Ali b. Abdullah b. Abbas from his father, from Ibn Abbas"],[5237,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting at al-Qahah, and he bled so much that he was feared for."],[5238,"Bakr narrated to us from Isa b. al-Mukhtar from Ibn Abi Layla from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through several channels that the Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while fasting, but they did not mention in their hadiths from Ibn Abbas: 'and he bled so much that he was feared for.'"],[5239,"He said regarding the fast of Ashura: Fast it and differ from the Jews in it, and fast a day before it and a day after it."],[5240,"Some people from Mudar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people from Mudar, a drought has struck us, and we have come to you with no stallion of ours bringing us and no provision of ours carrying us. The Prophet ﷺ said: O Allah, give us rain. They did not leave until they were given rain."],[5241,"The blessing of horses is in their chestnut color."],[5242,"The orphan's head is wiped like this—Salih described that he placed his palm on the middle of the head, then brought it down to the front, or to the forehead—and whoever has a father, like this—and he described that he placed his palm on the front of the head next to the forehead, then raised it to the middle of the head."],[5243,"O Allah, bless my community in its early morning."],[5244,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Kaaba, and around the Kaaba were such-and-such number of idols. He began striking them with a stick in his hand and saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished."],[5245,"Place the whip where the servant can see it."],[5246,"Clientage (wala') is not transferable nor changeable."],[5247,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder or some meat, then prayed without rinsing his mouth or touching water."],[5248,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5249,"That he married while in a state of ihram."],[5250,"That he married Maymunah while in a state of ihram."],[5251,"That the Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while in a state of ihram."],[5252,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5253,"Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5254,"Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5255,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5256,"And Ahmad b. 'Abdah narrated to us, from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr, from Jabir, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5257,"The muhrim may wear trousers if he cannot find an izar, and he may wear leather socks if he cannot find sandals."],[5258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed seven [rak'ahs] combined and eight [rak'ahs] combined."],[5259,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: eight and seven."],[5260,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have been enlisted in such-and-such a military expedition, and my wife wants me to perform Hajj with her.' He said: 'Return and perform Hajj with your wife.'"],[5261,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[5262,"He used to perform ablution with the leftover water of Maymunah."],[5263,"Every division that was made in the pre-Islamic era remains as it was divided, and every division that Islam came upon before it was divided is to be divided according to the division of Islam."],[5264,"Muhammad b. Abi 'Adi narrated to us from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5265,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5266,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the daughter of Hamzah, and the Prophet of Allah said: 'She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding, and whatever is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by breastfeeding.'"],[5267,"Breaking the fast while traveling is a firm determination."],[5268,"Ibn Abbas ؓ used to combine the two prayers while traveling and say: 'It is the Sunnah.'"],[5269,"I said to Jabir b. Zayd: 'What interrupts the prayer?' He said: 'Ibn Abbas said: the black dog and the menstruating woman.' He said: I said: 'He used to mention a third.' He said: 'What is it?' I said: 'The donkey.' He said: 'Slow down, the donkey.' I said: 'He used to mention a fourth.' He said: 'What is it?' I said: 'The uncircumcised disbeliever.' He said: 'If you can prevent any disbeliever or Muslim from passing in front of you, then do so.'"],[5270,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, and he raised it to the Prophet."],[5271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the ransom for the captives of the Jahiliyyah at four hundred."],[5272,"The evil eye is real."],[5273,"The servant's evil deeds and good deeds will be brought and deducted from one another; if a good deed remains for him, he will be given ample space in Paradise."],[5274,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a commander over an army, he would summon him and enjoin him to fear Allah and to treat those Muslims with him well. Then he would say: 'Fight in the name of Allah and in the cause of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not break your pledges, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the polytheists, call them to one of three options: invite them to Islam; if they respond, accept from them and withhold from them. Then invite them to emigrate, and inform them that they will have the same rights and duties as the emigrants. If they respond, accept from them and withhold from them. If they do not, inform them that they are like the Bedouin Muslims: they have no share in the fay' or the war booty, and the judgment of Allah that applies to the Muslims will apply to them. If they ask you to make a pact with them based on the judgment of Allah, do not do so, for you do not know whether you will hit upon the judgment of Allah concerning them or not. Rather, make a pact with them based on your own judgment. Then if they ask you to grant them the protection of Allah, do not do so; rather, grant them your protection and the protection of your companions, for if you violate your protection and the protection of your companions, it is better than violating the protection of Allah.'"],[5275,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded applying henna and forbade black dye."],[5276,"I am the most knowledgeable of you about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he performed ablution washing each part once."],[5277,"He performed ablution washing each part once."],[5278,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and washed his hands and face once each."],[5279,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped the outer and inner parts of his ears."],[5280,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution with one scoop of water at a time."],[5281,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and sprinkled water."],[5282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he scooped one handful (of water) and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose and washed his face. Then he scooped one handful and washed his right hand. Then he scooped one handful and washed his left hand. Then he scooped one handful and wiped his head and his ears, and he sprinkled water on his feet while he had two sandals on them, and he wiped their tops and their bottoms."],[5283,"One washing for each limb suffices when it reaches the parts of ablution."],[5284,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once (each part) once, and he combined sniffing water and rinsing the mouth with one handful."],[5285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder (of meat) then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[5286,"If one of you doubts in prayer and does not know how many he has prayed, three or four, let him pray one rak'ah and perform two prostrations while sitting before he greets (with salam). Then if the rak'ah he prayed was a fifth, he makes it even with these two prostrations, and if it was a fourth, they are a humiliation for Satan."],[5287,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the people were with him. He stood a long standing, about the length of Surat al-Baqarah. Then he bowed a long bowing. Then he stood a long standing, but less than the first standing. Then he bowed a long bowing, but less than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he did in the second rak'ah the like of that. Then he finished, and the sun had become clear. He said: 'The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. So when you see that, remember Allah.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reach for something in your place, then we saw you draw back.' He said: 'I saw Paradise, or Paradise was shown to me, and I reached for a bunch (of grapes) from it. If I had taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remains. And I saw the Fire, and I have never seen a sight like today. And I saw most of its inhabitants were women.' They said: 'Why, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Because of their ingratitude to their husbands.' Rawh said: 'And the husband is the spouse.' 'And because of their ingratitude for kindness. If you were to do good to one of them always, then she saw something from you, she would say: I have never seen any good from you.'"],[5288,"Three things do not break the fast: vomiting, cupping, and a wet dream."],[5289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while they were in a gathering, or in the mosque, and said: 'Shall I tell you of the best of people in condition?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'A man holding the rein of his horse in jihad in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. Shall I tell you of the one who comes next? A man secluded in a mountain pass who establishes prayer, gives zakah, and secludes himself from the evils of people. Shall I tell you of the worst of people? The one who is asked by Allah but does not give by Him.'"],[5290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing four: the ant, the bee, the frog, and the shrike."],[5291,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has not performed Hajj. If I carry him on a camel, he cannot stay on it, and if I tie him down, I am not sure he would be safe.' He said: 'Would you pay a debt on behalf of your father if he owed one?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[5292,"Hisham b. Hassan reported to us from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Yahya b. Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration. This hadith has been subject to disagreement: al-Zuhri reported from Sulayman b. Yasar contrary to what Yahya b. Abi Ishaq said. We will mention each hadith in its place with its wording. We do not know that Muhammad b. Sirin reported with a chain from Yahya b. Abi Ishaq other than this hadith."],[5293,"A woman from Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation upon His servants regarding Hajj has reached my father, an old man who cannot sit upright on a mount. Will it fulfill it for him if I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[5294,"Sulaymān b. Yasār narrated to me, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās, from al-Faḍl b. ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. This report is the correct one, and Yaḥyā b. Abī Isḥāq overlooked part of it. The correct version is the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Abī Salamah omitted one man from the chain and did not mention al-Faḍl."],[5295,"He passed by Abū Hurayrah while he was performing ablution and said: 'Do you know from what I am performing ablution? I am performing ablution from eating curds of dried milk. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat bread and meat and then pray without performing ablution.'"],[5296,"They used to trade at Minā, ʿArafah, and during the days of Hajj, but they feared doing business within the sanctuary. Then the verse was revealed: 'There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord during the seasons of Hajj.'"],[5297,"There was a woman who prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was one of the most beautiful of people. Some of the people would come forward in the row so as not to see her, and some would lag behind in the back row. When he bowed, he would turn and look. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed concerning her: 'And We know those who go forward among you, and We know those who lag behind.'"],[5298,"The scribe of the Prophet ﷺ was called al-Sijill."],[5299,"Glory be to Allah and with His praise; Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent; I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him. Whoever says them, they are written down as he said them and then attached to the Throne. No sin committed by their owner erases them until he meets Allah on the day he meets Him, while they are sealed as he said them."],[5300,"If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and then seek Allah's forgiveness, and He would forgive them."],[5301,"A man pitched his tent over a grave, not knowing that it was a grave. He recited Sūrat Tabārak (al-Mulk), and he heard someone from the grave saying: 'It is the deliverer! It is the deliverer!' He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'It is the deliverer from the punishment of the grave.'"],[5302,"When he finished the prayer, he would say: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things. O Allah, there is no one to withhold what You give, and no one to give what You withhold, and no one's wealth or fortune can benefit them against You.'"],[5303,"When the land is fertile, shorten your journeys and give the riding camels their due, for Allah is gentle and loves gentleness. When the land is barren, travel quickly upon it and journey by night, for the land is folded up at night. Beware of the middle of the road, for it is the abode of snakes and the resting place of wild beasts."],[5304,"The people of Paradise are those who do not die until they fill their ears with good praise."],[5305,"Abū Hilāl narrated to us, from ʿUqbah b. Abī Thubayt, from Abū al-Jawzāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, with a similar report. Ḥamdān said: I heard Muslim b. Ibrāhīm say: I heard that ʿUqbah b. Abī Thubayt used to call birds and they would respond to him. ʿUqbah was a trustworthy, reliable, devout man from Baṣrah."],[5306,"When it was the night I was taken on the Night Journey and I awoke in Makkah, I was distressed by my affair and knew that the people would deny me. So he sat apart, sad. The enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, passed by him, came and sat down, and said, as if mocking me: 'Has anything happened?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is it?' He said: 'I was taken on a night journey tonight.' He said: 'To where?' He said: 'To Jerusalem.' He said: 'Then you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'He did not show that he believed him, so he said: 'What do you think? If I call your people, will you tell them what you told me?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'O assembly of Banu Ka'b b. Lu'ayy!' The gatherings dispersed to him and they came and sat with him. He said: 'Tell your people what you told me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was taken on a night journey tonight.' They said: 'To where?' He said: 'To Jerusalem.' They said: 'And you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Some clapped and some put their hands on their heads in denial, rejecting it. They said: 'Can you describe the mosque for us?' He said: 'I went on describing, and I kept describing until some of the description became confused for me.' He said: 'The mosque was brought while I was looking at it, until it was placed near the house of Ghifar, or 'Aqil.' He said: 'I described it while I was looking at it.' He said: 'Among the people were those who had seen it, so the people said: 'As for the description, by Allah, he has got it right.'"],[5307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which deed is most beloved to Allah?' He said: 'The one who is constantly traveling (al-hall al-murtahil).' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is the one constantly traveling?' He said: 'The companion of the Qur'an, who traverses it from its beginning to its end; whenever he finishes, he starts again.'"],[5308,"A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5309,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night."],[5310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ashajj 'Abd al-Qays: 'You have two traits that Allah and His Messenger love: forbearance and deliberateness.'"],[5311,"The best of the people of the east are 'Abd al-Qays."],[5312,"I am the opponent of whoever wrongs 'Abd al-Qays."],[5313,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early mornings on Thursdays."],[5314,"The delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are this tribe from Rabi'ah, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with something we can act upon and call those behind us to.' He said: 'I command you with four things and forbid you from four: I command you to testify that there is no god but Allah, to establish prayer, to give zakah, and to give one-fifth of what you gain as booty for Allah. And I forbid you from dubba', hantam, muzaffat, and naqir.'"],[5315,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we slept through the prayer, the morning prayer, until the sun rose. The Prophet ﷺ ordered a mu'adhdhin, who called the adhan as he used to call every day, and he prayed two rak'ahs of Fajr as he used to pray every day, then prayed the morning prayer as he used to pray every day."],[5316,"A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: 'I am a man from the people of Iraq who makes these images.' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever makes an image will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection to blow life into it, but he will not be able to blow, or he will not be able to blow life into it.'"],[5317,"Yahya b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5318,"Isma'il b. Muslim reported to us from al-Hasan, from his brother Sa'id, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5319,"Ibn Abi 'Adiyy reported to us from 'Awf, from Sa'id b. Abi al-Hasan, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5320,"Whoever makes an image will be required to blow into it on the Day of Resurrection, but he will not be able to blow."],[5321,"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's. The Prophet ﷺ got up during the night to pray, so I performed ablution and went and stood on his left. When he realized that I wanted to pray, he moved me to his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and performed witr with five or seven [rak'ahs], then he moved me, then he slept until I heard his snoring. Then the prayer was announced and he prayed without performing ablution. Sa'id said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was protected."],[5322,"Whoever is pleased to forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, let him forbid nabidh made in earthenware jars."],[5323,"O youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Indeed, whoever Allah preserves his private parts for him will enter Paradise."],[5324,"Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah reported to us from Qatadah, from Abu Talib al-Duba'i, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[5325,"A cupper cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he was called Abu Taybah. So he gave him his fee and reduced his due from his yield. He said: Ibn 'Abbas used to say: If it had been unlawful, the Messenger of Allah would not have given it to him."],[5326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at Dhul-Hulayfah. I saw him mark his camel on the right side of its hump, then wipe the blood away from it. He garlanded it with two sandals, then mounted his riding camel. When he reached al-Bayda', he entered ihram and declared the talbiyah for Hajj."],[5327,"'Abd al-A'la reported to us from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This action we do not know anyone to have narrated from the Prophet ﷺ except Ibn 'Abbas, and we do not know for it from Ibn 'Abbas any route except this one."],[5328,"A man said to Ibn 'Abbas: What is this fatwa that has spread – or branched out – among the people, that whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram? He said: That is the sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, even if you dislike it."],[5329,"It is not appropriate for a servant to say, 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[5330,"He used to say at times of distress: There is no god but Allah, the All-Knowing, the Forbearing. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of the Noble Throne."],[5331,"A man's cloak was snatched away by the wind, and he cursed it. The Prophet ﷺ heard of that and said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded. And whoever curses something that does not deserve it, the curse returns upon its owner."],[5332,"This hadith was also narrated by Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah and Hisham b. Abi 'Abd Allah, both from Qatadah, from Abu al-'Aliyah, but they did not say: from Ibn 'Abbas. 5337 5331 - Abu Musa reported it to us from Mu'adh b. Hisham, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-'Aliyah."],[5333,"And on the authority of al-Ansari, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu al-'Aliyah."],[5334,"Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the illness of the sick, I would have delayed the last evening prayer; I think he said: until a third of the night."],[5335,"When something distressed the Prophet ﷺ, he would say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Mighty. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth and Lord of the Noble Throne. Then he would supplicate."],[5336,"I learned the muhkam, meaning the mufassal, during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when I was twelve, or twelve years old."],[5337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of people shooting arrows and said: Shoot, O sons of Isma'il, for your father was an archer."],[5338,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he traveled until he came to a mountain pass and said: Which pass is this? We said: It is Harsha, or Lift. He said: It is as if I am looking at Musa b. 'Imran on a red camel, wearing a woolen jubbah, with his camel's reins made of fiber, passing through this valley, saying the talbiyah."],[5339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the morning of Jam': Gather for me some pebbles like those used for khafdh. I brought them to him, and he placed them in his hand and said: With the like of these, with the like of these, beware of going to extremes, for those before you were destroyed only, I think he said, by going to extremes in religion."],[5340,"The worst food is the food of a walimah, to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out."],[5341,"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into Hell and saw that most of its inhabitants were women."],[5342,"Whoever sees from his ruler something he dislikes should be patient, for there is no one who leaves the community by a handspan and dies except that he dies a death of ignorance."],[5343,"Whoever intends a good deed, write it for him as one good deed. If he performs it, write it for him as ten. And whoever intends an evil deed, do not write it. If he leaves it, write it for him as one good deed, and if he performs it, write it as one evil deed."],[5344,"The likeness of the one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is the likeness of a donkey carrying books."],[5345,"Muhammad b. Mahan narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas."],[5346,"A delegation from Bakr b. Wa'il came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they finished their business, he said to them: 'Is there anyone among you who knows Quss b. Sa'ida al-Iyadi?' They said: 'Yes, all of us know him.' He said: 'What became of him?' They said: 'He died.' He said: 'I will never forget him at the market of Ukaz, in the sacred month, on a red camel, addressing the people, and he was saying: O people, gather, listen, and take heed. Everyone who lives dies, and everyone who dies is gone, and everything that is coming will come. Indeed, in the sky there is news, and indeed in the earth there are lessons: a spread bed, a raised roof, stars that move, seas that do not sink, and trade that does not perish. Quss swore truly: if in this matter there is contentment, there will surely be displeasure, and indeed Allah has a religion that is dearer to Him than the religion you are upon. Why do I see people going and not returning? Are they satisfied and staying, or left and sleeping?' Then he began to say: 'In the first ones who went from the generations, for us there are insights. When I saw watering places for death with no outlets, and I saw my people heading towards them, the elders and the young. The past does not return to me, and none of the remaining stay behind. I became certain that I will inevitably go where the people have gone.'"],[5347,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave."],[5348,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave."],[5349,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave and said four takbirs over it."],[5350,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave after three days."],[5351,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ over a grave, and he placed me on his right."],[5352,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ drink while standing from Zamzam."],[5353,"The Prophet ﷺ drank from Zamzam while standing."],[5354,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ one night and stood on his left, so he turned me around and made me stand on his right."],[5355,"When he was cupped, he was cupped in the two posterior neck veins. He (the narrator) said: He called a young servant of Banu Bayadah and gave the cupper his wage as one and a half mudds. He said: And he spoke to his masters, and they reduced half a mudd, and he owed two mudds."],[5356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established the prayer in travel as two rak'ahs, and it is complete, and the witr in travel is a sunnah."],[5357,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the spirit and the body."],[5358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Zamzam and asked for water. I brought him a bucket, and he drank while standing."],[5359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained of thirst. He said: Bring me water. They brought him a vessel containing water, and he placed his hand in the water, and water began to gush from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, as if it were the staff of Musa. The people drank and filled their vessels."],[5360,"Say: I do not ask of you any reward for it except affection for kinship. He said: Except that you maintain ties with my relatives."],[5361,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas similarly. This hadith has been reported from Ibn Abbas through various channels, and we do not know of a chain better than this chain, and we do not know that anyone reported this hadith from Shu'bah except Ali b. Nasr."],[5362,"This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Arafah: Today I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you and have approved for you Islam as religion."],[5363,"He passed by a pregnant woman at the door of a tent and said: Perhaps he intends to have relations with her. They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I was on the verge of cursing him with a curse that would enter with him into his grave. How can he make him an heir when he is not lawful for him? And how can he enslave him when he is not lawful for him?"],[5364,"Hassan, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Umar; that the Prophet ﷺ said: The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the day, so make the night prayer odd-numbered. This hadith regarding the Maghrib prayer being the witr of the day, we do not know that anyone reported it except Abdul Aziz, from Hisham, and the combination of the two hadiths about the night prayer being two by two is well-known from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Umar."],[5365,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi Adi narrated to us, from Yunus b. Ubayd, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5366,"The night prayer is two rak'ahs at a time, two rak'ahs at a time."],[5367,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in an army, and we met the enemy. When we returned to Madinah, we said: If only we could meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and if it would be in our favor. So we met him at the Fajr prayer and said to him: We are the ones who fled. He said: Rather, you are the ones who return to fight. They said: It was such-and-such, and they told him. He said: Do not do that, for I am the group of the Muslims. He said: And we kissed his hand."],[5368,"The Prophet ﷺ took the pre-dawn meal one night, and 'Alqamah b. 'Ulathah came. The Prophet ﷺ called for a head [of an animal] and began to eat from it. Then Bilal came to call him to the Fajr prayer, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: Easy, O Bilal, until 'Alqamah finishes his pre-dawn meal."],[5369,"A dabb lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and one of his wives found it repulsive, so he said: Eat it, it is lawful; there is no harm in it."],[5371,"Hellfire has seven gates; one of them is for whoever draws the sword against my Ummah, or he said: against the Ummah of Muhammad."],[5372,"I recited to Ibn 'Umar: 'Allah is the One who created you from weakness,' and he said: 'From weakness.' Then he said: I recited it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as 'from weakness.'"],[5373,"Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Then I met Ibn 'Umar at al-Balat and mentioned to him the hadith of Abu Sa'id from the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it."],[5374,"Whoever drags a garment of his clothing out of arrogance or pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5375,"Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven nights."],[5376,"The mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was made of palm trunks. It fell into ruin in the time of Abu Bakr, so he rebuilt it with palm trunks and stripped palm branches. Then it fell into ruin in the time of 'Umar, so he rebuilt it with palm trunks and stripped palm branches. Then it fell into ruin in the caliphate of 'Uthman, so he rebuilt it with baked bricks, and its construction has not ceased until now."],[5377,"Whoever hoards food has disowned Allah, and Allah has disowned him. He said: And any people of a neighborhood among whom a Muslim remains hungry overnight, Allah's protection has been withdrawn from them."],[5378,"Every tree has a fruit, and the fruit of the heart is the child. Allah does not have mercy on one who does not have mercy on his child. By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah has mercy only on the merciful—only on the merciful. We said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us have mercy. He said: It is not mercy that one of you has mercy on his companion; rather..."],[5379,"Five are part of faith; whoever lacks any of them has no faith: ... contentment with Allah’s decree, entrusting matters to Allah’s command, reliance upon Allah, and patience at ... A person does not attain the reality of Islam until people feel safe from him regarding their blood and property. A questioner said: O Messenger of Allah, ... which is best? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Signs like road markers: the testimony that ... alone, with no partner, establishing prayer, giving zakah, ruling by the Book of Allah, obeying the unlettered Prophet, and greeting the children of Adam when you meet them."],[5380,"He used to recite in Witr: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” “Say: O disbelievers,” and “Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.”"],[5381,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: “What do you think the earth rests upon?” He said: “The earth is upon water.” It was said: “Upon what is the water?” He said: “Upon a green rock.” It was said: “Upon what is the rock?” He said: “Upon the back of a whale whose two ends meet at the Throne.” It was said: “Upon what is the whale?” He said: “Upon the shoulders of an angel whose feet are in the air.”"],[5382,"The ruler is the shade of Allah on earth; every wronged one among His servants takes refuge in him. If he is just, he earns the reward and the subjects owe gratitude; if he oppresses, wrongs, or commits injustice, the burden is on him and the subjects must be patient. When rulers are oppressive, the sky withholds rain; when zakah is withheld, livestock perish; when adultery spreads, poverty and destitution spread; when the covenant is violated, the disbelievers are given the upper hand – or words to that effect."],[5383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Abu Bakr and Umar – may Allah have mercy on them both – about their Witr. Abu Bakr said: “I pray Witr at the beginning of the night.” He said: “Cautious.” Then he asked Umar, who said: “I pray Witr at the end of the night.” He said: “Strong and aided.”"],[5384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed coming out to his companions for the Fajr prayer until they said: “The sun has risen – or is about to rise.” Then he came out and led them in the Fajr prayer, and said: “Remain in your ranks.” Then he turned to them and said: “Do you know what kept me from you?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “I prayed in my prayer place, and sleep overcame me, and my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, came to me in the most beautiful form and said: ‘O Muhammad.’ I said: ‘At Your service, my Lord, and ready to obey.’ He said: ‘About what do the Highest Assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘I do not know, my Lord.’ He placed His hand between my shoulders until I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I knew what He asked me about. Then He said: ‘O Muhammad.’ I said: ‘At Your service, my Lord, and ready to obey.’ He said: ‘About what do the Highest Assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘About expiations and ranks.’ He said: ‘What are the expiations and ranks?’ I said: ‘The expiations are performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, walking on foot to Friday prayers, and sitting in the mosques after the prayers. As for the ranks: feeding others, speaking kindly, and prostrating at night while people sleep.’ My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: ‘Ask Me, O Muhammad.’ I said: ‘I ask You for doing good deeds, abandoning evil deeds, and love for the poor. I ask You to forgive me and have mercy on me. If You intend a trial for a people, take me to You without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and the love of deeds that bring me closer to Your love. O Allah, I ask You for faith that touches my heart so that I know nothing will befall me except what You have decreed for me, and contentment with what You have apportioned for me.’”"],[5385,"Three things break the back. Abu Bakr said: “One has passed me by.” [The remaining are:] a bad wife whom her husband trusts but she betrays him, and a leader who displeases Allah and pleases people. The example of a believing woman’s deed is like the deed of seventy truthful ones, and the deed of a wicked woman is like the wickedness of a thousand wicked women."],[5386,"He used to supplicate with these words: “O Allah – I think he said – faith that touches my heart so that I know nothing will befall me except what You have written for me, and contentment with the livelihood You have apportioned for me.”"],[5387,"Al-Kifl from the Children of Israel did not refrain from any sin he committed. A woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he have intercourse with her. When he sat from her as a man sits from his wife, she trembled and wept. He said: “What makes you weep?” She said: “Nothing, but this is a deed I have never done; only need drove me to it.” He said: “You do this and have never done it? Go, the dinars are yours.” And he said: “By Allah, I will never disobey Allah after this, ever.” He spent that night, and in the morning it was written on his door: “Allah has forgiven al-Kifl.”"],[5388,"I was with Ibn Umar when he called a slave of his who had angered him, and he set him free. Then he said: “I have no reward from him equal to this – or the amount of this. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever strikes his slave a prescribed punishment or slaps him – Abd al-Rahman was uncertain – its expiation is to set him free.’”"],[5389,"A man swore by the Kaaba, and Ibn Umar said: “Swear by the Lord of the Kaaba, for Umar used to swear by his father, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Do not swear by your father, for whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk.’”"],[5390,"Ahmad b. Amr b. Ubayda narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Sa’d b. Ubayda, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5391,"Whoever swears by other than God has committed shirk."],[5392,"Knowledge is about to be lifted up. He repeated it three times. Ziyad b. Labid said: \"O Prophet of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, how will knowledge be lifted from us while this is the Book of God, which we have read, and we teach it to our children, and our children will teach it to their children?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to him and said: \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ziyad b. Labid! I had considered you one of the jurists of the people of Madinah. Do not these Jews have the Torah and the Gospel? What did that avail them? God does not remove knowledge by lifting it up, but He removes it by taking away its bearers—I think he said—and no scholar of this nation passes away except that he leaves a breach in Islam that will not be filled until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5393,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ broke his fast, he would say: \"Thirst is gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is established, if God wills.\""],[5394,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah, he would say: \"O God, do not make our deaths therein until You bring us out of it.\""],[5395,"You will enlist armies. A man said: \"O Messenger of God, choose for me.\" He said: \"You should go to Syria, for it is God's chosen land from among His lands, and in it is God's chosen ones from among His servants. Whoever turns away from that, let him join his Najd, for God has guaranteed me Syria and its people.\""],[5396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse on the pulpit: 'They did not estimate God with His true estimation'—until he finished the verse, reaching 'Glorified be He and Exalted above what they associate.' He said: The pulpit moved like this, and it swayed back and forth three times."],[5397,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ trim his mustache closely."],[5398,"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[5399,"A slave woman is divorced twice, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles."],[5400,"Noah fasted the white days, which are the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[5401,"Forgive one another, and grudges will fall away between you."],[5402,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning slaves: 'If they do good, accept it; if they do wrong, pardon them; and if they overpower you, then sell them.'"],[5403,"There is no preemption for an absent person, nor for a minor. Preemption is like the loosening of a hobble."],[5404,"The prayer of combat is one rak'ah, in any manner. If a man performs it, it suffices him; and if - I think he said - he does that, he has not returned to it."],[5405,"Whoever maims his slave, then he is free, and he is the freedman of Allah and His Messenger."],[5406,"The gift given for temporary use is to be returned, and people are bound by their conditions as long as they agree with the truth."],[5407,"The sign of life of a newborn is sneezing."],[5408,"Cursed is the one who gives allegiance to other than his patrons; cursed is the one who claims descent from other than his father; and cursed is the one who changes the landmarks of the land."],[5409,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing praying in a single garment, so I stood on his left, and he turned me around until he placed me on his right."],[5410,"War is deceit."],[5411,"Al-Hasan b. 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Jarawi and Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, they said: Yahya b. Hassan narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Zayd b. Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar."],[5412,"When you see those who praise people to their faces, throw dust in their faces."],[5413,"Make the last of your prayers witr."],[5414,"It is not right for a Muslim man who has something to bequeath to spend two nights except that his will is written with him."],[5415,"It is not right for a man who has property and wants to make a will concerning it to pass two nights except with his will written and kept by him."],[5416,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5417,"Ahmad b. Thabit narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I think it is from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5418,"It is among the rights of a Muslim that he should not pass two nights without writing his will."],[5419,"Make some of your prayers in your houses, and do not make them graves."],[5420,"Pray in your houses, and do not make them graves."],[5421,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5422,"He forbade continuous fasting. They said: 'But you fast continuously, O Messenger of Allah!' He said: 'I am not like any one of you. I spend the night while I am fed and given drink.'"],[5423,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh b. 'Ubada narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And Musa b. 'Uqba narrated it, and 'Umar b. Shayba also narrated it, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, so we have contented ourselves with those we have named."],[5424,"I have not failed to touch these two corners, the Yamani and the Stone, since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching them in hardship and in ease."],[5425,"'Amr b. 'Ali narrated it to us, 'Asim b. Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abi Rawwad and others from Nafi', so they thus agreed with those we have named."],[5426,"When he was in a hurry while traveling, he would combine Maghrib and Isha after the twilight had disappeared, and he would say: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a hurry while traveling, he would combine Maghrib and Isha.'"],[5427,"5435 5429 - And it was narrated to us by Muhammad b. Ma'mar, who said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, who said: 'Umar b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[5428,"The crier came to Ibn 'Umar regarding Safiyyah at sunset. He said to the muezzin, 'The prayer,' then said, 'Travel on.' So he traveled until, just before the setting of the sun, when the twilight [appeared], he dismounted and prayed Maghrib. Then he waited until the twilight disappeared, then prayed 'Isha'. Then he said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a hurry, he would do the same as I have done.' So on that day and night he covered the distance of three [days' travel]."],[5429,"When he was in a hurry to travel, he would combine Maghrib and 'Isha'."],[5430,"When he was in a hurry to travel, he would delay Zuhr and hasten 'Asr, and delay Maghrib and hasten 'Isha'."],[5431,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Wahhab b. 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, saying: Yahya b. Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it—regarding hastening the prayer."],[5432,"That 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah and Salim b. 'Abd Allah spoke to 'Abd Allah when [the conflict] was between al-Hajjaj and Ibn al-Zubayr, and they said, 'It does not harm you not to perform Hajj this year, for we fear that there may be fighting among the people or that you may be prevented from reaching the House.' He said, 'If I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did when the disbelievers of Quraysh prevented him from the House: I call you to witness that I have made 'Umrah obligatory upon myself.' So he set out until he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah and made the Talbiyah for 'Umrah. Then he said, 'If I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did, and I was with him.' Then he recited, 'You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah an excellent exemplar.' Then he traveled until he was at the back of al-Bayda', and he said, 'Their matter is but one. If I am prevented from the 'Umrah, I am prevented from the Hajj. I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory upon myself along with my 'Umrah.' So he set out until he purchased a sacrificial animal at Qudayd. Then he performed a single Tawaf for both of them at the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and he did not exit the state of ihram from either of them—or from both—until the Day of Sacrifice."],[5433,"I learned the Talbiyah directly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.'"],[5434,"I received it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5435,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying the Talbiyah: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika lak.'"],[5436,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race between the trained horses from al-Hafya' to Thaniyyat al-Wada', and for those not trained from Thaniyyat al-Wada' to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."],[5437,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, saying: Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[5438,"That the Prophet ﷺ held a race between horses, sending those that had been trained from al-Hafya' to Thaniyyat al-Wada', and sending those that had not been trained from Thaniyyat al-Wada' to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."],[5439,"Those who make these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said to them: 'Bring to life what you have created.'"],[5440,"Those who make images will be the most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: 'Bring to life what you have created.'"],[5441,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. This hadith was narrated by more than one person whom we did not name, and we contented ourselves with those we mentioned."],[5442,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the night prayer. He said: 'Each of you should pray two by two, and if he fears the dawn, he should pray one rak'ah, which will make his prayer odd-numbered (witr).'"],[5443,"The night prayer is two by two, and the witr is one rak'ah."],[5444,"The night prayer is two rak'ahs, and if you fear the dawn, then perform witr with one."],[5445,"The night prayer is two by two, and if one of you fears the dawn, he should pray one single rak'ah, which will make his prayer odd-numbered."],[5446,"Amr b. Ali narrated to us, Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5447,"The night prayer is two by two, and if one of you fears the dawn, he should pray one single rak'ah, which will make his prayer odd-numbered."],[5448,"Five creatures, there is no blame on the one who kills them, even while in a state of ihram: the scorpion, the kite, the rabid dog, the crow, and the mouse."],[5449,"Sulayman b. Khallad narrated to us, Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. Meaning: regarding what the muhrim may kill."],[5450,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5451,"Five animals: the pilgrim commits no sin if he kills them: the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, and the rabid dog."],[5452,"He forbade that livestock be milked without the permission of their owners."],[5453,"And it was narrated to him by Muhammad b. al-Muthanna: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5454,"And it was narrated to him by Bishr b. Khalid: Sa'id b. Maslama narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Umayya, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5455,"None of you should milk the livestock of his brother. Would any of you like his upper room to be come to and its door broken? None of you should milk the livestock of another person except with his permission."],[5456,"None of you should milk the livestock of anyone without his permission. Would one of you be pleased that his upper room be come to and the door of his storeroom broken and its contents scattered? Indeed, their livestock's udders are their stores, so none should milk the livestock of anyone except with his permission."],[5457,"Whoever misses the afternoon prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and his property."],[5458,"It was narrated to him by Muhammad b. Uthman b. Karama: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5459,"Whoever leaves the afternoon prayer until it elapses him, it is as if he has lost his family and his property."],[5460,"The one who misses the afternoon prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and his property."],[5461,"And it was narrated to him by Amr b. Ali: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5462,"5470 5464 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us: Ubayd Allah b. al-Akhnas narrated to us, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5463,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the dabb lizard, and he said: 'I do not eat it, but I do not forbid it.'"],[5464,"5472 5466 - And Mu'ammal b. Hisham narrated it to us, Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5465,"He was asked about the dabb lizard, and he said: 'I do not eat it, but I do not forbid it.'"],[5466,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah, narrated to us, from Ya'la b. Hakim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5467,"A dabb lizard was brought to him, and he did not eat it, nor did he forbid it."],[5468,"The Prophet ﷺ made the charity of fitr obligatory upon the young and the old, the free and the slave."],[5469,"5477 5471 - And Mu'ammal b. Hisham narrated it to us, Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5470,"5478 5472 - And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5471,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5472,"Upon the young and the old, the free and the slave among the Muslims."],[5473,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated it to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5474,"And Bishr b. Khalid narrated it to us, Sa'id b. Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5475,"And Ibn Maʿmar narrated to us: Yaʿlā b. ʿUbayd narrated to us: Muḥammad b. Isḥāq narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly regarding the story of fiṭr. As for the ḥadīth of Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ which he mentioned and said: 'from the Muslims' – Ismāʿīl b. Jaʿfar followed him in his narration, from ʿUmar b. Nāfiʿ, from his father, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ. And the ḥadīth of Yaʿlā, from Muḥammad b. Isḥāq, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar – he did not mention in it: 'from the Muslims.'"],[5476,"A Muslim is required to obey in what he likes and dislikes, unless he is commanded to commit an act of disobedience. If he is commanded to commit an act of disobedience, then there is no obedience."],[5477,"And Muḥammad b. al-Muthannā narrated it to us: Khālid b. al-Ḥārith narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. Mūsā b. ʿUqbah also narrated this ḥadīth, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar similarly."],[5478,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is ḥarām."],[5479,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is ḥarām. Whoever drinks wine in this world and dies addicted to it will not drink it in the Hereafter."],[5480,"Every intoxicant is ḥarām."],[5481,"Every intoxicant is ḥarām, and every intoxicant is khamr."],[5482,"A man should not propose to a woman when his brother has already proposed to her, and he should not outbid his brother in a sale, unless he gives him permission."],[5483,"None of you should outbid another in a sale, and none of you should propose to a woman when another has already proposed to her."],[5484,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[5485,"5493 5487 - Al-Ḥusayn b. Mahdī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5486,"When one of you dies, his place is shown to him morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then he is from the people of Paradise; and if he is one of the people of the Fire, then he is from the people of the Fire. It is said: 'This is your place until you are resurrected.'"],[5487,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5488,"And al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5489,"My father narrated to me, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5490,"When one of you dies, his place is shown to him morning and evening. If he is among the people of Paradise, then among the people of Paradise; and if he is among the people of the Fire, then among the people of the Fire."],[5491,"Whoever carries weapons against us is not one of us."],[5492,"Whoever carries weapons against us is not one of us."],[5493,"The example of the one who has the Qur'an is like that of hobbled camels: if their owner ties them, he keeps them; but if he lets them loose, they wander off."],[5494,"Indeed, the example of the one who has the Qur'an is like that of hobbled camels: if he tends to them, he retains them; but if he neglects them, they wander off."],[5495,"And indeed, the one who has the Qur'an, if he recites it, he remembers it; but if he abandons it, he forgets it."],[5496,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh b. Ubadah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to the hadith of Ubayd Allah."],[5497,"He forbade al-shighar."],[5498,"He forbade al-shighar."],[5499,"He prohibited al-shighar."],[5500,"He prohibited going out to meet (caravans)."],[5501,"He prohibited going out to meet the riders, and for a town-dweller to sell on behalf of a desert-dweller, and al-najash."],[5502,"He prohibited the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[5503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating the domesticated donkey, and they had needed it on the day of Khaybar."],[5504,"He prohibited the meat of domesticated donkeys on the day of Khaybar."],[5505,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it."],[5506,"Wahb b. Yahya narrated to us, Maymun b. Zayd narrated to us, from Umar b. Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5507,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it."],[5508,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[5509,"I heard Nafi' narrate from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5510,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[5511,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees."],[5512,"Ahmad b. Sinan narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5513,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees."],[5514,"The prayer in congregation is superior to a man's prayer alone by twenty-some prayers."],[5515,"People used to sell foodstuffs in bulk without measuring, so the Prophet ﷺ forbade them from selling it until they moved it or transferred it."],[5516,"The dream of a believer is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."],[5517,"The dream of a believer is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."],[5518,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, I think something similar."],[5519,"He stood at the door of A'ishah, or Hafsah - Abu Musa was uncertain - and said: 'Indeed, the trial (fitnah) is from here, from where the horn of Satan emerges,' twice or three times."],[5520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood facing the east by the room of A'ishah and said: 'Indeed, the trial (fitnah) is from here,' saying it twice: 'from where the horn of Satan emerges.'"],[5521,"Al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5522,"When a slave is sincere to his master and perfects the worship of his Lord, he has his reward twice."],[5523,"Al-Hasan b. Yahya narrated it to us, Muhammad b. al-Fadl narrated to us, Sa'id b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[5524,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it. And the hadith of Ayyub—we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Nafi', except Sa'id b. Zayd, and Sa'id b. Zayd is acceptable."],[5525,"You will surely fight the Jews, until even the stone will say: 'O Muslim, this is a Jew, come and kill him.' And Abd al-Wahhab said: 'This is a Jew behind me.'"],[5526,"Al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[5527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah from the upper mountain pass and left from the lower one."],[5528,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand. The upper hand is the giving one, and the lower hand is the asking one."],[5529,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off (the hand) for a shield worth three dirhams."],[5530,"5532 - Amr b. Ali narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5531,"He cut off (the hand) for a shield whose value was three dirhams."],[5532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off (the hand of) a thief for a shield."],[5533,"He cursed the woman who tattoos, the woman who asks to be tattooed, the woman who extends hair, and the woman who asks for hair extensions."],[5534,"Before you is a cistern as (wide as the distance) between Jarba' and Adhruh."],[5535,"And al-'Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated it to us: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5536,"Indeed, before you is a cistern like the distance between such-and-such and such-and-such. Al-Fudayl doubted, but Hammad did not doubt. A man in the presence of Nafi' said: He doubted. So he said: It is true from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5537,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water. And 'Abd al-Wahhab said: So extinguish it with water."],[5538,"And Ibrahim b. Yusuf narrated it to us: 'Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it."],[5539,"Indeed, the two parties to a transaction have the option (khiyar) in their sale as long as they have not separated, unless the sale is based on option. Nafi' said: When Ibn 'Umar bought something that pleased him, he would separate from his companion."],[5540,"The two sellers have the option as long as they have not separated."],[5541,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it."],[5542,"And the sale is based on option."],[5543,"And al-Hasan b. 'Arafah narrated to us: he narrated to us from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it. The hadith of 'Umar b. Muhammad."],[5544,"Fudayl b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa b. 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet Muhammad."],[5545,"That the Prophet ﷺ conducted li'an between a man and his wife from the Ansar and separated them."],[5546,"Ibn 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy came to the Messenger of God ﷺ when his father died and said: Give us your shirt. So he gave him his shirt, and said: When you are done, inform me. When he wanted to pray over him, 'Umar pulled him and said: Has not God forbidden you from the hypocrites? He said: I am between two choices. He said: Seek forgiveness for them or do not seek forgiveness for them. So he prayed over him. Then God revealed: And do not pray over any of them who dies ever, and do not stand at his grave. So he abandoned praying over them."],[5547,"The one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5548,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[5549,"The one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5550,"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques."],[5551,"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from praying in the mosques."],[5552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed the name of Asiya and said: 'You are Jamila.'"],[5553,"He used to come to Quba riding and walking."],[5554,"He used to come to Quba riding and walking."],[5555,"A woman should not travel three (days) unless she has a mahram with her."],[5556,"The people of the pre-Islamic era used to sell the meat of a slaughtered camel until the offspring of the offspring. And the offspring of the offspring means that the she-camel gives birth to what is in her belly, then she becomes pregnant. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them from that."],[5557,"He forbade the sale of the offspring of the offspring."],[5558,"5566 5560 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar."],[5559,"He prohibited the sale of the offspring of an unborn camel (ḥabal al-ḥabala)."],[5560,"On the Day when people will stand before the Lord of the Worlds, he said: Until one of them stands in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."],[5561,"Bishr b. Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī narrated to us, Ḥammād b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5562,"ʿAbdullāh b. Saʿīd narrated to us, ʿĪsā b. Yūnus and Abū Usāma narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā, from ʿUbaydullāh. This ḥadīth, we do not know anyone who made it musnad from Ayyūb except Ḥammād, nor do we know anyone who made it musnad from Ibn ʿAwn except ʿĪsā b. Yūnus and Abū Usāma."],[5563,"Al-Faḍl b. Sahl narrated to us, Yaʿqūb b. Ibrāhīm narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ṣāliḥ b. Kaysān, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5564,"Ismāʿīl b. Masʿūd narrated to us, al-Fuḍayl b. Sulaymān narrated to us, from Mūsā b. ʿUqba, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to the ḥadīth of Ayyūb and Ibn ʿAwn."],[5565,"Trim the moustaches and let the beards grow."],[5566,"Two should not hold secret conversation to the exclusion of their companion."],[5567,"When they are three, two should not hold secret conversation to the exclusion of the third."],[5568,"Muḥammad b. Maʿmar narrated to us, Rawḥ narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5569,"That the Prophet ﷺ said during the battle of Khaybar: Whoever eats from this tree—meaning garlic—should not come to the mosque. Or he said: a mosque."],[5570,"A spear would be planted for him and he would pray facing it."],[5571,"When it was a rainy night, he would command a caller to announce: 'The prayer is to be performed in the dwellings,' after the call to prayer."],[5572,"Ahmad b. Aban narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5573,"One night he found [there was] severe cold, so he commanded the mu'adhdhin, and he gave the call to prayer with those who were with him, and he said: 'Pray in your dwellings, for the Messenger of God ﷺ, when it was like this, would command the people and they would pray in their dwellings.'"],[5574,"The Prophet ﷺ granted a concession to al-Abbas to spend the nights of Mina in Makkah for the sake of providing water [to the pilgrims]."],[5575,"May God have mercy on those who shave [their heads]. They said: 'And those who shorten [their hair]?' He said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave [their heads].' They said: 'And those who shorten [their hair]?' The fourth time he said: 'And those who shorten [their hair].'"],[5576,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar also narrated it to us: Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[5577,"When he returned from military expeditions, raiding parties, or the Hajj or Umrah, he would climb an elevated place and say: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things'—three times—'Returning, repentant, worshiping, praising our Lord. There is no god but God alone; He fulfilled His promise, was true to His word, and defeated the confederates alone.'"],[5578,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, what clothing may we wear when we enter ihram?' He said: 'Do not wear shirts, trousers, or leather socks, unless one of you cannot find sandals, in which case he may cut them below the ankles. And do not wear any garment touched by wars or saffron.'"],[5579,"5587 5579 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Uthman b. Umar narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5580,"(M) - Mu'ammal b. Hisham also narrated it to us: Ismail b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5581,"A man called out to the Prophet ﷺ: 'What clothing should the muhrim wear?' He said: 'Do not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, unless there are no sandals, in which case [wear] leather socks cut below the ankles. And do not wear any garment dyed with wars or saffron.'"],[5582,"Bishr b. Khalaf narrated to us: Sa'id b. Maslama narrated to us: Ismail b. Umayya narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Ayyub."],[5583,"Amr b. Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah: Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Ayyub."],[5584,"The month is thus, thus, and thus, and he clasped his ten fingers twice and tucked in his thumb the third time. And do not fast until you see it, and do not break your fast until you see it. If it is obscured from you, then estimate for it."],[5585,"The month is only twenty-nine, so do not fast until you see it, and do not break your fast until you see it."],[5586,"The Prophet ﷺ spent the night at Dhu Tuwa, and when morning came, he entered Makkah."],[5587,"He forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy, for fear that they would seize it."],[5588,"5596 5587 - And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5589,"And al-Husayn b. Abbad narrated to us: Muslim narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5590,"He forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy."],[5591,"He forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy; and I think he said: for fear that the enemy would seize it."],[5592,"Indeed Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer."],[5593,"Men and women used to perform ablution from a single vessel in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5594,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."],[5595,"I saw men and women during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ performing ablution from a single vessel."],[5596,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Usama b. Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, similarly."],[5597,"Whoever frees a share in a slave, that share is freed; if he has wealth reaching the slave's price, the slave becomes completely free from his wealth."],[5598,"Whoever frees a share or portion he owns in a slave, and he has wealth reaching the slave's price by fair valuation, the slave becomes completely free from his wealth; otherwise, only what he freed is freed."],[5599,"Whoever frees a share he owns in a slave, and he has wealth reaching the slave's price, the slave is valued at a fair price, then he pays his partners their shares—the slave becomes completely free from him; otherwise, only what he freed is freed."],[5600,"Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter unless he repents."],[5601,"Hafsa said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with the people? They have exited ihram, but you have not exited ihram from your Umrah? He said: I matted my hair, so I will not exit ihram until I sacrifice."],[5602,"Nasr b. Ali narrated to us, Kathir b. Hisham narrated to us, Ja'far b. Burqan narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that Hafsa said to the Prophet ﷺ, then he mentioned something similar."],[5603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ assigned two shares to the horse and one share to the foot soldier."],[5604,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed the spoils on the day of Hunayn: two shares for the horse and one share for its rider."],[5605,"Whoever declares his brother a disbeliever, one of them incurs it."],[5606,"Abdullah b. Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, my father and Raqaba narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5607,"Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[5608,"The Prophet ﷺ would not fast on the Day of Arafah, nor would Abu Bakr, nor Umar."],[5609,"Al-Hasan b. Yahya narrated to us; Muammal b. Ismail narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; from Ismail b. Umayyah; from Nafi'; from Ibn Umar; from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And this hadith, we do not know it being narrated from Ibn Umar except through these two ways that we have mentioned."],[5610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two afternoon prayers and he forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn said to him, \"Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?\" He said, \"None of that happened,\" until he was sure. Then he prayed what remained of his prayer and prostrated twice."],[5611,"He used to deliver two sermons, separating between them with a sitting."],[5612,"Do not pray at sunrise or at sunset."],[5613,"The intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."],[5614,"Ghifar: may Allah forgive it. Aslam: may Allah grant it peace."],[5615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the pulpit: Ghifar, may Allah forgive it; Aslam, may Allah grant it peace; and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[5616,"The likeness of the hypocrite is the likeness of a sheep wandering between two flocks; it inclines to these once and to those once, not knowing which of them to follow."],[5617,"The likeness of the hypocrite is the likeness of a sheep wandering between two flocks; it goes to this one once and to the other another time, not knowing which of them to follow."],[5618,"Al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us; Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us; my father narrated to me; from Salih b. Kaysan; from Nafi'; from Ibn Umar; from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5619,"I was presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Uhud, when I was fourteen years old, and he deemed me too young, so he sent me back with the boys. When it was the day of the Trench, I was presented to him and I was fifteen, so he allowed me."],[5620,"I was presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ when I was thirteen, and he did not accept me; and I was presented to him when I was fourteen, and he did not accept me; and I was presented to him when I was fifteen, and he allowed me."],[5621,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the false messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal) and said: 'Indeed your Lord is not one-eyed, and indeed the false messiah is one-eyed, his right eye as if it were a protruding grape.'"],[5622,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[5623,"Whoever attends Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[5624,"When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[5625,"And Ahmad b. Thabit narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5626,"And Bishr b. Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us, Sa'id b. Maslama narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Umayya, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5627,"5635 5626 - And Isma'il b. Mas'ud narrated to us, Fudayl b. Sulayman narrated to us, Musa b. 'Uqba narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5628,"And Muhammad b. 'Uthman b. Karama narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Sakhr b. Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5629,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar and Muhammad b. Karama narrated it to us, they said: 'Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5630,"5638 5629 - And Ahmad b. Mansur narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5631,"And Ahmad b. Mansur narrated to us, Ahmad b. Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Shihab, from Yunus, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[5632,"He said it on the pulpit"],[5633,"5641 5632 - And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Ya'la b. 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Uthman b. Hakim narrated to us"],[5634,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit .."],[5635,"5643 5634 - And al-Hasan b. Yahya narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah b. Muhammad b. Asma' narrated to us, Juwayriyah b. Asma' narrated to us:"],[5636,"5644 5635 - And Wahb b. Yahya al-Qaysi narrated to us, Maymun b. Zayd narrated to us, 'Umar b. Muhammad narrated to us:"],[5637,"5645 5636 - And Ahmad b. al-Faraj narrated to us, Abu Haywah Shurayh b. Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ayb b. Abi Hamzah narrated to us:"],[5638,"And Ma'mar b. Sahl narrated to us, Malik b. Isma'il narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir:"],[5639,"And Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym:"],[5640,"Indeed Allah - Blessed and Exalted is He - has a right upon every Muslim that he should wash one day in every seven days, and if he has perfume, he should touch it"],[5641,"Muhammad b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sulayman b. Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar"],[5642,"5650 5641 - And Muhammad b. Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Bishr b. Mubashshir narrated to us, al-Hakam b. Fudayl narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Nafi'"],[5643,"And narrated to us Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Shabbawayh al-Marwazi: narrated to us Yahya b. Salih: narrated to us Mu'awiya b. Sallam, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Nafi'."],[5644,"Whoever of you comes to Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5645,"I asked Nafi' about performing ghusl on Friday, and he said: Ibn Umar said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: Whoever comes to Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5646,"Whoever attends Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5647,"Whoever attends Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5648,"Narrated to us al-Hasan b. Hammad b. 'Anbasa al-Warraq: narrated to us Muhammad b. Sabiq: narrated to us Ibrahim b. Tahman, from Mansur, meaning Ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Nafi'."],[5649,"Whoever attends Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5650,"When one of you comes to Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5651,"Narrated to us al-Hasan b. Khalaf al-Wasiti: narrated to us Ishaq b. Yusuf al-Azraq: narrated to us al-Muthanna, meaning Ibn al-Sabbah, from Ayyub b. Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5652,"Ibn Umar was asked about performing ghusl on Friday, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded it."],[5653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched us in a military expedition, and our shares reached twelve camels, and we were given an extra camel each as nafl."],[5654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition toward Najd, and their shares reached twelve camels, and besides that they were given an extra camel each as nafl."],[5655,"Muhammad b. Yazid b. al-Rawwas narrated to us; Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us; Burd Abu al-'Ala' narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[5656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a raiding party, among whom was Abdullah b. Umar, toward Najd. They acquired spoils; their shares were twelve camels each. They took twelve camels each and were given an additional camel each as a bonus."],[5657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a raiding party, and they acquired many camels. We were given an additional camel each as a bonus. When we arrived, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us our shares, and each man among us received twelve camels in addition to the bonus camel we had been given. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not criticize what we had done, nor the one who gave us (the bonus)."],[5658,"We went on a military expedition and acquired spoils, which we divided. Each man among us received twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us an additional camel each as a bonus, so each man among us received thirteen camels."],[5659,"Ahmad b. al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us; Baqiyya b. al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[5660,"The Day of Ashura was a day the people of the Jahiliyya used to fast. When the fast of Ramadan was obligated, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, and he said: 'It is a day from the days of Allah, so whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it.'"],[5661,"They had been commanded to fast Ashura before Ramadan was obligated. When Ramadan was obligated, whoever wished fasted it and whoever wished left it."],[5662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted Ashura and commanded its fasting. When Ramadan was obligated, it was left."],[5663,"Ashura was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'It is a day that the people of the Jahiliyya used to fast. Whoever of you wishes, let him fast it, and whoever dislikes, let him leave it.'"],[5664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have a surah containing a prostration recited to him, and he would prostrate, and we would prostrate until none of us could find a place for his forehead."],[5665,"I divorced my wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umar went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Abdullah has divorced his wife while she is menstruating.' He said: 'Command him to take her back until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure. Then if he wishes, he may divorce her before having intercourse with her, and if he wishes, he may keep her. That is the waiting period which Allah has commanded.'"],[5666,"I divorced my wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umar b. al-Khattab asked about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Command him to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure. Then if he wishes, he may keep her afterwards, and if he wishes, he may divorce her before touching her. That is the manner in which Allah has commanded women to be divorced.'"],[5667,"I divorced a woman while she was menstruating. I asked the Prophet ﷺ and he ordered me to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure, then I may part from her if it seems right to me."],[5668,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and he ordered him to take her back, then give her respite until she menstruates once, then give her respite until she becomes pure, then divorce her before having intercourse with her if he did not want to keep her. That is the waiting period according to which God has commanded women to be divorced. Ibn ʿUmar, when asked about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating, would say: Do you know ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating."],[5669,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade gourds and vessels coated with pitch."],[5671,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had finished his sermon, and they said: He forbade gourds, green jars, and vessels coated with pitch."],[5672,"5680 5672 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Ansari reported to us, from Nafi', from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5673,"5681 5673 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. Idris narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allah reported to me, from Nafi', from Ibn ʿUmar."],[5674,"In the time of the Prophet ﷺ we used to sleep in the mosque and take midday naps in it."],[5675,"He would go out by the way of al-Shajara and return by the way of al-Mu'arras."],[5676,"All of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible for your flock. The commander over the people is a shepherd and is responsible for his flock. The man is a shepherd over his household and is responsible for them. The woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and is responsible. The slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is responsible for it. So all of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible."],[5677,"And ʿAbd al-Malik b. Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jaʿfar b. Sulayman narrated to us, Asmaʾ b. ʿUbayd narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5678,"And Muhammad b. Yahya al-Qutaʿi narrated it to us, Bishr b. ʿUmar narrated to us, al-Layth b. Saʿd narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ similar to the hadith of ʿUbayd Allah."],[5679,"Each of you is a shepherd."],[5680,"Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock."],[5681,"And the woman is a shepherd over the household of her husband and his child, and she is responsible for them."],[5682,"When one of you is invited to a wedding feast, let him accept."],[5683,"A wedding feast or a marriage banquet."],[5684,"Accept the invitation when you are invited. Ibn Umar would accept, even while fasting, at a marriage banquet."],[5685,"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."],[5686,"5694 5687 - Muhammad b. Maʿmar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[5687,"Muhammad b. Yahya al-Qatiʿi narrated to us, Bishr b. Umar narrated to us, al-Layth b. Saʿd narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to the hadith of ʿUbayd Allah."],[5688,"A Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had committed adultery were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered them to be stoned. He said: I saw the man shielding her with his own body."],[5689,"ʿAmr b. ʿAli narrated to us, ʿĀsim b. Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[5690,"Muhammad b. Maʿmar narrated to us, Rawḥ b. ʿUbadah narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to the hadith of ʿUbayd Allah."],[5691,"He stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."],[5692,"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads. They said: And those who shorten? He said it three times, and when it was the fourth time, he said: And those who shorten."],[5693,"5701 5694 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5694,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before Zuhr two rak'ahs, and after it two rak'ahs, and after Jumu'ah two rak'ahs. As for Maghrib, Isha, and Jumu'ah, the Prophet prayed in his house. As for Fajr, it was a time when no one would enter upon him, and Hafsah told me that he used to pray two light rak'ahs when dawn broke."],[5695,"He used to pray before Zuhr two rak'ahs, after it two rak'ahs, before Asr two rak'ahs, after Maghrib two rak'ahs, and after Jumu'ah two rak'ahs."],[5696,"Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated it to us, Yahya b. Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah b. Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ. And from Hafsah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5697,"When Allah gathers the first and the last, a banner will be raised for every treacherous person, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."],[5698,"Amr b. Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5699,"He saw him when his she-camel settled, he entered ihram from the mosque of Dhul-Hulayfah."],[5700,"He forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears, forbidding both the seller and the buyer."],[5701,"Until they become colorful, and the crop until it whitens and is safe from blight, forbidding both the seller and the buyer."],[5702,"Until they become colorful and the crop until it whitens."],[5703,"Do not sell fruits until their ripeness is evident."],[5704,"He saw some sputum in the direction of the qiblah, so he scraped it off. Then he turned to the people and said: 'When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of his face, for Allah is in front of the face of one of you when he is in prayer.'"],[5705,"He saw some sputum in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it with his hand. Then he turned to the people, became angry with them, and said: 'Allah is in front of the face of one of you in his prayer, so let none of you spit in front of his face in his prayer.'"],[5706,"He saw some sputum in the qiblah of the mosque while he was praying, so he said after he had finished his prayer."],[5707,"On the day of Eid, he would order that a spear be brought, then he would go out and pray facing it, with the people behind him. He used to do that also when traveling."],[5708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray the Eid prayer before the sermon, then they would deliver the sermon."],[5709,"When the evening meal is placed and the prayer is established, begin with the evening meal."],[5710,"Let him not hasten until he finishes it."],[5711,"Abu Kamil narrated to us: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abdullah b. Numayr."],[5712,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day: 'Tell me of a tree that resembles the Muslim, whose leaves do not fall, and it gives its fruit at all times by the permission of its Lord.' It occurred to me that it was the date palm. He said: The people remained silent. Then the Prophet said: 'It is the date palm.' I said to my father: 'It had occurred to me that it was the date palm.' He said: 'What prevented you from saying it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? If you had said it, it would have been dearer to me than such and such.' I said: 'You and Abu Bakr were among the people, and neither of you said anything, so I disliked to speak.'"],[5713,"No one endures the hardship and severity of Madinah but that I will be a witness or intercessor for him."],[5714,"Whoever patiently endures its hardship and severity, I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5715,"Abu al-Sa'ib Salm b. Junadah narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5716,"Storytelling was not practiced during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor during the time of Abu Bakr, nor Umar ؓ."],[5717,"We used to drink during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were walking, and eat while we were running."],[5718,"He used to pray facing a camel, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray facing his camel."],[5719,"When one of you passes by a walled garden, let him eat from it, but not take any away."],[5720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of wala' and its gift."],[5721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of wala' and its gift."],[5722,"I traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. They used to pray Zuhr and Asr as two rak'ahs each, and they did not pray before or after them."],[5723,"Faith will retreat to Madinah as a snake retreats to its hole."],[5724,"He said to Abu Bakr: 'When do you pray witr?' He replied: 'I pray witr then sleep.' He said: 'You have acted with prudence.' And he said to Umar: 'When do you pray witr?' He replied: 'I sleep then get up during the night and pray witr.' He said: 'You have acted with strength.'"],[5725,"The Prophet ﷺ burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir."],[5726,"The Prophet ﷺ cut down and burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir."],[5727,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw rain, he would say: “A copious, wholesome rain.”"],[5728,"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar are the chiefs of the mature men of Paradise, from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers. Do not inform them, O ʿAlī."],[5729,"Muhammad b. Hishām narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Mālik narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿUmar narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the ḥadīth of Yūnus b. Abī Isḥāq, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī. We do not know anyone who narrated this ḥadīth from ʿUbayd Allāh except ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Mālik b. Mighwal, and we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn ʿUmar except through this route. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is weak in ḥadīth."],[5730,"Whoever enters iḥrām for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah together, one ṭawāf suffices him."],[5731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān alighted at al-Abṭaḥ."],[5732,"They were with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Ḥijr, and they kneaded dough with water from the well of Thamūd and drew water from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to pour out the water and to feed the dough to the camels, and he said: “Draw water from the well of Ṣāliḥ.”"],[5733,"There was nothing but about twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5734,"Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand, so let each of you eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand."],[5735,"The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd b. Muʿādh."],[5736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased his sacrificial animal from Qudayd."],[5737,"The Prophet ﷺ purchased his sacrificial animal from Qudayd."],[5738,"We used to say: “The best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān.”"],[5739,"The adhan at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was twice (each phrase), and the iqamah was once, once."],[5740,"When he entered prayer he said the takbir and raised his hands, and when he bowed he raised his hands, and when he said: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he raised his hands. And he attributed that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5741,"A woman was admitted to the Fire because of a cat which she tied up, and she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth."],[5742,"A’ishah and Hafsah woke up fasting, and food was gifted to them, so they broke their fast. The Prophet ﷺ entered and one of them asked him—I think it was Hafsah—and he said: “Make up a day in its place.”"],[5743,"There was a woman who used to borrow jewelry and then keep it. Her case was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O so-and-so, stand and take her hand and cut it off.”"],[5744,"On the day Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh died, seventy thousand angels descended to the earth who had not descended before that, and the grave squeezed him with a squeeze."],[5745,"For the death of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, seventy thousand angels descended who had never before set foot on the earth. And when he was buried, he said: “Glory be to Allah! If anyone could have escaped the pressure of the grave, Sa‘d would have escaped it.”"],[5746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to camel herders that they may stone (the Jamrah) at night."],[5747,"An army obtained spoils of food and honey during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not take the fifth."],[5748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition and said: “O people, do not come to women at night, and do not approach them unannounced.”"],[5749,"Hospitality is three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity."],[5750,"I am only a servant; I eat as a servant eats."],[5751,"Whoever reviles my companions, upon him is the curse of Allah."],[5752,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Usama b. Zayd over an army in which were Abu Bakr and Umar, and the people criticized his appointment. The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"It has reached me that you criticized the appointment of Usama and the appointment of his father before him. Indeed his father was worthy of command, and indeed he (meaning Usama) is worthy of command, and he is among the most beloved of people to me, and I enjoin you to treat him well.\" I think he said: \"with good.\""],[5753,"When he sat in prayer, he placed his hands on his knees, raised his right finger which is next to the thumb and supplicated with it, and placed his left hand on his left knee, spread upon it."],[5754,"The best of your names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."],[5755,"He forbade silk and silk brocade."],[5756,"If there is healing in any of your medicines, then it is in the incision of a cupper—I think he said—or a lick of honey."],[5757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed Zuhr at Mina."],[5758,"Salm b. Junada b. Salm narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5759,"Amr b. Ali and Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated it to him—the wording is Muhammad's—they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa b. Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ ."],[5760,"Al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5761,"While three men were walking, rain caught them, so they took shelter in a cave in a mountain and entered it. A rock rolled down onto the mouth of their cave and sealed them in. They said to one another: \"Consider the righteous deeds you have done, and call upon Allah by them, perhaps He will open it or relieve us through them.\" One of them said: \"O Allah, I had two elderly parents, a wife, and small children. I used to tend flocks for them, and when I returned to them I would milk and begin with my parents, giving them drink before [the children]. One day I was delayed and did not come until evening; I found them asleep. I milked as I used to milk, brought the milk vessel, and stood by their heads, disliking to wake them and disliking to begin with the children before them, while the children were crying at my feet. That remained my practice and theirs until dawn broke. If You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then open for us an opening from which we may see the sky.\" So Allah opened an opening from it and they saw the sky. The second said: \"O Allah, if You know that I had a cousin whom I loved as intensely as a man can love women. I sought herself from her, but she refused until I brought her a hundred dinars. I worked until I brought a hundred dinars and came to her with them. When I was between her legs, she said: 'O servant of Allah, fear Allah, and do not break the seal except by its right.' So I got up from her. If You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then open for us an opening.\" So He opened for them an opening. The third said: \"O Allah, if You know that I hired a laborer for a measure of maize. When he finished his work, he said: 'Give me my right.' I offered him his measure, but he left it and disdained it. I continued to cultivate it until I gathered from it cows and their herder. Then he came to me and said: 'Fear Allah and do not wrong me; give me my right.' I said: 'Go to those cows and their herder.' He said: 'Fear Allah and do not mock me.' I said: 'I am not mocking you; take those cows and their herder.' So he took them and went away. If You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then open.\" So He opened it from them and they came out. I think he said: \"walking away.\" And the hadith of Ubayd Allah b. Umar we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ali b. Mushir and Junada b. Salm. Thus in the edition of Maktabat al-Ulum wal-Hikam, and the correct is: from us."],[5762,"Ali b. al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, my father and Raqaba narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Ubayd Allah from Nafi' from Ibn Umar. And the hadith of Raqaba and Fudayl we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Fudayl from them."],[5763,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[5764,"Mu'ammal b. Hisham also narrated it to us: Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[5765,"Any palm trees whose trunks are sold, their fruit belongs to the one who pollinated them, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[5766,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar also narrated it to us: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from 'Umar b. Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5767,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in Mina two rak'ahs, and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with 'Umar two rak'ahs, and with 'Uthman at the beginning of his reign two rak'ahs, then he later completed it."],[5768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted a ring of gold or silver, and he placed its stone facing his palm. The people adopted rings, so the Prophet ﷺ threw it away and said: 'I will never wear it.'"],[5769,"He had a gold ring, and he used to place its stone facing the inside of his palm. One day he threw it away, so the people threw away their rings. After that, he adopted a silver ring, which he used for sealing but did not wear."],[5770,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah also narrated it to us: 'Abd al-Warith informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a gold ring for three days. When his Companions saw it, gold rings became widespread among them, so he threw it away, and no one knows what happened to it. He then adopted a silver ring and ordered that it be engraved with: 'Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' It remained on the hand of the Prophet ﷺ until he died, on the hand of Abu Bakr until he died, on the hand of 'Umar until he died, and on the hand of 'Uthman for several years of his rule. When documents became numerous for him, he gave it to a man from the Ansar, who used it for sealing. The Ansari went out to the well of 'Uthman, and it fell from him and was not found. So he ordered a ring like it and engraved on it: 'Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[5772,"The Prophet ﷺ engraved on his ring: 'Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' and he said: 'No one should engrave on my ring.'"],[5773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted a gold ring, wore it on his right hand with its stone facing inward, and the people wore gold rings. He said: He ascended the pulpit, threw it away, and forbade wearing gold rings."],[5774,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day."],[5775,"5783 5777 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5776,"A man should not make another man get up from his seat and then sit in it; rather, make room and spread out."],[5777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man makes another man get up from his seat and then sits in it. I said: On Friday? He said: On Friday and other days."],[5778,"None of you should make a man get up from his seat and then sit in it."],[5779,"5787 5781 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5780,"Ibn Umar used to walk quickly (ramal) for three [circuits] and walk for four, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[5781,"Amr b. Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did ramal for three circuits and walked for four, for Hajj and 'Umrah."],[5783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, he and Uthman b. Talhah, Usamah b. Zayd, and Bilal. He stayed and prolonged his stay, then came out. I was the first of the people to enter after him, and Bilal was near the House. I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray? He said: Between the two front pillars."],[5784,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5785,"Bishr b. Khalid narrated it to us, Sa'id b. Maslamah informed us, from Isma'il b. Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to the hadith of Ubayd Allah."],[5786,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram when his riding camel stood up with him."],[5787,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih b. Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report."],[5788,"Ubayd b. Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."],[5789,"That 'Umar vowed to observe i'tikaf for a night during the Jahiliyyah. When he embraced Islam, he asked the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'Fulfill it.'"],[5790,"Saying subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."],[5791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us holding something in his hand. He opened his right hand and said: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. In it are the people of Paradise with their numbers, names, and lineages, summed up for them until the Day of Resurrection. None of them will be decreased, and none will be added to them. A blessed person may be made to follow the path of wretchedness until it is said: He is one of them and how closely he resembles them. Then he is moved to his blessedness before his death, even if by the interval between two milkings of a she-camel.' Then he opened his left hand and said: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. In it are the people of the Fire with their numbers, names, and lineages, summed up for them until the Day of Resurrection. None of them will be decreased, and none will be added to them. The wretched may be made to follow the path of the people of blessedness until it is said: He is one of them and how closely he resembles them. Then one of them is overtaken by his wretchedness before his death, even if by the interval between two milkings of a she-camel.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Actions are judged by their endings; actions are judged by their endings,' three times."],[5792,"Whoever swears an oath and says, 'If Allah wills,' has the choice: if he wishes, he may proceed with his oath, and if he wishes to go back, there is no blame on him."],[5793,"Whoever swears an oath and says, 'If Allah wills,' has not broken his oath."],[5794,"Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter."],[5795,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'What clothing should a muhrim wear?' He said: 'He should not wear a shirt, trousers, or leather socks, unless he cannot find sandals; nor a garment touched by saffron or wars.'"],[5796,"The Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ with two Jewish men who had committed adultery. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What do you find in your Book?' They said: 'They are flogged.' He said: 'You have lied; in it is stoning. Bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful.' Ibn Sallam said: 'We find in it stoning.' They brought the Torah. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring me a man from among you.' They brought him a young one-eyed man called Ibn Suriya. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Are you the most learned of them?' He said: 'They say that.' He said: 'Then recite.' He recited until he came to the place of stoning, and he placed his hand over it, meaning the verse of stoning. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Raise your hand.' The Jew said: 'O Muhammad, in it is stoning.' He said: 'So he ordered the two to be stoned.' Ibn 'Umar said: 'It is as if I can see him shielding her from the stones with his own body.'"],[5797,"And Yahya b. Habib b. 'Arabi narrated it to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report. This hadith was narrated by 'Ubayd Allah in an abbreviated form, and Ayyub added to it, so we repeated it because of the addition. We do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'ba, from Ayyub, except Yazid b. Zuray'."],[5798,"And 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated it to us, 'Asim b. Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report, or close to it."],[5799,"When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding their companion. He also forbade a man to make another man get up from his seat and then sit in it."],[5800,"Mu'ammal b. Hisham narrated it to us: Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5801,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they do not separate."],[5802,"Mu'ammal narrated to us: Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5803,"Do not prevent your women from the mosques."],[5804,"When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[5805,"Any man who sells palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[5806,"He forbade traveling with the Qur'an to enemy territory."],[5807,"Do not ... the mosques, and let them go out ..."],[5808,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from hajj or 'umrah and ascended a high ground—or he said: an elevation—he would say: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise and He has power over all things, returning repentant, to our Lord praising, Allah has fulfilled His promise and aided His servant and defeated the confederates alone."],[5809,"I saw as if in my hand a piece of silk brocade; I did not direct it to any place except that it flew with me there. Hafsah related it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Your brother is a righteous man. Or: Abdullah is a righteous man."],[5810,"People used to see dreams and relate them to the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I see that your dreams have concurred on the last seven nights, so whoever among you is seeking it, let him seek it in the last seven nights."],[5811,"He forbade muzabanah."],[5812,"He forbade that the fruit of the palm tree be sold until it ripens, and the ear of corn and the crop until it whitens and is safe from blight. He forbade the seller and the buyer."],[5813,"Muʾammal b. Hisham narrated to us: Ismaʿil b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This is authentic; Ibn ʿUlayyah also ascribed it, and it is the hadith of Ayyub."],[5814,"Indeed, the likeness of you and the Jews and the Christians is that of a man who employed laborers and said, \"Who will work for me from early morning until midday for a qirat?\" So the Jews worked. Then he said, \"Who will work for me from midday until the ʿAsr prayer for a qirat?\" So the Christians worked from midday until the ʿAsr prayer. Then he said, \"Who will work for me from the ʿAsr prayer until sunset for two qirats?\" So you worked. Then the Jews and the Christians became angry and said, \"We do more work but receive less pay?\" He said, \"Have I wronged you in anything?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then that is My bounty; I give it to whom I will.\""],[5815,"Indeed, the likeness of your lifespans in relation to the lifespans of those who came before is as the time between the ʿAsr prayer and sunset. And indeed, the likeness of you and the Jews and the Christians is that of a man who employed laborers."],[5816,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, from where do you command us to enter ihram?\" He said, \"The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn.\" He said, \"And they say: and the people of Yemen from Yalamlam.\""],[5817,"That he was summoned urgently for Safiyyah, so he traveled in one night the distance of three nights. He traveled until evening came. I said to him, \"The prayer.\" But he did not turn and traveled until it became dark. Then a man said, \"The prayer, the evening has come.\" He said, \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was in a hurry while traveling, would combine these two prayers. I intend to combine them.\" So he traveled until the twilight disappeared, then he dismounted and combined them."],[5818,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rakʿahs before Zuhr, two rakʿahs after it, two rakʿahs after Maghrib in his house, and two rakʿahs after ʿIsha. And Hafsah told me that he used to pray after dawn broke and the caller called to prayer two brief rakʿahs, and that was a time when no one would enter upon him."],[5819,"Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Shabbawayh narrated to us: Yahya b. Salih narrated to us: Muʿawiyah b. Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5820,"When you place your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."],[5821,"And Sawwar narrated it to us: Saʿid b. ʿAmir narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And the hadith of Ayyub, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Saʿid b. Abi ʿArubah except Saʿid b. ʿAmir."],[5822,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a woman over her husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten days."],[5823,"That Umar said: O Messenger of God, I vowed in the pre-Islamic era to observe i'tikaf for a day in the Sacred Mosque. He said: Go and fulfill your vow. And he had with him a boy from the captives of Hawazin, and he heard the people saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ freed the captives of Hawazin, so he said: Go, for you are free."],[5824,"And Ahmad b. 'Abda narrated to us, Hammad b. Zayd informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, in a similar manner, or close to it."],[5825,"That the Prophet ﷺ shaved his head during his Hajj."],[5826,"And Ali b. al-Husayn b. Ibrahim b. Ishkab narrated to us, Shuja' b. al-Walid narrated to us, Musa b. 'Uqba narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner."],[5827,"He used to pray on the khumra. I think he said: And he would pray and prostrate on it."],[5828,"That he said regarding the two handfuls: These are for this one, and these are for this one. He said: Then the people dispersed and they did not differ regarding the decree."],[5829,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his caller on a rainy, windy, and cold night during a journey: Pray in your dwellings."],[5830,"And Muhammad b. Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Sadaqa Bakr b. Sadaqa al-Juddi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner."],[5831,"A man from the people of Paradise will enter upon you. Then Sa'd entered. He said that for three days, each time Sa'd entered."],[5832,"Ibn Umar heard a man say: O son of the disciple of the Messenger of God. He said: If you are from the family of al-Zubayr, then yes; otherwise, no."],[5833,"Whoever sees an afflicted person and says: Praise be to God who has spared me from what He has afflicted you with and has favored me over many of His creation with a great favor - that calamity will never befall him."],[5834,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the jallala and riding it."],[5835,"We used to refrain from asking forgiveness for those who commit major sins until we heard our Prophet ﷺ say: “Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whomever He wills.” And he said: “I have delayed my intercession for the people of major sins among my community on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5836,"Indeed, Allah is Witr (single/odd) and loves witr."],[5837,"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for I will intercede for whoever dies in it."],[5838,"He used to perform witr on his mount."],[5839,"He forbade the burnus (a hooded cloak)."],[5840,"He was supplicating against four people, then the verse was revealed: “It is not for you [O Prophet] to decide anything; either He turns to them in mercy or punishes them, for indeed they are wrongdoers.”"],[5841,"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him."],[5842,"We would think badly of a man if we did not see him at the night and dawn prayers."],[5843,"We would think badly of a man if we did not see him at the morning prayer."],[5844,"He would drink in three breaths."],[5845,"When there are three people, two should not converse privately excluding the third. And when there are three on a journey, one of them should lead them in prayer."],[5846,"Do not come to your wives at night (unexpectedly)."],[5847,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day, leaning on Abu Bakr and Umar, and said: 'Thus shall we be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[5848,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah al-Rahman to his Companions, and they remained silent. He said: 'The jinn were better in response than you. Whenever I recited to them: \"So which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?\" they said: \"We deny none of Your favors, our Lord; to You be praise.\"'"],[5849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from leaning on his hands in prayer."],[5850,"Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats."],[5851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Sa'd b. 'Ubadah as a collector of zakat. He said: 'O Sa'd, beware lest you come on the Day of Resurrection with a camel carrying you that bellows.' Sa'd said: 'I will not take it; excuse me,' so he excused him."],[5852,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in the shade of the Ka'bah, sitting with his arms around his knees."],[5853,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[5854,"Whoever eats of this foul tree, or the foul herb, let him not approach our place of prayer."],[5855,"Al-Hasan b. Yazid b. Abi Yazid Abu 'Ali al-Baghdadi narrated to us: 'Ismah b. Muhammad al-Ansari, from the descendants of Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."],[5856,"Indeed, Allah placed truth upon the heart and tongue of 'Umar."],[5857,"O Allah, strengthen Islam with the more beloved of these two men to You: 'Umar b. al-Khattab or Abu Jahl b. Hisham."],[5858,"That 'Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have acquired land in Khaybar (and Ibn 'Awn said in his narration: I have acquired property in Khaybar); I have never acquired property more precious to me than it.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If you wish, you may give its fruit as charity and retain its origin.' So he gave it as charity: it is not to be sold, gifted, or inherited. He assigned it for the poor, the wayfarer, the freeing of slaves, relatives, and guests. There is no blame on the one who administers it to eat from it in a reasonable manner, without seeking wealth from it."],[5859,"A slave girl belonging to the family of Ka'b used to tend sheep. She feared that one of them would die, so she took a stone and slaughtered it with it. She mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that it be eaten."],[5860,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Marhum b. 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Dawud—meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman—narrated to us, from Musa b. 'Uqbah. And Ayyub b. Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mushir narrated to us: Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Yahya b. Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar except Yazid b. Harun and Ibn Numayr. People only narrate it from Yahya, from Nafi', as mursal. And we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Musa b. 'Uqbah except Dawud b. 'Abd al-Rahman, and he is weak. The hadith is only narrated by 'Ubayd Allah and al-Hajjaj, from Nafi', from Ibn Ka'b b. Malik, from his father. That is the correct version."],[5861,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman—then we would not compare anyone among his companions."],[5862,"He said to people who go to the ruler: 'What evil have you seen from him that you changed, or what good have you enjoined upon him?' They said: 'No, but when he says something we say: He spoke the truth, and when we leave his presence we say: We do not know.' He said: 'We used to consider this hypocrisy, or a form of hypocrisy.'"],[5863,"The Prophet ﷺ separated the two who had taken oaths of mutual cursing (li'an) and attached the child to his mother."],[5864,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus."],[5865,"He prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[5866,"Muhammad b. 'Ammar al-Razi narrated to us: Makki narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, and 'Abd Allah b. Ziyad b. Sam'an, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar. Abu Bakr said: 'I think that Makki carried the hadith of 'Abd Allah b. Sam'an, from Nafi', upon the hadith of Malik, so it became confused for him.'"],[5867,"He was asked about the prayer of fear, and he said: 'The imam goes forward with a group of people and leads them in one rak'ah, while another group stands between him and the enemy and has not yet prayed. When those with him have prayed one rak'ah, the others come and he leads them in one rak'ah, then he says the salam. Then each of the two groups stands and prays one rak'ah.' I think he traced this back to the Prophet ﷺ."],[5868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with one of the two groups one rak'ah and two prostrations, while the other group faced the enemy. The group that had been with the Prophet ﷺ departed, and the other group came, so he prayed with them one rak'ah and two prostrations, then said the salam. Then each of the two groups stood and prayed for themselves one rak'ah and two prostrations."],[5869,"He forbade the sale of uncertainty (gharar)."],[5870,"The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[5871,"Aisha wanted to buy a slave girl and then manumit her. Her owners said: 'We will sell her to you on the condition that her loyalty (wala') remains with us.' She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not let that prevent you, for loyalty belongs to the one who manumits.'"],[5872,"Aisha bargained for Barira. The Prophet ﷺ returned from prayer, and she said: 'They refused to sell her unless they stipulated the loyalty.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Loyalty belongs to the one who manumits.'"],[5873,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the dwelling of his daughter Fatimah, then turned back and did not enter. Ali came, and she mentioned that to him. He mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'I saw a curtain on her door.' Ali mentioned that to Fatimah, and she said: 'Command me with what he wishes.' Ali mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'Send it to the Banu so-and-so, for they have need of it.'"],[5874,"Bishr b. Adam narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yazid narrated to us; Sa'id b. Abi Ayyub narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman b. Ata' narrated to us; from Nafi'; from Ibn Umar; from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5875,"O Allah, bless us in our Syria. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and in our Yemen?' He said: 'O Allah, bless us in our Syria.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and in our Iraq?' He said: 'There will be earthquakes and tribulations, and from it' — or he said: 'from there' — 'the horn of Satan will appear.'"],[5876,"Whoever throws the pebbles — the Jamrah near al-Aqabah — with seven pebbles, then departs and slaughters his sacrificial animal, then shaves or shortens his hair, then everything that was forbidden to him regarding the matters of Hajj becomes permissible for him."],[5877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ran three circuits and walked four for Hajj and Umrah."],[5878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Umrah, but the disbelievers of Quraysh came between him and the House. So he slaughtered his sacrificial animal and shaved his head at al-Hudaybiyyah, on the condition that he would perform Umrah the following year. I think he said: 'And he would not enter upon them except with a token (sabuqan).' He performed Umrah the following year and entered as before. When he had stayed three days, he left."],[5879,"When a man becomes bankrupt, and another man finds his very property with him — meaning, with the bankrupt person — then he has more right to it."],[5880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from al-Baqi', Baqi' al-Gharqad, and said: 'Peace be upon the people of the dwellings, among the Muslims and the believers. May Allah have mercy on those who have gone before, and we, if Allah wills, shall follow.'"],[5881,"When you engage in 'inah transactions, take hold of the tails of cows, and abandon jihad, Allah will impose upon you a humiliation that He will not remove until you return to your religion."],[5882,"He forbade the sale of meat for animals."],[5883,"Whoever comes to a meal to which he was not invited enters as a thief and eats what is unlawful."],[5884,"When one of you sneezes, let him say: “All praise is due to Allah.”"],[5885,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the battle of Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: “But Hamzah has no women to weep for him.” That reached the Ansar, so their women came and wept over him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up when he heard their voices and said: “Woe to them! They have not ceased weeping since. Tell them to return to their homes and not weep for anyone who dies after today.”"],[5886,"Muhammad b. Uthman b. Karamah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, from Usamah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, likewise."],[5887,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his latrine facing the qiblah."],[5888,"We waited for the Prophet ﷺ until a third of the night had passed. He said: “There is no one among the followers of these religions who waits for the prayer except you. Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to pray at this hour.”"],[5889,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[5890,"And Sulayman b. Sayf narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: Ja'far b. al-Harith informed us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Isra'il."],[5891,"Do not travel by sea except as a pilgrim, a warrior, or a fighter in the cause of Allah."],[5892,"Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers."],[5893,"There is no zakat on less than five awsuq, nor on less than five awaq."],[5894,"There is no zakat on fewer than five camels."],[5895,"The king and the slave, and the husband and the wife, will be brought and the king and the slave, and the husband and the wife, will be called to account, until it will be said to the man: 'You drank on such-and-such a day for pleasure,' and it will be said to the husband: 'You proposed to so-and-so along with other suitors, and I married her to you and left them.'"],[5896,"Bishr b. Mu'adh narrated to us, Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: Either from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or from Umar."],[5897,"When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments, for Allah is most deserving of being adorned for."],[5898,"The sputum will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection in the qiblah, and it will be on the face of its owner."],[5899,"The Prophet ﷺ saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it off and then said: 'When one of you stands in prayer, let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left.'"],[5900,"We used to count for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a single sitting a hundred times saying: 'O Lord, forgive me and accept my repentance, indeed You are the Accepting of Repentance, the Forgiving.'"],[5901,"And Amr b. Ali narrated it to us, Ubayd Allah b. Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Malik b. Mighwal narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Suqah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[5902,"Ibrahim b. Sa'id narrated to us, Marwan b. Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Suqah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5903,"He used to come to a tree between Makkah and Madinah, and he would take a midday nap beneath it, and he would report that the Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[5904,"Abd al-A'la b. Hammad narrated to us, Muslim b. Khalid narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5905,"The sun eclipsed for the death of a great one among the great ones, so the Prophet ﷺ went out and prayed with the people. He prolonged the standing until it was said: He will not bow due to the length of the standing. Then he bowed until it was said: He will not raise due to the length of the bowing. Then he raised and prolonged the standing similar to his first standing. Then he bowed and prolonged the bowing similar to his first bowing. Then he raised his head and prostrated. Then he did in the other rak'ah the like of that, so it was four bowings and four prostrations. Then he turned to the people and said: 'O people, the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see them, hasten to prayer.'"],[5906,"Whoever frees a share, or a portion, or a partnership he has in a slave, and he has enough wealth to reach his value at a fair price, then he is free from his wealth."],[5907,"He forbade two sales in one sale, and he said: “Delay by a rich man is wrongdoing, and if one of you is transferred to a wealthy person, let him accept the transfer.”"],[5908,"He wrote to Nafiʿ asking him about supplication before fighting, so he wrote to him: The Messenger of God ﷺ raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were unaware and at peace, their livestock being watered at the water, and he killed their fighting men, took their offspring captive, and on that day he captured Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith."],[5909,"The likeness of the believer is that of a palm tree."],[5910,"He ordered us to empty our provision bags after three days."],[5911,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he prayed, would point with his finger and follow it with his gaze, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is harder on Satan than iron.”"],[5912,"Ibn ʿUmar would perform ablution while his sandals were on his feet, wipe over them, and say: Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do."],[5913,"A man from the Ansar saw in a dream, and it was said to him: “With what did your Prophet ﷺ command you?” He said: He commanded us to glorify thirty-three times, to magnify thirty-four times, and to praise thirty-three times. So he said: “That is one hundred times.” Then he said: “Glorify twenty-five times, praise twenty-five times, magnify twenty-five times, and declare the oneness of God twenty-five times; that is one hundred.” So that was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: “Do as the Ansari said.”"],[5914,"He would touch his beard during prayer without fidgeting."],[5915,"“Fire is an enemy, so beware of it.” He said: And Ibn ʿUmar would go through his family’s dwelling and extinguish it."],[5916,"The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer."],[5917,"The Jews of Banu al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he exiled Banu al-Nadir and left Qurayzah alone until Qurayzah fought after that; then he killed their men and divided their women, property, and children among the Muslims."],[5918,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the zakat al-fitr on the day of Eid al-Fitr to be given before the prayer."],[5919,"A person in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) or a menstruating woman should not recite anything from the Qur'an."],[5920,"We have seen ourselves when a Muslim man had no more right to his dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother."],[5921,"Sadaqah b. al-Fadl narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, something similar. We do not know anyone who reported this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah."],[5922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the Black Stone, touched it, then placed his lips upon it, weeping for a long time. He turned and saw 'Umar weeping, so he said: 'O 'Umar, here tears are shed.'"],[5923,"Prayer during travel is two rak'ahs; whoever opposes the Sunnah has disbelieved."],[5924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that captives from the disbelievers be set free as a favor; so free men are more entitled."],[5925,"He forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver."],[5926,"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad b. Mahan narrated to us: Musa b. A'yan narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. This hadith is only reported by the huffaz from Nafi', from Zayd b. 'Abdullah, from 'Abdullah b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah. We do not know anyone who said 'from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar' except Khusayf and Burd."],[5927,"Whoever gives the call to prayer (adhan) for twelve years, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and for each call sixty good deeds are written for him, and for each iqamah thirty good deeds."],[5928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from making another man get up from his seat, but if he returns, he is more entitled to it."],[5929,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding women in ihram from wearing gloves, face veils, and any clothing dyed with wars or saffron."],[5930,"If one of you becomes drowsy in his seat on Friday, he should move to another place."],[5931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two people from whispering privately with each other apart from the third when they are together, and that a man make another man get up from his seat and then return to it. And when a man returns to his seat, he has more right to it. And when he becomes drowsy on Friday, let him move from his place."],[5932,"The heat of fever is from the scorching of Hell, so cool it with water."],[5933,"I saw those who buy food in bulk being beaten during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they returned it to their dwellings."],[5934,"Ibrahim b. Yusuf al-Kufi narrated to us, Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."],[5935,"When he went out to the prayer place for al-Adha or al-Fitr, he would order for the spear, and it would be brought out in front of him until it was set up in the prayer place. It was an open space with nothing behind it to screen him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray toward it."],[5936,"He prohibited that goods be met before they are brought down to the markets, and he prohibited bid-rigging (najash)."],[5937,"He used to slaughter at the prayer place."],[5938,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Madinah for such and such a time, not abandoning the sacrifice."],[5939,"The people of al-Aliyah used to attend the Friday prayer with the Prophet ﷺ."],[5940,"While a man was looking at his garments, admiring himself, the earth suddenly swallowed him, and he will continue sinking until the Day of Resurrection."],[5941,"For what the sky waters, a tenth is due, and for what is watered by buckets, half a tenth."],[5942,"He prohibited sales involving uncertainty (gharar)."],[5943,"Al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated it to us: Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[5944,"The Prophet ﷺ came out while in the mosque there were nine people: four from the mawali (clients) and five from the Arabs. He said: \"There will be rulers over you. Whoever assists them in their wrongdoing, believes them in their lies, and frequents their doors is not of me, nor am I of him, and he will never come to me at the Pond. But whoever does not assist them in their wrongdoing and does not believe them in their lies, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond.\""],[5945,"He forbade that the fortified towers of Madinah be demolished."],[5946,"When the Prophet ﷺ bade farewell to a man, he would take him by the hand and would not let go of his hand until the man himself let go of the Prophet's hand, and he would say: \"I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the seal of your deeds.\""],[5947,"There will be in my Ummah sinking into the earth, transformation, and throwing of stones, and that will be among the people who deny predestination (Ahl al-Qadar)."],[5948,"\"O Ibn Umm 'Abd, do you know how Allah's ruling applies to those who rebel from this Ummah?\" He said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Its wounded are not dispatched, its captives are not killed, its fugitives are not pursued, and its spoils are not distributed.\""],[5949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of the unborn offspring of a pregnant animal until it gives birth and then its offspring gives birth. He forbade that, and he forbade selling animals for animals on credit."],[5950,"The false messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal) is blind in his right eye; his eye looks like a floating grape."],[5951,"There was a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who was cheated in his sales, so he complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He had a speech impediment, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you sell, say: 'No deception,' and when you buy, say: 'No deception.'\""],[5952,"So when he sold, he would say: \"No khiyabah,\" meaning \"no khilabah (deception).\""],[5953,"Habban b. Munqidh suffered a blow to his head that took away part of his intellect, so when he sold or bought, he would say: \"No deception (khilabah).\""],[5954,"Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear."],[5955,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed wine, its presser, the one who has it pressed, the carrier, the one to whom it is carried, the seller, the buyer, the pourer, and the drinker, and He forbade its price to the Muslims."],[5956,"Whoever touches his private part should perform ablution."],[5957,"He used to say the takbir in the prayer of the two Eids twelve times: seven in the first and five in the last."],[5958,"Whoever drinks wine, flog him — three times. Then if he returns for the fourth, kill him."],[5959,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought al-Nu'ayman who had drunk wine three times, so he ordered him to be beaten. When it was the fourth time, he was brought having drunk, so he was ordered and was flogged. Thus that abrogated the killing."],[5960,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[5961,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[5962,"Cupping on an empty stomach is more excellent, and in it is healing and blessing, and it increases reason and increases the memorizer in memorization. So cup yourselves in the name of God on Monday and Tuesday."],[5963,"Cupping on an empty stomach is more excellent, and in it is healing and blessing, and it increases reason and increases the memorizer in memorization. So whoever is to be cupped, in the name of God let him be cupped on Thursday, and avoid cupping on Friday, Saturday, Sunday, Monday, and Tuesday — meaning: cup yourselves on the two, the day on which affliction was turned away from Ayyub, meaning Tuesday, and avoid cupping on Wednesday, for it is a day on which a people were struck with affliction, and neither leprosy nor vitiligo begins except on Wednesday or Wednesday night. Then Abdullah b. Umar called for a son of his, three years old, and kissed his mouth."],[5964,"I did not pass by any heaven among the heavens except the angels said: O Muhammad, command your community to use cupping, for the best treatment they use is cupping, costus, and black seed."],[5965,"Whoever cheats us is not from us."],[5966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade qaza'."],[5967,"Muhammad b. Yahya al-Qati'i narrated to us: Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Umar b. Nafi', from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[5968,"He forbade al-qaza'."],[5969,"He forbade the stud fee of a stallion."],[5970,"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us: 'Ali b. al-Hakam narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know anyone who reports this hadith from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar except 'Ali b. al-Hakam, and he is a well-known man from the people of Basra."],[5971,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[5972,"When one of you has someone pass in front of him, let him repel him; if he returns, let him repel him; if he returns again, let him fight him, for he is a devil."],[5973,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter."],[5974,"I asked Sulayman al-Taymi: Does anyone come out of the Fire? He said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: By Allah, no one will come out of the Fire until he remains in it for ages (ahqab). He said: And a hiqba is eighty-some years, each year being three hundred and sixty days of what you count."],[5975,"The seal (taba') is hung on the leg of the Throne. When the womb is severed, sins are committed, and boldness is shown toward Allah, Allah sends the seal and it seals his heart, so that he no longer understands anything after that."],[5976,"That a man asked him about the night prayer, so he said: Two rak'ahs by two rak'ahs, then one."],[5977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray the two rak'ahs after Maghrib except in his house, and he would not pray after Jumu'ah except in his house."],[5978,"That a man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was urinating, and the man greeted him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned the greeting, then said: I only returned your greeting because I feared you would say, 'I greeted him and he did not return my greeting.' So when you see me in this state, do not greet me, for I will not return your greeting."],[5979,"A man greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting."],[5980,"I saw in a dream as if I was using a toothstick, and in my presence were two men. I gave it to the younger one, and it was said to me: 'Give it to the older.' So I handed it to the older one."],[5981,"Jibril ﷺ commanded me to say the takbir."],[5982,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection, so let no one violate Allah's protection concerning him. For whoever violates Allah's protection, Allah will throw him on his face into the Fire."],[5983,"Ibn Umar used to supplicate with these supplications and claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate with them: 'O Allah, apportion to us today such fear of You as will come between us and acts of disobedience to You, and such obedience to You as will bring us to Your mercy, and such certainty as will make the calamities of this world easy for us to bear. O Allah, let us enjoy our hearing and sight and make them remain with us until death, and make our vengeance upon those who have wronged us, and help us against those who are hostile to us. Do not make our affliction in our religion, and do not make this world our greatest concern, and do not give power over us to those who will not show us mercy.'"],[5984,"A man came wearing travel clothes and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placing his hands on his knees. He said: 'What is Islam?' He said: 'To testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to perform the five prayers, to fast the month of Ramadan, to pay zakat, and to perform Hajj to the House.' He said: 'If I do that, then I am a Muslim.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'What is faith (iman)?' He said: 'To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, the Resurrection, the Reckoning, Paradise, Hell, and the divine decree.' He said: 'If I do that, then I am a believer.' He said: 'Yes.' The man said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'What is excellence (ihsan)?' He said: 'To worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.' He said: 'If I do that, then I am a person of excellence.' He said: 'Yes.' The man said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: 'When is the Hour?' He said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the one asked about it is no more knowledgeable than the questioner. But I will tell you of its signs: when you see the barefoot, naked—meaning the Arabs, I think he said—competing in constructing tall buildings.' He said: Then he left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Bring the man back to me.' We went out but did not see anyone. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This was Jibril, who came to teach you your religion. He has never come to me in this form before.'"],[5985,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr was in a part of Madinah. He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placed his mouth on the Prophet's forehead, and began kissing him, saying: 'May my father and mother be your ransom. You were good alive and you are good dead.' When he came out, he passed by Umar, who was saying: 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah has not died, and he will not die until he kills the hypocrites.' The hypocrites had rejoiced at the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and raised their heads. Abu Bakr passed by him and said: 'O man, calm down, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has indeed died. Did you not hear Allah say: \"Indeed, you are to die, and indeed, they are to die\" (Q 39:30), and \"We have not granted immortality to any human before you; so if you die, will they live forever?\" (Q 21:34).' Then he went to the pulpit, ascended it, praised and extolled Allah, and said: 'O people, if Muhammad was your god whom you worship, then your god has died. But if your god is Allah, who is in heaven, then your god is alive and does not die.' Then he recited: \"Muhammad is not but a messenger; messengers have passed away before him\" (Q 3:144) until he completed the verse. Then he descended. The believers rejoiced greatly at that, and the hypocrites were overcome with gloom. Abdullah b. Umar said: 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it was as if there had been coverings over our faces, and they were removed.'"],[5986,"Allah's wrath is severe upon a woman who introduces into a people a child that is not theirs, so that he looks upon their private parts and shares in their wealth."],[5987,"A woman traveling with her slave is a cause of ruin."],[5988,"Whoever seeks a right, let him seek it with integrity, whether it is fulfilled or not."],[5989,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[5990,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent Adam down to the earth, the angels said: 'Our Lord, will You place upon it one who causes corruption therein and sheds blood, while we declare Your praise and sanctify You?' He said: 'Indeed, I know that which you do not know.' They said: 'We are more obedient to You than the children of Adam.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to the angels: 'Choose two angels from among the angels so that they may descend to the earth, and We shall see how they act.' They said: 'Our Lord, Harut and Marut.' So they were sent down to the earth, and the Venus woman was made to appear to them as one of the most beautiful of people. She came to them, and they asked her for herself. She said: 'No, by Allah, not until you commit shirk,' or something similar. They said: 'By Allah, we will never associate anything with Allah.' She left them, then returned carrying a child. They asked her for herself. She said: 'No, by Allah, not until you kill this child.' They said: 'By Allah, we will never kill him.' She left, then returned carrying a cup of wine. They asked her for herself. She said: 'No, by Allah, not until you drink this wine.' They drank it and became intoxicated, then they had intercourse with her and killed the child. When they sobered up, the woman said: 'By Allah, you did not leave anything that you had refused except that you did it when you were intoxicated.' At that point, they were given the choice between the punishment of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter, and they chose the punishment of this world."],[5991,"I never prayed behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him say when he finished: O Allah, forgive me my errors and my deliberate acts. O Allah, guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness or turns away their evil except You."],[5992,"Allah – blessed and exalted – loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His strict commands be taken, or: just as He hates that His disobedience be committed."],[5993,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[5994,"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call."],[5995,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man from the Ansar admonishing his brother about modesty, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Modesty is part of faith."],[5996,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he began the prayer, raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders; and when he intended to bow; and after he raised his head from bowing. He did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[5997,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father."],[5998,"Muhammad b. al-Layth narrated to us: Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Bakr b. Mudar narrated to us, from Ja‘far b. Rabi‘ah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, similarly."],[5999,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a white shirt on Umar and said: Is this garment of yours new or washed? He said: Washed. He said: Wear new, live praiseworthy, and die a martyr."],[6000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Khalid b. al-Walid to Banu Jadhimah. He invited them to Islam, but they could not say it correctly: 'We have submitted.' They kept saying: 'We have turned Sabian, we have turned Sabian.' Khalid began killing and taking captives, and he gave each man his captive. When morning came, Khalid ordered that each of us kill his captive. When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Khalid's action was mentioned to him, so he raised his hands and said three times: O Allah, I declare myself innocent before You of what Khalid has done."],[6001,"In the Fajr prayer, when he raised his head from the second rak‘ah, he would supplicate against certain people among the hypocrites. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.'"],[6002,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by al-Hijr and said: Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest what befell them befall you. Then he quickened his pace until he passed through the valley."],[6003,"I saw myself tonight being brought a cup, and I drank from it until I could see the quench flowing, then I handed my leftover to Umar. They said: What did you interpret that as, O Messenger of God? He said: Knowledge."],[6004,"He used to pray on his mount wherever it turned him."],[6005,"That a man asked him, saying: I saw the Night of Decree as if it were the night of the twenty-third. He said: I see that your visions have concurred on the last ten, so seek it in the ten, in the seven remaining, in the odd."],[6006,"You will be set upon them - meaning the Jews - until the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew - I think he said - so kill him."],[6007,"I saw the two of them when it was commanded regarding them - meaning the two Jews - that they be stoned, and I saw him shielding her with his hand to protect her from the stones. He said: And this verse was revealed regarding that: 'Indeed, We sent down the Torah, in it is guidance and light; the prophets who submitted judged by it,' and the Prophet ﷺ was among them."],[6008,"When the drop is created in the womb, the angel of the wombs says: O Lord, what shall I write? So He decrees to him his matter, and he says: Male or female? So He decrees to him his matter, and he writes, and He decrees what he will meet until he dies, even the calamity that will befall him."],[6009,"The sun's declining is its setting from the meridian."],[6010,"That Ghaylan b. Salama accepted Islam and had ten wives under him, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them."],[6011,"That Ghaylan b. Salama accepted Islam and had ten wives under him whom he had in the pre-Islamic era and they accepted Islam with him, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them."],[6012,"Ill omen is in three: the house, the woman, and the horse."],[6013,"Kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they blind the sight and cause miscarriage."],[6014,"That some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, we entered this house while we had abundant wealth and became poor, and our number was many and our number decreased, and our relations were good and our relations became bad. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is blameworthy. They said: O Messenger of God, how can we leave it? He said: Sell it, or give it away."],[6015,"He used to send the weak members of his family ahead, and they would stand at al-Mash'ar and depart before the people, or before the imam departed. Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of God ﷺ granted a concession in that for women."],[6016,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of the Friday prayer, let him pray another one to it."],[6017,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or in addition to her maternal aunt."],[6018,"Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."],[6019,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar did not wear their rings until Aban came to ʿUmar."],[6020,"Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."],[6021,"Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."],[6022,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to touch the Yemeni corner and the Black Stone."],[6023,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the ʿIsha' prayer one night, and ʿUmar called out to him: \"The women and children have slept.\" He said: \"No one on earth is waiting for this prayer except you.\""],[6024,"Do not prevent the maidservants of God from praying in the mosques."],[6025,"The night prayer is two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs, and when you fear the approach of dawn, then one rakʿah, which makes it odd."],[6026,"He used to send the weak members of his family ahead, and they would stand at al-Mashʿar and say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave permission to the weak members of his family.\""],[6027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: “I warn you of him, and indeed Nuh warned his people of him, but I will tell you something about him that no Prophet told his people: Allah is not one-eyed.”"],[6028,"I saw people in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being struck if a man bought food and then sold it before carrying it to his mount."],[6029,"None of you should make his brother get up from his seat and then sit in it."],[6030,"He used to pray two rak'ahs in his house on Friday when he returned."],[6031,"The Prophet ﷺ came to al-Hijr and said: “Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest what befell them befall you.” Then he quickened his pace until he passed the valley."],[6032,"I was with Ibn Umar when a man came and asked him about tamattu' (combining 'umrah with hajj). He said: “It is fine; there is no harm in it.” The man said: “But your father used to forbid it.” Ibn Umar became angry and said: “We follow the command of the Messenger of Allah.”"],[6033,"The Prophet ﷺ shaved his head during his Hajj."],[6034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the fear prayer with one group while the other group faced the enemy. Then they departed and stood in the place of their companions facing the enemy. Then those came, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in one rak'ah, then he said the salam. Then these completed one rak'ah and those completed one rak'ah."],[6035,"He forbade coming to women at night."],[6036,"A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."],[6037,"When he stoned the jamrah, he threw seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble. Then he descended to its right and stood facing the qiblah, raising his hands and supplicating, and he would prolong the standing. Then he came to the second jamrah and threw seven pebbles, saying takbir each time he threw a pebble. Then he descended to the left toward the valley and stood facing the House, raising his hands and supplicating. Then he came to the jamrah near the 'Aqabah and threw seven pebbles, saying takbir each time he threw a pebble. Then he departed and did not stand there."],[6038,"A fire is about to emerge before the Day of Resurrection from Hadramawt that will gather the people.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what do you command us?” He said: “Go to al-Sham.”"],[6039,"Whoever has a slave jointly owned between him and another, and one of them frees his share, then if he is wealthy, the slave is valued at the highest price, or valued with no decrease and no excess, then he is freed."],[6040,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a hurry to travel, he would delay this prayer."],[6041,"Umar b. al-Khattab went out to the mosque and found a striped silk garment, so he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not buy this garment and wear it when delegations come to you and on Friday? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Those are the clothes of one who has no share in the Hereafter. He stayed as long as Allah willed, then he sent Umar a brocade garment that had been gifted to him. Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me this while I heard you say what you said about it. He said: I did not send it to you to wear, but I sent it to you so that you may sell it and use it for some of your needs, or clothe some of your women."],[6042,"And al-Jarrah b. Makhlad narrated to us: Rawh b. Ubadah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[6043,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[6044,"There are three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of his gifts. And there are three who will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the masculine woman."],[6045,"There are three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the woman who imitates men. And there are three who will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the one who reminds others of his gifts, and the habitual drinker of wine."],[6046,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Usamah b. Zayd as a commander, they spoke about him, and that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I have been informed of what you said about Usamah. You said the same about his father before him. Indeed, he is worthy of leadership, and he is the most beloved of people to me—he did not make an exception for Fatimah or anyone else."],[6047,"The oath which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to swear by was: No, by the Turner of hearts."],[6048,"The one who drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, one side of my lower garment hangs loose. He said: You are not one of those who do it out of arrogance."],[6049,"I saw a black woman with disheveled hair leaving Madinah until she settled in Mahya'ah, which is al-Juhfah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ interpreted it as the plague of Madinah moving to al-Juhfah."],[6050,"Whoever takes a span of land, it will be made a collar around his neck from seven earths."],[6051,"He met Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah. That was before revelation came down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ presented to him a leather mat with meat on it. He said: 'We do not eat what you slaughter on your stone altars, and we do not eat except that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned.'"],[6052,"Ibn Maʿmar narrated it to us from ʿAffān, from Wuhayb, from Mūsā, from Sālim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enjoin brevity, and he would lead us in prayer with the sāffāt."],[6054,"I saw by the Kaʿbah a dark-complexioned man with lank hair, placing his hands on two men while water was being poured on his head—or dripping. I asked, 'Who is this?' It was said, 'ʿĪsā b. Maryam,' or 'the Messiah b. Maryam.' Ḥanẓalah said: 'I do not know which of the two it was.' He said: 'And I saw behind him a red-complexioned man with curly hair, blind in the left eye, the closest person I have seen resembling him is Ibn Qaṭan—meaning ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā b. Qaṭan. I asked, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"The false Messiah.\"'"],[6055,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was pointing toward Iraq: 'The fitnah is here, the fitnah is from where the horn of Satan rises.'"],[6056,"The fitnah is here."],[6057,"ʿUqbah b. Mukram narrated it to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us; ʿUmar b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from Sālim, from his father, from the Prophet, similarly."],[6058,"The fitnah will come from the direction of the east, from where the horn of Satan rises, while you are striking one another's necks. And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to Mūsā: 'And you killed a soul, but We saved you from distress and tried you with a trial.'"],[6059,"Whoever prays over a funeral will have a qīrāṭ, and whoever waits until it is buried will have two qīrāṭs."],[6060,"Whoever makes an image will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection to bring it to life."],[6061,"O Allah, bless us in our Shām, in our Yemen, in our mudd, and in our ṣāʿ."],[6062,"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[6063,"6073 6069 - Ali b. al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, Anas b. Iyad Abu Damrah narrated to us, Musa b. Uqbah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[6064,"And al-Fadl b. Sahl narrated to us, Nuh b. Maymun narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Mas'ud narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[6065,"Seek the counsel of women concerning themselves."],[6066,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a dog for livestock or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day. And in the hadith of Bukayr he said: a hunting dog, or a dog for livestock."],[6067,"Amr b. Ali and Uqbah b. Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, Umar b. Muhammad narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6068,"I saw in what the sleeper sees, as if I were at a well, and the people gathered around it. Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah forgive him. Then Umar came, and it turned in his hand into a large bucket, and I did not see a genius among men excel in his manner of drawing until the people had watered their camels."],[6069,"The one who lies about me will have a house built for him in the Fire."],[6070,"He forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."],[6071,"Do not strike the image."],[6072,"When women ask your permission to go to the mosques at night, grant them permission."],[6073,"Come, let me bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bid us farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the last of your deeds."],[6074,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna and Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah b. Abdullah b. Abdullah b. Umar narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6075,"That the stomach of any one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."],[6076,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[6077,"God, Blessed and Exalted, forbids you from swearing by your forefathers."],[6078,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Qabisah b. Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim b. Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[6079,"No man makes an image except that it will be said to him: Bring to life what you have created."],[6080,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in three garments."],[6081,"Regarding tayammum with earth: that you strike the ground with your palms, then wipe your face with them, then strike another time and wipe your forearms up to the elbows."],[6082,"Muhammad b. Thabit al-Asri has narrated it from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ. Muhammad b. Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Thabit narrated to us."],[6083,"The one who drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6084,"Ahmad b. al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Umar through several routes: Salim, Nafi, Abdullah b. Dinar, Zayd b. Aslam, and others narrated it. We have repeated it only because Qatadah did not narrate with a chain from Salim, from his father, any hadith other than this one. If we had omitted it, Qatadah's hadith from Salim would have been lost. Qudamah b. Musa also did not narrate with a chain from Salim, from his father, any hadith other than this one."],[6085,"It is not appropriate for a believer to be a curser."],[6086,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ among men from his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do you not know that I am the Messenger of God to you? They said: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. He said: Do you not know that God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed in His Book: Whoever obeys me has obeyed God. They said: We bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed God; God has commanded obedience to you. He said: Obey God and obey the Messenger, for obedience to God is obedience to me, and obedience to me is that you obey your leaders. If he prays sitting, then pray sitting."],[6087,"Use ithmid (antimony), for it makes the hair grow and clears the vision."],[6088,"Use the black seed, for in it there is healing for every disease except death."],[6089,"Your smiling in the face of your brother is recorded for you as charity, and your pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is recorded for you as charity."],[6090,"Your enjoining good and forbidding evil is recorded for you as charity, and your removing harm from the road is recorded for you as charity, and your guiding a lost person is recorded for you as charity."],[6091,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[6092,"When he traveled, he prayed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and when he stayed in a land, he performed voluntary prayers."],[6093,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, and with him were 'Uthman b. Shaybah and Bilal. They closed the door. I was a strong man, so I pushed until I reached the door, and I met him as he was coming out. I asked them how he prayed, and they said: He prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars."],[6094,"6104 6101 - Muhammad narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Salim and Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."],[6095,"He used to come to Quba riding and walking."],[6096,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, while he was holding 'Ali's hand: Whoever I am his mawla, this is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him."],[6097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of 'Eid and prayed without an adhan or iqamah."],[6098,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will fold the heavens and take them in His right hand, and fold the earth and take it in His other hand, then He will say: I am the King, where are the kings?"],[6099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner:"],[6100,"We used to pledge allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ on hearing and obedience. He would say to us: In as much as you are able."],[6101,"The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."],[6102,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the cessation of Your favor, the change of Your well-being, the suddenness of Your vengeance, and all of Your displeasure."],[6103,"Abdullah b. Shabib narrated to us, Ismail b. Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa b. Uqbah, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6104,"And Ubayd b. Ismail narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah b. Umar, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6105,"He forbade the sale of wala' (patronage) and its gift."],[6106,"Mu'ammal b. Hisham narrated to him, Ismail b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner."],[6107,"And Ahmad b. Abdah narrated to him, Sufyan b. Uyaynah informed us, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, in a similar manner."],[6108,"He used to pray on his mount, wherever it turned with him during travel."],[6109,"Ghifar, may Allah forgive them; Aslam, may Allah keep them safe; and Usayyah, they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[6110,"And Nasr b. Ali narrated to him, Abu Ahmad informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it."],[6111,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Hijr, he said: Do not enter the dwellings of these people who were punished, unless you are weeping. So do not enter upon them, lest what befell them befalls you."],[6112,"We used to dislike speaking during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, fearing that the Qur'an would be revealed concerning us. But when he passed away, we spoke."],[6113,"He used to come to the mosque of Quba' every Saturday, coming to it on foot and riding."],[6114,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog of livestock or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."],[6115,"When a Jew greets you, he only says: 'Al-sam 'alayk' (death be upon you), so say: 'Wa 'alayk' (and upon you)."],[6116,"When the Jews greet you, they say: 'Al-sam 'alaykum' (death be upon you), so say: 'Wa 'alaykum' (and upon you)."],[6117,"The Prophet ﷺ gestured with his hand toward the east and said: 'The trial is here' - or 'from here' - 'from where the horn of Satan appears.'"],[6118,"Every two parties to a sale have no sale between them until they separate, except the sale with option."],[6119,"Ahmad b. 'Abda narrated to us: Sufyan b. 'Uyayna informed us, from 'Abd Allah b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ with the like of it."],[6120,"Hatim was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'That is a man who wanted something and attained it.'"],[6121,"Among the most wicked of falsehoods is that a man claims to be the son of someone other than his father, and among the most wicked of falsehoods is that a man claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see, and among the most wicked of falsehoods is that a man says about me what I did not say."],[6122,"Two hungry wolves in a sheepfold, eating and causing corruption, are not more harmful to it than the love of honor and the love of wealth are to the religion of a Muslim man."],[6123,"Whoever owns a forbidden relative is free."],[6124,"Abu Bakr (may God have mercy on him) brought Abu Quhafa, leading him to the Messenger of God ﷺ, an elderly blind man, on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Why did you not leave the old man so that we could come to him?' He said: 'I wanted, O Messenger of God, for God to reward him. By the One who sent you with the truth, I was more overjoyed at the conversion of Abu Talib than at the conversion of my father, seeking thereby the delight of your eye.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[6125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade shighar, and the sale of inert livestock, and the sale of uncertainty, and the sale of deferred for deferred, and the sale of immediate for deferred."],[6126,"The poor believers complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about what their wealthy were favored with. They said: 'O Messenger of God, our brothers have believed as we believe, and have faith as we have faith, and fast as we fast, but they have wealth from which they give charity, maintain kinship ties, and spend in the path of God, while we are poor and unable to do that.' He said: 'Shall I not tell you something which, if you do it, you will attain the like of their virtue? Say after every prayer: Allahu akbar eleven times, and al-hamdu lillah the like of that, and la ilaha illa Allah the like of that, and subhan Allah the like of that — you will attain the like of their virtue.' They did so, then mentioned that to the wealthy, who also did the like of that. The poor returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, saying: 'These are our brothers; they have done the like of what we say.' He said: 'That is the bounty of God; He gives it to whom He wills. O company of the poor, shall I not give you glad tidings? The poor Muslims will enter Paradise half a day before their wealthy — five hundred years.' Musa b. Ubayda recited: 'And indeed a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of what you count.'"],[6127,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us; Buhlul narrated to us from Musa b. Ubayda; Sadaqa b. Yasar and Abdullah b. Dinar narrated to me from Ibn Umar."],[6128,"This surah was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina, during the middle of the days of Tashriq, in the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'When the victory of God and the conquest comes.' He knew that it was the farewell, so he ordered his she-camel, al-Qaswa, to be saddled for him, then he mounted and stood for the people at al-Aqaba. The Muslims gathered to him as God willed. He praised God and lauded Him as He deserves, then said: 'Now then, O people, every blood that was shed in the Jahiliyyah is forfeited, and the first of your blood I forfeit is the blood of Rabi'a b. al-Harith, who was being fostered among Banu Layth and was killed by Hudhayl. Every usury in the Jahiliyyah is abolished, and the first of your usury I abolish is the usury of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. O people, time has revolved to its state on the day God created the heavens and the earth. The number of months with God is twelve months, of which four are sacred: Rajab of Mudar, which is between Jumada and Sha'ban, and Dhu al-Qa'da, Dhu al-Hijja, and al-Muharram. That is the upright religion, so do not wrong yourselves therein. The postponement is only an increase in disbelief by which the disbelievers are led astray; they make it lawful one year and unlawful another year to match the number of what God has made sacred. They would make Safar lawful one year and unlawful al-Muharram one year, and make Safar unlawful one year and lawful al-Muharram one year; that is the postponement. O people, whoever has a trust, let him return it to the one who entrusted him with it. O people, Satan has despaired of being worshipped in your lands at the end of time, but he is pleased with the trivial acts of yours, so beware for your religion of the trivial acts. O people, women are like captives with you; you have taken them with the trust of God and made their private parts lawful with the word of God. You have rights over them and they have rights over you. Among your rights over them is that they should not allow anyone you dislike to tread on your beds, and they should not disobey you in what is proper. If they do that, then you have no way against them, and they have their provision and clothing in a proper manner. If you strike, then strike a blow that is not painful. It is not lawful for a man to take from his brother's wealth except what he gives willingly. O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will not go astray: the Book of God, so act upon it. O people, which day is this?' They said: 'A sacred day.' He said: 'Which land is this?' They said: 'A sacred land.' He said: 'Which month is this?' They said: 'A sacred month.' He said: 'Indeed, God, Blessed and Exalted, has made your blood, your wealth, and your honor as sacred as this day, this month, and this land. Let those present convey to those absent. There is no prophet after me, and no community after you.' Then he raised his hands and said: 'O God, bear witness.'"],[6129,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which of the people has the best recitation?' He said: 'The one who, when you hear him recite, you see that he fears God.'"],[6130,"The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble — Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim, may God bless them."],[6131,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ramal from the Stone to the Stone."],[6132,"One who remembers God among the heedless is like a fighter alongside those who flee."],[6133,"Whoever says in a market among the markets: 'There is no god but God, alone, without partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, He gives life and causes death, and He is living and does not die; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things' — if he says it once, God will record for him a thousand thousand good deeds, erase from him a thousand thousand bad deeds, and build for him a house in Paradise."],[6134,"When my community walks with a proud, swaggering gait and is served by the Persians and Romans, its enemy will be given power over it."],[6135,"This hadith is only known from the hadith of Musa b. Ubayda, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ. Yusuf b. Musa narrated it to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa b. Ubayda."],[6136,"I am the first over whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, then Abu Bakr, then Umar. Then I will come to al-Baqi‘ and they will be gathered with me. Then I will wait for the people of Makkah until I am gathered between the two Harams — or between the people of the two Harams."],[6137,"Ramadan in Makkah is better than a thousand Ramadans elsewhere than Makkah."],[6138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Dhu al-Hulayfa as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfa for the people of Sham, and Qarn for the people of Najd."],[6139,"When one of you prays, let him pray toward a sutra and not let anyone pass in front of him. If he refuses, then let him fight him, for with him is the qarin."],[6140,"The Prophet ﷺ had a room in the mosque where he would perform i‘tikaf during the last part of Ramadan, and he would pray in it. He put his head out from it and said: The one praying is confiding in his Lord, so let each of you consider what he confides, and let not some of you raise their voices over others."],[6141,"He forbade (the use of) gourds, green jars, and vessels smeared with pitch."],[6142,"Muhammad b. Ismail narrated it to us, from Asbat, from al-Shaybani, from Muharib, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6143,"The likeness of a hypocrite — or he said: the likeness of a Muslim — is the likeness of a green tree. He said: I thought it was the palm tree, and I wanted to say it, but I was a young man and felt shy. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: It is the palm tree. Ibn Umar said: I told my father what I had wanted to say, and he said: If you had said it, it would have been dearer to me than such and such."],[6144,"He traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he prayed at Mina the prayer of travel, and with Abu Bakr the prayer of travel, and with Umar the prayer of travel, and with Uthman the prayer of travel, then after that he prayed four (rak‘ahs)."],[6145,"The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was (in) pairs, pairs, and the iqama was (in) singles, singles, except that the mu'adhdhin used to say: Qad qamat al-salah — twice."],[6146,"Ahmad b. Abda narrated to us: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Budayl b. Maysara and Ayyub, from Abdullah b. Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar."],[6147,"6157 6155 - And Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated to us, 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn 'Umar"],[6148,"That a man asked the Prophet ﷺ - while I was between him and the questioner - about the night prayer. He said: \"Two by two, and when you sense or fear the approach of dawn, make the last of your prayer a witr.\""],[6149,"Benefit from this House, for it has been destroyed twice and will be raised in the third."],[6150,"It is part of the sunnah that a man performs ghusl when he intends to enter ihram."],[6151,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah. I mentioned that to Ibn 'Umar and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only entered ihram for Hajj.\""],[6152,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: \"Anas narrated to us that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Labbayka with 'Umrah and Hajjah.'\" He said: \"Anas has erred. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out and recited the talbiyah for Hajj, and we recited it with him. When he arrived, he ordered those who did not have a sacrificial animal with them to make it an 'Umrah.\" I mentioned that to Anas and he said: \"You consider us nothing but children.\""],[6153,"6163 6161 - 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated to us, Khalid b. al-Harith narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr"],[6154,"And 'Amr b. Yazid Abu Burayd narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bakr b. 'Abd Allah al-Muzani"],[6155,"Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak. And it is mentioned from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6156,"I asked Ibn 'Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: \"Do you know 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. 'Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and he ordered him to take her back.\" I said: \"Is the waiting period counted from that menstruation?\" He said: \"So what? What do you think if he is unable and acts foolishly?\""],[6157,"And 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated it to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Yunus b. Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And we do not know that Yunus b. Jubayr narrated from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ any hadith other than this."],[6158,"I was with Ibn 'Umar when a man came to him and said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what do you think about the witr? Is it a sunnah?\" He said: \"It is a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed witr and the Muslims performed witr.\""],[6159,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Which part of the night is most answered?” He said: “The middle of the last part of the night.”"],[6160,"When Ibn ʿUmar went to his bed, he would say: “O Allah, You created my soul and You take it. To You belongs its death and its life. O Allah, if You take it, forgive it, and if You return it, protect it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being.” A man from his children said: “Did Ibn ʿUmar say this?” He said: “Rather, someone better than Ibn ʿUmar used to say this.”"],[6161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muʿādh and Abū Mūsā, and said: “Consult each other and obey each other, and make things easy and do not make them difficult, and give good news and do not drive people away.”"],[6162,"I said to Ibn ʿUmar: “Do you pray the forenoon prayer?” He said: “No.” I said: “Did ʿUmar pray it?” He said: “No.” I said: “Did Abū Bakr pray it?” He said: “No.” I said: “Did the Prophet ﷺ pray it?” He said: “I do not think he used to pray it.”"],[6163,"A woman asked Ibn ʿUmar about silk. He said: “We used to say that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"],[6164,"I witnessed Ibn ʿUmar when a man asked him about a pilgrim killing a fly. He said: “O people of Iraq, you ask me about killing a fly while you have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘They are my two fragrant flowers in this world.’”"],[6165,"He used to pray two rakʿahs before ẓuhr, two after it, two after maghrib, two after ʿishāʾ, and two after fajr."],[6166,"“Every day He is in a matter.” He said: “He forgives a sin and removes a distress.”"],[6167,"We were with Ibn ʿUmar at Minā when a young man from the people of Basra came to ask him about something. He said: “I will tell you about that. I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the tenth of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd, Muʿādh, Ḥudhayfah, Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, another man he named, and myself. A young man from the Anṣār came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then sat down and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best?’ He said: ‘The best of them in character.’ He said: ‘Which of the believers is wisest?’ He said: ‘The most frequent of them in remembering death and the best in preparing for it before it comes upon them’—or he said: ‘upon him. Those are the wise ones.’ Then the young man fell silent and the Prophet ﷺ turned to us and said: ‘Indecency never appears among a people except that plague and pains appear among them that were not present among their ancestors. They do not cheat in weights and measures except that they are seized with years of famine, hardship, and the tyranny of rulers over them. They do not withhold the zakāt of their wealth except that rain is withheld from the sky, and were it not for the animals, they would not receive rain. They do not break the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger except that their enemy is set upon them and they lose some of what they had. When their leaders do not rule by the Book of Allah, Allah makes their might turn against one another.’ He said: Then he ordered ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf to prepare for a military expedition he placed him in command of. He appeared in the morning wearing a black cotton turban. The Prophet ﷺ called him, unwound it, and rewrapped it for him, leaving four fingers’ length hanging behind. Then he said: ‘Like this, O Ibn ʿAwf, wrap your turban, for it is more knowable and better.’ Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilāl to bring the banner to him, praised Allah, and said: ‘Go forth all together in the cause of Allah and fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. This is the covenant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his practice for you.’”"],[6168,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a vow. He said: “It does not bring anything forward nor delay it, but by it wealth is extracted from the miser.”"],[6169,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque of Minā when a man from the Anṣār and a man from Thaqīf came and greeted him, then said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you.” He said: “If you wish, I will inform you about what you came to ask me; if you wish, I will remain silent and you may ask.” They said: “Inform us, O Messenger of Allah.” The Thaqafī said to the Anṣārī: “Ask.” He said: “Inform me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “You came to ask me about your departure from your house heading to the Sacred House and what you have in it, about your two rakʿahs after ṭawāf and what you have in them, about your walking between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and what you have in it, about your standing on the evening of ʿArafah and what you have in it, about your stoning of the jamarāt and what you have in it, about your sacrifice and what you have in it, about shaving your head and what you have in it, and about your circumambulation of the House after that and what you have in it along with the ifāḍah.” He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, about this I came to ask you.” He said: “When you leave your house heading to the Sacred House, your camel does not place a hoof nor raise it except that Allah writes a good deed for you for it and erases a sin from you. As for your two rakʿahs after ṭawāf, they are like freeing a slave from the descendants of Ismāʿīl. As for your walking between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah after that, it is like freeing seventy slaves. As for your standing on the evening of ʿArafah, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of you to the angels, saying: ‘My servants have come to Me disheveled from every deep valley hoping for My mercy. If your sins were as many as the grains of sand, or as the drops of rain, or as the foam of the sea, He would forgive them’—or ‘I would forgive them.’ ‘Depart, My servants, forgiven for you and for those you intercede for.’ As for your stoning of the jamarāt, for every pebble you throw, you have a major sin among the destructive sins removed. As for your sacrifice, it is stored for you with your Lord. As for shaving your head, for every hair you shave, you have a good deed and a sin is erased from you. As for your circumambulation of the House after that, you circumambulate and you have no sin. An angel comes and places his hands between your shoulders and says: ‘Work for what is ahead, for what is past has been forgiven for you.’”"],[6170,"Women from the Anṣār entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “O women of the Anṣār, dye with henna five times, and trim but do not overdo it, for it is more pleasing to your husbands. And beware of ingratitude toward those who do good.”"],[6171,"Abu Talha prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent Anas b. Malik. He came until he entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among his companions, and he said: \"Did your father invite us?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Get up.\" Anas said: \"So I went to Abu Talha and informed him, and he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is only food that we wished to honor you with.' So he called for it, placed his hand upon it, and supplicated for blessing. Then he said: 'Admit ten.' So he admitted them and they ate until they were full. Then he said: 'Admit ten,' and he admitted them. I kept admitting ten at a time until they all ate their fill, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left for us the like of what we had prepared, or more.\""],[6172,"And Umar b. al-Khattab narrated it to us: Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid b. Yazid, from Sa'id b. Abi Hilal, from Muhammad b. Ka'b, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know that Muhammad b. Ka'b narrated from Anas any hadith other than this one, and we do not know that anything from Abu Salamah from Anas is authentic except this hadith, and we do not know that anyone narrated it from Muhammad b. Amr except Abu Usamah."],[6173,"The leaders are from Quraysh as long as they act upon three things: when they are asked for mercy they show mercy, when they make a covenant they fulfill it, and when they judge they are just."],[6174,"Ahmad b. Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Anas b. Iyad narrated to us, from Yusuf b. Abi Dhurrah, from Ja'far b. Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri, from Anas."],[6175,"Whoever Allah, Blessed and Exalted, grants a lifespan of forty years in Islam, Allah diverts from him various kinds of affliction: insanity, leprosy, and vitiligo. Abdul Malik al-Juddi said in his version: Allah withholds from him various kinds of affliction: leprosy, vitiligo, and the strangling of Satan. And whoever Allah grants a lifespan of fifty years in Islam, Allah makes the reckoning gentle for him. Abu Damrah said: Allah makes the reckoning easy for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever Allah grants a lifespan of sixty years in Islam, Allah grants him turning to Him in repentance with what Allah loves. Abu Damrah said: Allah grants him excellent turning to Him. And whoever Allah grants a lifespan of seventy years in Islam, the inhabitants of heaven and the inhabitants of earth love him. And whoever Allah grants a lifespan of eighty years in Islam, Allah erases his evil deeds and records his good deeds. Anas b. Iyad said in his version: His good deeds are recorded and his evil deeds are not recorded. And whoever Allah grants a lifespan of ninety years in Islam, Allah forgives him his sins, and he becomes a prisoner of Allah on His earth and an intercessor for his household on the Day of Resurrection. Anas b. Iyad said: He is a prisoner of Allah on His earth and intercedes for his household."],[6176,"The prayer of the hypocrite: he sits waiting for the sun until it turns yellow and is on the horns of Satan, or between the horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks out four [rak'ahs], not remembering Allah except a little."],[6177,"We entered upon Anas b. Malik after noon, and he stood to pray Asr. When he finished his prayer, we said to him: \"Do you hasten the prayer?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'That is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them sits until the sun turns yellow and is between the horns of Satan, or on the horns of Satan, then he stands and pecks out four [rak'ahs], not remembering Allah in them except a little.'\""],[6178,"He used to pray Jumu'ah when the sun declined, and when he went out to Makkah he prayed Zuhr at al-Shajarah with two prostrations [i.e., shortened it to two rak'ahs]."],[6179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to the people while they were praying sitting down due to illness, and he said: \"The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing.\""],[6180,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon one day, a man entered through a door that faced the pulpit and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, wealth has been destroyed and the roads have been cut off, so supplicate to Allah to send us rain.\" The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands and said: \"O Allah, give us rain; O Allah, give us rain; O Allah, give us rain.\" By Allah, no cloud or even a small piece of cloud could be seen in the sky, and there was no house or dwelling between us and Sal' [a mountain]. Then a cloud like a shield appeared from its corner, and when it reached the middle of the sky it spread. Anas said: \"By Allah, we did not see the sun for six [days]. Then a man came through that same door on the following Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing delivering the sermon. When he faced him while standing, he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, wealth has been destroyed and the roads have been cut off, so supplicate to Allah to remove it from us.' The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands and said: 'O Allah, around us and not upon us; O Allah, upon the hills and the rocky outcrops and the beds of the valleys and the places where trees grow.' He said: 'It cleared, and we went out walking in the sun.' Sharik said: 'I asked Anas: Was it the same man as the first? He said: I do not know.'\""],[6181,"Ahmad b. Aban narrated to us: Anas b. Iyad narrated to us: Sharik b. Abi Namir narrated to us, from Anas b. Malik."],[6182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and warned the people. A man stood and said: \"When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah?\" We said to him: \"Sit down, for you have asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ something he dislikes.\" Then he stood a second time and said: \"When is the Hour?\" The dislike became more apparent in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the first time. He said: \"We made him sit down.\" Then he stood a third time and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?\" He said: \"Woe to you, what have you prepared for it?\" The man said: \"I have prepared for it love of Allah and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sit down, for you will be with those you love.\""],[6183,"I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was lighter or more complete than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a child crying behind him, he would lighten the prayer for fear that its mother would be distressed."],[6184,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, a man entered on a camel and made it kneel in the mosque. Then he said to them, \"Which of you is Muhammad?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining among them. They said, \"We said: It is the white man who is reclining.\" The man said, \"I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you: Did Allah send you to all people?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Allah: Did Allah command you that we pray the five prayers in the day and night?\" He said, \"O Allah, yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Allah: Did Allah command you to take this charity from our rich and divide it among our poor?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, yes.\" The man said, \"I believe in what you have brought, and I am the messenger of those behind me of my people. I am Dimam b. Tha'labah, the brother of Banu Sa'd b. Bakr.\""],[6185,"The believer is the mirror of the believer."],[6186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out when the prayer had been called and saw people praying the two rak'ahs of Fajr. He said, \"Two prayers together.\" And he forbade praying them when the prayer had been called."],[6187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain before the prayer, faced the qiblah, and turned his cloak inside out. Then he descended and prayed two rak'ahs."],[6188,"The martyrs are three: A man who went out with his life and wealth, seeking reward in the path of Allah, not wanting to kill or be killed or fight, but to increase the numbers of the Muslims. If he dies or is killed, all his sins are forgiven him, and he is protected from the punishment of the grave, and secured from the greatest terror, and married to the wide-eyed houris, and the garment of honor is placed on him, and the crown of dignity and eternity is placed on his head. The second: A man who went out with his life and wealth, seeking reward, wanting to be killed and not to kill. If he dies or is killed, his knee will be with the knee of Ibrahim, the Friend of the Merciful, before Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in a seat of truth near an Omnipotent Sovereign. The third: A man who went out with his life and wealth, seeking reward, wanting to kill and be killed. If he dies or is killed, he will come on the Day of Resurrection brandishing his sword, placing it on his shoulder, while the people are kneeling on their knees, saying, 'Make way for us, for we have sacrificed our blood for Allah, Blessed and Exalted.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he said it to Ibrahim, the Friend of the Merciful, or to any prophet among the prophets, they would move aside from the path for them, because of the obligation of their right that he sees, until they come to pulpits of light on the right of the Throne, and sit on them, watching how judgment is passed among the people. They do not feel the agony of death, nor do they remain in the barzakh, nor does the shout frighten them, nor do the reckoning, the scales, or the bridge concern them. They watch how judgment is passed among the people, and they do not ask for anything but they are given it, and they do not intercede for anything but they are granted intercession in it. They are given from Paradise whatever they love, and they take their abode in Paradise wherever they love.'"],[6189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent at the age of forty. He stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he died at the age of sixty. There were not twenty white hairs on his head or beard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not excessively tall nor short, nor was he very white or dark, nor did he have very curly hair or very straight hair."],[6190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was neither white nor dark, neither tall nor short, and did not have curly hair. Revelation came to him when he was forty years old. He stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he ﷺ died at the age of sixty. On the day he died, there were not twenty white hairs on his head."],[6191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the head of al-Hasan or al-Husayn be shaved on his seventh day, and that silver equal to its weight be given in charity."],[6192,"Safwan b. al-Mughallis narrated to us, Mujja'ah b. Thabit narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from 'Umarah b. Ghaziyyah, from Rabi'ah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[6193,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ, and when he had finished his need, he went to the side of the mosque and urinated in it. The people shouted at him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ held the people back from him. Then he ordered a bucket of water and it was poured over his urine."],[6194,"Shall I not tell you of the best houses of the Ansar? We said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The best houses of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar.\" We said, \"Then which?\" He said, \"Then the houses of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the houses of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu Sa'idah.\" Then he made a gesture with his hand, moving it over them, and said, \"All the houses of the Ansar are good.\""],[6195,"He forbade al-muhaqalah – I think he said: and al-muzabanah – and he allowed al-ʿarāyā."],[6196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never shook hands with anyone and then parted from him until the man was the one who parted from him."],[6197,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain."],[6198,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[6199,"O God, give us water."],[6200,"I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter than the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6201,"In every house of the Ansar there is good."],[6202,"There were not twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6203,"Envy consumes good deeds as fire consumes firewood; charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire; prayer is the light of the believer; fasting is a shield from the Fire."],[6204,"Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ to invite him to a khazirah. I came to him while he was with his companions. When I drew near to him, he said: Did Abu Talhah invite us? I said: Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and those of his companions who were with him stood up. Then food was brought, and he invoked blessing upon it. He said: Call a group for me. So he called ten or so, and they ate from it until they were full, then they left. Then another ten entered and ate until they were full. Those with the Prophet ﷺ ate until they were full. I looked at what remained, and it was as it was before. He said: You have this, so satisfy your needs from it."],[6205,"This community will split into seventy-some sects. I know the most guided of them. They said: What is it, O Messenger of God? He said: The Jamāʿah."],[6206,"O assembly of the Ansar, your appointment is at my ḥawḍ. Its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky – or like the number of the stars of the sky – and its width is as the distance between me and Ṣanʿāʾ, or as the distance between me and ʿUmān."],[6207,"The Hour will not be established until time becomes shortened, so that a year is like a month, a month is like a week, a week is like a day, a day is like an hour, and an hour is like the burning of a firebrand."],[6208,"Whoever sees a person afflicted [with a calamity] and says: 'Praise be to Allah who has kept me safe from that which He has afflicted you with'—he will be protected from that affliction."],[6209,"'Abd Allah b. Shabib narrated to us: Mutarrif b. 'Abd Allah and Ishaq al-Farawi narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar narrated to us, from 'Abd Rabbihi b. Sa'id, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. We do not know of 'Abd Rabbihi having a chain of transmission from Anas except this hadith."],[6210,"The rewards of my community were shown to me, even [the reward for] a speck that a man removes from the mosque. And the sins of my community were shown to me, and I did not see a sin greater than [that of] a surah of the Qur'an, or a verse of the Qur'an—I think he said—which he learned and then forgot."],[6211,"A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'Love of Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'Then you will be with those whom you love.'"],[6212,"Three [qualities], if they are present in a person, he has tasted the sweetness of faith: that there is nothing more beloved to him than Allah and His Messenger; that being burned in the Fire is more beloved to him than abandoning his religion; and that he loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah."],[6213,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I love you.' He said: 'Then prepare yourself for poverty.'"],[6214,"Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: 'Intercede.' He will say: 'I am not the one for that. Go to Noah, for he is the first of the prophets and the greatest of them.' Then Noah will be brought and he will say: 'I am not your one. Go to Abraham, for Allah took him as an intimate friend.' Then Abraham will be brought and he will say: 'I am not your one. Go to Moses, for Allah spoke to him directly.' He said: Then Moses will be brought and he will say: 'I am not your one. Go to Jesus, for he is the spirit of Allah and His word.' He said: Then Jesus will be brought and he will say: 'I am not your one, but I will guide you to your one: go to Muhammad ﷺ.' He said: Then I will be brought, and I will ask permission, and when I look at the Most Merciful I will fall prostrate before Him, and I will remain—or he said: I will stay—as long as Allah wills. Then it will be said: 'Raise your head; speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and say: 'O Lord, my community.' Then it will be said: 'Go—or go forth—and do not leave anyone in whose heart there is a dinar's weight of faith, so that by that as many as Allah wills will come out.' Then I will fall prostrate a second time and remain as long as Allah wills. Then it will be said: 'Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and say: 'O Lord, my community.' Then it will be said: 'Go forth and do not leave in the Fire anyone in whose heart there is half a dinar's weight of faith except that you bring him out.' He said: Then by that as many as Allah wills will come out. Then I will fall prostrate a third time and remain as long as Allah wills. Then it will be said: 'Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and say: 'O Lord, my community.' Then it will be said: 'Go forth and do not leave in the Fire anyone in whose heart there is a grain's weight of faith except that you bring him out.' Then by that as many as Allah wills will come out, and none will remain except those in whom there is no good."],[6215,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not one who reviled others, nor cursed, nor was obscene. When he reproached one of us, he would say: 'What is the matter with him? May his forehead be rubbed in dust.'"],[6216,"We attended the funeral of a daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting by the grave. He said: I saw his eyes shedding tears. He said: Then he said: 'Is there among you a man who has not had intimate relations tonight?' Abu Talha said: 'I.' He said: 'Then descend [into the grave].'"],[6217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to our house, and with him were Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and some people from the Bedouins. I milked a sheep for them, then water from our well was poured over it, and he drank, with Abu Bakr on his left, 'Umar facing him, and the Bedouins on his right. So 'Umar wanted [to pass it to] Abu Bakr, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed it to the Bedouin and said: 'Those on the right, those on the right.'"],[6218,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over other women is like the excellence of tharid over other food—or over all other food."],[6219,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ supplicate and seek refuge with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from anxiety, grief, incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the burden of debt, and being overpowered by men."],[6220,"Ali b. Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated it to us: al-Husayn b. Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar b. Fulful, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[6221,"Nasr b. Ali narrated it to us: al-Mu'tamir reported to us, from his father, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a report similar to the hadith of Amr b. Abi Amr, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ. Amr b. Abi Amr is from the people of Madinah, al-Mukhtar b. Fulful is from the people of Kufa, and Sulayman Abu al-Mu'tamir is from the people of Basra. We have combined them only so that we do not repeat the hadith of each man when their wording is the same."],[6222,"I am not of idle play, nor is idle play of me."],[6223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared sacred what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah."],[6224,"Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."],[6225,"A man entered the mosque looking for a lost camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: May you not find it."],[6226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us, saying: Say: O Allah, we seek refuge with You from anxiety, grief, incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the burden of debt, and being overpowered by the children of Adam."],[6227,"and being overpowered by men."],[6228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on his she-camel al-Adba', which was not al-Jad'a', and said: O people, it is as if death in this world has been decreed for others besides us, and as if the truth in it has become binding upon others besides us, and as if the dead we escort are travelers who will return to us after a short while. We settle them in their graves and consume their inheritance, as if you will live forever after them. You have forgotten every admonition and felt secure from every calamity. Glad tidings to the one whose own fault distracts him from the faults of others, who humbles himself before Allah without any deficiency, who spends from wealth he gathered without disobedience, who mixes with people of understanding and avoids people of doubt and innovation, whose outward conduct is sound, and who keeps people safe from his evil."],[6229,"Another weak version: Aban b. Abi Ayyash narrated it from Anas. Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz b. Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Aban."],[6230,"We prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah the noon prayer as four rak'ahs, and at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs."],[6231,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and he prayed 'Asr at al-'Aqiq as two rak'ahs."],[6232,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and he prayed 'Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs, then he spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah until morning. When morning came, he mounted his she-camel, and when his riding beast stood upright, he entered ihram."],[6233,"The Prophet of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr with us in Madinah ..."],[6234,"There is no being an orphan after puberty."],[6235,"Make the Fajr prayer at a time when it is light, for that is greater in reward—or greater in your reward."],[6236,"We arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a companion of ours entered to relieve himself. He picked up a mud brick to clean himself with, and it crumbled into gold dust over him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Weigh it.' It was two hundred dirhams. He said: 'This is rikaz, and on it is one-fifth.'"],[6237,"Al-Hasan b. 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Jarawi and Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, saying: Bishr b. Bakr narrated to us, from Sa'id b. 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Anas."],[6238,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: 'Have you married?' He said: 'I do not have the means to marry.' He said: 'Do you not have \"Say: He is God, the One\"?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'It is a quarter of the Qur'an.' He said: 'Do you not have \"When God's help and victory comes\"?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'It is a quarter of the Qur'an.' He said: 'Do you not have \"Say: O disbelievers\"?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'It is a quarter of the Qur'an. Do you not have \"God—there is no god but He, the Living, the Self-Subsisting\"?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'It is a quarter of the Qur'an. Marry, marry.'"],[6239,"\"Say: O disbelievers\" is equal to a quarter of the Qur'an."],[6240,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Which supplication is best?' He said: 'Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being.' Then he came to him on the second day and said: 'Which supplication is best?' He said: 'Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.' Then he came to him on the third day and said: 'Which supplication is best?' He said: 'Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter, for if you are granted pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter, you will have succeeded.'"],[6241,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and no one followed him except 'Umar. He followed him with a clay vessel of water. He found him prostrating, so he withdrew from him until the Prophet ﷺ raised his head. Then he said: 'You did well, O 'Umar, when you withdrew from me. Gabriel came to me and said: Whoever sends one blessing upon you, God will send ten blessings upon him, and ten degrees will be raised for him.' I think he said: 'ten degrees.'"],[6242,"He said: 'Who is fasting today?' 'Umar said: 'I am.' He said: 'Who has visited a sick person?' 'Umar said: 'I have.' He said: 'Who has attended a funeral?' 'Umar said: 'I have.' He said: 'It is guaranteed, it is guaranteed.'"],[6243,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended a step of the pulpit and said: Amin. Then he ascended another step and said: Amin. Then he ascended the third and said: Amin. Then he sat down. He said: They asked him: For what did you say Amin, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril came to me and said: May the nose of a person be rubbed in dust, before whom you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you. I said: Amin. And may the nose of a person be rubbed in dust, who reaches one of his parents or both of them and does not enter Paradise. I said: Amin. And may the nose of a person be rubbed in dust, who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven. I said: Amin."],[6244,"Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday between the afternoon prayer and sunset."],[6245,"A place of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and all that is in it."],[6246,"I saw the cloak of Ukaydir when it was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Muslims began to marvel at it. He said: Do you marvel at this? By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."],[6247,"And narrated to us Yusuf b. Hammad: narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from 'Asim b. 'Umar, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6248,"We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ - I think he said the afternoon prayer - then a person would go to such and such a place while the sun was still as it was, unchanged."],[6249,"We left the noon prayer and went to Anas b. Malik with Kharijah b. Zayd. He said to the slave girl: Check whether the time for prayer has come."],[6250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell from a horse and injured his right side, so they entered upon him to visit him. He prayed with them sitting while they stood. He gestured to them to sit, so they sat. When he finished his prayer, he said: The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' say, 'Our Lord, to You belongs praise'; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he prays standing, pray standing; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you."],[6251,"6261 6259 - And narrated to us Muqaddam b. Muhammad: narrated to us my uncle Yahya b. 'Ali b. Muqaddam: narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Umar"],[6252,"6262 6260 - And narrated to us Muhammad b. Ma'mar: narrated to us Rawh: narrated to us Malik b. Anas"],[6253,"And narrated to us Ahmad b. Aban and Khalid b. Yusuf, they said: narrated to us Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah:"],[6254,"And narrated to us Muhammad Miskin: narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah b. Yusuf: narrated to me al-Layth b. Sa'd"],[6255,"And Muhammad b. Miskīn narrated it to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Ibn al-Hād and Yūnus narrated to me."],[6256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell from a horse."],[6257,"The last look I had of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the day he passed away. I looked at his face and it was like a page of the muṣḥaf. He drew back the curtain and gestured to the people, while the people were in rows behind Abū Bakr. He gestured to them to remain, then let the curtain fall. He passed away at the end of that day ﷺ."],[6258,"While the Muslims were in the dawn prayer on Monday, with Abū Bakr leading them, nothing startled them except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who had drawn back the curtain of ʿĀʾishah's room and looked at them while they were in the rows of prayer. Then he smiled and laughed. They thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to come out, so much so that they almost fell into temptation during their prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand, meaning: Complete your prayer. Then he entered the room and let the curtain down between him and them. That was the last I saw of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on that day."],[6259,"On Monday, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain of the room while Abū Bakr was leading the people in prayer. I looked at his face and it was like a page of the muṣḥaf, and he was smiling. We almost fell into temptation in our prayer out of joy at seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū Bakr wanted to step back, but he gestured to him: Stay as you are. Then he let the curtain fall, and he passed away on that day."],[6260,"And Bishr b. Khālid al-ʿAskarī and ʿUbayd b. Bakhīt narrated it to us. They said: Saʿīd b. Maslamah narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl b. Umayyah, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us in our house, so we milked a domestic sheep for him and mixed it with water from the well of the house. Abū Bakr was on his left, a Bedouin on his right, and ʿUmar to one side. The Prophet ﷺ drank, and ʿUmar said: Hand it to Abū Bakr. But he handed it to the Bedouin and said: The right, then the right."],[6262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank milk, with Abū Bakr on his left and a Bedouin on his right. He handed the leftover to the Bedouin and said: The right, then the right."],[6263,"6273 6271 - And Muḥammad b. al-Muthannā narrated to us: Bishr b. ʿUmar narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6264,"6274 6272 - And Muḥammad b. Miskīn narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us: Yūnus narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah."],[6265,"Muḥammad b. Maʿmar narrated it to us: Rawḥ narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj and Mālik b. Anas and Zakariyyā b. Isḥāq and Ṣāliḥ b. Abī al-Khaḍir and Muḥammad b. Abī Ḥafṣah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6266,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is called, begin with the evening meal."],[6267,"And it was narrated to us by Abd Allah b. Shabib: Ayyub b. Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Abi Uways, from Sulayman b. Bilal, from Yahya b. Saʿid al-Ansari, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[6268,"When the evening meal is brought, begin with the meal before you pray the Maghrib prayer. I think he said: And do not rush away from your dinner."],[6269,"When the evening meal is brought, begin with the meal before the Maghrib prayer."],[6270,"When the evening meal is brought and the prayer is present, begin with it before you pray the Maghrib prayer."],[6271,"Do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another; be, O servants of God, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[6272,"6282 6280 - And it was narrated to us by Muhammad b. Maʿmar: Rawh b. ʿUbadah narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[6273,"And it was narrated to us by Muhammad b. Miskin: Abd Allah b. Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah."],[6274,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[6275,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Hour. He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He mentioned that he had not prepared much action for it except that he said: 'I love God and His Messenger.' He said: 'You will be with those whom you love.'"],[6276,"A Bedouin confronted the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, when is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'I have not prepared much good for it except that I love God and His Messenger.' He said: 'Then you will be with those whom you love.'"],[6277,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade soaking (nabidh) in gourds and in vessels smeared with pitch."],[6278,"6288 6286 - And it was narrated to us by Muhammad b. al-Muthanna: Abd al-Aʿla narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[6279,"Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us: Sulayman b. Kathir narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."],[6280,"Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us: 'Abdullah b. Salih and 'Abd b. Yusuf narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab:"],[6281,"Do not make nabidh in gourds or in vessels smeared with pitch."],[6282,"The Prophet ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah with a helmet on his head. It was said to him, \"Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah.\" He said, \"Kill him.\""],[6283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest with a helmet on his head."],[6284,"We used to pray 'Asr, then a person would go to Quba' while the sun was still high."],[6285,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would leave while the sun was still high, and a person would go to al-'Awali while the sun was still like that."],[6286,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with dates and sawiq."],[6287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old. My mothers used to urge me to treat him kindly."],[6288,"He was ten years old when the Prophet ﷺ arrived. He said: My mothers used to keep me constant in serving the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah for ten years, and he died when I was twenty years old."],[6289,"The best act of worship is awaiting relief from Allah."],[6290,"Salamah b. Shabib and Zuhayr b. Muhammad narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."],[6291,"al-Hasan b. Ali was the one among them most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ in face."],[6292,"He used to recite quietly in the prayer."],[6293,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah during the Umrah of al-Qada, with Abd Allah b. Rawahah holding his saddle-girth and reciting rajaz: \"Clear the way, sons of the disbelievers, from his path. The Most Merciful has sent down in His revelation that the best killing is in His path.\""],[6294,"Some people from the Ansar on the day of Hunayn said, when God, Mighty and Majestic, granted His Messenger the spoils of Hawazin, and the Messenger of God ﷺ began giving men from Quraysh a hundred camels each, they said: \"May God forgive the Messenger of God; he gives to Quraysh and leaves us while our swords are dripping with their blood.\" Anas said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was told of their statement, so he sent for the Ansar and gathered them in a leather tent, and no one else was called with them. When they had gathered, the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and said: \"What is this talk that has reached me from you?\" The Ansar said: \"Those of us with sound judgment said nothing, but some young men among us said such-and-such,\" referring to this statement. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I give to men whose hearts I seek to win over, while you depart with the Messenger of God ﷺ to your dwellings. By God, what you depart with is better than what they depart with.\" They said: \"Indeed, O Messenger of God.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You will find, or you will see, after me severe selfishness, so be patient until you meet God and His Messenger, for I will precede you at the Pond.\" Anas said: We did not endure patiently."],[6295,"Umar b. al-Khattab narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas by a group; we confined ourselves to those we have named among them."],[6296,"Fifty prayers were made obligatory upon the Prophet ﷺ, then they were reduced until they were made five. Then it was proclaimed: \"O Muhammad, the word with Me is not changed, and indeed for you with these five are fifty.\""],[6297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out when the sun had declined and prayed Zuhr."],[6298,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cauterized Asad b. Zurarah on his median cubital vein."],[6299,"Muhammad b. Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us; Amr b. Khalid narrated to us; Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Uqayl that he heard Ibn Shihab reporting, from Anas b. Malik."],[6300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said one day to his companions: \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter from here.\" Ma'mar said in his hadith: \"His beard dripping water from the ablution he had performed, carrying his sandals.\" Then Sa'd entered. He said that twice, and each time Sa'd came. When Abd Allah b. Amr heard that, he went with him that night and said: \"O uncle, there was some talk between me and Amr, so I wanted to spend the night with you.\" He said: \"Yes, O son of my brother.\" So Abd Allah spent the night with him, and Sa'd slept. When he woke during the night, he remembered God. When morning came, he got up, performed ablution, prayed two rak'ahs, and then went out to the prayer. He did that for three nights, not adding anything to it. When morning came on the third day, Abd Allah said to him: \"By God, there was nothing between me and Amr except good, but I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you: 'A man from the people of Paradise will enter,' so I wanted to know what your deed was.\" Sa'd said to him: \"It is only what you have seen, O son of my brother, except that I do not spend the night bearing malice toward any Muslim,\" or words to that effect."],[6301,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to recite: \"Maliki yawmi al-din.\""],[6302,"O God, place in it twice the blessing You placed in Makkah."],[6303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ acquired a ring of silver, its stone was Abyssinian, and he placed its stone toward the inside of his palm."],[6304,"The Prophet ﷺ acquired a ring of silver, its stone was Abyssinian, and it was engraved: Muhammad is the Messenger of God."],[6305,"Muhammad b. Uqbah narrated it to us; Umar b. Harun al-Balkhi narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. This hadith, only Yunus mentioned: its stone was Abyssinian. We do not know anyone other than him who said: its stone was Abyssinian."],[6306,"He used to walk in front of the funeral procession, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[6307,"When the land is fertile, give—I think he said: the animals—their share of the pasture. When the land is barren, proceed through it with their lean condition. And upon you is traveling by night, for the earth is folded up during the night."],[6308,"Whoever loves that his provision be expanded for him and his life be prolonged, let him maintain ties of kinship."],[6309,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wore a ring on his right hand."],[6310,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding what is made in receptacles coated with pitch and in gourds. And every intoxicant is unlawful."],[6311,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[6312,"Whoever sleeps through a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it."],[6313,"When it was Monday—the day on which the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away—and the door was opened, the Messenger of God ﷺ came out until he stood at the door of Aisha ؓ. The Muslims almost became entranced with joy at seeing the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they dispersed. He gestured to them: remain in your prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled with delight at what he saw of their state in their prayer. I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ more beautiful in appearance than he was at that hour. Then he returned, and the people departed thinking that the Messenger of God ﷺ had recovered from his illness. Abu Bakr went back to his family."],[6314,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his voice in talbiyah for Umrah and Hajj."],[6315,"The Prophet ﷺ acquired a gold ring, and the people acquired rings. One day he threw it away, and the people threw away their rings. Then he never wore it again."],[6316,"He saw on the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a silver ring for just one day. Then the people crafted rings and wore them, so the Prophet ﷺ discarded his ring, and the people discarded their rings."],[6317,"6327 6325 - Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Salih narrated to us, al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us, 'Uqayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."],[6318,"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another valley, and nothing fills his mouth except dust. Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[6319,"I am the most knowledgeable of people about the matter of the veil when it was revealed. The first of what was revealed concerning the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was when he consummated his marriage with Zaynab bt. Jahsh. The Prophet ﷺ awoke as a bridegroom and invited the people. They had the food, then they left, but a group of them remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prolonged their stay. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and went out, and I went out with him, but they did not leave. He walked, and I walked with him until he came to 'A'ishah's room, thinking that they had left. He returned, and I returned with him, and there they were, having left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a curtain between me and him, and the veil was revealed."],[6320,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to combine two prayers – meaning in travel – he delayed Zuhr until the time of 'Asr entered, then combined them. And when he wanted to combine Maghrib and 'Isha, he delayed Maghrib until the time of 'Isha entered, then combined them."],[6321,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out before the sun declined, he delayed Zuhr until the time of 'Asr, then he dismounted and combined them. If the sun had declined before he set out, he prayed Zuhr and then mounted."],[6322,"He forbade a man to sell the stud service of his horse."],[6323,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was born from his slave woman Mariyah, something arose in the Prophet's ﷺ heart about him, until Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: 'Peace be upon you, Abu Ibrahim.'"],[6324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[6325,"The Prophet of Allah Ayyub ﷺ remained in his affliction for eighteen years. Near and far relatives shunned him except two men among his brothers who were among his most intimate companions. They would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion: 'By Allah, you know he has committed a sin that no one in all the worlds has committed.' His companion said: 'What is that?' He said: 'For eighteen years he has been afflicted and Allah has not shown him mercy by removing what he has. When he saw his condition, the man could not keep it to himself and mentioned that to him. Ayyub said: 'I do not know what you are saying, except that Allah knows from me that I used to pass by two men disputing, and they would mention Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, and I would return to my house and make atonement for them, disliking that they should mention Allah except in truth.' He used to go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would take him by the hand until he reached home. One day she was delayed for him, and it was revealed to Ayyub in his place: 'Strike the ground with your foot; this is a cool bathing place and a drink.' He said: 'She thought he was delayed, so she went looking for him. He came toward her, and Allah had removed the affliction he had, and he was the most handsome he had ever been. When she saw him, she said: 'May Allah bless you! Have you seen Allah's Prophet ﷺ, this afflicted one? By Allah, I have seen no one more like him than you when he was healthy.' He said: 'I am he.' He said: He had two threshing floors: one for wheat and one for barley. Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, sent two clouds. When one of them was over the wheat floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed. The other poured silver into the barley floor until it overflowed.'"],[6326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank milk while standing. On his right was a bedouin, and on his left was Abu Bakr. He gave the bedouin the remaining milk and said: 'The right, then the right.'"],[6327,"The Prophet ﷺ drank milk while standing."],[6328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent when he was forty years old. He remained in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he passed away when he was sixty years old, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."],[6329,"In my Basin there are as many pitchers as the number of stars in the sky."],[6330,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, continued to send revelation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the revelation was most frequent on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away."],[6331,"Most of the people of Paradise are the simple-minded."],[6332,"The Prophet ﷺ recited it: \"and the eye for the eye.\""],[6333,"If a believer were in a lizard's hole, Allah would send someone to harm him therein, or he said: a hypocrite to harm him."],[6334,"No servant who lives forty years in Islam but that Allah turns away from him various kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty years, Allah makes his reckoning easy. When he reaches sixty years, Allah grants him turning to Him with what He loves. When he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the people of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, Allah accepts his good deeds and overlooks his bad deeds. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives his past and future sins, and he is called the prisoner of Allah on His earth, and he is granted intercession for his household."],[6335,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hisham b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."],[6336,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6337,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna and Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Rawh b. 'Ubada narrated to us, Usama b. Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."],[6338,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: But Hamza has no weepers. This reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, then woke up while they were weeping. He said: Woe to them! They have been weeping since today? Let them stop, and let them not weep for any dead after today."],[6339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Hamza on the day of Uhud and stood over him, and saw that he had been mutilated. He said: 'Were it not that Safiyya would feel grieved, I would leave him until the wild beasts and birds devour him in their bellies.' Then he called for a striped cloak and shrouded him in it. When it was stretched over his feet, his head was uncovered; and when it was stretched over his head, his feet appeared. He said: The slain were many and the garments were few. He said: Two or three men were shrouded in a single garment, and then buried in one grave. The Messenger of God ﷺ began asking about them: 'Which of them knew more of the Qur'an?' and he would place him first toward the qibla. The Messenger of God ﷺ buried them without praying over them."],[6340,"I do not know it except from al-Zuhri, from Anas."],[6341,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a ring made, and when he entered the privy he removed his ring."],[6342,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband."],[6343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ drank milk and rinsed his mouth, and said: 'It has fat in it.'"],[6344,"Ahmad b. al-Miqdam and Muhammad b. Yahya narrated to us – and the wording is Muhammad's – both said: Muhammad b. Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."],[6345,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah while it was extremely hot, and entered the mosque while the people were praying seated. He said: 'The prayer of one seated is half the prayer of one standing.' So the people forced themselves to pray standing."],[6346,"I saw us selling the mothers of the children while the Messenger of God ﷺ was among us."],[6347,"The example of a sick person when he recovers and becomes healthy from his illness is like a hailstone falling from the sky in its purity and color."],[6348,"(M) - Harun b. Abi 'Alqama al-Farawi wrote to me, informing that Muhammad b. Fulayh narrated to him from Musa b. 'Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."],[6349,"6359 6356 - And Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad b. Fulayh narrated to us, Musa b. 'Uqba narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."],[6350,"The Ansar asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, permit us to forgo the ransom of our nephew al-'Abbas.' He said: 'No, not even a dirham.'"],[6351,"That some people from ʿUraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent them with his camels. They killed the shepherd and drove off the camels. The Prophet ﷺ cut off their hands and feet."],[6352,"ʿAbd Allah b. Ubayy had a slave girl called Muʿādhah whom he compelled to fornicate. When Islam came, it was revealed: 'And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution... to His saying: then indeed, Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful.'"],[6353,"I used to pour the water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's ablution for all his wives, or he said: water for his bath for all his wives."],[6354,"That a man was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when his son came, so he kissed him and seated him on his thigh. Then his daughter came, and he seated her in front of him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Will you not treat them equally?'"],[6355,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik in his tent during the caliphate of ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān, and he was distressed. I said: 'I hope that Allah has only kept you back so that you may be a witness over this ummah.' He said: 'They have begun and ended their day opposing those before them, except that they pray, and in prayer there is delay.'"],[6356,"The last look I had of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was when he fell ill and ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted the curtain of ʿĀʾishah's room while the people were looking, and I saw his face as if it were a page of a muṣḥaf, until Abu Bakr stepped back on his heels, thinking that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to lead the people in prayer. He signaled to them to complete their prayer, and he let down the curtain between them and him. He passed away that same day ﷺ."],[6357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell from a horse and injured his right side, so he prayed with them sitting. When he finished, he said: 'The imam is only appointed to be followed. If he prays standing, pray standing; if he bows, bow; if he rises, rise; if he prostrates, prostrate; and if he says: Allah hears the one who praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You be praise. And if he prays sitting, then all of you pray sitting.'"],[6358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl with five makākī (of water) and perform ablution with one makkūk."],[6359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl, he and some of his wives, from a single vessel."],[6360,"A sign of the hypocrite is hatred of the Anṣār, and a sign of faith is love of the Anṣār."],[6361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah: 'What prevents you from listening to what I enjoin upon you: that you say when you enter morning and evening: O Ever-Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek help; set right for me all my affairs, and do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye.'"],[6362,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a drink while Abu Bakr was on his left, a bedouin on his right, and ʿUmar facing him. He drank, then ʿUmar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Bakr,' indicating his place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Those on the right,' and gave it to the bedouin."],[6363,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from dyeing himself with saffron."],[6364,"He forbade dyeing with saffron."],[6365,"The supplication the Prophet ﷺ made most often was: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[6366,"Qatadah asked Anas: Which supplication did the Prophet ﷺ make most often? He said: The supplication he made most often was: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[6367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Khaybar. We prayed the dawn prayer near it in the dark. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted his riding animal, and Abu Talhah mounted, and I rode behind Abu Talhah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode through the lanes of Khaybar until his thigh was exposed, so that I saw the whiteness of the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he entered the village, he said: Allah is Greatest. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned - he said it three times. The people came out to their work and said: Muhammad and the army (al-khamis), and al-khamis means the army. We conquered it, and the captives were gathered. Dihyah came and said: O Prophet of Allah, give me a girl from the captives. He said: Go and take a girl. He went and took Safiyyah bint Huyayy. A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave Dihyah Safiyyah bint Huyayy, the mistress of Qurayzah and al-Nadir. She is only suitable for you. He said: Call him to bring her. He came with her. When the Prophet ﷺ looked at her, he said: Take another girl from the captives. He said: The Prophet ﷺ freed her and married her. I said: O Abu Hamzah, what did he give her as her dower? He said: She herself; he freed her and married her. When he was on the road, Umm Sulaym prepared her for him at night, and in the morning the Prophet ﷺ was a bridegroom. He said: Whoever has something, let him bring it to me. He spread a leather mat. A man would bring dried curd, another would bring dates, another would bring clarified butter, and another would bring barley meal, until they made a dish of mixed dates and butter (hays). That was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6368,"None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must wish for it, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me."],[6369,"When one of you supplicates, let him be resolute in supplication and not say: O Allah, if You will, give me, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, cannot be compelled."],[6370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would delay the prayer and complete it."],[6371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a ring made and said: I have had a ring made and engraved an inscription on it, so let no one engrave like it."],[6372,"The prayer was called, and a man approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need, so he did not stand for the prayer until the people slept."],[6373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice two rams."],[6374,"A funeral procession passed and good was said of the deceased. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: It is due, it is due, it is due. Another funeral procession passed and evil was said of the deceased, and he ﷺ said: It is due, it is due, it is due. Umar said: May my father and mother be your ransom. A funeral passed and good was said, and you said: It is due. A funeral passed and evil was said, and you said: It is due? He said: The one of whom you spoke good, Paradise is due for him, and the one of whom you spoke evil, the Fire is due for him. You are Allah's witnesses on earth."],[6375,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the privy, he would say: O God, I seek refuge with You from male and female devils."],[6376,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[6377,"Muʿādh b. Jabal used to lead his people in prayer. Ḥarām entered while he wanted to water his palm trees, so he entered the mosque to pray with the people. When he saw Muʿādh—I think he had lengthened the prayer—he shortened his prayer and went to his palm trees to water them. When Muʿādh finished the prayer, or completed it, it was said to him: So-and-so entered the mosque, and when he saw you lengthen the prayer, he shortened his prayer and went to his palm trees to water them. Then Ḥarām came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while Muʿādh was with him and said: O Prophet of God, I wanted to water my palm trees, so I entered the mosque to pray with the people. When he lengthened the prayer, I shortened my prayer and went to my palm trees to water them. He claims that I am a hypocrite. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to Muʿādh and said: Are you a source of temptation? Are you a source of temptation? Do not lengthen the prayer with them. Recite: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” “By the sun and its morning brightness,” and the like."],[6378,"Three things will persist in my community until the Hour begins: wailing, boasting about lineage, and attributing rain to the stars."],[6379,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for ten years, and he never said to me about anything I did, “Why did you do it?” nor about anything I did not do, “Why did you not do it?” or the like. And I never touched silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6380,"Whoever has three children die before reaching puberty, God will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them."],[6381,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man from dyeing his skin with saffron."],[6382,"He would breathe three times in the vessel."],[6383,"When a person supplicates for his brother in his absence, the angels say: Amen, and for you the like of it."],[6384,"The prophets are alive, praying in their graves."],[6385,"One who is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[6386,"No two Muslims meet with their swords but that both the killer and the killed are in the Fire."],[6387,"Hasten to [good] deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast, the private affair of one of you, and the affair of the general public."],[6388,"Time will only increase in severity, and people will only increase in miserliness, and the Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."],[6389,"He said to his companions: 'Indeed the world is sweet and green. Indeed Allah is making you successors in it, so He is watching how you act. So beware of the world and beware of women.'"],[6390,"There will be in my nation sinking into the earth, metamorphosis, and pelting with stones."],[6391,"Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning: they are those who do not cauterize, nor do they ask others to cauterize them, nor do they seek ruqyah, nor do they believe in bad omens, and upon their Lord they rely."],[6392,"He said to his companions: 'Let me not find any of you returning after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.'"],[6393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ — I think he said — used to command lightening the prayer."],[6394,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[6395,"Muhammad b. Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hisham b. Hassan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[6396,"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."],[6397,"He sacrificed two rams. Anas said: 'And I sacrifice two rams.'"],[6398,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and they praised it with good, so he said: 'It has become incumbent.' Then another funeral procession passed by and they praised it with evil, so he said: 'It has become incumbent.' 'Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you said for the first: It has become incumbent, and you said for the other: It has become incumbent?' He said: 'As for the first, Paradise became incumbent for him, and as for the other, the Fire became incumbent for him. You are Allah's witnesses on earth.'"],[6399,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hold a wedding feast for any of his wives more than the one he held for Zaynab, for he fed them bread and meat until they were full."],[6400,"The prayer was commenced—I think he said: He stood talking to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until his companions, or some of his companions, slept, then he stood and prayed."],[6401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Safiyyah and gave her a dower. I said: What did he give her as a dower? He said: Her freedom, and he married her."],[6402,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to the privy, he would say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."],[6403,"The Prophet ﷺ had curly hair that came down to his shoulders."],[6404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would make it brief yet complete—meaning the prayer."],[6405,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6406,"I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and I do not say this out of pride. I am the first for whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, and I do not say this out of pride. I am the first to enter Paradise, and I do not say this out of pride. I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession will be accepted. In my hand is the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection; Adam and all those beneath him are under my banner. Then I will come to my Lord, blessed and exalted be He, and it will be said to me: Who is it? I will say: Ahmad. Then it will be opened for me, and when I see my Lord, mighty and majestic be He, I will fall down in prostration before Him. I will praise Him with praises that no one before me or after me has used, which Allah, blessed and exalted be He, will inspire in me."],[6407,"The Dajjal will come until he encamps in a district of Madinah, and Madinah will quake with three tremors, after which every hypocrite will go out to him."],[6408,"Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to come to her house and pray in it, so that she could adopt it as a place of prayer. One day she went to a mat of theirs and sprinkled it with water, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed, and they prayed with him."],[6409,"Seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan—or of the Jewry of Isfahan—will follow the Dajjal, wearing cloaks."],[6410,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque wearing a thick Najrani cloak with a border, when a Bedouin came up from behind him, grabbed the two sides of the garment, and pulled it so hard that the border left marks on the side of the neck of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Bedouin said to him: Give us some of the wealth of Allah that He has given you. He ﷺ turned to him, smiled, and said: Order that he be given something, or: Give him something."],[6411,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, a woman sees what a man sees in a dream?\" Umm Salamah said: \"You have disgraced women, O Umm Sulaym.\" He said: \"If she sees that, let her perform ghusl.\" Umm Salamah said: \"Do women have any water?\" He said: \"Yes, they are but the counterparts of men.\""],[6412,"I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of God ﷺ, yet complete."],[6413,"The Dajjal will tread every land except Makkah and Madinah. As for Madinah, the angels—I think he said—over it, or they will prevent him from it, and it will quake three times, so no disbeliever or hypocrite will remain but he will come out to him."],[6414,"Abu Talhah used to shoot in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ and say: \"May my soul be a ransom for your soul, and my face a shield for your face.\""],[6415,"Umm Sulaym had an orphan girl. The Messenger of God ﷺ saw the orphan girl and said: \"You have grown up; may your age not increase.\" The orphan girl returned to Umm Sulaym crying. Umm Sulaym said: \"What is the matter with you, my dear daughter?\" She said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed against me that my age not increase.\" Umm Sulaym went out until she met the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"What is the matter with you, O Umm Sulaym?\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, you prayed against my orphan girl that her age not increase.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed, then said: \"O Umm Sulaym, do you not know my condition with my Lord, Mighty and Majestic? I made a condition with my Lord, and I said: I am only a human; I am pleased as humans are pleased and I become angry as humans become angry. Any person of my Ummah against whom I supplicate with a supplication that he does not deserve, then make it a purification, an increase, and a means of nearness by which You bring him near on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6416,"Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of God ﷺ having wrapped me in her head-cover and covered me with a face-veil. She said: \"O Messenger of God, this is Anas, my son. I have brought him to you so that you may supplicate for him.\" He said: \"O God, increase his wealth and his children.\" Anas said: \"By God, my wealth is indeed abundant and my children are so-and-so.\""],[6417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sought forgiveness for the Ansar, for the descendants of the Ansar, for the descendants of the descendants of the Ansar, and for the freed slaves of the Ansar."],[6418,"God is more intensely pleased with the repentance of His servant when he turns to Him than one of you would be who was on his mount, and it strayed from him while carrying his food and drink. He despaired of it, so he came to a tree and lay down in its shade, having given up on his mount. While he was in that state, suddenly the mount was standing before him. He took hold of its reins, and out of joy he said, out of overwhelming delight: \"You are my servant and I am your Lord,\" making a mistake due to intense joy."],[6419,"While we were in the mosque with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a Bedouin came and stood to urinate in the mosque. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to him, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not interrupt him.\" So they left him until he had urinated. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called him and said: \"These mosques are not suitable for any of this urine or filth; they are only for the remembrance of God, prayer, and recitation of the Quran.\" Then he said to a man from the group, and a man brought a bucket of water and poured it over the place."],[6420,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, we were in a land where our numbers were many and our wealth abundant, and we moved to a land—I think he said—where our numbers became few and our wealth became little.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave it, for it is blameworthy.\""],[6421,"And He sent down regarding them, meaning the companions of Bi'r Ma'unah, a Quranic passage: \"Convey to our people on our behalf that we have met our Lord and He is pleased with us and has made us pleased.\" Then it was abrogated and lifted, and was sent down: \"And do not consider those who were killed in the way of God as dead, but alive with their Lord, being provided for.\""],[6422,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to draw omens from names."],[6423,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought old dates, and he began to inspect them."],[6424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from coming to his family at night."],[6425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to enter upon any woman of the Ansar except upon Umm Sulaym. He said: 'I show compassion to her; her brother was killed alongside me.'"],[6426,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed an offense deserving a prescribed punishment, so carry it out on me.' He did not ask him about it. Then the prayer time came, and he prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed an offense deserving a prescribed punishment, so enforce upon me the Book of Allah.' He said: 'Did you not attend the prayer with us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then Allah has forgiven you.'"],[6427,"He forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhadarah."],[6428,"Whoever says: 'In the name of Allah; I rely upon Allah; there is no might and no power except with Allah,' it will be said: 'You are sufficed, protected, and the devil will distance himself from you.'"],[6429,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6430,"Aslam, Ghifar, and some men of Muzaynah and Juhaynah are better than the two allies Ghatafan and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah. Uyaynah b. Badr said: 'By Allah, to be among these in the Fire'—meaning Ghatafan and Banu Amir—'is dearer to me than to be with those in Paradise.'"],[6431,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why do you not marry among the Ansar?' He said: 'They have jealousy.'"],[6432,"Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with children, women, camels, and sheep, and arranged them in rows to outnumber the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Muslims and the polytheists met, and the Muslims turned their backs in flight, as Allah Almighty said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O slaves of Allah, I am the slave of Allah and His Messenger.' Then he said: 'O assembly of Ansar, I am the slave of Allah and His Messenger.' Then Allah defeated the polytheists, and he did not strike with a sword or thrust with a spear. The Prophet ﷺ said that day: 'Whoever kills an unbeliever, his spoils belong to him.' Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder strap, and he had a coat of mail, but I was too hurried to take it. See with whom it is.' A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I took it. Satisfy him with something from it and give it to me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent; he used not to be asked for something except that he gave it or remained silent. Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: 'Allah will not give it as spoils to one of His lions and then give it to you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: 'Umar spoke the truth.' Abu Talhah met Umm Sulaym, and she had a dagger. He said: 'O Umm Sulaym, what is this with you?' She said: 'By Allah, I intended that if one of them came near me, I would rip open his belly.' Abu Talhah informed the Prophet ﷺ of that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah has sufficed and been good.'"],[6433,"And I heard Sulayman b. Ubaydullah mention from Abu Dawud: Hammad b. Salamah and Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. We did not hear this hadith except from Sulayman, and he was truthful. I think Abu Dawud erred in the hadith of Hammad b. Salamah from Shu'bah, so he made a mistake in it, or Sulayman erred in it, and we found it in his book like this."],[6434,"The Prophet ﷺ was the most playful of people with a child."],[6435,"Four [things] are from wretchedness: dryness of the eye, hardness of the heart, prolonged hope, and greed for the world."],[6436,"Three [traits]—whoever has them deserves the reward and completes faith: a character by which he lives among people, piety that restrains him from what Allah has forbidden, and forbearance by which he repels the ignorance of the ignorant."],[6437,"A caller calls out: Leave the world to its people, leave the world to its people, leave the world to its people—three times. Whoever takes from the world more than what suffices him has taken a carcass while he does not perceive."],[6438,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and an orphan behind him, and our mother behind us."],[6439,"Differ from the Magians: trim the mustaches and leave the beards."],[6440,"The best gatherings are the most spacious."],[6441,"Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym to propose to her before he became Muslim. She said to him: Should I marry you while you worship a piece of wood carved by my servant so-and-so? If you become Muslim, I will marry you. He said: Then Abu Talhah became Muslim and married her upon his Islam."],[6442,"Perfume was never offered to the Prophet ﷺ but that he accepted it."],[6443,"Perfume was never offered to the Prophet ﷺ but that he accepted it."],[6444,"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted ones. So he enjoined good treatment of the Ansar: to accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers, for they have fulfilled what was upon them and what remains is what is owed to them."],[6445,"There was a camel belonging to some people of the Ansar which they used for drawing water. It became refractory and refused them its back. The Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we had a camel that we used for drawing water, and it became refractory and refused us its back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: Arise. So they arose with him, and he came to a garden while the camel was in a corner. It came walking toward him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it has become like a dog, and we fear for you from it—or we fear its attack upon you. He said: There is no harm to me from it. When the camel saw him, it came moving until it fell down prostrating before him. His companions said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a beast that does not reason, and we do reason. We are more deserving to prostrate to you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is not right for anything to prostrate to anything. Even if it were right for anything to prostrate to anything, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband because of the greatness of his right over her."],[6446,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he passed by a man standing in prayer. When the man finished the prayer and sat down, he recited the tashahhud and supplicated, saying: O Allah, I ask You by [the fact] that to You belongs praise; there is no god but You, the Bestower, O Possessor of majesty and honor. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do you know what he supplicated with? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He has supplicated by His greatest name, by which when He is called He answers, and when He is asked He gives."],[6447,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came to him and said: 'Peace be upon you and God's mercy.' The Prophet ﷺ replied: 'And upon you and God's mercy and His blessings.' When the man sat down, he said: 'Praise be to God, abundant, good, blessed praise, as our Lord loves to be praised.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'How did you say?' He repeated as he had said. He said: 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, ten angels rushed to it, wanting to write it down, but they did not know how to write it until they raised it to the Possessor of Majesty. He said: Write it as My servant said.'"],[6448,"There will be a people who pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game."],[6449,"He used to command marriage and strictly forbid celibacy, and he said: 'Marry the loving and fertile, for I will vie in numbers with the nations on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[6450,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to break his fast on the day of Eid al-Fitr with some dates, then go out."],[6451,"When Anas b. Malik wanted to combine two prayers during a journey, he would delay the noon prayer to the end of its time, then pray it, and pray the afternoon prayer at the beginning of its time; and he would pray the sunset prayer at the end of its time, and pray the evening prayer at the beginning of its time, and he would say: 'Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine two prayers during a journey.'"],[6452,"Many a disheveled, dusty person, to whom no attention is paid, if he swore by God, God would fulfill his oath."],[6453,"He forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets, and after the dawn prayer until the sun rises."],[6454,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[6455,"Three registers will be brought out for the son of Adam on the Day of Resurrection: a register containing his good deeds, a register containing his sins, and a register containing the blessings God bestowed upon him. God will say to the smallest blessing — I think he said: in the register of blessings — 'Take your price from his good deeds.' So his good deeds will be consumed. Then it is set aside and says: 'By Your might, I have not been fully repaid.' The sins and blessings remain, while all the good deeds are gone. If God wishes to have mercy on a servant, He says: 'My servant, I have multiplied your good deeds, and I have overlooked your evil deeds' — I think he said — 'and I have granted you My blessings.'"],[6456,"No two Muslims meet and one takes the hand of his companion except that it is incumbent upon God not to separate their hands until He forgives them."],[6457,"Whoever loves to have his life span extended and his provision increased, let him maintain his kinship ties."],[6458,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under God's protection."],[6459,"There is no Muslim servant who visits a brother of his for the sake of Allah, except that a caller from the sky calls out: 'You are pure, and Paradise is pure for you,' and unless Allah says in the dominion of His Throne: 'My servant visited for My sake, and upon Me is his hospitality.' Thus Allah is not pleased for him with any reward less than Paradise."],[6460,"There are no people who gather to remember Allah, seeking thereby nothing but His Face, except that a caller from the sky calls out: 'Arise, forgiven for you; your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.'"],[6461,"Whoever says after the prayer: 'Glory be to Allah, the Almighty, and with His praise; there is no might and no power except with Allah,' he rises forgiven."],[6462,"We entered upon Anas b. Malik and he recited Umm al-Kitab and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad, and he said: 'It is a third of the Quran,' from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6463,"The example of the righteous companion is like that of the perfume seller; if he does not give you some of his perfume, some of its fragrance will reach you."],[6464,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6465,"A son of al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam died, and he grieved over him. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, whoever has three children who die before reaching the age of sin, they will be a ransom for him from the Fire.'"],[6466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a kunya after a herb I used to gather."],[6467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O you with the two ears.'"],[6468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apply kohl an odd number of times."],[6469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a Jew seeking a loan until a time of ease. He said: 'Does he have any time of ease when he has no crop and no livestock?!' That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'The enemy of Allah has lied; indeed, I am the most faithful of them in repaying.'"],[6470,"I asked Anas about al-Safa and al-Marwa, and he said: 'They were among the rites of the Jahiliyyah. When Islam came, we refrained from them, and Allah revealed: \"Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go between them.\"'"],[6471,"I asked Anas about al-Safa and al-Marwa ..."],[6472,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment."],[6473,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the qunut, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut before the ruku'."],[6474,"Wine was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and their drink that day was only unripe dates and dry dates."],[6475,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."],[6476,"The prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of the individual, or the prayer of a man alone, by twenty-five prayers."],[6477,"Shall I not direct you to what Allah expiates sins with? Performing ablution thoroughly and taking many steps to the mosques."],[6478,"A people came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and among them was a man with a trace of khaluq on his hand. He continued to accept their pledge and delayed him, then said: The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and its color is hidden, and the perfume of women is that whose color is apparent and its scent is hidden."],[6479,"Praying between graves was forbidden."],[6480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between the Muhajirun and the Ansar in our house."],[6481,"He used to like gourd."],[6482,"The Jews used to keep away from women during menstruation, so they would not eat with them, nor drink with them, and they would turn them out of the houses ..."],[6483,"Three are expiations, and three are degrees, and three are deliverances, and three are destructive. As for the expiations: performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, waiting for the prayers after the prayers, and moving on foot to the Friday prayers. As for the degrees: feeding food, spreading peace, and praying at night while people are asleep. As for the deliverances: justice in anger and contentment, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of God in secret and in public. As for the destructive: obeyed miserliness, followed desire, and a person's admiration of himself."],[6484,"The five prayers and Friday to Friday are expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided. And indeed in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim, male or female, asks God for good but He gives it to him. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The likeness of the five prayers is that of a deep river at the door of one of you in which he bathes five times every day; what dirt would remain on him?"],[6485,"Wrongdoing is of three kinds: a wrongdoing that God does not forgive, a wrongdoing that He forgives, and a wrongdoing that God does not leave. As for the wrongdoing that God does not forgive, it is associating partners with Him; God said: 'Indeed, associating partners is a great wrongdoing.' As for the wrongdoing that God forgives, it is the wrongdoing of servants against themselves regarding their relationship with their Lord. As for the wrongdoing that God does not leave, it is the wrongdoing of servants against one another until some are repaid by others."],[6486,"Indeed, God has roaming bands of angels who seek out circles of remembrance. When they come upon them, they surround them, then they send their scout up to the heaven, to the Lord of Might, Blessed and Exalted. They say: 'Our Lord, we came upon servants of Your servants, who extol Your blessings, recite Your Book, invoke blessings upon Your Prophet ﷺ, and ask You for their hereafter and their worldly needs.' Then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'Cover them with My mercy.' They say: 'O Lord, among them is so-and-so, a great sinner; he only joined them casually.' Then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'Cover them with My mercy.' They are the companions; no one who sits with them is made wretched."],[6487,"Indeed, the womb has a hook clinging to the Throne, speaking with an eloquent tongue: 'O God, maintain ties with whoever maintains ties with me, and sever ties with whoever severs ties with me.' Then God, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'I am God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, I derived the womb (raḥim) from My name (al-Raḥmān). Whoever maintains it, I will maintain him; and whoever severs it, I will sever him.'"],[6488,"When Rajab entered, he would say: 'O God, bless us in Rajab and Shaʿban and enable us to reach Ramadan.' And when it was the night of Friday, he would say: 'This is a radiant night and a bright day.'"],[6489,"He mentioned this fire of yours, and said: 'Indeed, it is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell. It did not reach you until' – I think he said – 'it was doused twice with water so that it would give light for you. The fire of Hell is black and dark.'"],[6490,"O son of Adam, if you draw near to Me a handspan, I draw near to you a cubit; and if you draw near to Me a cubit, I draw near to you a fathom. And if you come to Me in repentance, I will come running. O son of Adam, if you were to sin until your sins reached the clouds of the sky, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you, and I would not mind."],[6491,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was distressed. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'O Abu Bakr, why do I see you distressed?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I was with my cousin so-and-so last night, and he was in the throes of death.' He said: 'Did you not prompt him to say: There is no god but God?' He said: 'I did prompt him.' He said: 'Did he say it?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Paradise is guaranteed for him.' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of God, then how is it for the living?' He said: 'It is more destructive, it is more destructive, it is more destructive – three times – for their sins.'"],[6492,"When you pass by the meadows of Paradise, then graze therein.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what are the meadows of Paradise in this world?' He said: 'Circles of remembrance.'"],[6493,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed the talbiyah for Hajj and ʿUmrah together."],[6494,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[6495,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh b. 'Ubadah narrated to us: Zurara narrated to us, from Anas."],[6496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey of his, and he had a camel driver driving them along who was called Anjasha. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came and said: \"O Anjasha, drive gently with the glass vessels.\""],[6497,"He used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr while the sun was white and clear, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr: sometimes he prayed it when dawn broke, and sometimes he delayed it."],[6498,"\"Who will find out for me what happened to Abu Jahl?\" Ibn Mas'ud said: \"I will.\" So he went and found that the two sons of 'Afra' had struck him until he became still. He said: \"I took hold of his beard and said: 'Are you Abu Jahl?'\" He said: \"He said: 'Is he anything but a man whom you have killed, or whom his people have killed?'\""],[6499,"A man would assign some palm trees to the Prophet ﷺ before Qurayza was conquered for him. When it was conquered, he began returning to them what they had given him. My family had given him something, so they ordered me to go to him and ask him to return it to them, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ had given it to Umm Ayman. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave them to me. Then Umm Ayman came, put the garment around my neck, and said: \"No, by Allah, I will not give them to you when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them to me.\" He said: \"O Umm Ayman, leave him, and you will have such-and-such.\" I think he said: \"He gave her more than them, or something like that.\""],[6500,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Every prophet asked for something, and every prophet has a supplication. I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6501,"\"I saw Paradise and Hell depicted for me in this wall, and I have never seen as much good and evil as I saw today.\""],[6502,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting the Talbiyah for both of them together."],[6503,"The supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."],[6504,"\"To pray the morning prayer and sit until the sun rises is dearer to me\"—I think he said—\"than freeing such-and-such a number of the descendants of Isma'il.\" I think he said about them: \"four slaves from the descendants of Isma'il.\""],[6505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with hais."],[6506,"There is no emigration beyond three days."],[6507,"I was standing over the neighborhood watering them — and I was the youngest of them in age — from a fadikh (beverage made from unripe and ripe dates) of theirs. He said: Then a man came and said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' They said: 'Spill it, O Anas.' I said to Anas: 'What was their drink?' He said: 'Fresh ripe dates and unripe dates.' Abu Bakr b. Anas said: 'Anas was present, and that was their wine at that time, and Anas did not deny that.'"],[6508,"No one remains who prayed toward both qiblahs except me."],[6509,"The Messenger of God ﷺ confided a secret to me, and I have not told it to anyone. Indeed, Umm Sulaym asked me, but I did not tell her."],[6510,"A boy from among us, from the Ansar, said on the day of Hunayn: 'We will not be defeated today due to lack of numbers.' But no sooner did we meet our enemy than the people fled. The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a mule of his, with Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith holding its bridle and al-Abbas, his uncle, holding its stirrup. We were in a sandy valley, and the dust rose so that none of us could see his own hand. Then a figure approached. He said to him: 'Come forward; who are you?' He said: 'I am Abu Bakr; may my father and mother be your ransom.' He had some ten-odd wounds. Then another figure approached, and he said: 'Come forward; who are you?' He said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab; may my father and mother be your ransom.' He had some ten-odd wounds. Then another figure approached with some twenty-odd wounds, and he said: 'Come forward; who are you?' He said: 'Uthman b. Affan; may my father and mother be your ransom.' Then another figure approached with some ten-odd wounds, and he said: 'Come forward; who are you?' He said: 'Ali b. Abi Talib; may my father and mother be your ransom.' Then the people advanced. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Is there not a man with a loud voice who can go and call out among the people?' A man went and shouted, and no sooner did his voice reach their ears than they came back. The Prophet ﷺ charged, and the Muslims charged with him, and the polytheists fled. Durayd b. al-Simmah withdrew to a small mountain — or he said: to a hill — with about six hundred men. Some of the people said to him: 'By God, I see a troop has come.' He said: 'Leave them to me.' He said: 'Their mark is such-and-such, from their appearance such-and-such.' He said: 'No harm to you; Quda'ah is moving off in the tracks of the people.' They said: 'By God, we see a rough troop has come.' He said: 'Leave them to me.' He said: 'Their mark is such-and-such, from their appearance such-and-such.' He said: 'No harm to you; this is Sulaym.' Then they said: 'We see a horseman has come.' He said: 'Woe to you! Alone?' They said: 'Alone.' He said: 'Leave him to me.' They said: 'He has wrapped his head with a black turban.' Durayd said: 'That, by God, is al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, and he, by God, is your killer and the one who will expel you from this place of yours.' He turned to them and said: 'Why are these left here?' Then he went on with those who followed him, and he killed about three hundred, and he cut off the head of Durayd b. al-Simmah and placed it before him."],[6511,"Indeed, God is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[6512,"Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the path of God until he returns."],[6513,"When you travel through fertile land, give the animals their due, or their share. When you travel through barren land, hurry on them. And keep to night travel, for the earth is folded up at night. And when you camp, do not camp on the middle of the road, for it is the abode of every beast."],[6514,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut until he died, Abu Bakr until he died, and Umar until he died."],[6515,"I am the first of people to come forth when they are resurrected, and I am their leader when they come as delegations, and I am their speaker when they listen, and I am their bringer of good tidings when they despair. The banner of honor on that day will be in my hand, and I am the noblest of the children of Adam in the sight of God, and no boast. A thousand servants will go around me as if they were hidden pearls."],[6516,"Whoever leaves this world upon sincerity to God, Blessed and Exalted, and worship of Him, not associating anything with Him, and upon establishing prayer and giving zakat, leaves it while God is pleased with him. That is the religion of God with which the messengers came and which they conveyed from their Lord before the clear-cut hadiths and the divergence of whims. Confirmation of that is in the Book of God: 'If they repent' — he says: if they cast off idols and worship of them — 'and establish prayer and give zakat, then leave their way clear,' and he recited another verse: 'If they repent and establish prayer and give zakat, then they are your brothers in religion.'"],[6517,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade plundering and said: 'Whoever plunders is not one of us.'"],[6518,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ in the appearance of a traveler and said: 'O Muhammad, what is Islam...'"],[6519,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, then a man married her, then divorced her before having intercourse with her; is she lawful for the first? He said: No, until the other tastes her honey and she tastes his honey."],[6520,"Paradise and the Fire were shown to me behind this wall, and I have not seen the like of good and evil."],[6521,"He forbade continuous fasting in the fast."],[6522,"When we supplicated, we would say: O Allah, place upon us the prayer of a righteous people, who are neither sinful nor wicked, who stand in the night and fast during the day."],[6523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward Jerusalem while praying Zuhr, then he turned his face toward the Kaaba. The foolish among the people said: What has turned them from their qiblah which they were upon?!"],[6524,"When the Prophet ﷺ traveled and encamped at a place, he bade farewell to the place with two rak'ahs, or with a prayer."],[6525,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ while people were with him, and a man with him said: I love this one. The Prophet ﷺ said: Stand up and inform him. So he stood up to him and informed him, and he said: May He for whose sake you loved me love you."],[6526,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves three of your companions. Then he came to him and said: O Muhammad, Paradise longs for three of your companions. Anas b. Malik said: I wanted to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but I was in awe of him. I met Abu Bakr ؓ and said: O Abu Bakr, I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Gabriel ﷺ said: O Muhammad, Paradise longs for three. Perhaps you are among them. Then I met Umar ؓ and said to him the like of that. Then I met Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ and said to him the like of what I said to Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ. Ali ؓ said: I will ask him. If I am among them, I praise Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and if I am not among them, I praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas..."],[6527,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the wage of a cupper, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage."],[6528,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ used to begin the recitation with 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds' and they would give one salutation."],[6529,"We were forbidden to pray in an elevated mosque."],[6530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not hold a wedding feast for any of his wives except Safiyyah."],[6531,"Seventy men of the Ansar were killed on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against those who killed them for fifteen days in prayer, after the ruku'."],[6532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage, and spoke to his masters, so they reduced his tax."],[6533,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar. He made brothers of Sa'd b. al-Rabi' and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. Sa'd said to me: 'I have wealth, and it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives; look, whichever of them is dearer to you, I will divorce her, and when her waiting period ends, marry her.' He said: 'May Allah bless you in your family and wealth. Direct me to the market.' So he directed him, and he did not return until he came back with dates and aqit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw traces of yellow perfume on him and said: 'Mahyam?' He said: 'I married a woman from the Ansar.' He said: 'What did you give her as a bridal gift?' He said: 'The weight of a date stone of gold.' He said: 'Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[6534,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man being supported between two men. He asked about him. They said: 'He vowed to perform Hajj walking.' He said: 'Tell him to ride.'"],[6535,"We discussed the earnings of the cupper in the presence of Anas b. Malik. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he ordered that a sa' of food be given to him, and he ordered his family to reduce his tax.'"],[6536,"The best thing with which you treat yourselves is cupping."],[6537,"Usamah b. Zayd was with the Prophet ﷺ while he was a boy. He saw Suhayl b. 'Amr and said: 'O my father, is this not the one who used to feed us tharid in Makkah?' The Prophet ﷺ turned away from him."],[6538,"Allah did not disgrace him with whiteness, meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[6539,"He was in one of the alleys of Madinah when he heard a man say: 'O Abu al-Qasim!' The Prophet ﷺ turned around and said: 'I did not mean you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah.'"],[6540,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came to Madinah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. Sa'd offered to him, and 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: 'May Allah bless you. Direct me to the market.' So he directed him to the market, and he bought and sold. The Prophet ﷺ saw traces of yellow perfume on him and said: 'Mahyam?' or a similar word. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman for the weight of a date stone of gold.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[6541,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came to Madinah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. He offered to him—I think he said his wealth—so he said: 'May Allah bless you in your family and wealth. Direct me to the market.' So he entered the market and profited from aqit and ghee. The Prophet ﷺ saw him after some days with traces of yellow perfume on him and said: 'Mahyam, O 'Abd al-Rahman?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman from the Ansar.' He said: 'What did you give her as a bridal gift?' He said: 'The weight of a date stone of gold.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[6542,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and he gave him his wage."],[6543,"Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet ﷺ, so he gave him a ṣāʿ or two ṣāʿs of food, and he spoke to his masters, so they reduced his tax."],[6544,"When the Prophet ﷺ dug the trench, the Anṣār said on that day: “We are those who pledged allegiance to Muḥammad upon jihād as long as we live, ever.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, the real good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn.”"],[6545,"The Prophet ﷺ was in prayer, then he spat in his garment and rubbed some of it together."],[6546,"He wanted to marry a woman, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Look at her, for it is more likely to create harmony between you two.” Then al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah married her."],[6547,"Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Mufaḍḍal al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Thābit b. Thawbān narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Anas; from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6548,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus when his death was announced. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over an Abyssinian slave?!” Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah.”"],[6549,"Close off every door in the mosque from me except the door of Abū Bakr. If I were to take a bosom friend, I would take Abū Bakr as a bosom friend."],[6550,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you?” He said: “ʿĀʾishah.” He said: “Among men?” He said: “Then her father.”"],[6551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a rope stretched out and said: “What is this rope?” They said: “So-and-so prays, and when she is overcome she holds onto it.” He said: “Let her pray as long as she is alert, and when she is overcome let her sleep.”"],[6552,"The Muslims heard the Prophet ﷺ calling out at night over the well of Badr: “O Abū Jahl b. Hishām, O ʿUtbah b. Rabīʿah, O Shaybah b. Rabīʿah, O Umayyah b. Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, are you calling people who have become corpses?” He said: “You are no more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot respond.”"],[6553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled to Badr and consulted the Muslims. Abū Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, advised him, then he consulted ʿUmar and he advised him, may Allah have mercy on him, then he consulted them. The Anṣār said: “O assembly of Anṣār, it is you whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ means.” They said: “Then we will not say what the Children of Israel said to Moses ﷺ : ‘Go, you and your Lord, and fight.’ By the One who sent you with the truth, if you struck with us the livers of camels to Bark al-Ghimād, we would follow you.”"],[6554,"When the Muslims fled on the day of Ḥunayn, and Umm Sulaym was with them, she began calling out: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they have been defeated,” or words to that effect. He said: “O Umm Sulaym, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has sufficed.” Abū Ṭalḥah found a pickaxe and said: “What is this, O Umm Sulaym?” She said: “I held onto it; if any of the polytheists came near me, I would rip open his belly.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, hear what Umm Sulaym says.”"],[6555,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: Accept Islam. He said: I find myself averse. He said: Accept Islam, even if you are averse."],[6556,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas stood in the place of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: We will protect you from what we protect ourselves and our children. So what is for us? He said: Paradise. He said: We are content."],[6557,"We reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its fruit was like large water jars, and its leaves like the ears of elephants. When it was covered by the command of Allah what covered it, it changed as Allah willed."],[6558,"Abdullah b. Salam came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon his arrival in Madinah and said: I will ask you about three things that none knows but a prophet: the first food the people of Paradise will eat, the child's resemblance to its father or mother, and the first signs of the Hour. He said: Jibril informed me of them just now. Abdullah b. Salam said: The enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: The first signs of the Hour is a fire that will gather them from the east to the west. As for the first food the people of Paradise will eat, it is an extra piece of fish liver. As for the child, if the man's fluid precedes, the child resembles him, and if the woman's fluid precedes, the child resembles her. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people, and if they learn of my Islam before you ask them about me, they will slander me before you. So he sent for the Jews and said: What kind of man is Abdullah b. Salam? They said: Our best and the son of our best, our master and the son of our master, and our most learned. He said: What if Abdullah b. Salam accepts Islam? They said: May Allah protect him from that. Then Abdullah b. Salam came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Rather, he is our worst, and they belittled him. Abdullah b. Salam said: This is what I feared, O Messenger of Allah."],[6559,"The front tooth of al-Rubayyi' was broken, so they asked them to forgive, but they refused except retaliation. Anas b. al-Nadr said: O Messenger of Allah, will the front tooth of al-Rubayyi' be broken? By the One who sent you with the truth, it will not be broken. He said: O Anas, the Book of Allah ordains retaliation. He said: Then the people were content and forgave. He said: Indeed, among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear by Allah, Blessed and Exalted, He fulfills it."],[6560,"A man came and reached the people out of breath, and when he stood in prayer he said: Praise be to Allah, much good and blessed praise. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said: Who spoke? Or: Who said? The people remained silent. Then he said: Who spoke? Or: Who said? For he has done well. Or he said: He did not say anything wrong. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I reached the row out of breath, or he said: I was panting. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to see which of them would take it up. Then he said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly, pray what he catches up with, and complete what he missed."],[6561,"The Prophet ﷺ swore to stay away from his wives for a month, and people came to him. When prayer time came, he prayed sitting while they were standing. When the next prayer time came, they started to stand, so he said: Follow your imam; if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and if he prays standing, pray standing. He remained for twenty-nine nights, then ended it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not swear a month? He said: The month is twenty-nine."],[6562,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the time of the dawn prayer, so he prayed when dawn broke, then later when it was bright. Then he said: Where is the one who asked about the time of the dawn prayer? Between these two is the time."],[6563,"Banu Salimah wanted to move from their homes to be near the mosque, but the Prophet ﷺ disliked that and said: O Banu Salimah, will you not count your footsteps? So they stayed."],[6564,"The prayer was called, and he turned to us before saying the takbir and said: Straighten your rows, for I see you behind my back."],[6565,"The Prophet ﷺ stood for prayer, then turned to us and said: Straighten your rows, straighten your rows, for I see you from behind my back."],[6566,"He was standing praying in one of his rooms at night, and some Muslims came to pray with him. He prayed, then entered his house for as long as Allah willed, then came out to them. He did that several times. When morning came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed with you last night, and we would like to imitate your prayer. He said: I knew your place, and I did it deliberately."],[6567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a she-camel called al-ʿAḍbāʾ that was never outrun. A Bedouin came on a young riding camel and outran it, which distressed the Muslims. When he saw what was in their faces, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, al-ʿAḍbāʾ has been outrun.\" He said, \"It is a duty upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that nothing of this world is raised except that He lowers it.\""],[6568,"A man among those who wrote between the hands of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite from al-Baqarah and Āl ʿImrān. He would dictate to him something of the names of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and he would say, \"Samīʿun ʿAlīm (All-Hearing, All-Knowing),\" and the other would say, \"Ghafūrun Raḥīm (Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful).\" He would say, \"Write whichever of them you wish.\" He then apostatized from Islam and joined the polytheists, saying, \"Do you teach me about Muhammad? I used to write whatever I wished.\" He died, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The earth will not accept him.\" He said: It was mentioned that Abū Ṭalḥah came to the land where the man died and found him cast out. He said, \"What is the matter with this?\" They said, \"We buried him many times, but the earth would not accept him.\""],[6569,"Shall I not tell you of the best dwellings of the Anṣār? The dwellings of Banū al-Najjār, then the dwellings of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the dwellings of Banū al-Ḥārith, then the Khazraj, then the dwellings of Banū Sāʿidah. And in all the dwellings of the Anṣār there is good."],[6570,"The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was moderate in length, and so was the prayer of Abū Bakr, but ʿUmar extended the dawn prayer."],[6571,"There was a small boy on the edge of the road. The Prophet ﷺ passed by with some people. When the boy's mother saw the group, she feared her son would be trampled, so she ran and carried him, saying, \"My son, my son!\" The people said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this woman would never throw her son into the Fire.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No, by Allah, and He will not throw His beloved into the Fire.\""],[6572,"A woman presented herself to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a need from you.\" He said, \"O Umm so-and-so, sit in whichever of the side streets you wish, and I will sit with you.\" So she sat, and he sat with her until he fulfilled her need."],[6573,"A morning outing in the path of Allah, or an evening outing, is better than this world and all it contains. And the space of a bow of any one of you is better than this world and all it contains. If a woman from the people of Paradise were to look upon the people of the earth, she would fill what is between them with fragrance, and her headscarf upon her head is better than this world and all it contains."],[6574,"The Prophet ﷺ was with one of the Mothers of the Believers, and she sent him a bowl containing food. She struck the messenger's hand, and the bowl fell and broke. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took one of the two broken pieces and joined one of them to the other, and he began collecting the food in them, saying, \"Your mother felt jealous.\" They ate until she herself brought a bowl from her house. The Prophet ﷺ gave the intact bowl to the messenger and left the broken one in the house of the one who had broken it."],[6575,"And Muhammad b. Ṣāliḥ al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Ḥarmalah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Wahb narrated to us: Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Sālim narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar, from Thābit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar to it."],[6576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it ripens. We said, \"O Abū Ḥamzah, what does 'ripens' mean?\" He said, \"It becomes red or yellow.\""],[6577,"I entered Paradise and found myself before a palace of gold. I said, \"For whom is this palace?\" They said, \"For a young man of Quraysh.\" I thought that I was him. They said, \"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.\""],[6578,"I entered Paradise and found myself before a palace of gold. I said, \"For whom is this palace?\" They said, \"For a young man of Quraysh.\" I said, \"For whom?\" They said, \"For ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. Were it not for what I know of your jealousy, I would have entered it.\" ʿUmar said, \"Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?\""],[6579,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while I was a boy among boys, and he greeted us. Then he took me by the hand and sent me on an errand. He sat in the shade of a wall until I returned. When I came to Umm Sulaym, she said, 'What kept you?' I said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand.' She said, 'What is it?' I said, 'It is a secret.' She said, 'Guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I never told anyone about it."],[6580,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi and Isma'il b. 'Ulayya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6581,"Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Habib narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, similar to the hadith of Khalid b. al-Harith, except that in the hadith of al-Taymi there is no 'he greeted us.'"],[6582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had his incisor broken on the Day of Uhud and was wounded, and the blood began to flow over his face. He wiped the blood from his face and said, 'How can a people prosper who have stained the face of their Prophet with blood while he calls them to their Lord?' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.'"],[6583,"When this verse was revealed: 'You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love,' or 'Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan,' Abu Talha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my garden in such-and-such a place is for Allah, Blessed and Exalted. If I could keep it secret, I would not make it public.' He said, 'Make it for the poor among your relatives, or for your household.'"],[6584,"Anas was asked about the voluntary prayer and fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'He would fast during the month until we would say, \"He does not want to break his fast at all,\" and he would not fast during the month until we would say, \"He does not want to fast at all.\" We never wished to see him praying at night except that we saw him, and we never saw him sleeping except that we saw him.'"],[6585,"This hadith, part of its wording, was narrated by Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, specifically about fasting."],[6586,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a mount, but he found him busy. He said, 'By Allah, I will not give you a mount.' When he turned away, he called him. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you swore that you would not give me a mount.' He said, 'And I swear that I will give you a mount.' So he gave him a mount."],[6587,"People will come to you who are more tender-hearted than you. Then the Ash'aris arrived."],[6588,"None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. But let him say: 'O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.'"],[6589,"Umm Sulaym took me when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Anas is a boy who can write and serve you.' I served him for nine years, and he never said to me about anything I did, 'You did badly,' nor 'How bad what you did.'"],[6590,"I entered Paradise and heard a rustling sound before me, and behold, it was al-Ghumaysa' bt. Milhan."],[6591,"There is no soul that dies and has good with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that would be pleased to return to this world even if it had the world and all that is in it—except the martyr, because of what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom; he would be pleased to return and be killed another time."],[6592,"The Hour will not come until there remains no one on the earth who says: Allah, Allah."],[6593,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: 'Return your butter to its container and your dates to their vessel, for I am fasting.' Then he went to a corner of the house and prayed a prayer that was not obligatory, and he supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Umm Sulaym said: 'I have a special request.' He said: 'What is it?' She said: 'Your servant Anas.' He did not omit any good of the Hereafter or this world but supplicated for me with it. Then he said: 'Provide him with wealth and children and bless him.' I think he said: 'in him.' He said: 'So I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar.' He said: 'And my daughter informed me that I had buried one hundred and twenty-some of my offspring before the arrival of al-Hajjaj to Basra.'"],[6594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a garden among the gardens of Madinah belonging to the Banu al-Najjar, and he heard a voice from a grave. He said: 'When was this one buried?' They said: 'In the pre-Islamic period.' He was pleased with that and said: 'Had it not been that you would refrain from burying one another, I would have called upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to make you hear the punishment of the grave.'"],[6595,"It is not necessary for you—or a word similar to it—to be impressed by anyone, or by anyone's deeds, until you see what end he meets. For a man may work for a period of time the deeds that, had he died upon them, he would have entered Paradise, then he performs the deeds of the people of the Fire. And a servant may work for a period of his life with deeds that, had he died upon them, he would have entered the Fire, then he performs the deeds of the people of Paradise."],[6596,"Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah loves his meeting. And whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah hates his meeting. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, all of us hates death.' He said: 'It is not the hatred of death, but when the believer is at the point of death, there comes to him the bringer of good tidings from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and nothing is more beloved to him than the meeting with Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So Allah loves his meeting and he loves the meeting with Allah, Blessed and Exalted.'"],[6597,"The Prophet ﷺ gave from the spoils of Khaybar: to al-Aqraʿ b. Habis one hundred camels, and to ʿUyayna b. Badr one hundred camels. Some of the Ansar said: 'We give our spoils to a people while our swords are dripping with their blood—or their blood is dripping from our swords!' When the Ansar gathered around him, he said: 'Is there anyone among you besides yourselves?' They said: 'No, except the son of our sister.' He said: 'The son of a people's sister is one of them.' Then he said: 'Are you not pleased, O Ansar, that the people go away with the world—or he said: with camels and sheep—while you take Muhammad ﷺ to your homes?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted ones. Were it not for the migration, I would have been a man of the Ansar.'"],[6598,"There are three things that, whoever has them, finds the sweetness of faith by them: whoever Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; whoever loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and whoever hates to return to disbelief just as he hates to be thrown into the Fire."],[6599,"There are three things that, whoever has them."],[6600,"I entered Paradise, and there I was with a river whose two banks were tents of pearl. I struck my hand into the flow of its water, and there I was with pungent musk. I said: 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said: 'This is al-Kawthar, which Allah has given you.'"],[6601,"which He has given you"],[6602,"There are coming to you peoples whose hearts are softer than yours. Then the Ashʿaris arrived, among them Abu Musa."],[6603,"Abu Talha was in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was raising his head looking at the spot where his arrows fell. He said: Abu Talha stretched himself up and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my soul be a ransom for yours, or he said: my neck before your neck."],[6604,"Have you considered if Allah withholds the fruit, then with what right do you consume your brother's wealth?"],[6605,"The prayer was called, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ had something between him and his wives, holding some of them back from others. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, came and said: Throw dust in their faces and go out to the prayer."],[6606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I think he said, was sitting in his house when a man looked in on him, so he made a movement toward him with a blade he had, and the man stepped back."],[6607,"He was asked about the punishment of the grave, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, cowardice, miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave."],[6608,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is called, begin with the evening meal."],[6609,"A man gave another man a life grant, so he asked the Prophet ﷺ? He said: It belongs to his heirs, or as he said."],[6610,"Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."],[6611,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[6612,"Abu Talha intended to divorce Umm Sulaym, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The divorce of Umm Sulaym is a grave sin."],[6613,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6614,"Remorse is repentance."],[6615,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brown-skinned."],[6616,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was neither tall nor short, and when he walked he leaned forward, and he was brown-skinned."],[6617,"Persist in saying “O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[6618,"A house in the highest part of Paradise, and a house in the courtyard of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise — for one who abandons lying even in jest, and for one who abandons quarreling even if he is right, and for one whose character is good."],[6619,"When he went out on a journey and then returned and drew near to Madinah, he would hasten toward it."],[6620,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khaybar for a half share, or for a third."],[6621,"When he raised his head from bowing, none of us would prostrate until we saw that he had prostrated."],[6622,"The wife of Thabit b. Shammas — he is Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas — came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said some words as if she disliked him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. The Prophet ﷺ sent to Thabit: Take that from her — I think he said: And divorce her."],[6623,"Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of God, a woman may have two husbands in this world, meaning one husband after another, and they enter Paradise. To which of them will she belong? He said: To the one with the better character."],[6624,"When the head of al-Husayn was brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, he began poking his front teeth with a stick, saying: He was, I think he said, handsome. I said: By God, I will grieve you. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing where your stick falls. He said: So he withdrew."],[6625,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Ayyub: Shall I guide you to a trade? He said: Yes. He said: Strive to reconcile between people when they have become corrupt, and draw them together when they have grown apart."],[6626,"Anas b. al-Nadr was absent from the fighting at Badr, and he said: I was absent from the first battle in which the Prophet ﷺ fought the polytheists? If God, Blessed and Exalted, lets me witness with the Messenger of God ﷺ a battle, God, Blessed and Exalted, will surely see how I act. On the day of Uhud, the Muslims were exposed, and he said: O God, I declare myself innocent to You of what these have brought — meaning the polytheists — and I apologize to You for what these have done — meaning the Muslims. Then he went forward with his sword, and Sa'd b. Mu'adh met him and said: Where, O Sa'd? By God, I find its scent before Uhud. He said: So he went on and fought. Anas said: We found on him more than eighty wounds, between sword strikes, spear thrusts, and arrow shots, and they mutilated him. He said: We only recognized him by his fingertips. He said: And this verse was revealed: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to God.”"],[6627,"The Dajjal has a defective left eye, upon it a thick protruding film, and between his eyes is written: K F R."],[6628,"Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise, with each one of the seventy, seventy thousand."],[6629,"No person was more beloved to them than the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when they saw him they would not stand for him, because he disliked that."],[6630,"The people of Yemen came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The people of Yemen have come to you; they are more tender of heart than you.' He was the first who brought the handshake."],[6631,"The Prophet ﷺ stood for prayer, then he turned his face toward us and said: 'Press together, press together; indeed I see you from behind my back.'"],[6632,"The Prophet ﷺ used to combine melon and fresh dates."],[6633,"Indeed God, blessed and exalted, supports the religion with people who have no share in the Hereafter."],[6634,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out leaning on a staff, so we stood up. He said: 'Do not stand as non-Arabs stand, showing reverence to one another.' It was as if we wished that he would supplicate for us, so he said: 'O God, forgive us, have mercy on us, be pleased with us, accept from us, admit us to Paradise, save us from the Fire, and set right all our affairs.' It was as if we wished that he would add more, so he said: 'I have combined for you the whole matter.'"],[6635,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of people who were being tested, and said: 'Would that these people ask God for well-being.'"],[6636,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no deity but God. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property, except [and by its rights they are answered] by God, blessed and exalted."],[6637,"Umm Sulaym had a son called Abu 'Umayr. The Prophet ﷺ would sometimes joke with him. One day he entered and found him sad, so he said: 'What is the matter with Abu 'Umayr?' They said: 'His little bird that he used to play with has died.' He began to say: 'Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the little bird?'"],[6638,"He forbade a town-dweller from selling on behalf of a desert-dweller."],[6639,"Sadaqah repels a bad death."],[6640,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, supports this religion with men who have no share (of good)."],[6641,"Ali will pay off my debt."],[6642,"In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it. Recite, if you wish: 'And extended shade' (Quran 56:30)."],[6643,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a drinker and he ordered him to be flogged, and he was flogged with palm branches and sandals."],[6644,"Ali ؓ proposed to Fatimah ؓ to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6645,"O young men, whoever among you has the means, let him marry; and whoever does not, let him fast - I think he said - for it is a shield for him."],[6646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out during his illness in which he died, leaning on Usamah, wrapped in a cotton garment, and he led the people in prayer."],[6647,"Abu Ziyad used to deny the Hawd (the Pool), so it was said to him: 'Anas b. Malik narrates from the Prophet ﷺ about the Hawd.' He sent to Anas and asked him. Anas said: 'I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: I will have a Hawd from such-and-such to such-and-such.'"],[6648,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: 'Ride it.' He said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Ride it.'"],[6649,"He said: Ahmad b. 'Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Hammad b. Mas'adah narrated to us, he said: 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And we do not know that 'Awf connected a hadith from al-Hasan, from Anas except this hadith, and no one narrated it from him in a connected form except Hammad b. Mas'adah, and we did not hear it except from Ahmad b. 'Abd Allah."],[6650,"The Prophet ﷺ and his companions entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah. When they arrived at Makkah, they circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to exit ihram, but they were reluctant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Exit ihram. Were it not that I have the sacrificial animal with me, I would exit ihram.' So they exited ihram until they were free to approach women."],[6651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, mentioning the Ḥawḍ: “Pitchers seen in it are more numerous than the number of stars in the sky.”"],[6652,"He forbade praying between graves."],[6653,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?” He said, “What have you prepared for it?” He said, “I have not prepared much for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, “A person will be with those whom he loves, and he will have what he has earned.”"],[6654,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to begin the recitation with “All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds.” And he was the lightest of people in prayer while still complete."],[6655,"“You should wear white garments. Let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them.”"],[6656,"“This son of mine is a leader,” meaning al-Ḥasan. He said: “And he resembled him,” or something like this."],[6657,"Wine was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and their drink at that time was nothing but unripe dates and dried dates."],[6658,"“The servant remains in good as long as he does not become hasty.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, how does he become hasty?” He said, “He says, ‘I have called upon my Lord, and He has not answered me.’”"],[6659,"Bilāl gave the call to prayer before dawn, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to go back and say, “Indeed, the servant has slept.” Bilāl then ascended while saying, “Would that Bilāl’s mother had lost him, and he became wet from the moisture of his forehead’s sweat.”"],[6660,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, they long for their brothers. The couch of one comes until it is alongside the couch of the other, and they converse. Each reclines, and they talk about what they used to do in the world. One says to his companion, “O so-and-so, do you know which day Allah forgave us? The day we were in such-and-such a place and called upon Allah, and He forgave us.”"],[6661,"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it is good and sufficient, but whoever performs the full bath, the bath is better."],[6662,"“I will not cease to intercede and be granted intercession” — or he said, “My Lord will grant me intercession” — “until I say, ‘O Lord, have You granted me intercession for those who said, “There is no god but Allah”?’ Then it is said, ‘O Muḥammad, this is not for you or for anyone. This is Mine, by My might and My mercy. I will not leave anyone in the Fire who says, “There is no god but Allah.”’”"],[6663,"It was said to him: Describe for us the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He called for a basin and performed ablution three times three times, and he passed his fingers through his beard, and said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution.'"],[6664,"The house in which the Qur'an is recited has abundant good, and the house in which the Qur'an is not recited has little good."],[6665,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, Fatimah, may God have mercy on her, said: 'What a grief, for the grief of my father!' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'There is no grief upon your father after this day.'"],[6666,"I was riding behind Abu Talhah when we came to Khaybar, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, when we descend upon the courtyard of a people, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.'"],[6667,"A Jewish woman gifted the Messenger of God ﷺ a roasted sheep. When he extended his hand to eat, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A limb of its limbs informs me that it is poisoned.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ refrained, and those with him refrained. He sent for the Jewish woman and said: 'What induced you to spoil it after you had prepared it?' She said: 'I wanted to know if you were a prophet, for you would know that; and if you were not a prophet, I would relieve the people of you.'"],[6668,"He used to deliver sermons leaning on a palm trunk before he adopted the pulpit. When he adopted the pulpit, the trunk yearned. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and embraced it, and it became still."],[6669,"Anas b. Malik narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ, and Jabir b. 'Abd Allah narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ, and 'Abd Allah b. Qudamah, who was a truthful man, narrated to me from al-Aswad b. Sari', from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: They stood up and said: 'We were close to being overcome regarding this old man.'"],[6670,"When you hear the muezzin, then say what he says."],[6671,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a man who had become like a fledgling, meaning from the severity of pain. The Prophet ﷺ asked him: 'Did you used to supplicate your Lord for anything?' He said: 'I used to say: O God, whatever punishment You would inflict upon me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world.' He said: 'Why did you not say—or why do you not say—: O God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us—or protect me—from the punishment of the Fire?' He said: The man said it, and he recovered."],[6672,"The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh."],[6673,"6683 6681 - Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, Asad b. Musa narrated to us, Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas."],[6674,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering a sermon, a man stood up to him and said: 'O Messenger of God, the people are exhausted and the land is barren—or he said: has become barren—so ask God for rain for us.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands and said: 'O God, give us rain.' He said: We did not see even a wisp of cloud in the sky. He said: The clouds gathered and they were rained upon until the like of it. Then that man or another stood up and said: 'O Messenger of God, the houses have collapsed and the roads have been cut off, so supplicate God to lift it from us.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O God, around us and not upon us.' He said: The sky cleared over Madinah, and it rained around it, but we were not rained upon."],[6675,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[6676,"'Umar b. al-Khattab entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was on a reed mat, and the mat had left marks on his side. 'Umar's eyes filled with tears, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What makes you weep, O 'Umar?\" He said: \"I remembered Chosroes and Caesar.\" He said: \"Would you not be content that they have this world and we have the Hereafter?\""],[6677,"Three men entered a cave ..."],[6678,"When the Muslims and the polytheists met on the day of the conquest of Makkah ..."],[6679,"Perform ablution from what fire has changed."],[6680,"I have never touched silk or anything else softer than the palm of the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor have I smelled musk or ambergris more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6681,"Accept from the good-doers of the Ansar and overlook their wrongdoers."],[6682,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar used to begin the recitation with \"Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.\""],[6683,"I was giving my uncles a drink made from unripe dates and dates, until the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announced that wine had been forbidden. He said: So we poured it out."],[6684,"A beggar came to the Prophet ﷺ and he gave him a date. He said: \"A prophet gives a date!\" and left. Then another came and asked, so he sent for some, and a date was brought, and he gave him a date. He said: \"A date from a prophet is much. By God, it will never leave me as long as I live.\""],[6685,"O son of Adam, one is for you, one is for Me, and one is between Me and you. As for the one that is for Me, you worship Me and do not associate anything with Me. As for the one that is for you, whatever deed you do—or whatever work—I will repay you for it. As for the one that is between Me and you, from you is supplication and upon Me is the answer."],[6686,"Beware of the wives of those who are away on military expeditions."],[6687,"Paradise longs for three: 'Ali, 'Ammar — and I think he said — and Abu Dharr."],[6688,"There are no two guardian angels who raise to Allah what they guarded during a day, and at the beginning of the record there is the recitation of Tabaraka wa Ta'ala and at its end a seeking of forgiveness, except that Tabaraka wa Ta'ala says: 'I have forgiven My servant for what is between the two ends of this record.'"],[6689,"The worst of rulers is the oppressive one (al-hutama)."],[6690,"The likeness of my Companions is the likeness of salt in food: food is only good with it."],[6691,"Whoever had two tongues in this world will have two tongues in the Fire."],[6692,"He prohibited sales involving uncertainty (bay' al-gharar)."],[6693,"He prohibited the sale of animals whose udders have been left unmilked to deceive buyers, and he said: 'Whoever buys them has the option (to return them).'"],[6694,"When one of you enters the lavatory, let him say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils.'"],[6695,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he performed qunut until he died."],[6696,"Whoever's intention is the Hereafter, Allah, Tabaraka wa Ta'ala, places richness in his heart, gathers his affairs for him, removes poverty from before his eyes, and the world comes to him submissively. Thus he rises only rich and evenings only rich. But whoever's intention is this world and its desires, Allah places poverty before his eyes, so he rises only poor and evenings only poor."],[6697,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was reciting the talbiyah: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.'"],[6698,"I do not recognize anything today from what we were upon during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except this prayer, although you have introduced into it what you have introduced."],[6699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed a man who leads a people in prayer while they dislike him, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and a man who hears 'Come to success' and does not respond."],[6700,"Two blessings in which many people are deceived: health and free time."],[6701,"Anas was asked about nushrah (a form of charm or spell), and he said: It was mentioned to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about it and he said: It is from the work of Satan."],[6702,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the qunut, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut after ruku'."],[6703,"6713 6711 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6704,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar and said: The donkeys have been eaten. And another came and said: The donkeys have been destroyed, O Messenger of Allah. So he ordered a crier to announce: Allah and His Messenger forbid you from domestic donkeys, for they are impure. He said: So the pots were overturned with the meat."],[6705,"Some people seized sheep as spoils, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a crier, and he announced: Allah and His Messenger forbid you from plunder."],[6706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Khaybar early in the morning, and they had come out with their shovels. He said: Allah is the Greatest, Khaybar is ruined. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."],[6707,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on the day of Eid, then delivered the sermon, then slaughtered, and said: Whoever slaughtered before our prayer should repeat it."],[6708,"I asked Anas: Did the Prophet ﷺ dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that - or - his gray hair did not reach that."],[6709,"Muhammad b. 'Uthman b. Karamah narrated to us, Khalid b. Makhlad narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Husayn narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas."],[6710,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned Jamrat al-'Aqabah, then left and slaughtered, then called the barber. He shaved one side of his head and gave it to Abu Talhah, and he shaved the other side and the people divided it among themselves."],[6711,"That when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: \"Or as he said.\""],[6712,"They used to write at the beginning of their wills: This is what so-and-so, son of so-and-so, has bequeathed: he bequeaths that we bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, that Paradise is true, that Hell is true, that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves. And he instructed whoever he left behind with what Ibrahim instructed his sons: \"O my sons, Allah has chosen for you the religion, so do not die except as Muslims.\""],[6713,"We were forbidden that a resident sell on behalf of a Bedouin."],[6714,"When 'Abdullah b. Abi Talha was born, Abu Talha said to me: \"Take him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he may perform tahnik on him.\" I brought him to him while he was in a livestock enclosure branding sheep. He performed tahnik on him with a date, and the boy began to chew it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The beloved of the Ansar is dates.\""],[6715,"The Prophet ﷺ used to be affectionate with us, to the point that he would say to a young brother of mine: \"Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the little bird?\""],[6716,"That the Prophet ﷺ threw the pebbles at the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then left and slaughtered, then shaved. He shaved one side of his head - I think he said: the right side of his head - and handed it to Abu Talha, then shaved the left side and distributed it among the people."],[6717,"That when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: \"Or as he said.\""],[6718,"That the Prophet ﷺ threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice, then left and slaughtered his sacrificial camels while the barber was sitting. He inclined his head toward him and said: \"Shave.\" He shaved one side of his head and distributed it - meaning among the people - and said to him: \"Shave the left side.\" He shaved it and handed it to me, and I handed it to Abu Talha."],[6719,"And a man asked him about a man who accuses his wife of adultery. He said: I asked Anas about that while I thought that he had knowledge about it. He said: The first one to engage in li'an with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was Hilal b. Umayyah; he accused his wife of being with Sharik b. al-Sahma', and he was the first to engage in li'an. Sharik was the maternal brother of al-Bara' b. Malik. So he conducted li'an between them and said: \"Observe her; if she gives birth to a white, straight-haired child, then he belongs to Hilal b. Umayyah, and if she gives birth to a child with kohl-like eyes, curly hair, and thin legs, then he belongs to Sharik.\" He said: I was informed that she gave birth to a child with kohl-like eyes, curly hair, and thin legs."],[6720,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Khaybar when a man came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been eaten.\" Another came and said: \"The donkeys have been exhausted.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller who announced: \"Allah and His Messenger forbid you from the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is impure.\" So the pots were overturned."],[6721,"And some people seized sheep as booty, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller who announced: \"Allah and His Messenger forbid you from taking spoils improperly.\""],[6722,"I asked Anas: Did the Prophet ﷺ dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that age, but Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam."],[6723,"A man said: O Messenger of God, my brother loves this surah, meaning: Say: He is God, the One. He said: Give your brother glad tidings of Paradise."],[6724,"His mother took a mudd of barley, ground it and milled it, and took a small skin of ghee and squeezed it. Then she sent me to the Prophet ﷺ and I came to him while he was among his companions and invited him. He said: And those with me? I went, meaning to Abu Talhah, and said: He said to me: And those with me? He said: Abu Talhah went out and said: O Messenger of God, it is only something Umm Sulaym prepared. He said: Bring it to me. He placed his hand over it, or the place where his hand was in it, and said: Admit ten for me. They ate until they were full. Then he said: Admit ten for me. They ate, until he counted forty. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ ate and stood up. I began to look and found that nothing had decreased from it."],[6725,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to be playful with us, so much so that he would say to a young brother of mine: Abu 'Umayr, what did the nughayr do?"],[6726,"When the head of al-Husayn was brought to Ziyad, he began to look at it and poke it with a stick, or turn it with a stick, and said: He was handsome. Anas said: I said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing it, or kissing him."],[6727,"They used to write at the beginning of their wills: This is what so-and-so son of so-and-so bequeathed..."],[6728,"We were forbidden to have a town-dweller sell for a desert-dweller."],[6729,"Abu Quhafah was brought on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and his head and beard were like a white thaghamah plant. The Prophet ﷺ ordered it to be changed and to avoid black."],[6730,"I asked Anas b. Malik: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ dye? He said: He did not reach that, but Abu Bakr dyed with henna."],[6731,"There was a drinking cup belonging to Umm Sulaym that the Prophet ﷺ used to drink from. It broke and was repaired with silver. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ drank from it."],[6732,"He had a small stick of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when he died it was buried with him between his side and his shirt."],[6733,"I asked Anas: Did 'Umar perform qunut? He said: One better than 'Umar performed qunut: the Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut."],[6734,"He prayed the dawn prayer behind the Prophet ﷺ, and when he raised his head from the second rak'ah he stood for a short while."],[6735,"We were forbidden from a town-dweller selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[6736,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping and gave the cupper his wages."],[6737,"Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like."],[6738,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[6739,"We were forbidden from a town-dweller selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[6740,"I asked Anas: Did the Prophet ﷺ dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that [age], but Abu Bakr dyed with henna."],[6741,"Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym and said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ hungry, so do you have anything? She said: A mudd, or half a mudd, of barley. He said: We will invite the Messenger of God ﷺ to it. So she made it into a loaf. Anas said: Abu Talhah sent me and said: Go and invite the Messenger of God ﷺ. I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, Abu Talhah invites you ..."],[6742,"On the day of Khaybar, the people fell upon the donkeys, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a caller, and he announced: God, Blessed and Exalted, and His Messenger forbid you from the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[6743,"There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah that was slow, or had a short gait. When he returned, he said: We found it to be a sea."],[6744,"When Ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, he began to look at it and turn it with a stick, and said: He was indeed handsome, or something similar. Anas said: I said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, or how often I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, kissing him, or kissing his lips."],[6745,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah."],[6746,"6756 6754 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6747,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for both of them together, meaning the Hajj and the Umrah. Then I met Ibn Umar and informed him, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram only for the Hajj.\" So I returned to Anas and informed him of Ibn Umar's statement, and he said: \"They consider us as nothing but children,\" or \"We were only children.\""],[6748,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for the Hajj and the Umrah."],[6749,"And I asked him: With what did the Prophet ﷺ enter ihram? He said: He entered ihram for the Hajj and the Umrah."],[6750,"Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, Amr b. al-Rabi' b. Tariq narrated to us, Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us from Humayd from Bakr from Anas. Mubarak b. Fadalah from Bakr."],[6751,"In the name of Allah. Then he wiped the loaf with it, and it swelled. Then he squeezed again, and something came out. He took it with his finger, then wiped the loaf with it, and it swelled. Then he squeezed a third time, and something came out of it. He took it with his finger, then said: In the name of Allah, and wiped the loaf with it, and it swelled until the bowl was full. Then he said: Permit ten. So I admitted ten, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand and spread his fingers in the middle of the bowl—or he said: he spread his fingers in the middle of the loaf—and said: Eat, in the name of Allah. So they ate until they were full. Then he said: Call for me another ten, while the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was hidden in the middle of the loaf, and he said: Eat, in the name of Allah. So they ate until they were full, then they left. They kept entering ten by ten, eating until they were full, and they were eighty-some men, and the middle of the loaf remained. And this hadith we do not know anyone who narrated it from Bakr, from Anas, except Mubarak b. Fadalah."],[6752,"O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you, no matter what it is, as long as you do not associate anything with Me."],[6753,"I used to give my paternal uncles a mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates to drink, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: \"Wine has been forbidden.\" He said: So we poured it out, and it was their drink that day."],[6754,"That a woman entered upon A'ishah, and with her were two daughters of hers. He said: A'ishah gave her three dates, and she gave each of them a date. Then she took a date to put it in her mouth. He said: The two girls looked at her. He said: She split it in two halves and gave each of them half of it, and she left. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and A'ishah told him what the woman had done, or about the woman's action. He said: \"She entered Paradise because of that.\""],[6755,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs."],[6756,"A group from 'Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, provide us with some milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go out to the camels.\" So they went out to the camels and drank from their milk and urine until they became fat. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drove away the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that someone go in pursuit of them. The sun had not yet declined when they were brought. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered concerning them, and their hands and feet were cut off, their eyes were gouged out with heated nails, and they were thrown into the harrah, asking for water but not given any, until they died."],[6757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to two horned rams and slaughtered them with his own hand."],[6758,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to a camel-driver named Anjashah: \"O Anjashah, drive gently with the glass vessels.\""],[6759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon Umm Sulaym, and she would spread a leather mat for him and he would take a midday nap on it. He used to sweat profusely, so she would take his sweat and put it in her perfume. And she would spread a small mat for him and he would pray on it."],[6760,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is established, then begin with the evening meal."],[6761,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[6762,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd, except for the iqamah."],[6763,"If you pray and do not know whether you finished on an even number or an odd one, then prostrate twice."],[6764,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?' He said, 'What have you prepared for it?' He said, 'Love of Allah and His Messenger.' He said, 'Then you are with whom you love.' He said: And he looked at a young boy. Anas said: He was of my age. He said, 'If this one lives—' I think he said, '—old age will not overtake him until the Hour is established.'"],[6765,"Some people of my nation will meet Jesus son of Mary ﷺ ."],[6766,"Abu Talhah cauterized me while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive, and more than one of the Ansar attended that."],[6767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to a household of the Ansar regarding ruqyah for fever and blistering."],[6768,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, supports this religion with men who have no share of reward."],[6769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding the well-trodden road that is approached from every direction: when its people dispute over it, its width is seven cubits. And he ruled that what you enclose is yours, and what they do not enclose belongs to Allah and His Messenger."],[6770,"The Hour will not be established until people boast about mosques."],[6771,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[6772,"A Jew crushed the head of a girl between two stones until she died, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded that the same be done to him."],[6773,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted seven [nights] for the virgin and three for the previously married."],[6774,"The Sunnah is seven for the virgin and three for the previously married."],[6775,"He said to his companions: You are better than your children, and your children are better than their children."],[6776,"When one of you becomes drowsy, let him leave until he knows what he is saying."],[6777,"The Prophet ﷺ used to travel and prolong his absence, and he would pray two rak'ahs until he returned."],[6778,"The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, and the strictest of them in the religion of Allah is 'Umar, and the most truthful in modesty of them is 'Uthman, and the most learned of them regarding the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh b. Jabal, and every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[6779,"The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, and the strictest of them in the religion of Allah is 'Umar, and the most truthful in modesty of them is 'Uthman, and the most learned of them regarding the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh b. Jabal, and the best reciter of them is Zayd b. Thabit, and every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[6780,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[6781,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar did not recite aloud 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim'."],[6782,"6792 6790 - Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, Muhammad b. Yusuf al-Faryabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from Abu Na'amah, from Anas, similarly."],[6783,"Humayd b. Hilal, from Anas. 6793. 6791 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas."],[6784,"I was riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting the talbiyah for Hajj and 'Umrah."],[6785,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us, Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Anas."],[6786,"The Prophet ﷺ announced the death of Ja'far when he was struck down, and his eyes were flowing with tears."],[6787,"It is as if I am looking at the dust of the procession of Jibril ﷺ rising among Banu Ghanm while he was heading toward Banu Qurayzah."],[6788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon Umm Sulaym, and she would spread for him a leather mat, and he would take a midday nap on it. She would take his sweat and put it in her perfume. And she would spread for him a small mat, and he would pray on it."],[6789,"The Prophet ﷺ prescribed for sciatica the tail fat of an Arabian ram, neither small nor large, which is melted and then one portion of it is drunk each day."],[6790,"He prescribed for sciatica the tail fat of an Arabian ram, neither small nor large, which is melted and divided into three portions, and one portion of it is drunk each day."],[6791,"A man from the Ansar prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he came to him. A mat was spread for him, and he prayed two rak'ahs on it. A man from the family of al-Jarud said to him, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the Duha prayer?\" He said, \"I never saw him pray it before that day.\""],[6792,"A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would come to us and pray—meaning in our home—so that we could take it as a place of prayer.\" So he came to him and prayed two rak'ahs of the Duha prayer in his house."],[6793,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on his mount."],[6794,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut in the Fajr prayer; I think he said: after the ruku'."],[6795,"The talbiyah of the Prophet ﷺ was: Labbayka ḥajjan ḥaqqan, taʿabbudan wa riqqan (Here I am, O Allah, for Hajj in truth, in devotion and servitude)."],[6796,"The talbiyah of Anas was: Labbayka ḥajjan ḥaqqan, taʿabbudan wa riqqan. And sometimes he said: He used to say that when he finished his talbiyah."],[6797,"Four will come out of the Fire—and Thābit said: two—then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will command that they be returned, or they will be returned to the Fire. Then the last of them will turn and say: 'O Lord, I thought that when You brought me out of it, You would not return me to it.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will command that he be taken to Paradise."],[6798,"A man stood up to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Where is my father?' He said: 'In the Fire.' When he turned away, he called him and said: 'Indeed, my father and your father are in the Fire.'"],[6799,"Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I will not marry women.' Others said: 'I will not eat meat.' Others said: 'I will not sleep on a bed.' Others said: 'I will fast and not break my fast.' This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'What is the matter with people who say such-and-such? But I pray and sleep, I fast and break my fast, and I marry women. Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me.'"],[6800,"I entered Paradise and heard a rustling sound in it. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'The daughter of Bilāl.' And I entered Paradise and heard a rustling sound in it. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'This is al-Ghumayṣāʾ, the daughter of Milḥān, and she is Umm Sulaym.'"],[6801,"A man will come out of the Fire, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'How did you find your abode?' He will say: 'O Lord, the worst abode.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'Would you ransom yourself from it with the world's weight in gold?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will say to him: 'You lie; I asked you for less than that and you did not do it.' And a man from the people of Paradise will be brought and it will be said to him: 'O son of Adam, how did you find your abode?' He will say: 'The best abode.' He will say: 'Then what do you ask of Me?' He will say: 'I do not ask You except that You return me to the world so that I may be killed in Your cause ten times.'"],[6802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah from one of his expeditions or journeys, and the black people of Madinah were dancing before him, saying in their dialect: 'Muhammad has come, a righteous man.'"],[6803,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and he gave him a flock of sheep between two mountains. He went to his people and said: 'O my people, embrace Islam, for Muhammad gives such gifts that he does not fear poverty.'"],[6804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was given al-Kawthar. I struck my hand upon its drinking place, and behold it was pungent musk, and behold its pebbles were pearls, and behold its two banks — I think he said — were domes running upon the earth, running without being split.'"],[6805,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Madinah, Abū Bakr — may Allah have mercy on him — was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū Bakr ؓ had been to Syria and was known, while the Prophet ﷺ was not known. They would say to Abū Bakr: 'Who is this in front of you?' He would say: 'This is the one who guides the way.' When they drew near to Madinah, he sent word to the Anṣār, and they came. Anas said: 'I have never seen a day more beautiful or more radiant than the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us, nor a day more ugly or darker than the day he died ﷺ.'"],[6806,"No person was more beloved to the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, yet they would not stand up for him because they knew he disliked that ﷺ."],[6807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lick his fingers when he ate."],[6808,"There are three qualities, whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything besides them; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to being a Jew or a Christian."],[6809,"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is recorded against him; but if he does it, an evil deed is recorded."],[6810,"Abu Talhah used to shoot in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was an archer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was behind him. Whenever he shot, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would raise himself to see where his arrow landed, and Abu Talhah would push the chest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from behind and say: \"Like this, so no arrow hits you.\""],[6811,"I saw people rushing to the pillars when the mu'adhdhin called the adhan for the Maghrib prayer, praying two rak'ahs before Maghrib."],[6812,"Abu Bakr said: 6822 6820 - And this hadith was narrated to us by al-Hasan b. Yahya al-Aruzzi: Muhammad b. al-Salt Abu Ya'la al-Thawri narrated to us: Abu Safwan al-Makki narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Thabit, from Anas, with something similar. And this hadith has been narrated from Thabit, from Anas, by more than one narrator, and we do not know of 'Ata' b. Abi Rabah narrating from Thabit, from Anas, except this hadith."],[6813,"A group of eighty men from the people of Makkah descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the mountain of al-Tan'im at the time of the Fajr prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took them as captives of war, then he pardoned them. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And it is He who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them' (Quran 48:24), the verse."],[6814,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam and formed him, Iblis began to circle around him. When he saw that he was a hollow creation, he knew that he would not be able to keep from disobeying—or words to that effect."],[6815,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."],[6816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to descend from the minbar on Friday, and a man would speak to him about his need until he reached his place of prayer."],[6817,"He recited on the minbar: 'So when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He made it collapse to dust' (Quran 7:143). He said: \"Like this,\" and he spread his palm and placed his thumb on his little finger. Humayd said to him: \"Do you narrate something like this?\" He struck him on his chest and said: \"What is the matter with you, O Humayd? Anas narrates it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you say this to me?\""],[6818,"The Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu 'Ubaydah and Abu Talhah."],[6819,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sleeping in the house of Umm Sulaym, and she came to him while he was uttering the istirjāʿ (saying 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'). She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why are you saying istirjāʿ?' He said, 'Because of an army that will come down from the direction of Iraq seeking a man from Madinah whom Allah will protect from them. When they ascend al-Baydāʾ from Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, they will be swallowed up, and neither will their highest reach their lowest nor their lowest reach their highest until the Day of Resurrection; and their places of destruction will be scattered.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how can they all be swallowed up while their places of destruction are scattered?' He said, 'Indeed among them—or in them—is one who was compelled.'"],[6820,"That Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās, when the verse 'Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet' was revealed, sat in his house and said, 'I am one of the people of the Fire. I used to raise my voice above that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Prophet ﷺ noticed his absence and said, 'Why do I not see Thābit? Is he ill?' Saʿd said, 'He is my neighbor, and I know of no complaint of his.' Saʿd mentioned that to Thābit and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has noticed your absence.' He said, 'This verse has been revealed, and I used to raise my voice above that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I am one of the people of the Fire.' Saʿd mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'Rather, he is one of the people of Paradise.'"],[6821,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some boys and greeted them."],[6822,"That he observed continuous fasting, and some of the people also observed continuous fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a way that would make those who go to extremes abandon their extremism. I am not like you; I remain in a state where my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.'"],[6823,"And ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Ghiyāth narrated to us: Ḥammād b. Salamah narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[6824,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said, 'Ride it.' He said, 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said, 'Ride it, even if it is a sacrificial camel.'"],[6825,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams that were white with black markings."],[6826,"That the Prophet ﷺ visited a sick man who had become like a fledgling. He said, 'What did you used to supplicate? Or what did you used to ask your Lord for well-being?' He said, 'I used to say: O Allah, whatever You would punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world.' He said, 'Glory be to Allah! You will never be able to bear it—or you cannot bear it. Why did you not say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire?' The man said it, and he recovered."],[6827,"That the Prophet ﷺ saw a man being supported between two men. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What is the matter with him?' They said, 'He vowed to walk to the Hajj.' He said, 'Order him to ride, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is not in need of his torturing himself.'"],[6828,"Indeed, when the prayer was about to be established, a man would present himself to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and speak to him about some need until some of the people would fall asleep."],[6829,"Muḥammad b. Miskīn narrated to us: ʿAmr b. al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, from Yaḥyā b. Ayyūb, from Ḥumayd, from Thābit, from Anas."],[6830,"And I found in my book from Muḥammad b. Sahl b. ʿAskar: Saʿīd b. al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Yaḥyā b. Ayyūb narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Thābit, from Anas."],[6831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment."],[6832,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a graveyard and heard a voice from a grave. He said: \"Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have made you hear the voice of this grave, or the voice of the one in the grave.\""],[6833,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[6834,"When he raised his head from bowing, he would stand so long that a person would say: He has forgotten. And when he raised his head from prostration, he would sit so long that we would say: He has forgotten."],[6835,"When he raised his head from bowing, he would stand so long that we would say: He has forgotten, due to the length of the standing."],[6836,"Muhammad b. Bashshar Bundar narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6837,"Patience is at the first shock."],[6838,"He did not raise his hands in any of his supplications except in the prayer for rain."],[6839,"A person is with the one he loves."],[6840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[6841,"Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection."],[6842,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling and a camel driver was chanting to drive the women's camels, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Drive gently with the glass vessels.\""],[6843,"None of you should wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him. But if he must do something, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take my soul when death is better for me."],[6844,"6854 6851 - Al-Jarrah b. Makhlad narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[6845,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on a mat."],[6846,"Abu Talhah would hardly fast during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ - meaning voluntary fasts - because of military campaigns. After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, they did not see him break his fast except on Eid al-Adha or Eid al-Fitr."],[6847,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin the recitation with 'All praise is due to Allah, Lord of all the worlds.'"],[6848,"Abdullah b. Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, Yazid b. Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas."],[6849,"The Ansar gathered. Someone said: Let us go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he may make our water flow freely, for the water-drawing camels have become hard upon us. They gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: Welcome to the Ansar, welcome to the Ansar, welcome to the Ansar - three times. You will not ask me for anything today but that I will give it to you, and I will not ask for anything for you today but that it will be granted to me. Some of them said to others: Seize the opportunity of his supplication and ask for forgiveness. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come so that you may ask Allah to forgive us. He said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."],[6850,"There was a black person in the mosque and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked about him, and they said: He has died. The Prophet ﷺ went to his grave and prayed over him."],[6851,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became seriously ill, distress kept overwhelming him. Fatimah supported him against her chest and said: Alas, the distress! For the distress of my father! The Prophet ﷺ said: There is no distress upon your father after today. She said: O my father, how close he is to his Lord! O my father, the Gardens of Firdaws are his abode. O my father, to Jibril we announce his death. O my father, he answered a Lord who called him. Anas said: Fatimah said: Or he said, then she said: O Anas! Are your souls pleased that you throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"],[6852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the most generous of people and the bravest of people. The people of Madinah were alarmed one night, and he went towards the sound. He met them riding a bareback horse belonging to Abu Talhah, with a sword around his neck, saying: O people, do not be alarmed, do not be alarmed. He said about the horse: We have found it to be a sea, or indeed it is a sea. The horse of Abu Talhah used to be slow, but it was never outrun after that."],[6853,"This verse was revealed: 'And you concealed within yourself what Allah was to disclose' regarding Zaynab bt. Jahsh."],[6854,"I have not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hold a wedding feast for any of his wives, or for any woman among his wives, as he did for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."],[6855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw on ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf a trace of yellow [perfume], so he said: 'Mah?' or 'What is this?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I married a woman for the weight of a date stone in gold.' He said: 'May God bless you. Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[6856,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah and established brotherhood between his companions. He paired ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf with Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ. Saʿd said to him: 'O my brother, I am among the wealthiest of the people of Madinah, so take half of my wealth. I have two wives; I will divorce whichever you wish [for you to marry].' ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to him: 'May God bless you in your family and wealth. Direct me to the market.' So he directed him to the market, and he bought and sold. He was absent from the Prophet ﷺ for some days. Then the Prophet ﷺ saw him with a trace of yellow on his garment, and said: 'Mahyam?' He said: 'I have married a woman.' He said: 'For how much?' He said: 'For the weight of a date stone in gold.' He said: 'May God bless you. Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[6857,"He was asked about the dyeing [of hair] of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'If I wished, I could count his white hairs.' He mentioned that he did not dye, but that Abū Bakr and ʿUmar did. Abū Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and ʿUmar dyed with pure henna."],[6858,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ called for water, and a wide shallow bowl was brought. The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his palm in it, and the people began performing ablution. We estimated them to be between ninety and one hundred. I kept looking at the water as if it was gushing from between his fingers."],[6859,"Whoever cares for two daughters, or three, or two sisters, or three, until they marry or he dies [leaving them], he and I will be in Paradise like these two - and Ḥammād joined his index and middle fingers."],[6860,"I was in the house of Abū Ṭalḥa - and he mentioned a group of the Prophet's companions on the day wine was forbidden. Their drink that day was nothing but faḍīkh, made from unripe dates and ripe dates. A crier called out. Some of the people said: 'Go out and see what he is saying.' So I went out, and there was the crier of the Messenger of God ﷺ proclaiming: 'Wine has been forbidden.' So [the wine] was poured out in the streets of Madinah. I said to Abū Ṭalḥa: 'What do you say?' He said: 'Spill it.' So I spilled it. Ḥammād said: 'I do not know whether this is part of the hadith or something Thābit said.' His companions said to him: 'So-and-so was killed on the day of Badr, and so-and-so, while it was still in their bellies.' Then God, blessed and exalted, sent down: 'There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds' [for what they consumed previously]."],[6861,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought something, he would say: 'Take it to the house of so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadījah.'"],[6862,"No two people love each other for the sake of God, blessed and exalted, except that the better of them is the one who has stronger love for his companion."],[6863,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, I love this sūrah,' meaning 'Say: He is God, the One.' He said: 'Your love for it will admit you to Paradise.'"],[6864,"On the day the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Madinah, everything in it was illuminated. On the day he died, everything in it became dark. We had not finished burying the Messenger of God ﷺ - we were still in the process of his burial - before we found our hearts changed."],[6865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to visit the Anṣār. When he came to the dwellings of the Anṣār, their children would gather around him, and he would supplicate for them, wipe their heads, and greet them. He came to the door of Saʿd and greeted them, saying: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.' Saʿd responded, but the Prophet ﷺ did not hear him, until he had greeted three times. The Prophet ﷺ would not exceed three greetings; if permission was granted, [he entered], otherwise he left. So the Prophet ﷺ turned back. Saʿd came rushing and said: 'O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I heard every greeting and responded to you, but I wanted you to increase our share of peace and mercy. Enter, O Messenger of God.' So he entered and sat down. Saʿd brought food close to him, and the Prophet ﷺ ate from it. When he wanted to leave, he said: 'The righteous have eaten your food, the fasting have broken their fast with you, and the angels have prayed for you.'"],[6866,"Rain fell on us while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and bared part of his garment so that the rain fell on him. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, why did you do this?' He said: 'Because it is newly come from its Lord.'"],[6867,"There was a man among the Ansar who was ill. The Prophet ﷺ came to visit him but met him in the market, so he greeted him and said, “How are you, O so-and-so?” He said, “I am well, O Messenger of God.” He said, “I hope for God and fear my sins.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “They do not come together in the heart of a servant in this situation except that God grants him what he hopes for and secures him from what he fears.”"],[6868,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ broke his fast, he would break it with dried dates or fresh dates; if there were none, he would sip a few sips of water."],[6869,"Let one of you ask his Lord for his need, or all his needs, even if he asks for his sandal strap when it breaks, and even if he asks for salt."],[6870,"When the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah, ʿAbd Allāh b. Rawāḥah walked in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “Clear the way, sons of the disbelievers, from his path. Today we strike you upon its interpretation, just as we struck you upon its revelation—a strike that removes the head from its resting place, and makes the friend forget his friend...” ʿUmar ؓ said, “O Ibn Rawāḥah, in front of the Messenger of God and in the sanctuary of God you recite poetry?” He said, “Leave him, for by Him in whose hand is my soul, this is harder on them than the striking of swords.”"],[6871,"ʿAlī b. Muslim narrated to us: Sayyār b. Ḥātim narrated to us, from Jaʿfar b. Sulaymān, from Thābit, from Anas."],[6872,"Women and perfume have been made dear to me, and the delight of my eye has been placed in prayer."],[6873,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to go on military expeditions with Umm Sulaym and women with her, and they would provide water and tend to the wounded."],[6874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was passing along a road, and a black woman passed by. A man said to her, “Make way.” She said, “The road is wide for him.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Leave her, for she is defiant.”"],[6875,"Whoever God has promised a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him; and whoever He has promised a punishment for a deed, He has the choice regarding it."],[6876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited to us: “He is worthy of piety and worthy of forgiveness” (74:56). He said: Your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: “I am worthy of piety, so no other should be associated with Me. And I am worthy to forgive the one who is pious and does not associate anything with Me.” Abū Qutaybah said in his hadith: “And whoever fears Me and does not set up with Me a partner, then I am worthy to forgive him.”"],[6877,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “Those who say, ‘Our Lord is God,’ and then remain steadfast” (41:30). He said: “People have said it, then most of them disbelieved. Whoever says it until he dies upon it is among those who remain steadfast.”"],[6878,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought dates of the Rayyān variety. He said, “How did you get these dates?” They said, “We had unpollinated dates, so we sold two sāʿs for one sāʿ.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Return it to its owner.”"],[6879,"A man said, “O Messenger of God, I have not left any need or want [unsatisfied].” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then this refuses that.”"],[6880,"The prophets are alive in their graves, praying."],[6881,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together."],[6882,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the best fasting. He said, “The best fasting is fasting Shaʿban in honor of Ramadan, and the best charity is charity in Ramadan.”"],[6883,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My father died without performing the Hajj of Islam.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do you think that if your father had a debt, you would pay it on his behalf?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then it is a debt upon him, so pay it.”"],[6884,"The Messenger of God ﷺ often said, “Are you unable to be like Abu Damdam?” They said, “O Messenger of God, who is Abu Damdam?” He said, “He was a man before us. When morning came, he would say: O God, I give my honor as charity to whoever wrongs me.”"],[6885,"The example of the believer is like a stalk of grain: it bends sometimes and stands upright sometimes."],[6886,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque, no one would raise his head to him out of awe except Abu Bakr and Umar. He would smile at them and they would smile at him — I think one of them said — they would smile at him and he would smile at them."],[6887,"They name them Muhammad, then they insult them?!"],[6888,"The example of my community is like rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[6889,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Umm Salamah for goods worth ten dirhams."],[6890,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad over a detachment of cavalry. When he came to him, he said, “How did you find it?” He said, “I saw them rising and falling until I thought that I was not that.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “That is it.” Al-Miqdad said, “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never act as a governor over any task.” They would say to him, “Come forward and lead us in prayer,” but he would refuse."],[6891,"Seven hundred camels belonging to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf arrived carrying all kinds of goods. The people of Madinah marveled, and 'A'ishah asked, \"What is this?\" They said, \"A caravan belonging to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf carrying all kinds of goods.\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: I saw 'Abd al-Rahman entering Paradise crawling on his hands and knees.\" The news reached him, so he said, \"O 'A'ishah, what is this report that has reached me?\" She mentioned it to him, and he said, \"I call upon you to witness that it—with its saddles, its saddlecloths, and its loads—is for the sake of Allah.\""],[6892,"The angel of rain sought permission to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day he said to Umm Salamah, \"O Umm Salamah, see who is at the door. Let no one enter upon us until he leaves.\" Al-Husayn came and entered, and he began to leap onto the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Prophet ﷺ began kissing him. He said, \"Do you love him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, your community will kill him. If you wish, I will show you the place where they will kill him.\" He grasped a handful, and there was red soil."],[6893,"The forerunners are four: I am the forerunner of the Arabs; Salman is the forerunner of the Persians; Bilal is the forerunner of the Abyssinians; and Suhayb is the forerunner of the Romans."],[6894,"When you see those who praise people, throw dust in their faces."],[6895,"\"O so-and-so, did you do such-and-such?\" He said, \"No, by the One besides whom there is no god, I did not do it,\" while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that he had done it. He repeated it to him several times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is expiated for you by your affirmation of 'there is no god but Allah.'\""],[6896,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you we are in one state, but when we part from you we are in another.\" He said, \"How are you with your Lord?\" They said, \"Allah is our Lord in secret and in public.\" He said, \"That is not hypocrisy.\""],[6897,"He forbade that a slave be led between two men."],[6898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Talhah, \"Convey peace to your people, and tell them that—as far as I know them—they are chaste and patient.\""],[6899,"Take the predawn meal, for there is blessing in the predawn meal."],[6900,"\"When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, graze freely.\" They said, \"What are the gardens of Paradise?\" He said, \"Circles of remembrance.\""],[6901,"Gabriel kept urging me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[6902,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."],[6903,"That ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, may God have mercy on him, came to Abū Bakr, may God have mercy on him, and said: O Abū Bakr, what prevents you from marrying Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: He will not marry me to her. He said: If he does not marry you to her, then who will he marry? For you are among the most honored of people to him and the earliest of them in Islam. He said: So Abū Bakr, may God have mercy on him, went to ʿĀʾishah ؓ and said: O ʿĀʾishah, when you see from the Messenger of God ﷺ good spirits and attention toward you, mention to him that I have mentioned Fāṭimah, perhaps God will make her easy for me. He said: So the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and she saw from him good spirits and attention, and she said: O Messenger of God, Abū Bakr mentioned Fāṭimah and ordered me to mention her to you. He said: Until the decree descends. He said: So Abū Bakr returned to her, and she said: O my father, I wish I had not mentioned to him what you mentioned. Then Abū Bakr met ʿUmar, and Abū Bakr told ʿUmar what ʿĀʾishah had informed him. So ʿUmar went to Ḥafṣah and said: O Ḥafṣah, when you see from the Messenger of God ﷺ attention, meaning toward you, mention me to him and mention Fāṭimah to him, perhaps God will make her easy for me. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ met Ḥafṣah, and she saw his good spirits and saw from him attention, so she mentioned Fāṭimah ؓ to him. He said: Until the decree descends. Then ʿUmar met Ḥafṣah, and she said: O my father, I wish I had not mentioned anything to him. So ʿUmar went to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and said: What prevents you from marrying Fāṭimah? He said: I fear that he will not marry me to her. He said: If he does not marry you to her, then who will he marry? For you are the nearest of God's creation to him. So ʿAlī went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he had no one like ʿĀʾishah or like Ḥafṣah. He said: So he met the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I want to marry Fāṭimah. He said: Then do so. He said: I have nothing but my armor. He said: Gather what you can and bring it to me. He said: So he brought him twelve ūqiyyahs — four hundred and eighty — and brought them to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who married him to Fāṭimah. He took three handfuls and gave them to Umm Ayman, saying: Set aside one handful for perfume — I think he said — and the rest for what a woman needs from household goods. When she finished the trousseau and brought them into a house, he said: O ʿAlī, do not approach your wife until I come to you. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them, and there was Fāṭimah veiled, ʿAlī sitting, and Umm Ayman in the house. He said: O Umm Ayman, bring me a bowl of water. She brought him a cup containing water. He drank from it, then rinsed his mouth into it, then handed it to Fāṭimah, and she drank from it. He took some of it and sprinkled it on her forehead, between her shoulders, and her chest. Then he gave it to ʿAlī and said: O ʿAlī, drink. Then he took some of it and sprinkled it on his forehead and between his shoulders. Then he said: O people of my house, remove from them the impurity and purify them thoroughly. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ and Umm Ayman left, and he said: O ʿAlī, your wife."],[6904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting in a circle, and he wanted to get up. A boy stood up and handed him his sandals. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You sought the pleasure of your Lord, ؓ. And that boy had a similar standing in Madinah until he was martyred."],[6905,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I commit sins. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When you sin, seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said: I seek forgiveness, then I go back and sin. He said: When you sin, go back and seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said: I seek forgiveness, then I go back and sin. He said: When you sin, go back and seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said it the fourth time, and he said: Seek forgiveness from your Lord until Satan is the one who is exhausted."],[6906,"I was with Anas b. Mālik, and he had a daughter with him. He said: A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and offered herself to him. She said: O Messenger of God, do you have any need for women? His daughter said: How little modesty she has, or something similar. He said: She is better than you. She desired the Messenger of God ﷺ and offered herself to him."],[6907,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say on the day of the Trench: By God, were it not for God, we would not have been guided, nor fasted, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us."],[6908,"The Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar. Al-Ḥajjāj b. ʿIlāṭ said: O Messenger of God, I have wealth in Makkah and family there, and I want to go to them. Am I absolved if I speak against you or say something? The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted him to say whatever he wished. When he arrived, he went to his wife and said: Gather whatever you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his companions, for they have been raided and their wealth has been taken. He said: That spread through Makkah, and the Muslims became despondent, while the polytheists showed joy and delight. He said: The news reached al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he sat in his gathering, unable to stand. Maʿmar said: ʿUthmān al-Jazarī reported to me from Miqsam, who said: Al-ʿAbbās took a son of his named Qutham, who resembled the Messenger of God ﷺ, and lay down, placing him on his chest, saying: My beloved Qutham, who resembles the one with the lofty nose, the Prophet of blessings, in spite of those who resent it. Maʿmar said: Thābit said, from Anas: Then he sent for al-Ḥajjāj b. ʿIlāṭ and said: Woe to you, what have you brought? Al-Ḥajjāj said to his servant: Convey greetings to Abū al-Faḍl and tell him: Let him prepare a private room for his son, for the matter is as he likes. His servant came, and when he reached the door, he said: Rejoice, Abū al-Faḍl. Al-ʿAbbās jumped up joyfully and kissed him between the eyes. The servant informed him of what al-Ḥajjāj had said, and al-ʿAbbās embraced him. Then al-Ḥajjāj came and informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoils, and God's shares were distributed among their wealth. The Messenger of God ﷺ chose Ṣafiyyah bt. Ḥuyayy and took her for himself. He gave her the choice between freeing her and her being his wife, or joining her family, and she chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for wealth I had here, to gather it and take it away. I asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he permitted me to say whatever I wished. So conceal my matter for three days, then say what you like. His wife gathered what she had of jewelry or goods and gave it to him. After three days, al-ʿAbbās came to the wife of al-Ḥajjāj and said: What has al-Ḥajjāj done? She told him that he had left and said: Do not be grieved, Abū al-Faḍl, by what you heard. He said: Indeed, God will not grieve me, and by the praise of God, it was only what we love."],[6909,"6919 6917 - Al-Ḥusayn b. Mahdī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed us, from Thābit, from Anas."],[6910,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ took the pledge from the women, he took from them that they would not wail. They said: O Messenger of God, there are women who helped us in the time of ignorance; shall we help them in Islam? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There is no helping in Islam, no shighār in Islam, no jalab, and no janab. Whoever plunders is not one of us."],[6911,"Al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah wanted to marry a woman and mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create harmony between you. And I saw in another place: to create harmony between you. He said: So he did and married her, and he mentioned their compatibility."],[6912,"I did not count on the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ except fourteen white hairs."],[6913,"A man will intercede for two men and three."],[6914,"There was a man from the desert people named Zāhir b. Ḥarām, or b. Ḥizām — ʿAbd al-Razzāq was unsure — and he used to send gifts to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the desert. The Prophet said: Zāhir is our desert, and we are — I think he said — people of a settled area, or his settled area. The Prophet ﷺ loved him, and he was an ugly man. The Prophet ﷺ came to him while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind until he pressed his back to his stomach. The man said: Release me from this. He said: The Prophet ﷺ turned to him and began saying: Who will buy the slave? The man said: O Messenger of God, by God, you will find me unsellable. The Prophet ﷺ said: But you are not unsellable with God. And he said: But you are with God profitable."],[6915,"The Hour will not come upon anyone saying: Allah, Allah."],[6916,"Modesty is never in a thing except that it adorns it, and obscenity is never in a thing except that it disgraces it."],[6917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed on behalf of Julaybib to a woman from the Ansar to her father. He said, 'Until I consult her mother.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Then yes.' The man went to his wife and mentioned that to her. She said, 'No, by Allah! Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ find no one but Julaybib? We have refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so.' The girl was in her curtain listening. He and his wife went intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ. The girl said, 'Where are you going? Do you intend to reject the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? If he has approved him for you, then marry me to him.' It was as if she had untied a fetter from her parents—or words to that effect. They said, 'You have spoken the truth.' Her father went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'If you are pleased with him, then we are pleased.' He said, 'So he married her to him. Then the people of Madinah were alarmed, and Julaybib rode out. They found him killed, and around him they found as many as Allah willed of the polytheists whom he had killed.' Anas said: 'I saw her, and she was the most generous widow in Madinah.'"],[6918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said a hadith at which we were not happier since we came to know Islam. He said: 'The believer is rewarded for guiding someone to the way, for removing harm from the road, and he is rewarded for expressing himself with his tongue on behalf of the non-Arab. He is rewarded for coming to his wife, even to the point that he is rewarded for a piece of merchandise at the edge of his garment: he touches it and ties its place—or words to that effect—and his heart beats for it, and Allah returns it to him and writes for him its reward.'"],[6919,"We were forbidden in the Qur'an to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ anything. It pleased us when an intelligent man from the people of the desert came and asked him while we listened. A man from the desert came and said: 'Your messenger came to us and informed us that you claim that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent you.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Who created the heaven?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who created the earth?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who set up the mountains?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who placed benefits in them?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Then by the One who created the heaven, created the earth, set up the mountains, and placed benefits in them, did Allah send you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that five prayers are due on us every day and night.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that zakah is due on our wealth.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that fasting a month in our year is due on us.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that pilgrimage to the House is due on whoever is able to make a way to it.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By the One who sent you, I will not add anything to them nor subtract anything from them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he is truthful, he will surely enter Paradise.'"],[6920,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer, people would come to him with their vessels—or vessels containing water—so that he would dip his hand in them, seeking the blessing of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sometimes they would come on a cold morning, and he would dip his hand in them."],[6921,"The Prophet ﷺ walked instead of a riding companion of his."],[6922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'A boy was born to me tonight, and I named him after my father Ibrahim ﷺ . Then I handed him to a woman called Umm Sayf, the wife of a blacksmith called Abu Yusuf.' He went off and I followed him. We came to Abu Yusuf, and the house was full. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the infant, embraced him, and said what Allah willed he should say. Anas said: 'I saw him struggling for breath, and the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ filled with tears. He said: \"The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we say only what pleases our Lord. By Allah, O Ibrahim, we are saddened by you.\"'"],[6923,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to the young men of Quraysh and said: 'O group of young men, whoever among you is able to afford marriage, let him marry—or let him get married—; otherwise, let him fast, for it is a means of suppressing desire for him.'"],[6924,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I intend to travel, so provide me with provisions.' He said: 'May Allah provide you with piety.' He said: 'Give me more, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'And may He forgive your sin.' He said: 'Give me more, by my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'And may He direct you to good wherever you are.'"],[6925,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up at night, he would cleanse himself, perform ablution, and use the toothstick, then he would send someone to seek perfume in the quarters of his wives."],[6926,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has servants who know people by discernment."],[6927,"If you did not sin, I would fear for you something greater than it: self-admiration."],[6928,"Shall I inform you of the best among you? They said: Yes. He said: Those of you with the best character—or he said—the best in conduct."],[6929,"When Adam prostrated, Satan said: The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate, and he prostrated, so he will have Paradise. I was commanded to prostrate, but I disobeyed, so I will have the Fire."],[6930,"When a man pleased him, he would order him to pray."],[6931,"It was said: O Messenger of God, who are the people of Paradise? He said: Whoever does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves. It was said: Who are the people of the Fire? He said: Whoever does not die until his ears are filled with what he hates."],[6932,"Those who frequent God's houses are God's people."],[6933,"An angel is entrusted with the Scale. The son of Adam is brought and made to stand between the two pans of the Scale. If his scale is heavy, an angel calls out in a voice audible to all creatures: So-and-so has attained happiness, after which he will never be wretched. If his scale is light, an angel calls out in a voice audible to all creatures: So-and-so has become wretched, after which he will never be happy."],[6934,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under God's protection—I think he said—so let not God demand anything of you in respect of His protection."],[6935,"The best of our young men are those who emulate our elders, and the worst of our elders are those who emulate our young men."],[6936,"God does not accept prayer without purification—I think he said—nor charity from misappropriated wealth."],[6937,"Barirah was a slave woman, then she was freed. She was given charity, and some of that charity was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. It was said to him: O Messenger of God, this is from what was given as charity to Barirah. He said: For her it is charity, and for us it is a gift."],[6938,"Creatures are God's dependents, and the most beloved of them to God is the one most beneficial to His dependents."],[6939,"The Prophet ﷺ met a man called Harithah in one of the alleys of Madinah and said, \"How are you this morning, O Harithah?\" He said, \"I have become a true believer.\" He said, \"Every faith has a reality, so what is the reality of your faith?\" He said, \"My soul turned away from the world, so I stayed thirsty (fasting) and spent my nights sleepless (in worship), and it is as if I see the Throne of my Lord appearing, and it is as if I see the people of Paradise in Paradise enjoying themselves, and the people of the Fire in the Fire being punished.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have hit the mark, so hold fast. A believer whose heart Allah has illumined.\""],[6940,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ for worship and striving, and he said, \"How does your companion remember death?\" They said, \"We do not hear him mention it.\" He said, \"Your companion is not there [i.e., not at the level of true devotion].\""],[6941,"Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are: Maryam bt. Imran, Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad."],[6942,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with his companions, a man came to him wearing travel clothes, weaving through the people until he sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted. He placed his hand on the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, what is Islam?\" He said, \"Testifying that there is no god but Allah, alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting the month of Ramadan, and performing pilgrimage to the House if you are able to make a way to it.\" He said, \"If I do that, am I a Muslim?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken truth.\" The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Look at him, he asks him and then confirms him, as if he knows more than him,\" and they did not recognize the man. Then he said, \"O Muhammad, what is faith?\" He said, \"Faith in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, the prophets, death, resurrection, reckoning, Paradise, the Fire, and all of the divine decree.\" He said, \"If I do that, am I a believer?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken truth.\" He said, \"O Muhammad, what is excellence (ihsan)?\" He said, \"To fear Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said, \"If I do that, am I a doer of excellence?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken truth.\" He said, \"O Muhammad, when is the Hour?\" He said, \"The one asked about it knows no more than the questioner.\" Then the man turned away and left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Bring me the man.\" They followed him, seeking him, but they saw nothing. They returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we followed the man and sought him, but we saw nothing.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"That was Gabriel ﷺ who came to you to teach you your religion.\""],[6943,"I was commanded to use the siwak so much that I feared I would become toothless, or until I feared for my gums and teeth."],[6944,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Aishah, \"When fresh dates come, congratulate me.\""],[6945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon when the people rose and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the rain has ceased, souls are exhausted, and the animals have perished. Pray to Allah to send us rain.\" He said, \"By Allah, we do not see in the sky even a wisp of cloud.\" Then a cloud formed and spread, and then it rained. They were rained upon until the next Friday. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to deliver the sermon, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and roads have been cut off. Pray to Allah to hold it back from us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, \"O Allah, around us and not upon us.\" The clouds dispersed from Madinah, and it rained around Madinah but not in it."],[6946,"Ismail b. Ishaq and Ibrahim b. Nasr narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us, from Hammad b. Zayd, from Yunus, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6947,"Muhammad b. Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Amr b. Rudayh narrated to us, from Ata b. Abi Maymunah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And no one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hammad b. Zayd."],[6948,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not done deeds like theirs.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[6949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night when half the night—or nearly half the night—had passed. He said, \"I began to look at the glint of his ring on his hand.\""],[6950,"When wine was forbidden, we overturned it and what was in it."],[6951,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he placed me on his right side."],[6952,"The expiation for a gathering is to say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance."],[6953,"Women came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have gone off with the merit and jihad in the path of Allah, so what deed do we have by which we can attain the deed of those who strive in the path of Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever of you remains—or a word like that—in her house, she attains the deed of the one who strives in the path of Allah."],[6954,"My intercession is for the people of major sins among my community."],[6955,"I was brought al-Buraq, and it is a white riding beast, taller than a donkey and shorter than a mule. It places its hoof at the limit of its sight. He said: I mounted it and it carried me until I came to the gate of Jerusalem. I tied the beast to the ring to which the prophets tie it. He said: Then I entered the mosque and prayed two units in it, then I came out. Then Jibril ﷺ came to me with a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk, and I chose the milk. Jibril said: You have chosen the natural disposition. Then he ascended with us to the lowest heaven, and Jibril ﷺ sought permission to enter. It was said: Who are you? He said: I am Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. He said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. He said: So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Adam. He welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the second heaven, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: I am Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. He said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. He said: So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw the two maternal cousins, Isa and Yahya. They welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the third heaven, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Yusuf, and indeed he had been given half of all beauty. He welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the fourth, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. He said: So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Idris. He welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: \"And We raised him to a high station\" (19:57). He said: Then he ascended with us to the fifth heaven, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. He said: So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Harun. He welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the sixth heaven, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad ﷺ. It was said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Musa ﷺ. He welcomed me and prayed for good. Then he ascended with us to the seventh heaven, and Jibril sought permission. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent to? He said: He has been sent to. So it was opened for us, and behold, I saw Ibrahim ﷺ, and he was leaning against the Much-Frequented House. He welcomed me and prayed for good for me. And indeed, seventy thousand angels enter it—meaning the Much-Frequented House—and then they do not return to it. Then he took me to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants, and its fruits were like large jars. When it was covered by what covered it of the command of Allah, it changed, and no one of Allah's creation could describe it because of its beauty. Then He revealed to me what He revealed, and He obligated upon me fifty prayers every day and night. I descended until I came to Musa, and he said: What has your Lord obligated upon your community? I said: Fifty prayers every day and night. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction, for your community will not be able to bear that. I tested the Children of Israel and came to know them. He said: So I returned to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and said: O Lord, lighten for my community. So He reduced five from me. He said: Then I returned to Musa, and he said: What did you do? I said: He reduced five from me. He said: Your community will not be able to bear that, so return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community. I kept going back between my Lord and Musa, and He reduced five each time, until He said: O Muhammad, they are five prayers every day and night, each prayer counting as ten, so that is fifty prayers. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him; if he does it, ten are written for him. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written; if he does it, one evil deed is written. He said: I descended until I came to Musa ﷺ and told him that. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. I said: I have returned to my Lord until I felt ashamed."],[6956,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, split open his chest, took out the heart, split the heart, and extracted from it a clot. He said: This is the share of Satan in you. Then he washed it in a golden basin with water of Zamzam, then he joined it together and returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother and said: Muhammad has been killed. He came to meet them, and his color was changed. Anas said: I used to see the trace of the stitching thread in his chest."],[6957,"A morning expedition in the path of Allah, or an evening expedition, is better than the world and all that it contains."],[6958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ practiced continuous fasting, and some people among his companions also practiced it. He said: If the month were extended for me, I would continue fasting in a way that would make those who go to extremes abandon their extremism. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."],[6959,"A Persian man who was a neighbor of the Prophet ﷺ made a fragrant broth. One day he came to the Prophet ﷺ while Aisha was at his side, and he gestured to him with his hand—meaning he signaled to him with his hand—indicating that he and Aisha should come. He said: No. Then he gestured to him again, indicating that he and Aisha should come, and he signaled to him: No. Then he gestured to him, and he signaled: Yes, so he came to us."],[6960,"When he retired to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah who has fed us, given us drink, and sheltered us. How many there are who have no one to suffice them and no shelter."],[6961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while Abdullah b. Salam was in his palm grove. When he heard of him, he came and said: O Muhammad, I will ask you about things that no one knows except a prophet. If you inform me of them, then you are the Messenger of Allah. He asked him about resemblance, about the first thing with which people will be gathered, and about the first thing the people of Paradise will eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Jibril informed me of them just now. Abdullah said: Indeed, that one is an enemy of the Jews. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: As for resemblance, if the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the child resembles him, and if the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the child resembles her. As for the first thing with which people will be gathered, it is a fire that will come from the direction of the east and gather the people to the west. And the first thing the people of Paradise will eat is the extra lobe of the fish's liver. So Ibn Salam believed and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people, and if they hear of my embracing Islam, they will slander me and speak against me. So hide me and send for them and ask them about me. He sent for them, and they came—while he had hidden him—and he said: What kind of man is Abdullah b. Salam among you? They said: He is our master and the son of our master, our best and the son of our best, our scholar and the son of our scholar. He said: What if he embraces Islam, would you embrace Islam? They said: May Allah protect him from that; he would never do it. He said: Come out, O Ibn Salam, to them. He came out and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. They said: Rather, he is our worst and the son of our worst, our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one. He said: Did I not tell you, O Messenger of Allah, that they are a slanderous people?"],[6962,"He used to launch raids at the time of the dawn prayer. He would listen, and if he heard the call to prayer, he would refrain; otherwise, he would raid. One day he listened and heard a man saying: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He is upon the natural disposition. Then the man said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: You have come out of the Fire."],[6963,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, when Ruqayyah died: 'No man who has had intercourse this night should enter the grave.' So 'Uthman did not enter."],[6964,"In Paradise there is a market containing dunes of musk. They come to it every Friday, and a north wind blows, and it scatters (musk) onto their faces, their clothes, and their houses, and they increase in beauty and loveliness. Then they return to their wives, having increased in beauty and loveliness, and their wives say to them: 'You have increased in beauty and loveliness,' and they say: 'And you too have increased in beauty and loveliness.'"],[6965,"A woman who had some mental impairment said: 'O Messenger of God, I have a need.' He said: 'O mother of so-and-so, look at whichever road you wish.' And he went aside with her until she fulfilled her need."],[6966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his companions: 'Who will take this sword?' Then he said: 'With its due.' The people held back, and Abu Dujanah took it, and he would strike with it the crowns of the polytheists."],[6967,"I was made to fear for the sake of God when no one else was made to fear, and I was harmed for the sake of God when no one else was harmed."],[6968,"Safiyyah fell to the share of Dihyah al-Kalbi, and the Messenger of God ﷺ bought her for seven heads (of cattle)."],[6969,"The Emigrants said: 'O Messenger of God, the Helpers have gone off with all the reward. We have never seen a people more generous in giving when they have much, nor more excellent in sharing when they have little. They have spared us the burden and shared with us the pleasant fruits.' He said: 'Do you not praise them for it and supplicate for them?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then that is in return for that.'"],[6970,"The people of Yemen came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Send with us a man who will teach us.' He took Abu 'Ubaydah by the hand and sent him with them, and said: 'This is the trustworthy one of this nation.'"],[6971,"The Hour will not come until 'God, God' is no longer said on earth, until the sky rains but the earth does not produce vegetation, until one man is the caretaker of fifty women, and until a woman passes by a sandal and says: 'A man once had this.'"],[6972,"A young man from the Helpers said: 'O Messenger of God, I want to equip myself (for an expedition), but I have nothing to equip myself with.' He said: 'Go to so-and-so, for he had equipped himself but fell ill.' The young man said (to the sick man): 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Hand over to me what you have equipped yourself with.' He said: 'It is for you.' Then he said: 'O so-and-so (his wife), give him what you equipped me with, and do not withhold anything from him. For by God, if you withhold anything from him, it will not be blessed for you.'"],[6973,"Eighty men from the people of Makkah descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and his companions from above the mountain, from the direction of al-Tan'im, to kill them. The Messenger of God ﷺ captured them peacefully and set them free. Then God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And He it is who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them...' until the end of the verse."],[6974,"Al-'Adba' was never outrun. One day a Bedouin came on a young camel of his and raced her, and he beat her. That distressed the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ and grieved them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It is a right upon God, Blessed and Exalted, that He does not raise anything of this world except that He lowers it.'"],[6975,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited a man from the Banū al-Najjār and said, \"O uncle, say: Lā ilāha illā Allāh (There is no god but God).\" He said, \"Is it uncle or paternal uncle?\" He said, \"Rather, uncle.\" He said, \"And is it better for me to say it?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[6976,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and Hell is surrounded by desires."],[6977,"When God, Blessed and Exalted, formed Adam, He left him for as long as God willed to leave him. Iblīs began to circle around him. When he saw that he was hollow, he knew that he would not be able to restrain himself."],[6978,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a gathering while they were laughing and said, \"Increase in remembrance of the destroyer of pleasures—I think he said—for no one remembers it during hardship of life except that it expands it for him, nor during ease except that it restricts it for him.\""],[6979,"There were two brothers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. One of them used to come to the Prophet ﷺ while the other used to work. The working one complained about his brother to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"Perhaps you are only being provided for because of him.\""],[6980,"The person who had the most comfortable life in this world will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said, \"Dip him once in the Fire.\" Then he will be brought and it will be said, \"O son of Adam, did you ever experience any comfort?\" He will say, \"No, by Your might, I never saw any good, nor any joy, nor any delight.\" He said: And the person who suffered the most severe trials, harm, and hardship will be brought and it will be said, \"Dip him once in Paradise.\" So he will be dipped in it. Then he will be brought and it will be said, \"O son of Adam, did you ever see any misery, or anything you disliked?\" He will say, \"No, by Your might, I never saw anything I disliked.\""],[6981,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by Mūsā b. ʿImrān ﷺ while he was praying in his grave."],[6982,"I saw last night as if I were in the house of ʿUqbah b. Rāfiʿ, and we were brought fresh dates from the dates of Ibn Ṭāb. He said: I interpreted that to mean that we have the world and well-being in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good for us."],[6983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a sound among the palm trees and said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"They are pollinating the palm trees.\" He said, \"If they left them, they would be fine.\" So they left them, and they became worthless. They informed him of that, and he said, \"You know better what is beneficial for you in your worldly affairs. As for the matter of your Hereafter, it is up to me.\""],[6984,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between Abū ʿUbaydah and Abū Ṭalḥah."],[6985,"He used to deliver sermons while leaning on a palm trunk. When he adopted the pulpit, he moved to it, and the trunk yearned. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and embraced it, and it became still. He said, \"If I had not embraced it, it would have continued to yearn until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6986,"The Jews used to keep away from women during menstruation: they would not eat with them, nor drink with them, and they would drive them out of the houses. Then the verse was revealed: 'And they ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation' [Qur'an 2:222]. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to eat with them and drink with them, and to do everything except intercourse. The Jews said, 'Muhammad does not want to leave anything of our affair except that he contradicts us in it.' So Usayd b. Ḥuḍayr and ʿAbbād b. Bishr came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, the Jews say such and such. Would you permit us to have intercourse with them?' The Messenger of God ﷺ became very angry at that, until we thought he was upset with the two of them because of it. So they left. Then some milk was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sent after them, and they came, and he gave them to drink from that milk. Thus we knew that he was not upset with them."],[6987,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: Teach me a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: Feed people, spread salam, speak good words, and pray at night while people are asleep; you will enter Paradise safely."],[6988,"Love of Quraysh is faith, and hatred of them is disbelief. Whoever loves the Arabs has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."],[6989,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and a vessel with a little water was brought to him. Water began to gush from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6990,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this surah, meaning: “Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.” He said: Your love of it will admit you into Paradise."],[6991,"A single trait may be present in a man by which Allah sets right all his deeds, and a man's purification for his prayer expiates his sins and leaves his prayer as a supererogatory act for him."],[6992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Abu Dharr and said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to two traits that are light on the back and heavier in the scale than anything else? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You must have good character and long silence. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, creation has not acted with the like of them."],[6993,"Gentleness is never in anything but it adorns it, and harshness is never in anything but it disgraces it. Indeed, Allah is gentle and loves gentleness."],[6994,"The first of the wealthy of my ummah to enter Paradise will be 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. By the One in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, he will enter it only crawling on his hands and knees."],[6995,"The treacherous leader will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and his subjects will dispute with him and prevail over him. Then it will be said to him: Fill a corner of the corners of Hellfire."],[6996,"Whoever recites “Say: He is Allah, [who is] One” two hundred times, Allah will erase from him the sins of two hundred years."],[6997,"“Say: He is Allah, [who is] One” equals one-third of the Quran, and “When the earth is shaken” equals one-fourth of the Quran."],[6998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from his companions to a man among the notables of the pre-Islamic era to call him to Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He said: What is your Lord to whom you call? Is He of copper? Is He of iron? Is He of silver? Is He of gold? The man came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ sent him a second time, and he said the like of that. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He sent him a third time, and he said the like of that. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent upon him a thunderbolt and burned him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has sent upon your companion a thunderbolt and burned him. Then this verse was revealed: “And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah. And He is severe in assault.”"],[6999,"There were orphans in the care of Abu Talha, and he had bought wine for them. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Shall I turn it into vinegar?\" He said: \"No.\" So he poured it out."],[7000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a date on the road and said: \"Were it not that I fear it might be from charity, I would have eaten it.\""],[7001,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and they used to begin the recitation with \"Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-ʿalamin\" (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds)."],[7002,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin the recitation with \"Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-ʿalamin\" (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds)."],[7003,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he heard the voice of a muezzin saying: \"Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah\" (Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah). He said: \"He has been sincere.\" Then he said: \"Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah\" (I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah). He said: \"He has come out of disbelief.\" Then we looked, and he was a shepherd; when the time for prayer came, he gave the call to prayer."],[7004,"I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas b. Malik."],[7005,"The general instruction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when death was present to him was: \"Prayer, and what your right hands possess,\" until he began to make a gurgling sound in his chest, and his tongue could no longer articulate it."],[7006,"When we returned from al-Hudaybiyyah, having been prevented from completing our rites, we were between grief and despondency. Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: \"Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest, that Allah may forgive you your past and future sins, and complete His favor upon you, and guide you to a straight path\" (Quran 48:1-2), or as Allah willed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world.\""],[7007,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the night journey, a river was shown to him whose banks were of hollowed rubies — or he said: \"perforated rubies.\" The angel who was with him struck his hand into it and extracted musk. Muhammad ﷺ said to the angel who was with him: \"What is this?\" He said: \"This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you.\" And the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary was raised for him, and he saw at it a tremendous affair."],[7008,"He mentioned al-Kawthar and said: \"I dipped my hand into it, and it was musk.\""],[7009,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it."],[7010,"And Bishr b. Muʿadh narrated it to us, saying: Yazid b. Zurayʿ narrated to us, saying: Saʿid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. Abu ʿAttab also narrated it from Saʿid, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, but he erred in it. Shuʿbah also narrated it from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuʿbah except Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi."],[7011,"I indeed repent to Allah one hundred times a day."],[7012,"As for the hadith of 'Imran — 7021 — Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Raja' narrated to us, 'Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7013,"When a disbeliever does a good deed, he is given a taste of it in this world; as for the believer, Allah defers for him or stores his good deeds for the Hereafter."],[7014,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of al-Hudaybiyah: 'Leave me to go with the sacrificial animal and slaughter it,' or as he said. Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad said: 'No, by Allah, we will not be like the council of the Children of Israel when they said to Moses: \"Go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are sitting right here.\" But rather: \"Go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are with you, fighting.\"' So he slaughtered the sacrificial animal at al-Hudaybiyah. Qatadah said: 'On that day they had seventy camels with them.'"],[7015,"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would seek a second valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And He turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[7016,"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would wish for, or seek, a second valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[7017,"'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj narrated it to us, Umayyah b. Khalid narrated to us, 'Ali b. Mas'adah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7018,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated it to us, al-Khalil b. 'Umar b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[7019,"The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they pressed him with questions. Once he said: 'Ask me, for you will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.' The people fell silent and feared that a great matter had befallen. Anas said: 'We began looking right and left, and I saw no one but every man wrapping his head in his garment.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying: 'Ask me, you will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.' A man stood up from the side of the mosque and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?' He said: 'Your father is Hudhafah.' The man's name was Kharijah. When 'Umar saw that, he stood and said: 'We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. We seek refuge in Allah from the evil of trials.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have never seen a day like today in good and evil. Paradise and Hell were depicted for me, and I saw them beyond that wall.'"],[7020,"The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they pressed him with questions. One day he ascended the pulpit and said: 'You will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.' Anas said: 'I began looking right and left at every person wrapping his head in his garment, weeping.' A man who, when he contended with men, was called by other than his father's name, rose and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?' He said: 'Your father is Hudhafah.' Then 'Umar rose and said: 'We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. We seek refuge in Allah from trials.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have never seen a day like today in good and evil. Paradise was depicted for me until I saw it behind this wall.'"],[7021,"What is between the two sides of my Hawd is like what is between Madinah and San'a'."],[7022,"Between his eyes is written 'disbeliever'."],[7023,"The believers will come to Adam on the Day of Resurrection and say: 'Allah made His angels prostrate to you, so intercede for us with Allah that He may give us relief.' He said: He will say: 'I am not in a position to do that. Go to Noah.' So they will come to Noah, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that.' So they will come to Abraham, the intimate friend of Allah, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that, but go to Jesus, the word of Allah and His spirit.' So they will come to Jesus, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that. Go to Muhammad ﷺ, for Allah has forgiven his past and future sins.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'So they will come to me, and I will go to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and ask His permission, and permission will be granted to me. When I look at my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, I will fall prostrate to Him, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say, or it will be said: \"Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.\" So He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, a second time. When I see my Lord, I will fall prostrate to Him, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say, or it will be said: \"Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.\" So I will praise my Lord with praises that He will teach me, and then I will intercede. He will set a limit for me, and I will admit them to Paradise, until I will say: \"There remains in the Fire only those whom the Qur'an has detained.\""],[7024,"They will be gathered and will be made to think about that, so they will come to Adam."],[7025,"In it will be seen pitchers of gold and silver, as many as the stars of the sky, or more."],[7026,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will he not enter Madinah?' He said: 'He will intend to go to it, but he will find the angels guarding it' – meaning the Dajjal."],[7027,"Taliq b. Muhammad narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, with something similar. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Yazid b. Harun."],[7028,"Take the predawn meal, for there is blessing in the predawn meal."],[7029,"Take the predawn meal, for there is blessing in the predawn meal."],[7030,"If I were invited to a trotter, I would go, and if it were gifted to me, I would accept."],[7031,"Al-Rubayyi' bt. al-Nadr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah was killed at the Battle of Badr as an onlooker. If he is in Paradise, I will be patient and seek reward; but if it is otherwise, I will strive in weeping.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There are many gardens in Paradise, and he has attained the highest Firdaws.'"],[7032,"The Prophet ﷺ executed a Jew for a slave girl whom he had killed over some ornaments of hers."],[7033,"A man called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Friday while he was delivering the sermon to the people in Madinah: 'O Messenger of Allah, the rain has withheld, so pray to your Lord to grant us rain.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ looked, and there was no trace of large clouds. He prayed for rain, and clouds began to gather one upon another until the water channels of Madinah flowed. They remained like that until the coming Friday, and it did not stop. Then that man, or another, stood while the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are drowned, so pray to Allah to hold it back from us.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ laughed, then said: 'O Allah, around us and not upon us; O Allah, around us and not upon us' – he laughed twice or three times. He said: The clouds began to break up from Madinah to the right and left; it rained around it, but nothing rained in it, so that Allah might show them the honor of His Prophet ﷺ and the answer to his supplication."],[7034,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, with something similar."],[7035,"Between his eyes is written 'kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer, whether unlettered or literate, will read."],[7036,"The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to show them a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."],[7037,"When the servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the sound of their sandals. He said: Two angels come to him, make him sit up in his grave, and ask him: 'What did you say about this man?' As for the believer, he says: 'I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' They say to him: 'Look at your seat in the Fire.' They show him his seat in Paradise and his seat in the Fire, and he sees them both together."],[7038,"When he is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the clatter of their sandals. He said: Two angels come to him and ask: 'What did you say about this man?' He said: As for the believer, he will say: 'I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' It is said to him: 'Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then he will see them both together.'"],[7039,"Once there was a fright, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah that had a short, sluggish gait. When he returned, he said: 'I found this horse of yours to be like a vast ocean.' After that, it was never outrun."],[7040,"Muhammad b. al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab b. 'Ata' narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, with something similar to it."],[7041,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to write to some groups and people among the non-Arabs. It was said to him: 'They do not accept a letter unless it has a seal on it.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a silver ring and engraved on it: 'Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah.' It is as if I can see the gleam of the ring on the finger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or in his palm."],[7042,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the grandchildren of the Ansar."],[7043,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the grandchildren of the Ansar."],[7044,"In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it. And he recited: 'And extended shade' (Qur'an 56:30)."],[7045,"What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky during their prayer? His words about that became stern, and he said: 'They must stop doing that, or their eyesight will be snatched away.'"],[7046,"When this verse was revealed: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, so that Allah may forgive your past and future sins' (Qur'an 48:1-2), on his return from al-Hudaybiyyah, while sadness and gloom were mixed with them, he said: 'A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we know what will be done with you.' He said: Then this verse was revealed: 'So that He may admit the believing men and believing women...' up to the words '...a mighty reward' (Qur'an 48:5)."],[7047,"\"Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.\" He said: Al-Hudaybiyyah."],[7048,"Do not practice wisal (continuous fasting). They said: O Prophet of Allah, you practice wisal. He said: I am not like any one of you; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."],[7049,"And Zayd b. Akhzam narrated it to me, from Abu Dawud, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, as far as I know, similarly."],[7050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam to wear silk shirts because of an itch they had."],[7051,"7061 7060 - Nasr narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas."],[7052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[7053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and married her, and made her emancipation her dower."],[7054,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[7055,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[7056,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[7057,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[7058,"He forbade a man from drinking while standing."],[7059,"A group from ʿUkl or ʿUraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were people of livestock and not people of settled cultivation, and they found Madinah unhealthy. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be given some milch camels and a shepherd, and that they go out with them and drink from their urine and milk. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, drove off the camels, and disbelieved after their Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought to him. He cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes with heated iron, and left them in the sun until they died."],[7060,"Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Taymī narrated to us: Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This wording has been narrated from Anas through many chains, and we do not know anyone who narrated this ḥadīth from Shuʿbah except Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān."],[7061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."],[7062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, may Allah have mercy on you, or woe to you."],[7063,"Complete the front row, for if there is any deficiency, it will be in the back."],[7064,"Complete the first and second rows, for if there is any deficiency, it will be in the third or fourth."],[7065,"The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; and the best rows of women are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones."],[7066,"He used to sacrifice two horned, black-and-white rams. He would place his foot on their sides and slaughter them with his own hand, saying: In the name of Allah, and Allah is greatest."],[7067,"He used to sacrifice two horned, black-and-white rams. He would say the name of Allah and say Allah is greatest, and I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."],[7068,"Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees that in her dream, she should perform ghusl. Umm Salamah said, and she felt shy about it: Does that happen? He said: Yes, and from what does resemblance come? The man's fluid is thick and white, and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow. Whichever of them prevails or comes first, the resemblance comes from it."],[7069,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recline on their sides [to sleep], and some of them would perform ablution and some would not."],[7070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Zayd b. Thābit took suḥūr, and when he finished his suḥūr, he entered into his prayer. We said to Anas: How long was it between his finishing suḥūr and his entering prayer? He said: The time it takes a man to recite fifty verses."],[7071,"I enter the prayer intending to lengthen it, then I hear a child's crying, so I shorten my prayer because I know how his mother feels due to his crying."],[7072,"Be moderate in prostration, and none of you should spread his forearms like a dog."],[7073,"Be moderate in prostration, and none of you should stretch his forearms like a dog."],[7074,"He ﷺ did not raise his hands in any supplication except for rain-seeking."],[7075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Zawra' when a vessel containing water that covered his fingers, or about enough to cover his fingers, was brought to him. He ordered his companions to perform ablution. He placed his palm in the vessel, and we began to see water gushing from between his fingers until the people performed ablution. We said to Anas: How many were you? He said: Three hundred, or about three hundred."],[7076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pawned a coat of mail of his for a wasq of barley, which he took for his family."],[7077,"A man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ and they said: He is cheated in trade, so impose a restriction on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When you sell, say: No deception."],[7078,"Al-Hasan b. al-Sabbah and al-Hasan b. Muhammad narrated it to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata' narrated to us from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from Anas except through this route with this chain."],[7079,"Whoever said 'There is no god but Allah' and had in his heart good the weight of an atom will come out of the Fire."],[7080,"There is no contagion and no hāmah. Then who infected the first?"],[7081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a man to visit him, and he was like a hāmah (i.e., extremely weak). He said to him: Did you ask your Lord for anything? He said: Yes, I said: O Allah, whatever you were going to punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. He said: Glory be to Allah! Why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. The man said it and was healed."],[7082,"The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, boasted. The Aws said: Among us is the one whose testimony was accepted as equal to the testimony of two men, Khuzaymah b. Thabit; among us is the one for whose death the Throne shook, Sa'd b. Mu'adh; among us is the one washed by the angels, Abdullah b. Hanzalah; and among us is the one protected by the hornets, 'Asim b. Thabit. The Khazrajis said: Among us are four who collected the Quran, and no one else collected it: Ubayy, Mu'adh, Zayd b. Thabit, and Abu Zayd."],[7083,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsa, then took her back."],[7084,"He used to go around to his wives in a single night."],[7085,"He used to go around to his wives in one night."],[7086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman followed him, and it trembled with them. He said, \"Be still; a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.\""],[7087,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."],[7088,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."],[7089,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a gathering when a Jew passed by and greeted him. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responded to him. He said, \"Do you know what he said?\" They said, \"Yes, he greeted.\" He said, \"He said, 'As-sam alaykum'—that is, 'may you be destroyed in your religion.' Return it to him.\" They said, \"How?\" He said, \"Say, 'As-sam alayk' (may death be upon you).\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When the People of the Book greet you, say, 'And upon you'—that is, 'upon you what you said.'\""],[7090,"You should use cupping and sea costus."],[7091,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best?\" He said, \"Long qunut.\""],[7092,"The Prophet ﷺ raised his voice in talbiyah for both of them together."],[7093,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together."],[7094,"Last night I entered Paradise and saw a palace in it. I said, \"For whom is this palace? Is it for a young man of Quraysh?\" I hoped that I would be him, but it was Umar b. al-Khattab."],[7095,"I saw young maidens—or I saw young maidens in it—so nothing prevented me from entering it except what I know of your jealousy."],[7096,"The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd b. Muʿādh."],[7097,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunūt for a month in prayer, supplicating against these clans: Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān. He said: And Anas reported to me that they recited by it a Qurʾānic verse: “Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.”"],[7098,"Complete the bowing and prostration, for indeed I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."],[7099,"Indeed, Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call."],[7100,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."],[7101,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."],[7102,"He was asked about the Night of Decree, and he reported to us from Qatādah, from Anas, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Seek it in the last ten nights, on the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.”"],[7103,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khaybar for half [of its produce]."],[7104,"The Prophet ﷺ acquired a ring and wore it on his left hand, and it is as if I am looking at its gleam on his hand."],[7105,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought the Burāq, it became difficult for him, so Jibrīl ﷺ said: “No one more honorable to God, Blessed and Exalted, than him has ever ridden you.” Then it broke out in a sweat."],[7106,"Indeed, God is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for it what He does not give for harshness."],[7107,"He used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[7108,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Dhul-Hulayfah and ordered that the sacrificial camels be marked."],[7109,"I have never touched silk, nor brocade, nor anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7110,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed along any road in Madinah, they would detect the scent of perfume from him and say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed along this road.'"],[7111,"The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."],[7112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ate at a table, nor from a small dish, until he met Allah."],[7113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ate at a table, nor from a small dish, nor was thin bread baked for him. He (the sub-narrator) said: 'I said: On what did they eat?' He said: 'On leather dining mats.'"],[7114,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never said to me about anything I did, 'Why did you do it?' nor about anything I did not do, 'Why did you not do it?'"],[7115,"A servant will be married to seventy wives in Paradise. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, can he bear it?' He said: 'He will be given the strength of a hundred.'"],[7116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her seclusion, and when he disliked something, we would recognize it in his face."],[7117,"None of you should spit in front of him during his prayer, but rather to his left or under his foot."],[7118,"A servant does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[7119,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray Maghrib while fasting without breaking his fast, even if only with a sip of water."],[7120,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'The People of the Book greet us, so how should we respond to them?' He said: 'Say: wa 'alaykum.'"],[7121,"When a servant draws near to Me a hand span, I draw near to him an arm's length; and when he draws near an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed."],[7122,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say—and I do not know whether it was something revealed or something he was saying—'If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would wish for—or seek—a second, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust.'"],[7123,"And it was narrated to us by 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj: Umayyah b. Khalid narrated to us: 'Ali b. Mas'adah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, similarly."],[7124,"Shall I not tell you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which no one after me will tell you having heard it from him? Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will be removed, ignorance will appear, fornication will spread, wine will be drunk, men will pass away, and women will remain until one man is in charge of fifty women."],[7125,"And it was narrated to us by Muhammad b. al-Muthanna: Nuh b. Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid b. Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith was also narrated by a group, from Qatadah, from Anas, but we have limited ourselves to those we have named."],[7126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Ka'b: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has commanded me to recite to you: \"Lam yakuni alladhina kafaru.\"' He said: 'Did he name me?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Ubayy wept.'"],[7127,"The Ansar are my inner circle and my close confidants. The people will increase in number while they will decrease, so accept the good among them and overlook the wrongdoers."],[7128,"Were it not that you would not bury each other, I would have supplicated to Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave."],[7129,"I and the Hour have been sent like these two."],[7130,"There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed a horse called Mandub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We did not see any fright, but if we had found him, he would have been a sea.'"],[7131,"None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child and all people."],[7132,"Three things, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that he loves a person only for the sake of God; that God and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; and that he would prefer to be thrown into the Fire rather than return to disbelief after God has saved him from it."],[7133,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gathered the Ansar and said: \"Is there any among you who is not of you?\" They said: \"No, except the son of a sister of ours.\" He said: \"The son of a people's sister is one of them.\" Then he said: \"Are you not pleased that the people return with the world while you return with the Messenger of God ﷺ to your homes? If the people were to take one path and the Ansar another, I would take the path of the Ansar.\""],[7134,"O God, the true life is the life of the Hereafter – or he said: There is no life but the life of the Hereafter – so forgive – or honor – the Ansar and the Muhajirun."],[7135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought some meat. It was said to him that it had been given as charity to Barīrah. He said: \"It is charity for her and a gift for us.\""],[7136,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, and I never heard any of them recite 'In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' aloud."],[7137,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to like gourd. Some food was brought to him, or he was invited to it. Anas said: So I began to search for it and place it before him, because I knew that he liked it."],[7138,"There is no prophet who has not warned his nation about the one-eyed liar. Indeed, he is one-eyed, and your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is: 'disbeliever.'"],[7139,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I am pleased by a good omen.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, what is a good omen?\" He said: \"A good word."],[7140,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I am pleased by a good omen.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, what is a good omen?\" He said: \"A good word."],[7141,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunūt for a month, cursing Riʿl and Dhakwān."],[7142,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunūt for a month, supplicating against a tribe of the Arabs, then he left it."],[7143,"None of the people of Paradise would wish to return to this world except the martyr, for he would love to return to this world and say: 'Until I am killed ten times,' because of what he sees of the honor that God has given him."],[7144,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, when is the Hour?' He said, 'And what have you prepared for it?' He replied, 'I have not prepared for it except that I love God and His Messenger.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Then you will be with those you love.' I never saw the Muslims rejoice over anything after Islam as much as they rejoiced over his saying."],[7145,"The son of Adam grows old, but two things remain with him: greed and hope."],[7146,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Mu’adh b. Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[7147,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a man who had drunk wine, and he flogged him with two palm branches about forty times. Abu Bakr did the same. When 'Umar came, he consulted the people, and ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf said, 'The lightest of the prescribed punishments is eighty,' so 'Umar ordered that."],[7148,"Bring out of the Fire anyone who said 'There is no god but God' and had in his heart good the weight of a speck, and bring out of the Fire anyone who said 'There is no god but God' and had in his heart good the weight of a grain, and I do not know which of the two he began with."],[7149,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to write to the Byzantines, they said, 'They do not read a letter unless it is sealed.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ acquired a silver ring; it is as if I can see its whiteness in the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ, with the inscription: 'Muhammad, Messenger of God.'"],[7150,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of completing the prayer."],[7151,"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7152,"Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, and be, O servants of God, brothers."],[7153,"I asked Anas about nabidh made in earthenware jars, and he said, 'I did not hear anything from the Prophet ﷺ about it, but he disliked it.'"],[7154,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to mix with us—or be kind to us—to the point that he would say to a young brother of mine, 'O Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?'"],[7155,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was always kind and playful with us, so much so that he would say to a young brother of mine: 'O Abu ʿUmayr, what happened to the nughayr (little bird)?'"],[7156,"A group of people testified before the Prophet ﷺ to the sighting of the crescent moon—the crescent of Shawwal—so he commanded them to break the fast and to go forth to their Eid."],[7157,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[7158,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a hullah (suit) of fine silk brocade, and the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ marveled at it. He said: 'Do you marvel at this? By the One in whose hand is my soul, the kerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿadh in Paradise are better than this.'"],[7159,"Hell will not cease saying: 'Am I full?' and saying: 'Is there any more?' until the Compeller, Blessed and Exalted, places His foot in it, and it will say: 'Enough, enough.'"],[7160,"Hell will not cease saying: 'Is there any more?' until God, Blessed and Exalted, places His foot, and it will say: 'Enough, enough.' And Paradise will not cease having extra space until God creates a creation and settles them in the extra space of Paradise."],[7161,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7162,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his community, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[7163,"And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muʿadh b. Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[7164,"Umm Sulaym said: 'O Messenger of God, Anas is your little servant, so supplicate to God for him.'"],[7165,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[7166,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Khaybar, he said: 'God is Greatest. Khaybar is ruined. When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned.'"],[7167,"Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."],[7168,"When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left or under his foot."],[7169,"I was giving drink to Abu Talhah and Suhayl b. Bayda' from a waterskin containing a mixture of unripe dates and dates when a visitor entered upon us and said, 'Something has happened today.' We said, 'What is it?' He said, 'Wine has been forbidden.' He said, 'So we overturned it.'"],[7170,"The garment most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to wear was the hibarah."],[7171,"The Prophet ﷺ found a date and said, 'Were it not that it might be charity, I would eat it.'"],[7172,"Two men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a dark night, and with them were what appeared like two lamps shining before them. When they separated, each one had one with him until he reached his family."],[7173,"He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with barley bread and rancid fat, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had pawned a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madinah and took from him barley for his family. I heard him say three times: 'No measure of wheat or dates has become available in the morning for the family of Muhammad,' and he had nine wives at that time."],[7174,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life and death.'"],[7175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more shy than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we recognized it in his face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Modesty is all good.'"],[7176,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram after a prayer."],[7177,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Hammad b. Mas'adah narrated to us from Qurrah, from Qatadah, from Anas."],[7178,"The Prophet ﷺ said about Uhud: 'A mountain that loves us and we love it.'"],[7179,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he came to Khaybar, said: \"When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who have been warned.\""],[7180,"There is no Muslim who plants a crop or plants a tree, and then a person, a bird, or an animal eats from it, except that it is charity for him."],[7181,"The people after Ismail ﷺ were upon Islam. Then the Shaitan would tell people something, intending to turn them away from Islam, until he introduced into the Talbiyah: \"Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka, illa sharikan huwa laka, tamlikuhu wa ma malak.\" He said: It did not cease until he brought them out of Islam into polytheism."],[7182,"Three men from among those who passed before, went out one day seeking provision for their families, but rain overtook them, so they entered a cave. Then a rock fell and blocked the entrance, so that they could not see any opening. They said to one another: \"The rock has fallen and the trace is hidden, and no one knows your place except Allah. So call upon Allah with the most trustworthy of your deeds.\" One of them said: \"O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them into their vessels, and I would come to them, and if I found them sleeping, I would stand at their heads until they woke up. O Allah, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us.\" He said: So a third of the rock moved. The second said: \"O Allah, if You know that a woman pleased me, and I gave her a payment, but when I was able to have her, I gave her the payment and she kept herself away. O Allah, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us.\" He said: So two-thirds of the rock moved. The third said: \"O Allah, if You know that I hired a worker for a job, and he came to me asking for his wage while I was angry, and I refused him, so he left and left his wage. Then I took his wage and gathered it and invested it until it became all this wealth. O Allah, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us\" - or \"relieve us\" - he said: So the rock moved away, and they went out walking."],[7183,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[7184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still making it complete."],[7185,"The son of Adam grows old, but two things in him remain young: greed for wealth and greed for life."],[7186,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents."],[7187,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and married her, and made her manumission her dower."],[7188,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[7189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never gave us a sermon except that he said in it: \"There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for the one who has no covenant.\""],[7190,"Seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, increase for us.\" He said: \"And like this,\" and Umar said: \"O Abu Bakr, if Allah wills, He will cause all of them to enter Paradise with one handful.\""],[7191,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar — and my strongest belief is the Prophet ﷺ — cut off [the hand] for a shield worth five dirhams."],[7192,"Whoever seeks to humiliate Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."],[7193,"He used to perform wudu with a mudd and perform ghusl with a sa'."],[7194,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: 'The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners.'"],[7195,"Wealth is not from an abundance of goods. It was said: 'Then what is wealth?' He said: 'Wealth of the soul.'"],[7196,"The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise."],[7197,"It is near that Allah will fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee; they will fight your fighters and eat your spoils."],[7198,"The sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two straps."],[7199,"Allah is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you who finds his camel in a desolate land after having lost it."],[7200,"His hair used to reach his shoulders."],[7201,"Umm Sulaym sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a basket with fresh dates on it. He began taking handfuls and sending them to some of his wives, then taking handfuls and sending them to some of his wives, then he sat down and ate like a man who is known to desire it."],[7202,"A man entered the prayer and said: 'Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'Which of you said such-and-such words?' The people remained silent. He said it three times. Then a man from the people said: 'I said them, and I intended only good.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Twelve angels rushed to it, vying over how to write it, until they asked their Lord, and He said: \"Write it as My servant said.\"'"],[7203,"I asked Anas, \"How many times did the Prophet ﷺ perform Hajj?\" He said, \"One Hajj and four 'Umrahs: his 'Umrah from al-Hudaybiyah, his 'Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah, his 'Umrah from al-Ji'ranah when he distributed the spoils of Hunayn, and his 'Umrah with his Hajj.\""],[7204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a camel driver with a beautiful voice. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Slow down, O Anjashah; do not break the glass vessels.\""],[7205,"He used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from madness, leprosy, leukoderma, and evil diseases.\""],[7206,"The Prophet ﷺ prescribed one-tenth for what is watered by the sky and springs, and half of one-tenth for what is watered by camels (drawing water)."],[7207,"The sleeve of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the wrist."],[7208,"He said: \"Who do you consider to be childless among you?\" They said, \"The one who has no child.\" He said, \"Rather, he is the one who has no child who died in infancy (to intercede for him).\""],[7209,"Whoever loves to have his life extended and his provision increased, let him fear Allah and maintain his family ties."],[7210,"The example of a believer is like a stalk of grain; it bends sometimes and stands straight sometimes."],[7211,"The example of a believer is like a stalk of grain which the wind turns over."],[7212,"Whoever has his two precious ones (eyes) taken, and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[7213,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how will people be gathered on their faces on the Day of Resurrection?\" He said, \"The One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.\""],[7214,"Malik b. al-Dukhshum was mentioned before the Prophet ﷺ, and they spoke ill of him, saying, \"He is the head of the hypocrites.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Leave my companions alone; do not revile my companions.\""],[7215,"He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, sin, debt, deafness, and muteness, and I seek refuge in You from dying of a snakebite. Abu Bakr said: And he mentioned other things that I have forgotten."],[7216,"Ukaidir of Dumat al-Jandal sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a robe of fine silk, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore it, and the people marveled at it. He said: Do you marvel at this? By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise are better than it. Then he gave it as a gift to Umar, who said: O Messenger of Allah, you dislike it and I should wear it? He said: O Umar, I only sent it to you so that you could send it somewhere and get some money for it. He said: That was before silk was forbidden."],[7217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr and Umar: These two are the masters of the elderly men of Paradise among the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers."],[7218,"There will be in my nation differences and division: a people who speak well but act badly, who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats. One of you would belittle his prayer compared to theirs, and his fasting compared to theirs. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game, and then they will not return until the arrow returns to its notch. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Blessed is the one who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah, but they have nothing to do with it. Whoever kills them is closer to Allah than they are. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they so that we may know them? He said: They are from our own skin, and they speak with our tongues. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving the head."],[7219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not dye his hair; he only had a little gray hair around the chin or near the chin, a little at the temples, and a little on the head."],[7220,"When he went on a military expedition, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and helper, and with You I fight."],[7221,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on a mat."],[7222,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the noon and afternoon prayers, and the sunset and night prayers, then slept a short sleep at Mina, then rode to the House and circumambulated it."],[7223,"Differ from the Jews and pray in your leather socks and sandals, for they do not pray in their leather socks or in their sandals."],[7224,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by people whose lips were being cut. I said: Who are these? He said: These are the preachers from your nation—I think he said—who say what they do not do."],[7225,"A man looked in on the Prophet ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ had a stick with him. He said: If I knew that you were looking at me, I would poke you in the eyes with it—or something like that."],[7226,"A man cursed a flea in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Do not curse it, for it woke up a prophet among the prophets for the morning prayer."],[7227,"He used to love green, or he said: The color most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was green."],[7228,"Faith is in the heart, and Islam is what is apparent, or he said: publicly."],[7229,"Every son of Adam is a sinner, and the best of sinners are those who repent."],[7230,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: How many prayers has Allah obligated upon His servants? He said: Five. He said: Is there anything before them or after them? He said: Allah has obligated five prayers upon His servants. The man swore that he would not add to them or subtract from them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He will succeed if he is truthful, or: If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise."],[7231,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to Bakr b. Wa'il: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Bakr b. Wa'il: Submit (become Muslims) and you will be safe. They found no one to read it to them except a man from Banu Dubay'ah, so they are called Banu al-Katib (the sons of the scribe)."],[7232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Kisra, Qaysar, and every tyrant, calling them to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."],[7233,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand between Paradise and Hell, then it will be slaughtered. It will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity and no death; O people of Hell, eternity and no death."],[7234,"He used to recite in the two rak'ahs of dawn: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[7235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon to his companions one day when the sun was about to set and only a little of it remained. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, what remains of this world compared to what has passed of it is only like what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it. We see only a little of the sun."],[7236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was admonishing his companions when three people passed by. One of them came and sat with the Prophet ﷺ, the second went a little further then sat, and the third went on his way. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Shall I tell you about these three? As for the one who came and sat with us, he repented and Allah turned to him. As for the one who went a little further then sat, he was shy and Allah was shy of him. As for the one who went on his way, he was self-sufficient and Allah was self-sufficient of him."],[7237,"To sit with a people remembering Allah from the dawn prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves—I think he said—from the descendants of Ishmael. And to sit with a people remembering Allah from the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves—I think he said—from the descendants of Ishmael."],[7238,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ gathered several people in one grave and placed first in the grave the one who had memorized the most Qur'an."],[7239,"He used to pray two rakʿahs after the witr, reciting in them: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say, He is Allah, the One.”"],[7240,"I asked him about the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “He used to prolong his voice with a prolonged elongation.”"],[7241,"The hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lank hair, neither curly nor straight, between his ears and his shoulder."],[7242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have cupping done on the two jugular veins and the withers."],[7243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had large feet and perspired profusely. I never saw anything more beautiful than him—or, I never saw anything more beautiful than him."],[7244,"The pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was made of silver."],[7245,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn."],[7246,"When we were with the Prophet ﷺ, we saw in ourselves what we liked; but when we returned to our families and mingled with them, we disapproved of ourselves. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “If you remained as you are when you are with me in seclusion, the angels would shake your hands with their wings—but [it is] an hour and an hour.”"],[7247,"When the funeral bier of Saʿd was carried, the hypocrites said: “How light his bier is!” And that was because of his judgment concerning Banū Qurayẓah. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about it, and he said: “No; rather, the angels were carrying him.”"],[7248,"The Burāq was brought to me on the night I was taken on the Night Journey, saddled and bridled. It became restive with him, so Jibrīl said to it: “O Burāq, is it with Muḥammad that you do this? No one more honorable before Allah than him has ever ridden you.” Then it broke out in a sweat."],[7249,"Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are: Maryam, Khadījah, Fāṭimah, and Āsiyah."],[7250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done on the top of his foot due to a pain he had."],[7251,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar and the children of the children of the Ansar."],[7252,"There will be disagreement and division in my nation, and there will come people whose appearance will please you and who will please themselves."],[7253,"Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen, so if only you would fix prices for us?' He said: 'Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is the Creator, the Provider, the One who fixes prices.'"],[7254,"He forbade iq'ā' (sitting on one's heels with buttocks on the ground and knees drawn up) and tawarruk (sitting with left buttock on the ground and both legs on the right side) in prayer."],[7255,"He used to recite in the Zhuhr and 'Asr prayers: 'Sabbiḥi isma rabbika al-a'lā' (Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High) and 'Hal atāka ḥadīthu al-ghāshiyah' (Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?)."],[7256,"The Hour will not come until people compete with one another in building mosques."],[7257,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and he stood up for it. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is a Jewish funeral.' He said: 'I only stood because of the angels that were with it,' or 'I only stood for the angels.'"],[7258,"There is no servant except that he has three companions: As for one companion, he says: 'What you spend is yours and what you hold back is not yours.' That is his wealth. As for another companion, he says: 'I am with you, but when you reach the door of the king, I will leave you and return.' That is his family and servants. And a companion who says: 'I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave.' That is his deeds. So he says: 'Indeed you were the least of the three to me.'"],[7259,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on a military expedition and appointed Ibn Umm Maktum to lead the people in prayer."],[7260,"He used to give one taslimah (salutation at the end of prayer)."],[7261,"The Prophet ﷺ broke his fast with some people and said: 'The fasting people have broken their fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have prayed for you.'"],[7262,"Are you unable to be like Abu Damdam? They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is Abu Damdam?' He said: 'A man who, when he woke in the morning, would say: O Allah, I have given my honor as charity to whoever wrongs me.'"],[7263,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people who were lifting a stone, and he said: “What are these people doing?” They said: “They are lifting a stone, seeking strength.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I not guide you to one who is stronger than him—or a word similar to that—the one among you who is most in control of himself at the time of anger.”"],[7264,"Whoever gives up wine while able to drink it, I will surely give him to drink from it in the enclosure of holiness; and whoever gives up silk while able to wear it, I will surely clothe him with it in the enclosure of holiness."],[7265,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people who were wrestling, and he said: “What is this?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so, the champion wrestler; he does not wrestle anyone except that he throws them down.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not guide you to one who is stronger than him: a man whom another man wrongs, so he suppresses his anger, and thus he overcomes him, and overcomes his own devil, and overcomes the devil of his companion.”"],[7266,"Ramadan entered, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This month has entered, and it is the blessed month of Allah. In it is a night; whoever is deprived of it has been deprived of all good, and none is deprived of its good except one who is truly deprived.”"],[7267,"Rule belongs to Quraysh. They have a right over you, and you have the like over them: as long as they judge and are just, are asked for mercy and show mercy, and make a covenant and fulfill it. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[7268,"When he wanted to sleep, he would say: “O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.”"],[7269,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ gave a parable of man, the appointed term, and hope, saying: “The appointed term is at his side, and hope is in front of him. While he is hoping ahead, his term comes to him and snatches him away.”"],[7270,"Change the gray hair—or he said: the best thing with which you change gray hair is henna and katam."],[7271,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is due, begin with the evening meal."],[7272,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[7273,"Everything has an adornment, and the adornment of the Qur’an is a beautiful voice."],[7274,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ‘aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a Prophet."],[7275,"There is a heart for everything, and the heart of the Qur’an is Ya-Sin."],[7276,"That ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf married a woman during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ for the weight of a date pit of gold. He said: Its value was three and a third dirhams."],[7277,"Indeed God has pardoned my community for what they say to themselves, as long as they do not speak it or act upon it."],[7278,"The one who strives in God’s cause is under my guarantee: if I take his soul, or if I return him; and if I return him, I return him with reward and spoils."],[7279,"When the Prophet ﷺ was commanded concerning the pledge of al-Ridwan, ‘Uthman b. ‘Affan was the envoy of the Messenger of God ﷺ to the people of Makkah, so he pledged on behalf of the people. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, ‘Uthman is engaged in Your service and the service of Your Messenger,” and he struck one hand over the other. Thus the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ for ‘Uthman was better for him than their own hands were for themselves."],[7280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking while standing, eating while standing, eating an animal that has been tied up and shot, eating an animal that feeds on filth, and drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[7281,"While I was passing the cup around to Abu Talhah, Abu ‘Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, Mu‘adh b. Jabal, Suhayl b. Bayda’, and Abu Dujanah until their heads began to sway, we heard a caller announcing: “Lo, wine has been forbidden.” No one entered upon us, no one left from us, but we poured out the drink, broke the jars, some of us performed ablution, some of us performed a full bath, and we applied some of Umm Sulaym’s perfume. Then we went out to the mosque, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was reciting: “O you who believe, wine, gambling, idolatrous altars, and divining arrows are nothing but filth from Satan’s work” until he reached “So will you desist?” A man said: “O Messenger of God, what is the status of one who dies while drinking it?” So God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: “There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they consumed” up to the end of the verse. A man said to Qatadah: “Did you hear it from Anas?” He said: “Yes.” And a man said to Anas: “Did you hear it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Yes—or” [he used a qualifier]."],[7282,"Seven deeds whose reward continues for the servant after his death while he is in his grave: one who teaches knowledge, digs a canal, digs a well, plants a palm tree, builds a mosque, bequeaths a copy of the Qur’an, or leaves a child who seeks forgiveness for him after his death."],[7283,"He used to stand in prayer until his feet became swollen. It was said to him: “Do you do this when God has forgiven your past and future sins?” He said: “Should I not be a grateful servant?”"],[7284,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community."],[7285,"He forbade continuous fasting. It was said: “O Messenger of God, but you fast continuously.” He said: “I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[7286,"Three things are destructive: obeyed greed, followed desire, and a person’s admiration of his own opinion."],[7287,"Which of creation is most amazing in faith? They said: The angels. He said: How could the angels not believe? They said: The prophets. He said: The prophets receive revelation, so how could they not believe? They said: The Companions. He said: The Companions are with the prophets, so how could they not believe? But the most amazing of people in faith are a people who will come after you, who will find a book of revelation and believe in it and follow it. They are the most amazing of people—or creation—in faith."],[7288,"Whoever seeks knowledge to vie with the scholars, to argue with the foolish, or to turn people's faces toward him is in the Fire."],[7289,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that he be given sheep between two mountains. He went to his people and said: O my people, embrace Islam, for Muhammad ﷺ gives a gift and does not fear poverty."],[7290,"You have left behind in Madinah men who, no valley you cross and no journey you travel but they are with you. They said: O Messenger of God, how can that be when they are in Madinah? He said: They were detained by a valid excuse."],[7291,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah."],[7292,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[7293,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: Who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so. He said: And there was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you.' Umar ؓ stood up and said: We are content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Paradise and the Fire were shown to me, and I have never seen good and evil as I have today."],[7294,"Paradise and the Fire were shown to me, and I have never seen good and evil as I have today. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so. Umar ؓ stood up and said: We are content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. He said: And this verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you.'"],[7295,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut for a month."],[7296,"I prayed, I and Abu Talhah, behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Umm Sulaym was behind us."],[7297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a perfume he used to scent himself with."],[7298,"The Ansar suffered from severe irrigation channels, so they came to the Prophet ﷺ to pray for them. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, and he said: Do not ask me for anything today but I will grant it to you. When they heard what the Prophet ﷺ said, they said: Supplicate to God for us. He said: O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the grandchildren of the Ansar."],[7299,"When I take the sight of My servant and he bears it patiently, I compensate My servant with Paradise."],[7300,"I sought refuge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him to intercede for me, and he said: 'I will do it.'"],[7301,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by. He asked: 'Whose funeral is this?' They said: 'The funeral of so-and-so son of so-and-so; he loved Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'It has become due,' three times. Then another passed by and he asked: 'Whose is this?' They said: 'The funeral of so-and-so son of so-and-so; he hated Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'It has become due,' three times."],[7302,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. If the people were to take one path—I think he said—and the Ansar another, I would take the path of the Ansar. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar."],[7303,"By the One who sent me with the truth, Allah Almighty has placed a male in her womb because of her patience over her son. She gave birth to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Go, O Anas, to your mother and tell her: When you cut the umbilical cord of your son, do not let him taste anything until you send him to me.' So I carried him on my arm until I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I placed him before him, and he said: 'Bring me three 'ajwah dates.' I brought them, and he removed their pits, then put a date in his own mouth and chewed it. Then he opened the boy's mouth and placed it inside. The boy began to smack his lips, and the Prophet said: 'An Ansari who loves dates.' Then he said: 'Go to your mother and say: May Allah bless him for you and make him righteous and devout.'"],[7304,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the house of a young tailor, and a bowl of tharid with gourd on it was brought near to him. The Prophet ﷺ began to pick out the gourd. I have loved gourd ever since that day."],[7305,"7315 7312 - And Salamah b. Shabib narrated it to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[7306,"He used to like gourd."],[7307,"The Prophet ﷺ used to enter upon Umm Sulaym and take a midday nap at her place on a leather mat. When he slept, she would take some of his sweat and put it in bottles, then mix it with her perfume."],[7308,"The ring of the Prophet ﷺ was with Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and with 'Uthman for six years, acting in accordance with their practices ؓ. Its engraving was in three lines: Muhammad on one line, Rasul on one line, and Allah on one line."],[7309,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, Qays was in his vanguard. Sa'd spoke to the Prophet ﷺ to divert him from the place where he was, fearing that he might advance upon something, so he diverted him from that."],[7310,"Qays b. Sa'd was to the Prophet ﷺ in the position of the chief of police to the commander."],[7311,"He used to breathe three times in the vessel, and Anas mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to breathe three times in the vessel."],[7312,"He would not refuse perfume, and Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ used to say: Do not refuse perfume."],[7313,"When he spoke a word, he would repeat it three times, and when he came to a people and greeted them, he would greet them three times."],[7314,"And Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. al-Muthanna, from Thumamah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7315,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked in the mirror, he would say: Praise be to Allah who perfected my creation and made my form beautiful, and adorned in me what He disfigured in others."],[7316,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it, for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other a cure."],[7317,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ when Umm Sulaym gave birth to her child, and I found with her a branding iron with which she branded the camels of the zakat. He chewed a date for him and named him 'Abd Allah."],[7318,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7319,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Cut them down, and he gestured with his hand to the throat."],[7320,"The Prophet ﷺ came to our home, and we gave him to drink from a well of ours in our house that was called al-Burur in the pre-Islamic era. He drank from it, and it was never exhausted after that."],[7321,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, will I enter Paradise? The Prophet ﷺ said: Yes. When he turned away, he said: Except for debt."],[7322,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man following a pigeon and said: A devil following a devil."],[7323,"Dye your hair with henna, for it increases your youthfulness and your marital vigor."],[7324,"The Prophet ﷺ took off his sandals during the prayer."],[7325,"When this verse was revealed: 'You will not attain righteousness until you spend from what you love,' or 'Who is it that will lend Allah a goodly loan?' Abu Talhah came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my garden is for Allah, and if I could have kept it secret I would not have made it public.' He said: 'Place it among the poor of your family or your relatives.' So he gave it to Hassan b. Thabit and Ubayy."],[7326,"The cup belonged to us, and the Prophet ﷺ used to come to the house of Umm Sulaym and sit on her leather mat and eat from her food and drink from the cup, and she would take his sweat and put it into her perfume."],[7327,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the slave girls of the Ansar met him, and they began to sing: 'We are slave girls from Banu al-Najjar; how wonderful is Muhammad as a neighbor!'"],[7328,"The caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'The qiblah has been changed,' while the imam was in prayer and had already prayed two rak'ahs. The caller said: 'The qiblah has been changed toward the Ka'bah,' so they prayed the remaining two rak'ahs toward the Ka'bah."],[7329,"I was serving them drinks when a caller came to us and said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' So I poured it out, and on that day it was fadikh (a drink made from unripe dates)."],[7330,"Four persons compiled the Quran during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Zayd b. Thabit, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Abu Zayd."],[7331,"A camel driver was singing to drive the camels with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Gently, drive slowly with the glass vessels (i.e., the women).'"],[7332,"Whoever sees something that pleases him and says: 'Whatever Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah,' it will not harm him."],[7333,"He forbade praying between the graves."],[7334,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about coitus interruptus (azl), and he said: 'If the fluid from which the child is formed were cast upon a rock, Allah would bring forth from it his child,' or 'He will bring forth from it a child,' and 'Allah will surely create every soul that He is to create.'"],[7335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey branded on its face and said: May Allah curse the one who did this."],[7336,"The Prophet ﷺ performed Hajj on a worn-out saddle, and beneath him was a velvet cloth. He said: A Hajj with no ostentation or reputation-seeking in it."],[7337,"O Allah, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirin."],[7338,"The son of a people's sister is one of them."],[7339,"The example of a good word: he said, 'It is the date-palm.' And the example of an evil word is like an evil tree: he said, 'It is the bitter colocynth.'"],[7340,"7350 7347 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from Anas: similar to it, but he did not attribute it to the Prophet."],[7341,"There is no soul that dies having something good with Allah that would love to return to this world, except the martyr."],[7342,"Every nation has a monasticism, and the monasticism of this nation is jihad in the cause of Allah."],[7343,"The supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."],[7344,"We have not seen the like of what has reached us from our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, then we did not expend for it every family and wealth: that He may overlook for us what is less than the major sins. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will expiate from you your minor sins and admit you to a noble entrance.'"],[7345,"Allah did not disgrace him with any white [blemish]."],[7346,"I do not recognize anything of what we used to be upon, meaning except this, except the prayer."],[7347,"Three are from roughness: that a man blows in his prostration, or wipes his forehead before finishing his prayer, and the third has slipped from me—Abu Bakr said."],[7348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen with his knee protruding before a sitting companion of his at all, nor did he shake a man's hand and then withdraw his hand from his until the man himself withdrew it."],[7349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the most merciful of people to children."],[7350,"Mu'ammal b. Hisham narrated to us; Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us from Ayyub, from 'Amr b. Sa'id, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it. This hadith was narrated by a group from Ayyub, from Anas, without mentioning 'Amr b. Sa'id except Wuhaib and Ibn 'Ulayyah."],[7351,"I was a riding companion of Abu Talhah on the day we came to Khaybar, and in their hands were hoes, bringing water. When they saw us, they threw what was in their hands and said: 'Muhammad and the army.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah is most great. Khaybar is ruined. When we descend upon a people's courtyard, evil is the morning of those who were warned.'"],[7352,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he came to the door of a woman he had recently married. He said: There were people with her. He went away, took care of his need, and waited. Then he returned and people were still with her. He went away again, took care of his need, then returned and they had left. He entered and let down a curtain between me and him. I mentioned this to Abu Talhah, who said: 'If it is as you say, something has been revealed about this.' Then the verse of hijab was revealed."],[7353,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should some of us bow to others when we meet?' He said: 'No.' It was said: 'Should some of us embrace others?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Should we shake hands?' He said: 'Shake hands.'"],[7354,"Muhammad b. Musa narrated to us; Hammad b. Zaid narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[7355,"Taliq b. Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid b. Harun narrated to us; Shu'bah reported to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of the hadith of Hisham from Hanzalah from Anas. We do not know that this speech was narrated except by Hanzalah, from Anas, and we mention it only because his hadith is with this hadith. We do not know that the hadith of Shu'bah from Hanzalah was narrated except by Yazid b. Harun."],[7356,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut in the dawn prayer, and I memorized from his supplication: 'And make their hearts like the hearts of disbelieving women.'"],[7357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to say more than 'And upon you' to the People of the Book."],[7358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Mubashshir, who had planted a plant, and said: 'There is no Muslim who plants a plant or sows a crop, and a bird, beast, or human eats from it, except that he has a reward in it for him.'"],[7359,"He prohibited nabīdh made in earthen jars, and prohibited keeping the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, and prohibited visiting graves. Then he said: 'I had prohibited you from nabīdh in earthen jars, so now make nabīdh in whatever vessels you wish, for a vessel does not make anything lawful or unlawful. I had prohibited you from keeping the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so now keep it as long as you wish. I had prohibited you from visiting graves, so now visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter.'"],[7360,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ from Yemen. He said to him: 'With what did you enter iḥrām?' He replied: 'I entered iḥrām with what the Messenger of God ﷺ entered iḥrām.' He said: 'Had I not brought the sacrificial animal, I would have exited iḥrām.'"],[7361,"I heard Anas say regarding this verse: 'Indeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers who set up another god with God': The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by and some of them winked at him. Then Jibrīl came—I think he said—and winked at them, and something like a stab wound appeared in their bodies until they died."],[7362,"God has people among mankind. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, who are they?' He said: 'They are the people of the Qurʾān; they are the people of God and His chosen ones.'"],[7363,"Two things may not be withheld: water and fire."],[7364,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the privy, a servant would follow him carrying a waterskin, and he would cleanse himself with water."],[7365,"No case involving retribution was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ but that he ordered forgiveness in it."],[7366,"Patience is at the first shock."],[7367,"Hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave whose head is like a raisin is placed in authority over you."],[7368,"And Yaḥyā b. Ḥabīb b. ʿArabī narrated to us: Khālid b. al-Ḥārith narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū al-Tayyāḥ, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this wording except Abū al-Tayyāḥ, from Anas. Abū al-Tayyāḥ's name is Yazīd b. Ḥumayd."],[7369,"Make things easy, do not make them difficult; give good tidings, do not drive people away."],[7370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray in sheepfolds before the mosque was built."],[7371,"And Yahya b. Habib reported it to us: Khalid b. al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu al-Tayyah from Anas."],[7372,"The Ansar said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"He gave to Quraysh. This is indeed strange—our swords are dripping with the blood of Quraysh, while our spoils are being returned to them.\" This reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he summoned the Ansar in private and said: \"What is this that has reached me about you?\"—and they were not ones to lie—so they said: \"It is what has reached you.\" Then he said: \"Are you not pleased that the people go home with the spoils while you return with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to your homes?\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the Ansar were to travel through a valley or a mountain pass, I would travel through the valley of the Ansar or their mountain pass.\""],[7373,"Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."],[7374,"And Yahya b. Habib reported it to us: Khalid b. al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration."],[7375,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted ruqyah for the evil eye and for fever."],[7376,"Today I do not recognize anything of what we were upon during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said: \"O Abu Hamzah, what about the prayer?\" He said: \"Have you not introduced into the prayer what you already know?\""],[7377,"I have not compared the people today, with their many cloaks in the mosque, except to the Jews of Khaybar."],[7378,"They will come out of the Fire—Abu Imran said: four, while Thabit said: two men—and they will be presented before Allah, then He will command that they be sent back to the Fire. One of them will turn and say: \"I had hoped in You that when You brought me out of it, You would not return me to it.\" He said: So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will save him from it."],[7379,"For the least punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: 'If you had all that is on the earth, would you ransom yourself with it?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then He will say to him: 'I desired from you something easier than that while you were—I think he said—'in the loins of your father Adam, or the loins of Adam: that you should not associate anything with Me. But you refused except to associate others with Me.'"],[7380,"We were given a time limit for trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, plucking the armpit hair, and shaving the pubic hair: forty days."],[7381,"The deeds of the children of Adam will be presented before Allah on the Day of Resurrection in sealed scrolls. Then Allah will say: 'Cast this aside and accept this.' The angels will say: 'O Lord, by Allah, we saw nothing but good from him.' Allah will say: 'His deed was for other than My sake, and today I accept no deed except what was intended for My sake.'"],[7382,"While I was sitting, Jibril ﷺ came and poked me between my shoulders. I rose and went to a tree in which there were two things like bird nests. He sat in one of them and I sat in the other. It grew and rose until it blocked the two horizons. I was turning my gaze, and if I had wished to touch the sky I would have touched it. Then Jibril turned to me, looking like a saddle blanket clinging close, and I recognized the superiority of his knowledge of Allah over mine. A gate of the gates of heaven was opened for me, and I saw the greatest light, and just below the veil there was the flutter of pearls and rubies. Then He revealed to me whatever He willed to reveal."],[7383,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some boys and greeted them."],[7384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to breathe three times in the vessel."],[7385,"He used to breathe three times in the vessel and say: 'It is more wholesome, more satisfying, and more beneficial.'"],[7386,"When you place your side on the bed and recite the Opening of the Book and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One', you are secure from everything except death."],[7387,"He used to pray in his sandals."],[7388,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. This is the correct version, and Abu Qutaybah erred in it."],[7389,"The Prophet ﷺ enjoined upon me five characteristics. He said: 'O Anas, perform ablution thoroughly, and your lifespan will be increased. Greet whomever you meet from my ummah, and your good deeds will increase. When you enter—meaning your house—greet your family, and the blessing of your house will increase. Pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-repentant before you. O Anas, show mercy to the young and honor the old, and you will be among my companions on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[7390,"On the day of Hunayn, Hawazin and Ghatafan came with their riding animals and their cattle, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ten thousand men with him, and with him were the released prisoners. They turned their backs on him until he remained alone. He called out twice that day with two calls between which nothing was mixed. He turned to his right and said: 'O company of the Ansar!' They said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah, we are with you.' He turned to his left and said: 'O company of the Ansar!' They said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah, we are with you.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a white mule.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and said: \"I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.\" The polytheists fled, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired much booty and divided it among the Muhajirun and the released prisoners, giving nothing to the Ansar. The Ansar said: \"When there is hardship, we are called, but the booty is given to others.\" This reached him, so he gathered them in a tent and said: \"O company of the Ansar, what is this talk that has reached me?\" They were silent. He said: \"O company of the Ansar, are you not content that the people go with this world while you go with Muhammad ﷺ to your homes?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are content.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the people were to take a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar.\""],[7391,"A Jewish woman brought the Prophet ﷺ a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was brought, and it was said: 'Will you not kill her, or shall we kill her?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'I continued to recognize its effect in the palate of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[7392,"Al-Sakan b. Sa'id narrated to us, Rawh b. 'Ubadah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham b. Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Khalid b. al-Harith and Rawh."],[7393,"We passed by and startled a rabbit at Marr al-Zahran, and we surrounded it until we caught it. I brought it to Abu Talhah, and he slaughtered it and sent its haunch and thigh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he accepted it."],[7394,"I entered with my grandfather Anas b. Malik upon al-Hakam b. Ayyub, and there were people who had set up a chicken as a target and were shooting at it. Anas said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that animals be made to suffer.'"],[7395,"A woman from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he was alone with her, so he said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are the most beloved of people to me.\""],[7396,"7406 7403 - Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Umm Sulaym."],[7397,"Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of God, Anas b. Malik — I think she said, your servant — supplicate to God for him. He said: \"O God, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him in what You have given him.\""],[7398,"He used to go around to his wives with a single washing."],[7399,"And Muhammad b. Amr b. Hanan narrated it to us, Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham b. Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Miskin b. Bukayr and Baqiyyah b. al-Walid."],[7400,"He used to like gourd."],[7401,"If the Hour arises and in the hand of one of you is a palm seedling, let him plant it."],[7402,"The Prophet ﷺ drank milk and did not rinse his mouth."],[7403,"Look for whoever is in the mosque and invite him. So I entered, meaning the mosque, and there were Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, so I invited them both. I brought him something and placed it before him, and he ate and they ate. Then they went out and the Messenger of God ﷺ led them in the dawn prayer."],[7404,"A time will come upon the people when the sky rains a general rain, but the earth does not grow anything."],[7405,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ saying with his hand: \"I took hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and rattled it.\""],[7406,"Abu Talhah used to kneel before the Messenger of God ﷺ in battle, then say: \"My face is the ransom for your face, and my soul is the protection for your soul.\" He said, and he said, meaning the Prophet ﷺ: \"The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a troop.\""],[7407,"Perhaps seventy slain from the Anṣār — meaning on the day of Uḥud, the day of Biʾr Maʿūnah, and two other days, one of which is the day of al-Yamāmah."],[7408,"I saw in what the sleeper sees as if the edge of my sword had broken, and as if I had mounted a ram behind me. I interpreted the breaking of my sword's edge as the killing of a man from my people, and my mounting a ram behind me as that I would kill the ram of the people. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ killed Ṭalḥah b. Abī Ṭalḥah — he was the standard-bearer of the polytheists — and Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib was killed."],[7409,"The first one to be clothed — I think he said: on the Day of Resurrection — with a garment of fire is Iblīs. He will place it over his eyebrows and drag it behind him. I think he said: And his offspring will follow behind him until he stands at the Fire and cries out: 'O his destruction!' And they will cry out: 'O their destruction!' Then it will be said to them: 'Do not call today for one destruction, but call for many destructions.'"],[7410,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: 'O Jibrīl, who are these?' He said: 'These are the orators from your community who command people to righteousness and forget themselves.'"],[7411,"He would pass by the house of Fāṭimah when he went out for the dawn prayer and say: 'O people of the house, the prayer! God only desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly.'"],[7412,"I certainly hear the crying of a child behind me while I am in prayer, so I shorten it — I think he said: because of what I know of his mother's distress."],[7413,"Mūsā was a very shy man, and he went — I think he said — to the water to bathe, and placed his clothes on a rock. His private parts were hardly ever seen, so the Children of Israel said: 'Mūsā has a hernia and an affliction,' meaning that he never removed his clothes. Then the rock carried away his clothes until it came opposite the gatherings of the Children of Israel, and they looked at Mūsā ﷺ as the best of men, or as he said. That is His saying: 'So God cleared him of what they said, and he was honorable in God's sight.'"],[7414,"When they pressed hard upon the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise?' A man from the Anṣār stood up and fought until he was killed. Then another stood up and fought until seven were killed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'We have not been fair to our companions.'"],[7415,"The head of al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī ؓ was brought to ʿUbayd Allāh b. Ziyād and placed before him. He began poking at his teeth with a stick in his hand and saying: 'His teeth were certainly beautiful,' and saying: 'By God, I will surely harm you.' I said: 'Indeed, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing the place where your stick is on his mouth.'"],[7416,"The king of Byzantium sent the Messenger of God ﷺ a fur-lined garment, either of fine silk brocade or of silk. Some of his companions touched it, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'The handkerchiefs of Saʿd in Paradise are better than it.'"],[7417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ knew that the mountain pass was better than the valley."],[7418,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ distributed the spoils of Ḥunayn, the Anṣār felt resentment and said: 'He divides the spoils among them while our swords are dripping with their blood.' This reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sat in a tent of hair and sent for the Anṣār, and they came. He said: 'O company of Anṣār, is there anyone among you other than yourselves?' They said: 'No, except a son of our sister.' He said: 'The son of a people's sister is one of them.' Then he said: 'O company of Anṣār, did I not come to you while you were astray, and God guided you through me?' They said: 'Yes.' Or he said: 'Did I not find you astray, and God guided you through me? Did I not come to you while you were humiliated, and God supported you through me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: Then he was silent for a little while, and said: 'If you wished, you could say: You came to us as one denied, and we believed you; you came to us as one expelled, and we sheltered you; you came to us as one forsaken, and we helped you. Are you not pleased that the people go with the sheep — I think he said — and the camel, while you return with the Messenger of God ﷺ to your homes?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'If the people took a valley and you took a mountain pass, I would take your mountain pass. And were it not for the emigration, I would have been a man of the Anṣār.'"],[7419,"We were rained upon with hail during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Talhah would eat from it while fasting. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Take from your uncle.”"],[7420,"I saw Abu Talhah eating hail while fasting, and he would say: “It is neither food nor drink.”"],[7421,"He is not a believer who spends the night satiated while his neighbor is hungry."],[7422,"The gardens of Paradise are not entered by one addicted to wine, nor one disobedient to parents, nor one who reminds others of his favors."],[7423,"A young girl would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and lead him wherever she wished, and he would not refuse her."],[7424,"The believer is the one from whom people are safe, and the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons evil. By the One in whose hand is my soul, a servant will not enter Paradise if his neighbor is not safe from his harm."],[7425,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will people be gathered on their faces?” He said: “The One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.”"],[7426,"The muezzin would give the call to prayer during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one would think it was the iqamah due to the large number of those who would stand and pray the two rak’ahs before Maghrib."],[7427,"Al-Hasan b. Yahya narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Salt narrated to us: Abu Safwan narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ‘Ata’, from Thabit, from Anas, similarly."],[7428,"Muhammad b. Ma’mar narrated it to us, from Abu Dawud, from Talhah b. ‘Amr, from Thabit, from Anas, similar to the hadith of ‘Ali b. Zayd. We do not know of ‘Ata’ narrating from Thabit from Anas except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Safwan. He was a man among those who resided in Makkah, and there is no harm in him. We do not know anyone who narrated this version except Anas, and it has been narrated from Anas through multiple channels, but it is contradicted by the hadith of Buraydah in which he said: “Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, except Maghrib.”"],[7429,"A servant girl from the people of Madinah would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would not pull his hand away from her until she took him wherever she wished."],[7430,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[7431,"Abu Kamil narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Shu'ayb b. al-Habhab, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7432,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Hammad b. Mas'ada narrated to us, from Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi 'Abd Allah, from Shu'ayb, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the like of it. We do not know that Yunus b. 'Ubayd attributed as musnad from Shu'ayb, from Anas, other than this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Yunus except al-Thawri, and a group narrated it from al-Thawri. And we do not know that Hisham attributed as musnad from Shu'ayb other than this hadith, and it is well-known from Shu'ayb."],[7433,"The Prophet ﷺ married Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower, and he held a wedding feast for her with hais."],[7434,"I have indeed emphasized to you the use of the siwak."],[7435,"The Dajjal is one-eyed, with 'kafir' written between his eyes, which every reader and non-reader can read."],[7436,"Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh b. 'Ubadah narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Humayd and Shu'ayb b. al-Habhab, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7437,"The most complete of people in faith is the best of them in character, and good character reaches the degree of fasting and prayer."],[7438,"The congregational prayer surpasses the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers."],[7439,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[7440,"Al-Azd are the Azd of Allah in His earth. People want to lower them, but Allah refuses except to raise them. The world will not come to an end until a man wishes and says: 'Would that my father were an Azdi! Would that my mother were an Azdiyyah!'"],[7441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed an obligatory prayer with us without saying when he turned his face toward us: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from every deed that disgraces, and I seek refuge with You from every companion who destroys, and I seek refuge with You from every hope that distracts, and I seek refuge with You from every poverty, or from poverty that causes forgetfulness, and I seek refuge with You from every wealth that causes tyranny.'"],[7442,"My mother said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, Anas—if you would supplicate for him with some supplications.' So he supplicated for me with three supplications: two in this world, and I have seen them, and I hope for the third in the Hereafter."],[7443,"A man looked in from one of the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ took a headless arrow or some headless arrows. Anas said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I think he went to him and threw it at him or stabbed him, but missed him."],[7444,"Indeed Allah has appointed an angel over the womb, and he says: 'O Lord, a drop; O Lord, a clot; O Lord, a lump of flesh.' Then when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills to create it, he says: 'O Lord, male or female, wretched or blessed, what is the provision and what is the lifespan?' He said: Then that is written while it is in its mother's belly."],[7445,"Yahya b. Habib b. Adi narrated to us, Khalid b. al-Harith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah b. Abi Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7446,"About the major sins: associating partners with Allah, Blessed and Exalted, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and bearing false witness."],[7447,"Bring out of the Fire—I think he said—whoever remembered Me one day or feared Me in a station."],[7448,"He forbade a man to put on his sandals while standing."],[7449,"He would not go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he had eaten some dates before going out."],[7450,"Help your brother whether he is wronging or wronged. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I help him if he is wronged, but how about if he is the wronger?' He said: 'You prevent him or restrain him from his wrongdoing,' or similar words."],[7451,"Some people from Uraynah or Ukl came to Madinah and found its climate unwholesome, so the Prophet ﷺ sent them to his camels, or to the camels of charity. When they recovered, they killed the shepherd and drove off the camels. The Prophet ﷺ sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes."],[7452,"The Prophet ﷺ only branded the eyes of the Uraynis because they had branded the eyes of the shepherds."],[7453,"The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off the prayer."],[7454,"And from the hadith of Muawiyah b. Qurrah also on the authority of Anas: 7464 7462 - Muhammad b. Ma'mar narrated to us, Husayn b. al-Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Simak from Muawiyah b. Qurrah, from Anas."],[7455,"A group of people from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, embraced Islam, and pledged allegiance to him. An epidemic—I think he said—had broken out in Madinah. They said, 'The epidemic has broken out in Madinah. If you would permit us, we would go out to the camels and stay among them.' So they went out, killed the shepherd, and took the camels away. With him were some young men of the Ansar, about twenty. The Prophet ﷺ sent them after them, and he sent with them a tracker to follow their traces. They were brought to him, and he cut off their hands and feet and put out their eyes."],[7456,"You indeed perform deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair, which we used to count in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ as destructive sins."],[7457,"The oldest of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ was Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, ؓ, and Suhayl b. 'Amr."],[7458,"The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise."],[7459,"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us: Mu'alla b. 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from Anas, with something similar, but he did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[7460,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the talbiyah for both of them together."],[7461,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to pass by his wives. He came to a woman with whom he had recently consummated marriage, and there were people with her. The Prophet ﷺ left, stayed away, and relieved himself. Then he came back after they had left. He said: He entered and let down a curtain between me and him. He said: I went to Abu Talhah—I think he said—and informed him. He said: If it is as you say, something will surely be revealed about this. Then the verse of the hijab was revealed."],[7462,"Whoever helps a distressed person, God writes for him seventy-three acts of forgiveness, one of which contains the rectification of all his affairs, and seventy-two until the Day of Resurrection—or He stores them for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[7463,"The king of Dhu Yazan sent a jar of manna as a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he accepted it."],[7464,"I have not seen anyone whose prayer more closely resembles the prayer of the Messenger of God than this lad—meaning 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz. We estimated in his bowing ten glorifications, and in his prostration ten glorifications."],[7465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by and saw a dome. He said: O Anas, whose dome is this? I said: So-and-so's. He said: Every building is a burden upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, unless he builds a house—meaning a mosque. This reached the Ansari man, so he demolished it."],[7466,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. He said: Who will guard us tonight? I said: I will. He slept, the people slept, and I slept. We did not wake up except by the heat of the sun. He said: O people, these souls are on loan in the bodies of servants; He seizes them and releases them as He wills. So take care of your needs at your leisure. So we took care of our needs at our leisure, performed ablution, and the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution. He prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr before the prayer, then led us in prayer."],[7467,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted ruqyah (incantation) for every venomous sting."],[7468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed one day, or smiled, and said: 'Will you not ask me about what I laughed at?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what did you laugh at?' He said: 'I marvel at the argument of the servant with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He says: \"O Lord, did You not promise me that You would not wrong me?\" He says: \"Yes.\" He says: \"I will not accept any witness against me except from myself.\" He says: Then the Blessed and Exalted says: \"Is it not sufficient for Me as a witness, and the noble recording angels as witnesses?\" He says: Then he repeats this speech many times. He says: Then his mouth is sealed and his limbs speak about what he used to do. He says: \"Away with you and perish! It was on your behalf that I used to argue, and you did not conceal [your deeds] so that your hearing, your sights, [and your skins] would not testify against you.\""],[7469,"Al-Thawri narrated it from 'Ubayd al-Muktib, from Fudayl b. 'Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ. 7479 7477 - Ibn Ibrahim b. 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad Abu Shaybah narrated it to us; Minjab narrated to us; Abu 'Amir al-Asadi narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from 'Ubayd al-Muktib, from Fudayl b. 'Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ. We do not know that al-Sha'bi narrated as musnad from Anas except these hadiths."],[7470,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[7471,"Ahmad b. 'Abdah narrated it to us; Hafs b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir b. Shinzir, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ. We do not know that al-Nakha'i narrated as musnad from Anas except this hadith. As for Ibrahim b. Sallam, we know of no one who narrated from him except Abu 'Asim. This hadith has been narrated from Anas through various routes and chains; all that is narrated in that regard from Anas is not strong, and the one we have mentioned is the best of them in chain."],[7472,"When a woman prays her five [prayers], fasts her month [Ramadan], guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she will enter Paradise."],[7473,"Whoever avoids four things will enter Paradise: bloodshed, [unlawful] wealth, [unlawful] private parts, and drinks."],[7474,"No time will come upon you except that the one after it will be worse than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard that from your Prophet ﷺ, or as he said. He said: If it is so, God willing."],[7475,"Whoever seeks judgment and asks intercessors for it will be left to himself, and whoever is compelled to it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends down an angel to guide him."],[7476,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: 'If she has a discharge like that of a man, she should perform ghusl.'"],[7477,"Verily, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is pleased with a servant who eats a meal or drinks a drink and praises Allah for it."],[7478,"I served the Prophet ﷺ for nine years, and he never said to me about anything: 'Why did you not do such?' Nor did he say: 'Why did you do—or—not do such?'"],[7479,"I am the first intercessor in Paradise, and I will have the largest following among the prophets on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, among the prophets there is one who will come on the Day of Resurrection with no one but one man—meaning, a single man."],[7480,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O best of creation.” He said, “That is my father Ibrahim.”"],[7481,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “O best of creation.” He said, “That is my father Ibrahim.”"],[7482,"I am the first to knock on the gate of Paradise."],[7483,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed—I think he said: When he finished, he said, “O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing or prostrating, and do not raise your heads—I think he said: before me—for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what did you see?” He said, “I saw Paradise and the Fire.”"],[7484,"I asked him about drinking from vessels. He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pitch-coated containers.” And he said, “Every intoxicant is unlawful.”"],[7485,"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, for it is a word of wisdom that those before you acted upon. And he said, “Every intoxicant is unlawful, and whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful.”"],[7486,"I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said, “For whom is this palace?” It was said, “For a man of Quraysh.” I asked, or it was said to me, “Umar b. al-Khattab.” I think he said, “Were it not for your jealousy, I would have entered it.” Umar said, “Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?”"],[7487,"The Prophet ﷺ dozed off in the mosque and woke up smiling. They said, “Why are you laughing?” He said, “A surah was revealed to me while I was dozing: ‘Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar.’ It was said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Kawthar?’ He said, ‘A river in which there is a basin, containing goblets as numerous as the stars of the sky. My nation will come to it, and a man from among them will be snatched away. I will say, “O Lord, my nation.” It will be said, “You do not know what they innovated after you.” Or I will say, “O Lord, one of my nation.” It will be said, “You do not know what he innovated after you.”’”"],[7488,"Safwan b. Mughallis narrated to us; Bakr b. Khidash narrated to us; al-Thawri narrated to us from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[7489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a man's orchard. A man came and asked for permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Anas, get up, open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he will assume leadership of my nation after me.” And behold, it was Abu Bakr."],[7490,"People will keep asking questions—or people will not cease asking questions—about everything, until they say, “This is Allah who created everything, so who created Him?”"],[7491,"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from anxiety, grief, incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."],[7492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the garden of a man from the Ansar when a man came and asked for permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Anas, get up, open for him, give him the glad tidings of Paradise, and tell him that he will assume authority over my nation after me.” So I got up and opened for him, and there was Abu Bakr ؓ. I gave him the glad tidings, and he praised Allah and entered. Then another came and knocked on the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Get up, O Anas, open for him, give him the glad tidings of Paradise, and tell him that he will assume the affairs of my nation after Abu Bakr.” So I opened for him, and there was Umar ؓ. I gave him the glad tidings, and he praised Allah and entered. Then another came and knocked on the door, and he said: “O Anas, get up, open for him, give him the glad tidings of Paradise — and I think he said: and tell him that he will assume the affairs of my nation after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that he will face severe hardship from the subjects, so command him at that time to refrain.” So I opened for him, and there was Uthman b. Affan ؓ. I gave him the glad tidings, and he praised Allah, and I informed him of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said."],[7493,"I met him in Kufa, on the authority of al-Mukhtar b. Fulful, from Anas, and according to both versions, they are not strong. We do not know that Abu Rawq narrated from Anas except this hadith."],[7494,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ one day while he was sitting in grief, some of the people of Makkah having struck him and stained him with blood. He said, “What is wrong with you?” He said, “These people did this to me.” He said, “Would you like me to show you a sign?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then he looked at a tree beyond the valley and said, ‘Call this tree.’ So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. Then he said to it, ‘Return,’ and it returned until it went back to its place. The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘That is enough for me.’”"],[7495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while he was angry and said: “Do not ask me about anything today except that I will tell you about it,” and we thought that Gabriel ﷺ was with him. A man stood up to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He said, “Your father is so-and-so,” referring to the one to whom he was attributed. They asked him about various things. Then Umar stood up to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we have only recently left the era of ignorance, so do not expose our faults or disgrace us by revealing our secrets. Pardon us, may Allah pardon you. We are content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger.” He said, “I have not seen a day like today in good and evil. Paradise and the Fire were shown to me just beyond this wall, and I have never seen a day with more weeping than that day.”"],[7496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day while he was angry, and we thought that Gabriel ﷺ was with him, until he ascended the pulpit. I have never seen a day with more weeping and veiling of faces than that. He said, “Ask me, for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it.” A man stood up to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He said, “Your father is Hudhafah, the one to whom you were attributed.” Another stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in the Fire?” He said, “No, rather in the Fire.” Another stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj obligatory upon us every year?” He said, “If I were to say it, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory, you would not be able to do it, and if you did not do it, you would be punished.” Then Umar b. al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, stood up and said, “We are content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. We have only recently left the era of ignorance, so do not expose our faults or disgrace us by revealing our secrets. Pardon us, may Allah pardon you.” He said, “Then his anger subsided, and he turned toward the wall and said, ‘I have not seen a day like today in good and evil; Paradise and the Fire were brought near to this wall.’”"],[7497,"Abbas b. Abd al-Azim narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas."],[7498,"They struck the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day until he fell unconscious. Abu Bakr stood up and said, “Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying, ‘My Lord is Allah’?” They said, “Who is this?” They said, “This is Ibn Abi Quhafah, the madman.” I think he said, “So they left him and turned to Abu Bakr ؓ.”"],[7499,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say frequently: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and in what you have brought, so do you fear for us?” He said, “Yes, indeed the hearts are between two of Allah's fingers, and He turns them.”"],[7500,"The example of the believer is like a feather in a desert, which the wind turns over at one time and sets upright at another."],[7501,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man of good appearance approached, and they mentioned something good about him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed I see on his face a scorch mark from the Fire.” When he came and greeted, the Prophet ﷺ said, “By Allah, did you come — he mentioned a word, I think he said: Did you say to yourself — or — do you consider yourself superior to the people?” He said, “Yes.” When he left, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed there has appeared in my nation — I think he said: a people, this man and his companions among them.” Abu Bakr said, “Shall I not kill him, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes.” Abu Bakr went and found him praying in the mosque, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I found him praying, so I was not able to kill him.” Umar said, “Shall I not kill him?” He said, “Yes.” Umar went and found him praying in the mosque, bowing, so he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I found him praying, so I was not able to kill him.” Ali said, “Shall I not kill him, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes, you will kill him if you find him.” Ali went but did not find him."],[7502,"There were twenty young men from the Ansar who kept close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his needs, and when he wanted something, he would send them for it."],[7503,"Whoever goes out in the cause of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his blood more abundant than it ever was, its color like saffron and its fragrance like musk, and upon him will be the seal of the martyrs."],[7504,"Two sounds are cursed in this world and the Hereafter: a flute at a blessing and a wail at a calamity."],[7505,"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he says, 'Praise be to Allah,' except that what he gives is better than what he takes."],[7506,"Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah, whether it falls short or reaches its target, will have the like of the reward of freeing four people from the descendants of Ishmael."],[7507,"He cursed ten with regard to wine: its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its buyer, its seller, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its pourer, and the one who consumes its price."],[7508,"Whoever goes out for a single expedition—meaning in the cause of Allah—will have, I think he said, whatever dust afflicts him as musk on the Day of Resurrection."],[7509,"Indeed among the signs of the Hour are: obscenity, the spread of obscenity, severing ties of kinship, and entrusting the treacherous—I think he said: and declaring the trustworthy to be treacherous, or a word similar to it."],[7510,"Hand me the small mat. She said, 'I am menstruating.' He said, 'Your menstruation is not in your hand.'"],[7511,"The one who guides to good is like the one who does it."],[7512,"The one who guides to good is like the one who does it, and Allah loves relieving the distressed."],[7513,"All spending is in the cause of Allah except this building, for there is no good in it."],[7514,"O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning on its Thursday."],[7515,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray 'Asr with us while the sun was white, still high — Mu'ammal added from al-Thawri in his hadith: Anas said: Then I would go to my family and say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has prayed, so get up and pray.'"],[7516,"My Cistern is from such-and-such to such-and-such. In it are vessels as numerous as the stars, more fragrant than musk, sweeter than honey, cooler than snow, and whiter than milk. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst again, and whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched again."],[7517,"Jibril ﷺ came to me with a white mirror in his hand, in which there was a black spot. I said, 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is Friday. Your Lord has made it obligatory for you, so that it may be a festival for you — or for your people after you. You will be the first, and the Jews and Christians will come after you.' He said, 'What do we have in it?' He said, 'You have good in it. In it there is an hour in which no servant supplicates his Lord for good that is allotted to him except that He gives it to him, or if it is not allotted to him, something greater is stored for him, or he seeks refuge in it from evil that is written against him except that He protects him from something greater than it.' He said, 'What is this black spot in it?' He said, 'It is the Hour that will occur on Friday. It is the master of days with us, and we call it in the Hereafter the Day of Increase.' He said, 'Why do you call it the Day of Increase?' He said, 'Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has taken in Paradise a valley of white musk, wide and open. When Friday comes, the Blessed and Exalted descends from 'Illiyyin to His Throne, then the Throne is surrounded with pulpits of light, and the prophets come and sit upon them. Then the pulpits are surrounded with chairs of gold, and the truthful ones and martyrs come and sit upon them. Then the people of Paradise come and sit upon the mound, and their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, manifests Himself to them until they look at His face, and He says: \"I am the One who fulfilled My promise to you and completed My favor upon you. This is the place of My honor, so ask Me.\" They ask Him for contentment, and He, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"My contentment has brought you into My abode and granted you My honor, so ask Me.\" They ask Him until their desires are exhausted, and at that time there is opened for them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined, until the time people depart from Friday. Then the Blessed and Exalted ascends upon His Throne, and with Him ascend the martyrs and the truthful ones — I think he said — and the people of the chambers return to their chambers of white pearl, neither cracked nor broken, or of red ruby, or of green chrysolite, from which their chambers and doors are made, with rivers flowing through them and fruits hanging down, and their spouses and servants therein. They are in need of nothing more than Friday, so that they may be increased in honor and look more upon His face, Blessed and Exalted, and for that reason it is called the Day of Increase.' This hadith has been narrated by a group, including Ibrahim b. Tahman, Muhammad b. Fudayl, and others, from Layth, from 'Uthman b. 'Umayr, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7518,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'And with Us is more' (Qaf 50:35), he said: He manifests Himself to them every Friday."],[7519,"O assembly of the Ansar, exchange gifts, for a gift removes rancor. If a foreleg were gifted to me, I would accept it, and if I were invited to a shoulder, I would respond."],[7520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting and looked at a hole, then said: 'If hardship were to come until it entered this hole, ease would come until it brought it out.' Then he said: 'Indeed, with hardship is ease' (Qur'an 94:6)."],[7521,"Whoever lies about me in narrating a hadith, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7522,"I was the waterer of the people with figs and raisins that we had mixed together. Among the people was a man called Abu Bakr, a man from Kinanah. When he drank, he said: 'Greet Umm Bakr with peace; is there for you, after your people, any peace? The Messenger tells us that we shall live again, but how can there be life for decayed skulls and bones?' While we were thus, with the people drinking, a man from the Muslims entered upon us and said: 'What are you doing? Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has sent down the prohibition of wine.' So we poured out the large bowl and overturned it. Then we went out and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing on the pulpit reciting this verse and repeating it: 'Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through wine and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?' (Qur'an 5:91)."],[7523,"Abu Anas died, and a man from the Ansar called Abu Talhah married his mother. It was not long before she bore him a son. The boy survived until he began to walk, and the child was beloved. His father went out and did not return until his son died. She shrouded him and closed his eyes. Abu Talhah came and said, 'How is my son?' She said, 'He is calmer than he has ever been, and today he is better for you.' She said, 'And he had intercourse with her, and they poured water over themselves.' Then she said, 'What do you say about people who borrowed a loan from people, and when they asked for it back, they became angry?' He said, 'How evil is what they did.' She said, 'The borrowed one is your son; he has died, and Allah has given you his reward.' She said, 'He said, \"Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we return.\" Then he went out to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him and what she had said. He said: \"O Allah, bless them in their encounter.\"' He said, 'It was not long before she bore him a son, and he named him 'Abdullah. He did not die until he had sons, all of them heads of households.'"],[7524,"A group from 'Uraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and found the land unhealthy, so their complexions turned yellow and their bellies swelled. The Prophet ﷺ ordered them to go to the charity camels and drink from their urine and milk. They became healthy, then they killed the shepherd and drove away — I think he said — the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seized them and cut off their hands and feet and gouged out — or burned — their eyes."],[7525,"People will not cease asking about everything until they say, 'This is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who created everything. So who created Him?'"],[7526,"A woman from the Ansar asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said, 'If she sees that, she should perform ghusl.' 'A'ishah said, 'O so-and-so, you have exposed women.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave her, for the women of the Ansar ask about fiqh.'"],[7527,"Abū Ṭalḥa prepared a pot of one mudd of food. He ordered me—or he said—he sent me to the Prophet ﷺ to invite him to the food. I came to him and said, “Abū Ṭalḥa has sent me to you regarding food he has made.” He said to the people, “Rise.” He said, “I came hurrying until I reached Abū Ṭalḥa, and he said, ‘What did you do?’ I said, ‘I invited the Prophet ﷺ and he invited the people.’ He said, ‘You know what we have, and you have embarrassed us with the Messenger of God.’ I said, ‘Yes, but I could not say anything to the Messenger of God ﷺ.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ came and called for ten people. The people sat down, and he placed the vessel in front of him. He spoke as God, Blessed and Exalted, willed him to speak. Then he said to the people—I think he said—‘Eat.’ They ate until they were full, then they stood. Then he called ten more, and they ate. They all ate, as I think, and there remained enough to satisfy his household.”"],[7528,"Isḥāq b. Ziyād al-Aylī narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh b. Mūsā narrated to us, Abū Saʿd Saʿīd b. al-Marzubān narrated to us, from Anas similarly. And we do not know that Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from Anas except this ḥadīth."],[7529,"Al-Layth narrated it, from Khālid, from Saʿīd b. Abī Hilāl, from Muḥammad b. Kaʿb, from Anas. 7539. And ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Khālid b. Yazīd, from Saʿīd b. Abī Hilāl, from Muḥammad b. Kaʿb, from Anas similarly. And we do not know that Muḥammad b. Kaʿb narrated from Anas except this ḥadīth."],[7530,"None of you believes until God and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else, and until being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after God, Blessed and Exalted, has saved him from it. And no servant believes until I am dearer to him than—and he mentioned something—and his child and all people."],[7531,"I heard Ṭalq b. Ḥabīb narrating from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And we do not know that Ṭalq b. Ḥabīb transmitted from Anas except this ḥadīth. Ṭalq b. Ḥabīb is a man from the people of Kūfa who held the view of irjāʾ, and he was truthful in ḥadīth."],[7532,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ camped at a place, he would not depart from it until he had prayed there."],[7533,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Ḥārith b. Hishām camped, and he was with al-Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf on one of his journeys. He wanted to depart near midday, and Anas said, “What prevents you from praying before you depart? For the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he was at a campsite, would pray there before departing.”"],[7534,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ camped at a place, he would not depart until he had prayed the noon prayer. A man said, “Even if it were midday?” He said, “Even if it were midday,” meaning he would stay until the time."],[7535,"When we camped at a place, we would not perform supererogatory prayers until the baggage was unloaded."],[7536,"I have not prayed behind any one man among the people whose prayer was lighter than the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, yet complete."],[7537,"Some birds were given as a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he divided them among his wives. Each woman received three. In the morning, some of his wives—Ṣafiyya or another—still had some, and she brought them to him. He said, “O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this.” I said, “O God, make him a man from the Anṣār.” Then ʿAlī, may God have mercy on him, came. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Anas, see who is at the door.” I looked and saw ʿAlī, and I said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ is occupied.” Then I came and stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said, “See who is at the door.” I looked and saw ʿAlī, until he did that three times. Then ʿAlī entered walking, with me behind him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Who prevented you, may God have mercy on you?” He said, “This is the last of three times that Anas turned me away, claiming that you were occupied.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “What made you do what you did?” I said, “O Messenger of God, I heard your supplication and I wanted it to be from my people.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A man may love his people, a man may love his people,” saying it three times."],[7538,"I was sitting with a man in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A servant does not believe until he loves for his Muslim brother what he loves for himself.” Anas said, “The man and I then went out to the market, and there was some merchandise being sold. I bargained with the owner, and he said, ‘Thirty.’ The man looked, and I said, ‘I have taken it for forty.’ Its owner said, ‘What makes you do this when I would give it to you for less than that?’ Then he looked again, and I said, ‘I have taken it for fifty.’ Its owner said, ‘What makes you do this when I would give it to you for less than that?’ He said, ‘I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “A servant does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself,” and I consider it fitting at fifty.’”"],[7539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he entered the privy, did not raise his garment until he drew near to the ground."],[7540,"When he needed to relieve himself, he would go far away."],[7541,"He used to perform ablution with the leftover water of his siwak."],[7542,"He was asked whether elderly women used to attend the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Yes, and the young women too."],[7543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man smoothing the pebbles during prayer. He said: That is your share of your prayer."],[7544,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Ramadan. He fasted and his Companions fasted. Then the call for the afternoon prayer was given, so he broke his fast, and some of his Companions broke their fast with him while others continued fasting."],[7545,"The prayer would be called for, and a man would present himself to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for some need, and he would detain him until some of the people dozed off."],[7546,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf married a woman for a gold nugget equivalent in weight to a date stone."],[7547,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ died, and they said: Rejoice in Paradise! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do you not know? Perhaps he spoke about what did not concern him."],[7548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands at Arafah supplicating. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: This is the earnest supplication. Then the she-camel became restless, so he opened one of his hands and took hold of it while keeping the other raised."],[7549,"A woman confessed to fornication four times while she was pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: Go back until you give birth. Then she came after she had given birth, and he said: Breastfeed him until you wean him. Then she came and was stoned. They mentioned her, and he said: She has repented with such a repentance that if a tax collector were to repent similarly, he would be forgiven."],[7550,"Abu Taybah passed by us—I think he said after the afternoon prayer—in Ramadan and said: I cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7551,"I entered upon al-Hajjaj and said: I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for nine years. Then he mentioned some words that passed between them."],[7552,"Woe to the owner from the owned, and woe to the owned from the owner; woe to the rich from the poor, and woe to the poor from the rich; woe to the strong from the weak, and woe to the weak from the strong."],[7553,"The Prophet ﷺ was sitting under a tree, and the tree shook. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up in alarm. He was asked about that, and he said: I thought it was the Hour—or as he said."],[7554,"The muezzins will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection."],[7555,"Regarding God's saying, mighty and majestic, \"and more upright of speech\" (Q 73:6), he said: and more truthful. It was said to him, \"It is read as 'wa-aqwamu'.\" He said: \"aqwamu\" and \"asdaqu\" are one and the same."],[7556,"I saw Anas b. Malik praying in Makkah, and when he prostrated he held his arms away from his sides until I saw the creases of his armpits."],[7557,"When food is brought near to one of you and he has sandals on his feet, let him remove his sandals, for that gives more rest to the feet."],[7558,"When you sit, take off your sandals—I think he said: your feet will rest."],[7559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing dates and raisins for making nabidh."],[7560,"Whoever prays for forty days—I think he said in congregation—a declaration of freedom from the Fire and a declaration of freedom from hypocrisy will be written for him."],[7561,"A man said: O Messenger of God, shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: No. He said: Then half? He said: No. He said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much."],[7562,"The commanders are from Quraysh, and this matter will remain among you."],[7563,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar on a donkey whose halter was made of palm fiber."],[7564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the sick, follow funerals, ride a donkey, and accept the invitation of a slave."],[7565,"A plate was brought with unripe and ripe dates, and he began eating the ripe dates and leaving the ones with worms."],[7566,"When the People of the Book greet you, say: 'And upon you' or 'And upon you.'"],[7567,"Amr b. Amir 7577 7578 - Ibrahim b. Ziyad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us, Mis'ar b. Kidam narrated to us, from Amr b. Amir, from Anas b. Malik."],[7568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped and did not wrong anyone in his payment."],[7569,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Khaybar on a share basis."],[7570,"Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Quran."],[7571,"7581 7582 - Amr b. Ali narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd b. Abi Maryam, from Anas."],[7572,"Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: 'O Allah, admit him into Paradise.' And whoever seeks refuge from the Fire three times, the Fire says: 'O Allah, protect him from the Fire.'"],[7573,"Amr narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus b. Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Maryam, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7574,"The supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."],[7575,"Al-Muzzāt is forbidden—meaning the mixture of unripe and ripe dates."],[7576,"When he dispatched a military expedition, he used to say: 'Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not mutilate, and do not kill a child.'"],[7577,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah."],[7578,"Abū Kāmil narrated to us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aṣamm, from Anas."],[7579,"He prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān; all of them said takbīr when they prostrated and when they raised [their heads]."],[7580,"The Prophet ﷺ sent ʿUmar a silk garment, and he returned it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Why did you return it? I only sent it to you so that you could sell it and benefit from it.'"],[7581,"I asked Anas b. Mālik: 'Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the noon prayer on the Day of Tarwiyah?' He said: 'At Minā.' I said: 'Then where did he pray the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice?' He said: 'At al-Abṭaḥ.' Then he added: 'Do as your leaders do.'"],[7582,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[7583,"Four will be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the infant, the insane, the one who died in the interval [between prophets], and the very old man. Each of them will present his plea. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to a neck of Hell—I think he said: 'Come forth.' Then He will say to them: 'I used to send to My servants messengers from among themselves, and I am the Messenger of Myself to you. Enter this.' Those for whom misery was decreed will say: 'O Lord, will You make us enter it when it is what we used to fear?' But those for whom happiness was decreed will proceed and plunge into it swiftly. He said: Then Allah will say: 'You disobeyed Me, and you were even more severe in denying and disobeying My messengers.' He said: Then He will admit these to Paradise and admit those to the Fire."],[7584,"The child born alive is in Paradise, and the buried alive is in Paradise. And he mentioned a third that I have forgotten."],[7585,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'So by your Lord, We will surely question them all about what they used to do' (Q 15:92–93). He said: 'About [the testimony] lā ilāha illā Allāh.'"],[7586,"Muḥammad b. al-Muthannā narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad narrated to us: Sharīk narrated to us, from Layth, from Bashīr, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ , with something similar."],[7587,"Spending in the way of Allah is multiplied to seven hundred times."],[7588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Umm Sulaym praying in her house and said: 'O Umm Sulaym, when you pray the obligatory prayer, say: Subhan Allah ten times, al-hamdu lillah ten times, and Allahu akbar ten times, then ask whatever you wish, for He will say to you: Yes, yes, yes—three times.'"],[7589,"Abu Talha would begin the day fasting voluntarily, then he would come to his family and say: 'Do you have anything?'"],[7590,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'I have not prepared much for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A person will be with the one he loves.'"],[7591,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7592,"I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ to hear and obey as much as I am able."],[7593,"The door of the Prophet ﷺ was knocked with fingernails."],[7594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a date on the road and said: 'Were it not that I fear it might be from charity, I would eat it.'"],[7595,"There were orphans in the care of Abu Talha, and he bought wine for them. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Shall I make it into vinegar?' He said: 'No.' So he poured it out."],[7596,"I asked Anas about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over them.'"],[7597,"Abu Talha had wine belonging to orphans. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, that was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'Pour it out.'"],[7598,"Yusuf narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Yahya b. 'Abbad, from Anas, with a similar report. End of the eighth part of the Musnad of Anas, may Allah have mercy on him, and praise be to Allah."],[7599,"That a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if a canopy was dripping with ghee and honey, and the people were between those taking much and those taking little. And behold, a rope reaching from the sky to the earth. Then you came, O Messenger of Allah, and took hold of it and ascended, and Allah elevated you. Then another man took hold of it and ascended by it. Then another man took hold of it and ascended by it. Then another man took hold of it, and it broke with him, then it was joined for him and he ascended by it.' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, let me interpret it.' He said: 'Interpret it.' He said: 'As for the canopy, it is the canopy of Islam. As for what was dripping of ghee and honey, it is the Quran and its sweetness. As for those taking much and those taking little, they are those who take much of the Quran and those who take little. As for the rope reaching from the sky to the earth, it is the truth that you are upon, so take hold of it and Allah will elevate you. Then after you a man will take hold of it and ascend by it. Then after him another man will take hold of it and ascend by it. Then another man will take hold of it and it will break, then it will be joined for him and he will ascend.' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[7600,"From Ibn Abbas that he was asked about al-lamam, and he said: 'I find nothing concerning it except what Abu Hurayrah said from the Prophet ﷺ: The zina of the eyes is looking, the zina of the hands is touching, and the zina of the feet is walking.'"],[7601,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, or a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, has caught it."],[7602,"Indeed, in Jumu'ah there is an hour in which no Muslim asks Allah for good while coinciding with it except that He gives it to him."],[7603,"Musaylimah the Liar came during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and he arrived in Madinah and began to say: 'If Muhammad makes the affair mine after him, I will follow him.' He came with a group of his people, and the Prophet ﷺ approached him, accompanied by Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, and in the Prophet's hand was a piece of palm stalk, until he stopped at Musaylimah—may the curse of Allah be upon him and his companions—and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'If you were to ask me for this piece, I would not give it to you, and you will never go beyond the decree of Allah concerning you. I will indeed show you what I was shown, and this is Thabit b. Qays who will answer you on my behalf,' then he turned away from him. Ibn Abbas said: 'I asked about the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: I will show you what I saw, or the dream that I saw concerning you.' He said: 'Abu Hurayrah informed me that the Prophet ﷺ said: While he was sleeping, he said: I saw in my hands two bracelets of gold, and it was revealed to me in the dream to blow on them, so I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as the two liars: al-Ansi and the other, Musaylimah, the companion of Yamamah.'"],[7604,"When a servant draws near to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a handspan, Allah draws near to him an arm's length. And when he draws near to Him an arm's length, He draws near to him a fathom."],[7605,"I saw Musa praying in his grave on the night I was taken on the Isra."],[7606,"As for Paradise, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will create for it a creation."],[7607,"He forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing wudu or ghusl from it."],[7608,"When one of you wakes from sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it."],[7609,"I came to Madinah and found Abu Ayyub narrating from Abu Hurayrah, so I said: 'You narrate from Abu Hurayrah even though you saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?!' He said: 'Indeed, he heard it.'"],[7610,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart."],[7611,"Between my grave and my pulpit is one of the meadows of the Garden, and a prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[7612,"My intimate friend ﷺ enjoined three things upon me: not to sleep except after performing Witr, to fast three days of every month, and to perform the major ablution on the day of Jumu'ah, if Allah wills."],[7613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[7614,"Black banners will come forth from the direction of the east."],[7615,"From Abu Hurayrah: that he said: He and Zayd b. Thabit disagreed about the Qur'an."],[7616,"That the Prophet ﷺ announced the death of the Negus on the day he died and said: 'A brother of yours has died, so pray over him.' He went out with the people to the prayer place, prayed, and they formed rows behind him, and he said four takbirs over him."],[7617,"We said to him ﷺ: 'What did the people fear when they entered a village or looked down upon a village, such that they would say: O Allah, grant us provision and settlement therein?' He said: 'They feared the tyranny of rulers and the withholding of rain.'"],[7618,"The lowest of the people of the Garden in share or portion is a people whom Allah will bring out from the Fire. The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will turn to them, for they did not associate anything with Allah. They will appear in the open and will grow as plants grow, until when the souls enter their bodies, they will say: 'Our Lord, You brought us out from the Fire and returned the souls to our bodies, so turn our faces away from the Fire.' He said: 'So He will turn their faces away from the Fire.'"],[7619,"The true dream is from Allah and the bad dream is from Satan. If one of you sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, for it will not harm him."],[7620,"Hasten with the funeral bier, for if it was righteous, you are advancing it to good, and if it was otherwise, then it is an evil you are casting off your necks."],[7621,"When the heat is intense, then delay the prayer until it is cooler, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[7622,"When the heat is intense, then delay the prayer until it is cooler—meaning the Zuhr prayer—for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[7623,"Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7624,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about praying in a single garment, and he said: \"Does every one of you find two garments?\""],[7625,"When you see the new moon, fast; and when you see it, break the fast. If it is obscured from you, then fast thirty days."],[7626,"When one of you wakes from sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know—I think he said—where his hand spent the night."],[7627,"I have been aided with awe and given the all-comprehensive words. While I was sleeping, the keys to the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hand. Abu Hurayra said: \"The Messenger of Allah has gone, and you are now extracting them.\""],[7628,"When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him shorten it, for among them are the sick, the elderly, and the one who has a need."],[7629,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the injury caused by a mine is without liability, and the injury caused by a well is without liability, and on buried treasure a fifth is due."],[7630,"The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."],[7631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced to the people the death of the Negus while he was in Madinah, and he prayed over him and said four takbirs."],[7632,"The congregational prayer surpasses the prayer of a man alone by twenty-some—I think he said—degrees."],[7633,"When the reciter says 'Amin', say 'Amin', for the imam says 'Amin' and the angels say 'Amin'. Whoever's saying of 'Amin' coincides with that of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven."],[7634,"Ibn Abi Hafsa, meaning Muhammad, reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7635,"Sufyan — meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah — narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd and Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7636,"Tasbīḥ is for men, and clapping is for women."],[7637,"Tasbīḥ is for men, and clapping is for women."],[7638,"The Jews and the Christians do not dye [their hair], so differ from them."],[7639,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer."],[7640,"Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other, killing her and the child in her womb. They brought the dispute about the blood money to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: The blood money for her fetus is a slave, male or female. He ruled that the blood money was to be paid by her ʿāqilah (paternal relatives), and he made her child her heir. Ḥamal b. Mālik said: How can I pay for one who did not drink, eat, speak, or cry out? Should the like of that be wasted? The Prophet ﷺ said: This man is one of the brothers of the soothsayers — because of the rhymed prose he used."],[7641,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim coincides with it while praying except that he is answered, and he [the Prophet] belittled it and made it seem small."],[7642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr or ʿAṣr and gave the salutation after two rakʿahs. Dhū al-Shimālayn b. ʿUmar b. Naḍlah al-Khuzāʿī, who was an ally of Banū Zuhrah, said to him: Has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God turned to the people and said: Is Dhū al-Shimālayn telling the truth? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God stood up, completed the prayer, and made two prostrations while seated."],[7643,"An ant bit one of the prophets, and he ordered that the ant colony be burned. God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him: Because one ant bit you, you destroyed a community among the communities that glorifies [God]?"],[7644,"The heart of an old man remains young in love of wealth and long hope."],[7645,"Do not withhold surplus water to withhold thereby the pasture."],[7646,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the dawn prayer and bowed and raised his head, he would say: God hears the one who praises Him. O God, our Lord, to You is all praise. Save al-Walīd b. al-Walīd, Salamah b. Hishām, ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿah, and the weak among the believers. O God, make Your punishment severe on Muḍar and make it years upon them like the years of Joseph."],[7647,"Whatever I forbade you from, avoid it; and whatever I commanded you to do, do as much of it as you are able. For the people before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets."],[7648,"Do not sell dates until their ripeness is apparent, and do not sell dates for dates."],[7649,"While a man was driving his cow that he had mounted, the cow turned to him and said: 'I was not created for this; I was created for plowing.' The people said: 'Glory be to Allah!' in amazement: 'A cow speaks?!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I believe in it, and so do Abu Bakr and Umar.'"],[7650,"We are more entitled to doubt than Ibrahim when he said: 'My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.' He said: 'Do you not believe?' He said: 'Yes, but to put my heart at rest.' And may Allah have mercy on Lut; he used to take refuge in a mighty support."],[7651,"Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Ubayd, from Abu Hurayra."],[7652,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the whole prayer, except that he makes up what he missed."],[7653,"If you say to your companion, 'Be quiet,' you have engaged in idle talk—meaning on Friday."],[7654,"When the prayer is commenced, do not come to it running; come to it walking, and maintain tranquility. Pray whatever you catch, and make up whatever you miss."],[7655,"When he said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' he would say: 'Our Lord, to You belongs all praise,' then he would say: 'Allah is greater' when he fell down in prostration."],[7656,"In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death."],[7657,"A man from the Muslims came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque and called out to him, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery.' He turned away from him until he had heard that four times. When he had testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: 'Have you been married?' He said: 'Yes.' He ﷺ said: 'Take him away and stone him.'"],[7658,"While a shepherd was tending his sheep, a wolf attacked them and took one. The shepherd pursued it until he rescued the sheep from it. The wolf turned to him and said: 'Who will guard them on the day of the wild beast, the day when there is no shepherd but me?' The people said: 'Glory be to Allah!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I believe in that, and so do Abu Bakr and Umar.'"],[7659,"I heard a man ask the Messenger of God ﷺ, 'May one of us pray in a single garment?' He said, 'Does every one of you find two garments?'"],[7660,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, were it not that some men among the Muslims would not be pleased to remain behind me, and I do not find what I can mount them upon, I would not stay behind from any raiding party that goes out in the path of God. By Him in whose hand is my soul, I wish I could be killed in the path of God, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed."],[7661,"The likeness of the one who strives in the path of God — and God knows best who strives in His path — is like the likeness of the one who fasts and stands in prayer, and God has undertaken — or he said, God has guaranteed — for the one who strives in His path that He will take his soul and admit him to Paradise, or return him safely with the reward and spoils he has obtained."],[7662,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade continuous fasting, so a man among the Muslims said, 'But you, O Messenger of God, fast continuously?' The Messenger of God said, 'Which of you is like me? I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink.' When they refused to stop continuous fasting, he fasted continuously with them for a day, then another day, then they sighted the new moon, and he said, 'Had it been delayed, I would have continued with you further' — as a punishment to them, meaning when they refused to stop."],[7663,"Do not soak [dates] in gourds or in vessels lined with pitch — or he said, in hollowed-out palm trunks."],[7664,"Hasten with your funerals, for if [the deceased] was good, you are sending him on to good, and if he was otherwise, you are putting him off your necks."],[7665,"A rabbi from the Jews came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, what becomes of the food of the people of Paradise?' He said, 'It becomes a perspiration like the bubbles of musk.'"],[7666,"The Prophet ﷺ stood up when it was revealed to him, 'And warn your nearest kinsfolk,' and said, 'Ransom yourselves from God; I can avail you nothing against God. O Banu 'Abd Manaf, I can avail you nothing against God. O Safiyya bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib, I can avail you nothing against God. O Fatima bt. Muhammad, I can avail you nothing against God; ask me of my wealth whatever you wish. O 'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, I can avail you nothing against God.'"],[7667,"Five are from the natural disposition: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit hair, trimming the nails, and clipping the moustache."],[7668,"Do not say 'grapevine' [for wine], for the 'grapevine' is the heart of the believer."],[7669,"A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, and he prayed two rak'ahs, then said, 'Have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone else with us.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'You have restricted something vast.' Then, before long, he urinated in a corner of the mosque, so the people rushed at him, but he forbade them and said, 'You have been sent as ones who make things easy, not as ones who make things difficult. Pour a bucket of water, or a large bucket of water,' meaning over the place."],[7670,"Do not revile time, for God is time, blessed and exalted."],[7671,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of Jumu'ah, let him join another to it."],[7672,"Whoever has three (children) die will not enter the Fire, or he said: the Fire will not touch him except to fulfill the oath."],[7673,"I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. 'Umar said to Abu Bakr: How will you fight the people while they say: There is no god but Allah? He said: If they withhold from me a camel hobble of what they used to pay to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would fight them over it."],[7674,"A Muslim man saw a Jewish man, and the Muslim said: By the One who chose Muhammad over mankind. The Jew said: By the One who chose Musa over mankind. So the Muslim slapped him. The Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what the Muslim had done. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not prefer me over Musa, for the people will fall unconscious on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to raise his head, and there I will find him at the leg of the Throne. I will not know whether he was among those who fell unconscious and then recovered, or was among those whom Allah exempted."],[7675,"Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from al-Nu'man, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7676,"Malik b. Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7677,"He decreed preemption in what has not been divided; when the boundaries are set, there is no preemption."],[7678,"Arguing about the Qur'an is disbelief."],[7679,"You say that Abu Hurayra narrates many hadiths from the Prophet ﷺ, and you say: Why do the Muhajirun and the Ansar not narrate from the Prophet ﷺ like Abu Hurayra's narration? My brothers among the Muhajirun were busy trading in the markets, and my brothers among the Ansar were busy working on their properties. I was a poor man from the poor of the Suffa, serving the Messenger of Allah for the fill of my stomach. I was present when they were absent, and I remembered when they forgot. And he said to me in a hadith he was narrating: There is no one who spreads his garment until I finish this statement of mine, then gathers his garment to himself, but will retain what I say. So I spread a striped cloak over myself, and when the Prophet ﷺ finished his statement, I gathered it to my chest, and I did not forget anything from that statement of the Messenger of Allah."],[7680,"A man from Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the mosque and called out: O Messenger of Allah, the other one committed zina—meaning himself. He turned away from him. He moved to the side of his face that he had turned away from and said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the other one committed zina. He turned away from him. He moved to the side of his face that he had turned away from and said: O Messenger of Allah, the other one committed zina. He turned away from him. He moved to the side of his face. When he testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: Is there madness in you? He said: No. He ﷺ said: Take him and stone him. And he had been married."],[7681,"The Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, parts of me have consumed other parts. So He permitted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The worst heat you experience is from the scorching blast of Jahannam, and the worst cold you experience is from the bitter cold of Jahannam."],[7682,"No journey should be undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[7683,"A man from Banu Fazarah came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife has given birth to a black boy! The Prophet said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there any gray among them? He said: Yes, among them are some gray ones. He said: What is the matter with that? He said: Perhaps a vein pulled it. The Prophet ﷺ said: And this one, perhaps a vein pulled him."],[7684,"The earth has been made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification."],[7685,"The worst food is the food of a wedding feast, to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. And whoever does not answer it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[7686,"Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah."],[7687,"He prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[7688,"The strong one is not the one who overcomes in wrestling, but the strong one is the one who controls himself when angry."],[7689,"If I saw gazelles grazing in Madinah, I would not hunt them, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What is between its two lava tracts is sacred."],[7690,"When a man says to his companion on Friday, 'Listen,' while the imam is delivering the khutbah, he has spoken improperly."],[7691,"The Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel al-Adba' was never outrun. Then a Bedouin came on a young camel and outran it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is a right upon Allah that He does not raise anything of this world except that He lowers it."],[7692,"May Allah curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."],[7693,"Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7694,"Al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7695,"May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."],[7696,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He said, “Does every one of you find two garments?”"],[7697,"The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone."],[7698,"Whoever eats from this stinking—or foul—plant should not come near our mosque."],[7699,"Whoever eats from this plant—meaning garlic—should not harm us in our mosque."],[7700,"He announced the death of the Negus on the day he died, and went out with them to the prayer place and prayed over him, saying four takbirs."],[7701,"No Muslim has three children die, and then the Fire touches him, except for the fulfillment of the oath."],[7702,"Congregational prayer is better than the prayer of any one of you alone by twenty-five degrees."],[7703,"When you finish the closing part of the Mother of the Book, say, “Amin.” Whoever’s Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels will have his previous sins forgiven. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Amin.”"],[7704,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, “There is no god but Allah.” Whoever says, “There is no god but Allah” has protected his wealth and his life from me, and his reckoning is with Allah."],[7705,"When Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will be spent in the cause of Allah."],[7706,"The example of a believer is like that of a crop: the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps being afflicted with trials. The example of a hypocrite is like that of a cedar tree: it keeps shaking until it is uprooted."],[7707,"Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until its burial is finished has two qirats. They said: And what are they? He said: The two qirats are like two mighty mountains."],[7708,"Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7709,"Whomever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion. I am only a divider, and Allah gives. And 'Abd al-A'la said: I am only a divider, and Allah gives."],[7710,"Time will draw close, knowledge will be seized, avarice will be cast, trials will appear, and harj will increase. They said: And what is harj? He said: Killing, killing."],[7711,"He was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said: It is taken and what is around it and thrown away. I think he said: And the rest is eaten."],[7712,"It is taken and what is around it and thrown away."],[7713,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood in his wall. Then Abu Hurayrah says: Why do I see you turning away from it? I will certainly throw it between your shoulders."],[7714,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me, and I reward it. And the breath of the fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk."],[7715,"There is no newborn except that Satan touches it, except the son of Maryam and his mother. Abu Hurayrah said: Recite if you wish: 'And I seek refuge for her and her offspring with You from Satan the accursed.'"],[7716,"You will leave Madinah as the best it has ever been; none will frequent it except the wild beasts and birds."],[7717,"Pride and arrogance are among the loud-voiced owners of camels from the people of the desert, while tranquility is among the owners of sheep, and faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[7718,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I was brought two vessels, in one of which was wine and in the other milk. It was said: Choose whichever you wish. I chose the milk. It was said to me: You have been guided to the fitrah, or you have attained the fitrah. Indeed, if you had taken the wine, your community would have gone astray."],[7719,"Every newborn is born upon the fiṭrah, then its parents make it a Jew or a Magian, just as an animal gives birth to a sound animal—do you find any mutilation in it? I think he said: any defect."],[7720,"A man asked him: Which deed is most excellent? He replied: Faith in Allah and struggle in the cause of Allah. He said: Then what? He replied: Then an accepted ḥajj."],[7721,"He proposed to Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have become old and I have dependents. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The best women who have ridden camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, most tender to a child in his infancy and most protective of a husband in what concerns his property."],[7722,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[7723,"A town-dweller must not sell on behalf of a desert-dweller, do not engage in najash, a man must not sell against the sale of his brother, must not propose against his proposal, and a woman must not ask for the divorce of her sister in order to empty her plate."],[7724,"The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five degrees, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day assemble at the dawn prayer."],[7725,"At the end of time a man with thin legs from Abyssinia will appear and destroy the Kaʿbah. He said, or I think he said: he will demolish it."],[7726,"At the end of time a man with thin legs from Abyssinia will appear and destroy the Kaʿbah."],[7727,"Mālik narrated to us, from Ziyād b. Saʿd, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[7728,"Yūnus narrated to me, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to the first."],[7729,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform iʿtikāf during the last ten days of Ramaḍān until Allah took him."],[7730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the mosque, and ʿUmar rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave them, O ʿUmar, for they are the Banū Arfidah."],[7731,"The likeness of the one who strives in the path of Allah—and Allah knows best who strives in His path—is that of the one who fasts, stands in prayer, is humble, bows, and prostrates."],[7732,"A pledge does not become forfeited from its owner who pledged it; he receives its benefit and bears its loss."],[7733,"Isma'il narrated to me, and he wrote to Muhammad b. Humayd informing me that Ibrahim b. al-Mukhtar narrated to him, from Ishaq b. Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7734,"Yahya b. Abi Unaysa narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ. And this hadith—those who transmitted it in mursal form are more reliable than those who connected it."],[7735,"There is no fara' and no 'atira."],[7736,"Muhammad b. Ziyad and Ahmad b. 'Abda narrated it to us, from Ibn 'Uyayna, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ. And we do not know that Shu'ba narrated with a full chain from Mu'ammar except this hadith and a hadith about which there is disagreement, narrated by 'Abbad b. 'Abbad."],[7737,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it; recite if you wish: 'and extended shade.'"],[7738,"The orphan girl is consulted regarding herself, and her silence is her consent."],[7739,"Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[7740,"A man complained to him that he feels something during prayer. He said: He should not leave until he smells an odor or hears a sound."],[7741,"Zam'a corroborated al-Haytham, narrating it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ with the like of that. Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated it to us, saying: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us."],[7742,"For the righteous owned slave there are two rewards. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayra, were it not for Hajj and jihad, I would not care if I died only as a slave."],[7743,"Indeed the woman was created from a rib. If you go to straighten it, you will break her; and if you leave her, you may enjoy her though there is crookedness in her."],[7744,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold the heaven in His right hand; then He will say: 'I am the King. Where are the kings of the earth?'"],[7745,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from his expedition to Khaybar, he traveled through the night until drowsiness overtook him, so he stopped to rest. He said to Bilal: 'Keep watch for us tonight.' Bilal prayed as much as was decreed for him, while the Messenger of Allah and his companions slept. When dawn approached, Bilal leaned against his mount facing the qiblah. His eyes overcame him while he was leaning against his mount. Neither the Prophet ﷺ, nor Bilal, nor any of his companions woke until the sun struck them. The Messenger of Allah was the first to wake, and he was alarmed. Bilal said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah; the same thing that overcame you overcame me.' The Messenger of Allah performed ablution, ordered Bilal to give the iqamah, and led them in the morning prayer. When he finished, he said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers it, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: \"Establish prayer for My remembrance.\" (Quran 20:14)'"],[7746,"Salih, meaning Ibn Abi al-Akhdar, narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7747,"The best charity is what is given from surplus wealth; and begin with those you support."],[7748,"Al-Layth narrated to us from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Khalid b. Musafir, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7749,"Swearing oaths promotes the sale of goods but erases the blessing."],[7750,"If I have insulted any believer, make that a means of drawing near to You for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[7751,"Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7752,"When one of you gets up at night, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he pours water over it two or three times, for none of you knows where his hand spent the night."],[7753,"Some people recited along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a prayer in which he recited audibly. When the Messenger of Allah finished his prayer, he turned to them and said: 'Did any of you recite with me just now?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Why am I being contested in reciting the Qur'an?'"],[7754,"Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that the deeds we do are something already decreed and finished, or something that is begun anew?' He said: 'Rather, something already decreed and finished.' Umar said: 'Then what is the point of action?' He said: 'Everyone is facilitated towards that for which he was created.'"],[7755,"A Muslim has five duties toward another Muslim: returning the greeting of peace when he meets him, visiting the sick, following funeral processions, accepting invitations, and responding to the one who sneezes."],[7756,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and the horses would become restive and bolt with us?' A man then said: 'O Messenger of Allah, was this in the earlier Book?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[7757,"You will certainly leave it — meaning Madinah — in the best condition it ever was, subdued for the foragers, meaning the beasts and birds."],[7758,"You should use the black seed, for in it there is healing for every disease except death."],[7759,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'Fasting is for Me, and I reward for it. And the odor of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the fragrance of musk.'"],[7760,"He forbade continuous fasting. They said: 'But you fast continuously.' He said: 'And which of you is like me? I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.'"],[7761,"Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, one qirat is deducted from his reward every day."],[7762,"Allah made mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine with Himself and sent down one part to the earth. From that one part comes all the mercy among creatures, so much so that a beast lifts its hoof away from its young for fear of harming it."],[7763,"I saw 'Amr b. 'Amir al-Khuza'i dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to let sā'ibah animals wander free for idols."],[7764,"The Hour will not begin until a fire comes out of the land of the Hijaz which illuminates — I think he said — the necks of camels in Busra."],[7765,"A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."],[7766,"My nephew Ibn al-Zuhri narrated to me from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. Zam'ah also narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father. Al-Walid b. Muhammad narrated it from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah. The hadith is the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."],[7767,"The Hour will not come until the buttocks of the women of Daws quiver around Dhu al-Khalasah."],[7768,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"While I was standing in Paradise, there was a woman performing ablution beside a palace. I said, 'For whom is this palace?' They said, 'For 'Umar.' I remembered his jealousy and turned away.\" Al-Zuhri said: 'Umar wept and said: \"Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom?\""],[7769,"I was sent with the most concise speech, and I was aided by fear (cast into the hearts of enemies), and while I was sleeping, I was brought the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand."],[7770,"He ruled regarding one who committed fornication and was not married: banishment for a year along with carrying out the prescribed punishment on him."],[7771,"While I was sleeping, I saw myself at the top of a well with a bucket on it. I drew water as much as Allah willed. Then Ibn Abi Quhafah took it and drew one or two buckets, and there was weakness in his drawing, and Allah will forgive him. Then the bucket turned into a large one, and 'Umar took it. I have never seen a master among the people draw water like 'Umar's drawing, until the people watered their camels to their fill."],[7772,"My example and the example of the messengers is like a beautiful building whose construction is sound; people find fault only with the place of one brick. I was that brick, and the building was completed."],[7773,"Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something happens to him should blame no one but himself."],[7774,"Qays narrated to us, from Bakr b. Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7775,"When you carry (a burden), delay the load, or regarding the load, for the leg is tied and the hand is suspended."],[7776,"The orphan girl is consulted about herself; if she remains silent, that is her permission, or a permission from her."],[7777,"When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, for the devil eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[7778,"Indeed, among the worst usury is a man's attack on the honor of his brother."],[7779,"He forbade al-malaqih, al-madamin, and habal al-habalah."],[7780,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he promised the Jews that he would give them half of the fruit on condition that they cultivate it, and then, 'I will let you remain as long as Allah lets you remain.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send 'Abdullah b. Rawahah to estimate the crop, then give them the choice to take it or leave it. The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one such occasion and complained to him about his estimate. He summoned 'Abdullah b. Rawahah and mentioned to him what they had said. 'Abdullah said, 'It is as I have, O Messenger of Allah. If they wish, they may take it; if they leave it, we will take it.' The Jews were satisfied and said, 'By this, the heavens and the earth are upheld.' Then the Messenger of Allah said during the illness in which he died, 'Two religions shall not coexist in the Arabian Peninsula.' When that reached 'Umar, he sent to the Jews of Khaybar and said, 'The Messenger of Allah gave you ownership of these properties and stipulated for you that we would let you remain as long as Allah let you remain. Allah has now permitted your expulsion.' So 'Umar expelled every Jew and Christian from the land of the Hijaz, then divided it among the people of Madinah."],[7781,"When you hear the mu'adhdhin, say as he says."],[7782,"Aban b. Sa'id al-Akbar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah had granted him victory at Khaybar, and asked him to assign a share for him and his companions, but he did not do so."],[7783,"He heard Abu Hurayrah describe the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'He was a man of medium height, closer to tall; very fair, with a black beard, good hair, long eyelashes, broad-shouldered, walking with his entire foot, with no hollowness in the soles; he would turn fully when he turned and walk away fully when he walked away. I have not seen the like of him before or since.'"],[7784,"Ihsan is of two kinds: ihsan of chastity and ihsan of marriage."],[7785,"Do you dispute about the moon on a full-moon night when there is no cloud beneath it? They said, 'No.' He said, 'Do you dispute about the sun when there is no cloud beneath it?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'You will see Him likewise. People will be held back on the Day of Resurrection, then it will be said: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. Some will follow the sun, some the moon, and some the false deities. This ummah will remain, including its hypocrites. Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will come to them and say: I am your Lord. They will say: You are our Lord. Then the sirat will be set up over the midst of Hell, and I will be the first of the messengers to cross with my ummah. None will speak that day except the messengers, and the messengers' supplication that day will be: O Allah, grant peace, grant peace. In Hell there will be hooks like the thorns of al-sa'dan. Have you seen the thorns of al-sa'dan? They said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'They are like the thorns of al-sa'dan. They will snatch people according to their deeds. Some will be cut to pieces (or he said: maimed), and some will be saved. Then when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills mercy for whomever He wills of the people of the Fire, He will command the angels to bring out those who worshipped Allah. They will bring them out, recognizing them by the marks of prostration. Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the mark of prostration. They will come out of the Fire charred. Then the water of life will be poured on them, and they will sprout as a seed sprouts in the silt of a flood. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will finish judging between the servants. While a man is between Paradise and the Fire—he is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise—turning his face toward the Fire, he will say: O Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its smell has afflicted me and its heat has burned me. He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: Would you perhaps, if I do that for you, ask Me for something else? He will say: No, by Your might. And he will give his Lord whatever covenant and pledge He wills. So Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. When he faces Paradise and sees its splendor, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: Did you not give covenants and pledges that you would not ask for anything other than what you asked? He will say: O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. He will say: Would you perhaps, if I give you that, ask Me for something else? He will say: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for anything else. And he will give his Lord whatever covenant and pledge He wills. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will bring him forward to the gate of Paradise. When he reaches its gate, it will open for him, and he will see its splendor and what is in it of freshness and joy, and he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, admit me into Paradise. He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! You have given covenants and pledges that you would not ask for anything other than what you were given. He will say: O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will laugh at him, then permit him to enter Paradise. Then He will say: Wish. He will wish, until when his wishes are exhausted, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: Thus—his Lord will remind him—until when his wishes come to an end, Allah, Exalted, will say: You shall have that and the like of it with it.' Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That and ten times the like of it.' Abu Hurayrah said: I did not memorize from the Messenger of Allah except that he said: 'You shall have that and the like of it with it.' Abu Sa'id said: I testify that I heard him say: 'You shall have that and ten times the like of it.' This hadith was narrated by Ma'mar, Ibrahim b. Sa'd, and others, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' b. Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id. We do not know anyone who combined 'Ata' b. Yazid and Sa'id b. al-Musayyib except Shu'ayb b. Abi Hamzah and Mu'awiyah b. Yahya al-Sadafi. They both agreed on Sa'id b. al-Musayyib and 'Ata' b. Yazid, and Shu'ayb is more reliable."],[7786,"Three will not smell the fragrance of Paradise: a man who claims descent from other than his father, a man who lies about his Prophet, and a man who lies about his own eyes."],[7787,"When one of you yawns in prayer, let him place his hand over his mouth."],[7788,"Whoever enters a horse between two horses while he fears being outrun, it is gambling. Whoever enters a horse between two horses while he does not care whether he is outrun, it is not gambling."],[7789,"Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise, their faces shining like the moon on a full-moon night. Abu Hurayrah said: 'Ukashah b. Mihsan al-Asadi stood up, raised a cloak over himself, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them. He said: O Allah, make him one of them. Abu Hurayrah said: Then another man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them. He said: 'Ukashah has preceded you to it.'"],[7790,"Speaking about qadar has been delayed for the worst of this ummah at the end of time, and disputing about the Qur'an is disbelief."],[7791,"He forbade killing the ant, the bee, the shrike, and the hoopoe. And he sometimes remained silent about the fourth."],[7792,"He said about those slain at Uhud: 'Wrap them in their wounds and their blood.'"],[7793,"The injury caused by a beast is of no liability."],[7794,"Whoever is cupped on Wednesday or Saturday and is then afflicted by leprosy, let him blame none but himself."],[7795,"You will certainly be sifted just as dates are sifted from the chaff; the best of you will pass away, and the worst of you will remain; so die if you can."],[7796,"There is no faraʿ and no ʿatīrah."],[7797,"The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose sandals are of hair, and whose faces are like hammered shields."],[7798,"A funeral was brought, and he stood up to pray over it, but they said: 'He owes a debt.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Take your companion away and pray over him.' A man said: 'His debt is upon me, so pray over him.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and prayed over him."],[7799,"God, Exalted is He, laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, yet He admits both to Paradise. It was said: 'How can that be?' He said: 'One of them is a disbeliever and kills the other, then he embraces Islam and is killed.'"],[7800,"In this black seed there is a cure for every disease except al-sām. It was said: 'What is al-sām?' He said: 'Death.'"],[7801,"Whoever is cupped on Saturday or Wednesday and is then afflicted by leprosy, let him blame none but himself."],[7802,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[7803,"A Prophet among the Prophets went on a military expedition after 'Asr and said: 'No man who has built a house but not yet lived in it should accompany me, nor one who has married a woman but not yet consummated the marriage with her.' He said: 'And nothing remained of the sun except a little.' He said: 'O Allah, the sun is commanded and I am commanded. O Allah, hold it back.' So Allah held it back for an hour until Allah granted him victory. He ordered the spoils of war to be gathered, and they were gathered. Then fire came but did not consume them. He said: 'There is misappropriation among you. Let one man from every tribe come forward so that we may pledge allegiance to him.' Then his hand stuck to the hand of one man or two men. He said: 'Among you is the misappropriation!' They brought out a head of a cow made of gold and threw it among the spoils, and the fire consumed them—meaning the spoils. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Spoils of war were not made lawful for anyone before us, and that is because Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saw our weakness and made them good for us.'"],[7804,"The price of a cat was forbidden."],[7805,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in two white garments and a Najrani burd."],[7806,"We were in a riding party with 'Umar. He said: 'Who will narrate to us?' Then the wind blew while I was at the rear of the people. 'Umar said: 'Which of you has heard anything from the Messenger of Allah about the wind?' I said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The wind is from the mercy of Allah. It brings mercy and punishment. When you see it, ask Allah for its good and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, and do not revile it, for it is commanded.\"'"],[7807,"When allegiance is pledged to two caliphs, kill the latter of them."],[7808,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'Pride is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment. Whoever disputes with Me over either of them, I will cast him—or he said: I will throw him—into the Fire.'"],[7809,"The thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing, and the adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer at the time of committing adultery, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer at the time of drinking it."],[7810,"There are no days in which deeds are more virtuous than the ten days—meaning the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. Fasting one day among them equals fasting a year, and standing in prayer one night among them equals standing in prayer on the Night of Decree. So increase in glorification, magnification, and remembrance of Allah."],[7811,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[7812,"A woman is not to be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[7813,"A Prophet among the Prophets went on a military expedition with his companions and said: 'No man who has built a house but not yet lived in it should accompany me, nor one who has married a woman but not yet consummated the marriage with her, nor one who has a need to return.' He met the enemy at sunset and said: 'O Allah, it is commanded and I am commanded, so hold it back for me until You judge between me and them.' So Allah held it back for him and granted him victory. The spoils of war were gathered, but the fire did not consume them. They used to send fire upon the spoils when they gained them, and it would consume them. Their Prophet said to them: 'You have misappropriated. Let one man from each of your tribes come to me and pledge allegiance to me.' They pledged allegiance to him, and the hand of one of them stuck to his hand. He said: 'Gather your companions, for they have misappropriated, and bring them to me to pledge allegiance to me.' They came to him, and his hand stuck to the hand of two of them. He said: 'You have misappropriated.' They said: 'Yes, we misappropriated images of a cow—meaning horns of a cow made of gold.' He said: 'So he brought it and threw it among the spoils. Then the fire was sent upon them and consumed them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, fed us spoils of war as a mercy with which He had mercy on us because of what He knows of our weakness.'"],[7814,"To Nuh were born Sam, Ham, and Yafith. From Sam were born the Arabs, Persia, and al-Rum, and the good is in them. From Yafith were born Ya'juj and Ma'juj, the Turks, and the Saqalibah, and there is no good in them. From Ham were born the Copts, the Berbers, and the Sudanese."],[7815,"Satan ties three knots on the nape of one of you when he sleeps. If he wakes and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he gets up and performs ablution, one knot is undone. If he gets up and prays, all his knots are undone, and he enters the morning energetic and good in spirit. And if he enters the morning without doing that, he enters the morning lazy and evil in spirit, having gained no good."],[7816,"I saw ʿAmr b. Luḥayy dragging his intestines in the Fire."],[7817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for the Negus."],[7818,"He forbade that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt."],[7819,"There is no leader of ten except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck."],[7820,"I was favored over the prophets with two traits: my devil was a disbeliever, and Allah helped me against him until he submitted, and I forgot the other trait."],[7821,"He is not one of us who incites a woman against her husband, or a slave against his master."],[7822,"Abraham circumcised himself with an adze—I think he said—when he had reached eighty years."],[7823,"Be kind to the goat, and remove harm from it, for it is one of the animals of Paradise."],[7824,"When one of you prays over a funeral, let him make sincere supplication for it."],[7825,"There will come people who lead you in prayer. If they complete it, then it is for them and for you; and if they do not complete it, then it is against them and for you."],[7826,"He forbade the ʿatīrah, which was a sacrifice they used to slaughter in Rajab; so he forbade them from it, and commanded them with the uḍḥiyah."],[7827,"Umar passed by Hassan b. Thabit while he was reciting poetry in the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said, \"Do you recite poetry in the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said, \"I have recited to one who is better than you.\" Abu Hurayra said, \"He spoke the truth.\""],[7828,"Satan concerns himself with one and two, but when they are three he does not concern himself with them."],[7829,"People will remain in good as long as they hasten the iftar and do not delay it as the people of shirk do."],[7830,"Whoever catches one rak'a of Jumu'a, let him add another to it."],[7831,"Fast three days of every month."],[7832,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, the two rak'as of al-duha, and not to sleep except upon witr."],[7833,"The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."],[7834,"The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."],[7835,"A man's prayer in congregation is superior to his prayer alone by twenty-five prayers."],[7836,"Ubayd Allah b. Mu'adh narrated to us from his father, from Ash'ath, from Dawud, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, its like. And we do not know that Ash'ath transmitted any hadith from Dawud other than this one, and Dawud did not transmit from Sa'id from Abu Hurayra except two hadiths, of which this is one, and the other is:"],[7837,"Three traits: whoever possesses them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, and claims to be a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays."],[7838,"The height of Adam was sixty cubits, with a width of seven cubits."],[7839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head after he had said the salam, and he was facing the qiblah, and said: O God, deliver Salamah b. Hisham, ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah, al-Walid b. al-Walid, and the weak among the Muslims who cannot find a way out and do not know the way."],[7840,"Your Lord — Blessed and Exalted is He — says: Every good deed is multiplied ten times its like, up to seven hundred times; and fasting is for Me and I reward it; fasting is a shield from the Fire; and the odor from the mouth of a fasting person is more pleasant to God than the scent of musk."],[7841,"There is no person but has wisdom in his head, and wisdom is in the hand of an angel. If he is humble, the angel is told: Raise the wisdom. And when he wants to rise, the angel is told: Lower his wisdom."],[7842,"Pride is My cloak and might is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I will fling him or cast him into the Fire."],[7843,"The last two men to come out of the Fire: God, Blessed and Exalted, says to one of them: O son of Adam, what have you prepared for this day? Have you ever done good? Have you hoped in Me or feared Me? He says: No, O Lord. So he is ordered to the Fire, and he is the most regretful of the people of the Fire. He says to the other: O son of Adam, what have you prepared for this day? Have you done any good? He says: No, except that I hoped in You. So a tree is raised for him, and he says: O Lord, seat me under this tree so I may shade myself with its shade, eat of its fruit, and drink of its water. He promises Him not to ask for anything but it. So he sits, or He seats him under it. Then another tree is raised for him that is better than the first, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree; I will not ask You for anything else; I will shade myself with its shade and drink of its water. He says: O son of Adam, did you not promise Me that you would not ask Me for anything but it? He says: Yes, O Lord, but this one. He promises Him not to ask for anything else, and He brings him near it. Then a tree is raised for him at the gate of Paradise that is better than the first two, and he says: This one, bring me near under it. He promises Him not to ask for anything else, and He brings him near it. He hears the voices of the people of Paradise, and he cannot restrain himself, so he says: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. I think he said: So he enters Paradise. Then God, Blessed and Exalted, says: Ask and wish. He asks and wishes for the amount of three days — I think he said: of the days of this world — and he wishes. When he finishes, He says: You will have what you asked for. Abu Hurayrah said: And the like of it with him. Abu Saʿid said: And ten times its like with him."],[7844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ told us that we will see everything except that he said: Men will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Put down your whips and enter the Fire."],[7845,"The peak of intellect after faith in God is showing affection to people."],[7846,"When revelation came down upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he got a headache and would wrap his head with henna."],[7847,"Satan comes to one of you and confuses him in his prayer so that he does not know how much he prayed. Whoever finds anything of that, let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting."],[7848,"God does not listen to anything as He listens to a prophet reciting the Quran beautifully."],[7849,"Al-Aqraʿ b. Habis saw the Prophet ﷺ kissing al-Hasan and said: I have ten children and have never kissed any of them. The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[7850,"In the black seed there is a cure for every disease except death."],[7851,"Whoever catches a rakʿah of the prayer has caught it."],[7852,"Whoever catches a rakʿah of the prayer has caught it."],[7853,"Whoever catches a rakʿah of the prayer has caught it."],[7854,"When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[7855,"Whoever stands in prayer during Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[7856,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure is one-fifth."],[7857,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure is one-fifth."],[7858,"He forbade preparing nabīdh in the gourd and the green glazed jar. He said: And avoid the ḥantam jars and the naqīr."],[7859,"Maʿmar reported to us from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7860,"When the Negus died, the Prophet ﷺ said: Pray for forgiveness for him."],[7861,"The child belongs to the bed, and the stone is for the adulterer."],[7862,"He would say takbīr whenever he lowered and raised, and he would say: I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7863,"I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He used to say the takbir every time he lowered and raised [himself]."],[7864,"Saying subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."],[7865,"And Khalid b. Yusuf narrated to us something similar."],[7866,"Two women, one of them threw at the other and caused her to miscarry a fetus. The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding the fetus that a male or female slave be given."],[7867,"Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other, striking her belly, killing her and causing her to miscarry her fetus. The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that her blood money be paid by the other's 'aqila, and that for the fetus a ghurra of a male or female slave be paid. A man said, 'Should we pay blood money for one who did not eat, drink, see, or cry out? Such a one is worthless.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'This is from the brethren of the soothsayers.'"],[7868,"The Prophet ﷺ stood at al-Hazwara and said: 'I know that you are the most beloved land to God—meaning Makkah—and had my people not expelled me from you, I would not have left.'"],[7869,"The poor person is not the one who is turned away by a date or two dates, nor by a morsel or two morsels. They asked, 'Then who is the poor person?' He said, 'The one who finds no sufficiency, and whose situation is not known so that charity may be given to him.'"],[7870,"There is no contagion, no hama, and no Safar. A Bedouin said, 'O Messenger of God, then what about camels that are like gazelles, and a mangy camel mixes with them and they all become mangy?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Then who infected the first one?'"],[7871,"Do not say 'the calamity of time,' for God is time."],[7872,"When the servant of one of you prepares food, let him seat him with him. If he refuses, then let him hand him a bite in his hand."],[7873,"When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If it is obscured for you, then fast thirty."],[7874,"He forbade continuous fasting. They said, 'O Messenger of God, you practice continuous fasting!' He said, 'My Lord, blessed and exalted, feeds me and gives me drink.' The Messenger of God ﷺ then continued fasting with them for two days and two nights, after which they sighted the new moon."],[7875,"The prayer was called, then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and stood at his prayer place, and he remembered that he had not performed the ritual bath. He left and said, “Stay as you are,” and we had already formed rows. The Messenger of God ﷺ returned with his head dripping, and he led us in prayer."],[7876,"God, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the worldly heaven when the last third of the night remains and says, “Who is calling upon Me that I may answer him? Who is seeking My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who is asking that I may give him?” Or he said, “Who is asking Me that I may give him?”"],[7877,"You will find that people are mines: the best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam."],[7878,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God. Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."],[7879,"Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7880,"Horses have goodness in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."],[7881,"A man asked, “O Messenger of God, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He replied, “Does every one of you find two garments?!”"],[7882,"Adam and Moses argued. Moses said, “O Adam, you are the one who caused your descendants to enter the Fire.” Adam said—as I think—“By how much do you find that decreed for me? meaning, written.” He said, “So Adam argued against Moses.”"],[7883,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for livestock or hunting, a qīrāṭ is deducted from his reward every day."],[7884,"“Shall I tell you about the best of the dwellings of the Anṣār?” They said, “Yes.” He ﷺ said, “The Banū al-Najjār.” They said, “Then who?” He said, “Then the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj, then the Banū Sāʿidah.” They said, “Then who, O Messenger of God?” He said, “And in all the dwellings of the Anṣār there is good.”"],[7885,"Maʿmar narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah and Sulaymān b. Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7886,"The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so be different from them."],[7887,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the noon and afternoon prayers and said the salam after two rakʿahs, then he left. Dhū al-Shimālayn b. ʿAbd b. ʿAmr—who was an ally of the Banū Zuhrah—said to him: O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What is Dhū al-Yadayn saying? They said: He has spoken the truth. So he completed with them the two rakʿahs that were missing. Al-Zuhrī said: Then he prostrated two prostrations after he finished."],[7888,"Whoever acquires a dog, except a livestock dog or a hunting dog, a qīrāṭ is deducted from his reward every day."],[7889,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in God and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."],[7890,"The Hour will not come until two factions fight each other while their claim is one."],[7891,"The Fire complained to its Lord and said: Parts of me have consumed one another. So He permitted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. That is the most intense heat you feel and the most intense cold you feel."],[7892,"Every matter of importance that is not begun with praise of God is cut off."],[7893,"God, Blessed and Exalted, said: The most beloved of My servants to Me are those who are quickest to break the fast."],[7894,"When the reciter says āmīn, say āmīn."],[7895,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am a young man, and I fear hardship for myself, and I do not find the means to marry women. Do you command me to castrate myself? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The pen has already run concerning being brought together. Castrate if you wish, or leave it."],[7896,"Our stopping place tomorrow, God willing, will be at the valley of Banū Kinānah where they swore allegiance to disbelief."],[7897,"ʿAbbād b. Juwayriyah reported to us, from al-Awzāʿī, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[7898,"There is no governor except that he has two inner circles: an inner circle that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and an inner circle that does not spare any effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from the evil of the latter has indeed been protected."],[7899,"Shortening the greeting is a sunnah."],[7900,"The Prophet ﷺ saw 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafah praying and he recited aloud, so he said: O 'Abd Allah, do not make me hear, but let Allah hear."],[7901,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the recitation of 'Abd Allah b. Qays and said: He has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud."],[7902,"A woman is like a rib: if you try to straighten it, you break it; and if you enjoy her, you enjoy her while there is a bend in her."],[7903,"I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves wealth, it goes to his heirs; and whoever leaves debt, it is upon me."],[7904,"No one endures its hardship but that I will be a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[7905,"Journeys are only made to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Mosque of Iliya'."],[7906,"Imru' al-Qays is the leader of the poets to Hellfire."],[7907,"Dignity and tranquility are among the owners of sheep, and pride and arrogance are among the owners of camels from the people of Najd."],[7908,"When he was worried, he would touch his beard more."],[7909,"A bedouin entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque and said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, and do not forgive anyone along with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You have restricted something vast. He said: Then the bedouin turned away until he came to a corner of the mosque and urinated in it, and he was not reproached or insulted. The Prophet ﷺ said: This mosque was built for the remembrance of Allah and prayer. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it."],[7910,"Al-Nu'man b. 'Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Nu'man."],[7911,"Delay the prayer until it is cooler, for the intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[7912,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about praying in a single garment. He said: Does every one of you have two garments?"],[7913,"The superiority of congregational prayer over the prayer of an individual is twenty-five degrees."],[7914,"The Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes to reveal a mountain of gold, and the people will fight over it. Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety will be killed."],[7915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every predator with fangs, beasts killed by being struck and left to die, and the domestic donkey on the day of Khaybar."],[7916,"In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is death? He said: Death is death."],[7917,"Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."],[7918,"I seek forgiveness from Allah one hundred times every day."],[7919,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I am the Most Merciful, and it is the womb. I derived its name from My name. Whoever maintains its ties, I will maintain ties with him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him."],[7920,"I entered Paradise and saw a palace. I said: For whom is this? It was said: For Umar. Nothing prevented me from entering it except what I knew of your jealousy, O Umar. He said: Umar wept and said: Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?"],[7921,"Muhammad b. Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[7922,"Charity is only given out of surplus wealth. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Begin with those whom you support."],[7923,"My pulpit is on one of the ridges of Paradise."],[7924,"The orphan girl is to be consulted about herself; if she remains silent, that is her consent, but if she refuses, there is no compulsion upon her."],[7925,"The poor believers will enter Paradise half a day of the days of the Hereafter before the rich; that is five hundred years."],[7926,"Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7927,"Sufyan narrated to us from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7928,"Indeed the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one is Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim."],[7929,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches—Muhammad said: I have some doubt—a rak'ah or two rak'ahs of Asr before the sun sets has caught it."],[7930,"Whoever sees me in a dream has seen the truth, for Satan cannot imitate me."],[7931,"In the year of the conquest, he stood at al-Hajun and said: By Allah, you are the best of Allah's land and the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left. It was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful for me for an hour of a day, then it is sacred at this hour of mine: its trees are not to be cut down, its herbage is not to be uprooted, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it. He said: A man said—and people claimed he was Abbas—O Messenger of Allah, except for idhkhir, for it is for our houses, our graves, and our furnaces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Except for idhkhir."],[7932,"A man from the Ansar heard a Jewish man say: By the One who chose Musa over all mankind. He raised his hand and slapped him. He brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Ansari said: He said, 'By the One who chose Musa over all mankind,' while you are among us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The trumpet will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and the earth will swoon, except whom Allah wills. Then it will be blown again, and I will be the first to raise his head, and there will be Musa holding onto one of the pillars of the Throne. I do not know whether he was among those whom Allah exempted or whether he raised his head before me. And whoever says: I am better than Yunus b. Matta, has lied."],[7933,"Ibrahim ﷺ was circumcised at the age of eighty with an adze."],[7934,"A funeral procession passed by him, and they praised it with good, mentioning the virtues of good. He said: It is affirmed. Then another passed by him, and they criticized it with evil, mentioning the faults of evil. He said: It is affirmed. Then he said: You are Allah's witnesses on earth."],[7935,"A sick person should not bring his disease to a healthy one."],[7936,"Change the gray hair and do not imitate the Jews and Christians."],[7937,"Ghifar, Aslam, and those from Juhayna are better than the two allies: Ghatafan, Asad, Hawazin, and Tamim."],[7938,"The fire of Hell has been favored over this fire of yours by seventy-six parts, or ninety-six parts. They said: O Messenger of God, if it were enough."],[7939,"The most complete of the believers in faith is the one with the best character."],[7940,"Modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."],[7941,"The best of you are those who are best to their wives."],[7942,"The best of you are the best to my wives after me. He said: So 'Abd al-Rahman bequeathed to them such and such, and it was sold for four hundred thousand."],[7943,"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye. The 'ajwa date is from Paradise, and it is a healing from poison."],[7944,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: A man from Quraysh passed by dragging his lower garment. He said: O my nephew, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: We have heard what you say. Then he passed by him a second time and said to him the same thing. He said: We have heard what you say. If you return, I will carry you on my shoulder and throw you to the ground. Abu Hurayra said: And I will not return."],[7945,"The religion will remain manifest as long as people hasten to break the fast, for the Jews and Christians delay it."],[7946,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. If they say: There is no god but God, then they have protected their blood and their property from me, except for its right, and their reckoning is with God."],[7947,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the recitation of a man and said, “Who is this?” They said, “Abdullah b. Qays.” He said, “He has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.”"],[7948,"Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[7949,"We find within ourselves things we would not like to speak of, and that we have what the sun rises upon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Have you found this?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “That is pure faith.”"],[7950,"Four rivers burst forth from Paradise: Sayhan, Jayhan, the Nile, and the Euphrates."],[7951,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection – I think Yazid said – in the form of a salt-and-pepper ram, and it will be said, “O people of Paradise!” They will look up, fearful and anxious, afraid that they will leave what they are in. Then it will be said, “Do you recognize this?” They will say, “Our Lord, this is death.” Then He will say, “O people of the Fire!” They will look up, rejoicing and glad, hoping to leave what they are in. Then He will say, “Do you recognize this?” They will say, “Yes, this is death.” Then it will be ordered to be slaughtered, and it will be said to the two groups, “Eternity, and no death therein ever.”"],[7952,"Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. If people were to take a valley or a mountain pass, and the Ansar took a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar and their mountain pass."],[7953,"Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."],[7954,"The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh – the most tender to an orphan in his childhood, and the most careful of a husband in respect of what he possesses."],[7955,"He used to pray and say the takbir whenever he raised and lowered; and when he finished, he would say, “I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[7956,"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7957,"Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[7958,"Madinah – whoever introduces an innovation therein, or shelters an innovator, or takes as allies other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor voluntary deeds will be accepted from him."],[7959,"The superiority of the congregational prayer over a man’s prayer alone is twenty-five degrees."],[7960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously! He said: You are not like me. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. And I do not know except that he said: So undertake of deeds what you are able."],[7961,"The angels continue to pray for one of you as long as he remains in his prayer-place where he prayed, so long as he does not get up or break his wudu, saying: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."],[7962,"Who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation? Then let them create a mosquito, or let them create a small ant."],[7963,"Perform wudu from what the fire has changed, even if from a piece of dried curd. Ibn Abbas said: O Abu Hurayrah, should we perform wudu with hot water after it has boiled on the fire, and with oil after it has been cooked on the fire? He said: O son of my brother, when you hear a hadith being narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, do not strike examples for it."],[7964,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[7965,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the heaven of this world in the last half of the night, or the last third, and says: Who is there who calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who is there who asks of Me, that I may give him? Who is there who seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Until the dawn breaks and the one who goes out for the morning prayer returns."],[7966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed in prayer, then raised his head and said: O Allah, save Ayyash b. Abi Rabiah, Salamah b. Hisham, and al-Walid b. al-Walid. O Allah, make Your seizure severe upon Mudar, and make it upon them like the years of Yusuf. Then he said the takbir and fell prostrate."],[7967,"Every deed of the son of Adam is his, a good deed multiplied ten times its like up to seven hundred times. But fasting is Mine, and I reward it: he leaves food, drink, and his desire for My sake. So it is Mine, and I reward it."],[7968,"Indeed the lowest of the people of Paradise in station is one who wishes upon Allah, and it is said to him: That is yours, and the like of it with it."],[7969,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[7970,"Satan appeared to me in my prayer, so I seized his neck and choked him, and I felt the coldness of his tongue on my palm. Had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up for you to see."],[7971,"No one endures its hardship—meaning Madinah—and its distress except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. And no one leaves it out of aversion to it except that Allah will replace in it someone better than him. And Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. And he said: It expels its impurities just as the bellows expel the impurities of iron."],[7972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy while he was in the shade of a fort, and he said: 'Ibn Abi Kabshah has covered us with dust.' His son 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by the One who honored you, if you wish I will bring you his head.' He said: 'No, but be dutiful to your father and keep good companionship with him.'"],[7973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: 'The Jews claim that it is the minor infanticide.' Then he said: 'The Jews have lied.'"],[7974,"A woman suffering from madness came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me.' He said: 'If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah for you and He will heal you; and if you wish, you will be patient and there will be no reckoning against you.' She said: 'Rather, I will be patient and there will be no reckoning against me.'"],[7975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a Bedouin: 'Has Umm Mildam (fever) ever afflicted you?' He said: 'What is Umm Mildam?' He said: 'A heat that occurs between the skin and the flesh.' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Has headache ever afflicted you?' He said: 'What is headache?' He said: 'A vein that throbs on a person in his head.' He said: 'I have never experienced this.' When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this one.'"],[7976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man lying on his stomach, and he said: 'This is a posture that Allah does not love.'"],[7977,"Muhammad b. 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7978,"The orphan girl is to be consulted regarding herself; if she remains silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, then there is no compulsion upon her."],[7979,"Al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[7980,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7981,"When one of you is an imam, let him shorten [the prayer], for behind him are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need; but when he prays alone, let him prolong as he wishes."],[7982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: 'Allah knows best what they would have done.'"],[7983,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about those who are heedless, and he said: “Allah knows best what they used to do.”"],[7984,"Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, then to me."],[7985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade (using) gourds and vessels smeared with pitch, and he said: “Every intoxicant is unlawful.”"],[7986,"Whoever washes a dead person should perform a full bath, and whoever carries him should perform ablution, and whoever follows a funeral should not sit until it is placed down."],[7987,"Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[7988,"He saw a man following a pigeon, and he said: “A devil following a devil.”"],[7989,"Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, likewise. And we do not know anyone who ascribed this hadith through Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah except Hammad b. Salamah and Muhammad b. Abdullah, while Sharik disagreed with them and narrated it from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha; and others we named mention it from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, as mursal."],[7990,"You bring disputes to me, and perhaps some of you is more eloquent in his argument than others, so I judge in his favor according to what I hear from him. Whoever I judge in his favor with something from his brother's right, let him not take it, for I am only cutting for him a piece of the Fire."],[7991,"Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah except Abd al-Rahim b. Sulayman and Muhammad b. Bishr."],[7992,"Affliction will continue to befall the believing man and the believing woman until they meet Allah Almighty with no sin upon them."],[7993,"The lifespans of my nation are between sixty and seventy, and few of them surpass that."],[7994,"Whoever is given something as a life tenure, it belongs to him."],[7995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand (in prayer) until his feet became swollen. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you do this when Allah has already forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[7996,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight, and make them my heir; support me against those who wrong me, and show me my retribution from them."],[7997,"The religion will remain manifest as long as people hasten to break the fast, for the Jews and Christians delay it."],[7998,"The two sons of al-As are believers: Hisham and Amr."],[7999,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, so he stood up for it. It was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. He said: Death is a cause for alarm."],[8000,"The morsel of Khaybar has kept recurring in me until this moment, when it has cut my aorta."],[8001,"\"Who is your chief, O Banu Salimah?\" They said: \"Al-Jadd b. Qays, though we consider him stingy.\" He said: \"And what disease is worse than stinginess? Rather, your chief is Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.\""],[8002,"Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."],[8003,"The Quran was revealed in seven modes, and disputing about the Quran is disbelief."],[8004,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. The lot fell to A'ishah for the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq. In the middle of the night, A'ishah went out to relieve herself, and her necklace came loose, so she went to look for it. Mistah was an orphan under the care of Abu Bakr and part of his household. When A'ishah returned, she did not see the army. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami used to lag behind the people, picking up the bowl, the sack, and the water-skin. I think he said: Is this A'ishah? He turned his face away from her, then brought his camel close to her. He caught up with the army, and they said something, or spoke about it. Then he mentioned the hadith until it ended. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come and stand at the door and say: How is that one of yours? Until one day he came and said: Rejoice, O A'ishah, for Allah has sent down your vindication. She said: We praise Allah, not you. He said: Ten verses were revealed about that: \"Indeed, those who came with the falsehood are a group among you.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged Mistah, Hannah, and Hassan."],[8005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on Friday and mentioned a surah. Abu Dharr said to Ubayy: When was this surah revealed? Ubayy turned away from him. When he finished, he said: You get nothing from your prayer except what you wasted. Then he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: He spoke the truth."],[8006,"The poet of Khuza'ah said: O Allah, I call upon Muhammad with the ancient pact of our father and his father. Grant him a mighty victory, O guided one, and summon the servants of Allah to come as reinforcements."],[8007,"If there is healing in anything you treat yourselves with, then it is in cupping."],[8008,"O Banu Bayadah, marry Abu Hind."],[8009,"When the verse \"And warn your closest kindred\" was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"O Banu Hashim, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, O Safiyyah, paternal aunt of the Prophet, O Abbas, I own nothing for you from Allah. Ask me after this whatever you wish from my wealth.\""],[8010,"Al-Harith al-Ghatafani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, share with us half the dates of Madinah, or else we will fill it against you with horses and men.\" He said: \"Until I consult the Sa'ds, Sa'd b. Ubadah and Sa'd b. Mu'adh,\" meaning he would consult them. They said: \"By Allah, we did not give the lowly concession from ourselves in the pre-Islamic era, so how can we when Allah has brought Islam?\" Al-Harith returned to him and informed him, and he said: \"You have acted treacherously, O Muhammad.\" He said: Then Hassan said: \"O neighbor, whoever of you betrays the protection of his neighbor, Muhammad does not betray. If you betray, treachery is one of your customs, and baseness grows in the roots of sakhbar. And the trustworthiness of the Prophet, wherever you encounter it, is like glass whose crack cannot be mended.\" He said: Then al-Harith said: \"Restrain Hassan's tongue from us, O Muhammad, for if seawater were mixed with it, it would stir it up.\""],[8011,"That no wailing was done over the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him."],[8012,"That a man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the time of the dawn prayer. He prayed the first day while it was still dark, then the next day it became light. He said: \"Where is the one asking about the time? Whatever is between the two is a time.\""],[8013,"I intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, or a Thaqafi."],[8014,"The arrogant will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in the forms of small ants."],[8015,"That on the day of Adha he said: \"Whoever has already slaughtered, I think he said before our prayer, let him repeat his sacrifice.\""],[8016,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered a garden and a camel came and prostrated to him. They said: \"We are more deserving of prostrating to you.\" He said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[8017,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by some people shooting arrows and said: \"Shoot, O Banu Isma'il, for your father was an archer.\""],[8018,"When perfume is placed before one of you, let him touch some of it and not refuse it. And when sweets are placed before one of you, let him eat some of it and not refuse it."],[8019,"Perform wudu' from what the fire has changed, even if it is from the residue of aqit (dried curd). Abu Salamah said: Does not one of us anoint himself with milk? He said: O my son, when the hadith comes from the Messenger of God ﷺ, do not strike examples for it."],[8020,"When the noble of a people comes to you, honor him."],[8021,"I do not combine two fears and two securities for My servant. If I make him fear in this world, I give him security in the Hereafter; and if I give him security in this world, I make him fear in the Hereafter."],[8022,"Muhammad b. 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[8023,"God's anger intensified against a people who smashed the egg on the head of their Prophet while he was calling them to God."],[8024,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Fatimah bt. Qays: Go to the house of Umm Sharik, and do not make us miss you."],[8025,"That the Prophet ﷺ was informed that Safiyyah had menstruated. He said: I do not think she is anything but holding us back. They said: She has already performed the tawaf al-ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: Then let her depart."],[8026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to love the good omen and dislike the evil omen."],[8027,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Umm 'Uthman b. Talhah: Send me the key of the Ka'bah. She said: No, by al-Lat and al-'Uzza, I will not send it to you. Someone said: Send to her by force. Her son 'Uthman said: O Messenger of God, she is new to disbelief, so send me to her until I bring it to you. He said: So he went to her and said: O my mother, a matter has come other than what was, and if you do not give me the key, I will be killed! He said: So she brought it out and handed it to him, and he came running with it. When he drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he stumbled and the key fell from his hand. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and leaned over it with his garment and took it. Then he came to the door—I think he said—and opened it. Then he stood at the corners of the House and its sides calling upon God, then he prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars."],[8028,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or in addition to her maternal aunt."],[8029,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for it what He does not give for harshness."],[8030,"Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created such-and-such? Until he says: Then who created God? So when one of you sees anything of that, let him say: I have believed in God."],[8031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in the fear prayer. He divided the people into two groups. One group stood behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the other group stood facing the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one rak'ah with those behind him – I think he said – and prostrated twice with them. Then they stood up with him. When he stood upright, those behind him went back behind them, and those others came forward – I think – and he prayed one rak'ah with them and two prostrations."],[8032,"Madinah expels its impurities just as the bellows expel the impurities of iron. No one leaves it out of aversion to it except that Allah replaces him."],[8033,"The devil comes to one of you – I think he said – and says: 'Who created Allah?' So if any of you sees anything of that, let him say: 'I believe in Allah.'"],[8034,"The best charity is that given out of surplus wealth. And let one of you begin with those he supports."],[8035,"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar report. We do not know that Abu al-Zinad transmitted from Urwah from Abu Hurayrah any hadith other than this one, and it is well known from the hadith of Hisham."],[8036,"A man was brought to account, and nothing good was found for him except a thorny branch that he removed from the path, and he was forgiven."],[8037,"A woman was punished on account of a cat that she confined until it died of hunger. She neither fed it nor let it go so it could eat from the small creatures of the earth."],[8038,"The last of the towns of Islam to be ruined will be Madinah."],[8039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a funeral over which people were weeping, and I was with him along with Umar b. al-Khattab. Umar rebuked the women. He said: 'Leave them, O Ibn al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted, the eye sheds tears, and the covenant is recent.'"],[8040,"Al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a similar report. This hadith was narrated by more than one from Hisham b. Urwah, from Muhammad b. Amr, from Salamah b. al-Azraq, from Abu Hurayrah. I think al-Layth made a mistake in its chain, and we do not know of anyone who agreed with al-Layth in his narration."],[8041,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a slave woman who commits adultery before she is married. He said: 'If she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her.' Then he said on the third or fourth time: 'Sell her, even for a hair rope.'"],[8042,"Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them said: 'O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah.' The other, who was the more learned of the two, said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah and allow me to speak.' He said: 'Speak.' He said: 'My son was a laborer for this man, and he committed adultery with a woman. They told me that my son must be stoned, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked some men of knowledge, and they told me that my son must be given a hundred lashes and exiled for a year.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for the sheep and the slave girl, they are to be returned to you. Your son is to receive a hundred lashes and be exiled for a year. And you, Unays, go to this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her.' She confessed, and he stoned her."],[8043,"If the one who drinks standing knew what is upon him, he would vomit."],[8044,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone with us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have restricted something vast.' Then the Bedouin stood up and urinated in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pour a bucket of water over his urine.'"],[8045,"There is no such thing as bad omen, and I love good omens. It was said: 'What is a good omen?' He said: 'A good word that one of you hears.'"],[8046,"A Bedouin stood and urinated in the mosque. The people rushed at him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pour a bucket of water over his urine, or a large bucket of water, for you have been sent to make things easy, not to make things difficult.'"],[8047,"The best of the dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar. They said: 'Then who, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.' They said: 'Then who, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Then Banu Sa'idah.' They said: 'Then who, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Then in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.'"],[8048,"If I had gold equal to Mount Uhud, it would please me that not three nights pass while I still have any of it, except something I set aside for a debt."],[8049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr and said the salam after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn b. 'Amr b. Nadlah al-Khuza'i, an ally of Banu Zuhrah, said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'I did not forget and it has not been shortened.' Dhu al-Shimalayn said: 'Some of that has happened.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to the people and said: 'Is Dhu al-Shimalayn telling the truth?' They said: 'Yes.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, completed the prayer, and prostrated twice while sitting."],[8050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt."],[8051,"There was a man who used to lend money to people. He said to his servant: 'If a debtor is in difficulty, overlook his debt, perhaps Allah will overlook our faults.' When he met Allah, He overlooked his faults."],[8052,"Abu Hurayrah and Ka'b met. Abu Hurayrah began to narrate from the Prophet ﷺ and Ka'b began to narrate from the scriptures. Abu Hurayrah said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every prophet has an answered supplication, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community.\"' Ka'b said: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' Ka'b said: 'May his father and mother be sacrificed for him.' And I will tell you about Ibrahim. Then he mentioned the story of Ibrahim and the sacrifice."],[8053,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts charity and accepts only that which is good. He accepts it with His right hand, Blessed and Exalted, and nurtures it for His servant as one of you nurtures his colt or his young weaned camel."],[8054,"Ma'mar informed us from Ayyub from al-Qasim b. Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith was narrated by some of the companions of 'Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Ayyub from a man from al-Qasim from Abu Hurayrah, and they believe that Ayyub heard it from 'Abbad b. Mansur, but 'Abd al-Wahid b. Sibrah traced it back to al-Qasim b. Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah."],[8055,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, accepts charity, and does not accept of it—I think he said—except the pure. He accepts it with His right hand, Blessed and Exalted is He, and nurtures it for His servant as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel, until it meets him on the Day of Resurrection like Mount Uhud."],[8056,"Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8057,"Indeed, the Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them."],[8058,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has a pillar of light before the Throne. When the servant says, 'There is no god but Allah,' that pillar shakes. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, says, 'Be still.' It says, 'How can I be still when You have not forgiven the one who said it?' He says, 'Indeed, I have forgiven him.' Then it becomes still at that."],[8059,"Whoever frees a believing slave, Allah will free, for every limb of his, a limb of it from the Fire."],[8060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and Abu Hurayrah was among them. He said, 'If you meet Habbār b. al-Aswad and Nāfiʿ b. ʿAbd ʿAmr, burn them with fire, but do not kill them.' They had goaded Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when she set out from Makkah to the Prophet ﷺ, and she remained ill until she died. When the Prophet ﷺ bid us farewell, he said, 'I had commanded you to burn Habbār and Nāfiʿ, but it is not appropriate for anyone to punish with the punishment of Allah. If you meet them, kill them.'"],[8061,"Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Bukayr, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, with a similar narration, or something close to it, as far as I know, that Salih narrated to me."],[8062,"I am a guarantor on behalf of Allah for a man who goes out in the path of Allah, seeking the pleasure of Allah and striving in His path, that He will admit him to Paradise, or return him to his family with the reward and booty he has obtained."],[8063,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every prayer."],[8064,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8065,"Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah."],[8066,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I had intercourse with my wife during the day in Ramadan.' He said, 'Free a slave.' He said, 'I do not have one.' He said, 'Fast two consecutive months.' He said, 'I am not able.' He said, 'Feed sixty poor persons.' He said, 'I cannot find.' He said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket of dates, and he said, 'Where is the man who said what he said just now? Take this and give it in charity.' He said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava fields more in need of it than us.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until we saw his molars, then said, 'Take it and eat it, and spend it on your family.'"],[8067,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ during Ramadan and said: O Messenger of God, he had sexual intercourse with his wife during the day. He said: Woe to you, free a slave. He said: I do not have one. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: O Messenger of God, have I not been afflicted except because of fasting? He said: Feed sixty poor people. He said: I cannot find any. He said: Sit down. Then a man came with his charity carrying it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Where is the man who spoke just now? Take this and give it in charity on your own behalf. He said: O Messenger of God, is charity not only for one who is a guardian? By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no one between its two lava fields more in need than us. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed and said: Take it and eat it and spend it on your family."],[8068,"A man said: O Messenger of God, I broke my fast one day in the month of Ramadan. He said: Free a slave."],[8069,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated it to us from Muammal b. Ismail, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. Hisham b. Sa'd narrated it and erred in its chain, narrating it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah. The meaning is the same even though the wording differs."],[8070,"A man wronged himself until when death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind. By God, if God is able to get hold of me, He will punish me with a punishment with which He has not punished anyone of His creation. He said: His family did that to him. God, Blessed and Exalted, said to every thing that took something from him: Return what you have taken. Then he was standing. God, Blessed and Exalted, said: What made you do what you did? He said: Fear of You. So God forgave him."],[8071,"Sadaqah b. Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus b. Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. Sadaqah said: And Ibn Sam'an narrated to me, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[8072,"Whoever spends a pair of his wealth, the angels call him. Whoever is of the people of jihad is called from the Gate of Jihad, and whoever is of the people of fasting is called from the Gate of al-Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, what is upon a man if he is called from any gate, and will anyone be called from all of them? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: I hope that you will be one of them."],[8073,"The strong one is not the one who throws others down. They said: Then who is the strong one? He said: The one who controls himself when angry."],[8074,"Whoever swears or says in his oath: By al-Lat, let him say: There is no god but God."],[8075,"Whoever says to his companion, 'I will gamble with you,' let him give charity. And whoever says in his oath, 'By al-Lat,' let him say: There is no god but God."],[8076,"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[8077,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her. Then if she commits adultery again, let him sell her, even for a rope."],[8078,"Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8079,"Adam and Musa argued. Musa said, \"You are Adam who caused your descendants to be expelled from Paradise.\" Adam said to him, \"You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, and you blame me for a matter that was decreed upon me before I was created.\" He said: Thus Adam got the better of Musa."],[8080,"Time will draw near, knowledge will be taken away, trials will appear, miserliness will be cast, and al-harj will increase.\" They said, \"What is al-harj?\" He said, \"Killing, killing.\""],[8081,"When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left or under his left foot."],[8082,"When he prayed for rain, he turned his cloak inside out and faced the qiblah."],[8083,"It is not fitting for anyone to say, 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[8084,"I was on the point of ordering the prayer to be established, then going to the houses of people who do not attend the prayer and burning them down."],[8085,"Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Ashja' are allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."],[8086,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have made the time of the Isha prayer extend to midnight."],[8087,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer; the thief does not steal while he is a believer; the drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer; and the plunderer does not plunder a valuable item—I think he said—while he is a believer."],[8088,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, he said the takbir; when he bowed, he said the takbir; then he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' straightening his back; then while standing he said, 'Our Lord, to You be praise'; then he said the takbir; then when he prostrated, he said the takbir; then he said the takbir when he raised his head; then when he prostrated again; then he said the takbir when he raised his head until he finished his prayer; and he said the takbir when he got up from the two rak'ahs. Abu Hurayrah said: And I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8089,"When a man becomes bankrupt, or whoever buys a commodity and then becomes bankrupt, its owner has the most right to it."],[8090,"Every one of my community is pardoned except those who commit sins openly. Indeed, part of committing openly is that a man does something secretly and then tells about it."],[8092,"My servant committed a sin, and said: 'O Lord, forgive me my sin.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and punishes for sin.' Then he returned and sinned again, and said: 'O Lord, forgive me my sin.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and punishes for sin.' Then he returned and sinned again, and said: 'O Lord, forgive me my sin.' Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and punishes for sin. Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you.'"],[8093,"Indeed, the first group to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night when it is full, then those who follow them [will be] like the most beautiful shining star in the sky. Their hearts will be [united] like one heart. For each man among them [will be] two wives from the hūr al-ʿīn, the marrow of whose legs will be seen from behind the flesh."],[8094,"I have not given you anything, nor have I withheld it from you. I am only a divider; I place [it] where I am commanded."],[8095,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and differing with their prophets. But when I forbid you from something, avoid it, and when I command you to do something, do as much of it as you are able."],[8096,"The space of a bow of one of you in Paradise is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets."],[8097,"Do not spy on one another, do not vie with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."],[8098,"Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech."],[8099,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say 'There is no deity but Allah.' When they say 'There is no deity but Allah,' they have protected their blood and their wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8100,"No one's deeds will save them. They said, 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with His grace and mercy. But remain moderate and rejoice.'"],[8101,"I am the closest of people to Jesus son of Mary. The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their fathers are diverse."],[8102,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider will travel for one hundred years. Recite, if you wish: 'And extended shade.'"],[8103,"It is imminent that Jesus son of Mary will descend as a just arbiter and an equitable imam. He will kill the pig and break the cross, and the call will be one."],[8104,"The believer is the mirror of the believer; he protects him from behind and guards his property for him."],[8105,"It is not appropriate for a two-faced person to be trustworthy with God."],[8106,"The lowest of them may grant protection to the Muslims."],[8107,"Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir b. Zayd, from al-Walid b. Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8108,"I will certainly give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger love. Then Ali entered while he had sore eyes, so he spat in his eye, then gave him the banner, and God granted victory through him."],[8109,"Hamzah b. Malik b. Hamzah b. Farwah b. Sufyan wrote to me, informing me that his uncle Sufyan b. Hamzah narrated to him, from Kathir b. Zayd, from al-Walid b. Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8110,"Fasting is for Me, and I reward it. By the oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ, the odor of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to God than the scent of musk. So whoever among you wakes up fasting must not use obscene language or act foolishly. If someone fights him, let him say: I am fasting. For they will have on the Day of Resurrection a basin that only the fasting will drink from."],[8111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: Amen, Amen, Amen. It was said: O Messenger of God, you have never done this before. He said: Gabriel said: May the nose of one who reaches Ramadan without being forgiven be rubbed in dust. May the nose of a servant be rubbed in dust, or may he be far removed. Then he said: May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust, or may he be far removed, who reaches his parents or one of them and does not enter Paradise. I said: Amen. Then he said: May the nose of a servant, or a man, be rubbed in dust, or may he be far removed, who hears me mentioned in his presence and does not send blessings upon you. I said: Amen."],[8112,"Settlement is permissible between Muslims."],[8113,"God does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ill-gotten gains."],[8114,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade cutting its trees or beating them to shed leaves."],[8115,"Wretched is the slave of the dinar and the dirham."],[8116,"Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir b. Zayd, from al-Walid b. Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8117,"When the gaze enters, there is no permission."],[8118,"Indeed, the people of polytheism let their mustaches grow and shave their beards, so differ from them: let the beards grow and trim the mustaches."],[8119,"The ally of a people is one of them, the client of a people is one of them, and the sister's son of a people is one of them."],[8120,"Whoever deceives us is not from us."],[8121,"Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni, and tranquility is among the people of sheep and cattle, and disbelief is towards the east, among those who scream loudly, the people of horses and camel hair."],[8122,"The lower garment is to the middle of the shin, or to the ankles; whatever is below that is in the Fire."],[8123,"O people, leave me as long as I leave you. Those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning and their disagreements with their prophets. Whatever I command you, do as much of it as you can; and whatever I forbid you, desist."],[8124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate in the house of al-Abbas, or in the house of Hamzah, and said: 'Some people of my nation will surely plunge into what Allah granted His Messenger as spoils, having no share other than that. The expiations of sins are perfecting ablution in difficult circumstances, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer.'"],[8125,"O Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah, ransom yourself from Allah, for I cannot avail you anything against Allah. O Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, ransom yourself from Allah, for I cannot avail you anything against Allah."],[8126,"O Aishah, ransom yourself from Allah, for I cannot avail you anything against Allah, even with half a date. O Aishah, let no beggar return from you, even with a burnt hoof."],[8127,"I would not love to have Mount Uhud in my house as gold, such that a night passes by me while I have a dinar of it—except if I set it aside for a debt or expenditure in the path of God."],[8128,"I was favored with six qualities that none before me was given: I was forgiven my past and future sins; war booty was made lawful for me, and it was not lawful for anyone before me; my community was made the best of communities; the earth was made a mosque and a purifier for me; I was given al-Kawthar; and I was aided by awe. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, indeed your companion is the holder of the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection, with Adam and those below him under it."],[8129,"The people are a covering, and the Ansar are an undergarment. Were it not for the emigration, I would have been a man from the Ansar. If the people were to traverse a valley and the Ansar another valley, I would traverse the mountain pass of the Ansar. Indeed you will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me at the Pool."],[8130,"There is no zakah due on a Muslim for his slave or his horse."],[8131,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of prayer has caught it."],[8132,"Do not turn away from your fathers."],[8133,"People must stop raising their eyes to the sky during supplication, lest it be snatched away—meaning, or their eyesight be snatched away."],[8134,"Aslam—may God grant it peace—and Ghifar—may God forgive it."],[8135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Siba' b. 'Urfutah as governor of Madinah. He recited, \"Woe to those who give short measure,\" so I said, \"So-and-so is ruined; he has two measures: a measure by which he gives and a measure by which he takes.\""],[8136,"There is no zakah due on a Muslim for his slave or his horse."],[8137,"I arrived in Madinah while the Messenger of God ﷺ was at Khaybar. I found a man from Banu Ghifar leading the people in prayer. In the first rak'ah he recited Surah Maryam, and in the second, \"Woe to those who give short measure.\" I believe he said: the dawn prayer."],[8138,"The Prophet ﷺ said: When a man becomes bankrupt and a man finds—I believe he said—his goods with the other, he has a greater right to it."],[8139,"that he was imprisoned on suspicion"],[8140,"he acted as guarantor for his suspicion"],[8141,"Slow down, by God, slow down. For indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, is severe in punishment. Were it not for suckling infants, men bowing in prayer, and grazing beasts, punishment would have been poured upon you abundantly, or punishment would have been sent down upon you."],[8142,"Whoever is given charge of any affair of the Muslims, God entrusts with him an angel on his right—I think he said—and an angel on his left, guiding him and directing him if good is intended for him. And whoever is given charge of any affair of the Muslims and other than that is intended for him, he is left to his own self."],[8143,"There are three whose supplication God has taken upon Himself not to reject: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the wronged person until he is vindicated, and the traveler until he returns."],[8144,"Caution does not avail against destiny, and supplication avails as long as the decree has not descended. Indeed, affliction and supplication meet between heaven and earth and wrestle with each other until the Day of Resurrection."],[8145,"Indeed, God has ninety-nine names—and in one place—indeed, in Friday there is an hour. So I paused concerning it until I look at the original."],[8146,"There is no zakat on a Muslim's horse—I think he said—nor on his slave."],[8147,"Indeed, at the entrances of Madinah there are angels; neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it."],[8148,"When one of you prays and then remains seated in his place, the angels do not cease praying for him: 'O God, forgive him; O God, have mercy on him.'"],[8149,"They asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: How shall we pray for you? He said: Say, 'O God, send prayers upon Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent prayers and blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim in all the worlds. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[8150,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took me by the hand one day, and we went to the market of Banu Qaynuqa'. When he returned, he entered the mosque and sat in it. Then al-Hasan came running until he sat in his lap. The Messenger of God opened his mouth, and he put his mouth into his, then said: 'O God, I love him, so love him and love those who love him.' Abu Hurayrah said: I never saw him except that my eyes overflowed with tears."],[8151,"He prayed behind him, and he said: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Then he recited the Mother of the Qur'an until he reached, \"not of those who have earned wrath, nor of those who go astray.\" He said: Amin, and the people said: Amin. And he would say whenever he prostrated: Allah is Greater. And he said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8152,"I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he recited, \"When the sky is split asunder\" and he prostrated in it. And he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in it."],[8153,"Whoever takes people's wealth intending to repay it, Allah will repay it on his behalf. And whoever takes it intending to destroy it, Allah will destroy him."],[8154,"The Surah of Friday was revealed upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited it until he reached, \"And others among them who have not yet joined them.\" They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He remained silent until they had said that three times. Then he struck his hand on Salman and said: If faith were at the Pleiades, or hanging from the Pleiades, this one and his companions would attain it."],[8155,"The one who strives on behalf of the widow and the needy is like the one who fights in the path of Allah."],[8156,"The Hour will not be established until a man from Qahtan comes forth driving the people with his staff."],[8157,"The one with thin legs from Abyssinia will destroy the House of Allah."],[8158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession for the sale of 'araya for less than five wasqs."],[8159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam."],[8160,"A town-dweller must not sell on behalf of a desert-dweller."],[8161,"Do not turn away from one another, do not bid against one another, do not hate one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."],[8162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives: It is only this one, then keep to the mats."],[8163,"He said to his wives: This is the Hajj, then the purification of the mats."],[8164,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property, except for its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8165,"Say to whoever announces a lost item in the mosque: May you not find it."],[8166,"Whoever washes a dead person, let him perform ghusl."],[8167,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except al-Masjid al-Haram."],[8168,"The tall and huge person will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and weighed, and he will not weigh the wing of a mosquito with Allah."],[8169,"The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and his seat in the Fire is a distance of three days' travel."],[8170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks and prayed."],[8171,"If the world equaled the wing of a mosquito with Allah, He would not give a disbeliever anything from it."],[8172,"Do not abandon the two rak'ahs of Fajr, even if horses trample you."],[8173,"Five that the muhrim may kill: the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the biting dog, and the snake."],[8174,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'Fleeing from a lion' - he said: The lion."],[8175,"Whoever performs wudu and does it well, then goes out and finds that the people have already prayed—Allah will give him the like of the reward of the one who prayed it and attended it, without that diminishing anything from their rewards."],[8176,"One or two sucklings do not make breastfeeding prohibited; only that which splits the intestines makes it prohibited."],[8177,"Seven [types of people] will be in the shade of the Throne, whom Allah will shade on a day when there is no shade but His: a just imam; a young man who grows up in the worship of Allah; a man who remembers Allah in private and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah; a man whom a woman of rank and wealth invites [to sin] and he says, 'Indeed I fear Allah'; a man who gives charity and conceals it so that his left hand does not know what his right hand has done, or what his right hand spends; a man whose heart is attached to the mosques, or to the mosque, when he leaves it until he returns to it; and two men who love each other for the sake of Allah, who meet upon that and part upon that."],[8178,"Indeed faith will shrink back to Madinah just as a snake shrinks back to its hole."],[8179,"Abd Allah b. Numayr and Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb b. Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs b. Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the like of it."],[8180,"He prohibited two ways of dressing and two ways of selling, and prayer at two times: after Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises. He also prohibited wrapping oneself in a single garment with no opening for the arms (ishtimal al-samma), sitting with one's legs drawn up and wrapped in a single garment exposing one's private parts to the sky, and the transactions of munabadhah and mulamasah."],[8181,"Sayhan, Jayhan, the Nile, and the Euphrates—each is among the rivers of Paradise."],[8182,"Sayhan, Jayhan, the Nile, and the Euphrates—each is among the rivers of Paradise."],[8183,"What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is over my basin (hawd)."],[8184,"What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[8185,"Delay the Zuhr prayer until it is cooler, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[8186,"The Euphrates is about to uncover a treasure of gold; whoever finds it should not take anything from it."],[8187,"Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, accepts charity, and He accepts from it only what is good. Then He nurtures it just as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel."],[8188,"Mubārak b. Faḍālah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Khubayb, from Ḥafṣ, from Abū Hurayrah, who raised it to the Prophet."],[8189,"When Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, created Ādam, he sneezed and said: 'Praise be to Allah.' His Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, said to him: 'May your Lord have mercy on you, O Ādam.'"],[8190,"Madinah has guards at its mountain passes – I think he said – from the angels. Plague and the Dajjāl cannot enter it."],[8191,"He forbade the sale by casting pebbles."],[8192,"A time is about to come upon people when the best of them will be one with a small flock of sheep, who establishes the prayer, gives the zakāh, and worships Allah until certainty (death) comes to him."],[8193,"Indeed a man may perform – or he said: the worker performs – the deeds of the people of the Fire for seventy years, then his life is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise. And the worker performs the deeds of the people of Paradise for seventy years, then his life is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire."],[8194,"Sayḥūn, Jayḥūn, the Nile, and the Euphrates: each is among the rivers of Paradise, and I have seen and drunk from each of them."],[8195,"What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon a water channel from the channels of Paradise."],[8196,"It is enough of a lie for a man to narrate everything he hears."],[8197,"I cursed fever in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Indeed it removes the sins of the believer just as the bellows removes the dross of iron.'"],[8198,"What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[8199,"What lies between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and a prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."],[8200,"The supplication of any one of you continues to be answered as long as he does not become impatient."],[8201,"For one of you to gather a bundle of firewood and carry it on his back is better for him than to come to a man and ask him, whether he gives him or refuses him."],[8202,"Let none of you wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him; rather let him say: 'O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me.'"],[8203,"The prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five degrees."],[8204,"Any woman who has touched incense should not attend the prayer with us."],[8205,"None of you will be saved by his deeds. A man said: 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His mercy.'"],[8206,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of 'Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches one rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."],[8207,"Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Zayd, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, Busr b. Sa'id, and 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration."],[8208,"When the day is hot, delay the prayer until it is cooler, for the intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[8209,"Dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham; there is no superiority between them."],[8210,"Whoever Allah intends good for, He afflicts him."],[8211,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from poverty, from scarcity and abasement, and I seek refuge in You lest I wrong or be wronged."],[8212,"There is no leader of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hands bound to his neck; the truth will either release him or destroy him."],[8213,"I was commanded to a town that consumes other towns. They call it Yathrib, and it is Madinah; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."],[8214,"The angels attend the dying person. If he is a righteous man, they say: 'Come out, O good soul that was in a good body; come out praiseworthy and rejoice in rest, sweet basil, and a Lord who is not angry.' This continues to be said to it until it comes out, then it is ascended with to heaven. Permission is sought for it, and it is said: 'Who is this?' They say: 'So-and-so.' They say: 'Welcome to the good soul that was in a good body; enter praiseworthy.' This continues to be said to it until it is brought before God, Blessed and Exalted. If he is an evil man, they say: 'Come out, O foul soul that was in a foul body; come out blameworthy and rejoice in boiling water and fetid pus, and other torments of its kind paired with it.' He said: It comes out, then it is ascended with to heaven. Permission is sought for it, and it is said: 'So-and-so.' They say: 'No welcome to the foul soul that was in a foul body; return blameworthy, for the gates of heaven will not be opened for you.' Then he goes to the grave. The righteous man is seated in his grave without terror or fear, and it is said to him: 'In what condition were you?' He says: 'In Islam.' It is said to him: 'What do you say about this man?' He says: 'He is the Messenger of God; he came to us with clear proofs from our Lord, and we believed in him and affirmed him.' It is said to him: 'Have you seen God?' He says: 'It is not fitting for anyone to see God.' Then an opening is made for him toward the Fire, and he looks at it, parts of it destroying others. It is said: 'Look at what God has protected you from.' Then an opening is made for him toward Paradise, and he looks at its beauty and what is in it. It is said to him: 'This is what God has prepared for you.' And it is said to him: 'Upon certainty you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised, if God wills.' The evil man is seated in his grave terrified and fearful, and it is said to him: 'In what condition were you?' He says: 'I do not know.' He says: 'What did you say about this man?' He says: 'I do not know; I heard the people saying something.' Then an opening is made for him toward Paradise, and he looks at its beauty and what is in it. It is said: 'Look at what God has turned away from you.' Then an opening is made for him toward the Fire, and he looks at it, parts of it destroying others. It is said: 'This is your seat and your abode; upon doubt you lived, and upon it you died, then you will be punished.' This hadith we do not know to be reported from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ except through this route with this chain."],[8215,"Learn from your lineages what enables you to maintain your ties of kinship, for maintaining kinship ties prolongs life and increases wealth."],[8216,"The grateful eater is like the patient faster."],[8217,"Dawood b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ma'n b. Muhammad, from Hanzalah b. Ali, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8218,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me and I reward it. He leaves his food and drink for My sake."],[8219,"Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Hanzalah b. Ali, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8220,"Stinginess and faith do not combine in the heart of a Muslim man, and dust in the path of God and the smoke of Hell do not combine in the heart of a Muslim man."],[8221,"There will come with me from my nation on the Day of Resurrection like the flood and the night, and a crushing crowd will crush, so the angels will say: 'Those who came with Muhammad are more than those who came with the rest of the nations or the prophets.'"],[8222,"When God, Blessed and Exalted, willed to confine Yunus in the belly of the whale, God revealed to the whale: 'Do not scratch his flesh or break his bone.' So it took him and plunged with him to its dwelling place in the sea. When it reached the bottom of the sea with him, Yunus heard a sound, and he said to himself: 'What is this?' God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him while he was in the belly of the whale: 'This is the glorification of the creatures of the earth.' So he glorified while in the belly of the whale. The angels heard his glorification and said: 'Our Lord, we hear a faint voice in a foreign land.' God, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'That is My servant Yunus; he disobeyed Me, so I confined him in the belly of the whale in the sea.' They said: 'The righteous servant from whom a good deed used to ascend to You every day and night?' He said: 'Yes.' So they interceded for him at that, and He commanded the whale, and it cast him onto the shore as God, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'And he was ill.'"],[8223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took me by the hand and said: \"God, Blessed and Exalted, created the soil on Saturday, created in it the mountains on Sunday, created the trees on Monday, created what is disliked on Tuesday, created light on Wednesday, and dispersed—I think he said—the creatures in it on Thursday, and created Adam after the afternoon of Friday, the last of creation in the last hour of Friday's hours, between the afternoon and the night.\""],[8224,"If your life is prolonged, it is likely that you will see a people who go out in the morning under the wrath of God and return in the evening under the curse of God, holding in their hands things like the tails of cattle."],[8225,"When one of you wakes up, he should not put his hand into the washing vessel—or he said into the water—until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[8226,"He forbade continuous fasting, so they said, \"You fast continuously.\" He said, \"I am not like you in that; God, Blessed and Exalted, feeds me and gives me drink. So take upon yourselves from deeds what you are able to bear.\""],[8227,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."],[8228,"My example and the example of the prophets before me is like a man who built a house, perfected it, and beautified it except for the place of one brick. People began to go around it and wonder at it, saying, \"We have never seen anything more beautiful than this, if only for the place of this brick.\" So I am the place of that brick."],[8229,"If I had the like of Mount Uhud in gold, it would please me to spend it in the path of God, and not three nights would pass while I still had a dinar or a dirham of it, except for something I set aside for a debt I owe."],[8230,"Fasting is a shield. When one of you is fasting, he should not use obscene language or act foolishly. If someone insults him, let him say, \"I am a fasting person.\""],[8231,"The odor of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to God than the scent of musk."],[8232,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him, except fasting; it is for Me, and I reward for it. A good deed is multiplied ten times its like up to seven hundred times, except fasting; it is for Me, and I reward for it."],[8233,"The poor person is not the one whom a date or two dates would turn away, but the poor person is the one who does not ask people and is not noticed so that he may be given."],[8234,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have stayed behind a detachment that raids in the path of God, but I do not find the means to carry them, and they do not find the means to follow me, and it does not please them to stay behind."],[8235,"Do not revile time, for God is time; He alternates the night and the day and brings the ages."],[8236,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and falling into a well is without liability, and [injury in] a mine is without liability, and on buried treasure a fifth is due."],[8237,"The delaying of payment by a rich man is injustice."],[8238,"The intense heat is from the blast of Hell, so cool down your prayer."],[8239,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ that he saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. The man said: It is a sacrificial camel! He said: Ride it."],[8240,"Do not wish to meet the enemy, for you do not know what will happen in that."],[8241,"No one leaves Madinah except that someone better than him is substituted in it."],[8242,"Whoever is named with my name must not use my kunyah, for I am Abu al-Qasim."],[8243,"Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied up should milk it; if he is satisfied with it, he keeps it, otherwise he returns it along with a sa' of dates."],[8244,"The bad breath of a fasting person is better in the sight of God than the fragrance of musk."],[8245,"Our dowry, when the Messenger of God ﷺ was among us, was ten awaq."],[8246,"God is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you - I think he said - who finds his lost mount, I think he said - in a waterless desert with his food and drink on it."],[8247,"The angels of the day succeed the angels of the night, and they gather at the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer. Then those who were among you ascend, and the Blessed and Exalted says, \"How did you leave My servants?\" They say, \"We came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying.\""],[8248,"In the end of time there will be tribulations like patches of dark night. The safest of people from them is the owner of a mountain peak who eats from his sheep, or from the milk of his sheep, and a man who takes hold of the rein of his horse, eating from the booty of his horse or his spear."],[8249,"A woman passed by him and he perceived from her the scent of perfume. Abu Hurayrah said to her, \"Do you intend the mosque?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"And for it you have perfumed yourself?\" She said, \"Yes.\" Then Abu Hurayrah said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Any woman who perfumes herself and then comes to the mosque, her prayer will not be accepted until she performs a ghusl like her ghusl from janabah.'\""],[8250,"God does not accept the prayer of a woman who perfumes herself for the mosque, or for this mosque, until she performs a ghusl like her ghusl from janabah."],[8251,"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? There is no might and no power except with God."],[8252,"I was with him when he passed by a courtyard, and he said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Many an oath does not ascend to God in this spot.'\" He said, \"Then I saw the slave dealers in it later.\""],[8253,"Eating any fanged beast of prey is forbidden."],[8254,"A thief was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and they said, \"He has stolen.\" He said, \"I do not think he has stolen.\" He said, \"Yes, I did it, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Take him and cut off his hand, then cauterize it, then bring him to me.\" So he was taken, his hand was cut, then it was cauterized, then he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Repent to God.\" He said, \"I repent to God.\" He said, \"May God accept your repentance,\" or he said, \"O God, accept his repentance.\""],[8255,"When you see a man selling in the mosque, say, \"May God not make your trade profitable.\" And when you see someone announcing a lost item in the mosque, say, \"May God not return your lost item to you.\""],[8256,"Whoever washes a dead body, let him perform ghusl, and whoever carries it, let him perform wudu."],[8257,"Abu Hurayrah prayed the Friday prayer and recited Surah al-Jumu'ah and 'When the hypocrites come to you' (Surah al-Munafiqun). Then he said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ reciting these two on Friday.\""],[8258,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said, \"God knows best what they would have done.\""],[8259,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, descends every night when the last third of the night remains to the lowest heaven and says: 'Who is calling upon Me that I may answer him? Who is asking My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who is asking Me that I may give him?' until dawn breaks."],[8260,"Do you dispute about the moon on the night of the full moon, when there is no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: Do you dispute about seeing the sun, when there is no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: Then you will see Him in the same way. The people will be held back on the Day of Resurrection, then it will be said: 'Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it.' Among them are those who follow the sun, among them those who follow the moon, and among them those who follow false deities. This community will remain, including its hypocrites, until the Blessed and Exalted comes to them and says: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'You are our Lord.' Then Allah will strike a wall of Hell between them, and I will be the first of the messengers to pass with my community. On that day no one will speak except the messengers, and the call of the messengers on that day will be: 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety.' In Hell there are hooks like the thorns of the Sa'dan plant. Have you seen the thorns of the Sa'dan? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorns of the Sa'dan, snatching people according to their deeds. Among them are those who are crushed, or he said: crushed, and among them are those who are saved. Until when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills mercy for whomever He wills among the people of the Fire, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands that they bring out those who used to worship Allah. They will bring them out, recognizing them by the marks of prostration. Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. They will come out of the Fire, having been burned, and water of life will be poured over them, and they will grow in it as a seed grows in the silt of a flood. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will finish judging between the servants, and one man will remain between Paradise and Hell, he is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise, facing the Fire. He will say: 'O Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its smell has afflicted me and its heat has burned me.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'Is it likely that if I do that for you, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, by Your might.' He will give his Lord whatever pledge and covenant He wills, and Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. When he faces Paradise and sees its splendor, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent, then he will say: 'O Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'Did you not give pledges and covenants that you would not ask for anything other than what you had asked?' He will say: 'O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation.' He will say: 'Is it likely that if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, by Your might, I will not ask You for anything else.' He said: He will give his Lord whatever pledge and covenant He wills, and He will bring him forward to the gate of Paradise. When he reaches its gate, it will open for him, and he will see its splendor and what is in it of freshness and joy. He will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent, then he will say: 'O Lord, admit me to Paradise.' The Blessed and Exalted will say: 'How treacherous you are, how treacherous you are. You have given pledges and covenants that you would not ask for anything other than what you were given.' He will say: 'O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation!' So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will laugh at him, then He will permit him to enter Paradise. Then He will say: 'Wish,' until when his wishes are exhausted, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say, and his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will remind him, until when his wishes come to an end, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'You will have that and the like of it with it.' Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will have that and ten times its like.' Abu Hurayrah said: I did not memorize from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he said: 'You will have that and the like of it with it.' Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I heard him say: 'You will have that and ten times its like.' This hadith was narrated by Shu'ayb and Mu'awiyah b. Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib and 'Ata' b. Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id."],[8261,"Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times after a prayer, praises Him thirty-three times, and magnifies Him thirty-three times, and says to complete one hundred: 'There is no deity except Allah alone, with no partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."],[8262,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, when a third of the night has passed, or the middle of the night, or He delays until a third of the night, or until the middle of the night, He commands a caller who calls out: 'Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him? Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any repentant that I may turn to him?'"],[8263,"Muhadir narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq and Habib, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[8264,"They both testified to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[8265,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, delays until a third of the night has passed, or remains, then He descends and says: 'Is there any supplicant whose prayer is answered? - I think he said: - Is there any asker who is given? - Any seeker of forgiveness from sin?'"],[8266,"Might is My waist-wrapper, and pride is My cloak. Whoever contends with Me for either of them, I will punish him."],[8267,"They both testified to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."],[8268,"Indeed, when a servant says: 'There is no deity except Allah, and Allah is greater,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken the truth; there is no deity except Me, and I am greater.' When the servant says: 'There is no deity except Allah alone,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'There is no deity except Me alone.' When the servant says: 'There is no deity except Allah alone, with no partner,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'There is no deity except Me alone, with no partner.' When the servant says: 'There is no deity except Allah alone, with no partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'There is no deity except Me alone, with no partner, Mine is the dominion and Mine is the praise.' When the servant says: 'There is no deity except Allah, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'There is no deity except Me, and there is no power and no strength except with Me.'"],[8269,"Whoever remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself. Whoever remembers Me in an assembly of people, I remember him in an assembly better and more numerous than them."],[8270,"Perform ablution from what the fire has cooked."],[8271,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is more virtuous than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[8272,"The congregational prayer equals twenty-five of the prayer of an individual, and a prayer in this mosque of mine is like a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque — I think he said: — and no one patiently endures its hardships and severity — meaning Madinah — except that I will be an intercessor and witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[8273,"It is not appropriate for a two-faced person to be trustworthy."],[8274,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[8275,"None of you should walk in a single sandal; let him remove both or wear both."],[8276,"When one of you wakes up at night and wakes his wife and they pray together, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember Allah much."],[8277,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will send a wind from Yemen, softer than silk, and it will not leave anyone in whose heart there is an atom's weight of faith except that it will take his soul."],[8278,"He never abandoned the Duha prayer, whether traveling or not."],[8279,"Whoever prays one hundred verses in a night is not recorded among the heedless, and whoever prays two hundred verses is recorded — I think he said — among the devout."],[8280,"The farthest of you, then the farthest, has the greatest reward."],[8281,"Allah is more intensely pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you is with his camel in a desolate land, fearing that thirst will kill him there."],[8282,"Narrated to us Salih b. Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata' b. Yazid and Abu 'Abdullah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[8283,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains and says: 'Who supplicates to Me that I may answer him? Who asks of Me that I may give him? Who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him?'"],[8284,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[8285,"When rain fell upon them in Madinah and the gutters flowed, he said: 'There will be no drought upon them this year.'"],[8286,"He used to trim his nails and clip his moustache on Friday before going out to the prayer."],[8287,"Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah,' it will benefit him one day of his lifetime, before which whatever befalls him will befall him."],[8288,"When Friday comes - I think he said - angels stand at the doors of the mosque recording the people, whoever comes first then next. When the imam comes out, the scrolls are rolled up and they come and listen to the remembrance."],[8289,"The likeness of one who hastens to go to Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel; then the next like one who offers a cow; then the next like one who offers a ram; then the next like one who offers a chicken; then the next like one who offers an egg."],[8290,"When two people insult each other, whatever they say is upon the one who initiated it, unless the one wronged transgresses."],[8291,"Rights will surely be restored to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, even the hornless sheep will be retaliated against the horned one for its goring."],[8292,"Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qur'an is not recited is deficient."],[8293,"The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."],[8294,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about backbiting and said: 'It is mentioning your brother with what he dislikes.' He said: 'What if what I say is true of my brother?' He said: 'If what you say is true of him, you have backbitten him, and if it is not true, you have slandered him.'"],[8295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the cemetery and said: Peace be upon the abodes of a believing people. He greeted its inhabitants and said: Indeed, if Allah wills, we will join you. I wish that we had seen our brothers. They said: Are we not your brothers? He said: You are my companions, and my brothers are a people who will come after me from my Ummah, and I will be at the forefront at the Basin. They said: How will you recognize those of your Ummah who have not yet come? He said: Consider if a man has horses with white blazes and white stockings among horses that are pure black—does he not recognize his horses? They said: Certainly, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They will come with white marks on their faces and limbs from the traces of ablution, and I will be your forerunner at the Basin. I will drive away some men from my Basin as a stray camel is driven away. I will say: Come here! But it will be said: They changed things after you. So I will say: Away, away!"],[8296,"I am the most self-sufficient of partners from association. Whoever does a deed for Me and associates someone else with Me in it—he mentioned a word, I think he said—then it is for My partner."],[8297,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they testify that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and what I have brought, they have protected—I think he said—from me their blood except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8298,"The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones. The best rows of women are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones."],[8299,"Madinah expels its wicked inhabitants."],[8300,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: My father died and left wealth but did not make a will. Will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf? He said: Yes."],[8301,"Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah raises ranks and erases sins? Abundant steps to the mosque, waiting for the next prayer after the prayer, and perfecting ablution despite difficulties."],[8302,"The believer—twice or three times—is jealous, and Allah is jealous, and Allah is more intensely jealous."],[8303,"When one of you supplicates, let him not say: If You will. But let him be firm in asking."],[8304,"I am the best of partners. Whoever does a deed and associates someone else with Me in it, I am free of it, and it is for the one he associated."],[8305,"Charity does not decrease wealth, nor does a man forgive an injustice except that Allah increases him in honor, nor does a man humble himself except that Allah raises him."],[8306,"He forbade making vows and said: It does not avert destiny; it only extracts from the miser."],[8307,"None of you should outbid his brother in a sale, nor propose to a woman when his brother has already proposed to her."],[8308,"A false oath makes goods sell but erases the blessing."],[8309,"Do you know what backbiting is? They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'Mentioning your brother in a way he dislikes.' It was said, 'What if my brother actually has what I say?' He said, 'If he has what you say, then you have backbitten him; and if he does not have what you say, then you have slandered him.'"],[8310,"The signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his promise, and when he is entrusted he betrays."],[8311,"Help your brother, whether he is the oppressor or the oppressed. If he is the oppressor, then prevent him from oppression, for that is helping him; and if he is the oppressed, then support him until he gets his right."],[8312,"Indeed, a man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise for a long time, but his final deeds are those of the people of Hell, so Allah makes him one of the people of Hell. And indeed, a man may do the deeds of the people of Hell for a long time, but Allah causes his final deeds to be those of the people of Paradise, so Allah makes him one of the people of Paradise."],[8313,"A black man used to clean the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ missed him, and they said, 'He has died.' The Prophet ﷺ came to his grave and prayed over him."],[8314,"Charity never decreases wealth."],[8315,"Whoever cheats us is not one of us."],[8316,"I asked My servant for a loan and he did not give Me, and he hurts Me saying, 'Woe to time!' and I am time."],[8317,"He came to the graveyard and said, 'Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you.' Then he said, 'I wish we could meet our brothers.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers?' He said, 'You are my companions, and my brothers are those who have not yet come after me, and I will precede them at the Basin.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation who have not yet come?' He said, 'Do you not see that if a man had horses with white blazes and white stockings among black horses, would he not recognize them?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'They will come on the Day of Resurrection with white marks from the traces of ablution, and I will precede them at the Basin. I think he said: I will drive people away from my Basin as a stray camel is driven away.' Then he mentioned a word and it was said, 'They changed after you; they kept turning back on their heels.' So I say, 'Away with them, away with them!'"],[8318,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whom I maintain ties with but they cut me off; I am good to them but they are bad to me; I am forbearing with them but they are ignorant.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'If it is as you say, it is as if you are feeding them hot ashes, and Allah will remain your supporter as long as you continue in that.'"],[8319,"At every gate of the mosque on Friday there are two angels recording the first, then the next, like one who presents a camel, and like one who presents a cow, and like one who presents a bird, and like one who presents an egg. When the imam sits, meaning on the pulpit, the scrolls are rolled up."],[8320,"The hour will not rise until thirty Dajjals appear, each claiming to be Allah's Messenger, and until wealth overflows, trials appear, and harj increases. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said: Killing, killing."],[8321,"Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah raises ranks and expiates sins: taking many steps to the mosques, waiting for the prayer after the prayer, and completing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties."],[8322,"When one of you supplicates - I think he said: - let him be firm, for Allah is not too great for anything He might give him."],[8323,"Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east."],[8324,"He forbade making nabidh in a gourd or a varnished jar."],[8325,"The sun does not rise on a day, or over a day, better than Friday - I think he said: - and there is nothing except that it is startled on Friday except the two heavy ones: the jinn and mankind."],[8326,"If a believer knew the punishment that is with Allah, he would never hope for Paradise; and if a disbeliever knew the mercy that is with Allah, he would never despair of mercy."],[8327,"A disbeliever and the Muslim who kills him will never both be together in the Fire."],[8328,"Whoever washes a corpse, meaning a deceased person, must bathe; and whoever carries it must perform ablution."],[8329,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole age."],[8330,"The Prophet ﷺ met Hudhayfah and wanted to shake his hand, but Hudhayfah withdrew. He said: I am junub. The Prophet ﷺ said: When a believer shakes his brother's hand, their sins fall off as leaves fall from a tree."],[8331,"Indeed, among the major sins is a man's overstepping against the honor of a man, or a Muslim man, without right; and among the major sins is the two-fold insult with an insult."],[8332,"The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar."],[8333,"Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever calls to misguidance will bear a sin like the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their sins."],[8334,"There is no disease but that in the black seed there is a cure for it, except death."],[8335,"Make the rows straight in prayer."],[8336,"The slave is entitled to his food and clothing, and he is not tasked with work except what he can bear."],[8337,"The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones, in prayer. And the best rows of women in prayer are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones."],[8338,"The majority are the few, except for those who say 'like this, and like this, and like this.'"],[8339,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have a neighbor who harms me.' He said to him: 'Take out your belongings and place them on the road.' So the man took his belongings and threw them on the road. Everyone who passed by him said: 'What is wrong with you?' He said: 'My neighbor harms me!' So they said: 'O Allah, curse him! O Allah, disgrace him!' The man then said: 'Return to your home, by Allah I will never harm you again.'"],[8340,"I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Hand me the foreleg.' So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg.' So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a sheep has only two forelegs.' He said: 'If you had looked for it, you would have found it.'"],[8341,"Abu 'Asim narrated to us from Ibn 'Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8342,"The likeness of one who goes early to Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers a sparrow, then like one who offers an egg. When the imam comes out and sits on the pulpit, the scrolls are folded up."],[8343,"Leave me with what I have left you. Those before you perished only because of their excessive questioning and disagreeing with their prophets. Whatever I forbid you, avoid it, and whatever I command you, do as much of it as you can."],[8344,"I was about to order that the prayer be established, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, then I would go off to some people who do not attend the prayer and burn them. If any one of them had been offered a fat bone or two trotters, he would have attended."],[8345,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[8346,"The best women who ride camels are the most tender to a child and the most careful of a husband's property on a night."],[8347,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling with his companions, he heard a man cursing his she-camel. He said: 'Where is the one cursing his she-camel? Make her go back, for you have been answered.'"],[8348,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for one hundred years. Recite, if you wish: 'And shade extended.'"],[8349,"Beware of continuous fasting. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously.' He said: 'I am not like you; my Lord gives me food and drink.'"],[8350,"Whoever carries weapons against us is not one of us."],[8351,"The parable of the son of Adam, his wealth, his family, and his deeds is like a man who had three brothers, or three companions. One of them said: 'I am with you during your life, but when you die, I am not of you and you are not of me.' The second said: 'I am with you, but when you reach that tree, I am not of you and you are not of me.' The third said: 'I am with you in life and in death.'"],[8352,"The best charity is that given from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."],[8353,"Ibrahim was circumcised with an adze after eighty years."],[8354,"Whoever wrongfully takes - I think he said - a span of land will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[8355,"Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be made to wear it around his neck from seven earths."],[8356,"Three people Allah will not look at: the lying leader, the adulterous old man, and the arrogant poor person."],[8357,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the sound of a child, so he shortened [the prayer]."],[8358,"The person with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be the one for whom two sandals of fire are placed, from which his brain boils."],[8359,"I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8360,"Do not combine my name and my kunya. I am Abu al-Qasim. Allah gives, and I distribute."],[8361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that any of you urinate in stagnant water, or bathe in it from janabah."],[8362,"If a man were to look into his neighbor's house and the neighbor threw a pebble at his eye, there would be nothing against him."],[8363,"Knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will appear, and harj will increase. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing."],[8364,"The woman is like a rib: if you try to straighten it, you will break it; if you enjoy her, you enjoy her with some crookedness."],[8365,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[8366,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created the creation, He wrote with His own hand upon Himself: My mercy prevails over My wrath."],[8367,"We have not made peace with them since we fought them, and whoever leaves any of them out of fear is not from us—meaning snakes."],[8368,"My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."],[8369,"Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent."],[8370,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ‘Amir b. al-Akwa‘: “Take from these little ones of yours.” He said: Then he said—I think—“By Allah, were it not for Allah, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed.”"],[8371,"La ilaha illa Allah will never cease to ward off from its people what they care not about as long as they care not about what befalls them in their religion when their worldly affairs are safe for them. When its people no longer care about what befalls them in their religion through the safety of their worldly affairs and they say La ilaha illa Allah, it will be said to them: “You have lied.”"],[8372,"Indeed I see those behind me just as I see those in front of me; straighten your rows and perfect your bowing and prostration."],[8373,"He was asked about riding a sacrificial camel. He said: “Ride it.” He said: “It is a budnah.” He said: “Ride it, woe to you—or may Allah have mercy on you.”"],[8374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a slave who is afflicted by the heat of the Fire—I think he said—“Call him, and if he refuses, put it in his hand. And when you strike them, do not strike their faces.”"],[8375,"Do not insult anyone while you are fasting. If someone insults you, say: “I am fasting.” By the One in whose hand is my soul, the breath of a fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the fragrance of musk."],[8376,"Let men cease from not attending the last ‘isha’ prayer, or I will burn their houses—or he said: around their houses—with bundles of firewood."],[8377,"Whoever leaves his seat—or from a gathering—and then returns is more entitled to it."],[8378,"Humayd b. al-Aswad narrated to us from Ibn ‘Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. We do not know of this hadith being reported from Ibn ‘Ajlan except through this route, and we have not heard it except from al-Hasan b. Qaza‘ah from Humayd, combining the two."],[8379,"The slave is entitled to his food and clothing, and he is not burdened with work beyond his capacity."],[8380,"A man's nobility is his wealth, and his honor is his piety — or he said: Nobility is wealth, and honor is piety."],[8381,"Ibn 'Ajlan reported to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8382,"Whoever attends a funeral in its family's home has a qirat; if he follows it, he has a qirat; if he prays over it, he has a qirat; and if he waits until it is buried, he has a qirat."],[8383,"Prayer in congregation is superior to prayer alone by twenty-five degrees."],[8384,"It is not lawful for a believer to abandon a believer for more than three days."],[8385,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[8386,"When he went out, we would stand for him until he entered his house."],[8387,"When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves so-and-so, so love him.' So Jibril loves him, then Jibril calls out to the inhabitants of heaven: 'Allah loves so-and-so, so love him.' So the inhabitants of heaven love him, and then acceptance is placed for him on earth."],[8388,"Wealth was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: There is no owner of gold or silver who does not pay its due except that it will be made into sheets for him on the Day of Resurrection, heated in the fire of Hell, and his forehead and sides will be cauterized with them. Whenever they cool, they will be reheated for him, until judgment is passed among the people, and he sees his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their due — and among their dues is milking them on the day they come to water — except that they will be gathered for him as large as they ever were, and they will trample him with their hooves. Whenever the first of them pass, the last of them return to him, until judgment is passed among the people or he sees his path."],[8389,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ passed by a mountain stream with water, and its pleasantness impressed him. He said: 'If only I could withdraw from the people and stay in this stream — but I will not do so until I seek the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not do that, for the standing of one of you in the path of Allah is better for him than his standing in his house for sixty years, or so many years. Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"],[8390,"None of you should breathe into the vessel when he is drinking from it, but if he wants to breathe, let him move it away and then breathe."],[8391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ — I think he said: — took me by the hand from the market of Banu Qaynuqa'. He did not speak to me nor did I speak to him until he stopped at the door of Fatimah and said: 'Is the little one there?' meaning al-Hasan. Abu Hurayrah said: I thought that his mother had detained him until she washed his face and dressed him — I think he said: in a necklace — then he came out to the Prophet ﷺ, who embraced him and said: 'O God, love him and love those who love him.'"],[8392,"Waraqa' narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid, from Nafi' b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[8393,"The prayer of the imam is more excellent than twenty-five prayers that he prays alone."],[8394,"People are followers of Quraysh in this matter: their good follow their good, and their wicked follow their wicked."],[8395,"A caller calls out every night, when as much of the night has passed as God wills: 'Who will call upon Me, that I may answer him? Who will ask of Me, that I may give him?'"],[8396,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[8397,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out an expedition, and they were men of military strength. He made each man among them recite the Quran — or he said: from the Quran. He came to a man who was the youngest of them in age and said: 'What do you have with you, O so-and-so?' He said: 'I have such-and-such and Surah al-Baqarah.' He said: 'You have Surah al-Baqarah with you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then go — I think he said: — for you are their commander.' A man said: 'By God, O Messenger of God, nothing prevented me from learning the Quran except fear that I might not act upon it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Recite it and sleep upon it, for the example of the Quran for one who learns it, recites it, and acts upon it is like a sack filled with musk whose fragrance spreads everywhere. And the example of one who learns it but sleeps while it is in his heart is like a sack tied over musk.'"],[8398,"Were it not that I would impose hardship on my community"],[8399,"The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful. It says: 'O my Lord, I have been wronged. O my Lord, I have been severed. O my Lord.' So its Lord, Blessed and Exalted, answers it and says: 'Will you not be content that I maintain ties with those who maintain you, and sever ties with those who sever you?'"],[8400,"Whoever dies as a frontier guard in the path of God, the reward of a fasting person's deeds will be run for him, his provision will be run for him, he will be safe from the testers, and God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection safe from the greatest terror."],[8401,"There is no competition prize except in a camel's foot or a horse's hoof."],[8402,"Indeed, some men will flee to their tribes, but Madinah is better for them if they only knew. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, none remains in it and endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor and witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. No one leaves it out of dislike for it except that God replaces him with someone better than him. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it expels the impurity of its people — I think he said: — as the bellows expel the impurity of iron."],[8403,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit me and said: 'Shall I not perform ruqyah on you with a ruqyah that Jibril performed on me?' I said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.' He said: 'In the name of Allah, I perform ruqyah on you, from every disease in you, from the evil of the blowers on knots, and from the evil of an envier when he envies.'"],[8404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a fitnah and brought it near. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if we live to see it, with whom should we be?' He said: 'With the trustworthy one and his companions, Uthman b. Affan.'"],[8405,"Whoever keeps a dog, except for farming or herding, or a hunting dog, his reward decreases every day by a qirat."],[8406,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, you will certainly follow the ways of those who came before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until even if they entered a lizard's hole, you would enter it."],[8407,"Beware of envy, for envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."],[8408,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer, he spread his fingers wide."],[8409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to raise his hands when he entered the prayer, extending them fully. He would pause before recitation, asking Allah of His bounty. He would say takbir when he went down and when he came up."],[8410,"And Amr narrated it to us, as I think, from Yahya or from Abu Asim."],[8411,"Whoever makes a gesture in his prayer that is understood from him, let him repeat his prayer, or it has become invalid. He said: And he ﷺ said: 'Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.'"],[8412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about praying in sheep pens. He said: 'Wipe its dust and pray in its resting place, for it is among the animals of Paradise.'"],[8413,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is the most noble of people?' He said: 'The most God-fearing of them.' They said: 'We are not asking you about this.' He said: 'Then you are asking about the origins of the Arabs? The best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam, if they acquire understanding.'"],[8414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque. A man entered and prayed, then came and greeted the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his greeting and said: 'Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' He went back and prayed as he had prayed, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' He did that three times. Then he said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I cannot do better than this, so teach me.' He said: 'When you stand for prayer, say takbir, then recite what is easy for you from the Quran, then bow until you are at rest in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, then rise until you are at rest sitting, then do that throughout your prayer.'"],[8415,"Women are married for four [reasons]: for her wealth, for her lineage, for her beauty, and for her religion. So attain the one with religion; may your hands be dusted [i.e., may you succeed]."],[8416,"When one of you comes to his bed, let him take off the inner garment of his lower garment and shake out his bed with it, then say: 'In Your name I have laid down my side, and by You I raise it. If You hold my soul, then have mercy on it, and if You release it, then guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants.'"],[8417,"Were it not that I would make it difficult for my Ummah, I would have made the siwak obligatory at every prayer."],[8418,"God, exalted be His praise, will surely send down Jesus son of Mary as a just judge and a fair imam, and he will surely travel through al-Rawha' as a pilgrim."],[8419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer, and there was a man in the last rows, or he was in the last rows. He said: 'O so-and-so, do you not fear God? Do you not look at how you pray? When one of you stands to pray, he stands to converse with his Lord, so let him look at how he prays. You think that I do not see you; by God, I see you from behind my back just as I see from in front of me.'"],[8420,"A Bedouin gifted a she-camel to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and the Messenger of God ﷺ compensated him for it, but he remained displeased. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and said: 'Some people give me gifts, and a man gifted me a she-camel from camels that I recognize as I recognize some of my family' - then he mentioned a word as if he was informing about rewarding him - 'and he remained displeased. By God, I will not accept from anyone among the Arabs after this standing of mine except from a Qurayshi, an Ansari, a Thaqafi, or a Dausi.'"],[8421,"O women of the believers, let none of you belittle anything for her neighbor, even a sheep's trotter. And a woman should not travel except with a mahram."],[8422,"A woman should not travel a distance of three days except with a mahram."],[8423,"Whoever does not abandon false speech and acting upon it, God has no need for him to leave his food and drink."],[8424,"Abu Qutaybah narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with its like."],[8425,"Whoever follows a funeral from its family until he prays over it will have a qirat, and whoever waits until its burial will have two qirats."],[8426,"Sneezing is from God, and yawning is from Satan. It is a duty upon whoever hears it to say: 'May God have mercy on you all.'"],[8427,"When any of you prays, let him place his sandals between his feet."],[8428,"The sun has neither risen nor set on any day better than Friday. Allah guided us to it and led the people astray from it, so the people follow us in it. It is ours, for the Jews it is Saturday, and for the Christians Sunday. Indeed in it there is an hour in which no believer coincides with it, asking Allah for something, except that He gives him."],[8429,"A woman should not travel for three [days] except with a mahram."],[8430,"When any of you steps with his leather socks or sandals on something, then their purification is dust."],[8431,"O Muslim women, let not a neighbor woman scorn [a gift] for her neighbor, even if it be a sheep's trotter."],[8432,"Indeed among the worst of usury is a man's overstepping against the honor of his brother."],[8433,"He used to say: There is no god but Allah alone. He aided His servant and defeated the confederates alone, so there is nothing after Him."],[8434,"There is no prophet among the prophets except that he was given signs the like of which—I think—people believed on account of. Indeed what I was given was revelation that Allah revealed to me, so I hope to have the most followers of them on the Day of Resurrection."],[8435,"Al-Maqburi narrated to us from Layth—meaning Ibn Sa'd—from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, likewise."],[8436,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years."],[8437,"It is not permissible for a Muslim woman to travel for three [days] except with a mahram."],[8438,"Indeed Allah does not tire until you tire. Indeed the most beloved of deeds to Allah is the most constant of them, even if small. Upon you is of the matter what you can bear."],[8439,"Indeed, the hypocrites have signs by which they are known: their greeting is a curse, their food is plunder, their spoils are embezzlement. They do not come to the mosques except reluctantly, and they do not come to prayer except at its end—sleeping logs by night, clamorous by day."],[8440,"He forbade fasting on six days of the year: the Day of Sacrifice, the Day of Breaking the Fast, the Days of Tashriq, and the day about which there is doubt as to whether it is from Ramadan."],[8441,"Indeed, God, blessed and exalted, has creatures He disperses in the night, so cover your vessels, tie your waterskins, and shut your doors, for nothing uncovers a cover or opens a door."],[8442,"A man may speak a word to make a people laugh, and by it he falls farther than the Pleiades."],[8443,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the noblest of people. He said: 'The most God-fearing of them.' They said: 'It is not about this that we ask you.' He said: 'Then is it about the origins of the Arabs that you ask?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'The best of you in the time of ignorance are the best of you in Islam, if they gain understanding.'"],[8444,"He forbade a settled person from selling on behalf of a bedouin."],[8445,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer, and I would delay the evening prayer until the first third of the night—or until half of it; the doubt is from 'Ubaydullah—for God, blessed and exalted, when the first third of the night—or half of it—has passed, descends to the lowest heaven and calls out: 'Is there any supplicant that I may answer? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive? Or any asker that I may give?' until dawn rises."],[8446,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us from 'Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."],[8447,"Indeed, God made sacred what lies between the two lava fields of Madinah—I think he said: upon my tongue. Then he came—I think he said: to Banu Harithah—and said: 'I do not see you but that you have gone out.' Then he looked and said: 'Rather, you are within it.'"],[8448,"Four does God hate: the swearing merchant, the arrogant poor person, the adulterous old man, and the treacherous leader."],[8449,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat which she tied up and did not feed, nor did she leave it to eat from the insects of the earth."],[8450,"When the slave-woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery, let him sell her, even for a hair-rope."],[8451,"Whoever offers the funeral prayer has a qirat. I think he said: And whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats."],[8452,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, wears his best clothes, comes early, does not separate between two people, and prays what is written for him, then when the imam comes out he listens and remains silent, he will have whatever is between that and the next Friday."],[8453,"A prophet among the prophets went on a military expedition after 'asr. He said: No one should follow me, or no one should go on the expedition with me, a man who has built a building and not finished it, nor a man who has married a woman and not consummated the marriage with her. He said: Only a little of the sun remained. He said: O Allah, the sun is commanded and I am commanded; O Allah, hold it back. So Allah held it back for an hour until Allah granted him victory. Then he ordered the spoils of war to be collected, and they were gathered. Then fire came and did not consume them. He said: There is stolen war booty (ghulul) among you, so let a man from each tribe come to me and we will pledge allegiance to him. His hand stuck to the hand of a man or two men. He said: Among you is the ghulul, so bring it out. They brought out a cow's head made of gold and threw it into the spoils. I think he said: The fire consumed it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: War spoils were not lawful for anyone before us, and that is because Allah saw our weakness and made them good for us."],[8454,"Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted be He, accepts charity and accepts only what is good. He nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or his colt."],[8455,"Thumamah b. Uthal embraced Islam, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to perform ghusl with water and sidr."],[8456,"You will fight people whose faces are like hammered shields."],[8457,"When the deceased is taken, or one of you, two black and blue angels come to him. One is called al-Munkar and the other al-Nakir. They say: What did you used to say about this man? He says: The servant of Allah and His Messenger. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They say: We knew that you used to say this. Then his grave is widened for him seventy cubits by seventy cubits, then it is illuminated for him. Then it is said to him: Sleep until you return to your family. He said: He sleeps like the sleep of one whom only the most beloved of his family wakes, until Allah raises him from that resting place. He said: Then the disbeliever is brought and it is said: What did you used to say about this man? He says: I saw people saying something and said it. They say: We knew that you would say that. Then it is said to the earth: Close in upon him. It closes in upon him, and his ribs become disjointed in it. He remains in it tormented until Allah raises him from that resting place."],[8458,"Allah does not love wasting wealth, excessive asking, nor qil and qal."],[8459,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her. Then if she commits adultery, let him flog her, three times, then sell her even for a hair rope."],[8460,"May his nose be rubbed in dust, a man before whom I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon me. May his nose be rubbed in dust, a man who attains old age of his parents and they do not cause him to enter Paradise. May his nose be rubbed in dust, a man upon whom Ramadan enters and then departs without being forgiven."],[8461,"Three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the old adulterer, the lying ruler, and the arrogant poor person."],[8462,"Five things are part of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit hair, trimming the nails, and clipping the moustache."],[8463,"Wealth is not abundance of goods; rather, wealth is contentment of the soul."],[8464,"I said, “O Messenger of God, who will be the happiest of people through your intercession on the Day of Resurrection?” He said, “I thought no one would ask me about this hadith other than you, because of what I have seen of your eagerness for knowledge—as I believe. The happiest of people through my intercession on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who says ‘There is no god but God’ sincerely from his own self.”"],[8465,"Many a one who stands in prayer gets from his standing only sleeplessness, and many a one who fasts gets from his fasting only hunger and thirst."],[8466,"The believer is to me in the position of every good: he praises me while I am drawing his soul from between his sides."],[8467,"Whoever is appointed to judge, or is made a judge, has been slaughtered without a knife."],[8468,"Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[8469,"I came to al-Tur, and Humayl b. Basra met me and said to me, “Where have you come from?” I said, “From al-Tur.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers anywhere else. If you had prayed in this mosque, it would have been better for you, and had I met you before you went, I would not have let you go to it.’”"],[8470,"A time will come upon people when a man will not care—I think he said—from what he takes wealth, whether from what is lawful or what is unlawful."],[8471,"Whoever has wronged his brother in any way should go to him and seek release from it before he is taken (on the Day of Judgment) with no dinar or dirham with him. If he has good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds; otherwise, sins will be taken from the other’s sins and placed upon his own."],[8472,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to travel a day’s journey except with a mahram from her family."],[8473,"When God, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam and breathed the spirit into him, he sneezed and said, “Praise be to God, by God’s permission.” His Lord said to him, “May your Lord have mercy on you, O Adam.” Then He said, “Go to that assembly of angels sitting there and say, ‘Peace be upon you.’” They said, “And upon you be peace and God’s mercy.” Then he returned to his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He said, “This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among themselves.” Then He said to him, with His hands closed, “Choose whichever of them you wish.” He said, “I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are right and blessed.” Then He opened it, and behold, in it were Adam and his descendants, and every human being had his lifespan written with him. Adam’s lifespan was a thousand years, and there were men among them upon whom was light, and among them was a man, the brightest of them or one of the brightest, for whom only forty years had been written. He said, “O Lord, who is this?” He said, “This is your son David.” He said, “O Lord, increase his lifespan.” He said, “That is what I have written for him.” He said, “Then I will reduce sixty years from my lifespan for him.” He said, “You and that.” Then Adam was settled in Paradise for as long as God willed, then he was sent down from it. He used to count for himself. The Angel of Death came to him and he said, “You have come early. Did not God write a thousand years for me?” He said, “Yes, but you gave sixty years of it to your son David.” He said, “I did not do that.” So he denied it, and his descendants denied it; and he forgot, and his descendants forgot. On that day, writing and witnesses were commanded."],[8474,"The earth will surely bolt with you like the bolting of a young camel—meaning the earth."],[8475,"He cursed the one who makes a woman lawful for her first husband (al-muḥill) and the one for whom that is done (al-muḥallal lahu)."],[8476,"Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."],[8477,"Beware of discord between people, for it is the shaver."],[8478,"I declare inviolable the right of the two weak ones: the woman and the orphan."],[8479,"Whoever is appointed a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[8480,"What is between the east and the west is a qiblah."],[8481,"Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity or obscene behavior. Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of stinginess, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to shed their blood, so they shed their blood; it commanded them to sever their ties of kinship, so they severed them; and it commanded them, so they made lawful their sacred things."],[8482,"Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you concerning the name of your prayer."],[8483,"I declare inviolable the right of the two weak ones: the woman and the orphan."],[8484,"Two matters of the pre-Islamic era that people will not abandon: wailing for the dead and defaming people's lineages."],[8485,"Give charity. A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar.' He said, 'Give it in charity for yourself.' He said, 'I have another.' He said, 'Give it in charity for your wife.' He said, 'I have another.' He said, 'Give it in charity for your child.' He said, 'I have another.' He said, 'Give it in charity for your servant.' He said, 'I have another.' He said, 'You know best.'"],[8486,"A man asked Abu Hurayrah, 'How much water is enough for the full bath after major ritual impurity?' He said, 'Pour water over your head three times.' He said, 'My hair is abundant.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had more hair than you and it was more fragrant.'"],[8487,"There is no leader of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, until justice releases him or injustice destroys him."],[8488,"Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will be made to wear it as a collar on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[8489,"It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to travel a distance — I do not know how far he said — unless she has a mahram with her."],[8490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting with Abu Bakr. A man began insulting Abu Bakr while the Messenger of God smiled. When the man went on at length, Abu Bakr answered back some of what he said. The Messenger of God ﷺ got up angry. Abu Bakr caught up with him and said, “O Messenger of God, he insulted me while you listened. When I answered him, you got up and left me!” He said, “An angel was answering him on your behalf. When you answered him, Satan appeared, and I would not sit with Satan.”"],[8491,"He used to say: “O God, I seek refuge with You from an evil neighbor in the permanent abode, for the neighbor of the desert moves on.”"],[8492,"Whoever prays over a funeral receives a qirat, and whoever follows it until its burial is completed receives two qirats."],[8493,"Say “yarhamuka Allah” to him three times; if he increases beyond that, it is only a cold."],[8494,"When you see those who praise people to their faces, throw dust in their faces."],[8495,"Three are entitled to God’s help: the one striving in the path of God, the one who marries to remain chaste, and the slave with a contract to earn his freedom who intends to pay."],[8496,"When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet with salam. When he wants to leave, let him greet with salam. The first is no more deserving than the last."],[8497,"May God have mercy on a man who gets up at night and wakes his wife; if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. May God have mercy on a woman who gets up at night, prays, and wakes her husband; if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face."],[8498,"When he intended to travel, he would say: “O God, You are the Companion in the journey and the Successor over the family. O God, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, and the evil sight in family and property. O God, fold the earth for us and make the journey easy for us.”"],[8499,"When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face. He should not say: May Allah make ugly your face and the face of whoever resembles your face, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam in His image."],[8500,"Whoever attends a funeral with its family and prays over it will have a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is concluded will have two qirats."],[8501,"When one of you rises from his bed at night and then returns to it, he does not know what he left behind in it after him, so let him shake it with his waist-wrapper or part of his waist-wrapper. When he lies down, let him say: 'In Your name I lay my side, and by You I raise it. If You withhold my soul, forgive it, and if You release it, protect it with what You protect Your righteous servants.'"],[8502,"A man gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a milch camel as a gift, and he rewarded him for it with six young she-camels, yet he remained displeased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'So-and-so gave me a milch camel as a gift, and I rewarded him with six young she-camels, yet he remains displeased'—or 'he is still displeased'—'By Allah, I have resolved not to accept a gift from any man of the Arabs except if he is a Qurayshi, an Ansari, a Dausi, or a Thaqafi.'"],[8503,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you yawns, that is only Satan laughing from inside him."],[8504,"No one endures its hardships but that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him."],[8505,"You shall enjoin good and forbid evil, or Allah will surely set over you your worst ones, and your best ones will supplicate but will not be answered."],[8506,"Indeed Allah created Adam ﷺ his height sixty cubits."],[8507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam after two rak'ahs. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I did not forget and the prayer has not been shortened.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you forgot.' So he prayed two more rak'ahs and prostrated two prostrations."],[8508,"By Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe—a neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what are his harms?' He said: 'His evil.'"],[8509,"The Seven Oft-Repeated (al-sab' al-mathani) is the Opening of the Book (Fatihah al-Kitab)."],[8510,"By Allah, he does not believe—three times—one whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what are his harms?' He said: 'His evil.'"],[8511,"By Allah, I indeed know best among you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he said: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs all praise,' and he would say the takbir when he rose and when he lowered and when he raised."],[8512,"I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ – I think he said – two vessels. As for one of them, I have disseminated it among the people; and as for the other, if I were to disseminate it, my throat would be cut."],[8513,"The Hour will not be established until – I think he said – this nation follows the ways of those before it, span by span and cubit by cubit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Just as Persia and Byzantium did.'"],[8514,"I do not know whether the prescribed punishments are expiations or not, and I do not know whether Tubba' was accursed or not, and I do not know whether 'Uzayr was a prophet or not."],[8515,"A woman should not travel a barid except with a mahram."],[8516,"The lifetime in which Allah excuses the son of Adam is sixty years, meaning: 'Did We not grant you life long enough for whoever would remember to remember therein?'"],[8517,"One of you gives charity with a date when it is from good [earnings], and Allah only accepts the good; then He nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal until it becomes in His hand like a mountain."],[8518,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him greet the Prophet and say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy,' and when he leaves, let him greet and say: 'O Allah, protect me from evil.'"],[8519,"Safwan b. al-Mu'attal asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Are there any hours of the night or day in which prayer is disliked?' He said: 'Yes; when you have prayed the dawn prayer, then abstain from prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil. Then pray, and the prayer is witnessed and accepted until the sun is directly above your head like a spear. When it is above your head like a spear, then abstain from prayer, for that is the hour in which Hell is stoked and its gates are opened, until the sun declines from your right eyebrow. When it declines or passes the meridian, then prayer is attended and accepted until you pray the afternoon prayer. Then abstain from prayer until the sun sets.'"],[8520,"When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."],[8521,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has removed from you the arrogance of the pre-Islamic era and its boasting about ancestors. People are children of Adam, and Adam is from dust. Men will certainly abandon boasting about peoples who are only coals from the coals of Hell, or they will be more insignificant to Allah than the dung beetles that push filth with their noses."],[8522,"When a slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery again, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery again, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery again, let him sell her, even for a rope of hair."],[8523,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ intending to travel and said, “O Messenger of God, give me advice.” He said, “I advise you to fear God and to say takbir upon every elevation.” When he turned away — or he said, “went away” — he said, “O God, roll up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.”"],[8524,"When the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her. Then if she commits adultery, let him sell her, even for a hair rope."],[8525,"Jesus son of Mary will descend as a just judge and an equitable imam, to break the cross, kill the pig, and the qiblah will become one."],[8526,"When it is the Day of Resurrection, a person will be called by the best of his deeds. If prayer was best, he will be called by it; if his fasting was best, he will be called by it; if jihad was best, he will be called by it. Then he will come to a gate of the gates of Paradise called al-Rayyan, from which the fasting will be called. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said, “O Messenger of God, is there anyone who will be called by two deeds?” He said, “Yes, you.”"],[8527,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, what is thoroughness?” He remained silent until the time of prayer came. He called for water and poured it over his hand, then washed his face and hands three times, wiped his head, washed his feet three times, and sprinkled the lower part of his garment. Then he said, “Thus is thoroughness in ablution.”"],[8528,"Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch, and when a hadith from me comes to him while he is reclining on his couch, he says, “Recite to me a Qur'an [verse]. What came to you of good, I said it, and if I did not say it, I say it now; and what came to you of evil, I do not say evil.”"],[8529,"O God, I seek refuge in You from deafness and dumbness, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt, and I seek refuge in You from sorrow — meaning drowning — and I seek refuge in You from decrepitude, and I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is an evil bedfellow, and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is an evil inner trait."],[8530,"You will surely follow the ways of the nations — or a similar word — before you, cubit by cubit, span by span, and fathom by fathom, until if one of them entered a lizard's hole, you would enter it — or you would enter them."],[8531,"A new moon would pass, then another, and no fire would be kindled in any of the houses of the Messenger of God ﷺ for bread or cooking. He said, “Then how did they live, O Abu Hurayrah?” He said, “By the two black things: dates and water. And he had neighbors among the Ansar, may God reward them well, who had milk animals and would send them some milk.”"],[8532,"The best of women is a woman who, when you look at her, pleases you; when you command her, she obeys you; and when you are absent from her, she guards you in herself and your property."],[8533,"Riba is seventy sins, the least of which — or the least of them — is like a man committing incest with his mother. And the worst riba is [assailing] the honor of a Muslim."],[8534,"There is no share in Islam for one who has no prayer, and there is no prayer for one who has no ablution."],[8535,"Indeed, among the rights of the child upon the parent is that he give him a good name and give him a good upbringing."],[8536,"I do not know whether the prescribed punishments are expiation for those who receive them or not; and I do not know whether ʿUzayr was a prophet or not; and I do not know whether Tubbaʿ was cursed or not."],[8537,"When you are reminded of Allah, then desist."],[8538,"When one of you comes to the mosque, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy.' And when he leaves, let him greet the Prophet ﷺ and say: 'O Allah, protect me from Satan.'"],[8539,"You will never encompass the people with your wealth, but they will be encompassed by your cheerful face and good character."],[8540,"Your oath is according to what your companion believes you by."],[8541,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī over Bahrain, and he asked Abū Hurayrah to accompany him. He stipulated that he would be a muʾadhdhin and would not precede him in saying 'Āmīn'."],[8542,"Recite the two shining ones: recite Sūrat al-Baqarah and Āl ʿImrān, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks."],[8543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have anyone take his hand and then withdraw his hand from his until the man himself let go; and his knees were not seen protruding beyond the knee of a companion; and no one shook hands with him except that he turned his face toward him and did not turn it away until he finished speaking."],[8544,"He recited this verse: 'On that Day it will report its news, because your Lord has inspired it.' He said: 'Do you know what its news is? Its news is that it will testify against every male and female servant about what he did on its surface. It will say: He did such and such on such and such a day. This is its news.'"],[8545,"How excellent is the believer's pre-dawn meal of dates."],[8546,"Whatever is above the ankles—or below the ankles—of the lower garment is, I think he said, in the Fire, or a word to that effect."],[8547,"When one of you passes his hand to his private part, with no cover or barrier between them, let him perform wudu'."],[8548,"Frequently say: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no might or power except with Allah), for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise."],[8549,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, wears the best of his clothes, touches perfume if he has any, goes early – meaning he arrives at the beginning of the time – and does not separate between two people, then prays what Allah has decreed for him until the imam comes out, then listens and remains silent until the imam finishes, he will be forgiven for what is between the two Fridays."],[8550,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, made his mount kneel at the door of the mosque, then came and stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Which of you is the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib?' They said: 'This fair-skinned one reclining.' He said: 'O Muhammad, I will ask you and will be harsh in the questioning.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Ask.' He said: 'I ask you by the Lord of those before you and the Lord of those after you: Did Allah send you?' He said: 'O Allah, yes.'"],[8551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral and said: 'O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our males and our females, our young and our old, our present and our absent. O Allah, whoever among us You keep alive, keep him alive upon faith, and whoever among us You cause to die, cause him to die upon Islam.'"],[8552,"Indeed a man says a word that brings Allah's wrath, seeing no harm in it, to make his companions laugh, and by it he falls into Hell for seventy autumns."],[8553,"The Dajjal will descend in Khuz and Kirman with eighty thousand, their sandals of hair, their garments of tayalisah, as if their faces are layered shields."],[8554,"Shall I not inform you of the best among you? They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'The best of you are those with the longest lives and the best character.'"],[8555,"When one of you prays over a funeral, let him devote the supplication sincerely for it."],[8556,"Whoever spends a pair in the way of Allah – two dinars, two camels – the keepers of Paradise will call him to Paradise: 'Come!' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, that is the one who will have no loss.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I hope that you will be among them, O Abu Bakr.'"],[8557,"Whoever spends a pair from his wealth in the way of Allah, the keepers of Paradise will call him at every gate of Paradise: 'Come, approach!' Abu Bakr said: 'That is the one who will have no loss.'"],[8558,"The natural practices are four: trimming the moustache, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit hair, and clipping the nails."],[8559,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a man who had drunk wine. He said: 'Beat him.' So they beat him, some with their hands, some with their clothes, and some with their sandals. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Rebuke him.' So they turned to the man saying: 'Do you not fear Allah? Do you not dread Allah? Are you not ashamed before Allah?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave him.'"],[8560,"Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to a Prophet with a beautiful voice reciting the Quran melodiously."],[8561,"He said: 'Do you think that if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times a day, would any of his dirt remain?' They said: 'No, none of his dirt would remain.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is the likeness of the five prayers: they erase sins.'"],[8562,"When you leave your house, pray two rak'ahs; they will protect you from an evil departure. And when you enter your house, pray two rak'ahs; they will protect you from an evil entry."],[8563,"Whoever washes a dead body should perform ghusl."],[8564,"If women ask your permission to go to the mosques, do not prevent them—I think he said—and let them go out unperfumed."],[8565,"Three eyes will not enter the Fire: an eye that lowers its gaze from what Allah has forbidden, an eye that keeps watch in the path of Allah, and an eye from which tears flow like the head of a fly out of fear of Allah."],[8566,"My ummah was given five things in Ramadan that no ummah before them was given: the breath of a fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the fragrance of musk; the angels seek forgiveness for them until they break their fast; the devils are chained in it so they cannot reach what they would reach in other months; then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'My righteous servants are about to cast off their burden and harm'—I think he said—'and it will come to them,' or 'they will come to their reward on the last night.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is it Laylat al-Qadr?' He said: 'No, but the worker is paid his wages when he finishes his work.'"],[8567,"I said to Ayyub: 'Did you memorize anything like the statement of al-Hasan about \"your affair is in your hand\"?' He said: 'No.' Then he said: 'I seek Allah's forgiveness. Qatadah narrated it to me from Kathir b. Kathir, from Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the like of al-Hasan's statement. And al-Hasan used to say: 'It is three.'"],[8568,"Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi and the beginning of Ha-Mim al-Mu'min (Surah Ghafir) will be protected that day from all evil."],[8569,"A useful portion of knowledge that a man learns is dearer to me than a thousand voluntary rak'ahs."],[8570,"Hilal b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Ata' b. Abi Maymunah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Dharr something similar. Hilal b. Abd al-Rahman is from Basra, and Ata' b. Abi Maymunah is from Basra; Shu'bah and others narrated from him, and he had Qadari views; Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated from him and he is truthful."],[8571,"When a judge rules and strives and is correct, he has two rewards; and if he rules and strives and errs, he has one reward."],[8572,"When you travel, the one among you most versed in the Quran should lead you in prayer, even if he is the youngest of you; and when he leads you, he is your commander."],[8573,"The prophets are half-brothers from different mothers; their mothers are various, but their father is one."],[8574,"Wrangling about the Quran is disbelief. The Quran was sent down in seven modes, so whatever you recognize, act upon it, and whatever you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower."],[8575,"My pulpit is upon one of the watercourses of Paradise."],[8576,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, the punishment of the Fire, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[8577,"A previously married woman is not married off until she is commanded, and a virgin is not married off until she is asked permission. They said: How is her permission? He said: Silence."],[8578,"A virgin is not married off until she is asked permission, and a previously married woman is not married off until she is commanded. It was said: What is the permission of a virgin? He said: Her silence."],[8579,"He used to say in the funeral prayer: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. O Allah, whomever You keep alive among us, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomever You cause to die among us, cause him to die upon faith."],[8580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut for a month, saying: O Allah, save al-Walid b. al-Walid, Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah, and Salamah b. Hisham. O Allah, save the weak among the believers."],[8581,"Musa met Adam, peace be upon them both, and said: You are Adam who brought people out of Paradise. Adam said to him: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His message and His speech, so how can you blame me for a deed Allah decreed for me before He created me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: So Adam out-argued Musa."],[8582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut in the last evening prayer after bowing."],[8583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in “When the sky is split asunder.”"],[8584,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven. And whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8585,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined three things upon me: the two rak‘ahs of Duha, not to sleep without praying Witr, and fasting three days every month."],[8586,"Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds every day, except a dog for farming or herding."],[8587,"He forbade (the use of) gourds and pitch-covered vessels (for making nabidh)."],[8588,"When the muezzin calls the adhan, Satan turns away, passing wind. When the adhan is finished, he comes back. When the iqamah is called, he turns away. When it is finished, he comes back, until he comes between a man and his own self, saying: “Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,” things he did not remember, until he does not know whether he prayed three or four (rak‘ahs). So if he does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate twice while sitting."],[8589,"Muhammad b. Kathir narrated to us from al-Awza‘i, from Yahya, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[8590,"The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday: on it Allah created Adam, on it He admitted him to Paradise, on it he was expelled from it, and on it the Hour will begin."],[8591,"Do not go ahead of the month—meaning by one day or two—except that one of you had a day he used to fast, then let him fast it."],[8592,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say the takbir whenever he lowered and raised himself."],[8593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought (some food) at Marr al-Zahran. He said to Abu Bakr and ‘Umar: “Come close and eat.” They said: “We are fasting.” He said: “Work for your two companions; prepare mounts for your two companions.”"],[8594,"The likeness of one who goes early to Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel, then the next like one who offers a cow, then the next like one who offers a sheep. Then when the imam sits on the pulpit, the records are rolled up and they sit to listen."],[8595,"Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, and the punishment of the Fire, and from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."],[8596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon, and a man called Abu Shah stood up and said, \"Write it down for me,\" or \"Write it down.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Write it down for Abu Shah.\""],[8597,"Do not name grapes 'al-karm.'"],[8598,"I am the first for whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection."],[8599,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is jealous, and indeed the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer should not commit what Allah has forbidden him."],[8600,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is jealous, and indeed the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer should not commit what Allah has forbidden him."],[8601,"My provision has been placed beneath the shade of my spear, and humiliation and abasement have been placed upon whoever opposes my command, and whoever imitates a people is one of them."],[8602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every fanged beast of prey, and he forbade the domestic donkey - I think he said: - and he forbade al-mujaththama (animals tied up and shot), al-khulsah (snatching), and al-nuhbah (plundering). And he said: \"Whoever eats from this tree should not come near us in our mosque.\""],[8603,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit down until he prays two rak'ahs."],[8604,"Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a Prophet to recite the Qur'an aloud in a melodious voice."],[8605,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a Prophet?\" He said, \"When Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[8606,"In Friday there is an hour in which no servant coincides with it while he is praying, asking Allah for something, but He gives it to him. He said: Then 'Abdullah b. Salam said, \"It is the last hour.\" I said, \"He only said, 'while he is praying,' and that is not a prayer time.\" He said, \"Have you not heard, or has it not reached you, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever waits for the prayer is in prayer'?!\""],[8607,"It was forbidden to anticipate Ramadan by fasting one or two days before it."],[8608,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with pebbles in his hand, count the number of these pebbles and say: Perform wudu' from what fire has touched."],[8609,"Al-Jarrah b. Makhlad narrated to us; Abu Qutaybah narrated to us from Yahya, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8610,"The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[8611,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of the 'Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught it."],[8612,"The People of the Book used to recite the Scripture in Hebrew and explain it in Arabic to the people of Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not believe the People of the Book nor disbelieve them, but say: We believe in what has been sent down to us and sent down to you."],[8613,"When a man says to his brother, 'O disbeliever', it returns to one of them."],[8614,"I hope that no one who witnessed Badr will enter the Fire, if Allah wills."],[8615,"When the imam says, 'Not of those who earned wrath nor of those who went astray', say 'Amin'; and when he says, 'Allah hears those who praise Him', say, 'O Allah, our Lord, to You be praise.'"],[8616,"The believer is naive and noble, while the wicked is treacherous and base."],[8617,"The believer is naive and noble, while the wicked is treacherous and base."],[8618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought forgiveness for the first row three times, for the second row twice, and for the third row once."],[8619,"Three [traits]; whoever has them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, and claims that he is a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his promise."],[8620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded killing the two black ones during prayer."],[8621,"Four [things] are in my community that they will not abandon: boasting about lineages, defaming ancestries, and wailing—on the Day of Resurrection, the wailing woman, if she does not repent, will be raised wearing a garment of tar."],[8622,"Wine is from these two trees, meaning dates and grapes."],[8623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: When one of you goes to his wife, let him cover himself; for if he does not cover himself, the angels feel shy and leave, while the devil remains. If a child results between them, the devil has a share in it."],[8624,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks. He said: For the resident, one day and one night; and for the traveler, three days and their nights."],[8625,"When you send a man to me, send one with a good face and a good name."],[8626,"One religious community does not inherit from another religious community."],[8627,"A woman should not be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[8628,"Allah does not accept charity from stolen property, nor prayer without purification."],[8629,"The Jews used to say that coitus interruptus is the lesser burial of a live infant. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: The Jews have lied. If Allah wants to create a creation, nothing can prevent it—I think he said: nothing."],[8630,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so daughter of so-and-so. He said: State your need. She said: My need is that so-and-so proposed to me, so inform me of the right of the husband over the wife. If it is something I can bear, I will marry him; if I cannot bear it, I will not marry. He said: It is part of the right of the husband over the wife that if his nostrils flowed blood and pus and she licked it, she would not have fulfilled his right. And if it were appropriate for any human to prostrate to another human, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband when he enters upon her. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry as long as I remain in this world."],[8631,"Three qualities: whoever possesses them, Allah will take him to an easy account and admit him to Paradise by His mercy. They said: What are they, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you? He said: You give to the one who deprives you, you maintain ties with the one who cuts you off, and you pardon the one who wrongs you. If you do that, He will admit you to Paradise by His mercy."],[8632,"By the One who sent me with the truth, this world will not come to an end until they are afflicted with sinking into the earth, pelting with stones, and transformation into animals. They said: When will that be, O Prophet of Allah? He said: When you see women riding on saddles, and singing girls become numerous, and false testimony becomes widespread, and men suffice with men and women with women."],[8633,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Abu Bakr: How do you perform witr? He said: I perform witr at the beginning of the night. He said: Cautious and prudent. Then he asked Umar: How do you perform witr? He said: At the end of the night. He said: Strong and aided."],[8634,"Whoever heads for this House from unlawful earnings, he has set out in disobedience to Allah. When he enters ihram and places his foot in the stirrup and his mount sets off with him, and he says: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk, a caller from the sky calls out to him: No labbayk and no sa'dayk; your earning is unlawful, your provision is unlawful, and your mount is unlawful. Return burdened with sin, not rewarded, and receive news of what will grieve you. But when a man goes out for Hajj with lawful wealth, places his foot in the stirrup, and his mount sets off with him, and he says: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk, a caller from the sky calls out to him: Labbayk and sa'dayk, I have answered you. Your mount is lawful, your clothes are lawful, and your provision is lawful. Return rewarded, not burdened with sin, and receive news of what will delight you."],[8635,"Whoever builds a house for Allah in which Allah is worshiped from lawful wealth, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[8636,"People sighted a crescent one night and said: How beautiful it is! How clear it is! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: How will you be when you are from your Lord like the moon on the night of the full moon? Only the keen-sighted among you will see Him."],[8637,"Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Ashja' are my allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."],[8638,"While a man was riding on a cow, it turned around and said: I was not created for this; I was only created for plowing. He said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: And a wolf seized a sheep, and the shepherd pursued it. The wolf said: Who will have it on the day of the beast, a day when it will have no shepherd other than me? Then he said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Salamah said: And they were not among the people that day."],[8639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs then said the salam. Some of the people asked him: Has the prayer been shortened? – I think he said – So he prayed two rak'ahs, then said the salam, then prostrated twice."],[8640,"Come to the prayer with calmness and dignity. Pray what you catch up with and make up what you missed."],[8641,"He forbade the delegation of Abd al-Qays, I think he said, from using gourds, green jars, and hollowed-out stumps."],[8642,"A cat does not invalidate the prayer; it is one of the household items."],[8643,"The cat is part of the household goods."],[8644,"My nation will continue upon the natural disposition as long as they delay the dawn prayer until it is bright."],[8645,"A man's prayer in congregation is superior to his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees."],[8646,"If he drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks it again, flog him; then if he drinks again, flog him; then if he drinks again, kill him."],[8647,"Every soul has been decreed its share of adultery."],[8648,"The most truthful word spoken by a poet is: Indeed, everything besides God is false."],[8649,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to his companions while they were in the mosque in separate circles. He said: 'Why do I see you in scattered groups?'"],[8650,"The one consulted is entrusted."],[8651,"Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8652,"There was a prophet among the prophets who used to practice geomancy. Whoever matches his markings—or whoever matches that marking—will know."],[8653,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed and said the salutation after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn caught up with him and said: 'O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said: 'It has not been shortened and I did not forget.' He said: 'Indeed, by the One who sent you with the truth.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' So he led the people in two rak'ahs."],[8654,"A woman may not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt."],[8655,"Allah has not listened to anything as He listens to a Prophet reciting the Qur'an in a melodious voice — or a phrase similar to that."],[8656,"He forbade muhaqala and muzabana."],[8657,"Arguing about the Qur'an is disbelief."],[8658,"Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Sa'd b. Ibrahim, from Umar b. Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8659,"The soul of a believer is suspended as long as he has a debt."],[8660,"The soul of a believer is suspended by his debt until it is paid on his behalf."],[8661,"When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."],[8662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves."],[8663,"When a slave steals, sell him, even for a rope of twisted hair."],[8664,"A woman may not be married together with her paternal aunt, nor a woman with her maternal aunt."],[8665,"Three things are obligatory upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending funerals, and responding to a sneezer when he praises Allah."],[8666,"When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face."],[8667,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us from 'Umar b. Abi Salama, from his father, from Abu Hurayra: Thus did Talut say."],[8668,"Give charity, for I intend to dispatch an expedition. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came and said: O Messenger of God, I have four thousand: two thousand I lend to my Lord, and two thousand for my family. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: May God bless you in what you gave and bless you in what you kept. A man from the Ansar came, having obtained two sa's of dates, and said: O Messenger of God, I obtained two sa's of dates: one sa' I lend to my Lord, and one sa' for my family. The hypocrites disparaged him and said: What Ibn 'Awf gave was only for show, and: Are God and His Messenger not free from need of this man's sa'? Then God, blessed and exalted, revealed: Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities and those who find nothing but their effort, to the end of the verse."],[8669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment."],[8670,"I was granted concise speech, and I was aided by terror. While I was sleeping, I was brought the keys to the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand. I was sent to all people, spoils of war were made lawful for me, and the prophets were sealed with me."],[8671,"Let the beards grow and trim the mustaches."],[8672,"When one of you hears the iqama, let him come with tranquility, and pray what he catches and make up what he missed."],[8673,"They are days of eating."],[8674,"Whoever takes a handspan of land will be made to wear it, or wear her, from seven earths."],[8675,"There is no omen except your omen."],[8676,"O God, I am Your servant and Your messenger. I have made sacred what lies between its two lava fields, just as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred."],[8677,"Change the gray hair and do not imitate the Jews."],[8678,"A man from the Children of Israel used to lend money to people. A man came to him and said: O so-and-so, lend me six hundred dinars. He said: Yes, where is your guarantor? He said: God is my guarantor. He said: Yes. So he counted out six hundred dinars for him and set a term. The other man traveled by sea with the money to trade with it. God decreed that the term arrived while the other man had not returned, and the sea rose between them. The owner of the money went to the shore to ask about him, and those he asked said: We left him at such-and-such a village. The owner of the money said: O God, I gave it to him only for Your sake. The debtor, when the term fell due, carved out a piece of wood, placed the money inside it, and wrote a letter: From so-and-so to so-and-so: I have delivered your money to my guarantor who guaranteed for me. Then he sealed the mouth of the wood and cast it into the middle of the sea. The sea carried it until it cast it upon the shore. The owner of the money went asking about his companion as he had been asking, and he found the piece of wood. He took it to his family and said: Burn this. The dinars and the letter fell out. He read it and recognized it, and he set a term for the other man. The debtor came after that, and the owner of the money met him and said: O so-and-so, you have been long in coming. He said: Yes. He said: As for me, I delivered it to my guarantor who guaranteed for me, and as for you, here is your money, take it. He said: Your guarantor has paid me in full. Abu Hurayra said: We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and our clamor and voices grew loud over which of them was more faithful."],[8679,"When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come to it with tranquility. Whatever he catches, let him pray, and whatever he misses, let him complete."],[8680,"People will keep asking questions until one of them says: 'This is created, so who created Allah?'"],[8681,"When he entered the morning, he would say: 'We have entered the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah, there is no partner with Him, there is no god but Allah, and to Him is the resurrection.' And when he entered the evening, he would say: 'We have entered the evening and the dominion and all praise belong to Allah, there is no partner with Him, there is no god but He, and to Him is the final return.'"],[8682,"I asked my Lord for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked my Lord not to destroy my Ummah with drought, and He did that. I asked my Lord not to destroy my Ummah by making them fight each other, and He withheld that from me. And I asked Him not to give an enemy from outside them power over them, and He did that."],[8683,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed two or three, let him prostrate twice while sitting."],[8684,"Time will draw near, knowledge will be taken away, tribulations will appear, and harj will increase. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is harj?' He said: 'Killing.'"],[8685,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by—and he described the prophets—and I placed my hand where the feet of the prophets are placed in the Sacred House. I passed by Jesus son of Mary, and the closest of people in resemblance to him was Urwah b. Mas'ud. And Moses was a curly-haired, well-built man, as if he were one of the men of Shanu'ah. And Abraham was shown to me— ﷺ —and the closest of people in resemblance to him was your companion ﷺ."],[8686,"The major sins: the first of them is associating partners with Allah, killing a soul without right, consuming riba, consuming the property of an orphan, fleeing on the day of battle, slandering chaste women, and turning back to the desert Arabs after having made hijrah."],[8687,"Allah is jealous, and the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that His servant should come to what He has forbidden him."],[8688,"No servant—male or female—swears a false oath by this minbar, even for a fresh tooth-stick, without the Fire being obligatory for him."],[8689,"When you see it—meaning the crescent of Ramadan—then fast, and when you see it—meaning the crescent of Shawwal—then break your fast."],[8690,"The surplus water is not to be withheld so that the pasture may be withheld by it."],[8691,"Six mudds suffice for the ghusl of janabah."],[8692,"The sun and the moon will be two bulls in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[8693,"The best of you are those who are best in repaying debts."],[8694,"Salama b. Kuhayl, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. This hadith was narrated from Salama by more than one, among them Shu'ba, al-Thawri, 'Ali b. Salih and others, and there is more discussion about it than this."],[8695,"There is an hour on Friday during which no believing person asks Allah for good while he is in prayer—he considers it short—but He gives it to him. He said: When Abu Hurayrah died, I blamed myself for not having asked him about it. Then I said: This is Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and he has earlier companionship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; perhaps I will find with him knowledge from the Messenger of Allah. I entered upon Abu Sa'id and I found him—I think—with date stalks in front of him. I said: What are these date stalks, O Abu Sa'id? He said: These are date stalks in which Allah has placed blessing for us, and the Prophet ﷺ used to lean on one, so we cut a stalk for him. While it was in his hand, he saw spittle in the mosque and scraped it with it, then he turned to the people and said: O people, when one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of him; let him spit to his left, or under his feet, and if he finds no place to spit—I think he said—then in his shoe or in his garment. He said: The sky became cloudy that day, so it coincided. A flash of lightning flashed on a dark night, and the Prophet ﷺ saw him, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I knew that the witnesses of prayer were few, so I wanted to attend it with you. He said: Then remain when you pray. When—I think he said—he prayed, he passed by him and he raised the stalk to him and said: Take it out, and if you see blackness in your house, strike it with it, for it is a devil. He did so. He said: I said: O Abu Sa'id, the hour on Friday? He said: We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said: I knew it—I think he said—then I was made to forget it. He said: Then I left him until I came to the house of a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I said: This is a man who has read the Torah and accompanied the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I entered upon him and I said..."],[8696,"He used to prostrate in 'When the sky splits open'."],[8697,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8698,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[8699,"Between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and a prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[8700,"Al-Fadl b. al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Miswar b. Rifa'a, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, with a similar report. We do not know that al-Miswar b. Rifa'a connected a chain from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayrah except in this hadith."],[8701,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of 'Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches one rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."],[8702,"'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Busr b. Sa'id, 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj and 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8703,"Abu Ghassan, that is Muhammad b. Mutarrif, narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Malik. Muhammad b. Mutarrif did not mention, from Zayd b. Aslam, Busr b. Sa'id or 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj. We do not know that Zayd b. Aslam transmitted from Busr b. Sa'id except this hadith."],[8704,"Do not prepare nabidh in gourds, in green jars, or in vessels smeared with pitch."],[8705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who adds hair extensions and the one who asks for them."],[8706,"Fasting is for Me, and I reward it. The change in the breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."],[8707,"Paradise has one hundred levels, and between each two levels is what is between the heaven and the earth."],[8708,"Whoever goes out in the morning or the evening to the mosque, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, prepares for him a hospitable gift in Paradise each time he goes out in the morning or the evening."],[8709,"The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, his thigh is like al-Bayda', and the thickness of his skin is forty-two cubits by the cubit of the Almighty."],[8710,"There will be rulers over you who pray for you. If they are correct, it is for you and for them; if they err, it is for you and against them."],[8711,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour that no Muslim coincides with, asking Allah for good, except that He gives it to him."],[8712,"We are the last and the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. They were given the Book before us, and we were given it after them. They sought Friday, and Allah guided us to it, so the people follow us in it: the Jews tomorrow, and the Christians the day after tomorrow."],[8713,"Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8714,"Whoever spends a pair of something from his wealth, the keepers of Paradise call him: O servant of Allah, this is good. If he is from the people of prayer, he will be called from the gate of prayer; if he is from the people of charity, he will be called from the gate of charity; if he is from the people of fasting, he will be called from the gate of al-Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: There is no distress upon anyone called from any of these gates. Will anyone be called from all of them? He said: Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them. And what blessings!"],[8715,"The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him or let him down. Every part of the Muslim is inviolable to the Muslim: his blood and his wealth. Piety is here — and he pointed with his hand to his chest. He said it twice."],[8716,"Khalid b. al-Walid is a sword among the swords of Allah."],[8717,"Whoever marries a woman with a dowry while intending not to pay it to her is an adulterer, and whoever incurs a debt while intending not to repay it to its owner — I think he said — is a thief."],[8718,"Muhammad b. Aban narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8719,"He used to combine two prayers during travel."],[8720,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice and said: How do you regard this ritual of ours? He said: The people of heaven boast of it. And know, O Muhammad, that a young sheep is better than the best goat, and know, O Muhammad, that a young sheep is better than the best cow or camel. Had Allah, blessed and exalted, known of anything better than this, He would have ransomed Abraham ﷺ with it."],[8721,"A woman was forgiven who passed by a dog panting at a well, so she took off her leather sock and gave it water to drink."],[8722,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about donkeys whether anything concerning them had been revealed to him. He said: Nothing has been revealed to me concerning them except this unique, comprehensive verse: 'Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.'"],[8723,"No pain, fatigue, worry, or grief afflicts the believer, not even a thorn that pricks him, except that Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."],[8724,"Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Amr, from Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8725,"Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Amr b. Ata', from Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly to the hadith of Muhammad b. Ishaq."],[8726,"The testimony of a Bedouin against a village dweller is not valid."],[8727,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer, and the one who plunders a valuable plunder does not plunder it while he is a believer."],[8728,"A man may utter a word to make his companions laugh, by which he falls farther than the Pleiades."],[8729,"To God, Blessed and Exalted, belong ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. God is Witr (Odd) and loves the odd."],[8730,"Recitation was made light for Dawud ﷺ; he would order his mount to be saddled, and before it was ready, he would finish."],[8731,"While a man was stealing, Isa ﷺ saw him. Isa said to him, 'Are you stealing?' He said, 'By God, I did not do it.' He said, 'I believe God and disbelieve my eyes.'"],[8732,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[8733,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Amr b. Dinar, from Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, as his own statement (mawquf), with the like of it. Thus the companions of Hammad narrated it from Hammad with this chain as mawquf. Abdul-Warith narrated it from Ayyub from Amr b. Dinar from Ata' b. Yasar from Abu Hurayra as mawquf."],[8734,"Abdul-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub from Amr b. Dinar from Ata' b. Yasar from Abu Hurayra as mawquf. Abdul-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated it from Ayyub as mawquf."],[8735,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr b. Dinar from Ata' b. Yasar from Abu Hurayra, and he did not raise it. Ma'mar narrated it from Ayyub from Amr b. Dinar as marfu'."],[8736,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[8737,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[8738,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[8739,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."],[8740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out from the privy, and food was brought to him. It was said, “Will you not perform ablution?” or “Shall we not bring you water for ablution?” He said, “I do not intend to pray.”"],[8741,"Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8742,"Zakariyya b. Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. Thus 'Abd al-A'la narrated it from Zakariyya, from 'Amr, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Abu 'Asim disagreed with him in its chain, narrating it from Zakariyya, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. The correct version is the hadith of 'Amr from 'Ata' b. Yasar. We do not know that Husayn al-Mu'allim transmitted from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith, and no one narrated it from him except 'Isa b. Yunus."],[8743,"Muhammad b. Muslim narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8744,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."],[8745,"When a man goes bankrupt and another man finds his very property with him, he is more entitled to it."],[8746,"Ibn 'Uyaynah reported to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Hisham b. Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. Ash'ath b. Sa'id Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman is weak in hadith due to the frequency of errors in what he narrates, even though a number of those who are attributed to knowledge have narrated from him."],[8747,"My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved than performing what I have made obligatory upon him. My servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him. When I love him, I become his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, and his hand with which he strikes. If he asks Me, I will surely give him, and if he seeks refuge in Me, I will surely grant him refuge. I have never hesitated about anything I do as I hesitate about the soul of the believer: he hates death, and I hate to grieve him."],[8748,"Three people's supplications are not rejected: the one who remembers God, the supplication of the oppressed, and the just ruler."],[8749,"The people of Paradise will see one another as the eastern star is seen from the western star in the horizon, rising in the distance of degrees. They said, “O Messenger of God, who are they?” He said, “People who believed in God and believed the messengers.”"],[8750,"Hell said, “O Lord, permit me to take two breaths, for I fear that I might overflow onto Your creatures.” So He permitted it two breaths every year, twice. Thus the intense heat is from its blaze, and the intense cold is from its freezing cold."],[8751,"The son of Adam grows old and his body diminishes, while his heart remains young in love of two things: long life and love of wealth."],[8752,"A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the blessing."],[8753,"The example of the believer is like a tender plant of the crop; wherever the wind reaches it, it bends it."],[8754,"All of my nation will enter Paradise except those who refuse. They said: 'O Messenger of God, who refuses?' He said: 'Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me enters the Fire.'"],[8755,"Whoever believes in God and His Messenger and establishes the prayer, it is a right upon God that He enters him into Paradise, whether he migrates in the way of God or sits in the land where his mother gave birth to him."],[8756,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was one day talking to his companions, he said: 'A man from the desert dwellers was admitted to Paradise, and he asked his Lord for permission to cultivate. He said: Are you not in whatever you wish? He said: I love to have more. He said: So He permitted him, and he sowed, and its growth, straightness, and ripening happened in the blink of an eye, and it came like mountains. Then it was said: O son of Adam, nothing satisfies you?'"],[8757,"Whoever fasts a day in the way of God, God will distance him from the Fire by seventy years."],[8758,"The exchange in pre-Islamic times was that a man would say to another man: 'Exchange wives with me, and I will exchange with you my wife. Give up your wife to me, and I will give up my wife to you.' Then God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And do not exchange them for other wives, even if their beauty pleases you' (Quran 4:129). Then 'Uyaynah b. Hisn al-Fazari entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while 'A'ishah, may God have mercy on her, was with him; he entered without permission. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Where is the asking of permission?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I have not asked permission of any man from Mudar since I reached maturity.' Then he said: 'Who is this fair-skinned woman beside you?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers.' He said: 'Shall I give up for you the most beautiful of creation?' He said: 'O 'Uyaynah, God, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden that.' When he left, 'A'ishah, may God have mercy on her, said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'A fool who is obeyed, and despite what you see, he is the chief of his people.'"],[8759,"While a man was praying with his lower garment hanging below his ankles, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Go and perform ablution.' So he went, performed ablution, and came back. Then he said: 'Go and perform ablution.' So he went, performed ablution, and came back. A man said: 'O Prophet of God, you ordered him to perform ablution, then you were silent about him.' He said: 'He was praying while his lower garment was hanging below his ankles, and God, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the prayer of a man whose lower garment hangs below his ankles.'"],[8760,"Do not write from me anything except the Quran, and whoever has written from me anything other than the Quran, let him erase it. And narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[8761,"Fasting is for Me, and I reward for it. And the change in the breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to God than the fragrance of musk."],[8762,"Gabriel kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[8763,"The Prophet ﷺ abandoned his wives. Shu'bah said: I think he said: for a month. He said: So 'Umar b. al-Khattab came to him while he was on a reed mat that had left marks on his side. He said: O Messenger of God, Chosroes — I think he said: and Caesar — drink from gold and silver while you are like this! The Prophet ﷺ said: Their good things have been hastened for them in their worldly life."],[8764,"We had no food during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ except the two black ones: dates and water."],[8765,"No one endures its hardships except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him."],[8766,"O God, indeed Ibrahim is Your servant and Your friend. He called upon You for the people of Makkah to bless their sa' and their mudd. Indeed I am Your servant and Your messenger, and I call upon You for the people of Madinah with what Ibrahim called upon You for the people of Makkah: to bless their sa' and their mudd, just as You blessed the people of Makkah in their sa' and their mudd."],[8767,"Honor goats and wipe away their nasal discharge, for they are among the animals of Paradise."],[8768,"A time will surely come upon people when a passerby will pass by a grave and say: I wish I were in your place instead of your companion."],[8769,"God, Blessed and Exalted, does not cease accepting repentance from His servant until he gurgles in his soul."],[8770,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting on the day of the conquest, and Abu Bakr was standing at his head with a sword."],[8771,"Whoever dies ill dies a martyr, is protected from the two trials of the grave, and provision from Paradise is brought to him morning and evening."],[8772,"Indeed in Paradise there are pillars of ruby, upon them chambers of chrysolite, with open doors that shine as the shining of a brilliant star. He said: We said: O Messenger of God, who will dwell in them? He said: Those who love one another for God, who spend on one another for God, and who meet one another for God."],[8773,"Gabriel ﷺ came to him and prayed with him the prayers at two times, two times, except Maghrib. He came to me and prayed Zuhr when it was like the strap of my sandal; then he came to me and prayed 'Asr with me when it was like me; then he came to me at Maghrib and prayed with me when the sun had set; then he came to me at 'Isha and prayed with me at the time of twilight; then he came to me at Fajr and prayed with me when dawn broke. Then he came to me the next day and prayed Zuhr with me when the shadow was like me; then he came to me at 'Asr and prayed with me when it was like me; then he came to me at Maghrib and prayed with me when the sun had set, not changing it from its first time; then he came to me at 'Isha and prayed with me when the first third of the night had passed; then he made it light for me at Fajr until I could not see a star in the sky. Then he said: Between these two is the time."],[8774,"Do not bid against one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not envy one another, and let none of you sell over the sale of another. Be, O servants of God, brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, does not forsake him, and does not despise him. Piety is here — pointing to his chest. All of a Muslim is inviolable to a Muslim: his blood and his honor. It is enough evil for a man to despise his Muslim brother."],[8775,"Whoever prays a prayer without reciting in it the Mother of the Qur'an, it is deficient, not complete. I said to him: 'O Abu Hurayrah, sometimes I am behind the imam.' He said: 'He squeezed my forearm and said: Recite it to yourself, O Persian; for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I have divided the prayer between Me and My servant into two halves; half of it is for Me and half is for My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite. The servant says: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has praised Me. He says: The Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has extolled Me. The servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has glorified Me. And this verse is between Me and My servant. The servant says: You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help. This is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks. The servant says: Guide us to the straight path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have incurred wrath, nor of those who are astray. These are for My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks."],[8776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in a prayer which we thought was the dawn prayer. Then he said: 'Did any of you recite behind me?' A man said: 'I did.' He said: 'I say, why am I contested in the Qur'an?' So the people stopped reciting in the prayers in which the Prophet ﷺ recited aloud."],[8777,"So the people stopped reciting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the prayers in which the Prophet ﷺ recited aloud, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8778,"There is no race prize except in hoofed animals or camels."],[8779,"If a fly falls into the drink of one of you, he should immerse it completely, then remove it; for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other a cure."],[8780,"I came along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he heard a man reciting: 'Say: He is Allah, the One' to its end. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is guaranteed.' It was said: 'What is, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Paradise.' Abu Hurayrah said: 'I wanted to go to the man and give him glad tidings, but I feared I would miss lunch with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I preferred lunch. Then I returned to the man and found he had left.'"],[8781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[8782,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood in his wall."],[8783,"If one of you asks his neighbor to place a piece of wood in his wall, he should not prevent him."],[8784,"When one of you prays in a single garment, he should wrap its ends in opposite directions."],[8785,"There is in Paradise a palace - I think he said: of pearl - in which there is no crack or weakness, which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has prepared for His close friend Ibrahim ﷺ as a hospitality gift."],[8786,"Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And this hadith we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad b. Salamah and attributed it as marfu' except Yazid b. Harun and al-Nadr b. Shumayl; others narrate it as mawquf."],[8787,"He saw a man driving a sacrificial camel, so he said: 'Ride it.' The man said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Ride it, woe to you,' or 'may you be ruined.'"],[8788,"He saw a man driving a sacrificial camel, so he said: 'Ride it.' He said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Ride it, woe to you,' or 'may you be ruined.'"],[8789,"A cat is part of the household goods."],[8790,"My beloved friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will not abandon whether traveling or not: fasting three days of every month, performing Witr before sleeping, and praying the two rak'ahs of Duha."],[8791,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour during which no servant asks Allah for something good except that He grants it to him."],[8792,"The Prophet ﷺ and his family, or some of his family, used to bathe from a single vessel."],[8793,"Whoever listens to the conversation of a people while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears."],[8794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on the Day of 'Arafah at 'Arafat."],[8795,"You came to us and asked us, so we gave you, and then you said what you said, and in the hearts of my companions there is something against you because of that. So when you come, say before them what you said before me so that it may leave their chests.' He said: 'Yes.' Al-Hakam narrated to me that 'Ikrimah said: Abu Hurayrah said: 'When the Bedouin came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your companion came to us and asked us, so we gave him, and he said what he said. We have called him and given him, and he claims that he is satisfied. Is that so?\" The Bedouin said: \"Yes, may Allah reward you well as family and kin.\" Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"My example and the example of this Bedouin is like a man who had a she-camel that strayed from him. People chased it but only made it more wild. The owner of the she-camel said to them: 'Leave me alone with my she-camel, for I am gentler with it and more knowledgeable about it.' He went towards it, picked up for it some dust from the ground, and called it until it came and responded. He tightened its saddle and mounted it. If I had obeyed you when he said what he said, he would have entered the Fire.\" And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this wording except through this route with this chain.'"],[8796,"People will keep asking: 'Allah was before everything, so what was before Him?'"],[8797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the Dajjal, and he said – I think he said: 'He will emerge from the sea of the east.'"],[8798,"I was with 'Ali when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to the people of Makkah with Bara'ah. He said: 'What were you calling out?' He said: 'We were calling out: No one will enter Paradise except a believer, and no one may circumambulate the House naked, and whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah, its term or its matter is up to four months; when the four months have passed, Allah and His Messenger are free from the polytheists, and no polytheist may perform Hajj after this year.' So I kept calling out until my voice became hoarse."],[8799,"Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabi', narrated to us from al-Shaybani from al-Sha'bi from al-Muharrar b. Abi Hurayrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Qays, except a report that reached me from al-Nadr b. Shumayl from Shu'bah, from al-Shaybani. The preserved version is what Ghundar narrated from Shu'bah from al-Mughirah."],[8800,"'Ubayd Allah b. 'Umar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Hanzalah b. 'Ali, from Abu Hurayrah."],[8801,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will surely raise the talbiyah at Fajj al-Rawha' as a pilgrim for Hajj or 'Umrah, or he will certainly combine them both."],[8802,"Juwayriyah narrated to us from Malik, from al-Zuhri that Hanzalah b. 'Ali al-Aslami said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. Then he mentioned something similar."],[8803,"The grateful eater is like the patient faster."],[8804,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it. He gives up food and drink for My sake."],[8805,"When one of you is sitting in the sun and it withdraws from him, he should move from his seat."],[8806,"When you see the crescent, fast; and when you see it, break your fast. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty days. Your breaking of the fast is on the day you break it, and your sacrifice is on the day you sacrifice. All of 'Arafah is a standing place, all of Jam' (Muzdalifah) is a standing place, all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, and all the ravines of Makkah are a place of sacrifice."],[8807,"The best of your kohl is ithmid (antimony); it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight."],[8808,"None of you should drink while standing; if someone forgets, he should make himself vomit."],[8809,"Saying subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."],[8810,"Every step one of you takes toward the prayer, a good deed is written for him, a sin is erased from him, and he is raised a degree by it."],[8811,"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that 'Ammar b. Aws informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ something similar. And we do not know that 'Abbad b. Aws or 'Ammar narrated anything except this hadith."],[8812,"The worst thing in a man is destructive miserliness and unnerving cowardice."],[8813,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited 'not of those who have incurred wrath nor of those who are astray,' he said, 'Amin,' until the first row could hear him."],[8814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr and 'Umar and 'Uthman ؓ used to begin the recitation with 'All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[8815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ promised us the expedition to India. If I witness it, I will spend my wealth and my life in it. If I am killed, then I am among the best of martyrs; and if I return, then I am Abu Hurayrah, the freed one."],[8816,"Whoever follows a funeral procession and prays over it, then returns, has one qirat; and whoever follows it until its burial is completed has two qirats. They said, 'What are the two qirats?' He said, 'The smaller of them is like Mount Uhud.'"],[8817,"He saw a man drinking while standing and said, 'Would you like a cat to drink with you?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then one worse than it has drunk with you: Satan.'"],[8818,"None of you will be saved by his deeds. They said, 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and grace from Him.'"],[8819,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood in his wall."],[8820,"Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith has been narrated by a group from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah."],[8821,"Whoever attends a funeral and prays over it has one qirat."],[8822,"On Friday, at every gate of the mosque there are angels who record the first to come, then the next."],[8823,"One of you is in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer."],[8824,"The best day on which the sun rises is Friday; on it Adam ﷺ was created, and on it the Hour will commence."],[8825,"Al-Layth narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This hadith has been narrated by others besides those we mentioned from al-Zuhri, and they contradicted those we named in its chain."],[8826,"My heirs will not divide a dinar or a dirham; whatever I leave is charity."],[8827,"Adam and Musa (peace be upon them) argued. Musa said to Adam: 'You are the one Allah created with His hand, breathed into you from His spirit, commanded the angels and they prostrated to you; you brought us out, or you brought your descendants out, of Paradise.' Adam ﷺ said: 'You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech—I think he said—and sent down the Torah upon you. Do you find that written against me before I was created?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So Adam confuted Musa.'"],[8828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in 'When the sky is split open' and 'Read in the name of your Lord who created.'"],[8829,"The strong believer is more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, and in each is good. Be keen on what benefits you, seek help from Allah, and do not be helpless. If something befalls you, do not say: 'If only it had been such and such,' but say: 'Allah decreed, and what He wills He does.'"],[8830,"The likeness of the believer is that of a tender stalk of a crop swayed by the winds; the likeness of the disbeliever is that of a cedar standing on its roots, nothing moves it until a wind blows and snaps it."],[8831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer and after the dawn prayer."],[8832,"Water may not be withheld to withhold thereby the pasture."],[8833,"The most beloved of places to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are the mosques, and the most hateful of places to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are their marketplaces."],[8834,"A vow does not bring near anything Allah has not already decreed, but through a vow the miser is made to bring out what he did not intend to bring out."],[8835,"Adam and Musa disputed. Musa said: \"O Adam, Allah created you with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit and commanded the angels, and they prostrated to you. Then He commanded you to dwell in Paradise and eat from wherever you wished freely, and He forbade you from one tree, but you disobeyed your Lord and ate from it.\" He said: \"O Musa, did you not know that that was decreed for me before He created me?\" He said: \"So Adam argued against Musa.\""],[8836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man being supported between two men. He asked about him, and they said: \"He vowed to perform Hajj walking.\" He said: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is self-sufficient and has no need of his vow — I think he said — command him to ride.\""],[8837,"None of you should refuse — or none of you should refrain from — giving to a beggar, even if he sees in his hands two bracelets of gold."],[8838,"Jibril ﷺ advised me: 'When you perform ablution, sprinkle water.'"],[8839,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood on his wall or upon his wall."],[8840,"The owner of the mount has more right to its front."],[8841,"The people should be led in prayer by the one most versed in the Book of Allah."],[8842,"The talbiyah of the Prophet ﷺ was: 'Labbayka ilaha al-haqq' (Here I am, O God of Truth)."],[8843,"Abd al-Rahman b. Thabit b. Thawban narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. al-Fadl, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[8844,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution twice, twice."],[8845,"Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years."],[8846,"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Jahannam, and from the trials of life and death, and from the trial of the Dajjal."],[8847,"Ibrahim ﷺ was circumcised with an adze after he had reached eighty years."],[8848,"No hāmah, no hāmah — twice."],[8849,"Whoever is offered perfume should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and pleasant in scent."],[8850,"Delay the noon prayer in intense heat, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell."],[8851,"The Jews sacrifice a ram for a boy and do not sacrifice for a girl — or slaughter, the doubt is from him or from his father — so sacrifice or slaughter two rams for a boy and one ram for a girl."],[8852,"The dowries of the ḥūr al-ʿīn are handfuls of dates and pieces of bread."],[8853,"A woman shall not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt."],[8854,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."],[8855,"Do you not wonder how Allah turns away from me the abuse and cursing of Quraysh? They abuse Muzammam and curse Muzammam, but I am Muhammad ﷺ."],[8856,"The most despicable name before Allah is a man who calls himself King of Kings."],[8857,"Delay by a wealthy man is wrongdoing, and if one of you is referred to a solvent person, let him accept the transfer."],[8858,"If the servant of one of you prepares his food and endures its heat and smoke, let him seat the servant with him; if he refuses, let him take a morsel and feed it to him."],[8859,"A vow does not bring upon the son of Adam anything that Allah has not decreed for him, but it is a means by which something is extracted from the miser."],[8860,"Excess water is not to be withheld to prevent thereby the herbage."],[8861,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me."],[8862,"You see my qiblah here; yet your humility and your bowing are not hidden from me."],[8863,"When My servant intends a good deed, record it for him as a good deed; if he does it, record it for him as ten times its like. If he intends an evil deed, do not record it; if he does it, record it as a single evil deed."],[8864,"The example of the spender and the miser is like two men upon whom are two coats of iron from their chests to their collarbones. When the spender intends to spend, the coat of mail expands over him until it covers his footsteps; and when the miser intends to spend, it contracts from behind him, so he keeps trying to loosen it but is unable, and he keeps trying to loosen it but is unable."],[8865,"Allah has guaranteed — or Allah has taken responsibility and Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has pledged — for whoever goes out as a warrior in the path of Allah, nothing sending him out except jihad and faith in Me and belief in My Messenger: if I cause him to die, I will admit him to Paradise, and if I return him to his home from which he went out, he will obtain what he attains of reward or booty."],[8866,"If a man were to look into his neighbor's house and he threw a pebble at his eye, there would be no liability upon him."],[8867,"Sulayman b. Dawud ﷺ said: 'Tonight I shall go around to such-and-such a number of women' — I think he said a hundred — 'each woman among them will give birth to a boy who will fight in the path of Allah.' He went around to them, but none of them conceived except one woman who, they say, gave birth to half a human being. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Had he made an exception, every woman among them would have conceived a boy who would fight in the path of Allah.'"],[8868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out by the gate of the tree and return by the path of al-Mu'arras."],[8869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined between two prayers in Madinah without fear."],[8870,"There is no protected pasture except for Allah and His Messenger."],[8871,"Beware of looking at lepers as you beware of the lion."],[8872,"Assistance comes from God according to the burden, and patience comes from God according to the trial."],[8873,"Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it; if it is obscured from you, then count thirty."],[8874,"The best day on which the sun rises is Friday. In it is an hour in which no Muslim man asks God for something but that he is forgiven."],[8875,"He forbade the sale of uncertainty and the sale by pebbles."],[8876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade shighar, the sale of uncertainty, and the sale by pebbles."],[8877,"The Euphrates will recede from a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it; ninety-nine out of every hundred will be killed."],[8878,"The dream of a believer is one of forty-five parts of prophethood."],[8879,"The angels pray for one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place: 'O God, forgive him; O God, have mercy on him.'"],[8880,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer."],[8881,"If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, he should wash it seven times - I think he said - one of them with earth."],[8882,"O God, I take a covenant with You, for I am only human. So whichever believer I have reviled or flogged, make that a prayer, a purification, and a means of nearness for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[8883,"The Hour will not be established until some thirty liars, all claiming to be the Messenger of God, are sent."],[8884,"God's hand is full; night and day do not diminish it."],[8885,"A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim: he does not betray him, lie to him, or abandon him. All of a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his honor, his wealth, and his blood. Piety is here. It is enough for a Muslim to shun his brother."],[8886,"When God created Adam, He wiped his back and every soul He would create until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back. Then He set a lifespan for each of them. Adam ﷺ said: 'Who are these?' He said - I think he said: 'Your descendants.' He said: And there was a man among them with light between his eyes. Adam said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'This is a man from your progeny, in the last of the nations, called David.' He said: 'And how much lifespan have You given him?' He said: 'Sixty years.' He said: 'Then add to him forty years from my lifespan.' When God completed Adam's lifespan, the Angel of Death came to him and he said: 'Forty years of my lifespan remain.' He said: 'Did you not give them to your son David?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'He denied, so his descendants denied; he forgot, so his descendants forgot; and he erred, so his descendants erred.'"],[8887,"Do not curse time; for God is time."],[8888,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. Your wife says: 'Spend on me or divorce me'; your child says: 'To whom are you entrusting me?'; and your slave says: 'Spend on me or sell me.'"],[8889,"O Messenger of God, whom should I support? He said: 'Your wife says: Feed me; your servant says: Feed me and employ me; your child says: To whom are you leaving me?'"],[8890,"The people of the highest degrees will be seen just as you see the shining star in the eastern and western horizon, from among the degrees. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, are those the prophets?' He said: 'No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, a people who believed in God and His Messenger and affirmed the messengers.'"],[8891,"A dirham surpassed a hundred thousand dirhams. They said: 'O Messenger of God, how did a dirham surpass a hundred thousand dirhams?' He said: 'A man had one dirham and gave it as charity, and a man had a hundred thousand dirhams and gave it as charity.'"],[8892,"The imam is appointed only to be followed; so when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; and when he recites, remain silent."],[8893,"There is no contagion, no hama, no ghoul, and no Safar."],[8894,"What I have told you is from God, and it is that about which there is no doubt."],[8895,"The religion is sincere counsel."],[8896,"A man removed a thorny branch from the road—or a tree he cut down, or perhaps (I think he said) something harmful—and removed it, so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."],[8897,"A man never did any good at all, and he used to lend money to people. He would say to his servant: 'Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, perhaps Allah will overlook us.' When he died, Allah—Blessed and Exalted—said: 'Did you ever do any good for Me?' He said: 'No, except that I had a servant and I used to say: Overlook, perhaps Allah will overlook us.' He said: 'Indeed I have overlooked you.'"],[8898,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the morning prayer before the sun rises has not missed it, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has not missed it."],[8899,"Malik narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Abu Salih and 'Ata' b. Yasar—I think he said—and Busr b. Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[8900,"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or waives for him, Allah will shade him under the shade of His Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade."],[8901,"Whoever fasts one day in the way of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy years."],[8902,"I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me."],[8903,"Allah—Blessed and Exalted—is more intensely joyful at the repentance of His servant—I think he said—than one of you who finds his lost camel in the desert."],[8904,"When a servant draws near to Allah—Blessed and Exalted—a handspan, Allah draws near to him a cubit; and when he draws near a cubit, Allah draws near to him an arm's length; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed."],[8905,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I devote half of my prayer to supplication for you?' He said: 'Whatever you wish.' He said: 'Then should I devote two-thirds of my prayer to supplication for you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then should I devote all of my prayer to supplication for you?' He said: 'Then Allah will suffice you for the concerns of this world and the Hereafter.'"],[8906,"Horses are three: for one man a reward, for another a cover, and upon another a burden. As for the one for which it is a reward: a man who keeps it tethered in the way of Allah and gives it a long tether in a meadow or garden; whatever it eats within the length of its tether in that meadow or garden counts as good deeds for him, and even if it breaks its tether and runs a hill or two, its urine and droppings are good deeds for him, and even if it passes by a river and drinks from it, that is good deeds for him—so it is a reward for him. Another man keeps it tethered out of self-restraint, not forgetting the right of Allah on its backs, so it is a cover for him. Another man keeps it tethered out of pride, ostentation, and enmity against the people of Islam, so it is a burden on him for that."],[8907,"The two eyes commit adultery and the tongue commits adultery, and the private parts confirm that or deny it."],[8908,"The first to let loose the sāʾibah animals, set up the nuṣub idols, and alter the covenant of Abū Ibrāhīm ﷺ was ʿAmr b. Luḥayy. I saw him in the Fire dragging his intestines."],[8909,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in the pledge of allegiance: in your activity and your hardship, and in preference over you."],[8910,"When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibrīl — I think he said: — “Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him.”"],[8911,"I insulted a man in Islam by his mother from the Jāhiliyyah, so he appealed against me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In you there is a trace of disbelief.” When he mentioned disbelief, my legs trembled, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will never insult a Muslim after this ever."],[8912,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of the ʿAṣr prayer before the sun sets has not missed the prayer, and whoever catches one rakʿah of the morning prayer before the sun rises has not missed the prayer."],[8913,"Whoever guards what is between his jaws and between his legs will enter Paradise."],[8914,"The believer is affable, and there is no good in one who is not affable and is not befriended."],[8915,"When the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her. Then if she commits adultery, let him flog her. Then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."],[8916,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed secretly, but if he is seen doing it, it pleases him. He said: He has the reward of the secret and the reward of the open."],[8917,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ demanding repayment of a loan of half a wasq. He gave him a wasq and said: Half a wasq is yours and half is from me. Then the owner of the wasq came demanding repayment, and he gave him two wasqs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A wasq is yours and a wasq is from me."],[8918,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."],[8919,"The imam is responsible and the mu'adhdhin is trusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[8920,"It is near that the livers of the riding camels will be struck, yet no scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Madinah will be found."],[8921,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my Ummah, I would not stay behind any expedition that goes out, but I do not find that which I can mount them upon, nor do they find that which they can ride, and it is difficult for them to stay behind from me. I would love that I be killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life."],[8922,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[8923,"May Allah have mercy on a man who gets up at night and prays and wakes his wife, and she prays; and if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. May Allah have mercy on a woman who gets up at night and prays and wakes her husband, and he prays; and if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face."],[8924,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it then take it out, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other a cure, and it begins with the disease, so immerse it then take it out."],[8925,"I am only to you like a father; I teach you: when one of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the Qiblah nor turn his back to it, and when one of you cleans himself, let him not clean himself with his right hand. And he used to command using three stones, and he forbade dung and bones."],[8926,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man supplicating like this with his finger, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Like this, one, one.'"],[8927,"The martyr feels no pain except like one of you feels a pinch."],[8928,"There is no one who goes out in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who goes out in His path - but he will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound gushing blood; the color is the color of blood and the smell is the smell of musk."],[8929,"When the believer commits a sin, there is a black spot on his heart. If he repents, desists, and seeks forgiveness, it is polished. If he returns, it increases until the heart becomes black. That is the covering which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, mentioned: 'Nay, but on their hearts is a covering because of what they used to earn.'"],[8930,"The religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, to His Book, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people."],[8931,"The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer."],[8932,"Indeed, part of the perfection of faith is good character."],[8933,"This affair—or upon this affair—a group from my ummah will continue, not harmed by those who oppose them, until the command of Allah comes to them."],[8934,"Do not leave the camels and sheep unmilked so their udders become full, for whoever buys them in that state, the buyer has the option: if he wishes he keeps it, and if he wishes he may return it along with a sa' of dates."],[8935,"The heart of an old man remains young in love of two things: long life and abundant wealth."],[8936,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is the one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives."],[8937,"The treasure of one of you on the Day of Resurrection will be a bald-headed snake that keeps pursuing him—I think he said—and it will bite his finger, or a similar word."],[8938,"Upon every soul of the children of Adam is written its share of fornication; it will inevitably reach that. The eye's fornication is looking, the ear's fornication is listening, the hand's fornication is seizing, the foot's fornication is walking, the tongue's fornication is speaking, and the heart desires and wishes, and the private part confirms that or denies it."],[8939,"Adam met Musa, and Musa said to him a word that escaped Abu Bakr al-Bazzar. Adam said to him: 'Are you Musa whom Allah gave the Torah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By how much do you find the Torah was written before my creation?' Musa said: 'By such and such.' Adam said: 'Do you not find in it my sin?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then do you blame me for something Allah decreed upon me before my creation?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'So Adam confuted Musa.'"],[8940,"Wealth is not from an abundance of worldly goods, but wealth is the wealth of the soul."],[8941,"A man came to a well to drink from it, and at the well there was a dog. He took off one of his leather socks, scooped water for it, and gave it to drink. Allah appreciated that and admitted him to Paradise."],[8942,"He was asked about a stray sheep, and he said: 'It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.' And he was asked about a stray camel, and he said: 'What is it to you? It has its own water-skin and its own hoofs; leave it until its owner finds it.'"],[8943,"There is no contagion, no ghoul, no hamah, and no Safar."],[8944,"I was sent only to perfect noble character."],[8945,"When he sneezed, he placed his hand or his garment over his face and lowered, or reduced, his voice with it."],[8946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded spreading the arms in prayer. The people complained to him of weakness, so he commanded them to seek support from the knees."],[8947,"Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn 'Ajlan from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know this hadith to be reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this route."],[8948,"The poor came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8949,"The poor complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken the high ranks and lasting bliss. They pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have wealth beyond that from which they give charity and free slaves.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Shall I tell you of something by which you catch up with those who preceded you and no one after you catches up with you except one who does the like of what you do?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Glorify Allah after every prayer ten times, say Allah is greatest ten times, and praise Him fifteen times.\""],[8950,"Whoever says when he enters upon morning and when he enters upon evening, 'Glory be to Allah and with His praise,' no one will come on the Day of Resurrection with anything better than what he brings."],[8951,"The accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and one 'Umrah to the next 'Umrah expiates what is between them."],[8952,"Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something afflicts him should blame no one but himself."],[8953,"The closest a servant is to Allah is while he is prostrating."],[8954,"'Umrah expiates what is between it and the next 'Umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[8955,"The poor came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"The wealthy have taken the high ranks and the enduring bliss.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And what is that?\" They said: \"They pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they have wealth by which they give charity and free slaves, and we cannot.\" He said: \"Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, no one who came before you will surpass you, and no one after you will catch up with you, except one who does the like of what you do: say 'Glory be to Allah' thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times.\" They did so, and the wealthy learned of that and did what the poor said, so they returned to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we did what you commanded us, but they do what we do.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is the bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills.\""],[8956,"Travel is a portion of torment; it prevents one of you from his drink and his sleep. So when one of you has fulfilled his need, let him hasten back to his family."],[8957,"If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row, and found no way except to draw lots for it, they would draw lots. And if they knew what is in going early, they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the night prayer and the dawn prayer, they would come to them even if crawling."],[8958,"An 'umrah expiates what is between it and the next 'umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[8959,"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah and praise Him,' Allah wipes away his sins, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."],[8960,"The martyrs are five: the one who dies of plague, the one who dies of a stomach disease, the one who dies under a collapse, the one who drowns, and the woman who dies in childbirth."],[8961,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[8962,"Whoever absolves a regretful person, Allah will absolve his stumble on the Day of Resurrection."],[8963,"A man passed by a thorny branch and moved it away from the road, so Allah admitted him to Paradise."],[8964,"A man - or a woman - passed by a dog eating moist earth from thirst, and the man or the woman took off a leather sock and began scooping water for it, or gave it water, or she gave it water, and Allah admitted him to Paradise, or admitted her to Paradise."],[8965,"When the imam says, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' then say, 'Our Lord, to You is the praise.'"],[8966,"He used to seek refuge from the attainment of misery, the evil of decree, and the gloating of enemies."],[8967,"Whoever prays over a funeral has one qīrāṭ, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qīrāṭs."],[8968,"The ʿumrah expiates what is between it and the next ʿumrah, and the accepted ḥajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[8969,"Faith has seventy-some or sixty-some branches, the best of which is the testimony that there is no god but God, and the lowest of which is removing harm from the road. And modesty is a branch of faith."],[8970,"Ibn ʿAjlān narrated to us, from ʿAbdullāh b. Dīnār, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[8971,"When God loves a servant — I think he said: — Gabriel calls out — I think he said: — in the heaven: “God loves so-and-so, so love him.” Then acceptance is placed for him on earth."],[8972,"When one of you sneezes, let him say, “Praise be to God,” and let his brother or companion say to him, “May God have mercy on you,” and let him say, “May God guide you and set your affairs aright.”"],[8973,"Whoever is given wealth by God but does not pay its zakāh, it will be made into a bald-headed poisonous snake with two fangs on the Day of Resurrection, which will seize him by his cheek on the Day of Resurrection and say, “I am your treasure.” Then he recited this verse: “And let not those who withhold…”"],[8974,"A servant may utter a word that pleases God, paying no attention to it, by which God raises him degrees. And a servant may utter a word that angers God, paying no attention to it, by which he falls into Hell."],[8975,"Whoever gives charity equal to a date from pure earnings — and nothing ascends to God, Blessed and Exalted, except what is pure — God, Blessed and Exalted, accepts it with His right hand and nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal until it becomes like a mountain."],[8976,"When God loves a servant, He calls Gabriel: “God loves so-and-so, so love him,” and Gabriel loves him. Then he calls out among the inhabitants of heaven: “God loves so-and-so, so love him,” and the inhabitants of heaven love him. Then acceptance is placed for him on earth."],[8977,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbdullāh b. Dīnār narrated to us, from his father, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah."],[8978,"Wretched is the slave of the dīnār and the slave of the dirham; wretched and fallen. If he is pricked by a thorn, may it not be removed. Blessed is a servant who takes hold of the reins of his horse: if he is on guard duty, he is on guard duty."],[8979,"The womb is a branch. Whoever maintains it, Allah maintains him, and whoever severs it, He severs him — or Allah severs him."],[8980,"A man passed by a thorny branch and moved it away from the path, so Allah appreciated him for it and admitted him to Paradise."],[8981,"A man saw a dog eating moist earth from thirst, so the man took his leather sock and began scooping water for it until he quenched its thirst, so Allah appreciated him for it and admitted him to Paradise."],[8982,"Three people Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection: a man who swears about a commodity that he was given more for it than he actually gave; a man who withholds surplus water, so Allah, blessed and exalted, says: 'Today I withhold My surplus from you as you withheld the surplus of what your hands did not make'; and a man who swears an oath after the afternoon prayer to thereby seize the wealth of a Muslim man."],[8983,"A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about poor memory, so he said: 'Use your right hand to aid your memory.'"],[8984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate with a leper and said: 'Out of faith in Allah and trust in Him.'"],[8985,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Aktham b. al-Jawn: 'O Aktham, I saw Amr b. Luhayy b. Qama'ah dragging his intestines in the Fire, and I have never seen a man more resembling another man than you resemble him.' Aktham said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me?' He said: 'No; he is a disbeliever. He was the first to change the religion of Ishmael, so he let loose the sā'ibah, slit the ear of the bahīrah, joined the wāsilah, and protected the hāmī.'"],[8986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from discord, hypocrisy, and evil character.'"],[8987,"I have left among you two things after which you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."],[8988,"A man's being killed in retaliation is an expiation for the sins before it."],[8989,"Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughīrah, from Abd al-Azīz b. Rufay', from Abū Sālih, from Abū Hurayrah."],[8990,"Two festivals coincided during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a single day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Two festivals have coincided on this day of yours. Whoever wishes among you, it will suffice him instead of the Friday prayer, but we shall hold the Friday prayer, if Allah wills.'"],[8991,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[8992,"And the dream of a believer is one part of forty-five parts of prophethood."],[8993,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."],[8994,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Advise me.' He said, 'Do not get angry.'"],[8995,"I and the Hour were sent like these two,\" and he gestured with his forefinger and the one next to it."],[8996,"Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."],[8997,"'Amr b. Khaza'a b. Luhayy b. Qama'a b. Jundub."],[8998,"There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no Safar."],[8999,"When it is the day of fasting of one of you, let him not engage in obscenity or disobedience. If someone insults him, let him say, 'I am a fasting person.'"],[9000,"Allah cursed the Jews; fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and consumed its price."],[9001,"Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves dependents—I think he said—then they are my responsibility."],[9002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting. They said, 'But you fast continuously.' He said, 'I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord, and He feeds me and gives me drink.'"],[9003,"Wretched is the slave of the dinar, the slave of the dirham, the slave of the velvet cloth, and the slave of the striped cloak. If he is given, he is pleased; and if he is not given, he is not pleased."],[9004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have the Qur'an presented to him once every year. In the year in which he passed away, it was presented to him twice. He used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, but in the year in which he passed away, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."],[9005,"Wealth is not from abundance of goods; rather, wealth is richness of the soul."],[9006,"I am the best of partners. Whoever associates anyone else with Me, then it is entirely for that [associate]."],[9007,"People are mines like mines of gold and silver. The best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam, if they gain understanding."],[9008,"A man passed by wearing two cloaks, walking with pride, and the earth swallowed him up. He will keep sinking until the Day of Resurrection."],[9009,"The Hour will not come—or the days will not pass—until a man rules who conquers Constantinople and the mountain of Daylam."],[9010,"The days of this world will not pass until a man from me rules. Even if only one day remained of the world, Allah would lengthen that day until he conquers Constantinople and Daylam."],[9011,"The mine is waste [no compensation], and the well is waste [no compensation], and on buried treasure there is one-fifth."],[9012,"The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh: the most compassionate toward a child and the most protective of a husband concerning what is in his hand."],[9013,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: O Allah, set right for me my religion, which is the safeguard of my affairs; set right for me my worldly life, in which is my livelihood; set right for me my hereafter, to which is my return; make life an increase for me in every good; and make death a relief for me from every evil."],[9014,"The best charity is what you give while you are wealthy, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. Begin with those you support. [Your wife says: Feed me or divorce me; your child says: To whom are you leaving us?; and your servant says: Spend on me—I think he said—or sell me.]"],[9015,"Death will be brought as a ram with large eyes and made to stand between Paradise and the Fire. It will be said, 'O people of Paradise,' and they will crane their necks and look. It will be said, 'O people of the Fire,' and they will crane their necks and look. Then it will be slaughtered, and it will be said, 'Eternity, no death.'"],[9016,"The Fire complained to its Lord, saying, 'Parts of me have consumed other parts.' So He gave it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The intense heat is from its scorching breath, and the intense cold is from its bitter cold."],[9017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once delayed the 'Isha' prayer until a third of the night had passed. He came and found the people feeling softness, and they were scattered in groups and circles. He became angry and said, 'If a man were to invite the people to a bone with meat or two sheep's trotters, they would respond, yet they stay behind from this prayer. I was about to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then order those who stay behind from this prayer to be burned in their homes with fire.'"],[9018,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, raises a man in rank, and he says, 'How did I attain this?' He says, 'By your child's supplication for you.'"],[9019,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."],[9020,"Hospitality is three days; anything beyond that is charity."],[9021,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer. Faith is removed from his heart, but if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance."],[9022,"The qintar is twelve thousand uqiyyah, each uqiyyah greater than what is between heaven and earth."],[9023,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has one hundred mercies. With Him are ninety-nine, and He placed among you one mercy by which you show compassion to one another. On the Day of Resurrection, He will add it to them."],[9024,"Jesus son of Mary will descend as a just judge and a fair leader. He will break the cross, kill the pig and apes, and prostration will be one for Allah, Lord of the worlds."],[9025,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' If they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[9026,"Draw near and be steadfast."],[9027,"The intense heat is from the scorching blast of Hell, so cool down the prayer at noon during intense heat."],[9028,"They said: O Messenger of God, a man finds in himself what he would dislike to speak of, even if he had all that is in this world? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: That is pure faith."],[9029,"The Qur'an will come on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Lord, adorn him—meaning the one who recited it—so he will be clothed with a crown of honor or a garment of honor. Then it will say: O Lord, give him more, so he will be clothed with a garment of honor. Then it will say: O Lord, give him more, so he will be adorned with a garment of honor. Then it will say: O Lord, be pleased with him, and He will be pleased with him."],[9030,"And Bishr b. Adam narrated it to us: 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And we do not know this hadith to have been narrated except by 'Abd al-Samad, from Shu'bah."],[9031,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the last evening prayer one night until a third of the night had passed or nearly so. Then he came out to us while the people were in separate groups, and he became intensely angry. Then he said: If a man were to invite the people to a fatty bone and two small arrows, they would respond, and yet they hear the call. I was on the verge of ordering men to carry bundles of firewood, then going to people who do not attend the prayer and setting their homes ablaze. Then Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man, came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I am a blind man with a distant home, and I have no guide to lead me, so do you find any concession for me? He said: Does the call reach you? He said: Yes. He said: I find no concession for you."],[9032,"A woman was punished because of a cat that she tied up and neither fed nor gave water, nor left it to eat from the vermin of the earth."],[9033,"It would not please me to have the amount of gold equal to Mount Uhud, such that I die on the day I die and still have a dirham of it, except a dirham set aside for a creditor."],[9034,"Leave my companions alone, for if one of you were to spend gold equal to Mount Uhud, he would not reach a mudd of one of them, nor half of it."],[9035,"Whoever is killed by the plague is a martyr, and whoever is killed by a stomach ailment is a martyr."],[9036,"The mine is a loss without liability, the well is a loss without liability, and in buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[9037,"The Fire was kindled for a thousand years until it turned red, then it was kindled for a thousand years until it turned white, and a thousand years until it turned black, so it is black and dark."],[9038,"I saw as if I were at a well drawing water. Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two, and in his drawing there was weakness—may God forgive him. Then 'Umar came and it turned into a large bucket, and I have never seen a mighty man among the people who could do as he did."],[9039,"Whoever leaves—I think he said—wealth and does not pay its due, it will be made on the Day of Resurrection into a bald serpent with two fangs that will pursue him until he puts his hand into its mouth, and it will keep biting until judgment is concluded among the servants—meaning the reckoning among the servants is finished."],[9040,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better for him than to have it filled with poetry."],[9041,"When Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, he said: 'O Allah, You are one in the heaven and I am one on earth, worshipping You.'"],[9042,"I was granted victory by awe, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind."],[9043,"Regarding 'They will abide therein for ages,' he said: 'A hiqb is eighty years.'"],[9044,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."],[9045,"Al-Hasan b. Qaza'ah narrated to us: Sallam b. Abi Khubzah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who raised it similarly. We do not know that anyone attributed this hadith except Yazid, from Hammad b. Zayd, and Sallam b. Abi Khubzah and others, except with his chain."],[9046,"When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies."],[9047,"Do not initiate the greeting of peace with the Jews and the Christians, and when you meet them on the roads, force them to the narrowest part of it."],[9048,"I will certainly give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him, and Allah will grant victory through his hands. 'Umar said: 'I never desired leadership except on that day.' Then he called 'Ali and dispatched him, saying: 'Go and fight until Allah grants victory through your hands, and do not turn back.' He walked for a while, then stopped without turning back, and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, on what basis should I fight?' He said: 'Fight them until they say: There is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. When they do that, they protect their blood and their property from you except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.'"],[9049,"The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he reaches maturity, from the sleeping person until he wakes, and from the insane person until he regains his sanity."],[9050,"Al-'Abbas branded a camel of his on its face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Why not on a bone other than the face?' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not brand except on the last bone of it,' so he branded it on the two haunches."],[9051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us [to cover the ablution water] and to tie the waterskin and to turn over the vessel."],[9052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when one of us took to his bed, to say: O Allah, You are the Lord of the heavens and the Lord of the earth, and Lord of everything, the Splitter of the grain and the date-stone, the Sender down of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Qur'an. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every possessor of evil whom You seize by the forelock. You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and the Last, so there is nothing after You, and the Outward, so there is nothing above You, and the Inward, so there is nothing below You. Settle my debt for me and enrich me from poverty."],[9053,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Do you not see the moon on the night of the full moon, with no crowding in seeing it? We said: Yes. He said: By Allah, you will surely see Him as you see the moon on the night of the full moon."],[9054,"Fatimah, may Allah have mercy on her, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for a servant. He said: Shall I not direct you to what is better for you than that? Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times."],[9055,"When a man gets up from his seat and then returns to it, he is more entitled to it."],[9056,"For one of you to sit on a live coal until his clothes burn is better for him than to sit on a grave."],[9057,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves a servant, He calls Jibril ﷺ : I have loved so-and-so, so love him. Then Jibril, may Allah bless him, calls out in the heaven, and then love for him is sent down among the people of the earth. That is His saying: Indeed, those who believe and do righteous deeds, the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection. And when He hates a servant, He calls Jibril, may Allah bless him: I have hated so-and-so. Then he calls out among the people of the heaven, and then hatred is sent down among the people of the earth."],[9058,"None of you should leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9059,"Muhammad b. Yahya al-Qati'i narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ."],[9060,"A man came and said: I did not sleep last night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: From what? He said: A scorpion stung me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you had said when evening came: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, nothing would have harmed you."],[9061,"Excellent is the man Abu Bakr, excellent is the man 'Umar b. al-Khattab, excellent is the man Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, excellent is the man Mu'adh b. 'Amr b. al-Jamuh, excellent is the man Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas."],[9062,"Spirits are assembled troops; those of them that knew one another become harmonious, and those of them that were repelled from one another differ."],[9063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution after eating a piece of dried curd, then he was seen eating a shoulder of a sheep, then he prayed without performing ablution."],[9064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Mount Hira with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Talha, and al-Zubayr. The rock shook, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Be still, for upon you are only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.\""],[9065,"The Hour will not come until wealth increases and overflows, until a man goes out with the zakat of his wealth and finds no one to accept it from him; and until killing (al-harj) becomes widespread. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is al-harj?\" He said: \"Killing.\" And until the land of the Arabs returns to being meadows and rivers."],[9066,"Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."],[9067,"A woman should not travel for more than three [days] unless she has a mahram with her."],[9068,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ congratulated a man on his marriage, he said: \"May Allah bless you, and bless upon you, and unite you in goodness.\""],[9069,"Some women of the Ansar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we cannot come to you with the men.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your appointment is the house of so-and-so.\" He came and spoke with them, then said: \"If any of you loses three children and seeks reward for it, she will enter Paradise.\" One of the women said: \"Or two?\" He said: \"Or two.\""],[9070,"There is no servant who does not pay the zakat of his wealth except that he will be brought with his wealth, and sheets of metal will be heated for him in the fire of Hell, and his forehead, brow, and back will be branded with them, until Allah the Exalted judges between His servants on a day whose length is a thousand years of what you count. Then he will see his way: either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no servant who does not pay the charity of his camels except that he will be brought with his camels, as numerous as they ever were, and a wide flat valley will be prepared for them, and they will trample him. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first will be returned to him, until Allah the Blessed and Exalted judges between His servants. Then he will see his way: either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no servant who does not pay the charity of his sheep except that he will be brought with his sheep, as numerous as they ever were, and a wide flat valley will be prepared for them, and they will trample him. [Every time] the last of them passes over him, the first will be returned to him; they will trample him with their hooves and gore him with their horns, none of them having twisted horns or being hornless, until Allah judges between His servants on a day whose length is fifty thousand years. Then he will see his way: either to Paradise or to the Fire. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about horses?\" He said: \"Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. Horses are of three kinds: for one man they are a reward, for another a covering, and for another a burden. As for the one for whom they are a reward, he is the one who keeps them for the cause of Allah and prepares them for it. They are a reward for him; nothing disappears into their stomachs except that a reward is written for him for it. Even if he passes by a meadow or two meadows and lets them graze there, a reward is written for him for what they eat. Even if they run up a hill or two hills, a reward is written for him for every step. Even if he comes to a river and gives them water, a reward is written for him for every drop that disappears into their stomachs from it.\" Until he mentioned the reward even for their dung and urine. \"As for the one for whom they are a covering, he is the one who keeps them for dignity, beauty, and concealment, and does not withhold their right of backs and bellies in their ease or hardship. As for the one for whom they are a burden, he is the one who keeps them out of pride, arrogance, and showing off to people, and he will regret it.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about donkeys?\" He said: \"Nothing has been revealed to me about them except this comprehensive, unique verse: 'Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.'\""],[9071,"When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and morning came, he said: \"A hearer has heard the praise of Allah and His favor and His good treatment of us. Our Lord, accompany us and bestow favor upon us.\""],[9072,"Two brothers came to Madinah, and a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ had been injured in his body by an arrow. The Prophet ﷺ said to his relatives: \"Seek someone to treat him.\" The two brothers were brought, and he said to them: \"Will you treat him with iron [surgery]?\" They said: \"No, we only practiced medicine in the pre-Islamic era.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Treat him.\" So they lanced him until he recovered."],[9073,"Whoever does the deed of the people of Lot, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done."],[9074,"A man gives charity with a morsel from good earnings and puts it in its rightful place, and Allah receives it with His right hand. It does not cease until He nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal, until it becomes greater than Mount Uhud."],[9075,"Barrenness is not that you are not rained upon, but barrenness is that the sky rains and the earth does not produce vegetation."],[9076,"The Hour will not come until the sky rains such rain that neither houses of mud will shelter from it, nor will any shelter from it except houses of hair."],[9077,"Whoever takes a span of land without its right will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[9078,"Indeed, a people will come after me, one of whom would wish to ransom his family and his wealth for seeing me."],[9079,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs every day, a house will be built for him in Paradise: two before dawn, four before zuhr, two after zuhr, two before 'asr, and two after maghrib."],[9080,"Do not say, 'The people are ruined.' Whoever says, 'The people are ruined,' he is the one who ruins them."],[9081,"Do not take my grave as an idol, and do not take your houses as graves."],[9082,"Umar did not take any mountain pass except that Satan took a different pass."],[9083,"He forbade a man to wear the clothing of a woman and a woman to wear the clothing of a man."],[9084,"The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."],[9085,"Do not make your houses graves; indeed, Satan flees from the house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited."],[9086,"Whoever kills a gecko in the first blow will have such and such a good deed, and whoever kills it in the second blow will have such and such a good deed, and whoever kills it in the third blow will have such and such a good deed."],[9087,"A child cannot repay his parent unless he finds him a slave, buys him, and then frees him."],[9088,"Whoever wants to pray after Jumu'ah should pray four [rak'ahs]."],[9089,"Whoever learns archery and then forgets it has rejected a blessing."],[9090,"The expiation for a gathering is for a man to say when he rises from it: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.'"],[9091,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six [days] from Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted for a lifetime."],[9092,"Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us: 'Amr narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report."],[9093,"Whoever cheats us is not one of us."],[9094,"No people sit in a gathering and then disperse without remembering Allah, except that it is as if they have dispersed from the carcass of a donkey."],[9095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-'Abbas: 'In you are prophethood and sovereignty.'"],[9096,"The best rows of men are the first, and the worst are the last. The best rows of women are the last, and the worst are the first."],[9097,"The poor came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken the high ranks and enduring bliss.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And what is that?' They said: 'They pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have wealth with which they give charity and free slaves, while we have nothing.' He said: 'Shall I not guide you to something that, if you do it, no one before you will have surpassed you, and no one after you will catch up with you except one who does the like of what you do?' He said: 'Say \"Glory be to Allah\" thirty-three times, \"Praise be to Allah\" thirty-three times, and \"Allah is greatest\" thirty-four times after every prayer.' They did so. This reached the wealthy, and they did the same as the poor had said. The poor returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have done what you commanded us, and they are doing what we do.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is the bounty of Allah, which He gives to whom He wills.'"],[9098,"When one of you sees someone in affliction, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah who has spared me from what He has afflicted you with and has favored me over many of those He created.' If he says that, it will be gratitude for that blessing."],[9099,"The Euphrates will recede from a mountain of gold, and the people will fight over it. Out of every hundred, ninety-nine will be killed."],[9100,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, addressed this western sea and addressed the eastern sea. He said to the western sea, 'I will carry in you servants of Mine, so how will you deal with them?' It said, 'I will drown them.' He said, 'Your might is in your regions'; He deprived it of adornment and game. And He addressed this eastern sea, saying, 'I will carry in you servants of Mine, so how will you deal with them?' It said, 'I will carry them on my hand; I will be like a mother to her child.' So He rewarded it with adornment and game."],[9101,"A woman must not travel for more than three days except with someone who is forbidden to her (i.e., a mahram)."],[9102,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, continues to aid a person as long as the person continues to aid his brother."],[9103,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him put on the right one before the left, then remove the left one before the right, so that the right one is the first to be put on and the last to be removed."],[9104,"Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning; their faces will be like the light of the moon on the night of the full moon. 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me one of them.' He said, 'You are one of them.' Then a man from the Muhajirun, from their best, stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me one of them.' He said, 'Ukkasha has preceded you to it.'"],[9105,"No one endures the hardship of Madinah – I think he said – and its severity, except that I will be an intercessor for him – or a witness – on the Day of Resurrection."],[9106,"No competition for a prize is allowed except in (racing) camels, horses, or arrows."],[9107,"Abbad b. Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah ؓ , from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9108,"No Muslim performs ablution for prayer and washes his face except that with the water – or with the drops of water – every sin his eyes committed is scattered. He does not rinse his mouth except that with every drop of water every sin his tongue uttered is scattered. He does not sniff water into his nose except that with every drop of water every sin whose smell he detected is scattered – or comes out. He does not wash his hands except that with every drop of water every sin his hands committed is come out. He does not wash any part of his feet except that with every drop of water every sin his feet walked toward comes out. Then when he goes out to the mosque, for every step he takes a good deed is written for him and a sin is erased, until he reaches his place."],[9109,"Your oath is according to what your companion believes you to be swearing about."],[9110,"The angels take turns among you: angels at night and angels by day, and they meet at the Fajr prayer and the 'Asr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He – though He knows best – Blessed and Exalted asks them, 'How did you leave My servants?' They say, 'We left them praying, and we came to them praying.' Then those who remained with you during the day ascend to Him, and He asks them – though He knows best about you – 'How did you leave My servants?' They say, 'We left them praying, and we came to them praying.'"],[9111,"Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest of speech. Do not spy, do not compete with one another, do not hate one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. Be servants of Allah as brothers."],[9112,"The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in the place where he prayed, so long as he does not invalidate his ablution, saying: 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'"],[9113,"While a man was driving a garlanded sacrificial camel, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to him: 'Ride it.' He said: 'It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah!' He said: 'Woe to you, ride it.' He said: 'It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah!' He said: 'Woe to you, ride it.'"],[9114,"Fasting is a shield. When one of you is fasting on a day, he should not engage in obscene speech or act foolishly. If someone fights him or insults him, let him say: 'I am fasting.'"],[9115,"A prophet among the prophets camped under a tree and an ant bit him. He returned and ordered his baggage to be moved out from under it, then ordered the ant colony to be burned with fire. Allah Almighty revealed to him: 'Why not just one ant?'"],[9116,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."],[9117,"Every good deed that the son of Adam does is multiplied ten times to seven hundred times - or up to seven hundredfold. Allah says: 'Fasting is for Me, and I reward it. The fasting person gives up his food, drink, and desire for My sake. Fasting is for Me, and I shall reward it.' Fasting is a shield. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he meets his Lord. The change in the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk."],[9118,"How much of the month has passed? We said: 'Twenty-two days and eight remain.' He said: 'No, rather twenty-two have passed and seven remain. Seek it tonight.' Then he said: 'The month is twenty-nine.'"],[9119,"The Night of Decree was mentioned - or we mentioned it - in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'How much of the month has passed?' We said: 'Twenty-two have passed and eight remain.' He said: 'No, rather seven remain.' We said: 'No, indeed eight remain.' He said: 'No, rather seven remain; the month is twenty-nine.'"],[9120,"Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever makes things easy for one in hardship, Allah will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter. Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother. Whoever follows a path seeking knowledge, Allah will make easy for him a path to Paradise. No people gather in a house from the houses of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves, except that tranquility descends upon them, mercy envelops them, and Allah mentions them to those with Him. Whoever is slowed by his deeds will not be hastened by his lineage."],[9121,"Whoever conceals his Muslim brother, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever relieves his brother of a distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the Hereafter. Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother."],[9122,"And whoever forgives a Muslim, Allah will forgive his slip on the Day of Resurrection."],[9123,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."],[9124,"Look at those who are below you, and do not look at those who are above you, for it is more likely that you will not belittle the favor of your Lord upon you."],[9125,"No wealth has benefited us as the wealth of Abu Bakr has benefited us."],[9126,"Seek refuge in God from the punishment of the grave. Seek refuge in God from the trial of life and death. Seek refuge from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[9127,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but God.' When they say, 'There is no god but God,' they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is with God Almighty."],[9128,"When a slave fulfills the right of God and the right of his masters, he will have two rewards."],[9129,"And Yusuf b. Musa narrated it to us: Jarir b. 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration."],[9130,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us: Jarir b. 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9131,"War spoils were not lawful for any people with black heads before you. A fire used to come from the sky and consume them. When the day of Badr came, he said: The people hastened to take the spoils, so God sent down: 'Had it not been for a previous ordinance from God, a severe punishment would have touched you for what you took.'"],[9132,"Every prophet has an answered supplication, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection. Every prophet hastened to use his supplication, and it is attainable, if God wills, for whoever dies not associating anything with God."],[9133,"The best charity is that which leaves one rich, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. Your wife says: 'Spend on me or divorce me.' Your slave says: 'Spend on me or sell me.' Your child says: 'To whom will you entrust me?'"],[9134,"I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me to himself, I remember him to Myself; and if he remembers Me in an assembly, I remember him in an assembly better than them."],[9135,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. Recite, if you wish: 'And no soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes as reward for what they used to do.'"],[9136,"The imam is responsible, and the muezzin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[9137,"The imam is responsible, and the muezzin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[9138,"I was told from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah. Nafi' b. Sulayman narrated this hadith from Muhammad b. Abi Salih, from his father, from 'A'ishah."],[9139,"Indeed, Allah has angels who are extra beyond the recorders of people's deeds; they roam about in remembrance—or on the earth—and seek out the people of remembrance. When they find a group remembering Allah, they call to one another: 'Come to what you seek!' Then they surround them with their wings up to the lowest heaven. He said: Then their Lord asks them, though He knows best: 'What are My servants saying?' They say: 'They praise You, glorify You, and extol You.' Then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'How would it be if they saw Me?' They say: 'If they saw You, they would be more intense in worship, more intense in praise, and more frequent in glorifying You.' Then He, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'What do they ask for?' He said: They say: 'They ask You for Paradise.' He said: Then He, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Have they seen it?' They say: 'No, by Allah, they have not seen it.' He said: Then He says: 'How would it be if they saw it?' He said: They say: 'They would be more eager for it, more earnest in seeking it, and greater in desire for it.' He said: Then He says: 'From what do they seek refuge?' He said: They say: 'From the Fire.' He said: Then He, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Have they seen it?' He said: They say: 'No, by Allah, they have not seen it.' He said: Then He says: 'How would it be if they saw it?' He said: They say: 'If they saw it, they would flee from it more intensely, run from it more vigorously, and fear it more greatly.' He said: Then He, Blessed and Exalted, says: 'I call you to witness that I have forgiven them.' He said: Then one of the angels says: 'Among them is so-and-so, who is not one of them; he only came for some need.' He said: 'They are the companions; their companion will not be wretched.'"],[9140,"'Amr b. 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah—or Abu Sa'id—from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9141,"Indeed, Allah has angels who travel about the earth. When they find a group remembering Allah, they call out: 'Come to what you seek!'"],[9142,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9143,"My likeness among the prophets before me is that of a house built by a man who perfected its construction, leaving in it a single brick. People would come and look at it, saying: 'How excellent this house is, if only that brick were put in place!' And I am that brick."],[9144,"There is none among you who will enter the Fire except that a man from the people of Paradise will inherit his abode. That is His saying: 'Those are the inheritors.'"],[9145,"Any believer whom I have cursed or flogged, make it for him a purification and a mercy."],[9146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed continuous fasting, and the people learned of it and also fasted continuously. He said: 'I am not like you; I remain with my Lord, and my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.'"],[9147,"Whoever performs wudu and perfects the wudu, then comes to the Friday prayer, remains silent, and listens, will be forgiven what is between that and the next Friday, plus three extra days. And whoever says, “Be quiet,” has engaged in idle talk."],[9148,"The first group of my ummah to enter Paradise will be in the form of the full moon. Then those who follow them will be like the brightest shining star in the sky. Then after that they will be in ranks. They will not cauterize themselves, nor seek ruqyah. Their combs will be of gold, their censers will be of aloeswood, their sweat will be musk, and their character will be like that of a single man. The stature of each of them will be sixty cubits."],[9149,"Adhere to what is right, draw near, and receive glad tidings, for no one’s deeds will save him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, not even you?” He said, “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy and grace from Him.”"],[9150,"Indeed the worst of people in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the two-faced one."],[9151,"You will find the worst of Allah’s servants on the Day of Resurrection to be the two-faced one, who comes to these with one kind of talk and comes to those with another kind of talk."],[9152,"None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts a day before it or a day after it."],[9153,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They have the softest hearts, and disbelief is from the direction of the east."],[9154,"Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."],[9155,"When one of you leads the people in prayer, he should keep it light, for among them are the old, the weak, and those with needs."],[9156,"There are three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment: a man who has surplus water on a road in a desert and withholds it from the wayfarer; a man who pledges allegiance to a leader only for worldly gain—if he gives him, he fulfills, and if he does not give him, he does not fulfill; and the one who associates partners with Allah."],[9157,"When the son of Adam recites the sajdah, the Satan withdraws and weeps, saying: “Woe to him! The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, so Paradise is his. I was commanded to prostrate and I disobeyed, so the Fire is mine.”"],[9158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—and a funeral procession passed by him, so he said: “How much did he leave behind?” They said, “Two dinars.” He said, “Two marks of cautery.” He said: So whenever a funeral procession passed by him, he would say, “Does he owe a debt?” If they said, “Yes,” he would say, “Did he leave enough to pay it?” If they said, “Yes,” he would pray over him, and if they said, “No,” he would not pray over him."],[9159,"I would not love for anyone to turn into gold for me such that I would have any of it after three days, except something I set aside for a debt. Indeed, those who have more are the ones who have less on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who says: like this, and like this, and like this — and how few they are — to his right, to his left, in front of him, and behind him."],[9160,"When Satan hears the call to prayer, he passes wind with a sound so that he does not hear its voice. When it stops, he returns to whisper. When he hears the iqamah, he goes away so that he does not hear its voice. When it stops, he returns and whispers."],[9161,"When one of you is fasting, he should not use obscene language or act foolishly. If someone insults him, let him say: 'I am fasting.'"],[9162,"When one of you gets up at night, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[9163,"There is no newborn except that he is born upon the fitrah, until his tongue becomes clear about him. Then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[9164,"Leave me as long as I leave you. Those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning and their disagreeing with their prophets."],[9165,"That I say: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest' is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon."],[9166,"Between the two blowings of the trumpet is forty."],[9167,"Amr b. Ali narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9168,"Whoever kills himself with a piece of iron, his piece of iron will be in his hand, stabbing himself with it in his belly in the fire of Hell, remaining therein forever, eternally. Whoever poisons himself, his poison will be in his hand, sipping it in the fire of Hell, remaining therein forever, eternally. Whoever throws himself from a mountain, he will be throwing himself in the fire of Hell, remaining therein forever, eternally."],[9169,"Allah has cursed the thief who steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and he steals a rope and his hand is cut off."],[9170,"Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Habib b. al-Shahid narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ similar to it. We do not know anyone who related this hadith with this wording except al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah. Some scholars have interpreted that the egg is the iron helmet made for war that is placed on the head as protection, and that the rope is a rope that Bedouins have, which they call risha'. Each of these two is worth more than a quarter of a dinar. Even if the wording is general, this is its meaning, and Allah knows best."],[9171,"You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something which if you do, you will love one another? Spread salam among yourselves."],[9172,"Shaytan ties three knots on the back of the head of any one of you when he sleeps. If he gets up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone; if he gets up and performs wudu, one knot is undone; and if he gets up to pray, all his knots are undone. So he becomes active and good in spirit. But if he wakes up without doing that, he becomes lazy and bad in spirit, having attained no good."],[9173,"The prayer in congregation is twenty-five times better than the prayer of a man alone."],[9174,"The smell from the mouth of a fasting person is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And every deed of the son of Adam is for him, except fasting, for it is for Me and I shall reward for it."],[9175,"Do not rush ahead of your imam in bowing or prostration. When he says the takbir, then say the takbir; and when he says, 'not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray' (i.e., the end of al-Fatihah), then say, 'Amin,' for whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven. And when he says, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' then say, 'O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise'."],[9176,"Whoever has his two beloved ones (i.e., eyes) taken away and is patient and seeks reward, I will not be content for him with any reward less than Paradise."],[9177,"Qamir b. Muhammad b. 'Umayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. As for the hadith of al-Thawri, we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except 'Abd al-Razzaq; this hadith was only known from the hadith of Jarir and Abu al-Ahwas, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: What do you say in prayer? He said: I bear witness (tashahhud) and remember Allah, then I say: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek refuge with You from the Fire. As for me, by Allah, I am not good at your murmuring nor the murmuring of Mu'adh! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is around them that Mu'adh and I murmur."],[9179,"The surplus of water should not be withheld to prevent the growth of herbage."],[9180,"He used to observe continuous fasting from before dawn to before dawn."],[9181,"Adam and Musa argued. Musa said to Adam: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit; you brought us out—or you brought your offspring out—of Paradise. He said: So Adam argued against Musa and won the argument."],[9182,"9192 9190 - 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah—or Abu Sa'id."],[9183,"When the expedition of Tabuk took place, the people suffered from hunger. They said: O Messenger of God, if only you would permit us to slaughter our camels used for carrying water, so we could eat and use their fat. He said: Do it. Then Umar came and said: O Messenger of God, if you do that, the riding animals will become few. But invite them to bring their surplus provisions, then pray to God for blessing over them; perhaps God will place in that—I think he said—good. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a leather mat, then invited them to bring their surplus provisions. A man would come with a handful of millet, another with a handful of dates, and another with a piece of bread, until it gathered on the mat. The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for blessing for them, and they did not leave any container in the army except that they filled it, and they ate and were satiated. And a surplus remained. The Prophet ﷺ then said: I bear witness that there is no god but God. No servant will meet God with it and be veiled from Paradise."],[9184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray until his feet became swollen. It was said to him about that, and he said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[9185,"My uncle Yahya b. Isa narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[9186,"He used to pray until his feet became swollen. It was said to him: Do you do that when God has forgiven you? He said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[9187,"When God created the creation, He wrote a book and placed it under the Throne: My mercy precedes My wrath."],[9188,"If one of you goes to his wife and hastens and fails to ejaculate, then no bathing is required."],[9189,"None of you will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: Not even me, unless God envelops me with mercy and grace from Him. And if He were to take me and Isa to account for what these two have earned, He would destroy us—and he pointed with his index and middle fingers."],[9190,"Everything of the son of Adam decays except the coccyx."],[9191,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw Sa'd supplicating with his two fingers and said: One, one."],[9192,"A human being has three hundred and sixty bones—or three hundred and sixty joints—upon him each day is charity. They said: O Messenger of God, what about one who cannot find anything? He said: He should enjoin good or forbid evil. They said: What about one who cannot? He said: Let him remove a bone from the road. They said: What about one who cannot? He said: Let him guide someone on a path. He said: What about one who cannot do that? Let him help a weak person. They said: What about one who cannot do that? He said: Let him refrain from harming people."],[9193,"Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine."],[9194,"There is no servant except that he has a reputation in the heaven. If his reputation in the heaven is good, it is placed on the earth; and if his reputation is bad, it is placed on the earth."],[9195,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry."],[9196,"Will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes. Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun and the moon? They said: No. He said: Then you will have no difficulty in seeing Him—or no disagreement about seeing Him—just as you have no difficulty—or no disagreement—in seeing them."],[9197,"I was only sent as a guided mercy."],[9198,"I was determined to order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then I would go with men carrying bundles of firewood to a people who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses down upon them."],[9199,"I was determined to order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then I would go with men carrying candles to a people who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses down upon them."],[9200,"Do not curse time, for God is time."],[9201,"Whoever prays over a funeral receives a carat, and whoever waits until it is buried receives two carats."],[9202,"Prayer has a first and a last time. The first time of the noon prayer is when the sun declines, and its last time is when the time of the afternoon prayer enters. The first time of the afternoon prayer is when its time enters, and its last time is when the sun turns yellow. The first time of the sunset prayer is when the sun sets, and its last time is when the twilight disappears. The first time of the evening prayer is when its time enters, and its last time is when half the night passes. The first time of the dawn prayer is when dawn breaks, and its last time is when the sun rises."],[9203,"Madinah is a sanctuary between its two lava fields. Whoever introduces an innovation in it, or gives shelter to an innovator, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[9204,"God, Mighty and Majestic, will say to His servant on the Day of Resurrection: Did I not carry you on horses and camels, and marry you to women, and make you a leader and a chief? Did you think that you would meet this day of yours? He will say: No. Then He will say: Today I forget you as you forgot Me."],[9205,"Do not race your imam in bowing or prostrating. When he says the takbir, say the takbir. When he says, 'not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray,' say: Amen. For whoever's Amen coincides with the angels' Amen, his previous sins are forgiven. And when he says, 'God hears the one who praises Him,' say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise."],[9206,"Regarding the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'And the recitation of dawn, indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed.' He said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day attend it."],[9207,"When he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, he would lie down on his right side."],[9208,"The prayer of one of you in congregation exceeds his prayer in his house and in his market by twenty-seven prayers. That is because when one of you performs ablution and does it well, then goes out to the prayer intending nothing but the prayer, nothing else driving him, a degree is raised for him with every step he takes and a sin is removed from him, until he enters the mosque. When he enters the mosque, he is in prayer as long as the prayer keeps him there, and the angels say: O Allah, send blessings upon him; O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, as long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[9209,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so prays at night, but when morning comes he steals. He said: What you say will soon stop him."],[9210,"I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. If he draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length. If he draws near to Me an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom. If he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."],[9211,"Whoever has one hundred Muslims pray over him will be forgiven."],[9212,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us finds within himself something that he would dislike to speak of, or that falling from the sky would be dearer to him than speaking of it. He said: That is pure faith."],[9213,"Shu'bah said: And 'Asim narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[9214,"A man should not outbid his brother, nor should he propose to a woman to whom his brother has proposed."],[9215,"The pledged animal may be ridden and milked."],[9216,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And We make some of them to excel others in produce' [Quran 13:4], he said: The sweet, the sour, and the unripe."],[9217,"Ubayd Allah b. Usamah Abu Usamah narrated to us: Sulayman b. Ayyub narrated to us: Ubayd Allah b. Amr narrated to us, from Zayd b. Abi Unaysah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This statement we do not know anyone narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah except Sayf b. Muhammad, and he is not strong. And the hadith of Zayd b. Abi Unaysah we do not know anyone narrated it except Sulayman b. Ayyub, from Ubayd Allah b. Amr."],[9218,"Muhammad b. Abd Allah al-Mukharrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us: Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9219,"Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something happens to him, let him blame no one but himself."],[9220,"If the one who drinks while standing knew what is upon him, he would induce vomiting."],[9221,"Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah except Ma'mar."],[9222,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about something. He went inside to look for something for him, and he found a morsel in one of his rooms. He brought it out and broke it into pieces, then placed his hand over it, then said, \"Eat, O bedouin.\" The bedouin ate and some of it remained. The bedouin kept raising his head, looking at him and saying, \"You are indeed a righteous man.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Embrace Islam,\" but he kept refusing Islam and saying, \"You are indeed a righteous man.\""],[9223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said, \"Which day is this?\" They said, \"A sacred day.\" He said, \"Indeed your blood and your wealth are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours.\""],[9224,"He saw a man gesturing with his two fingers, so he said, \"One, one.\""],[9225,"The molar of the disbeliever is like (Mount) Uhud, and the thickness of his skin is forty cubits."],[9226,"I was brought the keys of the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while you are extracting them or taking them out."],[9227,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran, and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a neighbor of his hears him and says, \"If only I had been given the like of what so-and-so was given, I would do with it the like of what he does.\" And a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it in truth, and a man says, \"If only I had been given the like of what so-and-so was given, I would do with it the like of what he does.\""],[9228,"Would any of you love, when he returns to his family, to find three large, fat pregnant camels?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then three verses that you recite are better for him than three large, fat pregnant camels.\""],[9229,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was praying, and a man entered upon me and saw me, and it pleased me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have two rewards: the reward of the secret and the reward of the open.\""],[9230,"Ibrahim b. al-Mustamirr al-'Uruqi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bakkar b. Bilal narrated to us: Sa'id b. Bashir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know of this statement being narrated from the hadith of al-A'mash except through the narration of Abu Waki' and Sa'id b. Bashir."],[9231,"I will tell you about people's affairs and their differences: A man who is quick to anger and quick to relent — there is nothing against him nor for him; it is even (a wash). A man who is slow to anger and quick to be pleased — that is for him and not against him. A man who is quick to anger and slow to be pleased — that is against him and not for him. A man who collects what is owed to him and pays what he owes — that is neither for him nor against him. A man who collects what is owed to him but delays paying people what is owed to them — that is against him and not for him."],[9232,"Whoever Allah gives wealth but he does not pay its zakah, it will be made into a bald-headed poisonous snake on the Day of Resurrection with two black spots over its eyes; it will seize him by his jaw and say, 'I am your treasure.' Then he recited: 'And let not those who are stingy...' the verse."],[9233,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer — and repentance is still open afterward."],[9234,"He disliked a man putting on his sandals while standing."],[9235,"The ruin of my ummah will be at the hands of young foolish men from Quraysh."],[9236,"The likeness of the five prayers is that of a river flowing at the door of one of you in which he bathes five times every day; what dirt would remain on him?"],[9237,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed by which I may enter Paradise.' He said, 'Do not get angry.' Another came and said, 'When will I know that I am doing good?' He said, 'When your neighbors say you are doing good, then you are doing good; and if they say you are doing evil, then you are doing evil.'"],[9238,"Wudu is required from whatever fire has cooked."],[9239,"Fatimah ؓ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for a servant, and he said, 'Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than a servant?'"],[9240,"Do not call grapes 'karm,' for the true karm (generous one) is the Muslim."],[9241,"The intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell, so cool down the Zuhr prayer during intense heat."],[9242,"When he wore a shirt, he began with his right side."],[9243,"'Umar b. al-Khattab narrated to us. 'Amr b. Khalid narrated to us. Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith has been narrated by more than one, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf. And 'Abd al-Samad traced it back as marfu' from Shu'bah, and Zuhayr followed him in raising it."],[9244,"When it is the first night of the month of Ramadan, the gates of Paradise are opened and the devils are chained. And indeed Allah has those whom He frees [from the Fire] at every breaking of the fast."],[9245,"Indeed Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[9246,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the morning prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of the 'asr prayer - or two rak'ahs - before the sun sets has caught it."],[9247,"Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound in the same condition as it was on the day he received it: its color is the color of blood and its smell is the smell of musk."],[9248,"Until one of them turns around and a shin is uncovered, and they fall down in prostration. And the spines of the hypocrites are fused together until they become a single bone, as if they were the horns of cattle."],[9249,"The poor believers will enter Paradise before their rich ones by five hundred years, or he said: by half a day."],[9250,"O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your ummah whom you have not seen? He said: They will have white marks from the traces of ablution."],[9251,"You will fight people with broad faces and small eyes, as if their faces were hammered shields and as if their eyes were locusts' eyes. They will wear sandals of hair, carry shields, and tie their horses to palm trees."],[9252,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a dark night, and al-Hasan and al-Husayn were with him. Lightning flashed, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Go back to your mother."],[9253,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[9254,"Do not prevent women from [going to] the mosques."],[9255,"People are minerals; the best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam, if they acquire understanding."],[9256,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[9257,"Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they are averse to him, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection."],[9258,"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you have left us competing over the adhan after you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: After me—or after you—there will be a people whose lowliest are their mu'adhdhins."],[9259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the food of two who vie in boasting."],[9260,"When it is the night of the middle of Sha'ban, Allah forgives His servants, except for a polytheist or one harboring malice."],[9261,"The gates of Paradise and the gates of heaven are opened every Thursday evening, and deeds are presented therein, and Allah forgives therein every servant except a polytheist or a servant between whom and his brother there is enmity."],[9262,"He looked at the sun at its setting on the edges of palm branches and said: What remains of your day compared to what has passed of it? He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, what remains? He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, what remains of this world compared to what has passed is only like what remains of your day compared to what has passed of it."],[9263,"Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours, but he is content with you in trivial matters."],[9264,"Whoever invites you to food, respond to him; whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge in Allah, grant him refuge; whoever does you a good turn, repay him. If you cannot repay him, supplicate for him until he knows that you have repaid him."],[9265,"Prayer is three thirds: purification is a third, bowing is a third, and prostration is a third. Whoever performs it with its due right, it is accepted from him and the rest of his deeds are accepted from him. Whoever has his prayer rejected, the rest of his deeds are rejected."],[9266,"The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer and the Asr prayer. They gather at the Fajr prayer: the angels of the night ascend and the angels of the day remain. They gather at the Asr prayer: the angels of the day ascend and the angels of the night remain. Their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, asks them: How did you leave My servants? They say: Our Lord, we came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying, so forgive them on the Day of Judgment."],[9267,"Indeed, the heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are the 'Isha' prayer and the Fajr prayer. If they knew what those two contained, they would come to them even if they had to crawl. And if one of you knew that when he comes to it he would find a marrow bone from a plump sheep or two fine arrow shafts, you would all come to it. I was about to order that the prayer be established and order a man to lead the people in prayer, then order bundles of firewood and burn down the houses of men who did not attend the prayer today."],[9268,"I would not love to have the whole of Mount Uhud in gold, such that after three days there would remain any of it with me except something I set aside for a debt. Indeed, those with the most are the ones with the least on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says with it like this and like this and like this—and few are they—to his right, to his left, in front of him, and behind him."],[9269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never criticized any food. When it was brought to him, if he desired it he ate it, and if he disliked it he remained silent."],[9270,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog, the earnings of a cupper, and the dowry of an adulteress."],[9271,"And it was narrated to him by Yusuf b. Musa: he said, narrated to us Waki', from Waki', from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar to it."],[9272,"Narrated to us 'Amr b. 'Ali: he said, narrated to us Yahya, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah."],[9273,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[9274,"There is no charity except from one who has surplus wealth. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. And begin with those you support."],[9275,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, created one hundred mercies. From them He made one mercy and distributed it among His creation, and He withheld ninety-nine until the Day of Resurrection."],[9276,"What was made clear to us, we make clear to you; and what was concealed from us, we conceal from you—meaning in the recitation during the prayer."],[9277,"The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer—I think he said—nor does one seize a plunder of great value while he is a believer."],[9278,"It was prohibited to earn the wages of a cupper, the dowry of an adulteress, and the price of a dog."],[9279,"A killer does not kill while he is a believer, and an adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and a thief does not steal while he is a believer, and a drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer, and one does not snatch a thing by stealth while he is a believer. Faith is stripped from him as his garment is stripped off. When he returns to faith, it returns to him, and when he returns, faith returns to him."],[9280,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times, three times."],[9281,"Muhammad b. 'Uthman b. Karamah narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us: Harun al-Thaqafi, known as al-Barbari, said: 'Ata' narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah."],[9282,"9292 9290 - And 'Abd Allah b. Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Habib b. al-Shahid narrated to us, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah."],[9283,"And 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Abu Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah."],[9284,"What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made us hear, we made you hear; and what he concealed from us, we concealed from you."],[9285,"When you are an imam, keep it light, for among the people are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Make the prayer cool, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell.'"],[9286,"The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast."],[9287,"And this hadith 9297 was narrated to us by Muhammad b. al-Muthanna: Mu'adh b. Mu'adh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf. 'Abd al-Malik b. Abi Sulayman also narrated it from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf. We know of no one who attributed it to the Prophet from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, except Dawud b. 'Abd al-Rahman. In fact, there is disagreement from 'Ata': Ibn Jurayj and 'Abd al-Malik narrated it from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah; Fitr narrated it from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas - thus Qabisah narrated it, and other than Qabisah sent it as mursal. Layth narrated it from 'Ata', from 'A'ishah, and from 'Ata', from 'Urwah b. 'Iyad, from 'A'ishah."],[9288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade trailing one's garment (in pride)."],[9289,"And 'Abd al-'Aziz b. al-Mukhtar, from 'Isl b. Sufyan, said: 'Ata' narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'The Pleiades has never risen while there was any affliction on earth except that it was lifted.'"],[9290,"Whoever is asked about knowledge he has and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[9291,"Muhammad b. al-Layth narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Bishr narrated to us: al-Hakam b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9292,"Muhammad b. al-Layth narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sadaqah b. Musa narrated to us, from Malik b. Dinar, from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9293,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire."],[9294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered the people and said: O people, repent to Allah, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day."],[9295,"Indeed, on Friday there is an hour during which no Muslim servant asks Allah, blessed and exalted is He, for anything good but that He grants it to him."],[9296,"Allah has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down a cure for it."],[9297,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I saw in a dream as if my head was struck, and I saw it in this hand of mine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Satan mocks one of you, then he goes about relating it."],[9298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade letting one's garment hang down and that a man cover his mouth during prayer."],[9299,"Charity is from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those whom you support."],[9300,"Indeed, I hear the cry of a child while I am praying, so I shorten it, fearing that his mother would be distressed."],[9301,"Do not anticipate the month; fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it — I think he said: — and if it is obscured from you, then complete the number."],[9302,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: the earth was made a means of purification and a place of prayer for me; I was granted victory through awe over the enemy from a distance of a month's journey; war booty was made lawful for me, and it was not lawful for anyone before me; I was sent to the red and the black, and no prophet was sent except to his own people; and there was no prophet but was given a gift that he hastened to receive, but I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation."],[9303,"When you are an imam, measure the people by their weakest, for among them are the old, the young, the sick, and the one with a need. But when you pray for yourself, lengthen as much as you are able."],[9304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, may God have mercy on him: \"Will you not graze in a meadow of the meadows of Paradise and find rest there?\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is grazing?\" He said, \"Alhamdu lillah, subhan Allah, la ilaha illa Allah, and Allahu akbar.\" Salman said, \"Everything has a planting, so what is the planting of Paradise?\" He said, \"Subhan Allah, alhamdu lillah, la ilaha illa Allah, and Allahu akbar.\""],[9305,"Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of God will have it as light on the Day of Resurrection."],[9306,"Indeed, everything has a heart, and the heart of the Quran is Ya-Sin."],[9307,"While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting with Abu Bakr ؓ, Ibn Mas'ud, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Nu'aym b. Salama, a courier came to the Prophet ﷺ from an expedition he had sent. Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of God, I have never seen an expedition return more quickly or with more spoils than these.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Abu Bakr, shall I direct you to what returns faster and has greater spoils? One who prays the morning prayer in congregation, then remembers God until the sun rises.\""],[9308,"O Abu Hurayrah, visit rarely and you will increase in love."],[9309,"Indeed, God, blessed and exalted, has given you at the time of your death a third of your wealth as an increase in your good deeds."],[9310,"Indeed, I hear the cry of a child and I lighten the prayer for fear that his mother may be put to trial."],[9311,"When you are an imam, measure the people by their weakest; and when you are the imam of yourself, then you and that matter."],[9312,"You will never encompass the people with your wealth, but your cheerfulness of face and good character will encompass them."],[9313,"Illicit gain is the earnings of a cupper, the fee of a prostitute, and the price of a dog."],[9314,"Abd Allah b. Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya b. Hammad narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Qays b. Sa'd, from Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, similarly or close to it."],[9315,"Shall I not inform you of the best among you? They said: Yes indeed. He said: The best among you are those who have the best character."],[9316,"Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of God, brothers."],[9317,"Glorifying God is for men and clapping is for women."],[9318,"Khallad b. Aslam narrated to us: al-Nadr b. Shumayl informed us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Qays b. Sa'd, from Ata', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9319,"He forbade the earnings of a cupper, the dower of a prostitute, and the price of a dog."],[9320,"In every prayer there is recitation. Whatever the Messenger of God ﷺ made us hear, we made you hear; and whatever he did not make us hear, we did not make you hear."],[9321,"And Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah, from Ata', from Abu Hurayrah."],[9322,"In every prayer there is recitation. Whatever the Prophet ﷺ made us hear, we made you hear; and whatever he kept silent from us, we kept silent from you."],[9323,"When one of you cleanses himself with stones, let him use an odd number; indeed God is odd and loves the odd. Do you not see that the heavens are seven, the earths are seven, the days are seven, and the circumambulation is seven? And he mentioned other things."],[9324,"I saw Abu Hurayrah say the takbir when he raised and when he lowered, and he reported that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do that."],[9325,"Indeed when the servant stands for prayer, he is—I think he said—before the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted. When he turns away, the Blessed and Exalted says: To whom do you turn? To something better than Me? Come forward, O son of Adam, to Me, for I am better than what you turn to."],[9326,"Whoever swears an oath and says \"God willing\" does not break his oath."],[9327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. . ."],[9328,"Indeed Sulayman said: “I will certainly go around tonight to a hundred women, each woman giving birth to a boy who will fight in the path of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Had he said: ‘If Allah wills,’ each woman among them would have given birth to a boy who fights in the path of Allah. And no child was born to him except from one woman, who gave birth to half a boy or part of a boy.”"],[9329,"The best women who have ridden camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most careful of a husband regarding what he possesses."],[9330,"Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest of speech."],[9331,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This hadith has been reported from Abu Hurayrah through more than one route, and we do not know of it being reported from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, except through these two routes."],[9332,"If I were at the Red Sandhill, I would show you the grave of Musa ﷺ ."],[9333,"Today a gap has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this — and he formed ninety with his fingers."],[9334,"The two eyes commit adultery and the two hands commit adultery. Or he said: The adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the hand is seizing, and the private part confirms that or denies it."],[9335,"Delay the Zuhr prayer in severe heat, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[9336,"On buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[9337,"Every Muslim must perform ghusl once every seven days, and that is on Friday."],[9338,"Muhammad b. Miskin narrated to us, Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid b. Yazid, from Sa'id b. Abi Hilal, from Aban b. Salih, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar or close to it."],[9339,"Adam and Moses argued. Moses said: 'You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit. You brought us out of Paradise — or you brought out your progeny.' Adam said: 'And you are Moses whom Allah chose with His messages and with His speech. Do you find that written against me before I was created?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So Adam defeated Moses in argument.'"],[9340,"Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition, and his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[9341,"Allah, blessed and exalted, taught Jesus ﷺ his argument."],[9342,"Every Muslim must perform a full-body washing every seven days, and that is the day of Friday."],[9343,"Allah led astray from Friday those who were before us, and Allah guided us to it. People are followers of us: the Jews have Saturday and the Christians have Sunday."],[9344,"People will be gathered — and sometimes he said: People will be resurrected — upon their intentions."],[9345,"He used to say the takbir whenever he lowered and raised, and he said: 'I am the most knowledgeable of you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[9346,"Whoever is killed in a blind fight with a stone or a stick, it is a mistake, and its blood-money is the blood-money of a mistake. Whoever is killed deliberately, then it is retaliation. Whoever prevents that, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath; neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him."],[9347,"Do not go out to meet the caravans, and a town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller. Whoever buys a camel or sheep that has been left unmilked, he has the option to return it and a saa' of food."],[9348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat by the Kaaba, drew up his legs, and wrapped his arms around them."],[9349,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, war booty was made lawful for me, the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification, I was aided with awe — I think he said — and I was given the comprehensive words."],[9350,"Gabriel kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought that he would make him an heir."],[9351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the foul medicine."],[9352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade (the use of) gourds, green jars, and vessels smeared with pitch."],[9353,"He forbade (the use of) gourds, green jars, and vessels smeared with pitch."],[9354,"Do not go out to meet the caravans (to buy goods), and a town-dweller should not sell on behalf of a desert-dweller."],[9355,"A servant does not (truly) believe until his neighbor is safe from his harm. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves the self-sufficient, forbearing, chaste person, and hates the foul-mouthed, wicked, persistent beggar."],[9356,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[9357,"If the slave-woman of any of you commits adultery, he should flog her. Then if she commits adultery (again), he should flog her. Then if she commits adultery a third or fourth time, he should sell her even for a rope of hair."],[9358,"Indeed, on Friday there is an hour in which no servant asks Allah for good but that He grants it to him."],[9359,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in (Surah) 'When the sky is split asunder' (al-Inshiqaq)."],[9360,"Any woman who perfumes herself and goes to the mosque to pray in it—Allah will not accept her prayer until she washes it off as she washes after major ritual impurity."],[9361,"Among the Companions of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ there is no one with a better memory for his hadith than me, except 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr; for he used to retain it with his heart and write it with his hand, while I used to retain it with my heart."],[9362,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which people are most severely tested?' He said: 'The Prophets, then the righteous.'"],[9363,"Send blessings upon me, for it is a purification for you. And ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me from Paradise. We asked him—"],[9364,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, (do you have pain?) I said: Yes, by my mother and father. He said: Pray, for in prayer there is healing."],[9365,"While a man was in a desert, he heard thunder in a cloud. He said: Then he heard a voice in the cloud: Water the garden of so-and-so Basim. So that cloud went to a stream and poured its water into it. He said: Then he went with the cloud until it reached a man standing in his garden. He said: What is your name, O servant of Allah? He said: I am so-and-so—by his name. He said: Then he said: What do you do with this garden of yours when you harvest it? He said: Since you have said that, I divide it into three thirds: I make one third for myself and my family, I return one third to it, and I give one third to the poor and the wayfarer."],[9366,"Adam and Musa (peace be upon them) argued. Musa said to Adam: You brought the people out—or you brought your descendants out—from Paradise. He said: Adam ﷺ said: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech. Do you find that written against me—I think he said: before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam confuted Musa."],[9367,"People are mines like mines of gold and silver. The best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam if they gain understanding. Souls are troops mustered together; those that recognized one another came together, and those that did not recognize one another parted."],[9368,"People will certainly ask you about everything, until they say: Allah created everything, so who created Him?"],[9369,"Richness is not from abundance of worldly goods, but richness is richness of the soul. By Allah, I do not fear for you error, but I fear for you deliberate transgression. I do not fear for you poverty, but I fear for you rivalry in worldly increase."],[9370,"I have from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two vessels. I have told you about one of them, and if I were to tell you about the other, you would do to me—and you would do."],[9371,"Trials will appear and killing will increase. We said: What is killing? He said: Murder. And knowledge will be taken away. Umar said: I did not hear Abu Hurayrah trace it back to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Indeed, the taking away of knowledge is not something that will be snatched from the chests of men, but it is the passing away of the scholars."],[9372,"I was about to order that the prayer be established, then go out with young men who have bundles of firewood and burn the houses of a people who hear the call to prayer but do not come to the prayer."],[9373,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: What do you think about His saying: 'And a garden whose width is the heavens and the earth'—so where is the Fire? He said: What do you think of the night when it covers everything—where is the day? He said: Wherever Allah wills. He said: And likewise it is wherever Allah wills."],[9374,"Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abdul-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated to us, Ubaydullah b. Abdullah b. al-Asamm narrated to us, from his uncle Yazid b. al-Asamm, from the Prophet ﷺ—and he did not say: from Abu Hurayrah."],[9375,"When he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, meaning because of how far he held them apart."],[9376,"A blind man complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the loss of his eyesight and that he had no one to lead him: “Is there any dispensation for me not to attend the prayer?” So he permitted him. Then he called him and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Do you hear the call?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then answer it.”"],[9377,"Al-Suhaymi from him. 9388 9385 - Muhammad b. Maʿmar narrated to us, ʿUmar b. Yunus narrated to us, ʿIkrimah b. ʿAmmar narrated to us, from Abu Kathir al-Suhaymi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9378,"Wine comes from these two trees: the date palm and the grapevine."],[9379,"By God, there is no believer who hears of me and does not see me but that he loves me. So I said: “And how do you know that, O Abu Hurayrah?” He said: “My mother was a polytheist, and I used to call her to Islam but she refused. One day I called her and she made me hear about the Prophet ﷺ what I disliked. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was weeping and said: ‘O Messenger of God, I used to call my mother to Islam but she refused me. Today I called her and she made me hear about you what I disliked. So supplicate God to guide Abu Hurayrah’s mother.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘O God, guide Abu Hurayrah’s mother.’ I went out running to give her the good news of the Messenger of God’s ﷺ supplication. When I reached the door, it was closed and I heard the splashing of water. She heard the rustle of my feet and said: ‘O Abu Hurayrah, stay where you are.’ She opened the door, and she had put on her shift but was too hasty for her head-covering. She said: ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.’ I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ weeping from joy just as I had wept from sorrow and said: ‘O Messenger of God, rejoice, for God has answered your supplication; God has guided Abu Hurayrah’s mother!’ Then I said: ‘O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to me.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘O God, make Your servant Abu Hurayrah and his mother beloved to Your believing servants and make them beloved to him.’ Abu Hurayrah said: ‘By God, there is no believer who hears of me but that he loves me.’”"],[9380,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, along with Abu Bakr and ʿUmar and a number of the Prophet’s ﷺ companions. The Prophet ﷺ went out from among us, and we feared that he would be cut off from us. I was among the first to become alarmed. I came to the walled garden of a man from the Ansar and looked for a gap but could not find one. Then I saw a spring of water coming out from behind it, and it dug through the ground the way a fox does, so I entered. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Abu Hurayrah?” I said: “Yes, O Prophet of God.” He said to me: “What is the matter with you?” I said: “We lost you, and we became alarmed and feared you would be cut off from us, while the people were calming down, with Abu Bakr and ʿUmar among them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take these sandals of mine, and whomever you meet behind this wall who bears witness that there is no god but God with a heart certain of it, give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” He said: I met ʿUmar and said to him: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: ‘Go out with these sandals of mine, and whomever you meet behind the wall who bears witness that there is no god but God with a heart certain of it, give him the glad tidings of Paradise.’” ʿUmar struck me with a blow on my chest, and I fell on my backside. I returned to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what ʿUmar had done, while I was sobbing. He said: “What made you do what Abu Hurayrah said?” He said: “Abu Hurayrah spoke the truth.” He said: “I fear that people will rely on it.” He said: “So leave them to act.”"],[9381,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[9382,"Kill dogs. The people of Madinah said: “O Messenger of God, they benefit us; they are with our sheep and our crops.” He said: “Then kill the solid black one among them—the solid black one that people say is a jinn.”"],[9383,"War is deception."],[9384,"Fire is junbar (no liability attaches for damage caused by fire)."],[9385,"He was named al-Khiḍr only because he prayed on a white fur and it stirred beneath him, green."],[9386,"It was said to the Children of Israel: “Enter the gate prostrating and say: ‘Hiṭṭah.’” But those who wronged said a saying other than what they were told; they said: “A grain in a barley,” dragging themselves on their buttocks."],[9387,"A good word is charity."],[9388,"While a man was stealing, Jesus saw him stealing and said, 'By Allah, I did not do it.' He replied, 'I believe in Allah and I disbelieve my eyes.'"],[9389,"The Hour will not come until you fight at the end of time a people from the non-Arabs: red-faced, snub-nosed, small-eyed, as if their faces were layered shields, wearing hair sandals."],[9390,"I wish I could be killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed—he repeated it several times—When a man is wounded in the path of Allah—and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path—he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color of blood and the fragrance of musk."],[9391,"He forbade a man to urinate in stagnant water and then perform ablution from it."],[9392,"Trustworthiness is in Azd, and judgment or judicial authority is in the Ansar."],[9393,"Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me the Duha prayer, fasting three days of every month, and sleeping after performing Witr."],[9394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a sheep be slaughtered and distributed among the neighbors. He said: So I slaughtered it and distributed it among the neighbors, and I gave the foreleg to the Prophet ﷺ, and the foreleg was the part of the sheep he liked most. When the Prophet ﷺ came, A'ishah said, 'Nothing remains with us from it except the foreleg.' He said, 'All of it remains except this,' meaning the foreleg."],[9395,"When one of you gets up at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[9396,"The one who lowers and raises before the imam—indeed his forelock is in the hand of a devil."],[9397,"A man who had been stung was brought to him, and he said, 'If he had said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, he would not have been stung or harmed.'"],[9398,"When you pay the zakah of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is due upon you."],[9399,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: “Then for him is a miserable livelihood” (Q 20:124), he said: The miserable livelihood is that which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: ninety-nine serpents are set upon him, biting his flesh until the Hour rises."],[9400,"The first thing for which the servant is called to account is that it is said to him: “Did I not make your body healthy and give you cool water to drink?”"],[9401,"Whoever dies in Jerusalem, it is as if he died in the heaven."],[9402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with al-Hasan and al-Husayn, one on each shoulder, kissing this one once and that one once, until he reached us. A man said to him: “Do you love them, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.”"],[9403,"Whoever fasts a day seeking the face of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire as far as a crow flies from when it is a fledgling until it dies of old age."],[9404,"Send blessings upon the prophets of Allah, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent them as He sent me."],[9405,"When a man says to his brother: “May Allah reward you with good,” he has reached the utmost in praise."],[9406,"O Allah, teach me what benefits me, benefit me with what You taught me, and increase me in knowledge. Praise be to Allah in every condition, and I seek refuge in Allah from the condition of the Fire."],[9407,"Among the worst of my nation are those who were nurtured in luxury and whose bodies grew upon it."],[9408,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: “Do the people of Paradise have intimate relations with their spouses?” He said: “Yes, with a member that does not tire, a private part that does not wear out, and desire that does not cease.”"],[9409,"The Prophet ﷺ led them in the afternoon or noon prayer, and stood up after two rak’ahs. They glorified Allah to alert him, but he continued his prayer. When he finished the prayer, he prostrated twice and then said the salam."],[9410,"I entered the mosque of Madinah seeking a companion of mine, and there was a man with gleaming front teeth, and beside him a dark-eyed, fair, handsome man, and they were in the shade of the mosque. The elder called me and said: “O Yemeni,” so I came, and he said: “Do not say: ‘By Allah, Allah will not admit you to Paradise,’ or ‘By Allah, Allah will not forgive you.’” I said: “Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?” He said: “Abu Hurayrah.” I said: “O Abu Hurayrah, by Allah, you have criticized something I used to say to my family and servants when I was angry with them.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There were two men among the Children of Israel who were brothers. One was diligent in worship and the other was a sinner. The diligent one kept saying to the sinner: “Refrain,” and the sinner said: “Leave me and my Lord.” Until one day he found him committing a grave sin, and said: “Refrain.” He said: “Leave me and my Lord. Were you sent as a watcher over me?” He said: “By Allah, Allah will not admit you to Paradise.” Then Allah sent an angel to them and took their souls. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to the sinner: “Enter Paradise by My mercy,” and said to the other: “Were you able to do what is in My hand? Could you withhold My mercy from My servant? Take him to the Fire.” Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He spoke a word that destroyed his worldly life and his hereafter.”’”"],[9411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Zuhr prayer, then he said the taslim after two rak'ahs and turned away. Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: \"Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget?\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of that happened.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he prayed two rak'ahs, then said the taslim, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting, then said the taslim."],[9412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of the two black (creatures) during prayer."],[9413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the one who had a right: \"Take your right in a decent manner, whether it is fulfilled or not.\""],[9414,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended a mountain, and with him were Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, and al-Zubayr. The mountain shook with them, so he said: \"Be still, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.\""],[9415,"This knowledge will be carried by the upright of every generation; they will repel from it the distortions of the extremists, the interpretations of the ignorant, and the claims of the falsifiers."],[9416,"Whoever does not ask Allah, He becomes angry with him."],[9417,"Al-Khuzi: he was called al-Khuzi because he used to stay in Makkah in the valley of al-Khuz."],[9418,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from the beginning of the seventy (years) and from the rule of children."],[9419,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a dark night, and with him were al-Hasan and al-Husayn. A flash of lightning flashed, so he said: \"Go to your mother.\""],[9420,"My beloved friend instructed me with three things: the witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of duha, and that I should not sleep except after praying witr."],[9421,"My beloved friend instructed me with three things: the witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and that I should not sleep except after praying witr."],[9422,"Nuh b. Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Wasi', from Ma'ruf, from Abu Hurayrah, with this hadith."],[9423,"When you disagree about the road, make it seven cubits."],[9424,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood in his wall."],[9425,"When one of you finds a louse in the mosque, he should bury it."],[9426,"He forbade a man, when putting on sandals, to begin with the left before the right, and said: 'Let him take them both off or put them both on.'"],[9427,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the robber does not rob a plunder of great value while he is a believer."],[9428,"I heard Muhammad b. Ali, and he was asked about the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: 'The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer.' He said: He drew a wide circle on the ground, then drew a circle in the middle of the circle, and said: The first circle is Islam, and the circle in the middle of the circle is faith. So when he commits adultery, he goes out of faith to Islam, and nothing takes him out of Islam except shirk."],[9429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to seek refuge with God from the punishment of the grave, from the punishment of Hell, and from the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[9430,"When one of you wakes up, he should not dip his hand into his vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[9431,"I saw Ibrahim ﷺ as if he were your companion, and I saw Musa ﷺ tall and dark brown, and I saw 'Isa ﷺ ruddy with curly hair."],[9432,"Ibn 'Abbas addressed us one day after 'Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people kept calling out to him: 'The prayer, the prayer!' Among the people there was a man from Banu Tamim. Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Are you teaching me the Sunnah? May you have no mother! I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ combine Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha'.' He said: Then I met Abu Hurayrah and he agreed with him."],[9433,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was between Dajnan and 'Usfan when the polytheists said: 'These people have a prayer that is dearer to them than their fathers and sons, and that is the 'Asr prayer. So resolve your matter and fall upon them in one assault.' And Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and ordered him to divide his companions into two groups, and pray with one group, and the other group would stand behind them, and these would take their guard and their weapons. Thus they would have one rak'ah each, and the Messenger of God ﷺ would have two rak'ahs."],[9434,"Shall I tell you about the people of Paradise? The weak and the oppressed. Shall I tell you about the people of the Fire? Every harsh, coarse person. Shall I tell you about the best of you? Those of you with the best character. Shall I tell you about the worst of you? The talkative, the boastful, the arrogant."],[9435,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the jalalah (an animal that eats filth), and from drinking its milk, eating it, and riding it."],[9436,"When you are told a hadith from me, and it agrees with the truth, then I said it."],[9437,"The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell."],[9438,"Whoever strikes a whip unjustly, retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[9439,"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth, and on those nights the angels on the earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles."],[9440,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my husband has divorced me, and he wants to take my son away from me, and he has drawn water for me from the well of Abu 'Inabah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O boy, this is your mother, and this is your father, and he gave him the choice between his father and his mother."],[9441,"I witnessed Abu Hurayrah give a boy the choice between his father and his mother, and he said: I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ give a boy the choice between his father and his mother."],[9442,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a found item, and he said: It is to be announced, and it is not to be hidden or concealed. If its owner comes, then [it goes to him]; otherwise, it is the wealth of God which He gives to whomever He wills."],[9443,"Regarding a slave owned by two men, and one of them frees his share, he said: He is responsible for [the value of] his partner's share if he is wealthy."],[9444,"Regarding a man who becomes bankrupt, and a man finds his exact goods, he said: He has more right to them."],[9445,"He forbade a gold ring."],[9446,"A gift for life (al-'umra) is permissible."],[9447,"Indeed Allah has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs, yet the prophets and martyrs will envy them on the Day of Resurrection."],[9448,"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then its parents make it a Jew or a Christian."],[9449,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[9450,"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."],[9451,"There is no contagion and no hāmah, and the best of omens is the auspicious sign, and the evil eye is real."],[9452,"When the believer dies, the angels of mercy take his soul, and his soul is placed in a white silk cloth, then he is taken up to the heaven. They say: 'We have never found a fragrance more pleasant than this.' They say: 'Leave him until he rests, for he was in the distress of the world.' And they say: 'What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do?' until they bring him to the heaven. As for the disbeliever, when he dies, the keepers say: 'We have never found a stench more foul than this,' and they take him to the lowest earth."],[9453,"The prayer is cut off by a dog, a donkey, and a woman."],[9454,"The first thing for which the servant will be brought to account is his prayer. If it is sound, he has succeeded and prospered; if it is deficient, he has failed and lost."],[9455,"Anas b. Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[9456,"Umar b. al-Khattab narrated to us, Muhammad b. Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus – meaning Ibn Ubayd – from Ghaylan b. Jarir, from Ziyad b. Matar, from Abu Hurayrah. This is how Sufyan narrated it from Yunus, and Hammad said: from Ghaylan b. Jarir, from Ziyad b. Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9457,"Whoever departs from obedience and separates from the community and dies upon that, then it is a death of ignorance. And whoever goes out among my ummah striking its righteous and its wicked, not fearing – or he said: not avoiding – its believer, and not fulfilling the covenant of its covenant-holder, then he is not of my ummah. And whoever is killed under a blind banner, out of zeal for a group, then his killing is a killing of ignorance."],[9458,"This is the month of Ramadan, a blessed month in which Allah has made fasting obligatory. In it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. In it there is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of it is truly deprived."],[9459,"Paradise has bricks of gold and bricks of silver, and its mortar is musk."],[9460,"Whoever enters Paradise will enjoy bliss and never suffer hardship, will live and never die, his clothes will not wear out, and his youth will not fade."],[9461,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left, or let him remove both together or put on both together."],[9462,"Seventy thousand from my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. A man stood up and said, \"Supplicate Allah to make me one of them.\" He said, \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Then another man stood up and said, \"Supplicate Allah to make me one of them.\" He said, \"ʿUkkāshah has preceded you in that.\""],[9463,"The poor person is not the one who goes around asking people and is turned away by a date or two dates or a morsel or two morsels. Rather, the poor person is the one who does not find enough to suffice him and does not beg people importunately."],[9464,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years and does not cross it."],[9465,"When one of you has his servant bring him his food and the servant has taken care of its heat and smoke (I think he said) or something like that, then let him seat him with him; if he does not seat him with him, then let him give him from his food."],[9466,"Woe to the heels (or the heels) from the Fire."],[9467,"The smell from the mouth of a fasting person is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk."],[9468,"Every deed is an expiation, and fasting is Mine, and I reward it."],[9469,"There is an hour on Friday during which no Muslim slave asks Allah for something but He gives it to him."],[9470,"The child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone."],[9471,"A woman tied up a cat of hers, and she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth, until it died, and Allah admitted her into the Fire."],[9472,"The mine is a loss, and the well is a loss, and the beast is a loss, and in the buried treasure there is one-fifth."],[9473,"When you put on sandals, begin with the right, and when you take them off, begin with the left, or take them both off, or put them both on."],[9474,"The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone."],[9475,"The Fire will have its people cast into it, and it will say, 'Is there any more?' until the Blessed and Exalted comes to it and places His foot in it, and it shrinks and says, 'Enough, enough.'"],[9476,"People are minerals in good and evil; the best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam if they gain understanding."],[9477,"When the servant of one of you brings his food, having taken care of its heat and its preparation, and he does not seat him with him to eat, then let him hand him a morsel from his food."],[9478,"I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9479,"Adam met Musa (peace be upon them). He said, 'Are you Adam whom Allah created with His hand, made to dwell in His Garden, made His angels prostrate to you, and breathed into you of His spirit, then you did what you did and brought your descendants out of the Garden?' Adam said, 'Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His messages, spoke to you, gave you the Torah, and brought you near as a confidant?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Am I older or the Remembrance?' He said, 'The Remembrance.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'So Adam defeated Musa, so Adam defeated Musa.'"],[9480,"Men will surely leave Madinah out of aversion to it, while Madinah is better for them if they only knew."],[9481,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in: 'When the sky is split open.'"],[9482,"Muhammad b. Yazid narrated to us, Badal narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' b. Abi Maymunah and Marwan al-Asghar, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar."],[9483,"Sāliḥ b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿUthmān b. ʿUmar narrated to us: Hishām b. Ḥassān narrated to us, from Yūnus, from Bakr, from Abū Rāfiʿ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. This ḥadīth has been narrated from Yūnus by more than one."],[9484,"And Zayd b. Akhzam narrated it to us: ʿAbd al-Qāhir narrated to us, from Hishām; and Muḥammad b. al-Zibriqān narrated it."],[9485,"A man is in prayer as long as he remains in his place of prayer, as long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[9486,"Whoever prays a rakʿah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises and then it rises, let him add another to it."],[9487,"Whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[9488,"The fasting person has two joys: a joy in this world at the time of breaking his fast, and a joy in the Hereafter."],[9489,"Zakariyyā, may Allah bless him, was a carpenter."],[9490,"Three men went out to seek extra provision for their families. They were caught by rain and took refuge in a cave. He said: A rock fell over them—I think he said—from the mouth of the cave and blocked the cave mouth, and it settled leaving a gap away from them. He said: The men said to one another: The tracks have been effaced, the rock has fallen, and none knows your place except Allah, the Exalted. So come, let each man of you call upon Allah with the most trustworthy deed he has ever done for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hoping that He will bring you out from your place. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I was dutiful to my parents, and that I had let my sheep rest one night, and I used to milk them for my parents, and I came to them while they were lying on their bed, so that I might give them drink with my own hand, and I came to them one of those nights, and I brought their drink, but I found them asleep. I began to desire for them to remain asleep, and I disliked waking them, and I disliked returning with the drink so that they would wake and not find me with them. So I stood in my place, standing at their heads like that until morning. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance, then open a way for us. He said: A third of the rock shifted—or a word like that—opening. They said to the next, 'O man,' and the second said: O Allah, if You know that I loved a cousin of mine with intense love, and I—I think he said—asked her family for her hand, but they refused me, until I made for her what she accepted between me and her. Then I summoned her and was alone with her, and I took from her the seat a man takes from a woman, but she said: 'It is not lawful for you to break the seal except by its right.' So my soul withdrew from her, and I honored her right over herself and over me. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance, then open a way for us. He said: The rock shifted—or a word like that—opening. And they said to the third, 'O you, say.' The third said: O Allah, if You know that a worker worked for me for a ṣāʿ of food, and the worker departed without taking his ṣāʿ, and remained away from me for a long time, I took his ṣāʿ and kept cultivating it until from that ṣāʿ there accumulated many cattle, many sheep, and much wealth. Then that worker came to me after a time seeking the ṣāʿ of food, and I said to him: 'Your ṣāʿ of food has become much wealth, many sheep, and many cattle, so take all this, for it is from that ṣāʿ.' He said to me: 'Are you mocking me?' I said to him: 'No, by Allah, but it is the truth.' So he went off driving all the wealth. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance, then open a way for us. The rock split and fell, and they came out walking. This ḥadīth, we do not know anyone who narrated it from ʿAwf, from Khilās, except al-Muʿtamir."],[9491,"Were it not for the Children of Israel, meat would not spoil; and were it not for Ḥawwāʾ, no woman would betray her husband."],[9492,"A delegation came to Muʿāwiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, and I was among them, along with Abū Hurayrah, and that was in Ramaḍān. Some of us would prepare food for the others, and Abū Hurayrah was among those who did so often and would invite to his camp. I said: 'Why don't I prepare food and then invite them to my camp?' He said: Then I met Abū Hurayrah after the evening prayer. I said: 'The invitation is with me tonight.' He said: 'You beat me to it?' I said: 'Yes.' So I invited them and they are with me. Abū Hurayrah said: 'Shall I not inform you of a ḥadīth of yours, O assembly of the Anṣār?' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he entered Makkah. He sent al-Zubayr over one of the two flanks, and sent Khālid b. al-Walīd over the other flank, and sent Abū ʿUbaydah over the infantry without armor—those who had no equipment. Quraysh had gathered their rabble and their followers. They said: 'We will send these forward; if they succeed, we will be with them; and if they are struck down, we will give what is asked.' They took the bottom of the valley, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a battalion. He looked and saw me, and said: 'O Abū Hurayrah.' I said: 'At your service, Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Do you see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers?' Then he said: 'Call out to the Anṣār, and let none come to me except an Anṣārī.' So he called them, and they came until they surrounded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Do you see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers?' Then he gestured with one hand over the other: 'Mow them down like harvest until you meet me at al-Ṣafā.' Abū Hurayrah said: We set off, and it was not the desire of any of us to kill whom he wished among them but he did so. Abū Sufyān came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the virgin daughter of Quraysh has been violated, or you have made lawful the green of Quraysh; there is no Quraysh after today.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.' He said: So the people closed their doors. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he reached the Black Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House with a bow in his hand, holding the upper end of the bow. He came upon an idol beside the House and began thrusting it in its eye, saying: 'Truth has come and falsehood has vanished.' Then he went on until he came to al-Ṣafā where he could see the House. He raised his hands and began praising Allah and supplicating, while the Anṣār were below him, saying to one another: 'As for the man, desire for his people and compassion for his clan have overcome him.' He said: Abū Hurayrah said: Then revelation came, and when it came, it did not remain hidden from them. No one raised his gaze to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the revelation was finished. When the revelation was finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O assembly of the Anṣār, did you say: As for the man, desire for his kin and compassion for his clan have overcome him?' They said: 'We did say that.' He said: 'Not at all. I am the slave of Allah and His Messenger. I emigrated to Allah and to you. The living is your living, and the dying is your dying.' They came to him weeping and saying: 'By Allah, we only said what we said out of concern for Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'Allah and His Messenger believe you and excuse you.'"],[9493,"Paradise has bricks of gold and bricks of silver."],[9494,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says, or has intercourse with a menstruating woman, or has intercourse with a woman in her anus, has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muḥammad ﷺ."],[9495,"If you contend over the road, then make it seven cubits."],[9496,"There is a surah in the Quran, thirty verses, which interceded for its reciter until he was forgiven: Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion, and He is over all things competent."],[9497,"I am Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And this hadith, we do not know it being narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."],[9498,"Sa'id b. al-'As sent me to Madinah. He said: I was with Marwan, and Abu Hurayrah passed by. He said: Some of your hadith, O Abu Hurayrah. He went on, then came back to him. We said: Now he will be caught. He said: How did you hear the Prophet ﷺ pray over the funeral? He replied: You created it - or You created him - and You guided it to Islam, and You took its soul. You know its secret and its open. We have come to You as intercessors, so forgive it."],[9499,"I witnessed Marwan asking Abu Hurayrah: How did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray over the funeral? He said: O God, You are its Lord, and You created it, and You guided it, and You are most knowing of its secret and its open. We have come as intercessors, so forgive it."],[9500,"Two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ asking him. He said: Go to these mountain passes, gather firewood, and sell it. So they went and gathered firewood, then came and sold it, and obtained food. Then they went and gathered firewood again, and came, and they did not cease until they bought two garments, then bought two donkeys. They said: God has blessed us in the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[9501,"The poor of this community will enter before their rich by forty years."],[9502,"Beware of suspicion, for it is the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not hate one another, do not sever ties, do not turn your backs on one another. Be, O servants of God, brothers."],[9503,"A man among those before you bought property from a man and found in it a jar of gold. He said to him: I bought the property from you, and I did not buy the gold from you. The seller said: I sold you the property with what was in it. He said: They took their dispute to one of those who was at that time. He said to one of them: Do you have a daughter? And he said to the other: Do you have a son? They said: Yes. He said: Then marry one of them to the other, and let them spend on themselves from this wealth."],[9504,"The bad breath of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk."],[9505,"When one of you is fasting, he should not use obscene language that day nor act foolishly. If someone fights him or insults him, let him say: I am fasting."],[9506,"None of you should urinate in stagnant water and then perform ablution from it."],[9507,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the best prayer after the obligatory one. He said: “The middle of the night.” And he was asked about the best fasting after the month of Ramadan. He said: “The month of Allah which you call al-Muḥarram.”"],[9508,"He was in al-Baṣrah, then he became a Bedouin. He settled in al-Lahābah, and his wealth and children increased there. Then his sons reviled each other among their people, saying: “O sons of the hypocrite! Your father abandoned the emigration and became a Bedouin.” He felt hurt that he was reviled for that. So he called his son Salmān, and he brought him three riding camels. He loaded his servant on one baggage camel, and he and his son mounted. Then he set out until he came to the Baqīʿ of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in al-Madīnah. Then he took his son Salmān by the hand until they came to al-Dawsī, Abū Hurayrah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he was narrating to the people. The first thing they understood from him was that he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: ‘Among the best of people are two men: a man who spends his wealth in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then goes on a military expedition himself until he descends upon lands whose descent displeases the enemy, then dies or is killed; or a man from the desert people with his camels who withdraws from the evils of people, establishes the five prayers, gives the due right of his wealth, and worships Allah until certainty comes to him.’” So Shihāb knelt on his knees until he faced him and said: “Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abū Hurayrah,” and he swore to it three times. Shihāb was satisfied with the legal ruling he had come seeking. Then he stood and performed several prostrations, then came to his mount and rode it until they left al-Madīnah behind their backs. He said to his son: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Shihāb, were it not that…”"],[9509,"Deceit and treachery are in the Fire."],[9510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a horse, which made every stride cover the farthest extent of his sight. He traveled, and Jibrīl ﷺ traveled with him. He came upon a people who sowed in a day and harvested in a day; whenever they harvested, it returned as it was. He said: “O Jibrīl, who are these?” He said: “These are the mujāhidūn in the cause of Allah; a good deed is multiplied for them by seven hundred times, and whatever they spend, He replaces it.” Then he came upon a people whose heads were being crushed with rocks; whenever they were crushed, they returned as they were, and nothing of that ceased for them. He said: “O Jibrīl, who are these?” He said: “These are those whose heads were too heavy for the prayer.” Then he came upon a people with patches on their backs and patches on their fronts, being herded as cattle are herded to ḍarīʿ, zaqqūm, and the hot stones of Hell. He said: “Who are these, O Jibrīl?” He said: “These are those who do not pay the zakāh of their wealth. Allah did not wrong them; Allah is not unjust to His servants.” Then he came upon a people with cooked meat in a pot before them, good and delicious, and another raw, foul meat. They ate the foul meat and left the cooked, good meat. He said: “O Jibrīl, who are these?” He said: “This is the man from your community who leaves his wife lawfully and comes to a wicked woman and spends the night with her until morning; and the woman who leaves her husband lawfully and good and comes to a wicked man and spends the night with him until morning.” Then he came upon a man who had gathered a huge bundle which he could not carry, and he wanted to add more to it. He said: “O Jibrīl, who is this?” He said: “This is the man from your community upon whom rests the trust of the people; he cannot fulfill it, and he adds to it.” Then he came upon a people whose lips and tongues were being cut with iron scissors; whenever they were cut, they returned as they were, and nothing of that ceased for them. He said: “O Jibrīl, who are these?” He said: “The orators of fitnah.” Then he came upon a small rock from which emerged a huge bull. The bull tried to enter from where it came out but could not. He said: “What is this, O Jibrīl?” He said: “This is the man who speaks a great word and regrets it, and wants to take it back but cannot.” Then he came upon a valley and found a pleasant scent and the scent of musk with a voice. He said: “What is this?” He said: “The voice of Paradise, saying: ‘O Lord, bring me my people and what You promised me. My plants have become many, and my silk, my fine silk, my brocade, my carpets, my coral, my silver, my gold, my cups, my plates, my pitchers, my fruits, my honey, my garments, my milk, my wine. Bring me what You promised me.’ He said: ‘For you is every Muslim man and Muslim woman, every believer man and believer woman, and whoever believes in Me and My messengers, does righteous deeds, and does not associate anything with Me, and does not take equals besides Me, he is secure. Whoever asks Me, I give him; whoever lends Me, I repay him; whoever relies on Me, I suffice him. Indeed I am Allah; there is no god but I; My promise is never broken. The believers have succeeded. Blessed is Allah, the Best of Creators.’ She said: ‘I am pleased.’ Then he came upon a valley and heard a dreadful voice. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, what is this voice?’ He said: ‘This is the voice of Hell, saying: ‘O Lord, bring me my people and what You promised me. My chains have become many, and my shackles, my blazing fire, my boiling water, my ghassāq, my ghislin. My depth has become far and my heat intense. Bring me what You promised me.’ He said: ‘For you is every polytheist man and polytheist woman, every wicked man and wicked woman, and every tyrant who does not believe in the Day of Reckoning.’ She said: ‘I am pleased.’ Then he traveled until he came to Jerusalem and dismounted. He tied his horse to a rock and prayed with the angels. When the prayer ended, they said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this with you?’ He said: ‘This is Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah, the Seal of the Prophets.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor.’ Then they met the souls of the prophets, and they praised their Lord. Ibrāhīm ﷺ said: ‘O Allah, the One who took me as a friend, gave me a great kingdom, made me a devout nation, chose me for His messages, and saved me from the fire, and made it coolness and peace for me.’ Then Mūsā (peace and blessings be upon him) praised his Lord and said: ‘Praise be to Allah who spoke to me directly, chose me, sent down the Torah to me, made the destruction of the people of Pharaoh at my hand, and the deliverance of the Children of Israel at my hand.’ Then Dāwūd ﷺ praised his Lord and said: ‘Praise be to Allah who gave me a kingdom, sent down the Zabūr to me, made iron soft for me, subjected the mountains to glorify with me and the birds, and gave me wisdom and decisive speech.’ Then Sulaymān praised his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and said: ‘Praise be to Allah who subjected the winds to me, the jinn and mankind, and subjected the devils to me working whatever I wished of sanctuaries, statues, basins like reservoirs, and fixed cauldrons; and taught me the language of the birds, made a spring of molten copper flow for me, and gave me a kingdom that is not fitting for anyone after me.’ Then ʿĪsā ﷺ praised his Lord and said: ‘Praise be to Allah who taught me the Torah and the Injīl, made me heal the blind and the leper, raise the dead by His permission, raised me and purified me from those who disbelieved, and protected me and my mother from the accursed Satan, so Satan had no way over us.’ And Muḥammad ﷺ praised his Lord and said: ‘All of you have praised your Lord, and I praise my Lord. Praise be to Allah who sent me as a mercy to the worlds and to all people, as a bearer of good tidings and a warner; sent down to me the Furqān, in which is an explanation of everything; made my community the best community brought forth for mankind; made my community a middle community; made my community the first and the last; expanded my breast; removed my burden; raised my mention; and made me an opener and a seal.’ Ibrāhīm ﷺ said: ‘By this Muḥammad ﷺ has surpassed you.’ Then three covered vessels were brought. A vessel was handed to him, and it was said to him: ‘Drink; it contains water.’ Then another vessel was handed to him containing milk, and he drank from it until he was quenched. Then another vessel was handed to him containing wine, and he said: ‘I have drunk enough; I will not taste it.’ It was said to him: ‘You have done right. Indeed it will be forbidden to your community. If you had drunk it, only a few of your community would have followed you.’ Then he ascended to the heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. It was said: ‘Who is this?’ He said: ‘Jibrīl.’ It was said: ‘And who is with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ He entered, and there was a seated old man, perfect in form, with nothing lacking from his form as it lacks from human forms. On his right was a door from which a pleasant scent emerged, and on his left a door from which a foul scent emerged. When he looked at the door on his right, he laughed, and when he looked at the door on his left, he wept and grieved. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this old man, and what are these two doors?’ He said: ‘This is your father Ādam. The door on his right is the door of Paradise; when he sees one of his descendants entering it, he laughs and rejoices. When he looks at the door on his left, the door of Hell, at one of his descendants entering it, he weeps and grieves.’ Then he ascended to the second heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. It was said: ‘Who is this?’ He said: ‘Jibrīl.’ They said: ‘And who is with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ He entered, and there were two young men. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who are these two young men?’ He said: ‘This is ʿĪsā and Yaḥyā, the two sons of maternal aunts.’ Then he ascended to the third heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. They said: ‘Who is this with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ He entered, and there was a man who had been favored over people in beauty as the full moon is favored over the other stars. He said: ‘Who is this, O Jibrīl?’ He said: ‘Your brother Yūsuf ﷺ.’ Then he ascended to the fourth heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. They said: ‘Who is this with you?’ He said: ‘This is Muḥammad ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ He entered, and there was a man. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this seated man?’ He said: ‘This is your brother Idrīs; Allah raised him to a high place.’ Then he ascended to the fifth heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. They said to him: ‘Who is this with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ There was a seated man narrating to them. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this, and who are these around him?’ He said: ‘This is Hārūn ﷺ, left behind among his people, and these around him are his people from the Children of Israel.’ Then he ascended to the sixth heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. They said: ‘Who is this with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ There was a seated man, and he passed by him, and the man wept. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this?’ He said: ‘This is Mūsā ﷺ.’ He said: ‘What makes him weep?’ He said: ‘The Children of Israel claim that I am the best of creation, and this one has succeeded me. If it were only him alone, but with him is his entire community.’ Then he ascended to the seventh heaven, and Jibrīl asked for it to be opened. They said: ‘Who is with you?’ He said: ‘Muḥammad ﷺ.’ They said: ‘Has he been sent to him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ They said: ‘May Allah greet him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and what an excellent successor, and what an excellent coming has come.’ There was a gray-haired man seated on a chair at the door of Paradise, and with him were people sitting with something in their colors – ʿĪsā, meaning Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī, said: And I heard him once say: ‘black-faced’ – so those who had something in their colors stood up and entered a river called ‘the Blessing of Allah,’ bathed in it, and came out with some of the color gone from them. Then they entered another river called ‘the Mercy of Allah,’ bathed in it, and came out with some of the color gone from them. Then they entered another river, and that is His saying: ‘And their Lord gave them a purifying drink,’ and they came out with their colors purified like the colors of their companions, and they sat with their companions. He said: ‘O Jibrīl, who is this gray-haired seated man? And who are these white-faced ones? And what are these who had something in their colors, who entered these rivers and bathed in them, then came out with their colors purified?’ He said: ‘This is your father Ibrāhīm ﷺ, the first to have gray hair on earth. These white-faced people are a people who did not mix their faith with wrongdoing. And these who had something in their colors mixed righteous deeds with bad ones; they repented, and Allah accepted their repentance.’ Then he went on to the Lote Tree. It was said to him: ‘This is the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary; every one of your community who passes on your path ends here. It is the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, from whose roots flow rivers of water that does not become stagnant, rivers of milk whose taste does not change, rivers of wine delicious to those who drink, and rivers of purified honey. It is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for seventy years, and a leaf of it shades the creation. Light covered it, and the angels covered it’ – ʿĪsā said: ‘That is His saying: “When the Lote Tree was covered with what covered it.”’ Then He, Blessed and Exalted, said to him: ‘Ask.’ He said: ‘You took Ibrāhīm as a friend, gave him a great kingdom, spoke to Mūsā directly, gave Dāwūd a great kingdom, made iron soft for him, subjected the mountains to him, gave Sulaymān a great kingdom, subjected the jinn, mankind, devils, and winds to him, gave him a kingdom not fitting for anyone after him, taught ʿĪsā the Torah and the Injīl, made him heal the blind and the leper, and protected him and his mother from the accursed Satan, so he had no way over them.’ His Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said to him: ‘I have taken you as a friend. It is written in the Torah: Muḥammad is the beloved of the Most Merciful. I have sent you to all people, made your community the first and the last, made your community such that no sermon is valid for them until they testify that you are My servant and messenger, made you the first of the prophets in creation and the last of them in sending, given you the seven oft-repeated verses which I did not give to any prophet before you, and given you the closing verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne which I did not give to any prophet before you, and made you an opener and a seal.’ And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, favored me with six things: He cast terror into the hearts of my enemy at a distance of a month’s journey; He made booty lawful for me, and it was not lawful for anyone before me; the earth was made a mosque and a means of purification for me; I was given the openings of speech and its comprehensive words; my community was shown to me, and the follower and the followed among them were not hidden from me; I saw them coming upon a people who wear hair sandals, and I saw them coming upon a people with broad faces and small eyes, and I recognized what they were; and I was commanded with fifty prayers.’ So he returned to Mūsā, and Mūsā said to him: ‘With how many prayers were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Fifty prayers.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ So Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked Allah for reduction, and He removed ten from him. He returned to Mūsā, and he said to him: ‘With how many were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Forty prayers.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ So Muḥammad ﷺ returned and asked Him for reduction, and He removed ten from him. He returned to Mūsā, and he said to him: ‘With how many were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Thirty.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ So Muḥammad returned and asked his Lord for reduction, and He removed ten from him. He returned to Mūsā, and he said to him: ‘With how many were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Twenty.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ So he returned and asked his Lord for reduction, and He removed ten from him. He returned to Mūsā, and he said to him: ‘With how many were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Ten.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction for your community, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ So Muḥammad returned and asked his Lord for reduction, and He removed five from him. He returned to Mūsā, and he said to him: ‘With how many were you commanded?’ He said: ‘Five.’ He said: ‘Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction, for your community is the weakest of communities, and I encountered severity from the Children of Israel.’ He said: ‘I have returned to my Lord until I felt ashamed, and I will not return to Him.’ It was said to him: ‘As you have been patient with the five, it will count for you as fifty; every good deed is multiplied tenfold.’ ʿĪsā said: ‘It reached me that the Prophet ﷺ said: Mūsā ﷺ was the harshest of them to me at first and the best of them at last.’ And this hadith we do not know is narrated except with this isnad from this way."],[9511,"“O Abū Hurayrah, do you have anything with you?” I said: “Yes.” So I took out dates from a provision bag I had, and there were twenty-seven dates in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed them down while people were with him and said: “Eat in the name of Allah.” They ate, and some remained. He said: “O Abū Hurayrah, put it back in the provision bag. If you want to take something from it, put your hand in it and do not overturn it.” He said: “It remained with me until ʿUthmān ؓ was killed.”"],[9512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Abū Hurayrah, do you have anything with you?” He said: I said: “Yes.” He said: So I took out dates from a provision bag I had, and there were twenty-seven dates in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed them down with him."],[9513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “From whom are you?” I said: “From Daws.” He said: “I did not think that anyone in Daws had any good in him.”"],[9514,"Abū Hurayrah was on a journey. When they stopped, the tables were set, and they sent for him while he was praying. He said: “I am fasting.” When they had almost finished, he came and ate. The people looked at their messenger, and he said: “What are you looking at? By Allah, indeed...”"],[9515,"“My close friend advised me three things: the witr before sleep, the two rakʿahs of ḍuḥā, and fasting three days of every month.”"],[9516,"I heard Abū ʿUthmān narrating from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know that anyone narrated it from Abū Shimr, from Abū ʿUthmān, except Shuʿbah. This wording has been narrated from Abū Hurayrah through many paths: Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib, Abū Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, ʿIkrimah, Mujāhid, Saʿīd b. Jubayr, al-Shaʿbī, ʿAṭāʾ b. Abī Rabāḥ, Abū Zurʿah, al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, Muḥammad b. Sīrīn, Muḥammad b. Ziyād, and others narrated it. Something similar has been narrated from Abū al-Dardāʾ and Abū Dharr with different wording."],[9517,"“Allah, Blessed and Exalted, multiplies a good deed for His believing servant by a million good deeds.” So I went and met Abū Hurayrah and said: “It has reached me that you say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Allah, Blessed and Exalted, multiplies a good deed by a million good deeds’?” He said: “Yes, I heard him say: ‘For a good deed there are two million good deeds.’ Then he recited this verse: ‘Indeed Allah does not wrong even the weight of an atom’ until His saying: ‘a great reward.’ So who can know the magnitude of what Allah said as ‘great’?”"],[9518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to announce that there is no prayer except with the recitation of the Opening of the Book, and whatever more."],[9519,"I am the first to open the gate of Paradise. Then a woman calls me, so I say to her: Who are you? She says: I am a woman who remained with my orphans."],[9520,"I entered Paradise and saw in it a servant who had done no good deed except that he used to remove harm from the path of the Muslims. Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise because of that."],[9521,"When your rulers are the best of you, your wealthy are the generous of you, and your affairs are conducted by consultation among you, then the surface of the earth is better for you than its interior. When your rulers are the worst of you, your wealthy are the miserly of you, and your affairs are delegated to your women, then the interior of the earth is better for you than its surface."],[9522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib when he was martyred and looked at a sight more painful to the heart than any other he had seen, or he said: to his heart. He looked at him and saw that he had been mutilated, so he said: May Allah have mercy on you. You were, as far as I know, one who maintained ties of kinship and did good deeds. By Allah, were it not for the grief of those after you, it would please me to leave you until Allah gathers you from the bellies of beasts – or something similar. By Allah, I will mutilate seventy like your mutilation. Then Jibril ﷺ came down to Muhammad ﷺ with this chapter and recited: And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted, to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ atoned and refrained from that."],[9523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed dates among us, and I received five dates, or four dates and a dry inferior one. I found the dry inferior one to be the hardest of them on my molar."],[9524,"Shaqiq 9535 9532 - Muhammad b. Amr b. al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abdullah b. Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9525,"The best of my nation are the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them – then Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not – then there will arise a people who love fatness and make vows but do not fulfill them."],[9526,"When the soul of a believer departs, two angels meet it and ascend with it. He said: He mentioned its pleasant scent and mentioned musk. He said: The inhabitants of heaven say: A good soul has come from the direction of the earth; may Allah bless you and the body you used to inhabit. He said: It is taken to its Lord, Blessed and Exalted. He said: It is said: Go with it, meaning to the end of the two terms. He said: And he mentioned the disbeliever. He said: He mentioned its stench. He said: It is ascended with. He said: The inhabitants of heaven say: A vile soul has come from the direction of the earth, and he mentioned the curse. So they go with it to its Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and it is said: Go with it to the end of the two terms. Abu Hurayrah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the stench, he moved his hand or his garment over his nose."],[9527,"Whoever strikes a whip unjustly will be retaliated against on the Day of Resurrection."],[9528,"\" bound=\"3710\" type=\"narrators\">Abdullah b. Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9529,"It would not please me to have the like of Uhud in gold, which I spend in the cause of Allah, and then die while I still have a dinar of it."],[9530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, from the punishment of Hell, and from the false messiah."],[9531,"When one of you wakes up, he should not dip his hand into his vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[9532,"I saw Ibrahim ﷺ as if he were your companion, and I saw Musa ﷺ tall and dark-skinned, and I saw 'Isa ﷺ reddish with curly hair."],[9533,"Ibn 'Abbas once addressed us after 'Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people began calling out to him: 'The prayer, the prayer.' Among the people was a man from Banu Tamim. Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Are you teaching me the Sunnah, woe to you? I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combining Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha'.' He said: 'Then I met Abu Hurayrah, and he concurred with him.'"],[9534,"When a believer is at the point of death, the angels come to him with a piece of silk containing musk and bundles of basil. His soul is drawn out as a hair is drawn out of dough, and it is said: 'O tranquil soul, come out content and well-pleasing to your Lord, to the mercy of Allah and His honor.' When his soul departs, it is placed upon that musk and basil, the silk is folded over it, and it is taken up to 'Illiyyin. When a disbeliever is at the point of death, the angels come to him with a coarse haircloth containing a live coal. His soul is violently torn out, and it is said: 'O wicked soul, come out wrathful and with wrath upon you, to the humiliation of Allah and His punishment.' When his soul departs, it is placed upon that live coal, the haircloth is folded over it, and it is taken down to Sijjin."],[9535,"When a believer is at the point of death, the angels of mercy come to him with a white piece of silk and say: 'Come out content and well-pleasing to your Lord, to the mercy of Allah, sweet basil, and a Lord who is not angry.' It comes out with the sweetest scent of musk, so much so that they pass it to one another, smelling it, until they bring it to the gate of heaven. The angels there say: 'How sweet is this scent that has come to you from the earth.' Whenever they bring it to a heaven, they say the same to them, until they bring it to the souls of the believers. They are more delighted with it than one of you is with his absent loved one when he arrives. They ask: 'What did so-and-so do?' They say: 'Leave him until he rests, for he was in the distress of the world.' When he recovers or rests, he says to them: 'Has he not come to you? He has died!' They say: 'He has gone to his mother, the Abyss.' As for the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him with a coarse haircloth and say: 'Come out wrathful and with wrath upon you, to the punishment of Allah and His anger.' It comes out with the foulest stench of a corpse, and they take him to the gate of the earth."],[9536,"Zurarah reported from Abu Hurayrah: Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah b. Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:"],[9537,"And 'Amr b. 'Ali narrated it to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ:"],[9538,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has pardoned my Ummah for what their souls whisper, as long as they do not speak of it or act upon it."],[9539,"If a woman spends the night forsaking her husband's bed, the angels curse her until he is pleased with her — or he said: until she returns."],[9540,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with some food, and he said: 'Put it in the low ground,' or he said: 'on the ground.'"],[9541,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when I see you, my eye is cooled and my soul is at ease, but when I do not see you, my soul is not at ease,' or words to that effect."],[9542,"I said to Abu Hurayrah: 'I have two sons. Will you narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by which our souls may be at ease concerning our deceased?' He said: 'Yes, their little ones are the small creatures of Paradise. One of them meets his father and takes hold of his garment — or he said: by his hand — just as I am taking hold of the edge of this garment of yours, and he does not stop until he brings him into Paradise.'"],[9543,"A man visited a brother of his for the sake of God while he was in another village, so God, Blessed and Exalted, stationed an angel on his path. The angel said, \"Where do you intend to go?\" He said, \"A brother of mine in this village whom I am visiting.\" The angel said, \"Does he owe you any favor that you are seeking to nurture?\" He said, \"No, I love him for the sake of God.\" He said, \"Then I am a messenger of God, Blessed and Exalted, to you: He loves you as you have loved him for His sake.\""],[9544,"Gold locusts were rained down upon Ayyub, and he began to pick them up. He said, \"O Ayyub, have I not granted you abundance?\" He said, \"O Lord, who can be satiated from Your mercy?\""],[9545,"Whoever has two wives and inclines more toward one of them than the other will come on the Day of Resurrection with one side of his body fallen."],[9546,"Sometimes the Prophet ﷺ would pat my shoulder and say: \"Love Banu Tamim, Abu al-Qasim, for by God, if you were granted the like of them...\""],[9547,"Whoever looks into a people's house without their permission and they gouge out his eye, there is no blood money for him and no retaliation."],[9548,"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer and then the sun rises should pray another one to complete it."],[9549,"Nothing is more honorable to God than supplication."],[9550,"Three men from those before you went out seeking provisions for their families, and rain overtook them, so they took refuge in a mountain or a cave, and a rock fell upon them - meaning it fell upon the mouth of the cave. They said to one another, \"The rock has fallen, the trail is obliterated, and no one knows your location except God, so call upon God by the most trustworthy of your deeds.\" One of them said, \"O God, if You know that I had two elderly parents, and I used to milk for them into their vessel. When I came to them while they were sleeping, I would stand upright until they woke up, whenever they woke up, for I disliked that the milk should turn while they slept. When they woke up, they would drink. O God, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us of this rock.\" He said, \"So a third of the rock moved.\" The second said, \"O God, if You know that there was a woman who pleased me, and I desired her, but she refused to yield to me until I made a payment for her. When she took the payment and her soul was at rest, I left her. O God, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us of this rock.\" He said, \"So a third of the rock moved.\" The third said, \"O God, if You know that I hired a laborer to work for me for a day, and he worked, then he came seeking his wages, and I gave him but he would not take them and was displeased, so I invested them for him until they became all the wealth. Then he came seeking his wages, and I said, 'Take all of this, and had I wished I would not have given him except his original wage.' O God, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us of this rock.\" He said, \"So the rock moved, and they went out walking.\""],[9551,"He cursed the women who imitate men among women, and the men who imitate women among men."],[9552,"\"Who will preserve a word or two or three from what God has obligated upon him, and act upon them and teach them?\" I said, \"I will.\" So I spread out my cloak, and he narrated to me until the speech of the Messenger of God ﷺ was finished, then I gathered it to myself. So I hope that I will not forget anything I heard from him."],[9553,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a cloud passed by. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do you know what this is?\" We said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"This is the cloud, and it is driven to a people of a land who do not worship Him\" - I think he said: \"and do not ask Him\" - \"Do you know what is above that?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"A restrained wave and a guarded roof. Do you know what is above that?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Above that is a sky. Do you know what is above that?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Above that is a sky. Do you know what is between them?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Between them is a distance of five hundred years\" - until he counted seven heavens, between each sky a distance of five hundred years - then he said, \"Do you know what is above that?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Above that is the Throne.\" And he said, \"Between them is what is between the two skies.\" And he said, \"Do you know what this is?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"This is the earth.\" He said, \"Do you know what is beneath it?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Between them is a distance of five hundred years.\" Then he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul\" - I think he said - \"if one of you, or if one of you were to work down to the seven earths, or in the seven earths, to the lowest, he would still end up with God.\" Or words to that effect, then he recited: \"He is the First and the Last, the Outward and the Inward\" - the verse."],[9554,"Hasten to good deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the private matter of one of you, the affair of the common people, and the beast of the earth."],[9555,"The women who seek khul' are the female hypocrites."],[9556,"al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9557,"A time will come upon people when they will consume riba; whoever among them does not consume it will be affected by its dust."],[9558,"Whoever departs from obedience and separates from the community and dies upon that, then it is a death of Jahiliyyah. And whoever goes out among my Ummah striking its righteous and its wicked, not sparing—or he said: not avoiding—any believer among them, nor fulfilling the covenant of those under protection, then he is not from me. And whoever is killed under a banner of partisanship, getting angry for the sake of tribalism, then his killing is a killing of Jahiliyyah."],[9559,"Sufyan—meaning al-Thawri—narrated to us, from Yunus b. 'Ubayd, from Ghaylan b. Jarir, from Ziyad b. Matar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, and the correct version is the hadith of Hammad b. Zayd."],[9560,"He is not from us who turns a woman against her husband, or a slave against his master."],[9561,"Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Isma'il b. Hakim narrated to us, from Yunus b. 'Ubayd, from 'Ali b. Zayd, from Anas b. Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9562,"The first thing for which the servant will be brought to account is the prayer. If it is complete, then fine; otherwise it is said: 'Does he have any voluntary prayers?' Then the obligatory prayer is completed from his voluntary prayers."],[9563,"The first thing for which the servant will be brought to account is his prayer. If it is sound, then he has succeeded and triumphed; but if it is deficient, then he has failed and lost."],[9564,"Thinking well of Allah is part of the excellence of worshiping Allah."],[9565,"If My servants were to obey Me, I would give them rain by night and bring forth the sun upon them by day, and I would not make them hear the sound of thunder."],[9566,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, prescribed the Friday prayer for those before us, but they differed concerning it, and Allah guided us to it. The people are followers of us in that: the Jews have Saturday, and the Christians have Sunday."],[9567,"From Abd al-Rahman b. Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. This hadith was narrated by Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and by Abu Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, similarly to it. It was also narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various routes, and from Hudhayfah and others, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9568,"From Abd al-Rahman b. Adam, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9569,"From Abd al-Rahman b. Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9570,"From Abd al-Rahman b. Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9571,"The prophets are paternal brothers; their mothers are different, but their religion is one. I am the closest of people to Isa b. Maryam ﷺ ; there was no prophet between him and me. He will come, and when you see him, recognize him: a man of medium height, between red and white, as if his head is dripping though no moisture touches it, between two slightly yellowish garments. He will break the cross, kill the pig, distribute wealth, abolish the jizyah, and destroy all religions except Islam. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will destroy the false messiah, the Dajjal, and security will be placed on the earth so that the lion grazes with the camels, the wolf with the sheep, and children play with snakes without harm. He will remain for forty years, then he will die and the Muslims will pray over him."],[9572,"I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah when a man from Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah passed by. They said: 'This is the wealthiest man of the Amir tribe.' He said: 'Bring him back to me.' They brought him back. He said to him: 'I have been told that you have much wealth.' He said: 'By Allah, I have a hundred reddish camels and a hundred dusky ones,' until he enumerated the colors of camels, herds of slaves, and tethered horses. Abu Hurayrah said: 'Beware of the camels' hooves and the sheep's cloven hooves.' He repeated that until the Amir man's complexion changed. He said: 'What is that, O Abu Hurayrah?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever has camels and does not pay their due in their time of strength and their time of ease — we said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their time of strength and their time of ease? He said: In their hardship and their ease — they will come on the Day of Resurrection as fat and as large as they ever were, and a flat, barren plain will be spread for them, and they will trample him with their hooves. Whenever the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him, in a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and then he will see his path. And if he has cattle and does not give their due in their time of strength and their time of ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection as fat and as large as they ever were, and a flat, barren plain will be spread for them, and they will trample him, every hoofed one with its hoof, and every horned one will gore him with its horn. Whenever the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him, in a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and then he will see his path. And if he has sheep and does not give their due in their time of strength and their time of ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection as fat and as large as they ever were, and a flat, barren plain will be spread for them, and every horned one will gore him with its horn, and every hoofed one will trample him with its hoof. Whenever the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him, in a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and then he will see his path.' They said: 'O Abu Hurayrah, what is the due of camels?' He said: 'He gives the noble one, grants the abundant milk one, lends the stallion for breeding, and gives milk to drink.'"],[9573,"From al-Ghadani, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith. We do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Qatadah. More than one narrator reported it from Qatadah, so we limited ourselves to those we heard. It was also narrated from Abu Hurayrah through the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, something similar. And it was narrated from the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9574,"Hasten to do good deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the private affair of one of you, and the affair of the general public."],[9575,"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."],[9576,"When you disagree about the road, make its width seven cubits."],[9577,"People will be gathered in three groups: a third riding on animals, a third on their feet, and a third on their faces."],[9578,"The example of one who hears wisdom but only acts upon its worst part is like a man who came to a shepherd and said: 'Give me a sheep from your flock as a sacrifice.' He said: 'Go and take hold of the best-eared sheep.' He went and took hold of the ear of the flock's dog."],[9579,"The Beast will come forth with the seal of Solomon and the staff of Moses; it will brighten the faces of the believers with the staff, and mark the noses of the disbelievers with the seal, so much so that the people of the hamlet will gather and one will say, 'O believer,' and another will say, 'O disbeliever.'"],[9580,"I arrived in Madinah and stayed with Abu Hurayrah for a month. He told me that he fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and said, 'Where is the Dawsī lad?' It was said, 'There he is, in a corner of the mosque, ill.' He came and placed his hand on me and said something kind. Then he said, 'If Shayṭān causes me to forget something in my prayer, let the men say subḥān Allāh and the women clap.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in prayer, and behind him were two rows of men and one row of women, or two rows of women and one row of men, and he prayed without forgetting anything. When he finished his prayer, he praised and extolled Allah, then said, 'To proceed: Does one of you perhaps lock his door, draw his curtain, and conceal himself with Allah's concealment, then go out and say, \"I did such-and-such with my wife, and I did such-and-such with my wife?\"' A full-breasted slave girl stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, they do that, and they (women) do that.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Shall I tell you the likeness of that?' They said, 'What is its likeness?' He said, 'The likeness of a male Shayṭān who meets a female Shayṭān in a road and mates with her while people watch.' Then he said, 'Indeed, a woman should not touch a woman, nor a man a man, except for a child and a parent.' Then he said, 'The perfume of men is one whose scent is apparent but its color is not, and the perfume of women is one whose color is apparent but its scent is not.'"],[9581,"Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[9582,"Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, wonders at people who will be led to Paradise in chains."],[9583,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[9584,"Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah."],[9585,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Hajj: is it every year? I think he said, 'If I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory, only a few would perform it.'"],[9586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought some dates from the charity dates. When they were set down, al-Ḥasan took a date from them and his saliva flowed. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Kikh! Do you not know that the family of Muḥammad ﷺ do not eat charity?'"],[9587,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to the soul, 'Come out.' It says, 'I will not come out except reluctantly.' He says, 'Come out, even if you dislike it.'"],[9588,"Regarding this verse, 'By the witness and the witnessed' (Q 85:3), he said: The Day of ʿArafah and the Day of Friday, and the Promised Day is the Day of Resurrection."],[9589,"I never witnessed a battle alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he allotted me a share of its spoils, except on the day of Khaybar, for it was exclusively for the people of Ḥudaybiyyah. Abu Hurayrah and Abu Mūsá had arrived between Ḥudaybiyyah and Khaybar."],[9590,"The Angel of Death used to come to people openly. He came to Moses son of ʿImrān ﷺ , and Moses struck him and gouged out his eye. The Angel of Death ascended and said, 'O Lord, Your servant Moses did such-and-such to me, and were it not for his honor with You, I would have made it hard for him.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said, 'Go to Moses, My servant, and give him the choice between placing his hand on the back of an ox, and for every hair covered by his palm he will have one year, and between dying now.' He came to him and gave him the choice. Moses said, 'What after that?' He said, 'Death.' He said, 'Then now.' He said, 'So he took his soul, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, restored his sight—meaning to the Angel of Death—and after that he came to people in concealment.'"],[9591,"When he sits between her four parts and then strives hard upon her, ghusl becomes obligatory. In the narration of Matar: even if he does not ejaculate."],[9592,"And 'Abd al-Quddus b. Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Karim narrated to us; 'Amr b. 'Asim narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah and Matar, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar report. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording from the Prophet ﷺ except by Abu Hurayrah with this chain."],[9593,"If one of them knew that when he attends the prayer he would have a limb of a fat sheep, he would do it, and the reward he attains is greater than that."],[9594,"The deaf man who cannot hear anything, the fool, the very old man, and a man who died in the interval [between prophets] will be brought before Allah. The deaf man will say: 'My Lord, Islam came and I could not hear anything.' The fool will say: 'My Lord, Islam came and I could not understand anything.' The one who died in the interval will say: 'My Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me.' - Abu Bakr al-Bazzar said: 'And I forgot what the fourth one said.' - He said: He will take their covenant to obey Him, then He, Blessed and Exalted, will send to them: 'Enter the Fire.' By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, if they entered it, it would have been coolness and peace for them."],[9595,"Whoever enters it, it will be coolness and peace for him; and whoever does not enter it will enter the Fire."],[9596,"If the Children of Israel had taken the least cow, it would have sufficed them, or it would have sufficed on their behalf."],[9597,"He forbade fasting on Friday."],[9598,"Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and neither had evidence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to cast lots for the oath, whether they liked it or not."],[9599,"If you knew, or they knew - Abu Qatan was uncertain - what is in the first row, there would be nothing but drawing lots."],[9600,"Zakariyya ﷺ was a carpenter."],[9601,"There was a black woman who used to sweep the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ missed her and asked about her, and they said she had died. He came to her grave and prayed over her."],[9602,"The most mendacious of people are the dyers and the goldsmiths."],[9603,"O Abu Hurayrah, what do you say about this: “The phantom of Salma and a phantom that conceals—the two phantoms wandered and stirred up illness. They drove a plump one and a prominent heel. She stood showing you fear of being cut off.” Abu Hurayrah said: “We used to recite this at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not find fault with it.”"],[9604,"Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise from beneath the Throne? It is that you say: “There is no power except with Allah.” Allah says: “My servant has submitted and surrendered.”"],[9605,"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise from beneath the Throne? “There is no power except with Allah.”"],[9606,"Whoever loves to find the taste of faith, let him love a person whom he loves only for the sake of Allah."],[9607,"From Amr b. Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah from Ash'ath b. Abi al-Sha'tha' with this chain except Yazid b. Harun, and he was not corroborated in it. In my view, the correct one is the hadith of Abu Balj from Amr b. Maymun from Abu Hurayrah."],[9608,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[9609,"A woman is not to be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor the paternal aunt in addition to her brother's daughter; and a woman is not to be married in addition to her maternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt in addition to her sister's daughter; and the elder is not to be married in addition to the younger, nor the younger in addition to the elder."],[9610,"From al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[9611,"Whoever prays over a funeral will have a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried or its judgment is concluded will have two qirats."],[9612,"Adam and Moses argued. Moses said: “You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit, and you brought us out of Paradise.” He said: “And you are Moses whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech. Do you find that written against me before I was created?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “So Adam defeated Moses in argument.”"],[9613,"Three things I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning Banu Tamim; after them I will never hate Banu Tamim. A'ishah had an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Ishmael. Some captives were taken from Banu al-Anbar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O A'ishah, if it pleases you to fulfill your vow, then set free a slave from these.” So he made them from the descendants of Ishmael. Some camels from the zakat livestock of Banu Sa'd were brought, and when he saw their smell, he said: “This is the livestock of my people.” So he made them his people. And he said: “They are the fiercest of people in fighting during the great battles.”"],[9614,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no servant coincides while asking Allah for good in it except that He gives it to him."],[9615,"… the Prophet…"],[9616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of pebbles."],[9617,"Indeed, the people of the highest ranks are seen by those below them just as the shining star is seen in the horizon of the sky; and indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among them and are excellent."],[9618,"A riding animal may be ridden when it is pledged, with its expenses; and the milk of a milking animal may be drunk when it is pledged; and upon the one who drinks and rides is its expense."],[9619,"I am the first from whom the earth will be split open. I will raise my head and there will be Musa b. Imran. I do not know whether he is among those whom Allah exempted or whether he raised his head before me."],[9620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided dates among his companions, and some of them would pair them up. The Prophet ﷺ forbade pairing them up except with the permission of his companion."],[9621,"If there were in the mosque a hundred thousand or more, and then a man from the people of Hell were to breathe, he would burn them."],[9622,"My intimate friend advised me with three things: that I not sleep except upon odd (witr), fasting three days of every month, and performing the ritual bath on Friday, or two rak'ahs of al-Ḍuḥa."],[9623,"He would hear the muezzin giving the call to prayer and would say: 'I bear witness to it with every witness, and I carry it on behalf of every denier.'"],[9624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to sleep upon odd (witr), to perform the ritual bath on Friday, and to fast three days of every month."],[9625,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person nor for one who is strong and healthy."],[9626,"Indeed charity is not lawful for a rich person nor for one who is strong and healthy."],[9627,"A man will soon wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades and that he had not taken charge of any of the people's affairs."],[9628,"The destruction of the Arabs will be at the hands of young boys—or he said, youths—from Quraysh. Marwan said, 'What evil youths those are.'"],[9629,"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near."],[9630,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but God.' If they say, 'There is no god but God,' their blood and their wealth become inviolable except by its right, and their reckoning is with God."],[9631,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees."],[9632,"In Friday there is an hour in which a person does not ask God for anything but He gives it to him."],[9633,"Shall I not teach you a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? 'There is no power and no strength except with God.'"],[9634,"Kumayl b. Ziyad al-Nakha'i, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9635,"He did not pray the forenoon prayer except once."],[9636,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray until his feet became cracked. It was said to him about that, and he said, 'Should I not be a grateful servant?'"],[9637,"Yahya b. Fudayl narrated to us, al-Hasan b. Salih narrated to us, from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. I do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Nu'man b. 'Abd al-Salam, nor from al-Hasan b. Salih except Yahya b. Fudayl."],[9638,"Every sermon that does not contain the testimony of faith is like a leprous hand."],[9639,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[9640,"The one-eyed Dajjal, the Messiah of misguidance, will emerge toward the east, in a time of discord among the people and division. He will reach whatever Allah wills him to reach of the earth in forty days—Allah knows best what their measure is. The believers will meet severe hardship. Then ʿĪsā b. Maryam ﷺ will descend from heaven and lead the people in prayer. When he raises his head from his bowing, he will say: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him. Allah has killed the Dajjal and the believers have prevailed.' I swear that the Messenger of Allah, Abū al-Qāsim, the truthful, the one who is believed, ﷺ said: 'It is true, and indeed it is near, for everything that is coming is near.'"],[9641,"Indeed this fire of yours and every fire that is kindled—or they kindle it—is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell."],[9642,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand. The best charity is what leaves one self-sufficient. Begin with those you support."],[9643,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Shayṭān cannot take my form."],[9644,"The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like (Mount) Uḥud, and his thigh is like (Mount) Wariqān, and the thickness of his skin is forty cubits."],[9645,"The most fearful thing I fear for you is the two hollow organs: the mouth and the private part."],[9646,"The dream is one part of forty-six, or forty-seven, parts of prophethood."],[9647,"Two rivers are from Paradise: the Nile and the Euphrates."],[9648,"9659 9650 - Ibrāhīm b. Mālik narrated to us, Yaḥyā b. Zakariyyā narrated to us, from Idrīs, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9649,"You will never encompass the people with your wealth, but what will encompass them from you is a cheerful face and good character."],[9650,"Indeed the first of people to perish will be Fāris (Persia), and on their heels will be the Arabs."],[9651,"None of you should pray while he has any impurity on him, or while he is suppressing the need to relieve himself."],[9652,"9663 9654 - Ahmad b. Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us; a man whom he named narrated to us - his name has slipped my mind at this time - from Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad, from Dawud and Idris, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9653,"Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla."],[9654,"Beware of swearing oaths, for it sells the goods but wipes out the blessing - I think he said: the blessing."],[9655,"The praised station is intercession."],[9656,"Do you know what admits people into Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Fear of Allah and good character. Do you know what most admits people into the Fire? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The two hollow organs: the mouth and the private parts."],[9657,"I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him? He said: O Allah, yes."],[9658,"Bad luck is in the woman, the house, and the horse."],[9659,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the fourth forever until the Hour arises."],[9660,"Sa'd came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Indeed, in the face of Sa'd there is good. He said: O Messenger of Allah, Chosroes has perished. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The first people to perish are the Persians and the Arabs."],[9661,"When the Prophet ﷺ stood for the night prayer, he would sometimes lower his voice and sometimes raise it."],[9662,"O son of Adam, devote your heart to Me and I will fill your heart with richness and suffice your need; but if you do not devote your heart to Me, I will fill your heart with poverty and will not suffice your need."],[9663,"We were with Abu Hurayrah in the mosque, then the muezzin called the adhan, and a man left the mosque. Abu Hurayrah said: 'As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[9664,"Abu Bakr ؓ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, command me with something I should say when I enter upon morning and when I enter upon evening.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my self and from the evil of Shaytan and his shirk. Say it when you enter upon morning and when you enter upon evening and when you take to your bed.'"],[9665,"From 'Amr b. 'Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know that 'Amr b. 'Asim narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."],[9666,"The destruction of my Ummah will be at the hands of young boys from Quraysh."],[9667,"From Malik b. Zalim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And we do not know that Malik b. Zalim narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."],[9668,"Whoever prays over a funeral will have a qirat, and whoever waits until it is buried will have two qirats. Ibn 'Umar objected to that, so they sent to 'A'ishah and asked her, and she said: 'He has spoken the truth' — meaning Abu Hurayrah."],[9669,"We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection."],[9670,"There is no Kisra after Kisra, and no Caesar after Caesar. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the cause of Allah."],[9671,"None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds. They said: 'Not even you?' He said: 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and grace from Him.'"],[9672,"The guest has three (days of) right upon the one he stays with. Whatever is beyond that is charity. And the guest must depart, so as not to cause sin upon the people of the house."],[9673,"Everything has a purest essence, and the purest essence of prayer is the first takbir."],[9674,"From Abu Alqama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9675,"He used to seek refuge from five: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the trial of the false messiah."],[9676,"When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him."],[9677,"9688 9679 - Ibrahim b. Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, Yunus b. Khabbab narrated to us, from Abu Alqama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9678,"And Ibrahim b. Yusuf narrated to us, Ubayd Allah al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Yunus b. Khabbab, from Abu Alqama, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9679,"No servant seeks refuge from the Fire seven times but the Fire says: O Allah, protect him from me; and he does not ask for Paradise seven times but Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to me, or a word similar to it."],[9680,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me. The commander is a shield. When he says 'Allahu Akbar', say 'Allahu Akbar'; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate. If he prays sitting, then pray sitting. When he says, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him', say, 'O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise.' When he recites 'nor of those who go astray,' say 'Amen'. If the people of heaven coincide with the people of earth in their saying, the servant is forgiven his previous sins."],[9681,"When one of you gets up at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[9682,"And Amr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9683,"When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. And when the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in a single sandal."],[9684,"And al-Hasan b. Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated it to us, Muhammad b. Abi Ya'qub al-Karmani narrated to us, Hassan b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban b. Taghlib narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ in a similar manner."],[9685,"When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in a single sandal until he repairs his strap."],[9686,"Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I am a blind man and my house is far, and I have a guide who does not accommodate me. Is there any concession for me? He said: Do you hear the call? He said: Yes. He said: I find no excuse for you. Or he said: concession."],[9687,"Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether related to him or not, he and I will be in Paradise like these two — and he joined his two fingers. And whoever provides for three daughters, he will be in Paradise, and he will have the reward of a mujahid in the path of Allah, fasting and standing in prayer."],[9688,"There are no two Muslims who lose three children and seek reward for them, except that they will be a barrier for them between them and the Fire."],[9689,"Whoever loses three children who have not reached puberty, he will enter Paradise. They said: And two? He said: And two."],[9690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted me with three things that I should not abandon: the Duha prayer, that I should not sleep except after praying Witr, and that I should fast three days of every month."],[9691,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once, and he said: Whoever spreads out his garment, I will not narrate a hadith — I think he said: except that he will memorize it — so I spread out my garment. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated many hadiths, and I gathered my garment, and I did not forget anything from his hadith."],[9692,"When a servant draws near to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a handspan, He draws near to him a cubit."],[9693,"Four things from the affairs of Jahiliyyah that people will not abandon: defaming lineages, wailing, and their saying: We were given rain by such-and-such a star."],[9694,"Four things from the affairs of Jahiliyyah that people will not abandon: wailing, reviling lineages, their saying: We were given rain by such-and-such a star, and contagion. A camel got mange and infected a hundred. Who infected the first one?"],[9695,"No one is wronged by an injustice and leaves it except that Allah increases him in honor by it. And give charity, for charity never decreases wealth, but rather increases it."],[9696,"When the servant of one of you brings his food, let him seat him and eat with him; if he does not do so, let him give him — meaning a morsel."],[9697,"When the verse 'And warn your closest kindred' was revealed, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood and called out: O Banu Ka'b b. Lu'ayy, save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu 'Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire. I do not possess for you anything from Allah, except that you have kinship ties which I will maintain."],[9698,"Musa b. Talha, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[9699,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a rabbit he had roasted, and he brought with it its condiment and seasoning. He placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ refrained and did not eat, but he ordered his companions to eat. The Bedouin also refrained and did not eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What prevents you from eating?\" He said: \"I fast three days of every month.\" He said: \"If you are fasting, then fast the white days (ayyam al-ghurr).\""],[9700,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about the muezzin: \"He is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing that hears him responds for him, and the one who attends the prayer has twenty-five good deeds written for him.\""],[9701,"The best sacrificial animal is a jadha' (one-year-old) sheep."],[9702,"We came to Abu Hurayrah to greet him, and we said: \"Narrate to us.\" He said: \"I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for three years. There were never years in which I was more intelligent than in those, nor more desirous that I should retain what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. And I saw him saying with his hand: 'Shortly before the Hour, you will fight a people whose sandals are hair, and you will fight a people with red faces and small eyes, as if they were layered shields. By Allah, for one of you to go out in the morning, gather firewood on his back, sell it, and seek help from it and give charity from it, is better for him than coming to a man and asking him, who may give him or withhold from him. That is because the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. And the breath of a fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk.'\""],[9703,"From Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[9704,"The imam is a guarantor. If he prays standing, then pray standing; if he prays sitting, then pray sitting; and when he says takbir, then say takbir."],[9705,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah after Hunayn — I think he said: by three (days) — and on the night I intended to enter Madinah, a servant of mine got lost from me. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O night, how long it is and how wearisome, yet from the land of disbelief it delivered me.\" While I was speaking to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, there was my servant."],[9706,"The ruin of my nation will be at the hands of young men from Quraysh."],[9707,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it was praised well, so he said: \"It has become due.\" Another funeral passed by him and it was criticized, so he said: \"It has become due.\" Then he said: \"You are witnesses over one another.\""],[9708,"A man called Abu Ma'qil came to me and said: \"Write.\" So I wrote: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. I heard Abu Hurayrah say: 'My close friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined me to fast three days of every month, to sleep on witr (odd-numbered prayer), and to glorify Allah in the forenoon (Duha).'\""],[9709,"A man asked him: \"Are you the one who forbade people from fasting on Friday?\" He said: \"No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, I did not forbid it. Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Friday, unless one fasts a day before it or a day after it.\""],[9710,"And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals."],[9711,"And this hadith was narrated to us by Muhammad b. al-Muthanna: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from a man of Balharith, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[9712,"And that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day prayed the dawn prayer, then said: 'This is the wolf; and what is the wolf! It has come to you asking you to give it or to make it a partner in your wealth.' A man threw a stone at it, and it passed by or turned away, howling."],[9713,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'So-and-so fasts during the day, stands in prayer at night, but harms her neighbors.' He said: 'There is no good in her; she is among the people of the Fire.' And it was said: 'So-and-so performs the prescribed prayers and does not harm her neighbors.' He said: 'She is among the people of Paradise.'"],[9714,"The restraint of faith is assassination; no believer assassinates."],[9715,"Indeed, the deceased hears the tapping of their sandals when they turn away from him — meaning, departing."],[9716,"The thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer; faith is more precious to Allah than that."],[9717,"Concerning the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: 'On the Day We shall call every people by their imam,' he said: 'One of them will be called and given his book in his right hand; his body will be extended for him; his face will become white; a crown of radiant pearl will be placed on his head; and he will go to his companions, who will see him from afar and say: O Allah, bring us this one and bless us in him. He will come to them and say: Rejoice, for each man among you has the like of this. As for the disbeliever, his face will become black and his body will be extended for him; his companions will see him and say: We seek refuge in Allah from this one, or from the evil of this one; O Allah, do not bring him to us. He will come to them and they will say: O Allah, disgrace him. He will say: May Allah distance you, for each man among you has the like of this.'"],[9718,"Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it; and if it is obscured for you, then complete the count, and do not precede the month."],[9719,"We have not seen the like of the Fire: its fleer slept; and we have not seen the like of Paradise: its seeker slept."],[9720,"When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. — I think he said: one of them with earth."],[9721,"The two 'umrahs expiate what is between them, and the accepted hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[9722,"Whoever performs hajj to the House and does not engage in obscenity or wickedness, returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[9723,"Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not engage in obscene speech or commit sin, returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[9724,"There is no abandonment [of a Muslim] beyond three [days]."],[9725,"Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is able-bodied and strong."],[9726,"The pilgrim is forgiven, and the one for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness."],[9727,"The invitation on the first day is a Sunnah, on the second is a kindness, and on the third is ostentation and seeking reputation."],[9728,"When a man invites his wife to his bed, she should respond even if she is on a camel saddle. If he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until morning."],[9729,"There are three to whom Allah will not speak: the lying ruler, the arrogant poor person, and the adulterous old man."],[9730,"If a foreleg were gifted to me, I would accept it; and if I were invited to a shoulder, I would respond."],[9731,"He never criticized any food: if he desired it, he ate it; and if he did not desire it, he left it."],[9732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog and the earnings of a prostitute."],[9733,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper."],[9734,"Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not engage in obscene speech or commit sin, returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[9735,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: “Whoever loves me, let him love them both.”"],[9736,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: “O God, I love them both, so love them both.”"],[9737,"The best of the children of Adam are five: Noah, Abraham, Jesus, Moses, and Muhammad; and the best of them is Muhammad ﷺ, and he prayed for all of them together."],[9738,"Indeed the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and indeed the Muslim eats in one intestine."],[9739,"Whoever leaves behind pasture, it belongs to God and His Messenger; and whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to his heirs."],[9740,"He forbade that a woman ask for the divorce of her sister."],[9741,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade meeting caravans (before they reach the market), a muhājir selling on behalf of a bedouin, a man outbidding his brother, and (he forbade) leaving animals unmilked (to deceive the buyer) and artificial bidding."],[9742,"Indeed God is good and accepts only what is good; and indeed God, blessed and exalted, commanded the believers with what He commanded the messengers, saying: “O messengers, eat from the good things and act righteously,” and He said: “O you who believe, spend from the good things you have earned.”"],[9743,"Whoever lives in the desert becomes coarse, whoever follows game becomes heedless, and whoever follows the ruler is put to trial."],[9744,"A man was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ for him to pray over him, and it was said to him: “He left behind two dinars or three.” He said: “Two cauterizations or three.”"],[9745,"The quickest of the Arab tribes to perish is Quraysh; and the Hour will not come until a woman passes by a sandal and says: “This is the sandal of a Qurashī.”"],[9746,"He performed ablution and began to make the water reach close to his armpits; I said to him (about that), and he said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘The ornament reaches from ablution the places of purification.’”"],[9747,"I will certainly drive people away from my basin just as a camel-herder drives [strange] camels away from his watering-place. They said: O Messenger of God, will you recognize us? He said: Yes, my community will come to me with gleaming foreheads and limbs from the traces of this ablution, a mark that no one besides you among the nations has. By Him in whose hand is my soul, it is farther than from Aylah to ʿAdan—meaning his basin ﷺ—its vessels are more numerous than the stars, and it is sweeter than honey and colder than snow. No servant will drink a single drink from it and then thirst as long as the heavens and the earth endure. Some of you will surely be turned away from it, and I will say: My companions? Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."],[9748,"There is no deficiency in prayer or in the greeting of peace."],[9749,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should honor his guest. It was said: O Messenger of God, what is honoring the guest? He said: Three days; whatever is beyond that is charity. And whoever believes in God and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. And treat women well, for woman was created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its upper part. If you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, you will not see crookedness in it. So treat women well."],[9750,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited in the two rakʿahs of dawn: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is God, the One.”"],[9751,"I asked my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, for permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me. And I asked Him for permission to visit her grave, and He permitted me."],[9752,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his uncle: Say: There is no god but God; I will testify for you with it on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Were it not that the women of Quraysh would reproach me, saying that only despair drove him to it, I would delight your eye by affirming it. Then God, Exalted, revealed: “Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but God guides whom He wills.”"],[9753,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the mosque, he said: Hand me the garment, O ʿĀʾishah. She said: I am not praying. He said: It is not in your hand. So she handed it to him."],[9754,"He said: Who among you began this day fasting? Abū Bakr ؓ said: I. He said: Who among you fed a poor person today? Abū Bakr said: I. He said: Who among you visited a sick person today? Abū Bakr said: I. He said: Who among you attended a funeral today? Abū Bakr said: I. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: These have never come together in a man in a single day except that he enters Paradise."],[9755,"There is no man who calls his wife to his bed and she refuses to respond to him, but the One in heaven is angry with her until he is pleased with her."],[9756,"It was said: O Messenger of God, will you not invoke God against the polytheists? He said: I was only sent as a mercy, and I was not sent as a punishment."],[9757,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have married a woman from the Anṣār. He said: Did you look at her? For in the eyes of the Anṣār there is something. He said: Yes. He said: For how much did you marry her? He said: For four ūqiyyahs. The Prophet ﷺ said: For four ūqiyyahs?! It is as if you are carving silver from the side of this mountain."],[9758,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when we heard a loud thud. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do you know what this is? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a stone—or a rock—that fell for seventy autumns in the Fire of Hell, and this is when it settled, or reached its bottom."],[9759,"A man stayed late with the Prophet ﷺ, then returned to his family and found his children had been put to sleep. He swore he would not eat, but then changed his mind and said to his wife, 'Wake the children.' So he ate. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him atone for his oath and do that better thing.'"],[9760,"When death descends upon a believer and he sees what he sees, he wishes his soul would come out, while Allah loves to meet him. The believer's soul is taken up to heaven, and the souls of the believers come to him and ask him about their acquaintances among the people of earth. If he says, 'I left so-and-so in the world,' that pleases them. But if he says, 'So-and-so has died,' they say, 'He was not brought to us.' The believer is made to sit in his grave and is asked, 'Who is your Lord?' He says, 'My Lord is Allah.' Then it is said, 'Who is your Prophet?' He says, 'My Prophet is Muhammad ﷺ.' Then it is said, 'What is your religion?' He says, 'My religion is Islam.' A door is opened for him in his grave, and it is said, 'Look at your place.' Then he sees the grave, and it is as if it had been only a short nap. But if he was an enemy of Allah, death descends upon him and he sees what he sees, and he never wants his soul to come out, while Allah hates to meet him. When he is seated in his grave, it is said to him, 'Who is your Lord?' He says, 'I do not know.' It is said, 'You did not know.' A door of Hell is opened for him, then he is struck with a blow that every creature hears except the two heavy ones (jinn and humans). Then it is said to him, 'Sleep as one bitten sleeps.' I said to Abu Hurayra, 'What is manhush?' He said, 'One whom beasts and snakes bite.' Then his grave closes in on him."],[9761,"A man took his son near the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do you have mercy on him, O so-and-so?' He said, 'Yes, by Allah, I do have mercy on him.' He said, 'Allah is more merciful to him than you.'"],[9762,"No servant says 'There is no god but Allah' except that the gates of the heavens are opened for it until it reaches the Throne, so long as major sins are avoided."],[9763,"Instruct your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah."],[9764,"I shall recite to you—or, gather so that I may recite to you—a third of the Qur'an. Then he recited to them: 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[9765,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded those who overslept the dawn prayer to pray after the sun had risen."],[9766,"People will be gathered—meaning on the Day of Resurrection—and will come to Adam, saying, 'O our father, ask for the opening of the Garden for us.' He says, 'Did anything but the sin of your father Adam expel you from the Garden? I am not the one for that. Go to Ibrahim, the friend of his Lord.' Ibrahim says, 'I am not the one for that. I was only a friend from behind, behind. Go to the one to whom Allah spoke directly.' They come to Musa ﷺ , and he says, 'I am not the one for that. Go to the Word of Allah and His Spirit, 'Isa ﷺ .' He says, 'I am not the one for that. Go to Muhammad ﷺ.' They come to Muhammad ﷺ and he intercedes. Then the bridge is laid down, and the first of you pass like lightning. I said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom.' Then like the wind, and birds, and the running of men. Your Prophet is on the bridge, saying, 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety,' until the people cross. A man comes who can only crawl. On the sides of the bridge are hanging hooks that seize those they are commanded to seize. Some are scratched and saved, and some are piled up in the Fire."],[9767,"Allah caused those before us to miss the Friday prayer. The Jews have Saturday and the Christians Sunday. We are the last in this world, but the first on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven before all creatures."],[9768,"I was among seventy of the people of the suffa, and none of them had a cloak. They would tie their lower garments around their necks; some reached halfway down their shins, and some reached their ankles, indicating with his hand out of dislike that his private parts be seen."],[9769,"The earth will vomit out the pieces of its liver. The thief will pass by and say, 'For this my hand was cut off.' The murderer will come and say, 'For this I killed.' The one who severed kinship will come and say, 'For this I severed my kinship.' Then they will leave it and not take anything from it."],[9770,"The certainty has been seen by the first believer, and it is said to the wicked—and he mentioned a word—and there will not remain any creature on earth but it will enter his body."],[9771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a man to pray over him, and it was said to him: He left behind two dinars or three. He said: Two cauterizations or three."],[9772,"Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad rub his face in the dirt among you? They said: Yes. He said: By al-Lat and al-'Uzza, if I see him doing that I will tread on his neck and rub his face in the dust. He said: One day it was said to him: There he is praying. He came, asserting he would do to him what he said. He said: The people were not surprised except that he was retreating on his heels and guarding himself with his hands. The people came to him and said: What is the matter with you, O Abu al-Hakam? He said: Between me and him is a trench of fire, and terror, and wings. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If he had come near me, the angels would have snatched him limb by limb. He said: So God sent down upon His Prophet: Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays? Have you seen if he is upon guidance or enjoins righteousness? Have you seen if he denies and turns away? Does he not know that God sees? No! If he does not desist, We will surely drag him by the forelock - a lying, sinful forelock. Then let him call his associates; We will call the guards of Hell. He said: The angels said: No! Do not obey him. He said: And he was commanded with what he was commanded."],[9773,"Three whom God hates: a lying king, an arrogant poor person, and a miserly rich person."],[9774,"Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not have intercourse nor commit sin returns as his mother gave birth to him."],[9775,"Whoever asks people for their wealth, it is as if he asks for burning coals, so let him take little or much."],[9776,"O God, forgive those who shave their heads. He said on the third time: And those who shorten their hair."],[9777,"Who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation? Let him create a mosquito."],[9778,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house of reeds."],[9779,"The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its place of setting. When it rises - I think he said - no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."],[9780,"Two words, light on the tongue, heavy on the scale, beloved to the Most Merciful: Glory be to God and with His praise."],[9781,"Beware of continuous fasting - he said it three times. They said: But you fast continuously? He said: Which of you is like me in that? I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. So take on of deeds what you are able to do."],[9782,"O God, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient."],[9783,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to travel, he would say: O God, You are the companion in travel and the deputy among the family. O God, accompany us with success – this is how I think it was, or similar wording – and return us with protection. O God, contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us. O God, I seek refuge with You from the hardships of travel and the gloom of the return."],[9784,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us: Jarir and Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us, from Talq b. Mu'awiya, from Abu Zur'a, from Abu Hurayra."],[9785,"Whoever has three of his children die – I think he said before reaching puberty – the Fire will not touch him."],[9786,"Intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell, so delay the prayer in intense heat."],[9787,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[9788,"Al-Husayn b. Mahdi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yusuf narrated to us: Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'a, from Abu Hurayra."],[9789,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, two rak'ahs of duha, and fasting three days of every month."],[9790,"A prophet among the prophets camped under a tree and an ant stung him, so he ordered the tree to be burned – meaning with all the ants on it. Then God revealed to him: 'Why not just one ant in place of one ant?'"],[9791,"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[9792,"He used to wipe over the leather socks."],[9793,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us: Jarir – meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Hamid – narrated to us, from 'Umara b. al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'a, from Abu Hurayra."],[9794,"I will not cease to love Banu Tamim after three things I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ saying about them. He said: 'They are the severest of my community against the Dajjal.' 'A'isha had to free a slave from the descendants of Ishmael, and captives from them arrived, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Free this one – meaning one of them – for she is from the descendants of Ishmael.' And their charity came, and he said: 'This is the charity of our people.'"],[9795,"The best charity is that you give it while you are healthy and miserly, hoping for life and fearing poverty, and do not delay until when it reaches the throat, and you say, 'For so-and-so is such-and-such,' when it has already become for so-and-so."],[9796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remain silent for a little while between the takbir and the recitation. I said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what do you say during your silences between the takbir and the recitation?' He said, 'I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You have distanced the East from the West; O Allah, purify me from my sins as a white garment is purified from filth; O Allah, wash me from my sins with snow, hail, and cold water.'"],[9797,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has taken it upon Himself for the one who goes out as a mujahid in the path of Allah, nothing drives him out except faith in Me and belief in My Messenger, that He is a guarantor for him: either to admit him to Paradise or to return him to his home from which he set out, attaining whatever he may attain of reward or spoils."],[9798,"I am the master of the people on the Day of Resurrection. When his companions saw that, he said, 'Will you not say: How?' They said, 'How, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The people will stand before the Lord of the Worlds; the caller will make them hear, and the sight will pierce them, and the sun will draw near to their heads, its heat will intensify upon them, and its nearness will be hard on them. They will reach extreme distress and anguish from what they are in. They will come to Adam ﷺ and say, \"O Adam, you are the father of mankind; Allah created you with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit, and commanded the angels and they prostrated to you. Will you not intercede for us with your Lord? Do you not see the evil we are in?\" Adam will say, \"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has become angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after. He commanded me with a command and I disobeyed Him and obeyed Satan; He forbade me from eating from the tree and I disobeyed Him. I fear that He may cast me into the Fire. Go to someone other than me; myself, myself.\" They will go to Noah ﷺ and say, \"O Noah, you are the Prophet of Allah and the first one sent; intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the evil we are in?\" Noah will say, \"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has become angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after. I had a supplication and I supplicated against my people and they were destroyed. I fear that He may cast me into the Fire. Go to someone other than me; myself, myself.\" They will go to Abraham ﷺ and say, \"O Abraham, you are the close friend of Allah; the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth have heard of your friendship. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the evil we are in?\" He will say, \"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has become angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after, and I fear that He may cast me into the Fire.\" And he mentioned his saying about the star, \"This is my Lord,\" and his saying, \"Rather, the biggest of them did it,\" and his saying, \"Indeed, I am ill.\" \"Go to someone other than me; myself, myself.\" They will go to Moses ﷺ and say, \"O Moses, you are the Prophet of Allah; Allah chose you with His messages and spoke to you directly. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the evil we are in?\" Moses ﷺ will say, \"My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has become angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after. I killed a soul for which I was not commanded, and I fear that He may cast me into the Fire. Go to someone other than me; myself, myself.\" They will go to Jesus ﷺ and say, \"O Jesus, you are the Prophet of Allah, His word and His spirit which He cast to Mary. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the evil we are in?\" He will say, \"My Lord has become angry today with an anger the like of which He has never been angry before and will never be angry after, and I fear that He may cast me into the Fire.\" Umarah said, \"I do not know if he mentioned a sin.\" \"Go to someone other than me; myself, myself.\" They will come to me and say, \"You are the Messenger of Allah and the seal of the prophets; Allah has forgiven you your past sins and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord.\" I will go and come beneath the Throne and fall prostrate to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted. He will raise me to a station that no one before me has stood and no one after me will stand. He will say, \"O Muhammad, intercede and you will be interceded; ask and you will be given.\" I will say, \"My ummah, O Lord, my ummah.\" He will say, \"O Muhammad, admit those who have no reckoning from the right gate, and they share with the people in the other gates. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, what is between the two sides of the gate is as far as the distance between Busra and Makkah, or Makkah and Hajar.\" Umarah said, \"I do not know which of them he said.\" This hadith is not known to be narrated from the Prophet ﷺ with this wording except from this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Umarah except Jarir."],[9799,"A son of Fatimah ؓ became gravely ill, so she sent for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to call him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Go back, for to Him belongs what He takes and to Him belongs what He leaves, and everything has an appointed term by measure.\" When he was near death, she sent for him, and he said to us, \"Get up.\" When he sat down, he began reciting: \"Then why, when it reaches the throat, and you are at that time looking on\" until the boy passed away. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ filled with tears. Sa'd said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you weep while you forbade weeping!\" He said, \"It is only mercy, and Allah shows mercy to the merciful among His servants.\""],[9800,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who among people is most deserving of my good companionship?\" He said, \"Your mother.\" He said, \"Then who?\" He said, \"Then your mother.\" He said, \"Then who?\" He said, \"Then your father, then the next nearest and the next nearest.\""],[9801,"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three: adultery after marriage, disbelief after Islam, or killing a soul intentionally, in which case he is killed for it."],[9802,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up for the second unit - meaning in prayer - he would begin with \"All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the Worlds\" and he did not pause."],[9803,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is?\" Mu'adh said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"His right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you know what the servants' right upon Allah is if they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him?\" Mu'adh said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He ﷺ said, \"Their right upon Him is that He admits them to Paradise.\" Mu'adh said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go to the people and give them glad tidings?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No, leave them so that they may act.\""],[9804,"Jibril sat with the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, this angel has not descended since the day he was created. When he descended, he said, 'O Muhammad, I am a messenger from your Lord to you, to choose between your Lord making you a king or a servant messenger.'\" Jibril said to him, \"Humble yourself before your Lord, O Muhammad.\" He said, \"A servant messenger.\""],[9805,"Jibril ﷺ came to me last night and admitted me into Paradise, and showed me the gate from which I and my ummah will enter. Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"I wish I had been with you, O Messenger of Allah.\" He took him by the hand and said, \"You and I are the first of my ummah to enter from it.\""],[9806,"A time will surely come upon people when a man will go to his brother's grave, place his hand on the grave, and say, 'Would that I were in your place, and that I had not seen what I have seen.'"],[9807,"I was commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but God, and they establish the prayer and give the zakat. If they do that, their blood and their property become inviolable for me, and their reckoning is with God."],[9808,"I said: O Messenger of God, what is lawful for one of us from the property of his brother? He said: He may eat and not carry away, and he may drink and not carry away."],[9809,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and there we saw camels with their udders tied with tree bark. We dispersed among them and started milking them. Then a call was made among us, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, praised God and extolled Him, and then said: These camels belong to a Muslim household, and in their udders is their sustenance. So do not milk them except with the permission of their owners. A man said: Then what is allowed for one of us from the property of his brother if he is so commanded? He said: He may eat and drink and not carry away."],[9810,"The day of Ashura is the festival of a prophet who was before you, so fast it yourselves."],[9811,"O God, I am only a human being; I become angry as humans become angry, and I become pleased as humans become pleased. So any servant whom I have cursed not deserving it, make it a prayer and a reward for him, or a prayer and a mercy."],[9812,"Nothing remains of prophethood except the righteous dream, and it is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[9813,"Every Muslim has to give charity every day. A man said: Who can do that, O Messenger of God? He said: Your removing something harmful from the road is charity; your directing a man to the road is charity; your visiting the sick is charity; your following a funeral is charity; your commanding what is right and forbidding what is wrong is charity; and a Muslim's returning the greeting to a Muslim is charity."],[9814,"The example of knowledge that does not benefit is like the example of a treasure that is not spent in the way of God."],[9815,"When one of you prays, he should not perform a voluntary prayer in the same place; let him move forward or backward, or to his right or his left. And perhaps he said: Is one of you unable to move forward?"],[9816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the earnings of a prostitute, the price of a dog, and the stud fee of a stallion. And Abu Hurayrah said: These are from my own knowledge."],[9817,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight. Whoever gives more, it is usury."],[9818,"Whoever accuses his slave of immorality while he is innocent of what he said, he will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said."],[9819,"Teach your children the prayer when they reach seven, and strike them for it when they reach ten, and separate them in the beds."],[9820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one of the two evening prayers—he said: My strongest assumption is that it was the noon prayer—then he went to a piece of wood in the mosque and placed his hands on it, one over the other. The swiftest of the people departed saying, 'The prayer has been shortened.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and they were too awed to speak to him. Then a man stood up—either short of hands or long of them—called Dhu al-Yadayn, and said, 'O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said, 'It was not shortened and I did not forget.' He said, 'Yes, you forgot.' So he said, 'Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken the truth?' They said, 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ led us in two rak'ahs, then gave the greeting, then pronounced the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and pronounced the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and pronounced the takbir."],[9821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the greeting."],[9822,"A man stood up to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said, 'Does every one of you find two garments?'"],[9823,"No one's deeds will save any of you. They said, 'Not even you, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Not even me, unless God envelops me with mercy and grace from Him.'"],[9824,"When time draws near, the dream of a Muslim will scarcely be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful—I think he said: in speech—and the dream of a Muslim is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. Dreams are of three kinds: among them is glad tidings from God, a dream of grief from Satan, and a dream from what a person tells himself. So if one of you sees what he dislikes, let him get up and pray, and not tell people about it. He loves the fetter and hates the shackle, and the fetter is steadfastness in religion."],[9825,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunya."],[9826,"Al-Husayn b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah. More than one narrator transmitted it from Ibn Sirin, and it was also transmitted from other than Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah."],[9827,"Aslam—may God grant it peace—and Ghifar—may God forgive it."],[9828,"People are mines. The best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam, if they gain understanding."],[9829,"He forbade two ways of dressing: that a man wrap himself in a single garment with no covering over his private parts, and that he wrap himself in the garment from below his elbows—I think he said: over his shoulder—and he forbade two types of sales: the touch sale and the toss sale."],[9830,"They used to forbid the toss sale and the touch sale."],[9831,"He forbade placing the hand on the waist, meaning in prayer."],[9832,"Sulayman b. Dawud had so many wives. He said: 'I will go around to them tonight, so that each woman among them will give birth to a boy who will fight in the cause of Allah.' He said: So he went around to them, but none of them conceived except one woman, and they say she gave birth to half a human being. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he had said \"if Allah wills\", every woman among them would have conceived a boy who would fight in the cause of Allah.'"],[9833,"If Aslam, Ghifar, and Muzaynah are better than the two allies - Asad and Ghatafan and Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah - then they have failed and lost."],[9834,"Do not call grapes 'karm'."],[9835,"The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is that which is given out of surplus wealth."],[9836,"Repentance will continue to be accepted as long as the sun does not rise from its west."],[9837,"Sa'id b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. And this hadith was narrated from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, by more than one narrator, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ except Ma'mar and Sa'id b. Zayd."],[9838,"Yahya b. Habib b. 'Arabi narrated to us, Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[9839,"Indeed, there is an hour on Friday during which no Muslim stands in prayer asking Allah for good but that He grants it to him. Then he gestured with his hand, indicating that it is short and belittling it."],[9840,"When one of you is invited, let him accept. If he is fasting, let him pray."],[9841,"The people of Yemen have come to you; they have the softest hearts. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[9842,"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[9843,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."],[9844,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, if a dog laps in it, is to wash it seven times, the first of which is with dust."],[9845,"Muhammad b. al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with a similar report."],[9846,"Do not curse time, for indeed Allah is time."],[9847,"If one of you points at his brother with a piece of iron, the angels curse him until he puts it down, even if he is his brother through his mother and father."],[9848,"He said: 'What do you consider a martyr among you?' They said: 'Being killed in the path of Allah.' He said: 'Then the martyrs of my nation would be few. Being killed is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and the woman whose child kills her is martyrdom.'"],[9849,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt, nor may a woman ask for the divorce of her sister in order to empty her plate."],[9850,"I was given the opening of speech, and I was aided by awe. While I was sleeping last night, I was brought the keys of the treasures of - I think he said - the earth. Abu Hurayrah said: 'So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed while you are taking from them.'"],[9851,"The Fire and Paradise disputed. The Fire said: 'The tyrants and the arrogant will enter me.' Paradise said: 'The weak among people and the lowly will enter me.' So He said to the Fire: 'You are My punishment; with you I afflict whomever I will.' And He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; with you I bestow mercy on whomever I will.' Then on the Day of Resurrection, it will be thrown into the Fire and it will say: 'Is there any more?' until He places His foot in it, and it shrinks and says: 'Enough, enough!'"],[9852,"Adam and Moses argued. Moses said: 'O Adam, you are the one whom Allah created with His hand, made to dwell in His Paradise, and to whom He made His angels prostrate, yet you drove people out of Paradise and made them wretched.' Adam said: 'You are Moses whom Allah chose with His speech and His messages, and to whom He sent down the Torah. Do you find in the Torah that it was written upon me before He created me?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'So Adam argued against Moses.'"],[9853,"One day they boasted in his presence and said: 'Are men more numerous in Paradise or women?' Abu Hurayrah said: 'Did not Abu al-Qasim ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the moon on the night of the full moon, then those who follow them will be like the brightest shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shanks can be seen from behind the flesh. And by the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no bachelor in it.\"'"],[9854,"The vessel is washed seven times, the first of which is with dust."],[9855,"When one of you comes to the prayer, let him not rush to it, but let him walk with tranquility and dignity. Let him pray whatever he catches and make up whatever he missed."],[9856,"He prostrated in 'When the sky has split' and said: 'One better than me prostrated in it; the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated in it.'"],[9857,"People will continue to question about knowledge until they say: 'This is God who created us, so who created God?' Abu Hurayra said: 'After the Messenger of God ﷺ two men asked me, and this is the third.'"],[9858,"People will continue to question about knowledge."],[9859,"Whoever buys an animal that has been left unmilked for some time, he milks it. If he is pleased with it, he keeps it; otherwise he returns it along with a saa' of dates."],[9860,"A man will meet his father on the Day of Resurrection and say: 'O father, will you obey me today, or will you benefit me today?' He will say: 'Yes.' He will take him by the hand and lead him until he brings him before God, Blessed and Exalted, while He is presenting the creation. He will say: 'O Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me.' So God, Blessed and Exalted, turns away from him. Then he says the same again, so God turns his father into a hyena, and he falls into the Fire. He says: 'Your father?' He says: 'I do not know you.'"],[9861,"The angels pray for one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer: 'O God, forgive him; O God, have mercy on him,' as long as he remains in his place of prayer waiting for the prayer."],[9862,"Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam, and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it, without any of their rewards being diminished."],[9863,"A man's messenger to another man is his permission."],[9864,"Al-Hasan b. Yahya narrated to us, Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. We do not know this hadith to have been narrated from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra except by Hammad b. Salama. Ibn Mahdi narrated it from Hammad, from Habib, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra. Amr b. Ali narrated it to us from Abd al-Rahman."],[9865,"The child belongs to the bed, and the stone is for the adulterer."],[9866,"9879 9870 - Al-Husayn b. Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9867,"None of you should urinate in standing water and then bathe from it."],[9868,"Do not leave the udders of camels and sheep unmilked."],[9869,"If a fly falls into the vessel of any of you, let him immerse it, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other a cure."],[9870,"Whoever eats out of forgetfulness, Allah has fed him and given him drink."],[9871,"He forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."],[9872,"A woman was forgiven who passed by a dog panting and gave it water."],[9873,"Those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and their opposition to their prophets. When I forbid you something, avoid it; and when I command you something, do it — I think he said — as much as you are able."],[9874,"Muhammad narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9875,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a young man appeared to us from a mountain pass. When he came near us, we said: If only this young man would devote his youth and strength to the cause of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard our words and said: Is the cause of Allah only for one who is killed? Whoever strives to support his parents is in the cause of Allah, and whoever strives to accumulate wealth is in the cause of Taghut."],[9876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given a choice between two matters but that he chose the easier of them."],[9877,"Three traits, whoever has them is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays, and claims to be a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his promise."],[9878,"Saying subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."],[9879,"Love your beloved moderately, for perhaps he may become your enemy one day; and hate your enemy moderately, for perhaps he may become your beloved one day."],[9880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people and removed his sandals. When the people noticed, they removed their sandals. When he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: \"The angel came to me and informed me that my sandals had some impurity. So when any of you comes to the mosque, let him turn over his sandals; if he sees something in them, let him wipe it off and then pray in them.\""],[9881,"\"Were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah, I would not have narrated to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then he recited: \"Indeed, those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance after We made it clear...\" — the verse."],[9882,"When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk in his normal manner; let him pray what he catches up with and make up what he missed."],[9883,"\"May one of us pray in a single garment?\" He said: \"Does every one of you have two garments?\""],[9884,"The angels pray for one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer: \"O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him,\" as long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[9885,"Ishaq b. Shahin narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9886,"He forbade urinating in stagnant water."],[9887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the afternoon prayers and said the salam after two rak'ahs. Then he went to a piece of wood lying across the mosque, and some people hurried out. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?\" He said: \"It has not been shortened, nor did I forget.\" He said: \"Indeed, you said the salam after two rak'ahs.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?\" They said: \"Yes.\" So he went back and prayed two rak'ahs, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam and prostrated twice."],[9888,"Ahmad b. Mansur b. Sayyar narrated it to us; Musa b. Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, Hisham, Yunus — I think he said — and Humayd and others, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9889,"And this hadith we do not know from the hadith of Yunus except through Hammad b. Salamah, except for a shaykh we had in Basra, who was called Abu Muhammad, a hadith scholar who narrated it from his father, from Mubarak b. Fadalah, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Bilal, and with him were piles of dates. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I am storing it.\" He said: \"Do you not fear that you will see steam from it in the fire of Hell? Spend, Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[9891,"He forbade prayer during three hours: when the sun rises until it has risen — meaning until it has ascended — when it sets until it sets, and halfway through the day."],[9892,"Part of the perfection of faith is good character."],[9893,"The women of Paradise: the marrow of their legs will be visible from behind the flesh."],[9894,"If a dog laps from a vessel, wash it seven times, the first or last of them with dust."],[9895,"The dream of a believing servant is one of forty parts of prophethood."],[9896,"When time draws near, the dream of a believer will hardly be false. I like fetters and dislike the iron collar."],[9897,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about praying in a single garment. He said, \"Does every one of you have two garments?\""],[9898,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been kept unmilked has the option of the two choices: if he returns it, he returns with it a saa' of dates, not wheat."],[9899,"If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he repairs the other."],[9900,"People follow Quraysh in good and evil."],[9901,"My father narrated to me, from 'Anbasah b. 'Abd al-Wahid, from Yunus b. 'Ubayd, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who raised it with similar wording. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except 'Anbasah, and we have only heard it from 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Fadl, from his father."],[9902,"Its inhabitants will be thrown into the Fire, and it will say, 'Is there more?' As for Paradise, from it will remain as much as Allah wills, and Allah will bring forth for it a creation and cause them to dwell in it."],[9903,"He forbade that a woman be married together with her paternal aunt or together with her maternal aunt."],[9904,"When one of you is invited, let him respond. Then if he wishes he may eat, and if he wishes he may refrain."],[9905,"Indeed on Friday there is an hour during which no Muslim servant asks Allah for good except that He grants it to him."],[9906,"No one's deeds will admit him to Paradise. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, unless Allah covers me with forgiveness and mercy from Him. Ibn Awn placed his palm on his head, describing the action of the Prophet ﷺ."],[9907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the two evening prayers. He prayed two rak'ahs, then said the salam, then stood by a piece of wood placed across the mosque. He placed his hand on it - and Ibn Awn described that he placed one of his hands over the other, and placed his hand on it as if he were angry. Then the hasteners among the people hurried out of the doors of the mosque, saying: The prayer has been shortened. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, but they were too awed by him to speak to him. Among the people was a man with long hands called Dhu'l-Yadayn. He said: O Messenger of Allah, was the prayer shortened or did you forget? He said: I did not forget, nor was it shortened. He said: Is it as Dhu'l-Yadayn says? They said: Yes. So he went back and prayed what he had omitted, then said the salam, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said the takbir, then prostrated."],[9908,"The people of Yemen have come to you; they have the most tender hearts. Faith is Yemeni, jurisprudence is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[9909,"A man called out to the Prophet ﷺ: May one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Does every one of you find two garments?"],[9910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the delegation of Abd al-Qays: I forbid you from using the dubba', the naqir, the muqayyar, the hantam, and the mazada that has been cut, but drink from your water-skin and tie its mouth."],[9911,"And Ziyad b. Yahya narrated to us: Nuh b. Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Nuh b. Qays."],[9912,"One of you continues to be in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer."],[9913,"The angels continue to pray for one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer."],[9914,"Repentance continues to be accepted as long as the sun has not risen from its west."],[9915,"Ma‘mar b. Sahl narrated to us, Yahya b. Khalifah b. ‘Uqbah narrated to us, from Ibn ‘Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9916,"Adam and Musa disputed. Musa said to him: “Are you Adam, who made people miserable and expelled them from the Garden?” Adam said: “Are you Musa, whom Allah chose with His messages and His words, and upon whom He sent down the Torah?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Did you find that He decreed that upon me before He created me?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then Adam defeated Musa in argument. Adam defeated Musa in argument” — three times."],[9917,"When the heat becomes intense, then cool down from the prayer, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[9918,"When one of you is invited, let him respond; and if he is fasting, let him pray."],[9919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out for prayer. When the rows were aligned, he gestured to them with his hand, then entered (his house) and returned with his head dripping, and led them in prayer."],[9920,"The angels curse any of you who points a piece of iron at his brother, even if he is his brother by father and mother."],[9921,"Let none of you urinate in stagnant water, or he forbade urinating in stagnant water."],[9922,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters the Garden."],[9923,"Do not curse time, for Allah is time."],[9924,"Do not call grapes ‘karm’, for the true karm is the Muslim."],[9925,"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is recorded for him. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is recorded against him; but if he does it, one evil deed is recorded against him."],[9926,"I said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me these things; I will never abandon them: fasting three days of every month, the major ablution on Friday, and not sleeping except on odd (prayers)."],[9927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Bilal while he had a heap of wealth — or he said, dates — and said: \"Spend, Bilal, and do not fear any decrease from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[9928,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt; and a man may not propose to a woman when his brother has already proposed to her, nor may he outbid his brother."],[9929,"When one of you comes to prayer, let him approach with tranquility; let him pray whatever he catches up with, and make up whatever he missed."],[9930,"Under every hair there is janabah (major ritual impurity), so wet the hair and cleanse the skin."],[9931,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[9932,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?\" He replied: \"Does every one of you find two garments?\""],[9933,"From 'Asim al-Ahwal and others, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[9934,"And 'Abdah b. 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Suwayd b. 'Amr narrated to us: Zuhayr b. Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah. And Hammad b. Salamah also narrated it: Abu Musa narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Hammad."],[9935,"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[9936,"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[9937,"He forbade the use of pitch-coated water-skins; and one of them said: \"earthenware jars,\" and the other said: \"pottery.\""],[9938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two afternoon prayers as two rak'ahs, then gave the salutation. The people who were in a hurry left, saying: \"The prayer has been shortened.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood by a pillar and placed his hand on it, and anger was recognizable in his face. Abu Bakr and 'Umar were among the people, but they were too awed to speak to him. Dhu al-Yadayn said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?\" He said: \"It has not been shortened, and I do not know that I forgot.\" He said: \"Indeed, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said to the people, and they said: \"He has spoken the truth.\" He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his place and prayed two rak'ahs, then gave the salutation to his right and to his left, and prostrated two prostrations, and sat for a little while. 'Asim said: Abu Qilabah said: Then he gave the salutation."],[9939,"When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come to it with tranquility. Let him pray whatever he catches up with and make up whatever he missed."],[9940,"The injury caused by an animal without a rider is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure the fifth is due."],[9941,"He was asked: 'May one of us pray in a single garment?' He said: 'Does every one of you have two garments?'"],[9942,"When time draws near, the dream of a Muslim will hardly be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful in speech. Dreams are of three kinds: a dream that is good news from Allah, a dream from what a person tells himself, and a dream that is a cause of grief from Satan."],[9943,"The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[9944,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said: 'Does every one of you have two garments?'"],[9945,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said: 'Does every one of you have two garments?'"],[9946,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said: 'Does every one of you have two garments?'"],[9947,"When a dog licks a vessel, it should be washed seven times, the last of which with dust."],[9948,"\" linkage=\"5183\" type=\"narrators_of_hadith\">Qatada, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ. As for the hadith of al-Hakam b. Abd al-Malik:"],[9949,"\" linkage=\"5183\" type=\"narrators_of_hadith\">Qatada, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9950,"\" linkage=\"5183\" type=\"narrators_of_hadith\">Qatada, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ"],[9951,"Qatada, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra."],[9952,"When time draws near, the dream of a believer will scarcely be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful in speech. Dreams are of three kinds: a dream from what a man talks to himself about, a true dream, and a dream of grief from Satan. I love the fetter and hate the iron collar. If one of you sees what he dislikes, let him get up and pray."],[9953,"Qatada, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra."],[9954,"And from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[9955,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-five, or of forty-some parts, of prophethood."],[9956,"Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one. Whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[9957,"Qatada, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[9958,"And he recited this verse: 'To Allah belong the most beautiful names, so call upon Him by them' [Quran 7:180]."],[9959,"Any fasting person who eats or drinks out of forgetfulness should not break his fast, for it is provision that Allah has provided him."],[9960,"If one of you eats while fasting, it is only Allah who has fed him and given him drink."],[9961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots on the day of Khaybar, and they were overturned, so we overturned them."],[9962,"When you come to prayer, come to it with tranquility. Whatever you catch, pray, and whatever you miss, make it up."],[9963,"Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."],[9964,"Indeed, Jahannam sought permission from its Lord to breathe twice every year; so the extreme heat is from its scorching blaze, and the extreme cold is from its intense frost."],[9965,"The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender-hearted. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[9966,"Paradise and the Fire argued. The Fire said: 'The arrogant will enter me.' Paradise said: 'None will enter me except the weak and the poor.' So Allah revealed to them: 'Each of you will be filled to capacity.' Then the people of the Fire will be thrown into it, and it will say: 'Are there any more?' People will be thrown into it, and it will say: 'Are there any more?' Then the Blessed and Exalted will place His foot upon it, and it will shrink. As for Paradise, much of it will remain, so Allah will create for it a new creation."],[9967,"Let none of you say 'my slave' or 'my slave girl'; let him say 'my young man' and 'my young woman'."],[9968,"Whoever buys a musarrah (an animal whose udder has been tied to accumulate milk) has the option; if he wishes he may keep it, but if he returns it, he must return with it a sa' of wheat, not of white wheat."],[9969,"The mine is jurbar (no liability for injury), the well is jurbar, and on buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[9970,"The mine is jurbar, the well is jurbar, and on buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[9971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn after the salam."],[9972,"Muhammad b. al-Aswad al-'Ammi narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Sadaqah narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ the story of Dhu al-Yadayn."],[9973,"Whoever sees me (in a dream), it is truly me, for Satan cannot take my form. And he used to say: 'Do not relate a dream except to a scholar or a sincere advisor.'"],[9974,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade two types of clothing and prayer at two times: prayer when the sun rises, meaning until it is high, and when it sets until it disappears; and a man wrapping himself in a single garment with nothing covering his private parts, and the other one I forgot."],[9975,"\" Linked=\"5183\" type=\"Narrators of the Hadith\">Qatada, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. And this Ibn Abi Nasr is, in my view, Nasr b. Tarif. His hadith was abandoned, and he was from the people of Basra, well-known."],[9976,"Wala' belongs to the one who paid the price."],[9977,"Ibrahim ﷺ did not lie except for three lies: two concerning Allah, the Exalted—his saying: “Rather, the eldest of them did this,” then he glanced at the stars and said, “Indeed, I am sick”—and he passed by a tyrant and his wife was with him, so he said: “Say he is my brother, for I am your brother in faith and you are my sister in faith. There is no believer on earth besides us.” He feared that if he said “my wife,” the tyrant would overpower him and take her."],[9978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn two prostrations—the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[9979,"\" Linked=\"5183\" type=\"Narrators of the Hadith\">Qatada, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. This hadith was narrated by Ibn Wahb, from 'Amr b. al-Harith. As for the hadith of Yahya b. Ayyub, from 'Amr b. al-Harith, we have not heard it except from Ibn"],[9980,"None of you should say 'my slave' or 'my slave girl', nor should a slave say 'my lord' or 'my lady'. The owner should say 'my young man' and 'my young woman', and the slave should say 'my master' and 'my mistress', for you are all slaves and the Lord is Allah."],[9981,"Do not curse time, for Allah is time."],[9982,"The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."],[9983,"The mouse is a Jew. Do you not see that it does not drink camel milk?"],[9984,"My beloved friend enjoined upon me three things that I will not abandon: the Witr before sleep, the ghusl on Friday, and fasting three days each month."],[9985,"With the boy there is an 'aqiqa, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."],[9986,"The illness of a believer is an expiation for his sins."],[9987,"There is no contagion (ʿadwā) and no evil omen (ṭiyarah)."],[9988,"Yaḥyā b. ʿAtīq, from Muḥammad, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the story of Dhū al-Yadayn that he prayed with them, then he mentioned similar to the ḥadīth of Ayyūb. We do not know of anyone who narrated the ḥadīth of ṭiyarah except ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Mukhtār, and no one narrated the story of Dhū al-Yadayn except Ḥammād, and no one narrated it from him except Sulaymān b. Ḥarb."],[9989,"None of you should urinate in stagnant water and then perform ablution from it."],[9990,"When one of you gets up at night, he should begin his prayer with two brief rakʿahs."],[9991,"If a dog licks the vessel of one of you, he should wash it seven times."],[9992,"A man said to him: O Messenger of God, may one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Does every one of you have two garments?"],[9993,"Whoever loves the Anṣār, God loves him."],[9994,"A prophet among the prophets alighted under a tree and an ant stung him, so he ordered that tree to be burned. Then God revealed to him: Why not just one ant?"],[9995,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the mouse. He said: A nation among the nations—or he said—it is said that a nation among the nations was lost, so I do not know whether it is that one or not. When camel milk is placed for it, it does not drink it."],[9996,"And Muḥammad b. ʿUmārah and Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Hayyāj narrated to us, saying: Qabīṣah narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Khālid, from Muḥammad, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ with something similar. This ḥadīth is well-known from Khālid, narrated by more than one from him."],[9997,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."],[9998,"Whoever points a piece of iron at his brother, the angels curse him."],[9999,"Do not curse time, for Allah is time."],[10000,"The people of Yemen have come to you: most tender of hearts. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[10001,"No one of you will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy and bounty from Him."],[10002,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya."],[10003,"Patience is at the first shock."],[10004,"No one's deeds will admit him to Paradise or save him from the Fire. They said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy and bounty from Him."],[10005,"Umar saw a silk garment being sold and said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you buy this garment and wear it for the delegations that come to you. He said: Silk is worn only by one who has no share in the Hereafter."],[10006,"When time draws near, the dream of a believer will hardly be false, and the most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful in speech."],[10007,"It is forbidden to place the hand on the hip during prayer."],[10008,"The five prayers, and one Friday prayer to the next, are expiations for what is between them."],[10009,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or maternal aunt, and a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her plate and get married, for she will have only what Allah has decreed for her."],[10010,"When one of you wakes from sleep, he should not dip his hand into his purification water until he pours over it and washes it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[10011,"The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh. They are the most compassionate toward a child in his infancy and the most careful with regard to a husband's property."],[10012,"He forbade the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays, when they came to him, from using [the vessels called] al-dubba', al-hantam, al-naqir, al-muzaffat, and the slit mazada. And he said: 'Soak [raisins] in your waterskin and tie it, and drink it sweet and good.' A man said: 'O Messenger of God, permit me [to use] something like this.' He said: 'Then you would make it like this,' and he described one larger than it."],[10013,"On Friday there is an hour during which no Muslim servant asks God for good but that He grants it to him, and he indicated with his hand how short that hour is."],[10014,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a town-dweller from selling on behalf of a desert-dweller."],[10015,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that caravans be met [on the way to the market]. Whoever meets one and buys something from it, its owner has the option [to cancel the sale] when he reaches the market."],[10016,"A good deed is [rewarded] ten times its like, and fasting is for Me and I shall reward it."],[10017,"If one of you forgets while fasting and eats or drinks, then it is God who has fed him and given him drink."],[10018,"The injury caused by livestock is without liability, the well is without liability, and on buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[10019,"When one of you is invited, let him accept. If he is fasting, let him pray."],[10020,"A man wore a fine garment and strutted in it, so the earth swallowed him, and he will sink into it until the Day of Resurrection."],[10021,"Do not curse time, for God is time."],[10022,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said: 'Does every one of you find two garments?'"],[10023,"He forbade the earnings of a female singer and the price of a dog."],[10024,"When one of you rises at night, let him begin his prayer with two brief rak'ahs."],[10025,"If you find only camel resting places and sheep pens, then pray in the sheep pens, and do not pray in the camel resting places."],[10026,"The purification of the vessel of one of you when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust."],[10027,"Indeed, Allah is Witr (Odd), and He loves the odd."],[10028,"The angels send blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer, so long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[10029,"Let none of you urinate in stagnant water and then bathe from it."],[10030,"Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied up (to accumulate milk) has the option for three days. If he returns it, he should return with it a saa' of wheat, not of inferior quality."],[10031,"He forbade two ways of wearing clothes: that a man wrap himself in a single garment with nothing covering his private parts, and that he cover himself in a single garment."],[10032,"It is near that whoever lives among you will meet 'Isa b. Maryam as a rightly-guided imam and a just judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig, and war will lay down its burdens."],[10033,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya."],[10034,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."],[10035,"\"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise.\""],[10036,"\"People are minerals (of different natures). The best of them in the pre-Islamic period are the best of them in Islam, if they acquire understanding.\""],[10037,"\"Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah will accept his repentance.\""],[10038,"\"Delay the prayer (until it becomes cooler). For the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Hell.\""],[10039,"\"When the call to prayer is given, none of you should hasten to it, but let him walk with tranquility. He should pray whatever he catches and complete what he missed.\""],[10040,"\"Indeed, the angels curse one of you if he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his brother from the same father and mother.\""],[10041,"\"None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds alone.\" They asked, \"Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Not even me, unless Allah covers me with His mercy.\""],[10042,"\"Either wear both of them, or take off both of them.\""],[10043,"\"There is no infectious disease (inherent) and no evil omen; but I like a good omen.\""],[10044,"\"A woman entered Hell because of a cat which she tied up: she neither fed it, nor gave it water, nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth.\""],[10045,"\"None of you should outbid his brother in a sale, nor propose to a woman already engaged to his brother.\""],[10046,"\"Saying Subhan-Allah (glorifying Allah) is for men, and clapping is for women.\""],[10047,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed one of the two evening prayers with them—and my stronger assumption is that it was Zuhr—then he went to a piece of wood at the front of the mosque and placed his hands on it, one over the other. He said: Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and they were in awe of him and did not speak to him. He said: The swift among the people left and said, “The prayer has been shortened! The prayer has been shortened!” He said: A man with long arms stood up—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call him Dhu al-Yadayn—and said, “O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?” He said, “I did not forget and the prayer has not been shortened.” He said, “Indeed, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken the truth?” They said, “Yes.” So he returned and prayed the remaining two rakʿahs with us, then he said the salam. Then he said the takbir while sitting, and prostrated like his prostration or longer. Then he raised his head and said the takbir. Then he prostrated like his prostration or longer. Then he raised his head and said the takbir."],[10048,"None of you should say ‘my slave’ or ‘my slave girl’; let him say ‘my young man’ and ‘my young woman.’"],[10049,"Sulayman ﷺ said, “I will go around tonight to one hundred women, and each woman among them will give birth to a boy who will strike with the sword in the path of Allah.” So he went around to one hundred women, and none of them gave birth except one woman; she gave birth to half a human being. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Had he made an exception, every woman among them would have given birth to a boy who would strike with the sword in the path of Allah.”"],[10050,"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near."],[10051,"Ibrahim ﷺ never lied except for three lies, all of them concerning Allah: his saying, “I am sick”; his saying, “Rather, the biggest of them did it”; and while he was traveling in the land of a tyrant among the tyrants, he stopped at a place. The tyrant was told, “A man has stopped here with a woman who is among the most beautiful of people.” So he sent to him and asked him about her. He said, “She is my sister.” When he returned to her, he said, “This man asked me about you, and I said that you are my sister. Indeed, today there is no Muslim other than me and you, and you are my sister, so do not give me the lie before him.” So she was taken to him. When he went to reach for her, he was seized. He said, “Supplicate Allah and I will not harm you.” So she supplicated for him and he was released. He went to reach for her and was seized similarly or more severely. He said, “Supplicate Allah for me and I will not harm you.” So she supplicated and he was released three times. Then he called the closest of his servants and said, “You have not brought me a human being; rather, you have brought me a devil. Take her out and give her Hajar.” So she came while Ibrahim was standing praying. When he sensed her, he finished and said, “What is the matter?” She said, “Allah has sufficed against the plot of the wrongdoer, and he gave her Hajar as a servant.”"],[10052,"Adam and Musa disputed. Musa said to him, “Are you Adam, who made people miserable and expelled them from Paradise?” Adam said to him, “Are you Musa, whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, and upon whom He sent down the Torah?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Did you find that Allah decreed that upon me before He created me?” He said, “Yes.” So Adam argued against Musa, peace be upon them both."],[10053,"It was argued in his presence—or mentioned in his presence—and he said, “What are you discussing?” They said, “Are men more numerous or women?” Abu Hurayrah said, “The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the moon on the night of its fullness, and those who follow them will be like the most brilliant shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives; the marrow of their shins will be seen from behind the flesh. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no bachelor in it.”"],[10054,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it fully; for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other is a cure."],[10055,"A woman may not give a woman in marriage, nor may a woman give herself in marriage; for the adulteress is the one who gives herself in marriage."],[10056,"Milk in a dream is [a sign of] the fitrah."],[10057,"Hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is charity."],[10058,"Supplicate Allah while you are certain of the response, and know that Allah does not accept supplication from a heedless, distracted heart."],[10059,"Whoever would be pleased to know what he has with Allah, let him know what Allah has with him."],[10060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while we were disputing about divine decree. He became angry until his face turned red, as if pomegranate seeds had been burst on his cheeks. Then he turned to us and said: “Is this what you have been commanded? Is this what I was sent to you with? Those before you perished only when they disputed about this matter. I adjure you not to dispute about it.”"],[10061,"None of you should say: “I cultivated,” but let him say: “I tilled.”"],[10062,"A prostitute saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue lolling from thirst. She took off her shoe and gave it water, so she was forgiven."],[10063,"Indeed, men will be carried away by questioning until they say: “Allah created the creation, so who created Him?”"],[10064,"I saw myself falling down between the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the room of Aisha, and I would faint from hunger. I would be carried, and I would say: “It is not that; it is only hunger.”"],[10065,"Clean earth is the ablution of a Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years. When he finds water, let him fear Allah and let it touch his skin, for that is better."],[10066,"People must stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will be snatched away."],[10067,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I love beauty, and I have been given of it such that I would not like anyone among people to surpass me—either he said: by a shoestring, or by a sandal strap. Is that arrogance?” He said: “No, but arrogance is rejecting the truth and despising people.”"],[10068,"The sandals of the Prophet ﷺ had two straps."],[10069,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise?” He said: “Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul. Indeed, a man will have intercourse with a hundred virgins in a single day.”"],[10070,"A man came to his family and saw their need. He went out to the desert, and his wife said: “O Allah, provide us with what we may grind, or what we may knead and bake.” Then suddenly the bowl was full of bread, the mill was grinding, and the oven was full of roasted sides. Her husband came and said: “Do you have anything?” She said: “Allah’s provision, or Allah has provided.” He lifted the mill and swept around it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If he had left it, it would have ground until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10071,"A man should not lie naked with a man, nor a woman with a woman."],[10072,"He prohibited plundering."],[10073,"The worst food is the food of a wedding feast: the rich are invited, and the poor are left out. Whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[10074,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man supplicating and pointing with his two fingers, so he grasped one of them, or said: 'One, one.'"],[10075,"He prohibited selling food until the two measures (sa's) have been applied to it, so that the increase belongs to its owner and the decrease is upon him."],[10076,"Speech about predestination has been deferred to the worst of people in the end of time."],[10077,"Whoever says: 'There is no god but God,' will enter Paradise."],[10078,"God's treasuries are speech: when He wills something, He says to it: 'Be,' and it is."],[10079,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited blowing into food and drink."],[10080,"\"Pay the alms, fast Ramadan, give the fifth of the spoils of war. And I forbid you four things: the gourd vessel, the green jar, the pitch-coated vessel, and the hollowed-out stump.\" They said: 'O Messenger of God, what do you know about the hollowed-out stump?' He said: 'It is the trunk that they hollow out and put dates and water into, and when its boiling subsides you drink it, until one of you strikes his cousin with the sword.'—and among the people was a man who had been wounded in that way; he began to hide it from the Messenger of God ﷺ—They said: 'O Messenger of God, in what shall we drink?' He said: 'In tanned waterskins whose mouths are tied.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, our land has many rats, and they leave us no tanned waterskins.' He said: 'Even if the rats eat them, even if the rats eat them'—twice or three times."],[10081,"He prohibited soaking (making nabidh) in the green jar, the pitch-coated vessel, and the gourd, and mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with ripe dates."],[10082,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited praying after dawn until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets. And he prohibited fasting on two days: the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice."],[10083,"Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[10084,"Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity."],[10085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to recite in our prayer the Opening of the Book and whatever is easy."],[10086,"Perform the Witr before morning comes."],[10087,"\"A man from my Ummah\"—or he said, \"from me,\" I think he said—\"with an aquiline nose and a broad forehead will rule, filling the earth with justice and equity as it was filled with tyranny and oppression. He will live thus\"—and he spread his left hand and two fingers of his right, the index and thumb, and held three fingers together."],[10088,"My Ummah will become two factions, between which a deviant group will emerge; the one of the two closest to the truth will undertake fighting them."],[10089,"We were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, discussing, one citing a verse and another citing a verse. He said: Then he said: \"What are these? For this were you sent? Or by this were you commanded? Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\""],[10090,"Suwayd narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas—similar to it. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated it except Suwayd Abu Hatim, the food merchant. He is Suwayd b. Ibrahim; Safwan b. 'Isa and a group narrated from him, and there is no harm in him. 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Mubarak is trustworthy, a Basran."],[10091,"\"And whoever turns his back to them that day\"—he said: It was revealed on the day of Badr."],[10092,"It was revealed on the day of Badr: \"And whoever turns his back to them that day.\""],[10093,"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it is good and sufficient; but whoever performs the full bath, the full bath is better."],[10094,"He used to combine the two prayers while traveling."],[10095,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, what drink is lawful for us? He said: Do not drink from naqir. They said: What is naqir? He said: A palm trunk hollowed out, in which nabidh is made. Nor from dubba, nor hantam... And upon you (is to use) water-skins with their mouths tied shut. Upon you (is to use) water-skins with their mouths tied shut."],[10096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with truffles in his hand and said: These are from manna, and they are a cure for the eye."],[10097,"When one of you wakes at night and wakes his wife, and they pray two rak'ahs together, they will be recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember Allah much."],[10098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man reciting Surah al-Kahf. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ, he fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the gathering with which I was commanded to keep myself patiently."],[10099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while a man was reciting Surah al-Hijr - or Surah al-Kahf - and he fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the gathering with which I was commanded to keep myself patiently with them."],[10100,"No people sit remembering Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, but the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, mentions them among those with Him."],[10101,"I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, from a single vessel."],[10102,"I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel. He would begin and wash what had touched him, then perform wudu as for prayer, then run his fingers through his hair twice, then pour water over his head three times, then pour the remaining water over his body."],[10103,"Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet ﷺ - similarly. This hadith was narrated by Ayyub and Ubayd Allah, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ubayd Allah except al-Mu'tamir. We did not hear it except from Muhammad b. Amr, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub. It is well-known from Aisha."],[10104,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have istihadah (non-menstrual bleeding) and do not become pure; should I abandon the prayer? He said: That is not menstruation; that is only a vein. When the menstrual period comes, abandon the prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray."],[10105,"He used to make the two rak'ahs of dawn brief."],[10106,"A boy was brought to the Prophet ﷺ and he urinated in his lap, so he followed it with water."],[10107,"\"And do not recite [too] loudly in your prayer or [too] quietly\" - she said: It was revealed regarding supplication."],[10108,"A garment from the clothes of Syria, called dhawāt al-khayl, was gifted to us, and I made it into a curtain. She said: When he came and saw it, he tore it down - meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[10109,"\"Eat ripe dates with unripe dates, for Satan grieves when he sees the son of Adam eating them and says: The son of Adam has lived until he ate the old with the new.\""],[10110,"The Prophet ﷺ heard sounds and said: \"What are these sounds?\" They said: \"The palm trees - they are pollinating them.\" He said: \"If they did not do it, it would be fine.\" So they refrained from it, and it turned into poor-quality dates. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If it is something of your worldly affairs, then it is your concern; and if it is something of your religious affairs, then it is to me.\""],[10111,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."],[10112,"Hind bt. ʿUtba said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man and does not give me what suffices me and my child, unless I take from him without his knowledge.\" He said: \"Take what suffices you and your child in a reasonable manner.\""],[10113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ruqya, saying: \"O Allah, remove the affliction, Lord of the people; none removes the harm except You.\""],[10114,"When the prayer is established and the evening meal is brought near, then eat, then pray."],[10115,"Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham b. ʿUrwa, from his father, from ʿAʾisha. (This appears to be only a chain, not a matn.)"],[10116,"When the evening meal is placed and the prayer is established, then begin with the evening meal."],[10117,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel. He would begin and wash what had touched him, then perform his ablution for prayer, then pass his fingers through his head twice, then pour water over his head three times, then pour the remaining water over his body."],[10118,"A slow, deliberate killing (qatl al-ṣabr) does not pass by any sin except that it erases it."],[10119,"Do not seek breastfeeding from a foolish woman, for milk transmits inheritance."],[10120,"Bilal came to the Messenger of God ﷺ during his illness and said: The prayer, O Messenger of God. He said: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aisha said: O Messenger of God, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; when he stands in your place, he will weep. He said: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She repeated, and he said: You are like the companions of Yusuf."],[10121,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'a: When you enter ihram, say: My place of release is where You detain me."],[10122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during his illness: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. I said to Hafsa: Say: When Abu Bakr stands, the people will not hear him due to weeping. Hafsa said that to him, and he said: You are like the companions of Yusuf. Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer."],[10123,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ married me, they fattened me up but I did not gain weight, until they fattened me with cucumber and fresh dates, and I gained the best weight."],[10124,"Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aisha - similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha except Muhammad b. Ishaq."],[10125,"Marry suitable matches."],[10126,"Khawla bt. Hakim came to me, and she was married to Uthman b. Maz'un. The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed her disheveled appearance and said: O Aisha, how disheveled Khawla looks! She said: A woman with no husband; he fasts by day and prays by night, so she is like one without a husband, and she has neglected and ruined herself. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Uthman b. Maz'un and said: Are you averse to my sunna? He said: No, by God, but I seek your sunna. He said: I sleep and pray, I fast and break my fast, and I marry women. Fear God, O Uthman, for your family has a right over you, your eyes have a right over you, and your self has a right over you. So fast and break your fast, pray and sleep."],[10127,"When he heard the muezzin, he would say: And I, and I."],[10128,"Someone came to me while I was at al-Aqiq and said: You are in a blessed valley."],[10129,"No harm for a woman who stays between two houses of the Ansar or stays with her parents."],[10130,"Excellent condiment is vinegar."],[10131,"No house is left destitute if it has dates."],[10132,"He would give one taslim."],[10133,"What is wrong with any of you that he does not take two garments for his Friday prayer other than his work clothes?"],[10134,"The likeness of a woman is like a rib; if you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you enjoy it, you enjoy it while it has crookedness."],[10135,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the bed."],[10136,"Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid."],[10137,"The people used to depart - and he mentioned a word - so it was revealed: 'Then depart from where the people depart.'"],[10138,"He used to pray five rak'ahs at night."],[10139,"Aflah b. Abi al-Qu'ays came asking permission to enter upon me, but I refused to allow him. He said, 'I am your paternal uncle.' I said, 'It was the woman who suckled me, not the man.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and I told him, so he said, 'He is your paternal uncle, so let him enter upon you.'"],[10140,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in three white Suhuli garments of cotton, with no shirt and no turban among them."],[10141,"Safiyyah was among the chosen ones."],[10142,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[10143,"He used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night."],[10144,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aisha."],[10145,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is established, begin with the evening meal."],[10146,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform wudu' as he did for prayer—meaning, in the ghusl for janabah."],[10147,"He only alighted at al-Abtah—meaning the Messenger of God ﷺ—to make his departure easier."],[10148,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of God, I suffer from istihadah; should I abandon the prayer?\" He said: \"That is only a vein. When the menstruation comes, abandon the prayer, and when it departs, perform ghusl and pray.\""],[10149,"No caution avails against decree, but supplication avails—I think he said—as long as the decree has not descended. And supplication encounters affliction, and they wrestle with each other until the Day of Resurrection."],[10150,"Regarding His saying: \"And do not recite [too] loudly in your prayer or [too] quietly,\" she said: \"It was revealed concerning supplication.\""],[10151,"Gentleness was never present in a people except that it benefited them, nor was harshness present in a people except that it harmed them."],[10152,"I said: \"How is it that all your wives have kunyahs?\" So give me a kunyah—I think he said—so he gave me the kunyah Umm 'Abd Allah."],[10153,"A group of people raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes."],[10154,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer."],[10155,"And Ahmad b. Aban narrated it to us, from al-Darawardi, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah - as a mawquf report."],[10156,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not interpret anything from the Quran except certain verses that Gabriel taught him."],[10157,"Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aishah."],[10158,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj as ifrad."],[10159,"The Prophet ﷺ was using the tooth stick while two men were with him, one of them older than the other. God revealed to him regarding the virtue of the tooth stick that he should give it to the elder."],[10160,"When the polytheists were defeated on the day of Uhud with a defeat known among them, a caller shouted: 'Where are the servants of God?' He said: Then their front ranks returned and fought with their rear ranks. Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman looked and saw his father, so he said: 'My father, my father.' She said: By God, they did not stop until they killed him. Hudhayfa said: 'May God forgive you.' Urwa said: That remained in Hudhayfa until he met God."],[10161,"O Aishah, every Prophet has a close disciple (hawari), and my close disciple is al-Zubayr."],[10162,"Salma, the freedwoman of the Messenger of God ﷺ and wife of Abu Rafi', came and said: 'He beats her.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abu Rafi': 'What is the matter between you and her?' He said: 'She annoys me, O Messenger of God.' She said: 'By God, O Messenger of God, I do not annoy him with anything. But he broke wind while praying, and I said to him: O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the Muslims that if one of them passes wind, he should perform ablution. So he got up and beat me.' She said: The Messenger of God began to laugh and said: 'O Abu Rafi', she only commanded you to do good.'"],[10163,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness are for any addition or omission."],[10164,"That the Prophet ﷺ set up a pulpit for Hassan b. Thabit to satirize the polytheists from it."],[10165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bought a camel from a Bedouin for a wasq of pressed dates. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked for dates but did not find them. The Bedouin objected and shouted: 'What treachery!' The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O enemy of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for the one who has a right has a say.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Khawla bt. Hakim and said: 'Tell her: I bought from this Bedouin a camel for a wasq of pressed dates and did not find them with my family. So lend me a wasq of pressed dates for this Bedouin.' She responded to him. When the Bedouin took possession, he returned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: 'Have you received it?' He said: 'Yes, you have fulfilled and been good.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The best of people are those who fulfill and are good.'"],[10166,"When he ate food, his hand did not go beyond what was in front of him. But when dates were brought, his hand moved about."],[10167,"When the servant says, 'O Lord, O Lord,' four times, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, says: 'I am here, My servant. Ask and you shall be given.'"],[10168,"When the deceased dies, leave him alone."],[10169,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a woman from shaving her head."],[10170,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, his daughter Zaynab set out from Makkah with Kinana — or the son of Kinana. Some people went after her and Habbār b. al-Aswad caught up with her. He kept thrusting at her camel with his spear until it threw her off, and she miscarried and bled. She became a source of contention between Banu Hashim and Banu Umayya. Banu Umayya said, 'We have more right to her,' because she was married to their cousin Abu al-ʿĀṣ. She was with Hind bt. ʿUtba b. Rabīʿa, and Hind would say to her, 'This is because of your father.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zayd b. Ḥāritha, 'Will you go and bring Zaynab?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Take my ring and give it to her.' Zayd went and kept being discreet until he met a shepherd and asked, 'For whom do you tend?' He replied, 'For Abu al-ʿĀṣ.' He asked, 'Whose sheep are these?' He replied, 'They belong to Zaynab bt. Muḥammad.' He walked with him a little, then said, 'Would you like me to give you something to give to her, and not mention it to anyone?' He said, 'Yes.' So he gave him the ring. The shepherd went and brought his sheep in and gave the ring to her. She recognized it and asked, 'Who gave you this?' He said, 'A man.' She said, 'Where did you leave him?' He said, 'At such-and-such a place.' She waited until nightfall, then went out to him. When she came to Zayd, he said to her, 'Ride in front of me on the camel.' She said, 'No, but you ride in front of me.' So he rode and she mounted behind him until they arrived. The Messenger of Allah used to say, 'She is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted because of me.' This reached ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn, who went to ʿUrwa and said, 'What is this report I heard that you narrate, diminishing Fāṭima's right?' ʿUrwa said, 'By Allah, I would not like to have all that is between the east and the west and to diminish any right that belongs to Fāṭima. But after this, I will never narrate it again.'"],[10171,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own hands using al-dharīra (a kind of perfume) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, for the state of being out of ihram and upon entering ihram, and when he stoned the Jamra on the Day of Sacrifice before performing the circumambulation of the House."],[10172,"Indeed Buṭḥān is upon one of the pools — a pool of Paradise."],[10173,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Should a woman perform ghusl if she has a wet dream and sees semen?' ʿĀʾisha ؓ said to her, 'May your hands be soiled!' The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Leave her alone. From what else does resemblance come? When her fluid prevails over the man's, the child resembles his maternal uncles; and when the man's fluid prevails over hers, the child resembles him.'"],[10174,"No affliction befalls the believer, not even a thorn prick, except that it removes — or expiates — some of his sins."],[10175,"Whoever comes to Jumuʿa should perform ghusl."],[10176,"Whoever humiliates a friend of Mine has declared war on Me. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than performing what I have made obligatory upon him. And My servant continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts until I love him. When I love him, I become his eye with which he sees, his ear with which he hears, his hand with which he strikes, his heart with which he reasons, and his tongue with which he speaks. If he asks Me, I will surely give him, and if he seeks refuge in Me, I will surely grant him refuge. I have not hesitated in anything I do as I hesitate in taking the soul of My believing servant, for he hates death and I hate to hurt him."],[10177,"Whoever abandons Jumuʿa three times, his heart is sealed."],[10178,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that those killed in battle be dragged to the pit and thrown into it — except for Umayya b. Khalaf, whose body swelled and filled his armor. They tried to pull him out, but he disintegrated, so they left him and threw earth and stones over him. When they were thrown into the pit, the Messenger of Allah stood over them and said, 'O people of the pit, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to people who are dead?' He said, 'They have come to know that what I promised them is true.' ʿĀʾisha said, 'People say, \"They have heard what you said,\" but it is only, \"They have come to know.\"'"],[10179,"I recited to Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid b. Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet ﷺ said something similar. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know anyone who narrated it in full except Yazid b. Ruman, and some of it has been narrated from other sources."],[10180,"To you, Angel of the Mountains. Then the Angel of the Mountains called me and greeted me and said: O Muhammad, Allah has heard the words of your people and how they responded to you. He has sent me to you so that you may command me as you wish. If you wish, I will crush them between the two mountains. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Rather, I hope that Allah will bring forth from their loins those who worship Allah alone and do not associate anything with Him."],[10181,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people after He has given it to them, but He takes it away by the death of scholars. Whenever a scholar dies, the knowledge he had goes with him, until there remain people who do not know, and they go astray and lead others astray."],[10182,"No affliction befalls a Muslim except that Allah expiates his sins through it, even a thorn that pricks him."],[10183,"He would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity, then dawn would overtake him while he was still in that state in Ramadan, without having had a wet dream. Then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[10184,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came and sat before the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have slaves who betray me, lie to me, and disobey me. I insult them and beat them. How will I be recompensed regarding them? He said: Your punishment and their sins will be weighed. If your punishment was less than their sins, you will have a reward. If your punishment was equal to their sins, then it is even, nothing for you or against you. If your punishment was more severe than their sins, then they will be avenged from you on the Day of Resurrection. The man began to wail and weep before the Prophet ﷺ. He said: What is the matter with you? Do you not recite the Book of Allah: 'And We shall set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection' [Quran 21:47]? The man said: O Messenger of Allah, then they are free."],[10185,"The virtue of prayer with siwak over prayer without siwak is seventy times greater."],[10186,"Two rak'ahs with siwak are better than seventy rak'ahs without siwak."],[10187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would test the women during the pledge of allegiance by reciting this verse to them: 'When the believing women come to you pledging allegiance to you on the condition that they will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery' [Quran 60:12]. By Allah, his hand never touched the hand of a woman in any pledge of allegiance."],[10188,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of Asr before the sun sets, or one rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises, has caught the prayer."],[10189,"The gecko is a devil."],[10190,"From Asbagh, from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."],[10191,"Amputation is for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[10192,"During his illness, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, he would say: O Aisha, I still feel the pain of the food I ate at Khaybar. This is the time I feel my aorta being severed from that poison."],[10193,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night and prostrate in it for as long as one of you would recite fifty verses."],[10194,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[10195,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[10196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eleven rak'ahs at night, saying the salam after every two, and he would make the witr one."],[10197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer, and the women and children slept. The Prophet ﷺ came out and said: The women and children have slept while you are waiting for the prayer."],[10198,"The Prophet ﷺ fasted Ashura and commanded its fasting."],[10199,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded fasting on the day of Ashura, the tenth day."],[10200,"When a believer falls ill, Allah purifies him as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[10201,"Abu Bakr sought permission to enter upon us while I had two servant girls singing, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying on his bed. Abu Bakr scolded me, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his face and said: Leave them, for these are days of Eid."],[10202,"A physiognomist came in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Usama and Zayd were lying down, and he said: These feet are some from some. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with that and it delighted him."],[10203,"He used to pray eleven rak'ahs, making one of them witr. When he finished, he would lie down on his right side."],[10204,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived and performed tawaf of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwah as a single tawaf. Those who had entered ihram for 'umrah performed tawaf of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwah after returning from Mina."],[10205,"I asked Aishah about the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: 'Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'umrah, there is no blame upon him to walk between them' (2:158). I said, 'By Allah, there is no blame on anyone not to walk between them.' She said, 'How bad is what you said, O son of my sister! If it were as you interpreted it, it would be: \"there is no blame upon him not to walk between them.\" But it was only revealed because the Ansar, before they embraced Islam, used to consecrate themselves to the idol Manat, which they worshipped near the House. Whoever had walked around it would deem it sinful to walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah. When they embraced Islam, they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, we deem it sinful to walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah.\" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'umrah, there is no blame upon him to walk between them.\" Aishah said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established the sunnah of walking between them, so it is not appropriate for anyone to abandon walking between them.\""],[10206,"Allah will gather people barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."],[10207,"Apply kohl with ithmid (antimony), for it clears the eyesight and strengthens the hair – or: the hair."],[10208,"Whoever touches his private part must perform wudu'."],[10209,"The servants are the servants of Allah, and the lands are the lands of Allah. Whoever revives any dead land, it belongs to him, and a wrongful vein has no right."],[10210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while I was wearing two bracelets of gold. He said, 'Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than this and finer?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Make it into silver, then perfume it so it will be as if it were gold.'"],[10211,"Whoever receives a favor and mentions it has thanked for it, and whoever pretends to have what he has not been given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."],[10212,"Any woman married without her guardian's consent, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated with her, she is entitled to her dower because of what he has obtained from her. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."],[10213,"Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ja'far b. Rabi'ah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ – similarly. This hadith was narrated by Sulayman b. Musa, Ja'far b. Rabi'ah, and al-Hajjaj b. Artah, all from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."],[10214,"Abdullah b. Wahb narrated to us, from Usamah b. Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."],[10215,"Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He leaves the 'Asr prayer until it is between the two horns of Shaytan—or: upon the two horns of Shaytan—then he stands and pecks them like the pecks of a rooster, not remembering Allah in them except a little."],[10216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith, so he said: \"O 'A'ishah, come so that I may show you my cousin who satirized me.\""],[10217,"When revelation came to me—or: I was informed, or a word similar to it—I did not pass by any stone or tree except that it said: \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[10218,"Whoever stands in Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[10219,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Jabir: \"Shall I give you glad tidings?\" He said: \"May Allah give you glad tidings of good.\" He said: \"Are you aware that Allah brought your father back to life and said: 'My servant, wish upon Me whatever you wish, I will give it to you'? He said: 'O Lord, I wish that You return me so that I may be killed another time.' He said: 'It has already preceded from Me that you will not return to it.'\""],[10220,"Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth. A woman sees in her dream what a man sees; should she perform ghusl?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[10221,"'A'ishah said: \"I said to her: 'Does a woman see that?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to her and said: 'May your right hand be in the dust! Then from where does resemblance come?'\""],[10222,"Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, from Sufyan b. Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah."],[10223,"Ibrahim b. Humayd narrated to us, from Salih, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah."],[10224,"I and Hafsah woke up fasting, then food was gifted to us—and food was scarce on that day—so we broke our fast. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Fast a day in its place.\""],[10225,"Al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated to us, from Salih b. Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah and 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet ﷺ—similarly. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri as mursal, but those we named connected it."],[10226,"He forbade cutting palm trees at night."],[10227,"I used to scrape off the traces of janaba (ritual impurity) from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[10228,"Our mother came to us in Madinah while she was a polytheist, during the truce that was between Quraysh and the Messenger of God ﷺ. We said, 'O Messenger of God, our mother has come to us desiring [contact]; should we maintain ties with her?' He said, 'Yes, so maintain ties with her.'"],[10229,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak (toothstick) at every prayer."],[10230,"‘O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harmful talk about my family has reached me? By God, I have known nothing but good from my family, and they have mentioned a man of whom I have known nothing but good, and he would not visit my family except with me.’ Saʿd b. Muʿādh stood and said, ‘O Messenger of God, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers the Khazraj, you will command us and we will carry out your command.’ She said: Then Saʿd b. ʿUbāda stood — and he was the chief of the Khazraj at that time, and before that he had been a righteous man, but zeal carried him away — and said, ‘You have lied, by the life of God! You will not kill him, by the life of God, and you are not able to kill him.’ Usayd b. Ḥuḍayr stood — and he was the cousin of Saʿd b. Muʿādh — and said to Saʿd b. ʿUbāda, ‘You have lied, by the life of God! We will surely kill him. You are but a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.’ Then the two tribes, the Aws and the Khazraj, rose up against each other until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was standing on the minbar. The Messenger of God ﷺ kept calming them until they settled — or fell silent. She said: I wept that entire day, my tears did not stop, and I could not sleep. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept through the night, unable to sleep, my tears not stopping, and they thought that weeping would split my liver. She said: While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Anṣār asked permission to enter upon me. I gave her permission, and she sat weeping with me. While we were in that state, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, greeted, and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since the time the talk had been said before that, and a month had passed without revelation coming to him. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ pronounced the testimony of faith and then said, ‘Now then, O ʿĀʾisha, it has reached me about you such-and-such. If you are innocent, God will soon declare your innocence; but if you have fallen into a sin, ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges his sin and then repents to God, God turns to him in forgiveness.’ She said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his speech, my tears dried up, so that I did not feel a single drop of them. I said to my father, ‘Respond to the Messenger of God ﷺ about what he said.’ He said, ‘By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.’ I said to my mother, ‘Respond to the Messenger of God about what he said.’ She said, ‘I do not know what to answer the Messenger of God.’ I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Qur’an. I said, ‘By God, if I say that I am innocent — and God knows that I am innocent — you will not believe me in that; and if I confess to a sin — and God knows that I am innocent — you will believe me. By God, I find no example for myself and for you except the father of Yūsuf when he said: “So patience is most fitting, and God is the One sought for help against what you describe.”’ She said: Then I turned away and lay down on my bed. She said: At that time I knew that I was innocent, and that God, Blessed and Exalted, would declare my innocence because of my innocence. But by God, I did not think that God, Blessed and Exalted, would send down revelation concerning my affair that would be recited. My affair in my own estimation was too insignificant for God to speak about me in a matter that would be recited. But I hoped that the Messenger of God ﷺ would see a dream in which God would declare my innocence. She said: By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ had not left when revelation came to him, and he was seized with what would seize him of the intense discomfort, until beads of sweat like pearls would pour from him on a cold day, because of the weight of the speech that was coming down to him. When that state left him, he was relieved, and he was smiling. The first word he spoke was, ‘Indeed, God has sent down your innocence.’ My mother said, ‘Get up and go to the Messenger of God.’ I said, ‘By God, I will not get up to go to him, and I praise none but God.’ She said: Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you” — the ten verses, all of them. She said: When God sent down this concerning my innocence, Abū Bakr said — and he used to spend on Misṭaḥ because of his kinship to him and his poverty — ‘By God, I will not spend on Misṭaḥ after what he said about ʿĀʾisha.’ Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin…” up to His saying: “…that God may forgive you, and God is Forgiving, Merciful.” Abū Bakr said, ‘Yes, by God, I love that God should forgive me,’ and he resumed giving Misṭaḥ the allowance he used to give him, and said, ‘By God, I will never take it away from him.’ ʿĀʾisha said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had consulted Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh about my affair, and she said, ‘O Messenger of God, I guard my hearing and my sight. By God, I have known nothing but good.’ She said: God protected her through her piety, but as for her sister, she perished among those who perished. Al-Zuhrī said: This is what has reached us of the account of these people who narrated to me from ʿĀʾisha."],[10231,"Marriage in the pre-Islamic era was of four types. One of them was the marriage of people today: a man proposes to a man for a woman, gives her a dowry, then marries her. Another type: a man would say to his wife when she became pure from her menses, 'Send word to so-and-so,' and her husband would keep away from her and not touch her at all until her pregnancy from that man became clear; then when her pregnancy became clear, her husband would have intercourse with her. He did that only out of fear of [claiming] the child, and this was called 'marriage.' Another type: a group of men would gather and enter upon a woman, each of them having intercourse with her. When she became pregnant and gave birth, and some nights passed after she delivered, she would send for them, and none of them could refuse to come until they gathered at her place. She would say to them, 'You know what your affair was; I have given birth, and he is your son, or your daughter, O so-and-so,' naming whichever of them she wished by name, and the child would be attributed to that man, who could not refuse. The fourth type: many people would gather and enter upon a woman, and she would not refuse anyone who came to her — these were the prostitutes. They would set up flags at their doors, and whoever wanted them would enter upon them. When one of them became pregnant and gave birth, they would gather for her the physiognomists, then attach the child to the one they thought [was the father], without him being able to refuse. Then when God sent Muḥammad ﷺ with the truth, He abolished the marriages of the pre-Islamic era except the marriage of Islam."],[10232,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not speak rapidly the way you do, but he spoke in a clear, distinct manner that everyone who heard him could memorize."],[10233,"This verse was revealed concerning ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy: 'And the one who took upon himself the greater part of it among them.'"],[10234,"When God, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: 'And let them draw their veils over their bosoms,' the women of the early emigrants came and tore their outer garments and used them as headcovers."],[10235,"The Prophet ﷺ did not fight on behalf of anyone from the people of polytheism except on behalf of the people of the covenant (dhimmis)."],[10236,"When he ﷺ prayed the two rakʿas of the dawn prayer, he would lie down."],[10237,"I knocked on the door while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying, and he walked during his prayer — either to his right or to his left — until he opened it for me."],[10238,"They claim that the woman, the donkey, and the dog cut off the prayer. I saw myself in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ on his family's bed, between him and the qibla."],[10239,"Indeed, there is wisdom in poetry."],[10240,"Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Isa, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwa, from 'A'isha."],[10241,"Fasting on the days of Tashriq is not permitted except for one who is prevented (from completing Hajj) or one performing Tamattu'."],[10242,"When he fell ill, he would recite over himself the Mu'awwidhat and blow."],[10243,"He used to pray eleven rak'ahs, making them odd with one. Then, when he finished his prayer, he would lie down on his right side."],[10244,"The child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone."],[10245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and some people prayed behind him. Then again the following night. Then on the third or fourth night, they gathered in large numbers, but he did not come out to them. When morning came, he said: 'I saw what you did. Nothing prevented me from coming out to you except the fear that it might be made obligatory upon you.'"],[10246,"The teacher of good: everything seeks forgiveness for him, even the fish in the sea."],[10247,"Verily, the seeker of knowledge: the angels spread their wings for him and seek forgiveness for him."],[10248,"The death of a scholar is a breach in Islam that cannot be filled as long as night and day alternate."],[10249,"Quraysh lampooned (the Muslims). The Muslims came to Ka'b b. Malik and said: 'Respond on our behalf.' He said: 'Ask permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They asked permission of the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave permission. So he strove but did not achieve (the desired effect). Then they came to Hassan b. Thabit and invited him. Hassan came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I fear that you may lampoon Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith.' Hassan said: 'I will pluck you from them as a hair is plucked from dough. Verily, I have a tongue (skill in poetry) such that I would not be pleased to have the tongue of anyone else in exchange for it.' Then he stuck out his tongue, as if it were the tongue of a snake, with a black mole at its tip. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him permission, and he cured, satisfied, and sufficed."],[10250,"I entered upon 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz while he was governor of Madinah, and with him were a group of his companions. Scholars from various regions had gathered with him, and they were asking about this verse: 'And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans, then marry those that please you of women' until His saying: 'And give the women their dowers graciously.' 'Urwa said: 'A'isha ؓ narrated to me that it was revealed concerning orphan girls under the guardianship of men. An orphan girl would be in the care of a man, and she would be unattractive, but possess wealth. He would not marry her because of her unattractiveness, nor would he let her marry someone else, until she died and he would inherit from her. If he did marry her, he would keep her without being just to her in giving her due. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans, then leave them and do not marry them. Marry those that please you of women, two, three, or four. But if you fear that you will not be just, then one, or those your right hands possess. That is more suitable that you may not incline (to injustice),' meaning: so that you do not deviate. 'And give the women their dowers graciously'—an obligatory gift. Then after this verse was revealed: 'And they ask you concerning women. Say: Allah gives you a ruling about them and what is recited to you in the Book concerning orphan girls to whom you do not give what is prescribed for them, and you desire to marry them.' Thus this other verse lightened (the matter)."],[10251,"They poured over me from seven water-skins without untying their ties."],[10252,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to sleep, he would join his hands, blow into them, and then recite: “Say, He is God, the One,” “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,” and “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn.” Then he would wipe with them his face, his head, and the rest of his body."],[10253,"I did not comprehend my parents except that they were following the religion, and not a day passed without the Messenger of God ﷺ coming to us at the two ends of the day, morning and evening. When the Muslims were tested, Abu Bakr set out as an emigrant toward Abyssinia until, when he reached al-Ghimad, Ibn al-Daghinah met him and said, “Where do you intend to go, O Abu Bakr?” Abu Bakr said, “My people have driven me out, so I intend to wander in the land and worship my Lord.” Ibn al-Daghinah said, “O Abu Bakr, someone like you does not go out. You provide for the destitute, maintain family ties, bear the burden of the weak, host the guest, and assist in the calamities of truth. So I am your protector; return and worship your Lord in your own land.” So he returned, and Ibn al-Daghinah traveled with him. Ibn al-Daghinah went around among the nobles of Quraysh in the evening and said to them, “Abu Bakr should not go out; a man like him does not go out, who provides for the destitute, maintains family ties, bears the burden of the weak, hosts the guest, and assists in the calamities of truth.” Quraysh did not reject the words of Ibn al-Daghinah and said, “Tell Abu Bakr to worship his Lord in his house and pray in it, and not harm us nor make it public, for we fear he will tempt our sons and women.” Zayd b. al-Daghinah said, “He will not make his prayer public nor recite outside his house.” Then he told Abu Bakr what they said and what they replied. So Abu Bakr took a mosque in the courtyard of his house and would recite the Qur'an, and the women and children of the polytheists would pass by him and look at him. He was a man who wept much and could not control his eyes when reciting the Qur'an. That alarmed the nobles of Quraysh among the polytheists, so they sent to Ibn al-Daghinah and said, “We sheltered Abu Bakr under your protection on condition that he worship his Lord in his house, but he has made prayer and recitation public, and we fear he will tempt our sons and women. He has violated—I think he said—what you had stipulated for him, that he worship his Lord in his house, so let him return your protection.” Aisha said: So Ibn al-Daghinah came to Abu Bakr and said, “You know what I pledged to you. Either you do that—or something similar—or you return my protection to me, for I hate that the Arabs should say that I betrayed a man to whom I had given protection.” Abu Bakr said, “I have returned your protection to you.” Abu Bakr prepared to emigrate and bought two riding camels, and he fed them leaves of the samur tree—that is, khabet—for four months. Ibn Shihab said: Urwah said: Aisha said: While we were sitting one day in Abu Bakr's house at noon, a man said to Abu Bakr, “This is the Messenger of God coming”—I think he said, and it was a time when he had not been coming to us—so Abu Bakr said, “By God, nothing has brought him at this hour except a matter.” She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came and asked permission, and he was granted permission and entered. The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, “Send out those who are with you.” Abu Bakr said, “They are only your family, may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God said, “For I have been permitted to depart.” Abu Bakr said, “The companionship, may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of God?” The Messenger of God said, “Yes.” Abu Bakr said, “Then take, may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of God, one of my two riding camels.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “For its price.” Aisha said: So he took one of them, and we prepared them and made for them a provision in a leather bag. Asma’ cut one of her belts and tied with it the mouth of the bag, and from that she was called Dhat al-Nitaq. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Bakr went to a cave called Thawr. Abdullah b. Abu Bakr, a young boy, would stay the night with them, then leave them at the end of the night and be with Quraysh in Makkah by morning. He would hear no matter without memorizing it, and would bring them that. Amir b. Fuhayrah would pasture for them a ewe given as a gift, and would bring it to them to rest when an hour of the night had passed. He did that every night of those three nights."],[10254,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade men and women from bathhouses, then he permitted men to use them with waist-wrappers."],[10255,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out at night, and I followed him. He came to al-Baqi’—or she said: the graveyard—and said, “Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people, and we, God willing, will join you. O God, do not deprive us of their reward and do not test us after them.”"],[10256,"Umar came upon him in the market while he was bargaining for a woolen cloak, and said, “What is this, O Amr?” He said, “A cloak I am buying to give as charity.” Umar said to him, “Then you are you, indeed.” Then he came upon him later and said, “O Amr, what happened with the cloak?” He said, “I gave it as charity.” He said, “To whom?” He said, “To a thin woman he had married…” He said, “Did you not claim that you would give it as charity?” He said, “Yes, but I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whatever you give them is charity for you.’” He said: Umar said, “O Amr, do not lie about the Messenger of God ﷺ!” He said, “By God, I will not leave you until you come to the Mother of the Believers, Aisha.” He said, “O Amr, do not lie about the Messenger of God!” So they asked permission to see Aisha, and Amr said, “I adjure you by God, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whatever you give them is charity for you’?” She said, “O God, yes. O God, yes.” Umar said, “Where was I from this? The striking of deals in the markets distracted me.”"],[10257,"I and Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman entered upon Aisha, and Aisha told us: A poor man came to the door while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, so I ordered a woman who was with me to hand him something. When she took it to hand it to the poor man, I said, “Bring it so I may look.” He said, “O Aisha, does nothing go out except with your knowledge?” I said, “Nothing goes out except with my knowledge.” He said, “Do not count, lest God count against you.”"],[10258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed six rak’ahs with four prostrations."],[10259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was not more steadfast in any supererogatory prayer than he was—or: more committed than he was—to the two rak’ahs—I think she said: to the two rak’ahs after Dhuhr."],[10260,"Aisha told me that she said to the players: I wish I could see them. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, and I stood at the door looking between his ear and his shoulder while they were playing in the mosque."],[10261,"The sun eclipsed, and she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood with the people for a long standing, then bowed and prostrated. When he bowed he said, “God is greater,” and when he raised his head he said, “God hears whoever praises Him.” Then he prayed six rak’ahs in it until men fainted, until buckets of water were poured on them. When the sun cleared, he addressed us, praised God and extolled Him, then said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of God by which He frightens His servants. Whichever of them eclipses, pray until it clears.” And he prayed with them until it cleared."],[10262,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not die until women were made lawful for him."],[10263,"(M) - Ibn Jurayj said: And Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard a man relating it to 'Ata from 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr: :"],[10264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until women became lawful for him as many as he wished."],[10265,"It is not lawful to kill a Muslim except in three cases: a married adulterer who is stoned, a man who kills another deliberately and is executed for it, and a man who leaves Islam and is killed."],[10266,"Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufay', from 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet ﷺ."],[10267,"When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory."],[10268,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from one vessel."],[10269,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from one vessel, both of us dipping into it together. And I would not do more than pour three handfuls over my head."],[10270,"The Prophet ﷺ used to stay with Zaynab bt. Jahsh and drink honey at her place. Hafsah and I agreed that if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon either of us, she should say: 'I find the smell of maghafir on you; have you eaten maghafir?' Then he entered upon one of them, and she said that to him. He said: 'No, rather I drank honey at Zaynab bt. Jahsh's, and I will not do it again.' Then it was revealed: 'O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you...' up to His saying: 'And when the Prophet confided to one of his wives a certain matter' - his saying: 'Rather, I drank honey.'"],[10271,"'Umar b. Hafs narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Thabit b. 'Ubayd, from al-Qasim, from 'A'ishah - with a similar meaning."],[10272,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, (what about) those who give what they give' or he said: '[and those who give what they give] while their hearts are trembling?'"],[10273,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, 'Abd Allah b. Jud'an used to feed the guest, keep ties of kinship, and do (good deeds). Will that benefit him?' He said: 'No. He never once said: Forgive me my sin on the Day of Reckoning.'"],[10274,"When definitive verses were revealed - they are the foundation of the Book - and others ambiguous, 'as for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous of it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you see those who dispute about it, they are the ones Allah, Blessed and Exalted, meant; so beware of them.'"],[10275,"My father narrated to me, from ‘Ali b. Zayd, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ — similarly. This hadith was narrated thus by Ayyub, ‘Ali b. Zayd, and Abu ‘Amir al-Khazzaz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah. And it was narrated by Hammad b. Salamah and Yazid b. Ibrahim, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."],[10276,"Whoever is questioned closely about the reckoning will be punished. She said: I said, “O Messenger of God, does not God, blessed and exalted be He, say: ‘He will be judged with an easy reckoning’?” He said: “That is the presentation, and whoever is questioned closely about the reckoning will be punished.”"],[10277,"Do not count, lest He count against you."],[10278,"The Jews passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “Al-sam (death be upon you).” He said, “And upon you.” I said, “Rather upon you be death and the curse.” He said, “O Aishah, did you not hear me reply to them? God loves gentleness.”"],[10279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away between my chest and my throat, in my house and on my day."],[10280,"No trait was more hateful to the Messenger of God ﷺ than lying. If he learned that someone had done anything of that, it would not leave his heart until he knew that the person had made repentance."],[10281,"He is not one of us who does not chant the Quran."],[10282,"He is not one of us who does not chant the Quran."],[10283,"When I was accused of what I was accused of, I wanted to throw myself into a well."],[10284,"Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah."],[10285,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded ‘Abd al-Rahman to have Aishah perform ‘umrah — I think he said: from al-Tan’im."],[10286,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded ‘Abd al-Rahman to have her perform ‘umrah from al-Tan’im."],[10287,"That he cursed — or a word like it — those who imitate the creation of God."],[10288,"No trait was more hateful to the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ than lying. A man would tell a lie in the Prophet’s ﷺ presence, and it would remain in his heart against him until he knew that he had repented of it."],[10289,"It reached Aishah that a woman had worn sandals, and Aishah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the masculine-acting women."],[10290,"The most hateful of men to God is the quarrelsome disputant."],[10291,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the meat of sacrificial animals, then later allowed it. He also forbade visiting graves, then later allowed it — I think he said: For it reminds of the Hereafter."],[10292,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, reciting at night. He said: Praise be to God, who has placed in my community someone like him."],[10293,"When he saw a cloud formation, his face would change; and when it rained, his face cleared."],[10294,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram, I perfumed him with the best of my perfume."],[10295,"The month is twenty-nine [days]."],[10296,"The nephew of a people is one of them."],[10297,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a woman suffering from istihadah: Perform ghusl and do wudu for every prayer."],[10298,"The quickest of people to perish are your people. I said: Why, may God make me your ransom? He said: This clan of Quraysh — death finds them sweet, and people envy them. I said: What then is the survival of people after them? He said: They are the backbone of humanity; when they perish, humanity perishes."],[10299,"How excellent a condiment is vinegar."],[10300,"Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak cannot take their right from the strong."],[10301,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his bed, and I thought that he had gone to one of his wives. Then I found him. He stood up quickly and took his cloak on his shoulder, and I took my waist-wrapper. I said: What is he doing? He went out and I went out behind him. Whenever he hastened, I hastened, until he came to al-Baqi'. He raised his hands supplicating three times, then he left. He hastened and I hastened, until I entered the house and he entered after me. He said: What is the matter with you? Did you fear that Allah and His Messenger would be unjust to you? Jibril ﷺ came to me and commanded me to go to the people of al-Baqi' and seek forgiveness for them."],[10302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a lamp in the house of al-Zubayr, so he said: O Aishah, I think Asma' has given birth. Do not name him until I name him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and named him and chewed a date and put it in his mouth (tahnik)."],[10303,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ with her image on a green piece of cloth and said: O Muhammad, this is your wife in this world and the Hereafter."],[10304,"I said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, a man divorced his wife three times, and she married another man, and she threw her headcover down in front of him, then he divorced her. Is she lawful for the first husband? She said: O son of my sister, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was asked about the like of what you asked me, and he said: She is not lawful for the latter until he tastes her sweetness (i.e., has intercourse with her)."],[10305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me while he was glad of eye and good of soul, and he returned while he was sad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you left me while you were glad of eye and good of soul, and you returned while you were sad! He said: I entered the Ka'bah, and I wish I had not entered it - or that I had not done it - I fear that I may have caused hardship for my Ummah."],[10306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and saw some meat, so he said: Who sent this? I said: Uthman. She said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his hands supplicating for Uthman."],[10307,"I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them; and from the meat of sacrifices - I think he said: that you should keep them - so eat them. Or she said: He granted a concession regarding them for them."],[10308,"We had a slave girl who used to sing. The Prophet ﷺ entered while she was in that state. Then Umar sought permission to enter, and she jumped up. The Prophet ﷺ laughed, so I said: Why are you laughing, O Messenger of Allah? So she informed him, and he said: I will not leave until I hear what you heard - or: what the Prophet ﷺ heard from her. So he ordered her and she made him listen."],[10309,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[10310,"That the Prophet ﷺ said about this verse: 'It is He who sent down upon you the Book; in it are verses that are precise - they are the foundation of the Book - and others unspecific.' He said: When you see those who follow what is unspecific of it, they are those, so beware of them."],[10311,"When the pain of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became severe, he said: “Bring me an inkwell and a shoulder blade—or a sheet—so that I may write for Abu Bakr a document, after which the people will not differ concerning him.” Then he said: “Allah forbid that the people should differ concerning Abu Bakr.”"],[10312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a pot, took a bone with meat from it, ate, then went to prayer without performing ablution, but rinsed his mouth."],[10313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For a boy, two sheep of equal age—I think he said—and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[10314,"Do not count, lest it be counted against you."],[10315,"Musa b. Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ with the like of it."],[10316,"At night, three covered vessels would be placed for the Prophet ﷺ: a vessel for his purification, a vessel for his drink, and a vessel for his tooth-stick."],[10317,"Regarding tayammum: two strikes—one strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows."],[10318,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in ihram."],[10319,"“Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning will perish.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, as for one who is given his book in his right hand, he will be judged with an easy reckoning!” He said, “That is the presentation.”"],[10320,"He used to pray while I was in front of him."],[10321,"The Prophet ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity during Ramadan without having had a wet dream, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[10322,"I perfumed him with the best perfume I could find—may my father and mother be his ransom ﷺ."],[10323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never entered upon me after the afternoon prayer except that he prayed two rak'ahs."],[10324,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw a cloud, his face would change, and he would go back and forth. Then when it rained, he would be relieved. I mentioned that to him, and he said: \"I am not sure that it might be as He said: 'When they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys' (Quran 46:24).\""],[10325,"Allah and His Messenger are the mawla of one who has no mawla, and the maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir."],[10326,"Do not revile the dead, for they have reached what they sent ahead."],[10327,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and he turned to him. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is this not so-and-so?\" He said: \"The worst of people in station is the one whom people avoid due to his obscenity.\""],[10328,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and he brought him near and seated him close. When he left, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is this not so-and-so whom you used to mention with evil?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"You flattered him—or brought him near—and seated him close.\" He said: \"The worst of people are those who are honored to avoid their evil.\""],[10329,"Safiyyah menstruated, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is she holding us back?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, she had already performed the circumambulation of the House when she made her final departure.\" He said: \"Then let her depart.\""],[10330,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were in a state of ihram. When a group of travelers passed by and drew near us, we lowered a part of our veils over our faces."],[10331,"I saw the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a state of ihram."],[10332,"When the sins of a servant become many and he finds nothing to expiate them, Allah afflicts him with grief to expiate his sins."],[10333,"There was a wild animal with us. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was present, it settled and remained in its place, neither coming nor going. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, it would come and go."],[10334,"When her innocence was revealed, Abu Bakr kissed her head. She said: \"Will you not excuse me?\" He said: \"Which sky would shade me or which earth would carry me if I said what I do not know?\""],[10335,"Jibril kept enjoining me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[10336,"A woman washing her private parts is from the Sunnah."],[10337,"Whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the Muslims and intends good therein, Allah appoints for him a righteous minister: if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he assists him."],[10338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him."],[10339,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[10340,"What did the Prophet ﷺ used to do in his house? She said: He mended his sandal and sewed his garment."],[10341,"Spirits are assembled troops."],[10342,"He used to recite in the Witr: in the first rak'ah, 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'; in the second, 'Say: O disbelievers'; and in the third, 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[10343,"I asked Aishah: What did the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Witr? She said: He used to recite in the two rak'ahs after which he performed the Witr: in the first of them 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' and in the second 'Say: O disbelievers,' then he said the salam. And he used to recite in the rak'ah in which he performed the Witr: 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak,' and 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind.'"],[10344,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to observe i'tikaf, he prayed the Fajr prayer, then entered his place of i'tikaf. And when he intended to observe i'tikaf in the last ten nights of Ramadan, he ordered that his tent be set up, and it was pitched. When he had prayed Fajr, he looked and saw that the tents had been pitched."],[10345,"She was asked about performing ghusl on Friday. She said: The people used to be laborers for themselves, so it was said to them: 'If only you would perform ghusl.' – I think the hadith contains: 'So they would go to the prayer in their working clothes, and it was said to them: If only you would perform ghusl.'"],[10346,"Abu Bakr entered upon me while a Jewish woman was reciting ruqyah over me, and he said: Treat her with the Book of Allah. A Jewish woman came and I gave her a piece of bread, and she said: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. The Prophet ﷺ entered and I informed him of her words, and he said: The punishment of the grave is true. I never saw him after any prayer he prayed except that he sought refuge in it from the punishment of the grave."],[10347,"Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ—similarly."],[10348,"I never saw him after any prayer he performed except that he sought refuge in it from the punishment of the grave."],[10349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rak'ahs during the eclipse."],[10350,"When Ja'far's death was announced, it was said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Would you prohibit weeping?\" He said—I think he said to a man: \"Go to them and prohibit them.\" He said: \"I went, but they did not obey me. Then a second time, then a third time. He said: 'Return to them and throw dust in their faces.'\"—and I was peeking through the crack of the door—so I said to the man: \"May Allah rub your nose in the dust! By Allah, you have not left the Messenger of Allah alone, and you are not going to do it\"—meaning, what he commanded him to do, to throw dust in their faces."],[10351,"I used to play with dolls, and my playmates would come to me, but they would feel shy. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, he would send them in to me."],[10352,"\"The quickest of you to join me will be the one with the longest hand.\" So they would measure to see which of them had the longest hand."],[10353,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with five nights remaining of Dhu al-Qa'dah, intending only Hajj. When we approached Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded those who did not have a sacrificial animal to exit ihram after circumambulating the House. On the Day of Sacrifice, meat was brought to us. I said, \"What is this?\" It was said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered cows on behalf of his wives.\""],[10354,"I used to comb the Prophet's ﷺ hair while he was in i'tikaf, and he would not enter the house except for a need—or: for a human need. He would bring his head close to me, and I would comb it while he was in i'tikaf."],[10355,"If a slave woman commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery again, flog her. Then sell her, even for a rope."],[10356,"Amputation is for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[10357,"Amputation is for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[10358,"I entered Paradise and heard a recitation in it. I said, \"Who is this?\" It was said, \"Harithah b. al-Nu'man.\" Thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness."],[10359,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the voice of Abu Musa reciting, and said: “This one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud.”"],[10360,"He used to treat the sick by incantation, placing his finger on the ground and saying: “With the dust of our land and the saliva of some of us, our sick one is healed by the permission of our Lord.”"],[10361,"Breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking it when he was alive."],[10362,"The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[10363,"The Messenger of God cursed the briber and the one who accepts a bribe."],[10364,"I perfumed the Messenger of God ﷺ with my own hands before he departed (from Muzdalifah)."],[10365,"Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr b. Muhammad b. Amr b. Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ – similar to that."],[10366,"Aflah b. Abi al-Quays came to me asking permission to enter after the veil had been prescribed for me, so I refused him. He was my paternal uncle by breastfeeding. She said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “What would it have mattered if you had allowed him? He is your uncle.” She said: I said, “O Messenger of God, it was the woman who breastfed me, not the man.” He said: “He is your uncle.” He said: Aishah used to say: “Breastfeeding makes forbidden what is forbidden by birth.”"],[10367,"Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, similar to that – meaning from the Prophet ﷺ."],[10368,"We did not realize the burial of the Messenger of God ﷺ until we heard the sound of the shovels in the last part of the night."],[10369,"Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died when he was eighteen months old, and no funeral prayer was offered over him."],[10370,"We used to hear that Isaf and Na'ilah were a man and a woman from Jurhum who committed adultery inside the Kaaba, and they were transformed into two stones."],[10371,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw from the women what we see, he would have forbidden them as the women of the Children of Israel were forbidden. I have seen us praying the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in our cloaks, and none of us recognized the faces of the others."],[10372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ screened himself with a mat and began to pray, and the people began to pray behind him. He said: O people, take upon yourselves such deeds as you are able, for Allah does not grow weary until you grow weary. And know that the most beloved of deeds to Allah is the most constant, even if it is little."],[10373,"Some men complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about their wives, so he permitted them to strike them. That night, many women visited his wives, and she said: What the Muslim women have encountered! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Strike them, but the best of you will not strike - I think he said."],[10374,"Abd al-A'la b. Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Abdullah b. Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah."],[10375,"The verse of stoning and of suckling was revealed, and they were in a sheet under my bed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, we were distracted by his death, and a domestic animal entered and ate it."],[10376,"I saw the elephant driver and its keeper, both blind and crippled, begging for food in Makkah."],[10377,"Hafsah and I began the day fasting voluntarily. A gift was given to us, and we ate from it. Hafsah quickly went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Fast another day in its place."],[10378,"When he began the prayer, he said the takbir, then said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You."],[10379,"Sahl b. Amir narrated to us, from Malik b. Mighwal, from Ata, who said: I and Ubayd b. Umayr entered upon Aishah, and she mentioned from the Prophet ﷺ - regarding the opening of the prayer - something similar to what Harithah narrated from Amrah from Aishah."],[10380,"There is no zakat on wealth until a year has passed over it."],[10381,"The surplus of water is not to be withheld, nor the water of a well."],[10382,"The one who pretends to have what he has not attained - or: attains - is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."],[10383,"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ began ablution, he would mention the name of Allah."],[10384,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest.\""],[10385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never omitted two rakʿahs after ʿAṣr."],[10386,"He had instructed them not to eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, then he gave them a concession – I think he said: for them."],[10387,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his wives: “The one with the longest hand among you will follow me (i.e., die first).” ʿĀʾishah said: After the death of the Prophet ﷺ, whenever we gathered in the house of one of us, we would stretch our hands against the wall, measuring ourselves. We continued doing that until Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh b. Riʾāb, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, passed away. She was a short woman and was not the tallest of us, so we knew then that by the length of the hand the Prophet ﷺ meant charity. She said: Zaynab was a woman with skillful hands; she used to work, sew – meaning she would work – and give charity in the path of Allah."],[10388,"He would go out in the depths of the night to Baqīʿ al-Gharqad and supplicate for its people. She said: Sometimes he would do that more than once in a single night."],[10389,"Women used to attend the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped in their cloaks, unrecognizable due to the darkness before dawn."],[10390,"Foster relationships make unlawful what birth relationships make unlawful."],[10391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray sitting. When he wanted to bow, he would stand for as long as it takes a person to recite – I think he said: forty verses."],[10392,"The Prophet ﷺ entered and heard the sound of a child crying. He said: “What is the matter with your child that he is crying? Will you not seek a ruqyah for him against the evil eye?”"],[10393,"The people of the Jāhiliyyah used to dye a piece of cotton on the day of ʿaqīqah, then shave the child’s head and place it on his head. The Prophet ﷺ ordered them to put perfume in place of the blood."],[10394,"She wanted to buy Barīrah, but they stipulated her walāʾ (patronage). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Buy her and set her free, for walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free.” Some meat was brought to him, and it was said to him: “This is from what was given in charity to Barīrah.” He said: “It is charity for her and a gift for us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice, and her husband was a free man."],[10395,"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ wanted to sleep or eat while he was junub, he would perform wudu’ as he did for prayer."],[10396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought food from a Jew on credit and gave him his shield as collateral."],[10397,"Indeed, the best of what a man eats is from his own earnings, and his child is from his earnings."],[10398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Safiyyah, so we said, 'She has menstruated.' He said, 'Aqra! — or: Halqa! — I think she will hold us back.' We said, 'She has already performed tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice.' He said, 'Then no; tell her to depart.'"],[10399,"Muhammad b. Ja'far and Ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[10400,"I asked Aishah, 'How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ behave with his family?' She said, 'He was in the service of his family, and when the prayer time came, he would get up for prayer.'"],[10401,"Some people say that prayer is invalidated by a dog, a donkey, and a woman. Many times I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying at night while I was between him and the qiblah. If I needed something, I would slip away from the foot of the bed, disliking [to disturb him]."]]);
